/* GENERATED by lib/ — do not hand-edit; edit exams/<id>/research/q*.json then run lib/merge.py */
window.EXAM_DATA=window.EXAM_DATA||{};window.EXAM_DATA["sapc02"]=[{"id":1,"question_en":"A company needs to architect a hybrid DNS solution. This solution will use an Amazon Route 53 private hosted zone for the domain cloud.example.com for the resources stored within VPCs. The company has the following DNS resolution requirements: On-premises systems should be able to resolve and connect to cloud.example.com. All VPCs should be able to resolve cloud.example.com. There is already an AWS Direct Connect connection between the on-premises corporate network and AWS Transit Gateway. Which architecture should the company use to meet these requirements with the HIGHEST performance?","question_zh":"一家公司需要构建混合 DNS 解决方案。此解决方案将使用域 cloud.example.com 的 Amazon Route 53 私有托管区域来存储 VPC 内的资 源。 该公司有以下 DNS 解析要求： 本地系统应能够解析并连接到 cloud.example.com。 所有 VPC 都应该能够解析 cloud.example.com。 本地企业网络和 AWS Transit Gateway 之间已存在 AWS Direct Connect 连接。 公司应该使用哪种架构来满足这些要求并具有最高的性能？","options_en":{"A":"Associate the private hosted zone to all the VPCs. Create a Route 53 inbound resolver in the shared services VPC. Attach all VPCs to the transit gateway and create forwarding rules in the on-premises DNS server for cloud.example.com that point to the inbound resolver.","B":"Associate the private hosted zone to all the VPCs. Deploy an Amazon EC2 conditional forwarder in the shared services VPC. Attach all VPCs to the transit gateway and create forwarding rules in the on-premises DNS server for cloud.example.com that point to the conditional forwarder.","C":"Associate the private hosted zone to the shared services VPCreate a Route 53 outbound resolver in the shared services VPAttach all VPCs to the transit gateway and create forwarding rules in the on-premises DNS server for cloud.example.com that point to the outbound resolver.","D":"Associate the private hosted zone to the shared services VPC. Create a Route 53 inbound resolver in the shared services VPC. Attach the shared services VPC to the transit gateway and create forwarding rules in the on-premises DNS server for cloud.example.com that point to the inbound resolver."},"options_zh":{"A":"将私有托管区域关联到所有 VPC。在共享服务 VPC 中创建 Route 53 入站解析器。将所有 VPC 连接到中转网关，并在 cloud.example.com 的本地 DNS 服务器中创建指向入站解析器的转发规则。","B":"将私有托管区域关联到所有 VPC。在共享服务 VPC 中部署 Amazon EC2 条件转发器。将所有 VPC 连接到中转网关，并在 cloud.example.com 的本地 DNS 服务器中创建指向条件转发器的转发规则。","C":"将私有托管区域关联到共享服务 VP 在共享服务 VP 中创建 Route 53 出站解析程序将所有 VPC 连接到中转网关，并在 cloud.example.com 的本地 DNS 服务器中创建指向出站的转发规则解析器。","D":"将私有托管区域关联到共享服务 VPC。在共享服务 VPC 中创建 Route 53 入站解析器。将共享服务 VPC 连接到中转网关，并在 cloud.example.com 的本地 DNS 服务器中创建指向入站解析器的转发规则。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":82,"D":18},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Two requirements decide this and HIGHEST performance is the tiebreaker. (1) ALL VPCs must resolve cloud.example.com. A Route 53 private hosted zone (PHZ) is resolvable only from inside VPCs that are ASSOCIATED with it: AWS docs state 'To get an answer from a private hosted zone you also have to be running an EC2 instance in one of the associated VPCs' and 'the VPC Resolver detects that queries are within a private namespace based on VPC to hosted zone associations.' Transit Gateway provides network reachability, NOT DNS resolution; each VPC still uses its own VPC+2 Resolver, which only knows a PHZ if that VPC is associated. So the PHZ must be associated with ALL VPCs. (2) On-premises must resolve cloud.example.com. The correct, AWS-managed construct is an INBOUND Resolver endpoint: on-prem DNS forwards cloud.example.com to the inbound endpoint, which hands the query to the VPC Resolver of the VPC the endpoint sits in. AWS docs are explicit: 'If you want VPC Resolver to resolve inbound DNS queries using records in a private hosted zone, associate the private hosted zone with the VPC that you created the inbound endpoint in.' Option A does exactly this: PHZ associated to ALL VPCs (which includes the shared services VPC hosting the inbound endpoint), a managed inbound Resolver endpoint in the shared services VPC, and all VPCs attached to the Transit Gateway. Option D fails requirement (1): associating the PHZ only to the shared services VPC and attaching only that VPC means instances in the other VPCs cannot resolve cloud.example.com via their own resolver. Option C uses an OUTBOUND endpoint (wrong direction, VPC->on-prem) and again associates the PHZ only to the shared services VPC. Option B replaces the managed Resolver endpoint with a self-managed EC2 conditional forwarder, which is higher operational overhead and lower availability/performance, so it is not 'HIGHEST performance.' Verdict: A. The exam-dump answer D is wrong; the community answer A is correct.","explanation_zh":"本題由兩個需求決定，而 HIGHEST performance（最高效能）是決勝條件。(1) 所有 VPC 都必須能解析 cloud.example.com。Route 53 private hosted zone（PHZ）只能在已與其關聯（associated）的 VPC 內部被解析：AWS 文件明言「要從 private hosted zone 取得回應，你的 EC2 實例必須跑在其中一個已關聯的 VPC 中」，且「VPC Resolver 是依據 VPC 與 hosted zone 的關聯關係來判斷查詢屬於私有命名空間」。Transit Gateway 只提供網路可達性，並不提供 DNS 解析；每個 VPC 仍使用自己的 VPC+2 Resolver，只有該 VPC 被關聯時才能解析 PHZ。因此 PHZ 必須關聯到所有 VPC。(2) 地端（on-premises）必須能解析 cloud.example.com。正確且由 AWS 管理的架構是 INBOUND Resolver endpoint：地端 DNS 將 cloud.example.com 轉發到 inbound endpoint，再交給該 endpoint 所在 VPC 的 VPC Resolver。AWS 文件明確說明：「若要讓 VPC Resolver 使用 private hosted zone 中的記錄解析 inbound 查詢，請將該 private hosted zone 關聯到你建立 inbound endpoint 的那個 VPC」。選項 A 正是如此：PHZ 關聯到所有 VPC（包含承載 inbound endpoint 的 shared services VPC）、在 shared services VPC 內建立受管理的 inbound Resolver endpoint，並將所有 VPC 連接到 Transit Gateway。選項 D 不滿足需求 (1)：僅將 PHZ 關聯到 shared services VPC、且只連接該 VPC，意味著其他 VPC 的實例無法透過自己的 resolver 解析 cloud.example.com。選項 C 使用 OUTBOUND endpoint（方向錯誤，VPC->地端），並同樣只將 PHZ 關聯到 shared services VPC。選項 B 以自建自管的 EC2 conditional forwarder 取代受管理的 Resolver endpoint，運維負擔更高、可用性與效能更低，不符合「最高效能」。結論：A。考古題庫答案 D 是錯的；社群答案 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"It correctly associates the PHZ to all VPCs and uses the inbound direction, but replaces the AWS-managed Route 53 Resolver inbound endpoint with a self-managed EC2 conditional forwarder. That adds operational overhead and a single point of failure, with lower availability and throughput than the AZ-redundant managed Resolver endpoint, so it does not meet the 'HIGHEST performance' qualifier.","why_zh":"它正確地將 PHZ 關聯到所有 VPC 並使用 inbound 方向，但以自建自管的 EC2 conditional forwarder 取代由 AWS 管理的 Route 53 Resolver inbound endpoint。這增加了運維負擔與單點故障，可用性和吞吐量低於具 AZ 冗餘的受管理 Resolver endpoint，因此不符合「最高效能」要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Two errors. First, it uses an OUTBOUND Resolver endpoint, which forwards queries FROM VPCs TO on-premises, the wrong direction for letting on-prem resolve cloud.example.com (that needs an inbound endpoint). Second, it associates the PHZ only to the shared services VPC, so the other VPCs cannot resolve cloud.example.com.","why_zh":"兩個錯誤。第一，它使用 OUTBOUND Resolver endpoint，那是將查詢從 VPC 轉發到地端（方向相反），無法讓地端解析 cloud.example.com（那需要 inbound endpoint）。第二，它只將 PHZ 關聯到 shared services VPC，其他 VPC 因此無法解析 cloud.example.com。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the exam-dump answer but it is wrong. It associates the PHZ only to the shared services VPC and attaches only that VPC to the TGW. The other VPCs' instances use their own VPC+2 Resolver, which has no association with the PHZ, so they CANNOT resolve cloud.example.com, violating the requirement that ALL VPCs must resolve it. TGW reachability does not equal DNS resolution. The inbound endpoint in the shared services VPC does satisfy the on-prem requirement, but the all-VPCs requirement fails.","why_zh":"這是題庫答案，但是錯的。它只將 PHZ 關聯到 shared services VPC，並只將該 VPC 連到 TGW。其他 VPC 的實例使用自己的 VPC+2 Resolver，與 PHZ 無關聯，因此無法解析 cloud.example.com，違反「所有 VPC 都必須能解析」的要求。TGW 可達性不等於 DNS 解析。shared services VPC 中的 inbound endpoint 確實滿足地端解析的要求，但「所有 VPC」這個要求未滿足。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/resolver.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/resolver-overview-forward-network-to-vpc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/hosted-zones-private.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/resolver-choose-vpc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/hosted-zone-private-associate-vpcs.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":2,"question_en":"A company is providing weather data over a REST-based API to several customers. The API is hosted by Amazon API Gateway and is integrated with different AWS Lambda functions for each API operation. The company uses Amazon Route 53 for DNS and has created a resource record of weather.example.com. The company stores data for the API in Amazon DynamoDB tables. The company needs a solution that will give the API the ability to fail over to a different AWS Region. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司通过基于 REST 的 API 向多个客户提供天气数据。该 API 由 Amazon API Gateway 托管，并针对每个 API 操作与不同的 AWS Lambda 函数集成。该公司使用 Amazon Route 53 作为 DNS，并创建了weather.example.com 的资源记录。该公司将 API 的数据存储在 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。该公司需要一种解决方案，使 API 能够故障转移到不同的 AWS 区域。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy a new set of Lambda functions in a new Region. Update the API Gateway API to use an edge-optimized API endpoint with Lambda functions from both Regions as targets. Convert the DynamoDB tables to global tables.","B":"Deploy a new API Gateway API and Lambda functions in another Region. Change the Route 53 DNS record to a multivalue answer. Add both API Gateway APIs to the answer. Enable target health monitoring. Convert the DynamoDB tables to global tables.","C":"Deploy a new API Gateway API and Lambda functions in another Region. Change the Route 53 DNS record to a failover record. Enable target health monitoring. Convert the DynamoDB tables to global tables.","D":"Deploy a new API Gateway API in a new Region. Change the Lambda functions to global functions. Change the Route 53 DNS record to a multivalue answer. Add both API Gateway APIs to the answer. Enable target health monitoring. Convert the DynamoDB tables to global tables."},"options_zh":{"A":"在新区域中部署一组新的 Lambda 函数。更新 API Gateway API 以使用边缘优化的 API 终端节点，并将来自两个区域的 Lambda 函数作为目标。将 DynamoDB 表转换为全局表。","B":"在另一个区域部署新的 API Gateway API 和 Lambda 函数。将 Route 53 DNS 记录更改为多值答案。将两个 API Gateway API 添加 到答案中。启用目标健康监控。将 DynamoDB 表转换为全局表。","C":"在另一个区域部署新的 API Gateway API 和 Lambda 函数。将 Route 53 DNS 记录更改为故障转移记录。启用目标健康监控。将 DynamoDB 表转换为全局表。","D":"在新区域中部署新的 API Gateway API。将 Lambda 函数更改为全局函数。将 Route 53 DNS 记录更改为多值答案。将两个 API Gateway API 添加到答案中。启用目标健康监控。将 DynamoDB 表转换为全局表。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":97},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":3,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations with a single OU named Production to manage multiple accounts. All accounts are members of the Production OU. Administrators use deny list SCPs in the root of the organization to manage access to restricted services. The company recently acquired a new business unit and invited the new unit’s existing AWS account to the organization. Once onboarded, the administrators of the new business unit discovered that they are not able to update existing AWS Config rules to meet the company’s policies. Which option will allow administrators to make changes and continue to enforce the current policies without introducing additional long-term maintenance?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 和名为 Production 的单个 OU 来管理多个账户。所有帐户都是生产 OU 的成员。管理员使用组织根目 录中的拒绝列表 SCP 来管理对受限服务的访问。 该公司最近收购了一个新的业务部门，并邀请该新部门的现有 AWS 账户加入该组织。入职后，新业务部门的管理员发现他们无法更 新现有的 AWS Config 规则以满足公司的政策。 哪个选项将允许管理员进行更改并继续执行当前策略，而无需引入额外的长期维护？","options_en":{"A":"Remove the organization’s root SCPs that limit access to AWS Config. Create AWS Service Catalog products for the company’s standard AWS Config rules and deploy them throughout the organization, including the new account.","B":"Create a temporary OU named Onboarding for the new account. Apply an SCP to the Onboarding OU to allow AWS Config actions. Move the new account to the Production OU when adjustments to AWS Config are complete.","C":"Convert the organization’s root SCPs from deny list SCPs to allow list SCPs to allow the required services only. Temporarily apply an SCP to the organization’s root that allows AWS Config actions for principals only in the new account.","D":"Create a temporary OU named Onboarding for the new account. Apply an SCP to the Onboarding OU to allow AWS Config actions. Move the organization’s root SCP to the Production OU. Move the new account to the Production OU when adjustments to AWS Config are complete."},"options_zh":{"A":"删除组织限制对 AWS Config 访问的根 SCP。为公司的标准 AWS Config 规则创建 AWS Service Catalog 产品，并将其部署到整个 组织（包括新账户）。","B":"为新帐户创建一个名为 Onboarding 的临时 OU。将 SCP 应用到 Onboarding OU 以允许 AWS Config 操作。对 AWS Config 的调整完 成后，将新账户移至生产 OU。","C":"将组织的根 SCP 从拒绝列表 SCP 转换为允许列表 SCP，以仅允许所需的服务。临时将 SCP 应用于组织的根，仅允许新账户中 的委托人执行 AWS Config 操作。","D":"为新帐户创建一个名为 Onboarding 的临时 OU。将 SCP 应用到 Onboarding OU 以允许 AWS Config 操作。将组织的根 SCP 移至生 产 OU。对 AWS Config 的调整完成后，将新账户移至生产 OU。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":83},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The root cause is a deny-list SCP attached at the organization ROOT that blocks AWS Config actions. Per the AWS Organizations SCP evaluation rules, for a permission to be denied for an account, ANY SCP in the direct path from the root through each OU to the account can deny it, and a Deny applied at the root or an OU is evaluated for all OUs and member accounts underneath it and cannot be overridden by an Allow at a lower OU. This means Option B fails: creating an Onboarding OU with an Allow-Config SCP does nothing while the root-level Config deny still reaches every account beneath the root, including the Onboarding OU. Option D works because it relocates the deny SCP off the root and onto the Production OU; the new account is placed in a separate Onboarding OU that is a sibling of Production and therefore not in the deny's direct path, so administrators can update Config rules. When adjustments are complete, the account is moved into the Production OU where the deny now lives, restoring full enforcement. Because all existing accounts already reside in Production, moving the guardrail from root to Production preserves identical coverage and introduces no additional long-term maintenance.","explanation_zh":"問題根源是掛在組織 root 的 deny-list SCP，它封鎖了 AWS Config 動作。依照 AWS Organizations 的 SCP 評估規則：要拒絕某帳戶的權限，從 root 經各 OU 到該帳戶直接路徑上的「任何一個」SCP 都能拒絕，且掛在 root 或 OU 的 Deny 會套用到其下所有 OU 與成員帳戶，無法被較低 OU 的 Allow 覆寫。因此選項 B 無效：即使建立 Onboarding OU 並加上允許 Config 的 SCP，root 層的 Config deny 仍會延伸到 root 底下每個帳戶（含 Onboarding OU）。選項 D 可行，因為它把 deny SCP 從 root 移到 Production OU；新帳戶放進與 Production 並列（sibling）的 Onboarding OU，不在 deny 的直接路徑上，管理員即可更新 Config 規則。調整完成後把帳戶移入 Production OU（deny 已改掛於此），即恢復完整強制。由於現有所有帳戶原本就都在 Production，把護欄從 root 移到 Production 可維持完全相同的涵蓋範圍，且不引入額外的長期維運負擔。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Removing the root SCP guardrail abandons the preventive deny-list enforcement that blocks restricted services org-wide. AWS Service Catalog products only deploy/standardize Config rules; they do not create a deny boundary, and maintaining the products and their versions is ongoing work — violating 'continue to enforce current policies without additional long-term maintenance.'","why_zh":"移除 root SCP 護欄等於放棄封鎖限制服務、涵蓋全組織的預防性 deny-list 強制。AWS Service Catalog 產品只是部署／標準化 Config 規則，不會建立 deny 邊界，且維護產品與其版本是持續性工作，違反『繼續強制現行政策且不增加長期維護』的要求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Technically broken: the root-level deny SCP on AWS Config still applies to the account no matter which OU it sits in, because an explicit Deny in the direct path (the root) cannot be overridden by an Allow at a lower OU. The new account would remain blocked from updating Config rules.","why_zh":"技術上不可行：root 層級對 AWS Config 的 deny SCP 不論帳戶在哪個 OU 都仍會套用，因為直接路徑上（root）的明確 Deny 無法被較低 OU 的 Allow 覆寫。新帳戶仍無法更新 Config 規則。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Converting all root deny-list SCPs to allow-list SCPs is a large, error-prone redesign requiring enumeration of every permitted service and perpetual upkeep as services change (high long-term maintenance), and a root-level Allow for Config still cannot override an existing Deny in the path (Deny beats Allow), so it does not reliably unblock the new account.","why_zh":"把所有 root deny-list SCP 轉成 allow-list SCP 是大規模且易出錯的重新設計，需列舉每個允許的服務並隨服務演進永久維護（高長期維運成本）；而且在 root 加上允許 Config 的 Allow 仍無法覆寫路徑上既有的 Deny（Deny 勝過 Allow），無法可靠解封新帳戶。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":4,"question_en":"A company is running a two-tier web-based application in an on-premises data center. The application layer consists of a single server running a stateful application. The application connects to a PostgreSQL database running on a separate server. The application’s user base is expected to grow significantly, so the company is migrating the application and database to AWS. The solution will use Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL, Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling, and Elastic Load Balancing. Which solution will provide a consistent user experience that will allow the application and database tiers to scale?","question_zh":"一家公司正在本地数据中心运行基于 Web 的两层应用程序。应用程序层由运行有状态应用程序的单个服务器组成。该应用程序连接 到在单独服务器上运行的 PostgreSQL 数据库。该应用程序的用户群预计将大幅增长，因此该公司正在将应用程序和数据库迁移到 AWS。该解决方案将使用 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL、Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 和 Elastic Load Balancing。 哪种解决方案将提供一致的用户体验，从而允许应用程序和数据库层扩展？","options_en":{"A":"Enable Aurora Auto Scaling for Aurora Replicas. Use a Network Load Balancer with the least outstanding requests routing algorithm and sticky sessions enabled.","B":"Enable Aurora Auto Scaling for Aurora writers. Use an Application Load Balancer with the round robin routing algorithm and sticky sessions enabled.","C":"Enable Aurora Auto Scaling for Aurora Replicas. Use an Application Load Balancer with the round robin routing and sticky sessions enabled.","D":"Enable Aurora Scaling for Aurora writers. Use a Network Load Balancer with the least outstanding requests routing algorithm and sticky sessions enabled."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 Aurora 副本启用 Aurora Auto Scaling。使用网络负载均衡器，并启用最少未完成请求路由算法和粘性会话。","B":"为 Aurora writer 启用 Aurora Auto Scaling。使用启用了循环路由算法和粘性会话的应用程序负载均衡器。","C":"为 Aurora 副本启用 Aurora Auto Scaling。使用启用了循环路由和粘性会话的应用程序负载均衡器。","D":"为 Aurora writer 启用 Aurora Scaling。使用网络负载均衡器，并启用最少未完成请求路由算法和粘性会话。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":95},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":5,"question_en":"A company uses a service to collect metadata from applications that the company hosts on premises. Consumer devices such as TVs and internet radios access the applications. Many older devices do not support certain HTTP headers and exhibit errors when these headers are present in responses. The company has configured an on-premises load balancer to remove the unsupported headers from responses sent to older devices, which the company identified by the User-Agent headers. The company wants to migrate the service to AWS, adopt serverless technologies, and retain the ability to support the older devices. The company has already migrated the applications into a set of AWS Lambda functions. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"公司使用服务从公司本地托管的应用程序收集元数据。电视和网络收音机等消费设备可以访问这些应用程序。许多旧设备不支持某 些 HTTP 标头，并且当这些标头出现在响应中时会出现错误。该公司已配置本地负载均衡器，以从发送到旧设备的响应中删除不受 支持的标头，该公司通过用户代理标头识别这些标头。 该公司希望将服务迁移到 AWS，采用无服务器技术，并保留支持旧设备的能力。该公司已经将应用程序迁移到一组 AWS Lambda 函 数中。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution for the metadata service. Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Configure the CloudFront distribution to forward requests to the ALB. Configure the ALB to invoke the correct Lambda function for each type of request. Create a CloudFront function to remove the problematic headers based on the value of the User-Agent header.","B":"Create an Amazon API Gateway REST API for the metadata service. Configure API Gateway to invoke the correct Lambda function for each type of request. Modify the default gateway responses to remove the problematic headers based on the value of the User-Agent header.","C":"Create an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API for the metadata service. Configure API Gateway to invoke the correct Lambda function for each type of request. Create a response mapping template to remove the problematic headers based on the value of the User-Agent. Associate the response data mapping with the HTTP API.","D":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution for the metadata service. Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Configure the CloudFront distribution to forward requests to the ALB. Configure the ALB to invoke the correct Lambda function for each type of request. Create a Lambda@Edge function that will remove the problematic headers in response to viewer requests based on the value of the User- Agent header."},"options_zh":{"A":"为元数据服务创建 Amazon CloudFront 分配。创建应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB)。配置 CloudFront 分配以将请求转发到 ALB。配置 ALB 以针对每种类型的请求调用正确的 Lambda 函数。创建一个 CloudFront 函数，以根据 User-Agent 标头的值删除有问题的标 头。","B":"为元数据服务创建 Amazon API Gateway REST API。配置 API Gateway 为每种类型的请求调用正确的 Lambda 函数。修改默认网 关响应以根据 User-Agent 标头的值删除有问题的标头。","C":"为元数据服务创建 Amazon API Gateway HTTP API。配置 API Gateway 为每种类型的请求调用正确的 Lambda 函数。创建响应映 射模板以根据用户代理的值删除有问题的标头。将响应数据映射与 HTTP API 关联。","D":"为元数据服务创建 Amazon CloudFront 分配。创建应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB)。配置 CloudFront 分配以将请求转发到 ALB。配置 ALB 以针对每种类型的请求调用正确的 Lambda 函数。创建一个 Lambda@Edge 函数，该函数将根据 User-Agent 标头的值删除有 问题的标头，以响应查看器请求。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":35,"D":30,"B":19},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to serverlessly and conditionally strip unsupported response headers for older devices identified by their User-Agent request header, after the applications were moved to Lambda. Option A places a CloudFront distribution in front of an ALB (which can invoke Lambda as a target) and uses a CloudFront Function to remove the problematic headers. This works because the CloudFront Functions event object exposes BOTH a request object and a response object, and the function's eventType can be viewer-response. In a viewer-response function you read event.request.headers['user-agent'] to detect older devices, then delete the offending keys from event.response.headers before CloudFront returns the response - exactly replicating the on-premises load balancer behavior with a lightweight, high-scale, purpose-built serverless component. Options B and C misuse API Gateway response mechanisms, and Option D triggers Lambda@Edge on the viewer-request event, where the origin response does not yet exist, so response headers cannot be modified there.","explanation_zh":"需求是以 serverless 方式、依 User-Agent 請求標頭辨識舊裝置，並有條件地移除回應中不支援的標頭（應用已搬到 Lambda）。選項 A 在 ALB 前放 CloudFront distribution（ALB 可將 Lambda 當作 target 調用），並用 CloudFront Function 移除問題標頭。可行的關鍵在於 CloudFront Functions 的 event 物件同時包含 request 與 response 物件，且 eventType 可為 viewer-response；在 viewer-response function 中即可讀取 event.request.headers['user-agent'] 判斷舊裝置，並於 CloudFront 回傳前刪除 event.response.headers 中的問題標頭，正好複製地端 load balancer 的行為，且是輕量、高擴展、專為此類標頭操作設計的 serverless 元件。選項 B、C 誤用 API Gateway 的回應機制；選項 D 將 Lambda@Edge 掛在 viewer-request 事件，此時 origin 回應尚不存在，無法修改回應標頭。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"API Gateway 'gateway responses' are only the responses API Gateway itself generates for error/protocol conditions (e.g., 4XX/5XX, throttling, missing authentication), not the successful integration responses returned by the Lambda functions. They also cannot conditionally branch on the request User-Agent to strip headers from normal responses, so they do not replicate the device-specific behavior.","why_zh":"API Gateway 的 gateway responses 僅涵蓋 API Gateway 自身在錯誤／協定情境（如 4XX/5XX、throttling、缺少授權）所產生的回應，並非 Lambda 整合成功回傳的回應；也無法依請求的 User-Agent 條件去剝除一般回應中的標頭，因此無法重現依裝置的行為。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"HTTP APIs do not support VTL 'response mapping templates' or a 'response data mapping' association (those are REST-API concepts). HTTP API parameter mapping can do remove:header, but it is applied statically per route/status code and cannot conditionally evaluate the User-Agent value, so it cannot selectively strip headers only for older devices.","why_zh":"HTTP API 不支援 VTL 的 'response mapping template' 或 'response data mapping' 關聯（那屬於 REST API）。HTTP API 的 parameter mapping 雖可 remove:header，但是依 route／狀態碼靜態套用，無法依 User-Agent 值做條件判斷，因此無法只針對舊裝置選擇性移除標頭。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The option triggers Lambda@Edge 'in response to viewer requests' (the viewer-request event). At the viewer-request trigger the origin response does not yet exist, so response headers cannot be modified. Removing response headers requires an origin-response or viewer-response trigger, making this configuration incorrect.","why_zh":"此選項把 Lambda@Edge 掛在 'viewer request'（viewer-request 事件）。在 viewer-request 觸發點，origin 回應尚未產生，因而無法修改回應標頭；要移除回應標頭需用 origin-response 或 viewer-response 觸發，故此配置錯誤。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/functions-event-structure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/cloudfront-functions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/http-api-parameter-mapping.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/api-gateway-gatewayResponse-definition.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/lambda-edge-event-request-response.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識・多選項拉鋸"},{"id":6,"question_en":"A retail company needs to provide a series of data files to another company, which is its business partner. These files are saved in an Amazon S3 bucket under Account A, which belongs to the retail company. The business partner company wants one of its IAM users, User_DataProcessor, to access the files from its own AWS account (Account B). Which combination of steps must the companies take so that User_DataProcessor can access the S3 bucket successfully? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家零售公司需要向另一家公司（其业务合作伙伴）提供一系列数据文件。这些文件保存在属于零售公司的账户 A 下的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。该业务合作伙伴公司希望其 IAM 用户之一 User_DataProcessor 从其自己的 AWS 账户（账户 B）访问文件。 公司必须采取哪些步骤组合才能使 User_DataProcessor 能够成功访问 S3 存储桶？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Turn on the cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) feature for the S3 bucket in Account A.","B":"In Account A, set the S3 bucket policy to the following:\n{\n  \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n  \"Action\": [\n    \"s3:GetObject\",\n    \"s3:ListBucket\"\n  ],\n  \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::AccountABucketName/*\"\n}","C":"In Account A, set the S3 bucket policy to the following:\n{\n  \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n  \"Principal\": {\n    \"AWS\": \"arn:aws:iam::AccountB:user/User_DataProcessor\"\n  },\n  \"Action\": [\n    \"s3:GetObject\",\n    \"s3:ListBucket\"\n  ],\n  \"Resource\": [\n    \"arn:aws:s3:::AccountABucketName/*\"\n  ]\n}","D":"In Account B, set the permissions of User_DataProcessor to the following:\n{\n  \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n  \"Action\": [\n    \"s3:GetObject\",\n    \"s3:ListBucket\"\n  ],\n  \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::AccountABucketName/*\"\n}","E":"In Account B, set the permissions of User_DataProcessor to the following:\n{\n  \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n  \"Principal\": {\n    \"AWS\": \"arn:aws:iam::AccountB:user/User_DataProcessor\"\n  },\n  \"Action\": [\n    \"s3:GetObject\",\n    \"s3:ListBucket\"\n  ],\n  \"Resource\": [\n    \"arn:aws:s3:::AccountABucketName/*\"\n  ]\n}"},"options_zh":{"A":"為 Account A 中的 S3 bucket 開啟 cross-origin resource sharing (CORS)。","B":"在 Account A 中，將 S3 bucket policy 設為以下內容：","C":"在 Account A 中，將 S3 bucket policy 設為以下內容：","D":"在 Account B 中，將 User_DataProcessor 的權限設為以下內容：","E":"在 Account B 中，將 User_DataProcessor 的權限設為以下內容："},"answer":["C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"C":63,"D":34},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Cross-account access to an S3 bucket requires an explicit Allow on BOTH sides of the trust. AWS states plainly: \"In cross account access, a principal needs an Allow in the identity policy AND the resource-based policy.\" Account A owns the bucket, so it must attach a resource-based bucket policy that names the Account B IAM user as the Principal (option C) — a bucket policy is a resource-based policy and MUST contain a Principal element. Separately, Account B must attach an identity-based policy to User_DataProcessor delegating the matching S3 actions on the Account A bucket (option D) — an identity policy grants permissions to the identity it is attached to and does NOT contain a Principal element. Because this is a choose-two question and both the resource-side grant and the identity-side delegation are mandatory, C and D are both required. The community's single-answer 'C' is wrong: a bucket policy alone is insufficient — without D, User_DataProcessor's own account has never delegated the permission, so the request is denied.","explanation_zh":"跨帳號存取 S3 bucket 必須在信任關係的「雙邊」都有明確的 Allow。AWS 官方文件明白指出：「在跨帳號存取中，principal 需要在 identity policy 「以及」 resource-based policy 兩邊都得到 Allow。」Account A 擁有 bucket，因此必須掛上一個把 Account B 的 IAM user 列為 Principal 的 resource-based bucket policy（選項 C）——bucket policy 屬於 resource-based policy，「必須」含有 Principal 元素。另一方面，Account B 必須對 User_DataProcessor 掛上 identity-based policy，將對應的 S3 動作委派到 Account A 的 bucket（選項 D）——identity policy 是授權給它所附掛的身分，「不含」Principal 元素。因為本題為複選（選二），resource 端授權與 identity 端委派兩者都是必要條件，所以 C 與 D 都需要。社群單選『C』是錯的：只有 bucket policy 並不足夠——若缺少 D，User_DataProcessor 自己所屬的帳號從未委派該權限，請求仍會被拒絕。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CORS controls browser cross-origin JavaScript requests to S3; it has nothing to do with IAM cross-account authorization and does not grant any access to User_DataProcessor.","why_zh":"CORS 控制的是瀏覽器對 S3 的跨來源 JavaScript 請求，與 IAM 跨帳號授權完全無關，也不會賦予 User_DataProcessor 任何存取權。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"This is presented as an Account A bucket (resource-based) policy but has no Principal element, so it is an invalid bucket policy and grants access to no one; a resource-based policy must specify who the principal is.","why_zh":"此為要放在 Account A 的 bucket（resource-based）policy，卻缺少 Principal 元素，因此是無效的 bucket policy，不會授權給任何人；resource-based policy 必須指明 principal 是誰。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"This is meant to be the identity policy attached to User_DataProcessor in Account B, but identity-based policies do NOT contain a Principal element (the identity is implicit). Including Principal makes it an invalid IAM user permission policy.","why_zh":"此應為掛在 Account B 之 User_DataProcessor 上的 identity policy，但 identity-based policy 「不含」Principal 元素（身分是隱含的）。加入 Principal 使其成為無效的 IAM user 權限政策。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies-cross-account-resource-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/example-walkthroughs-managing-access-example2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_elements_principal.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・複選"},{"id":7,"question_en":"A company is running a traditional web application on Amazon EC2 instances. The company needs to refactor the application as microservices that run on containers. Separate versions of the application exist in two distinct environments: production and testing. Load for the application is variable, but the minimum load and the maximum load are known. A solutions architect needs to design the updated application with a serverless architecture that minimizes operational complexity. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 Amazon EC2 实例上运行传统 Web 应用程序。该公司需要将应用程序重构为在容器上运行的微服务。应用程序的不同 版本存在于两个不同的环境中：生产和测试。应用的负载是可变的，但最小负载和最大负载是已知的。解决方案架构师需要使用无 服务器架构来设计更新的应用程序，以最大限度地降低操作复杂性。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Upload the container images to AWS Lambda as functions. Configure a concurrency limit for the associated Lambda functions to handle the expected peak load. Configure two separate Lambda integrations within Amazon API Gateway: one for production and one for testing.","B":"Upload the container images to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). Configure two auto scaled Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) clusters with the Fargate launch type to handle the expected load. Deploy tasks from the ECR images. Configure two separate Application Load Balancers to direct tra®c to the ECS clusters.","C":"Upload the container images to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). Configure two auto scaled Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) clusters with the Fargate launch type to handle the expected load. Deploy tasks from the ECR images. Configure two separate Application Load Balancers to direct tra®c to the EKS clusters.","D":"Upload the container images to AWS Elastic Beanstalk. In Elastic Beanstalk, create separate environments and deployments for production and testing. Configure two separate Application Load Balancers to direct tra®c to the Elastic Beanstalk deployments."},"options_zh":{"A":"将容器映像作为函数上传到 AWS Lambda。为关联的 Lambda 函数配置并发限制以处理预期的峰值负载。在 Amazon API Gateway 中配置两个单独的 Lambda 集成：一个用于生产，一个用于测试。","B":"将容器映像上传到 Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR)。使用 Fargate 启动类型配置两个自动扩展的 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 集群来处理预期负载。从 ECR 映像部署任务。配置两个单独的应用程序负载均衡器以将流量引导 至 ECS 集群。","C":"将容器映像上传到 Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR)。使用 Fargate 启动类型配置两个自动扩展的 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 集群来处理预期负载。从 ECR 映像部署任务。配置两个单独的应用程序负载均衡器以将流量引 导至 EKS 集群。","D":"将容器映像上传到 AWS Elastic Beanstalk。在 Elastic Beanstalk 中，为生产和测试创建单独的环境和部署。配置两个单独的 Application Load Balancer 以将流量引导至 Elastic Beanstalk 部署。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":83},"tags":["Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":8,"question_en":"A company has a multi-tier web application that runs on a ­eet of Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The instances are in an Auto Scaling group. The ALB and the Auto Scaling group are replicated in a backup AWS Region. The minimum value and the maximum value for the Auto Scaling group are set to zero. An Amazon RDS Multi-AZ DB instance stores the application’s data. The DB instance has a read replica in the backup Region. The application presents an endpoint to end users by using an Amazon Route 53 record. The company needs to reduce its RTO to less than 15 minutes by giving the application the ability to automatically fail over to the backup Region. The company does not have a large enough budget for an active-active strategy. What should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个多层 Web 应用程序，该应用程序在应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面的一组 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。这些实例位于 Auto Scaling 组中。ALB 和 Auto Scaling 组将复制到备份 AWS 区域中。Auto Scaling 组的最小值和最大值设置为零。Amazon RDS 多可 用区数据库实例存储应用程序的数据。数据库实例在备份区域中有一个只读副本。该应用程序使用 Amazon Route 53 记录向最终用 户提供终端节点。 该公司需要通过赋予应用程序自动故障转移到备份区域的能力，将 RTO 减少到 15 分钟以下。该公司没有足够大的预算来实施主动- 主动策略。 解决方案架构师应该建议什么来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Reconfigure the application’s Route 53 record with a latency-based routing policy that load balances tra®c between the two ALBs. Create an AWS Lambda function in the backup Region to promote the read replica and modify the Auto Scaling group values. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that is based on the HTTPCode_Target_5XX_Count metric for the ALB in the primary Region. Configure the CloudWatch alarm to invoke the Lambda function.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function in the backup Region to promote the read replica and modify the Auto Scaling group values. Configure Route 53 with a health check that monitors the web application and sends an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) notification to the Lambda function when the health check status is unhealthy. Update the application’s Route 53 record with a failover policy that routes tra®c to the ALB in the backup Region when a health check failure occurs.","C":"Configure the Auto Scaling group in the backup Region to have the same values as the Auto Scaling group in the primary Region. Reconfigure the application’s Route 53 record with a latency-based routing policy that load balances tra®c between the two ALBs. Remove the read replica. Replace the read replica with a standalone RDS DB instance. Configure Cross-Region Replication between the RDS DB instances by using snapshots and Amazon S3.","D":"Configure an endpoint in AWS Global Accelerator with the two ALBs as equal weighted targets. Create an AWS Lambda function in the backup Region to promote the read replica and modify the Auto Scaling group values. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that is based on the HTTPCode_Target_5XX_Count metric for the ALB in the primary Region. Configure the CloudWatch alarm to invoke the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用基于延迟的路由策略重新配置应用程序的 Route 53 记录，以平衡两个 ALB 之间的流量负载。在备份区域中创建 AWS Lambda 函数以提升只读副本并修改 Auto Scaling 组值。创建基于主要区域中 ALB 的 HTTPCode_Target_5XX_Count 指标的 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。配置 CloudWatch 警报以调用 Lambda 函数。","B":"在备份区域中创建 AWS Lambda 函数以提升只读副本并修改 Auto Scaling 组值。使用运行状况检查配置 Route 53，该运行状况 检查可监控 Web 应用程序，并在运行状况检查状态不正常时向 Lambda 函数发送 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 通知。使用故障转移策略更新应用程序的 Route 53 记录，该策略在发生运行状况检查失败时将流量路由到备份区域中的 ALB。","C":"将备份区域中的 Auto Scaling 组配置为与主区域中的 Auto Scaling 组具有相同的值。使用基于延迟的路由策略重新配置应用程 序的 Route 53 记录，以平衡两个 ALB 之间的流量负载。删除只读副本。将只读副本替换为独立的 RDS 数据库实例。使用快照和 Amazon S3 在 RDS 数据库实例之间配置跨区域复制。","D":"在 AWS Global Accelerator 中配置终端节点，将两个 ALB 作为相等权重的目标。在备份区域中创建 AWS Lambda 函数以提升只读 副本并修改 Auto Scaling 组值。创建基于主要区域中 ALB 的 HTTPCode_Target_5XX_Count 指标的 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。配置 CloudWatch 警报以调用 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":9,"question_en":"A company is hosting a critical application on a single Amazon EC2 instance. The application uses an Amazon ElastiCache for Redis single- node cluster for an in-memory data store. The application uses an Amazon RDS for MariaDB DB instance for a relational database. For the application to function, each piece of the infrastructure must be healthy and must be in an active state. A solutions architect needs to improve the application's architecture so that the infrastructure can automatically recover from failure with the least possible downtime. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在单个 Amazon EC2 实例上托管关键应用程序。该应用程序使用 Amazon ElastiCache for Redis 单节点集群作为内存数据存 储。该应用程序使用 Amazon RDS for MariaDB 数据库实例作为关系数据库。为了使应用程序正常运行，基础设施的每个部分都必须 健康并且必须处于活动状态。 解决方案架构师需要改进应用程序的架构，以便基础架构能够以尽可能少的停机时间自动从故障中恢复。 哪种步骤组合可以满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use an Elastic Load Balancer to distribute tra®c across multiple EC2 instances. Ensure that the EC2 instances are part of an Auto Scaling group that has a minimum capacity of two instances.","B":"Use an Elastic Load Balancer to distribute tra®c across multiple EC2 instances. Ensure that the EC2 instances are configured in unlimited mode.","C":"Modify the DB instance to create a read replica in the same Availability Zone. Promote the read replica to be the primary DB instance in failure scenarios.","D":"Modify the DB instance to create a Multi-AZ deployment that extends across two Availability Zones.","E":"Create a replication group for the ElastiCache for Redis cluster. Configure the cluster to use an Auto Scaling group that has a minimum capacity of two instances.","F":"Create a replication group for the ElastiCache for Redis cluster. Enable Multi-AZ on the cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用弹性负载均衡器在多个 EC2 实例之间分配流量。确保 EC2 实例属于 Auto Scaling 组的一部分，该组的容量至少为两个实 例。","B":"使用弹性负载均衡器在多个 EC2 实例之间分配流量。确保 EC2 实例配置为无限制模式。","C":"修改数据库实例以在同一可用区中创建只读副本。在故障场景中将只读副本提升为主数据库实例。","D":"修改数据库实例以创建跨两个可用区的多可用区部署。","E":"为 ElastiCache for Redis 集群创建复制组。将集群配置为使用至少具有两个实例容量的 Auto Scaling 组。","F":"为 ElastiCache for Redis 集群创建复制组。在集群上启用多可用区。"},"answer":["A","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ADF":97},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":10,"question_en":"A retail company is operating its ecommerce application on AWS. The application runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The company uses an Amazon RDS DB instance as the database backend. Amazon CloudFront is configured with one origin that points to the ALB. Static content is cached. Amazon Route 53 is used to host all public zones. After an update of the application, the ALB occasionally returns a 502 status code (Bad Gateway) error. The root cause is malformed HTTP headers that are returned to the ALB. The webpage returns successfully when a solutions architect reloads the webpage immediately after the error occurs. While the company is working on the problem, the solutions architect needs to provide a custom error page instead of the standard ALB error page to visitors. Which combination of steps will meet this requirement with the LEAST amount of operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家零售公司正在 AWS 上运行其电子商务应用程序。该应用程序在应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。该 公司使用 Amazon RDS 数据库实例作为数据库后端。Amazon CloudFront 配置有一个指向 ALB 的源。静态内容被缓存。Amazon Route 53 用于托管所有公共区域。 更新应用程序后，ALB 偶尔会返回 502 状态代码（错误网关）错误。根本原因是返回到 ALB 的 HTTP 标头格式错误。当解决方案架 构师在错误发生后立即重新加载网页时，网页会成功返回。 当公司正在解决该问题时，解决方案架构师需要向访问者提供自定义错误页面，而不是标准 ALB 错误页面。 哪种步骤组合能够以最少的运营开销满足这一要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure the S3 bucket to host a static webpage. Upload the custom error pages to Amazon S3.","B":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to invoke an AWS Lambda function if the ALB health check response Target.FailedHealthChecks is greater than 0. Configure the Lambda function to modify the forwarding rule at the ALB to point to a publicly accessible web server.","C":"Modify the existing Amazon Route 53 records by adding health checks. Configure a fallback target if the health check fails. Modify DNS records to point to a publicly accessible webpage.","D":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to invoke an AWS Lambda function if the ALB health check response Elb.InternalError is greater than 0. Configure the Lambda function to modify the forwarding rule at the ALB to point to a public accessible web server.","E":"Add a custom error response by configuring a CloudFront custom error page. Modify DNS records to point to a publicly accessible web page."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 Amazon S3 存储桶。配置 S3 存储桶以托管静态网页。将自定义错误页面上传到 Amazon S3。","B":"如果 ALB 运行状况检查响应 Target.FailedHealthChecks 大于 0，则创建 Amazon CloudWatch 警报以调用 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数以修改 ALB 上的转发规则以指向可公开访问的 Web 服务器。","C":"通过添加运行状况检查来修改现有 Amazon Route 53 记录。配置健康检查失败时的回退目标。修改 DNS 记录以指向可公开访问 的网页。","D":"如果 ALB 运行状况检查响应 Elb.InternalError 大于 0，则创建 Amazon CloudWatch 警报以调用 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数以修改 ALB 上的转发规则以指向公共可访问的 Web 服务器。","E":"通过配置 CloudFront 自定义错误页面来添加自定义错误响应。修改 DNS 记录以指向可公开访问的网页。"},"answer":["C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AE":94},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Scenario: CloudFront -> ALB -> EC2/RDS. The ALB intermittently returns HTTP 502 (Bad Gateway) because targets return malformed/invalid HTTP response headers (AWS lists 'the target response is malformed or contains HTTP headers that are not valid' as a direct cause of an ALB 502). Because an immediate reload succeeds, this is a transient per-request error on otherwise-healthy targets, NOT an endpoint outage and NOT a health-check failure. The goal is to show a custom error page with the LEAST operational overhead. Since CloudFront is already in front of the ALB, the lowest-overhead solution is a native CloudFront custom error response (E): CloudFront explicitly supports custom error pages for 5xx status codes including 502. The custom error page must be reachable even when the ALB origin is failing - AWS documentation recommends storing custom error pages in a separate Amazon S3 origin so that, when the primary origin returns 5xx errors, CloudFront can still fetch the error page (a distribution cache behavior with a path pattern routes error-page requests to the S3 origin). Option A provides exactly that: an S3 bucket hosting the static custom error pages. A + E together form a complete, fully managed, low-overhead solution. The dump answer C/E is wrong: Route 53 failover (C) operates at the DNS/endpoint level and only fails over when the ALB endpoint itself is unhealthy - it cannot detect or react to intermittent per-request 502s from malformed headers on a healthy ALB, so it would never trigger for this failure mode, and it is higher overhead than a CloudFront custom error response. Options B and D are high-overhead, fragile Lambda-based rewrite schemes that also cite metrics that do not exist (Target.FailedHealthChecks and Elb.InternalError are not real ALB CloudWatch metrics; the real ones are UnHealthyHostCount and HTTPCode_ELB_5XX_Count) and respond to health-check/aggregate signals rather than per-request errors. Therefore the community answer AE is correct.","explanation_zh":"場景: CloudFront -> ALB -> EC2/RDS。ALB 因後端 target 回傳格式錯誤/無效的 HTTP headers 而間歇性回傳 HTTP 502 (Bad Gateway)。AWS 官方文件明確將「target response 格式錯誤或含不合法 HTTP headers」列為 ALB 502 的直接成因。立即重新整理即成功,代表這是健康 target 上的暫時性逐請求 (per-request) 錯誤,並非端點當機,也不是 health check 失敗。目標是以最少維運成本顯示自訂錯誤頁面。由於 CloudFront 已位於 ALB 前方,維運成本最低的方案就是使用 CloudFront 原生 custom error response (選項 E):CloudFront 明確支援針對 5xx (含 502) 回傳自訂錯誤頁面。而該錯誤頁面必須存放在即使 ALB origin 失效時 CloudFront 仍能取得的位置 — AWS 文件建議把 custom error pages 放在獨立的 Amazon S3 origin,如此當主 origin 回 5xx 時 CloudFront 仍能抓到錯誤頁 (透過 distribution 的 cache behavior 以 path pattern 將錯誤頁請求導向 S3 origin)。選項 A 正好提供這點:以 S3 bucket 託管靜態自訂錯誤頁面。A + E 一起構成完整、全託管、低維運成本的解法。Dump 答案 C/E 是錯的:Route 53 failover (C) 運作在 DNS/端點層級,只有當 ALB 端點本身不健康時才會切換,無法偵測或回應健康 ALB 上由無效 headers 造成的間歇性逐請求 502,因此在此故障模式下不會觸發,且維運成本高於 CloudFront custom error response。選項 B 與 D 是高成本、脆弱的 Lambda 改寫方案,且引用了不存在的指標 (Target.FailedHealthChecks 與 Elb.InternalError 並非真實 ALB CloudWatch 指標;真實指標為 UnHealthyHostCount 與 HTTPCode_ELB_5XX_Count),並回應健康檢查/聚合訊號而非逐請求錯誤。因此社群答案 AE 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Cites 'Target.FailedHealthChecks' which is not a real ALB CloudWatch metric (the real metric is UnHealthyHostCount). The 502s come from malformed response headers on healthy targets, so health checks are not failing and the alarm would not fire. The Lambda-rewrites-ALB-rules-to-a-separate-web-server design is far higher operational overhead than a CloudFront custom error response and does not produce a styled per-request error page.","why_zh":"引用了不存在的 ALB CloudWatch 指標『Target.FailedHealthChecks』(真實指標為 UnHealthyHostCount)。502 來自健康 target 的無效回應 headers,health check 並未失敗,警報不會觸發。用 Lambda 改寫 ALB 規則指向另一台 Web 伺服器,維運成本遠高於 CloudFront custom error response,且無法產生逐請求的客製化錯誤頁面。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but is wrong. Route 53 failover/health checks operate at the DNS endpoint level and only switch targets when the ALB endpoint itself is unhealthy. They cannot detect intermittent per-request 502s caused by malformed headers on an otherwise-healthy ALB, so failover would not trigger for this failure mode. It is also higher operational overhead than the already-present CloudFront custom error response.","why_zh":"這是 dump 建議答案,但是錯的。Route 53 failover/health check 運作在 DNS 端點層級,只有當 ALB 端點本身不健康時才切換 target。它無法偵測健康 ALB 上由無效 headers 造成的間歇性逐請求 502,因此在此故障模式下不會觸發。其維運成本也高於既有 CloudFront 上的 custom error response。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Cites 'Elb.InternalError' which is not a valid ALB CloudWatch metric (the real 5xx metric is HTTPCode_ELB_5XX_Count). Like B, the Lambda-driven ALB rule rewrite to a separate public web server is complex, fragile, reactive at the aggregate-metric level, and high operational overhead, and it does not serve a clean custom error page for the individual failing request.","why_zh":"引用了無效的 ALB CloudWatch 指標『Elb.InternalError』(真實 5xx 指標為 HTTPCode_ELB_5XX_Count)。與 B 相同,以 Lambda 改寫 ALB 規則指向另一台公開 Web 伺服器的做法複雜、脆弱、以聚合指標被動回應,維運成本高,且無法為個別失敗請求提供乾淨的自訂錯誤頁面。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/GeneratingCustomErrorResponses.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/custom-error-pages-procedure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/creating-custom-error-pages.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/custom-error-pages-different-locations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-troubleshooting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/HostingWebsiteOnS3Setup.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":11,"question_en":"A company has many AWS accounts and uses AWS Organizations to manage all of them. A solutions architect must implement a solution that the company can use to share a common network across multiple accounts. The company’s infrastructure team has a dedicated infrastructure account that has a VPC. The infrastructure team must use this account to manage the network. Individual accounts cannot have the ability to manage their own networks. However, individual accounts must be able to create AWS resources within subnets. Which combination of actions should the solutions architect perform to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司拥有许多 AWS 账户，并使用 AWS Organizations 来管理所有账户。解决方案架构师必须实施一个解决方案，公司可以使用该 解决方案在多个帐户之间共享公共网络。 该公司的基础设施团队有一个拥有 VPC 的专用基础设施账户。基础设施团队必须使用此帐户来管理网络。个人帐户无法管理自己的 网络。但是，个人账户必须能够在子网内创建 AWS 资源。 解决方案架构师应该执行哪些操作组合来满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a transit gateway in the infrastructure account.","B":"Enable resource sharing from the AWS Organizations management account.","C":"Create VPCs in each AWS account within the organization in AWS Organizations. Configure the VPCs to share the same CIDR range and subnets as the VPC in the infrastructure account. Peer the VPCs in each individual account with the VPC in the infrastructure account.","D":"Create a resource share in AWS Resource Access Manager in the infrastructure account. Select the specific AWS Organizations OU that will use the shared network. Select each subnet to associate with the resource share.","E":"Create a resource share in AWS Resource Access Manager in the infrastructure account. Select the specific AWS Organizations OU that will use the shared network. Select each prefix list to associate with the resource share."},"options_zh":{"A":"在基础设施帐户中创建中转网关。","B":"从 AWS Organizations 管理账户启用资源共享。","C":"在 AWS Organizations 的组织内的每个 AWS 账户中创建 VPC。将 VPC 配置为与基础设施账户中的 VPC 共享相同的 CIDR 范围和 子网。将每个单独账户中的 VPC 与基础设施账户中的 VPC 对等。","D":"在 AWS Resource Access Manager 的基础设施账户中创建资源共享。选择将使用共享网络的特定 AWS Organizations OU。选择与 资源共享关联的每个子网。","E":"在 AWS Resource Access Manager 的基础设施账户中创建资源共享。选择将使用共享网络的特定 AWS Organizations OU。选择与 资源共享关联的每个前缀列表。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BD":86},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is classic VPC sharing (subnet sharing) via AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM): the infrastructure account owns and centrally manages one VPC, participant accounts cannot manage the network but can launch resources into shared subnets. The official VPC 'Shared subnet prerequisites' page lists exactly two required steps that map to the answer: (1) enable resource sharing in the AWS RAM console FROM the organization's MANAGEMENT account (Option B) and (2) create a resource share in RAM specifying the subnets and the target principal such as an Organizations OU (Option D). Enabling sharing with AWS Organizations must be done by a principal in the management account, which is why B (not the infrastructure account) is correct. The resource share itself is created in the infrastructure account (the resource owner) and associates the specific subnets with an OU. The dump's suggested A+D is wrong because a transit gateway interconnects separate VPCs and does not let accounts share subnets or launch resources inside a single centrally-managed VPC; the scenario explicitly wants one shared common network, not multiple peered/interconnected networks.","explanation_zh":"本題是典型的 VPC 共用（子網路共用），透過 AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM) 實作：基礎架構帳戶擁有並集中管理一個 VPC，成員帳戶無法管理網路，但可在共用子網路中建立資源。官方 VPC「Shared subnet prerequisites」頁面明確列出兩個必要步驟：(1) 必須由組織的「management account」在 AWS RAM 主控台啟用資源共用（選項 B）；(2) 在 RAM 中建立 resource share，指定要共用的子網路與目標 principal（例如 Organizations OU）（選項 D）。啟用與 AWS Organizations 的共用必須由 management account 的 principal 執行，因此 B 正確而非由基礎架構帳戶執行。resource share 本身則在資源擁有者（基礎架構帳戶）中建立，並將特定子網路關聯到 OU。dump 建議的 A+D 錯誤，因為 transit gateway 是連接多個獨立 VPC，並不能讓帳戶共用子網路或在單一集中管理的 VPC 中建立資源；題目明確要求單一共用的共同網路，而非多個對等／互連的網路。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A transit gateway interconnects multiple separate VPCs; it does not share subnets or let participant accounts launch resources inside one centrally-managed VPC. The scenario needs a single shared common network (VPC sharing), not VPC interconnection.","why_zh":"transit gateway 用於連接多個獨立的 VPC，無法共用子網路，也無法讓成員帳戶在單一集中管理的 VPC 中建立資源。本題需要單一共用的共同網路（VPC 共用），而非 VPC 互連。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Creating separate VPCs with the same CIDR and peering them is invalid: VPC peering requires non-overlapping CIDR ranges, and this gives each account its own VPC to manage, violating the requirement that individual accounts cannot manage their own networks.","why_zh":"在每個帳戶建立相同 CIDR 的 VPC 並對等連線是無效的：VPC peering 需要 CIDR 不可重疊，且此作法讓每個帳戶各自擁有可管理的 VPC，違反「成員帳戶不可管理自己網路」的需求。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Sharing prefix lists does not share network capacity. A prefix list is just a set of CIDR blocks for use in security groups/route tables; it does not let participant accounts launch resources into the infrastructure account's subnets. You must share the subnets, not prefix lists.","why_zh":"共用 prefix list 無法共用網路容量。prefix list 只是供安全群組／路由表使用的 CIDR 集合，無法讓成員帳戶在基礎架構帳戶的子網路中建立資源。必須共用的是子網路，而非 prefix list。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-share-prerequisites.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-sharing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ram/latest/userguide/getting-started-sharing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/services-that-can-integrate-ram.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・複選"},{"id":12,"question_en":"A company wants to use a third-party software-as-a-service (SaaS) application. The third-party SaaS application is consumed through several API calls. The third-party SaaS application also runs on AWS inside a VPC. The company will consume the third-party SaaS application from inside a VPC. The company has internal security policies that mandate the use of private connectivity that does not traverse the internet. No resources that run in the company VPC are allowed to be accessed from outside the company’s VPC. All permissions must conform to the principles of least privilege. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司想要使用第三方软件即服务 (SaaS) 应用程序。第三方 SaaS 应用程序通过多个 API 调用来使用。第三方 SaaS 应用程序也在 VPC 内的 AWS 上运行。 该公司将从 VPC 内部使用第三方 SaaS 应用程序。该公司制定了内部安全政策，要求使用不穿越互联网的私人连接。公司VPC内运行 的资源不允许从公司VPC外部访问。所有权限都必须符合最小权限原则。 哪种解决方案满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS PrivateLink interface VPC endpoint. Connect this endpoint to the endpoint service that the third-party SaaS application provides. Create a security group to limit the access to the endpoint. Associate the security group with the endpoint.","B":"Create an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection between the third-party SaaS application and the company VPC. Configure network ACLs to limit access across the VPN tunnels.","C":"Create a VPC peering connection between the third-party SaaS application and the company VPUpdate route tables by adding the needed routes for the peering connection.","D":"Create an AWS PrivateLink endpoint service. Ask the third-party SaaS provider to create an interface VPC endpoint for this endpoint service. Grant permissions for the endpoint service to the specific account of the third-party SaaS provider."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 AWS PrivateLink 接口 VPC 终端节点。将此端点连接到第三方 SaaS 应用程序提供的端点服务。创建安全组以限制对端点的 访问。将安全组与端点关联。","B":"在第三方 SaaS 应用程序和公司 VPC 之间创建 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 连接。配置网络 ACL 以限制通过 VPN 隧道的访问。","C":"通过添加对等连接所需的路由，在第三方 SaaS 应用程序和公司 VPUpdate 路由表之间创建 VPC 对等连接。","D":"创建 AWS PrivateLink 终端节点服务。要求第三方 SaaS 提供商为此端点服务创建接口 VPC 端点。将端点服务的权限授予第三方 SaaS 提供商的特定帐户。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":91},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":13,"question_en":"A company needs to implement a patching process for its servers. The on-premises servers and Amazon EC2 instances use a variety of tools to perform patching. Management requires a single report showing the patch status of all the servers and instances. Which set of actions should a solutions architect take to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要为其服务器实施修补流程。本地服务器和 Amazon EC2 实例使用各种工具来执行修补。管理需要一份显示所有服务器 和实例的补丁状态的单一报告。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪组操作来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Systems Manager to manage patches on the on-premises servers and EC2 instances. Use Systems Manager to generate patch compliance reports.","B":"Use AWS OpsWorks to manage patches on the on-premises servers and EC2 instances. Use Amazon QuickSight integration with OpsWorks to generate patch compliance reports.","C":"Use an Amazon EventBridge rule to apply patches by scheduling an AWS Systems Manager patch remediation job. Use Amazon Inspector to generate patch compliance reports.","D":"Use AWS OpsWorks to manage patches on the on-premises servers and EC2 instances. Use AWS X-Ray to post the patch status to AWS Systems Manager OpsCenter to generate patch compliance reports."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 管理本地服务器和 EC2 实例上的补丁。使用 Systems Manager 生成补丁合规性报告。","B":"使用 AWS OpsWorks 管理本地服务器和 EC2 实例上的补丁。使用 Amazon QuickSight 与 OpsWorks 集成来生成补丁合规性报告。","C":"使用 Amazon EventBridge 规则通过安排 AWS Systems Manager 补丁修复作业来应用补丁。使用 Amazon Inspector 生成补丁合规 性报告。","D":"使用 AWS OpsWorks 管理本地服务器和 EC2 实例上的补丁。使用 AWS X-Ray 将补丁状态发布到 AWS Systems Manager OpsCenter 以生成补丁合规性报告。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":14,"question_en":"A company is running an application on several Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer. The load on the application varies throughout the day, and EC2 instances are scaled in and out on a regular basis. Log files from the EC2 instances are copied to a central Amazon S3 bucket every 15 minutes. The security team discovers that log files are missing from some of the terminated EC2 instances. Which set of actions will ensure that log files are copied to the central S3 bucket from the terminated EC2 instances?","question_zh":"一家公司正在应用程序负载均衡器后面的 Auto Scaling 组中的多个 Amazon EC2 实例上运行应用程序。应用程序的负载全天都在变 化，EC2 实例会定期扩展和缩减。EC2 实例中的日志文件每 15 分钟复制一次到中央 Amazon S3 存储桶。安全团队发现某些已终止的 EC2 实例缺少日志文件。 哪组操作将确保日志文件从已终止的 EC2 实例复制到中央 S3 存储桶？","options_en":{"A":"Create a script to copy log files to Amazon S3, and store the script in a file on the EC2 instance. Create an Auto Scaling lifecycle hook and an Amazon EventBridge rule to detect lifecycle events from the Auto Scaling group. Invoke an AWS Lambda function on the autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATING transition to send ABANDON to the Auto Scaling group to prevent termination, run the script to copy the log files, and terminate the instance using the AWS SDK.","B":"Create an AWS Systems Manager document with a script to copy log files to Amazon S3. Create an Auto Scaling lifecycle hook and an Amazon EventBridge rule to detect lifecycle events from the Auto Scaling group. Invoke an AWS Lambda function on the autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATING transition to call the AWS Systems Manager API SendCommand operation to run the document to copy the log files and send CONTINUE to the Auto Scaling group to terminate the instance.","C":"Change the log delivery rate to every 5 minutes. Create a script to copy log files to Amazon S3, and add the script to EC2 instance user data. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to detect EC2 instance termination. Invoke an AWS Lambda function from the EventBridge rule that uses the AWS CLI to run the user-data script to copy the log files and terminate the instance.","D":"Create an AWS Systems Manager document with a script to copy log files to Amazon S3. Create an Auto Scaling lifecycle hook that publishes a message to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. From the SNS notification, call the AWS Systems Manager API SendCommand operation to run the document to copy the log files and send ABANDON to the Auto Scaling group to terminate the instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个脚本以将日志文件复制到 Amazon S3，并将该脚本存储在 EC2 实例上的文件中。创建 Auto Scaling 生命周期挂钩和 Amazon EventBridge 规则以检测来自 Auto Scaling 组的生命周期事件。在 autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATING 转换上调用 AWS Lambda 函数以将 ABANDON 发送到 Auto Scaling 组以防止终止，运行脚本以复制日志文件，并使用 AWS 开发工具包终止实例。","B":"创建一个 AWS Systems Manager 文档，其中包含用于将日志文件复制到 Amazon S3 的脚本。创建 Auto Scaling 生命周期挂钩和 Amazon EventBridge 规则以检测来自 Auto Scaling 组的生命周期事件。在 autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATING 转换上调用 AWS Lambda 函数，以调用 AWS Systems Manager API SendCommand 操作来运行文档以复制日志文件并将 CONTINUE 发送到 Auto Scaling 组以终止实例。","C":"将日志传送速率更改为每 5 分钟一次。创建一个脚本以将日志文件复制到 Amazon S3，并将该脚本添加到 EC2 实例用户数据。 创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则来检测 EC2 实例终止。从 EventBridge 规则调用 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数使用 AWS CLI 运行用户数 据脚本来复制日志文件并终止实例。","D":"创建一个 AWS Systems Manager 文档，其中包含用于将日志文件复制到 Amazon S3 的脚本。创建一个 Auto Scaling 生命周期挂 钩，将消息发布到 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 主题。从 SNS 通知中，调用 AWS Systems Manager API SendCommand 操作来运行文档以复制日志文件并将 ABANDON 发送到 Auto Scaling 组以终止实例。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":15,"question_en":"A company is using multiple AWS accounts. The DNS records are stored in a private hosted zone for Amazon Route 53 in Account A. The company’s applications and databases are running in Account B. A solutions architect will deploy a two-tier application in a new VPC. To simplify the configuration, the db.example.com CNAME record set for the Amazon RDS endpoint was created in a private hosted zone for Amazon Route 53. During deployment, the application failed to start. Troubleshooting revealed that db.example.com is not resolvable on the Amazon EC2 instance. The solutions architect confirmed that the record set was created correctly in Route 53. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect take to resolve this issue? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用多个 AWS 账户。DNS 记录存储在账户 A 中 Amazon Route 53 的私有托管区域中。该公司的应用程序和数据库在账 户 B 中运行。 解决方案架构师将在新的 VPC 中部署两层应用程序。为了简化配置，在 Amazon Route 53 的私有托管区域中创建了 Amazon RDS 终端 节点的 db.example.com CNAME 记录集。 在部署期间，应用程序无法启动。故障排除显示 db.example.com 在 Amazon EC2 实例上无法解析。解决方案架构师确认在 Route 53 中正确创建了记录集。 解决方案架构师应采取哪些步骤组合来解决此问题？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the database on a separate EC2 instance in the new VPC. Create a record set for the instance’s private IP in the private hosted zone.","B":"Use SSH to connect to the application tier EC2 instance. Add an RDS endpoint IP address to the /etc/resolv.conf file.","C":"Create an authorization to associate the private hosted zone in Account A with the new VPC in Account B.","D":"Create a private hosted zone for the example com domain in Account B. Configure Route 53 replication between AWS accounts.","E":"Associate a new VPC in Account B with a hosted zone in Account A. Delete the association authorization in Account A."},"options_zh":{"A":"将数据库部署在新 VPC 中的单独 EC2 实例上。在私有托管区域中为实例的私有 IP 创建记录集。","B":"使用 SSH 连接到应用层 EC2 实例。将 RDS 端点 IP 地址添加到 /etc/resolv.conf 文件。","C":"创建授权以将账户 A 中的私有托管区域与账户 B 中的新 VPC 关联。","D":"在账户 B 中为示例 com 域创建私有托管区域。在 AWS 账户之间配置 Route 53 复制。","E":"将账户 B 中的新 VPC 与账户 A 中的托管区域关联。删除账户 A 中的关联授权。"},"answer":["B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{"CE":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The db.example.com record exists and is correct, so the failure is not the record itself but that the new VPC in Account B cannot query the private hosted zone (PHZ) that lives in Account A. A Route 53 PHZ only answers DNS queries from VPCs that are explicitly associated with it, and this new VPC is not associated. AWS documents a two-step cross-account association procedure: (1) using the account that CREATED the hosted zone (Account A), authorize the association with CreateVPCAssociationAuthorization / create-vpc-association-authorization -- this is option C; and (2) using the account that CREATED the VPC (Account B), call AssociateVPCWithHostedZone to actually associate the VPC, then (recommended) delete the authorization -- this is option E. Completing both C and E makes db.example.com resolvable from the EC2 instance, so the community CE answer is correct and the dump's B,C is wrong.","explanation_zh":"db.example.com 紀錄已存在且正確，因此問題不在紀錄本身，而在於 Account B 的新 VPC 無法查詢位於 Account A 的 private hosted zone (PHZ)。Route 53 PHZ 只會回應「已明確關聯」之 VPC 的 DNS 查詢，而此新 VPC 尚未關聯。AWS 官方記載的跨帳戶關聯程序分兩步：(1) 使用建立 hosted zone 的帳戶 (Account A) 呼叫 CreateVPCAssociationAuthorization / create-vpc-association-authorization 授權關聯 -- 即選項 C；(2) 使用建立 VPC 的帳戶 (Account B) 呼叫 AssociateVPCWithHostedZone 實際建立關聯，之後（建議）刪除該授權 -- 即選項 E。同時完成 C 與 E 才能讓 EC2 instance 解析 db.example.com，因此社群的 CE 正確，dump 的 B,C 錯誤。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The database is Amazon RDS, not an EC2-hosted DB. Moving the DB to a separate EC2 instance and adding a private-IP record does not address the actual root cause -- that the new VPC is not associated with the cross-account private hosted zone. It is irrelevant re-architecture.","why_zh":"資料庫是 Amazon RDS，而非 EC2 自建資料庫。將 DB 改放到另一台 EC2 並新增私有 IP 紀錄並未解決真正根因（新 VPC 未與跨帳戶 PHZ 關聯），屬於無關的重構。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"/etc/resolv.conf holds nameserver (DNS resolver) IP addresses, not the IPs of individual records, so putting an RDS endpoint IP there cannot resolve db.example.com. RDS endpoint IPs are also dynamic and change on failover, so hardcoding them is brittle and wrong. This does not fix DNS resolution and is the dump's incorrect choice.","why_zh":"/etc/resolv.conf 存放的是 nameserver (DNS 解析器) 的 IP，而非個別紀錄的 IP，故把 RDS endpoint IP 放進去無法解析 db.example.com。RDS endpoint IP 為動態，故障切換時會改變，硬編碼既脆弱又錯誤。此做法無法修復 DNS 解析，為 dump 的錯誤選項。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Route 53 has no native cross-account 'replication' feature for private hosted zones. The supported mechanisms for sharing a PHZ across accounts are VPC association authorization (options C/E) or Route 53 Profiles -- not zone replication. This option is fabricated.","why_zh":"Route 53 並無針對 private hosted zone 的原生跨帳戶『複寫 (replication)』功能。跨帳戶共用 PHZ 的支援方式為 VPC association authorization（選項 C/E）或 Route 53 Profiles，而非 zone replication。此選項為杜撰。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/hosted-zone-private-associate-vpcs-different-accounts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/APIReference/API_CreateVPCAssociationAuthorization.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/APIReference/API_AssociateVPCWithHostedZone.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/route53/create-vpc-association-authorization.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":16,"question_en":"A company used Amazon EC2 instances to deploy a web ­eet to host a blog site. The EC2 instances are behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and are configured in an Auto Scaling group. The web application stores all blog content on an Amazon EFS volume. The company recently added a feature for bloggers to add video to their posts, attracting 10 times the previous user tra®c. At peak times of day, users report buffering and timeout issues while attempting to reach the site or watch videos. Which is the MOST cost-e®cient and scalable deployment that will resolve the issues for users?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 Amazon EC2 实例部署 Web 队列来托管博客网站。EC2 实例位于应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面，并在 Auto Scaling 组 中配置。Web 应用程序将所有博客内容存储在 Amazon EFS 卷上。 该公司最近添加了一项功能，让博主可以在自己的帖子中添加视频，吸引的用户流量是之前的 10 倍。在一天的高峰时段，用户在尝 试访问网站或观看视频时报告缓冲和超时问题。 哪个是最具成本效益和可扩展的部署，可以解决用户的问题？","options_en":{"A":"Reconfigure Amazon EFS to enable maximum I/O.","B":"Update the blog site to use instance store volumes for storage. Copy the site contents to the volumes at launch and to Amazon S3 at shutdown.","C":"Configure an Amazon CloudFront distribution. Point the distribution to an S3 bucket, and migrate the videos from EFS to Amazon S3.","D":"Set up an Amazon CloudFront distribution for all site contents, and point the distribution at the ALB."},"options_zh":{"A":"重新配置 Amazon EFS 以启用最大 I/O。","B":"更新博客站点以使用实例存储卷进行存储。在启动时将站点内容复制到卷，在关闭时将站点内容复制到 Amazon S3。","C":"配置 Amazon CloudFront 分配。将分配指向 S3 存储桶，并将视频从 EFS 迁移到 Amazon S3。","D":"为所有站点内容设置 Amazon CloudFront 分配，并将该分配指向 ALB。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":90},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":17,"question_en":"A company with global o®ces has a single 1 Gbps AWS Direct Connect connection to a single AWS Region. The company’s on-premises network uses the connection to communicate with the company’s resources in the AWS Cloud. The connection has a single private virtual interface that connects to a single VPC. A solutions architect must implement a solution that adds a redundant Direct Connect connection in the same Region. The solution also must provide connectivity to other Regions through the same pair of Direct Connect connections as the company expands into other Regions. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家在全球设有办事处的公司拥有与单个 AWS 区域的单个 1 Gbps AWS Direct Connect 连接。公司的本地网络使用该连接与 AWS 云中 的公司资源进行通信。该连接具有连接到单个 VPC 的单个私有虚拟接口。 解决方案架构师必须实施在同一区域添加冗余 Direct Connect 连接的解决方案。当公司扩展到其他区域时，该解决方案还必须通过同 一对 Direct Connect 连接提供与其他区域的连接。 哪种解决方案满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Provision a Direct Connect gateway. Delete the existing private virtual interface from the existing connection. Create the second Direct Connect connection. Create a new private virtual interface on each connection, and connect both private virtual interfaces to the Direct Connect gateway. Connect the Direct Connect gateway to the single VPC.","B":"Keep the existing private virtual interface. Create the second Direct Connect connection. Create a new private virtual interface on the new connection, and connect the new private virtual interface to the single VPC.","C":"Keep the existing private virtual interface. Create the second Direct Connect connection. Create a new public virtual interface on the new connection, and connect the new public virtual interface to the single VPC.","D":"Provision a transit gateway. Delete the existing private virtual interface from the existing connection. Create the second Direct Connect connection. Create a new private virtual interface on each connection, and connect both private virtual interfaces to the transit gateway. Associate the transit gateway with the single VPC."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 Direct Connect 网关。从现有连接中删除现有专用虚拟接口。创建第二个 Direct Connect 连接。在每个连接上创建一个新的 私有虚拟接口，并将两个私有虚拟接口连接到 Direct Connect 网关。将专线网关连接到单个 VPC。","B":"保留现有的私有虚拟接口。创建第二个 Direct Connect 连接。在新连接上创建新的私有虚拟接口，并将新的私有虚拟接口连接 到单个 VPC。","C":"保留现有的私有虚拟接口。创建第二个 Direct Connect 连接。在新连接上创建新的公有虚拟接口，并将新的公有虚拟接口连接 到单个 VPC。","D":"配置中转网关。从现有连接中删除现有专用虚拟接口。创建第二个 Direct Connect 连接。在每个连接上创建一个新的专用虚拟 接口，并将两个专用虚拟接口连接到中转网关。将中转网关与单个 VPC 关联。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":18,"question_en":"A company has a web application that allows users to upload short videos. The videos are stored on Amazon EBS volumes and analyzed by custom recognition software for categorization. The website contains static content that has variable tra®c with peaks in certain months. The architecture consists of Amazon EC2 instances running in an Auto Scaling group for the web application and EC2 instances running in an Auto Scaling group to process an Amazon SQS queue. The company wants to re-architect the application to reduce operational overhead using AWS managed services where possible and remove dependencies on third-party software. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个网络应用程序，允许用户上传短视频。这些视频存储在 Amazon EBS 卷上，并由自定义识别软件进行分析以进行分 类。 该网站包含静态内容，流量可变，在某些月份达到峰值。该架构由在 Auto Scaling 组中运行的用于 Web 应用程序的 Amazon EC2 实例 和在 Auto Scaling 组中运行的用于处理 Amazon SQS 队列的 EC2 实例组成。该公司希望重新架构应用程序，以尽可能使用 AWS 托管 服务减少运营开销，并消除对第三方软件的依赖。 哪种解决方案满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon ECS containers for the web application and Spot instances for the Auto Scaling group that processes the SQS queue. Replace the custom software with Amazon Rekognition to categorize the videos.","B":"Store the uploaded videos in Amazon EFS and mount the file system to the EC2 instances for the web application. Process the SQS queue with an AWS Lambda function that calls the Amazon Rekognition API to categorize the videos.","C":"Host the web application in Amazon S3. Store the uploaded videos in Amazon S3. Use S3 event notification to publish events to the SQS queue. Process the SQS queue with an AWS Lambda function that calls the Amazon Rekognition API to categorize the videos.","D":"Use AWS Elastic Beanstalk to launch EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group for the web application and launch a worker environment to process the SQS queue. Replace the custom software with Amazon Rekognition to categorize the videos."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 Amazon ECS 容器用于 Web 应用程序，并将 Spot 实例用于处理 SQS 队列的 Auto Scaling 组。使用 Amazon Rekognition 替换自 定义软件来对视频进行分类。","B":"将上传的视频存储在 Amazon EFS 中，并将文件系统挂载到 Web 应用程序的 EC2 实例。使用 AWS Lambda 函数处理 SQS 队列， 该函数调用 Amazon Rekognition API 对视频进行分类。","C":"在 Amazon S3 中托管 Web 应用程序。将上传的视频存储在 Amazon S3 中。使用 S3 事件通知将事件发布到 SQS 队列。使用 AWS Lambda 函数处理 SQS 队列，该函数调用 Amazon Rekognition API 对视频进行分类。","D":"使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 在 Web 应用程序的 Auto Scaling 组中启动 EC2 实例，并启动工作线程环境来处理 SQS 队列。使用 Amazon Rekognition 替换自定义软件来对视频进行分类。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":87},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifiers are 'reduce operational overhead using AWS managed services where possible' and 'remove dependencies on third-party software.' Option C is fully serverless and eliminates every EC2 fleet and EBS volume: the static website content is hosted directly in Amazon S3, uploaded videos are stored in S3, an S3 Event Notification publishes to an Amazon SQS queue (SQS standard queues are an explicitly supported S3 event notification destination), and an AWS Lambda function processes the queue and calls the Amazon Rekognition API to categorize the videos. Amazon Rekognition performs stored-video and image label/moderation analysis on content in S3, which cleanly replaces the custom third-party recognition software. This design has no servers to patch or scale, giving the lowest operational overhead. Option D is inferior because it still launches and scales EC2 instances (a web Auto Scaling group plus an Elastic Beanstalk worker environment), so it does not use managed services 'where possible' and retains server-management overhead. The dump's suggested answer of D is wrong; the community answer C is correct.","explanation_zh":"關鍵限定條件是「盡量使用 AWS 受管服務以降低運維負擔」與「移除對第三方軟體的依賴」。選項 C 完全無伺服器化，去除所有 EC2 機群與 EBS 磁碟：靜態網站內容直接託管於 Amazon S3，上傳的影片存於 S3，透過 S3 Event Notification 發佈事件到 Amazon SQS 佇列（SQS 標準佇列是 S3 事件通知明確支援的目的地），再由 AWS Lambda 處理佇列並呼叫 Amazon Rekognition API 對影片進行分類。Amazon Rekognition 可對存放於 S3 的影片與影像做標籤／內容審核分析，正好取代自訂的第三方辨識軟體。此設計沒有伺服器需要修補或擴縮，運維負擔最低。選項 D 較差，因為它仍啟動並擴縮 EC2 執行個體（Web Auto Scaling 群組加 Elastic Beanstalk worker 環境），並未「盡量」使用受管服務，仍保留伺服器管理負擔。Dump 建議答案 D 有誤，社群答案 C 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Although it correctly swaps in Amazon Rekognition, it keeps an ECS container fleet for the web app and an EC2 Spot Auto Scaling group for the SQS worker, so it still requires capacity/scaling/cluster management rather than using managed services where possible. Spot also risks worker interruption, and videos are not moved off EBS to managed storage.","why_zh":"雖然正確改用 Amazon Rekognition，但 Web 應用仍維持 ECS 容器機群，SQS worker 仍使用 EC2 Spot Auto Scaling group，因此仍需管理容量／擴縮／叢集，未盡可能採用受管服務，且 Spot 有中斷風險，影片也未從 EBS 移至受管儲存。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"It still runs EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group for the web application (now backed by EFS), so server patching and scaling overhead remains; only the worker is moved to Lambda/Rekognition. It does not minimize operational overhead the way the fully serverless Option C does, which also moves the static site off servers into S3.","why_zh":"Web 應用仍在 Auto Scaling group 中執行 EC2 執行個體（改用 EFS 後援），伺服器修補與擴縮負擔依舊存在；僅將 worker 改成 Lambda／Rekognition。未能像完全無伺服器的選項 C 那樣將運維負擔降到最低，選項 C 還把靜態站點移出伺服器至 S3。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it is wrong. AWS Elastic Beanstalk still provisions and scales EC2 instances for both the web Auto Scaling group and the worker environment, so you continue managing a server fleet. This contradicts 'use AWS managed services where possible' and does not minimize operational overhead, even though Rekognition replaces the custom software. It is technically inferior to the fully serverless Option C.","why_zh":"這是 dump 的建議答案，但並不正確。AWS Elastic Beanstalk 仍為 Web Auto Scaling group 與 worker 環境佈建並擴縮 EC2 執行個體，因此你仍需管理伺服器機群。這與「盡量使用 AWS 受管服務」相違，未能將運維負擔降到最低，即使 Rekognition 取代了自訂軟體。技術上劣於完全無伺服器的選項 C。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/EventNotifications.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/notification-how-to-event-types-and-destinations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/WebsiteHosting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-sqs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/video.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/labels.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":19,"question_en":"A company has a serverless application comprised of Amazon CloudFront, Amazon API Gateway, and AWS Lambda functions. The current deployment process of the application code is to create a new version number of the Lambda function and run an AWS CLI script to update. If the new function version has errors, another CLI script reverts by deploying the previous working version of the function. The company would like to decrease the time to deploy new versions of the application logic provided by the Lambda functions, and also reduce the time to detect and revert when errors are identified. How can this be accomplished?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个由 Amazon CloudFront、Amazon API Gateway 和 AWS Lambda 函数组成的无服务器应用程序。应用程序代码的当前 部署过程是创建 Lambda 函数的新版本号并运行 AWS CLI 脚本进行更新。如果新函数版本出现错误，另一个 CLI 脚本将通过部署该函 数的先前工作版本来恢复。该公司希望减少部署 Lambda 函数提供的新版本应用程序逻辑的时间，并减少发现错误时检测和恢复的 时间。 如何才能做到这一点？","options_en":{"A":"Create and deploy nested AWS CloudFormation stacks with the parent stack consisting of the AWS CloudFront distribution and API Gateway, and the child stack containing the Lambda function. For changes to Lambda, create an AWS CloudFormation change set and deploy; if errors are triggered, revert the AWS CloudFormation change set to the previous version.","B":"Use AWS SAM and built-in AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the new Lambda version, gradually shift tra®c to the new version, and use pre- tra®c and post-tra®c test functions to verify code. Rollback if Amazon CloudWatch alarms are triggered.","C":"Refactor the AWS CLI scripts into a single script that deploys the new Lambda version. When deployment is completed, the script tests execute. If errors are detected, revert to the previous Lambda version.","D":"Create and deploy an AWS CloudFormation stack that consists of a new API Gateway endpoint that references the new Lambda version. Change the CloudFront origin to the new API Gateway endpoint, monitor errors and if detected, change the AWS CloudFront origin to the previous API Gateway endpoint."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建并部署嵌套的 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈，其中父堆栈由 AWS CloudFront 分配和 API Gateway 组成，子堆栈包含 Lambda 函 数。对于 Lambda 的更改，创建 AWS CloudFormation 更改集并部署；如果触发错误，请将 AWS CloudFormation 更改集恢复为之前 的版本。","B":"使用AWS SAM和内置的AWS CodeDeploy部署新的Lambda版本，逐步将流量转移到新版本，并使用流量前和流量后测试功能来 验证代码。如果触发 Amazon CloudWatch 警报则回滚。","C":"将 AWS CLI 脚本重构为部署新 Lambda 版本的单个脚本。部署完成后，将执行脚本测试。如果检测到错误，请恢复到之前的 Lambda 版本。","D":"创建并部署一个 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈，其中包含引用新 Lambda 版本的新 API Gateway 终端节点。将 CloudFront 源更改为 新的 API Gateway 终端节点，监控错误，如果检测到错误，则将 AWS CloudFront 源更改为之前的 API Gateway 终端节点。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":20,"question_en":"A company is planning to store a large number of archived documents and make the documents available to employees through the corporate intranet. Employees will access the system by connecting through a client VPN service that is attached to a VPC. The data must not be accessible to the public. The documents that the company is storing are copies of data that is held on physical media elsewhere. The number of requests will be low. Availability and speed of retrieval are not concerns of the company. Which solution will meet these requirements at the LOWEST cost?","question_zh":"一家公司计划存储大量存档文档，并通过公司内部网向员工提供这些文档。员工将通过连接到 VPC 的客户端 VPN 服务进行连接来访 问系统。这些数据不得向公众开放。 公司存储的文档是其他地方物理介质上保存的数据的副本。请求的数量将会很少。可用性和检索速度不是公司关心的问题。 哪种解决方案能够以最低的成本满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure the S3 bucket to use the S3 One Zone-Infrequent Access (S3 One Zone-IA) storage class as default. Configure the S3 bucket for website hosting. Create an S3 interface endpoint. Configure the S3 bucket to allow access only through that endpoint.","B":"Launch an Amazon EC2 instance that runs a web server. Attach an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system to store the archived data in the EFS One Zone-Infrequent Access (EFS One Zone-IA) storage class Configure the instance security groups to allow access only from private networks.","C":"Launch an Amazon EC2 instance that runs a web server Attach an Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume to store the archived data. Use the Cold HDD (sc1) volume type. Configure the instance security groups to allow access only from private networks.","D":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure the S3 bucket to use the S3 Glacier Deep Archive storage class as default. Configure the S3 bucket for website hosting. Create an S3 interface endpoint. Configure the S3 bucket to allow access only through that endpoint."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 Amazon S3 存储桶。将 S3 存储桶配置为默认使用 S3 One Zone-Infrequent Access (S3 One Zone-IA) 存储类别。配置用于网站 托管的 S3 存储桶。创建 S3 接口端点。将 S3 存储桶配置为仅允许通过该端点进行访问。","B":"启动运行 Web 服务器的 Amazon EC2 实例。附加 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统以将存档数据存储在 EFS One Zone-Infrequent Access (EFS One Zone-IA) 存储类中 将实例安全组配置为仅允许从私有网络进行访问。","C":"启动运行 Web 服务器的 Amazon EC2 实例附加 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 卷来存储存档数据。使用冷 HDD (sc1) 卷 类型。配置实例安全组以仅允许从专用网络访问。","D":"创建 Amazon S3 存储桶。将 S3 存储桶配置为默认使用 S3 Glacier Deep Archive 存储类别。配置用于网站托管的 S3 存储桶。创 建 S3 接口端点。将 S3 存储桶配置为仅允许通过该端点进行访问。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":66,"D":33},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The system must SERVE archived documents to employees on demand through S3 static website hosting (an HTTP GET returns the object directly). AWS docs state that objects stored in the S3 Glacier Deep Archive storage class are not immediately accessible: to read one you must first issue a RestoreObject request and wait for a temporary copy, and website hosting performs no restore, so a GET against a Deep Archive object fails with InvalidObjectState. This makes option D non-functional for intranet serving despite its lowest per-GB storage price. Option A uses S3 One Zone-IA, a non-archival class with millisecond, real-time GET access that works with website hosting. Because the documents are copies of data held on physical media elsewhere (reproducible), the single-AZ reduced redundancy of One Zone-IA is an appropriate cost optimization, and S3 avoids the continuous EC2/instance charges of the EFS (B) and EBS sc1 (C) web-server designs. Among the options that actually let employees retrieve the files, A is the lowest cost.","explanation_zh":"此系統必須透過 S3 static website hosting 隨選提供文件給員工（HTTP GET 直接回傳物件內容）。AWS 官方文件指出，存放在 S3 Glacier Deep Archive 儲存類別的物件無法即時存取：要讀取必須先發出 RestoreObject 請求並等待取得暫時副本，而 website hosting 本身不會執行還原，因此對 Deep Archive 物件發出 GET 會回傳 InvalidObjectState 錯誤。所以選項 D 雖然每 GB 儲存費最低，卻無法實際提供內網服務。選項 A 使用 S3 One Zone-IA，屬非封存類別，支援毫秒級即時 GET，可與 website hosting 搭配運作。由於這些文件是實體媒介上資料的副本（可重製），One Zone-IA 的單一 AZ 較低冗餘正好是合理的成本最佳化；而 S3 也避免了 B（EFS）與 C（EBS sc1）web-server 方案的持續 EC2 執行個體費用。在真正能讓員工取回檔案的選項中，A 成本最低。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"An EC2 web server plus an EFS One Zone-IA file system incurs continuous compute and instance charges 24/7 that dwarf the storage cost of a low-request archive, so it is far more expensive than an S3-based solution.","why_zh":"EC2 web server 加上 EFS One Zone-IA 檔案系統會產生全天候持續的運算與執行個體費用，遠超過低請求量封存的儲存成本，因此比以 S3 為基礎的方案昂貴許多。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An EC2 web server with a Cold HDD (sc1) EBS volume also carries always-on instance costs and pays for provisioned EBS capacity regardless of usage; EBS is single-AZ block storage tied to one instance and is not a cost-effective way to serve rarely accessed documents compared with S3.","why_zh":"EC2 web server 搭配 Cold HDD (sc1) EBS 磁碟同樣有常開執行個體費用，且不論使用量都要支付佈建的 EBS 容量；EBS 為綁定單一執行個體的單一 AZ 區塊儲存，相較 S3 並非提供極少存取文件的低成本方式。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 Glacier Deep Archive is the cheapest storage per GB, but its objects are archived and not immediately readable — a GET (as issued by S3 website hosting) fails until a RestoreObject request completes hours later. Website hosting cannot restore objects, so this design cannot serve documents through the intranet on demand and fails the core functional requirement.","why_zh":"S3 Glacier Deep Archive 每 GB 儲存最便宜，但其物件為封存狀態、無法即時讀取——S3 website hosting 發出的 GET 在 RestoreObject 請求數小時後完成前都會失敗。website hosting 無法還原物件，因此此設計無法隨選透過內網提供文件，未滿足核心功能需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/restoring-objects.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/storage-class-intro.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/glacier-storage-classes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/WebsiteHosting.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":21,"question_en":"A company is using an on-premises Active Directory service for user authentication. The company wants to use the same authentication service to sign in to the company’s AWS accounts, which are using AWS Organizations. AWS Site-to-Site VPN connectivity already exists between the on-premises environment and all the company’s AWS accounts. The company’s security policy requires conditional access to the accounts based on user groups and roles. User identities must be managed in a single location. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用內部部署的 Active Directory 服務進行使用者驗證。該公司希望使用同一個驗證服務登入該公司使用 AWS Organizations 管理的 AWS 帳戶。內部部署環境與公司所有 AWS 帳戶之間已經存在 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 連線。該公司的安全政策要求根據使用者群組與角色實施條件式存取，且使用者身分必須集中管理於單一位置。哪個解決方案能滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) to connect to Active Directory by using SAML 2.0. Enable automatic provisioning by using the System for Cross-domain Identity Management (SCIM) v2.0 protocol. Grant access to the AWS accounts by using attribute-based access controls (ABACs).","B":"Configure AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) by using IAM Identity Center as an identity source. Enable automatic provisioning by using the System for Cross-domain Identity Management (SCIM) v2.0 protocol. Grant access to the AWS accounts by using IAM Identity Center permission sets.","C":"In one of the company’s AWS accounts, configure AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) to use a SAML 2.0 identity provider. Provision IAM users that are mapped to the federated users. Grant access that corresponds to appropriate groups in Active Directory. Grant access to the required AWS accounts by using cross-account IAM users.","D":"In one of the company’s AWS accounts, configure AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) to use an OpenID Connect (OIDC) identity provider. Provision IAM roles that grant access to the AWS account for the federated users that correspond to appropriate groups in Active Directory. Grant access to the required AWS accounts by using cross-account IAM roles."},"options_zh":{"A":"設定 AWS IAM Identity Center（AWS Single Sign-On），透過 SAML 2.0 連接到 Active Directory。使用 System for Cross-domain Identity Management（SCIM）v2.0 協定啟用自動佈建。使用屬性型存取控制（ABAC）授予對 AWS 帳戶的存取權。","B":"設定 AWS IAM Identity Center（AWS Single Sign-On），使用 IAM Identity Center 本身作為身分來源。使用 System for Cross-domain Identity Management（SCIM）v2.0 協定啟用自動佈建。使用 IAM Identity Center 權限集授予對 AWS 帳戶的存取權。","C":"在公司其中一個 AWS 帳戶中，設定 AWS Identity and Access Management（IAM）使用 SAML 2.0 身分提供者。佈建對應到聯合使用者的 IAM 使用者。依 Active Directory 中對應的群組授予適當存取權。透過跨帳戶 IAM 使用者授予對所需 AWS 帳戶的存取權。","D":"在公司其中一個 AWS 帳戶中，設定 AWS Identity and Access Management（IAM）使用 OpenID Connect（OIDC）身分提供者。為對應到 Active Directory 中適當群組的聯合使用者佈建可存取該 AWS 帳戶的 IAM 角色。透過跨帳戶 IAM 角色授予對所需 AWS 帳戶的存取權。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":78},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"All four requirements point to AWS IAM Identity Center as the org-wide single sign-on layer fronting the existing on-premises Active Directory: users authenticate once with their corporate AD credentials, identities remain managed in a single location (the on-prem AD), access is centralized across every AWS Organizations account, and conditional access by group/role is implemented with ABAC, which derives session tags from directory user attributes/group membership to scale permissions. Option A is the only choice that combines IAM Identity Center + AD as the identity source + org-wide centralized access grants, so it is the best answer. Option B fails because it uses IAM Identity Center's own internal (default) directory as the identity source, which means identities are no longer managed in the corporate AD and authentication no longer uses AD. Options C and D are the legacy per-account IAM federation pattern (IAM users or IAM roles in one account plus cross-account access) which does not provide native, Organizations-wide centralized administration; C is further broken because 'IAM users mapped to federated users' is not a valid pattern, and D uses OIDC, which is not the federation protocol Active Directory uses (AD federates via SAML through ADFS). Note that A's literal wording ('connect IAM Identity Center to Active Directory by SAML 2.0' plus SCIM) is technically imprecise, because a self-managed on-prem AD is connected through AWS Directory Service (AD Connector or an AWS Managed Microsoft AD two-way trust) rather than SAML/SCIM; SAML/SCIM is how external IdPs connect. Despite that imprecision, A's overall architecture is the only one that satisfies all four requirements, so it remains correct over the dump's suggested D.","explanation_zh":"四項需求都指向以 AWS IAM Identity Center 作為橫跨整個 AWS Organizations 的 SSO 層，並以既有的地端 Active Directory 為身分來源：使用者用公司 AD 帳密登入一次、身分只集中管理在地端 AD 這個單一位置、對所有帳號集中授權，並以 ABAC（依目錄使用者屬性／群組成員產生 session tags）落實依群組與角色的條件式存取。選項 A 是唯一同時具備『IAM Identity Center ＋ AD 身分來源 ＋ 組織層級集中授權』的組合，故為最佳解。選項 B 錯在把 IAM Identity Center 內建（預設）目錄當身分來源，導致身分不再集中於公司 AD、也不再用 AD 驗證。選項 C 與 D 屬於舊式單帳號 IAM 聯合（在單一帳號建 IAM users 或 IAM roles 再跨帳號存取），無法提供 Organizations 原生的集中管理；C 的『IAM users mapped to federated users』本身就不是有效做法，D 用 OIDC 也不是 AD 的聯合協定（AD 走 ADFS 的 SAML）。須留意 A 字面上的『以 SAML 2.0 連接 AD』加 SCIM 用詞並不精確——地端自管 AD 實際上是透過 AWS Directory Service（AD Connector 或 AWS Managed Microsoft AD 雙向信任）連接，SAML/SCIM 是外部 IdP 的連法；但即便措辭不精確，A 的整體架構仍是唯一滿足四項需求者，優於 dump 建議的 D。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Uses IAM Identity Center's own internal default directory as the identity source, so identities are no longer managed in the single corporate AD location and authentication no longer uses the on-prem AD, violating two of the requirements.","why_zh":"以 IAM Identity Center 內建預設目錄為身分來源，身分不再集中於公司 AD、也不用 AD 驗證，違反兩項需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Legacy single-account IAM SAML federation that then 'provisions IAM users mapped to federated users' — federation issues temporary credentials, not standing IAM users, and 'cross-account IAM users' is not a real construct; it also lacks Organizations-wide centralized administration.","why_zh":"舊式單帳號 IAM SAML 聯合，還要『建 IAM users 對應聯合使用者』——聯合發的是臨時憑證而非常設 IAM 使用者，且『跨帳號 IAM users』並非真實機制，也缺乏組織層級集中管理。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Dump's suggested answer. OIDC is not the protocol Active Directory uses to federate (AD uses SAML via ADFS), and the per-account IAM IdP + cross-account IAM roles pattern is the operationally heavy legacy approach that lacks native Organizations-wide centralized SSO administration.","why_zh":"dump 建議答案。OIDC 並非 AD 的聯合協定（AD 走 ADFS 的 SAML），且單帳號 IAM IdP ＋跨帳號 IAM roles 是營運沉重的舊式做法，缺乏組織層級原生集中 SSO 管理。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/gs-ad.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/manage-your-identity-source-ad.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/manage-your-identity-source-change.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/configure-abac-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/configure-abac-attributes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/permissionsetsconcept.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":22,"question_en":"A software company has deployed an application that consumes a REST API by using Amazon API Gateway, AWS Lambda functions, and an Amazon DynamoDB table. The application is showing an increase in the number of errors during PUT requests. Most of the PUT calls come from a small number of clients that are authenticated with specific API keys. A solutions architect has identified that a large number of the PUT requests originate from one client. The API is noncritical, and clients can tolerate retries of unsuccessful calls. However, the errors are displayed to customers and are causing damage to the API’s reputation. What should the solutions architect recommend to improve the customer experience?","question_zh":"一家軟體公司部署了一個應用程式，透過 Amazon API Gateway、AWS Lambda 函式和 Amazon DynamoDB 表格來使用 REST API。該應用程式在 PUT 請求期間顯示的錯誤數量正在增加。大多數 PUT 呼叫來自少數使用特定 API 金鑰驗證的客戶端。解決方案架構師發現大量 PUT 請求來自單一客戶端。此 API 並非關鍵服務，客戶端可以容忍重試失敗的呼叫。然而，這些錯誤會顯示給客戶，並損害該 API 的聲譽。解決方案架構師應建議什麼方案來改善客戶體驗？","options_en":{"A":"Implement retry logic with exponential backoff and irregular variation in the client application. Ensure that the errors are caught and handled with descriptive error messages.","B":"Implement API throttling through a usage plan at the API Gateway level. Ensure that the client application handles code 429 replies without error.","C":"Turn on API caching to enhance responsiveness for the production stage. Run 10-minute load tests. Verify that the cache capacity is appropriate for the workload.","D":"Implement reserved concurrency at the Lambda function level to provide the resources that are needed during sudden increases in tra®c."},"options_zh":{"A":"在客戶端應用程式中實作具有指數退避（exponential backoff）與不規則變化的重試邏輯。確保錯誤被攔截並以描述性的錯誤訊息處理。","B":"在 API Gateway 層級透過使用計劃（usage plan）實作 API 節流。確保客戶端應用程式能正常處理 429 錯誤碼回應，不視為錯誤。","C":"為生產階段（production stage）開啟 API 快取以提升回應速度。執行 10 分鐘的負載測試。確認快取容量適合該工作負載。","D":"在 Lambda 函式層級實作預留並行（reserved concurrency），以在流量突增時提供所需資源。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":72,"A":26},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":23,"question_en":"A company is running a data-intensive application on AWS. The application runs on a cluster of hundreds of Amazon EC2 instances. A shared file system also runs on several EC2 instances that store 200 TB of data. The application reads and modifies the data on the shared file system and generates a report. The job runs once monthly, reads a subset of the files from the shared file system, and takes about 72 hours to complete. The compute instances scale in an Auto Scaling group, but the instances that host the shared file system run continuously. The compute and storage instances are all in the same AWS Region. A solutions architect needs to reduce costs by replacing the shared file system instances. The file system must provide high performance access to the needed data for the duration of the 72-hour run. Which solution will provide the LARGEST overall cost reduction while meeting these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上執行資料密集型應用程式。該應用程式運行於數百個 Amazon EC2 執行個體組成的叢集上。另有一個共用檔案系統運行於數個 EC2 執行個體上，儲存 200 TB 的資料。該應用程式會讀取並修改共用檔案系統上的資料並產生報表。此工作每月執行一次，讀取檔案系統中的部分檔案，耗時約 72 小時才能完成。運算執行個體在 Auto Scaling 群組中伸縮，但承載共用檔案系統的執行個體則持續運行。運算與儲存執行個體皆位於同一 AWS 區域。解決方案架構師需要透過替換共用檔案系統執行個體來降低成本。該檔案系統必須在 72 小時執行期間提供對所需資料的高效能存取。哪個解決方案能在滿足這些需求的同時提供最大的整體成本降低？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate the data from the existing shared file system to an Amazon S3 bucket that uses the S3 Intelligent-Tiering storage class. Before the job runs each month, use Amazon FSx for Lustre to create a new file system with the data from Amazon S3 by using lazy loading. Use the new file system as the shared storage for the duration of the job. Delete the file system when the job is complete.","B":"Migrate the data from the existing shared file system to a large Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume with Multi-Attach enabled. Attach the EBS volume to each of the instances by using a user data script in the Auto Scaling group launch template. Use the EBS volume as the shared storage for the duration of the job. Detach the EBS volume when the job is complete","C":"Migrate the data from the existing shared file system to an Amazon S3 bucket that uses the S3 Standard storage class. Before the job runs each month, use Amazon FSx for Lustre to create a new file system with the data from Amazon S3 by using batch loading. Use the new file system as the shared storage for the duration of the job. Delete the file system when the job is complete.","D":"Migrate the data from the existing shared file system to an Amazon S3 bucket. Before the job runs each month, use AWS Storage Gateway to create a file gateway with the data from Amazon S3. Use the file gateway as the shared storage for the job. Delete the file gateway when the job is complete."},"options_zh":{"A":"將資料從現有共用檔案系統遷移至使用 S3 Intelligent-Tiering 儲存類別的 Amazon S3 儲存桶。在每月工作執行前，使用 Amazon FSx for Lustre 透過延遲載入（lazy loading）從 Amazon S3 建立一個新檔案系統。在工作執行期間使用該新檔案系統作為共用儲存。工作完成後刪除該檔案系統。","B":"將資料從現有共用檔案系統遷移至已啟用 Multi-Attach 的大型 Amazon Elastic Block Store（Amazon EBS）磁碟區。透過 Auto Scaling 群組啟動範本中的使用者資料腳本，將該 EBS 磁碟區附加到每個執行個體。在工作執行期間使用該 EBS 磁碟區作為共用儲存。工作完成後卸離該 EBS 磁碟區。","C":"將資料從現有共用檔案系統遷移至使用 S3 Standard 儲存類別的 Amazon S3 儲存桶。在每月工作執行前，使用 Amazon FSx for Lustre 透過批次載入（batch loading）從 Amazon S3 建立一個新檔案系統。在工作執行期間使用該新檔案系統作為共用儲存。工作完成後刪除該檔案系統。","D":"將資料從現有共用檔案系統遷移至 Amazon S3 儲存桶。在每月工作執行前，使用 AWS Storage Gateway 透過 Amazon S3 中的資料建立一個檔案閘道（file gateway）。在工作期間使用該檔案閘道作為共用儲存。工作完成後刪除該檔案閘道。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":86},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The cost problem is the fleet of EC2 instances that host the 200 TB shared file system and run continuously, even though the job runs only ~72 hours per month and reads only a subset of the files. Option A eliminates that by moving the durable 200 TB to an Amazon S3 bucket using S3 Intelligent-Tiering, which automatically moves objects to the most cost-effective access tier (Infrequent Access, Archive Instant Access) with no retrieval fees and no operational overhead — ideal for data that sits mostly idle between monthly runs. Before each run it creates an Amazon FSx for Lustre file system linked to that bucket with lazy loading, which pulls a file's contents from S3 only on first access; because the job reads just a subset, you avoid loading the full 200 TB and pay for the high-performance Lustre file system only for the 72-hour window, deleting it afterward. This combines the cheapest at-rest storage with pay-only-when-running high-performance compute, giving the LARGEST overall cost reduction while still providing high-performance POSIX access. Option C is functionally valid but uses more expensive S3 Standard and batch/preloads all data (paying to load files never read), so its reduction is smaller.","explanation_zh":"成本痛點在於承載 200 TB 共享檔案系統、且持續不停運行的那批 EC2 執行個體，然而作業每月只跑約 72 小時、且只讀取檔案的子集。選項 A 將長期保存的 200 TB 移至使用 S3 Intelligent-Tiering 的 Amazon S3 儲存桶，該儲存類別會自動把物件移到最具成本效益的存取層（Infrequent Access、Archive Instant Access），無取回費用、無需人工管理，非常適合在每月執行之間大多閒置的資料。每次執行前，建立一個以 lazy loading 連結該儲存桶的 Amazon FSx for Lustre 檔案系統：lazy loading 只在應用程式首次存取檔案時才從 S3 拉取該檔內容，因為作業只讀子集，便可避免載入完整 200 TB，並且只在 72 小時視窗內為高效能 Lustre 檔案系統付費，完成後即刪除。這同時兼具最便宜的靜態儲存與「僅在運行時付費」的高效能運算，在仍提供高效能 POSIX 存取的前提下帶來最大的整體成本縮減。選項 C 功能上可行但使用較貴的 S3 Standard 且以 batch loading 預載全部資料（為從未讀取的檔案付出載入成本），整體縮減較小。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"EBS Multi-Attach is limited to at most 16 Nitro instances in a single AZ and only on io1/io2 Provisioned IOPS SSD volumes; this cluster has hundreds of instances, so it cannot serve them. It also requires a clustered file system because standard EXT4/XFS are not safe for concurrent multi-writer access. It is technically infeasible here.","why_zh":"EBS Multi-Attach 最多只能連接同一 AZ 內 16 個 Nitro 執行個體，且僅支援 io1/io2 Provisioned IOPS SSD 磁碟區；本叢集有數百個執行個體，無法滿足。它還需要叢集檔案系統，因為標準的 EXT4/XFS 不適合多寫入者並發存取。在此情境下技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Functionally similar to A but uses S3 Standard (more expensive at-rest than Intelligent-Tiering for once-monthly access) and batch/preloads all data into Lustre. Preloading the full 200 TB when the job reads only a subset wastes load time and provides no benefit, so the overall cost reduction is smaller than A.","why_zh":"功能上與 A 相似，但使用 S3 Standard（對於每月一次的存取，其靜態成本高於 Intelligent-Tiering），並以 batch loading 預載全部資料至 Lustre。當作業只讀取子集時預載整個 200 TB 浪費載入時間且無益處，因此整體成本縮減小於 A。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Storage Gateway file gateway provides NFS/SMB cached access to S3 for hybrid/on-premises scenarios; it is not a high-performance parallel file system and cannot deliver the throughput hundreds of HPC compute instances need. It fails the high-performance requirement.","why_zh":"AWS Storage Gateway file gateway 為混合/地端情境提供對 S3 的 NFS/SMB 快取存取；它並非高效能平行檔案系統，無法提供數百個 HPC 運算執行個體所需的吞吐量，不符合高效能需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/LustreGuide/importing-files-dra.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/LustreGuide/create-dra-linked-data-repo.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/intelligent-tiering.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/storage-class-intro.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ebs/latest/userguide/ebs-volumes-multi.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":24,"question_en":"A company is developing a new service that will be accessed using TCP on a static port. A solutions architect must ensure that the service is highly available, has redundancy across Availability Zones, and is accessible using the DNS name my.service.com, which is publicly accessible. The service must use fixed address assignments so other companies can add the addresses to their allow lists. Assuming that resources are deployed in multiple Availability Zones in a single Region, which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在开发一项新服务，将在静态端口上使用 TCP 进行访问。解决方案架构师必须确保服务高度可用、跨可用区具有冗余， 并且可以使用可公开访问的 DNS 名称 my.service.com 进行访问。该服务必须使用固定地址分配，以便其他公司可以将地址添加到其 允许列表中。 假设资源部署在单个Region的多个可用区，哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create Amazon EC2 instances with an Elastic IP address for each instance. Create a Network Load Balancer (NLB) and expose the static TCP port. Register EC2 instances with the NLB. Create a new name server record set named my.service.com, and assign the Elastic IP addresses of the EC2 instances to the record set. Provide the Elastic IP addresses of the EC2 instances to the other companies to add to their allow lists.","B":"Create an Amazon ECS cluster and a service definition for the application. Create and assign public IP addresses for the ECS cluster. Create a Network Load Balancer (NLB) and expose the TCP port. Create a target group and assign the ECS cluster name to the NLCreate a new A record set named my.service.com, and assign the public IP addresses of the ECS cluster to the record set. Provide the public IP addresses of the ECS cluster to the other companies to add to their allow lists.","C":"Create Amazon EC2 instances for the service. Create one Elastic IP address for each Availability Zone. Create a Network Load Balancer (NLB) and expose the assigned TCP port. Assign the Elastic IP addresses to the NLB for each Availability Zone. Create a target group and register the EC2 instances with the NLB. Create a new A (alias) record set named my.service.com, and assign the NLB DNS name to the record set.","D":"Create an Amazon ECS cluster and a service definition for the application. Create and assign public IP address for each host in the cluster. Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and expose the static TCP port. Create a target group and assign the ECS service definition name to the ALB. Create a new CNAME record set and associate the public IP addresses to the record set. Provide the Elastic IP addresses of the Amazon EC2 instances to the other companies to add to their allow lists."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 Amazon EC2 实例，并为每个实例分配一个弹性 IP 地址。创建网络负载均衡器 (NLB) 并公开静态 TCP 端口。向 NLB 注册 EC2 实例。创建名为 my.service.com 的新名称服务器记录集，并将 EC2 实例的弹性 IP 地址分配给该记录集。将 EC2 实例的弹性 IP 地址提供给其他公司以添加到其允许列表中。","B":"为应用程序创建 Amazon ECS 集群和服务定义。为ECS集群创建并分配公网IP地址。创建网络负载均衡器 (NLB) 并公开 TCP 端 口。创建目标组并将ECS集群名称分配给NL创建一个名为my.service.com的新A记录集，并将ECS集群的公共IP地址分配给该记录 集。将 ECS 集群的公共 IP 地址提供给其他公司以添加到他们的允许列表中。","C":"为服务创建 Amazon EC2 实例。为每个可用区创建一个弹性 IP 地址。创建网络负载均衡器 (NLB) 并公开分配的 TCP 端口。将弹 性 IP 地址分配给每个可用区的 NLB。创建目标组并向 NLB 注册 EC2 实例。创建名为 my.service.com 的新 A（别名）记录集，并 将 NLB DNS 名称分配给该记录集。","D":"为应用程序创建 Amazon ECS 集群和服务定义。为集群中的每台主机创建并分配公共 IP 地址。创建应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 并公开静态 TCP 端口。创建目标组并将 ECS 服务定义名称分配给 ALB。创建新的 CNAME 记录集并将公共 IP 地址关联到记录集。 将 Amazon EC2 实例的弹性 IP 地址提供给其他公司以添加到其允许列表中。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":25,"question_en":"A company uses an on-premises data analytics platform. The system is highly available in a fully redundant configuration across 12 servers in the company’s data center. The system runs scheduled jobs, both hourly and daily, in addition to one-time requests from users. Scheduled jobs can take between 20 minutes and 2 hours to finish running and have tight SLAs. The scheduled jobs account for 65% of the system usage. User jobs typically finish running in less than 5 minutes and have no SLA. The user jobs account for 35% of system usage. During system failures, scheduled jobs must continue to meet SLAs. However, user jobs can be delayed. A solutions architect needs to move the system to Amazon EC2 instances and adopt a consumption-based model to reduce costs with no long- term commitments. The solution must maintain high availability and must not affect the SLAs. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司使用本地数据分析平台。该系统在公司数据中心的 12 台服务器上采用完全冗余配置，具有高可用性。 除了用户的一次性请求之外，系统每小时和每天运行预定作业。计划作业可能需要 20 分钟到 2 小时才能完成运行，并且具有严格的 SLA。计划作业占系统使用量的 65%。用户作业通常会在 5 分钟内完成运行，并且没有 SLA。用户作业占系统使用量的 35%。在系统 故障期间，计划的作业必须继续满足 SLA。但是，用户作业可能会延迟。 解决方案架构师需要将系统迁移到 Amazon EC2 实例，并采用基于消耗的模型来降低成本，而无需做出长期承诺。该解决方案必须 保持高可用性，并且不得影响 SLA。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Split the 12 instances across two Availability Zones in the chosen AWS Region. Run two instances in each Availability Zone as On- Demand Instances with Capacity Reservations. Run four instances in each Availability Zone as Spot Instances.","B":"Split the 12 instances across three Availability Zones in the chosen AWS Region. In one of the Availability Zones, run all four instances as On-Demand Instances with Capacity Reservations. Run the remaining instances as Spot Instances.","C":"Split the 12 instances across three Availability Zones in the chosen AWS Region. Run two instances in each Availability Zone as On- Demand Instances with a Savings Plan. Run two instances in each Availability Zone as Spot Instances.","D":"Split the 12 instances across three Availability Zones in the chosen AWS Region. Run three instances in each Availability Zone as On- Demand Instances with Capacity Reservations. Run one instance in each Availability Zone as a Spot Instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 12 个实例拆分到所选 AWS 区域中的两个可用区。在每个可用区中运行两个实例作为具有容量预留的按需实例。每个可用区 中运行四个实例作为 Spot 实例。","B":"将 12 个实例拆分到所选 AWS 区域中的三个可用区。在可用区之一中，将所有四个实例作为具有容量预留的按需实例运行。将 其余实例作为 Spot 实例运行。","C":"将 12 个实例拆分到所选 AWS 区域中的三个可用区。在每个可用区中运行两个实例作为具有 Savings Plan 的按需实例。每个可 用区中运行两个实例作为 Spot 实例。","D":"将 12 个实例拆分到所选 AWS 区域中的三个可用区。在每个可用区中运行三个实例作为具有容量预留的按需实例。在每个可用 区中运行一个实例作为 Spot 实例。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":91},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Two hard requirements drive the answer. (1) 'Consumption-based, no long-term commitments': AWS Savings Plans require a commitment to a specified amount of compute for a one- or three-year term, so Option C is disqualified by definition. On-Demand Capacity Reservations, by contrast, can be created for immediate use at any time, are billed at On-Demand rates only while active, and can be cancelled anytime with no term commitment — they guarantee capacity in a specific AZ without any long-term obligation. (2) 'During failures the scheduled jobs (65% of usage, tight SLA) must continue to meet SLAs while user jobs (35%, no SLA) can be delayed': the SLA-bound work must run on reliable, capacity-assured instances that survive an AZ failure, while deferrable no-SLA user work can safely run on interruptible Spot. Option D places 3 On-Demand instances backed by Capacity Reservations in EACH of 3 AZs (9 guaranteed = 75% of the fleet, comfortably covering the 65% scheduled workload) plus 1 Spot per AZ (3 Spot for the cheap, deferrable user jobs). If one AZ fails, only 3 On-Demand are lost, leaving 6 capacity-reserved instances still distributed across the two surviving AZs, and user jobs can be shed to keep scheduled jobs within SLA. It is the only option that avoids a long-term commitment AND keeps guaranteed, AZ-distributed capacity to protect the SLA during a failure, using the cheapest viable mix (Spot only for the no-SLA portion). The community answer (D) is correct; the dump's suggested 'C' is wrong because Savings Plans are a long-term commitment.","explanation_zh":"兩個硬性條件決定答案。(1)「按用量計費、無長期承諾」：AWS Savings Plans 需要承諾一年或三年期的特定運算量，屬長期承諾，因此選項 C 直接不合格。相對地，On-Demand Capacity Reservations 可隨時建立供立即使用、僅在啟用期間以 On-Demand 費率計費、且可隨時取消而無任何期限承諾——既保證特定 AZ 的容量，又符合「無長期承諾」的按用量模式。(2)「故障期間排程作業（占用量 65%、SLA 嚴格）必須持續達成 SLA，而使用者作業（35%、無 SLA）可延後」：受 SLA 約束的工作必須跑在可靠、容量有保證且能撐過單一 AZ 故障的執行個體上；可延後、無 SLA 的使用者工作則可安全地放在可被中斷的 Spot。選項 D 在 3 個 AZ 的每一個都放 3 台由 Capacity Reservation 背書的 On-Demand（共 9 台保證容量＝機隊 75%，足以涵蓋 65% 排程工作並留有餘裕），再各放 1 台 Spot（共 3 台便宜且可延後的使用者作業）。若一個 AZ 故障，只損失 3 台 On-Demand，仍有 6 台保證容量分散在其餘兩個 AZ，且可犧牲使用者作業以確保排程作業達成 SLA。這是唯一同時避免長期承諾、又能保有跨 AZ 分散之保證容量以在故障時保護 SLA 的選項，並以最省成本的組合（僅無 SLA 部分用 Spot）達成。社群答案 D 正確；題庫建議的 C 因 Savings Plans 屬長期承諾而錯誤。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Only two AZs reduces high availability, and just 4 On-Demand+Capacity Reservation instances (33% of the fleet) cannot reliably host the 65% SLA-bound scheduled workload. If one AZ fails you are left with only 2 guaranteed instances (~17%), far short of the scheduled demand, so the SLA-bound work would spill onto interruptible Spot and risk breaches.","why_zh":"僅用兩個 AZ 降低可用性，且只有 4 台 On-Demand+Capacity Reservation（機隊 33%）無法可靠承載占 65% 的 SLA 排程工作。一個 AZ 故障後只剩 2 台保證容量（約 17%），遠低於排程需求，SLA 工作勢必溢流到可被中斷的 Spot 而有違約風險。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Concentrating ALL four On-Demand (Capacity Reservation) instances in a single AZ creates a single point of failure: if that one AZ fails, 100% of the guaranteed capacity is lost and the SLA-bound scheduled jobs have no reliable capacity, directly violating 'scheduled jobs must continue during failures'. The other eight instances are Spot and can be reclaimed at any time.","why_zh":"把全部 4 台 On-Demand（Capacity Reservation）集中在單一 AZ 形成單點故障：一旦該 AZ 故障，100% 的保證容量全失，SLA 排程作業沒有可靠容量，直接違反「故障期間排程作業必須持續」。其餘 8 台皆為 Spot，可能隨時被回收。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Uses a Savings Plan, which by definition requires a one- or three-year commitment (per the Savings Plans user guide), directly violating the explicit 'no long-term commitments' / consumption-based requirement — so it is invalid regardless of its otherwise reasonable 3-AZ layout. It also provides only 6 On-Demand instances (50%), below the 65% SLA workload. This is the dump's suggested answer and it is wrong.","why_zh":"使用 Savings Plan，依定義需要一年或三年承諾（見 Savings Plans 使用者指南），直接違反明確的「無長期承諾」按用量需求，因此即使其 3-AZ 佈局看似合理仍不合格。且僅提供 6 台 On-Demand（50%），低於 65% 的 SLA 工作量。此為題庫建議答案，實為錯誤。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/savingsplans/latest/userguide/what-is-savings-plans.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/capacity-reservations-using.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/ec2-capacity-reservations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/using-spot-instances.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":26,"question_en":"A security engineer determined that an existing application retrieves credentials to an Amazon RDS for MySQL database from an encrypted file in Amazon S3. For the next version of the application, the security engineer wants to implement the following application design changes to improve security: The database must use strong, randomly generated passwords stored in a secure AWS managed service. The application resources must be deployed through AWS CloudFormation. The application must rotate credentials for the database every 90 days. A solutions architect will generate a CloudFormation template to deploy the application. Which resources specified in the CloudFormation template will meet the security engineer’s requirements with the LEAST amount of operational overhead?","question_zh":"安全工程师确定现有应用程序从 Amazon S3 中的加密文件检索 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库的凭证。对于应用程序的下一版本，安 全工程师希望实施以下应用程序设计更改以提高安全性： 数据库必须使用存储在安全 AWS 托管服务中的随机生成的强密码。 应用程序资源必须通过 AWS CloudFormation 部署。 应用程序必须每 90 天轮换数据库的凭据。 解决方案架构师将生成 CloudFormation 模板来部署应用程序。 CloudFormation 模板中指定的哪些资源将以最少的运营开销满足安全工程师的要求？","options_en":{"A":"Generate the database password as a secret resource using AWS Secrets Manager. Create an AWS Lambda function resource to rotate the database password. Specify a Secrets Manager RotationSchedule resource to rotate the database password every 90 days.","B":"Generate the database password as a SecureString parameter type using AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Create an AWS Lambda function resource to rotate the database password. Specify a Parameter Store RotationSchedule resource to rotate the database password every 90 days.","C":"Generate the database password as a secret resource using AWS Secrets Manager. Create an AWS Lambda function resource to rotate the database password. Create an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule resource to trigger the Lambda function password rotation every 90 days.","D":"Generate the database password as a SecureString parameter type using AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Specify an AWS AppSync DataSource resource to automatically rotate the database password every 90 days."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Secrets Manager 生成数据库密码作为秘密资源。创建 AWS Lambda 函数资源以轮换数据库密码。指定 Secrets Manager RotationSchedule 资源以每 90 天轮换一次数据库密码。","B":"使用 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store 将数据库密码生成为 SecureString 参数类型。创建 AWS Lambda 函数资源以轮换数 据库密码。指定 Parameter Store RotationSchedule 资源以每 90 天轮换一次数据库密码。","C":"使用 AWS Secrets Manager 生成数据库密码作为秘密资源。创建 AWS Lambda 函数资源以轮换数据库密码。创建 Amazon EventBridge 计划规则资源以每 90 天触发一次 Lambda 函数密码轮换。","D":"使用 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store 将数据库密码生成为 SecureString 参数类型。指定 AWS AppSync 数据源资源以每 90 天自动轮换数据库密码。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"AWS Secrets Manager is the secure AWS managed service purpose-built to generate strong, random passwords (via the GenerateSecretString capability) and to natively rotate database credentials. In CloudFormation you create the secret with AWS::SecretsManager::Secret and turn on managed automatic rotation with the AWS::SecretsManager::RotationSchedule resource, which references a rotation Lambda and a RotationRules schedule (e.g., AutomaticallyAfterDays: 90). This native RotationSchedule resource is the AWS-managed, built-in scheduling mechanism, so it is the LEAST-operational-overhead approach. Option C also uses Secrets Manager and a Lambda but replaces the native RotationSchedule with a hand-built EventBridge scheduled rule, which bypasses Secrets Manager's rotation orchestration (the createSecret/setSecret/testSecret/finishSecret state machine and version staging) and adds undifferentiated heavy lifting, so it has more operational overhead. The qualifier 'LEAST amount of operational overhead' decides between A and C in favor of A.","explanation_zh":"AWS Secrets Manager 是專為產生強隨機密碼（透過 GenerateSecretString 功能）並原生輪替資料庫憑證而設計的安全 AWS 受管服務。在 CloudFormation 中，使用 AWS::SecretsManager::Secret 建立密碼，並以 AWS::SecretsManager::RotationSchedule 資源開啟受管自動輪替，該資源參照輪替用的 Lambda 與 RotationRules 排程（例如 AutomaticallyAfterDays: 90）。此原生 RotationSchedule 資源即 AWS 受管的內建排程機制，因此營運負擔最低。選項 C 雖同樣使用 Secrets Manager 與 Lambda，卻以自行建立的 EventBridge 排程規則取代原生 RotationSchedule，繞過 Secrets Manager 的輪替編排（createSecret/setSecret/testSecret/finishSecret 狀態機與版本暫存），增加額外營運負擔。題目限定『最少營運負擔』，故在 A 與 C 之間應選 A。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"There is no 'Parameter Store RotationSchedule' CloudFormation resource and SSM Parameter Store SecureString has no native automatic credential rotation. AWS docs recommend Secrets Manager (not Parameter Store) for credentials that require automatic rotation; B references a non-existent resource.","why_zh":"並不存在『Parameter Store RotationSchedule』這個 CloudFormation 資源，且 SSM Parameter Store 的 SecureString 沒有原生自動輪替憑證的功能。AWS 文件建議需自動輪替的憑證應使用 Secrets Manager 而非 Parameter Store；B 引用了不存在的資源。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Technically workable (Secrets Manager + Lambda + EventBridge) but it discards the native AWS::SecretsManager::RotationSchedule resource and instead hand-builds an EventBridge schedule, bypassing Secrets Manager's built-in rotation orchestration and version staging. That is more operational overhead than A, which the 'LEAST operational overhead' qualifier rules out.","why_zh":"技術上可行（Secrets Manager + Lambda + EventBridge），但放棄原生的 AWS::SecretsManager::RotationSchedule 資源，改以自建 EventBridge 排程，繞過 Secrets Manager 內建的輪替編排與版本暫存，營運負擔高於 A；在『最少營運負擔』限定下被排除。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS AppSync is a managed GraphQL API service; there is no 'AppSync DataSource' feature that rotates database passwords. Parameter Store SecureString also lacks native rotation. The proposed mechanism does not exist.","why_zh":"AWS AppSync 是受管的 GraphQL API 服務，並沒有任何『AppSync DataSource』可輪替資料庫密碼的功能；且 Parameter Store SecureString 亦無原生輪替。所述機制根本不存在。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-secretsmanager-rotationschedule.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/cloudformation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/rotate-secrets_how.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-parameter-store.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/reference_available-rotation-templates.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":27,"question_en":"A company is storing data in several Amazon DynamoDB tables. A solutions architect must use a serverless architecture to make the data accessible publicly through a simple API over HTTPS. The solution must scale automatically in response to demand. Which solutions meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司将数据存储在多个 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。解决方案架构师必须使用无服务器架构，通过 HTTPS 上的简单 API 公开访问数 据。该解决方案必须根据需求自动扩展。 哪些解决方案满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon API Gateway REST API. Configure this API with direct integrations to DynamoDB by using API Gateway’s AWS integration type.","B":"Create an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API. Configure this API with direct integrations to Dynamo DB by using API Gateway’s AWS integration type.","C":"Create an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API. Configure this API with integrations to AWS Lambda functions that return data from the DynamoDB tables.","D":"Create an accelerator in AWS Global Accelerator. Configure this accelerator with AWS Lambda@Edge function integrations that return data from the DynamoDB tables.","E":"Create a Network Load Balancer. Configure listener rules to forward requests to the appropriate AWS Lambda functions."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 Amazon API Gateway REST API。使用 API Gateway 的 AWS 集成类型配置此 API，使其直接集成到 DynamoDB。","B":"创建 Amazon API Gateway HTTP API。使用 API Gateway 的 AWS 集成类型配置此 API，使其直接集成到 Dynamo DB。","C":"创建 Amazon API Gateway HTTP API。通过与从 DynamoDB 表返回数据的 AWS Lambda 函数的集成来配置此 API。","D":"在 AWS Global Accelerator 中创建加速器。使用从 DynamoDB 表返回数据的 AWS Lambda@Edge 函数集成配置此加速器。","E":"创建网络负载均衡器。配置侦听器规则以将请求转发到适当的 AWS Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AC":81},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is a fully serverless, auto-scaling, publicly accessible HTTPS API over data in DynamoDB tables. (A) An API Gateway REST API can integrate directly with DynamoDB using the AWS integration type and mapping templates (for example a POST method targeting DynamoDB PutItem/Query), a documented serverless pattern that needs no Lambda and scales automatically over HTTPS. (C) An API Gateway HTTP API fronting Lambda functions that read the DynamoDB tables is the canonical serverless CRUD pattern; both API Gateway and Lambda scale automatically and serve HTTPS. (B) is the key trap: HTTP APIs only support a fixed set of first-class AWS service integration subtypes - EventBridge-PutEvents, SQS (Send/Receive/Delete/Purge), AppConfig-GetConfiguration, Kinesis-PutRecord, and Step Functions (Start/StartSync/Stop). DynamoDB is not in that list, so a direct HTTP API-to-DynamoDB AWS integration is impossible. (D) Lambda@Edge is a CloudFront feature, not a Global Accelerator feature; Global Accelerator is a Layer 4 accelerator that routes to endpoints like ALB/NLB/EC2/EIP and cannot run Lambda@Edge, so the architecture is invalid. (E) A Network Load Balancer operates at Layer 4 and cannot invoke Lambda functions as targets - only an Application Load Balancer supports Lambda targets - and an NLB is not a simple serverless HTTPS API. The dump's suggested 'C,D' is wrong because D is not a valid integration.","explanation_zh":"需求是完全 serverless、可自動擴展、以 HTTPS 對外公開、讀取 DynamoDB tables 資料的簡單 API。(A) API Gateway REST API 可透過 AWS integration type 搭配 mapping template 直接整合 DynamoDB（例如 POST 方法對應 DynamoDB PutItem/Query），是官方記載的 serverless 模式，無需 Lambda、自動擴展並提供 HTTPS。(C) API Gateway HTTP API 前置 Lambda 函式讀取 DynamoDB tables，是標準 serverless CRUD 模式；API Gateway 與 Lambda 皆自動擴展並提供 HTTPS。(B) 是主要陷阱：HTTP API 的 AWS service（first-class）直接整合僅支援固定的 integration subtypes——EventBridge-PutEvents、SQS（Send/Receive/Delete/Purge）、AppConfig-GetConfiguration、Kinesis-PutRecord、Step Functions（Start/StartSync/Stop），DynamoDB 不在清單內，故 HTTP API 直連 DynamoDB 無法實現。(D) Lambda@Edge 是 CloudFront 的功能，而非 Global Accelerator 的功能；Global Accelerator 為 L4 加速器，導向 ALB/NLB/EC2/EIP 等端點，無法執行 Lambda@Edge，架構不成立。(E) Network Load Balancer 為 L4，無法以 Lambda 函式作為 target（僅 Application Load Balancer 支援 Lambda target），且 NLB 並非簡單的 serverless HTTPS API。Dump 建議的 'C,D' 有誤，因為 D 不是有效整合。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"HTTP APIs support first-class AWS service integrations only for a fixed subtype list (EventBridge-PutEvents, SQS actions, AppConfig-GetConfiguration, Kinesis-PutRecord, Step Functions actions). DynamoDB is not included, so a direct HTTP API-to-DynamoDB AWS integration cannot be created.","why_zh":"HTTP API 的 AWS service（first-class）整合僅限固定 subtype 清單（EventBridge-PutEvents、SQS 操作、AppConfig-GetConfiguration、Kinesis-PutRecord、Step Functions 操作），不含 DynamoDB，故無法建立 HTTP API 直連 DynamoDB 的整合。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Lambda@Edge is a CloudFront feature, not a Global Accelerator feature. Global Accelerator is a Layer 4 network accelerator that routes to endpoints like ALB/NLB/EC2/EIP and cannot run Lambda@Edge functions, so this architecture is not valid.","why_zh":"Lambda@Edge 是 CloudFront 的功能，而非 Global Accelerator 的功能。Global Accelerator 是 L4 網路加速器，導向 ALB/NLB/EC2/EIP 等端點，無法執行 Lambda@Edge，架構不成立。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"A Network Load Balancer operates at Layer 4 and cannot target Lambda functions; only an Application Load Balancer supports Lambda targets. An NLB also lacks content-based listener rules and is not a simple public serverless HTTPS API for DynamoDB data.","why_zh":"Network Load Balancer 為 L4，無法以 Lambda 為 target（僅 Application Load Balancer 支援 Lambda target），且 NLB 沒有基於內容的 listener rule，也非簡單的公開 serverless HTTPS API。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/http-api-develop-integrations-aws-services-reference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/set-up-data-transformations-in-api-gateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/api-gateway-overview-developer-experience.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/solutions/latest/constructs/aws_apigateway_dynamodb.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/global-accelerator/latest/dg/introduction-how-it-works.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・複選"},{"id":28,"question_en":"A company has registered 10 new domain names. The company uses the domains for online marketing. The company needs a solution that will redirect online visitors to a specific URL for each domain. All domains and target URLs are defined in a JSON document. All DNS records are managed by Amazon Route 53. A solutions architect must implement a redirect service that accepts HTTP and HTTPS requests. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect take to meet these requirements with the LEAST amount of operational effort? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"某公司注册了 10 个新域名。该公司使用这些域名进行在线营销。该公司需要一种解决方案，将在线访问者重定向到每个域的特定 URL。所有域和目标 URL 均在 JSON 文档中定义。所有 DNS 记录均由 Amazon Route 53 管理。 解决方案架构师必须实施接受 HTTP 和 HTTPS 请求的重定向服务。 解决方案架构师应采取哪种步骤组合才能以最少的操作工作量满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a dynamic webpage that runs on an Amazon EC2 instance. Configure the webpage to use the JSON document in combination with the event message to look up and respond with a redirect URL.","B":"Create an Application Load Balancer that includes HTTP and HTTPS listeners.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function that uses the JSON document in combination with the event message to look up and respond with a redirect URL.","D":"Use an Amazon API Gateway API with a custom domain to publish an AWS Lambda function.","E":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution. Deploy a Lambda@Edge function.","F":"Create an SSL certificate by using AWS Certificate Manager (ACM). Include the domains as Subject Alternative Names."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建在 Amazon EC2 实例上运行的动态网页。配置网页以结合使用 JSON 文档和事件消息来查找重定向 URL 并进行响应。","B":"创建包含 HTTP 和 HTTPS 侦听器的应用程序负载均衡器。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数结合使用 JSON 文档和事件消息来查找重定向 URL 并进行响应。","D":"使用具有自定义域的 Amazon API Gateway API 来发布 AWS Lambda 函数。","E":"创建 Amazon CloudFront 分配。部署 Lambda@Edge 函数。","F":"使用 AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) 创建 SSL 证书。包括域作为主题备用名称。"},"answer":["B","C","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"CEF":47,"BCF":35},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C","E","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is LEAST operational effort for a service that accepts both HTTP and HTTPS and redirects each of 10 domains to a target URL defined in a JSON document. The fully serverless edge pattern wins: (C) an AWS Lambda function reads the request event plus the JSON document and returns a 301/302 redirect; (E) a CloudFront distribution with that function deployed as Lambda@Edge on the viewer-request event performs the redirect at the edge while CloudFront natively accepts both HTTP and HTTPS (no separate listeners needed); (F) a single ACM certificate listing all 10 domains as Subject Alternative Names is attached to the distribution so every custom domain is served over HTTPS. URL redirect is an explicitly documented Lambda@Edge/CloudFront edge-function use case, and CloudFront for HTTPS requires an ACM cert in us-east-1 (where Lambda@Edge is also authored), so CEF is internally consistent and removes all standing servers. The dump's BCF introduces an Application Load Balancer, which is standing regional infrastructure requiring a VPC, subnets, security groups, and target wiring; CloudFront + Lambda@Edge is the lower operational-effort, AWS-canonical edge-redirect design, so B is not part of the best answer.","explanation_zh":"決定性條件是「最少維運負擔」，需提供同時接受 HTTP 與 HTTPS、並依 JSON 文件將 10 個網域各自轉址到目標 URL 的服務。完全無伺服器的邊緣方案勝出：(C) 建立 AWS Lambda 函式，讀取請求事件與 JSON 文件後回傳 301/302 轉址；(E) 建立 CloudFront distribution 並將該函式部署為 Lambda@Edge 掛在 viewer-request 事件上，在邊緣執行轉址，且 CloudFront 原生即可接受 HTTP 與 HTTPS（不需另設 listener）；(F) 以單一 ACM 憑證將 10 個網域全列為 Subject Alternative Names 並掛到 distribution，使所有自訂網域皆以 HTTPS 提供。URL 轉址是 AWS 官方明列的 Lambda@Edge/CloudFront edge function 用途，且 CloudFront 的 HTTPS 憑證必須位於 us-east-1（也是撰寫 Lambda@Edge 的區域），因此 CEF 彼此一致且不需任何常駐伺服器。題庫的 BCF 引入 Application Load Balancer，屬於需要 VPC、子網路、安全群組與 target 串接的常駐區域基礎設施；CloudFront + Lambda@Edge 才是維運負擔更低、AWS 標準的邊緣轉址設計，所以 B 不屬於最佳答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A dynamic webpage on an EC2 instance is the highest operational-overhead option: it requires OS patching, capacity/scaling, and availability management for what is a trivial stateless redirect. It directly contradicts the LEAST operational effort requirement.","why_zh":"在 EC2 執行動態網頁是維運負擔最高的選項：需處理作業系統修補、容量與擴展、可用性管理，卻只是做一個無狀態的簡單轉址，完全違反「最少維運負擔」的要求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"An Application Load Balancer with HTTP/HTTPS listeners technically works but adds standing regional infrastructure (VPC, subnets, security groups, Lambda-as-target wiring) and ongoing hourly cost. CloudFront natively accepts both HTTP and HTTPS and, with Lambda@Edge, performs the redirect serverlessly, making ALB unnecessary and higher-effort.","why_zh":"具 HTTP/HTTPS listener 的 Application Load Balancer 技術上可行，但會引入常駐的區域基礎設施（VPC、子網路、安全群組、Lambda 作為 target 的串接）與持續的時數費用。CloudFront 原生即接受 HTTP 與 HTTPS，搭配 Lambda@Edge 即可無伺服器完成轉址，使 ALB 變得多餘且維運負擔更高。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"API Gateway with a custom domain maps one custom domain per configuration, so 10 domains means 10 custom-domain setups and base-path mappings, which is more operational effort than fronting all 10 domains with one CloudFront distribution and a single SAN certificate. It is a heavier, less clean fit for a simple multi-domain redirect.","why_zh":"API Gateway 的自訂網域每個設定僅對應一個網域，10 個網域就需要 10 組自訂網域與 base-path 對應設定，比用單一 CloudFront distribution 加單一 SAN 憑證承載全部 10 個網域更費工。對於簡單的多網域轉址而言，它較笨重也較不貼切。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/edge-functions-choosing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/lambda-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/using-https-alternate-domain-names.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/cnames-and-https-requirements.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/CNAMEs.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識・複選"},{"id":29,"question_en":"A company that has multiple AWS accounts is using AWS Organizations. The company’s AWS accounts host VPCs, Amazon EC2 instances, and containers. The company’s compliance team has deployed a security tool in each VPC where the company has deployments. The security tools run on EC2 instances and send information to the AWS account that is dedicated for the compliance team. The company has tagged all the compliance- related resources with a key of “costCenter” and a value or “compliance”. The company wants to identify the cost of the security tools that are running on the EC2 instances so that the company can charge the compliance team’s AWS account. The cost calculation must be as accurate as possible. What should a solutions architect do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"拥有多个 AWS 账户的公司正在使用 AWS Organizations。该公司的 AWS 账户托管 VPC、Amazon EC2 实例和容器。 公司的合规团队已在公司部署的每个 VPC 中部署了安全工具。安全工具在 EC2 实例上运行，并将信息发送到合规团队专用的 AWS 账户。该公司已使用键“costCenter”和值或“compliance”标记所有与合规性相关的资源。 该公司希望确定 EC2 实例上运行的安全工具的成本，以便公司可以向合规团队的 AWS 账户收取费用。成本计算必须尽可能准确。 解决方案架构师应该怎样做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"In the management account of the organization, activate the costCenter user-defined tag. Configure monthly AWS Cost and Usage Reports to save to an Amazon S3 bucket in the management account. Use the tag breakdown in the report to obtain the total cost for the costCenter tagged resources.","B":"In the member accounts of the organization, activate the costCenter user-defined tag. Configure monthly AWS Cost and Usage Reports to save to an Amazon S3 bucket in the management account. Schedule a monthly AWS Lambda function to retrieve the reports and calculate the total cost for the costCenter tagged resources.","C":"In the member accounts of the organization activate the costCenter user-defined tag. From the management account, schedule a monthly AWS Cost and Usage Report. Use the tag breakdown in the report to calculate the total cost for the costCenter tagged resources.","D":"Create a custom report in the organization view in AWS Trusted Advisor. Configure the report to generate a monthly billing summary for the costCenter tagged resources in the compliance team’s AWS account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织的管理账户中，激活costCenter自定义标签。配置每月 AWS 成本和使用情况报告以保存到管理账户中的 Amazon S3 存储 桶。使用报告中的标签细分来获取 costCenter 标记资源的总成本。","B":"在组织的会员账户中，激活costCenter自定义标签。配置每月 AWS 成本和使用情况报告以保存到管理账户中的 Amazon S3 存储 桶。安排每月一次的 AWS Lambda 函数来检索报告并计算 costCenter 标记资源的总成本。","C":"在组织的成员账户中激活costCenter用户定义标签。从管理账户中，安排每月的 AWS 成本和使用情况报告。使用报告中的标签 细分来计算 costCenter 标记资源的总成本。","D":"在 AWS Trusted Advisor 的组织视图中创建自定义报告。配置报告以生成合规团队 AWS 账户中 costCenter 标记资源的每月账单 摘要。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":95},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":30,"question_en":"A company has 50 AWS accounts that are members of an organization in AWS Organizations. Each account contains multiple VPCs. The company wants to use AWS Transit Gateway to establish connectivity between the VPCs in each member account. Each time a new member account is created, the company wants to automate the process of creating a new VPC and a transit gateway attachment. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司拥有 50 个 AWS 账户，这些账户是 AWS Organizations 中某个组织的成员。每个账户包含多个VPC。该公司希望使用 AWS Transit Gateway 在每个成员账户中的 VPC 之间建立连接。每次创建新成员帐户时，该公司都希望自动执行创建新 VPC 和中转网关附 件的过程。 哪种步骤组合可以满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"From the management account, share the transit gateway with member accounts by using AWS Resource Access Manager.","B":"From the management account, share the transit gateway with member accounts by using an AWS Organizations SCP.","C":"Launch an AWS CloudFormation stack set from the management account that automatically creates a new VPC and a VPC transit gateway attachment in a member account. Associate the attachment with the transit gateway in the management account by using the transit gateway ID.","D":"Launch an AWS CloudFormation stack set from the management account that automatically creates a new VPC and a peering transit gateway attachment in a member account. Share the attachment with the transit gateway in the management account by using a transit gateway service-linked role.","E":"From the management account, share the transit gateway with member accounts by using AWS Service Catalog."},"options_zh":{"A":"在管理账户中，使用 AWS Resource Access Manager 与成员账户共享中转网关。","B":"在管理账户中，使用 AWS Organizations SCP 与成员账户共享中转网关。","C":"从管理账户启动 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈集，该堆栈集会自动在成员账户中创建新的 VPC 和 VPC 中转网关附件。使用中转网 关 ID 将附件与管理账户中的中转网关相关联。","D":"从管理账户启动 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈集，该堆栈集会自动在成员账户中创建新的 VPC 和对等中转网关附件。使用中转网 关服务相关角色与管理帐户中的中转网关共享附件。","E":"在管理账户中，使用 AWS Service Catalog 与成员账户共享中转网关。"},"answer":["A","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AC":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":31,"question_en":"An enterprise company wants to allow its developers to purchase third-party software through AWS Marketplace. The company uses an AWS Organizations account structure with full features enabled, and has a shared services account in each organizational unit (OU) that will be used by procurement managers. The procurement team’s policy indicates that developers should be able to obtain third-party software from an approved list only and use Private Marketplace in AWS Marketplace to achieve this requirement. The procurement team wants administration of Private Marketplace to be restricted to a role named procurement-manager-role, which could be assumed by procurement managers. Other IAM users, groups, roles, and account administrators in the company should be denied Private Marketplace administrative access. What is the MOST e®cient way to design an architecture to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家大型企業公司希望允許其開發人員透過 AWS Marketplace 購買第三方軟體。該公司使用已啟用全部功能的 AWS Organizations 帳戶結構，並在每個組織單位（OU）中設有一個共用服務帳戶，供採購經理使用。採購團隊的政策要求開發人員只能從核准清單取得第三方軟體，並使用 AWS Marketplace 中的 Private Marketplace 來達成此需求。採購團隊希望將 Private Marketplace 的管理限制為僅由名為 procurement-manager-role 的角色執行，該角色可由採購經理擔任。公司中其他所有 IAM 使用者、群組、角色及帳戶管理員都應被拒絕存取 Private Marketplace 管理功能。設計此架構最有效率的方式是什麼？","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM role named procurement-manager-role in all AWS accounts in the organization. Add the PowerUserAccess managed policy to the role. Apply an inline policy to all IAM users and roles in every AWS account to deny permissions on the AWSPrivateMarketplaceAdminFullAccess managed policy.","B":"Create an IAM role named procurement-manager-role in all AWS accounts in the organization. Add the AdministratorAccess managed policy to the role. Define a permissions boundary with the AWSPrivateMarketplaceAdminFullAccess managed policy and attach it to all the developer roles.","C":"Create an IAM role named procurement-manager-role in all the shared services accounts in the organization. Add the AWSPrivateMarketplaceAdminFullAccess managed policy to the role. Create an organization root-level SCP to deny permissions to administer Private Marketplace to everyone except the role named procurement-manager-role. Create another organization root-level SCP to deny permissions to create an IAM role named procurement-manager-role to everyone in the organization.","D":"Create an IAM role named procurement-manager-role in all AWS accounts that will be used by developers. Add the AWSPrivateMarketplaceAdminFullAccess managed policy to the role. Create an SCP in Organizations to deny permissions to administer Private Marketplace to everyone except the role named procurement-manager-role. Apply the SCP to all the shared services accounts in the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"在組織中所有 AWS 帳戶中建立名為 procurement-manager-role 的 IAM 角色。將 PowerUserAccess 受管政策加到該角色。對每個 AWS 帳戶中所有 IAM 使用者與角色套用內嵌政策，拒絕 AWSPrivateMarketplaceAdminFullAccess 受管政策的權限。","B":"在組織中所有 AWS 帳戶中建立名為 procurement-manager-role 的 IAM 角色。將 AdministratorAccess 受管政策加到該角色。定義一個包含 AWSPrivateMarketplaceAdminFullAccess 受管政策的權限邊界（permissions boundary），並將其附加到所有開發人員角色。","C":"在組織中所有共用服務帳戶中建立名為 procurement-manager-role 的 IAM 角色。將 AWSPrivateMarketplaceAdminFullAccess 受管政策加到該角色。在組織根層級建立一個 SCP，拒絕除 procurement-manager-role 角色以外所有人管理 Private Marketplace 的權限。再建立另一個組織根層級 SCP，拒絕組織中所有人建立名為 procurement-manager-role 的 IAM 角色的權限。","D":"在所有將由開發人員使用的 AWS 帳戶中建立名為 procurement-manager-role 的 IAM 角色。將 AWSPrivateMarketplaceAdminFullAccess 受管政策加到該角色。在 Organizations 中建立一個 SCP，拒絕除 procurement-manager-role 角色以外所有人管理 Private Marketplace 的權限。將該 SCP 套用到組織中所有共用服務帳戶。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":92},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Procurement managers operate from the shared services account in each OU, so the procurement-manager-role must be created in the shared services accounts and given AWSPrivateMarketplaceAdminFullAccess (the managed policy that grants Private Marketplace administration). The requirement is that EVERYONE except that role be denied PMP admin access. A root-level SCP that denies the Private Marketplace administrative actions to all principals except procurement-manager-role enforces this guardrail across the entire organization (all OUs, all accounts, including account administrators). A second root-level SCP that denies creating an IAM role named procurement-manager-role to everyone closes the privilege-escalation loophole, preventing anyone from minting a same-named role to inherit the allowed permissions. This is the AWS reference pattern. Option D is wrong because it puts the role in developer accounts (not the shared services accounts where procurement managers work) and applies the SCP only to the shared services accounts, leaving developer accounts and other account admins free to administer PMP and not blocking role creation.","explanation_zh":"Procurement managers 從每個 OU 的 shared services account 操作，因此 procurement-manager-role 必須建立在 shared services accounts 中，並掛上 AWSPrivateMarketplaceAdminFullAccess（授予 Private Marketplace 管理權限的 managed policy）。需求是除了該 role 之外，所有人都要被拒絕 PMP 管理權限。在 organization root 層級建立一個 SCP，拒絕除 procurement-manager-role 以外所有 principal 的 Private Marketplace 管理動作，即可在整個組織（所有 OU、所有帳戶，包括 account administrators）強制此 guardrail。第二個 root 層級 SCP 拒絕所有人建立名為 procurement-manager-role 的 IAM role，封堵權限提升漏洞，避免有人自行建立同名 role 來繼承被允許的權限。這正是 AWS 的參考架構。D 選項錯誤，因為它把 role 放在 developer accounts（而非 procurement managers 實際使用的 shared services accounts），且 SCP 只套用到 shared services accounts，使 developer accounts 與其他帳戶管理員仍能管理 PMP，也未阻止同名 role 的建立。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Applying an inline deny policy to all IAM users and roles in every account does not scale, is not efficient, and is easily removed by an account administrator; it also fails to prevent admins from regaining access. PowerUserAccess is also the wrong policy for the procurement role.","why_zh":"對每個帳戶的所有 IAM users 與 roles 套用 inline deny policy 無法擴展、不具效率，且可被 account administrator 輕易移除；也無法防止管理員重新取得權限。PowerUserAccess 對 procurement role 而言也是錯誤的 policy。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A permissions boundary is a maximum-permission ceiling, not an org-wide deny; attaching AWSPrivateMarketplaceAdminFullAccess as a boundary to developer roles would not deny other users, groups, or account admins across the org, and AdministratorAccess on the procurement role is excessive and does not restrict PMP administration to that role alone.","why_zh":"permissions boundary 是權限上限，並非全組織的 deny；把 AWSPrivateMarketplaceAdminFullAccess 當作 boundary 掛到 developer roles，並無法拒絕組織內其他 users、groups 或 account admins，而 procurement role 使用 AdministratorAccess 權限過大，也無法將 PMP 管理限制在該 role。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creates the role in developer accounts instead of the shared services accounts where procurement managers actually operate, and scopes the SCP only to the shared services accounts. That leaves developer accounts and account administrators in other accounts able to administer Private Marketplace, violating the deny-everyone-else requirement, and it does not prevent anyone from creating a same-named role to escalate.","why_zh":"把 role 建立在 developer accounts，而非 procurement managers 實際操作的 shared services accounts，且 SCP 只套用在 shared services accounts。這使 developer accounts 與其他帳戶的 account administrators 仍能管理 Private Marketplace，違反「拒絕其他所有人」的需求，也未阻止他人建立同名 role 進行權限提升。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/marketplace/latest/buyerguide/it-administrator.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/marketplace/latest/buyerguide/get-started.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-managed-policy/latest/reference/AWSPrivateMarketplaceAdminFullAccess.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":32,"question_en":"A company is in the process of implementing AWS Organizations to constrain its developers to use only Amazon EC2, Amazon S3, and Amazon DynamoDB. The developers account resides in a dedicated organizational unit (OU). The solutions architect has implemented the following SCP on the developers account: When this policy is deployed, IAM users in the developers account are still able to use AWS services that are not listed in the policy. What should the solutions architect do to eliminate the developers’ ability to use services outside the scope of this policy?","question_zh":"一家公司正在实施 AWS Organizations，以限制其开发人员仅使用 Amazon EC2、Amazon S3 和 Amazon DynamoDB。开发人员帐户驻留 在专用的组织单位 (OU) 中。解决方案架构师已在开发人员账户上实施以下 SCP： 部署此策略后，开发人员账户中的 IAM 用户仍然能够使用策略中未列出的 AWS 服务。 解决方案架构师应该怎样做才能消除开发人员使用本政策范围之外的服务的能力？","options_en":{"A":"Create an explicit deny statement for each AWS service that should be constrained.","B":"Remove the FullAWSAccess SCP from the developers account’s OU.","C":"Modify the FullAWSAccess SCP to explicitly deny all services.","D":"Add an explicit deny statement using a wildcard to the end of the SCP."},"options_zh":{"A":"为每个应受到约束的 AWS 服务创建显式拒绝语句。","B":"从开发人员帐户的 OU 中删除 FullAWSAccess SCP。","C":"修改 FullAWSAccess SCP 以明确拒绝所有服务。","D":"在 SCP 末尾添加使用通配符的显式拒绝语句。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":65,"D":31},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The architect wrote an allow-list SCP permitting only EC2, S3, and DynamoDB, but the AWS-managed FullAWSAccess SCP (Effect Allow on Action '*') is still attached to the OU/account. SCPs follow a deny-by-default model where Allow statements at the same level are combined, so FullAWSAccess keeps allowing every service, making the new allow-list redundant. AWS documentation states you replace FullAWSAccess with a policy that allows only a set of services: 'The organization administrator can detach the FullAWSAccess policy and attach this one instead.' Removing FullAWSAccess from the developers OU leaves the developers' allow-list SCP as the only Allow, so all services except EC2/S3/DynamoDB fall to the implicit deny. This is the canonical, minimal allow-list strategy.","explanation_zh":"架構師撰寫了一個允許清單 (allow-list) SCP，僅允許 EC2、S3 與 DynamoDB，但 AWS 受管的 FullAWSAccess SCP（Effect Allow、Action 為 '*'）仍附加在該 OU/帳戶上。SCP 採用預設拒絕模型，同一層級的多個 Allow 陳述會合併，因此 FullAWSAccess 仍允許所有服務，使新增的允許清單形同無效。AWS 文件指出，應將 FullAWSAccess 替換為僅允許特定服務集合的政策：『組織管理員可以卸除 FullAWSAccess 政策並改附加此政策。』從 developers OU 移除 FullAWSAccess 後，開發者的允許清單 SCP 成為唯一的 Allow，因此除 EC2/S3/DynamoDB 以外的所有服務都會落入隱含拒絕。這正是標準且最精簡的允許清單策略。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Adding an explicit Deny for each service to be constrained is the deny-list strategy, not the allow-list the architect built. It is operationally unworkable (hundreds of services plus new ones constantly) and AWS does not recommend it here. It also fails to make the existing allow-list effective; the real problem is the residual FullAWSAccess Allow '*'.","why_zh":"為每個要限制的服務新增明確 Deny 屬於拒絕清單策略，而非架構師建立的允許清單。這在運維上不可行（服務數以百計且不斷新增），且 AWS 在此情境並不建議。它也無法讓既有允許清單生效；真正的問題是殘留的 FullAWSAccess Allow '*'。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"FullAWSAccess is an AWS-managed SCP and cannot be modified or edited. You can only detach it, not change its contents to deny all services.","why_zh":"FullAWSAccess 是 AWS 受管 SCP，無法被修改或編輯。你只能卸除它，無法更改其內容使其拒絕所有服務。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Adding an explicit Deny with a wildcard ('Deny' on Action '*') would override every Allow, because an explicit deny always beats an explicit allow. This would block EC2, S3, and DynamoDB too, locking developers out of all services rather than restricting them to the three allowed ones.","why_zh":"新增使用萬用字元的明確 Deny（對 Action '*' 進行 Deny）會覆蓋所有 Allow，因為明確拒絕永遠勝過明確允許。這會連 EC2、S3、DynamoDB 一併封鎖，使開發者無法使用任何服務，而非限縮在三個被允許的服務。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_evaluation-logic_policy-eval-denyallow.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":33,"question_en":"A company is hosting a monolithic REST-based API for a mobile app on five Amazon EC2 instances in public subnets of a VPC. Mobile clients connect to the API by using a domain name that is hosted on Amazon Route 53. The company has created a Route 53 multivalue answer routing policy with the IP addresses of all the EC2 instances. Recently, the app has been overwhelmed by large and sudden increases to tra®c. The app has not been able to keep up with the tra®c. A solutions architect needs to implement a solution so that the app can handle the new and varying load. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 VPC 公有子网中的五个 Amazon EC2 实例上托管移动应用程序的基于 REST 的整体 API。移动客户端使用 Amazon Route 53 上托管的域名连接到 API。该公司已使用所有 EC2 实例的 IP 地址创建了 Route 53 多值应答路由策略。最近，该应用程序因流量突 然大幅增加而不堪重负。该应用程序无法跟上流量。 解决方案架构师需要实现一个解决方案，以便应用程序可以处理新的和变化的负载。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Separate the API into individual AWS Lambda functions. Configure an Amazon API Gateway REST API with Lambda integration for the backend. Update the Route 53 record to point to the API Gateway API.","B":"Containerize the API logic. Create an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster. Run the containers in the cluster by using Amazon EC2. Create a Kubernetes ingress. Update the Route 53 record to point to the Kubernetes ingress.","C":"Create an Auto Scaling group. Place all the EC2 instances in the Auto Scaling group. Configure the Auto Scaling group to perform scaling actions that are based on CPU utilization. Create an AWS Lambda function that reacts to Auto Scaling group changes and updates the Route 53 record.","D":"Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in front of the API. Move the EC2 instances to private subnets in the VPC. Add the EC2 instances as targets for the ALB. Update the Route 53 record to point to the ALB."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 API 分成单独的 AWS Lambda 函数。为后端配置具有 Lambda 集成的 Amazon API Gateway REST API。更新 Route 53 记录以指 向 API Gateway API。","B":"容器化 API 逻辑。创建 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 集群。使用 Amazon EC2 运行集群中的容器。创建 Kubernetes 入口。更新 Route 53 记录以指向 Kubernetes 入口。","C":"创建 Auto Scaling 组。将所有 EC2 实例放入 Auto Scaling 组中。配置 Auto Scaling 组以执行基于 CPU 利用率的扩展操作。创建 一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数对 Auto Scaling 组更改做出反应并更新 Route 53 记录。","D":"在 API 前面创建应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB)。将 EC2 实例移至 VPC 中的私有子网。添加 EC2 实例作为 ALB 的目标。更新 Route 53 记录以指向 ALB。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":43,"D":32,"C":25},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The deciding qualifier is LEAST operational overhead. The existing workload is a monolithic REST API already running on EC2; the only problem is that the Route 53 multivalue routing policy does not load-balance or scale well under sudden traffic spikes. Option D fronts the unchanged monolith with an Application Load Balancer, moves the instances to private subnets, registers them as ALB targets, and points Route 53 at the ALB. The ALB distributes incoming traffic so no single instance is overwhelmed and integrates natively with EC2 Auto Scaling (instances launched/terminated are automatically registered/deregistered), letting the fleet scale with demand. Critically, this requires zero application code changes. Option A also scales well at runtime, but it requires separating the monolith into individual Lambda functions, a substantial re-architecting and code-rewrite effort that is the opposite of LEAST operational overhead. So D wins on the qualifier.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定詞是 LEAST operational overhead（最少維運負擔）。現有工作負載是已經跑在 EC2 上的單體式 REST API，唯一問題是 Route 53 multivalue answer 路由策略在流量突增時無法有效負載平衡或擴展。選項 D 在不更動單體應用程式的前提下，在前方放置 Application Load Balancer，將執行個體移到私有子網並註冊為 ALB 目標，再把 Route 53 指向 ALB。ALB 會分散流量使單一執行個體不會被壓垮，並與 EC2 Auto Scaling 原生整合（啟動/終止的執行個體會自動註冊/取消註冊），讓機群隨需求擴展。最關鍵的是這完全不需要修改應用程式碼。選項 A 在執行期同樣能良好擴展，但需要把單體拆解成個別的 Lambda 函式，這是大量的重新架構與重寫程式碼的工作，與「最少維運負擔」恰好相反。因此依限定詞判定 D 勝出。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Separating a monolithic REST API into individual Lambda functions is a major re-architecting and code-rewrite effort (decompose the monolith, restructure handlers, re-package, change the invocation model). Although serverless scales well at runtime, the migration work makes this far from the LEAST operational overhead. This is the community top vote, but it misreads the qualifier.","why_zh":"把單體式 REST API 拆解成個別 Lambda 函式是重大的重新架構與程式碼重寫工作（拆解單體、重組 handler、重新封裝、改變呼叫模型）。雖然 serverless 執行期擴展良好，但遷移工作量使其遠非最少維運負擔。這是社群最高票，但誤判了限定詞。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Building and self-managing an Amazon EKS cluster on EC2 plus containerizing the app and configuring a Kubernetes ingress is the HIGHEST operational overhead of all options, the exact opposite of the requirement.","why_zh":"建置並自行管理跑在 EC2 上的 Amazon EKS 叢集、容器化應用程式並設定 Kubernetes ingress，是所有選項中維運負擔最高的，與需求完全相反。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This keeps the brittle DNS-based multivalue distribution and adds custom Lambda code to react to Auto Scaling events and rewrite Route 53 records. DNS-level load balancing suffers from client caching/TTL and eventual consistency, and the custom Lambda is undifferentiated heavy lifting to build and maintain. A load balancer with ASG handles registration natively with no custom code, so C has higher operational overhead than D.","why_zh":"此方案保留脆弱的 DNS multivalue 分流，並加上自訂 Lambda 程式碼來反應 Auto Scaling 事件並改寫 Route 53 記錄。DNS 層級的負載平衡受客戶端快取/TTL 與最終一致性影響，且自訂 Lambda 是需要自行建置與維護的無差異化苦工。負載平衡器搭配 ASG 原生處理註冊且不需自訂程式碼，因此 C 的維運負擔高於 D。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/autoscaling-load-balancer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/attach-load-balancer-asg.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/as-scaling-target-tracking.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識・多選項拉鋸"},{"id":34,"question_en":"A company has created an OU in AWS Organizations for each of its engineering teams. Each OU owns multiple AWS accounts. The organization has hundreds of AWS accounts. A solutions architect must design a solution so that each OU can view a breakdown of usage costs across its AWS accounts. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Organizations 中為每個工程團隊建立了一個 OU。每個 OU 擁有多個 AWS 帳戶。該組織有數百個 AWS 帳戶。解決方案架構師必須設計一個方案，使每個 OU 都能查看其 AWS 帳戶間使用成本的細項分析。哪個解決方案能滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Cost and Usage Report (CUR) for each OU by using AWS Resource Access Manager. Allow each team to visualize the CUR through an Amazon QuickSight dashboard.","B":"Create an AWS Cost and Usage Report (CUR) from the AWS Organizations management account. Allow each team to visualize the CUR through an Amazon QuickSight dashboard.","C":"Create an AWS Cost and Usage Report (CUR) in each AWS Organizations member account. Allow each team to visualize the CUR through an Amazon QuickSight dashboard.","D":"Create an AWS Cost and Usage Report (CUR) by using AWS Systems Manager. Allow each team to visualize the CUR through Systems Manager OpsCenter dashboards."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Resource Access Manager 為每個 OU 建立一份 AWS Cost and Usage Report（CUR）。讓每個團隊透過 Amazon QuickSight 儀表板將 CUR 視覺化。","B":"從 AWS Organizations 管理帳戶建立一份 AWS Cost and Usage Report（CUR）。讓每個團隊透過 Amazon QuickSight 儀表板將 CUR 視覺化。","C":"在每個 AWS Organizations 成員帳戶中建立一份 AWS Cost and Usage Report（CUR）。讓每個團隊透過 Amazon QuickSight 儀表板將 CUR 視覺化。","D":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 建立一份 AWS Cost and Usage Report（CUR）。讓每個團隊透過 Systems Manager OpsCenter 儀表板將 CUR 視覺化。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":89},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":35,"question_en":"A company is storing data on premises on a Windows file server. The company produces 5 GB of new data daily. The company migrated part of its Windows-based workload to AWS and needs the data to be available on a file system in the cloud. The company already has established an AWS Direct Connect connection between the on-premises network and AWS. Which data migration strategy should the company use?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 Windows 文件服务器上存储本地数据。该公司每天产生 5 GB 的新数据。 该公司将部分基于 Windows 的工作负载迁移到 AWS，并需要云中文件系统上的数据可用。该公司已经在本地网络和 AWS 之间建立了 AWS Direct Connect 连接。 公司应该使用哪种数据迁移策略？","options_en":{"A":"Use the file gateway option in AWS Storage Gateway to replace the existing Windows file server, and point the existing file share to the new file gateway.","B":"Use AWS DataSync to schedule a daily task to replicate data between the on-premises Windows file server and Amazon FSx.","C":"Use AWS Data Pipeline to schedule a daily task to replicate data between the on-premises Windows file server and Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS).","D":"Use AWS DataSync to schedule a daily task to replicate data between the on-premises Windows file server and Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Storage Gateway 中的文件网关选项替换现有的 Windows 文件服务器，并将现有文件共享指向新的文件网关。","B":"使用 AWS DataSync 安排日常任务以在本地 Windows 文件服务器和 Amazon FSx 之间复制数据。","C":"使用 AWS Data Pipeline 安排日常任务以在本地 Windows 文件服务器和 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 之间复制数据。","D":"使用 AWS DataSync 安排日常任务以在本地 Windows 文件服务器和 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 之间复制数据。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":64,"A":36},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":36,"question_en":"A company’s solutions architect is reviewing a web application that runs on AWS. The application references static assets in an Amazon S3 bucket in the us-east-1 Region. The company needs resiliency across multiple AWS Regions. The company already has created an S3 bucket in a second Region. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司的解決方案架構師正在審查一個在 AWS 上執行的網頁應用程式。該應用程式從 us-east-1 區域的 Amazon S3 儲存桶引用靜態資產。公司需要跨多個 AWS 區域的復原能力。公司已在第二個區域建立了一個 S3 儲存桶。哪個解決方案能以最少的運維負擔滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the application to write each object to both S3 buckets. Set up an Amazon Route 53 public hosted zone with a record set by using a weighted routing policy for each S3 bucket. Configure the application to reference the objects by using the Route 53 DNS name.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function to copy objects from the S3 bucket in us-east-1 to the S3 bucket in the second Region. Invoke the Lambda function each time an object is written to the S3 bucket in us-east-1. Set up an Amazon CloudFront distribution with an origin group that contains the two S3 buckets as origins.","C":"Configure replication on the S3 bucket in us-east-1 to replicate objects to the S3 bucket in the second Region. Set up an Amazon CloudFront distribution with an origin group that contains the two S3 buckets as origins.","D":"Configure replication on the S3 bucket in us-east-1 to replicate objects to the S3 bucket in the second Region. If failover is required, update the application code to load S3 objects from the S3 bucket in the second Region."},"options_zh":{"A":"設定應用程式將每個物件同時寫入兩個 S3 儲存桶。為每個 S3 儲存桶設定一個使用加權路由政策（weighted routing policy）記錄集的 Amazon Route 53 公開託管區域。設定應用程式使用 Route 53 DNS 名稱來引用物件。","B":"建立一個 AWS Lambda 函式，將物件從 us-east-1 的 S3 儲存桶複製到第二個區域的 S3 儲存桶。每次有物件寫入 us-east-1 的 S3 儲存桶時觸發該 Lambda 函式。設定一個 Amazon CloudFront 分發，其原點群組（origin group）包含這兩個 S3 儲存桶作為來源。","C":"在 us-east-1 的 S3 儲存桶上設定複製，將物件複製到第二個區域的 S3 儲存桶。設定一個 Amazon CloudFront 分發，其原點群組包含這兩個 S3 儲存桶作為來源。","D":"在 us-east-1 的 S3 儲存桶上設定複製，將物件複製到第二個區域的 S3 儲存桶。如需容錯移轉，更新應用程式程式碼以從第二個區域的 S3 儲存桶載入 S3 物件。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":95},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is LEAST operational overhead combined with resiliency across Regions. Both C and D use Amazon S3 Cross-Region Replication, which is a fully managed, automatic, asynchronous feature that copies objects to the second-Region bucket with no custom code. The difference is the failover mechanism. Option C fronts both buckets with a CloudFront distribution configured with an origin group: when the primary S3 origin is unavailable or returns a failure status code (e.g., 500, 502, 503, 504), CloudFront automatically routes requests to the secondary bucket with zero human action and zero code changes. Option D relies on manually updating the application code at failover time ('If failover is required, update the application code to load S3 objects from the S3 bucket in the second Region'), which is a manual, reactive process that adds operational overhead and delays recovery. Therefore C meets the resiliency requirement with the least operational overhead.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定條件是「最少的維運負擔(LEAST operational overhead)」加上跨 Region 的韌性。C 與 D 都使用 Amazon S3 Cross-Region Replication,這是一個全受管、自動、非同步的功能,會把物件複製到第二個 Region 的 bucket,且不需要自訂程式碼。差別在於故障切換機制。選項 C 在兩個 bucket 前面放置設定了 origin group 的 CloudFront distribution:當主要 S3 origin 不可用或回傳失敗狀態碼(例如 500、502、503、504)時,CloudFront 會自動把請求導向次要 bucket,完全不需人工介入也不需修改程式碼。選項 D 則必須在故障切換時手動更新應用程式程式碼(『If failover is required, update the application code...』),這是一個被動且人工的流程,會增加維運負擔並拖慢復原速度。因此 C 在滿足韌性需求的同時具有最少的維運負擔。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Writing each object to both buckets requires modifying the application's write path (custom code, dual-write error handling), which is more operational overhead than managed S3 replication. Route 53 weighted routing for two S3 website endpoints does load distribution, not health-based automatic failover, and S3 buckets cannot be reached via a single Route 53 DNS name for object reads in the way implied; this does not provide clean automatic failover for static asset reads.","why_zh":"把每個物件同時寫入兩個 bucket 需要修改應用程式的寫入路徑(自訂程式碼、雙寫錯誤處理),比受管的 S3 replication 增加更多維運負擔。Route 53 加權路由是做流量分配而非以健康檢查為基礎的自動故障切換,無法為靜態資產讀取提供乾淨的自動容錯。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Building and maintaining a custom Lambda function to copy objects on every S3 write reinvents what S3 Cross-Region Replication does natively and fully managed. The CloudFront origin-group failover part is correct, but the Lambda-based replication adds unnecessary code, error handling, retries, and operational overhead compared with native replication, so it is not the LEAST overhead option.","why_zh":"建立並維護一個自訂 Lambda 函式在每次 S3 寫入時複製物件,等於重造 S3 Cross-Region Replication 原生且全受管的功能。CloudFront origin group 故障切換的部分是正確的,但基於 Lambda 的複製增加了不必要的程式碼、錯誤處理、重試與維運負擔,因此不是最少負擔的選項。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Although it uses managed S3 replication, failover requires a human to manually update application code ('If failover is required, update the application code'). That is a reactive, manual process with significant operational overhead and slow, error-prone recovery, versus C's automatic CloudFront origin-group failover that needs no intervention or code change.","why_zh":"雖然它使用受管的 S3 replication,但故障切換需要人工手動更新應用程式程式碼(『If failover is required, update the application code』)。這是被動且人工的流程,具有顯著的維運負擔且復原緩慢易出錯,相較之下 C 的 CloudFront origin group 自動故障切換不需任何介入或程式碼變更。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/high_availability_origin_failover.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":37,"question_en":"A company is hosting a three-tier web application in an on-premises environment. Due to a recent surge in tra®c that resulted in downtime and a significant financial impact, company management has ordered that the application be moved to AWS. The application is written in .NET and has a dependency on a MySQL database. A solutions architect must design a scalable and highly available solution to meet the demand of 200,000 daily users. Which steps should the solutions architect take to design an appropriate solution?","question_zh":"一家公司在內部部署環境中託管一個三層式網頁應用程式。由於近期流量激增造成停機並帶來重大財務損失，公司管理層要求將該應用程式遷移到 AWS。該應用程式以 .NET 撰寫，並依賴 MySQL 資料庫。解決方案架構師必須設計一個可擴充且高可用的解決方案，以滿足每日 200,000 名使用者的需求。解決方案架構師應採取哪些步驟來設計適當的解決方案？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Elastic Beanstalk to create a new application with a web server environment and an Amazon RDS MySQL Multi-AZ DB instance. The environment should launch a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in front of an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group in multiple Availability Zones. Use an Amazon Route 53 alias record to route tra®c from the company’s domain to the NLB.","B":"Use AWS CloudFormation to launch a stack containing an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in front of an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group spanning three Availability Zones. The stack should launch a Multi-AZ deployment of an Amazon Aurora MySQL DB cluster with a Retain deletion policy. Use an Amazon Route 53 alias record to route tra®c from the company’s domain to the ALB.","C":"Use AWS Elastic Beanstalk to create an automatically scaling web server environment that spans two separate Regions with an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in each Region. Create a Multi-AZ deployment of an Amazon Aurora MySQL DB cluster with a cross- Region read replica. Use Amazon Route 53 with a geoproximity routing policy to route tra®c between the two Regions.","D":"Use AWS CloudFormation to launch a stack containing an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in front of an Amazon ECS cluster of Spot instances spanning three Availability Zones. The stack should launch an Amazon RDS MySQL DB instance with a Snapshot deletion policy. Use an Amazon Route 53 alias record to route tra®c from the company’s domain to the ALB."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 建立一個新應用程式，包含一個網頁伺服器環境與一個 Amazon RDS MySQL Multi-AZ DB 執行個體。該環境應在多個可用區域中的 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 群組前啟動一個 Network Load Balancer（NLB）。使用 Amazon Route 53 別名記錄將流量從公司網域路由到 NLB。","B":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 啟動一個堆疊，其中包含一個位於跨三個可用區域的 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 群組前的 Application Load Balancer（ALB）。該堆疊應啟動一個具有 Retain 刪除政策的 Amazon Aurora MySQL DB 叢集 Multi-AZ 部署。使用 Amazon Route 53 別名記錄將流量從公司網域路由到 ALB。","C":"使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 建立一個橫跨兩個獨立區域的自動擴充網頁伺服器環境，每個區域各有一個 Application Load Balancer（ALB）。建立一個具有跨區域讀取副本的 Amazon Aurora MySQL DB 叢集 Multi-AZ 部署。使用具有地理鄰近路由政策（geoproximity routing policy）的 Amazon Route 53 在兩個區域間路由流量。","D":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 啟動一個堆疊，其中包含一個位於跨三個可用區域的 Spot 執行個體 Amazon ECS 叢集前的 Application Load Balancer（ALB）。該堆疊應啟動一個具有 Snapshot 刪除政策的 Amazon RDS MySQL DB 執行個體。使用 Amazon Route 53 別名記錄將流量從公司網域路由到 ALB。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":90},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is a scalable, highly available home for a .NET + MySQL three-tier web app serving 200,000 daily users. Option B satisfies this cleanly: an Application Load Balancer (Layer 7, correct for HTTP/HTTPS web traffic) in front of an EC2 Auto Scaling group across three AZs (scalability + HA), a Multi-AZ Amazon Aurora MySQL DB cluster (MySQL-compatible, highly available with fast automatic failover and up to 15 replicas), a Retain deletion policy to protect the production database if the stack is deleted, and a Route 53 alias record to the ALB. Option C (the dump's answer) is technically wrong because a single Elastic Beanstalk web server environment is scoped to one Region and cannot 'span two separate Regions,' a cross-Region read replica is read-only (no write-tier HA), and geoproximity routing addresses geographic distribution rather than the stated HA/scalability need, adding unwarranted multi-Region complexity. Option A is an anti-pattern (NLB is Layer 4 and inappropriate for HTTP web routing). Option D fails HA because Spot instances can be interrupted and a single RDS MySQL instance (no Multi-AZ) is a single point of failure.","explanation_zh":"需求是為服務每日 200,000 名使用者的 .NET + MySQL 三層 Web 應用程式提供可擴展且高可用的架構。選項 B 完整符合：以 Application Load Balancer（Layer 7，適用於 HTTP/HTTPS Web 流量）置於跨三個可用區的 EC2 Auto Scaling group 前方（兼具擴展性與高可用性），搭配 Multi-AZ 的 Amazon Aurora MySQL DB cluster（相容 MySQL、具快速自動故障轉移與最多 15 個 replica 的高可用性），使用 Retain deletion policy 在 stack 被刪除時保護正式資料庫，並以 Route 53 alias record 指向 ALB。選項 C（dump 的答案）在技術上有誤：單一 Elastic Beanstalk Web 環境僅限於單一 Region，無法「橫跨兩個不同 Region」；cross-Region read replica 為唯讀（寫入層無高可用性）；geoproximity routing 處理的是地理分流而非題目要求的 HA/擴展性，且引入不必要的多 Region 複雜度。選項 A 為反模式（NLB 是 Layer 4，不適合 HTTP Web 路由）。選項 D 高可用性不足，因為 Spot 執行個體可能被中斷，且單一 RDS MySQL 執行個體（無 Multi-AZ）為單一故障點。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses a Network Load Balancer (Layer 4) in front of the web tier; an HTTP/HTTPS three-tier web app should use an Application Load Balancer (Layer 7) for proper request/content routing. NLB here is an anti-pattern.","why_zh":"在 Web 層前方使用 Network Load Balancer（Layer 4）；HTTP/HTTPS 三層 Web 應用程式應使用 Application Load Balancer（Layer 7）進行適當的請求/內容路由。此處用 NLB 屬反模式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A single Elastic Beanstalk web server environment cannot span two Regions; a cross-Region read replica is read-only (no write HA); and geoproximity routing targets geographic distribution, not the required HA/scalability. Over-engineered and factually incorrect.","why_zh":"單一 Elastic Beanstalk Web 環境無法橫跨兩個 Region；cross-Region read replica 為唯讀（無寫入高可用性）；geoproximity routing 針對的是地理分流而非所需的 HA/擴展性。過度設計且事實有誤。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Spot instances can be reclaimed at any time, undermining HA for an app that just suffered downtime; and a single RDS MySQL instance with no Multi-AZ is a single point of failure. Snapshot deletion policy does not fix the runtime HA gap.","why_zh":"Spot 執行個體可能隨時被回收，破壞剛經歷停機的應用程式的高可用性；單一 RDS MySQL 執行個體（無 Multi-AZ）為單一故障點。Snapshot deletion policy 無法彌補執行期的高可用性缺口。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Concepts.AuroraHighAvailability.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-attribute-deletionpolicy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/choosing-the-right-aws-service-for-your-microservice-endpoints/app-load-balancer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Overview.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":38,"question_en":"A company is using AWS Organizations to manage multiple AWS accounts. For security purposes, the company requires the creation of an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic that enables integration with a third-party alerting system in all the Organizations member accounts. A solutions architect used an AWS CloudFormation template to create the SNS topic and stack sets to automate the deployment of CloudFormation stacks. Trusted access has been enabled in Organizations. What should the solutions architect do to deploy the CloudFormation StackSets in all AWS accounts?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS Organizations 来管理多个 AWS 账户。出于安全目的，该公司要求创建一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 主题，以便与所有组织成员账户中的第三方警报系统集成。 解决方案架构师使用 AWS CloudFormation 模板创建 SNS 主题和堆栈集，以自动部署 CloudFormation 堆栈。组织中已启用可信访问。 解决方案架构师应该如何在所有 AWS 账户中部署 CloudFormation StackSet？","options_en":{"A":"Create a stack set in the Organizations member accounts. Use service-managed permissions. Set deployment options to deploy to an organization. Use CloudFormation StackSets drift detection.","B":"Create stacks in the Organizations member accounts. Use self-service permissions. Set deployment options to deploy to an organization. Enable the CloudFormation StackSets automatic deployment.","C":"Create a stack set in the Organizations management account. Use service-managed permissions. Set deployment options to deploy to the organization. Enable CloudFormation StackSets automatic deployment.","D":"Create stacks in the Organizations management account. Use service-managed permissions. Set deployment options to deploy to the organization. Enable CloudFormation StackSets drift detection."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织成员帐户中创建堆栈集。使用服务管理的权限。设置部署选项以部署到组织。使用 CloudFormation StackSets 漂移检 测。","B":"在组织成员帐户中创建堆栈。使用自助服务权限。设置部署选项以部署到组织。启用 CloudFormation StackSets 自动部署。","C":"在组织管理帐户中创建堆栈集。使用服务管理的权限。设置部署选项以部署到组织。启用 CloudFormation StackSets 自动部 署。","D":"在组织管理帐户中创建堆栈。使用服务管理的权限。设置部署选项以部署到组织。启用 CloudFormation StackSets 漂移检测。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":39,"question_en":"A company wants to migrate its workloads from on premises to AWS. The workloads run on Linux and Windows. The company has a large on- premises infrastructure that consists of physical machines and VMs that host numerous applications. The company must capture details about the system configuration, system performance, running processes, and network connections of its on-premises workloads. The company also must divide the on-premises applications into groups for AWS migrations. The company needs recommendations for Amazon EC2 instance types so that the company can run its workloads on AWS in the most cost-effective manner. Which combination of steps should a solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司希望将其工作负载从本地迁移到 AWS。工作负载在 Linux 和 Windows 上运行。该公司拥有大型本地基础设施，由托管大量 应用程序的物理机和虚拟机组成。 公司必须捕获有关其本地工作负载的系统配置、系统性能、运行进程和网络连接的详细信息。该公司还必须将本地应用程序分组以 进行 AWS 迁移。该公司需要针对 Amazon EC2 实例类型的建议，以便该公司能够以最具成本效益的方式在 AWS 上运行其工作负载。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Assess the existing applications by installing AWS Application Discovery Agent on the physical machines and VMs.","B":"Assess the existing applications by installing AWS Systems Manager Agent on the physical machines and VMs.","C":"Group servers into applications for migration by using AWS Systems Manager Application Manager.","D":"Group servers into applications for migration by using AWS Migration Hub.","E":"Generate recommended instance types and associated costs by using AWS Migration Hub.","F":"Import data about server sizes into AWS Trusted Advisor. Follow the recommendations for cost optimization."},"options_zh":{"A":"通过在物理机和虚拟机上安装 AWS Application Discovery Agent 来评估现有应用程序。","B":"通过在物理机和虚拟机上安装 AWS Systems Manager 代理来评估现有应用程序。","C":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 应用程序管理器将服务器分组到应用程序中以进行迁移。","D":"将服务器分组到应用程序中，以便使用 AWS Migration Hub 进行迁移。","E":"使用 AWS Migration Hub 生成推荐的实例类型和相关成本。","F":"将有关服务器大小的数据导入 AWS Trusted Advisor。遵循成本优化建议。"},"answer":["B","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ADE":95},"tags":["Migration","Compute","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement to capture system configuration, system performance, running processes, and network connections of on-premises Linux and Windows physical machines and VMs is met word-for-word by the AWS Application Discovery Agent (Discovery Agent), so A is correct. The AWS docs state the Discovery Agent 'capture[s] system configuration, system performance, running processes, and details of the network connections between systems' and supports physical servers and VMs on Linux and Windows. To divide on-premises applications into groups for migration, you group discovered servers into applications in the AWS Migration Hub console, so D is correct. To get the most cost-effective EC2 instance types and associated costs, AWS Migration Hub generates Amazon EC2 instance recommendations (the most cost-effective instance type matching server specs and utilization, with cost data), so E is correct. The dump's B (Systems Manager Agent) is wrong because SSM Agent is for operating/managing instances (Run Command, patching, inventory), not for migration discovery of on-premises workloads.","explanation_zh":"需求中要擷取地端 Linux 與 Windows 實體機與 VM 的系統組態、系統效能、執行中的程序與網路連線，這與 AWS Application Discovery Agent（Discovery Agent）的功能逐字吻合，因此 A 正確。AWS 文件明確指出 Discovery Agent 會「擷取 system configuration、system performance、running processes 以及系統間的 network connections 詳情」，並支援 Linux 與 Windows 的實體伺服器與 VM。要將地端應用程式分組以進行遷移，需在 AWS Migration Hub 主控台將探索到的伺服器分組成 applications，因此 D 正確。要取得最具成本效益的 EC2 執行個體類型與相關成本，AWS Migration Hub 會產生 Amazon EC2 instance recommendations（依伺服器規格與使用率比對最具成本效益的執行個體類型並附成本資料），因此 E 正確。題庫建議答案的 B（Systems Manager Agent）錯誤，因為 SSM Agent 用於操作與管理執行個體（Run Command、修補、清查），並非用於地端工作負載的遷移探索。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Systems Manager Agent is for operating and managing servers (Run Command, patch management, inventory) once they are SSM-managed; it does not perform migration discovery capturing system configuration, performance, running processes, and network connections of on-premises workloads. That discovery role belongs to the AWS Application Discovery Agent.","why_zh":"AWS Systems Manager Agent 用於操作與管理伺服器（Run Command、修補管理、清查），不負責擷取地端工作負載的系統組態、效能、執行中程序與網路連線的遷移探索；該探索角色屬於 AWS Application Discovery Agent。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Systems Manager Application Manager groups and manages AWS resources (CloudFormation stacks, resource groups) for operational tasks, not for grouping discovered on-premises servers into applications for migration. Grouping servers for migration is done in AWS Migration Hub.","why_zh":"Systems Manager Application Manager 用於將 AWS 資源（CloudFormation 堆疊、資源群組）分組與管理以進行營運作業，而非將探索到的地端伺服器分組成 applications 以進行遷移。遷移用的伺服器分組是在 AWS Migration Hub 中完成。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Trusted Advisor performs cost-optimization checks on existing AWS resources; you cannot import on-premises server sizes into it, and it does not generate EC2 instance-type recommendations for migrating on-premises workloads. Migration Hub provides those right-sizing/cost recommendations.","why_zh":"Trusted Advisor 針對既有 AWS 資源執行成本最佳化檢查；無法將地端伺服器規格匯入其中，也不會為遷移地端工作負載產生 EC2 執行個體類型建議。這類調整大小與成本建議由 Migration Hub 提供。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/discovery-agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/applications.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/migrationhub/latest/ug/how-ec2-recommendations-work.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/migrationhub/latest/ug/generating-ec2-recommendations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/migrationhub/latest/ug/ec2-recommendation-prerequisites.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":40,"question_en":"A company is hosting an image-processing service on AWS in a VPC. The VPC extends across two Availability Zones. Each Availability Zone contains one public subnet and one private subnet. The service runs on Amazon EC2 instances in the private subnets. An Application Load Balancer in the public subnets is in front of the service. The service needs to communicate with the internet and does so through two NAT gateways. The service uses Amazon S3 for image storage. The EC2 instances retrieve approximately 1 ТВ of data from an S3 bucket each day. The company has promoted the service as highly secure. A solutions architect must reduce cloud expenditures as much as possible without compromising the service’s security posture or increasing the time spent on ongoing operations. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上的 VPC 中托管图像处理服务。VPC 跨越两个可用区。每个可用区包含 1 个公有子网和 1 个私有子网。 该服务在私有子网中的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。公有子网中的应用程序负载均衡器位于服务前面。该服务需要与 Internet 进行通 信，并通过两个 NAT 网关进行通信。该服务使用 Amazon S3 进行图像存储。EC2 实例每天从 S3 存储桶检索大约 1TB 数据。 该公司将该服务宣传为高度安全的。解决方案架构师必须在不影响服务安全状况或增加持续运营时间的情况下，尽可能减少云支 出。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Replace the NAT gateways with NAT instances. In the VPC route table, create a route from the private subnets to the NAT instances.","B":"Move the EC2 instances to the public subnets. Remove the NAT gateways.","C":"Set up an S3 gateway VPC endpoint in the VPAttach an endpoint policy to the endpoint to allow the required actions on the S3 bucket.","D":"Attach an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) volume to the EC2 instances. Host the images on the EFS volume."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 NAT 网关替换为 NAT 实例。在 VPC 路由表中，创建从私有子网到 NAT 实例的路由。","B":"将 EC2 实例移至公有子网。删除 NAT 网关。","C":"在 VPA 中设置 S3 网关 VPC 终端节点，将终端节点策略附加到该终端节点以允许对 S3 存储桶执行所需的操作。","D":"将 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 卷附加到 EC2 实例。将映像托管在 EFS 卷上。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":41,"question_en":"A company recently deployed an application on AWS. The application uses Amazon DynamoDB. The company measured the application load and configured the RCUs and WCUs on the DynamoDB table to match the expected peak load. The peak load occurs once a week for a 4-hour period and is double the average load. The application load is close to the average load for the rest of the week. The access pattern includes many more writes to the table than reads of the table. A solutions architect needs to implement a solution to minimize the cost of the table. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司最近在 AWS 上部署了一个应用程序。该应用程序使用 Amazon DynamoDB。该公司测量了应用程序负载，并在 DynamoDB 表 上配置了 RCU 和 WCU，以匹配预期的峰值负载。峰值负载每周出现一次，持续 4 小时，是平均负载的两倍。应用程序负载接近本周 剩余时间的平均负载。访问模式包括对表的写入比对表的读取多得多。 解决方案架构师需要实施一个解决方案来最大限度地降低表的成本。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Application Auto Scaling to increase capacity during the peak period. Purchase reserved RCUs and WCUs to match the average load.","B":"Configure on-demand capacity mode for the table.","C":"Configure DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) in front of the table. Reduce the provisioned read capacity to match the new peak load on the table.","D":"Configure DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) in front of the table. Configure on-demand capacity mode for the table."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Application Auto Scaling 在高峰期增加容量。购买预留的 RCU 和 WCU 以匹配平均负载。","B":"配置表的按需扩容模式。","C":"在表前面配置 DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX)。减少预配置的读取容量以匹配表上的新峰值负载。","D":"在表前面配置 DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX)。为表配置按需容量模式。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":70,"B":18},"tags":["Compute","Database","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The workload is steady and predictable for ~96% of the week (close to average load) with a known, recurring 4-hour peak once a week at double the average, and it is write-heavy. For predictable, high-utilization workloads, provisioned capacity is far cheaper than on-demand (on-demand per-request rates are roughly 6-7x the provisioned per-unit-hour rate). The biggest cost lever is reserved capacity, which discounts the provisioned baseline by up to 54% (1-year) or 77% (3-year). Option A buys reserved capacity matching the average load (running almost all week) and uses Application Auto Scaling to add the extra provisioned capacity only during the brief, predictable weekly peak, with that excess billed at standard provisioned rates. This minimizes cost while covering both reads and writes. DAX (C, D) is a read-only cache that does nothing for a write-heavy workload and adds node cost; on-demand alone (B) is more expensive for steady, high-utilization, predictable traffic.","explanation_zh":"此工作負載在一週約 96% 的時間（接近平均負載）穩定且可預測，每週有一次已知、固定的 4 小時尖峰（為平均的兩倍），且寫入遠多於讀取。對於可預測、高使用率的工作負載，provisioned capacity 遠比 on-demand 便宜（on-demand 的每請求費率約為 provisioned 每單位小時費率的 6-7 倍）。最大的省錢槓桿是 reserved capacity，可對 provisioned 基準折扣最多 54%（一年）或 77%（三年）。選項 A 以 reserved capacity 對應幾乎整週運行的平均負載，並用 Application Auto Scaling 僅在每週短暫且可預測的尖峰期間增加額外 provisioned capacity，超出部分以標準 provisioned 費率計費，同時涵蓋讀取與寫入，達到最低成本。DAX（C、D）只是唯讀快取，對寫入密集的工作負載毫無幫助且增加節點成本；單用 on-demand（B）對穩定、高使用率、可預測的流量而言更貴。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"On-demand mode charges per request with no commitment, but its per-request rate is roughly 6-7x the provisioned per-unit-hour rate. For a steady, predictable, high-utilization workload like this, on-demand is more expensive than provisioned with reserved capacity, so it does not minimize cost.","why_zh":"On-demand 按請求計費且無承諾，但其每請求費率約為 provisioned 每單位小時費率的 6-7 倍。對此種穩定、可預測、高使用率的工作負載，on-demand 比 provisioned 加 reserved capacity 更貴，無法達到最低成本。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"DAX is a read-through caching layer that only offloads and accelerates reads; the workload is write-heavy, so DAX provides almost no benefit and adds cluster node cost. DAX also cannot reduce write capacity, and 'reduce read capacity to match the new peak' is incoherent for a write-dominated table.","why_zh":"DAX 是讀取快取層，只能卸載與加速讀取；此工作負載以寫入為主，DAX 幾乎無益且增加叢集節點成本。DAX 也無法降低寫入容量，對寫入為主的資料表而言「降低讀取容量以符合新尖峰」毫無意義。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it is wrong: DAX only caches reads and the workload is write-heavy, so DAX adds node cost without write savings. Pairing DAX with on-demand still pays the higher on-demand per-request rate for the dominant write traffic, which is not cost-minimizing for a predictable workload.","why_zh":"這是題庫建議答案但錯誤：DAX 只快取讀取，而此工作負載以寫入為主，DAX 增加節點成本卻無寫入節省。DAX 搭配 on-demand 仍以較高的 on-demand 每請求費率支付主要的寫入流量，對可預測工作負載並非最省成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/reserved-capacity.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/capacity-mode.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/on-demand-capacity-mode.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/AutoScaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/DAX.concepts.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":42,"question_en":"A solutions architect needs to advise a company on how to migrate its on-premises data processing application to the AWS Cloud. Currently, users upload input files through a web portal. The web server then stores the uploaded files on NAS and messages the processing server over a message queue. Each media file can take up to 1 hour to process. The company has determined that the number of media files awaiting processing is significantly higher during business hours, with the number of files rapidly declining after business hours. What is the MOST cost-effective migration recommendation?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师需要就如何将其本地数据处理应用程序迁移到 AWS 云向公司提供建议。目前，用户通过门户网站上传输入文件。然 后，Web 服务器将上传的文件存储在 NAS 上，并通过消息队列向处理服务器发送消息。每个媒体文件最多可能需要 1 小时来处理。 该公司已确定，在工作时间内等待处理的媒体文件数量显着增加，而在工作时间之后文件数量迅速下降。 最具成本效益的迁移建议是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Create a queue using Amazon SQS. Configure the existing web server to publish to the new queue. When there are messages in the queue, invoke an AWS Lambda function to pull requests from the queue and process the files. Store the processed files in an Amazon S3 bucket.","B":"Create a queue using Amazon MQ. Configure the existing web server to publish to the new queue. When there are messages in the queue, create a new Amazon EC2 instance to pull requests from the queue and process the files. Store the processed files in Amazon EFS. Shut down the EC2 instance after the task is complete.","C":"Create a queue using Amazon MQ. Configure the existing web server to publish to the new queue. When there are messages in the queue, invoke an AWS Lambda function to pull requests from the queue and process the files. Store the processed files in Amazon EFS.","D":"Create a queue using Amazon SQS. Configure the existing web server to publish to the new queue. Use Amazon EC2 instances in an EC2 Auto Scaling group to pull requests from the queue and process the files. Scale the EC2 instances based on the SQS queue length. Store the processed files in an Amazon S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon SQS 创建队列。配置现有 Web 服务器以发布到新队列。当队列中有消息时，调用 AWS Lambda 函数从队列中提取 请求并处理文件。将处理后的文件存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。","B":"使用 Amazon MQ 创建队列。配置现有 Web 服务器以发布到新队列。当队列中有消息时，创建一个新的 Amazon EC2 实例以从 队列中提取请求并处理文件。将处理后的文件存储在 Amazon EFS 中。任务完成后关闭 EC2 实例。","C":"使用 Amazon MQ 创建队列。配置现有 Web 服务器以发布到新队列。当队列中有消息时，调用 AWS Lambda 函数从队列中提取 请求并处理文件。将处理后的文件存储在 Amazon EFS 中。","D":"使用 Amazon SQS 创建队列。配置现有 Web 服务器以发布到新队列。使用 EC2 Auto Scaling 组中的 Amazon EC2 实例从队列中提 取请求并处理文件。根据 SQS 队列长度扩展 EC2 实例。将处理后的文件存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":96},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":43,"question_en":"A company is using Amazon OpenSearch Service to analyze data. The company loads data into an OpenSearch Service cluster with 10 data nodes from an Amazon S3 bucket that uses S3 Standard storage. The data resides in the cluster for 1 month for read-only analysis. After 1 month, the company deletes the index that contains the data from the cluster. For compliance purposes, the company must retain a copy of all input data. The company is concerned about ongoing costs and asks a solutions architect to recommend a new solution. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 Amazon OpenSearch Service 来分析数据。该公司将数据从使用 S3 标准存储的 Amazon S3 存储桶加载到具有 10 个 数据节点的 OpenSearch Service 集群中。数据在集群中驻留 1 个月，用于只读分析。1 个月后，该公司从集群中删除包含数据的索 引。出于合规性目的，公司必须保留所有输入数据的副本。 该公司担心持续的成本，并要求解决方案架构师推荐新的解决方案。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Replace all the data nodes with UltraWarm nodes to handle the expected capacity. Transition the input data from S3 Standard to S3 Glacier Deep Archive when the company loads the data into the cluster.","B":"Reduce the number of data nodes in the cluster to 2 Add UltraWarm nodes to handle the expected capacity. Configure the indexes to transition to UltraWarm when OpenSearch Service ingests the data. Transition the input data to S3 Glacier Deep Archive after 1 month by using an S3 Lifecycle policy.","C":"Reduce the number of data nodes in the cluster to 2. Add UltraWarm nodes to handle the expected capacity. Configure the indexes to transition to UltraWarm when OpenSearch Service ingests the data. Add cold storage nodes to the cluster Transition the indexes from UltraWarm to cold storage. Delete the input data from the S3 bucket after 1 month by using an S3 Lifecycle policy.","D":"Reduce the number of data nodes in the cluster to 2. Add instance-backed data nodes to handle the expected capacity. Transition the input data from S3 Standard to S3 Glacier Deep Archive when the company loads the data into the cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"将所有数据节点替换为 UltraWarm 节点以处理预期容量。当公司将数据加载到集群中时，将输入数据从 S3 Standard 转换到 S3 Glacier Deep Archive。","B":"将集群中的数据节点数量减少到 2 个 添加 UltraWarm 节点来处理预期容量。配置索引以在 OpenSearch 服务摄取数据时转换到 UltraWarm。1 个月后，使用 S3 生命周期策略将输入数据转移到 S3 Glacier Deep Archive。","C":"将集群中的数据节点数量减少到 2。添加 UltraWarm 节点来处理预期容量。配置索引以在 OpenSearch 服务摄取数据时转换到 UltraWarm。将冷存储节点添加到集群 将索引从 UltraWarm 转换为冷存储。1 个月后使用 S3 生命周期策略从 S3 存储桶中删除输入 数据。","D":"将集群中的数据节点数量减少到 2。添加实例支持的数据节点来处理预期容量。当公司将数据加载到集群中时，将输入数据从 S3 Standard 转换到 S3 Glacier Deep Archive。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":94},"tags":["Storage","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":44,"question_en":"A company has 10 accounts that are part of an organization in AWS Organizations. AWS Config is configured in each account. All accounts belong to either the Prod OU or the NonProd OU. The company has set up an Amazon EventBridge rule in each AWS account to notify an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic when an Amazon EC2 security group inbound rule is created with 0.0.0.0/0 as the source. The company’s security team is subscribed to the SNS topic. For all accounts in the NonProd OU, the security team needs to remove the ability to create a security group inbound rule that includes 0.0.0.0/0 as the source. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司有 10 个账户，这些账户属于 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织。AWS Config 在每个账户中配置。所有帐户都属于 Prod OU 或 NonProd OU。 该公司在每个 AWS 账户中设置了一条 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以便在使用 0.0.0.0/0 作为源创建 Amazon EC2 安全组入站规则时通 知 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 主题。公司的安全团队订阅了 SNS 主题。 对于 NonProd OU 中的所有账户，安全团队需要删除创建包含 0.0.0.0/0 作为源的安全组入站规则的功能。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Modify the EventBridge rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to remove the security group inbound rule and to publish to the SNS topic. Deploy the updated rule to the NonProd OU.","B":"Add the vpc-sg-open-only-to-authorized-ports AWS Config managed rule to the NonProd OU.","C":"Configure an SCP to allow the ec2:AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress action when the value of the aws:SourceIp condition key is not 0.0.0.0/0. Apply the SCP to the NonProd OU.","D":"Configure an SCP to deny the ec2:AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress action when the value of the aws:SourceIp condition key is 0.0.0.0/0. Apply the SCP to the NonProd OU."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改 EventBridge 规则以调用 AWS Lambda 函数来删除安全组入站规则并发布到 SNS 主题。将更新的规则部署到 NonProd OU。","B":"将 vpc-sg-open-only-to-authorized-ports AWS Config 托管规则添加到 NonProd OU。","C":"配置 SCP 以在 aws:SourceIp 条件键的值不是 0.0.0.0/0 时允许 ec2:AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress 操作。将 SCP 应用到 NonProd OU。","D":"配置 SCP 以在 aws:SourceIp 条件键的值为 0.0.0.0/0 时拒绝 ec2:AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress 操作。将 SCP 应用到 NonProd OU。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":58,"A":39},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to remove the ability to create a 0.0.0.0/0 inbound security group rule for every account in the NonProd OU with the least operational overhead. A service control policy (SCP) applied at the OU level is the lowest-overhead, organization-wide preventive control: one policy covers all current and future accounts in the OU with no per-account work, no Lambda, and no remediation logic. The decisive distinction between C and D is the Allow-vs-Deny SCP semantics. SCPs are guardrails: an explicit Deny statement that targets ec2:AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress is the correct way to 'remove the ability' to perform that action. Option C uses an Allow effect, but an SCP Allow statement does not deny anything on its own; SCPs that contain Allow statements act as an allowlist filter that can unintentionally block unrelated permissions and would not reliably remove the specific dangerous action. Therefore D is the intended best answer and C is the classic SCP Allow-vs-Deny trap. (Technical caveat: the aws:SourceIp global condition key actually evaluates the IP address of the API caller, not the source CIDR embedded inside the security group rule, so strictly speaking neither SCP's condition can inspect the 0.0.0.0/0 value in the rule. Given that the exam forces a single choice between C and D and treats aws:SourceIp as the rule source, D — which uses the correct Deny construction — is the only defensible answer.)","explanation_zh":"需求是以最少維運成本移除 NonProd OU 中所有帳戶建立 0.0.0.0/0 入站 security group 規則的能力。在 OU 層級套用 service control policy (SCP) 是維運成本最低的全組織預防性控制：一份政策即涵蓋 OU 內所有現有與未來帳戶，無需逐帳戶設定、不需 Lambda、也無需修復邏輯。C 與 D 的關鍵差異在於 SCP 的 Allow 與 Deny 語意。SCP 屬於 guardrail：以明確的 Deny 陳述針對 ec2:AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress 才是『移除執行該動作能力』的正確做法。選項 C 使用 Allow，但 SCP 的 Allow 陳述本身並不會拒絕任何動作；含 Allow 的 SCP 會變成允許清單過濾器，可能誤擋無關權限，且無法可靠地移除該特定危險動作。因此 D 是預期的最佳答案，而 C 正是典型的 SCP Allow-vs-Deny 陷阱。（技術補充：aws:SourceIp 全域條件鍵實際比對的是發出 API 呼叫者的 IP，而非寫入 security group 規則內的來源 CIDR，因此嚴格而言兩個 SCP 的條件都無法檢視規則中的 0.0.0.0/0 值。但考題強制在 C 與 D 間二選一並將 aws:SourceIp 視為規則來源，採用正確 Deny 結構的 D 才是唯一站得住腳的答案。）","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Using EventBridge to trigger a Lambda that deletes the rule after creation is detective/reactive remediation, not prevention; it does not 'remove the ability' to create the rule and adds substantial operational overhead (Lambda code, IAM roles, maintenance) deployed across the OU.","why_zh":"用 EventBridge 觸發 Lambda 在規則建立後刪除，屬於偵測/事後修復而非預防；無法『移除建立規則的能力』，且需在 OU 內部署並維護 Lambda 與 IAM 角色，維運成本明顯較高。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Config managed rules (e.g., vpc-sg-open-only-to-authorized-ports) only evaluate and flag/remediate non-compliant resources after they exist; Config rules cannot prevent the API call, so they do not remove the ability to create the rule, and that specific rule checks authorized ports rather than blocking 0.0.0.0/0.","why_zh":"AWS Config 受管規則（如 vpc-sg-open-only-to-authorized-ports）僅在資源建立後評估並標示/修復不合規項目，無法阻擋 API 呼叫，因此不能移除建立規則的能力；該規則檢查的是授權連接埠，而非封鎖 0.0.0.0/0。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An SCP that uses an Allow effect does not deny the dangerous action; SCP Allow statements function as an allowlist filter and do not by themselves remove any ability, making this the wrong SCP construction (Allow-vs-Deny trap). To prevent an action you must use an explicit Deny.","why_zh":"使用 Allow 效果的 SCP 並不會拒絕危險動作；SCP 的 Allow 陳述只作為允許清單過濾器，本身無法移除任何能力，屬於錯誤的 SCP 結構（Allow-vs-Deny 陷阱）。要阻止某動作必須使用明確的 Deny。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_condition-keys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-policy-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_examples_aws_deny-ip.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":45,"question_en":"A company hosts a Git repository in an on-premises data center. The company uses webhooks to invoke functionality that runs in the AWS Cloud. The company hosts the webhook logic on a set of Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group that the company set as a target for an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The Git server calls the ALB for the configured webhooks. The company wants to move the solution to a serverless architecture. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司在本地数据中心托管 Git 存储库。该公司使用 Webhook 来调用在 AWS 云中运行的功能。该公司将 Webhook 逻辑托管在 Auto Scaling 组中的一组 Amazon EC2 实例上，该公司将这些实例设置为应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 的目标。Git 服务器为配置的 Webhook 调用 ALB。该公司希望将解决方案迁移到无服务器架构。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"For each webhook, create and configure an AWS Lambda function URL. Update the Git servers to call the individual Lambda function URLs.","B":"Create an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API. Implement each webhook logic in a separate AWS Lambda function. Update the Git servers to call the API Gateway endpoint.","C":"Deploy the webhook logic to AWS App Runner. Create an ALB, and set App Runner as the target. Update the Git servers to call the ALB endpoint.","D":"Containerize the webhook logic. Create an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster, and run the webhook logic in AWS Fargate. Create an Amazon API Gateway REST API, and set Fargate as the target. Update the Git servers to call the API Gateway endpoint."},"options_zh":{"A":"对于每个 Webhook，创建并配置 AWS Lambda 函数 URL。更新 Git 服务器以调用各个 Lambda 函数 URL。","B":"创建 Amazon API Gateway HTTP API。在单独的 AWS Lambda 函数中实现每个 Webhook 逻辑。更新 Git 服务器以调用 API 网关端 点。","C":"将 Webhook 逻辑部署到 AWS App Runner。创建 ALB，并将 App Runner 设置为目标。更新 Git 服务器以调用 ALB 端点。","D":"容器化 webhook 逻辑。创建 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 集群，并在 AWS Fargate 中运行 Webhook 逻辑。创建 Amazon API Gateway REST API，并将 Fargate 设置为目标。更新 Git 服务器以调用 API 网关端点。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":74,"A":16},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is a fully serverless architecture with the LEAST operational overhead for receiving Git webhooks. Option B (an API Gateway HTTP API fronting one Lambda function per webhook) is the canonical serverless webhook pattern: AWS Prescriptive Guidance explicitly lists 'Webhook and event handling' for events from external systems such as GitHub as an API Gateway use case, and the HTTP API type is the low-cost, low-overhead flavor. It gives the Git server a single managed endpoint that routes to separate Lambda functions, with no servers, scaling groups, or load balancers to manage. Option C is technically invalid: an Application Load Balancer target group only supports the target types instance, ip, and lambda (plus an ALB-as-target), so you cannot 'set App Runner as the target' of an ALB; App Runner exposes its own managed URL and is not registered behind an ALB, and adding an ALB also adds overhead rather than reducing it.","explanation_zh":"需求是建立完全 serverless 且維運負擔最少的架構來接收 Git webhook。選項 B（以 API Gateway HTTP API 作為入口，每個 webhook 對應一個 Lambda function）是標準的 serverless webhook 模式：AWS Prescriptive Guidance 明確將「Webhook 與事件處理」（例如來自 GitHub 等外部系統的事件）列為 API Gateway 的使用情境，而 HTTP API 類型正是低成本、低維運負擔的選擇。它讓 Git 伺服器只需呼叫單一受管端點，並分流到各個 Lambda function，完全不需管理伺服器、Auto Scaling group 或負載平衡器。選項 C 在技術上不可行：Application Load Balancer 的 target group 只支援 instance、ip、lambda（以及 ALB 作為目標）這幾種 target type，無法將 App Runner『設為 ALB 的目標』；App Runner 會自行提供受管 URL，並非註冊在 ALB 後方，且加上 ALB 反而增加維運負擔。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Lambda function URLs are serverless but force you to create and manage a separate URL per webhook and reconfigure the Git server to call many individual endpoints, with no unified entry point, throttling, WAF, or routing layer. This is more operational overhead than a single API Gateway endpoint.","why_zh":"Lambda function URL 雖然是 serverless，但需為每個 webhook 各自建立並管理一個 URL，並讓 Git 伺服器分別呼叫多個端點，缺乏統一入口、節流、WAF 與路由層，維運負擔比單一 API Gateway 端點更高。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Technically invalid: an ALB target group supports only instance, ip, and lambda target types, so App Runner cannot be set as an ALB target. App Runner exposes its own managed URL and is not placed behind an ALB; adding an ALB also increases rather than reduces operational overhead.","why_zh":"技術上不可行：ALB 的 target group 只支援 instance、ip、lambda 這些 target type，因此無法把 App Runner 設為 ALB 的目標。App Runner 會自帶受管 URL，不會放在 ALB 後方；加上 ALB 也只會增加而非降低維運負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"ECS on Fargate requires containerizing the logic, defining task definitions, and managing a cluster, which is substantially more operational overhead than Lambda. A REST API also carries more overhead and cost than an HTTP API, and you cannot directly 'set Fargate as the target' of an API Gateway REST API without additional integration plumbing (e.g., a VPC link to an NLB/ALB).","why_zh":"ECS on Fargate 需將邏輯容器化、定義 task definition 並管理叢集，維運負擔遠高於 Lambda。REST API 相較 HTTP API 也有更高的負擔與成本，且無法直接把 Fargate『設為 API Gateway REST API 的目標』，仍需額外整合（例如透過 VPC link 連到 NLB/ALB）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/choosing-the-right-aws-service-for-your-microservice-endpoints/api-gateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-target-groups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/http-api-dynamo-db.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-apigateway.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":46,"question_en":"A company is planning to migrate 1,000 on-premises servers to AWS. The servers run on several VMware clusters in the company’s data center. As part of the migration plan, the company wants to gather server metrics such as CPU details, RAM usage, operating system information, and running processes. The company then wants to query and analyze the data. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司计划将 1,000 台本地服务器迁移到 AWS。这些服务器在公司数据中心的多个 VMware 集群上运行。作为迁移计划的一部分， 该公司希望收集服务器指标，例如 CPU 详细信息、RAM 使用情况、操作系统信息和正在运行的进程。然后该公司想要查询和分析数 据。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy and configure the AWS Agentless Discovery Connector virtual appliance on the on-premises hosts. Configure Data Exploration in AWS Migration Hub. Use AWS Glue to perform an ETL job against the data. Query the data by using Amazon S3 Select.","B":"Export only the VM performance information from the on-premises hosts. Directly import the required data into AWS Migration Hub. Update any missing information in Migration Hub. Query the data by using Amazon QuickSight.","C":"Create a script to automatically gather the server information from the on-premises hosts. Use the AWS CLI to run the put-resource- attributes command to store the detailed server data in AWS Migration Hub. Query the data directly in the Migration Hub console.","D":"Deploy the AWS Application Discovery Agent to each on-premises server. Configure Data Exploration in AWS Migration Hub. Use Amazon Athena to run predefined queries against the data in Amazon S3."},"options_zh":{"A":"在本地主机上部署并配置 AWS Agentless Discovery Connector 虚拟设备。在 AWS Migration Hub 中配置数据探索。使用 AWS Glue 对数据执行 ETL 作业。使用 Amazon S3 Select 查询数据。","B":"仅从本地主机导出 VM 性能信息。将所需数据直接导入 AWS Migration Hub。更新 Migration Hub 中任何缺失的信息。使用 Amazon QuickSight 查询数据。","C":"创建一个脚本以自动从本地主机收集服务器信息。使用 AWS CLI 运行 put-resource-attributes 命令以将详细的服务器数据存储在 AWS Migration Hub 中。直接在 Migration Hub 控制台中查询数据。","D":"将 AWS Application Discovery Agent 部署到每个本地服务器。在 AWS Migration Hub 中配置数据探索。使用 Amazon Athena 对 Amazon S3 中的数据运行预定义查询。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":90},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to gather server metrics including CPU details, RAM usage, OS information, and running processes, then query and analyze that data. Only the AWS Application Discovery Agent (agent-based discovery), installed on each on-premises server, collects detailed system configuration, time-series performance data, AND running processes. The AWS docs explicitly state the Agentless Collector 'cannot figure out what processes are running on each VM,' which disqualifies the agentless approaches. Once the Discovery Agent is deployed and Data Exploration is turned on, agent data is stored in Amazon S3 and exposed through the application_discovery_service_database (tables such as os_info_agent, sys_performance_agent, processes_agent), which you query with Amazon Athena using predefined queries. This is exactly what option D describes, making it the only fully correct, low-overhead solution.","explanation_zh":"需求是收集伺服器指標（包含 CPU 細節、RAM 使用量、作業系統資訊與執行中的處理程序），然後查詢與分析資料。只有部署在每台地端伺服器上的 AWS Application Discovery Agent（agent-based 探索）能收集詳細的系統組態、時間序列效能資料以及執行中的處理程序。AWS 文件明確指出 Agentless Collector「無法判斷每個 VM 上正在執行哪些處理程序」，因此排除了 agentless 方案。當部署 Discovery Agent 並開啟 Data Exploration 後，agent 資料會儲存在 Amazon S3，並透過 application_discovery_service_database（例如 os_info_agent、sys_performance_agent、processes_agent 等表）公開，可用 Amazon Athena 搭配 predefined queries 進行查詢。這正是選項 D 所描述的，是唯一完全正確且低營運負擔的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The Agentless Discovery Connector / Agentless Collector cannot collect running processes (AWS docs: it cannot look inside VMs to see processes or network connections). Data Exploration writes to S3, but Athena is the documented query engine, not S3 Select via a Glue ETL job; this overcomplicates the workflow and misses required process data.","why_zh":"Agentless Discovery Connector / Agentless Collector 無法收集執行中的處理程序（AWS 文件：它無法深入 VM 看到處理程序或網路連線）。Data Exploration 雖會寫入 S3，但文件記載的查詢引擎是 Athena，而非透過 Glue ETL 再用 S3 Select；此流程過度複雜且缺少必要的處理程序資料。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Exporting only VM performance information and manually importing/updating data in Migration Hub is a file-based import path that does not capture running processes at scale and requires manual data backfill for 1,000 servers, which is impractical and incomplete.","why_zh":"僅匯出 VM 效能資訊並手動匯入／更新 Migration Hub 屬於 file-based import 路徑，無法大規模擷取執行中的處理程序，且對 1,000 台伺服器需手動補齊資料，既不切實際也不完整。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Scripting collection and using put-resource-attributes is impractical and incorrect: put-resource-attributes only attaches a limited set of identifying attributes (e.g., IP/MAC/hostname) to existing resources for matching, not detailed CPU/RAM/process telemetry, and Migration Hub console is not a SQL analytics query tool. This is the dump's suggested answer but is technically wrong.","why_zh":"以指令稿收集並使用 put-resource-attributes 既不切實際也不正確：put-resource-attributes 只能將少量識別屬性（如 IP/MAC/主機名稱）附加到既有資源以供比對，並非用來儲存詳細的 CPU/RAM/處理程序遙測，且 Migration Hub 主控台並非 SQL 分析查詢工具。這是題庫建議答案，但技術上錯誤。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/discovery-agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/what-is-appdiscovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/explore-direct-in-ate.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/predefined-queries.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":47,"question_en":"A company is building a serverless application that runs on an AWS Lambda function that is attached to a VPC. The company needs to integrate the application with a new service from an external provider. The external provider supports only requests that come from public IPv4 addresses that are in an allow list. The company must provide a single public IP address to the external provider before the application can start using the new service. Which solution will give the application the ability to access the new service?","question_zh":"一家公司正在构建一个在附加到 VPC 的 AWS Lambda 函数上运行的无服务器应用程序。该公司需要将该应用程序与外部提供商的新 服务集成。外部提供商仅支持来自允许列表中的公共 IPv4 地址的请求。 在应用程序可以开始使用新服务之前，公司必须向外部提供商提供单个公共 IP 地址。 哪种解决方案将使应用程序能够访问新服务？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy a NAT gateway. Associate an Elastic IP address with the NAT gateway. Configure the VPC to use the NAT gateway.","B":"Deploy an egress-only internet gateway. Associate an Elastic IP address with the egress-only internet gateway. Configure the elastic network interface on the Lambda function to use the egress-only internet gateway.","C":"Deploy an internet gateway. Associate an Elastic IP address with the internet gateway. Configure the Lambda function to use the internet gateway.","D":"Deploy an internet gateway. Associate an Elastic IP address with the internet gateway. Configure the default route in the public VPC route table to use the internet gateway."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署NAT网关。将弹性 IP 地址与 NAT 网关关联。配置VPC使用NAT网关。","B":"部署仅出口互联网网关。将弹性 IP 地址与仅出口互联网网关关联。在 Lambda 函数上配置弹性网络接口以使用仅出口互联网 网关。","C":"部署互联网网关。将弹性 IP 地址与互联网网关关联。配置 Lambda 函数以使用互联网网关。","D":"部署互联网网关。将弹性 IP 地址与互联网网关关联。在公共 VPC 路由表中配置默认​路由以使用 Internet 网关。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":92},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"A VPC-attached Lambda function must be placed in private subnets, and the only supported way to give it outbound internet access is to route 0.0.0.0/0 to a public NAT gateway in a public subnet (AWS's own 'Enable internet access for VPC-connected Lambda functions' guide builds exactly this: private subnets + NAT gateway + internet gateway). A public NAT gateway has an associated Elastic IP, so all outbound traffic is source-NAT'd to that single, fixed public IPv4 address - precisely what the external provider's allow list requires. AWS even documents 'Access your network using allow-listed IP addresses' as a NAT gateway use case. Option A is the only choice that produces a single stable public IPv4 and works with a VPC-attached Lambda.","explanation_zh":"附加到 VPC 的 Lambda function 必須放在私有子網路中，給它對外網際網路存取的唯一受支援方式，是將 0.0.0.0/0 路由到公有子網路中的公有 NAT gateway（AWS 官方的『Enable internet access for VPC-connected Lambda functions』指南正是這樣建置：私有子網路 + NAT gateway + internet gateway）。公有 NAT gateway 會關聯一個 Elastic IP，因此所有對外流量都會被來源 NAT 轉換為這個單一、固定的公有 IPv4 位址，正好符合外部供應商允許清單的需求。AWS 也將『使用允許清單 IP 位址存取網路』列為 NAT gateway 的使用情境。選項 A 是唯一能產生單一穩定公有 IPv4 且可與附加 VPC 的 Lambda 搭配運作的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"An egress-only internet gateway is for IPv6 outbound traffic only; it does not support Elastic IP association and does not provide a public IPv4 address. The provider requires a public IPv4 address, and you cannot 'configure the ENI to use' an egress-only IGW.","why_zh":"egress-only internet gateway 僅用於 IPv6 對外流量，不支援關聯 Elastic IP，也不提供公有 IPv4 位址。供應商要求的是公有 IPv4 位址，且無法讓 ENI『使用』egress-only IGW。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"You cannot associate an Elastic IP with an internet gateway - an IGW is not an EIP-attachable resource. Also a VPC-attached Lambda runs in private subnets with Hyperplane ENIs that have no public IP, so it cannot reach the internet through an IGW. This is the dump's suggested answer but it is technically invalid.","why_zh":"無法將 Elastic IP 關聯到 internet gateway，IGW 並非可附加 EIP 的資源。而且附加 VPC 的 Lambda 在私有子網路中使用沒有公有 IP 的 Hyperplane ENI，因此無法透過 IGW 連上網際網路。這是題庫建議答案，但技術上不成立。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same fatal flaw: an Elastic IP cannot be associated with an internet gateway. Even with a default route to the IGW, the Lambda Hyperplane ENI has no public/Elastic IP of its own, so an IGW (which only does 1:1 NAT for resources with their own public IP) cannot give it outbound access, and there is no single fixed public IP to provide.","why_zh":"同樣的致命缺陷：Elastic IP 無法關聯到 internet gateway。即使設定預設路由指向 IGW，Lambda 的 Hyperplane ENI 本身沒有公有/Elastic IP，而 IGW 只對擁有自身公有 IP 的資源做 1:1 NAT，因此無法提供對外存取，也沒有單一固定的公有 IP 可提供給供應商。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-vpc-internet.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-vpc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/nat-gateway-scenarios.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-nat-gateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/egress-only-internet-gateway.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":48,"question_en":"A solutions architect has developed a web application that uses an Amazon API Gateway Regional endpoint and an AWS Lambda function. The consumers of the web application are all close to the AWS Region where the application will be deployed. The Lambda function only queries an Amazon Aurora MySQL database. The solutions architect has configured the database to have three read replicas. During testing, the application does not meet performance requirements. Under high load, the application opens a large number of database connections. The solutions architect must improve the application’s performance. Which actions should the solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"解决方案架构师开发了一个使用 Amazon API Gateway 区域终端节点和 AWS Lambda 函数的 Web 应用程序。Web 应用程序的使用者都 靠近将部署该应用程序的 AWS 区域。Lambda 函数仅查询 Amazon Aurora MySQL 数据库。解决方案架构师已将数据库配置为具有三个 只读副本。 在测试过程中，应用程序不满足性能要求。在高负载下，应用程序打开大量数据库连接。解决方案架构师必须提高应用程序的性 能。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪些行动来满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Use the cluster endpoint of the Aurora database.","B":"Use RDS Proxy to set up a connection pool to the reader endpoint of the Aurora database.","C":"Use the Lambda Provisioned Concurrency feature.","D":"Move the code for opening the database connection in the Lambda function outside of the event handler.","E":"Change the API Gateway endpoint to an edge-optimized endpoint."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Aurora 数据库的集群终端节点。","B":"使用 RDS Proxy 设置到 Aurora 数据库的读取器终端节点的连接池。","C":"使用 Lambda 预置并发功能。","D":"将 Lambda 函数中用于打开数据库连接的代码移至事件处理程序之外。","E":"将 API 网关端点更改为边缘优化端点。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BD":98},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":49,"question_en":"A company is planning to host a web application on AWS and wants to load balance the tra®c across a group of Amazon EC2 instances. One of the security requirements is to enable end-to-end encryption in transit between the client and the web server. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司計劃在 AWS 上託管一個網頁應用程式，並希望在一組 Amazon EC2 執行個體間進行流量負載平衡。其中一項安全需求是在用戶端與網頁伺服器之間啟用端對端傳輸加密（end-to-end encryption in transit）。哪個解決方案能滿足此需求？","options_en":{"A":"Place the EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Provision an SSL certificate using AWS Certificate Manager (ACM), and associate the SSL certificate with the ALB. Export the SSL certificate and install it on each EC2 instance. Configure the ALB to listen on port 443 and to forward tra®c to port 443 on the instances.","B":"Associate the EC2 instances with a target group. Provision an SSL certificate using AWS Certificate Manager (ACM). Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution and configure it to use the SSL certificate. Set CloudFront to use the target group as the origin server.","C":"Place the EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) Provision an SSL certificate using AWS Certificate Manager (ACM), and associate the SSL certificate with the ALB. Provision a third-party SSL certificate and install it on each EC2 instance. Configure the ALB to listen on port 443 and to forward tra®c to port 443 on the instances.","D":"Place the EC2 instances behind a Network Load Balancer (NLB). Provision a third-party SSL certificate and install it on the NLB and on each EC2 instance. Configure the NLB to listen on port 443 and to forward tra®c to port 443 on the instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"將 EC2 執行個體置於 Application Load Balancer（ALB）之後。使用 AWS Certificate Manager（ACM）佈建 SSL 憑證，並將該 SSL 憑證與 ALB 關聯。匯出該 SSL 憑證並安裝於每個 EC2 執行個體上。設定 ALB 監聽 443 埠並將流量轉發到執行個體的 443 埠。","B":"將 EC2 執行個體與目標群組（target group）關聯。使用 AWS Certificate Manager（ACM）佈建 SSL 憑證。建立一個 Amazon CloudFront 分發並設定其使用該 SSL 憑證。設定 CloudFront 使用該目標群組作為原始伺服器（origin server）。","C":"將 EC2 執行個體置於 Application Load Balancer（ALB）之後。使用 AWS Certificate Manager（ACM）佈建 SSL 憑證，並將該 SSL 憑證與 ALB 關聯。佈建一個第三方 SSL 憑證並安裝於每個 EC2 執行個體上。設定 ALB 監聽 443 埠並將流量轉發到執行個體的 443 埠。","D":"將 EC2 執行個體置於 Network Load Balancer（NLB）之後。佈建一個第三方 SSL 憑證並安裝於 NLB 與每個 EC2 執行個體上。設定 NLB 監聽 443 埠並將流量轉發到執行個體的 443 埠。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":52,"D":38},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識"},{"id":50,"question_en":"A company wants to migrate its data analytics environment from on premises to AWS. The environment consists of two simple Node.js applications. One of the applications collects sensor data and loads it into a MySQL database. The other application aggregates the data into reports. When the aggregation jobs run, some of the load jobs fail to run correctly. The company must resolve the data loading issue. The company also needs the migration to occur without interruptions or changes for the company’s customers. What should a solutions architect do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望将其数据分析环境从本地迁移到 AWS。该环境由两个简单的 Node.js 应用程序组成。其中一个应用程序收集传感器数 据并将其加载到 MySQL 数据库中。另一个应用程序将数据聚合到报告中。聚合作业运行时，部分加载作业无法正常运行。 公司必须解决数据加载问题。该公司还需要在不中断或不改变公司客户的情况下进行迁移。 解决方案架构师应该怎样做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up an Amazon Aurora MySQL database as a replication target for the on-premises database. Create an Aurora Replica for the Aurora MySQL database, and move the aggregation jobs to run against the Aurora Replica. Set up collection endpoints as AWS Lambda functions behind a Network Load Balancer (NLB), and use Amazon RDS Proxy to write to the Aurora MySQL database. When the databases are synced, disable the replication job and restart the Aurora Replica as the primary instance. Point the collector DNS record to the NLB.","B":"Set up an Amazon Aurora MySQL database. Use AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to perform continuous data replication from the on-premises database to Aurora. Move the aggregation jobs to run against the Aurora MySQL database. Set up collection endpoints behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) as Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group. When the databases are synced, point the collector DNS record to the ALDisable the AWS DMS sync task after the cutover from on premises to AWS.","C":"Set up an Amazon Aurora MySQL database. Use AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to perform continuous data replication from the on-premises database to Aurora. Create an Aurora Replica for the Aurora MySQL database, and move the aggregation jobs to run against the Aurora Replica. Set up collection endpoints as AWS Lambda functions behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB), and use Amazon RDS Proxy to write to the Aurora MySQL database. When the databases are synced, point the collector DNS record to the ALB. Disable the AWS DMS sync task after the cutover from on premises to AWS.","D":"Set up an Amazon Aurora MySQL database. Create an Aurora Replica for the Aurora MySQL database, and move the aggregation jobs to run against the Aurora Replica. Set up collection endpoints as an Amazon Kinesis data stream. Use Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to replicate the data to the Aurora MySQL database. When the databases are synced, disable the replication job and restart the Aurora Replica as the primary instance. Point the collector DNS record to the Kinesis data stream."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 Amazon Aurora MySQL 数据库设置为本地数据库的复制目标。为 Aurora MySQL 数据库创建 Aurora 副本，并将聚合作业移动 到针对 Aurora 副本运行。将收集终端节点设置为网络负载均衡器 (NLB) 后面的 AWS Lambda 函数，并使用 Amazon RDS 代理写入 Aurora MySQL 数据库。数据库同步后，禁用复制作业并重新启动 Aurora 副本作为主实例。将收集器 DNS 记录指向 NLB。","B":"设置 Amazon Aurora MySQL 数据库。使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 执行从本地数据库到 Aurora 的连续数据复 制。将聚合作业移至针对 Aurora MySQL 数据库运行。将 Application Load Balancer (ALB) 后面的收集终端节点设置为 Auto Scaling 组中的 Amazon EC2 实例。同步数据库后，将收集器 DNS 记录指向 ALDisable 从本地切换到 AWS 后的 AWS DMS 同步任务。 C。 设置 Amazon Aurora MySQL 数据库。使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 执行从本地数据库到 Aurora 的连续数据 复制。为 Aurora MySQL 数据库创建 Aurora 副本，并将聚合作业移动到针对 Aurora 副本运行。将收集终端节点设置为应用程序负 载均衡器 (ALB) 后面的 AWS Lambda 函数，并使用 Amazon RDS 代理写入 Aurora MySQL 数据库。同步数据库后，将收集器 DNS 记 录指向 ALB。从本地切换到 AWS 后禁用 AWS DMS 同步任务。","D":"设置 Amazon Aurora MySQL 数据库。为 Aurora MySQL 数据库创建 Aurora 副本，并将聚合作业移动到针对 Aurora 副本运行。将 收集终端节点设置为 Amazon Kinesis 数据流。使用 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 将数据复制到 Aurora MySQL 数据库。数据库同 步后，禁用复制作业并重新启动 Aurora 副本作为主实例。将收集器 DNS 记录指向 Kinesis 数据流。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":95},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":51,"question_en":"A health insurance company stores personally identifiable information (PII) in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company uses server-side encryption with S3 managed encryption keys (SSE-S3) to encrypt the objects. According to a new requirement, all current and future objects in the S3 bucket must be encrypted by keys that the company’s security team manages. The S3 bucket does not have versioning enabled. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家健康保险公司将个人身份信息 (PII) 存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。该公司使用带有 S3 托管加密密钥 (SSE-S3) 的服务器端加密来 加密对象。根据新要求，S3 存储桶中当前和未来的所有对象都必须使用公司安全团队管理的密钥进行加密。S3 存储桶未启用版本控 制。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"In the S3 bucket properties, change the default encryption to SSE-S3 with a customer managed key. Use the AWS CLI to re-upload all objects in the S3 bucket. Set an S3 bucket policy to deny unencrypted PutObject requests.","B":"In the S3 bucket properties, change the default encryption to server-side encryption with AWS KMS managed encryption keys (SSE- KMS). Set an S3 bucket policy to deny unencrypted PutObject requests. Use the AWS CLI to re-upload all objects in the S3 bucket.","C":"In the S3 bucket properties, change the default encryption to server-side encryption with AWS KMS managed encryption keys (SSE- KMS). Set an S3 bucket policy to automatically encrypt objects on GetObject and PutObject requests.","D":"In the S3 bucket properties, change the default encryption to AES-256 with a customer managed key. Attach a policy to deny unencrypted PutObject requests to any entities that access the S3 bucket. Use the AWS CLI to re-upload all objects in the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 S3 存储桶属性中，使用客户管理的密钥将默认加密更改为 SSE-S3。使用 AWS CLI 重新上传 S3 存储桶中的所有对象。设置 S3 存储桶策略以拒绝未加密的 PutObject 请求。","B":"在 S3 存储桶属性中，将默认加密更改为使用 AWS KMS 托管加密密钥 (SSE-KMS) 的服务器端加密。设置 S3 存储桶策略以拒绝 未加密的 PutObject 请求。使用 AWS CLI 重新上传 S3 存储桶中的所有对象。","C":"在 S3 存储桶属性中，将默认加密更改为使用 AWS KMS 托管加密密钥 (SSE-KMS) 的服务器端加密。设置 S3 存储桶策略以自动 加密 GetObject 和 PutObject 请求上的对象。","D":"在 S3 存储桶属性中，使用客户管理的密钥将默认加密更改为 AES-256。附加策略以拒绝对访问 S3 存储桶的任何实体的未加密 PutObject 请求。使用 AWS CLI 重新上传 S3 存储桶中的所有对象。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":62,"D":37},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is that all current and future objects be encrypted with keys the security team manages, which in S3 means SSE-KMS using a customer managed KMS key (SSE-S3/AES-256 always uses keys that Amazon S3 manages, not the customer's security team). Option B correctly changes the bucket's default encryption to SSE-KMS so future uploads use the managed key, adds a bucket policy denying unencrypted PutObject requests to enforce the standard, and re-uploads existing objects via the AWS CLI. Re-uploading is necessary because changing the default encryption configuration does not re-encrypt objects that already exist in the bucket. Options A and D are technically invalid because SSE-S3 and AES-256 cannot be paired with a customer managed key (those modes use S3-managed keys by definition). Option C uses SSE-KMS but invents a nonexistent 'encrypt on GetObject' behavior (GetObject is a read) and never re-encrypts the existing objects, so it fails the 'all current objects' requirement.","explanation_zh":"需求是所有現有與未來的物件都必須使用安全團隊管理的金鑰加密；在 S3 中這代表必須使用 SSE-KMS 搭配 customer managed KMS key（SSE-S3／AES-256 一律使用 Amazon S3 管理的金鑰，而非客戶安全團隊管理）。選項 B 正確地將儲存貯體的預設加密改為 SSE-KMS，使未來上傳的物件使用受管金鑰；再加上拒絕未加密 PutObject 的 bucket policy 來強制標準；並透過 AWS CLI 重新上傳現有物件。由於變更預設加密設定並不會重新加密儲存貯體中既有的物件，因此重新上傳是必要的。選項 A 與 D 在技術上不成立，因為 SSE-S3 與 AES-256 無法搭配 customer managed key（這兩種模式本質上使用 S3 管理的金鑰）。選項 C 雖然用了 SSE-KMS，但杜撰了不存在的「在 GetObject 時加密」行為（GetObject 是讀取），且從未重新加密既有物件，因此無法滿足『所有現有物件』的要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"'SSE-S3 with a customer managed key' is a contradiction: SSE-S3 by definition uses keys that Amazon S3 manages, so it cannot satisfy the requirement for security-team-managed keys.","why_zh":"『SSE-S3 搭配 customer managed key』是矛盾的：SSE-S3 依定義使用 Amazon S3 管理的金鑰，無法滿足由安全團隊管理金鑰的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"SSE-KMS is correct, but there is no S3 feature that 'automatically encrypts objects on GetObject' (GetObject is a read operation), and it never re-encrypts the existing objects, so current PII objects remain SSE-S3 encrypted.","why_zh":"SSE-KMS 是對的，但 S3 並沒有『在 GetObject 時自動加密物件』的功能（GetObject 是讀取操作），而且完全沒有重新加密既有物件，導致現有的 PII 物件仍維持 SSE-S3 加密。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"'AES-256 with a customer managed key' is invalid: AES-256 in S3 default encryption is SSE-S3 (S3-managed keys) and cannot be combined with a customer managed KMS key, so it does not give the security team key management.","why_zh":"『AES-256 搭配 customer managed key』不成立：S3 預設加密中的 AES-256 即 SSE-S3（S3 管理的金鑰），無法與 customer managed KMS key 結合，因此無法讓安全團隊管理金鑰。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/default-bucket-encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/UsingEncryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/bucket-encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/example-bucket-policies.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":52,"question_en":"A company is running a web application in the AWS Cloud. The application consists of dynamic content that is created on a set of Amazon EC2 instances. The EC2 instances run in an Auto Scaling group that is configured as a target group for an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The company is using an Amazon CloudFront distribution to distribute the application globally. The CloudFront distribution uses the ALB as an origin. The company uses Amazon Route 53 for DNS and has created an A record of www.example.com for the CloudFront distribution. A solutions architect must configure the application so that itis highly available and fault tolerant. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 云中运行 Web 应用程序。该应用程序由在一组 Amazon EC2 实例上创建的动态内容组成。EC2 实例在配置为应用 程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 目标组的 Auto Scaling 组中运行。 该公司正在使用 Amazon CloudFront 发行版在全球范围内分发该应用程序。CloudFront 发行版使用 ALB 作为源。该公司使用 Amazon Route 53 作为 DNS，并为 CloudFront 分配创建了 www.example.com 的 A 记录。 解决方案架构师必须配置应用程序，使其具有高可用性和容错能力。 哪种解决方案满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Provision a full, secondary application deployment in a different AWS Region. Update the Route 53 A record to be a failover record. Add both of the CloudFront distributions as values. Create Route 53 health checks.","B":"Provision an ALB, an Auto Scaling group, and EC2 instances in a different AWS Region. Update the CloudFront distribution, and create a second origin for the new ALCreate an origin group for the two origins. Configure one origin as primary and one origin as secondary.","C":"Provision an Auto Scaling group and EC2 instances in a different AWS Region. Create a second target for the new Auto Scaling group in the ALB. Set up the failover routing algorithm on the ALB.","D":"Provision a full, secondary application deployment in a different AWS Region. Create a second CloudFront distribution, and add the new application setup as an origin. Create an AWS Global Accelerator accelerator. Add both of the CloudFront distributions as endpoints."},"options_zh":{"A":"在不同的 AWS 区域中配置完整的辅助应用程序部署。将 Route 53 A 记录更新为故障转移记录。添加两个 CloudFront 分配作为 值。创建 Route 53 运行状况检查。","B":"在不同的 AWS 区域中配置 ALB、Auto Scaling 组和 EC2 实例。更新 CloudFront 分配，并为新 AL 创建第二个源为两个源创建一 个源组。将一个源配置为主要源，将一个源配置为辅助源。","C":"在不同的 AWS 区域中配置 Auto Scaling 组和 EC2 实例。为 ALB 中的新 Auto Scaling 组创建第二个目标。在 ALB 上设置故障转移 路由算法。","D":"在不同的 AWS 区域中配置完整的辅助应用程序部署。创建第二个 CloudFront 分配，并将新的应用程序设置添加为源。创建 AWS Global Accelerator 加速器。将两个 CloudFront 分配添加为端点。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":53,"question_en":"A company has an organization in AWS Organizations that has a large number of AWS accounts. One of the AWS accounts is designated as a transit account and has a transit gateway that is shared with all of the other AWS accounts. AWS Site-to-Site VPN connections are configured between all of the company’s global o®ces and the transit account. The company has AWS Config enabled on all of its accounts. The company’s networking team needs to centrally manage a list of internal IP address ranges that belong to the global o®ces. Developers will reference this list to gain access to their applications securely. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST amount of operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Organizations 中擁有大量 AWS 帳戶。其中一個 AWS 帳戶被指定為轉接帳戶（transit account），並具有一個與所有其他 AWS 帳戶共用的傳輸閘道（transit gateway）。公司所有全球辦公室與該轉接帳戶之間都已設定 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 連線。該公司在所有帳戶中都已啟用 AWS Config。該公司的網路團隊需要集中管理一份屬於全球辦公室的內部 IP 位址範圍清單。開發人員將參考此清單以安全地存取其應用程式。哪個解決方案能以最少的運維負擔滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a JSON file that is hosted in Amazon S3 and that lists all of the internal IP address ranges. Configure an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic in each of the accounts that can be invoked when the JSON file is updated. Subscribe an AWS Lambda function to the SNS topic to update all relevant security group rules with the updated IP address ranges.","B":"Create a new AWS Config managed rule that contains all of the internal IP address ranges. Use the rule to check the security groups in each of the accounts to ensure compliance with the list of IP address ranges. Configure the rule to automatically remediate any noncompliant security group that is detected.","C":"In the transit account, create a VPC prefix list with all of the internal IP address ranges. Use AWS Resource Access Manager to share the prefix list with all of the other accounts. Use the shared prefix list to configure security group rules in the other accounts.","D":"In the transit account, create a security group with all of the internal IP address ranges. Configure the security groups in the other accounts to reference the transit account’s security group by using a nested security group reference of “/sg-1a2b3c4d”."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個託管於 Amazon S3 的 JSON 檔案，列出所有內部 IP 位址範圍。在每個帳戶中設定一個 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主題，於該 JSON 檔案更新時觸發。訂閱一個 AWS Lambda 函式到該 SNS 主題，以使用更新後的 IP 位址範圍更新所有相關的安全群組規則。","B":"建立一個包含所有內部 IP 位址範圍的新 AWS Config 受管規則。使用該規則檢查每個帳戶中的安全群組，確保符合該 IP 位址範圍清單。設定該規則自動修復任何被偵測到不合規的安全群組。","C":"在轉接帳戶中，建立一個包含所有內部 IP 位址範圍的 VPC 前綴清單（prefix list）。使用 AWS Resource Access Manager 將該前綴清單與所有其他帳戶共用。使用該共用的前綴清單在其他帳戶中設定安全群組規則。","D":"在轉接帳戶中，建立一個包含所有內部 IP 位址範圍的安全群組。設定其他帳戶中的安全群組，透過巢狀安全群組參照「/sg-1a2b3c4d」來參照該轉接帳戶的安全群組。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":54,"question_en":"A company runs a new application as a static website in Amazon S3. The company has deployed the application to a production AWS account and uses Amazon CloudFront to deliver the website. The website calls an Amazon API Gateway REST API. An AWS Lambda function backs each API method. The company wants to create a CSV report every 2 weeks to show each API Lambda function’s recommended configured memory, recommended cost, and the price difference between current configurations and the recommendations. The company will store the reports in an S3 bucket. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST development time?","question_zh":"一家公司在 Amazon S3 中运行一个新应用程序作为静态网站。该公司已将该应用程序部署到生产 AWS 账户，并使用 Amazon CloudFront 交付该网站。该网站调用 Amazon API Gateway REST API。AWS Lambda 函数支持每个 API 方法。 该公司希望每两周创建一个 CSV 报告，以显示每个 API Lambda 函数的建议配置内存、建议成本以及当前配置与建议之间的价格差 异。该公司将把报告存储在 S3 存储桶中。 哪种解决方案能够以最短的开发时间满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a Lambda function that extracts metrics data for each API Lambda function from Amazon CloudWatch Logs for the 2-week period. Collate the data into tabular format. Store the data as a .csv file in an S3 bucket. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to schedule the Lambda function to run every 2 weeks.","B":"Opt in to AWS Compute Optimizer. Create a Lambda function that calls the ExportLambdaFunctionRecommendations operation. Export the .csv file to an S3 bucket. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to schedule the Lambda function to run every 2 weeks.","C":"Opt in to AWS Compute Optimizer. Set up enhanced infrastructure metrics. Within the Compute Optimizer console, schedule a job to export the Lambda recommendations to a .csv file. Store the file in an S3 bucket every 2 weeks.","D":"Purchase the AWS Business Support plan for the production account. Opt in to AWS Compute Optimizer for AWS Trusted Advisor checks. In the Trusted Advisor console, schedule a job to export the cost optimization checks to a .csv file. Store the file in an S3 bucket every 2 weeks."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Lambda 函数，从 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中提取 2 周内每个 API Lambda 函数的指标数据。将数据整理成表格格 式。将数据以 .csv 文件形式存储在 S3 存储桶中。创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则以安排 Lambda 函数每 2 周运行一次。","B":"选择加入 AWS Compute Optimizer。创建一个调用 ExportLambdaFunctionRecommendations 操作的 Lambda 函数。将 .csv 文件导 出到 S3 存储桶。创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则以安排 Lambda 函数每 2 周运行一次。","C":"选择加入 AWS Compute Optimizer。设置增强的基础设施指标。在 Compute Optimizer 控制台中，安排一项作业以将 Lambda 建 议导出到 .csv 文件。每两周将文件存储在 S3 存储桶中。","D":"为生产账户购买 AWS 业务支持计划。选择加入 AWS Compute Optimizer 以进行 AWS Trusted Advisor 检查。在 Trusted Advisor 控 制台中，安排作业将成本优化检查导出到 .csv 文件。每两周将文件存储在 S3 存储桶中。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":81},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":55,"question_en":"A company’s factory and automation applications are running in a single VPC. More than 20 applications run on a combination of Amazon EC2, Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS), and Amazon RDS. The company has software engineers spread across three teams. One of the three teams owns each application, and each time is responsible for the cost and performance of all of its applications. Team resources have tags that represent their application and team. The teams use IAM access for daily activities. The company needs to determine which costs on the monthly AWS bill are attributable to each application or team. The company also must be able to create reports to compare costs from the last 12 months and to help forecast costs for the next 12 months. A solutions architect must recommend an AWS Billing and Cost Management solution that provides these cost reports. Which combination of actions will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"公司的工厂和自动化应用程序在单个 VPC 中运行。超过 20 个应用程序在 Amazon EC2、Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 和 Amazon RDS 的组合上运行。 该公司的软件工程师分布在三个团队中。三个团队之一拥有每个应用程序，并且每次都对其所有应用程序的成本和性能负责。团队 资源具有代表其应用程序和团队的标签。团队使用 IAM 访问权限进行日常活动。 公司需要确定每月 AWS 账单上的哪些成本可归因于每个应用程序或团队。公司还必须能够创建报告来比较过去 12 个月的成本并帮 助预测未来 12 个月的成本。解决方案架构师必须推荐提供这些成本报告的 AWS 账单和成本管理解决方案。 哪种行动组合可以满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Activate the user-define cost allocation tags that represent the application and the team.","B":"Activate the AWS generated cost allocation tags that represent the application and the team.","C":"Create a cost category for each application in Billing and Cost Management.","D":"Activate IAM access to Billing and Cost Management.","E":"Create a cost budget.","F":"Enable Cost Explorer."},"options_zh":{"A":"激活代表应用程序和团队的用户定义成本分配标签。","B":"激活 AWS 生成的代表应用程序和团队的成本分配标签。","C":"在计费和成本管理中为每个应用程序创建一个成本类别。","D":"激活 IAM 对账单和成本管理的访问权限。","E":"制定成本预算。","F":"启用 Cost Explorer。"},"answer":["A","C","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ACF":56,"ADF":44},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Containers"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・複選"},{"id":56,"question_en":"An AWS customer has a web application that runs on premises. The web application fetches data from a third-party API that is behind a firewall. The third party accepts only one public CIDR block in each client’s allow list. The customer wants to migrate their web application to the AWS Cloud. The application will be hosted on a set of Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in a VPC. The ALB is located in public subnets. The EC2 instances are located in private subnets. NAT gateways provide internet access to the private subnets. How should a solutions architect ensure that the web application can continue to call the third-party API after the migration?","question_zh":"AWS 客户有一个在本地运行的 Web 应用程序。Web 应用程序从防火墙后面的第三方 API 获取数据。第三方仅接受每个客户端的允许 列表中的一个公共 CIDR 块。 客户希望将其 Web 应用程序迁移到 AWS 云。该应用程序将托管在 VPC 中应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面的一组 Amazon EC2 实例 上。ALB 位于公共子网中。EC2 实例位于私有子网中。NAT 网关提供对私有子网的互联网访问。 解决方案架构师应该如何确保Web应用程序在迁移后可以继续调用第三方API？","options_en":{"A":"Associate a block of customer-owned public IP addresses to the VPC. Enable public IP addressing for public subnets in the VPC.","B":"Register a block of customer-owned public IP addresses in the AWS account. Create Elastic IP addresses from the address block and assign them to the NAT gateways in the VPC.","C":"Create Elastic IP addresses from the block of customer-owned IP addresses. Assign the static Elastic IP addresses to the ALB.","D":"Register a block of customer-owned public IP addresses in the AWS account. Set up AWS Global Accelerator to use Elastic IP addresses from the address block. Set the ALB as the accelerator endpoint."},"options_zh":{"A":"将客户拥有的公共 IP 地址块关联到 VPC。为 VPC 中的公有子网启用公有 IP 寻址。","B":"在 AWS 账户中注册客户拥有的公共 IP 地址块。从地址块创建弹性 IP 地址并将其分配给 VPC 中的 NAT 网关。","C":"从客户拥有的 IP 地址块创建弹性 IP 地址。将静态弹性 IP 地址分配给 ALB。","D":"在 AWS 账户中注册客户拥有的公共 IP 地址块。设置 AWS Global Accelerator 以使用地址块中的弹性 IP 地址。将 ALB 设置为加 速器端点。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":57,"question_en":"A company with several AWS accounts is using AWS Organizations and service control policies (SCPs). An administrator created the following SCP and has attached it to an organizational unit (OU) that contains AWS account 1111-1111-1111: Developers working in account 1111-1111-1111 complain that they cannot create Amazon S3 buckets. How should the administrator address this problem?","question_zh":"一家擁有多個 AWS 帳戶的公司使用 AWS Organizations 與服務控制政策（SCP）。管理員建立了以下 SCP 並將其附加到一個包含 AWS 帳戶 1111-1111-1111 的組織單位（OU）：開發人員在帳戶 1111-1111-1111 中抱怨他們無法建立 Amazon S3 儲存桶。管理員應如何解決此問題？","options_en":{"A":"Add s3:CreateBucket with “Allow” effect to the SCP.","B":"Remove the account from the OU, and attach the SCP directly to account 1111-1111-1111.","C":"Instruct the developers to add Amazon S3 permissions to their IAM entities.","D":"Remove the SCP from account 1111-1111-1111."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 SCP 中新增一條效果為「Allow」的 s3:CreateBucket 陳述。","B":"將該帳戶從該 OU 中移除，並將該 SCP 直接附加到帳戶 1111-1111-1111。","C":"指示開發人員在其 IAM 實體上新增 Amazon S3 權限。","D":"從帳戶 1111-1111-1111 移除該 SCP。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":89},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":58,"question_en":"A company has a monolithic application that is critical to the company’s business. The company hosts the application on an Amazon EC2 instance that runs Amazon Linux 2. The company’s application team receives a directive from the legal department to back up the data from the instance’s encrypted Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume to an Amazon S3 bucket. The application team does not have the administrative SSH key pair for the instance. The application must continue to serve the users. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"公司拥有对公司业务至关重要的整体应用程序。该公司在运行 Amazon Linux 2 的 Amazon EC2 实例上托管该应用程序。该公司的应用 程序团队收到法律部门的指示，将数据从实例的加密 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 卷备份到 Amazon S3 存储桶。应用程序 团队没有实例的管理 SSH 密钥对。应用程序必须继续为用户服务。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Attach a role to the instance with permission to write to Amazon S3. Use the AWS Systems Manager Session Manager option to gain access to the instance and run commands to copy data into Amazon S3.","B":"Create an image of the instance with the reboot option turned on. Launch a new EC2 instance from the image. Attach a role to the new instance with permission to write to Amazon S3. Run a command to copy data into Amazon S3.","C":"Take a snapshot of the EBS volume by using Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager (Amazon DLM). Copy the data to Amazon S3.","D":"Create an image of the instance. Launch a new EC2 instance from the image. Attach a role to the new instance with permission to write to Amazon S3. Run a command to copy data into Amazon S3."},"options_zh":{"A":"将角色附加到有权写入 Amazon S3 的实例。使用 AWS Systems Manager 会话管理器选项获取对实例的访问权限并运行命令以将 数据复制到 Amazon S3 中。","B":"创建启用重启选项的实例的映像。从映像启动新的 EC2 实例。将具有写入 Amazon S3 权限的角色附加到新实例。运行命令将 数据复制到 Amazon S3 中。","C":"使用 Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager (Amazon DLM) 拍摄 EBS 卷的快照。将数据复制到 Amazon S3。","D":"创建实例的镜像。从映像启动新的 EC2 实例。将具有写入 Amazon S3 权限的角色附加到新实例。运行命令将数据复制到 Amazon S3 中。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":51,"C":47},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識"},{"id":59,"question_en":"A solutions architect needs to copy data from an Amazon S3 bucket m an AWS account to a new S3 bucket in a new AWS account. The solutions architect must implement a solution that uses the AWS CLI. Which combination of steps will successfully copy the data? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"解决方案架构师需要将数据从 AWS 账户中的 Amazon S3 存储桶复制到新 AWS 账户中的新 S3 存储桶。解决方案架构师必须实施使用 AWS CLI 的解决方案。 哪种步骤组合可以成功复制数据？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a bucket policy to allow the source bucket to list its contents and to put objects and set object ACLs in the destination bucket. Attach the bucket policy to the destination bucket.","B":"Create a bucket policy to allow a user in the destination account to list the source bucket’s contents and read the source bucket’s objects. Attach the bucket policy to the source bucket.","C":"Create an IAM policy in the source account. Configure the policy to allow a user in the source account to list contents and get objects in the source bucket, and to list contents, put objects, and set object ACLs in the destination bucket. Attach the policy to the user.","D":"Create an IAM policy in the destination account. Configure the policy to allow a user in the destination account to list contents and get objects in the source bucket, and to list contents, put objects, and set objectACLs in the destination bucket. Attach the policy to the user.","E":"Run the aws s3 sync command as a user in the source account. Specify the source and destination buckets to copy the data.","F":"Run the aws s3 sync command as a user in the destination account. Specify the source and destination buckets to copy the data."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建桶策略，允许源桶列出其内容，并允许在目标桶中放置对象并设置对象 ACL。将存储桶策略附加到目标存储桶。","B":"创建存储桶策略以允许目标账户中的用户列出源存储桶的内容并读取源存储桶的对象。将存储桶策略附加到源存储桶。","C":"在源账户中创建 IAM 策略。配置策略以允许源账户中的用户在源存储桶中列出内容和获取对象，以及在目标存储桶中列出内 容、放置对象和设置对象 ACL。将策略附加到用户。","D":"在目标账户中创建 IAM 策略。配置策略以允许目标账户中的用户在源存储桶中列出内容和获取对象，以及在目标存储桶中列 出内容、放置对象和设置对象ACL。将策略附加到用户。","E":"以源账户中的用户身份运行 aws s3sync 命令。指定复制数据的源桶和目标桶。","F":"以目标账户中的用户身份运行 aws s3sync 命令。指定复制数据的源桶和目标桶。"},"answer":["A","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BDF":95},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"For a cross-account S3 copy, the copying identity must live in the DESTINATION account because that account will own the newly written objects, and cross-account access requires permission on BOTH sides: an identity-based (IAM) policy in the caller's account AND a resource-based (bucket) policy on the resource owned by the other account. (D) gives the destination-account user an IAM policy allowing list/get on the SOURCE bucket plus list/put/put-ACL on the DESTINATION bucket. (B) is the matching resource policy attached to the SOURCE bucket that grants that destination-account user permission to list and read the source objects (the source bucket is owned by the other account, so its owner must explicitly delegate access). (F) runs 'aws s3 sync' as the destination-account user, which reads from source and writes to destination so the destination account owns the copies. The destination bucket needs no separate cross-account bucket policy because the user and that bucket are in the same account, so the IAM policy alone authorizes writes. This matches the AWS Prescriptive Guidance pattern for copying S3 data across accounts via the AWS CLI.","explanation_zh":"跨帳號 S3 複製時，執行複製的身分必須位於「目的地帳號」，因為新寫入的物件由目的地帳號擁有；而跨帳號存取需要兩邊都授權：呼叫者帳號內的身分型 (IAM) 政策，以及由另一帳號擁有之資源上的資源型 (bucket) 政策。(D) 為目的地帳號使用者建立 IAM 政策，允許對來源 bucket 進行 list/get，並對目的地 bucket 進行 list/put/put-ACL。(B) 是對應的資源政策，附加在「來源 bucket」上，授權該目的地帳號使用者列出並讀取來源物件（來源 bucket 由另一帳號擁有，必須由其擁有者明確委派存取權）。(F) 由目的地帳號使用者執行 'aws s3 sync'，從來源讀取並寫入目的地，使複本由目的地帳號擁有。目的地 bucket 不需另外的跨帳號 bucket 政策，因為使用者與該 bucket 同屬一個帳號，僅靠 IAM 政策即可授權寫入。此符合 AWS Prescriptive Guidance 透過 AWS CLI 跨帳號複製 S3 資料的範式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A bucket cannot be a 'principal', so allowing 'the source bucket to put objects' is not a valid policy. Moreover, the DESTINATION bucket does not need a cross-account bucket policy at all: the user runs from the destination account, so its identity-based policy (D) already authorizes writes to a same-account bucket. The resource policy is needed on the SOURCE bucket (B), not the destination.","why_zh":"bucket 不能當作『主體 (principal)』，因此『允許來源 bucket 放置物件』並非有效政策。此外目的地 bucket 根本不需要跨帳號 bucket 政策：使用者由目的地帳號執行，其身分型政策 (D) 已可授權寫入同帳號的 bucket。需要資源政策的是『來源 bucket』(B)，而非目的地。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The IAM policy and user must be in the DESTINATION account, not the source account. A source-account user could not be granted ownership-conferring writes into the destination bucket via a source-account identity policy, and the whole flow is designed around the destination account performing the copy.","why_zh":"IAM 政策與使用者必須位於『目的地帳號』，而非來源帳號。來源帳號使用者無法透過來源帳號的身分政策對目的地 bucket 寫入並取得擁有權，整個流程是以目的地帳號執行複製為設計核心。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Running 'aws s3 sync' as a source-account user is wrong: the copy must run from the destination account so the destination account owns the copied objects and so the same-account identity policy authorizes the writes. A source-account caller would lack cross-account write authorization to the destination bucket under this design.","why_zh":"以來源帳號使用者執行 'aws s3 sync' 是錯誤的：複製必須由目的地帳號執行，使目的地帳號擁有複製的物件，並讓同帳號身分政策授權寫入。在此設計下，來源帳號呼叫者缺少對目的地 bucket 的跨帳號寫入授權。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/patterns/copy-data-from-an-s3-bucket-to-another-account-and-region-by-using-the-aws-cli.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/access-policy-language-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/example-bucket-policies.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":60,"question_en":"A company built an application based on AWS Lambda deployed in an AWS CloudFormation stack. The last production release of the web application introduced an issue that resulted in an outage lasting several minutes. A solutions architect must adjust the deployment process to support a canary release. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司基于部署在 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈中的 AWS Lambda 构建了一个应用程序。Web 应用程序的最后一个生产版本引入了一 个问题，导致持续几分钟的中断。解决方案架构师必须调整部署流程以支持金丝雀版本。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an alias for every new deployed version of the Lambda function. Use the AWS CLI update-alias command with the routing-config parameter to distribute the load.","B":"Deploy the application into a new CloudFormation stack. Use an Amazon Route 53 weighted routing policy to distribute the load.","C":"Create a version for every new deployed Lambda function. Use the AWS CLI update-function-configuration command with the routing- config parameter to distribute the load.","D":"Configure AWS CodeDeploy and use CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime in the Deployment configuration to distribute the load."},"options_zh":{"A":"为每个新部署的 Lambda 函数版本创建一个别名。使用带有routing-config 参数的AWS CLI update-alias 命令来分配负载。","B":"将应用程序部署到新的 CloudFormation 堆栈中。使用 Amazon Route 53 加权路由策略来分配负载。","C":"为每个新部署的 Lambda 函数创建一个版本。使用带有routing-config 参数的 AWS CLI update-function-configuration 命令来分配负 载。","D":"配置 AWS CodeDeploy 并在部署配置中使用 CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime 来分配负载。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":98},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":61,"question_en":"A finance company hosts a data lake in Amazon S3. The company receives financial data records over SFTP each night from several third parties. The company runs its own SFTP server on an Amazon EC2 instance in a public subnet of a VPC. After the files are uploaded, they are moved to the data lake by a cron job that runs on the same instance. The SFTP server is reachable on DNS sftp.example.com through the use of Amazon Route 53. What should a solutions architect do to improve the reliability and scalability of the SFTP solution?","question_zh":"一家金融公司在 Amazon S3 中托管数据湖。该公司每天晚上通过 SFTP 从多个第三方接收财务数据记录。该公司在 VPC 公有子网中 的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行自己的 SFTP 服务器。文件上传后，通过在同一实例上运行的 cron 作业将它们移至数据湖。可通过使用 Amazon Route 53 在 DNS sftp.example.com 上访问 SFTP 服务器。 解决方案架构师应该如何提高 SFTP 解决方案的可靠性和可扩展性？","options_en":{"A":"Move the EC2 instance into an Auto Scaling group. Place the EC2 instance behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Update the DNS record sftp.example.com in Route 53 to point to the ALB.","B":"Migrate the SFTP server to AWS Transfer for SFTP. Update the DNS record sftp.example.com in Route 53 to point to the server endpoint hostname.","C":"Migrate the SFTP server to a file gateway in AWS Storage Gateway. Update the DNS record sftp.example.com in Route 53 to point to the file gateway endpoint.","D":"Place the EC2 instance behind a Network Load Balancer (NLB). Update the DNS record sftp.example.com in Route 53 to point to the NLB."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 EC2 实例移至 Auto Scaling 组中。将 EC2 实例放置在应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面。更新 Route 53 中的 DNS 记录 sftp.example.com 以指向 ALB。","B":"将 SFTP 服务器迁移到 AWS Transfer for SFTP。更新 Route 53 中的 DNS 记录 sftp.example.com 以指向服务器终端节点主机名。","C":"将 SFTP 服务器迁移到 AWS Storage Gateway 中的文件网关。更新 Route 53 中的 DNS 记录 sftp.example.com 以指向文件网关终 端节点。","D":"将 EC2 实例放置在网络负载均衡器 (NLB) 后面。更新 Route 53 中的 DNS 记录 sftp.example.com 以指向 NLB。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":62,"question_en":"A company wants to migrate an application to Amazon EC2 from VMware Infrastructure that runs in an on-premises data center. A solutions architect must preserve the software and configuration settings during the migration. What should the solutions architect do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望将应用程序从在本地数据中心运行的 VMware Infrastructure 迁移到 Amazon EC2。解决方案架构师必须在迁移期间保留 软件和配置设置。 解决方案架构师应该怎样做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the AWS DataSync agent to start replicating the data store to Amazon FSx for Windows File Server. Use the SMB share to host the VMware data store. Use VM Import/Export to move the VMs to Amazon EC2.","B":"Use the VMware vSphere client to export the application as an image in Open Virtualization Format (OVF) format. Create an Amazon S3 bucket to store the image in the destination AWS Region. Create and apply an IAM role for VM Import. Use the AWS CLI to run the EC2 import command.","C":"Configure AWS Storage Gateway for files service to export a Common Internet File System (CIFS) share. Create a backup copy to the shared folder. Sign in to the AWS Management Console and create an AMI from the backup copy. Launch an EC2 instance that is based on the AMI.","D":"Create a managed-instance activation for a hybrid environment in AWS Systems Manager. Download and install Systems Manager Agent on the on-premises VM. Register the VM with Systems Manager to be a managed instance. Use AWS Backup to create a snapshot of the VM and create an AMI. Launch an EC2 instance that is based on the AMI."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS DataSync 代理以开始将数据存储复制到 Amazon FSx for Windows File Server。使用 SMB 共享来托管 VMware 数据存 储。使用 VM Import/Export 将 VM 移动到 Amazon EC2。","B":"使用 VMware vSphere 客户端将应用程序导出为开放虚拟化格式 (OVF) 格式的映像。创建 Amazon S3 存储桶以将映像存储在目 标 AWS 区域中。创建并应用用于 VM 导入的 IAM 角色。使用 AWS CLI 运行 EC2 导入命令。","C":"配置 AWS Storage Gateway for files 服务以导出通用 Internet 文件系统 (CIFS) 共享。创建共享文件夹的备份副本。登录 AWS 管理 控制台并从备份副本创建 AMI。启动基于 AMI 的 EC2 实例。","D":"在 AWS Systems Manager 中为混合环境创建托管实例激活。在本地 VM 上下载并安装 Systems Manager 代理。使用 Systems Manager 将 VM 注册为托管实例。使用 AWS Backup 创建 VM 快照并创建 AMI。启动基于 AMI 的 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Migration","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"This is the canonical AWS VM Import/Export image-import workflow for migrating a VMware VM to EC2 while preserving the OS, installed software, and configuration. The documented steps are exactly: export the VM from the virtualization environment as an image (OVA/OVF/VMDK), upload/store it in an Amazon S3 bucket located in the destination Region, create the IAM service role named vmimport, then run the AWS CLI 'aws ec2 import-image' command, which produces an AMI you launch as an EC2 instance. Because VM Import/Export imports the complete disk image, all software and configuration settings carry over intact. Option B matches this process precisely (vSphere OVF export, S3 bucket in destination Region, IAM role for VM Import, AWS CLI import command).","explanation_zh":"這是 AWS VM Import/Export 影像匯入的標準流程，用於將 VMware VM 遷移到 EC2 並保留作業系統、已安裝軟體與組態設定。官方文件記載的步驟正是：從虛擬化環境將 VM 匯出為映像檔（OVA/OVF/VMDK），上傳並儲存到位於目的地 Region 的 Amazon S3 儲存貯體，建立名為 vmimport 的 IAM 服務角色，然後執行 AWS CLI 的 'aws ec2 import-image' 指令，產生可啟動為 EC2 執行個體的 AMI。由於 VM Import/Export 匯入的是完整磁碟映像，所有軟體與組態設定都會原封不動保留。選項 B 完全符合此流程（vSphere OVF 匯出、目的地 Region 的 S3 儲存貯體、VM Import 的 IAM 角色、AWS CLI 匯入指令）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"DataSync to FSx for Windows over SMB is a file/data transfer service, not a VM disk-image migration path. The notion of hosting a 'VMware data store' on the SMB share and then running VM Import/Export against it is conflated and not a supported workflow; VM Import/Export imports an OVA/OVF/VMDK image from S3, not from an FSx SMB share.","why_zh":"透過 SMB 將 DataSync 複製到 FSx for Windows 是檔案/資料傳輸服務，並非 VM 磁碟映像遷移方式。把『VMware data store』放在 SMB 共用再對其執行 VM Import/Export 的說法是混淆且不受支援；VM Import/Export 是從 S3 匯入 OVA/OVF/VMDK 映像，而非從 FSx SMB 共用匯入。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Storage Gateway File service (CIFS/SMB share) provides file storage backed by S3; you cannot create a bootable EC2 AMI by copying a 'backup' into a file-share folder. AMIs are created from EBS volumes/snapshots, not from arbitrary files in a Storage Gateway share, so this does not produce a working migrated VM.","why_zh":"Storage Gateway 檔案服務（CIFS/SMB 共用）提供以 S3 為後端的檔案儲存；無法藉由把『備份』複製到檔案共用資料夾來建立可開機的 EC2 AMI。AMI 是從 EBS 磁碟區/快照建立，而非從 Storage Gateway 共用中的任意檔案，因此無法產生可運作的遷移 VM。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but is technically invalid. SSM managed-instance activation lets you manage/patch on-premises servers as hybrid managed instances, but AWS Backup cannot take a snapshot of an arbitrary on-premises VM and turn it into a bootable EC2 AMI. There is no AWS Backup -> on-prem VM snapshot -> AMI path; this workflow is fabricated.","why_zh":"這是題庫建議答案，但技術上不成立。SSM 受管執行個體啟用可讓你將地端伺服器當作混合受管執行個體進行管理/修補，但 AWS Backup 無法對任意地端 VM 建立快照並轉換成可開機的 EC2 AMI。並不存在 AWS Backup -> 地端 VM 快照 -> AMI 的路徑，此流程是虛構的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vm-import/latest/userguide/import-vm-image.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vm-import/latest/userguide/image-import.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vm-import/latest/userguide/required-permissions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vm-import/latest/userguide/vmie_prereqs.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":63,"question_en":"A video processing company has an application that downloads images from an Amazon S3 bucket, processes the images, stores a transformed image in a second S3 bucket, and updates metadata about the image in an Amazon DynamoDB table. The application is written in Node.js and runs by using an AWS Lambda function. The Lambda function is invoked when a new image is uploaded to Amazon S3. The application ran without incident for a while. However, the size of the images has grown significantly. The Lambda function is now failing frequently with timeout errors. The function timeout is set to its maximum value. A solutions architect needs to refactor the application’s architecture to prevent invocation failures. The company does not want to manage the underlying infrastructure. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"视频处理公司有一个应用程序，该应用程序从 Amazon S3 存储桶下载图像、处理图像、将转换后的图像存储在第二个 S3 存储桶中， 并更新 Amazon DynamoDB 表中有关图像的元数据。该应用程序是用 Node.js 编写的，并使用 AWS Lambda 函数运行。当新图像上传 到 Amazon S3 时，将调用 Lambda 函数。 该应用程序运行了一段时间没有发生任何事件。然而，图像的大小显着增加。Lambda 函数现在经常因超时错误而失败。函数超时设 置为其最大值。解决方案架构师需要重构应用程序的架构以防止调用失败。该公司不想管理底层基础设施。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Modify the application deployment by building a Docker image that contains the application code. Publish the image to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR).","B":"Create a new Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) task definition with a compatibility type of AWS Fargate. Configure the task definition to use the new image in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). Adjust the Lambda function to invoke an ECS task by using the ECS task definition when a new file arrives in Amazon S3.","C":"Create an AWS Step Functions state machine with a Parallel state to invoke the Lambda function. Increase the provisioned concurrency of the Lambda function.","D":"Create a new Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) task definition with a compatibility type of Amazon EC2. Configure the task definition to use the new image in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). Adjust the Lambda function to invoke an ECS task by using the ECS task definition when a new file arrives in Amazon S3.","E":"Modify the application to store images on Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) and to store metadata on an Amazon RDS DB instance. Adjust the Lambda function to mount the EFS file share."},"options_zh":{"A":"通过构建包含应用程序代码的 Docker 映像来修改应用程序部署。将映像发布到 Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR)。","B":"使用 AWS Fargate 兼容性类型创建新的 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 任务定义。配置任务定义以使用 Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) 中的新映像。调整 Lambda 函数以在新文件到达 Amazon S3 时使用 ECS 任务定义调用 ECS 任务。","C":"创建具有并行状态的 AWS Step Functions 状态机以调用 Lambda 函数。增加 Lambda 函数的预置并发数。","D":"创建一个兼容类型为 Amazon EC2 的新 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 任务定义。配置任务定义以使用 Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) 中的新映像。调整 Lambda 函数以在新文件到达 Amazon S3 时使用 ECS 任务定义调用 ECS 任务。","E":"修改应用程序以将图像存储在 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 上并将元数据存储在 Amazon RDS 数据库实例上。调整 Lambda 函数以挂载 EFS 文件共享。"},"answer":["D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AB":89},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The root cause is the Lambda 15-minute hard execution limit; the function is already at max timeout and large images push processing past it. The constraint 'does not want to manage the underlying infrastructure' demands a serverless solution. The correct refactor is to containerize the Node.js app, push the image to Amazon ECR (A), then run it on AWS Fargate via an ECS task definition with the Fargate compatibility type and have the existing S3-triggered Lambda invoke an ECS RunTask when a new image arrives (B). Per the AWS Fargate-or-Lambda decision guide, Fargate is a serverless compute engine that automatically manages infrastructure, is ideal for long-running and batch processing, and has no hard execution-time limit, whereas Lambda is capped at 15 minutes. This pair removes the timeout without introducing servers to manage.","explanation_zh":"問題的根本原因是 AWS Lambda 的 15 分鐘硬性執行時間上限；函式逾時已設為最大值，而大型影像使處理超過該上限。「不想管理底層基礎設施」這個限制要求採用無伺服器解決方案。正確的重構方式是將 Node.js 應用程式容器化、把映像推送到 Amazon ECR（A），再透過相容類型為 AWS Fargate 的 ECS task definition 在 Fargate 上執行，並讓現有由 S3 觸發的 Lambda 在新影像到達時呼叫 ECS RunTask（B）。根據 AWS 的 Fargate-or-Lambda 決策指南，Fargate 是無伺服器運算引擎，會自動管理基礎設施，適合長時間執行與批次處理，且沒有硬性執行時間上限；而 Lambda 上限為 15 分鐘。此組合可在不引入需自行管理伺服器的前提下消除逾時問題。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"A Step Functions Parallel state plus provisioned concurrency increases parallelism and reduces cold starts, but it does not extend a single invocation's duration. Each Lambda processing one large image still hits the 15-minute hard limit, so timeouts persist.","why_zh":"Step Functions 的 Parallel 狀態加上 provisioned concurrency 只增加平行度並減少冷啟動，但無法延長單次調用的執行時間。每個處理單張大型影像的 Lambda 仍會撞上 15 分鐘硬上限，逾時問題依舊存在。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An ECS task definition with the EC2 compatibility type requires you to provision, patch, scale, and manage the underlying EC2 container instances. That directly violates the stated requirement that the company does not want to manage the underlying infrastructure; Fargate (option B) is the serverless choice.","why_zh":"相容類型為 EC2 的 ECS task definition 需要你自行佈建、修補、擴展與管理底層 EC2 容器執行個體，這直接違反「公司不想管理底層基礎設施」的需求。Fargate（選項 B）才是無伺服器的選擇。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Storing images on EFS and metadata on RDS while still running the logic in Lambda does not address the root cause: the workload still executes inside the Lambda function and remains bound by the 15-minute limit. It also needlessly replaces working DynamoDB with a provisioned RDS instance, adding cost and operational burden.","why_zh":"把影像存到 EFS、metadata 存到 RDS，但邏輯仍在 Lambda 中執行，並未解決根本原因：工作負載仍在 Lambda 函式內執行，依舊受 15 分鐘上限限制。而且還不必要地用佈建型 RDS 取代原本可正常運作的 DynamoDB，增加成本與運維負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/decision-guides/latest/fargate-or-lambda/fargate-or-lambda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-timeout.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/fargate-tasks-services.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/security-fargate-ec2.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・複選"},{"id":64,"question_en":"A company has an organization in AWS Organizations. The company is using AWS Control Tower to deploy a landing zone for the organization. The company wants to implement governance and policy enforcement. The company must implement a policy that will detect Amazon RDS DB instances that are not encrypted at rest in the company’s production OU. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Organizations 中拥有一个组织。该公司正在使用 AWS Control Tower 为组织部署登陆区。该公司希望实施治理和政策 执行。公司必须实施一项策略来检测公司生产 OU 中未静态加密的 Amazon RDS 数据库实例。 哪种解决方案可以满足这个要求？","options_en":{"A":"Turn on mandatory guardrails in AWS Control Tower. Apply the mandatory guardrails to the production OU.","B":"Enable the appropriate guardrail from the list of strongly recommended guardrails in AWS Control Tower. Apply the guardrail to the production OU.","C":"Use AWS Config to create a new mandatory guardrail. Apply the rule to all accounts in the production OU.","D":"Create a custom SCP in AWS Control Tower. Apply the SCP to the production OU."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS Control Tower 中打开强制护栏。将强制护栏应用于生产 OU。","B":"从 AWS Control Tower 中强烈推荐的护栏列表中启用适当的护栏。将护栏应用到生产 OU。","C":"使用 AWS Config 创建新的强制护栏。将规则应用于生产 OU 中的所有帐户。","D":"在 AWS Control Tower 中创建自定义 SCP。将 SCP 应用到生产 OU。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":93},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Database"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":65,"question_en":"A startup company hosts a ­eet of Amazon EC2 instances in private subnets using the latest Amazon Linux 2 AMI. The company’s engineers rely heavily on SSH access to the instances for troubleshooting. The company’s existing architecture includes the following: • A VPC with private and public subnets, and a NAT gateway. • Site-to-Site VPN for connectivity with the on-premises environment. • EC2 security groups with direct SSH access from the on-premises environment. The company needs to increase security controls around SSH access and provide auditing of commands run by the engineers. Which strategy should a solutions architect use?","question_zh":"一家初创公司使用最新的 Amazon Linux 2 AMI 在私有子网中托管一组 Amazon EC2 实例。该公司的工程师严重依赖对实例的 SSH 访问 来进行故障排除。 该公司的现有架构包括以下内容： • 具有私有和公有子网以及NAT 网关的VPC。 • 用于与本地环境连接的站点到站点VPN。 • 可从本地环境直接进行SSH 访问的EC2 安全组。 该公司需要加强对 SSH 访问的安全控制，并对工程师运行的命令进行审核。 解决方案架构师应该使用哪种策略？","options_en":{"A":"Install and configure EC2 Instance Connect on the ­eet of EC2 instances. Remove all security group rules attached to EC2 instances that allow inbound TCP on port 22. Advise the engineers to remotely access the instances by using the EC2 Instance Connect CLI.","B":"Update the EC2 security groups to only allow inbound TCP on port 22 to the IP addresses of the engineer’s devices. Install the Amazon CloudWatch agent on all EC2 instances and send operating system audit logs to CloudWatch Logs.","C":"Update the EC2 security groups to only allow inbound TCP on port 22 to the IP addresses of the engineer’s devices. Enable AWS Config for EC2 security group resource changes. Enable AWS Firewall Manager and apply a security group policy that automatically remediates changes to rules.","D":"Create an IAM role with the AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore managed policy attached. Attach the IAM role to all the EC2 instances. Remove all security group rules attached to the EC2 instances that allow inbound TCP on port 22. Have the engineers install the AWS Systems Manager Session Manager plugin for their devices and remotely access the instances by using the start-session API call from Systems Manager."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 EC2 实例队列上安装并配置 EC2 Instance Connect。删除附加到 EC2 实例的所有允许端口 22 上的入站 TCP 的安全组规则。建 议工程师使用 EC2 Instance Connect CLI 远程访问实例。","B":"更新 EC2 安全组以仅允许端口 22 上的入站 TCP 到工程师设备的 IP 地址。在所有 EC2 实例上安装 Amazon CloudWatch 代理并将 操作系统审核日志发送到 CloudWatch Logs。","C":"更新 EC2 安全组以仅允许端口 22 上的入站 TCP 到工程师设备的 IP 地址。为 EC2 安全组资源更改启用 AWS Config。启用 AWS Firewall Manager 并应用自动修复规则更改的安全组策略。","D":"创建附加了 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 托管策略的 IAM 角色。将 IAM 角色附加到所有 EC2 实例。删除附加到 EC2 实例的 所有允许端口 22 上的入站 TCP 的安全组规则。让工程师为其设备安装 AWS Systems Manager 会话管理器插件，并使用 Systems Manager 中的启动会话 API 调用远程访问实例。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":91},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":66,"question_en":"A company that uses AWS Organizations allows developers to experiment on AWS. As part of the landing zone that the company has deployed, developers use their company email address to request an account. The company wants to ensure that developers are not launching costly services or running services unnecessarily. The company must give developers a fixed monthly budget to limit their AWS costs. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"使用 AWS Organizations 的公司允许开发人员在 AWS 上进行实验。作为公司部署的登陆区的一部分，开发人员使用他们的公司电子邮 件地址来请求帐户。该公司希望确保开发人员不会推出昂贵的服务或运行不必要的服务。公司必须为开发人员提供固定的每月预 算，以限制他们的 AWS 成本。 哪种步骤组合可以满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an SCP to set a fixed monthly account usage limit. Apply the SCP to the developer accounts.","B":"Use AWS Budgets to create a fixed monthly budget for each developer’s account as part of the account creation process.","C":"Create an SCP to deny access to costly services and components. Apply the SCP to the developer accounts.","D":"Create an IAM policy to deny access to costly services and components. Apply the IAM policy to the developer accounts.","E":"Create an AWS Budgets alert action to terminate services when the budgeted amount is reached. Configure the action to terminate all services.","F":"Create an AWS Budgets alert action to send an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) notification when the budgeted amount is reached. Invoke an AWS Lambda function to terminate all services."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 SCP 以设置固定的每月帐户使用限制。将 SCP 应用到开发者帐户。","B":"作为帐户创建过程的一部分，使用 AWS Budgets 为每个开发人员的帐户创建固定的每月预算。","C":"创建 SCP 以拒绝访问昂贵的服务和组件。将 SCP 应用到开发者帐户。","D":"创建 IAM 策略以拒绝访问昂贵的服务和组件。将 IAM 策略应用到开发者账户。","E":"创建 AWS 预算警报操作，以在达到预算金额时终止服务。配置终止所有服务的操作。","F":"创建 AWS 预算警报操作，以在达到预算金额时发送 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 通知。调用 AWS Lambda 函 数来终止所有服务。"},"answer":["B","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BCF":80,"BDF":19},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The scenario is an AWS Organizations landing zone where each developer gets a separate account. Three requirements must be met: prevent launching costly services, enforce a fixed monthly budget, and act when the budget is reached. (B) AWS Budgets lets you create a fixed monthly cost budget per account during account creation, directly satisfying the budget requirement. (C) A service control policy (SCP) is the correct Organizations-level guardrail to deny access to costly services; it sets a maximum-permission boundary on every IAM principal in the member account and cannot be removed by the developer from within their own account. (F) AWS Budgets natively supports only three action types (apply an IAM policy, attach an SCP, or stop specific EC2/RDS instances); to actually terminate arbitrary services you send an SNS notification at the threshold and invoke a Lambda function to perform the teardown. The dump's BDF is wrong because (D) an IAM deny policy is per-identity inside an account and can be altered by the account holder, whereas an SCP enforced from the management account is the robust centralized control for an Organizations landing zone.","explanation_zh":"情境是一個 AWS Organizations landing zone，每位開發者各自擁有獨立帳戶。需滿足三項需求：防止啟動昂貴服務、強制每月固定預算、以及達到預算時採取行動。(B) AWS Budgets 可在建立帳戶流程中為每個帳戶建立固定的每月成本預算，直接滿足預算需求。(C) service control policy (SCP) 是在 Organizations 層級拒絕昂貴服務存取的正確護欄；它對成員帳戶中所有 IAM 主體設定最大權限邊界，且開發者無法在自己帳戶內移除它。(F) AWS Budgets 原生只支援三種 action（套用 IAM policy、附加 SCP、或停止特定 EC2/RDS 執行個體）；若要真正終止任意服務，需在門檻時發送 SNS 通知並觸發 Lambda function 執行清除。Dump 的 BDF 錯誤，因為 (D) IAM deny policy 是帳戶內針對 identity 的，帳戶持有者可自行修改，而從管理帳戶強制套用的 SCP 才是 Organizations landing zone 穩固的集中式控制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SCPs only allow or deny API actions; they cannot define a dollar or usage spend limit, so an SCP cannot set a fixed monthly account usage limit.","why_zh":"SCP 只能允許或拒絕 API 動作，無法定義金額或用量花費上限，因此 SCP 無法設定固定的每月帳戶用量限制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An IAM deny policy is scoped to identities within a single account and can be modified or removed by the developer who controls that account; the centralized, tamper-resistant control across Organizations member accounts is an SCP (option C), making D inferior.","why_zh":"IAM deny policy 的範圍僅限單一帳戶內的 identity，且掌控該帳戶的開發者可修改或移除；跨 Organizations 成員帳戶且不易被竄改的集中式控制是 SCP（選項 C），故 D 較差。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"AWS Budgets has no 'terminate all services' action. The only supported budget action types are applying an IAM policy, attaching an SCP, or stopping specific EC2/RDS instances, so configuring an action to terminate all services is not possible.","why_zh":"AWS Budgets 並無『終止所有服務』的 action。唯一支援的 budget action 類型是套用 IAM policy、附加 SCP，或停止特定 EC2/RDS 執行個體，因此設定終止所有服務的 action 並不可行。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-action-configure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-managing-costs.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・複選"},{"id":67,"question_en":"A company has applications in an AWS account that is named Source. The account is in an organization in AWS Organizations. One of the applications uses AWS Lambda functions and stores inventory data in an Amazon Aurora database. The application deploys the Lambda functions by using a deployment package. The company has configured automated backups for Aurora. The company wants to migrate the Lambda functions and the Aurora database to a new AWS account that is named Target. The application processes critical data, so the company must minimize downtime. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在名为 Source 的 AWS 账户中拥有应用程序。该账户位于 AWS Organizations 中的组织中。其中一个应用程序使用 AWS Lambda 函数并将库存数据存储在 Amazon Aurora 数据库中。应用程序使用部署包部署 Lambda 函数。该公司为 Aurora 配置了自动备 份。 该公司希望将 Lambda 函数和 Aurora 数据库迁移到名为 Target 的新 AWS 账户。该应用程序处理关键数据，因此公司必须最大限度地 减少停机时间。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Download the Lambda function deployment package from the Source account. Use the deployment package and create new Lambda functions in the Target account. Share the automated Aurora DB cluster snapshot with the Target account.","B":"Download the Lambda function deployment package from the Source account. Use the deployment package and create new Lambda functions in the Target account. Share the Aurora DB cluster with the Target account by using AWS Resource Access Manager {AWS RAM). Grant the Target account permission to clone the Aurora DB cluster.","C":"Use AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) to share the Lambda functions and the Aurora DB cluster with the Target account. Grant the Target account permission to clone the Aurora DB cluster.","D":"Use AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) to share the Lambda functions with the Target account. Share the automated Aurora DB cluster snapshot with the Target account."},"options_zh":{"A":"从​源账户下载 Lambda 函数部署包。使用部署包并在目标账户中创建新的 Lambda 函数。与目标账户共享自动 Aurora 数据库集 群快照。","B":"从源账户下载 Lambda 函数部署包。使用部署包并在目标账户中创建新的 Lambda 函数。使用 AWS Resource Access Manager {AWS RAM) 与目标账户共享 Aurora 数据库集群。授予目标帐户克隆 Aurora 数据库集群的权限。","C":"使用 AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) 与目标账户共享 Lambda 函数和 Aurora 数据库集群。授予目标帐户克隆 Aurora 数据库集群的权限。","D":"使用 AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) 与目标账户共享 Lambda 函数。与目标账户共享自动 Aurora 数据库集群快照。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":97},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Migration","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Two facts decide this question. First, AWS Lambda is NOT a resource type that AWS RAM can share; the RAM 'Shareable AWS resources' page lists every shareable type and Lambda is absent (Lambda only supports cross-account invocation via resource-based policies, not sharing the function itself). This eliminates options C and D, both of which try to share Lambda functions with RAM. The only valid way to move the functions to the Target account is to download the deployment package and recreate them, which both A and B do. Second, for the database the requirement is to minimize downtime. Amazon Aurora DB clusters (rds:Cluster) ARE shareable via AWS RAM, with the documented use case of letting another account clone the shared cluster, and AWS states cross-account cloning is 'much faster than creating and restoring a database snapshot.' Option B uses RAM to share the Aurora DB cluster and grants the Target account permission to clone it, which minimizes downtime. Option A instead shares an automated snapshot and restores from it, which is slower (more downtime) and is also problematic because automated snapshots cannot be shared directly with another account (they must first be copied to a manual snapshot). Therefore B is correct. The dump's suggested answer C is technically impossible.","explanation_zh":"兩個事實決定了本題。第一，AWS Lambda 不是 AWS RAM 可分享的資源類型；RAM 的「Shareable AWS resources」頁面列出所有可分享類型，當中沒有 Lambda（Lambda 只能透過 resource-based policy 進行跨帳號 invoke，無法分享 function 本身）。這直接排除了試圖用 RAM 分享 Lambda 的選項 C 與 D。將 function 移到 Target 帳號的唯一可行方法是下載 deployment package 並重新建立，A 與 B 都這樣做。第二，資料庫方面要求最小化停機時間。Amazon Aurora DB cluster（rds:Cluster）可透過 AWS RAM 分享，官方用例正是讓另一帳號 clone 共享的 cluster，且 AWS 說明跨帳號 cloning「比建立並還原 snapshot 快得多」。選項 B 用 RAM 分享 Aurora DB cluster 並授權 Target 帳號 clone，能最小化停機時間。選項 A 改為分享 automated snapshot 並還原，速度較慢（停機較久），且 automated snapshot 無法直接分享給其他帳號（必須先複製成 manual snapshot）。因此 B 正確。Dump 建議答案 C 在技術上不可能。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Lambda recreation from the deployment package is fine, but sharing the automated Aurora snapshot and restoring from it does not minimize downtime (restore is slower than a clone), and automated snapshots cannot be shared directly with another account without first copying them to a manual snapshot.","why_zh":"用 deployment package 重建 Lambda 沒問題，但分享 automated Aurora snapshot 並還原無法最小化停機（還原比 clone 慢），且 automated snapshot 無法直接分享給其他帳號，必須先複製成 manual snapshot。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS RAM cannot share Lambda functions; Lambda is not in the RAM list of shareable resource types. This makes the option technically impossible despite being the dump's suggested answer.","why_zh":"AWS RAM 無法分享 Lambda function；Lambda 不在 RAM 可分享資源類型清單中。雖是 dump 建議答案，但技術上不可能。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same fatal flaw as C: Lambda is not shareable via AWS RAM. Additionally it shares an automated snapshot, which cannot be shared directly and is slower to restore.","why_zh":"與 C 相同致命缺陷：Lambda 無法透過 AWS RAM 分享。此外它分享 automated snapshot，無法直接分享且還原較慢。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ram/latest/userguide/shareable.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Managing.Clone.Cross-Account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Managing.Clone.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/access-control-resource-based.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/USER_CopyDBClusterSnapshot.CrossAccount.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":68,"question_en":"A company runs a Python script on an Amazon EC2 instance to process data. The script runs every 10 minutes. The script ingests files from an Amazon S3 bucket and processes the files. On average, the script takes approximately 5 minutes to process each file The script will not reprocess a file that the script has already processed. The company reviewed Amazon CloudWatch metrics and noticed that the EC2 instance is idle for approximately 40% of the time because of the file processing speed. The company wants to make the workload highly available and scalable. The company also wants to reduce long- term management overhead. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司在 Amazon EC2 实例上运行 Python 脚本来处理数据。该脚本每 10 分钟运行一次。该脚本从 Amazon S3 存储桶提取文件并处 理这些文件。平均而言，该脚本大约需要 5 分钟来处理每个文件。该脚本不会重新处理该脚本已经处理过的文件。 该公司查看了 Amazon CloudWatch 指标并注意到，由于文件处理速度的原因，EC2 实例大约有 40% 的时间处于空闲状态。该公司希 望使工作负载具有高可用性和可扩展性。该公司还希望减少长期管理费用。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate the data processing script to an AWS Lambda function. Use an S3 event notification to invoke the Lambda function to process the objects when the company uploads the objects.","B":"Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Configure Amazon S3 to send event notifications to the SQS queue. Create an EC2 Auto Scaling group with a minimum size of one instance. Update the data processing script to poll the SQS queue. Process the S3 objects that the SQS message identifies.","C":"Migrate the data processing script to a container image. Run the data processing container on an EC2 instance. Configure the container to poll the S3 bucket for new objects and to process the resulting objects.","D":"Migrate the data processing script to a container image that runs on Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) on AWS Fargate. Create an AWS Lambda function that calls the Fargate RunTaskAPI operation when the container processes the file. Use an S3 event notification to invoke the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"将数据处理脚本迁移到 AWS Lambda 函数。公司上传对象时，使用S3事件通知调用Lambda函数处理对象。","B":"创建 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列。配置 Amazon S3 以将事件通知发送到 SQS 队列。创建一个最小大小为 1 个实例的 EC2 Auto Scaling 组。更新数据处理脚本以轮询 SQS 队列。处理SQS消息标识的S3对象。","C":"将数据处理脚本迁移到容器镜像中。在 EC2 实例上运行数据处理容器。配置容器以轮询 S3 存储桶以查找新对象并处理生成的 对象。","D":"将数据处理脚本迁移到在 AWS Fargate 上的 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 上运行的容器映像。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数在容器处理文件时调用 Fargate RunTaskAPI 操作。使用 S3 事件通知调用 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":68,"D":32},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The workload is intermittent, event-driven file processing where each file takes about 5 minutes to process, well within AWS Lambda's 900-second (15-minute) maximum timeout. Option A migrates the script to Lambda and uses an S3 event notification to invoke the function on object upload. This is fully serverless: Lambda auto-scales and is inherently highly available across AZs, you pay only for actual execution time (eliminating the ~40% EC2 idle cost), and there are no servers to patch or manage, giving the lowest long-term operational overhead. Because the original script does not reprocess files and S3 fires one event per new object, the event-driven invocation naturally maps one file to one Lambda execution. Option D (ECS on Fargate triggered by a Lambda that calls RunTask) is over-engineered and more expensive for a 5-minute job that fits within Lambda limits, adding a second compute layer and Fargate task startup latency/cost for no benefit, so A is the most cost-effective choice.","explanation_zh":"此工作負載屬於間歇性、事件驅動的檔案處理，每個檔案約需 5 分鐘處理，遠在 AWS Lambda 的 900 秒（15 分鐘）最大逾時限制之內。選項 A 將腳本遷移到 Lambda，並使用 S3 event notification 在物件上傳時觸發函式。這是完全的 serverless 架構：Lambda 會自動擴展且天生跨可用區高可用，只需為實際執行時間付費（消除約 40% 的 EC2 閒置成本），且無需修補或管理伺服器，長期營運負擔最低。由於原腳本不會重複處理檔案，而 S3 對每個新物件觸發一個事件，事件驅動的呼叫自然將一個檔案對應到一次 Lambda 執行。選項 D（由呼叫 RunTask 的 Lambda 觸發 ECS on Fargate）對於可在 Lambda 限制內完成的 5 分鐘任務而言過度設計且更昂貴，額外增加第二層運算與 Fargate 任務啟動延遲與成本卻無實質好處，因此 A 是最具成本效益的選擇。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Creating an EC2 Auto Scaling group with a minimum size of one instance keeps an always-on EC2 instance running, so the ~40% idle cost is not eliminated and you must still patch and manage instances. It is more costly and higher overhead than serverless Lambda.","why_zh":"建立最小數量為一台的 EC2 Auto Scaling group 會持續運行一台常駐 EC2 執行個體，因此約 40% 的閒置成本並未消除，且仍須修補與管理執行個體。相較於 serverless 的 Lambda，成本更高、負擔更重。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Running the container on a single EC2 instance that polls S3 is not highly available and does not scale, and you still manage the EC2 instance. It fails the high-availability, scalability, and low-management requirements.","why_zh":"在單一 EC2 執行個體上運行容器並輪詢 S3 既不具高可用性也無法擴展，且仍需管理 EC2 執行個體，無法滿足高可用、可擴展與低管理的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"ECS on Fargate invoked by a Lambda that calls RunTask works but is over-engineered for a 5-minute job that fits within Lambda's 15-minute limit. It adds a second compute layer plus Fargate task launch latency and per-task billing, making it more complex and more expensive than directly invoking Lambda, so it is not the MOST cost-effective option.","why_zh":"由呼叫 RunTask 的 Lambda 觸發 ECS on Fargate 雖可行，但對於可在 Lambda 15 分鐘限制內完成的 5 分鐘任務而言過度設計。它額外增加第二層運算以及 Fargate 任務啟動延遲與按任務計費，比直接呼叫 Lambda 更複雜且更昂貴，因此並非最具成本效益的選項。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-timeout.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/concepts-event-driven-architectures.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":69,"question_en":"A financial services company in North America plans to release a new online web application to its customers on AWS. The company will launch the application in the us-east-1 Region on Amazon EC2 instances. The application must be highly available and must dynamically scale to meet user tra®c. The company also wants to implement a disaster recovery environment for the application in the us-west-1 Region by using active-passive failover. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"北美的一家金融服务公司计划在 AWS 上向其客户发布新的在线 Web 应用程序。该公司将在 us-east-1 区域的 Amazon EC2 实例上启动 该应用程序。应用程序必须具有高可用性，并且必须动态扩展以满足用户流量。该公司还希望通过使用主动-被动故障转移为 us- west-1 区域中的应用程序实施灾难恢复环境。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a VPC in us-east-1 and a VPC in us-west-1. Configure VPC peering. In the us-east-1 VPC, create an Application Load Balancer (ALB) that extends across multiple Availability Zones in both VPCs. Create an Auto Scaling group that deploys the EC2 instances across the multiple Availability Zones in both VPCs. Place the Auto Scaling group behind the ALB.","B":"Create a VPC in us-east-1 and a VPC in us-west-1. In the us-east-1 VPC, create an Application Load Balancer (ALB) that extends across multiple Availability Zones in that VPC. Create an Auto Scaling group that deploys the EC2 instances across the multiple Availability Zones in the us-east-1 VPC. Place the Auto Scaling group behind the ALSet up the same configuration in the us-west-1 VPC. Create an Amazon Route 53 hosted zone. Create separate records for each ALEnable health checks to ensure high availability between Regions.","C":"Create a VPC in us-east-1 and a VPC in us-west-1. In the us-east-1 VPC, create an Application Load Balancer (ALB) that extends across multiple Availability Zones in that VPCreate an Auto Scaling group that deploys the EC2 instances across the multiple Availability Zones in the us-east-1 VPPlace the Auto Scaling group behind the ALB. Set up the same configuration in the us-west-1 VPCreate an Amazon Route 53 hosted zone. Create separate records for each ALB. Enable health checks and configure a failover routing policy for each record.","D":"Create a VPC in us-east-1 and a VPC in us-west-1. Configure VPC peering. In the us-east-1 VPC, create an Application Load Balancer (ALB) that extends across multiple Availability Zones in both VPCs. Create an Auto Scaling group that deploys the EC2 instances across the multiple Availability Zones in both VPCs. Place the Auto Scaling group behind the ALB. Create an Amazon Route 53 hosted zone. Create a record for the ALB."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 us-east-1 中创建一个 VPC，在 us-west-1 中创建一个 VPC。配置 VPC 对等互连。在 us-east-1 VPC 中，创建一个跨两个 VPC 中 的多个可用区扩展的应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB)。创建一个 Auto Scaling 组，用于跨两个 VPC 中的多个可用区部署 EC2 实例。将 Auto Scaling 组放置在 ALB 后面。","B":"在 us-east-1 中创建一个 VPC，在 us-west-1 中创建一个 VPC。在 us-east-1 VPC 中，创建一个跨该 VPC 中的多个可用区扩展的应 用程序负载均衡器 (ALB)。创建一个 Auto Scaling 组，用于跨 us-east-1 VPC 中的多个可用区部署 EC2 实例。将 Auto Scaling 组放在 AL 后面，在 us-west-1 VPC 中设置相同的配置。创建 Amazon Route 53 托管区域。为每个 ALEnable 运行状况检查创建单独的记 录，以确保区域之间的高可用性。","C":"在 us-east-1 中创建一个 VPC，在 us-west-1 中创建一个 VPC。在 us-east-1 VPC 中，创建一个跨该 VP 中多个可用区扩展的应用 程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 创建一个 Auto Scaling 组，跨 us-east-1 VPC 中的多个可用区部署 EC2 实例。 ALB 后面的扩展组。在 us- west-1 VP 中设置相同的配置创建 Amazon Route 53 托管区域。为每个 ALB 创建单独的记录。启用健康检查并为每个记录配置故 障转移路由策略。","D":"在 us-east-1 中创建一个 VPC，在 us-west-1 中创建一个 VPC。配置 VPC 对等互连。在 us-east-1 VPC 中，创建一个跨两个 VPC 中 的多个可用区扩展的应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB)。创建一个 Auto Scaling 组，用于跨两个 VPC 中的多个可用区部署 EC2 实例。将 Auto Scaling 组放置在 ALB 后面。创建 Amazon Route 53 托管区域。为 ALB 创建记录。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":70,"question_en":"A company has an environment that has a single AWS account. A solutions architect is reviewing the environment to recommend what the company could improve specifically in terms of access to the AWS Management Console. The company’s IT support workers currently access the console for administrative tasks, authenticating with named IAM users that have been mapped to their job role. The IT support workers no longer want to maintain both their Active Directory and IAM user accounts. They want to be able to access the console by using their existing Active Directory credentials. The solutions architect is using AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) to implement this functionality. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司的环境只有一个 AWS 账户。解决方案架构师正在审查环境，以建议公司在访问 AWS 管理控制台方面可以具体改进哪些方 面。该公司的 IT 支持人员目前访问控制台执行管理任务，通过已映射到其工作角色的指定 IAM 用户进行身份验证。 IT 支持人员不再希望同时维护其 Active Directory 和 IAM 用户帐户。他们希望能够使用现有的 Active Directory 凭据访问控制台。解决 方案架构师正在使用 AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) 来实现此功能。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an organization in AWS Organizations. Turn on the IAM Identity Center feature in Organizations. Create and configure a directory in AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory (AWS Managed Microsoft AD) with a two-way trust to the company’s on-premises Active Directory. Configure IAM Identity Center and set the AWS Managed Microsoft AD directory as the identity source. Create permission sets and map them to the existing groups within the AWS Managed Microsoft AD directory.","B":"Create an organization in AWS Organizations. Turn on the IAM Identity Center feature in Organizations. Create and configure an AD Connector to connect to the company’s on-premises Active Directory. Configure IAM Identity Center and select the AD Connector as the identity source. Create permission sets and map them to the existing groups within the company’s Active Directory.","C":"Create an organization in AWS Organizations. Turn on all features for the organization. Create and configure a directory in AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory (AWS Managed Microsoft AD) with a two-way trust to the company’s on-premises Active Directory. Configure IAM Identity Center and select the AWS Managed Microsoft AD directory as the identity source. Create permission sets and map them to the existing groups within the AWS Managed Microsoft AD directory.","D":"Create an organization in AWS Organizations. Turn on all features for the organization. Create and configure an AD Connector to connect to the company’s on-premises Active Directory. Configure IAM Identity Center and set the AD Connector as the identity source. Create permission sets and map them to the existing groups within the company’s Active Directory."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS Organizations 中创建一个组织。在组织中打开 IAM 身份中心功能。在 AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory (AWS Managed Microsoft AD) 中创建和配置目录，并与公司的本地 Active Directory 建立双向信任。配置 IAM Identity Center 并将 AWS Managed Microsoft AD 目录设置为身份源。创建权限集并将其映射到 AWS Managed Microsoft AD 目录中的现有组。","B":"在 AWS Organizations 中创建组织。在组织中打开 IAM 身份中心功能。创建并配置 AD 连接器以连接到公司的本地 Active Directory。配置 IAM Identity Center 并选择 AD Connector 作为身份源。创建权限集并将其映射到公司 Active Directory 中的现有组。","C":"在 AWS Organizations 中创建组织。打开组织的所有功能。在 AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory (AWS Managed Microsoft AD) 中创建和配置目录，并与公司的本地 Active Directory 建立双向信任。配置 IAM Identity Center 并选择 AWS Managed Microsoft AD 目录作为身份源。创建权限集并将其映射到 AWS Managed Microsoft AD 目录中的现有组。","D":"在 AWS Organizations 中创建组织。打开组织的所有功能。创建并配置 AD 连接器以连接到公司的本地 Active Directory。配置 IAM Identity Center 并将 AD Connector 设置为身份源。创建权限集并将其映射到公司 Active Directory 中的现有组。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":82},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":71,"question_en":"A video streaming company recently launched a mobile app for video sharing. The app uploads various files to an Amazon S3 bucket in the us- east-1 Region. The files range in size from 1 GB to 10 GB. Users who access the app from Australia have experienced uploads that take long periods of time. Sometimes the files fail to completely upload for these users. A solutions architect must improve the app’s performance for these uploads. Which solutions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家视频流媒体公司最近推出了一款用于视频共享的移动应用程序。该应用程序将各种文件上传到 us-east-1 区域中的 Amazon S3 存 储桶。文件大小范围从 1 GB 到 10 GB。 从澳大利亚访问该应用程序的用户都经历过上传需要很长时间的情况。有时这些用户的文件无法完全上传。解决方案架构师必须提 高应用程序的这些上传性能。 哪些解决方案可以满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Enable S3 Transfer Acceleration on the S3 bucket. Configure the app to use the Transfer Acceleration endpoint for uploads.","B":"Configure an S3 bucket in each Region to receive the uploads. Use S3 Cross-Region Replication to copy the files to the distribution S3 bucket.","C":"Set up Amazon Route 53 with latency-based routing to route the uploads to the nearest S3 bucket Region.","D":"Configure the app to break the video files into chunks. Use a multipart upload to transfer files to Amazon S3.","E":"Modify the app to add random prefixes to the files before uploading."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 S3 存储桶上启用 S3 传输加速。配置应用程序以使用传输加速端点进行上传。","B":"在每个区域中配置一个 S3 存储桶来接收上传。使用 S3 跨区域复制将文件复制到分发 S3 存储桶。","C":"使用基于延迟的路由设置 Amazon Route 53，以将上传内容路由到最近的 S3 存储桶区域。","D":"配置应用程序以将视频文件分成块。使用分段上传将文件传输到 Amazon S3。","E":"修改应用程序以在上传之前向文件添加随机前缀。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AD":97},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":72,"question_en":"An application is using an Amazon RDS for MySQL Multi-AZ DB instance in the us-east-1 Region. After a failover test, the application lost the connections to the database and could not re-establish the connections. After a restart of the application, the application re-established the connections. A solutions architect must implement a solution so that the application can re-establish connections to the database without requiring a restart. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"应用程序正在 us-east-1 区域中使用 Amazon RDS for MySQL 多可用区数据库实例。故障转移测试后，应用程序丢失了与数据库的连 接，并且无法重新建立连接。重新启动应用程序后，应用程序重新建立连接。 解决方案架构师必须实现一个解决方案，以便应用程序可以重新建立与数据库的连接，而无需重新启动。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Aurora MySQL Serverless v1 DB instance. Migrate the RDS DB instance to the Aurora Serverless v1 DB instance. Update the connection settings in the application to point to the Aurora reader endpoint.","B":"Create an RDS proxy. Configure the existing RDS endpoint as a target. Update the connection settings in the application to point to the RDS proxy endpoint.","C":"Create a two-node Amazon Aurora MySQL DB cluster. Migrate the RDS DB instance to the Aurora DB cluster. Create an RDS proxy. Configure the existing RDS endpoint as a target. Update the connection settings in the application to point to the RDS proxy endpoint.","D":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket. Export the database to Amazon S3 by using AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS). Configure Amazon Athena to use the S3 bucket as a data store. Install the latest Open Database Connectivity (ODBC) driver for the application. Update the connection settings in the application to point to the Athena endpoint"},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 Amazon Aurora MySQL Serverless v1 数据库实例。将 RDS 数据库实例迁移到 Aurora Serverless v1 数据库实例。更新应用程 序中的连接设置以指向 Aurora 读取器端点。","B":"创建 RDS 代理。将现有 RDS 端点配置为目标。更新应用程序中的连接设置以指向 RDS 代理终端节点。","C":"创建一个两节点 Amazon Aurora MySQL 数据库集群。将 RDS 数据库实例迁移到 Aurora 数据库集群。创建 RDS 代理。将现有 RDS 端点配置为目标。更新应用程序中的连接设置以指向 RDS 代理终端节点。","D":"创建 Amazon S3 存储桶。使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 将数据库导出到 Amazon S3。配置 Amazon Athena 以 使用 S3 存储桶作为数据存储。为应用程序安装最新的开放数据库连接 (ODBC) 驱动程序。更新应用程序中的连接设置以指向 Athena 端点"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage","Database","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":73,"question_en":"A company is building a solution in the AWS Cloud. Thousands or devices will connect to the solution and send data. Each device needs to be able to send and receive data in real time over the MQTT protocol. Each device must authenticate by using a unique X.509 certificate. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 云中构建解决方案。数千台设备将连接到该解决方案并发送数据。每个设备都需要能够通过 MQTT 协议实时发送 和接收数据。每个设备必须使用唯一的 X.509 证书进行身份验证。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up AWS IoT Core. For each device, create a corresponding Amazon MQ queue and provision a certificate. Connect each device to Amazon MQ.","B":"Create a Network Load Balancer (NLB) and configure it with an AWS Lambda authorizer. Run an MQTT broker on Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group. Set the Auto Scaling group as the target for the NLConnect each device to the NLB.","C":"Set up AWS IoT Core. For each device, create a corresponding AWS IoT thing and provision a certificate. Connect each device to AWS IoT Core.","D":"Set up an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API and a Network Load Balancer (NLB). Create integration between API Gateway and the NLB. Configure a mutual TLS certificate authorizer on the HTTP API. Run an MQTT broker on an Amazon EC2 instance that the NLB targets. Connect each device to the NLB."},"options_zh":{"A":"设置 AWS IoT Core。对于每个设备，创建相应的 Amazon MQ 队列并预置证书。将每个设备连接到 Amazon MQ。","B":"创建网络负载均衡器 (NLB) 并使用 AWS Lambda 授权方对其进行配置。在 Auto Scaling 组中的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行 MQTT 代 理。将 Auto Scaling 组设置为 NLConnect 每个设备到 NLB 的目标。","C":"设置 AWS IoT Core。对于每个设备，创建相应的 AWS IoT 事物并预置证书。将每个设备连接到 AWS IoT Core。","D":"设置 Amazon API Gateway HTTP API 和网络负载均衡器 (NLB)。在 API Gateway 和 NLB 之间创建集成。在 HTTP API 上配置相互 TLS 证书授权者。在 NLB 定位的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行 MQTT 代理。将每个设备连接到 NLB。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":97},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"AWS IoT Core is a fully managed service purpose-built for this exact scenario. It natively supports the MQTT protocol for real-time bidirectional publish/subscribe messaging, scales to millions of devices, and uses X.509 client certificate (mutual TLS) authentication where each device is registered as an AWS IoT thing with its own unique certificate attached. This eliminates the need to provision, patch, scale, or operate any broker infrastructure, giving the LEAST operational overhead. Option C maps directly to the canonical AWS IoT Core device-onboarding model (thing + certificate + policy).","explanation_zh":"AWS IoT Core 是專為此情境打造的全託管服務。它原生支援 MQTT 協定進行即時雙向的發布/訂閱訊息傳遞，可擴展至數百萬台裝置，並使用 X.509 用戶端憑證 (mutual TLS) 進行驗證，每台裝置都註冊為一個 AWS IoT thing 並附加其專屬憑證。這免去了佈建、修補、擴展或維運任何 broker 基礎設施的需求，因此營運負擔最低。選項 C 完全對應 AWS IoT Core 標準的裝置上線模型 (thing + certificate + policy)。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon MQ is a managed message broker (ActiveMQ/RabbitMQ) but it is not how AWS IoT Core devices connect, and provisioning a dedicated MQ queue per device for thousands of devices is unnecessary, costly, and high overhead. IoT Core itself is the broker; layering Amazon MQ on top is redundant and not the intended design.","why_zh":"Amazon MQ 是託管訊息 broker (ActiveMQ/RabbitMQ)，但並非 AWS IoT Core 裝置的連線方式，且為數千台裝置各自佈建專屬 MQ queue 既不必要、成本高又營運負擔大。IoT Core 本身就是 broker，再疊加 Amazon MQ 是多餘且非預期設計。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Running a self-managed MQTT broker on EC2 in an Auto Scaling group behind an NLB requires you to install, patch, scale, monitor, and operate the broker and the certificate/auth logic yourself via a Lambda authorizer. This is the opposite of least operational overhead compared to the fully managed IoT Core.","why_zh":"在 NLB 後方的 Auto Scaling group EC2 上自管 MQTT broker，需自行安裝、修補、擴展、監控並維運 broker，還要透過 Lambda authorizer 自行處理憑證/驗證邏輯。相較全託管的 IoT Core，這與最低營運負擔背道而馳。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it is wrong: it requires a self-managed MQTT broker on EC2 plus an NLB plus an API Gateway HTTP API with an mTLS authorizer. API Gateway HTTP APIs are request/response HTTP front ends and do not broker persistent real-time MQTT pub/sub sessions; the architecture is convoluted and carries very high operational overhead versus the managed IoT Core.","why_zh":"這是 dump 建議答案但屬錯誤：它需要在 EC2 上自管 MQTT broker，加上 NLB，再加上設定 mTLS authorizer 的 API Gateway HTTP API。API Gateway HTTP API 是請求/回應式的 HTTP 前端，無法代理持久的即時 MQTT 發布/訂閱工作階段；此架構繁複且相較託管的 IoT Core 營運負擔極高。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/protocols.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/mqtt.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/x509-client-certs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/device-certs-create.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":74,"question_en":"A company is running several workloads in a single AWS account. A new company policy states that engineers can provision only approved resources and that engineers must use AWS CloudFormation to provision these resources. A solutions architect needs to create a solution to enforce the new restriction on the IAM role that the engineers use for access. What should the solutions architect do to create the solution?","question_zh":"一家公司在单个 AWS 账户中运行多个工作负载。新的公司政策规定，工程师只能预置经批准的资源，并且工程师必须使用 AWS CloudFormation 来预置这些资源。解决方案架构师需要创建一个解决方案来对工程师用于访问的 IAM 角色实施新的限制。 解决方案架构师应该做什么来创建解决方案？","options_en":{"A":"Upload AWS CloudFormation templates that contain approved resources to an Amazon S3 bucket. Update the IAM policy for the engineers’ IAM role to only allow access to Amazon S3 and AWS CloudFormation. Use AWS CloudFormation templates to provision resources.","B":"Update the IAM policy for the engineers’ IAM role with permissions to only allow provisioning of approved resources and AWS CloudFormation. Use AWS CloudFormation templates to create stacks with approved resources.","C":"Update the IAM policy for the engineers’ IAM role with permissions to only allow AWS CloudFormation actions. Create a new IAM policy with permission to provision approved resources, and assign the policy to a new IAM service role. Assign the IAM service role to AWS CloudFormation during stack creation.","D":"Provision resources in AWS CloudFormation stacks. Update the IAM policy for the engineers’ IAM role to only allow access to their own AWS CloudFormation stack."},"options_zh":{"A":"将包含已批准资源的 AWS CloudFormation 模板上传到 Amazon S3 存储桶。更新工程师 IAM 角色的 IAM 策略，以仅允许访问 Amazon S3 和 AWS CloudFormation。使用 AWS CloudFormation 模板来预置资源。","B":"更新工程师 IAM 角色的 IAM 策略，使其具有仅允许预置已批准资源和 AWS CloudFormation 的权限。使用 AWS CloudFormation 模板创建具有批准资源的堆栈。","C":"更新工程师 IAM 角色的 IAM 策略，使其具有仅允许 AWS CloudFormation 操作的权限。创建一个具有预置批准资源权限的新 IAM 策略，并将该策略分配给新的 IAM 服务角色。在堆栈创建期间将 IAM 服务角色分配给 AWS CloudFormation。","D":"在 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈中配置资源。更新工程师 IAM 角色的 IAM 策略，以仅允许访问他们自己的 AWS CloudFormation 堆 栈。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":98},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The policy has two independent requirements: engineers may provision only approved resources, AND engineers must use CloudFormation to do it. A CloudFormation service role satisfies both. In option C, the engineers' IAM role is granted only CloudFormation actions, so they have no direct permissions to create any resources themselves; the only way they can create resources is by launching a CloudFormation stack. A separate IAM service role (trusted by cloudformation.amazonaws.com) holds the permissions to provision the approved resources, and CloudFormation assumes that service role during stack creation. Per AWS Prescriptive Guidance, this exact pattern means the identity-based policy on the principal does not need permissions for the resources in the template, IAM principals follow least privilege, and 'to create, update, or delete AWS resources, IAM principals must use CloudFormation.' Option B fails the second requirement: granting the engineers' role direct permissions to provision the approved resources lets them create those resources outside CloudFormation (console/CLI), so it does not enforce that CloudFormation must be used.","explanation_zh":"公司政策有兩個獨立要求：工程師只能佈建已核准的資源，而且必須透過 CloudFormation 來佈建。CloudFormation service role 同時滿足兩者。選項 C 中，工程師的 IAM role 只被授予 CloudFormation 動作權限，因此他們自身沒有任何直接建立資源的權限；唯一能建立資源的途徑就是啟動 CloudFormation stack。另一個獨立的 IAM service role（信任 cloudformation.amazonaws.com）才持有佈建已核准資源的權限，CloudFormation 在建立 stack 時會 assume 此 service role。根據 AWS Prescriptive Guidance，這個模式正是：principal 的 identity-based policy 不需要 template 中資源的權限、IAM principal 遵循最小權限，且『要建立、更新或刪除 AWS 資源，IAM principal 必須使用 CloudFormation』。選項 B 不符合第二項要求：把佈建已核准資源的直接權限給工程師的 role，會讓他們可以在 CloudFormation 之外（主控台/CLI）建立這些資源，因此無法強制必須使用 CloudFormation。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Storing templates in S3 and allowing access only to S3 and CloudFormation does not give CloudFormation any permission to actually create the underlying resources, so stacks would fail. It also does nothing to restrict which resources are 'approved' and does not address the provisioning permissions model.","why_zh":"把範本放在 S3、僅允許存取 S3 與 CloudFormation，並未賦予 CloudFormation 實際建立底層資源的權限，stack 會失敗。它也無法限制哪些資源是『已核准』的，且未處理佈建權限模型。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Granting the engineers' role direct permissions to provision the approved resources means they can create those resources outside CloudFormation (console or CLI). This violates the requirement that engineers MUST use CloudFormation; it only enforces the 'approved resources' part, not the 'must use CloudFormation' part.","why_zh":"把佈建已核准資源的直接權限給工程師的 role，代表他們可以在 CloudFormation 之外（主控台或 CLI）建立這些資源。這違反『工程師必須使用 CloudFormation』的要求；只達成了『已核准資源』，未達成『必須使用 CloudFormation』。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Limiting engineers to only their own CloudFormation stack controls stack-level access but does not restrict provisioning to approved resources, and by itself does not prevent direct resource creation outside CloudFormation. It does not implement the service-role least-privilege model the policy requires.","why_zh":"只讓工程師存取自己的 CloudFormation stack 是 stack 層級的存取控制，並未限制只能佈建已核准資源，本身也無法阻止在 CloudFormation 之外直接建立資源。它沒有實作政策所需的 service role 最小權限模型。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-iam-servicerole.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/least-privilege-cloudformation/service-roles-for-cloudformation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_passrole.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":75,"question_en":"A solutions architect is designing the data storage and retrieval architecture for a new application that a company will be launching soon. The application is designed to ingest millions of small records per minute from devices all around the world. Each record is less than 4 KB in size and needs to be stored in a durable location where it can be retrieved with low latency. The data is ephemeral and the company is required to store the data for 120 days only, after which the data can be deleted. The solutions architect calculates that, during the course of a year, the storage requirements would be about 10-15 TB. Which storage strategy is the MOST cost-effective and meets the design requirements?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师正在为一家公司即将推出的新应用程序设计数据存储和检索架构。该应用程序旨在每分钟从世界各地的设备中获取 数百万条小记录。每条记录的大小小于 4 KB，需要存储在持久位置，以便以低延迟进行检索。数据是短暂的，公司只能将数据存储 120 天，之后可以删除数据。 解决方案架构师计算出，一年内的存储需求约为 10-15 TB。 哪种存储策略最具成本效益且满足设计要求？","options_en":{"A":"Design the application to store each incoming record as a single .csv file in an Amazon S3 bucket to allow for indexed retrieval. Configure a lifecycle policy to delete data older than 120 days.","B":"Design the application to store each incoming record in an Amazon DynamoDB table properly configured for the scale. Configure the DynamoDB Time to Live (TTL) feature to delete records older than 120 days.","C":"Design the application to store each incoming record in a single table in an Amazon RDS MySQL database. Run a nightly cron job that runs a query to delete any records older than 120 days.","D":"Design the application to batch incoming records before writing them to an Amazon S3 bucket. Update the metadata for the object to contain the list of records in the batch and use the Amazon S3 metadata search feature to retrieve the data. Configure a lifecycle policy to delete the data after 120 days."},"options_zh":{"A":"设计应用程序以将每个传入记录作为单个 .csv 文件存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中，以允许索引检索。配置生命周期策略以删除 超过 120 天的数据。","B":"设计应用程序以将每个传入记录存储在针对规模正确配置的 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。配置 DynamoDB 生存时间 (TTL) 功能以删 除超过 120 天的记录。","C":"设计应用程序以将每个传入记录存储在 Amazon RDS MySQL 数据库的单个表中。运行每晚 cron 作业，该作业运行查询以删除 任何超过 120 天的记录。","D":"设计应用程序以在将传入记录写入 Amazon S3 存储桶之前对其进行批处理。更新对象的元数据以包含批次中的记录列表，并 使用 Amazon S3 元数据搜索功能检索数据。配置生命周期策略以在 120 天后删除数据。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":83,"D":17},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":76,"question_en":"A retail company is hosting an ecommerce website on AWS across multiple AWS Regions. The company wants the website to be operational at all times for online purchases. The website stores data in an Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance. Which solution will provide the HIGHEST availability for the database?","question_zh":"一家零售公司在多个 AWS 区域的 AWS 上托管一个电子商务网站。该公司希望该网站能够随时运行以进行在线购买。该网站将数据 存储在 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库实例中。 哪种解决方案将为数据库提供最高的可用性？","options_en":{"A":"Configure automated backups on Amazon RDS. In the case of disruption, promote an automated backup to be a standalone DB instance. Direct database tra®c to the promoted DB instance. Create a replacement read replica that has the promoted DB instance as its source.","B":"Configure global tables and read replicas on Amazon RDS. Activate the cross-Region scope. In the case of disruption, use AWS Lambda to copy the read replicas from one Region to another Region.","C":"Configure global tables and automated backups on Amazon RDS. In the case of disruption, use AWS Lambda to copy the read replicas from one Region to another Region.","D":"Configure read replicas on Amazon RDS. In the case of disruption, promote a cross-Region and read replica to be a standalone DB instance. Direct database tra®c to the promoted DB instance. Create a replacement read replica that has the promoted DB instance as its source."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon RDS 上配置自动备份。在发生中断的情况下，将自动备份提升为独立的数据库实例。将数据库流量引导至升级的数 据库实例。创建以升级的数据库实例作为源的替换只读副本。","B":"在 Amazon RDS 上配置全局表和只读副本。激活跨区域范围。如果出现中断，请使用 AWS Lambda 将只读副本从一个区域复制 到另一个区域。","C":"在 Amazon RDS 上配置全局表和自动备份。如果出现中断，请使用 AWS Lambda 将只读副本从一个区域复制到另一个区域。","D":"在 Amazon RDS 上配置只读副本。在发生中断的情况下，将跨区域和只读副本提升为独立的数据库实例。将数据库流量引导至 升级的数据库实例。创建以升级的数据库实例作为源的替换只读副本。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":93},"tags":["Compute","Database"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":77,"question_en":"Example Corp. has an on-premises data center and a VPC named VPC A in the Example Corp. AWS account. The on-premises network connects to VPC A through an AWS Site-To-Site VPN. The on-premises servers can properly access VPC A. Example Corp. just acquired AnyCompany, which has a VPC named VPC B. There is no IP address overlap among these networks. Example Corp. has peered VPC A and VPC B. Example Corp. wants to connect from its on-premise servers to VPC B. Example Corp. has properly set up the network ACL and security groups. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"Example Corp. 在 Example Corp. AWS 账户中拥有一个本地数据中心和一个名为 VPC A 的 VPC。本地网络通过 AWS Site-To-Site VPN 连接 到 VPC A。本地服务器可以正常访问VPC A。Example Corp.刚刚收购了AnyCompany，该公司有一个名为VPC B的VPC。这些网络之间没 有IP地址重叠。Example Corp. 已对 VPC A 和 VPC B 建立对等关系。Example Corp. 希望从其本地服务器连接到 VPC B。Example Corp. 已正确设置网络 ACL 和安全组。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的操作工作量满足此要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a transit gateway. Attach the Site-to-Site VPN, VPC A, and VPC B to the transit gateway. Update the transit gateway route tables for all networks to add IP range routes for all other networks.","B":"Create a transit gateway. Create a Site-to-Site VPN connection between the on-premises network and VPC B, and connect the VPN connection to the transit gateway. Add a route to direct tra®c to the peered VPCs, and add an authorization rule to give clients access to the VPCs A and B.","C":"Update the route tables for the Site-to-Site VPN and both VPCs for all three networks. Configure BGP propagation for all three networks. Wait for up to 5 minutes for BGP propagation to finish.","D":"Modify the Site-to-Site VPN’s virtual private gateway definition to include VPC A and VPC B. Split the two routers of the virtual private getaway between the two VPCs."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建中转网关。将 Site-to-Site VPN、VPC A 和 VPC B 连接到中转网关。更新所有网络的中转网关路由表，以添加所有其他网络 的 IP 范围路由。","B":"创建中转网关。在本地网络和 VPC B 之间创建站点到站点 VPN 连接，并将该 VPN 连接连接到中转网关。添加路由以将流量引 导至对等 VPC，并添加授权规则以允许客户端访问 VPC A 和 B。","C":"更新所有三个网络的 Site-to-Site VPN 和两个 VPC 的路由表。为所有三个网络配置 BGP 传播。等待最多 5 分钟，让 BGP 传播完 成。","D":"修改 Site-to-Site VPN 的虚拟专用网关定义以包括 VPC A 和 VPC B。在两个 VPC 之间拆分虚拟专用网关的两个路由器。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":91},"tags":["Networking/DNS"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The blocker here is that VPC peering does not support transitive (edge-to-edge) routing. AWS docs state explicitly: 'If VPC A has a VPN connection to a corporate network, resources in VPC B can't use the VPN connection to communicate with the corporate network.' So even though on-prem reaches VPC A over the Site-to-Site VPN and VPC A is peered with VPC B, on-prem traffic cannot transit VPC A's peering to reach VPC B. AWS's documented remedy is to use a transit gateway in place of the peering as the hub. Option A creates a TGW and attaches the VPN, VPC A, and VPC B, then adds the required routes in the TGW route tables, giving full any-to-any (including on-prem to VPC B) connectivity with the least operational effort. Option A is the standard AWS hub-and-spoke pattern and the lowest-effort architectural fix.","explanation_zh":"本題的根本障礙是 VPC peering 不支援轉送(transitive / edge-to-edge)路由。AWS 文件明確指出:『若 VPC A 有連到企業網路的 VPN 連線,VPC B 的資源無法使用該 VPN 連線與企業網路通訊。』因此即使地端透過 Site-to-Site VPN 連到 VPC A,且 VPC A 與 VPC B 已建立 peering,地端流量仍無法經由 VPC A 的 peering 邊界抵達 VPC B。AWS 文件建議的解法是以 transit gateway 作為中樞取代 peering。選項 A 建立 TGW,並將 VPN、VPC A、VPC B 都附加上去,再於 TGW 路由表加入所需路由,即可達成任意對任意(含地端到 VPC B)的連線,且操作負擔最低。A 是標準的 hub-and-spoke 架構,也是最省力的修正方式。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Creating a second, separate Site-to-Site VPN to VPC B is more operational effort than a single TGW hub, and the step 'add an authorization rule to give clients access to VPCs A and B' is an AWS Client VPN concept, not Site-to-Site VPN. The option mixes incompatible features and is not the least-effort approach.","why_zh":"另外建立一條到 VPC B 的 Site-to-Site VPN 比單一 TGW 中樞更費工,且『新增 authorization rule 讓 clients 存取 VPC A 與 B』是 Client VPN 的概念,並非 Site-to-Site VPN。此選項混用了不相容的功能,也非最省力方案。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"No amount of route table edits or BGP propagation can overcome VPC peering's non-transitive nature. Traffic from on-prem destined for VPC B arrives at VPC A's virtual private gateway but cannot be forwarded across the peering edge to VPC B (edge-to-edge routing is unsupported). This is technically impossible, not just slow.","why_zh":"再多的路由表編輯或 BGP 傳播都無法克服 VPC peering 的非轉送特性。地端要往 VPC B 的流量會抵達 VPC A 的 virtual private gateway,但無法跨過 peering 邊界轉送到 VPC B(不支援 edge-to-edge 路由)。這在技術上根本不可行,並非只是慢。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Fabricated/impossible. A virtual private gateway (VGW) attaches to exactly one VPC; you cannot 'include VPC A and VPC B' in one VGW definition. The two VPN tunnel endpoints exist for high availability, not for 'splitting' across VPCs. This is not a real AWS capability. This is the dump's suggested answer and it is wrong.","why_zh":"屬虛構/不可行。Virtual private gateway(VGW)只能附加到單一 VPC,無法在一個 VGW 定義中『同時包含 VPC A 與 VPC B』。兩個 VPN tunnel endpoints 是為了高可用,而非用來『拆分』給不同 VPC。這並非真實的 AWS 功能。此為題庫建議答案,實為錯誤。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/peering/vpc-peering-basics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/how-transit-gateways-work.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/what-is-transit-gateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/s2svpn/VPNRoutingTypes.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":78,"question_en":"A company recently completed the migration from an on-premises data center to the AWS Cloud by using a replatforming strategy. One of the migrated servers is running a legacy Simple Mail Transfer Protocol (SMTP) service that a critical application relies upon. The application sends outbound email messages to the company’s customers. The legacy SMTP server does not support TLS encryption and uses TCP port 25. The application can use SMTP only. The company decides to use Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) and to decommission the legacy SMTP server. The company has created and validated the SES domain. The company has lifted the SES limits. What should the company do to modify the application to send email messages from Amazon SES?","question_zh":"一家公司最近使用平台重构策略完成了从本地数据中心到 AWS 云的迁移。其中一台迁移的服务器正在运行关键应用程序所依赖的旧 版简单邮件传输协议 (SMTP) 服务。该应用程序向公司的客户发送出站电子邮件。旧版 SMTP 服务器不支持 TLS 加密并使用 TCP 端口 25。应用程序只能使用 SMTP。 该公司决定使用 Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) 并停用旧版 SMTP 服务器。该公司已创建并验证了 SES 域。该公司已取消 SES 限制。 公司应该如何修改应用程序以从 Amazon SES 发送电子邮件？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the application to connect to Amazon SES by using TLS Wrapper. Create an IAM role that has ses:SendEmail and ses:SendRawEmail permissions. Attach the IAM role to an Amazon EC2 instance.","B":"Configure the application to connect to Amazon SES by using STARTTLS. Obtain Amazon SES SMTP credentials. Use the credentials to authenticate with Amazon SES.","C":"Configure the application to use the SES API to send email messages. Create an IAM role that has ses:SendEmail and ses:SendRawEmail permissions. Use the IAM role as a service role for Amazon SES.","D":"Configure the application to use AWS SDKs to send email messages. Create an IAM user for Amazon SES. Generate API access keys. Use the access keys to authenticate with Amazon SES."},"options_zh":{"A":"将应用程序配置为使用 TLS Wrapper 连接到 Amazon SES。创建具有 ses:SendEmail 和 ses:SendRawEmail 权限的 IAM 角色。将 IAM 角色附加到 Amazon EC2 实例。","B":"将应用程序配置为使用 STARTTLS 连接到 Amazon SES。获取 Amazon SES SMTP 凭证。使用凭证通过 Amazon SES 进行身份验 证。","C":"配置应用程序以使用 SES API 发送电子邮件。创建具有 ses:SendEmail 和 ses:SendRawEmail 权限的 IAM 角色。使用 IAM 角色作 为 Amazon SES 的服务角色。","D":"配置应用程序以使用 AWS 开发工具包发送电子邮件。为 Amazon SES 创建 IAM 用户。生成 API 访问密钥。使用访问密钥通过 Amazon SES 进行身份验证。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":86},"tags":["Migration","Security/IAM","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The application can use SMTP only, which eliminates the SES API (C) and the AWS SDKs (D). The legacy app already uses TCP port 25 and does not support TLS, but the Amazon SES SMTP endpoint requires all connections to be TLS-encrypted via STARTTLS or TLS Wrapper. STARTTLS upgrades an existing unencrypted connection to encrypted on ports 25, 587, or 2587, so it works on the same port 25 the application already uses, requiring the fewest changes. Amazon SES SMTP authentication uses SMTP credentials (a generated SMTP user name and password), which are explicitly different from AWS access keys or IAM role credentials, so Option B (configure STARTTLS, obtain SES SMTP credentials, and authenticate with them) is exactly what AWS documents. Option A is wrong because an IAM role attached to an EC2 instance authenticates the SES API, not the SMTP interface, and TLS Wrapper would require switching to port 465/2465.","explanation_zh":"應用程式只能使用 SMTP，因此排除使用 SES API 的 C 與使用 AWS SDK 的 D。舊版應用程式已使用 TCP port 25 且不支援 TLS，但 Amazon SES SMTP 端點要求所有連線都必須透過 STARTTLS 或 TLS Wrapper 進行 TLS 加密。STARTTLS 會在 port 25、587 或 2587 上將既有的未加密連線升級為加密連線，因此可沿用應用程式現有的 port 25，改動最少。Amazon SES SMTP 的驗證使用 SMTP credentials（產生的 SMTP 使用者名稱與密碼），AWS 文件明確指出這與 AWS access keys 或 IAM role credentials 不同，所以 B 選項（設定 STARTTLS、取得 SES SMTP credentials 並用其驗證）正是 AWS 所記載的作法。A 選項錯誤，因為附加在 EC2 instance 的 IAM role 是驗證 SES API，而非 SMTP 介面，且 TLS Wrapper 需改用 port 465/2465。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The SES SMTP interface authenticates with SMTP credentials (username/password), not an IAM role attached to an EC2 instance; an IAM role with ses:SendEmail/ses:SendRawEmail authorizes the SES API, not SMTP auth. TLS Wrapper also forces a port change to 465/2465 instead of keeping the app's existing port 25.","why_zh":"SES SMTP 介面使用 SMTP credentials（使用者名稱/密碼）驗證，而非附加在 EC2 instance 的 IAM role；具 ses:SendEmail/ses:SendRawEmail 的 IAM role 授權的是 SES API 而非 SMTP 驗證。TLS Wrapper 也需改用 port 465/2465，無法沿用應用程式既有的 port 25。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The requirement states the application can use SMTP only, so it cannot call the SES API. Also 'use the IAM role as a service role for Amazon SES' is not a valid way to send email from an application.","why_zh":"需求明確指出應用程式只能使用 SMTP，因此無法呼叫 SES API。此外『將 IAM role 當作 Amazon SES 的 service role』並非從應用程式寄信的有效方式。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Using AWS SDKs violates the 'SMTP only' constraint. It also relies on a long-lived IAM user with API access keys, which is not a recommended credential approach and is unnecessary here.","why_zh":"使用 AWS SDK 違反『只能使用 SMTP』的限制。它還依賴具長期 API access keys 的 IAM user，這並非建議的憑證做法，且在此情境下也不必要。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ses/latest/dg/smtp-connect.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ses/latest/dg/send-email-smtp.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ses/latest/dg/smtp-credentials.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":79,"question_en":"A company recently acquired several other companies. Each company has a separate AWS account with a different billing and reporting method. The acquiring company has consolidated all the accounts into one organization in AWS Organizations. However, the acquiring company has found it di®cult to generate a cost report that contains meaningful groups for all the teams. The acquiring company’s finance team needs a solution to report on costs for all the companies through a self-managed application. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司最近收购了其他几家公司。每家公司都有一个单独的 AWS 账户，并采用不同的计费和报告方法。收购公司已将所有账户整 合到 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织中。然而，收购公司发现很难生成包含对所有团队有意义的组的成本报告。 收购公司的财务团队需要一个解决方案，通过自我管理的应用程序报告所有公司的成本。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Cost and Usage Report for the organization. Define tags and cost categories in the report. Create a table in Amazon Athena. Create an Amazon QuickSight dataset based on the Athena table. Share the dataset with the finance team.","B":"Create an AWS Cost and Usage Report for the organization. Define tags and cost categories in the report. Create a specialized template in AWS Cost Explorer that the finance department will use to build reports.","C":"Create an Amazon QuickSight dataset that receives spending information from the AWS Price List Query API. Share the dataset with the finance team.","D":"Use the AWS Price List Query API to collect account spending information. Create a specialized template in AWS Cost Explorer that the finance department will use to build reports."},"options_zh":{"A":"为组织创建 AWS 成本和使用情况报告。在报告中定义标签和成本类别。在 Amazon Athena 中创建一个表。基于 Athena 表创建 Amazon QuickSight 数据集。与财务团队共享数据集。","B":"为组织创建 AWS 成本和使用情况报告。在报告中定义标签和成本类别。在 AWS Cost Explorer 中创建专用模板，财务部门将使 用该模板来构建报告。","C":"创建一个 Amazon QuickSight 数据集，用于从 AWS 价目表查询 API 接收支出信息。与财务团队共享数据集。","D":"使用 AWS 价目表查询 API 收集账户支出信息。在 AWS Cost Explorer 中创建专用模板，财务部门将使用该模板来构建报告。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Cost Optimization","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The finance team needs actual cost/spending data grouped meaningfully and consumed through a self-managed application. The AWS Cost and Usage Report (CUR) is the most comprehensive source of actual cost and usage data; it supports user-defined tags and AWS Cost Categories to create meaningful groupings, and it can be delivered to S3 and integrated with Amazon Athena for SQL queries. An Amazon QuickSight dataset built on the Athena table, then shared with the finance team, is the canonical AWS-documented pattern for a self-managed, customizable cost-reporting application. Options C and D fail because the AWS Price List Query API returns product pricing/rates (what AWS charges for services), not an account's actual spending, so it cannot report on company costs. Option B is invalid because Cost Explorer does not provide 'specialized templates' that a finance department builds custom self-managed reports from; Cost Explorer is a managed visualization tool, not a self-managed application platform.","explanation_zh":"財務團隊需要實際的成本/支出資料，並依有意義的方式分組，且透過自行管理的應用程式存取。AWS Cost and Usage Report (CUR) 是最完整的實際成本與用量資料來源，支援使用者自訂 tags 以及 AWS Cost Categories 來建立有意義的分組，並可交付至 S3 再整合 Amazon Athena 進行 SQL 查詢。以 Athena 資料表為基礎建立 Amazon QuickSight dataset 並分享給財務團隊，正是 AWS 文件中用於自行管理、可自訂成本報表應用的標準模式。選項 C 與 D 都錯，因為 AWS Price List Query API 回傳的是產品定價/費率（AWS 對服務收取的價格），而非帳戶的實際支出，無法用來報告各公司成本。選項 B 也不正確，因為 Cost Explorer 並不提供讓財務部門用來建立自行管理自訂報表的『specialized template』；Cost Explorer 是受管的視覺化工具，並非自行管理的應用平台。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CUR with tags/cost categories is the right data source, but Cost Explorer does not offer 'specialized templates' for finance to build a self-managed reporting application; Cost Explorer is a managed AWS visualization tool, not a self-managed app.","why_zh":"搭配 tags/cost categories 的 CUR 是正確資料來源，但 Cost Explorer 並未提供讓財務建立自行管理報表應用的『specialized template』；Cost Explorer 是 AWS 受管視覺化工具，非自行管理應用程式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The AWS Price List Query API returns product pricing and rates (what AWS charges), not the account's actual spending, so a QuickSight dataset fed by it cannot report real company costs.","why_zh":"AWS Price List Query API 回傳的是產品定價與費率（AWS 收費價格），並非帳戶實際支出，因此以它為來源的 QuickSight dataset 無法報告各公司真實成本。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Doubly wrong: the Price List Query API provides pricing, not account spending, and Cost Explorer does not provide specialized templates for building self-managed finance reports.","why_zh":"兩處皆錯：Price List Query API 提供的是定價而非帳戶支出，且 Cost Explorer 並未提供建立自行管理財務報表的 specialized template。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cur/latest/userguide/what-is-cur.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cur/latest/userguide/cur-query-athena.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/using-price-list-query-api.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-what-is.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":80,"question_en":"A company runs an IoT platform on AWS. IoT sensors in various locations send data to the company’s Node.js API servers on Amazon EC2 instances running behind an Application Load Balancer. The data is stored in an Amazon RDS MySQL DB instance that uses a 4 TB General Purpose SSD volume. The number of sensors the company has deployed in the field has increased over time, and is expected to grow significantly. The API servers are consistently overloaded and RDS metrics show high write latency. Which of the following steps together will resolve the issues permanently and enable growth as new sensors are provisioned, while keeping this platform cost-e®cient? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上运行 IoT 平台。不同位置的 IoT 传感器将数据发送到在 Application Load Balancer 后面运行的 Amazon EC2 实例上的 公司 Node.js API 服务器。数据存储在使用 4 TB 通用 SSD 卷的 Amazon RDS MySQL 数据库实例中。 随着时间的推移，该公司在现场部署的传感器数量不断增加，预计将大幅增长。API 服务器持续过载，RDS 指标显示写入延迟较高。 以下哪一项步骤将永久解决问题并随着新传感器的配置而实现增长，同时保持该平台的成本效益？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Resize the MySQL General Purpose SSD storage to 6 TB to improve the volume’s IOPS.","B":"Re-architect the database tier to use Amazon Aurora instead of an RDS MySQL DB instance and add read replicas.","C":"Leverage Amazon Kinesis Data Streams and AWS Lambda to ingest and process the raw data.","D":"Use AWS X-Ray to analyze and debug application issues and add more API servers to match the load.","E":"Re-architect the database tier to use Amazon DynamoDB instead of an RDS MySQL DB instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 MySQL 通用 SSD 存储大小调整为 6 TB 以提高卷的 IOPS。","B":"重新架构数据库层以使用 Amazon Aurora 而不是 RDS MySQL 数据库实例并添加只读副本。","C":"利用 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams 和 AWS Lambda 提取和处理原始数据。","D":"使用 AWS X-Ray 分析和调试应用程序问题并添加更多 API 服务器以匹配负载。","E":"重新架构数据库层以使用 Amazon DynamoDB 而不是 RDS MySQL 数据库实例。"},"answer":["C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"CE":69,"BC":18},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・複選"},{"id":81,"question_en":"A company is building an electronic document management system in which users upload their documents. The application stack is entirely serverless and runs on AWS in the eu-central-1 Region. The system includes a web application that uses an Amazon CloudFront distribution for delivery with Amazon S3 as the origin. The web application communicates with Amazon API Gateway Regional endpoints. The API Gateway APIs call AWS Lambda functions that store metadata in an Amazon Aurora Serverless database and put the documents into an S3 bucket. The company is growing steadily and has completed a proof of concept with its largest customer. The company must improve latency outside of Europe. Which combination of actions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在构建一个电子文档管理系统，用户可以在其中上传文档。该应用程序堆栈完全无服务器，并在 eu-central-1 区域的 AWS 上运行。该系统包括一个 Web 应用程序，该应用程序使用 Amazon CloudFront 发行版以 Amazon S3 作为源进行交付。Web 应用程序 与 Amazon API Gateway 区域终端节点进行通信。API Gateway API 调用 AWS Lambda 函数，这些函数将元数据存储在 Amazon Aurora Serverless 数据库中，并将文档放入 S3 存储桶中。 该公司正在稳步发展，并已与其最大客户完成了概念验证。该公司必须改善欧洲以外地区的延迟。 哪种行动组合可以满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Enable S3 Transfer Acceleration on the S3 bucket. Ensure that the web application uses the Transfer Acceleration signed URLs.","B":"Create an accelerator in AWS Global Accelerator. Attach the accelerator to the CloudFront distribution.","C":"Change the API Gateway Regional endpoints to edge-optimized endpoints.","D":"Provision the entire stack in two other locations that are spread across the world. Use global databases on the Aurora Serverless cluster.","E":"Add an Amazon RDS proxy between the Lambda functions and the Aurora Serverless database."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 S3 存储桶上启用 S3 传输加速。确保 Web 应用程序使用 Transfer Acceleration 签名的 URL。","B":"在 AWS Global Accelerator 中创建加速器。将加速器附加到 CloudFront 分配。","C":"将 API Gateway 区域端点更改为边缘优化端点。","D":"在分布在世界各地的另外两个位置配置整个堆栈。在 Aurora Serverless 集群上使用全局数据库。","E":"在 Lambda 函数和 Aurora Serverless 数据库之间添加 Amazon RDS 代理。"},"answer":["A","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AC":60,"CD":31},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・複選"},{"id":82,"question_en":"An adventure company has launched a new feature on its mobile app. Users can use the feature to upload their hiking and rafting photos and videos anytime. The photos and videos are stored in Amazon S3 Standard storage in an S3 bucket and are served through Amazon CloudFront. The company needs to optimize the cost of the storage. A solutions architect discovers that most of the uploaded photos and videos are accessed infrequently after 30 days. However, some of the uploaded photos and videos are accessed frequently after 30 days. The solutions architect needs to implement a solution that maintains millisecond retrieval availability of the photos and videos at the lowest possible cost. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家冒险公司在其移动应用程序上推出了一项新功能。用户可以使用该功能随时上传远足和漂流照片和视频。照片和视频存储在 S3 存储桶中的 Amazon S3 标准存储中，并通过 Amazon CloudFront 提供服务。 公司需要优化存储成本。解决方案架构师发现，大多数上传的照片和视频在 30 天后就很少被访问。然而，一些上传的照片和视频在 30天后被频繁访问。解决方案架构师需要实施一种解决方案，以尽可能低的成本维持照片和视频的毫秒级检索可用性。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure S3 Intelligent-Tiering on the S3 bucket.","B":"Configure an S3 Lifecycle policy to transition image objects and video objects from S3 Standard to S3 Glacier Deep Archive after 30 days.","C":"Replace Amazon S3 with an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system that is mounted on Amazon EC2 instances.","D":"Add a Cache-Control: max-age header to the S3 image objects and S3 video objects. Set the header to 30 days."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 S3 存储桶上配置 S3 智能分层。","B":"配置 S3 生命周期策略，以在 30 天后将图像对象和视频对象从 S3 Standard 过渡到 S3 Glacier Deep Archive。","C":"将 Amazon S3 替换为安装在 Amazon EC2 实例上的 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统。","D":"将 Cache-Control: max-age 标头添加到 S3 图像对象和 S3 视频对象。将标题设置为 30 天。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":97},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The workload has a mixed, unpredictable access pattern: most photos/videos become infrequently accessed after 30 days, but some remain frequently accessed, and the requirement is millisecond retrieval at the lowest cost. S3 Intelligent-Tiering is purpose-built for exactly this. It automatically moves objects to the Infrequent Access tier after 30 consecutive days of no access and automatically moves them back to the Frequent Access tier when accessed again, all without retrieval fees and without operational overhead. Critically, the Frequent, Infrequent, and Archive Instant Access tiers all provide the same low-latency millisecond retrieval, so availability is preserved. Because the per-object access pattern varies and isn't known in advance, a blanket lifecycle rule cannot optimize cost as well as Intelligent-Tiering's per-object automatic tiering.","explanation_zh":"此工作負載具有混合且無法預測的存取模式：多數相片/影片在 30 天後變為不常存取，但部分仍頻繁存取，且需求是以最低成本維持毫秒級擷取。S3 Intelligent-Tiering 正是為此設計：它會在物件連續 30 天未被存取後自動移至 Infrequent Access 層，並在再次被存取時自動移回 Frequent Access 層，全程無擷取費用且無營運負擔。關鍵在於 Frequent、Infrequent 與 Archive Instant Access 層都提供相同的低延遲毫秒級擷取，因此可用性得以維持。由於每個物件的存取模式各異且事先未知，固定的 Lifecycle 規則無法像 Intelligent-Tiering 的逐物件自動分層那樣有效最佳化成本。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"S3 Glacier Deep Archive is archival storage with average retrieval times of 9 to 48 hours, which violates the millisecond retrieval requirement. A blanket lifecycle rule would also wrongly archive the objects that are still frequently accessed after 30 days.","why_zh":"S3 Glacier Deep Archive 為封存式儲存，平均擷取時間 9 至 48 小時，違反毫秒級擷取需求；且固定 Lifecycle 規則會錯誤地封存 30 天後仍頻繁存取的物件。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon EFS plus EC2 is more expensive than S3, adds significant operational overhead, and does not provide automated cost tiering; it also breaks the simple S3-as-CloudFront-origin design. It does not optimize cost.","why_zh":"Amazon EFS 加 EC2 比 S3 更昂貴，且帶來大量營運負擔，也不提供自動分層成本最佳化，並破壞 S3 作為 CloudFront 來源的簡單架構，無法達到成本最佳化。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A Cache-Control: max-age header only controls how long CloudFront caches objects at the edge; it has no effect on S3 storage class or storage cost, so it does not address the cost-optimization requirement at all.","why_zh":"Cache-Control: max-age 標頭僅控制 CloudFront 邊緣快取物件的時間，對 S3 儲存類別或儲存成本毫無影響，完全無法滿足成本最佳化需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/intelligent-tiering-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/intelligent-tiering.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/glacier-storage-classes.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":83,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon S3 to store files and images in a variety of storage classes. The company's S3 costs have increased substantially during the past year. A solutions architect needs to review data trends for the past 12 months and identity the appropriate storage class for the objects. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 Amazon S3 将文件和图像存储在各种存储类别中。该公司的S3成本在过去一年中大幅增加。 解决方案架构师需要查看过去 12 个月的数据趋势并确定对象的适当存储类别。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Download AWS Cost and Usage Reports for the last 12 months of S3 usage. Review AWS Trusted Advisor recommendations for cost savings.","B":"Use S3 storage class analysis. Import data trends into an Amazon QuickSight dashboard to analyze storage trends.","C":"Use Amazon S3 Storage Lens. Upgrade the default dashboard to include advanced metrics for storage trends.","D":"Use Access Analyzer for S3. Download the Access Analyzer for S3 report for the last 12 months. Import the .csv file to an Amazon QuickSight dashboard."},"options_zh":{"A":"下载过去 12 个月 S3 使用情况的 AWS 成本和使用情况报告。查看 AWS Trusted Advisor 建议以节省成本。","B":"使用S3存储类分析。将数据趋势导入 Amazon QuickSight 仪表板以分析存储趋势。","C":"使用 Amazon S3 存储镜头。升级默认仪表板以包含存储趋势的高级指标。","D":"使用 S3 的访问分析器。下载过去 12 个月的 S3 访问分析器报告。将 .csv 文件导入 Amazon QuickSight 控制面板。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":78},"tags":["Storage","Cost Optimization","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement has two decisive qualifiers: review data trends for the PAST 12 months, across a VARIETY of storage classes. S3 Storage Lens with advanced metrics retains data for queries for 15 months, which covers a 12-month historical trend review, and it provides account/organization-wide visibility across all storage classes plus advanced cost-optimization metrics and recommendations. Upgrading the default Storage Lens dashboard to advanced metrics is exactly the right tool. S3 storage class analysis (Option B) fails on both counts: AWS docs state it 'only provides recommendations for Standard to Standard IA classes' and it observes access patterns going forward from configuration (30+ days) rather than analyzing the past 12 months, so it cannot review last year's trends and does not cover the variety of storage classes in use.","explanation_zh":"需求有兩個決定性限定條件：檢視過去 12 個月的資料趨勢，且涵蓋多種 storage classes。S3 Storage Lens 搭配 advanced metrics 可保留資料供查詢長達 15 個月，足以涵蓋 12 個月的歷史趨勢分析，並提供跨整個帳戶/組織、所有 storage classes 的可見性，以及進階的成本最佳化指標與建議。將預設 Storage Lens dashboard 升級為 advanced metrics 正是正確做法。S3 storage class analysis（選項 B）兩點皆不符：AWS 文件明確指出它『只提供 Standard 到 Standard IA 的建議』，而且它是從設定後才開始往前觀察存取模式（30 天以上），並非分析過去 12 個月，因此無法檢視去年的趨勢，也無法涵蓋使用中的多種 storage classes。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Cost and Usage Reports and Trusted Advisor surface cost line items and generic savings recommendations, but neither analyzes per-object access patterns by storage class to identify the appropriate storage class for objects. This is higher operational overhead and does not directly meet the storage-class identification goal.","why_zh":"Cost and Usage Reports 與 Trusted Advisor 只呈現成本明細與一般性節省建議，兩者都不會依 storage class 分析個別物件的存取模式以判定合適的 storage class，操作負擔較高且未直接達成目標。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"S3 storage class analysis only recommends STANDARD to STANDARD_IA transitions and observes access patterns prospectively from configuration (30+ days), so it cannot review the PAST 12 months of trends nor cover the variety of storage classes in use.","why_zh":"S3 storage class analysis 只建議 STANDARD 轉 STANDARD_IA，且從設定後才往前觀察存取模式（30 天以上），無法檢視過去 12 個月趨勢，也無法涵蓋多種 storage classes。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Access Analyzer for S3 is a security/access-permissions tool that flags buckets shared with external entities; it has nothing to do with storage classes, storage trends, or cost optimization.","why_zh":"Access Analyzer for S3 是安全/存取權限工具，用於標示與外部實體共用的儲存貯體，與 storage classes、儲存趨勢或成本最佳化完全無關。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/storage_lens_metrics_glossary.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/storage_lens_basics_metrics_recommendations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/analytics-storage-class.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":84,"question_en":"A company has its cloud infrastructure on AWS. A solutions architect needs to define the infrastructure as code. The infrastructure is currently deployed in one AWS Region. The company’s business expansion plan includes deployments in multiple Regions across multiple AWS accounts. What should the solutions architect do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上拥有云基础设施。解决方案架构师需要将基础设施定义为代码。该基础设施目前部署在一个 AWS 区域中。该公 司的业务扩展计划包括跨多个 AWS 账户在多个区域进行部署。 解决方案架构师应该怎样做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudFormation templates. Add IAM policies to control the various accounts, Deploy the templates across the multiple Regions.","B":"Use AWS Organizations. Deploy AWS CloudFormation templates from the management account Use AWS Control Tower to manage deployments across accounts.","C":"Use AWS Organizations and AWS CloudFormation StackSets. Deploy a Cloud Formation template from an account that has the necessary IAM permissions.","D":"Use nested stacks with AWS CloudFormation templates. Change the Region by using nested stacks."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 模板。添加 IAM 策略来控制各个账户，跨多个区域部署模板。","B":"使用 AWS Organizations。从管理账户部署 AWS CloudFormation 模板 使用 AWS Control Tower 管理跨账户的部署。","C":"使用 AWS Organizations 和 AWS CloudFormation StackSets。从具有必要 IAM 权限的账户部署 Cloud Formation 模板。","D":"将嵌套堆栈与 AWS CloudFormation 模板结合使用。使用嵌套堆栈更改区域。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":85,"question_en":"A company has its cloud infrastructure on AWS. A solutions architect needs to define the infrastructure as code. The infrastructure is currently deployed in one AWS Region. The company’s business expansion plan includes deployments in multiple Regions across multiple AWS accounts. What should the solutions architect do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上拥有云基础设施。解决方案架构师需要将基础设施定义为代码。该基础设施目前部署在一个 AWS 区域中。该公 司的业务扩展计划包括跨多个 AWS 账户在多个区域进行部署。 解决方案架构师应该怎样做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudFormation templates. Add IAM policies to control the various accounts, Deploy the templates across the multiple Regions.","B":"Use AWS Organizations. Deploy AWS CloudFormation templates from the management account Use AWS Control Tower to manage deployments across accounts.","C":"Use AWS Organizations and AWS CloudFormation StackSets. Deploy a Cloud Formation template from an account that has the necessary IAM permissions.","D":"Use nested stacks with AWS CloudFormation templates. Change the Region by using nested stacks."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 模板。添加 IAM 策略来控制各个账户，跨多个区域部署模板。","B":"使用 AWS Organizations。从管理账户部署 AWS CloudFormation 模板 使用 AWS Control Tower 管理跨账户的部署。","C":"使用 AWS Organizations 和 AWS CloudFormation StackSets。从具有必要 IAM 权限的账户部署 Cloud Formation 模板。","D":"将嵌套堆栈与 AWS CloudFormation 模板结合使用。使用嵌套堆栈更改区域。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":86,"question_en":"A company plans to refactor a monolithic application into a modern application design deployed on AWS. The CI/CD pipeline needs to be upgraded to support the modern design for the application with the following requirements: • It should allow changes to be released several times every hour. • It should be able to roll back the changes as quickly as possible. Which design will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司计划将单体应用程序重构为部署在 AWS 上的现代应用程序设计。CI/CD 管道需要升级以支持具有以下要求的应用程序的现 代设计： • 它应该允许每小时发布多次更改。 • 它应该能够尽快回滚更改。 哪种设计能够满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy a CI/CD pipeline that incorporates AMIs to contain the application and their configurations. Deploy the application by replacing Amazon EC2 instances.","B":"Specify AWS Elastic Beanstalk to stage in a secondary environment as the deployment target for the CI/CD pipeline of the application. To deploy, swap the staging and production environment URLs.","C":"Use AWS Systems Manager to re-provision the infrastructure for each deployment. Update the Amazon EC2 user data to pull the latest code artifact from Amazon S3 and use Amazon Route 53 weighted routing to point to the new environment.","D":"Roll out the application updates as part of an Auto Scaling event using prebuilt AMIs. Use new versions of the AMIs to add instances. and phase out all instances that use the previous AMI version with the configured termination policy during a deployment event."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署包含 AMI 的 CI/CD 管道以包含应用程序及其配置。通过替换 Amazon EC2 实例来部署应用程序。","B":"指定 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 在辅助环境中暂存，作为应用程序 CI/CD 管道的部署目标。要进行部署，请交换暂存环境和生产环 境 URL。","C":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 为每个部署重新配置基础设施。更新 Amazon EC2 用户数据以从 Amazon S3 提取最新的代码工件并 使用 Amazon Route 53 加权路由指向新环境。","D":"使用预构建的 AMI 将应用程序更新作为 Auto Scaling 事件的一部分推出。使用新版本的 AMI 添加实例。并在部署事件期间逐步 淘汰使用先前 AMI 版本以及配置的终止策略的所有实例。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":87,"question_en":"A company has an application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances. A solutions architect is designing VPC infrastructure in an AWS Region where the application needs to access an Amazon Aurora DB Cluster. The EC2 instances are all associated with the same security group. The DB cluster is associated with its own security group. The solutions architect needs to add rules to the security groups to provide the application with least privilege access to the DB Cluster. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司有一个在 Amazon EC2 实例上运行的应用程序。解决方案架构师正在 AWS 区域中设计 VPC 基础设施，其中应用程序需要访 问 Amazon Aurora 数据库集群。EC2 实例均与同一安全组关联。数据库集群与其自己的安全组关联。 解决方案架构师需要向安全组添加规​则，以便为应用程序提供对数据库集群的最小权限访问权限。 哪种步骤组合可以满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Add an inbound rule to the EC2 instances' security group. Specify the DB cluster's security group as the source over the default Aurora port.","B":"Add an outbound rule to the EC2 instances' security group. Specify the DB cluster's security group as the destination over the default Aurora port.","C":"Add an inbound rule to the DB cluster's security group. Specify the EC2 instances' security group as the source over the default Aurora port.","D":"Add an outbound rule to the DB cluster's security group. Specify the EC2 instances' security group as the destination over the default Aurora port.","E":"Add an outbound rule to the DB cluster's security group. Specify the EC2 instances' security group as the destination over the ephemeral ports."},"options_zh":{"A":"将入站规则添加到 EC2 实例的安全组。将数据库集群的安全组指定为默认 Aurora 端口上的源。","B":"将出站规则添加到 EC2 实例的安全组。将数据库集群的安全组指定为默认 Aurora 端口上的目标。","C":"将入站规则添加到数据库集群的安全组。将 EC2 实例的安全组指定为默认 Aurora 端口上的源。","D":"将出站规则添加到数据库集群的安全组。将 EC2 实例的安全组指定为默认 Aurora 端口上的目标。","E":"将出站规则添加到数据库集群的安全组。将 EC2 实例的安全组指定为临时端口上的目标。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BC":77,"AC":23},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Security groups are stateful, so once a connection is allowed in one direction, return traffic is automatically permitted without an explicit rule. The EC2 instances initiate the connection TO the Aurora DB cluster on the default Aurora port (3306 for MySQL-compatible, 5432 for PostgreSQL-compatible). Least privilege therefore requires an OUTBOUND rule on the EC2 security group whose destination is the DB cluster's security group over the Aurora port (B), and an INBOUND rule on the DB cluster's security group whose source is the EC2 security group over the Aurora port (C). This is exactly the rule pair AWS itself creates with RDS/Aurora automatic EC2 connectivity: an inbound rule on the database SG referencing the EC2 SG and an outbound rule on the EC2 SG referencing the database SG. Referencing security groups (rather than CIDR ranges) is the least-privilege approach. The dump's suggested A,B is wrong because A points an inbound rule at the EC2 instances on the Aurora port, which is the wrong direction.","explanation_zh":"Security group 是有狀態的 (stateful)，因此一旦某個方向的連線被允許，回程流量會自動被放行，不需要額外規則。EC2 instances 主動向 Aurora DB cluster 在預設 Aurora port (MySQL 相容為 3306、PostgreSQL 相容為 5432) 發起連線。基於最小權限原則，需要在 EC2 security group 加入一條 OUTBOUND 規則，目的地為 DB cluster 的 security group，使用 Aurora port (B)；並在 DB cluster 的 security group 加入一條 INBOUND 規則，來源為 EC2 的 security group，使用 Aurora port (C)。這正是 AWS 在 RDS/Aurora 自動 EC2 連線功能中所建立的規則組合：資料庫 SG 上一條以 EC2 SG 為來源的 inbound 規則，以及 EC2 SG 上一條以資料庫 SG 為目的地的 outbound 規則。以 security group 互相參照 (而非 CIDR) 是最小權限做法。Dump 建議的 A,B 是錯的，因為 A 把 inbound 規則放到 EC2 端的 Aurora port，方向相反。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Wrong direction. This adds an inbound rule to the EC2 SG on the Aurora port, implying something connects to the EC2 instances on the DB port. The EC2 instances are the clients that initiate outbound connections to Aurora, so they need an outbound rule, not an inbound DB-port rule.","why_zh":"方向錯誤。這是在 EC2 SG 加入 Aurora port 的 inbound 規則，等於允許別人從 DB port 連到 EC2。EC2 是主動向 Aurora 發起連線的用戶端，需要的是 outbound 規則，而非 DB port 的 inbound 規則。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Not needed. Security groups are stateful, so the DB cluster's response traffic back to the EC2 instances is automatically allowed by the inbound rule that permitted the request. Adding an explicit outbound rule on the DB SG over the Aurora port is unnecessary (and the port would be wrong anyway).","why_zh":"不需要。Security group 有狀態，DB cluster 回給 EC2 的回程流量會因為放行請求的 inbound 規則而自動被允許。在 DB SG 額外加 Aurora port 的 outbound 規則是多餘的 (而且 port 也不對)。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Not needed. This describes a stateless construct (allowing return traffic on ephemeral ports), which applies to network ACLs, not security groups. Because security groups are stateful, no ephemeral-port outbound rule on the DB SG is required.","why_zh":"不需要。這描述的是無狀態 (stateless) 的做法 (用 ephemeral ports 放行回程流量)，適用於 network ACL 而非 security group。因為 security group 有狀態，DB SG 不需要 ephemeral port 的 outbound 規則。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/ec2-rds-connect.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/security-group-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/Overview.RDSSecurityGroups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_VPC.Scenarios.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・複選"},{"id":88,"question_en":"A company wants to change its internal cloud billing strategy for each of its business units. Currently, the cloud governance team shares reports for overall cloud spending with the head of each business unit. The company uses AWS Organizations to manage the separate AWS accounts for each business unit. The existing tagging standard in Organizations includes the application, environment, and owner. The cloud governance team wants a centralized solution so each business unit receives monthly reports on its cloud spending. The solution should also send notifications for any cloud spending that exceeds a set threshold. Which solution is the MOST cost-effective way to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望更改其每个业务部门的内部云计费策略。目前，云治理团队与每个业务部门的负责人共享总体云支出的报告。该公司 使用 AWS Organizations 管理每个业务部门的单独 AWS 账户。组织中现有的标记标准包括应用程序、环境和所有者。云治理团队需要 一个集中式解决方案，以便每个业务部门都能收到有关其云支出的月度报告。该解决方案还应该针对任何超过设定阈值的云支出发 送通知。 哪种解决方案是满足这些要求的最具成本效益的方式？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS Budgets in each account and configure budget alerts that are grouped by application, environment, and owner. Add each business unit to an Amazon SNS topic for each alert. Use Cost Explorer in each account to create monthly reports for each business unit.","B":"Configure AWS Budgets in the organization's management account and configure budget alerts that are grouped by application, environment, and owner. Add each business unit to an Amazon SNS topic for each alert. Use Cost Explorer in the organization's management account to create monthly reports for each business unit.","C":"Configure AWS Budgets in each account and configure budget alerts that are grouped by application, environment, and owner. Add each business unit to an Amazon SNS topic for each alert. Use the AWS Billing and Cost Management dashboard in each account to create monthly reports for each business unit.","D":"Enable AWS Cost and Usage Reports in the organization's management account and configure reports grouped by application, environment. and owner. Create an AWS Lambda function that processes AWS Cost and Usage Reports, sends budget alerts, and sends monthly reports to each business unit's email list."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个账户中配置 AWS 预算，并配置按应用程序、环境和所有者分组的预算警报。将每个业务部门添加到每个警报的 Amazon SNS 主题。在每个账户中使用 Cost Explorer 为每个业务部门创建月度报告。","B":"在组织的管理账户中配置 AWS 预算，并配置按应用程序、环境和所有者分组的预算警报。将每个业务部门添加到每个警报的 Amazon SNS 主题。在组织的管理账户中使用 Cost Explorer 为每个业务部门创建月度报告。","C":"在每个账户中配置 AWS 预算，并配置按应用程序、环境和所有者分组的预算警报。将每个业务部门添加到每个警报的 Amazon SNS 主题。使用每个账户中的 AWS Billing and Cost Management 仪表板为每个业务部门创建每月报告。","D":"在组织的管理账户中启用 AWS 成本和使用情况报告，并配置按应用程序、环境分组的报告。和所有者。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于处理 AWS 成本和使用情况报告、发送预算警报以及向每个业务部门的电子邮件列表发送每月报告。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":89,"question_en":"A company is using AWS CloudFormation to deploy its infrastructure. The company is concerned that, if a production CloudFormation stack is deleted, important data stored in Amazon RDS databases or Amazon EBS volumes might also be deleted. How can the company prevent users from accidentally deleting data in this way?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署其基礎架構。該公司擔心如果生產環境的 CloudFormation 堆疊被刪除，儲存在 Amazon RDS 資料庫或 Amazon EBS 磁碟區中的重要資料也可能一併被刪除。該公司如何防止使用者以此方式意外刪除資料？","options_en":{"A":"Modify the CloudFormation templates to add a DeletionPolicy attribute to RDS and EBS resources.","B":"Configure a stack policy that disallows the deletion of RDS and EBS resources.","C":"Modify IAM policies lo deny deleting RDS and EBS resources that are tagged with an \"aws:cloudformation:stack-name\" tag.","D":"Use AWS Config rules to prevent deleting RDS and EBS resources."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改 CloudFormation 範本，為 RDS 與 EBS 資源新增 DeletionPolicy 屬性。","B":"設定一個堆疊政策（stack policy），禁止刪除 RDS 與 EBS 資源。","C":"修改 IAM 政策，拒絕刪除標記有「aws:cloudformation:stack-name」標籤的 RDS 與 EBS 資源。","D":"使用 AWS Config 規則來防止刪除 RDS 與 EBS 資源。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":85,"B":15},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":90,"question_en":"A company has VPC ­ow logs enabled for Its NAT gateway. The company is seeing Action = ACCEPT for inbound tra®c that comes from public IP address 198.51.100.2 destined for a private Amazon EC2 instance. A solutions architect must determine whether the tra®c represents unsolicited inbound connections from the internet. The first two octets of the VPC CIDR block are 203.0. Which set of steps should the solutions architect take to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司已為其 NAT 閘道啟用 VPC 流程日誌（VPC flow logs）。該公司發現來自公開 IP 位址 198.51.100.2、目的地為私有 Amazon EC2 執行個體的傳入流量顯示 Action = ACCEPT。解決方案架構師必須判定這些流量是否代表來自網際網路的未經授權傳入連線。該 VPC CIDR 區塊的前兩個八位元組（octet）為 203.0。解決方案架構師應採取哪些步驟來滿足此需求？","options_en":{"A":"Open the AWS CloudTrail console. Select the log group that contains the NAT gateway's elastic network interface and the private instance's elastic network interlace. Run a query to filter with the destination address set as \"like 203.0\" and the source address set as \"like 198.51.100.2\". Run the stats command to filter the sum of bytes transferred by the source address and the destination address.","B":"Open the Amazon CloudWatch console. Select the log group that contains the NAT gateway's elastic network interface and the private instance's elastic network interface. Run a query to filter with the destination address set as \"like 203.0\" and the source address set as \"like 198.51.100.2\". Run the stats command to filter the sum of bytes transferred by the source address and the destination address.","C":"Open the AWS CloudTrail console. Select the log group that contains the NAT gateway's elastic network interface and the private instance’s elastic network interface. Run a query to filter with the destination address set as \"like 198.51.100.2\" and the source address set as \"like 203.0\". Run the stats command to filter the sum of bytes transferred by the source address and the destination address.","D":"Open the Amazon CloudWatch console. Select the log group that contains the NAT gateway's elastic network interface and the private instance's elastic network interface. Run a query to filter with the destination address set as \"like 198.51.100.2\" and the source address set as \"like 203.0\". Run the stats command to filter the sum of bytes transferred by the source address and the destination address."},"options_zh":{"A":"開啟 AWS CloudTrail 主控台。選取包含該 NAT 閘道彈性網路介面與該私有執行個體彈性網路介面的日誌群組。執行查詢，篩選目的地位址「like 203.0」且來源位址「like 198.51.100.2」。執行 stats 指令，篩選來源位址與目的地位址間傳輸的位元組總和。","B":"開啟 Amazon CloudWatch 主控台。選取包含該 NAT 閘道彈性網路介面與該私有執行個體彈性網路介面的日誌群組。執行查詢，篩選目的地位址「like 203.0」且來源位址「like 198.51.100.2」。執行 stats 指令，篩選來源位址與目的地位址間傳輸的位元組總和。","C":"開啟 AWS CloudTrail 主控台。選取包含該 NAT 閘道彈性網路介面與該私有執行個體彈性網路介面的日誌群組。執行查詢，篩選目的地位址「like 198.51.100.2」且來源位址「like 203.0」。執行 stats 指令，篩選來源位址與目的地位址間傳輸的位元組總和。","D":"開啟 Amazon CloudWatch 主控台。選取包含該 NAT 閘道彈性網路介面與該私有執行個體彈性網路介面的日誌群組。執行查詢，篩選目的地位址「like 198.51.100.2」且來源位址「like 203.0」。執行 stats 指令，篩選來源位址與目的地位址間傳輸的位元組總和。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":67,"D":33},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"VPC Flow Logs publish network traffic records to Amazon CloudWatch Logs (or S3), and you query them with CloudWatch Logs Insights using filter/stats commands. AWS CloudTrail records management/API activity, not packet-level network flows, so options A and C are wrong on the console alone. That leaves B vs D, which differ only in the source/destination filter direction. The scenario describes INBOUND traffic from public IP 198.51.100.2 destined for the private EC2 instance in the VPC whose CIDR begins 203.0. In the flow log record for that inbound packet, srcaddr is the external public IP (198.51.100.2) and dstaddr is the internal VPC address (203.0.x.x). To investigate whether this is unsolicited inbound traffic you must filter destination 'like 203.0' and source 'like 198.51.100.2', which is exactly option B. Option D reverses these (destination 198.51.100.2, source 203.0), which would describe OUTBOUND traffic from the VPC to that IP (a solicited response), not the inbound connection in question.","explanation_zh":"VPC Flow Logs 會將網路流量記錄發佈到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs（或 S3），並使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 的 filter/stats 指令查詢。AWS CloudTrail 記錄的是管理/API 活動，而非封包層級的網路流量，因此選項 A 與 C 光是用錯主控台就不正確。剩下 B 與 D，兩者僅在來源/目的地過濾方向上不同。情境描述的是來自公網 IP 198.51.100.2 的「入站」流量，目的地是 VPC（CIDR 開頭為 203.0）中的私有 EC2 執行個體。對該入站封包的 flow log 記錄而言，srcaddr 是外部公網 IP（198.51.100.2），dstaddr 是內部 VPC 位址（203.0.x.x）。要判斷這是否為未經請求的入站流量，必須過濾 destination 'like 203.0' 且 source 'like 198.51.100.2'，這正是選項 B。選項 D 將兩者顛倒（destination 198.51.100.2、source 203.0），描述的是從 VPC 流向該 IP 的「出站」流量（已被請求的回應），而非問題所指的入站連線。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses the AWS CloudTrail console; CloudTrail records API/management events, not VPC packet-level flow logs. Flow logs are queried in CloudWatch Logs. Also reverses src/dst.","why_zh":"使用 AWS CloudTrail 主控台；CloudTrail 記錄 API/管理事件，而非 VPC 封包層級的 flow logs。Flow logs 應在 CloudWatch Logs 中查詢。且來源/目的地也顛倒。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Wrong console (CloudTrail instead of CloudWatch) and the filter reverses source/destination (destination 198.51.100.2, source 203.0), describing outbound rather than the inbound traffic in question.","why_zh":"主控台錯誤（用 CloudTrail 而非 CloudWatch），且過濾的來源/目的地顛倒（destination 198.51.100.2、source 203.0），描述的是出站而非問題所指的入站流量。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Correct console (CloudWatch) but the filter direction is reversed: destination 198.51.100.2 and source 203.0 would match outbound traffic from the VPC to that IP (a solicited response), not the inbound connection from 198.51.100.2 to the private instance.","why_zh":"主控台正確（CloudWatch），但過濾方向顛倒：destination 198.51.100.2、source 203.0 會比對到從 VPC 流向該 IP 的出站流量（已被請求的回應），而非從 198.51.100.2 到私有執行個體的入站連線。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/flow-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/view-flow-log-records-cwl.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/flow-logs-records-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_QuerySyntax-examples.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":91,"question_en":"A company consists or two separate business units. Each business unit has its own AWS account within a single organization in AWS Organizations. The business units regularly share sensitive documents with each other. To facilitate sharing, the company created an Amazon S3 bucket in each account and configured low-way replication between the S3 buckets. The S3 buckets have millions of objects. Recently, a security audit identified that neither S3 bucket has encryption at rest enabled. Company policy requires that all documents must be stored with encryption at rest. The company wants to implement server-side encryption with Amazon S3 managed encryption keys (SSE- S3). What is the MOST operationally e®cient solution that meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司由兩個獨立的業務單位組成。每個業務單位在同一個 AWS Organizations 組織中擁有各自的 AWS 帳戶。這些業務單位經常互相分享敏感文件。為方便分享，該公司在每個帳戶中建立了一個 Amazon S3 儲存桶，並在這些 S3 儲存桶間設定了雙向複製。這些 S3 儲存桶擁有數百萬個物件。近期一次安全稽核發現，這兩個 S3 儲存桶都未啟用靜態加密（encryption at rest）。公司政策要求所有文件都必須以靜態加密方式儲存。該公司希望使用 Amazon S3 受管加密金鑰（SSE-S3）實作伺服器端加密。哪個解決方案是滿足這些需求最具運維效率的方式？","options_en":{"A":"Turn on SSE-S3 on both S3 buckets. Use S3 Batch Operations to copy and encrypt the objects in the same location.","B":"Create an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key in each account. Turn on server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS) on each S3 bucket by using the corresponding KMS key in that AWS account. Encrypt the existing objects by using an S3 copy command in the AWS CLI.","C":"Turn on SSE-S3 on both S3 buckets. Encrypt the existing objects by using an S3 copy command in the AWS CLI.","D":"Create an AWS Key Management Service, (AWS KMS) key in each account. Turn on server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS) on each S3 bucket by using the corresponding KMS key in that AWS account. Use S3 Batch Operations to copy the objects into the same location."},"options_zh":{"A":"在兩個 S3 儲存桶上開啟 SSE-S3。使用 S3 Batch Operations 在原位置複製並加密這些物件。","B":"在每個帳戶中建立一個 AWS Key Management Service（AWS KMS）金鑰。使用該帳戶對應的 KMS 金鑰，在每個 S3 儲存桶上開啟使用 AWS KMS 金鑰的伺服器端加密（SSE-KMS）。使用 AWS CLI 中的 S3 複製指令加密現有物件。","C":"在兩個 S3 儲存桶上開啟 SSE-S3。使用 AWS CLI 中的 S3 複製指令加密現有物件。","D":"在每個帳戶中建立一個 AWS Key Management Service（AWS KMS）金鑰。使用該帳戶對應的 KMS 金鑰，在每個 S3 儲存桶上開啟使用 AWS KMS 金鑰的伺服器端加密（SSE-KMS）。使用 S3 Batch Operations 將物件複製到原位置。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":90},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Company policy requires SSE-S3 specifically, so the SSE-KMS options (B and D) are over-engineered: they add per-account KMS keys, KMS RPS quotas, key management, and cross-account key-permission complexity for the existing bi-directional replication, increasing operational overhead rather than reducing it. Turning on SSE-S3 default encryption only affects NEW objects; per AWS docs, 'There is no change to the encryption of the objects that existed in the bucket before default encryption was enabled,' so the millions of existing objects must be rewritten (copied) to become encrypted. The decision between A and C is the qualifier MOST operationally efficient. S3 Batch Operations (A) is a fully managed, serverless, auditable service that can copy/re-encrypt billions of objects with automatic manifest generation, progress tracking, retries, notifications, and a completion report. Scripting an AWS CLI copy across millions of objects (C) requires the operator to enumerate objects, run and babysit the job on a host, and handle errors/retries manually, which is far more operational effort at this scale. Therefore A is the most operationally efficient way to encrypt the existing objects with SSE-S3.","explanation_zh":"公司政策明確要求使用 SSE-S3，因此採用 SSE-KMS 的選項（B 與 D）屬於過度設計：它們為每個帳戶新增 KMS key、受 KMS RPS 配額限制、需要金鑰管理，並對現有的雙向 replication 增加跨帳戶金鑰權限的複雜度，反而提高而非降低營運負擔。開啟 SSE-S3 預設加密只會影響新物件；根據 AWS 文件，『啟用預設加密之前已存在於 bucket 中的物件其加密狀態不會改變』，因此數百萬個既有物件必須被重新寫入（copy）才能變成已加密。A 與 C 的取捨在於『最具營運效率（MOST operationally efficient）』這個限定詞。S3 Batch Operations（A）是完全受管、無伺服器、可稽核的服務，能對數十億物件執行 copy/重新加密，並自動產生 manifest、追蹤進度、重試、發送通知並提供完成報告。對數百萬物件以 AWS CLI copy 指令逐一處理（C），需要操作者自行列舉物件、在主機上執行並照看任務、手動處理錯誤與重試，在此規模下營運成本高出許多。因此 A 是以 SSE-S3 加密既有物件最具營運效率的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Uses SSE-KMS, but policy requires SSE-S3. Per-account KMS keys add key management, cross-account key permissions for the existing replication, and KMS request quotas. Also, scripting a CLI copy across millions of objects is far less operationally efficient than Batch Operations.","why_zh":"使用 SSE-KMS，但政策要求 SSE-S3。每帳戶 KMS key 會增加金鑰管理、現有 replication 的跨帳戶金鑰權限以及 KMS 請求配額。且以 CLI copy 腳本處理數百萬物件，營運效率遠不如 Batch Operations。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Correctly chooses SSE-S3 but uses an AWS CLI copy command to encrypt millions of existing objects. At that scale this requires manual object enumeration, running/monitoring on a host, and manual retry/error handling, which is much higher operational overhead than the managed, auditable S3 Batch Operations approach in A.","why_zh":"正確選擇 SSE-S3，但以 AWS CLI copy 指令加密數百萬既有物件。在此規模下需手動列舉物件、在主機上執行與監控、並手動處理重試與錯誤，營運負擔遠高於 A 中受管且可稽核的 S3 Batch Operations。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Uses SSE-KMS instead of the required SSE-S3, adding per-account KMS keys, cross-account key-permission complexity for bi-directional replication, and KMS quotas. It is over-engineered relative to the stated requirement even though it correctly uses Batch Operations.","why_zh":"使用 SSE-KMS 而非要求的 SSE-S3，並為每帳戶新增 KMS key、為雙向 replication 增加跨帳戶金鑰權限複雜度以及 KMS 配額。雖正確使用 Batch Operations，但相對於需求仍屬過度設計。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/default-bucket-encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/batch-ops.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/UsingServerSideEncryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/batch-ops-copy-object.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":92,"question_en":"A company is running an application in the AWS Cloud. The application collects and stores a large amount of unstructured data in an Amazon S3 bucket. The S3 bucket contains several terabytes of data and uses the S3 Standard storage class. The data increases in size by several gigabytes every day. The company needs to query and analyze the data. The company does not access data that is more than 1 year old. However, the company must retain all the data indefinitely for compliance reasons. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 云中运行应用程序。该应用程序收集大量非结构化数据并将其存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。S3 存储桶包含数 TB 的数据并使用 S3 标准存储类别。数据的大小每天都会增加几千兆字节。 公司需要对数据进行查询和分析。该公司不会访问超过 1 年的数据。然而，出于合规原因，公司必须无限期保留所有数据。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use S3 Select to query the data. Create an S3 Lifecycle policy to transition data that is more than 1 year old to S3 Glacier Deep Archive.","B":"Use Amazon Redshift Spectrum to query the data. Create an S3 Lifecycle policy to transition data that is more than 1 year old 10 S3 Glacier Deep Archive.","C":"Use an AWS Glue Data Catalog and Amazon Athena to query the data. Create an S3 Lifecycle policy to transition data that is more than 1 year old to S3 Glacier Deep Archive.","D":"Use Amazon Redshift Spectrum to query the data. Create an S3 Lifecycle policy to transition data that is more than 1 year old to S3 Intelligent-Tiering."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用S3 Select查询数据。创建 S3 生命周期策略，将 1 年以上的数据转移到 S3 Glacier Deep Archive。","B":"使用 Amazon Redshift Spectrum 查询数据。创建 S3 生命周期策略以转换 1 年以上的数据 10 S3 Glacier Deep Archive。","C":"使用 AWS Glue 数据目录和 Amazon Athena 查询数据。创建 S3 生命周期策略，将 1 年以上的数据转移到 S3 Glacier Deep Archive。","D":"使用 Amazon Redshift Spectrum 查询数据。创建 S3 生命周期策略以将 1 年以上的数据转换到 S3 智能分层。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":92},"tags":["Storage","Database","Cost Optimization","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to query/analyze several terabytes of unstructured data spread across many S3 objects (growing daily), while transitioning data older than 1 year (never accessed) to the cheapest storage and retaining everything indefinitely for compliance. AWS Glue Data Catalog plus Amazon Athena is the canonical serverless, pay-per-query pattern for analyzing large datasets in S3 at TB scale with no cluster to provision, making it the most cost-effective query option. S3 Glacier Deep Archive is the lowest-cost storage class, appropriate for data that is known to never be accessed but must be retained for compliance. Option A fails because S3 Select can query only one object per request (it cannot analyze a multi-TB, multi-object dataset), is no longer available to new customers, and explicitly cannot query objects stored in S3 Glacier Deep Archive, so its own query mechanism would break on the archived data. Redshift Spectrum (B/D) requires a provisioned, running Redshift cluster, which is more expensive than serverless Athena, and D additionally uses Intelligent-Tiering (for unknown/changing access patterns) instead of Deep Archive, which is more costly for data known to be cold.","explanation_zh":"需求是查詢與分析散布於眾多 S3 物件、且每日成長的數 TB 非結構化資料，同時把超過一年（不再存取）的資料轉移到最便宜的儲存層，並為合規無限期保留全部資料。AWS Glue Data Catalog 搭配 Amazon Athena 是分析 S3 大型資料集的標準無伺服器、按查詢計費模式，TB 等級不需佈建任何叢集，因此是最具成本效益的查詢方案。S3 Glacier Deep Archive 是成本最低的儲存類別，適合已知不再存取但須為合規保留的資料。選項 A 不可行：S3 Select 每次請求只能查詢單一物件（無法分析跨多物件的數 TB 資料集），且已不開放新客戶使用，更明確規定無法查詢儲存在 S3 Glacier Deep Archive 的物件，因此其查詢機制在封存資料上會失效。Redshift Spectrum（B/D）需要佈建並持續運行的 Redshift 叢集，成本高於無伺服器的 Athena；而 D 還用 Intelligent-Tiering（適用於未知或變動的存取模式）取代 Deep Archive，對已知冷資料而言成本更高。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"S3 Select queries only one object per request and cannot analyze a multi-TB, multi-object dataset; it is no longer available to new customers; and it explicitly cannot query objects in S3 Glacier Deep Archive, so after the lifecycle transition the query tool would not work on the archived data.","why_zh":"S3 Select 每次請求僅能查詢單一物件，無法分析跨多物件的數 TB 資料集；已不開放新客戶使用；且明確無法查詢 S3 Glacier Deep Archive 中的物件，故生命週期轉移後查詢工具對封存資料失效。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Storage tier is correct (Glacier Deep Archive), but Redshift Spectrum requires a provisioned, continuously running Redshift cluster, which costs more than serverless pay-per-query Athena, so it is not the MOST cost-effective.","why_zh":"儲存層正確（Glacier Deep Archive），但 Redshift Spectrum 需要佈建並持續運行的 Redshift 叢集，成本高於無伺服器按查詢計費的 Athena，因此不是最具成本效益的選項。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Both legs are weaker: Redshift Spectrum needs a running cluster (costlier than Athena), and S3 Intelligent-Tiering targets unknown/changing access patterns; for data known to never be accessed after 1 year, Glacier Deep Archive is far cheaper.","why_zh":"兩個面向都較弱：Redshift Spectrum 需要運行中的叢集（成本高於 Athena），而 S3 Intelligent-Tiering 針對未知或變動的存取模式；對於已知一年後不再存取的資料，Glacier Deep Archive 便宜得多。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/selecting-content-from-objects.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/querying-athena-tables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/storage-class-intro.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/glacier-storage-classes.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":93,"question_en":"A video processing company wants to build a machine learning (ML) model by using 600 TB of compressed data that is stored as thousands of files in the company's on-premises network attached storage system. The company does not have the necessary compute resources on premises for ML experiments and wants to use AWS. The company needs to complete the data transfer to AWS within 3 weeks. The data transfer will be a one-time transfer. The data must be encrypted in transit. The measured upload speed of the company's internet connection is 100 Mbps. and multiple departments share the connection. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家视频处理公司希望使用 600 TB 的压缩数据构建机器学习 (ML) 模型，这些数据在公司的本地网络附加存储系统中存储为数千个 文件。该公司没有本地进行 ML 实验所需的计算资源，因此希望使用 AWS。 该公司需要在3周内完成数据传输到AWS。数据传输将是一次性传输。数据在传输过程中必须加密。测得该公司互联网连接的上传速 度为100 Mbps。并且多个部门共享连接。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Order several AWS Snowball Edge Storage Optimized devices by using the AWS Management Console. Configure the devices with a destination S3 bucket. Copy the data to the devices. Ship the devices back to AWS.","B":"Set up a 10 Gbps AWS Direct Connect connection between the company location and the nearest AWS Region. Transfer the data over a VPN connection into the Region to store the data in Amazon S3.","C":"Create a VPN connection between the on-premises network attached storage and the nearest AWS Region. Transfer the data over the VPN connection.","D":"Deploy an AWS Storage Gateway file gateway on premises. Configure the file gateway with a destination S3 bucket. Copy the data to the file gateway."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS 管理控制台订购多个 AWS Snowball Edge Storage Optimized 设备。使用目标 S3 存储桶配置设备。将数据复制到设 备。将设备运回 AWS。","B":"在公司地点和最近的 AWS 区域之间建立 10 Gbps AWS Direct Connect 连接。通过 VPN 连接将数据传输到区域以将数据存储在 Amazon S3 中。","C":"在本地网络附加存储和最近的 AWS 区域之间创建 VPN 连接。通过 VPN 连接传输数据。","D":"在本地部署 AWS Storage Gateway 文件网关。使用目标 S3 存储桶配置文件网关。将数据复制到文件网关。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Security/IAM","Storage","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":94,"question_en":"A company has migrated Its forms-processing application to AWS. When users interact with the application, they upload scanned forms as files through a web application. A database stores user metadata and references to files that are stored in Amazon S3. The web application runs on Amazon EC2 instances and an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database. When forms are uploaded, the application sends notifications to a team through Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS). A team member then logs in and processes each form. The team member performs data validation on the form and extracts relevant data before entering the information into another system that uses an API. A solutions architect needs to automate the manual processing of the forms. The solution must provide accurate form extraction. minimize time to market, and minimize tong-term operational overhead. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司已将其表单处理应用程序迁移到 AWS。当用户与应用程序交互时，他们通过 Web 应用程序将扫描的表单作为文件上传。数 据库存储用户元数据以及对 Amazon S3 中存储的文件的引用。Web 应用程序在 Amazon EC2 实例和 Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL 数据 库上运行。 上传表单后，应用程序通过 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 向团队发送通知。然后，团队成员登录并处理每个表 单。团队成员在将信息输入到使用 API 的另一个系统之前，对表单执行数据验证并提取相关数据。 解决方案架构师需要自动化表单的手动处理。该解决方案必须提供准确的表单提取。最大限度地缩短上市时间，并最大限度地减少 长期运营费用。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Develop custom libraries to perform optical character recognition (OCR) on the forms. Deploy the libraries to an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster as an application tier. Use this tier to process the forms when forms are uploaded. Store the output in Amazon S3. Parse this output by extracting the data into an Amazon DynamoDB table. Submit the data to the target system's APL. Host the new application tier on EC2 instances.","B":"Extend the system with an application tier that uses AWS Step Functions and AWS Lambda. Configure this tier to use artificial intelligence and machine learning (AI/ML) models that are trained and hosted on an EC2 instance to perform optical character recognition (OCR) on the forms when forms are uploaded. Store the output in Amazon S3. Parse this output by extracting the data that is required within the application tier. Submit the data to the target system's API.","C":"Host a new application tier on EC2 instances. Use this tier to call endpoints that host artificial intelligence and machine teaming (AI/ML) models that are trained and hosted in Amazon SageMaker to perform optical character recognition (OCR) on the forms. Store the output in Amazon ElastiCache. Parse this output by extracting the data that is required within the application tier. Submit the data to the target system's API.","D":"Extend the system with an application tier that uses AWS Step Functions and AWS Lambda. Configure this tier to use Amazon Textract and Amazon Comprehend to perform optical character recognition (OCR) on the forms when forms are uploaded. Store the output in Amazon S3. Parse this output by extracting the data that is required within the application tier. Submit the data to the target system's API."},"options_zh":{"A":"开发自定义库以在表单上执行光学字符识别 (OCR)。将库作为应用程序层部署到 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 集群。上传表单时使用此层处理表单。将输出存储在 Amazon S3 中。通过将数据提取到 Amazon DynamoDB 表中来解析此输 出。将数据提交到目标系统的 APL。在 EC2 实例上托管新的应用程序层。","B":"通过使用 AWS Step Functions 和 AWS Lambda 的应用程序层扩展系统。配置此层以使用在 EC2 实例上训练和托管的人工智能和 机器学习 (AI/ML) 模型，以便在上传表单时对表单执行光学字符识别 (OCR)。将输出存储在 Amazon S3 中。通过提取应用程序层 所需的数据来解析此输出。将数据提交到目标系统的API。","C":"在 EC2 实例上托管新的应用程序层。使用此层调用托管在 Amazon SageMaker 中训练和托管的人工智能和机器组合 (AI/ML) 模 型的终端节点，以在表单上执行光学字符识别 (OCR)。将输出存储在 Amazon ElastiCache 中。通过提取应用程序层中所需的数据 来解析此输出。将数据提交到目标系统的API。","D":"通过使用 AWS Step Functions 和 AWS Lambda 的应用程序层扩展系统。配置此层以在上传表单时使用 Amazon Textract 和 Amazon Comprehend 对表单执行光学字符识别 (OCR)。将输出存储在 Amazon S3 中。通过提取应用程序层所需的数据来解析此输 出。将数据提交到目标系统的API。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":95,"question_en":"A company is refactoring its on-premises order-processing platform in the AWS Cloud. The platform includes a web front end that is hosted on a ­eet of VMs, RabbitMQ to connect the front end to the backend, and a Kubernetes cluster to run a containerized backend system to process the orders. The company does not want to make any major changes to the application. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在將其內部部署的訂單處理平台重構至 AWS 雲端。該平台包括一個運行於一組 VM 上的網頁前端、用於連接前端與後端的 RabbitMQ，以及一個運行容器化後端系統以處理訂單的 Kubernetes 叢集。該公司不希望對應用程式做出任何重大變更。哪個解決方案能以最少的運維負擔滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AMI of the web server VM. Create an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group that uses the AMI and an Application Load Balancer. Set up Amazon MQ to replace the on-premises messaging queue. Configure Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) to host the order-processing backend.","B":"Create a custom AWS Lambda runtime to mimic the web server environment. Create an Amazon API Gateway API to replace the front- end web servers. Set up Amazon MQ to replace the on-premises messaging queue. Configure Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) to host the order-processing backend.","C":"Create an AMI of the web server VM. Create an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group that uses the AMI and an Application Load Balancer. Set up Amazon MQ to replace the on-premises messaging queue. Install Kubernetes on a ­eet of different EC2 instances to host the order-processing backend.","D":"Create an AMI of the web server VM. Create an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group that uses the AMI and an Application Load Balancer. Set up an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue to replace the on-premises messaging queue. Configure Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) to host the order-processing backend."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立網頁伺服器 VM 的 AMI。建立一個使用該 AMI 與 Application Load Balancer 的 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 群組。設定 Amazon MQ 以取代內部部署的訊息佇列。設定 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service（Amazon EKS）以承載訂單處理後端。","B":"建立一個自訂 AWS Lambda 執行環境（runtime）以模擬網頁伺服器環境。建立一個 Amazon API Gateway API 以取代前端網頁伺服器。設定 Amazon MQ 以取代內部部署的訊息佇列。設定 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service（Amazon EKS）以承載訂單處理後端。","C":"建立網頁伺服器 VM 的 AMI。建立一個使用該 AMI 與 Application Load Balancer 的 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 群組。設定 Amazon MQ 以取代內部部署的訊息佇列。在一組不同的 EC2 執行個體上安裝 Kubernetes 以承載訂單處理後端。","D":"建立網頁伺服器 VM 的 AMI。建立一個使用該 AMI 與 Application Load Balancer 的 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 群組。設定 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）佇列以取代內部部署的訊息佇列。設定 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service（Amazon EKS）以承載訂單處理後端。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":93},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":96,"question_en":"A solutions architect needs to implement a client-side encryption mechanism for objects that will be stored in a new Amazon S3 bucket. The solutions architect created a CMK that is stored in AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) for this purpose. The solutions architect created the following IAM policy and attached it to an IAM role: During tests, the solutions architect was able to successfully get existing test objects in the S3 bucket. However, attempts to upload a new object resulted in an error message. The error message stated that the action was forbidden. Which action must the solutions architect add to the IAM policy to meet all the requirements?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师需要为将存储在新 Amazon S3 存储桶中的对象实施客户端加密机制。为此，解决方案架构师创建了一个存储在 AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) 中的 CMK。 解决方案架构师创建了以下 IAM 策略并将其附加到 IAM 角色： 在测试期间，解决方案架构师能够成功获取 S3 存储桶中的现有测试对象。但是，尝试上传新对象会导致错误消息。错误消息指出该 操作被禁止。 解决方案架构师必须将哪些操作添加到 IAM 策略才能满足所有要求？ A.kms :生成数据密钥 B.kms :GetKeyPolicy C.kms :GetPublicKey D.kms ：标志","options_en":{"A":"kms:GenerateDataKey","B":"kms:GetKeyPolicy","C":"kms:GetPublicKey","D":"kms:Sign"},"options_zh":{},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":97,"question_en":"A company has developed a web application. The company is hosting the application on a group of Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer. The company wants to improve the security posture of the application and plans to use AWS WAF web ACLs. The solution must not adversely affect legitimate tra®c to the application. How should a solutions architect configure the web ACLs to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司开发了一个网络应用程序。该公司将该应用程序托管在应用程序负载均衡器后面的一组 Amazon EC2 实例上。该公司希望 改善应用程序的安全状况，并计划使用 AWS WAF Web ACL。该解决方案不得对应用程序的合法流量产生不利影响。 解决方案架构师应如何配置 Web ACL 以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set the action of the web ACL rules to Count. Enable AWS WAF logging. Analyze the requests for false positives. Modify the rules to avoid any false positive. Over time, change the action of the web ACL rules from Count to Block.","B":"Use only rate-based rules in the web ACLs, and set the throttle limit as high as possible. Temporarily block all requests that exceed the limit. Define nested rules to narrow the scope of the rate tracking.","C":"Set the action of the web ACL rules to Block. Use only AWS managed rule groups in the web ACLs. Evaluate the rule groups by using Amazon CloudWatch metrics with AWS WAF sampled requests or AWS WAF logs.","D":"Use only custom rule groups in the web ACLs, and set the action to Allow. Enable AWS WAF logging. Analyze the requests for false positives. Modify the rules to avoid any false positive. Over time, change the action of the web ACL rules from Allow to Block."},"options_zh":{"A":"将Web ACL 规则的操作设置为“计数”。启用 AWS WAF 日志记录。分析误报请求。修改规则以避免任何误报。随着时间的推移， 将 Web ACL 规则的操作从计数更改为阻止。","B":"在 Web ACL 中仅使用基于速率的规则，并将限制设置得尽可能高。暂时阻止所有超出限制的请求。定义嵌套规则以缩小速率 跟踪的范围。","C":"将Web ACL 规则的操作设置为阻止。仅在 Web ACL 中使用 AWS 托管规则组。通过将 Amazon CloudWatch 指标与 AWS WAF 采样 请求或 AWS WAF 日志结合使用来评估规则组。","D":"仅使用 Web ACL 中的自定义规则组，并将操作设置为允许。启用 AWS WAF 日志记录。分析误报请求。修改规则以避免任何误 报。随着时间的推移，将 Web ACL 规则的操作从允许更改为阻止。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":98,"question_en":"A company has an organization that has many AWS accounts in AWS Organizations. A solutions architect must improve how the company manages common security group rules for the AWS accounts in the organization. The company has a common set of IP CIDR ranges in an allow list in each AWS account to allow access to and from the company’s on- premises network. Developers within each account are responsible for adding new IP CIDR ranges to their security groups. The security team has its own AWS account. Currently, the security team notifies the owners of the other AWS accounts when changes are made to the allow list. The solutions architect must design a solution that distributes the common set of CIDR ranges across all accounts. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST amount of operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司的组织在 AWS Organizations 中拥有许多 AWS 账户。解决方案架构师必须改进公司管理组织中 AWS 账户的通用安全组规则 的方式。 该公司在每个 AWS 账户的允许列表中都有一组通用的 IP CIDR 范围，以允许访问和来自公司的本地网络。每个帐户内的开发人员负 责向其安全组添加新的 IP CIDR 范围。安全团队拥有自己的 AWS 账户。目前，当允许列表发生更改时，安全团队会通知其他 AWS 账 户的所有者。 解决方案架构师必须设计一个解决方案，在所有帐户之间分配一组通用的 CIDR 范围。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic in the security team's AWS account. Deploy an AWS Lambda function in each AWS account. Configure the Lambda function to run every time an SNS topic receives a message. Configure the Lambda function to take an IP address as input and add it to a list of security groups in the account. Instruct the security team to distribute changes by publishing messages to its SNS topic.","B":"Create new customer-managed prefix lists in each AWS account within the organization. Populate the prefix lists in each account with all internal CIDR ranges. Notify the owner of each AWS account to allow the new customer-managed prefix list IDs in their accounts in their security groups. Instruct the security team to share updates with each AWS account owner.","C":"Create a new customer-managed prefix list in the security team’s AWS account. Populate the customer-managed prefix list with all internal CIDR ranges. Share the customer-managed prefix list with the organization by using AWS Resource Access Manager. Notify the owner of each AWS account to allow the new customer-managed prefix list ID in their security groups.","D":"Create an IAM role in each account in the organization. Grant permissions to update security groups. Deploy an AWS Lambda function in the security team’s AWS account. Configure the Lambda function to take a list of internal IP addresses as input, assume a role in each organization account, and add the list of IP addresses to the security groups in each account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在安全团队的 AWS 账户中设置 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 主题。在每个 AWS 账户中部署 AWS Lambda 函 数。将 Lambda 函数配置为在每次 SNS 主题收到消息时运行。配置 Lambda 函数以将 IP 地址作为输入并将其添加到账户中的安全 组列表中。指示安全团队通过将消息发布到其 SNS 主题来分发更改。","B":"在组织内的每个 AWS 账户中创建新的客户管理的前缀列表。使用所有内部 CIDR 范围填充每个账户中的前缀列表。通知每个 AWS 账户的所有者在其安全组中的账户中允许新的客户管理的前缀列表 ID。指示安全团队与每个 AWS 账户所有者共享更新。","C":"在安全团队的 AWS 账户中创建新的客户管理的前缀列表。使用所有内部 CIDR 范围填充客户管理的前缀列表。使用 AWS Resource Access Manager 与组织共享客户管理的前缀列表。通知每个 AWS 账户的所有者在其安全组中允许新的客户管理的前缀 列表 ID。","D":"在组织中的每个账户中创建 IAM 角色。授予更新安全组的权限。在安全团队的 AWS 账户中部署 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数以将内部 IP 地址列表作为输入，在每个组织账户中承担角色，并将 IP 地址列表添加到每个账户中的安全组。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":88},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":99,"question_en":"A company has introduced a new policy that allows employees to work remotely from their homes if they connect by using a VPN. The company is hosting internal applications with VPCs in multiple AWS accounts. Currently, the applications are accessible from the company's on-premises o®ce network through an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection. The VPC in the company's main AWS account has peering connections established with VPCs in other AWS accounts. A solutions architect must design a scalable AWS Client VPN solution for employees to use while they work from home. What is the MOST cost-effective solution that meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司引入了一項新政策，允許員工在使用 VPN 連線的情況下於家中遠端工作。該公司在多個 AWS 帳戶的 VPC 中託管內部應用程式。目前，這些應用程式可透過 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 連線從公司內部部署的辦公室網路存取。該公司主要 AWS 帳戶中的 VPC 已與其他 AWS 帳戶中的 VPC 建立對等連線（peering connections）。解決方案架構師必須為員工居家工作時設計一個可擴充的 AWS Client VPN 解決方案。哪個解決方案是滿足這些需求最具成本效益的方式？","options_en":{"A":"Create a Client VPN endpoint in each AWS account. Configure required routing that allows access to internal applications.","B":"Create a Client VPN endpoint in the main AWS account. Configure required routing that allows access to internal applications.","C":"Create a Client VPN endpoint in the main AWS account. Provision a transit gateway that is connected to each AWS account. Configure required routing that allows access to internal applications.","D":"Create a Client VPN endpoint in the main AWS account. Establish connectivity between the Client VPN endpoint and the AWS Site-to- Site VPN."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每個 AWS 帳戶中建立一個 Client VPN 端點。設定所需的路由以存取內部應用程式。","B":"在主要 AWS 帳戶中建立一個 Client VPN 端點。設定所需的路由以存取內部應用程式。","C":"在主要 AWS 帳戶中建立一個 Client VPN 端點。佈建一個連接到每個 AWS 帳戶的傳輸閘道（transit gateway）。設定所需的路由以存取內部應用程式。","D":"在主要 AWS 帳戶中建立一個 Client VPN 端點。在該 Client VPN 端點與 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 之間建立連通性。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":52,"B":48},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The qualifier is MOST cost-effective. The main account VPC already has VPC peering connections to the VPCs in the other accounts, so connectivity between accounts exists. AWS Client VPN's documented 'Access a peered VPC using Client VPN' scenario shows that a single Client VPN endpoint associated with a subnet in the main (target) VPC can reach resources in all peered VPCs simply by adding a Client VPN route and an authorization rule for each peered VPC CIDR range. This requires no new infrastructure and only one endpoint, so it is both scalable and the cheapest. Option C adds a transit gateway (per-attachment hourly charge plus per-GB data processing) that is redundant because peering already provides the path, making it more expensive. Option A deploys an endpoint per account, multiplying hourly and per-connection charges. Option D connects to the Site-to-Site VPN, which leads to on-premises, not to the peered application VPCs, so it does not meet the requirement. Therefore B is the most cost-effective correct answer.","explanation_zh":"題目限定條件是 MOST cost-effective（最具成本效益）。主帳號的 VPC 已與其他帳號的 VPC 建立 VPC peering 連線，因此跨帳號連通性已存在。AWS Client VPN 文件中的「Access a peered VPC using Client VPN」情境明確說明：只要在主（目標）VPC 的子網路上建立單一 Client VPN endpoint，再為每個 peered VPC 的 CIDR 新增 Client VPN 路由與授權規則（authorization rule），即可存取所有 peered VPC 的資源。此做法不需新增任何基礎設施、只用一個 endpoint，因此既可擴充又最便宜。選項 C 額外建置 transit gateway（每個 attachment 有每小時費用，加上每 GB 資料處理費），但 peering 已提供路徑，屬於多餘且更昂貴。選項 A 在每個帳號各建一個 endpoint，會倍增每小時與每連線費用。選項 D 連接 Site-to-Site VPN，那是通往地端網路，而非通往 peered 的應用程式 VPC，無法滿足需求。因此 B 是最具成本效益的正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creating a Client VPN endpoint in every account multiplies the hourly endpoint charges and per-connection-hour charges, making it the most expensive option, and it duplicates work the existing peering already supports.","why_zh":"在每個帳號各建一個 Client VPN endpoint 會倍增每小時 endpoint 費用與每連線小時費用，是最昂貴的選項，且重複了現有 peering 已能支援的工作。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A transit gateway is unnecessary because the main account VPC already has VPC peering to the other VPCs; TGW adds per-attachment hourly fees plus per-GB data processing on top of Client VPN, so it is not the most cost-effective even though it would technically work.","why_zh":"transit gateway 並非必要，因為主帳號 VPC 已與其他 VPC 建立 peering；TGW 在 Client VPN 之外還增加每個 attachment 的每小時費用與每 GB 資料處理費，雖然技術上可行但並非最具成本效益。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Linking the Client VPN endpoint to the Site-to-Site VPN routes traffic toward the on-premises network, not toward the internal application VPCs in the peered accounts, so it fails to provide the required access.","why_zh":"將 Client VPN endpoint 連到 Site-to-Site VPN 會把流量導向地端網路，而非導向其他 peered 帳號中的內部應用程式 VPC，因此無法提供所需的存取。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/scenario.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/no-internet-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/cvpn-working-routes-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/cvpn-working-rule-authorize-add.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識"},{"id":100,"question_en":"A company is running an application in the AWS Cloud. Recent application metrics show inconsistent response times and a significant increase in error rates. Calls to third-party services are causing the delays. Currently, the application calls third-party services synchronously by directly invoking an AWS Lambda function. A solutions architect needs to decouple the third-party service calls and ensure that all the calls are eventually completed. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 云中运行应用程序。最近的应用程序指标显示响应时间不一致且错误率显着增加。对第三方服务的调用导致了延 误。目前，应用程序通过直接调用AWS Lambda函数来同步调用第三方服务。 解决方案架构师需要解耦第三方服务调用并确保所有调用最终完成。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue to store events and invoke the Lambda function.","B":"Use an AWS Step Functions state machine to pass events to the Lambda function.","C":"Use an Amazon EventBridge rule to pass events to the Lambda function.","D":"Use an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to store events and Invoke the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列来存储事件并调用 Lambda 函数。","B":"使用 AWS Step Functions 状态机将事件传递到 Lambda 函数。","C":"使用 Amazon EventBridge 规则将事件传递到 Lambda 函数。","D":"使用 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 主题存储事件并调用 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":101,"question_en":"A company is running applications on AWS in a multi-account environment. The company's sales team and marketing team use separate AWS accounts in AWS Organizations. The sales team stores petabytes of data in an Amazon S3 bucket. The marketing team uses Amazon QuickSight for data visualizations. The marketing team needs access to data that the sates team stores in the S3 bucket. The company has encrypted the S3 bucket with an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key. The marketing team has already created the IAM service role for QuickSight to provide QuickSight access in the marketing AWS account. The company needs a solution that will provide secure access to the data in the S3 bucket across AWS accounts. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 上的多账户环境中运行应用程序。该公司的销售团队和营销团队在 AWS Organizations 中使用单独的 AWS 账户。 销售团队在 Amazon S3 存储桶中存储 PB 级的数据。营销团队使用 Amazon QuickSight 进行数据可视化。营销团队需要访问国家团队 存储在 S3 存储桶中的数据。该公司已使用 AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) 密钥对 S3 存储桶进行加密。营销团队已为 QuickSight 创建 IAM 服务角色，以在营销 AWS 账户中提供 QuickSight 访问权限。该公司需要一种解决方案，能够跨 AWS 账户安全地 访问 S3 存储桶中的数据。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new S3 bucket in the marketing account. Create an S3 replication rule in the sales account to copy the objects to the new S3 bucket in the marketing account. Update the QuickSight permissions in the marketing account to grant access to the new S3 bucket.","B":"Create an SCP to grant access to the S3 bucket to the marketing account. Use AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) to share the KMS key from the sates account with the marketing account. Update the QuickSight permissions in the marketing account to grant access to the S3 bucket.","C":"Update the S3 bucket policy in the marketing account to grant access to the QuickSight role. Create a KMS grant for the encryption key that is used in the S3 bucket. Grant decrypt access to the QuickSight role. Update the QuickSight permissions in the marketing account to grant access to the S3 bucket.","D":"Create an IAM role in the sales account and grant access to the S3 bucket. From the marketing account, assume the IAM role in the sales account to access the S3 bucket. Update the QuickSight rote, to create a trust relationship with the new IAM role in the sales account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在营销帐户中创建一个新的 S3 存储桶。在销售账户中创建 S3 复制规则，以将对象复制到营销账户中的新 S3 存储桶。更新营 销帐户中的 QuickSight 权限以授予对新 S3 存储桶的访问权限。","B":"创建 SCP 以向营销帐户授予对 S3 存储桶的访问权限。使用 AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) 将 sates 账户中的 KMS 密 钥与营销账户共享。更新营销帐户中的 QuickSight 权限以授予对 S3 存储桶的访问权限。","C":"更新营销帐户中的 S3 存储桶策略以授予对 QuickSight 角色的访问权限。为 S3 存储桶中使用的加密密钥创建 KMS 授权。向 QuickSight 角色授予解密访问权限。更新营销帐户中的 QuickSight 权限以授予对 S3 存储桶的访问权限。","D":"在销售账户中创建 IAM 角色并授予对 S3 存储桶的访问权限。从营销账户中，承担销售账户中的 IAM 角色以访问 S3 存储桶。 更新 QuickSight 死记硬背，以与销售账户中的新 IAM 角色创建信任关系。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":61,"C":26},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Analytics"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":102,"question_en":"A company is planning to migrate its business-critical applications from an on-premises data center to AWS. The company has an on-premises installation of a Microsoft SQL Server Always On cluster. The company wants to migrate to an AWS managed database service. A solutions architect must design a heterogeneous database migration on AWS. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正计划将其关键业务应用程序从本地数据中心迁移到 AWS。该公司在本地安装了 Microsoft SQL Server Always On 集群。该公 司希望迁移到 AWS 托管数据库服务。解决方案架构师必须在 AWS 上设计异构数据库迁移。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate the SQL Server databases to Amazon RDS for MySQL by using backup and restore utilities.","B":"Use an AWS Snowball Edge Storage Optimized device to transfer data to Amazon S3. Set up Amazon RDS for MySQL. Use S3 integration with SQL Server features, such as BULK INSERT.","C":"Use the AWS Schema Conversion Tool to translate the database schema to Amazon RDS for MySQL. Then use AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to migrate the data from on-premises databases to Amazon RDS.","D":"Use AWS DataSync to migrate data over the network between on-premises storage and Amazon S3. Set up Amazon RDS for MySQL. Use S3 integration with SQL Server features, such as BULK INSERT."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用备份和恢复实用程序将 SQL Server 数据库迁移到 Amazon RDS for MySQL。","B":"使用 AWS Snowball Edge Storage Optimized 设备将数据传输到 Amazon S3。设置 Amazon RDS for MySQL。使用 S3 与 SQL Server 功能的集成，例如 BULK INSERT。","C":"使用 AWS Schema Conversion Tool 将数据库架构转换为 Amazon RDS for MySQL。然后使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 将数据从本地数据库迁移到 Amazon RDS。","D":"使用 AWS DataSync 通过网络在本地存储和 Amazon S3 之间迁移数据。设置 Amazon RDS for MySQL。使用 S3 与 SQL Server 功能 的集成，例如 BULK INSERT。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":103,"question_en":"A publishing company's design team updates the icons and other static assets that an ecommerce web application uses. The company serves the icons and assets from an Amazon S3 bucket that is hosted in the company's production account. The company also uses a development account that members of the design team can access. After the design team tests the static assets in the development account, the design team needs to load the assets into the S3 bucket in the production account. A solutions architect must provide the design team with access to the production account without exposing other parts of the web application to the risk of unwanted changes. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"出版公司的设计团队更新电子商务 Web 应用程序使用的图标和其他静态资源。该公司通过托管在公司生产账户中的 Amazon S3 存储 桶提供图标和资产。该公司还使用设计团队成员可以访问的开发帐户。 设计团队测试开发账户中的静态资产后，设计团队需要将资产加载到生产账户中的S3存储桶中。解决方案架构师必须为设计团队提 供对生产帐户的访问权限，而不会使 Web 应用程序的其他部分面临不必要的更改的风险。 哪种步骤组合可以满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"In the production account, create a new IAM policy that allows read and write access to the S3 bucket.","B":"In the development account, create a new IAM policy that allows read and write access to the S3 bucket.","C":"In the production account, create a role Attach the new policy to the role. Define the development account as a trusted entity.","D":"In the development account, create a role. Attach the new policy to the role Define the production account as a trusted entity.","E":"In the development account, create a group that contains all the IAM users of the design team Attach a different IAM policy to the group to allow the sts:AssumeRole action on the role In the production account.","F":"In the development account, create a group that contains all the IAM users of the design team Attach a different IAM policy to the group to allow the sts:AssumeRole action on the role in the development account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在生产账户中，创建一个新的 IAM 策略，允许对 S3 存储桶进行读写访问。","B":"在开发账户中，创建一个新的 IAM 策略，允许对 S3 存储桶进行读写访问。","C":"在生产帐户中，创建一个角色，将新策略附加到该角色。将开发帐户定义为可信实体。","D":"在开发账户中，创建一个角色。将新策略附加到角色将生产帐户定义为可信实体。","E":"在开发账户中，创建一个包含设计团队的所有 IAM 用户的组 将不同的 IAM 策略附加到该组，以允许对生产账户中的角色执行 sts:AssumeRole 操作。","F":"在开发账户中，创建一个包含设计团队的所有 IAM 用户的组 将不同的 IAM 策略附加到该组，以允许对开发账户中的角色执行 sts:AssumeRole 操作。"},"answer":["A","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ACE":95},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"This is the canonical AWS cross-account delegation pattern from the IAM tutorial 'Delegate access across AWS accounts using IAM roles.' The resource (the S3 bucket) lives in the production account, which is the trusting (Destination) account. The development account holds the design-team users and is the trusted (Originating) account. (A) The permissions policy that grants read/write access to the S3 bucket must be created in the production account because the policy is attached to the role that lives there. (C) The role is created in the production account, the bucket-access policy is attached to it, and the development account is defined as the trusted entity in the role's trust policy. (E) In the development account, the design-team users are placed in a group whose identity-based policy allows sts:AssumeRole on the role that lives in the production account. Scoping access to a dedicated role with only S3 bucket read/write permissions satisfies the requirement of granting access without exposing the rest of the web application to unwanted changes.","explanation_zh":"這是 AWS IAM 教學「Delegate access across AWS accounts using IAM roles」中的標準跨帳號委派模式。資源（S3 bucket）位於 production 帳號，也就是受信任方（trusting / Destination）帳號；development 帳號擁有設計團隊的使用者，是被信任方（trusted / Originating）帳號。(A) 授予 S3 bucket 讀寫權限的 IAM policy 必須建立在 production 帳號，因為該 policy 會附加到位於 production 帳號的 role。(C) Role 建立在 production 帳號，將 bucket 存取 policy 附加上去，並在 role 的信任政策中將 development 帳號定義為 trusted entity。(E) 在 development 帳號中，把設計團隊使用者放入一個群組，並為該群組附加一個 identity-based policy，允許對 production 帳號中的那個 role 執行 sts:AssumeRole。由於該 role 僅具備 S3 bucket 讀寫權限，因此可在不暴露其他 web application 部分、避免不必要變更的情況下提供存取。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The read/write S3 policy must be created in the production account (where the bucket and the role live), not in the development account. The policy is attached to the cross-account role, which resides in production.","why_zh":"讀寫 S3 的 policy 必須建立在 production 帳號（bucket 與 role 所在處），而非 development 帳號。該 policy 會附加到位於 production 的跨帳號 role。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Backwards. The role must be created in the production account (the trusting/Destination account that owns the S3 bucket) with the development account as the trusted entity. Creating the role in the development account trusting production does not grant any access to the production S3 bucket.","why_zh":"方向相反。Role 必須建立在 production 帳號（擁有 S3 bucket 的 trusting/Destination 帳號），並以 development 帳號作為 trusted entity。在 development 帳號建立並信任 production 的 role 無法取得 production S3 bucket 的任何存取權。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"The sts:AssumeRole permission for the development-team group must target the role in the production account, because that is where the cross-account role lives. There is no role in the development account to assume, so allowing AssumeRole on a development-account role accomplishes nothing.","why_zh":"development 團隊群組的 sts:AssumeRole 權限必須指向 production 帳號中的 role，因為跨帳號 role 位於該處。development 帳號中並沒有可供承接的 role，因此允許承接 development 帳號的 role 沒有任何作用。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/tutorial_cross-account-with-roles.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies-cross-account-resource-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_create_for-user.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":104,"question_en":"A company developed a pilot application by using AWS Elastic Beanstalk and Java. To save costs during development, the company's development team deployed the application into a single-instance environment. Recent tests indicate that the application consumes more CPU than expected. CPU utilization is regularly greater than 85%, which causes some performance bottlenecks. A solutions architect must mitigate the performance issues before the company launches the application to production. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 和 Java 开发了一个试点应用程序。为了节省开发成本，该公司的开发团队将应用程序部署到单 实例环境中。最近的测试表明该应用程序消耗的 CPU 超出预期。CPU 利用率通常大于 85%，这会导致一些性能瓶颈。 在公司将应用程序投入生产之前，解决方案架构师必须缓解性能问题。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new Elastic Beanstalk application. Select a load-balanced environment type. Select all Availability Zones. Add a scale-out rule that will run if the maximum CPU utilization is over 85% for 5 minutes.","B":"Create a second Elastic Beanstalk environment. Apply the tra®c-splitting deployment policy. Specify a percentage of incoming tra®c to direct to the new environment in the average CPU utilization is over 85% for 5 minutes.","C":"Modify the existing environment’s capacity configuration to use a load-balanced environment type. Select all Availability Zones. Add a scale-out rule that will run if the average CPU utilization is over 85% for 5 minutes.","D":"Select the Rebuild environment action with the load balancing option. Select an Availability Zones. Add a scale-out rule that will run if the sum CPU utilization is over 85% for 5 minutes."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的 Elastic Beanstalk 应用程序。选择负载平衡的环境类型。选择所有可用区。添加一个横向扩展规则，如果最大 CPU 利用率超过 85% 持续 5 分钟，该规则将运行。","B":"创建第二个 Elastic Beanstalk 环境。应用分流部署策略。指定在平均 CPU 利用率超过 85% 持续 5 分钟的情况下定向到新环境的 传入流量的百分比。","C":"修改现有环境的容量配置以使用负载平衡的环境类型。选择所有可用区。添加一个横向扩展规则，如果平均 CPU 利用率超过 85% 持续 5 分钟，该规则将运行。","D":"选择带有负载平衡选项的重建环境操作。选择可用区。添加一个横向扩展规则，如果 CPU 利用率总和超过 85% 持续 5 分钟， 该规则将运行。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":95},"tags":["Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to mitigate CPU bottlenecks in an existing single-instance Elastic Beanstalk environment with the LEAST operational overhead. AWS documentation explicitly states you can change an environment from single-instance to load-balanced/scalable simply by editing the existing environment's Capacity configuration (Configuration > Capacity > Edit > Environment Type), with no need to create a new application or rebuild. Option C does exactly this and adds an Auto Scaling trigger using the Average CPU utilization statistic over a breach duration, which matches the documented trigger configuration (the default Statistic is Average). This in-place edit is far less overhead than Option A, which creates an entirely new Elastic Beanstalk application (requiring redeployment, DNS re-pointing, and managing duplicate resources). Therefore C is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求是以最少的維運負擔來緩解既有 single-instance Elastic Beanstalk 環境的 CPU 瓶頸。AWS 官方文件明確指出，只需編輯既有環境的 Capacity 設定（Configuration > Capacity > Edit > Environment Type）即可將環境從 single-instance 變更為 load-balanced/scalable，無需建立新的 application 或 rebuild。選項 C 正是如此做法，並新增以 Average CPU utilization 統計值搭配 breach duration 的 Auto Scaling 觸發器，符合文件記載的觸發器設定（預設 Statistic 為 Average）。此就地編輯遠比選項 A 建立全新 application（需重新部署、重新指向 DNS、管理重複資源）的負擔小。因此 C 為正解。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creating a brand-new Elastic Beanstalk application is unnecessary and adds significant operational overhead (redeploy, cutover, DNS changes, duplicate resources). AWS supports changing environment type in place. It also uses 'maximum' CPU statistic, whereas the documented/default trigger statistic is Average.","why_zh":"建立全新的 Elastic Beanstalk application 並非必要，且增加大量維運負擔（重新部署、切換、DNS 變更、重複資源）。AWS 支援就地變更 environment type。此外它使用 'maximum' CPU 統計值，而文件/預設的觸發器統計值為 Average。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Traffic-splitting is a deployment policy used for canary releases of new application versions, not a mechanism to scale capacity or fix CPU bottlenecks. It also requires creating a second environment, adding overhead, and does not actually increase compute capacity for the load.","why_zh":"Traffic-splitting 是用於新版本金絲雀部署的部署策略，並非用來擴充容量或解決 CPU 瓶頸的機制。它還需建立第二個環境而增加負擔，且實際上並未為負載增加運算容量。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Rebuild environment terminates and recreates all resources (more disruptive/overhead and risks data loss on coupled resources). It uses 'sum' CPU utilization, which is not a meaningful statistic for percentage-based CPU, and selecting a single Availability Zone undermines scalability/resilience.","why_zh":"Rebuild environment 會終止並重建所有資源（更具破壞性、負擔更高，並可能造成耦合資源資料遺失）。它使用 'sum' CPU utilization，對百分比型 CPU 而言並非有意義的統計值，且僅選擇單一 Availability Zone 會削弱擴展性與韌性。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features-managing-env-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/environments-cfg-autoscaling-triggers.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":105,"question_en":"A finance company is running its business-critical application on current-generation Linux EC2 instances. The application includes a self- managed MySQL database performing heavy I/O operations. The application is working fine to handle a moderate amount of tra®c during the month. However, it slows down during the final three days of each month due to month-end reporting, even though the company is using Elastic Load Balancers and Auto Scaling within its infrastructure to meet the increased demand. Which of the following actions would allow the database to handle the month-end load with the LEAST impact on performance?","question_zh":"一家金融公司正在当前一代 Linux EC2 实例上运行其关键业务应用程序。该应用程序包括一个自我管理的 MySQL 数据库，执行大量 I/O 操作。该应用程序运行良好，可以处理该月的中等流量。然而，尽管该公司在其基础设施中使用弹性负载均衡器和自动扩展来满 足不断增长的需求，但由于月末报告，它在每个月的最后三天会放缓。 以下哪项操作可以让数据库处理月末负载，同时对性能的影响最小？","options_en":{"A":"Pre-warming Elastic Load Balancers, using a bigger instance type, changing all Amazon EBS volumes to GP2 volumes.","B":"Performing a one-time migration of the database cluster to Amazon RDS, and creating several additional read replicas to handle the load during end of month.","C":"Using Amazon CloudWatch with AWS Lambda to change the type, size, or IOPS of Amazon EBS volumes in the cluster based on a specific CloudWatch metric.","D":"Replacing all existing Amazon EBS volumes with new PIOPS volumes that have the maximum available storage size and I/O per second by taking snapshots before the end of the month and reverting back afterwards."},"options_zh":{"A":"预热弹性负载均衡器，使用更大的实例类型，将所有 Amazon EBS 卷更改为 GP2 卷。","B":"将数据库集群一次性迁移到 Amazon RDS，并创建多个额外的只读副本来处理月底的负载。","C":"将 Amazon CloudWatch 与 AWS Lambda 结合使用，根据特定的 CloudWatch 指标更改集群中 Amazon EBS 卷的类型、大小或 IOPS。","D":"通过在月底之前拍摄快照并在月底恢复回来，将所有现有 Amazon EBS 卷替换为具有最大可用存储大小和每秒 I/O 的新 PIOPS 卷。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":93},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":106,"question_en":"A company runs a Java application that has complex dependencies on VMs that are in the company's data center. The application is stable. but the company wants to modernize the technology stack. The company wants to migrate the application to AWS and minimize the administrative overhead to maintain the servers. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST code changes?","question_zh":"某公司运行的 Java 应用程序对公司数据中心内的虚拟机具有复杂的依赖关系。应用稳定。但该公司希望实现技术堆栈的现代化。该 公司希望将应用程序迁移到 AWS 并最大限度地减少维护服务器的管理开销。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的代码更改满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate the application to Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) on AWS Fargate by using AWS App2Container. Store container images in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). Grant the ECS task execution role permission 10 access the ECR image repository. Configure Amazon ECS to use an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Use the ALB to interact with the application.","B":"Migrate the application code to a container that runs in AWS Lambda. Build an Amazon API Gateway REST API with Lambda integration. Use API Gateway to interact with the application.","C":"Migrate the application to Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) on EKS managed node groups by using AWS App2Container. Store container images in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). Give the EKS nodes permission to access the ECR image repository. Use Amazon API Gateway to interact with the application.","D":"Migrate the application code to a container that runs in AWS Lambda. Configure Lambda to use an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Use the ALB to interact with the application."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS App2Container 将应用程序迁移到 AWS Fargate 上的 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS)。将容器映像存储 在 Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) 中。授予ECS任务执行角色10访问ECR镜像仓库的权限。配置 Amazon ECS 以使 用应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB)。使用 ALB 与应用程序交互。","B":"将应用程序代码迁移到在 AWS Lambda 中运行的容器。使用 Lambda 集成构建 Amazon API Gateway REST API。使用 API Gateway 与应用程序交互。","C":"使用 AWS App2Container 将应用程序迁移到 EKS 托管节点组上的 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS)。将容器映像 存储在 Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) 中。授予 EKS 节点访问 ECR 映像存储库的权限。使用 Amazon API Gateway 与应用程序交互。","D":"将应用程序代码迁移到在 AWS Lambda 中运行的容器。配置 Lambda 以使用应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB)。使用 ALB 与应用程序 交互。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":93},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The application is a stable Java app on VMs with complex dependencies, and the goal is migration to AWS with the LEAST code changes plus minimal server administration. AWS App2Container (A2C) is purpose-built to lift-and-shift on-premises Java applications into containers managed by Amazon ECS or EKS WITHOUT needing source code, automatically analyzing runtime dependencies and generating the Dockerfile, ECR image, ECS task definition, and ALB configuration. Running those containers on AWS Fargate is serverless, so there are no EC2 nodes to patch or manage, satisfying 'minimize the administrative overhead to maintain the servers.' Option A combines A2C + ECS on Fargate + ECR + ALB, which is the exact A2C-supported path and requires essentially no code changes. Option C uses EKS managed node groups, which still require managing EC2 worker nodes (more overhead than Fargate) and adds Kubernetes complexity. Options B and D try to put a complex, dependency-heavy, long-running Java app into Lambda, which would require major re-architecture (the MOST code changes), and A2C does not target Lambda, so they fail the 'LEAST code changes' qualifier.","explanation_zh":"此應用是執行在 VM 上、具有複雜相依性的穩定 Java 應用，目標是以最少程式碼變更遷移到 AWS，同時最小化伺服器管理負擔。AWS App2Container (A2C) 專為將地端 Java 應用「lift-and-shift」成由 Amazon ECS 或 EKS 管理的容器而設計，且不需要原始碼，會自動分析執行階段相依性並產生 Dockerfile、ECR 映像、ECS task definition 與 ALB 設定。將這些容器執行在 AWS Fargate 上屬於 serverless，無需修補或管理 EC2 節點，符合「最小化維護伺服器的管理負擔」。選項 A 結合 A2C + ECS on Fargate + ECR + ALB，正是 A2C 支援的標準路徑，幾乎不需任何程式碼變更。選項 C 使用 EKS managed node groups，仍需管理 EC2 worker 節點（比 Fargate 負擔更高）並增加 Kubernetes 複雜度。選項 B 與 D 嘗試把複雜、相依性高且長時間執行的 Java 應用放進 Lambda，需要大幅重新架構（最多的程式碼變更），且 A2C 並不以 Lambda 為目標，因此不符合「最少程式碼變更」的條件。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Repackaging a complex, dependency-heavy, long-running Java app to run as a Lambda container behind API Gateway requires major re-architecture (statelessness, 15-min timeout, no process/port dependencies), i.e. the MOST code changes, not the least. App2Container does not target Lambda. This is the dump's suggested answer and it is wrong.","why_zh":"把複雜、相依性高且長時間執行的 Java 應用改造成 Lambda 容器並透過 API Gateway 存取，需要大幅重新架構（無狀態、15 分鐘逾時、無法依賴常駐程序/通訊埠），是最多而非最少的程式碼變更。App2Container 也不以 Lambda 為目標。這是題庫的建議答案，但它是錯的。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"App2Container does support EKS, but EKS managed node groups still require managing EC2 worker nodes (scaling, patching), which is more administrative overhead than serverless Fargate, and Kubernetes adds operational complexity. It loses on 'minimize the administrative overhead to maintain the servers.'","why_zh":"App2Container 確實支援 EKS，但 EKS managed node groups 仍需管理 EC2 worker 節點（擴縮、修補），管理負擔高於 serverless 的 Fargate，且 Kubernetes 增加運維複雜度，因此在「最小化維護伺服器的管理負擔」上落敗。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same fundamental problem as B: Lambda cannot host a complex, dependency-heavy, persistent Java application without major re-architecture, so it violates the LEAST-code-changes requirement. Putting an ALB in front of Lambda does not solve the runtime/dependency mismatch.","why_zh":"與 B 的根本問題相同：Lambda 無法在不大幅重新架構的情況下承載複雜、相依性高的常駐 Java 應用，違反最少程式碼變更的要求。在 Lambda 前面加 ALB 並不能解決執行階段/相依性的不相容。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/app2container/latest/UserGuide/what-is-a2c.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/app2container/latest/UserGuide/compatibility-a2c.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/patterns/migrate-on-premises-java-applications-to-aws-using-aws-app2container.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/AWS_Fargate.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":107,"question_en":"A company has an asynchronous HTTP application that is hosted as an AWS Lambda function. A public Amazon API Gateway endpoint invokes the Lambda function. The Lambda function and the API Gateway endpoint reside in the us-east-1 Region. A solutions architect needs to redesign the application to support failover to another AWS Region. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个作为 AWS Lambda 函数托管的异步 HTTP 应用程序。公共 Amazon API Gateway 终端节点调用 Lambda 函数。Lambda 函数和 API Gateway 终端节点位于 us-east-1 区域。解决方案架构师需要重新设计应用程序以支持故障转移到另一个 AWS 区域。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an API Gateway endpoint in the us-west-2 Region to direct tra®c to the Lambda function in us-east-1. Configure Amazon Route 53 to use a failover routing policy to route tra®c for the two API Gateway endpoints.","B":"Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Configure API Gateway to direct tra®c to the SQS queue instead of to the Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to pull messages from the queue for processing.","C":"Deploy the Lambda function to the us-west-2 Region. Create an API Gateway endpoint in us-west-2 10 direct tra®c to the Lambda function in us-west-2. Configure AWS Global Accelerator and an Application Load Balancer to manage tra®c across the two API Gateway endpoints.","D":"Deploy the Lambda function and an API Gateway endpoint to the us-west-2 Region. Configure Amazon Route 53 to use a failover routing policy to route tra®c for the two API Gateway endpoints."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 us-west-2 区域中创建 API 网关终端节点，以将流量引导至 us-east-1 中的 Lambda 函数。配置 Amazon Route 53 以使用故障转 移路由策略来路由两个 API Gateway 终端节点的流量。","B":"创建 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列。配置 API Gateway 将流量引导至 SQS 队列而不是 Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数以从队列中提取消息进行处理。","C":"将 Lambda 函数部署到 us-west-2 区域。在 us-west-2 中创建 API 网关终端节点 10 将流量直接传输到 us-west-2 中的 Lambda 函 数。配置 AWS Global Accelerator 和 Application Load Balancer 以管理两个 API Gateway 终端节点之间的流量。","D":"将 Lambda 函数和 API 网关终端节点部署到 us-west-2 区域。配置 Amazon Route 53 以使用故障转移路由策略来路由两个 API Gateway 终端节点的流量。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":94},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The application needs to fail over to a second AWS Region, so a complete standby stack must exist in that region. Option D deploys both the Lambda function and an API Gateway endpoint to us-west-2, then uses an Amazon Route 53 failover (active-passive) routing policy with health checks across the two regional API Gateway endpoints. This is exactly the AWS-documented active-passive cross-region failover pattern: Route 53 serves the primary (us-east-1) endpoint while healthy and switches to the secondary (us-west-2) endpoint when the primary is unhealthy. Option B (the dump's answer) only adds an SQS queue in front of the single us-east-1 stack; it decouples processing but provides zero cross-region resilience, and if us-east-1 fails everything is still down. The decisive qualifier is 'support failover to another AWS Region,' which requires duplicating the compute (Lambda) AND the entry point (API Gateway) in the second region plus DNS-level failover routing.","explanation_zh":"此應用必須能夠故障轉移到第二個 AWS 區域，因此第二個區域中必須存在完整的待命堆疊。選項 D 將 Lambda 函式與 API Gateway 端點同時部署到 us-west-2，再使用 Amazon Route 53 failover（主動-被動）路由策略搭配健康檢查，跨兩個區域的 API Gateway 端點進行路由。這正是 AWS 文件記載的跨區域主動-被動故障轉移模式：當主要端點（us-east-1）健康時 Route 53 提供主要端點，當其不健康時切換到次要端點（us-west-2）。選項 B（dump 建議答案）只是在單一 us-east-1 堆疊前加上 SQS 佇列；它解耦了處理流程但完全沒有跨區域韌性，若 us-east-1 失效則整體仍然停擺。決定性的限定詞是『支援故障轉移到另一個 AWS 區域』，這需要在第二個區域同時複製運算（Lambda）與入口（API Gateway），並搭配 DNS 層級的故障轉移路由。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creating a second API Gateway in us-west-2 that still points back to the single Lambda in us-east-1 provides no regional failover. If us-east-1 fails, the only Lambda is gone and both API Gateway endpoints fail. There is no standby compute in the second region.","why_zh":"在 us-west-2 建立第二個 API Gateway 但仍指回 us-east-1 中唯一的 Lambda，無法提供區域故障轉移。若 us-east-1 失效，唯一的 Lambda 不存在，兩個 API Gateway 端點都會失敗，第二區域沒有待命運算資源。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Adding an SQS queue only decouples request ingestion from processing within the same single region (us-east-1). It does nothing for cross-region failover; if us-east-1 becomes unavailable the entire stack is down. The requirement is regional failover, not async decoupling.","why_zh":"加入 SQS 佇列只是在同一個單一區域（us-east-1）內解耦請求接收與處理，對跨區域故障轉移毫無幫助；若 us-east-1 不可用，整個堆疊都會停擺。需求是區域故障轉移，而非非同步解耦。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This architecture is invalid. An Application Load Balancer cannot front or 'manage traffic across' API Gateway endpoints (API Gateway is not a valid ALB target type), and AWS Global Accelerator does not target API Gateway endpoints. Route 53 (as in D), not Global Accelerator + ALB, is the documented way to fail over between regional API Gateway endpoints.","why_zh":"此架構無效。Application Load Balancer 無法作為 API Gateway 端點的前端或『跨端點管理流量』（API Gateway 不是有效的 ALB 目標類型），且 AWS Global Accelerator 不以 API Gateway 端點為目標。在區域 API Gateway 端點之間進行故障轉移的文件做法是 Route 53（如選項 D），而非 Global Accelerator + ALB。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-to-api-gateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-configuring.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-apigateway.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":108,"question_en":"A retail company has structured its AWS accounts to be part of an organization in AWS Organizations. The company has set up consolidated billing and has mapped its departments to the following OUs: Finance, Sales, Human Resources (HR), Marketing, and Operations. Each OU has multiple AWS accounts, one for each environment within a department. These environments are development, test, pre-production, and production. The HR department is releasing a new system that will launch in 3 months. In preparation, the HR department has purchased several Reserved Instances (RIs) in its production AWS account. The HR department will install the new application on this account. The HR department wants to make sure that other departments cannot share the RI discounts. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家零售公司已将其 AWS 账户构建为 AWS Organizations 中组织的一部分。该公司已设置合并计费并将其部门映射到以下 OU：财 务、销售、人力资源 (HR)、营销和运营。每个 OU 都有多个 AWS 账户，一个部门对应一个环境。这些环境是开发、测试、预生产和 生产。 人力资源部门正在发布一个新系统，将于 3 个月后推出。在准备过程中，人力资源部门在其生产 AWS 账户中购买了多个预留实例 (RI)。人力资源部门将在此帐户上安装新应用程序。人力资源部门希望确保其他部门不能分享 RI 折扣。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？ 答： 在 HR 部门生产账户的 AWS Billing and Cost Management 控制台中，关闭 RI 共享。","options_en":{"A":"In the AWS Billing and Cost Management console for the HR department's production account turn off RI sharing.","B":"Remove the HR department's production AWS account from the organization. Add the account 10 the consolidating billing configuration only.","C":"In the AWS Billing and Cost Management console. use the organization’s management account 10 turn off RI Sharing for the HR departments production AWS account.","D":"Create an SCP in the organization to restrict access to the RIs. Apply the SCP to the OUs of the other departments."},"options_zh":{"B":"从组织中删除人力资源部门的生产 AWS 账户。仅将帐户 10 添加到合并计费配置。","C":"在 AWS 账单和成本管理控制台中。使用组织的管理帐户 10 关闭 HR 部门生产 AWS 帐户的 RI 共享。","D":"在组织中创建 SCP 以限制对 RI 的访问。将 SCP 应用到其他部门的 OU。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":80},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":109,"question_en":"A large company is running a popular web application. The application runs on several Amazon EC2 Linux instances in an Auto Scaling group in a private subnet. An Application Load Balancer is targeting the instances in the Auto Scaling group in the private subnet. AWS Systems Manager Session Manager is configured, and AWS Systems Manager Agent is running on all the EC2 instances. The company recently released a new version of the application. Some EC2 instances are now being marked as unhealthy and are being terminated. As a result, the application is running at reduced capacity. A solutions architect tries to determine the root cause by analyzing Amazon CloudWatch logs that are collected from the application, but the logs are inconclusive. How should the solutions architect gain access to an EC2 instance to troubleshoot the issue?","question_zh":"一家大公司正在运行一个流行的 Web 应用程序。该应用程序在私有子网的 Auto Scaling 组中的多个 Amazon EC2 Linux 实例上运行。 应用程序负载均衡器的目标是私有子网中 Auto Scaling 组中的实例。AWS Systems Manager 会话管理器已配置，并且 AWS Systems Manager 代理正在所有 EC2 实例上运行。 该公司最近发布了该应用程序的新版本。一些 EC2 实例现在被标记为不健康并正在终止。因此，应用程序的运行能力会降低。解决 方案架构师尝试通过分析从应用程序收集的 Amazon CloudWatch 日志来确定根本原因，但这些日志并没有得出结论。 解决方案架构师应如何访问 EC2 实例来解决问题？","options_en":{"A":"Suspend the Auto Scaling group’s HealthCheck scaling process. Use Session Manager to log in to an instance that is marked as unhealthy.","B":"Enable EC2 instance termination protection. Use Session Manager to log in to an instance that is marked as unhealthy.","C":"Set the termination policy to OldestInstance on the Auto Scaling group. Use Session Manager to log in to an instance that is marked an unhealthy.","D":"Suspend the Auto Scaling group’s Terminate process. Use Session Manager to log in to an instance that is marked as unhealthy."},"options_zh":{"A":"暂停 Auto Scaling 组的 HealthCheck 扩展进程。使用会话管理器登录到标记为不正常的实例。","B":"启用 EC2 实例终止保护。使用会话管理器登录到标记为不正常的实例。","C":"将 Auto Scaling 组上的终止策略设置为 OldestInstance。使用会话管理器登录到标记为不正常的实例。","D":"暂停 Auto Scaling 组的 Terminate 进程。使用会话管理器登录到标记为不正常的实例。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":93},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":110,"question_en":"A company wants to deploy an AWS WAF solution to manage AWS WAF rules across multiple AWS accounts. The accounts are managed under different OUs in AWS Organizations. Administrators must be able to add or remove accounts or OUs from managed AWS WAF rule sets as needed. Administrators also must have the ability to automatically update and remediate noncompliant AWS WAF rules in all accounts. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST amount of operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司想要部署 AWS WAF 解决方案来管理跨多个 AWS 账户的 AWS WAF 规则。这些账户在 AWS Organizations 中的不同 OU 下进行 管理。 管理员必须能够根据需要在托管 AWS WAF 规则集中添加或删除账户或 OU。管理员还必须能够自动更新和修复所有账户中不合规的 AWS WAF 规则。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Firewall Manager to manage AWS WAF rules across accounts in the organization. Use an AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store parameter to store account numbers and OUs to manage. Update the parameter as needed to add or remove accounts or OUs. Use an Amazon EventBridge rule to identify any changes to the parameter and to invoke an AWS Lambda function to update the security policy in the Firewall Manager administrative account.","B":"Deploy an organization-wide AWS Config rule that requires all resources in the selected OUs to associate the AWS WAF rules. Deploy automated remediation actions by using AWS Lambda to fix noncompliant resources. Deploy AWS WAF rules by using an AWS CloudFormation stack set to target the same OUs where the AWS Config rule is applied.","C":"Create AWS WAF rules in the management account of the organization. Use AWS Lambda environment variables to store account numbers and OUs to manage. Update environment variables as needed to add or remove accounts or OUs. Create cross-account IAM roles in member accounts. Assume the roles by using AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) in the Lambda function to create and update AWS WAF rules in the member accounts.","D":"Use AWS Control Tower to manage AWS WAF rules across accounts in the organization. Use AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) to store account numbers and OUs to manage. Update AWS KMS as needed to add or remove accounts or OUs. Create IAM users in member accounts. Allow AWS Control Tower in the management account to use the access key and secret access key to create and update AWS WAF rules in the member accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Firewall Manager 跨组织中的账户管理 AWS WAF 规则。使用 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store 参数来存储要管理 的帐号和 OU。根据需要更新参数以添加或删除帐户或 OU。使用 Amazon EventBridge 规则来识别对参数的任何更改，并调用 AWS Lambda 函数来更新 Firewall Manager 管理账户中的安全策略。","B":"部署组织范围内的 AWS Config 规则，该规则要求所选 OU 中的所有资源关联 AWS WAF 规则。使用 AWS Lambda 部署自动修复 操作来修复不合规资源。使用 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈集部署 AWS WAF 规则，以定位应用 AWS Config 规则的相同 OU。","C":"在组织的管理账户中创建 AWS WAF 规则。使用 AWS Lambda 环境变量来存储要管理的帐号和 OU。根据需要更新环境变量以添 加或删除帐户或 OU。在成员账户中创建跨账户 IAM 角色。通过在 Lambda 函数中使用 AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) 来承 担角色，以在成员账户中创建和更新 AWS WAF 规则。","D":"使用 AWS Control Tower 管理组织中账户之间的 AWS WAF 规则。使用 AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) 存储要管理的帐号 和 OU。根据需要更新 AWS KMS 以添加或删除账户或 OU。在成员账户中创建 IAM 用户。允许管理账户中的 AWS Control Tower 使 用访问密钥和秘密访问密钥在成员账户中创建和更新 AWS WAF 规则。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"AWS Firewall Manager is the purpose-built service for centrally managing AWS WAF rules across multiple accounts and OUs in AWS Organizations. A Firewall Manager AWS WAF policy lets you scope the policy to a specific list of included (or excluded) account numbers and Organizations OUs, and you can enable automatic remediation so noncompliant resources are fixed and web ACLs are applied automatically, including to new in-scope accounts. Option A is the only choice that uses Firewall Manager and native auto-remediation; the Parameter Store + EventBridge + Lambda layer to update the policy scope is slightly over-engineered but is far less operational overhead than building custom solutions, and it correctly performs automatic remediation. The dump's suggested answer D is technically invalid: AWS Control Tower does not manage AWS WAF rules, AWS KMS is for cryptographic keys (not storing account/OU lists), and using IAM users with long-lived access keys across member accounts is an anti-pattern with high overhead. Therefore the community answer A is correct.","explanation_zh":"AWS Firewall Manager 是專為在 AWS Organizations 多帳戶與多個 OU 之間集中管理 AWS WAF 規則而設計的服務。Firewall Manager 的 AWS WAF policy 可將政策範圍設定為特定的「納入（或排除）」帳戶編號與 Organizations OU 清單，並可啟用自動修復（automatic remediation），讓不合規資源自動被修正、web ACL 自動套用，且新加入範圍的帳戶也會自動套用。選項 A 是唯一使用 Firewall Manager 與原生自動修復的方案；雖然加上 Parameter Store + EventBridge + Lambda 來更新政策範圍稍嫌多餘，但相較於自行開發的方案，其營運負擔仍遠低，且能正確執行自動修復。Dump 標示的 D 在技術上不成立：AWS Control Tower 不管理 AWS WAF 規則，AWS KMS 是用於加密金鑰（不是儲存帳戶/OU 清單），且在成員帳戶使用長期 IAM access key 是反模式且營運負擔高。因此社群答案 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Config detects compliance but does not natively associate AWS WAF rules; you would have to build the remediation logic with Lambda and deploy WAF via CloudFormation StackSets. This is substantial custom development and far more operational overhead than Firewall Manager's native scoping and auto-remediation.","why_zh":"AWS Config 可偵測合規性，但無法原生關聯 AWS WAF 規則；你必須以 Lambda 自建修復邏輯並用 CloudFormation StackSet 部署 WAF。相較於 Firewall Manager 原生的範圍設定與自動修復，這需要大量自訂開發、營運負擔高得多。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Storing account numbers and OUs in Lambda environment variables and writing custom code that assumes cross-account IAM roles to create and update WAF rules is the highest-overhead, most brittle option. It reimplements what Firewall Manager provides natively and does not give automatic remediation.","why_zh":"把帳戶編號與 OU 存在 Lambda 環境變數，再寫自訂程式碼透過跨帳戶 IAM 角色去建立與更新 WAF 規則，是營運負擔最高、最脆弱的方案。等於重新實作 Firewall Manager 原生功能，且不提供自動修復。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Technically invalid: AWS Control Tower governs account provisioning and guardrails but does not manage AWS WAF rules; AWS KMS is for cryptographic keys, not for storing account/OU lists; and granting Control Tower the use of IAM user access keys/secret keys in member accounts is a security anti-pattern with high overhead. This is the dump's suggested answer and is wrong.","why_zh":"技術上不成立：AWS Control Tower 負責帳戶佈建與護欄，但不管理 AWS WAF 規則；AWS KMS 用於加密金鑰，而非儲存帳戶/OU 清單；讓 Control Tower 使用成員帳戶的 IAM user access key/secret key 是安全反模式且負擔高。這是 dump 標示的答案，是錯的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/fms-chapter.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/working-with-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/policy-scope.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/how-fms-manages-web-acls.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":111,"question_en":"A solutions architect is auditing the security setup or an AWS Lambda function for a company. The Lambda function retrieves, the latest changes from an Amazon Aurora database. The Lambda function and the database run in the same VPC. Lambda environment variables are providing the database credentials to the Lambda function. The Lambda function aggregates data and makes the data available in an Amazon S3 bucket that is configured for server-side encryption with AWS KMS managed encryption keys (SSE-KMS). The data must not travel across the Internet. If any database credentials become compromised, the company needs a solution that minimizes the impact of the compromise. What should the solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师正在审核公司的安全设置或 AWS Lambda 函数。Lambda 函数从 Amazon Aurora 数据库检索最新更改。Lambda 函数和 数据库在同一 VPC 中运行。Lambda 环境变量向 Lambda 函数提供数据库凭据。 Lambda 函数聚合数据并使数据在 Amazon S3 存储桶中可用，该存储桶配置为使用 AWS KMS 托管加密密钥 (SSE-KMS) 进行服务器端 加密。数据不得通过互联网传输。如果任何数据库凭据遭到泄露，公司需要一种解决方案来最大限度地减少泄露的影响。 解决方案架构师应该建议什么来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable IAM database authentication on the Aurora DB cluster. Change the IAM role for the Lambda function to allow the function to access the database by using IAM database authentication. Deploy a gateway VPC endpoint for Amazon S3 in the VPC.","B":"Enable IAM database authentication on the Aurora DB cluster. Change the IAM role for the Lambda function to allow the function to access the database by using IAM database authentication. Enforce HTTPS on the connection to Amazon S3 during data transfers.","C":"Save the database credentials in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Set up password rotation on the credentials in Parameter Store. Change the IAM role for the Lambda function to allow the function to access Parameter Store. Modify the Lambda function to retrieve the credentials from Parameter Store. Deploy a gateway VPC endpoint for Amazon S3 in the VPC.","D":"Save the database credentials in AWS Secrets Manager. Set up password rotation on the credentials in Secrets Manager. Change the IAM role for the Lambda function to allow the function to access Secrets Manager. Modify the Lambda function to retrieve the credentials from Secrets Manager. Enforce HTTPS on the connection to Amazon S3 during data transfers."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Aurora 数据库集群上启用 IAM 数据库身份验证。更改 Lambda 函数的 IAM 角色以允许该函数使用 IAM 数据库身份验证访问 数据库。在 VPC 中部署 Amazon S3 的网关 VPC 终端节点。","B":"在 Aurora 数据库集群上启用 IAM 数据库身份验证。更改 Lambda 函数的 IAM 角色以允许该函数使用 IAM 数据库身份验证访问 数据库。在数据传输期间对与 Amazon S3 的连接强制执行 HTTPS。","C":"将数据库凭证保存在 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store 中。在 Parameter Store 中的凭据上设置密码轮换。更改 Lambda 函 数的 IAM 角色以允许该函数访问 Parameter Store。修改 Lambda 函数以从 Parameter Store 检索凭证。在 VPC 中部署 Amazon S3 的 网关 VPC 终端节点。","D":"将数据库凭证保存在 AWS Secrets Manager 中。在 Secrets Manager 中的凭证上设置密码轮换。更改 Lambda 函数的 IAM 角色以 允许该函数访问 Secrets Manager。修改 Lambda 函数以从 Secrets Manager 检索凭证。在数据传输期间对与 Amazon S3 的连接强 制执行 HTTPS。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":87},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Two requirements decide this question: (1) minimize the impact of compromised database credentials, and (2) data must not travel across the Internet. IAM database authentication is the strongest answer to (1): the Lambda function uses its IAM role to request a short-lived authentication token (15-minute lifetime, generated with SigV4) instead of a stored password, so there are no static credentials in Lambda environment variables to compromise. For (2), a gateway VPC endpoint for Amazon S3 routes S3 traffic privately within the AWS network without an internet gateway or NAT device, so the data never traverses the public Internet. Option A combines both, satisfying both requirements. Options B and D fail requirement (2) because enforcing HTTPS only encrypts data in transit; the traffic still flows over the public Internet, which the requirement explicitly forbids. Option D (the dump's suggestion) also still relies on a static stored secret, a weaker credential mitigation than removing passwords entirely.","explanation_zh":"本題由兩項需求決定：(1) 將資料庫憑證遭洩漏的影響降到最低；(2) 資料不得經過網際網路傳輸。IAM database authentication 是 (1) 的最佳解：Lambda 函式以其 IAM role 取得短效的 authentication token（壽命 15 分鐘、以 SigV4 產生）來連線，而非使用儲存的密碼，因此 Lambda environment variables 中不再有可被竊取的靜態憑證。對於 (2)，Amazon S3 的 gateway VPC endpoint 會讓 S3 流量在 AWS 內部網路私有路由，不需 internet gateway 或 NAT device，資料完全不經過公共網際網路。選項 A 同時涵蓋兩者，符合兩項需求。選項 B 與 D 不符合需求 (2)，因為強制使用 HTTPS 只是加密傳輸中的資料，流量仍會走公共網際網路，這違反明確的需求。選項 D（dump 建議答案）同時仍依賴儲存的靜態 secret，憑證防護弱於完全移除密碼的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"IAM database authentication is good, but enforcing HTTPS to S3 only encrypts the data in transit; the traffic still travels over the public Internet, violating the explicit 'data must not travel across the Internet' requirement. A gateway VPC endpoint is needed instead.","why_zh":"IAM database authentication 很好，但對 S3 強制 HTTPS 只加密傳輸資料，流量仍走公共網際網路，違反「資料不得經過網際網路」的明確需求；應改用 gateway VPC endpoint。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The gateway VPC endpoint correctly keeps S3 traffic off the Internet, but storing the password in Parameter Store still keeps a static credential, and standard Parameter Store does not natively rotate RDS/Aurora credentials. IAM database authentication (eliminating the password entirely with 15-minute tokens) is a stronger mitigation of credential compromise.","why_zh":"gateway VPC endpoint 確實能讓 S3 流量不經網際網路，但把密碼存於 Parameter Store 仍保留靜態憑證，且標準 Parameter Store 不原生輪換 RDS/Aurora 憑證。IAM database authentication（以 15 分鐘 token 完全移除密碼）是更強的防護。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it fails requirement (2): enforcing HTTPS encrypts but still sends data over the public Internet rather than via a private gateway endpoint. It also still stores a static secret in Secrets Manager, a weaker credential mitigation than IAM database authentication which removes passwords entirely.","why_zh":"這是 dump 建議答案，但不符需求 (2)：強制 HTTPS 只是加密，資料仍走公共網際網路而非私有 gateway endpoint。它也仍在 Secrets Manager 保存靜態 secret，憑證防護弱於完全移除密碼的 IAM database authentication。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/UsingWithRDS.IAMDBAuth.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/gateway-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/vpc-endpoints-s3.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":112,"question_en":"A large mobile gaming company has successfully migrated all of its on-premises infrastructure to the AWS Cloud. A solutions architect is reviewing the environment to ensure that it was built according to the design and that it is running in alignment with the Well-Architected Framework. While reviewing previous monthly costs in Cost Explorer, the solutions architect notices that the creation and subsequent termination of several large instance types account for a high proportion of the costs. The solutions architect finds out that the company’s developers are launching new Amazon EC2 instances as part of their testing and that the developers are not using the appropriate instance types. The solutions architect must implement a control mechanism to limit the instance types that only the developers can launch. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家大型移动游戏公司已成功将其所有本地基础设施迁移到 AWS 云。解决方案架构师正在审查环境，以确保它是根据设计构建的， 并且它的运行符合架构完善的框架。 在检查 Cost Explorer 中之前的每月成本时，解决方案架构师注意到，多个大型实例类型的创建和后续终止占据了成本的很大一部 分。解决方案架构师发现，公司的开发人员正在启动新的 Amazon EC2 实例作为测试的一部分，并且开发人员没有使用适当的实例 类型。 解决方案架构师必须实现控制机制来限制只有开发人员可以启动的实例类型。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a desired-instance-type managed rule in AWS Config. Configure the rule with the instance types that are allowed. Attach the rule to an event to run each time a new EC2 instance is launched.","B":"In the EC2 console, create a launch template that specifies the instance types that are allowed. Assign the launch template to the developers’ IAM accounts.","C":"Create a new IAM policy. Specify the instance types that are allowed. Attach the policy to an IAM group that contains the IAM accounts for the developers","D":"Use EC2 Image Builder to create an image pipeline for the developers and assist them in the creation of a golden image."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS Config 中创建所需实例类型托管规则。使用允许的实例类型配置规则。将规则附加到事件以在每次启动新的 EC2 实例 时运行。","B":"在 EC2 控制台中，创建一个启动模板，指定允许的实例类型。将启动模板分配给开发人员的 IAM 账户。","C":"创建新的 IAM 策略。指定允许的实例类型。将策略附加到包含开发人员的 IAM 账户的 IAM 组","D":"使用 EC2 Image Builder 为开发人员创建镜像管道，并协助他们创建黄金镜像。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":113,"question_en":"A company is developing and hosting several projects in the AWS Cloud. The projects are developed across multiple AWS accounts under the same organization in AWS Organizations. The company requires the cost for cloud infrastructure to be allocated to the owning project. The team responsible for all of the AWS accounts has discovered that several Amazon EC2 instances are lacking the Project tag used for cost allocation. Which actions should a solutions architect lake to resolve the problem and prevent it from happening in the future? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 云中开发和托管多个项目。这些项目是跨 AWS Organizations 中同一组织下的多个 AWS 账户开发的。该公司要求 将云基础设施的成本分配给自己的项目。负责所有 AWS 账户的团队发现，多个 Amazon EC2 实例缺少用于成本分配的项目标签。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪些行动来解决问题并防止将来再次发生？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Config rule in each account to find resources with missing tags.","B":"Create an SCP in the organization with a deny action for ec2:RunInstances if the Project tag is missing.","C":"Use Amazon Inspector in the organization to find resources with missing tags.","D":"Create an IAM policy in each account with a deny action for ec2:RunInstances if the Project tag is missing.","E":"Create an AWS Config aggregator for the organization to collect a list of EC2 instances with the missing Project tag.","F":"Use AWS Security Hub to aggregate a list of EC2 instances with the missing Project tag."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个账户中创建 AWS Config 规则以查找缺少标签的资源。","B":"如果缺少项目标签，则在组织中创建一个 SCP，并对 ec2:RunInstances 执行拒绝操作。","C":"在组织中使用 Amazon Inspector 查找缺少标签的资源。","D":"如果缺少项目标签，请在每个账户中创建一个 IAM 策略，并对 ec2:RunInstances 执行拒绝操作。","E":"为组织创建一个 AWS Config 聚合器，以收集缺少项目标签的 EC2 实例列表。","F":"使用 AWS Security Hub 聚合缺少项目标签的 EC2 实例列表。"},"answer":["C","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ABE":81},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The question has two goals: resolve the current state (find existing EC2 instances missing the Project tag) and prevent recurrence (stop creation of untagged instances). A is correct: the AWS Config managed rule required-tags (REQUIRED_TAGS) supports AWS::EC2::Instance and flags resources missing specified tags such as Project, providing the per-account detection mechanism. E is correct: an AWS Config aggregator consolidates configuration and compliance data (including required-tags rule results) from an entire AWS Organization into a single read-only view, giving the central team the consolidated list of noncompliant instances. B is correct for prevention: an SCP is the organization-wide guardrail that denies ec2:RunInstances when the Project tag is absent (using an aws:RequestTag condition), and the AWS Organizations tag-policy best-practices doc explicitly recommends an SCP to set guardrails around resource-creation requests because account administrators can otherwise still create untagged resources. B is preferred over D because an SCP is centrally enforced across all member accounts, whereas D (an IAM policy in each account) must be authored, attached to every principal, and maintained per account with far higher operational overhead and no guarantee of org-wide coverage.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個目標：解決現況（找出缺少 Project 標籤的現有 EC2 執行個體）以及防止再發生（阻止建立未加標籤的執行個體）。A 正確：AWS Config 受管規則 required-tags（REQUIRED_TAGS）支援 AWS::EC2::Instance，可標示缺少指定標籤（如 Project）的資源，提供各帳戶層級的偵測機制。E 正確：AWS Config aggregator 可將整個 AWS Organizations 內各帳戶的組態與合規資料（含 required-tags 規則結果）彙整成單一唯讀檢視，讓中央團隊取得不合規執行個體的整合清單。B 正確（用於預防）：SCP 是組織層級的防護機制，可在缺少 Project 標籤時拒絕 ec2:RunInstances（使用 aws:RequestTag 條件）；AWS Organizations 的 tag policy 最佳實務文件明確建議使用 SCP 對資源建立請求設定防護，因為帳戶管理員仍可能建立未加標籤的資源。B 優於 D，因為 SCP 由組織集中強制套用至所有成員帳戶，而 D（在每個帳戶建立 IAM 政策）必須逐帳戶撰寫、附加到每個主體並維護，營運負擔高且無法保證全組織涵蓋。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Inspector is a vulnerability and security assessment service (CVEs, network reachability, software vulnerabilities); it does not detect resources with missing cost-allocation tags.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是漏洞與安全評估服務（CVE、網路可達性、軟體漏洞），無法偵測缺少成本分配標籤的資源。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An identity-based IAM policy created in each account must be attached to every principal and maintained per account, giving high operational overhead and no org-wide guarantee; the SCP in B is the centrally enforced organization-wide guardrail and is the correct prevention mechanism.","why_zh":"在每個帳戶建立的身分型 IAM 政策必須附加到每個主體並逐帳戶維護，營運負擔高且無組織層級保證；選項 B 的 SCP 才是集中強制的組織層級防護，是正確的預防機制。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"AWS Security Hub aggregates security findings from sources like GuardDuty, Inspector, and Config security standards; it is not used to produce a list of EC2 instances missing a specific cost-allocation tag.","why_zh":"AWS Security Hub 彙整來自 GuardDuty、Inspector 及 Config 安全標準等來源的安全發現，並非用來產出缺少特定成本分配標籤的 EC2 執行個體清單。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/required-tags.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/aggregate-data.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・複選"},{"id":114,"question_en":"A company has an on-premises monitoring solution using a PostgreSQL database for persistence of events. The database is unable to scale due to heavy ingestion and it frequently runs out of storage. The company wants to create a hybrid solution and has already set up a VPN connection between its network and AWS. The solution should include the following attributes: • Managed AWS services to minimize operational complexity. • A buffer that automatically scales to match the throughput of data and requires no ongoing administration. • A visualization tool to create dashboards to observe events in near-real time. • Support for semi-structured JSON data and dynamic schemas. Which combination of components will enable the company to create a monitoring solution that will satisfy these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个使用 PostgreSQL 数据库来持久保存事件的本地监控解决方案。由于大量摄取，数据库无法扩展，并且经常耗尽存 储空间。 该公司希望创建一个混合解决方案，并且已经在其网络和 AWS 之间建立了 VPN 连接。该解决方案应包括以下属性： • 托管AWS 服务，以最大限度地降低运营复杂性。 • 缓冲区可自动扩展以匹配数据吞吐量，且无需持续管理。 • 可视化工具，用于创建仪表板以近乎实时地观察事件。 • 支持半结构化JSON 数据和动态模式。 哪种组件组合将使公司能够创建满足这些要求的监控解决方案？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to buffer events. Create an AWS Lambda function to process and transform events.","B":"Create an Amazon Kinesis data stream to buffer events. Create an AWS Lambda function to process and transform events.","C":"Configure an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster to receive events. Use Amazon QuickSight to read from the database and create near-real-time visualizations and dashboards.","D":"Configure Amazon Elasticsearch Service (Amazon ES) to receive events. Use the Kibana endpoint deployed with Amazon ES to create near-real-time visualizations and dashboards.","E":"Configure an Amazon Neptune DB instance to receive events. Use Amazon QuickSight to read from the database and create near-real- time visualizations and dashboards."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 缓冲事件。创建 AWS Lambda 函数来处理和转换事件。","B":"创建 Amazon Kinesis 数据流来缓冲事件。创建 AWS Lambda 函数来处理和转换事件。","C":"配置 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群以接收事件。使用 Amazon QuickSight 从数据库中读取数据并创建近乎实时的可视 化和仪表板。","D":"配置 Amazon Elasticsearch Service (Amazon ES) 以接收事件。使用与 Amazon ES 一起部署的 Kibana 终端节点来创建近乎实时的 可视化和仪表板。","E":"配置 Amazon Neptune 数据库实例以接收事件。使用 Amazon QuickSight 从数据库中读取数据并创建近乎实时的可视化和仪表 板。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AD":93},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":115,"question_en":"A team collects and routes behavioral data for an entire company. The company runs a Multi-AZ VPC environment with public subnets, private subnets, and in internet gateway. Each public subnet also contains a NAT gateway. Most of the company’s applications read from and write to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams. Most of the workloads run in private subnets. A solutions architect must review the infrastructure. The solution architect needs to reduce costs and maintain the function of the applications. The solutions architect uses Cost Explorer and notices that the cost in the EC2-Other category is consistently high. A further review shows that NatGateway-Bytes charges are increasing the cost in the EC2-Other category. What should the solutions architect do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"团队收集并传送整个公司的行为数据。该公司运行具有公共子网、私有子网和互联网网关的多可用区 VPC 环境。每个公共子网还包 含一个 NAT 网关。该公司的大多数应用程序都会读取和写入 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams。大多数工作负载在私有子网中运行。 解决方案架构师必须审查基础架构。解决方案架构师需要降低成本并维护应用程序的功能。解决方案架构师使用 Cost Explorer 并注 意到 EC2-其他类别的成本始终很高。进一步的审查表明，NatGateway-Bytes 收费正在增加 EC2-其他类别的成本。 解决方案架构师应该怎样做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable VPC Flow Logs. Use Amazon Athena to analyze the logs for tra®c that can be removed. Ensure that security groups are blocking tra®c that is responsible for high costs.","B":"Add an interface VPC endpoint for Kinesis Data Streams to the VPC. Ensure that applications have the correct IAM permissions to use the interface VPC endpoint.","C":"Enable VPC Flow Logs and Amazon Detective. Review Detective findings for tra®c that is not related to Kinesis Data Streams. Configure security groups to block that tra®c.","D":"Add an interface VPC endpoint for Kinesis Data Streams to the VPC. Ensure that the VPC endpoint policy allows tra®c from the applications."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 VPC 流日志。使用 Amazon Athena 分析日志以查找可以删除的流量。确保安全组阻止导致高成本的流量。","B":"将 Kinesis Data Streams 的接口 VPC 终端节点添加到 VPC。确保应用程序具有正确的 IAM 权限来使用接口 VPC 终端节点。","C":"启用 VPC 流日志和 Amazon Detective。查看与 Kinesis Data Streams 无关的流量的检测结果。配置安全组以阻止该流量。","D":"将 Kinesis Data Streams 的接口 VPC 终端节点添加到 VPC。确保 VPC 终端节点策略允许来自应用程序的流量。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":92},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Security/IAM","Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":116,"question_en":"A retail company has an on-premises data center in Europe. The company also has a multi-Region AWS presence that includes the eu-west-1 and us-east-1 Regions. The company wants to be able to route network tra®c from its on-premises infrastructure into VPCs in either of those Regions. The company also needs to support tra®c that is routed directly between VPCs in those Regions. No single points of failure can exist on the network. The company already has created two 1 Gbps AWS Direct Connect connections from its on-premises data center. Each connection goes into a separate Direct Connect location in Europe for high availability. These two locations are named DX-A and DX-B, respectively. Each Region has a single AWS Transit Gateway that is configured to route all inter-VPC tra®c within that Region. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家零售公司在欧洲拥有一个本地数据中心。该公司还拥有多区域 AWS 业务，其中包括 eu-west-1 和 us-east-1 区域。该公司希望能 够将网络流量从其本地基础设施路由到这两个区域中的 VPC。该公司还需要支持在这些区域的 VPC 之间直接路由的流量。网络上不 能存在单点故障。 该公司已经从其本地数据中心创建了两个 1 Gbps AWS Direct Connect 连接。每个连接都会进入欧洲的一个单独的 Direct Connect 位 置，以实现高可用性。这两个位置分别命名为 DX-A 和 DX-B。每个区域都有一个 AWS Transit Gateway，配置为路由该区域内的所有 VPC 间流量。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a private VIF from the DX-A connection into a Direct Connect gateway. Create a private VIF from the DX-B connection into the same Direct Connect gateway for high availability. Associate both the eu-west-1 and us-east-1 transit gateways with the Direct Connect gateway. Peer the transit gateways with each other to support cross-Region routing.","B":"Create a transit VIF from the DX-A connection into a Direct Connect gateway. Associate the eu-west-1 transit gateway with this Direct Connect gateway. Create a transit VIF from the DX-8 connection into a separate Direct Connect gateway. Associate the us-east-1 transit gateway with this separate Direct Connect gateway. Peer the Direct Connect gateways with each other to support high availability and cross-Region routing.","C":"Create a transit VIF from the DX-A connection into a Direct Connect gateway. Create a transit VIF from the DX-B connection into the same Direct Connect gateway for high availability. Associate both the eu-west-1 and us-east-1 transit gateways with this Direct Connect gateway. Configure the Direct Connect gateway to route tra®c between the transit gateways.","D":"Create a transit VIF from the DX-A connection into a Direct Connect gateway. Create a transit VIF from the DX-B connection into the same Direct Connect gateway for high availability. Associate both the eu-west-1 and us-east-1 transit gateways with this Direct Connect gateway. Peer the transit gateways with each other to support cross-Region routing."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建从 DX-A 连接到 Direct Connect 网关的专用 VIF。创建从 DX-B 连接到同一 Direct Connect 网关的专用 VIF，以实现高可用性。 将 eu-west-1 和 us-east-1 中转网关与 Direct Connect 网关关联。将中转网关彼此对等以支持跨区域路由。","B":"创建从 DX-A 连接到 Direct Connect 网关的中转 VIF。将 eu-west-1 中转网关与此 Direct Connect 网关关联。创建从 DX-8 连接到单 独的 Direct Connect 网关的中转 VIF。将 us-east-1 中转网关与此单独的 Direct Connect 网关关联。将 Direct Connect 网关彼此对等 以支持高可用性和跨区域路由。","C":"创建从 DX-A 连接到 Direct Connect 网关的中转 VIF。创建从 DX-B 连接到同一 Direct Connect 网关的中转 VIF，以实现高可用性。 将 eu-west-1 和 us-east-1 中转网关与此 Direct Connect 网关关联。配置 Direct Connect 网关以在中转网关之间路由流量。","D":"创建从 DX-A 连接到 Direct Connect 网关的中转 VIF。创建从 DX-B 连接到同一 Direct Connect 网关的中转 VIF，以实现高可用性。 将 eu-west-1 和 us-east-1 中转网关与此 Direct Connect 网关关联。将中转网关彼此对等以支持跨区域路由。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":95},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"To associate a Direct Connect gateway with a transit gateway you must use a transit VIF (a private VIF associates only with a virtual private gateway), which immediately rules out Option A. A single, globally available Direct Connect gateway can have up to six Regional transit gateways associated with it and is itself highly available (it acts as a distributed set of BGP route reflectors with no single point of failure), so one DX gateway with two transit VIFs (one over DX-A and one over DX-B into separate DX locations) satisfies the no-single-point-of-failure requirement and lets on-premises reach VPCs in both eu-west-1 and us-east-1. However, AWS docs explicitly state that a Direct Connect gateway does NOT allow gateway associations on the same DX gateway to send traffic to each other, so it cannot provide direct cross-Region VPC-to-VPC routing between the two transit gateways. Direct cross-Region VPC-to-VPC traffic must be handled by transit gateway inter-Region peering, which is exactly what Option D adds. Option D is therefore the only choice that meets all requirements: transit VIFs into one DX gateway for HA + both TGWs associated for on-prem reachability + TGW peering for direct inter-Region traffic.","explanation_zh":"要將 Direct Connect gateway 與 transit gateway 關聯，必須使用 transit VIF（private VIF 只能與 virtual private gateway 關聯），這直接排除選項 A。單一且全球可用的 Direct Connect gateway 最多可關聯六個區域的 transit gateway，且本身具備高可用性（它作為分散式 BGP route reflector，沒有單點故障），因此用一個 DX gateway 搭配兩條 transit VIF（一條走 DX-A、一條走 DX-B，分別進入不同的 DX location）即可滿足無單點故障的需求，並讓地端能連到 eu-west-1 與 us-east-1 兩個區域的 VPC。然而 AWS 文件明確指出，同一個 Direct Connect gateway 上的 gateway association 之間「不允許」互相傳送流量，因此無法在兩個 transit gateway 之間提供直接的跨區域 VPC 對 VPC 路由。直接的跨區域 VPC 對 VPC 流量必須透過 transit gateway 的跨區域 peering 來處理，而這正是選項 D 所增加的設定。因此 D 是唯一同時滿足所有需求的答案：transit VIF 進入單一 DX gateway 達成 HA、兩個 TGW 關聯以提供地端連通性、TGW peering 提供直接的跨區域流量。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses private VIFs into a Direct Connect gateway, but a private VIF associates only with a virtual private gateway, not a transit gateway. Associating transit gateways requires a transit VIF, so this configuration is technically invalid.","why_zh":"使用 private VIF 連入 Direct Connect gateway，但 private VIF 只能與 virtual private gateway 關聯，無法關聯 transit gateway。關聯 transit gateway 需要 transit VIF，因此此設定在技術上無效。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Uses two separate Direct Connect gateways (one per Region) and tries to 'peer the Direct Connect gateways with each other.' Direct Connect gateways cannot be peered with one another, and this design also creates separate single-VIF paths per Region rather than HA across both DX connections for each Region.","why_zh":"使用兩個獨立的 Direct Connect gateway（每區域一個），並試圖讓兩個 DX gateway 互相 peering。Direct Connect gateway 之間無法 peering，且此設計使每個區域只有單一 VIF 路徑，而非為每個區域提供跨兩條 DX 連線的高可用性。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Claims you can 'configure the Direct Connect gateway to route traffic between the transit gateways.' AWS docs explicitly state a Direct Connect gateway does not allow gateway associations on the same DX gateway to send traffic to each other, so it cannot route inter-TGW (cross-Region VPC-to-VPC) traffic. This requirement needs transit gateway peering.","why_zh":"聲稱可以「設定 Direct Connect gateway 在 transit gateway 之間路由流量」。AWS 文件明確指出，同一個 DX gateway 上的 gateway association 之間不允許互相傳送流量，因此無法路由 TGW 之間（跨區域 VPC 對 VPC）的流量。此需求須透過 transit gateway peering 達成。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directconnect/latest/UserGuide/direct-connect-transit-gateways.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directconnect/latest/UserGuide/direct-connect-gateways-intro.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/designing-control-tower-landing-zone/transit-vif.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/tgw-peering.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":117,"question_en":"A company is running an application in the AWS Cloud. The company's security team must approve the creation of all new IAM users. When a new IAM user is created, all access for the user must be removed automatically. The security team must then receive a notification to approve the user. The company has a multi-Region AWS CloudTrail trail in the AWS account. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 云中运行应用程序。公司的安全团队必须批准所有新 IAM 用户的创建。创建新的 IAM 用户时，必须自动删除该用 户的所有访问权限。然后，安全团队必须收到批准用户的通知。该公司在 AWS 账户中拥有多区域 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪。 哪种步骤组合可以满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge (Amazon CloudWatch Events) rule. Define a pattern with the detail-type value set to AWS API Call via CloudTrail and an eventName of CreateUser.","B":"Configure CloudTrail to send a notification for the CreateUser event to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic.","C":"Invoke a container that runs in Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) with AWS Fargate technology to remove access.","D":"Invoke an AWS Step Functions state machine to remove access.","E":"Use Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to notify the security team.","F":"Use Amazon Pinpoint to notify the security team."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 Amazon EventBridge (Amazon CloudWatch Events) 规则。定义一个模式，将详细信息类型值设置为通过 CloudTrail 进行的 AWS API 调用，并将 eventName 设置为 CreateUser。","B":"配置 CloudTrail 以将 CreateUser 事件的通知发送到 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 主题。","C":"使用 AWS Fargate 技术调用在 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 中运行的容器以删除访问权限。","D":"调用 AWS Step Functions 状态机以删除访问权限。","E":"使用 Amazon Simple notification Service (Amazon SNS) 通知安全团队。","F":"使用 Amazon Pinpoint 通知安全团队。"},"answer":["A","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ADE":71},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・複選"},{"id":118,"question_en":"A company wants to migrate to AWS. The company wants to use a multi-account structure with centrally managed access to all accounts and applications. The company also wants to keep the tra®c on a private network. Multi-factor authentication (MFA) is required at login, and specific roles are assigned to user groups. The company must create separate accounts for development. staging, production, and shared network. The production account and the shared network account must have connectivity to all accounts. The development account and the staging account must have access only to each other. Which combination of steps should a solutions architect take 10 meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司想要迁移到 AWS。该公司希望使用多帐户结构来集中管理对所有帐户和应用程序的访问。该公司还希望将流量保留在专用 网络上。登录时需要多重身份验证（MFA），并将特定角色分配给用户组。 公司必须为开发创建单独的账户。登台、制作和共享网络。生产帐户和共享网络帐户必须连接到所有帐户。开发帐户和临时帐户必 须只能相互访问。 解决方案架构师应采取哪些步骤组合才能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Deploy a landing zone environment by using AWS Control Tower. Enroll accounts and invite existing accounts into the resulting organization in AWS Organizations.","B":"Enable AWS Security Hub in all accounts to manage cross-account access. Collect findings through AWS CloudTrail to force MFA login.","C":"Create transit gateways and transit gateway VPC attachments in each account. Configure appropriate route tables.","D":"Set up and enable AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On). Create appropriate permission sets with required MFA for existing accounts.","E":"Enable AWS Control Tower in all accounts to manage routing between accounts. Collect findings through AWS CloudTrail to force MFA login.","F":"Create IAM users and groups. Configure MFA for all users. Set up Amazon Cognoto user pools and Identity pools to manage access to accounts and between accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Control Tower 部署登陆区环境。注册账户并邀请现有账户加入 AWS Organizations 中生成的组织。","B":"在所有账户中启用 AWS Security Hub 以管理跨账户访问。通过 AWS CloudTrail 收集结果以强制 MFA 登录。","C":"在每个账户中创建中转网关和中转网关 VPC 连接。配置适当的路由表。","D":"设置并启用 AWS IAM Identity Center（AW​S 单点登录）。为现有帐户创建具有所需 MFA 的适当权限集。","E":"在所有账户中启用 AWS Control Tower 以管理账户之间的路由。通过 AWS CloudTrail 收集结果以强制 MFA 登录。","F":"创建 IAM 用户和组。为所有用户配置 MFA。设置 Amazon Cognoto 用户池和身份池来管理对账户以及账户之间的访问。"},"answer":["B","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ACD":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Migration","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The three requirements map cleanly to three services. (A) AWS Control Tower deploys a landing zone that orchestrates AWS Organizations, AWS Service Catalog, and IAM Identity Center, and supports enrolling/inviting existing accounts, giving the centrally governed multi-account structure (dev, staging, production, shared network). (D) IAM Identity Center (AWS SSO) provides centralized workforce access with permission sets (roles mapped to user groups) and enforced MFA at login. (C) AWS Transit Gateway with VPC attachments and transit gateway route tables keeps traffic on a private network and provides the selective routing needed: associate prod and shared-network attachments to a route table that reaches all VPCs, and put dev and staging in their own route table that only propagates each other's routes, so they reach only each other. The dump's BDF is wrong: AWS Security Hub aggregates security findings and does not manage cross-account access, AWS CloudTrail only logs API calls and cannot force MFA, and Amazon Cognito is for application end-user identity rather than centralized workforce/console access across accounts.","explanation_zh":"三項需求恰好對應三個服務。(A) AWS Control Tower 部署 landing zone，協調 AWS Organizations、AWS Service Catalog 與 IAM Identity Center，並支援將既有帳戶 enroll/invite 進來，提供集中治理的多帳戶結構 (dev、staging、production、shared network)。(D) IAM Identity Center (AWS SSO) 提供集中式人員存取，透過 permission sets (對應使用者群組的角色) 並在登入時強制 MFA。(C) AWS Transit Gateway 搭配 VPC attachments 與 transit gateway route tables，可讓流量保持在私有網路並達成選擇性路由：把 production 與 shared network 的 attachment 關聯到可達所有 VPC 的 route table，而把 dev 與 staging 放在僅互相 propagate 路由的獨立 route table，使其只能互通。dump 的 BDF 錯誤：AWS Security Hub 是彙整安全 findings，無法管理跨帳戶存取；AWS CloudTrail 只記錄 API 呼叫，無法強制 MFA；Amazon Cognito 用於應用程式終端使用者身分，而非跨帳戶集中的人員/主控台存取。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Security Hub aggregates security findings; it does not manage cross-account access. CloudTrail only records API activity and cannot force MFA at login.","why_zh":"AWS Security Hub 彙整安全 findings，並非管理跨帳戶存取；CloudTrail 只記錄 API 活動，無法在登入時強制 MFA。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"AWS Control Tower governs accounts/OUs and applies guardrails; it does not manage VPC routing between accounts. CloudTrail cannot force MFA.","why_zh":"AWS Control Tower 治理帳戶/OU 並套用 guardrails，不負責帳戶間的 VPC 路由；CloudTrail 也無法強制 MFA。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Per-account IAM users are not centrally managed SSO, and Amazon Cognito user/identity pools provide application end-user identity, not workforce console access across AWS accounts.","why_zh":"各帳戶各自建立 IAM users 並非集中管理的 SSO；Amazon Cognito user/identity pools 提供應用程式終端使用者身分，而非跨 AWS 帳戶的人員主控台存取。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/what-is-control-tower.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/enroll-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/tgw-route-tables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/tgw-vpc-attachments.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":119,"question_en":"A company runs its application in the eu-west-1 Region and has one account for each of its environments: development, testing, and production. All the environments are running 24 hours a day, 7 days a week by using stateful Amazon EC2 instances and Amazon RDS for MySQL databases. The databases are between 500 GB and 800 GB in size. The development team and testing team work on business days during business hours, but the production environment operates 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. The company wants to reduce costs. All resources are tagged with an environment tag with either development, testing, or production as the key. What should a solutions architect do to reduce costs with the LEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"一家公司在 eu-west-1 区域运行其应用程序，并为其每个环境（开发、测试和生产）拥有一个帐户。所有环境都使用有状态 Amazon EC2 实例和 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库，每周 7 天、每天 24 小时运行。数据库大小在 500 GB 到 800 GB 之间。 开发团队和测试团队在工作日上班时间工作，但生产环境每周7天、每天24小时运行。该公司希望降低成本。所有资源都标有环境标 签，以开发、测试或生产为键。 解决方案架构师应该如何做才能以最少的运营工作来降低成本？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that runs once every day. Configure the rule to invoke one AWS Lambda function that starts or slops instances based on me tag, day, and time.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that runs every business day in the evening. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function that stops instances based on the tag. Create a second EventBridge rule that runs every business day in the morning. Configure the second rule lo invoke another Lambda function that starts instances based on the tag.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that runs every business day in the evening, Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function that terminates, instances based on the lag. Create a second EventBridge rule that runs every business day in the morning. Configure the second rule lo invoke another Lambda function that restores the instances from their last backup based on the tag.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that runs every hour. Configure the rule to invoke one AWS Lambda function that terminates or restores instances from their last backup based on the tag. day, and time."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建每天运行一次的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。配置规则以调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数根据我的标签、日期和时间启 动或停止实例。","B":"创建在每个工作日晚上运行的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。配置规则以调用根据标签停止实例的 AWS Lambda 函数。创建第二个 在每个工作日早上运行的 EventBridge 规则。配置第二条规则以调用另一个 Lambda 函数，该函数根据标签启动实例。","C":"创建一个在每个工作日晚上运行的 Amazon EventBridge 规则，配置该规则以调用根据延迟终止实例的 AWS Lambda 函数。创建 第二个在每个工作日早上运行的 EventBridge 规则。配置第二条规则以调用另一个 Lambda 函数，该函数根据标签从上次备份中 恢复实例。","D":"创建每小时运行一次的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。配置规则以调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数根据标签终止实例或从上次 备份恢复实例。日期和时间。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The instances are stateful, so they must be stopped/started (not terminated) to preserve state; this immediately eliminates options C and D, which terminate instances and restore from backup (operationally heavy, slow, and risky for stateful workloads). Between A and B, both use stop/start, but the requirement is to stop dev/test in the evening and start them in the morning on business days only. Stopping and starting happen at two different times of day, so a single rule that runs 'once every day' (option A) cannot perform both the morning start and the evening stop with a single daily trigger. Option B correctly uses two EventBridge schedules: one in the evening to stop tagged instances and one in the morning to start them, and 'every business day' naturally keeps dev/test off over weekends while production (not started by these rules) stays running 24/7. This is the standard, low-effort pattern AWS documents (Instance Scheduler on AWS / EventBridge scheduled rules invoking Lambda by tag).","explanation_zh":"這些執行個體是有狀態（stateful）的，因此必須以停止/啟動（stop/start）而非終止（terminate）的方式來保留狀態；這立即排除了 C 與 D，因為它們會終止執行個體並從備份還原，對有狀態工作負載而言操作繁重、緩慢且有風險。在 A 與 B 之間，兩者都採用 stop/start，但需求是在工作日的傍晚停止 dev/test、早上再啟動。停止與啟動發生在一天中的兩個不同時間，因此單一條「每天執行一次」的規則（選項 A）無法用一次每日觸發同時完成早上啟動與傍晚停止。選項 B 正確地使用兩條 EventBridge 排程：傍晚一條依 tag 停止執行個體、早上一條啟動，且『每個工作日』自然讓 dev/test 在週末保持關閉，而 production（不被這些規則啟動）維持 24/7 運行。這正是 AWS 文件記載的標準、低操作量做法（Instance Scheduler on AWS / EventBridge 排程規則依 tag 觸發 Lambda）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A single EventBridge rule that runs 'once every day' fires at one time of day, so it cannot perform both the morning start and the evening stop. Starting and stopping require two different trigger times, which one daily rule cannot provide.","why_zh":"單一條『每天執行一次』的 EventBridge 規則只在一天中的某個時間觸發，無法同時完成早上啟動與傍晚停止。啟動與停止需要兩個不同的觸發時間，一條每日規則無法提供。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Terminating stateful EC2 instances destroys instance state, and restoring from backup each morning is slow, error-prone, and high operational effort, violating both 'stateful' and 'least operational effort'.","why_zh":"終止有狀態的 EC2 執行個體會摧毀執行個體狀態，每天早上從備份還原既緩慢又易出錯且操作量大，違反『有狀態』與『最少操作量』兩項要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Running every hour to terminate/restore stateful instances is even more disruptive and operationally costly; terminating destroys state and frequent restore-from-backup is impractical for 500-800 GB databases.","why_zh":"每小時執行一次來終止/還原有狀態執行個體更具破壞性且操作成本更高；終止會摧毀狀態，而對 500-800 GB 資料庫頻繁從備份還原並不實際。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/solutions/latest/instance-scheduler-on-aws/instance-shutdown-behavior.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/optimize-costs-microsoft-workloads/windows-ec2-schedules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-create-rule-schedule.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_StopInstance.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":120,"question_en":"A company is building a software-as-a-service (SaaS) solution on AWS. The company has deployed an Amazon API Gateway REST API with AWS Lambda integration in multiple AWS Regions and in the same production account. The company offers tiered pricing that gives customers the ability to pay for the capacity to make a certain number of API calls per second. The premium tier offers up to 3,000 calls per second, and customers are identified by a unique API key. Several premium tier customers in various Regions report that they receive error responses of 429 Too Many Requests from multiple API methods during peak usage hours. Logs indicate that the Lambda function is never invoked. What could be the cause of the error messages for these customers?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 上构建软件即服务 (SaaS) 解决方案。该公司已在多个 AWS 区域和同一生产账户中部署了与 AWS Lambda 集成的 Amazon API Gateway REST API。 该公司提供分级定价，使客户能够为每秒进行一定数量的 API 调用的容量付费。高级层每秒提供多达 3,000 个调用，并且通过唯一 的 API 密钥来识别客户。不同区域的多个高级客户报告称，他们在高峰使用时段收到来自多个 API 方法的 429 Too Many Requests 错 误响应。日志表明 Lambda 函数从未被调用。 这些客户收到错误消息的原因可能是什么？","options_en":{"A":"The Lambda function reached its concurrency limit.","B":"The Lambda function its Region limit for concurrency.","C":"The company reached its API Gateway account limit for calls per second.","D":"The company reached its API Gateway default per-method limit for calls per second."},"options_zh":{"A":"Lambda 函数达到了并发限制。","B":"Lambda 函数的并发区域限制。","C":"该公司达到了其 API 网关帐户每秒调用的限制。","D":"该公司达到了 API 网关默认的每个方法每秒调用次数限制。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":96},"tags":["Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":121,"question_en":"A financial company is planning to migrate its web application from on premises to AWS. The company uses a third-party security tool to monitor the inbound tra®c to the application. The company has used the security tool for the last 15 years, and the tool has no cloud solutions available from its vendor. The company's security team is concerned about how to integrate the security tool with AWS technology. The company plans to deploy the application migration to AWS on Amazon EC2 instances. The EC2 instances will run in an Auto Scaling group in a dedicated VPC. The company needs to use the security tool to inspect all packets that come in and out of the VPC. This inspection must occur in real time and must not affect the application's performance. A solutions architect must design a target architecture on AWS that is highly available within an AWS Region. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家金融公司正计划将其 Web 应用程序从本地迁移到 AWS。该公司使用第三方安全工具来监控应用程序的入站流量。该公司在过去 15 年中一直使用该安全工具，并且该工具的供应商没有提供任何云解决方案。该公司的安全团队关心的是如何将安全工具与AWS技 术集成。 该公司计划在 Amazon EC2 实例上将应用程序迁移部署到 AWS。EC2 实例将在专用 VPC 中的 Auto Scaling 组中运行。公司需要使用安 全工具对进出VPC的所有数据包进行检查。此检查必须实时进行，并且不得影响应用程序的性能。解决方案架构师必须在 AWS 上设 计一个在 AWS 区域内高度可用的目标架构。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the security tool on EC2 instances m a new Auto Scaling group in the existing VPC","B":"Deploy the web application behind a Network Load Balancer","C":"Deploy an Application Load Balancer in front of the security tool instances","D":"Provision a Gateway Load Balancer for each Availability Zone to redirect the tra®c to the security tool","E":"Provision a transit gateway to facilitate communication between VPCs."},"options_zh":{"A":"在现有 VPC 中的新 Auto Scaling 组中的 EC2 实例上部署安全工具","B":"在网络负载均衡器后面部署 Web 应用程序","C":"在安全工具实例之前部署应用程序负载均衡器","D":"为每个可用区配置网关负载均衡器，以将流量重定向到安全工具","E":"配置中转网关以促进 VPC 之间的通信。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"DE":50,"AD":48},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario requires inserting a third-party security appliance (that has no cloud-native version and must run on EC2) inline to inspect ALL packets in and out of a single dedicated VPC, in real time, highly available, without affecting application performance. The AWS-purpose-built mechanism for this is the Gateway Load Balancer (GWLB), which operates at OSI Layer 3, transparently forwards all IP packets via the GENEVE protocol to registered appliances, scales with demand, and supports multi-AZ HA via GWLB endpoints and route tables (option D). The appliances themselves must be deployed and made highly available/scalable, which means running the security tool on EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group registered as the GWLB target group (option A). A and D are interdependent: GWLB is useless without appliance targets, and EC2 appliances need GWLB to receive transparent inline traffic. Option E (Transit Gateway) addresses VPC-to-VPC or centralized multi-VPC inspection; the question specifies a single dedicated VPC, so a Transit Gateway is unnecessary, and E does not deploy the security tool at all.","explanation_zh":"情境要求將無雲端版本、必須在 EC2 上執行的第三方安全工具以 inline 方式插入,即時檢查單一專用 VPC 進出的所有封包,且需高可用並不影響應用程式效能。AWS 為此設計的機制是 Gateway Load Balancer (GWLB):它運作於 OSI 第三層,透過 GENEVE 協定將所有 IP 封包透明地轉送給已註冊的設備,隨需求自動擴展,並透過 GWLB endpoint 與 route table 達成跨 AZ 高可用 (選項 D)。設備本身必須部署且具備高可用與擴展能力,也就是把安全工具部署在 Auto Scaling group 的 EC2 instances 上,並註冊為 GWLB 的 target group (選項 A)。A 與 D 互相依存:沒有設備目標,GWLB 毫無用處;EC2 設備也需要 GWLB 才能接收透明的 inline 流量。選項 E (Transit Gateway) 用於 VPC 對 VPC 或集中式多 VPC 檢查;題目明確指出是單一專用 VPC,因此不需要 Transit Gateway,且 E 根本沒有部署安全工具。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A Network Load Balancer in front of the web application distributes client traffic to the app but does nothing to route packets through the third-party inspection appliance; it does not provide transparent inline packet inspection of all VPC traffic.","why_zh":"在 web 應用程式前放 Network Load Balancer 只是把用戶流量分配給應用程式,無法將封包導向第三方檢查設備,也無法對所有 VPC 流量做透明的 inline 封包檢查。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An Application Load Balancer is an OSI Layer 7 HTTP/HTTPS proxy and cannot transparently forward arbitrary IP packets to inspection appliances. ALB terminates connections and is not the correct insertion mechanism for a packet-inspection appliance; GWLB (Layer 3, GENEVE) is required instead.","why_zh":"Application Load Balancer 是 OSI 第七層的 HTTP/HTTPS 代理,無法將任意 IP 封包透明轉送給檢查設備。ALB 會終止連線,並非封包檢查設備的正確插入機制;此處需要的是 GWLB(第三層、GENEVE)。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Transit Gateway is the inter-VPC/centralized hub used for VPC-to-VPC or multi-VPC inspection designs. The scenario uses a single dedicated VPC, so a Transit Gateway is not needed; furthermore E does not deploy the actual security appliances, which is a mandatory step.","why_zh":"Transit Gateway 是用於 VPC 對 VPC 或多 VPC 集中式檢查的中樞。本情境只有單一專用 VPC,因此不需要 Transit Gateway;此外 E 根本沒有部署實際的安全設備,而部署設備是必要步驟。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/gateway/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/vpce-gateway-load-balancer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/inline-traffic-inspection-third-party-appliances/solution-options.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/gateway/edit-load-balancer-attributes.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識・複選"},{"id":122,"question_en":"A company has purchased appliances from different vendors. The appliances all have IoT sensors. The sensors send status information in the vendors' proprietary formats to a legacy application that parses the information into JSON. The parsing is simple, but each vendor has a unique format. Once daily, the application parses all the JSON records and stores the records in a relational database for analysis. The company needs to design a new data analysis solution that can deliver faster and optimize costs. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司从不同的供应商购买了设备。这些设备都配有物联网传感器。传感器以供应商专有格式将状态信息发送到遗留应用程序， 该应用程序将信息解析为 JSON。解析很简单，但每个供应商都有独特的格式。应用程序每天一次解析所有 JSON 记录并将记录存储 在关系数据库中以供分析。 该公司需要设计一种新的数据分析解决方案，可以更快地交付并优化成本。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Connect the IoT sensors to AWS IoT Core. Set a rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to parse the information and save a .csv file to Amazon. S3 Use AWS Glue to catalog the files. Use Amazon Athena and Amazon QuickSight for analysis.","B":"Migrate the application server to AWS Fargate, which will receive the information from IoT sensors and parse the information into a relational format. Save the parsed information to Amazon Redshlft for analysis.","C":"Create an AWS Transfer for SFTP server. Update the IoT sensor code to send the information as a .csv file through SFTP to the server. Use AWS Glue to catalog the files. Use Amazon Athena for analysis.","D":"Use AWS Snowball Edge to collect data from the IoT sensors directly to perform local analysis. Periodically collect the data into Amazon Redshift to perform global analysis."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 IoT 传感器连接到 AWS IoT Core。设置规则以调用 AWS Lambda 函数来解析信息并将 .csv 文件保存到 Amazon。S3 使用 AWS Glue 对文件进行编目。使用 Amazon Athena 和 Amazon QuickSight 进行分析。","B":"将应用程序服务器迁移到 AWS Fargate，它将接收来自 IoT 传感器的信息并将信息解析为关系格式。将解析的信息保存到 Amazon Redshlft 进行分析。","C":"创建 AWS Transfer for SFTP 服务器。更新 IoT 传感器代码以通过 SFTP 将信息作为 .csv 文件发送到服务器。使用 AWS Glue 对文 件进行编目。使用 Amazon Athena 进行分析。","D":"使用 AWS Snowball Edge 直接从 IoT 传感器收集数据以执行本地分析。定期将数据收集到 Amazon Redshift 中以执行全局分析。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":82,"B":18},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Analytics","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirements are to deliver analysis faster (replace the once-daily batch with near-real-time processing) and to optimize costs. Option A is a fully serverless pipeline: connect sensors to AWS IoT Core, use a Rules Engine rule to asynchronously invoke a Lambda function that performs the simple per-vendor parsing, write the results as files to Amazon S3, catalog them with AWS Glue, and query/visualize with Amazon Athena and Amazon QuickSight. AWS docs confirm the IoT Rules Engine can select message payload data and invoke Lambda, and that S3 + Glue + Athena + QuickSight form the standard serverless data-lake analytics stack. This removes the daily batch latency and the always-on legacy app server and relational database, so it is both faster and lower cost (pay-per-query Athena). Option A is the only choice that addresses both qualifiers while preserving the per-vendor parsing logic.","explanation_zh":"需求是讓分析更快（以近即時處理取代每日一次的批次）並優化成本。選項 A 是完全無伺服器的管線：將感測器連到 AWS IoT Core，使用 Rules Engine 規則以非同步方式觸發 AWS Lambda 進行各廠商簡單的解析，將結果以檔案寫入 Amazon S3，再用 AWS Glue 建立目錄，並以 Amazon Athena 與 Amazon QuickSight 查詢與視覺化。AWS 文件確認 IoT Rules Engine 可從訊息酬載選取資料並觸發 Lambda，而 S3 + Glue + Athena + QuickSight 是標準的無伺服器資料湖分析架構。此方案移除了每日批次延遲，也移除了長時間運行的舊版應用伺服器與關聯式資料庫，因此既更快又更省成本（Athena 按查詢計費）。A 是唯一同時滿足兩個限定條件又保留各廠商解析邏輯的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Migrating the parsing app to AWS Fargate and storing in Amazon Redshift keeps an always-running compute service and a provisioned, always-on data warehouse cluster. This does not optimize costs and retains the monolithic parsing application rather than simplifying it.","why_zh":"將解析應用遷移到 AWS Fargate 並存入 Amazon Redshift，會保留持續運行的運算服務與長時間開啟的佈建型資料倉儲叢集，無法優化成本，也仍保留笨重的解析應用。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but is wrong: it requires modifying proprietary IoT sensor firmware from multiple vendors to act as SFTP clients sending CSV, which IoT sensors generally cannot do. SFTP also performs no parsing, so the core proprietary-to-JSON parsing problem is left unsolved.","why_zh":"這是題庫建議答案但錯誤：它要求修改多家廠商的專有 IoT 感測器韌體，使其充當 SFTP 用戶端傳送 CSV，而 IoT 感測器通常無法做到。SFTP 也不執行任何解析，核心的專有格式轉 JSON 問題仍未解決。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Snowball Edge is an offline/edge data transfer and compute appliance, not a streaming IoT ingestion or analytics service. Periodically loading into Amazon Redshift is slow (not faster) and uses an always-on warehouse, so it neither speeds up analysis nor optimizes cost.","why_zh":"AWS Snowball Edge 是離線/邊緣資料傳輸與運算裝置，並非串流 IoT 擷取或分析服務。定期載入 Amazon Redshift 速度慢（並非更快）且使用長時間開啟的倉儲，因此既無法加速分析也無法優化成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-iot.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/iot-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/aws-serverless-data-analytics-pipeline/serverless-data-lake-centric-analytics-architecture.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/what-is-glue.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/what-is.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":123,"question_en":"A company is migrating some of its applications to AWS. The company wants to migrate and modernize the applications quickly after it finalizes networking and security strategies. The company has set up an AWS Direct Connect connection in a central network account. The company expects to have hundreds of AWS accounts and VPCs in the near future. The corporate network must be able to access the resources on AWS seamlessly and also must be able to communicate with all the VPCs. The company also wants to route its cloud resources to the internet through its on-premises data center. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在将其部分应用程序迁移到 AWS。该公司希望在最终确定网络和安全策略后迅速迁移应用程序并使其现代化。该公司已 在中央网络帐户中建立了 AWS Direct Connect 连接。 该公司预计在不久的将来将拥有数百个 AWS 账户和 VPC。公司网络必须能够无缝访问AWS上的资源，并且必须能够与所有VPC通 信。该公司还希望通过其本地数据中心将其云资源路由到互联网。 哪种步骤组合可以满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a Direct Connect gateway in the central account. In each of the accounts, create an association proposal by using the Direct Connect gateway and the account ID for every virtual private gateway.","B":"Create a Direct Connect gateway and a transit gateway in the central network account. Attach the transit gateway to the Direct Connect gateway by using a transit VIF.","C":"Provision an internet gateway. Attach the internet gateway to subnets. Allow internet tra®c through the gateway.","D":"Share the transit gateway with other accounts. Attach VPCs to the transit gateway.","E":"Provision VPC peering as necessary.","F":"Provision only private subnets. Open the necessary route on the transit gateway and customer gateway to allow outbound internet tra®c from AWS to ­ow through NAT services that run in the data center."},"options_zh":{"A":"在中央账户中创建专线网关。在每个帐户中，使用 Direct Connect 网关和每个虚拟专用网关的帐户 ID 创建关联提案。","B":"在中央网络帐户中创建 Direct Connect 网关和中转网关。使用中转 VIF 将中转网关连接到 Direct Connect 网关。","C":"配置互联网网关。将 Internet 网关连接到子网。允许互联网流量通过网关。","D":"与其他账户共享中转网关。将 VPC 连接到中转网关。","E":"根据需要配置 VPC 对等互连。","F":"仅配置私有子网。在中转网关和客户网关上打开必要的路由，以允许来自 AWS 的出站互联网流量流经数据中心中运行的 NAT 服务。"},"answer":["B","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BDF":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":124,"question_en":"A company has hundreds of AWS accounts. The company recently implemented a centralized internal process for purchasing new Reserved Instances and modifying existing Reserved Instances. This process requires all business units that want to purchase or modify Reserved Instances to submit requests to a dedicated team for procurement. Previously, business units directly purchased or modified Reserved Instances in their own respective AWS accounts autonomously. A solutions architect needs to enforce the new process in the most secure way possible. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司拥有数百个 AWS 账户。该公司最近实施了一个集中的内部流程来购买新的预留实例和修改现有的预留实例。此流程要求所 有想要购买或修改预留实例的业务部门向专门的团队提交采购请求。此前，业务部门直接在各自的 AWS 账户中自主购买或修改预留 实例。 解决方案架构师需要以尽可能最安全的方式实施新流程。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择两个。） 答： 确保所有 AWS 账户都是 AWS Organizations 中某个组织的一部分，并启用了所有功能。","options_en":{"A":"Ensure that all AWS accounts are part of an organization in AWS Organizations with all features enabled.","B":"Use AWS Config to report on the attachment of an IAM policy that denies access to the ec2:PurchaseReservedInstancesOffering action and the ec2:ModifyReservedInstances action.","C":"In each AWS account, create an IAM policy that denies the ec2:PurchaseReservedInstancesOffering action and the ec2:ModifyReservedInstances action.","D":"Create an SCP that denies the ec2:PurchaseReservedInstancesOffering action and the ec2:ModifyReservedInstances action. Attach the SCP to each OU of the organization.","E":"Ensure that all AWS accounts are part of an organization in AWS Organizations that uses the consolidated billing feature."},"options_zh":{"B":"使用 AWS Config 报告拒绝访问 ec2:PurchaseReservedInstancesOffering 操作和 ec2:ModifyReservedInstances 操作的 IAM 策略附 件。","C":"在每个 AWS 账户中，创建拒绝 ec2:PurchaseReservedInstancesOffering 操作和 ec2:ModifyReservedInstances 操作的 IAM 策略。","D":"创建拒绝 ec2:PurchaseReservedInstancesOffering 操作和 ec2:ModifyReservedInstances 操作的 SCP。将 SCP 附加到组织的每个 OU。","E":"确保所有 AWS 账户均属于 AWS Organizations 中使用合并账单功能的组织的一部分。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AD":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":125,"question_en":"A company is running a critical application that uses an Amazon RDS for MySQL database to store data. The RDS DB instance is deployed in Multi-AZ mode. A recent RDS database failover test caused a 40-second outage to the application. A solutions architect needs to design a solution to reduce the outage time to less than 20 seconds. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在运行一个关键应用程序，该应用程序使用 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库来存储数据。RDS实例采用多可用区模式部 署。 最近的 RDS 数据库故障转移测试导致应用程序中断 40 秒。解决方案架构师需要设计一种解决方案，将中断时间减少到 20 秒以内。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon ElastiCache for Memcached in front of the database","B":"Use Amazon ElastiCache for Redis in front of the database","C":"Use RDS Proxy in front of the database.","D":"Migrate the database to Amazon Aurora MySQL.","E":"Create an Amazon Aurora Replica.","F":"Create an RDS for MySQL read replica"},"options_zh":{"A":"在数据库前面使用 Amazon ElastiCache for Memcached","B":"在数据库前面使用 Amazon ElastiCache for Redis","C":"在数据库前面使用RDS Proxy。","D":"将数据库迁移到 Amazon Aurora MySQL。","E":"创建 Amazon Aurora 副本。","F":"创建 RDS for MySQL 只读副本"},"answer":["B","C","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"CDE":90},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["C","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Standard RDS for MySQL Multi-AZ failover is DNS-based and typically takes 60-120 seconds; the observed 40 seconds is normal. To get reliably under 20 seconds you must change both the engine and the connection path. (D) Migrating to Aurora MySQL gives a much faster failover mechanism: per AWS docs, with a replica to promote, service is typically restored in less than 60 seconds and often less than 30 seconds, and promoting a replica is far faster than recreating an instance. (E) Creating an Aurora Replica is what makes that fast promotion possible: AWS recommends at least one reader in another AZ so Aurora promotes it on failure instead of building a new primary (which can take up to ~10 minutes). (C) Putting RDS Proxy in front preserves application connections and bypasses DNS caching, reducing failover times by up to 66% for Aurora Multi-AZ databases. Together, Aurora + a replica + RDS Proxy drive the outage well below 20 seconds.","explanation_zh":"標準的 RDS for MySQL Multi-AZ 容錯移轉是以 DNS 為基礎，通常需要 60-120 秒，題目觀察到的 40 秒屬於正常範圍。要可靠地降到 20 秒以下，必須同時改變資料庫引擎與連線路徑。(D) 遷移到 Aurora MySQL 可提供更快的容錯移轉機制：根據 AWS 文件，當有可提升的 replica 時，服務通常在 60 秒內、且常在 30 秒內恢復，而提升 replica 遠快於重新建立執行個體。(E) 建立 Aurora Replica 是讓這個快速提升成為可能的關鍵：AWS 建議在另一個 AZ 至少放一個 reader，這樣 Aurora 在故障時會提升它，而不是建立新的 primary（後者可能需時約 10 分鐘）。(C) 在前面加上 RDS Proxy 可保留應用程式連線並繞過 DNS 快取，使 Aurora Multi-AZ 的容錯移轉時間最多縮短 66%。Aurora + replica + RDS Proxy 三者結合，可將中斷時間明顯壓到 20 秒以下。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"ElastiCache for Memcached is a read-side cache; it does not shorten the database failover window. During a Multi-AZ failover, write operations still fail until the new primary is available, and Memcached (no replication/persistence) cannot serve as a write failover path.","why_zh":"ElastiCache for Memcached 是讀取側快取，無法縮短資料庫容錯移轉的時間。Multi-AZ 容錯移轉期間寫入仍會失敗直到新 primary 就緒，且 Memcached（無複寫/持久化）無法作為寫入容錯路徑。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"ElastiCache for Redis likewise caches reads and does not reduce the write-path failover outage of the RDS database. The dump's choice of B addresses performance/offload, not the failover recovery time the question targets.","why_zh":"ElastiCache for Redis 同樣只是快取讀取，無法縮短 RDS 資料庫寫入路徑的容錯移轉中斷時間。題目針對的是容錯移轉恢復時間，而非效能/卸載，因此 dump 選 B 不正確。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"An RDS for MySQL read replica uses asynchronous replication and is NOT an automatic Multi-AZ failover target. It would require manual promotion and does not reduce the existing Multi-AZ failover time. RDS Proxy also cannot associate with a read replica, only the writer.","why_zh":"RDS for MySQL read replica 使用非同步複寫，並不是 Multi-AZ 的自動容錯移轉目標，需要手動提升，也無法縮短現有 Multi-AZ 容錯移轉時間。此外 RDS Proxy 只能關聯 writer，無法關聯 read replica。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Concepts.AuroraHighAvailability.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/rds-proxy.howitworks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/rds-proxy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-failover.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":126,"question_en":"An AWS partner company is building a service in AWS Organizations using its organization named org1. This service requires the partner company to have access to AWS resources in a customer account, which is in a separate organization named org2. The company must establish least privilege security access using an API or command line tool to the customer account. What is the MOST secure way to allow org1 to access resources in org2?","question_zh":"一家 AWS 合作伙伴公司正在使用其名为 org1 的组织在 AWS Organizations 中构建服务。此服务要求合作伙伴公司能够访问客户账户 中的 AWS 资源，该账户位于名为 org2 的单独组织中。公司必须使用 API 或命令行工具对客户帐户建立最低权限安全访问。 允许 org1 访问 org2 中的资源的最安全方法是什么？ 答： 客户应向合作伙伴公司提供其 AWS 账户访问密钥以登录并执行所需的任务。","options_en":{"A":"The customer should provide the partner company with their AWS account access keys to log in and perform the required tasks.","B":"The customer should create an IAM user and assign the required permissions to the IAM user. The customer should then provide the credentials to the partner company to log in and perform the required tasks.","C":"The customer should create an IAM role and assign the required permissions to the IAM role. The partner company should then use the IAM role’s Amazon Resource Name (ARN) when requesting access to perform the required tasks.","D":"The customer should create an IAM role and assign the required permissions to the IAM role. The partner company should then use the IAM role’s Amazon Resource Name (ARN), including the external ID in the IAM role’s trust policy, when requesting access to perform the required tasks."},"options_zh":{"B":"客户应创建一个 IAM 用户并为该 IAM 用户分配所需的权限。然后，客户应向合作伙伴公司提供凭据以登录并执行所需的任 务。","C":"客户应创建 IAM 角色并将所需的权限分配给 IAM 角色。然后，合作伙伴公司在请求访问权限以执行所需任务时应使用 IAM 角 色的 Amazon 资源名称 (ARN)。","D":"客户应创建 IAM 角色并向 IAM 角色分配所需的权限。然后，在请求访问权限以执行所需任务时，合作伙伴公司应使用 IAM 角 色的 Amazon 资源名称 (ARN)，包括 IAM 角色的信任策略中的外部 ID。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":127,"question_en":"A delivery company needs to migrate its third-party route planning application to AWS. The third party supplies a supported Docker image from a public registry. The image can run in as many containers as required to generate the route map. The company has divided the delivery area into sections with supply hubs so that delivery drivers travel the shortest distance possible from the hubs to the customers. To reduce the time necessary to generate route maps, each section uses its own set of Docker containers with a custom configuration that processes orders only in the section's area. The company needs the ability to allocate resources cost-effectively based on the number of running containers. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家快递公司需要将其第三方路线规划应用程序迁移到 AWS。第三方从公共注册表提供受支持的 Docker 映像。该映像可以根据需要 在任意多个容器中运行以生成路线图。 该公司将配送区域划分为具有供应中心的区域，以便送货司机从中心到客户的距离尽可能短。为了减少生成路线图所需的时间，每 个部分都使用自己的一组 Docker 容器，并具有自定义配置，仅处理该部分区域中的订单。 公司需要能够根据运行的容器数量经济高效地分配资源。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster on Amazon EC2. Use the Amazon EKS CLI to launch the planning application in pods by using the --tags option to assign a custom tag to the pod.","B":"Create an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster on AWS Fargate. Use the Amazon EKS CLI to launch the planning application. Use the AWS CLI tag-resource API call to assign a custom tag to the pod.","C":"Create an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster on Amazon EC2. Use the AWS CLI with run-tasks set to true to launch the planning application by using the --tags option to assign a custom tag to the task.","D":"Create an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster on AWS Fargate. Use the AWS CLI run-task command and set enableECSManagedTags to true to launch the planning application. Use the --tags option to assign a custom tag to the task."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon EC2 上创建 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 集群。使用 Amazon EKS CLI 在 Pod 中启动规划应用程 序，方法是使用 --tags 选项为 Pod 分配自定义标签。","B":"在 AWS Fargate 上创建 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 集群。使用 Amazon EKS CLI 启动规划应用程序。使用 AWS CLI 标签资源 API 调用将自定义标签分配给 Pod。","C":"在 Amazon EC2 上创建 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 集群。使用 AWS CLI 将 run-tasks 设置为 true 来启动规划应 用程序，并使用 --tags 选项为任务分配自定义标签。","D":"在 AWS Fargate 上创建 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 集群。使用 AWS CLI run-task 命令并将 enableECSManagedTags 设置为 true 以启动规划应用程序。使用 --tags 选项为任务分配自定义标签。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":82,"B":18},"tags":["Migration","Compute","Cost Optimization","Containers"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":128,"question_en":"A software company hosts an application on AWS with resources in multiple AWS accounts and Regions. The application runs on a group of Amazon EC2 instances in an application VPC located in the us-east-1 Region with an IPv4 CIDR block of 10.10.0.0/16. In a different AWS account, a shared services VPC is located in the us-east-2 Region with an IPv4 CIDR block of 10.10.10.0/24. When a cloud engineer uses AWS CloudFormation to attempt to peer the application VPC with the shared services VPC, an error message indicates a peering failure. Which factors could cause this error? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家软件公司在 AWS 上托管一个应用程序，并在多个 AWS 账户和区域中拥有资源。该应用程序在位于 us-east-1 区域的应用程序 VPC 中的一组 Amazon EC2 实例上运行，IPv4 CIDR 块为 10.10.0.0/16。在另一个 AWS 账户中，共享服务 VPC 位于 us-east-2 区域，其 IPv4 CIDR 块为 10.10.10.0/24。当云工程师使用 AWS CloudFormation 尝试将应用程序 VPC 与共享服务 VPC 对等互连时，会出现一条错 误消息，指示对等互连失败。 哪些因素可能导致此错误？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"The IPv4 CIDR ranges of the two VPCs overlap","B":"The VPCs are not in the same Region","C":"One or both accounts do not have access to an Internet gateway","D":"One of the VPCs was not shared through AWS Resource Access Manager","E":"The IAM role in the peer accepter account does not have the correct permissions"},"options_zh":{"A":"两个VPC的IPv4 CIDR范围重叠","B":"VPC不在同一个Region","C":"一个或两个帐户无法访问 Internet 网关","D":"其中一个 VPC 未通过 AWS Resource Access Manager 共享","E":"对等接受方账户中的 IAM 角色没有正确的权限"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AE":88},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・複選"},{"id":129,"question_en":"An external audit of a company’s serverless application reveals IAM policies that grant too many permissions. These policies are attached to the company's AWS Lambda execution roles. Hundreds of the company's Lambda functions have broad access permissions such as full access to Amazon S3 buckets and Amazon DynamoDB tables. The company wants each function to have only the minimum permissions that the function needs to complete its task. A solutions architect must determine which permissions each Lambda function needs. What should the solutions architect do to meet this requirement with the LEAST amount of effort?","question_zh":"对公司无服务器应用程序的外部审计揭示了授予过多权限的 IAM 策略。这些策略附加到公司的 AWS Lambda 执行角色。该公司的数 百个 Lambda 函数拥有广泛的访问权限，例如对 Amazon S3 存储桶和 Amazon DynamoDB 表的完全访问权限。该公司希望每个功能仅 拥有该功能完成其任务所需的最低权限。 解决方案架构师必须确定每个 Lambda 函数需要哪些权限。 解决方案架构师应该如何做才能以最少的努力满足此要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up Amazon CodeGuru to profile the Lambda functions and search for AWS API calls. Create an inventory of the required API calls and resources for each Lambda function. Create new IAM access policies for each Lambda function. Review the new policies to ensure that they meet the company's business requirements.","B":"Turn on AWS CloudTrail logging for the AWS account. Use AWS Identity and Access Management Access Analyzer to generate IAM access policies based on the activity recorded in the CloudTrail log. Review the generated policies to ensure that they meet the company's business requirements.","C":"Turn on AWS CloudTrail logging for the AWS account. Create a script to parse the CloudTrail log, search for AWS API calls by Lambda execution role, and create a summary report. Review the report. Create IAM access policies that provide more restrictive permissions for each Lambda function.","D":"Turn on AWS CloudTrail logging for the AWS account. Export the CloudTrail logs to Amazon S3. Use Amazon EMR to process the CloudTrail logs in Amazon S3 and produce a report of API calls and resources used by each execution role. Create a new IAM access policy for each role. Export the generated roles to an S3 bucket. Review the generated policies to ensure that they meet the company’s business requirements."},"options_zh":{"A":"设置 Amazon CodeGuru 以分析 Lambda 函数并搜索 AWS API 调用。为每个 Lambda 函数创建所需 API 调用和资源的清单。为每 个 Lambda 函数创建新的 IAM 访问策略。审查新政策以确保它们满足公司的业务要求。","B":"为 AWS 账户打开 AWS CloudTrail 日志记录。使用 AWS Identity and Access Management 访问分析器根据 CloudTrail 日志中记录的 活动生成 IAM 访问策略。检查生成的策略以确保它们满足公司的业务要求。","C":"为 AWS 账户打开 AWS CloudTrail 日志记录。创建脚本来解析 CloudTrail 日志、按 Lambda 执行角色搜索 AWS API 调用并创建摘 要报告。查看报告。创建 IAM 访问策略，为每个 Lambda 函数提供更多限制性权限。","D":"为 AWS 账户打开 AWS CloudTrail 日志记录。将 CloudTrail 日志导出到 Amazon S3。使用 Amazon EMR 处理 Amazon S3 中的 CloudTrail 日志并生成每个执行角色使用的 API 调用和资源的报告。为每个角色创建新的 IAM 访问策略。将生成的角色导出到 S3 存储桶。检查生成的策略以确保它们满足公司的业务要求。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":130,"question_en":"A solutions architect must analyze a company’s Amazon EC2 instances and Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes to determine whether the company is using resources e®ciently. The company is running several large, high-memory EC2 instances to host database clusters that are deployed in active/passive configurations. The utilization of these EC2 instances varies by the applications that use the databases, and the company has not identified a pattern. The solutions architect must analyze the environment and take action based on the findings. Which solution meets these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师必须分析公司的 Amazon EC2 实例和 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 卷，以确定公司是否有效地使用资源。 该公司正在运行多个大型高内存 EC2 实例来托管以主动/被动配置部署的数据库集群。这些 EC2 实例的利用率因使用数据库的应用程 序而异，该公司尚未确定一种模式。 解决方案架构师必须分析环境并根据结果采取行动。 哪种解决方案最经济高效地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a dashboard by using AWS Systems Manager OpsCenter. Configure visualizations for Amazon CloudWatch metrics that are associated with the EC2 instances and their EBS volumes. Review the dashboard periodically, and identify usage patterns. Rightsize the EC2 instances based on the peaks in the metrics.","B":"Turn on Amazon CloudWatch detailed monitoring for the EC2 instances and their EBS volumes. Create and review a dashboard that is based on the metrics. Identify usage patterns. Rightsize the EC2 instances based on the peaks in the metrics.","C":"Install the Amazon CloudWatch agent on each of the EC2 instances. Turn on AWS Compute Optimizer, and let it run for at least 12 hours. Review the recommendations from Compute Optimizer, and rightsize the EC2 instances as directed.","D":"Sign up for the AWS Enterprise Support plan. Turn on AWS Trusted Advisor. Wait 12 hours. Review the recommendations from Trusted Advisor, and rightsize the EC2 instances as directed."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager OpsCenter 创建控制面板。配置与 EC2 实例及其 EBS 卷关联的 Amazon CloudWatch 指标的可视化。 定期查看仪表板并确定使用模式。根据指标中的峰值调整 EC2 实例的大小。","B":"打开对 EC2 实例及其 EBS 卷的 Amazon CloudWatch 详细监控。创建并查看基于指标的仪表板。确定使用模式。根据指标中的 峰值调整 EC2 实例的大小。","C":"在每个 EC2 实例上安装 Amazon CloudWatch 代理。打开 AWS Compute Optimizer，并让它运行至少 12 小时。查看 Compute Optimizer 的建议，并按照指示调整 EC2 实例的大小。","D":"注册 AWS 企业支持计划。打开 AWS Trusted Advisor。等12小时。查看 Trusted Advisor 的建议，并按照指示调整 EC2 实例的大 小。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":97},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":131,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations for a multi-account setup in the AWS Cloud. The company uses AWS Control Tower for governance and uses AWS Transit Gateway for VPC connectivity across accounts. In an AWS application account, the company’s application team has deployed a web application that uses AWS Lambda and Amazon RDS. The company's database administrators have a separate DBA account and use the account to centrally manage all the databases across the organization. The database administrators use an Amazon EC2 instance that is deployed in the DBA account to access an RDS database that is deployed m the application account. The application team has stored the database credentials as secrets in AWS Secrets Manager in the application account. The application team is manually sharing the secrets with the database administrators. The secrets are encrypted by the default AWS managed key for Secrets Manager in the application account. A solutions architect needs to implement a solution that gives the database administrators access to the database and eliminates the need to manually share the secrets. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 在 AWS 云中进行多账户设置。该公司使用 AWS Control Tower 进行治理，并使用 AWS Transit Gateway 实现跨账户的 VPC 连接。 在 AWS 应用程序账户中，该公司的应用程序团队部署了一个使用 AWS Lambda 和 Amazon RDS 的 Web 应用程序。公司的数据库管理 员拥有独立的DBA帐户，并使用该帐户集中管理整个组织内的所有数据库。数据库管理员使用部署在 DBA 账户中的 Amazon EC2 实例 来访问部署在应用程序账户中的 RDS 数据库。 应用程序团队已将数据库凭证作为机密存储在应用程序账户的 AWS Secrets Manager 中。应用程序团队正在与数据库管理员手动共享 机密。这些密钥由应用程序账户中 Secrets Manager 的默认 AWS 托管密钥进行加密。解决方案架构师需要实现一个解决方案，使数 据库管理员能够访问数据库，并且无需手动共享机密。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) to share the secrets from the application account with the DBA account. In the DBA account, create an IAM role that is named DBA-Admin. Grant the role the required permissions to access the shared secrets. Attach the DBA-Admin role to the EC2 instance for access to the cross-account secrets.","B":"In the application account, create an IAM role that is named DBA-Secret. Grant the role the required permissions to access the secrets. In the DBA account, create an IAM role that is named DBA-Admin. Grant the DBA-Admin role the required permissions to assume the DBA- Secret role in the application account. Attach the DBA-Admin role to the EC2 instance for access to the cross-account secrets","C":"In the DBA account create an IAM role that is named DBA-Admin. Grant the role the required permissions to access the secrets and the default AWS managed key in the application account. In the application account, attach resource-based policies to the key to allow access from the DBA account. Attach the DBA-Admin role to the EC2 instance for access to the cross-account secrets.","D":"In the DBA account, create an IAM role that is named DBA-Admin. Grant the role the required permissions to access the secrets in the application account. Attach an SCP to the application account to allow access to the secrets from the DBA account. Attach the DBA-Admin role to the EC2 instance for access to the cross-account secrets."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) 与 DBA 账户共享应用程序账户中的密钥。在 DBA 账户中，创建名为 DBA-Admin 的 IAM 角色。授予角色访问共享机密所需的权限。将 DBA 管理员角色附加到 EC2 实例以访问跨账户机密。","B":"在应用程序账户中，创建一个名为 DBA-Secret 的 IAM 角色。授予角色访问机密所需的权限。在 DBA 账户中，创建名为 DBA- Admin 的 IAM 角色。授予 DBA-Admin 角色所需的权限，以在应用程序帐户中担任 DBA-Secret 角色。将 DBA 管理员角色附加到 EC2 实例以访问跨账户机密","C":"在 DBA 账户中创建一个名为 DBA-Admin 的 IAM 角色。授予角色访问应用程序账户中的密钥和默认 AWS 托管密钥所需的权限。 在应用程序帐户中，将基于资源的策略附加到密钥以允许从 DBA 帐户进行访问。将 DBA 管理员角色附加到 EC2 实例以访问跨账 户机密。","D":"在 DBA 账户中，创建名为 DBA-Admin 的 IAM 角色。授予角色访问应用程序帐户中的机密所需的权限。将 SCP 附加到应用程序 帐户以允许从 DBA 帐户访问机密。将 DBA 管理员角色附加到 EC2 实例以访问跨账户机密。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":83},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive constraint is that the secrets are encrypted with the default AWS managed key (aws/secretsmanager). AWS documentation states explicitly that you cannot use the AWS managed key for cross-account access; true cross-account secret retrieval requires a customer managed KMS key plus both a resource policy on the secret and a key policy on the CMK. None of the options changes the encryption key, so any option relying on direct cross-account access to the secret/key fails. Option B avoids the cross-account KMS limitation entirely: it creates an IAM role (DBA-Secret) IN the application account with permissions to the secret, and the EC2 instance role (DBA-Admin) in the DBA account assumes that role. Once assumed, the session operates as a principal local to the application account, so accessing the secret and decrypting it with the AWS managed key is a same-account operation that works. This also eliminates manual sharing and is the standard cross-account access pattern.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限制在於這些 secrets 是用 Secrets Manager 的預設 AWS managed key（aws/secretsmanager）加密的。AWS 文件明確指出，AWS managed key 無法用於跨帳戶存取；真正的跨帳戶 secret 取用需要使用 customer managed KMS key，並同時設定 secret 的 resource policy 與 CMK 的 key policy。四個選項都沒有更換加密金鑰，因此任何依賴直接跨帳戶存取 secret/金鑰的方案都會失敗。選項 B 完全避開跨帳戶 KMS 的限制：它在 application account 內建立一個對該 secret 有權限的 IAM role（DBA-Secret），再讓 DBA account 的 EC2 instance role（DBA-Admin）去 assume 該 role。assume 後，該 session 等同於 application account 內的本地 principal，存取 secret 並用 AWS managed key 解密屬於同帳戶操作，可以正常運作。此方式同時消除了手動分享，是標準的跨帳戶存取模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS RAM cannot share Secrets Manager secrets; Secrets Manager is not a RAM shareable resource type. Secrets are shared via resource-based policies, not RAM. It also does not address the AWS managed key limitation.","why_zh":"AWS RAM 無法分享 Secrets Manager 的 secret；Secrets Manager 不屬於 RAM 可分享的資源類型，secret 是透過 resource-based policy 分享，而非 RAM。此方案也未處理 AWS managed key 的限制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"You cannot attach or modify a resource-based (key) policy on the default AWS managed key aws/secretsmanager; it is managed by AWS. Cross-account access also explicitly cannot use the AWS managed key, so this approach is impossible.","why_zh":"你無法為預設的 AWS managed key（aws/secretsmanager）附加或修改 key policy，它由 AWS 管理。跨帳戶存取明確無法使用 AWS managed key，因此此方案不可行。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SCPs are guardrails that only restrict/filter permissions; they never grant access. An SCP cannot give the DBA account access to the secret, and this still relies on impossible cross-account use of the AWS managed key.","why_zh":"SCP 是防護欄，只能限制／過濾權限，永遠無法授予存取權。SCP 無法讓 DBA account 取得 secret 的存取權，且此方案仍依賴對 AWS managed key 不可能的跨帳戶使用。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/auth-and-access_examples_cross.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/security-encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/auth-and-access_resource-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ram/latest/userguide/shareable.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":132,"question_en":"A company manages multiple AWS accounts by using AWS Organizations. Under the root OU, the company has two OUs: Research and DataOps. Because of regulatory requirements, all resources that the company deploys in the organization must reside in the ap-northeast-1 Region. Additionally, EC2 instances that the company deploys in the DataOps OU must use a predefined list of instance types. A solutions architect must implement a solution that applies these restrictions. The solution must maximize operational e®ciency and must minimize ongoing maintenance. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 管理多个 AWS 账户。在根 OU 下，公司有两个 OU：Research 和 DataOps。 由于法规要求，公司在组织中部署的所有资源都必须驻留在 ap-northeast-1 区域。此外，公司在 DataOps OU 中部署的 EC2 实例必须 使用预定义的实例类型列表。 解决方案架构师必须实施应用这些限制的解决方案。该解决方案必须最大限度地提高运营效率，并最大限度地减少持续维护。 哪种步骤组合可以满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM role in one account under the DataOps OU. Use the ec2:InstanceType condition key in an inline policy on the role to restrict access to specific instance type.","B":"Create an IAM user in all accounts under the root OU. Use the aws:RequestedRegion condition key in an inline policy on each user to restrict access to all AWS Regions except ap-northeast-1.","C":"Create an SCP. Use the aws:RequestedRegion condition key to restrict access to all AWS Regions except ap-northeast-1. Apply the SCP to the root OU.","D":"Create an SCP. Use the ec2:Region condition key to restrict access to all AWS Regions except ap-northeast-1. Apply the SCP to the root OU, the DataOps OU, and the Research OU.","E":"Create an SCP. Use the ec2:InstanceType condition key to restrict access to specific instance types. Apply the SCP to the DataOps OU."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 DataOps OU 下的一个账户中创建 IAM 角色。在角色的内联策略中使用 ec2:InstanceType 条件键来限制对特定实例类型的访 问。","B":"在根 OU 下的所有账户中创建 IAM 用户。在每个用户的内联策略中使用 aws:RequestedRegion 条件键来限制对除 ap-northeast-1 之外的所有 AWS 区域的访问。","C":"创建一个 SCP。使用 aws:RequestedRegion 条件键限制对除 ap-northeast-1 之外的所有 AWS 区域的访问。将 SCP 应用到根 OU。","D":"创建一个 SCP。使用 ec2:Region 条件键限制对除 ap-northeast-1 之外的所有 AWS 区域的访问。将 SCP 应用到根 OU、DataOps OU 和 Research OU。","E":"创建一个 SCP。使用 ec2:InstanceType 条件键限制对特定实例类型的访问。将 SCP 应用到 DataOps OU。"},"answer":["C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"CE":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":133,"question_en":"A company runs a serverless application in a single AWS Region. The application accesses external URLs and extracts metadata from those sites. The company uses an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to publish URLs to an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. An AWS Lambda function uses the queue as an event source and processes the URLs from the queue. Results are saved to an Amazon S3 bucket. The company wants to process each URL in other Regions to compare possible differences in site localization. URLs must be published from the existing Region. Results must be written to the existing S3 bucket in the current Region. Which combination of changes will produce multi-Region deployment that meets these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司在单个 AWS 区域中运行无服务器应用程序。该应用程序访问外部 URL 并从这些站点提取元数据。该公司使用 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 主题将 URL 发布到 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列。AWS Lambda 函数使用 队列作为事件源并处理队列中的 URL。结果保存到 Amazon S3 存储桶中。 该公司希望处理其他区域中的每个 URL，以比较网站本地化中可能存在的差异。URL 必须从现有区域发布。结果必须写入当前区域 中的现有 S3 存储桶。 哪种更改组合将产生满足这些要求的多区域部署？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the SQS queue with the Lambda function to other Regions.","B":"Subscribe the SNS topic in each Region to the SQS queue.","C":"Subscribe the SQS queue in each Region to the SNS topic.","D":"Configure the SQS queue to publish URLs to SNS topics in each Region.","E":"Deploy the SNS topic and the Lambda function to other Regions."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Lambda 函数将 SQS 队列部署到其他区域。","B":"将每个 Region 中的 SNS 主题订阅到 SQS 队列。","C":"将每个 Region 中的 SQS 队列订阅 SNS 主题。","D":"配置 SQS 队列以将 URL 发布到每个区域中的 SNS 主题。","E":"将 SNS 主题和 Lambda 函数部署到其他区域。"},"answer":["A","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AC":100},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":134,"question_en":"A company runs a proprietary stateless ETL application on an Amazon EC2 Linux instances. The application is a Linux binary, and the source code cannot be modified. The application is single-threaded, uses 2 GB of RAM, and is highly CPU intensive. The application is scheduled to run every 4 hours and runs for up to 20 minutes. A solutions architect wants to revise the architecture for the solution. Which strategy should the solutions architect use?","question_zh":"一家公司在 Amazon EC2 Linux 实例上运行专有的无状态 ETL 应用程序。该应用程序是 Linux 二进制文件，源代码无法修改。该应用 程序是单线程的，使用 2 GB RAM，并且是高度 CPU 密集型的。该应用程序计划每 4 小时运行一次，最多运行 20 分钟。解决方案架 构师想要修改解决方案的架构。 解决方案架构师应该使用哪种策略？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Lambda to run the application. Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs to invoke the Lambda function every 4 hours.","B":"Use AWS Batch to run the application. Use an AWS Step Functions state machine to invoke the AWS Batch job every 4 hours.","C":"Use AWS Fargate to run the application. Use Amazon EventBridge (Amazon CloudWatch Events) to invoke the Fargate task every 4 hours.","D":"Use Amazon EC2 Spot Instances to run the application. Use AWS CodeDeploy to deploy and run the application every 4 hours."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Lambda 运行应用程序。使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 每 4 小时调用一次 Lambda 函数。","B":"使用 AWS Batch 运行应用程序。使用 AWS Step Functions 状态机每 4 小时调用一次 AWS Batch 作业。","C":"使用 AWS Fargate 运行应用程序。使用 Amazon EventBridge (Amazon CloudWatch Events) 每 4 小时调用一次 Fargate 任务。","D":"使用 Amazon EC2 Spot 实例运行应用程序。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 每 4 小时部署并运行一次应用程序。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":89},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":135,"question_en":"A company is creating a sequel for a popular online game. A large number of users from all over the world will play the game within the first week after launch. Currently, the game consists of the following components deployed in a single AWS Region: • Amazon S3 bucket that stores game assets • Amazon DynamoDB table that stores player scores A solutions architect needs to design a multi-Region solution that will reduce latency, improve reliability, and require the least effort to implement. What should the solutions architect do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在为一款流行的在线游戏制作续集。游戏上线后的第一周内就会有大量来自世界各地的用户玩游戏。目前，该游戏由部 署在单个 AWS 区域中的以下组件组成： • 用于存储游戏资产的 Amazon S3 存储桶 • 用于存储玩家得分的 Amazon DynamoDB 表 解决方案架构师需要设计一个多区域解决方案，以减少延迟、提高可靠性，并且需要最少的努力来实施。 解决方案架构师应该怎样做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution to serve assets from the S3 bucket. Configure S3 Cross-Region Replication. Create a new DynamoDB table in a new Region. Use the new table as a replica target for DynamoDB global tables.","B":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution to serve assets from the S3 bucket. Configure S3 Same-Region Replication. Create a new DynamoDB table in a new Region. Configure asynchronous replication between the DynamoDB tables by using AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) with change data capture (CDC).","C":"Create another S3 bucket in a new Region, and configure S3 Cross-Region Replication between the buckets. Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution and configure origin failover with two origins accessing the S3 buckets in each Region. Configure DynamoDB global tables by enabling Amazon DynamoDB Streams, and add a replica table in a new Region.","D":"Create another S3 bucket in the sine Region, and configure S3 Same-Region Replication between the buckets. Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution and configure origin failover with two origins accessing the S3 buckets. Create a new DynamoDB table in a new Region. Use the new table as a replica target for DynamoDB global tables."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 Amazon CloudFront 分配以提供 S3 存储桶中的资产。配置S3跨区域复制。在新区域中创建新的 DynamoDB 表。使用新表作 为 DynamoDB 全局表的副本目标。","B":"创建 Amazon CloudFront 分配以提供 S3 存储桶中的资产。配置S3同区域复制。在新区域中创建新的 DynamoDB 表。使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 和变更数据捕获 (CDC) 配置 DynamoDB 表之间的异步复制。","C":"在新的 Region 中创建另一个 S3 存储桶，并在存储桶之间配置 S3 跨区域复制。创建 Amazon CloudFront 分配并配置源故障转 移，让两个源访问每个区域中的 S3 存储桶。通过启用 Amazon DynamoDB Streams 配置 DynamoDB 全局表，并在新区域中添加副 本表。","D":"在正弦区域中创建另一个 S3 存储桶，并在存储桶之间配置 S3 同区域复制。创建 Amazon CloudFront 分配并配置源故障转移， 使两个源访问 S3 存储桶。在新区域中创建新的 DynamoDB 表。使用新表作为 DynamoDB 全局表的副本目标。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":88},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage","Database"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":136,"question_en":"A company has an on-premises website application that provides real estate information for potential renters and buyers. The website uses a Java backend and a NoSQL MongoDB database to store subscriber data. The company needs to migrate the entire application to AWS with a similar structure. The application must be deployed for high availability, and the company cannot make changes to the application. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个本地网站应用程序，可为潜在租户和买家提供房地产信息。该网站使用 Java 后端和 NoSQL MongoDB 数据库来存储 订阅者数据。 该公司需要将整个应用程序迁移到具有类似结构的AWS。必须部署应用程序以实现高可用性，并且公司不能对应用程序进行更改。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use an Amazon Aurora DB cluster as the database for the subscriber data. Deploy Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group across multiple Availability Zones for the Java backend application.","B":"Use MongoDB on Amazon EC2 instances as the database for the subscriber data. Deploy EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group in a single Availability Zone for the Java backend application.","C":"Configure Amazon DocumentDB (with MongoDB compatibility) with appropriately sized instances in multiple Availability Zones as the database for the subscriber data. Deploy Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group across multiple Availability Zones for the Java backend application.","D":"Configure Amazon DocumentDB (with MongoDB compatibility) in on-demand capacity mode in multiple Availability Zones as the database for the subscriber data. Deploy Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group across multiple Availability Zones for the Java backend application."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Aurora 数据库集群作为订阅者数据的数据库。在跨多个可用区的 Auto Scaling 组中为 Java 后端应用程序部署 Amazon EC2 实例。","B":"使用 Amazon EC2 实例上的 MongoDB 作为订阅者数据的数据库。在 Java 后端应用程序的单个可用区的 Auto Scaling 组中部署 EC2 实例。","C":"在多个可用区中使用适当大小的实例配置 Amazon DocumentDB（与 MongoDB 兼容）作为订阅者数据的数据库。在跨多个可用 区的 Auto Scaling 组中为 Java 后端应用程序部署 Amazon EC2 实例。","D":"在多个可用区中以按需容量模式配置 Amazon DocumentDB（兼容 MongoDB）作为订阅者数据的数据库。在跨多个可用区的 Auto Scaling 组中为 Java 后端应用程序部署 Amazon EC2 实例。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":88},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The application uses MongoDB and cannot be changed, so the migration target should be Amazon DocumentDB (with MongoDB compatibility), which is API-compatible with MongoDB and requires no application changes. DocumentDB achieves high availability by distributing a primary instance and up to 15 read-replica instances across multiple Availability Zones, with automatic failover. Option C correctly configures DocumentDB with appropriately sized (provisioned) instances across multiple AZs, plus an EC2 Auto Scaling group across multiple AZs for the Java backend, satisfying both the MongoDB compatibility and high-availability requirements. Option D is technically invalid because DocumentDB has no 'on-demand capacity mode' — that capacity model belongs to Amazon DynamoDB and Amazon Keyspaces, not DocumentDB; DocumentDB offers only provisioned (instance-based) and serverless (DCU min/max) configurations. Therefore the dump's suggested answer D references a nonexistent DocumentDB feature, and C is the genuinely correct answer.","explanation_zh":"應用程式使用 MongoDB 且不可修改，因此遷移目標應為 Amazon DocumentDB (with MongoDB compatibility)，它與 MongoDB API 相容，無需更改應用程式。DocumentDB 透過將一個主要 (primary) 執行個體與最多 15 個唯讀複本 (replica) 執行個體分散在多個 Availability Zones，並提供自動容錯移轉 (failover) 來達成高可用性。選項 C 正確地以適當大小的 (provisioned) 執行個體跨多個 AZ 部署 DocumentDB，並為 Java 後端使用跨多個 AZ 的 EC2 Auto Scaling group，同時滿足 MongoDB 相容性與高可用性需求。選項 D 在技術上無效，因為 DocumentDB 並沒有 'on-demand capacity mode'，該容量模式屬於 Amazon DynamoDB 與 Amazon Keyspaces，而非 DocumentDB；DocumentDB 只提供 provisioned (以執行個體為基礎) 與 serverless (DCU 最小/最大) 兩種設定。因此 dump 建議的答案 D 引用了不存在的 DocumentDB 功能，C 才是真正正確的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Aurora is a relational (MySQL/PostgreSQL-compatible) database, not a NoSQL document store. Migrating MongoDB data to Aurora would require re-architecting the data model and application code, which violates the 'cannot make changes to the application' constraint.","why_zh":"Amazon Aurora 是關聯式 (相容 MySQL/PostgreSQL) 資料庫，並非 NoSQL 文件資料庫。將 MongoDB 資料遷移到 Aurora 需要重新設計資料模型與應用程式碼，違反了「不可變更應用程式」的限制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Self-managed MongoDB on EC2 is possible, but deploying both the database and the backend Auto Scaling group in a single Availability Zone fails the high-availability requirement; a single-AZ design has no protection against an AZ failure.","why_zh":"在 EC2 上自行管理 MongoDB 是可行的，但將資料庫與後端 Auto Scaling group 都部署在單一 Availability Zone，無法滿足高可用性需求；單一 AZ 設計無法抵禦 AZ 故障。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon DocumentDB does not have an 'on-demand capacity mode.' That term applies to Amazon DynamoDB and Amazon Keyspaces. DocumentDB supports only provisioned (instance-based) and serverless (DCU min/max) capacity, so this option references a nonexistent feature and is invalid.","why_zh":"Amazon DocumentDB 沒有 'on-demand capacity mode'。該名詞適用於 Amazon DynamoDB 與 Amazon Keyspaces。DocumentDB 只支援 provisioned (以執行個體為基礎) 與 serverless (DCU 最小/最大) 容量，因此此選項引用了不存在的功能，屬無效選項。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/devguide/replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/devguide/db-clusters-understanding.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/devguide/db-cluster-fault-tolerance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/devguide/docdb-serverless-how-it-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/on-demand-capacity-mode.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":137,"question_en":"A digital marketing company has multiple AWS accounts that belong to various teams. The creative team uses an Amazon S3 bucket in its AWS account to securely store images and media files that are used as content for the company’s marketing campaigns. The creative team wants to share the S3 bucket with the strategy team so that the strategy team can view the objects. A solutions architect has created an IAM role that is named strategy_reviewer in the Strategy account. The solutions architect also has set up a custom AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key in the Creative account and has associated the key with the S3 bucket. However, when users from the Strategy account assume the IAM role and try to access objects in the S3 bucket, they receive an Access Denied error. The solutions architect must ensure that users in the Strategy account can access the S3 bucket. The solution must provide these users with only the minimum permissions that they need. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家数字营销公司拥有多个属于不同团队的 AWS 账户。创意团队在其 AWS 账户中使用 Amazon S3 存储桶来安全地存储用作公司营 销活动内容的图像和媒体文件。创意团队希望与策略团队共享 S3 存储桶，以便策略团队可以查看对象。 解决方案架构师在策略账户中创建了一个名为strategy_reviewer 的 IAM 角色。解决方案架构师还在 Creative 账户中设置了自定义 AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) 密钥，并将该密钥与 S3 存储桶相关联。但是，当策略账户的用户承担 IAM 角色并尝试访问 S3 存 储桶中的对象时，他们会收到“访问被拒绝”错误。 解决方案架构师必须确保策略帐户中的用户可以访问 S3 存储桶。该解决方案必须仅向这些用户提供他们所需的最低权限。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a bucket policy that includes read permissions for the S3 bucket. Set the principal of the bucket policy to the account ID of the Strategy account.","B":"Update the strategy_reviewer IAM role to grant full permissions for the S3 bucket and to grant decrypt permissions for the custom KMS key.","C":"Update the custom KMS key policy in the Creative account to grant decrypt permissions to the strategy_reviewer IAM role.","D":"Create a bucket policy that includes read permissions for the S3 bucket. Set the principal of the bucket policy to an anonymous user.","E":"Update the custom KMS key policy in the Creative account to grant encrypt permissions to the strategy_reviewer IAM role.","F":"Update the strategy_reviewer IAM role to grant read permissions for the S3 bucket and to grant decrypt permissions for the custom KMS key."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建包含 S3 存储桶读取权限的存储桶策略。设置桶策略的principal为策略账户的账户ID。","B":"更新strategy_reviewer IAM 角色以授予对S3 存储桶的完全权限以及对自定义KMS 密钥的解密权限。","C":"更新 Creative 账户中的自定义 KMS 密钥策略，以向 Strategy_reviewer IAM 角色授予解密权限。","D":"创建包含 S3 存储桶读取权限的存储桶策略。设置桶策略的主体为匿名用户。","E":"更新 Creative 账户中的自定义 KMS 密钥策略，以向 Strategy_reviewer IAM 角色授予加密权限。","F":"更新strategy_reviewer IAM 角色以授予S3 存储桶的读取权限并授予自定义KMS 密钥的解密权限。"},"answer":["B","C","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ACF":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Cross-account access to a KMS-encrypted S3 bucket via an assumed role requires three policy planes to all allow access: the S3 bucket policy (resource-based) in the Creative account, the KMS key policy in the Creative account, and the strategy_reviewer IAM role policy in the Strategy account. (A) A bucket policy granting read (s3:GetObject/s3:ListBucket) with the Principal set to the Strategy account ID is a valid cross-account delegation: per the IAM Principal reference, specifying an account ID delegates authority to that account, which the role's identity policy then scopes down. (C) The KMS key policy must explicitly grant kms:Decrypt to the strategy_reviewer role so it can decrypt SSE-KMS objects; the AWS Bedrock and SageMaker Canvas cross-account guides show this exact added key-policy statement. (F) The IAM role needs read permissions on S3 plus kms:Decrypt, which is the least-privilege identity-side grant. The qualifier 'only the minimum permissions' decides the wrong options: B grants FULL S3 permissions (violates least privilege), and E grants Encrypt instead of Decrypt (viewing objects needs Decrypt only). D sets an anonymous (public) principal, violating both security and least privilege. The dump answer BCF is wrong because B's full permissions contradict the stated minimum-permissions requirement.","explanation_zh":"透過 assumed role 跨帳號存取以 KMS 加密的 S3 bucket，需要三個政策層面都允許：Creative 帳號的 S3 bucket policy（資源型）、Creative 帳號的 KMS key policy，以及 Strategy 帳號的 strategy_reviewer IAM role policy。(A) bucket policy 授予讀取權限（s3:GetObject/s3:ListBucket）並將 Principal 設為 Strategy 帳號 ID，這是有效的跨帳號委派；依 IAM Principal 參考文件，指定帳號 ID 會將授權委派給該帳號，再由 role 的身分政策收斂範圍。(C) KMS key policy 必須明確授予 strategy_reviewer role kms:Decrypt，才能解密 SSE-KMS 物件；AWS Bedrock 與 SageMaker Canvas 的跨帳號指南都展示了這個新增的 key policy 陳述式。(F) IAM role 需要 S3 讀取權限加上 kms:Decrypt，這是身分側的最小權限授予。題目限定詞「only the minimum permissions」決定了錯誤選項：B 授予 S3 完整權限（違反最小權限），E 授予 Encrypt 而非 Decrypt（檢視物件只需 Decrypt）。D 將 Principal 設為匿名（公開），同時違反安全與最小權限。dump 答案 BCF 錯誤，因為 B 的完整權限與最小權限要求矛盾。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Granting 'full permissions' for the S3 bucket directly violates the explicit requirement to provide only the minimum permissions needed (read/view access). The decrypt grant in B is fine, but the full S3 permission breaks least privilege.","why_zh":"對 S3 bucket 授予「完整權限」直接違反僅提供最小必要權限（讀取/檢視）的明確要求。B 的解密授權沒問題，但完整 S3 權限破壞了最小權限原則。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Setting the bucket policy Principal to an anonymous user makes the bucket public, violating the security requirement and the minimum-permissions principle. Only the Strategy account/role should be granted access.","why_zh":"將 bucket policy 的 Principal 設為匿名使用者會使 bucket 公開，違反安全需求與最小權限原則。應只授予 Strategy 帳號/role 存取權。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"The strategy team only needs to VIEW (read) objects, which requires kms:Decrypt to decrypt SSE-KMS data. Granting Encrypt (kms:Encrypt) is unnecessary and does not enable reading, so it neither fixes the Access Denied nor follows least privilege.","why_zh":"strategy 團隊只需檢視（讀取）物件，需要 kms:Decrypt 來解密 SSE-KMS 資料。授予 Encrypt（kms:Encrypt）既不必要也無法讓使用者讀取，因此既無法解決 Access Denied 也不符合最小權限。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/cross-account-access-cmi.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/canvas-permissions-cross-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/key-policy-modifying-external-accounts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_elements_principal.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/example-walkthroughs-managing-access-example2.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":138,"question_en":"A life sciences company is using a combination of open source tools to manage data analysis work­ows and Docker containers running on servers in its on-premises data center to process genomics data. Sequencing data is generated and stored on a local storage area network (SAN), and then the data is processed. The research and development teams are running into capacity issues and have decided to re-architect their genomics analysis platform on AWS to scale based on workload demands and reduce the turnaround time from weeks to days. The company has a high-speed AWS Direct Connect connection. Sequencers will generate around 200 GB of data for each genome, and individual jobs can take several hours to process the data with ideal compute capacity. The end result will be stored in Amazon S3. The company is expecting 10-15 job requests each day. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家生命科学公司正在使用开源工具组合来管理数据分析工作流程，并使用在其本地数据中心的服务器上运行的 Docker 容器来处理 基因组数据。生成测序数据并将其存储在本地存储区域网络（SAN）上，然后对数据进行处理。研发团队遇到了容量问题，并决定 在 AWS 上重新构建其基因组分析平台，以根据工作负载需求进行扩展，并将周转时间从几周缩短到几天。 该公司拥有高速 AWS Direct Connect 连接。测序仪将为每个基因组生成大约 200 GB 的数据，并且单个作业可能需要几个小时才能以 理想的计算能力处理数据。最终结果将存储在 Amazon S3 中。该公司预计每天会收到 10-15 个工作请求。 哪种解决方案满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use regularly scheduled AWS Snowball Edge devices to transfer the sequencing data into AWS. When AWS receives the Snowball Edge device and the data is loaded into Amazon S3, use S3 events to trigger an AWS Lambda function to process the data.","B":"Use AWS Data Pipeline to transfer the sequencing data to Amazon S3. Use S3 events to trigger an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group to launch custom-AMI EC2 instances running the Docker containers to process the data.","C":"Use AWS DataSync to transfer the sequencing data to Amazon S3. Use S3 events to trigger an AWS Lambda function that starts an AWS Step Functions work­ow. Store the Docker images in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) and trigger AWS Batch to run the container and process the sequencing data.","D":"Use an AWS Storage Gateway file gateway to transfer the sequencing data to Amazon S3. Use S3 events to trigger an AWS Batch job that executes on Amazon EC2 instances running the Docker containers to process the data."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用定期安排的 AWS Snowball Edge 设备将测序数据传输到 AWS。当 AWS 收到 Snowball Edge 设备并将数据加载到 Amazon S3 中时，使用 S3 事件触发 AWS Lambda 函数来处理数据。","B":"使用 AWS Data Pipeline 将测序数据传输到 Amazon S3。使用 S3 事件触发 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 组启动运行 Docker 容器的自 定义 AMI EC2 实例来处理数据。","C":"使用 AWS DataSync 将测序数据传输到 Amazon S3。使用 S3 事件触发启动 AWS Step Functions 工作流程的 AWS Lambda 函数。将 Docker 映像存储在 Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) 中并触发 AWS Batch 运行容器并处理排序数据。","D":"使用 AWS Storage Gateway 文件网关将排序数据传输到 Amazon S3。使用 S3 事件触发 AWS Batch 作业，该作业在运行 Docker 容 器的 Amazon EC2 实例上执行以处理数据。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":76,"D":24},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":139,"question_en":"A company runs a content management application on a single Windows Amazon EC2 instance in a development environment. The application reads and writes static content to a 2 TB Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume that is attached to the instance as the root device. The company plans to deploy this application in production as a highly available and fault-tolerant solution that runs on at least three EC2 instances across multiple Availability Zones. A solutions architect must design a solution that joins all the instances that run the application to an Active Directory domain. The solution also must implement Windows ACLs to control access to file contents. The application always must maintain exactly the same content on all running instances at any given point in time. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST management overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司在开发环境中的单个 Windows Amazon EC2 实例上运行内容管理应用程序。该应用程序读取静态内容并将其写入作为根设备 附加到实例的 2 TB Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 卷。该公司计划在生产中将此应用程序部署为一个高度可用且容错的解决 方案，该解决方案在跨多个可用区的至少三个 EC2 实例上运行。 解决方案架构师必须设计一个解决方案，将运行应用程序的所有实例加入到 Active Directory 域。该解决方案还必须实现 Windows ACL 来控制对文件内容的访问。应用程序始终必须在任何给定时间点在所有正在运行的实例上维护完全相同的内容。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的管理开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file share. Create an Auto Scaling group that extends across three Availability Zones and maintains a minimum size of three instances. Implement a user data script to install the application, join the instance to the AD domain, and mount the EFS file share.","B":"Create a new AMI from the current EC2 Instance that is running. Create an Amazon FSx for Lustre file system. Create an Auto Scaling group that extends across three Availability Zones and maintains a minimum size of three instances. Implement a user data script to join the instance to the AD domain and mount the FSx for Lustre file system.","C":"Create an Amazon FSx for Windows File Server file system. Create an Auto Scaling group that extends across three Availability Zones and maintains a minimum size of three instances. Implement a user data script to install the application and mount the FSx for Windows File Server file system. Perform a seamless domain join to join the instance to the AD domain.","D":"Create a new AMI from the current EC2 instance that is running. Create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. Create an Auto Scaling group that extends across three Availability Zones and maintains a minimum size of three Instances. Perform a seamless domain join to join the instance to the AD domain."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件共享。创建一个跨三个可用区的 Auto Scaling 组，并保持至少三个实例的大 小。实施用户数据脚本来安装应用程序、将实例加入 AD 域并挂载 EFS 文件共享。","B":"从当前正在运行的 EC2 实例创建新的 AMI。创建 Amazon FSx for Lustre 文件系统。创建一个跨三个可用区的 Auto Scaling 组， 并保持至少三个实例的大小。实施用户数据脚本以将实例加入 AD 域并挂载 FSx for Lustre 文件系统。","C":"创建 Amazon FSx for Windows File Server 文件系统。创建一个跨三个可用区的 Auto Scaling 组，并保持至少三个实例的大小。实 施用户数据脚本来安装应用程序并挂载 FSx for Windows File Server 文件系统。执行无缝域加入以将实例加入 AD 域。","D":"从当前正在运行的 EC2 实例创建新的 AMI。创建 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统。创建一个跨越三个可用区 的 Auto Scaling 组，并保持至少三个实例的大小。执行无缝域加入以将实例加入 AD 域。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":95},"tags":["Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirements demand Windows EC2 instances joined to Active Directory, shared identical content across all instances at all times, and Windows ACLs for file-level access control, with the least management overhead. Amazon FSx for Windows File Server is purpose-built managed Windows file storage over SMB that natively integrates with Active Directory and enforces standard Windows ACLs for fine-grained file- and folder-level access control. A single FSx for Windows file system mounted by every instance guarantees exactly the same content on all instances at any point in time, and a seamless domain join is the AWS-supported low-overhead way to join Windows EC2 instances to the AD domain. Option C therefore meets every requirement with the least overhead. The dump's suggested answer B (FSx for Lustre) is wrong because Lustre is a Linux/POSIX high-performance file system that does not support SMB or Windows ACLs, and options A and D fail because AWS explicitly states Amazon EFS is not supported with Windows EC2 instances and EFS uses NFS/POSIX permissions rather than Windows ACLs.","explanation_zh":"本題要求 Windows EC2 執行個體加入 Active Directory、所有執行個體在任何時間點維持完全相同的共用內容，並使用 Windows ACL 控管檔案層級存取，且管理負擔最低。Amazon FSx for Windows File Server 是專為 Windows 設計的全代管 SMB 檔案儲存，原生整合 Active Directory，並以標準 Windows ACL 強制執行細緻的檔案與資料夾層級存取控制。所有執行個體掛載同一個 FSx for Windows 檔案系統，可保證任何時間點所有執行個體內容完全一致；而 seamless domain join（無縫網域加入）是 AWS 支援的低負擔方式，可將 Windows EC2 執行個體加入 AD 網域。因此選項 C 以最低負擔滿足所有要求。題庫建議答案 B（FSx for Lustre）錯誤，因為 Lustre 是 Linux/POSIX 高效能檔案系統，不支援 SMB 或 Windows ACL；選項 A 與 D 也錯誤，因為 AWS 明確指出 Amazon EFS 不支援 Windows EC2 執行個體，且 EFS 使用 NFS/POSIX 權限而非 Windows ACL。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon EFS is explicitly not supported with Windows EC2 instances, and EFS uses NFS/POSIX permissions, not Windows ACLs, so it cannot satisfy the Windows ACL requirement.","why_zh":"Amazon EFS 明確不支援 Windows EC2 執行個體，且 EFS 使用 NFS/POSIX 權限而非 Windows ACL，無法滿足 Windows ACL 要求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"FSx for Lustre is a Linux/POSIX high-performance compute file system that does not support SMB or Windows ACLs; it cannot enforce Windows file-level access control, and creating an AMI adds overhead without ensuring shared identical content.","why_zh":"FSx for Lustre 是 Linux/POSIX 高效能運算檔案系統，不支援 SMB 或 Windows ACL，無法強制執行 Windows 檔案層級存取控制；且建立 AMI 增加負擔卻無法保證共用且相同的內容。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same fatal flaw as A: EFS is not supported on Windows instances and provides no Windows ACLs; the seamless domain join alone does not fix the unsupported storage choice.","why_zh":"與 A 相同的致命缺陷：EFS 不支援 Windows 執行個體且不提供 Windows ACL；僅靠 seamless domain join 無法彌補不受支援的儲存選擇。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/WindowsGuide/limit-access-file-folder.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/WindowsGuide/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/WindowsGuide/aws-ad-integration-fsxW.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/troubleshooting-efs-mounting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directoryservice/latest/admin-guide/ms_ad_join_instance.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":140,"question_en":"A software as a service (SaaS) based company provides a case management solution to customers A3 part of the solution. The company uses a standalone Simple Mail Transfer Protocol (SMTP) server to send email messages from an application. The application also stores an email template for acknowledgement email messages that populate customer data before the application sends the email message to the customer. The company plans to migrate this messaging functionality to the AWS Cloud and needs to minimize operational overhead. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家基于软件即服务 (SaaS) 的公司向客户提供案例管理解决方案 A3 解决方案的一部分。该公司使用独立的简单邮件传输协议 (SMTP) 服务器从应用程序发送电子邮件。该应用程序还存储用于确认电子邮件消息的电子邮件模板，该模板在应用程序将电子邮件 消息发送给客户之前填充客户数据。 该公司计划将此消息传递功能迁移到 AWS 云，并需要最大限度地减少运营开销。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up an SMTP server on Amazon EC2 instances by using an AMI from the AWS Marketplace. Store the email template in an Amazon S3 bucket. Create an AWS Lambda function to retrieve the template from the S3 bucket and to merge the customer data from the application with the template. Use an SDK in the Lambda function to send the email message.","B":"Set up Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) to send email messages. Store the email template in an Amazon S3 bucket. Create an AWS Lambda function to retrieve the template from the S3 bucket and to merge the customer data from the application with the template. Use an SDK in the Lambda function to send the email message.","C":"Set up an SMTP server on Amazon EC2 instances by using an AMI from the AWS Marketplace. Store the email template in Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) with parameters for the customer data. Create an AWS Lambda function to call the SES template and to pass customer data to replace the parameters. Use the AWS Marketplace SMTP server to send the email message.","D":"Set up Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) to send email messages. Store the email template on Amazon SES with parameters for the customer data. Create an AWS Lambda function to call the SendTemplatedEmail API operation and to pass customer data to replace the parameters and the email destination."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Marketplace 中的 AMI 在 Amazon EC2 实例上设置 SMTP 服务器。将电子邮件模板存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。创建 一个 AWS Lambda 函数以从 S3 存储桶检索模板，并将应用程序中的客户数据与模板合并。使用 Lambda 函数中的 SDK 发送电子 邮件。","B":"设置 Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) 以发送电子邮件。将电子邮件模板存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数以从 S3 存储桶检索模板，并将应用程序中的客户数据与模板合并。使用 Lambda 函数中的 SDK 发送电子邮件。","C":"使用 AWS Marketplace 中的 AMI 在 Amazon EC2 实例上设置 SMTP 服务器。将电子邮件模板与客户数据参数一起存储在 Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) 中。创建 AWS Lambda 函数来调用 SES 模板并传递客户数据以替换参数。使用 AWS Marketplace SMTP 服务器发送电子邮件。","D":"设置 Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) 以发送电子邮件。将电子邮件模板与客户数据参数一起存储在 Amazon SES 上。 创建 AWS Lambda 函数来调用 SendTemplatedEmail API 操作并传递客户数据以替换参数和电子邮件目标。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":97},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The qualifier is MOST cost-effective with minimized operational overhead. Amazon SES is a fully managed sending service, so options A and C (running an SMTP server on EC2 from a Marketplace AMI) are eliminated: they add the cost of always-on instances plus patching/scaling/HA overhead. Between the two SES options, SES natively supports stored email templates created with CreateTemplate/CreateEmailTemplate and renders them with replacement variables when you call SendTemplatedEmail (v1) or SendEmail with a stored template (v2). Option D leverages this built-in templating and merge capability, requiring no extra storage and no custom merge code. Option B instead stores the template in S3 and writes custom Lambda logic to fetch and merge the data, which duplicates functionality SES already provides for free, adding S3 cost and Lambda development/maintenance overhead. Therefore D is both more cost-effective and lower operational overhead, making it the best answer; the community vote (D) is correct and the dump's suggested answer (B) is wrong.","explanation_zh":"題目限定條件為「最具成本效益」且「最小化營運負擔」。Amazon SES 是全代管的寄信服務，因此選項 A 與 C（以 AWS Marketplace AMI 在 EC2 上自建 SMTP 伺服器）可直接排除，因為需付出常駐執行個體的成本，並承擔修補、擴展與高可用性的營運負擔。在兩個使用 SES 的選項之間，SES 原生支援以 CreateTemplate/CreateEmailTemplate 建立並儲存 email 範本，並在呼叫 SendTemplatedEmail（v1）或帶入已儲存範本的 SendEmail（v2）時，使用替換變數自動渲染合併客戶資料。選項 D 直接善用此內建的範本與合併能力，無需額外儲存體，也不需自行撰寫合併程式碼。相對地，選項 B 將範本存在 S3 並自行撰寫 Lambda 程式碼擷取與合併資料，重複實作 SES 已免費提供的功能，徒增 S3 成本與 Lambda 開發維護負擔。因此 D 同時更具成本效益且營運負擔更低，為最佳答案；社群票選（D）正確，而題庫建議答案（B）錯誤。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Running a self-managed SMTP server on EC2 (Marketplace AMI) incurs always-on instance cost plus patching, scaling and HA overhead, and still requires custom S3 storage and Lambda merge code; it is the opposite of low cost / low operational overhead.","why_zh":"在 EC2（Marketplace AMI）上自管 SMTP 伺服器需付常駐執行個體成本，並承擔修補、擴展與高可用性負擔，且仍需自建 S3 儲存與 Lambda 合併程式碼；與低成本、低營運負擔的需求背道而馳。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Although SES handles sending, storing the template in S3 and writing custom Lambda code to fetch and merge data re-implements SES's native templating/merge feature, adding S3 cost and Lambda development and maintenance overhead unnecessarily.","why_zh":"雖然以 SES 寄信，但將範本存於 S3 並自行撰寫 Lambda 擷取與合併資料，重複實作 SES 原生的範本/合併功能，徒增 S3 成本及 Lambda 開發與維護負擔，並無必要。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This still runs an EC2-based SMTP server (high cost and operational overhead) and oddly mixes SES template storage with a non-SES SMTP sender; if you store templates in SES you would simply send through SES, so keeping the EC2 SMTP server is wasteful.","why_zh":"仍須運行 EC2 上的 SMTP 伺服器（高成本與高營運負擔），且不合理地將 SES 範本儲存與非 SES 的 SMTP 寄送混用；若範本存於 SES，直接以 SES 寄送即可，保留 EC2 SMTP 伺服器純屬浪費。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ses/latest/APIReference/API_SendTemplatedEmail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ses/latest/dg/send-personalized-email-api.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ses/latest/dg/send-email-api.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":141,"question_en":"A company is processing videos in the AWS Cloud by Using Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group. It takes 30 minutes to process a video Several EC2 instances scale in and out depending on the number of videos in an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. The company has configured the SQS queue with a redrive policy that specifies a target dead-letter queue and a maxReceiveCount of 1. The company has set the visibility timeout for the SQS queue to 1 hour. The company has set up an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to notify the development team when there are messages in the dead-letter queue. Several times during the day. the development team receives notification that messages are in the dead-letter queue and that videos have not been processed property. An investigation finds no errors m the application logs. How can the company solve this problem?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 Auto Scaling 组中的 Amazon EC2 实例处理 AWS 云中的视频。处理一个视频需要 30 分钟 多个 EC2 实例根据 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列中的视频数量进行扩展和扩展。 该公司已使用指定目标死信队列和 maxReceiveCount 1 的重新驱动策略配置了 SQS 队列。该公司已将 SQS 队列的可见性超时设置为 1 小时。该公司设置了 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，以便在死信队列中有消息时通知开发团队。 白天好几次。开发团队收到消息位于死信队列中且视频尚未得到处理的通知。调查发现应用程序日志中没有错误。 公司如何解决这个问题？","options_en":{"A":"Turn on termination protection tor the EC2 Instances","B":"Update the visibility timeout for the SQS queue to 3 hours","C":"Configure scale-in protection for the instances during processing","D":"Update the redrive policy and set maxReceiveCount to 0."},"options_zh":{"A":"打开 EC2 实例的终止保护","B":"将 SQS 队列的可见性超时更新为 3 小时","C":"配置处理过程中实例的缩容保护","D":"更新重新驱动策略并将 maxReceiveCount 设置为 0。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":71,"D":26},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The root cause is that the Auto Scaling group scales in and terminates EC2 instances while they are still processing a video (processing takes 30 minutes). When an instance is terminated, its in-flight message returns to the queue; because maxReceiveCount is 1, the message moves to the dead-letter queue on its very next receive. The application never errored, which is why the logs are clean. AWS documents this exact pattern in the 'Amazon SQS and instance scale-in protection' section: messages not processed when an instance is terminated are returned to the queue, and for long-running tasks you should use instance scale-in protection so the ASG does not terminate workers that are actively processing. Configuring scale-in protection during processing prevents the mid-task termination and therefore stops messages from being driven to the DLQ. The visibility timeout (1 hour) already exceeds the 30-minute processing time, so timeout expiry is not the cause.","explanation_zh":"根本原因是 Auto Scaling group 在 scale in 時終止了仍在處理影片的 EC2 instance（每支影片需 30 分鐘）。instance 被終止後，其 in-flight 訊息會回到 queue；由於 maxReceiveCount 設為 1，該訊息在下一次被接收時就會立即被移到 dead-letter queue。應用程式本身並未出錯，這也是為什麼日誌中沒有錯誤。AWS 文件在 'Amazon SQS and instance scale-in protection' 章節清楚描述此情境：instance 終止時尚未處理完成的訊息會被退回 queue，對於長時間執行的工作應使用 instance scale-in protection，讓 ASG 不會終止正在處理的 worker。在處理期間設定 scale-in protection 可避免任務中途被終止，進而停止訊息被送進 DLQ。visibility timeout（1 小時）已超過 30 分鐘處理時間，因此並非逾時造成。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"EC2 termination protection (DisableApiTermination) only blocks manual API/console termination; it does not prevent Auto Scaling group scale-in from terminating the instance, so the mid-processing termination still occurs.","why_zh":"EC2 termination protection（DisableApiTermination）只會阻擋手動 API/主控台終止，無法阻止 Auto Scaling group 的 scale in 終止 instance，因此處理中途被終止的問題依舊存在。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The visibility timeout is already 1 hour, far longer than the 30-minute processing time, so the timeout is not expiring. Raising it to 3 hours does nothing about instances being killed by scale-in.","why_zh":"visibility timeout 已是 1 小時，遠長於 30 分鐘的處理時間，因此並未逾時。改為 3 小時對 scale in 終止 instance 的問題毫無幫助。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"maxReceiveCount cannot be 0; the valid range is 1 to 1000. A value of 0 is invalid, and conceptually it would send messages to the DLQ even sooner, worsening the problem rather than fixing it.","why_zh":"maxReceiveCount 不能設為 0，有效範圍是 1 到 1000。設為 0 是無效的，且觀念上會讓訊息更快被送進 DLQ，反而使問題惡化而非修復。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/as-using-sqs-queue.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-auto-scaling-instance-protection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-dead-letter-queues.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-visibility-timeout.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":142,"question_en":"A company has developed APIs that use Amazon API Gateway with Regional endpoints. The APIs call AWS Lambda functions that use API Gateway authentication mechanisms. After a design review, a solutions architect identifies a set of APIs that do not require public access. The solutions architect must design a solution to make the set of APIs accessible only from a VPC. All APIs need to be called with an authenticated user Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST amount of effort?","question_zh":"一家公司开发了将 Amazon API Gateway 与区域终端节点结合使用的 API。API 调用使用 API Gateway 身份验证机制的 AWS Lambda 函 数。经过设计审查后，解决方案架构师确定了一组不需要公共访问的 API。 解决方案架构师必须设计一个解决方案，使这组 API 只能从 VPC 访问。所有 API 都需要由经过身份验证的用户调用 哪种解决方案能够以最少的努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an internal Application Load Balancer (ALB). Create a target group. Select the Lambda function to call. Use the ALB DNS name to call the API from the VPC.","B":"Remove the DNS entry that is associated with the API in API Gateway. Create a hosted zone in Amazon Route 53. Create a CNAME record in the hosted zone. Update the API in API Gateway with the CNAME record. Use the CNAME record to call the API from the VPC.","C":"Update the API endpoint from Regional to private in API Gateway. Create an interface VPC endpoint in the VPCreate a resource policy, and attach it to the API. Use the VPC endpoint to call the API from the VPC.","D":"Deploy the Lambda functions inside the VPC Provision an EC2 instance, and install an Apache server. From the Apache server, call the Lambda functions. Use the internal CNAME record of the EC2 instance to call the API from the VPC."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建内部应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB)。创建一个目标组。选择要调用的 Lambda 函数。使用 ALB DNS 名称从 VPC 调用 API。","B":"删除 API Gateway 中与 API 关联的 DNS 条目。在 Amazon Route 53 中创建托管区域。在托管区域中创建 CNAME 记录。使用 CNAME 记录更新 API Gateway 中的 API。使用CNAME记录从VPC调用API。","C":"在 API Gateway 中将 API 端点从区域更新为私有。在 VP 中创建接口 VPC 终端节点创建资源策略，并将其附加到 API。使用VPC 端点从VPC调用API。","D":"在 VPC 内部署 Lambda 函数 配置 EC2 实例，并安装 Apache 服务器。从 Apache 服务器调用 Lambda 函数。使用 EC2 实例的内 部 CNAME 记录从 VPC 调用 API。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to make a set of existing API Gateway Regional APIs accessible only from a VPC while still using API Gateway's authentication mechanisms, with the least effort. AWS's native, documented pattern for this is a private REST API: change the endpoint type from Regional to private (supported migration per the API Gateway docs), create an interface VPC endpoint (powered by AWS PrivateLink) for the execute-api service in the VPC, and attach a resource policy to the API that restricts access to that VPC endpoint. Clients in the VPC then invoke the API through the interface endpoint's private IPs. This reuses the existing API Gateway + Lambda + authorizer setup and adds no new compute, load balancers, or DNS rewrites, so it is the least-effort solution. Option C describes exactly this flow (private endpoint + interface VPC endpoint + resource policy + invoke via the VPC endpoint), matching the AWS 'Create a private API' procedure.","explanation_zh":"需求是讓一組現有的 API Gateway Regional API 僅能從 VPC 存取，同時仍沿用 API Gateway 的驗證機制，並以最少工作量達成。AWS 原生且有文件記載的做法就是 private REST API：將 endpoint 類型從 Regional 改為 private（API Gateway 文件明確支援此遷移），在 VPC 中為 execute-api 服務建立一個 interface VPC endpoint（由 AWS PrivateLink 提供），並在 API 上掛上 resource policy 限制只允許該 VPC endpoint 存取。VPC 內的用戶端即可透過 interface endpoint 的私有 IP 呼叫 API。此方案重用既有的 API Gateway + Lambda + authorizer 架構，不需新增運算資源、負載平衡器或重寫 DNS，因此工作量最少。選項 C 精確描述了此流程（private endpoint + interface VPC endpoint + resource policy + 經由 VPC endpoint 呼叫），與 AWS 'Create a private API' 程序一致。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An internal ALB with a Lambda target group bypasses API Gateway entirely, which means you lose the existing API Gateway authentication mechanisms (authorizers) the question requires keeping. It also re-architects the solution rather than simply restricting access, so it is more effort and breaks the auth requirement.","why_zh":"使用內部 ALB 搭配 Lambda target group 會完全繞過 API Gateway，等於失去題目要求保留的 API Gateway 驗證機制（authorizer）。這也是重新架構而非單純限制存取，工作量更大且違反驗證需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Removing DNS entries and creating a Route 53 CNAME does not make an API private; a Regional API remains publicly reachable over the internet regardless of DNS records. DNS only changes the name used, not the network reachability or access scope, so it fails the 'accessible only from a VPC' requirement.","why_zh":"移除 DNS 記錄並建立 Route 53 CNAME 並不會讓 API 變成私有；無論 DNS 記錄如何，Regional API 仍可從網際網路公開存取。DNS 只改變使用的名稱，不改變網路可達性或存取範圍，因此無法滿足『僅能從 VPC 存取』的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but is wrong: deploying Lambda in the VPC and fronting it with an EC2/Apache server discards API Gateway and its authentication, requires building and operating a proxy server (high effort and operational overhead), and an 'internal CNAME of an EC2 instance' is not a real API endpoint. It is the most complex, least-effort-violating option.","why_zh":"這是題庫建議答案，但是錯的：將 Lambda 部署到 VPC 並用 EC2/Apache 伺服器當前端會捨棄 API Gateway 及其驗證機制，且需自行建置與維運代理伺服器（高工作量與營運負擔），而『EC2 執行個體的內部 CNAME』也不是真正的 API endpoint。這是最複雜、最違反最少工作量的選項。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-private-apis.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-private-api-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-api-migration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-vpc-endpoint-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/api-gateway-api-endpoint-types.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":143,"question_en":"A weather service provides high-resolution weather maps from a web application hosted on AWS in the eu-west-1 Region. The weather maps are updated frequently and stored in Amazon S3 along with static HTML content. The web application is fronted by Amazon CloudFront. The company recently expanded to serve users in the us-east-1 Region, and these new users report that viewing their respective weather maps is slow from time to time. Which combination of steps will resolve the us-east-1 performance issues? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"气象服务通过 eu-west-1 区域 AWS 上托管的 Web 应用程序提供高分辨率气象图。天气图经常更新并与静态 HTML 内容一起存储在 Amazon S3 中。该 Web 应用程序以 Amazon CloudFront 为前端。 该公司最近扩展到为 us-east-1 区域的用户提供服务，这些新用户报告说，查看各自的天气图有时会很慢。 哪种步骤组合可以解决 us-east-1 性能问题？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure the AWS Global Accelerator endpoint for the S3 bucket in eu-west-1. Configure endpoint groups for TCP ports 80 and 443 in us-east-1.","B":"Create a new S3 bucket in us-east-1. Configure S3 cross-Region replication to synchronize from the S3 bucket in eu-west-1.","C":"Use Lambda@Edge to modify requests from North America to use the S3 Transfer Acceleration endpoint in us-east-1.","D":"Use Lambda@Edge to modify requests from North America to use the S3 bucket in us-east-1.","E":"Configure the AWS Global Accelerator endpoint for us-east-1 as an origin on the CloudFront distribution. Use Lambda@Edge to modify requests from North America to use the new origin."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 eu-west-1 中的 S3 存储桶配置 AWS Global Accelerator 终端节点。在 us-east-1 中配置 TCP 端口 80 和 443 的端点组。","B":"在 us-east-1 中创建一个新的 S3 存储桶。配置 S3 跨区域复制以从 eu-west-1 中的 S3 存储桶进行同步。","C":"使用 Lambda@Edge 修改来自北美的请求以使用 us-east-1 中的 S3 Transfer Acceleration 终端节点。","D":"使用 Lambda@Edge 修改来自北美的请求以使用 us-east-1 中的 S3 存储桶。","E":"将 us-east-1 的 AWS Global Accelerator 终端节点配置为 CloudFront 分配上的源。使用 Lambda@Edge 修改来自北美的请求以使用 新源。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BD":96},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":144,"question_en":"A solutions architect is investigating an issue in which a company cannot establish new sessions in Amazon Workspaces. An initial analysis indicates that the issue involves user profiles. The Amazon Workspaces environment is configured to use Amazon FSx for Windows File Server as the profile share storage. The FSx for Windows File Server file system is configured with 10 TB of storage. The solutions architect discovers that the file system has reached Its maximum capacity. The solutions architect must ensure that users can regain access. The solution also must prevent the problem from occurring again. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师正在调查公司无法在 Amazon Workspaces 中建立新会话的问题。初步分析表明该问题涉及用户配置文件。Amazon Workspaces 环境配置为使用 Amazon FSx for Windows File Server 作为配置文件共享存储。FSx for Windows 文件服务器文件系统配置有 10 TB 的存储空间。 解决方案架构师发现文件系统已达到其最大容量。解决方案架构师必须确保用户可以重新获得访问权限。解决方案还必须防止问题 再次发生。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Remove old user profiles to create space. Migrate the user profiles to an Amazon FSx for Lustre file system.","B":"Increase capacity by using the update-file-system command. Implement an Amazon CloudWatch metric that monitors free space. Use Amazon EventBridge to invoke an AWS Lambda function to increase capacity as required.","C":"Monitor the file system by using the FreeStorageCapacity metric in Amazon CloudWatch. Use AWS Step Functions to increase the capacity as required.","D":"Remove old user profiles to create space. Create an additional FSx for Windows File Server file system. Update the user profile redirection for 50% of the users to use the new file system."},"options_zh":{"A":"删除旧的用户配置文件以创建空间。将用户配置文件迁移到 Amazon FSx for Lustre 文件系统。","B":"使用 update-file-system 命令增加容量。实施监控可用空间的 Amazon CloudWatch 指标。使用 Amazon EventBridge 调用 AWS Lambda 函数以根据需要增加容量。","C":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 中的 FreeStorageCapacity 指标监控文件系统。使用 AWS Step Functions 根据需要增加容量。","D":"删除旧的用户配置文件以创建空间。创建额外的 FSx for Windows 文件服务器文件系统。更新 50% 用户的用户配置文件重定向 以使用新文件系统。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":88},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The file system is already at its 10 TB maximum, so WorkSpaces sessions fail now. The requirement has two parts: (1) restore access immediately, and (2) prevent recurrence. Option B does both: it runs the documented update-file-system command to increase capacity right away (FSx for Windows allows raising storage capacity to up to 65,536 GiB, with each increase at least 10% over current), restoring user access, and then sets up a CloudWatch metric on free storage plus an event-driven Lambda that automatically increases capacity going forward. AWS's own reference architecture (Increasing the storage capacity of an FSx for Windows File Server file system dynamically) uses a CloudWatch alarm on free storage capacity that invokes a Lambda function which calls the FSx UpdateFileSystem API. Using EventBridge to invoke Lambda from the CloudWatch alarm is a valid equivalent of that pattern. Option C only establishes future auto-scaling and never performs the immediate remediation that lets currently locked-out users regain access, and it uses Step Functions rather than the documented Lambda mechanism, so it fails the first requirement.","explanation_zh":"FSx for Windows File Server 檔案系統已達到 10 TB 上限，因此 WorkSpaces 工作階段目前無法建立。需求有兩部分：(1) 立即恢復存取，(2) 防止問題再次發生。選項 B 兩者兼顧：先以文件記載的 update-file-system 指令立即增加容量（FSx for Windows 可將儲存容量提高至最多 65,536 GiB，每次增加至少需比現值多 10%），恢復使用者存取；再建立 CloudWatch 監控可用空間的指標，並透過事件驅動的 Lambda 自動依需求擴充容量。AWS 官方參考架構（Increasing the storage capacity of an FSx for Windows File Server file system dynamically）即是以針對可用儲存容量的 CloudWatch alarm 觸發 Lambda 呼叫 FSx UpdateFileSystem API。使用 EventBridge 從 CloudWatch alarm 觸發 Lambda 與該模式等效。選項 C 僅設定未來的自動擴充，從未執行讓目前被鎖定使用者立即恢復存取的補救動作，且使用 Step Functions 而非文件記載的 Lambda 機制，因此無法滿足第一項需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"FSx for Lustre is a high-performance parallel file system for HPC/ML workloads and does not provide Windows SMB shares with Active Directory integration that WorkSpaces user profiles require. Migrating profiles there is technically unworkable, and manually deleting profiles is a one-off fix that does not prevent recurrence.","why_zh":"FSx for Lustre 是用於 HPC/ML 的高效能平行檔案系統，無法提供 WorkSpaces 使用者設定檔所需的 Windows SMB 共享與 Active Directory 整合。將設定檔遷移過去技術上行不通，且手動刪除設定檔只是一次性處理，無法防止再次發生。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This only configures future monitoring/auto-scaling and never increases capacity now, so currently locked-out users do not regain access (the file system is already at max). It also uses Step Functions, whereas the documented dynamic-increase pattern uses a CloudWatch alarm invoking a Lambda function that calls UpdateFileSystem.","why_zh":"此選項僅設定未來的監控/自動擴充，並未立即增加容量，因此已被鎖定的使用者無法恢復存取（檔案系統已達上限）。且使用 Step Functions，而文件記載的動態擴充模式是以 CloudWatch alarm 觸發 Lambda 呼叫 UpdateFileSystem。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creating a second file system and manually redirecting 50% of users is high operational overhead and does not prevent recurrence (either file system can still fill up). Deleting old profiles is a manual stopgap, and there is no automated scaling.","why_zh":"建立第二個檔案系統並手動將 50% 使用者重新導向，操作負擔高且無法防止再次發生（兩個檔案系統都可能再次被填滿）。刪除舊設定檔只是手動權宜之計，且沒有自動擴充機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/WindowsGuide/automate-storage-capacity-increase.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/WindowsGuide/increase-storage-capacity.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/WindowsGuide/managing-storage-configuration.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":145,"question_en":"An international delivery company hosts a delivery management system on AWS. Drivers use the system to upload confirmation of delivery. Confirmation includes the recipient’s signature or a photo of the package with the recipient. The driver’s handheld device uploads signatures and photos through FTP to a single Amazon EC2 instance. Each handheld device saves a file in a directory based on the signed-in user, and the file name matches the delivery number. The EC2 instance then adds metadata to the file after querying a central database to pull delivery information. The file is then placed in Amazon S3 for archiving. As the company expands, drivers report that the system is rejecting connections. The FTP server is having problems because of dropped connections and memory issues in response to these problems, a system engineer schedules a cron task to reboot the EC2 instance every 30 minutes. The billing team reports that files are not always in the archive and that the central system is not always updated. A solutions architect needs to design a solution that maximizes scalability to ensure that the archive always receives the files and that systems are always updated. The handheld devices cannot be modified, so the company cannot deploy a new application. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家国际配送公司在 AWS 上托管一个配送管理系统。司机使用该系统上传交货确认信息。确认包括收件人的签名或收件人与包裹的 合影。驾驶员的手持设备通过 FTP 将签名和照片上传到单个 Amazon EC2 实例。每个手持设备根据登录用户在目录中保存一个文 件，文件名与发货编号匹配。然后，EC2 实例在查询中央数据库以提取传递信息后将元数据添加到文件中。然后该文件被放置在 Amazon S3 中进行存档。 随着公司的扩张，司机报告说系统拒绝连接。由于连接丢失和内存问题，FTP 服务器出现问题，为了应对这些问题，系统工程师安 排了一个 cron 任务，每 30 分钟重新启动一次 EC2 实例。计费团队报告说，文件并不总是在存档中，并且中央系统并不总是更新。 解决方案架构师需要设计一个能够最大限度提高可扩展性的解决方案，以确保存档始终接收文件并且系统始终更新。手持设备无法 修改，因此公司无法部署新的应用程序。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AMI of the existing EC2 instance. Create an Auto Scaling group of EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer. Configure the Auto Scaling group to have a minimum of three instances.","B":"Use AWS Transfer Family to create an FTP server that places the files in Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS). Mount the EFS volume to the existing EC2 instance. Point the EC2 instance to the new path for file processing.","C":"Use AWS Transfer Family to create an FTP server that places the files in Amazon S3. Use an S3 event notification through Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to invoke an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to add the metadata and update the delivery system.","D":"Update the handheld devices to place the files directly in Amazon S3. Use an S3 event notification through Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) to invoke an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to add the metadata and update the delivery system."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建现有 EC2 实例的 AMI。在 Application Load Balancer 后面创建 EC2 实例的 Auto Scaling 组。将 Auto Scaling 组配置为至少具 有三个实例。","B":"使用 AWS Transfer Family 创建将文件放置在 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 中的 FTP 服务器。将 EFS 卷挂载到现有 EC2 实例。将 EC2 实例指向文件处理的新路径。","C":"使用 AWS Transfer Family 创建将文件放置在 Amazon S3 中的 FTP 服务器。通过 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 使用 S3 事件通知来调用 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数以添加元数据并更新交付系统。","D":"更新手持设备以将文件直接放入 Amazon S3 中。通过 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 使用 S3 事件通知来调用 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数以添加元数据并更新交付系统。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":74,"B":26},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The goal is to maximize scalability while ensuring files always reach the archive (S3) and the central system is always updated, and the handheld devices cannot be modified (so they must keep using FTP). AWS Transfer Family provides a fully managed FTP endpoint that writes files directly into Amazon S3, removing the single overloaded EC2 instance that was dropping connections and running out of memory. An S3 event notification (via SNS) then invokes a Lambda function that adds the metadata and updates the delivery system. This design is fully serverless and elastically scalable, decouples ingestion from processing, and the devices keep using FTP unchanged. Option C is correct.","explanation_zh":"目標是最大化可擴展性，同時確保檔案一定會送達封存區 (S3) 且中央系統一定會被更新，而且手持裝置不能修改（必須繼續使用 FTP）。AWS Transfer Family 提供完全託管的 FTP 端點，可直接將檔案寫入 Amazon S3，移除了原本因連線中斷與記憶體不足而失敗的單一 EC2 執行個體。接著由 S3 事件通知（透過 SNS）觸發 Lambda 函數，加入中繼資料並更新交付系統。此設計完全無伺服器且具彈性擴展，將擷取與處理解耦，裝置維持使用 FTP 不變。選項 C 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An Application Load Balancer does not support FTP (FTP uses separate control/data channels and ephemeral data ports, requiring an NLB at best), and this only replicates the same fragile EC2-based processing design rather than fixing the architectural bottleneck. It does not maximize scalability.","why_zh":"Application Load Balancer 不支援 FTP（FTP 使用獨立的控制/資料通道與動態資料埠，最多需用 NLB），且此方案只是複製同樣脆弱的 EC2 處理架構，並未解決架構瓶頸，無法最大化可擴展性。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"This uses Transfer Family but routes files to EFS and keeps the SAME single existing EC2 instance doing all the metadata processing. That EC2 instance remains the bottleneck and single point of failure (the original cause of memory issues and lost updates), so it does not maximize scalability. This is the dump's suggested answer but it is wrong.","why_zh":"此方案雖使用 Transfer Family，但檔案送到 EFS 後仍由同一個既有 EC2 執行個體執行所有中繼資料處理。該 EC2 仍是瓶頸與單點故障（正是記憶體問題與更新遺失的原因），因此無法最大化可擴展性。這是題庫建議答案但是錯誤的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"It requires updating the handheld devices to upload directly to S3, which is explicitly prohibited by the requirement that the devices cannot be modified and no new application can be deployed.","why_zh":"此方案要求更新手持裝置以直接上傳至 S3，但需求明確禁止修改裝置或部署新應用程式，因此違反限制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transfer/latest/userguide/what-is-aws-transfer-family.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transfer/latest/userguide/create-server-ftp.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/EventNotifications.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-s3.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":146,"question_en":"A company is running an application in the AWS Cloud. The application runs on containers m an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster. The ECS tasks use the Fargate launch type. The application's data is relational and is stored in Amazon Aurora MySQL. To meet regulatory requirements, the application must be able to recover to a separate AWS Region in the event of an application failure. In case of a failure, no data can be lost. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST amount of operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 云中运行应用程序。该应用程序在 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 集群中的容器上运行。ECS 任务 使用 Fargate 启动类型。该应用程序的数据是关系数据，存储在 Amazon Aurora MySQL 中。为了满足监管要求，应用程序必须能够在 应用程序发生故障时恢复到单独的 AWS 区域。如果出现故障，任何数据都不会丢失。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Provision an Aurora Replica in a different Region.","B":"Set up AWS DataSync for continuous replication of the data to a different Region.","C":"Set up AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to perform a continuous replication of the data to a different Region.","D":"Use Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager (Amazon DLM) to schedule a snapshot every 5 minutes."},"options_zh":{"A":"在不同区域配置 Aurora 副本。","B":"设置 AWS DataSync 以将数据持续复制到不同区域。","C":"设置 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 以将数据连续复制到不同区域。","D":"使用 Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager (Amazon DLM) 计划每 5 分钟生成一次快照。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Migration","Compute","Database","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":147,"question_en":"A financial services company receives a regular data feed from its credit card servicing partner. Approximately 5,000 records are sent every 15 minutes in plaintext, delivered over HTTPS directly into an Amazon S3 bucket with server-side encryption. This feed contains sensitive credit card primary account number (PAN) data. The company needs to automatically mask the PAN before sending the data to another S3 bucket for additional internal processing. The company also needs to remove and merge specific fields, and then transform the record into JSON format. Additionally, extra feeds are likely to be added in the future, so any design needs to be easily expandable. Which solutions will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家金融服务公司从其信用卡服务合作伙伴处定期接收数据源。每 15 分钟就会以明文形式发送大约 5,000 条记录，通过 HTTPS 直接 传送到具有服务器端加密的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。此 Feed 包含敏感的信用卡主帐号 (PAN) 数据。该公司需要在将数据发送到另一个 S3 存储桶进行额外的内部处理之前自动屏蔽 PAN。该公司还需要删除并合并特定字段，然后将记录转换为 JSON 格式。此外，未来 可能会添加额外的提要，因此任何设计都需要易于扩展。 哪些解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Invoke an AWS Lambda function on file delivery that extracts each record and writes it to an Amazon SQS queue. Invoke another Lambda function when new messages arrive in the SQS queue to process the records, writing the results to a temporary location in Amazon S3. Invoke a final Lambda function once the SQS queue is empty to transform the records into JSON format and send the results to another S3 bucket for internal processing.","B":"Invoke an AWS Lambda function on file delivery that extracts each record and writes it to an Amazon SQS queue. Configure an AWS Fargate container application to automatically scale to a single instance when the SQS queue contains messages. Have the application process each record, and transform the record into JSON format. When the queue is empty, send the results to another S3 bucket for internal processing and scale down the AWS Fargate instance.","C":"Create an AWS Glue crawler and custom classifier based on the data feed formats and build a table definition to match. Invoke an AWS Lambda function on file delivery to start an AWS Glue ETL job to transform the entire record according to the processing and transformation requirements. Define the output format as JSON. Once complete, have the ETL job send the results to another S3 bucket for internal processing.","D":"Create an AWS Glue crawler and custom classifier based upon the data feed formats and build a table definition to match. Perform an Amazon Athena query on file delivery to start an Amazon EMR ETL job to transform the entire record according to the processing and transformation requirements. Define the output format as JSON. Once complete, send the results to another S3 bucket for internal processing and scale down the EMR cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"在文件传输时调用 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数提取每条记录并将其写入 Amazon SQS 队列。当新消息到达 SQS 队列时调用另一 个 Lambda 函数来处理记录，将结果写入 Amazon S3 中的临时位置。一旦 SQS 队列为空，调用最终 Lambda 函数，将记录转换为 JSON 格式，并将结果发送到另一个 S3 存储桶进行内部处理。","B":"在文件传输时调用 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数提取每条记录并将其写入 Amazon SQS 队列。将 AWS Fargate 容器应用程序配置 为在 SQS 队列包含消息时自动扩展到单个实例。让应用程序处理每条记录，并将记录转换为 JSON 格式。当队列为空时，将结果 发送到另一个 S3 存储桶进行内部处理并缩小 AWS Fargate 实例。","C":"根据数据源格式创建 AWS Glue 爬网程序和自定义分类器，并构建匹配的表定义。在文件传输时调用 AWS Lambda 函数来启动 AWS Glue ETL 作业，以根据处理和转换要求转换整个记录。定义输出格式为 JSON。完成后，让 ETL 作业将结果发送到另一个 S3 存储桶以进行内部处理。","D":"根据数据源格式创建 AWS Glue 爬网程序和自定义分类器，并构建匹配的表定义。对文件传输执行 Amazon Athena 查询以启动 Amazon EMR ETL 作业，根据处理和转换要求转换整个记录。定义输出格式为 JSON。完成后，将结果发送到另一个 S3 存储桶进 行内部处理并缩小 EMR 集群规模。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Analytics","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":148,"question_en":"A company wants to use AWS to create a business continuity solution in case the company's main on-premises application fails. The application runs on physical servers that also run other applications. The on-premises application that the company is planning to migrate uses a MySQL database as a data store. All the company's on-premises applications use operating systems that are compatible with Amazon EC2. Which solution will achieve the company's goal with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司希望使用 AWS 创建业务连续性解决方案，以防公司的主要本地应用程序出现故障。该应用程序在还运行其他应用程序的物 理服务器上运行。该公司计划迁移的本地应用程序使用 MySQL 数据库作为数据存储。该公司的所有本地应用程序都使用与 Amazon EC2 兼容的操作系统。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销实现公司的目标？","options_en":{"A":"Install the AWS Replication Agent on the source servers, including the MySQL servers. Set up replication for all servers. Launch test instances for regular drills. Cut over to the test instances to fail over the workload in the case of a failure event.","B":"Install the AWS Replication Agent on the source servers, including the MySQL servers. Initialize AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery in the target AWS Region. Define the launch settings. Frequently perform failover and fallback from the most recent point in time.","C":"Create AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) replication servers and a target Amazon Aurora MySQL DB cluster to host the database. Create a DMS replication task to copy the existing data to the target DB cluster. Create a local AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) change data capture (CDC) task to keep the data synchronized. Install the rest of the software on EC2 instances by starting with a compatible base AMI.","D":"Deploy an AWS Storage Gateway Volume Gateway on premises. Mount volumes on all on-premises servers. Install the application and the MySQL database on the new volumes. Take regular snapshots. Install all the software on EC2 Instances by starting with a compatible base AMI. Launch a Volume Gateway on an EC2 instance. Restore the volumes from the latest snapshot. Mount the new volumes on the EC2 instances in the case of a failure event."},"options_zh":{"A":"在源服务器（包括 MySQL 服务器）上安装 AWS Replication Agent。为所有服务器设置复制。启动常规演习的测试实例。在发生 故障事件时切换到测试实例以对工作负载进行故障转移。","B":"在源服务器（包括 MySQL 服务器）上安装 AWS Replication Agent。在目标 AWS 区域中初始化 AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery。定 义启动设置。经常从最近的时间点执行故障转移和回退。","C":"创建 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 复制服务器和目标 Amazon Aurora MySQL 数据库集群来托管数据库。创建DMS 复制任务，将现有数据复制到目标数据库集群。创建本地 AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) 更改数据捕获 (CDC) 任务以保持 数据同步。从兼容的基础 AMI 开始，在 EC2 实例上安装其余软件。","D":"在本地部署 AWS Storage Gateway 卷网关。在所有本地服务器上安装卷。在新卷上安装应用程序和 MySQL 数据库。定期拍摄快 照。从兼容的基础 AMI 开始，在 EC2 实例上安装所有软件。在 EC2 实例上启动卷网关。从最新快照恢复卷。发生故障事件时， 在 EC2 实例上装载新卷。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":81,"C":19},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The company wants a disaster recovery / business continuity solution to fail over when its on-premises application fails, with the LEAST operational overhead. AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery (DRS) is the purpose-built service for this. Per the DRS getting-started workflow, you initialize DRS in the target AWS Region, install the AWS Replication Agent on the source servers (including the MySQL servers, where block-level replication captures the database too), define the launch settings, and then perform failover and failback from the most recent point in time. This requires no re-architecture and gives low RPO/RTO with minimal ongoing compute cost, exactly matching Option B. Option C (DMS + SCT CDC to Aurora MySQL plus manually rebuilding the rest on EC2 base AMIs) is a database-modernization/migration approach with far higher operational overhead and unnecessary SCT for homogeneous MySQL-to-MySQL.","explanation_zh":"公司要的是災難復原 / 業務持續性方案，當地端應用程式失效時可進行容錯移轉 (failover)，且要求最低營運負擔。AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery (DRS) 正是為此設計的服務。依官方入門流程：在目標 AWS 區域初始化 DRS、在來源伺服器（含 MySQL 伺服器，區塊層級複寫會一併涵蓋資料庫）安裝 AWS Replication Agent、定義啟動設定 (launch settings)，再從最近的時間點執行 failover 與 failback。此作法無須重新架構，可達到低 RPO/RTO 且持續複寫期間的運算成本極低，完全對應選項 B。選項 C（用 DMS + SCT CDC 遷到 Aurora MySQL，再用基礎 AMI 手動重建其餘元件）屬於資料庫現代化/遷移作法，營運負擔高出許多，且同質 MySQL 對 MySQL 不需要 SCT。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses migration terminology: DRS launches drill and recovery instances, not 'test instances' that you 'cut over' to (cutover is Application Migration Service/MGN language for one-time migration, not ongoing DR). It also omits initializing DRS and defining launch settings, and mischaracterizes the failover step.","why_zh":"用了遷移用語：DRS 啟動的是 drill 與 recovery 執行個體，而非可「cutover」的 test 執行個體（cutover 是 Application Migration Service/MGN 的一次性遷移用語，非持續性 DR）。且未提初始化 DRS 與定義啟動設定，並錯誤描述 failover 步驟。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"High operational overhead: splits the DB into Aurora MySQL via DMS and adds an SCT CDC task (SCT/schema conversion is unneeded for homogeneous MySQL-to-MySQL), then manually rebuilds the rest of the app on EC2 from base AMIs. This is a re-platform/migration, not a low-overhead coordinated DR failover.","why_zh":"營運負擔高：用 DMS 把資料庫拆出到 Aurora MySQL 並加 SCT CDC 任務（同質 MySQL 對 MySQL 不需要 SCT/結構轉換），還要從基礎 AMI 手動重建其餘應用。這是重新平台化/遷移，而非低負擔的協調式 DR failover。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Storage Gateway Volume Gateway requires installing the app and MySQL onto new volumes and manually restoring from snapshots onto EC2 in a failure — disruptive, manual, and very high operational overhead; it is not a DR replication service.","why_zh":"Storage Gateway Volume Gateway 需把應用與 MySQL 安裝到新磁碟區，並在故障時手動從快照還原到 EC2——具破壞性、手動且營運負擔極高，並非 DR 複寫服務。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/what-is-drs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/getting-started.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/failback.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/agent-installation.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":149,"question_en":"A company is subject to regulatory audits of its financial information. External auditors who use a single AWS account need access to the company's AWS account. A solutions architect must provide the auditors with secure, read-only access to the company's AWS account. The solution must comply with AWS security best practices. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"公司须接受对其财务信息的监管审计。使用单个 AWS 账户的外部审计员需要访问公司的 AWS 账户。解决方案架构师必须为审核员 提供对公司 AWS 账户的安全、只读访问权限。该解决方案必须符合 AWS 安全最佳实践。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"In the company's AWS account, create resource policies for all resources in the account to grant access to the auditors' AWS account. Assign a unique external ID to the resource policy.","B":"In the company's AWS account, create an IAM role that trusts the auditors' AWS account. Create an IAM policy that has the required permissions. Attach the policy to the role. Assign a unique external ID to the role's trust policy.","C":"In the company's AWS account, create an IAM user. Attach the required IAM policies to the IAM user. Create API access keys for the IAM user. Share the access keys with the auditors.","D":"In the company's AWS account, create an IAM group that has the required permissions. Create an IAM user in the company's account for each auditor. Add the IAM users to the IAM group."},"options_zh":{"A":"在公司的 AWS 账户中，为账户中的所有资源创建资源策略，以授予对审核员 AWS 账户的访问权限。为资源策略分配唯一的外 部 ID。","B":"在公司的 AWS 账户中，创建信任审计员 AWS 账户的 IAM 角色。创建具有所需权限的 IAM 策略。将策略附加到角色。为角色的 信任策略分配唯一的外部 ID。","C":"在公司的 AWS 账户中，创建 IAM 用户。将所需的 IAM 策略附加到 IAM 用户。为 IAM 用户创建 API 访问密钥。与审核员共享访 问密钥。","D":"在公司的 AWS 账户中，创建具有所需权限的 IAM 组。在公司账户中为每位审核员创建一个 IAM 用户。将 IAM 用户添加到 IAM 组。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":150,"question_en":"A company has a latency-sensitive trading platform that uses Amazon DynamoDB as a storage backend. The company configured the DynamoDB table to use on-demand capacity mode. A solutions architect needs to design a solution to improve the performance of the trading platform. The new solution must ensure high availability for the trading platform. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST latency?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个对延迟敏感的交易平台，该平台使用 Amazon DynamoDB 作为存储后端。该公司将 DynamoDB 表配置为使用按需容 量模式。解决方案架构师需要设计一个解决方案来提高交易平台的性能。新的解决方案必须确保交易平台的高可用性。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的延迟满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a two-node DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster. Configure an application to read and write data by using DAX.","B":"Create a three-node DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster. Configure an application to read data by using DAX and to write data directly to the DynamoDB table.","C":"Create a three-node DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster. Configure an application to read data directly from the DynamoDB table and to write data by using DAX.","D":"Create a single-node DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster. Configure an application to read data by using DAX and to write data directly to the DynamoDB table."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个两节点 DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) 集群。配置应用程序以使用 DAX 读取和写入数据。","B":"创建一个三节点 DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) 集群。配置应用程序以使用 DAX 读取数据并将数据直接写入 DynamoDB 表。","C":"创建一个三节点 DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) 集群。配置应用程序以直接从 DynamoDB 表读取数据并使用 DAX 写入数据。","D":"创建单节点 DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) 集群。配置应用程序以使用 DAX 读取数据并将数据直接写入 DynamoDB 表。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":91},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The question demands the LEAST latency for a latency-sensitive trading platform while also ensuring high availability. AWS explicitly states two relevant facts. First, for high availability/production workloads, AWS recommends provisioning a DAX cluster with at least three nodes placed in different Availability Zones; a single-node cluster has no fault tolerance and a two-node cluster is below the recommended minimum, so options A and D fail the HA requirement. Second, for write latency, the DAX docs say that writing through DAX incurs an extra network hop and is slower than writing directly to DynamoDB, so latency-sensitive applications should write directly to DynamoDB (the write-around pattern) while still benefiting from microsecond cached reads via DAX. Option B (three-node DAX cluster, read via DAX, write directly to DynamoDB) is the only choice that satisfies both HA (3 nodes/multi-AZ) and lowest latency (write-around avoids the extra hop). Option C inverts this by writing through DAX and reading directly from DynamoDB, which gives the worst read latency (no cache benefit) and slowest writes.","explanation_zh":"題目要求在確保高可用性的同時，為延遲敏感的交易平台提供最低延遲。AWS 文件明確指出兩個關鍵事實。第一，為達到高可用性與生產環境需求，AWS 建議 DAX cluster 至少佈署三個節點並分散於不同的 Availability Zones；單節點 cluster 沒有容錯能力，兩節點低於建議下限，因此選項 A 與 D 不符合 HA 要求。第二，關於寫入延遲，DAX 文件說明透過 DAX 寫入會多一個網路跳轉（extra network hop），比直接寫入 DynamoDB 慢，因此延遲敏感的應用應直接寫入 DynamoDB（write-around 模式），同時仍可透過 DAX 享受微秒級的快取讀取。選項 B（三節點 DAX cluster、讀取走 DAX、寫入直接到 DynamoDB）是唯一同時滿足 HA（3 節點/多 AZ）與最低延遲（write-around 避免額外跳轉）的答案。選項 C 則相反，寫入走 DAX、讀取直接到 DynamoDB，導致最差的讀取延遲（無快取效益）與最慢的寫入。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A two-node DAX cluster is below the AWS-recommended minimum of three nodes for high availability, and writing through DAX adds an extra network hop, increasing write latency on a latency-sensitive platform. It fails both the HA and least-latency requirements.","why_zh":"兩節點 DAX cluster 低於 AWS 建議的高可用性三節點下限，且透過 DAX 寫入會多一個網路跳轉，增加延遲敏感平台的寫入延遲。同時不符合 HA 與最低延遲要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This reads directly from DynamoDB (millisecond latency, no DAX microsecond cache benefit) and writes through DAX (extra hop, slower writes). It produces the worst latency of all options and defeats the purpose of adding a cache.","why_zh":"此選項直接從 DynamoDB 讀取（毫秒級延遲，沒有 DAX 微秒級快取效益），並透過 DAX 寫入（多一跳、寫入更慢）。在所有選項中產生最差的延遲，違背了加入快取的目的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A single-node DAX cluster has no fault tolerance whatsoever, directly violating the high-availability requirement, even though writing directly to DynamoDB is the correct low-latency write strategy.","why_zh":"單節點 DAX cluster 完全沒有容錯能力，直接違反高可用性要求，儘管直接寫入 DynamoDB 是正確的低延遲寫入策略。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/DAX.consistency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/dax-cluster-sizing.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":151,"question_en":"A company has migrated an application from on premises to AWS. The application frontend is a static website that runs on two Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The application backend is a Python application that runs on three EC2 instances behind another ALB. The EC2 instances are large, general purpose On-Demand Instances that were sized to meet the on-premises specifications for peak usage of the application. The application averages hundreds of thousands of requests each month. However, the application is used mainly during lunchtime and receives minimal tra®c during the rest of the day. A solutions architect needs to optimize the infrastructure cost of the application without negatively affecting the application availability. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司已将应用程序从本地迁移到 AWS。应用程序前端是一个静态网站，在应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面的两个 Amazon EC2 实 例上运行。应用程序后端是一个 Python 应用程序，在另一个 ALB 后面的三个 EC2 实例上运行。EC2 实例是大型通用按需实例，其大 小可满足应用程序峰值使用的本地规范。 该应用程序平均每月有数十万个请求。然而，该应用程序主要在午餐时间使用，在一天的其余时间接收的流量很少。 解决方案架构师需要优化应用程序的基础架构成本，而不会对应用程序可用性产生负面影响。 哪种步骤组合可以满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Change all the EC2 instances to compute optimized instances that have the same number of cores as the existing EC2 instances.","B":"Move the application frontend to a static website that is hosted on Amazon S3.","C":"Deploy the application frontend by using AWS Elastic Beanstalk. Use the same instance type for the nodes.","D":"Change all the backend EC2 instances to Spot Instances.","E":"Deploy the backend Python application to general purpose burstable EC2 instances that have the same number of cores as the existing EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"将所有 EC2 实例更改为具有与现有 EC2 实例相同核心数量的计算优化实例。","B":"将应用程序前端移至 Amazon S3 上托管的静态网站。","C":"使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 部署应用程序前端。节点使用相同的实例类型。","D":"将所有后端 EC2 实例更改为 Spot 实例。","E":"将后端 Python 应用程序部署到与现有 EC2 实例具有相同核心数量的通用可突发 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BE":90},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":152,"question_en":"A company is running an event ticketing platform on AWS and wants to optimize the platform's cost-effectiveness. The platform is deployed on Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) with Amazon EC2 and is backed by an Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance. The company is developing new application features to run on Amazon EKS with AWS Fargate. The platform experiences infrequent high peaks in demand. The surges in demand depend on event dates. Which solution will provide the MOST cost-effective setup for the platform?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 上运行一个活动票务平台，并希望优化该平台的成本效益。该平台部署在带有 Amazon EC2 的 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 上，并由 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库实例提供支持。该公司正在开发新的应用程序功能，以便通 过 AWS Fargate 在 Amazon EKS 上运行。 该平台很少出现需求高峰。需求的激增取决于活动日期。 哪种解决方案将为平台提供最具成本效益的设置？","options_en":{"A":"Purchase Standard Reserved Instances for the EC2 instances that the EKS cluster uses in its baseline load. Scale the cluster with Spot Instances to handle peaks. Purchase 1-year All Upfront Reserved Instances for the database to meet predicted peak load for the year.","B":"Purchase Compute Savings Plans for the predicted medium load of the EKS cluster. Scale the cluster with On-Demand Capacity Reservations based on event dates for peaks. Purchase 1-year No Upfront Reserved Instances for the database to meet the predicted base load. Temporarily scale out database read replicas during peaks.","C":"Purchase EC2 Instance Savings Plans for the predicted base load of the EKS cluster. Scale the cluster with Spot Instances to handle peaks. Purchase 1-year All Upfront Reserved Instances for the database to meet the predicted base load. Temporarily scale up the DB instance manually during peaks.","D":"Purchase Compute Savings Plans for the predicted base load of the EKS cluster. Scale the cluster with Spot Instances to handle peaks. Purchase 1-year All Upfront Reserved Instances for the database to meet the predicted base load. Temporarily scale up the DB instance manually during peaks."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 EKS 集群在其基准负载中使用的 EC2 实例购买标准预留实例。使用 Spot 实例扩展集群以应对峰值。为数据库购买 1 年期的 预付预留实例，以满足当年的预测峰值负载。","B":"针对 EKS 集群的预测中等负载购买计算节省计划。根据高峰事件日期，通过按需容量预留来扩展集群。为数据库购买 1 年期 无预付费用预留实例以满足预测的基本负载。在高峰期间临时横向扩展数据库只读副本。","C":"为 EKS 集群的预测基本负载购买 EC2 实例节省计划。使用 Spot 实例扩展集群以应对峰值。为数据库购买 1 年期的预付预留实 例以满足预测的基本负载。在高峰期临时手动扩容实例。","D":"针对 EKS 集群的预测基本负载购买计算节省计划。使用 Spot 实例扩展集群以应对峰值。为数据库购买 1 年期的预付预留实例 以满足预测的基本负载。在高峰期临时手动扩容实例。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":61,"D":32},"tags":["Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Containers"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":153,"question_en":"A company has deployed an application on AWS Elastic Beanstalk. The application uses Amazon Aurora for the database layer. An Amazon CloudFront distribution serves web requests and includes the Elastic Beanstalk domain name as the origin server. The distribution is configured with an alternate domain name that visitors use when they access the application. Each week, the company takes the application out of service for routine maintenance. During the time that the application is unavailable, the company wants visitors to receive an informational message instead of a CloudFront error message. A solutions architect creates an Amazon S3 bucket as the first step in the process. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect take next to meet the requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 上部署了一个应用程序。该应用程序使用 Amazon Aurora 作为数据库层。Amazon CloudFront 分配服 务 Web 请求并包含 Elastic Beanstalk 域名作为源服务器。该分发配置了访问者在访问应用程序时使用的备用域名。 每周，该公司都会停止该应用程序的服务以进行日常维护。在应用程序不可用期间，该公司希望访问者收到信息性消息，而不是 CloudFront 错误消息。 解决方案架构师创建 Amazon S3 存储桶作为该流程的第一步。 解决方案架构师下一步应该采取哪些步骤组合来满足要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Upload static informational content to the S3 bucket.","B":"Create a new CloudFront distribution. Set the S3 bucket as the origin.","C":"Set the S3 bucket as a second origin in the original CloudFront distribution. Configure the distribution and the S3 bucket to use an origin access identity (OAI).","D":"During the weekly maintenance, edit the default cache behavior to use the S3 origin. Revert the change when the maintenance is complete.","E":"During the weekly maintenance, create a cache behavior for the S3 origin on the new distribution. Set the path pattern to \\ Set the precedence to 0. Delete the cache behavior when the maintenance is complete.","F":"During the weekly maintenance, configure Elastic Beanstalk to serve tra®c from the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"将静态信息内容上传到 S3 存储桶。","B":"创建新的 CloudFront 分配。将 S3 存储桶设置为原点。","C":"将 S3 存储桶设置为原始 CloudFront 分配中的第二个源。配置分配和 S3 存储桶以使用源访问身份 (OAI)。","D":"在每周维护期间，编辑默认缓存行为以使用 S3 源。维护完成后恢复更改。","E":"在每周维护期间，为新发行版上的 S3 源创建缓存行为。将路径模式设置为\\ 将优先级设置为0。维护完成后删除缓存行为。","F":"在每周维护期间，配置 Elastic Beanstalk 以服务来自 S3 存储桶的流量。"},"answer":["A","C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ACD":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":154,"question_en":"A company gives users the ability to upload images from a custom application. The upload process invokes an AWS Lambda function that processes and stores the image in an Amazon S3 bucket. The application invokes the Lambda function by using a specific function version ARN. The Lambda function accepts image processing parameters by using environment variables. The company often adjusts the environment variables of the Lambda function to achieve optimal image processing output. The company tests different parameters and publishes a new function version with the updated environment variables after validating results. This update process also requires frequent changes to the custom application to invoke the new function version ARN. These changes cause interruptions for users. A solutions architect needs to simplify this process to minimize disruption to users. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司让用户能够从自定义应用程序上传图像。上传过程调用 AWS Lambda 函数来处理图像并将其存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。 应用程序使用特定函数版本 ARN 调用 Lambda 函数。 Lambda 函数使用环境变量接受图像处理参数。公司经常调整Lambda函数的环境变量以达到最佳的图像处理输出。该公司测试了不 同的参数，并在验证结果后发布了具有更新的环境变量的新函数版本。此更新过程还需要频繁更改自定义应用程序以调用新功能版 本 ARN。这些更改会导致用户中断。 解决方案架构师需要简化此流程，以最大程度地减少对用户的干扰。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Directly modify the environment variables of the published Lambda function version. Use the SLATEST version to test image processing parameters.","B":"Create an Amazon DynamoDB table to store the image processing parameters. Modify the Lambda function to retrieve the image processing parameters from the DynamoDB table.","C":"Directly code the image processing parameters within the Lambda function and remove the environment variables. Publish a new function version when the company updates the parameters.","D":"Create a Lambda function alias. Modify the client application to use the function alias ARN. Reconfigure the Lambda alias to point to new versions of the function when the company finishes testing."},"options_zh":{"A":"直接修改已发布的Lambda函数版本的环境变量。使用SLATEST版本测试图像处理参数。","B":"创建 Amazon DynamoDB 表来存储图像处理参数。修改 Lambda 函数以从 DynamoDB 表中检索图像处理参数。","C":"直接在Lambda函数中编写图像处理参数并删除环境变量。当公司更新参数时发布新的功能版本。","D":"创建 Lambda 函数别名。修改客户端应用程序以使用函数别名 ARN。当公司完成测试时，重新配置 Lambda 别名以指向该函数 的新版本。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":155,"question_en":"A global media company is planning a multi-Region deployment of an application. Amazon DynamoDB global tables will back the deployment to keep the user experience consistent across the two continents where users are concentrated. Each deployment will have a public Application Load Balancer (ALB). The company manages public DNS internally. The company wants to make the application available through an apex domain. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST effort?","question_zh":"一家全球媒体公司正在计划应用程序的多区域部署。Amazon DynamoDB 全局表将支持部署，以在用户集中的两大洲保持用户体验一 致。每个部署都将有一个公共应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB)。该公司内部管理公共 DNS。该公司希望通过顶级域提供该应用程序。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate public DNS to Amazon Route 53. Create CNAME records for the apex domain to point to the ALB. Use a geolocation routing policy to route tra®c based on user location.","B":"Place a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in front of the ALMigrate public DNS to Amazon Route 53. Create a CNAME record for the apex domain to point to the NLB’s static IP address. Use a geolocation routing policy to route tra®c based on user location.","C":"Create an AWS Global Accelerator accelerator with multiple endpoint groups that target endpoints in appropriate AWS Regions. Use the accelerator’s static IP address to create a record in public DNS for the apex domain.","D":"Create an Amazon API Gateway API that is backed by AWS Lambda in one of the AWS Regions. Configure a Lambda function to route tra®c to application deployments by using the round robin method. Create CNAME records for the apex domain to point to the API's URL."},"options_zh":{"A":"将公共 DNS 迁移到 Amazon Route 53。为顶级域创建 CNAME 记录以指向 ALB。使用地理位置路由策略根据用户位置路由流 量。","B":"将网络负载均衡器 (NLB) 放置在 ALMigrate 公共 DNS 到 Amazon Route 53 的前面。为顶点域创建 CNAME 记录以指向 NLB 的静 态 IP 地址。使用地理位置路由策略根据用户位置路由流量。","C":"创建一个具有多个终端节点组的 AWS Global Accelerator 加速器，这些终端节点组以适当的 AWS 区域中的终端节点为目标。使 用加速器的静态 IP 地址在公共 DNS 中为顶级域创建记录。","D":"在 AWS 区域之一创建由 AWS Lambda 支持的 Amazon API Gateway API。配置 Lambda 函数以使用循环方法将流量路由到应用程 序部署。为顶级域创建 CNAME 记录以指向 API 的 URL。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":156,"question_en":"A company is developing a new serverless API by using Amazon API Gateway and AWS Lambda. The company integrated the Lambda functions with API Gateway to use several shared libraries and custom classes. A solutions architect needs to simplify the deployment of the solution and optimize for code reuse. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 Amazon API Gateway 和 AWS Lambda 开发新的无服务器 API。该公司将 Lambda 函数与 API Gateway 集成，以使用 多个共享库和自定义类。 解决方案架构师需要简化解决方案的部署并优化代码重用。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the shared libraries and custom classes into a Docker image. Store the image in an S3 bucket. Create a Lambda layer that uses the Docker image as the source. Deploy the API's Lambda functions as Zip packages. Configure the packages to use the Lambda layer.","B":"Deploy the shared libraries and custom classes to a Docker image. Upload the image to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). Create a Lambda layer that uses the Docker image as the source. Deploy the API's Lambda functions as Zip packages. Configure the packages to use the Lambda layer.","C":"Deploy the shared libraries and custom classes to a Docker container in Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) by using the AWS Fargate launch type. Deploy the API's Lambda functions as Zip packages. Configure the packages to use the deployed container as a Lambda layer.","D":"Deploy the shared libraries, custom classes, and code for the API's Lambda functions to a Docker image. Upload the image to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). Configure the API's Lambda functions to use the Docker image as the deployment package."},"options_zh":{"A":"将共享库和自定义类部署到 Docker 映像中。将图像存储在 S3 存储桶中。创建使用 Docker 映像作为源的 Lambda 层。将 API 的 Lambda 函数部署为 Zip 包。配置包以使用 Lambda 层。","B":"将共享库和自定义类部署到 Docker 映像。将映像上传到 Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR)。创建使用 Docker 映像 作为源的 Lambda 层。将 API 的 Lambda 函数部署为 Zip 包。配置包以使用 Lambda 层。","C":"使用 AWS Fargate 启动类型将共享库和自定义类部署到 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 中的 Docker 容器。将 API 的 Lambda 函数部署为 Zip 包。配置包以使用已部署的容器作为 Lambda 层。","D":"将 API 的 Lambda 函数的共享库、自定义类和代码部署到 Docker 映像。将映像上传到 Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR)。配置 API 的 Lambda 函数以使用 Docker 映像作为部署包。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":69,"B":31},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Per AWS docs, a Lambda layer is fundamentally a .zip file archive containing supplementary code/data; it is created by packaging dependencies into a .zip, not from a Docker image. There is no mechanism to create a layer 'that uses a Docker image as the source,' which makes options A and B technically impossible. Furthermore, layers can only be used with functions deployed as .zip archives; for functions defined as a container image, you must package the runtime and all dependencies into the image itself. Option D is the only technically valid approach: deploy the shared libraries, custom classes, and the Lambda function code into a Docker image, push it to Amazon ECR, and configure the Lambda functions to use that container image as the deployment package. This satisfies both requirements (simplified deployment via a single image and code reuse through shared libraries baked into the image).","explanation_zh":"根據 AWS 文件，Lambda layer 本質上是一個包含補充程式碼/資料的 .zip 檔案封存，它是透過把相依套件打包成 .zip 來建立，而非來自 Docker image。並不存在「以 Docker image 作為來源」建立 layer 的機制，因此選項 A 與 B 在技術上不可行。此外，layer 只能用於以 .zip 封存部署的函式；對於以 container image 定義的函式，必須把 runtime 與所有相依項目打包進 image 本身。選項 D 是唯一技術上成立的方法：將共用程式庫、自訂類別與 Lambda 函式程式碼部署到 Docker image，推送到 Amazon ECR，並設定 Lambda 函式使用該 container image 作為部署封裝。這同時滿足兩項需求（透過單一 image 簡化部署，以及將共用程式庫烘焙進 image 達成程式碼重用）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A Lambda layer is a .zip archive and cannot be created 'using a Docker image as the source.' Also, layers are not stored in/sourced from an S3 bucket Docker image; this is not a supported mechanism.","why_zh":"Lambda layer 是 .zip 封存，無法「以 Docker image 作為來源」建立。layer 也不會從 S3 bucket 中的 Docker image 取得來源，這不是受支援的機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same fatal flaw as A: a Lambda layer cannot use a Docker image (even one in ECR) as its source. Layers are .zip archives only. The dump's suggested answer is wrong because no such layer-from-image capability exists.","why_zh":"與 A 相同的致命缺陷：Lambda layer 無法以 Docker image（即便在 ECR 中）作為來源。layer 僅能是 .zip 封存。題庫的建議答案錯誤，因為不存在這種以 image 建立 layer 的功能。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"You cannot configure an ECS/Fargate container as a Lambda layer. A running container is not a layer source, and layers must be .zip archives attached to .zip-packaged functions.","why_zh":"無法將 ECS/Fargate 容器設定為 Lambda layer。執行中的容器不是 layer 來源，且 layer 必須是附加到以 .zip 封裝函式上的 .zip 封存。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/chapter-layers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/images-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/python-image.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":157,"question_en":"A manufacturing company is building an inspection solution for its factory. The company has IP cameras at the end of each assembly line. The company has used Amazon SageMaker to train a machine learning (ML) model to identify common defects from still images. The company wants to provide local feedback to factory workers when a defect is detected. The company must be able to provide this feedback even if the factory’s internet connectivity is down. The company has a local Linux server that hosts an API that provides local feedback to the workers. How should the company deploy the ML model to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家制造公司正在为其工厂构建检查解决方案。该公司在每条装配线的末端都配备了 IP 摄像头。该公司已使用 Amazon SageMaker 训练机器学习 (ML) 模型，以识别静态图像中的常见缺陷。 该公司希望在检测到缺陷时向工厂工人提供本地反馈。即使工厂的互联网连接中断，公司也必须能够提供此反馈。该公司有一个本 地 Linux 服务器，托管一个 API，为员工提供本地反馈。 公司应该如何部署ML模型来满足这些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up an Amazon Kinesis video stream from each IP camera to AWS. Use Amazon EC2 instances to take still images of the streams. Upload the images to an Amazon S3 bucket. Deploy a SageMaker endpoint with the ML model. Invoke an AWS Lambda function to call the inference endpoint when new images are uploaded. Configure the Lambda function to call the local API when a defect is detected.","B":"Deploy AWS IoT Greengrass on the local server. Deploy the ML model to the Greengrass server. Create a Greengrass component to take still images from the cameras and run inference. Configure the component to call the local API when a defect is detected.","C":"Order an AWS Snowball device. Deploy a SageMaker endpoint the ML model and an Amazon EC2 instance on the Snowball device. Take still images from the cameras. Run inference from the EC2 instance. Configure the instance to call the local API when a defect is detected.","D":"Deploy Amazon Monitron devices on each IP camera. Deploy an Amazon Monitron Gateway on premises. Deploy the ML model to the Amazon Monitron devices. Use Amazon Monitron health state alarms to call the local API from an AWS Lambda function when a defect is detected."},"options_zh":{"A":"设置从每个 IP 摄像机到 AWS 的 Amazon Kinesis 视频流。使用 Amazon EC2 实例拍摄流的静态图像。将图像上传到 Amazon S3 存储桶。使用 ML 模型部署 SageMaker 端点。上传新图像时调用 AWS Lambda 函数来调用推理终端节点。配置 Lambda 函数以在 检测到缺陷时调用本地 API。","B":"在本地服务器上部署 AWS IoT Greengrass。将 ML 模型部署到 Greengrass 服务器。创建一个 Greengrass 组件以从相机获取静态 图像并运行推理。配置组件以在检测到缺陷时调用本地 API。","C":"订购 AWS Snowball 设备。在 Snowball 设备上部署 SageMaker 终端节点、ML 模型和 Amazon EC2 实例。从相机中拍摄静态图 像。从 EC2 实例运行推理。配置实例以在检测到缺陷时调用本地 API。","D":"在每个 IP 摄像机上部署 Amazon Monitron 设备。在本地部署 Amazon Monitron 网关。将 ML 模型部署到 Amazon Monitron 设备。 当检测到缺陷时，使用 Amazon Monitron 运行状况警报从 AWS Lambda 函数调用本地 API。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":93},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive requirement is that the solution must provide local defect feedback even when the factory's internet connectivity is down, using an existing local Linux server. AWS IoT Greengrass is purpose-built for this: it runs on a Linux device, deploys ML models (including SageMaker-trained models) to the edge, runs predictions locally, and reacts autonomously to local events without depending on cloud connectivity. A Greengrass component can capture still images from the IP cameras, run inference locally, and call the local API when a defect is detected, so it keeps working offline. Option D is technically invalid because Amazon Monitron uses fixed vibration/temperature sensors for predictive maintenance and cannot be attached to IP cameras, process images, or host a custom SageMaker computer-vision model. The dump's suggested answer (D) is therefore wrong, and the community answer (B) is correct.","explanation_zh":"決定性需求是：即使工廠網路中斷，解決方案仍須在現場提供瑕疵回饋，並利用既有的本地 Linux 伺服器。AWS IoT Greengrass 正是為此而生：它可在 Linux 裝置上執行、將 ML 模型（含 SageMaker 訓練的模型）部署到邊緣、在本地執行推論，並能在不依賴雲端連線的情況下自主回應本地事件。Greengrass component 可從 IP 攝影機擷取靜態影像、在本地執行推論，並在偵測到瑕疵時呼叫本地 API，因此可離線持續運作。選項 D 在技術上不可行，因為 Amazon Monitron 使用固定式振動／溫度感測器做預測性維護，無法接到 IP 攝影機、無法處理影像，也無法託管自訂的 SageMaker 電腦視覺模型。因此 dump 建議答案 (D) 錯誤，社群答案 (B) 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"This is a fully cloud-based pipeline (Kinesis Video Streams, EC2, S3, SageMaker endpoint, Lambda). It cannot provide feedback when internet connectivity is down because inference happens in the AWS Cloud, violating the core offline requirement.","why_zh":"這是完全雲端的流程（Kinesis Video Streams、EC2、S3、SageMaker endpoint、Lambda）。推論在 AWS 雲端進行，網路中斷時無法提供回饋，違反核心的離線需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Snowball is a temporary data-transfer/edge-compute appliance ordered for limited durations, not a permanent production inference platform for a factory line. It is high cost and high operational overhead, and unnecessary given the company already has a local Linux server suited to Greengrass.","why_zh":"AWS Snowball 是短期租借的資料傳輸／邊緣運算設備，並非工廠產線長期使用的正式推論平台。成本高、營運負擔大，且公司已有適合 Greengrass 的本地 Linux 伺服器，並無必要。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Monitron uses fixed vibration/temperature sensors for predictive maintenance with a managed ML model. It cannot be attached to IP cameras, cannot process still images, and cannot host a custom SageMaker computer-vision model, making this option technically impossible.","why_zh":"Amazon Monitron 使用固定式振動／溫度感測器搭配受管 ML 模型做預測性維護。無法接到 IP 攝影機、無法處理靜態影像，也無法託管自訂 SageMaker 電腦視覺模型，因此此選項技術上不可行。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/greengrass/v2/developerguide/what-is-iot-greengrass.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/greengrass/v2/developerguide/ml-tutorial-image-classification.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Monitron/latest/admin-guide/admin_what-is-monitron.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Monitron/latest/user-guide/gsg-sensors.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":158,"question_en":"A solutions architect must create a business case for migration of a company's on-premises data center to the AWS Cloud. The solutions architect will use a configuration management database (CMDB) export of all the company's servers to create the case. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师必须创建一个将公司的本地数据中心迁移到 AWS 云的业务案例。解决方案架构师将使用公司所有服务器的配置管理 数据库 (CMDB) 导出来创建案例。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Well-Architected Tool to import the CMDB data to perform an analysis and generate recommendations.","B":"Use Migration Evaluator to perform an analysis. Use the data import template to upload the data from the CMDB export.","C":"Implement resource matching rules. Use the CMDB export and the AWS Price List Bulk API to query CMDB data against AWS services in bulk.","D":"Use AWS Application Discovery Service to import the CMDB data to perform an analysis."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Well-Architected Tool 导入 CMDB 数据以执行分析并生成建议。","B":"使用迁移评估器执行分析。使用数据导入模板从 CMDB 导出上传数据。","C":"实施资源匹配规则。使用 CMDB 导出和 AWS Price List Bulk API 根据 AWS 服务批量查询 CMDB 数据。","D":"使用 AWS Application Discovery Service 导入 CMDB 数据以执行分析。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":89},"tags":["Migration","Database","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to create a migration business case from a CMDB export, most cost-effectively. AWS Migration Evaluator is purpose-built for this: AWS Prescriptive Guidance lists it under 'Business case analysis migration tools' and documents that it can import IT asset data from discovery tools 'such as CMDB extract' via a data import template, then produces a Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) business case for AWS planning and migration decisions. It carries no charge, satisfying the MOST cost-effective qualifier. By contrast, AWS Application Discovery Service is categorized as a discovery/planning/recommendation tool that collects server usage and configuration data for migration planning; it does not itself generate a business case (you must export its data into a separate cost model). The Well-Architected Tool reviews workload architecture against best-practice pillars and has no CMDB-import or business-case function, and building a custom resource-matching pipeline against the Price List Bulk API is high-effort and not cost-effective. Therefore Migration Evaluator with the CMDB data import template is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求是以最具成本效益的方式，依據 CMDB 匯出資料建立遷移商業案例。AWS Migration Evaluator 正是為此設計：AWS Prescriptive Guidance 將其列在「Business case analysis migration tools」分類下，並記載它可透過資料匯入範本匯入來自探索工具的 IT 資產資料（例如 CMDB extract），進而產出 TCO 商業案例供 AWS 規劃與遷移決策使用，且此服務免費，符合 MOST cost-effective 的限定條件。相對地，AWS Application Discovery Service 屬於探索／規劃／建議工具，用於收集伺服器使用與設定資料以利遷移規劃，本身並不產生商業案例（需將其匯出的資料再輸入另一個成本模型）。Well-Architected Tool 是依最佳實務支柱檢視工作負載架構，沒有 CMDB 匯入或商業案例功能；而自建以 Price List Bulk API 比對資源的流程則工作量大、不具成本效益。因此正確答案是使用 Migration Evaluator 的 CMDB 資料匯入範本。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Well-Architected Tool reviews workloads against the framework's pillars and generates architectural improvement plans; it cannot import CMDB data or produce a migration TCO business case.","why_zh":"AWS Well-Architected Tool 依框架支柱檢視工作負載並產生架構改進計畫；無法匯入 CMDB 資料，也不會產出遷移 TCO 商業案例。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Building a custom pipeline with resource-matching rules and the AWS Price List Bulk API is high operational effort and not cost-effective; it also lacks rightsizing, utilization, and license TCO modeling that Migration Evaluator provides for free.","why_zh":"以資源比對規則加上 AWS Price List Bulk API 自建流程作業負擔高、不具成本效益，且缺少 Migration Evaluator 免費提供的 rightsizing、使用率與授權 TCO 建模。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Application Discovery Service is a discovery/planning tool that collects on-premises usage and configuration data; it does not itself generate a business case, and you would still need a separate cost model, so it does not meet the requirement most cost-effectively.","why_zh":"AWS Application Discovery Service 是探索／規劃工具，收集地端使用與設定資料；本身不產生商業案例，仍需另一個成本模型，因此無法最具成本效益地滿足需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/migration-tools/business-case-migration-evaluator.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/migration-tools/business-case.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/what-is-appdiscovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/migration-tools/discovery-app-discovery-service.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":159,"question_en":"A company has a website that runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The instances are in an Auto Scaling group. The ALB is associated with an AWS WAF web ACL. The website often encounters attacks in the application layer. The attacks produce sudden and significant increases in tra®c on the application server. The access logs show that each attack originates from different IP addresses. A solutions architect needs to implement a solution to mitigate these attacks. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个在应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行的网站。这些实例位于 Auto Scaling 组中。ALB 与 AWS WAF Web ACL 关联。 网站经常遭遇应用层攻击。这些攻击会导致应用程序服务器上的流量突然显着增加。访问日志显示，每次攻击都源自不同的IP地 址。解决方案架构师需要实施一个解决方案来减轻这些攻击。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that monitors server access. Set a threshold based on access by IP address. Configure an alarm action that adds the IP address to the web ACL’s deny list.","B":"Deploy AWS Shield Advanced in addition to AWS WAF. Add the ALB as a protected resource.","C":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that monitors user IP addresses. Set a threshold based on access by IP address. Configure the alarm to invoke an AWS Lambda function to add a deny rule in the application server’s subnet route table for any IP addresses that activate the alarm.","D":"Inspect access logs to find a pattern of IP addresses that launched the attacks. Use an Amazon Route 53 geolocation routing policy to deny tra®c from the countries that host those IP addresses."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报来监控服务器访问。根据IP地址的访问设置阈值。配置将 IP 地址添加到 Web ACL 拒绝列表 的警报操作。","B":"除了 AWS WAF 之外，还部署 AWS Shield Advanced。将 ALB 添加为受保护资源。","C":"创建监控用户 IP 地址的 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。根据IP地址的访问设置阈值。配置警报以调用 AWS Lambda 函数，以在应用 程序服务器的子网路由表中为激活警报的任何 IP 地址添加拒绝规则。","D":"检查访问日志以查找发起攻击的 IP 地址模式。使用 Amazon Route 53 地理位置路由策略拒绝来自托管这些 IP 地址的国家/地区 的流量。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":89},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The attacks are application-layer (layer 7) HTTP floods that cause sudden traffic spikes and originate from constantly changing IP addresses. Because the source IPs differ each time, any reactive solution that blocks individual IPs after the fact is ineffective and high-effort. AWS Shield Advanced is the AWS-recommended managed solution: when you add the ALB as a protected resource, Shield Advanced provides automatic application layer DDoS mitigation. It establishes a baseline of normal traffic, compares current patterns against that baseline to detect deviations, and automatically creates, evaluates, and deploys custom AWS WAF rules (including rate-based rules) in the existing web ACL to block attack traffic from distributed sources. This is fully managed and works with the WAF web ACL already attached to the ALB, giving the LEAST operational overhead. Option C is technically invalid because subnet route tables route by destination prefix and have no source-IP allow/deny capability, and traffic reaching the EC2 subnet behind an ALB carries the ALB's IP, not the attacker's.","explanation_zh":"此攻擊屬於應用層 (layer 7) 的 HTTP flood，造成流量突然暴增，且每次來自不同的 IP 位址。由於來源 IP 不斷變化，任何事後封鎖個別 IP 的被動式作法都無效且維運負擔高。AWS Shield Advanced 是 AWS 建議的受管解決方案：將 ALB 加入為受保護資源後，Shield Advanced 提供自動的應用層 DDoS 緩解。它會建立正常流量基準，比對目前流量模式以偵測偏差，並在既有的 web ACL 中自動建立、評估並部署自訂的 AWS WAF 規則 (包含 rate-based rules) 來封鎖來自分散來源的攻擊流量。此為全受管，且直接搭配 ALB 上既有的 WAF web ACL，維運負擔最低。選項 C 在技術上不成立，因為子網路的 route table 是依目的地前綴路由、不具來源 IP 的允許/拒絕能力，且經由 ALB 抵達 EC2 子網的流量帶的是 ALB 的 IP 而非攻擊者的 IP。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A CloudWatch-alarm-to-deny-list approach is reactive and high-maintenance, and it cannot keep up with attacks that come from constantly different IP addresses; CloudWatch alarms also cannot directly add IPs to a WAF deny list without custom automation. It does not scale to distributed source IPs.","why_zh":"用 CloudWatch alarm 觸發加入拒絕清單的作法屬被動式且維護成本高，無法應付來源 IP 不斷變化的攻擊；CloudWatch alarm 也無法在沒有自訂自動化的情況下直接把 IP 加入 WAF 拒絕清單，且無法擴展到分散來源 IP。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Technically broken and high overhead. Subnet route tables route by destination prefix and have no source-IP allow/deny semantics, so a Lambda cannot 'add a deny rule' there. Also, behind an ALB the EC2 subnet sees the ALB's IP, not the attacker's source IP, so per-attacker filtering at that layer is impossible.","why_zh":"技術上錯誤且維運負擔高。子網路 route table 依目的地前綴路由，沒有來源 IP 的允許/拒絕語意，Lambda 無法在此「新增拒絕規則」。此外，在 ALB 後方，EC2 子網看到的是 ALB 的 IP 而非攻擊者來源 IP，因此無法在此層級依攻擊者過濾。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Geolocation routing in Route 53 controls DNS responses, not packet/request filtering, and cannot block an attack in progress. Attackers from constantly changing IPs across many countries make country-level blocking both ineffective and likely to block legitimate users. It is a manual, brittle response.","why_zh":"Route 53 的地理位置路由是控制 DNS 回應，並非封包/請求過濾，無法阻擋進行中的攻擊。攻擊者來自不斷變化、橫跨多國的 IP，依國家封鎖既無效又可能誤擋合法使用者，屬手動且脆弱的作法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/what-is-aws-waf.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/ddos-automatic-app-layer-response.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/ddos-app-layer-rbr.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/ddos-overview.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":160,"question_en":"A company has a critical application in which the data tier is deployed in a single AWS Region. The data tier uses an Amazon DynamoDB table and an Amazon Aurora MySQL DB cluster. The current Aurora MySQL engine version supports a global database. The application tier is already deployed in two Regions. Company policy states that critical applications must have application tier components and data tier components deployed across two Regions. The RTO and RPO must be no more than a few minutes each. A solutions architect must recommend a solution to make the data tier compliant with company policy. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司有一个关键应用程序，其中数据层部署在单个 AWS 区域中。数据层使用 Amazon DynamoDB 表和 Amazon Aurora MySQL 数据 库集群。当前的 Aurora MySQL 引擎版本支持全局数据库。应用程序层已部署在两个区域中。 公司政策规定，关键应用程序必须跨两个区域部署应用程序层组件和数据层组件。RTO 和 RPO 各自不得超过几分钟。解决方案架构 师必须推荐一个解决方案，使数据层符合公司政策。 哪种步骤组合可以满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Add another Region to the Aurora MySQL DB cluster","B":"Add another Region to each table in the Aurora MySQL DB cluster","C":"Set up scheduled cross-Region backups for the DynamoDB table and the Aurora MySQL DB cluster","D":"Convert the existing DynamoDB table to a global table by adding another Region to its configuration","E":"Use Amazon Route 53 Application Recovery Controller to automate database backup and recovery to the secondary Region"},"options_zh":{"A":"将另一个区域添加到 Aurora MySQL 数据库集群","B":"将另一个区域添加到 Aurora MySQL 数据库集群中的每个表","C":"为 DynamoDB 表和 Aurora MySQL 数据库集群设置计划的跨区域备份","D":"通过将另一个区域添加到其配置中，将现有 DynamoDB 表转换为全局表","E":"使用 Amazon Route 53 应用程序恢复控制器自动将数据库备份和恢复到辅助区域"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AD":86},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"An Aurora global database operates at the DB cluster level, not the table level. To make the Aurora MySQL data tier span two Regions, you add a secondary AWS Region to the Aurora global database / DB cluster (option A) using the 'Add AWS Region' action, which creates a cross-Region read replica cluster with sub-second replication and managed failover/switchover that meets an RTO/RPO of a few minutes. Option B ('add another Region to each table') is technically invalid because Aurora MySQL is a relational engine and you do not add Regions per table. For DynamoDB, you make the existing table compliant by converting it to a global table, which is done by adding a replica in a second Region (option D); global tables replicate within about a second, satisfying the few-minutes RPO/RTO. Scheduled cross-Region backups (C) yield an RPO equal to the backup interval and a slow restore-based RTO, far exceeding a few minutes. Route 53 Application Recovery Controller (E) manages failover routing and readiness, not database backup/recovery, so it does not satisfy the requirement.","explanation_zh":"Aurora global database 是以 DB cluster (叢集) 為單位運作，而非以資料表為單位。要讓 Aurora MySQL 資料層橫跨兩個 Region，需透過 'Add AWS Region' 動作為 Aurora global database / DB cluster 新增一個次要 Region (選項 A)，這會建立跨 Region 的唯讀複本叢集，具備秒級以下的複寫延遲以及受管的 failover/switchover，可達成數分鐘內的 RTO/RPO。選項 B ('為每個資料表新增 Region') 技術上不成立，因為 Aurora MySQL 是關聯式引擎，無法以資料表為單位新增 Region。對於 DynamoDB，將既有資料表透過在第二個 Region 新增 replica 來轉換為 global table (選項 D)；global tables 約在一秒內完成複寫，符合數分鐘的 RPO/RTO。排程的跨 Region 備份 (C) 的 RPO 等於備份間隔，且還原式 RTO 緩慢，遠超過數分鐘。Route 53 Application Recovery Controller (E) 管理 failover 路由與就緒狀態，並非資料庫備份/還原，不符合需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Aurora MySQL is relational; you do not add a Region 'to each table.' Aurora global databases are configured at the DB cluster level via 'Add AWS Region,' so this phrasing is technically invalid.","why_zh":"Aurora MySQL 是關聯式資料庫，無法以 '每個資料表' 為單位新增 Region。Aurora global database 是以 DB cluster 層級透過 'Add AWS Region' 設定，因此此敘述技術上無效。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Scheduled cross-Region backups produce an RPO equal to the backup interval and a slow restore-based RTO, both far larger than the required few minutes.","why_zh":"排程的跨 Region 備份其 RPO 等於備份間隔、RTO 為緩慢的還原流程，皆遠大於所需的數分鐘。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Route 53 Application Recovery Controller handles failover routing controls and readiness checks, not automated database backup and recovery, so it does not make the data tier multi-Region compliant.","why_zh":"Route 53 Application Recovery Controller 處理 failover 路由控制與就緒檢查，並非自動化資料庫備份與還原，無法使資料層達成多 Region 合規。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database-attaching.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database-disaster-recovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/V2globaltables_HowItWorks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/V2globaltables.tutorial.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・複選"},{"id":161,"question_en":"A telecommunications company is running an application on AWS. The company has set up an AWS Direct Connect connection between the company's on-premises data center and AWS. The company deployed the application on Amazon EC2 instances in multiple Availability Zones behind an internal Application Load Balancer (ALB). The company's clients connect from the on-premises network by using HTTPS. The TLS terminates in the ALB. The company has multiple target groups and uses path-based routing to forward requests based on the URL path. The company is planning to deploy an on-premises firewall appliance with an allow list that is based on IP address. A solutions architect must develop a solution to allow tra®c ­ow to AWS from the on-premises network so that the clients can continue to access the application. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家电信公司正在 AWS 上运行一个应用程序。该公司已在公司的本地数据中心和 AWS 之间建立了 AWS Direct Connect 连接。该公司 将该应用程序部署在内部应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面的多个可用区中的 Amazon EC2 实例上。该公司的客户端使用 HTTPS 从本地 网络进行连接。TLS 在 ALB 中终止。公司有多个目标群体，采用基于路径的路由，根据URL路径转发请求。 该公司计划部署具有基于 IP 地址的允许列表的本地防火墙设备。解决方案架构师必须开发一种解决方案，允许流量从本地网络流向 AWS，以便客户端可以继续访问应用程序。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the existing ALB to use static IP addresses. Assign IP addresses in multiple Availability Zones to the ALB. Add the ALB IP addresses to the firewall appliance.","B":"Create a Network Load Balancer (NLB). Associate the NLB with one static IP addresses in multiple Availability Zones. Create an ALB- type target group for the NLB and add the existing ALAdd the NLB IP addresses to the firewall appliance. Update the clients to connect to the NLB.","C":"Create a Network Load Balancer (NLB). Associate the LNB with one static IP addresses in multiple Availability Zones. Add the existing target groups to the NLB. Update the clients to connect to the NLB. Delete the ALB Add the NLB IP addresses to the firewall appliance.","D":"Create a Gateway Load Balancer (GWLB). Assign static IP addresses to the GWLB in multiple Availability Zones. Create an ALB-type target group for the GWLB and add the existing ALB. Add the GWLB IP addresses to the firewall appliance. Update the clients to connect to the GWLB."},"options_zh":{"A":"将现有 ALB 配置为使用静态 IP 地址。将多个可用区中的 IP 地址分配给 ALB。将 ALB IP 地址添加到防火墙设备。","B":"创建网络负载均衡器 (NLB)。将 NLB 与多个可用区中的一个静态 IP 地址关联。为 NLB 创建 ALB 类型目标组并将现有 AL 添加 NLB IP 地址到防火墙设备。更新客户端以连接到 NLB。","C":"创建网络负载均衡器 (NLB)。将 LNB 与多个可用区中的一个静态 IP 地址关联。将现有目标组添加到 NLB。更新客户端以连接 到 NLB。删除 ALB 将 NLB IP 地址添加到防火墙设备。","D":"创建网关负载均衡器 (GWLB)。为多个可用区中的 GWLB 分配静态 IP 地址。为 GWLB 创建 ALB 类型目标组并添加现有 ALB。将 GWLB IP 地址添加到防火墙设备。更新客户端以连接到 GWLB。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":92},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Application Load Balancers do not support user-assigned static IP addresses (their IPs are managed by AWS and can change), so Option A is technically impossible and is ruled out immediately. The documented solution is to place a Network Load Balancer in front of the ALB: an NLB can be associated with one static (Elastic) IP per Availability Zone and can use an 'alb' target type, registering the existing ALB as its single target. This is exactly the AWS-documented pattern that combines the NLB's static IPs (for the on-premises firewall IP allow-list) with the ALB's layer 7 features (TLS termination, HTTPS, path-based routing across the multiple target groups), all of which must be preserved. Clients connect to the NLB's static IPs and traffic is forwarded to the existing ALB unchanged. Option C is wrong because moving the EC2 target groups directly to the NLB and deleting the ALB destroys layer 7 path-based routing and TLS termination (NLB is layer 4). Option D is wrong because a Gateway Load Balancer operates at layer 3 using GENEVE on port 6081 to insert inline appliances and is not a client-facing application endpoint, and it does not support an ALB target type.","explanation_zh":"Application Load Balancer 不支援使用者指定的靜態 IP 位址（其 IP 由 AWS 管理且可能變動），因此選項 A 在技術上不可行，可立即排除。AWS 官方文件的解決方案是在 ALB 前面放置一個 Network Load Balancer：NLB 可在每個 Availability Zone 關聯一個靜態（Elastic）IP，並可使用 'alb' 類型的 target group，將既有的 ALB 註冊為其唯一目標。這正是文件記載的模式，結合了 NLB 的靜態 IP（供地端防火牆以 IP 建立允許清單）與 ALB 的第 7 層功能（TLS 終止、HTTPS、跨多個 target group 的路徑式路由），這些功能都必須保留。用戶端連線至 NLB 的靜態 IP，流量再原封不動地轉發至既有 ALB。選項 C 錯誤，因為將 EC2 target group 直接移到 NLB 並刪除 ALB 會破壞第 7 層路徑式路由與 TLS 終止（NLB 屬第 4 層）。選項 D 錯誤，因為 Gateway Load Balancer 運作於第 3 層，使用 GENEVE（port 6081）插入內聯設備，並非面向用戶端的應用程式端點，且不支援 ALB target 類型。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Application Load Balancers do not support assigning static IP addresses; their front-end IPs are AWS-managed and can change, so this configuration cannot be created.","why_zh":"Application Load Balancer 不支援指定靜態 IP 位址；其前端 IP 由 AWS 管理且可能變動，因此此設定無法建立。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Adding the existing (ALB) target groups directly to the NLB and deleting the ALB removes layer 7 capabilities; an NLB is layer 4 and cannot do URL path-based routing or TLS termination, violating the requirement to keep path-based routing.","why_zh":"將既有（ALB）target group 直接加到 NLB 並刪除 ALB 會移除第 7 層功能；NLB 為第 4 層，無法進行 URL 路徑式路由或 TLS 終止，違反保留路徑式路由的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A Gateway Load Balancer is for inserting transparent inline layer 3 network/security appliances using the GENEVE protocol (port 6081); it is not a client-facing application endpoint and does not support an ALB target type, so clients cannot connect to it for HTTPS application traffic.","why_zh":"Gateway Load Balancer 用於以 GENEVE 通訊協定（port 6081）插入透明的內聯第 3 層網路／安全設備；它不是面向用戶端的應用程式端點，也不支援 ALB target 類型，因此用戶端無法用它連線進行 HTTPS 應用流量。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/network/application-load-balancer-target.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/network/network-load-balancers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-ip-address-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/gateway/introduction.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":162,"question_en":"A company runs an application on a ­eet of Amazon EC2 instances that are in private subnets behind an internet-facing Application Load Balancer (ALB). The ALB is the origin for an Amazon CloudFront distribution. An AWS WAF web ACL that contains various AWS managed rules is associated with the CloudFront distribution. The company needs a solution that will prevent internet tra®c from directly accessing the ALB. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司在一组 Amazon EC2 实例上运行应用程序，这些实例位于面向互联网的应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面的私有子网中。ALB 是 Amazon CloudFront 发行版的起源。包含各种 AWS 托管规则的 AWS WAF Web ACL 与 CloudFront 分配关联。 该公司需要一种解决方案来阻止互联网流量直接访问 ALB。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new web ACL that contains the same rules that the existing web ACL contains. Associate the new web ACL with the ALB.","B":"Associate the existing web ACL with the ALB.","C":"Add a security group rule to the ALB to allow tra®c from the AWS managed prefix list for CloudFront only.","D":"Add a security group rule to the ALB to allow only the various CloudFront IP address ranges."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的 Web ACL，其中包含与现有 Web ACL 相同的规则。将新的 Web ACL 与 ALB 关联。","B":"将现有 Web ACL 与 ALB 关联。","C":"将安全组规则添加到 ALB，以仅允许来自 CloudFront 的 AWS 托管前缀列表的流量。","D":"向 ALB 添加安全组规则，以仅允许各种 CloudFront IP 地址范围。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"AWS publishes the CloudFront AWS-managed prefix list (com.amazonaws.global.cloudfront.origin-facing) which contains the IP address ranges of all CloudFront origin-facing servers. By adding a single security group inbound rule on the ALB that allows traffic only from this managed prefix list (and removing other inbound rules), only CloudFront can reach the ALB, preventing direct internet access. CloudFront maintains this list automatically so it always stays current, giving the LEAST operational overhead. Option D (manually entering CloudFront IP ranges) is technically possible but requires you to track and update the ranges from ip-ranges.json continuously, and security groups cannot even hold the dozens of CloudFront CIDRs within default rule limits without using the prefix list. The qualifier 'LEAST operational overhead' decisively favors C over D because the managed prefix list eliminates ongoing maintenance.","explanation_zh":"AWS 提供 CloudFront 的 AWS-managed prefix list (com.amazonaws.global.cloudfront.origin-facing)，其中包含所有 CloudFront origin-facing 伺服器的 IP 位址範圍。在 ALB 的 security group 加上一條 inbound 規則，僅允許來自此 managed prefix list 的流量（並移除其他 inbound 規則），就只有 CloudFront 能存取 ALB，阻止直接的網際網路存取。CloudFront 會自動維護此清單，使其永遠保持最新，因此營運負擔最低。選項 D（手動輸入 CloudFront IP 範圍）技術上可行，但你必須持續從 ip-ranges.json 追蹤並更新範圍，而且 security group 在預設規則上限下甚至無法容納數十個 CloudFront CIDR（除非使用 prefix list）。題目限定詞 'LEAST operational overhead' 決定性地讓 C 優於 D，因為 managed prefix list 免除了持續維護。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS WAF web ACLs do not block traffic from bypassing the ALB at the network layer; an attacker hitting the public ALB DNS directly is still reaching the ALB. WAF filters request content but does not restrict the source so that only CloudFront can connect. Duplicating the web ACL on the ALB also adds management overhead and does not meet the requirement of preventing direct ALB access.","why_zh":"AWS WAF web ACL 無法在網路層阻止流量繞過 ALB；攻擊者直接打公開的 ALB DNS 仍能到達 ALB。WAF 只過濾請求內容，並不會限制來源使其僅允許 CloudFront 連線。在 ALB 上複製 web ACL 還增加管理負擔，且無法達成阻止直接存取 ALB 的需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same flaw as A: associating a WAF web ACL with the ALB inspects/filters requests but does not stop clients from connecting directly to the internet-facing ALB. It does not enforce that traffic originate from CloudFront, so direct internet access to the ALB is still possible.","why_zh":"與 A 相同的缺陷：將 WAF web ACL 關聯到 ALB 只是檢查／過濾請求，並不能阻止用戶端直接連線到面向網際網路的 ALB。它無法強制流量必須來自 CloudFront，因此仍可能直接從網際網路存取 ALB。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Technically restricts access to CloudFront IPs, but manually entering and continually updating the many CloudFront IP CIDR ranges from ip-ranges.json is high operational overhead and error-prone, and risks hitting security group rule quotas. The AWS-managed prefix list in option C achieves the same isolation with no manual maintenance, so D loses on the 'LEAST operational overhead' qualifier.","why_zh":"技術上能限制存取至 CloudFront IP，但從 ip-ranges.json 手動輸入並持續更新眾多 CloudFront IP CIDR 範圍營運負擔高、容易出錯，且可能觸及 security group 規則配額上限。選項 C 的 AWS-managed prefix list 在無需手動維護的情況下達成相同隔離，因此 D 在『LEAST operational overhead』限定詞上落敗。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/LocationsOfEdgeServers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/restrict-access-to-load-balancer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/working-with-aws-managed-prefix-lists.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":163,"question_en":"A company is running an application that uses an Amazon ElastiCache for Redis cluster as a caching layer. A recent security audit revealed that the company has configured encryption at rest for ElastiCache. However, the company did not configure ElastiCache to use encryption in transit. Additionally, users can access the cache without authentication. A solutions architect must make changes to require user authentication and to ensure that the company is using end-to-end encryption. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在运行一个使用 Amazon ElastiCache for Redis 集群作为缓存层的应用程序。最近的安全审计显示，该公司已为 ElastiCache 配置静态加密。但是，该公司并未将 ElastiCache 配置为使用传输中加密。此外，用户无需身份验证即可访问缓存。 解决方案架构师必须进行更改以要求用户身份验证并确保公司使用端到端加密。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AUTH token. Store the token in AWS System Manager Parameter Store, as an encrypted parameter. Create a new cluster with AUTH, and configure encryption in transit. Update the application to retrieve the AUTH token from Parameter Store when necessary and to use the AUTH token for authentication.","B":"Create an AUTH token. Store the token in AWS Secrets Manager. Configure the existing cluster to use the AUTH token, and configure encryption in transit. Update the application to retrieve the AUTH token from Secrets Manager when necessary and to use the AUTH token for authentication.","C":"Create an SSL certificate. Store the certificate in AWS Secrets Manager. Create a new cluster, and configure encryption in transit. Update the application to retrieve the SSL certificate from Secrets Manager when necessary and to use the certificate for authentication.","D":"Create an SSL certificate. Store the certificate in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store, as an encrypted advanced parameter. Update the existing cluster to configure encryption in transit. Update the application to retrieve the SSL certificate from Parameter Store when necessary and to use the certificate for authentication."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 AUTH 令牌。将令牌作为加密参数存储在 AWS System Manager Parameter Store 中。使用 AUTH 创建新集群，并配置传输加 密。更新应用程序以在必要时从 Parameter Store 检索 AUTH 令牌并使用 AUTH 令牌进行身份验证。","B":"创建 AUTH 令牌。将令牌存储在 AWS Secrets Manager 中。配置现有集群以使用 AUTH 令牌，并配置传输加密。更新应用程序以 在必要时从 Secrets Manager 检索 AUTH 令牌并使用 AUTH 令牌进行身份验证。","C":"创建 SSL 证书。将证书存储在 AWS Secrets Manager 中。创建一个新集群，并配置传输加密。更新应用程序以在必要时从 Secrets Manager 检索 SSL 证书并使用该证书进行身份验证。","D":"创建 SSL 证书。将证书作为加密的高级参数存储在 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store 中。更新现有集群以配置传输中加 密。更新应用程序以在必要时从 Parameter Store 检索 SSL 证书并使用该证书进行身份验证。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":93},"tags":["Security/IAM","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"ElastiCache for Redis performs user authentication with the Redis AUTH command (an AUTH token/password) or RBAC, while SSL/TLS certificates provide encryption in transit, not authentication. Therefore any option that proposes using an 'SSL certificate for authentication' (C and D) is technically wrong. AWS docs require encryption in transit (TLS) to be enabled before AUTH can be used, and they explicitly document 'Enabling authentication on an existing cluster' via ModifyReplicationGroup with the ROTATE then SET auth-token-update-strategy, so no new cluster is needed. Between A and B (both use an AUTH token), B is correct because it modifies the existing cluster (fewer changes, no unnecessary re-creation) and stores the token in AWS Secrets Manager, the purpose-built credential store that ElastiCache integrates with and supports rotation. The application retrieves the AUTH token from Secrets Manager and authenticates, achieving user authentication plus end-to-end encryption (encryption at rest already enabled, plus TLS in transit).","explanation_zh":"ElastiCache for Redis 的使用者驗證是透過 Redis AUTH 指令（AUTH token/密碼）或 RBAC 達成，而 SSL/TLS 憑證提供的是傳輸中加密，並非驗證機制。因此任何主張「使用 SSL 憑證進行驗證」的選項（C 與 D）在技術上都是錯誤的。AWS 文件指出必須先啟用傳輸中加密（TLS）才能使用 AUTH，且明確記載可在現有叢集上啟用驗證（透過 ModifyReplicationGroup 搭配 ROTATE 再 SET 的 auth-token-update-strategy），因此不需要建立新叢集。在同樣使用 AUTH token 的 A 與 B 之間，B 正確，因為它修改現有叢集（變更較少、不需重建），並將 token 存放在 AWS Secrets Manager 這個專為憑證設計、與 ElastiCache 整合且支援輪替的服務。應用程式從 Secrets Manager 取得 AUTH token 進行驗證，即可同時達成使用者驗證與端對端加密（靜態加密已啟用，加上傳輸中 TLS）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Technically functional (AUTH token + TLS) but it needlessly creates a NEW cluster when ElastiCache supports enabling both encryption in transit and AUTH on the existing cluster (ModifyReplicationGroup ROTATE/SET). It also stores the token in Parameter Store rather than the purpose-built Secrets Manager. More operational overhead and migration risk than B.","why_zh":"技術上可行（AUTH token + TLS），但在 ElastiCache 已支援於現有叢集啟用傳輸中加密與 AUTH（ModifyReplicationGroup ROTATE/SET）的情況下，卻不必要地建立新叢集；且將 token 存於 Parameter Store 而非專用的 Secrets Manager。相較 B 有更高的維運負擔與遷移風險。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Fundamentally wrong: an SSL certificate provides TLS encryption in transit, not user authentication, in ElastiCache for Redis. You cannot 'use the certificate for authentication' to require users to authenticate. It also unnecessarily creates a new cluster.","why_zh":"根本性錯誤：在 ElastiCache for Redis 中，SSL 憑證提供的是傳輸中 TLS 加密，並非使用者驗證；無法「用憑證進行驗證」來要求使用者驗證。且又不必要地建立新叢集。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same fundamental flaw as C: an SSL certificate is not an authentication mechanism in ElastiCache for Redis, so retrieving and 'using the certificate for authentication' does not satisfy the user-authentication requirement. Storage location (Parameter Store advanced parameter) does not fix the conceptual error.","why_zh":"與 C 相同的根本缺陷：SSL 憑證在 ElastiCache for Redis 中並非驗證機制，因此取得並「用憑證進行驗證」無法滿足使用者驗證需求。存放位置（Parameter Store 進階參數）並無法修正此概念性錯誤。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonElastiCache/latest/dg/auth.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonElastiCache/latest/dg/in-transit-encryption-enable.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonElastiCache/latest/dg/in-transit-encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/integrating_ELC.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonElastiCache/latest/dg/encryption.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":164,"question_en":"A company is running a compute workload by using Amazon EC2 Spot Instances that are in an Auto Scaling group. The launch template uses two placement groups and a single instance type. Recently, a monitoring system reported Auto Scaling instance launch failures that correlated with longer wait times for system users. The company needs to improve the overall reliability of the workload. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 Auto Scaling 组中的 Amazon EC2 Spot 实例运行计算工作负载。启动模板使用两个置放群组和单个实例类型。 最近，监控系统报告 Auto Scaling 实例启动失败，这与系统用户等待时间较长有关。公司需要提高工作负载的整体可靠性。 哪种解决方案可以满足这个要求？","options_en":{"A":"Replace the launch template with a launch configuration to use an Auto Scaling group that uses attribute-based instance type selection.","B":"Create a new launch template version that uses attribute-based instance type selection. Configure the Auto Scaling group to use the new launch template version.","C":"Update the launch template Auto Scaling group to increase the number of placement groups.","D":"Update the launch template to use a larger instance type."},"options_zh":{"A":"将启动模板替换为启动配置，以使用使用基于属性的实例类型选择的 Auto Scaling 组。","B":"创建使用基于属性的实例类型选择的新启动模板版本。配置 Auto Scaling 组以使用新的启动模板版本。","C":"更新启动模板 Auto Scaling 组以增加置放群组的数量。","D":"更新启动模板以使用更大的实例类型。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The launch failures stem from using a single instance type for Spot Instances, which draws from only one or two Spot capacity pools; when those pools run out of capacity, Auto Scaling reports launch failures (e.g., 'There is no Spot capacity available' / insufficient capacity). The AWS-recommended fix is instance type flexibility. Attribute-based instance type selection lets Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling choose from a wide range of matching instance types, which AWS explicitly states 'meets the Spot best practice of being flexible about instance types, which gives the Amazon EC2 Spot service a better chance of finding and allocating your required amount of compute capacity,' directly improving reliability. Attribute-based instance type selection is a launch template + mixed instances policy feature, so creating a new launch template version and pointing the Auto Scaling group at it (Option B) is the correct, supported approach.","explanation_zh":"launch failures 的根本原因是 Spot Instances 只使用單一 instance type，僅能從一兩個 Spot capacity pool 取得容量；當這些 pool 容量不足時，Auto Scaling 就會回報 launch failures（例如 'There is no Spot capacity available' 或容量不足）。AWS 建議的解法是 instance type 的彈性化。Attribute-based instance type selection 讓 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 能從大量符合條件的 instance types 中挑選，AWS 文件明確指出這符合 Spot 的最佳實務，能讓 EC2 Spot 服務更有機會找到並配置所需的運算容量，直接提升可靠度。Attribute-based instance type selection 屬於 launch template 搭配 mixed instances policy 的功能，因此建立新的 launch template version 並讓 Auto Scaling group 改用它（選項 B）才是正確且受支援的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Launch configurations do NOT support attribute-based instance type selection; that feature requires a launch template with a mixed instances policy. AWS also no longer supports creating new launch configurations, so replacing a launch template with one is a regression and technically invalid.","why_zh":"Launch configuration 不支援 attribute-based instance type selection，該功能需要 launch template 搭配 mixed instances policy。AWS 也不再支援建立新的 launch configuration，因此將 launch template 換成 launch configuration 是倒退且技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it is wrong. Increasing the number of placement groups does not address Spot capacity availability for a single instance type. Placement groups (especially cluster) constrain placement and can make capacity harder to obtain, not easier; the failures are capacity/diversity related, not placement-count related.","why_zh":"這是 dump 的建議答案但其實是錯的。增加 placement group 數量無法解決單一 instance type 的 Spot 容量可用性問題。Placement group（尤其是 cluster）會限制配置方式，反而可能更難取得容量，而非更容易；這些失敗與容量/多樣性有關，與 placement group 數量無關。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Using a larger single instance type still relies on one Spot pool. A larger or more specialized instance type often has even less Spot capacity, which would not improve and could worsen launch reliability. It does not add the instance type diversity that Spot best practices require.","why_zh":"改用更大的單一 instance type 仍然只依賴一個 Spot pool。較大或較專門的 instance type 往往 Spot 容量更少，不僅無法改善，反而可能惡化 launch 可靠度。它並未提供 Spot 最佳實務所需的 instance type 多樣性。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/create-mixed-instances-group-attribute-based-instance-type-selection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/allocation-strategies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ts-as-instancelaunchfailure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/create-launch-template.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":165,"question_en":"A company is migrating a document processing workload to AWS. The company has updated many applications to natively use the Amazon S3 API to store, retrieve, and modify documents that a processing server generates at a rate of approximately 5 documents every second. After the document processing is finished, customers can download the documents directly from Amazon S3. During the migration, the company discovered that it could not immediately update the processing server that generates many documents to support the S3 API. The server runs on Linux and requires fast local access to the files that the server generates and modifies. When the server finishes processing, the files must be available to the public for download within 30 minutes. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST amount of effort?","question_zh":"一家公司正在将文档处理工作负载迁移到 AWS。该公司已经更新了许多应用程序，以本地使用 Amazon S3 API 来存储、检索和修改 处理服务器以大约每秒 5 个文档的速度生成的文档。文档处理完成后，客户可以直接从Amazon S3下载文档。 在迁移过程中，该公司发现无法立即更新生成许多文档以支持 S3 API 的处理服务器。服务器在 Linux 上运行，需要快速本地访问服 务器生成和修改的文件。服务器完成处理后，文件必须在 30 分钟内可供公众下载。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate the application to an AWS Lambda function. Use the AWS SDK for Java to generate, modify, and access the files that the company stores directly in Amazon S3.","B":"Set up an Amazon S3 File Gateway and configure a file share that is linked to the document store. Mount the file share on an Amazon EC2 instance by using NFS. When changes occur in Amazon S3, initiate a RefreshCache API call to update the S3 File Gateway.","C":"Configure Amazon FSx for Lustre with an import and export policy. Link the new file system to an S3 bucket. Install the Lustre client and mount the document store to an Amazon EC2 instance by using NFS.","D":"Configure AWS DataSync to connect to an Amazon EC2 instance. Configure a task to synchronize the generated files to and from Amazon S3."},"options_zh":{"A":"将应用程序迁移到 AWS Lambda 函数。使用适用于 Java 的 AWS 开发工具包生成、修改和访问公司直接存储在 Amazon S3 中的 文件。","B":"设置 Amazon S3 文件网关并配置链接到文档存储的文件共享。使用 NFS 将文件共享挂载到 Amazon EC2 实例上。当 Amazon S3 中发生更改时，启动 RefreshCache API 调用以更新 S3 文件网关。","C":"使用导入和导出策略配置 Amazon FSx for Lustre。将新文件系统链接到 S3 存储桶。安装 Lustre 客户端并使用 NFS 将文档存储 挂载到 Amazon EC2 实例。","D":"配置 AWS DataSync 以连接到 Amazon EC2 实例。配置任务以将生成的文件同步到 Amazon S3 或从 Amazon S3 同步。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":67,"C":29},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The legacy Linux processing server cannot be changed to use the S3 API yet but needs fast local file access and the generated files must reach S3 for public download within 30 minutes. Amazon S3 File Gateway is the purpose-built, lowest-effort pattern for this: it exposes an S3 bucket through a standard NFS (or SMB) mount, so the unchanged application keeps reading/writing files locally with low-latency cached access, while the gateway asynchronously uploads written files to S3 where customers download them. This satisfies fast local access, zero application changes, and timely availability in S3. The RefreshCache detail in option B is technically misapplied (RefreshCache only updates the gateway's cached inventory to reflect objects added/removed/replaced DIRECTLY in S3 outside the gateway - it does not upload files written through the gateway, which the gateway does automatically), but the overall architecture is the correct and least-effort fit, so B is still the best answer. Option C (FSx for Lustre) is wrong on the protocol - Lustre is mounted with the Lustre client, not NFS - and is a far heavier, more expensive HPC file system requiring export configuration, i.e. more effort.","explanation_zh":"舊有的 Linux 處理伺服器暫時無法改用 S3 API，但需要快速的本機檔案存取，且產生的檔案必須在 30 分鐘內進入 S3 供公開下載。Amazon S3 File Gateway 正是為此情境設計、最省力的方案：它透過標準 NFS（或 SMB）掛載點將 S3 儲存貯體呈現為檔案系統，未經修改的應用程式可繼續以低延遲的本機快取存取讀寫檔案，而 Gateway 會非同步地將寫入的檔案上傳至 S3，客戶即可從 S3 下載。這同時滿足快速本機存取、零應用程式變更與及時於 S3 可用三項需求。選項 B 中的 RefreshCache 敘述在技術上用錯了（RefreshCache 只會更新 Gateway 快取的物件清單，以反映「直接在 S3 中」被新增/移除/替換的物件，並不會上傳透過 Gateway 寫入的檔案；後者 Gateway 會自動完成），但整體架構仍是正確且最省力的選擇，因此 B 仍是最佳答案。選項 C（FSx for Lustre）在協定上就錯了 - Lustre 是用 Lustre client 掛載而非 NFS - 且它是更重、更昂貴且需設定匯出的 HPC 檔案系統，工作量更大。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The scenario explicitly states the processing server could NOT be updated to support the S3 API, so rewriting it as a Lambda function using the S3 SDK is impossible and the highest effort, and Lambda cannot provide the required fast local file access for a continuous file-modifying server.","why_zh":"題目明確指出處理伺服器無法被改寫成使用 S3 API，因此把它重寫為使用 S3 SDK 的 Lambda 函式既不可行又工作量最大，且 Lambda 無法為持續修改檔案的伺服器提供所需的快速本機檔案存取。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"FSx for Lustre is mounted with the Lustre client, not NFS, so the stated 'mount by using NFS' is technically wrong. It is also a heavyweight, costlier HPC file system that requires export configuration/tasks to push data to S3, making it more effort than an S3 File Gateway for a simple ~5 docs/sec workload.","why_zh":"FSx for Lustre 是用 Lustre client 掛載而非 NFS，因此題目所述「以 NFS 掛載」在技術上是錯的。它也是較重、較貴的 HPC 檔案系統，需要設定匯出政策/任務才能將資料推送至 S3，對於僅約每秒 5 份文件的簡單工作負載而言，比 S3 File Gateway 更費工。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"DataSync runs scheduled/periodic synchronization tasks rather than presenting a live file-system interface to the server; it does not give the legacy server a transparent local mount backed by S3, adds task-scheduling and orchestration overhead, and is a poorer fit for continuous, near-real-time availability.","why_zh":"DataSync 執行的是排程/週期性的同步任務，而非為伺服器提供即時的檔案系統介面；它無法讓舊有伺服器透明地以 S3 為後端進行本機掛載，還增加了任務排程與協調的負擔，對於持續、近即時可用性的需求較不適合。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/filegateway/latest/files3/what-is-file-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/filegateway/latest/files3/GettingStartedAccessFileShare.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/filegateway/latest/files3/refresh-cache.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/LustreGuide/fsx-data-repositories.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/LustreGuide/export-changed-data-meta-dra.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":166,"question_en":"A delivery company is running a serverless solution in the AWS Cloud. The solution manages user data, delivery information, and past purchase details. The solution consists of several microservices. The central user service stores sensitive data in an Amazon DynamoDB table. Several of the other microservices store a copy of parts of the sensitive data in different storage services. The company needs the ability to delete user information upon request. As soon as the central user service deletes a user, every other microservice must also delete its copy of the data immediately. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家送货公司正在 AWS 云中运行无服务器解决方案。该解决方案管理用户数据、送货信息和过去的购买详细信息。该解决方案由多 个微服务组成。中央用户服务将敏感数据存储在 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。其他几个微服务将部分敏感数据的副本存储在不同的存储 服务中。 公司需要能够根据请求删除用户信息。一旦中央用户服务删除用户，其他所有微服务也必须立即删除其数据副本。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Activate DynamoDB Streams on the DynamoDB table. Create an AWS Lambda trigger for the DynamoDB stream that will post events about user deletion in an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Configure each microservice to poll the queue and delete the user from the DynamoDB table.","B":"Set up DynamoDB event notifications on the DynamoDB table. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic as a target for the DynamoDB event notification. Configure each microservice to subscribe to the SNS topic and to delete the user from the DynamoDB table.","C":"Configure the central user service to post an event on a custom Amazon EventBridge event bus when the company deletes a user. Create an EventBridge rule for each microservice to match the user deletion event pattern and invoke logic in the microservice to delete the user from the DynamoDB table.","D":"Configure the central user service to post a message on an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue when the company deletes a user. Configure each microservice to create an event filter on the SQS queue and to delete the user from the DynamoDB table."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 DynamoDB 表上激活 DynamoDB Streams。为 DynamoDB 流创建一个 AWS Lambda 触发器，该触发器将在 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列中发布有关用户删除的事件。配置每个微服务以轮询队列并从 DynamoDB 表中删除用户。","B":"在 DynamoDB 表上设置 DynamoDB 事件通知。创建 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 主题作为 DynamoDB 事件通 知的目标。配置每个微服务以订阅 SNS 主题并从 DynamoDB 表中删除用户。","C":"配置中央用户服务，以便在公司删除用户时在自定义 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线上发布事件。为每个微服务创建一个 EventBridge 规则，以匹配用户删除事件模式，并调用微服务中的逻辑以从 DynamoDB 表中删除用户。","D":"配置中央用户服务，以便在公司删除用户时在 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列上发布消息。配置每个微服务以 在 SQS 队列上创建事件筛选器并从 DynamoDB 表中删除用户。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":67,"A":28},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is a fan-out: when the central user service deletes a user, every other microservice must immediately delete its own copy. Amazon EventBridge with a custom event bus is the canonical AWS pattern for this. The central service posts a user-deletion event; each microservice creates its own EventBridge rule that matches the deletion event pattern and invokes its own delete logic against whatever storage it uses. Per the AWS SQS/SNS/EventBridge decision guide, EventBridge is event-driven (rules match events and route to multiple targets) and is recommended for event-driven, decoupled microservice architectures, while a single SQS queue is pull-based and 'can't decide consumer based on message' (competing-consumers: each message goes to only ONE poller). That makes A and D unworkable for fan-out. The other options also contain technical errors: each of A, B, and D ends with each microservice deleting the user 'from the DynamoDB table', but only the central user service owns the DynamoDB table; the other microservices store copies in different storage services. B invents a nonexistent 'DynamoDB event notifications' feature. Therefore C is the only correct solution.","explanation_zh":"需求是 fan-out：當中央 user service 刪除使用者時，其他每個 microservice 都必須立即刪除自己那份副本。Amazon EventBridge 搭配 custom event bus 正是 AWS 對此情境的標準做法。中央服務發佈一個使用者刪除事件；每個 microservice 各自建立一條 EventBridge rule，比對該刪除事件的 event pattern，並觸發自己的刪除邏輯去清除其各自儲存服務中的資料。根據 AWS 的 SQS/SNS/EventBridge decision guide，EventBridge 是事件驅動（rules 比對事件並路由到多個 targets），適合事件驅動、解耦的 microservice 架構；而單一 SQS queue 是 pull-based，且『無法依訊息決定消費者』（competing-consumers：每則訊息只會被一個 poller 取得），因此 A 與 D 無法達成 fan-out。其他選項還有技術錯誤：A、B、D 最後都讓每個 microservice 去『從 DynamoDB table 刪除使用者』，但 DynamoDB table 只屬於中央 user service，其他 microservice 的副本存在不同的儲存服務。B 還杜撰了不存在的『DynamoDB event notifications』功能。因此 C 是唯一正確的解法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A single SQS standard queue is a competing-consumers (point-to-point) model: each message is received by only ONE poller, so multiple microservices polling the same queue would NOT each get a copy of the deletion event. It also wrongly has each microservice delete from 'the DynamoDB table', which only the central service owns.","why_zh":"單一 SQS standard queue 是 competing-consumers（點對點）模型：每則訊息只會被一個 poller 取得，多個 microservice 輪詢同一 queue 不會各自拿到一份刪除事件。且它錯誤地要求各 microservice 從『DynamoDB table』刪除，但該 table 只屬於中央服務。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"DynamoDB has no feature called 'DynamoDB event notifications' (it has DynamoDB Streams / Kinesis / EventBridge integration, not S3-style event notifications). The option is built on a nonexistent feature, and again wrongly has every microservice delete from the central DynamoDB table.","why_zh":"DynamoDB 並沒有名為『DynamoDB event notifications』的功能（它有 DynamoDB Streams／Kinesis／EventBridge 整合，而非 S3 那種 event notifications）。此選項建立在不存在的功能上，且同樣錯誤地讓每個 microservice 去刪除中央 DynamoDB table。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"There is no such thing as creating an 'event filter on an SQS queue' to fan out to multiple subscribers; SQS is pull-based and cannot decide the consumer based on message content, so a single queue cannot deliver a copy to every microservice. It also wrongly has each microservice delete from 'the DynamoDB table'. (This is the dump's suggested answer, which is wrong.)","why_zh":"並不存在在 SQS queue 上建立『event filter』來向多個訂閱者 fan-out 的做法；SQS 是 pull-based 且無法依訊息內容決定消費者，單一 queue 無法把副本送到每個 microservice。它也錯誤地讓各 microservice 從『DynamoDB table』刪除。（這是 dump 的建議答案，但它是錯的。）"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/decision-guides/latest/sns-or-sqs-or-eventbridge/sns-or-sqs-or-eventbridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/modernization-integrating-microservices/eventbridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-what-is-how-it-works-concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-event-patterns.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":167,"question_en":"A company is running a web application in a VPC. The web application runs on a group of Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The ALB is using AWS WAF. An external customer needs to connect to the web application. The company must provide IP addresses to all external customers. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 VPC 中运行 Web 应用程序。Web 应用程序在应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面的一组 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。ALB 使 用 AWS WAF。 外部客户需要连接到 Web 应用程序。公司必须向所有外部客户提供 IP 地址。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Replace the ALB with a Network Load Balancer (NLB). Assign an Elastic IP address to the NLB.","B":"Allocate an Elastic IP address. Assign the Elastic IP address to the ALProvide the Elastic IP address to the customer.","C":"Create an AWS Global Accelerator standard accelerator. Specify the ALB as the accelerator's endpoint. Provide the accelerator's IP addresses to the customer.","D":"Configure an Amazon CloudFront distribution. Set the ALB as the origin. Ping the distribution's DNS name to determine the distribution's public IP address. Provide the IP address to the customer."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 ALB 替换为网络负载均衡器 (NLB)。为 NLB 分配弹性 IP 地址。","B":"分配弹性IP地址。将弹性 IP 地址分配给 AL向客户提供弹性 IP 地址。","C":"创建 AWS Global Accelerator 标准加速器。将 ALB 指定为加速器的端点。向客户提供加速器的 IP 地址。","D":"配置 Amazon CloudFront 分配。将 ALB 设置为原点。对分配的 DNS 名称执行 Ping 操作以确定分配的公共 IP 地址。向客户提供 IP 地址。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":92},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to provide static IP addresses to external customers while keeping the existing ALB (with AWS WAF) and minimizing operational overhead. AWS Global Accelerator, by default, provides two static anycast IPv4 addresses that you associate with the accelerator, and a standard accelerator explicitly supports an Application Load Balancer as an endpoint. The ALB keeps its WAF association, and the customer is given the accelerator's static IPs. This is a managed, low-overhead solution. Option B is technically impossible: an Application Load Balancer cannot have an Elastic IP assigned to it; ALBs only expose a DNS name backed by ELB-managed IPs that can change. Therefore C is correct and B (the dump's suggested answer) is wrong.","explanation_zh":"需求是要提供靜態 IP 給外部客戶，同時保留現有的 ALB（含 AWS WAF）並將維運負擔降到最低。AWS Global Accelerator 預設會提供兩個靜態 anycast IPv4 位址供你關聯到 accelerator，且 standard accelerator 明確支援以 Application Load Balancer 作為 endpoint。ALB 仍維持其 WAF 關聯，將 accelerator 的靜態 IP 提供給客戶即可，屬於受管、低維運負擔的方案。選項 B 在技術上不可行：Application Load Balancer 無法指派 Elastic IP，ALB 只提供 DNS 名稱，背後是由 ELB 管理且可能變動的 IP。因此正確答案是 C，而 dump 建議的 B 是錯誤的。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Replacing the ALB with an NLB does allow an Elastic IP, but it discards the AWS WAF integration (WAF cannot attach directly to an NLB) and is a much larger change with high operational overhead, contradicting the LEAST-overhead and existing-WAF requirements.","why_zh":"把 ALB 換成 NLB 雖可指派 Elastic IP，但會失去 AWS WAF 整合（WAF 無法直接掛在 NLB 上），且屬於大幅改動、維運負擔高，違反「最少維運負擔」與保留 WAF 的需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Technically impossible: an Application Load Balancer does not support assigning an Elastic IP address. An ALB only provides a DNS name whose underlying IPs are managed by ELB and can change, so it cannot give the customer a stable static IP.","why_zh":"技術上不可行：Application Load Balancer 不支援指派 Elastic IP。ALB 只提供 DNS 名稱，背後 IP 由 ELB 管理且會變動，無法提供穩定的靜態 IP 給客戶。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudFront does not provide stable, customer-facing static IPs; pinging the distribution DNS returns ephemeral edge IPs that change frequently and differ by location, so they cannot be reliably provided to customers as a fixed IP list.","why_zh":"CloudFront 不提供穩定、可給客戶使用的靜態 IP；對 distribution DNS 做 ping 取得的是會頻繁變動且依地點不同的 edge IP，無法可靠地作為固定 IP 清單提供給客戶。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/global-accelerator/latest/dg/what-is-global-accelerator.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/application-load-balancers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/network/network-load-balancers.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":168,"question_en":"A company has a few AWS accounts for development and wants to move its production application to AWS. The company needs to enforce Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) encryption at rest current production accounts and future production accounts only. The company needs a solution that includes built-in blueprints and guardrails. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司有几个用于开发的 AWS 账户，并希望将其生产应用程序迁移到 AWS。该公司只需对当前生产账户和未来生产账户执行静态 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 加密。该公司需要一个包含内置蓝图和护栏的解决方案。 哪种步骤组合可以满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy AWS Config rules on production accounts.","B":"Create a new AWS Control Tower landing zone in an existing developer account. Create OUs for accounts. Add production and development accounts to production and development OUs, respectively.","C":"Create a new AWS Control Tower landing zone in the company’s management account. Add production and development accounts to production and development OUs. respectively.","D":"Invite existing accounts to join the organization in AWS Organizations. Create SCPs to ensure compliance.","E":"Create a guardrail from the management account to detect EBS encryption.","F":"Create a guardrail for the production OU to detect EBS encryption."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 在生产账户上部署 AWS Config 规则。","B":"在现有开发人员账户中创建新的 AWS Control Tower 登陆区。为帐户创建 OU。分别将生产和开发帐户添加到生产和开发 OU。","C":"在公司管理账户中创建新的 AWS Control Tower 登陆区。将生产和开发帐户添加到生产和开发 OU。分别。","D":"邀请现有账户加入 AWS Organizations 中的组织。创建 SCP 以确保合规性。","E":"从管理帐户创建护栏以检测 EBS 加密。","F":"为生产 OU 创建护栏以检测 EBS 加密。 正确答案：公元前 社区投票分布 中非发展基金 (72%) 14% 10%"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"CDF":70,"ACF":15},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to enforce EBS encryption at rest on current and future PRODUCTION accounts only, using a solution with built-in blueprints and guardrails - this points squarely at AWS Control Tower. (C) An AWS Control Tower landing zone must be deployed in the organization's management account; AWS docs state 'AWS Control Tower performs the following actions in your management account on your behalf,' creating OUs, blueprints (Account Factory), and guardrails. (D) The existing development/production accounts must be brought under governance, which is done by inviting them to join the organization in AWS Organizations so they can be placed in OUs and governed by Control Tower. (F) Control Tower controls (guardrails) are enabled per-OU, and the strongly recommended detective control 'Detect Whether Encryption is Enabled for Amazon EBS Volumes Attached to Amazon EC2 Instances' (implemented as an AWS Config rule) applied to the production OU enforces detection on all current and future production accounts only - satisfying the 'production accounts only' scope automatically as new accounts join that OU.","explanation_zh":"需求是僅針對目前與未來的「生產帳戶」強制 EBS 靜態加密，且方案需具備內建 blueprints 與 guardrails，這明確指向 AWS Control Tower。(C) AWS Control Tower landing zone 必須部署在組織的 management account；AWS 文件明確指出 'AWS Control Tower 會代表您在 management account 中執行這些動作'，建立 OUs、blueprints（Account Factory）與 guardrails。(D) 現有的開發/生產帳戶必須納入治理，做法是在 AWS Organizations 中邀請它們加入組織，如此才能放入 OU 並受 Control Tower 治理。(F) Control Tower 的 controls（guardrails）是以 OU 為單位啟用，將 strongly recommended detective control 'Detect Whether Encryption is Enabled for Amazon EBS Volumes Attached to Amazon EC2 Instances'（以 AWS Config rule 實作）套用在 production OU，即可對所有目前與未來的生產帳戶強制偵測加密，並隨新帳戶加入該 OU 自動套用，符合『僅生產帳戶』的範圍要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudFormation StackSets deploying AWS Config rules works mechanically but does NOT provide the 'built-in blueprints and guardrails' the question explicitly requires (that is Control Tower's value), and it is unnecessary once Control Tower's OU-scoped detective control is used. It is a custom DIY approach, not the managed guardrail solution requested.","why_zh":"用 CloudFormation StackSets 部署 AWS Config rules 雖在機制上可行，但並未提供題目明確要求的『內建 blueprints 與 guardrails』（那是 Control Tower 的價值），且在使用 Control Tower 以 OU 為範圍的 detective control 後即屬多餘。這是自行打造的方案，而非題目要求的受管 guardrail 解決方案。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"An AWS Control Tower landing zone cannot be created in an existing developer account. The landing zone is set up in (and requires) the organization's management account, where Control Tower creates the OUs and shared accounts. Deploying it into a developer account is not supported.","why_zh":"AWS Control Tower landing zone 無法建立在現有的開發帳戶中。Landing zone 必須在組織的 management account 中設定（並以其為前提），Control Tower 會在該帳戶建立 OUs 與共享帳戶。將其部署到開發帳戶並不受支援。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"You cannot create a guardrail 'from the management account' to govern it the way described - detective controls are applied to OUs, and per AWS docs controls are not applied to the management account. A management-account-level guardrail would not scope detection to production accounts only.","why_zh":"無法以『從 management account』的方式建立 guardrail 來如描述般治理——detective controls 是套用在 OU 上，且依 AWS 文件，controls 不會套用到 management account。以 management account 層級設定 guardrail 也無法將偵測範圍限定在僅生產帳戶。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/how-control-tower-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/how-controls-work.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/control-considerations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/detective-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/aws-multi-account-landing-zone.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・複選"},{"id":169,"question_en":"A company is running a critical stateful web application on two Linux Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) with an Amazon RDS for MySQL database. The company hosts the DNS records for the application in Amazon Route 53. A solutions architect must recommend a solution to improve the resiliency of the application. The solution must meet the following objectives: • Application tier: RPO of 2 minutes. RTO of 30 minutes • Database tier: RPO of 5 minutes. RTO of 30 minutes The company does not want to make significant changes to the existing application architecture. The company must ensure optimal latency after a failover. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面的两个 Linux Amazon EC2 实例上运行一个关键的有状态 Web 应用程序，其中包含 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库。该公司在 Amazon Route 53 中托管应用程序的 DNS 记录。解决方案架构师必须推荐一种解决方案来 提高应用程序的弹性。 该解决方案必须满足以下目标： • 应用程序层：RPO 为2 分钟。RTO 为30 分钟 • 数据库层：RPO 为5 分钟。RTO 为 30 分钟 该公司不想对现有应用程序架构进行重大更改。公司必须确保故障转移后的最佳延迟。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the EC2 instances to use AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery. Create a cross-Region read replica for the RDS DB instance. Create an ALB in a second AWS Region. Create an AWS Global Accelerator endpoint, and associate the endpoint with the ALBs. Update DNS records to point to the Global Accelerator endpoint.","B":"Configure the EC2 instances to use Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager (Amazon DLM) to take snapshots of the EBS volumes. Configure RDS automated backups. Configure backup replication to a second AWS Region. Create an ALB in the second Region. Create an AWS Global Accelerator endpoint, and associate the endpoint with the ALBs. Update DNS records to point to the Global Accelerator endpoint.","C":"Create a backup plan in AWS Backup for the EC2 instances and RDS DB instance. Configure backup replication to a second AWS Region. Create an ALB in the second Region. Configure an Amazon CloudFront distribution in front of the ALB. Update DNS records to point to CloudFront.","D":"Configure the EC2 instances to use Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager (Amazon DLM) to take snapshots of the EBS volumes. Create a cross-Region read replica for the RDS DB instance. Create an ALB in a second AWS Region. Create an AWS Global Accelerator endpoint, and associate the endpoint with the ALBs."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 EC2 实例以使用 AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery。为RDS数据库实例创建跨区域只读副本。在第二个 AWS 区域中创建 ALB。 创建 AWS Global Accelerator 终端节点，并将该终端节点与 ALB 关联。更新 DNS 记录以指向 Global Accelerator 端点。","B":"配置 EC2 实例以使用 Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager (Amazon DLM) 拍摄 EBS 卷的快照。配置 RDS 自动备份。配置到第二个 AWS 区域的备份复制。在第二个区域中创建 ALB。创建 AWS Global Accelerator 终端节点，并将该终端节点与 ALB 关联。更新 DNS 记录以指向 Global Accelerator 端点。","C":"在 AWS Backup 中为 EC2 实例和 RDS 数据库实例创建备份计划。配置到第二个 AWS 区域的备份复制。在第二个区域中创建 ALB。在 ALB 前面配置 Amazon CloudFront 分配。更新 DNS 记录以指向 CloudFront。","D":"配置 EC2 实例以使用 Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager (Amazon DLM) 拍摄 EBS 卷的快照。为RDS数据库实例创建跨区域只读副 本。在第二个 AWS 区域中创建 ALB。创建 AWS Global Accelerator 终端节点，并将该终端节点与 ALB 关联。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":96},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The objectives demand near-continuous replication: application tier RPO 2 min / RTO 30 min and database tier RPO 5 min / RTO 30 min, with no significant architecture changes and optimal post-failover latency. AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery (DRS) performs continuous block-level replication of the Linux EC2 instances, giving a crash-consistent RPO of seconds (meets 2 min) and an RTO of 5-20 min for Linux boot (meets 30 min) without re-architecting the app. An RDS cross-Region read replica replicates asynchronously and continuously, giving an RPO of seconds-to-minutes (meets 5 min) and is promoted to standalone within minutes (meets 30 min). AWS Global Accelerator with an endpoint group across both Regions' ALBs uses the AWS global network and anycast static IPs to route clients to the nearest healthy Region, delivering optimal latency and near-instant failover; updating the Route 53 record to the Global Accelerator endpoint completes the design. This is the only option that satisfies every objective.","explanation_zh":"需求要求接近連續的複製：應用層 RPO 2 分鐘 / RTO 30 分鐘，資料庫層 RPO 5 分鐘 / RTO 30 分鐘，且不對架構做重大變更，並在故障轉移後保持最佳延遲。AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery (DRS) 對 Linux EC2 執行連續區塊層級複製，提供以秒計的 crash-consistent RPO（符合 2 分鐘），Linux 開機的 RTO 約 5-20 分鐘（符合 30 分鐘），且無需重構應用程式。RDS 跨區域唯讀複本以非同步且連續的方式複製，RPO 為秒到分鐘級（符合 5 分鐘），可在數分鐘內提升為獨立執行個體（符合 30 分鐘）。AWS Global Accelerator 將端點群組關聯到兩個區域的 ALB，透過 AWS 全球網路與 anycast 靜態 IP 把使用者導向最近的健康區域，提供最佳延遲與近乎即時的故障轉移；將 Route 53 記錄更新指向 Global Accelerator 端點即完成設計。這是唯一同時滿足所有目標的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon DLM EBS snapshots are scheduled (practical minimum granularity is hours, not minutes), so they cannot achieve the 2-minute application RPO, and recovering instances from snapshots plus restoring from replicated RDS automated backups is far too slow for a 30-minute RTO. This is the dump's suggested answer but it fails the core RPO/RTO targets.","why_zh":"Amazon DLM EBS 快照是排程式的（實務最小粒度為小時級，非分鐘級），無法達成 2 分鐘的應用 RPO；從快照重建執行個體並從複製的 RDS 自動備份還原對 30 分鐘 RTO 來說太慢。此為題庫建議答案，但無法滿足核心 RPO/RTO 目標。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Backup creates scheduled point-in-time backups that cannot meet RPO 2 min (app) or 5 min (DB), and restoring from backup is slow for RTO. Also CloudFront is a content-delivery CDN, not a multi-Region active/passive failover router; Global Accelerator is the appropriate choice for optimal-latency cross-Region failover of ALBs.","why_zh":"AWS Backup 產生排程式的時間點備份，無法滿足應用 2 分鐘或資料庫 5 分鐘的 RPO，且從備份還原對 RTO 太慢。此外 CloudFront 是內容傳遞 CDN，並非多區域主備故障轉移的路由器；Global Accelerator 才是對 ALB 進行最佳延遲跨區域故障轉移的正確選擇。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"DLM EBS snapshots again cannot meet the 2-minute application RPO, and critically this option never updates the Route 53 DNS record to point at the Global Accelerator endpoint, so client traffic would not actually be routed to the accelerator during failover. Both flaws make it non-functional for the stated objectives.","why_zh":"DLM EBS 快照同樣無法滿足 2 分鐘的應用 RPO，而且關鍵在於此選項從未把 Route 53 DNS 記錄更新指向 Global Accelerator 端點，因此故障轉移時用戶流量實際上不會被導向加速器。兩項缺陷使其無法滿足題目目標。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/CloudEndure-Concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/what-is-drs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_ReadRepl.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/global-accelerator/latest/dg/what-is-global-accelerator.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/global-accelerator/latest/dg/about-endpoints-endpoint-weights.unhealthy-endpoints.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":170,"question_en":"A solutions architect wants to cost-optimize and appropriately size Amazon EC2 instances in a single AWS account. The solutions architect wants to ensure that the instances are optimized based on CPU, memory, and network metrics. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"解决方案架构师希望在单个 AWS 账户中优化成本并适当调整 Amazon EC2 实例的大小。解决方案架构师希望确保实例根据 CPU、内 存和网络指标进行优化。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Purchase AWS Business Support or AWS Enterprise Support for the account.","B":"Turn on AWS Trusted Advisor and review any “Low Utilization Amazon EC2 Instances” recommendations.","C":"Install the Amazon CloudWatch agent and configure memory metric collection on the EC2 instances.","D":"Configure AWS Compute Optimizer in the AWS account to receive findings and optimization recommendations.","E":"Create an EC2 Instance Savings Plan for the AWS Regions, instance families, and operating systems of interest."},"options_zh":{"A":"为账户购买 AWS Business Support 或 AWS Enterprise Support。","B":"打开 AWS Trusted Advisor 并查看任何“低利用率 Amazon EC2 实例”建议。","C":"在 EC2 实例上安装 Amazon CloudWatch 代理并配置内存指标收集。","D":"在 AWS 账户中配置 AWS Compute Optimizer 以接收结果和优化建议。","E":"为感兴趣的 AWS 区域、实例系列和操作系统创建 EC2 实例节省计划。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"CD":93},"tags":["Compute","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is that instances must be optimized based on CPU, memory, AND network metrics. AWS Compute Optimizer (D) is the purpose-built rightsizing service: by default it analyzes CloudWatch metrics including CPUUtilization, NetworkIn/NetworkOut, disk, and EBS metrics to produce instance rightsizing recommendations. However, EC2 does not publish memory utilization to CloudWatch by default. AWS documentation explicitly states that Compute Optimizer analyzes the MemoryUtilization metric only for 'EC2 instances with the CloudWatch agent that's installed on them' (or via third-party observability ingestion). Therefore installing and configuring the CloudWatch agent for memory collection (C) is required so that Compute Optimizer can factor memory into its recommendations. Together C and D cover all three required dimensions. Option B (Trusted Advisor 'Low Utilization EC2 Instances') only considers CPU and network I/O and ignores memory, so it cannot meet the explicit memory requirement.","explanation_zh":"決定性條件是執行個體必須依據 CPU、記憶體與網路三項指標進行最佳化。AWS Compute Optimizer (D) 是專門的調整大小服務：預設會分析 CloudWatch 指標，包括 CPUUtilization、NetworkIn/NetworkOut、磁碟與 EBS 指標，以產生執行個體調整大小建議。然而 EC2 預設不會將記憶體使用率發佈到 CloudWatch。AWS 文件明確指出，Compute Optimizer 只會針對『已安裝 CloudWatch agent 的 EC2 執行個體』(或透過第三方可觀測性產品擷取) 分析 MemoryUtilization 指標。因此必須安裝並設定 CloudWatch agent 收集記憶體指標 (C)，Compute Optimizer 才能將記憶體納入建議。C 與 D 合起來涵蓋三項所需維度。選項 B (Trusted Advisor『Low Utilization Amazon EC2 Instances』) 只考量 CPU 與網路 I/O，不含記憶體，無法滿足明確的記憶體需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Purchasing Business/Enterprise Support only unlocks the full Trusted Advisor check set; it collects no metrics itself and is only relevant if B were the answer, which it is not. It does nothing for CPU/memory/network rightsizing.","why_zh":"購買 Business/Enterprise Support 只是解鎖完整的 Trusted Advisor 檢查；它本身不收集任何指標，且僅在 B 為正解時才相關，而 B 並非正解。對 CPU/記憶體/網路的調整大小毫無幫助。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The Trusted Advisor 'Low Utilization Amazon EC2 Instances' check evaluates only CPU utilization and network I/O over a period; it does not consider memory. Since the requirement explicitly includes memory metrics, this check cannot satisfy it.","why_zh":"Trusted Advisor『Low Utilization Amazon EC2 Instances』檢查只評估一段期間的 CPU 使用率與網路 I/O，不考量記憶體。由於需求明確包含記憶體指標，此檢查無法滿足。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"An EC2 Instance Savings Plan is a billing/pricing commitment that lowers cost for chosen instance families; it does not analyze utilization or appropriately size instances based on CPU, memory, or network metrics.","why_zh":"EC2 Instance Savings Plan 是針對選定執行個體系列降低成本的計費/定價承諾；它不會分析使用率，也不會依 CPU、記憶體或網路指標適當調整執行個體大小。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/compute-optimizer/latest/ug/ec2-metrics-analyzed.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/compute-optimizer/latest/ug/what-is-compute-optimizer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/metrics-collected-by-CloudWatch-agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awssupport/latest/user/trusted-advisor.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":171,"question_en":"A company uses an AWS CodeCommit repository. The company must store a backup copy of the data that is in the repository in a second AWS Region. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS CodeCommit 存储库。公司必须在第二个 AWS 区域的存储库中存储数据的备份副本。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery to replicate the CodeCommit repository data to the second Region.","B":"Use AWS Backup to back up the CodeCommit repository on an hourly schedule. Create a cross-Region copy in the second Region.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke AWS CodeBuild when the company pushes code to the repository. Use CodeBuild to clone the repository. Create a .zip file of the content. Copy the file to an S3 bucket in the second Region.","D":"Create an AWS Step Functions work­ow on an hourly schedule to take a snapshot of the CodeCommit repository. Configure the work­ow to copy the snapshot to an S3 bucket in the second Region"},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery 以将 CodeCommit 存储库数据复制到第二个区域。","B":"使用 AWS Backup 按小时计划备份 CodeCommit 存储库。在第二个区域中创建跨区域副本。","C":"创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以便在公司将代码推送到存储库时调用 AWS CodeBuild。使用 CodeBuild 克隆存储库。创建内 容的 .zip 文件。将文件复制到第二个区域中的 S3 存储桶。","D":"按小时计划创建 AWS Step Functions 工作流程以拍摄 CodeCommit 存储库的快照。配置工作流程以将快照复制到第二个区域中 的 S3 存储桶"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":97},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":172,"question_en":"A company has multiple business units that each have separate accounts on AWS. Each business unit manages its own network with several VPCs that have CIDR ranges that overlap. The company’s marketing team has created a new internal application and wants to make the application accessible to all the other business units. The solution must use private IP addresses only. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司有多个业务部门，每个部门在 AWS 上都有单独的账户。每个业务部门都通过多个 VPC 管理自己的网络，这些 VPC 的 CIDR 范围重叠。该公司的营销团队创建了一个新的内部应用程序，并希望所有其他业务部门都可以访问该应用程序。该解决方案必须仅 使用私有 IP 地址。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Instruct each business unit to add a unique secondary CIDR range to the business unit's VPC. Peer the VPCs and use a private NAT gateway in the secondary range to route tra®c to the marketing team.","B":"Create an Amazon EC2 instance to serve as a virtual appliance in the marketing account's VPC. Create an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection between the marketing team and each business unit's VPC. Perform NAT where necessary.","C":"Create an AWS PrivateLink endpoint service to share the marketing application. Grant permission to specific AWS accounts to connect to the service. Create interface VPC endpoints in other accounts to access the application by using private IP addresses.","D":"Create a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in front of the marketing application in a private subnet. Create an API Gateway API. Use the Amazon API Gateway private integration to connect the API to the NLB. Activate IAM authorization for the API. Grant access to the accounts of the other business units."},"options_zh":{"A":"指示每个业务部门向该业务部门的 VPC 添加唯一的辅助 CIDR 范围。对 VPC 进行对等并使用辅助范围中的私有 NAT 网关将流 量路由到营销团队。","B":"创建一个 Amazon EC2 实例作为营销账户的 VPC 中的虚拟设备。在营销团队和每个业务部门的 VPC 之间创建 AWS 站点到站点 VPN 连接。必要时执行 NAT。","C":"创建 AWS PrivateLink 终端节点服务以共享营销应用程序。向特定 AWS 账户授予连接到服务的权限。在其他账户中创建接口 VPC端点，以使用私有IP地址访问应用程序。","D":"在私有子网中的营销应用程序前面创建网络负载均衡器 (NLB)。创建 API 网关 API。使用 Amazon API Gateway 私有集成将 API 连接到 NLB。激活API的IAM授权。授予对其他业务部门帐户的访问权限。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":94},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"AWS PrivateLink is purpose-built for sharing a service across AWS accounts using private IP addresses only, and it works even when consumer VPCs have overlapping CIDR ranges. The marketing team puts the application behind a Network Load Balancer and creates a VPC endpoint service, then grants permission to specific business-unit AWS accounts. Each consumer creates an interface VPC endpoint, which provisions an elastic network interface with a private IP drawn from the consumer's own subnet. Because traffic flows through these endpoints rather than via VPC-to-VPC routing, there is no CIDR conflict and no need for peering, secondary CIDRs, NAT, or VPN. This is the lowest-operational-overhead solution that satisfies 'private IP addresses only.' Option D (API Gateway + NLB private integration + IAM auth) does not cleanly meet 'private IP only' (the API endpoint is regional/public by default unless built as a private REST API with interface endpoints, which the option omits) and forces all business units to SigV4-sign requests, adding application changes and overhead.","explanation_zh":"AWS PrivateLink 專為跨 AWS 帳戶且僅使用私有 IP 位址來共用服務而設計，即使消費端 VPC 的 CIDR 範圍重疊也能運作。marketing 團隊將應用程式置於 Network Load Balancer 之後並建立 VPC endpoint service，再授權特定業務單位的 AWS 帳戶。各消費端建立 interface VPC endpoint，會在自身子網內配置具私有 IP 的 elastic network interface。由於流量經由這些 endpoint 而非 VPC 對 VPC 路由，因此不會有 CIDR 衝突，也不需要 peering、次要 CIDR、NAT 或 VPN，是符合「僅使用私有 IP」且營運負擔最低的方案。選項 D（API Gateway + NLB private integration + IAM 授權）無法乾淨地滿足「僅私有 IP」（API endpoint 預設為 regional/public，除非建為含 interface endpoint 的 private REST API，而該選項並未描述），且會強迫所有業務單位以 SigV4 簽署請求，增加應用程式變更與營運負擔。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Adding a unique secondary CIDR to every business unit's VPC, peering all VPCs, and deploying private NAT gateways is a large, multi-account networking effort with the highest operational overhead, not the least.","why_zh":"為每個業務單位 VPC 新增唯一次要 CIDR、對所有 VPC 進行 peering 並部署 private NAT gateway，是跨多帳戶的大型網路工程，營運負擔最高而非最低。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A self-managed EC2 virtual appliance plus Site-to-Site VPN to each business unit with manual NAT is the most operationally heavy, least scalable option and requires ongoing patching/management of the appliance.","why_zh":"自行管理的 EC2 虛擬設備搭配對每個業務單位的 Site-to-Site VPN 與手動 NAT，是營運負擔最重、最不可擴展的選項，且需持續修補與管理設備。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"API Gateway's default endpoint is regional/public, so it does not satisfy 'private IP addresses only' unless built as a private REST API with interface endpoints (not described). IAM authorization also forces every consumer to SigV4-sign requests, adding application changes and more overhead than PrivateLink.","why_zh":"API Gateway 預設 endpoint 為 regional/public，除非建為含 interface endpoint 的 private REST API（選項未描述），否則無法滿足「僅私有 IP」。IAM 授權也強迫每個消費端以 SigV4 簽署請求，增加應用程式變更，營運負擔高於 PrivateLink。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/privatelink-share-your-services.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/endpoint-services-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-private-apis.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":173,"question_en":"A company needs to audit the security posture of a newly acquired AWS account. The company’s data security team requires a notification only when an Amazon S3 bucket becomes publicly exposed. The company has already established an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic that has the data security team's email address subscribed. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要审核新收购的 AWS 账户的安全状况。仅当 Amazon S3 存储桶公开时，该公司的数据安全团队才需要通知。该公司已经 建立了一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 主题，并订阅了数据安全团队的电子邮件地址。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an S3 event notification on all S3 buckets for the isPublic event. Select the SNS topic as the target for the event notifications.","B":"Create an analyzer in AWS Identity and Access Management Access Analyzer. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for the event type “Access Analyzer Finding” with a filter for “isPublic: true.” Select the SNS topic as the EventBridge rule target.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for the event type “Bucket-Level API Call via CloudTrail” with a filter for “PutBucketPolicy.” Select the SNS topic as the EventBridge rule target.","D":"Activate AWS Config and add the cloudtrail-s3-dataevents-enabled rule. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for the event type “Config Rules Re-evaluation Status” with a filter for “NON_COMPLIANT.” Select the SNS topic as the EventBridge rule target."},"options_zh":{"A":"在所有 S3 存储桶上为 isPublic 事件创建 S3 事件通知。选择 SNS 主题作为事件通知的目标。","B":"在 AWS Identity and Access Management 访问分析器中创建分析器。为事件类型“访问分析器查找”创建 Amazon EventBridge 规 则，并使用“isPublic: true”过滤器。选择 SNS 主题作为 EventBridge 规则目标。","C":"为事件类型“通过 CloudTrail 进行存储桶级 API 调用”创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则，并使用“PutBucketPolicy”过滤器。选择 SNS 主题作为 EventBridge 规则目标。","D":"激活 AWS Config 并添加 cloudtrail-s3-dataevents-enabled 规则。为事件类型“配置规则重新评估状态”创建 Amazon EventBridge 规 则，并使用“NON_COMPLIANT”过滤器。选择 SNS 主题作为 EventBridge 规则目标。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":94},"tags":["Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"IAM Access Analyzer continuously analyzes resource policies (including S3 bucket policies, ACLs, and access points) and generates a finding when a resource grants access to an external entity, flagging public exposure with an isPublic attribute. Access Analyzer sends each finding to Amazon EventBridge with detail-type 'Access Analyzer Finding' and a detail object containing isPublic. You create an EventBridge rule matching that detail-type with an event pattern filtering on detail.isPublic = true, and target the existing SNS topic so the data security team is emailed only when a bucket becomes public. This precisely satisfies 'notify only when an S3 bucket becomes publicly exposed.' Option A is invalid because S3 event notifications only support object-level/lifecycle event types (ObjectCreated, ObjectRemoved, ObjectRestore, replication, etc.) — there is no 'isPublic' event type.","explanation_zh":"IAM Access Analyzer 會持續分析資源政策（包含 S3 bucket policy、ACL 與 access point），當資源授予外部實體存取時產生 finding，並以 isPublic 屬性標示是否為公開。Access Analyzer 會將每個 finding 以 detail-type 為「Access Analyzer Finding」送到 Amazon EventBridge，detail 物件中包含 isPublic。建立一個比對該 detail-type 並以 detail.isPublic = true 過濾的 EventBridge 規則，將既有的 SNS topic 設為目標，便能在 bucket 變為公開時才通知資料安全團隊，完全符合「僅在 S3 bucket 公開暴露時通知」的需求。選項 A 不成立，因為 S3 event notifications 只支援物件層級或生命週期事件類型（ObjectCreated、ObjectRemoved、ObjectRestore、replication 等），並沒有 isPublic 這種事件類型。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"S3 event notifications do not support an 'isPublic' event type. Supported types are object-level and management events such as s3:ObjectCreated:*, s3:ObjectRemoved:*, s3:ObjectRestore:*, replication, and lifecycle events. There is no native S3 notification that fires when a bucket becomes public, so this configuration cannot be created.","why_zh":"S3 event notifications 不支援「isPublic」事件類型。支援的類型為物件層級與管理事件，例如 s3:ObjectCreated:*、s3:ObjectRemoved:*、s3:ObjectRestore:*、replication 與生命週期事件。沒有任何原生 S3 通知會在 bucket 變公開時觸發，因此此設定無法建立。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Filtering CloudTrail PutBucketPolicy calls would notify on every bucket policy change, not specifically when a bucket becomes public, producing many false positives. It also ignores other public-exposure vectors (ACLs, public access block changes, access points) and does not evaluate whether the resulting policy actually grants public access.","why_zh":"過濾 CloudTrail 的 PutBucketPolicy 呼叫會在每次 bucket policy 變更時都通知，而非只在 bucket 變公開時，會產生大量誤報。它也忽略其他公開暴露途徑（ACL、public access block 變更、access point），且不會判斷產生的政策是否真的授予公開存取。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The cloudtrail-s3-dataevents-enabled Config rule checks whether CloudTrail logs S3 object-level data events — it has nothing to do with public bucket exposure. The 'Config Rules Re-evaluation Status' event type also reports re-evaluation status, not compliance results, so this combination does not detect or notify on public buckets.","why_zh":"cloudtrail-s3-dataevents-enabled 這個 Config rule 檢查的是 CloudTrail 是否記錄 S3 物件層級資料事件，與 bucket 公開暴露毫無關係。「Config Rules Re-evaluation Status」事件類型回報的是重新評估狀態而非合規結果，因此此組合無法偵測或通知公開 bucket。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access-analyzer-eventbridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-access-analyzer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/access-analyzer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/notification-how-to-event-types-and-destinations.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":174,"question_en":"A solutions architect needs to assess a newly acquired company’s portfolio of applications and databases. The solutions architect must create a business case to migrate the portfolio to AWS. The newly acquired company runs applications in an on-premises data center. The data center is not well documented. The solutions architect cannot immediately determine how many applications and databases exist. Tra®c for the applications is variable. Some applications are batch processes that run at the end of each month. The solutions architect must gain a better understanding of the portfolio before a migration to AWS can begin. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师需要评估新收购的公司的应用程序和数据库组合。解决方案架构师必须创建一个业务案例以将产品组合迁移到 AWS。新收购的公司在本地数据中心运行应用程序。数据中心没有很好的记录。解决方案架构师无法立即确定存在多少应用程序和 数据库。应用程序的流量是可变的。有些应用程序是在每个月底运行的批处理过程。 在开始迁移到 AWS 之前，解决方案架构师必须更好地了解产品组合。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Server Migration Service (AWS SMS) and AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to evaluate migration. Use AWS Service Catalog to understand application and database dependencies.","B":"Use AWS Application Migration Service. Run agents on the on-premises infrastructure. Manage the agents by using AWS Migration Hub. Use AWS Storage Gateway to assess local storage needs and database dependencies.","C":"Use Migration Evaluator to generate a list of servers. Build a report for a business case. Use AWS Migration Hub to view the portfolio. Use AWS Application Discovery Service to gain an understanding of application dependencies.","D":"Use AWS Control Tower in the destination account to generate an application portfolio. Use AWS Server Migration Service (AWS SMS) to generate deeper reports and a business case. Use a landing zone for core accounts and resources."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Server Migration Service (AWS SMS) 和 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 评估迁移。使用 AWS Service Catalog 了解应用程序和数据库依赖项。","B":"使用 AWS Application Migration Service。在本地基础设施上运行代理。使用 AWS Migration Hub 管理代理。使用 AWS Storage Gateway 评估本地存储需求和数据库依赖性。","C":"使用迁移评估器生成服务器列表。构建业务案例报告。使用 AWS Migration Hub 查看产品组合。使用 AWS Application Discovery Service 了解应用程序依赖性。","D":"在目标账户中使用 AWS Control Tower 生成应用程序组合。使用 AWS Server Migration Service (AWS SMS) 生成更深入的报告和业 务案例。使用核心帐户和资源的登陆区域。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":97},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The scenario is the pre-migration assess/discovery phase: the data center is poorly documented, the number of applications and databases is unknown, and the architect must build a business case before any migration starts. Migration Evaluator is AWS's purpose-built business case / TCO analysis tool that generates a list of servers and produces a report to justify migration. AWS Application Discovery Service collects usage and configuration data about on-premises servers and databases and exports network connection data so you can determine dependencies and group servers into applications. AWS Migration Hub aggregates discovered inventory into a single console to view the portfolio. Only option C combines assessment/business-case and dependency-discovery tools; every other option relies on migration execution/replication tools (SMS, Application Migration Service/MGN, DMS, Storage Gateway, Control Tower) that move workloads rather than assess them, which is premature given the requirement to understand the portfolio first.","explanation_zh":"此情境屬於遷移前的評估／探索階段：資料中心文件不完整、應用程式與資料庫數量未知，架構師必須在任何遷移開始前先建立 business case。Migration Evaluator 是 AWS 專門用於 business case／TCO 分析的工具，可產生伺服器清單並輸出報告以佐證遷移決策。AWS Application Discovery Service 收集地端伺服器與資料庫的使用率與組態資料，並匯出網路連線資料以判斷相依性、將伺服器歸類為應用程式。AWS Migration Hub 將探索到的清單彙整到單一主控台以檢視整個 portfolio。只有選項 C 結合了評估／business case 與相依性探索工具；其餘選項都依賴遷移執行／複寫工具（SMS、Application Migration Service/MGN、DMS、Storage Gateway、Control Tower），這些是用來搬移工作負載而非評估，在尚未了解 portfolio 之前使用為時過早。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS SMS and DMS are migration execution tools (server and database replication), not assessment or business-case tools. AWS Service Catalog manages curated catalogs of approved IT products; it does not discover or map application/database dependencies.","why_zh":"AWS SMS 與 DMS 是遷移執行工具（伺服器與資料庫複寫），並非評估或 business case 工具。AWS Service Catalog 用於管理經核准的 IT 產品目錄，無法探索或對應應用程式／資料庫的相依性。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but is wrong. AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) is a rehost/replication tool for actually migrating servers, not for discovery or building a business case. Storage Gateway provides hybrid storage access and cannot assess database dependencies. It produces no business-case report.","why_zh":"這是題庫建議答案，但有誤。AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) 是用於實際遷移伺服器的 rehost／複寫工具，並非用於探索或建立 business case。Storage Gateway 提供混合雲儲存存取，無法評估資料庫相依性，也無法產生 business case 報告。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Control Tower sets up and governs a multi-account AWS landing zone; it does not generate an application portfolio from an on-premises data center. AWS SMS is a migration replication tool and does not produce business-case reports or dependency analysis.","why_zh":"AWS Control Tower 用於建立與治理多帳戶的 AWS landing zone，無法從地端資料中心產生應用程式 portfolio。AWS SMS 是遷移複寫工具，無法產生 business case 報告或相依性分析。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/migration-tools/business-case-migration-evaluator.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/what-is-appdiscovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/discovery-agent.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":175,"question_en":"A company has an application that runs as a ReplicaSet of multiple pods in an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster. The EKS cluster has nodes in multiple Availability Zones. The application generates many small files that must be accessible across all running instances of the application. The company needs to back up the files and retain the backups for 1 year. Which solution will meet these requirements while providing the FASTEST storage performance?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个应用程序，该应用程序在 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 集群中作为多个 Pod 的 ReplicaSet 运行。 EKS 集群在多个可用区中拥有节点。该应用程序会生成许多小文件，这些文件必须可以在该应用程序的所有正在运行的实例中访 问。公司需要对文件进行备份，并保留备份1年。 哪种解决方案能够满足这些要求，同时提供最快的存储性能？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system and a mount target for each subnet that contains nodes in the EKS cluster. Configure the ReplicaSet to mount the file system. Direct the application to store files in the file system. Configure AWS Backup to back up and retain copies of the data for 1 year.","B":"Create an Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume. Enable the EBS Multi-Attach feature. Configure the ReplicaSet to mount the EBS volume. Direct the application to store files in the EBS volume. Configure AWS Backup to back up and retain copies of the data for 1 year.","C":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure the ReplicaSet to mount the S3 bucket. Direct the application to store files in the S3 bucket. Configure S3 Versioning to retain copies of the data. Configure an S3 Lifecycle policy to delete objects after 1 year.","D":"Configure the ReplicaSet to use the storage available on each of the running application pods to store the files locally. Use a third-party tool to back up the EKS cluster for 1 year."},"options_zh":{"A":"为包含 EKS 集群中的节点的每个子网创建 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统和挂载目标。配置ReplicaSet挂载文 件系统。指示应用程序将文件存储在文件系统中。配置 AWS Backup 以备份数据副本并保留 1 年。","B":"创建 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 卷。启用 EBS 多重附加功能。配置 ReplicaSet 以挂载 EBS 卷。指示应用程序将文 件存储在 EBS 卷中。配置 AWS Backup 以备份数据副本并保留 1 年。","C":"创建 Amazon S3 存储桶。配置 ReplicaSet 以挂载 S3 存储桶。指示应用程序将文件存储在 S3 存储桶中。配置 S3 版本控制以保 留数据副本。配置 S3 生命周期策略以在 1 年后删除对象。","D":"将 ReplicaSet 配置为使用每个正在运行的应用程序 Pod 上可用的存储来在本地存储文件。使用第三方工具备份EKS集群1年。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":176,"question_en":"A company runs a customer service center that accepts calls and automatically sends all customers a managed, interactive, two-way experience survey by text message. The applications that support the customer service center run on machines that the company hosts in an on-premises data center. The hardware that the company uses is old, and the company is experiencing downtime with the system. The company wants to migrate the system to AWS to improve reliability. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST ongoing operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司运营着一个客户服务中心，该中心接听电话并自动通过短信向所有客户发送托管、交互式、双向体验调查。支持客户服务 中心的应用程序在公司托管在本地数据中心的计算机上运行。该公司使用的硬件陈旧，并且该公司正在经历系统停机。该公司希望 将系统迁移到AWS以提高可靠性。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的持续运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Connect to replace the old call center hardware. Use Amazon Pinpoint to send text message surveys to customers.","B":"Use Amazon Connect to replace the old call center hardware. Use Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to send text message surveys to customers.","C":"Migrate the call center software to Amazon EC2 instances that are in an Auto Scaling group. Use the EC2 instances to send text message surveys to customers.","D":"Use Amazon Pinpoint to replace the old call center hardware and to send text message surveys to customers."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Connect 替换旧的呼叫中心硬件。使用 Amazon Pinpoint 向客户发送短信调查。","B":"使用 Amazon Connect 替换旧的呼叫中心硬件。使用 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 向客户发送短信调查。","C":"将呼叫中心软件迁移到 Auto Scaling 组中的 Amazon EC2 实例。使用 EC2 实例向客户发送短信调查。","D":"使用 Amazon Pinpoint 替换旧的呼叫中心硬件并向客户发送短信调查。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Migration","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":177,"question_en":"A company is building a call center by using Amazon Connect. The company’s operations team is defining a disaster recovery (DR) strategy across AWS Regions. The contact center has dozens of contact ­ows, hundreds of users, and dozens of claimed phone numbers. Which solution will provide DR with the LOWEST RTO?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 Amazon Connect 构建呼叫中心。该公司的运营团队正在制定跨 AWS 区域的灾难恢复 (DR) 策略。该联络中心拥有 数十个联系流、数百个用户和数十个已认领的电话号码。 哪种解决方案将为灾难恢复提供最低的 RTO？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function to check the availability of the Amazon Connect instance and to send a notification to the operations team in case of unavailability. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function every 5 minutes. After notification, instruct the operations team to use the AWS Management Console to provision a new Amazon Connect instance in a second Region. Deploy the contact ­ows, users, and claimed phone numbers by using an AWS CloudFormation template.","B":"Provision a new Amazon Connect instance with all existing users in a second Region. Create an AWS Lambda function to check the availability of the Amazon Connect instance. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function every 5 minutes. In the event of an issue, configure the Lambda function to deploy an AWS CloudFormation template that provisions contact ­ows and claimed numbers in the second Region.","C":"Provision a new Amazon Connect instance with all existing contact ­ows and claimed phone numbers in a second Region. Create an Amazon Route 53 health check for the URL of the Amazon Connect instance. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for failed health checks. Create an AWS Lambda function to deploy an AWS CloudFormation template that provisions all users. Configure the alarm to invoke the Lambda function.","D":"Provision a new Amazon Connect instance with all existing users and contact ­ows in a second Region. Create an Amazon Route 53 health check for the URL of the Amazon Connect instance. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for failed health checks. Create an AWS Lambda function to deploy an AWS CloudFormation template that provisions claimed phone numbers. Configure the alarm to invoke the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来检查 Amazon Connect 实例的可用性，并在不可用时向运营团队发送通知。创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则以每 5 分钟调用一次 Lambda 函数。收到通知后，指示运营团队使用 AWS 管理控制台在第二个区域中预置新的 Amazon Connect 实例。使用 AWS CloudFormation 模板部署联系流、用户和声明的电话号码。","B":"为第二个区域中的所有现有用户配置一个新的 Amazon Connect 实例。创建 AWS Lambda 函数来检查 Amazon Connect 实例的可 用性。创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则以每 5 分钟调用一次 Lambda 函数。如果出现问题，请配置 Lambda 函数以部署 AWS CloudFormation 模板，该模板在第二个区域中配置联系流和已申请的号码。","C":"在第二个区域中配置一个新的 Amazon Connect 实例，其中包含所有现有联系流和已声明的电话号码。为 Amazon Connect 实例 的 URL 创建 Amazon Route 53 运行状况检查。为失败的运行状况检查创建 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。创建 AWS Lambda 函数以部 署配置所有用户的 AWS CloudFormation 模板。配置警报以调用 Lambda 函数。","D":"在第二个区域中配置一个包含所有现有用户和联系流的新 Amazon Connect 实例。为 Amazon Connect 实例的 URL 创建 Amazon Route 53 运行状况检查。为失败的运行状况检查创建 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。创建 AWS Lambda 函数来部署 AWS CloudFormation 模板，该模板可配置所声明的电话号码。配置警报以调用 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":86},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":178,"question_en":"A company runs an application on AWS. The company curates data from several different sources. The company uses proprietary algorithms to perform data transformations and aggregations. After the company performs ETL processes, the company stores the results in Amazon Redshift tables. The company sells this data to other companies. The company downloads the data as files from the Amazon Redshift tables and transmits the files to several data customers by using FTP. The number of data customers has grown significantly. Management of the data customers has become di®cult. The company will use AWS Data Exchange to create a data product that the company can use to share data with customers. The company wants to confirm the identities of the customers before the company shares data. The customers also need access to the most recent data when the company publishes the data. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上运行应用程序。该公司从多个不同来源收集数据。该公司使用专有算法来执行数据转换和聚合。公司执行 ETL 流 程后，将结果存储在 Amazon Redshift 表中。该公司将这些数据出售给其他公司。该公司从 Amazon Redshift 表中以文件形式下载数 据，并使用 FTP 将文件传输给多个数据客户。数据客户数量大幅增长。数据客户的管理变得困难。 该公司将使用 AWS Data Exchange 创建一个数据产品，该公司可以使用该产品与客户共享数据。该公司希望在共享数据之前确认客 户的身份。当公司发布数据时，客户还需要访问最新的数据。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Data Exchange for APIs to share data with customers. Configure subscription verification. In the AWS account of the company that produces the data, create an Amazon API Gateway Data API service integration with Amazon Redshift. Require the data customers to subscribe to the data product.","B":"In the AWS account of the company that produces the data, create an AWS Data Exchange datashare by connecting AWS Data Exchange to the Redshift cluster. Configure subscription verification. Require the data customers to subscribe to the data product.","C":"Download the data from the Amazon Redshift tables to an Amazon S3 bucket periodically. Use AWS Data Exchange for S3 to share data with customers. Configure subscription verification. Require the data customers to subscribe to the data product.","D":"Publish the Amazon Redshift data to an Open Data on AWS Data Exchange. Require the customers to subscribe to the data product in AWS Data Exchange. In the AWS account of the company that produces the data, attach IAM resource-based policies to the Amazon Redshift tables to allow access only to verified AWS accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Data Exchange for API 与客户共享数据。配置订阅验证。在生成数据的公司的 AWS 账户中，创建与 Amazon Redshift 集成的 Amazon API Gateway 数据 API 服务。要求数据客户订阅数据产品。","B":"在生成数据的公司的 AWS 账户中，通过将 AWS Data Exchange 连接到 Redshift 集群来创建 AWS Data Exchange 数据共享。配置 订阅验证。要求数据客户订阅数据产品。","C":"定期将数据从 Amazon Redshift 表下载到 Amazon S3 存储桶。使用 AWS Data Exchange for S3 与客户共享数据。配置订阅验证。 要求数据客户订阅数据产品。","D":"将 Amazon Redshift 数据发布到 AWS Data Exchange 上的开放数据。要求客户订阅 AWS Data Exchange 中的数据产品。在生成数 据的公司的 AWS 账户中，将 IAM 基于资源的策略附加到 Amazon Redshift 表，以仅允许访问经过验证的 AWS 账户。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":91},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":179,"question_en":"A solutions architect is designing a solution to process events. The solution must have the ability to scale in and out based on the number of events that the solution receives. If a processing error occurs, the event must move into a separate queue for review. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师正在设计处理事件的解决方案。解决方案必须能够根据解决方案接收的事件数量进行扩展和扩展。如果发生处理错 误，则该事件必须移至单独的队列中以供审核。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Send event details to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Configure an AWS Lambda function as a subscriber to the SNS topic to process the events. Add an on-failure destination to the function. Set an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue as the target.","B":"Publish events to an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Create an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group. Configure the Auto Scaling group to scale in and out based on the ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage metric of the queue. Configure the application to write failed messages to a dead-letter queue.","C":"Write events to an Amazon DynamoDB table. Configure a DynamoDB stream for the table. Configure the stream to invoke an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to process the events.","D":"Publish events to an Amazon EventBndge event bus. Create and run an application on an Amazon EC2 instance with an Auto Scaling group that is behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Set the ALB as the event bus target. Configure the event bus to retry events. Write messages to a dead-letter queue if the application cannot process the messages."},"options_zh":{"A":"将事件详细信息发送到 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 主题。将 AWS Lambda 函数配置为 SNS 主题的订阅者以 处理事件。向该函数添加失败时目标。将 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列设置为目标。","B":"将事件发布到 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列。创建 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 组。配置 Auto Scaling 组以根据 队列的 ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage 指标进行扩展和扩展。配置应用程序以将失败的消息写入死信队列。","C":"将事件写入 Amazon DynamoDB 表。为表配置 DynamoDB 流。配置流以调用 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数来处理事件。","D":"将事件发布到 Amazon EventBndge 事件总线。在具有应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面的 Auto Scaling 组的 Amazon EC2 实例上创 建并运行应用程序。将 ALB 设置为事件总线目标。配置事件总线以重试事件。如果应用程序无法处理消息，则将消息写入死信 队列。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":63,"B":37},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Amazon SNS invokes Lambda functions asynchronously, and asynchronous invocations support an on-failure destination. After Lambda exhausts its retries on a processing error, it automatically routes the failed event to the configured destination, which can be a standard SQS queue for review. Lambda also natively scales concurrency in and out based on the number of incoming events, so option A satisfies both requirements (event-count scaling and a separate failure queue) with the least operational overhead and no custom code. Option B works mechanically but uses ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage, which AWS explicitly advises against for queue-based target tracking (it does not scale proportionally; AWS recommends a backlog-per-instance metric), describes a DLQ as something the application writes to rather than a redrive policy SQS performs automatically, and adds EC2/Auto Scaling operational overhead. Option C scales by DynamoDB stream shards (tied to table partitions, not event count) and provides no review queue, and option D is invalid because an Application Load Balancer is not a supported EventBridge event-bus target.","explanation_zh":"Amazon SNS 以非同步方式 (asynchronous) 觸發 Lambda 函式，而非同步呼叫支援 on-failure destination。當 Lambda 在處理錯誤時用盡重試次數後，會自動將失敗事件送到設定好的目的地，可以是標準 SQS queue 供後續檢視。Lambda 也會依進入事件數量自動水平擴展與縮減併發量，因此選項 A 以最少維運負擔且不需自訂程式碼，同時滿足「依事件數量擴縮」與「失敗事件進入獨立 queue」兩項需求。選項 B 機制上可行，但使用 ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage，AWS 明確不建議用此類原始 queue 指標做 target tracking (它不會與負載成比例，AWS 建議用 backlog-per-instance 指標)；且描述為「應用程式自行寫入 DLQ」而非 SQS 透過 redrive policy 自動搬移，並額外帶來 EC2/Auto Scaling 維運負擔。選項 C 是依 DynamoDB stream 分片 (與資料表分割區綁定，而非事件數) 擴展且無檢視 queue；選項 D 無效，因為 Application Load Balancer 不是 EventBridge event bus 支援的目標。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage is a poor scaling metric (AWS recommends backlog-per-instance, not raw queue metrics), the DLQ should be configured via an SQS redrive policy rather than the application writing failures, and EC2 Auto Scaling adds far more operational overhead than serverless Lambda.","why_zh":"ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage 不是好的擴縮指標 (AWS 建議用 backlog-per-instance，而非原始 queue 指標)；DLQ 應透過 SQS redrive policy 設定，而非由應用程式自行寫入失敗訊息；且 EC2 Auto Scaling 的維運負擔遠高於無伺服器 Lambda。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"DynamoDB Streams scale by shards tied to table partitions, not by the number of events, and the design provides no separate queue to capture events that fail processing for review.","why_zh":"DynamoDB Streams 依與資料表分割區綁定的分片擴展，而非依事件數量；且此設計沒有提供獨立 queue 來收集處理失敗的事件供檢視。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An Application Load Balancer is not a supported EventBridge event-bus target, so EventBridge cannot deliver events to an ALB this way; the architecture is technically invalid and also operationally heavy.","why_zh":"Application Load Balancer 不是 EventBridge event bus 支援的目標，EventBridge 無法以此方式將事件送到 ALB；此架構在技術上無效且維運負擔大。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/invocation-async.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/invocation-async-retain-records.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/invocation-async-error-handling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/as-using-sqs-queue.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":180,"question_en":"A company runs a processing engine in the AWS Cloud. The engine processes environmental data from logistics centers to calculate a sustainability index. The company has millions of devices in logistics centers that are spread across Europe. The devices send information to the processing engine through a RESTful API. The API experiences unpredictable bursts of tra®c. The company must implement a solution to process all data that the devices send to the processing engine. Data loss is unacceptable. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 云中运行处理引擎。该引擎处理来自物流中心的环境数据以计算可持续性指数。该公司在遍布欧洲的物流中心拥有 数百万台设备。设备通过 RESTful API 将信息发送到处理引擎。 API 会经历不可预测的流量突发。公司必须实施一个解决方案来处理设备发送到处理引擎的所有数据。数据丢失是不可接受的。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB) for the RESTful API. Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Create a listener and a target group for the ALB Add the SQS queue as the target. Use a container that runs in Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) with the Fargate launch type to process messages in the queue.","B":"Create an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API that implements the RESTful API. Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Create an API Gateway service integration with the SQS queue. Create an AWS Lambda function to process messages in the SQS queue.","C":"Create an Amazon API Gateway REST API that implements the RESTful API. Create a ­eet of Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group. Create an API Gateway Auto Scaling group proxy integration. Use the EC2 instances to process incoming data.","D":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution for the RESTful API. Create a data stream in Amazon Kinesis Data Streams. Set the data stream as the origin for the distribution. Create an AWS Lambda function to consume and process data in the data stream."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 RESTful API 创建应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB)。创建 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列。为 ALB 创建侦听器和目 标组 将 SQS 队列添加为目标。使用在 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 中运行且具有 Fargate 启动类型的容器来处 理队列中的消息。","B":"创建实现 RESTful API 的 Amazon API Gateway HTTP API。创建 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列。创建与 SQS 队 列的 API 网关服务集成。创建 AWS Lambda 函数来处理 SQS 队列中的消息。","C":"创建实现 RESTful API 的 Amazon API Gateway REST API。在 Auto Scaling 组中创建 Amazon EC2 实例队列。创建 API Gateway Auto Scaling 组代理集成。使用 EC2 实例处理传入数据。","D":"为 RESTful API 创建 Amazon CloudFront 分配。在 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams 中创建数据流。将数据流设置为分发的来源。创 建 AWS Lambda 函数来使用和处理数据流中的数据。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":91},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":181,"question_en":"A company is designing its network configuration in the AWS Cloud. The company uses AWS Organizations to manage a multi-account setup. The company has three OUs. Each OU contains more than 100 AWS accounts. Each account has a single VPC, and all the VPCs in each OU are in the same AWS Region. The CIDR ranges for all the AWS accounts do not overlap. The company needs to implement a solution in which VPCs in the same OU can communicate with each other but cannot communicate with VPCs in other OUs. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 云中设计其网络配置。该公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理多账户设置。该公司拥有三个 OU。每个 OU 包含 100 多个 AWS 账户。每个账户都有一个 VPC，并且每个 OU 中的所有 VPC 都位于同一 AWS 区域。 所有 AWS 账户的 CIDR 范围不重叠。公司需要实现一个解决方案，同一OU内的VPC可以互相通信，但不能与其他OU内的VPC通信。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CloudFormation stack set that establishes VPC peering between accounts in each OU. Provision the stack set in each OU.","B":"In each OU, create a dedicated networking account that has a single VPC. Share this VPC with all the other accounts in the OU by using AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM). Create a VPC peering connection between the networking account and each account in the OU.","C":"Provision a transit gateway in an account in each OU. Share the transit gateway across the organization by using AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM). Create transit gateway VPC attachments for each VPC.","D":"In each OU, create a dedicated networking account that has a single VPC. Establish a VPN connection between the networking account and the other accounts in the OU. Use third-party routing software to route transitive tra®c between the VPCs."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈集，在每个 OU 中的账户之间建立 VPC 对等互连。在每个 OU 中配置堆栈集。","B":"在每个 OU 中，创建一个具有单个 VPC 的专用网络帐户。使用 AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) 与 OU 中的所有其他账 户共享此 VPC。在网络帐户和 OU 中的每个帐户之间创建 VPC 对等连接。","C":"在每个 OU 的帐户中配置中转网关。使用 AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) 在整个组织中共享中转网关。为每个 VPC 创 建中转网关 VPC 连接。","D":"在每个 OU 中，创建一个具有单个 VPC 的专用网络帐户。在网络帐户与 OU 中的其他帐户之间建立 VPN 连接。使用第三方路由 软件在 VPC 之间路由传输流量。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":76},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is full intra-OU VPC connectivity with isolation between OUs, across 100+ accounts per OU, with the LEAST operational overhead. AWS Transit Gateway is the recommended hub-and-spoke service for interconnecting many VPCs at scale. You provision one transit gateway per OU, share it across the organization with AWS RAM, and create a transit gateway VPC attachment for each VPC. Because each OU has its own transit gateway (and the non-overlapping CIDRs propagate within that TGW's route table), VPCs in the same OU communicate while VPCs in other OUs are isolated. This scales linearly (one attachment per VPC) and avoids per-pair management. VPC peering (options A and B) is not transitive and is not designed for transitive/full-mesh routing among 100+ VPCs, requiring thousands of connections and manual route entries on both sides. Option B's hub-and-spoke peering still cannot route transitively between spokes, and option D's self-managed VPN with third-party routing software adds the most operational overhead and is explicitly the kind of design TGW replaces.","explanation_zh":"需求是在每個 OU 內超過 100 個帳戶的 VPC 之間達成完整互通，同時隔離不同 OU，且要求最少維運負擔。AWS Transit Gateway 是 AWS 推薦用於大規模互連多個 VPC 的中樞輻射 (hub-and-spoke) 服務。做法是每個 OU 佈署一個 transit gateway，透過 AWS RAM 在組織內共享，再為每個 VPC 建立 transit gateway VPC attachment。由於每個 OU 各有自己的 transit gateway（不重疊的 CIDR 會傳播到該 TGW 的路由表），同一 OU 的 VPC 可互通，而其他 OU 的 VPC 被隔離。此方案隨 VPC 數量線性擴展（每個 VPC 一個 attachment），無需逐對管理。VPC peering（選項 A、B）不具傳遞性，不適合在 100+ VPC 間做全網狀/傳遞路由，需要數千條連線並在雙方手動維護路由。選項 B 的中樞輻射式 peering 仍無法在輻射端之間傳遞路由；選項 D 的自管 VPN 加第三方路由軟體維運負擔最大，正是 TGW 所要取代的設計。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"VPC peering is not transitive, so a CloudFormation stack set would have to build a full mesh of N*(N-1)/2 peering connections per OU (over 5,000 for 100+ VPCs), each needing manual route table entries on both sides. This is the highest operational overhead, not the least, and does not scale.","why_zh":"VPC peering 不具傳遞性，因此 stack set 需在每個 OU 建立 N*(N-1)/2 條全網狀 peering 連線（100+ VPC 時超過 5000 條），且每條都要在雙方手動加路由。維運負擔最高而非最少，且無法擴展。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A hub VPC shared via RAM plus peering between the hub and each spoke still cannot route traffic transitively between spoke VPCs, because VPC peering connections do not forward transitive traffic. Spokes would not be able to reach each other, failing the requirement.","why_zh":"透過 RAM 共享的中樞 VPC 加上中樞與各輻射端的 peering，仍無法在輻射 VPC 之間傳遞流量，因為 VPC peering 不轉送傳遞流量。輻射端彼此無法互通，不符合需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Building VPN connections plus third-party routing software (e.g., EC2-based routers) to achieve transitive routing introduces the most operational overhead: managing appliances, licensing, scaling, patching, and HA. Transit Gateway is the managed service AWS provides precisely to replace this self-managed pattern. This is the dump's suggested answer and is wrong.","why_zh":"建置 VPN 連線並用第三方路由軟體（如 EC2 路由器）來達成傳遞路由，帶來最高維運負擔：要管理設備、授權、擴展、修補與高可用。Transit Gateway 正是 AWS 用來取代這種自管模式的代管服務。此為題庫建議答案，但錯誤。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/what-is-transit-gateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/tgw-route-tables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/peering/vpc-peering-basics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/designing-control-tower-landing-zone/inter-vpc.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":182,"question_en":"A company is migrating an application to AWS. It wants to use fully managed services as much as possible during the migration. The company needs to store large important documents within the application with the following requirements: 1. The data must be highly durable and available 2. The data must always be encrypted at rest and in transit 3. The encryption key must be managed by the company and rotated periodically Which of the following solutions should the solutions architect recommend?","question_zh":"一家公司正在将应用程序迁移到 AWS。它希望在迁移过程中尽可能多地使用完全托管的服务。公司需要在应用程序中存储大型重要 文档，并满足以下要求： 1. 数据必须高度持久且可用 2. 数据在静态和传输过程中必须始终加密 3. 加密密钥必须由公司管理并定期轮换 解决方案架构师应推荐以下哪些解决方案？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the storage gateway to AWS in file gateway mode. Use Amazon EBS volume encryption using an AWS KMS key to encrypt the storage gateway volumes.","B":"Use Amazon S3 with a bucket policy to enforce HTTPS for connections to the bucket and to enforce server-side encryption and AWS KMS for object encryption.","C":"Use Amazon DynamoDB with SSL to connect to DynamoDB. Use an AWS KMS key to encrypt DynamoDB objects at rest.","D":"Deploy instances with Amazon EBS volumes attached to store this data. Use EBS volume encryption using an AWS KMS key to encrypt the data."},"options_zh":{"A":"将存储网关以文件网关方式部署到AWS。使用 Amazon EBS 卷加密（使用 AWS KMS 密钥）来加密存储网关卷。","B":"将 Amazon S3 与存储桶策略结合使用，强制执行 HTTPS 来连接到存储桶，并强制执行服务器端加密和 AWS KMS 来进行对象加 密。","C":"使用带有 SSL 的 Amazon DynamoDB 连接到 DynamoDB。使用 AWS KMS 密钥加密静态 DynamoDB 对象。","D":"部署附加 Amazon EBS 卷的实例来存储此数据。使用 EBS 卷加密（使用 AWS KMS 密钥来加密数据）。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Migration","Security/IAM","Storage","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":183,"question_en":"A company’s public API runs as tasks on Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS). The tasks run on AWS Fargate behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and are configured with Service Auto Scaling for the tasks based on CPU utilization. This service has been running well for several months. Recently, API performance slowed down and made the application unusable. The company discovered that a significant number of SQL injection attacks had occurred against the API and that the API service had scaled to its maximum amount. A solutions architect needs to implement a solution that prevents SQL injection attacks from reaching the ECS API service. The solution must allow legitimate tra®c through and must maximize operational e®ciency. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"公司的公共 API 作为 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 上的任务运行。这些任务在应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面的 AWS Fargate 上运行，并根据 CPU 利用率为任务配置了 Service Auto Scaling。这项服务已经运行良好几个月了。 最近，API 性能下降并导致应用程序无法使用。该公司发现该 API 发生了大量 SQL 注入攻击，并且 API 服务已扩展到最大数量。 解决方案架构师需要实现一个解决方案，防止 SQL 注入攻击到达 ECS API 服务。该解决方案必须允许合法流量通过，并且必须最大 限度地提高运营效率。 哪种解决方案满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new AWS WAF web ACL to monitor the HTTP requests and HTTPS requests that are forwarded to the ALB in front of the ECS tasks.","B":"Create a new AWS WAF Bot Control implementation. Add a rule in the AWS WAF Bot Control managed rule group to monitor tra®c and allow only legitimate tra®c to the ALB in front of the ECS tasks.","C":"Create a new AWS WAF web ACL. Add a new rule that blocks requests that match the SQL database rule group. Set the web ACL to allow all other tra®c that does not match those rules. Attach the web ACL to the ALB in front of the ECS tasks.","D":"Create a new AWS WAF web ACL. Create a new empty IP set in AWS WAF. Add a new rule to the web ACL to block requests that originate from IP addresses in the new IP set. Create an AWS Lambda function that scrapes the API logs for IP addresses that send SQL injection attacks, and add those IP addresses to the IP set. Attach the web ACL to the ALB in front of the ECS tasks."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建新的 AWS WAF Web ACL 以监控在 ECS 任务之前转发到 ALB 的 HTTP 请求和 HTTPS 请求。","B":"创建新的 AWS WAF 机器人控制实施。在 AWS WAF Bot Control 托管规则组中添加规则以监控流量并仅允许合法流量流向 ECS 任 务之前的 ALB。","C":"创建新的 AWS WAF Web ACL。添加一条新规则，阻止与 SQL 数据库规则组匹配的请求。设置 Web ACL 以允许与这些规则不匹 配的所有其他流量。将 Web ACL 附加到 ECS 任务前面的 ALB。","D":"创建新的 AWS WAF Web ACL。在 AWS WAF 中创建新的空 IP 集。向 Web ACL 添加新规则以阻止源自新 IP 集中 IP 地址的请求。 创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于抓取发送 SQL 注入攻击的 IP 地址的 API 日志，并将这些 IP 地址添加到 IP 集中。将 Web ACL 附 加到 ECS 任务前面的 ALB。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":184,"question_en":"An environmental company is deploying sensors in major cities throughout a country to measure air quality. The sensors connect to AWS IoT Core to ingest timeseries data readings. The company stores the data in Amazon DynamoDB. For business continuity, the company must have the ability to ingest and store data in two AWS Regions. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家环保公司正在全国主要城市部署传感器来测量空气质量。传感器连接到 AWS IoT Core 以获取时间序列数据读数。该公司将数据 存储在 Amazon DynamoDB 中。 为了实现业务连续性，公司必须能够在两个 AWS 区域中提取和存储数据。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Route 53 alias failover routing policy with values for AWS IoT Core data endpoints in both Regions Migrate data to Amazon Aurora global tables.","B":"Create a domain configuration for AWS IoT Core in each Region. Create an Amazon Route 53 latency-based routing policy. Use AWS IoT Core data endpoints in both Regions as values. Migrate the data to Amazon MemoryDB for Redis and configure cross-Region replication.","C":"Create a domain configuration for AWS IoT Core in each Region. Create an Amazon Route 53 health check that evaluates domain configuration health. Create a failover routing policy with values for the domain name from the AWS IoT Core domain configurations. Update the DynamoDB table to a global table.","D":"Create an Amazon Route 53 latency-based routing policy. Use AWS IoT Core data endpoints in both Regions as values. Configure DynamoDB streams and cross-Region data replication."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用两个区域中的 AWS IoT Core 数据终端节点的值创建 Amazon Route 53 别名故障转移路由策略 将数据迁移到 Amazon Aurora 全局表。","B":"在每个区域中为 AWS IoT Core 创建域配置。创建 Amazon Route 53 基于延迟的路由策略。使用两个区域中的 AWS IoT Core 数据 终端节点作为值。将数据迁移到 Amazon MemoryDB for Redis 并配置跨区域复制。","C":"在每个区域中为 AWS IoT Core 创建域配置。创建评估域配置运行状况的 Amazon Route 53 运行状况检查。使用 AWS IoT Core 域 配置中的域名值创建故障转移路由策略。将 DynamoDB 表更新为全局表。","D":"创建 Amazon Route 53 基于延迟的路由策略。使用两个区域中的 AWS IoT Core 数据终端节点作为值。配置 DynamoDB 流和跨区 域数据复制。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":185,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations for a multi-account setup in the AWS Cloud. The company's finance team has a data processing application that uses AWS Lambda and Amazon DynamoDB. The company's marketing team wants to access the data that is stored in the DynamoDB table. The DynamoDB table contains confidential data. The marketing team can have access to only specific attributes of data in the DynamoDB table. The finance team and the marketing team have separate AWS accounts. What should a solutions architect do to provide the marketing team with the appropriate access to the DynamoDB table?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 在 AWS 云中进行多账户设置。该公司的财务团队拥有一个使用 AWS Lambda 和 Amazon DynamoDB 的数据处理应用程序。该公司的营销团队想要访问存储在 DynamoDB 表中的数据。 DynamoDB 表包含机密数据。营销团队只能访问 DynamoDB 表中数据的特定属性。财务团队和营销团队拥有独立的 AWS 账户。 解决方案架构师应该如何为营销团队提供对 DynamoDB 表的适当访问权限？","options_en":{"A":"Create an SCP to grant the marketing team's AWS account access to the specific attributes of the DynamoDB table. Attach the SCP to the OU of the finance team.","B":"Create an IAM role in the finance team's account by using IAM policy conditions for specific DynamoDB attributes (fine-grained access control). Establish trust with the marketing team's account. In the marketing team's account, create an IAM role that has permissions to assume the IAM role in the finance team's account.","C":"Create a resource-based IAM policy that includes conditions for specific DynamoDB attributes (fine-grained access control). Attach the policy to the DynamoDB table. In the marketing team's account, create an IAM role that has permissions to access the DynamoDB table in the finance team's account.","D":"Create an IAM role in the finance team's account to access the DynamoDB table. Use an IAM permissions boundary to limit the access to the specific attributes. In the marketing team's account, create an IAM role that has permissions to assume the IAM role in the finance team's account."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 SCP 以授予营销团队的 AWS 账户访问 DynamoDB 表的特定属性的权限。将 SCP 附加到财务团队的 OU。","B":"通过使用特定 DynamoDB 属性的 IAM 策略条件（细粒度访问控制），在财务团队的账户中创建 IAM 角色。与营销团队的帐户 建立信任。在营销团队的账户中，创建一个 IAM 角色，该角色有权代入财务团队账户中的 IAM 角色。","C":"创建基于资源的 IAM 策略，其中包括特定 DynamoDB 属性的条件（细粒度访问控制）。将策略附加到 DynamoDB 表。在营销团 队的账户中，创建一个 IAM 角色，该角色有权访问财务团队账户中的 DynamoDB 表。","D":"在财务团队的账户中创建 IAM 角色以访问 DynamoDB 表。使用 IAM 权限边界来限制对特定属性的访问。在营销团队的账户 中，创建一个 IAM 角色，该角色有权代入财务团队账户中的 IAM 角色。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":91},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":186,"question_en":"A solutions architect is creating an application that stores objects in an Amazon S3 bucket. The solutions architect must deploy the application in two AWS Regions that will be used simultaneously. The objects in the two S3 buckets must remain synchronized with each other. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"解决方案架构师正在创建一个将对象存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中的应用程序。解决方案架构师必须在将同时使用的两个 AWS 区域中 部署应用程序。两个 S3 存储桶中的对象必须保持彼此同步。 哪种步骤组合能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an S3 Multi-Region Access Point Change the application to refer to the Multi-Region Access Point","B":"Configure two-way S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) between the two S3 buckets","C":"Modify the application to store objects in each S3 bucket","D":"Create an S3 Lifecycle rule for each S3 bucket to copy objects from one S3 bucket to the other S3 bucket","E":"Enable S3 Versioning for each S3 bucket","F":"Configure an event notification for each S3 bucket to invoke an AWS Lambda function to copy objects from one S3 bucket to the other S3 bucket"},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 S3 多区域接入点 更改应用程序以引用多区域接入点","B":"在两个 S3 存储桶之间配置双向 S3 跨区域复制 (CRR)","C":"修改应用程序以在每个 S3 存储桶中存储对象","D":"为每个 S3 存储桶创建一条 S3 生命周期规则，将对象从一个 S3 存储桶复制到另一个 S3 存储桶","E":"为每个 S3 存储桶启用 S3 版本控制","F":"为每个 S3 存储桶配置事件通知，以调用 AWS Lambda 函数将对象从一个 S3 存储桶复制到另一个 S3 存储桶"},"answer":["A","B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ABE":100},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":187,"question_en":"A company has an IoT platform that runs in an on-premises environment. The platform consists of a server that connects to IoT devices by using the MQTT protocol. The platform collects telemetry data from the devices at least once every 5 minutes. The platform also stores device metadata in a MongoDB cluster. An application that is installed on an on-premises machine runs periodic jobs to aggregate and transform the telemetry and device metadata. The application creates reports that users view by using another web application that runs on the same on-premises machine. The periodic jobs take 120-600 seconds to run. However, the web application is always running. The company is moving the platform to AWS and must reduce the operational overhead of the stack. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个在本地环境中运行的 IoT 平台。该平台由使用 MQTT 协议连接到 IoT 设备的服务器组成。该平台至少每 5 分钟从设 备收集一次遥测数据。该平台还将设备元数据存储在 MongoDB 集群中。 安装在本地计算机上的应用程序运行定期作业来聚合和转换遥测数据和设备元数据。该应用程序创建用户通过使用在同一本地计算 机上运行的另一个 Web 应用程序查看的报告。定期作业需要 120-600 秒才能运行。但是，Web 应用程序始终在运行。 该公司正在将平台迁移到 AWS，并且必须减少堆栈的运营开销。 哪种步骤组合能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Lambda functions to connect to the IoT devices","B":"Configure the IoT devices to publish to AWS IoT Core","C":"Write the metadata to a self-managed MongoDB database on an Amazon EC2 instance","D":"Write the metadata to Amazon DocumentDB (with MongoDB compatibility)","E":"Use AWS Step Functions state machines with AWS Lambda tasks to prepare the reports and to write the reports to Amazon S3. Use Amazon CloudFront with an S3 origin to serve the reports","F":"Use an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster with Amazon EC2 instances to prepare the reports. Use an ingress controller in the EKS cluster to serve the reports"},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Lambda 函数连接到 IoT 设备","B":"配置 IoT 设备以发布到 AWS IoT Core","C":"将元数据写入 Amazon EC2 实例上的自管理 MongoDB 数据库","D":"将元数据写入 Amazon DocumentDB（与 MongoDB 兼容）","E":"将 AWS Step Functions 状态机与 AWS Lambda 任务结合使用来准备报告并将报告写入 Amazon S3。使用具有 S3 源的 Amazon CloudFront 来提供报告","F":"使用 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 集群和 Amazon EC2 实例来准备报告。使用 EKS 集群中的入口控制器来提 供报告"},"answer":["B","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BDE":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":188,"question_en":"A global manufacturing company plans to migrate the majority of its applications to AWS. However, the company is concerned about applications that need to remain within a specific country or in the company's central on-premises data center because of data regulatory requirements or requirements for latency of single-digit milliseconds. The company also is concerned about the applications that it hosts in some of its factory sites, where limited network infrastructure exists. The company wants a consistent developer experience so that its developers can build applications once and deploy on premises, in the cloud, or in a hybrid architecture. The developers must be able to use the same tools, APIs, and services that are familiar to them. Which solution will provide a consistent hybrid experience to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家全球制造公司计划将其大部分应用程序迁移到 AWS。然而，由于数据监管要求或对个位数毫秒延迟的要求，该公司担心需要保 留在特定国家或公司的中央本地数据中心内的应用程序。该公司还担心一些工厂站点托管的应用程序，这些工厂的网络基础设施有 限。 该公司希望获得一致的开发人员体验，以便开发人员只需构建一次应用程序即可在本地、云端或混合架构中进行部署。开发人员必 须能够使用他们熟悉的相同工具、API 和服务。 哪种解决方案将提供一致的混合体验来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate all applications to the closest AWS Region that is compliant. Set up an AWS Direct Connect connection between the central on- premises data center and AWS. Deploy a Direct Connect gateway.","B":"Use AWS Snowball Edge Storage Optimized devices for the applications that have data regulatory requirements or requirements for latency of single-digit milliseconds. Retain the devices on premises. Deploy AWS Wavelength to host the workloads in the factory sites.","C":"Install AWS Outposts for the applications that have data regulatory requirements or requirements for latency of single-digit milliseconds. Use AWS Snowball Edge Compute Optimized devices to host the workloads in the factory sites.","D":"Migrate the applications that have data regulatory requirements or requirements for latency of single-digit milliseconds to an AWS Local Zone. Deploy AWS Wavelength to host the workloads in the factory sites."},"options_zh":{"A":"将所有应用程序迁移到最近的合规 AWS 区域。在本地中央数据中心和 AWS 之间设置 AWS Direct Connect 连接。部署 Direct Connect 网关。","B":"对于具有数据监管要求或要求个位数毫秒延迟的应用程序，请使用 AWS Snowball Edge Storage Optimized 设备。将设备保留在 现场。部署 AWS Wavelength 以托管工厂站点中的工作负载。","C":"为有数据监管要求或要求个位数毫秒延迟的应用程序安装 AWS Outposts。使用 AWS Snowball Edge 计算优化设备托管工厂站点 中的工作负载。","D":"将有数据监管要求或延迟为个位数毫秒的应用程序迁移到 AWS 本地区域。部署 AWS Wavelength 以托管工厂站点中的工作负 载。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":82,"D":18},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":189,"question_en":"A company is updating an application that customers use to make online orders. The number of attacks on the application by bad actors has increased recently. The company will host the updated application on an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster. The company will use Amazon DynamoDB to store application data. A public Application Load Balancer (ALB) will provide end users with access to the application. The company must prevent attacks and ensure business continuity with minimal service interruptions during an ongoing attack. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在更新客户用于在线订购的应用程序。最近，不良行为者对应用程序的攻击数量有所增加。 该公司将在 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 集群上托管更新后的应用程序。该公司将使用 Amazon DynamoDB 来存储应 用程序数据。公共应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 将为最终用户提供对应用程序的访问权限。公司必须防止攻击并确保业务连续性，并 在持续攻击期间将服务中断降至最低。 哪种步骤组合能够最经济有效地满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution with the ALB as the origin. Add a custom header and random value on the CloudFront domain. Configure the ALB to conditionally forward tra®c if the header and value match.","B":"Deploy the application in two AWS Regions. Configure Amazon Route 53 to route to both Regions with equal weight.","C":"Configure auto scaling for Amazon ECS tasks Create a DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster.","D":"Configure Amazon ElastiCache to reduce overhead on DynamoDB.","E":"Deploy an AWS WAF web ACL that includes an appropriate rule group. Associate the web ACL with the Amazon CloudFront distribution."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建以 ALB 作为源的 Amazon CloudFront 分配。在 CloudFront 域上添加自定义标头和随机值。将 ALB 配置为在标头和值匹配时 有条件地转发流量。","B":"在两个 AWS 区域中部署应用程序。配置 Amazon Route 53 以同等权重路由到两个区域。","C":"为 Amazon ECS 任务配置自动扩展 创建 DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) 集群。","D":"配置 Amazon ElastiCache 以减少 DynamoDB 的开销。","E":"部署包含适当规则组的 AWS WAF Web ACL。将 Web ACL 与 Amazon CloudFront 分配关联。"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AE":93},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":190,"question_en":"A company runs a web application on AWS. The web application delivers static content from an Amazon S3 bucket that is behind an Amazon CloudFront distribution. The application serves dynamic content by using an Application Load Balancer (ALB) that distributes requests to a ­eet of Amazon EC2 instances in Auto Scaling groups. The application uses a domain name setup in Amazon Route 53. Some users reported occasional issues when the users attempted to access the website during peak hours. An operations team found that the ALB sometimes returned HTTP 503 Service Unavailable errors. The company wants to display a custom error message page when these errors occur. The page should be displayed immediately for this error code. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上运行 Web 应用程序。Web 应用程序从 Amazon CloudFront 分配后面的 Amazon S3 存储桶传送静态内容。该应用程 序通过使用应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 提供动态内容，该负载均衡器将请求分发到 Auto Scaling 组中的一组 Amazon EC2 实例。该应 用程序使用 Amazon Route 53 中的域名设置。 一些用户报告在高峰时段尝试访问网站时偶尔会出现问题。运营团队发现 ALB 有时会返回 HTTP 503 服务不可用错误。该公司希望 在发生这些错误时显示自定义错误消息页面。应立即显示此错误代码的页面。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up a Route 53 failover routing policy. Configure a health check to determine the status of the ALB endpoint and to fail over to the failover S3 bucket endpoint.","B":"Create a second CloudFront distribution and an S3 static website to host the custom error page. Set up a Route 53 failover routing policy. Use an active-passive configuration between the two distributions.","C":"Create a CloudFront origin group that has two origins. Set the ALB endpoint as the primary origin. For the secondary origin, set an S3 bucket that is configured to host a static website Set up origin failover for the CloudFront distribution. Update the S3 static website to incorporate the custom error page.","D":"Create a CloudFront function that validates each HTTP response code that the ALB returns. Create an S3 static website in an S3 bucket. Upload the custom error page to the S3 bucket as a failover. Update the function to read the S3 bucket and to serve the error page to the end users."},"options_zh":{"A":"设置 Route 53 故障转移路由策略。配置运行状况检查以确定 ALB 端点的状态并故障转移到故障转移 S3 存储桶端点。","B":"创建第二个 CloudFront 分配和一个 S3 静态网站来托管自定义错误页面。设置 Route 53 故障转移路由策略。在两个发行版之间 使用主动-被动配置。","C":"创建一个具有两个源的 CloudFront 源组。将 ALB 端点设置为主要原点。对于辅助源，设置配置为托管静态网站的 S3 存储桶 为 CloudFront 分配设置源故障转移。更新 S3 静态网站以合并自定义错误页面。","D":"创建一个 CloudFront 函数来验证 ALB 返回的每个 HTTP 响应代码。在 S3 存储桶中创建 S3 静态网站。将自定义错误页面上传到 S3 存储桶作为故障转移。更新函数以读取 S3 存储桶并向最终用户提供错误页面。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":60,"D":40},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":191,"question_en":"A company is planning to migrate an application to AWS. The application runs as a Docker container and uses an NFS version 4 file share. A solutions architect must design a secure and scalable containerized solution that does not require provisioning or management of the underlying infrastructure. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正计划将应用程序迁移到 AWS。该应用程序作为 Docker 容器运行并使用 NFS 版本 4 文件共享。 解决方案架构师必须设计一个安全且可扩展的容器化解决方案，该解决方案不需要配置或管理底层基础设施。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the application containers by using Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) with the Fargate launch type. Use Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) for shared storage. Reference the EFS file system ID, container mount point, and EFS authorization IAM role in the ECS task definition.","B":"Deploy the application containers by using Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) with the Fargate launch type. Use Amazon FSx for Lustre for shared storage. Reference the FSx for Lustre file system ID, container mount point, and FSx for Lustre authorization IAM role in the ECS task definition.","C":"Deploy the application containers by using Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) with the Amazon EC2 launch type and auto scaling turned on. Use Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) for shared storage. Mount the EFS file system on the ECS container instances. Add the EFS authorization IAM role to the EC2 instance profile.","D":"Deploy the application containers by using Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) with the Amazon EC2 launch type and auto scaling turned on. Use Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes with Multi-Attach enabled for shared storage. Attach the EBS volumes to ECS container instances. Add the EBS authorization IAM role to an EC2 instance profile."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 和 Fargate 启动类型来部署应用程序容器。使用 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 进行共享存储。在ECS任务定义中引用EFS文件系统ID、容器挂载点和EFS授权IAM角色。","B":"使用具有 Fargate 启动类型的 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 来部署应用程序容器。使用 Amazon FSx for Lustre 进行共享存储。在 ECS 任务定义中引用 FSx for Lustre 文件系统 ID、容器挂载点和 FSx for Lustre 授权 IAM 角色。","C":"使用 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 部署应用程序容器，并启用 Amazon EC2 启动类型和自动扩展。使用 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 进行共享存储。在ECS容器实例上挂载EFS文件系统。将 EFS 授权 IAM 角色添加到 EC2 实 例配置文件。","D":"使用 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 部署应用程序容器，并启用 Amazon EC2 启动类型和自动扩展。使用启用了 多重附加的 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 卷来实现共享存储。将 EBS 卷附加到 ECS 容器实例。将 EBS 授权 IAM 角色添 加到 EC2 实例配置文件。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Migration","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":192,"question_en":"A company is running an application in the AWS Cloud. The core business logic is running on a set of Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group. An Application Load Balancer (ALB) distributes tra®c to the EC2 instances. Amazon Route 53 record api.example.com is pointing to the ALB. The company's development team makes major updates to the business logic. The company has a rule that when changes are deployed, only 10% of customers can receive the new logic during a testing window. A customer must use the same version of the business logic during the testing window. How should the company deploy the updates to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 云中运行应用程序。核心业务逻辑在 Auto Scaling 组中的一组 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 将流量分配到 EC2 实例。Amazon Route 53 记录 api.example.com 指向 ALB。 公司开发团队对业务逻辑进行了重大更新。该公司有一条规则，即部署更改后，只有 10% 的客户可以在测试窗口期间收到新逻辑。 客户在测试窗口期间必须使用相同版本的业务逻辑。 公司应如何部署更新来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a second ALB, and deploy the new logic to a set of EC2 instances in a new Auto Scaling group. Configure the ALB to distribute tra®c to the EC2 instances. Update the Route 53 record to use weighted routing, and point the record to both of the ALBs.","B":"Create a second target group that is referenced by the ALDeploy the new logic to EC2 instances in this new target group. Update the ALB listener rule to use weighted target groups. Configure ALB target group stickiness.","C":"Create a new launch configuration for the Auto Scaling group. Specify the launch configuration to use the AutoScalingRollingUpdate policy, and set the MaxBatchSize option to 10. Replace the launch configuration on the Auto Scaling group. Deploy the changes.","D":"Create a second Auto Scaling group that is referenced by the ALB. Deploy the new logic on a set of EC2 instances in this new Auto Scaling group. Change the ALB routing algorithm to least outstanding requests (LOR). Configure ALB session stickiness."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建第二个 ALB，并将新逻辑部署到新 Auto Scaling 组中的一组 EC2 实例。配置 ALB 以将流量分配到 EC2 实例。更新 Route 53 记录以使用加权路由，并将记录指向两个 ALB。","B":"创建 AL 引用的第二个目标组，将新逻辑部署到此新目标组中的 EC2 实例。更新 ALB 侦听器规则以使用加权目标组。配置 ALB 目标组粘性。","C":"为 Auto Scaling 组创建新的启动配置。指定启动配置以使用 AutoScalingRollingUpdate 策略，并将 MaxBatchSize 选项设置为 10。替换 Auto Scaling 组上的启动配置。部署更改。","D":"创建 ALB 引用的第二个 Auto Scaling 组。在此新 Auto Scaling 组中的一组 EC2 实例上部署新逻辑。将 ALB 路由算法更改为最少 未完成请求 (LOR)。配置 ALB 会话粘性。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":193,"question_en":"A large education company recently introduced Amazon Workspaces to provide access to internal applications across multiple universities. The company is storing user profiles on an Amazon FSx for Windows File Server file system. The file system is configured with a DNS alias and is connected to a self-managed Active Directory. As more users begin to use the Workspaces, login time increases to unacceptable levels. An investigation reveals a degradation in performance of the file system. The company created the file system on HDD storage with a throughput of 16 MBps. A solutions architect must improve the performance of the file system during a defined maintenance window. What should the solutions architect do to meet these requirements with the LEAST administrative effort?","question_zh":"一家大型教育公司最近推出了 Amazon Workspaces，以提供对多所大学内部应用程序的访问。该公司将用户配置文件存储在 Amazon FSx for Windows File Server 文件系统上。文件系统配置有 DNS 别名并连接到自我管理的 Active Directory。随着越来越多的用户开始使 用工作区，登录时间会增加到不可接受的水平。 调查显示文件系统的性能下降。该公司在 HDD 存储上创建了吞吐量为 16 MBps 的文件系统。解决方案架构师必须在定义的维护时段 内提高文件系统的性能。 解决方案架构师应该如何做才能以最少的管理工作满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Backup to create a point-in-time backup of the file system. Restore the backup to a new FSx for Windows File Server file system. Select SSD as the storage type. Select 32 MBps as the throughput capacity. When the backup and restore process is completed, adjust the DNS alias accordingly. Delete the original file system.","B":"Disconnect users from the file system. In the Amazon FSx console, update the throughput capacity to 32 MBps. Update the storage type to SSD. Reconnect users to the file system.","C":"Deploy an AWS DataSync agent onto a new Amazon EC2 instance. Create a task. Configure the existing file system as the source location. Configure a new FSx for Windows File Server file system with SSD storage and 32 MBps of throughput as the target location. Schedule the task. When the task is completed, adjust the DNS alias accordingly. Delete the original file system.","D":"Enable shadow copies on the existing file system by using a Windows PowerShell command. Schedule the shadow copy job to create a point-in-time backup of the file system. Choose to restore previous versions. Create a new FSx for Windows File Server file system with SSD storage and 32 MBps of throughput. When the copy job is completed, adjust the DNS alias. Delete the original file system."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Backup 创建文件系统的时间点备份。将备份还原到新的 FSx for Windows File Server 文件系统。选择SSD作为存储类 型。选择 32 MBps 作为吞吐量。备份和恢复过程完成后，相应地调整 DNS 别名。删除原来的文件系统。","B":"断开用户与文件系统的连接。在 Amazon FSx 控制台中，将吞吐量更新为 32 MBps。将存储类型更新为SSD。将用户重新连接到 文件系统。","C":"将 AWS DataSync 代理部署到新的 Amazon EC2 实例上。创建任务。将现有文件系统配置为源位置。配置新的 FSx for Windows 文件服务器文件系统，将 SSD 存储和 32 MBps 的吞吐量作为目标位置。安排任务。任务完成后，相应地调整 DNS 别名。删除原 来的文件系统。","D":"使用 Windows PowerShell 命令在现有文件系统上启用卷影副本。安排卷影复制作业以创建文件系统的时间点备份。选择恢复以 前的版本。使用 SSD 存储和 32 MBps 的吞吐量创建新的 FSx for Windows 文件服务器文件系统。复制作业完成后，调整 DNS 别 名。删除原来的文件系统。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":53,"A":47},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Amazon FSx for Windows File Server supports modifying both throughput capacity and storage type in place on an existing file system, with no need to migrate data, rebuild the file system, or repoint the DNS alias. You can convert from HDD to SSD storage directly via the console/CLI (update-file-system with --storage-type SSD), and you can change throughput capacity to a valid value such as 32 MBps the same way. Because these operations happen during a brief window (Single-AZ file systems experience a very brief period of unavailability during a throughput change, which fits the defined maintenance window), option B accomplishes the performance improvement with the LEAST administrative effort. Options A, C, and D all unnecessarily build a brand-new file system, migrate data, and re-cut the DNS alias - far more work than the supported in-place updates. Note: changing both throughput and storage type are two separate AdministrativeActions, but both are simple managed operations and still constitute the lowest-effort path.","explanation_zh":"Amazon FSx for Windows File Server 支援在現有檔案系統上原地修改 throughput capacity 與 storage type，不需要遷移資料、重建檔案系統或重新指向 DNS alias。可以直接透過 console 或 CLI（update-file-system 搭配 --storage-type SSD）把 HDD 轉換為 SSD，也能以同樣方式把 throughput capacity 變更為 32 MBps 等有效值。由於這些操作只需短暫時間完成（Single-AZ 檔案系統在 throughput 變更時會有極短暫的不可用，符合題目所述的維護視窗），選項 B 以最少的管理工作達成效能提升。選項 A、C、D 都不必要地建立全新的檔案系統、遷移資料並重新切換 DNS alias，遠比受支援的原地更新繁瑣。注意：變更 throughput 與 storage type 屬於兩個獨立的 AdministrativeAction，但兩者都是簡單的受管操作，仍是工作量最低的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Using AWS Backup to restore to a new file system, then re-cutting the DNS alias and deleting the original, is far more administrative effort than the supported in-place SSD and throughput updates. There is no need to rebuild the file system at all.","why_zh":"用 AWS Backup 還原到新檔案系統，再重新切換 DNS alias 並刪除原系統，比受支援的原地 SSD 與 throughput 更新繁瑣許多，根本不需要重建檔案系統。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Deploying a DataSync agent on a new EC2 instance, building a new file system, scheduling a migration task, and re-cutting DNS is the most heavyweight option - the opposite of LEAST administrative effort.","why_zh":"在新的 EC2 上部署 DataSync agent、建立新檔案系統、排程遷移任務並重新切換 DNS，是最繁重的方案，與「最少管理工作」相反。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Shadow copies (VSS) are for end-user previous-version recovery, not for migrating an entire file system to new storage. This approach is technically inappropriate and also requires building a new file system and re-cutting DNS.","why_zh":"Shadow copies (VSS) 是供使用者還原檔案先前版本之用，並非用來把整個檔案系統遷移到新儲存。此做法技術上不合適，且同樣需要建立新檔案系統並重新切換 DNS。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/WindowsGuide/updating-storage-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/WindowsGuide/increase-throughput-capacity.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/WindowsGuide/managing-storage-configuration.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識"},{"id":194,"question_en":"A company hosts an application on AWS. The application reads and writes objects that are stored in a single Amazon S3 bucket. The company must modify the application to deploy the application in two AWS Regions. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上托管一个应用程序。该应用程序读取和写入存储在单个 Amazon S3 存储桶中的对象。该公司必须修改应用程序才 能将应用程序部署在两个 AWS 区域中。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up an Amazon CloudFront distribution with the S3 bucket as an origin. Deploy the application to a second Region Modify the application to use the CloudFront distribution. Use AWS Global Accelerator to access the data in the S3 bucket.","B":"Create a new S3 bucket in a second Region. Set up bidirectional S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) between the original S3 bucket and the new S3 bucket. Configure an S3 Multi-Region Access Point that uses both S3 buckets. Deploy a modified application to both Regions.","C":"Create a new S3 bucket in a second Region Deploy the application in the second Region. Configure the application to use the new S3 bucket. Set up S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) from the original S3 bucket to the new S3 bucket.","D":"Set up an S3 gateway endpoint with the S3 bucket as an origin. Deploy the application to a second Region. Modify the application to use the new S3 gateway endpoint. Use S3 Intelligent-Tiering on the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"设置以 S3 存储桶为源的 Amazon CloudFront 分配。将应用程序部署到第二个区域 修改应用程序以使用 CloudFront 发行版。使 用 AWS Global Accelerator 访问 S3 存储桶中的数据。","B":"在第二个区域中创建新的 S3 存储桶。在原始 S3 存储桶和新 S3 存储桶之间设置双向 S3 跨区域复制 (CRR)。配置使用两个 S3 存储桶的 S3 多区域接入点。将修改后的应用程序部署到两个区域。","C":"在第二个区域中创建新的 S3 存储桶 在第二个区域中部署应用程序。配置应用程序以使用新的 S3 存储桶。设置从原始 S3 存储 桶到新 S3 存储桶的 S3 跨区域复制 (CRR)。","D":"设置以 S3 存储桶为源的 S3 网关端点。将应用程序部署到第二个区域。修改应用程序以使用新的 S3 网关端点。在 S3 存储桶 上使用 S3 智能分层。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":81,"C":19},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":195,"question_en":"An online gaming company needs to rehost its gaming platform on AWS. The company's gaming application requires high performance computing (HPC) processing and has a leaderboard that changes frequently. An Ubuntu instance that is optimized for compute generation hosts a Node.js application for game display. Game state is tracked in an on-premises Redis instance. The company needs a migration strategy that optimizes application performance. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家在线游戏公司需要在 AWS 上重新托管其游戏平台。该公司的游戏应用程序需要高性能计算（HPC）处理，并且排行榜经常变 化。针对计算生成进行优化的 Ubuntu 实例托管用于游戏显示的 Node.js 应用程序。游戏状态在本地 Redis 实例中进行跟踪。 该公司需要一个优化应用程序性能的迁移策略。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Auto Scaling group of m5.large Amazon EC2 Spot Instances behind an Application Load Balancer. Use an Amazon ElastlCache for Redis cluster to maintain the leaderboard.","B":"Create an Auto Scaling group of c5.large Amazon EC2 Spot Instances behind an Application Load Balancer. Use an Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster to maintain the leaderboard.","C":"Create an Auto Scaling group of c5.large Amazon EC2 On-Demand Instances behind an Application Load Balancer. Use an Amazon ElastiCache for Redis cluster to maintain the leaderboard.","D":"Create an Auto Scaling group of m5.large Amazon EC2 On-Demand Instances behind an Application Load Balancer. Use an Amazon DynamoDB table to maintain the leaderboard."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Application Load Balancer 后面创建 m5.large Amazon EC2 Spot 实例的 Auto Scaling 组。使用 Amazon ElastlCache for Redis 集群 来维护排行榜。","B":"在 Application Load Balancer 后面创建一个由 c5.large Amazon EC2 Spot 实例组成的 Auto Scaling 组。使用 Amazon OpenSearch Service 集群来维护排行榜。","C":"在应用程序负载均衡器后面创建 c5.large Amazon EC2 按需实例的 Auto Scaling 组。使用 Amazon ElastiCache for Redis 集群来维 护排行榜。","D":"在应用程序负载均衡器后面创建 m5.large Amazon EC2 按需实例的 Auto Scaling 组。使用 Amazon DynamoDB 表来维护排行榜。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":196,"question_en":"A solutions architect is designing an application to accept timesheet entries from employees on their mobile devices. Timesheets will be submitted weekly, with most of the submissions occurring on Friday. The data must be stored in a format that allows payroll administrators to run monthly reports. The infrastructure must be highly available and scale to match the rate of incoming data and reporting requests. Which combination of steps meets these requirements while minimizing operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"解决方案架构师正在设计一个应用程序来接受员工在移动设备上输入的时间表条目。时间表将每周提交一次，大部分提交发生在周 五。数据的存储格式必须允许薪资管理员运行月度报告。基础设施必须具有高可用性并可扩展，以匹配传入数据和报告请求的速 率。 哪种步骤组合可以满足这些要求，同时最大限度地减少运营开销？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the application to Amazon EC2 On-Demand Instances with load balancing across multiple Availability Zones. Use scheduled Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling to add capacity before the high volume of submissions on Fridays.","B":"Deploy the application in a container using Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) with load balancing across multiple Availability Zones. Use scheduled Service Auto Scaling to add capacity before the high volume of submissions on Fridays.","C":"Deploy the application front end to an Amazon S3 bucket served by Amazon CloudFront. Deploy the application backend using Amazon API Gateway with an AWS Lambda proxy integration.","D":"Store the timesheet submission data in Amazon Redshift. Use Amazon QuickSight to generate the reports using Amazon Redshift as the data source.","E":"Store the timesheet submission data in Amazon S3. Use Amazon Athena and Amazon QuickSight to generate the reports using Amazon S3 as the data source."},"options_zh":{"A":"将应用程序部署到 Amazon EC2 按需实例，并在多个可用区之间实现负载平衡。使用计划的 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 在周五大 量提交之前增加容量。","B":"使用 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 在容器中部署应用程序，并在多个可用区之间实现负载平衡。使用计划的 服务 Auto Scaling 在周五大量提交之前增加容量。","C":"将应用程序前端部署到由 Amazon CloudFront 提供服务的 Amazon S3 存储桶。使用 Amazon API Gateway 与 AWS Lambda 代理集 成来部署应用程序后端。","D":"将时间表提交数据存储在 Amazon Redshift 中。使用 Amazon QuickSight 以 Amazon Redshift 作为数据源生成报告。","E":"将时间表提交数据存储在 Amazon S3 中。使用 Amazon Athena 和 Amazon QuickSight 以 Amazon S3 作为数据源生成报告。"},"answer":["B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"CE":46,"BE":38},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Analytics","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The question asks for two steps that are highly available, scale to match both incoming data (Friday spikes) and reporting requests, while MINIMIZING operational overhead. C provides a fully serverless front/back end: a static S3+CloudFront frontend and an API Gateway + Lambda proxy backend. API Gateway and Lambda scale automatically and instantly to absorb the unpredictable Friday submission spike with no capacity planning, no servers/containers to manage, and built-in multi-AZ high availability. E stores submissions in Amazon S3 (durable, infinitely scalable, HA) and uses Athena + QuickSight for monthly reports; per AWS docs, Athena is serverless with 'no infrastructure to set up or manage' and 'scales automatically,' making it ideal for infrequent monthly batch reporting at lowest overhead. Together C and E form an end-to-end serverless solution. B technically works but carries more operational overhead (ECS cluster/container management) and relies on SCHEDULED scaling that must predict capacity for an approximate ('most on Friday') load, whereas serverless reactively absorbs the spike. D (Redshift) is a provisioned data-warehouse cluster requiring sizing/management and is overkill for small weekly timesheet ingest plus monthly reports.","explanation_zh":"題目要求兩個步驟必須具備高可用、能隨進入資料量（週五尖峰）與報表需求自動擴展，並且把營運負擔降到最低。C 提供完全無伺服器的前後端：S3+CloudFront 的靜態前端，加上 API Gateway + Lambda proxy 整合的後端。API Gateway 與 Lambda 會自動且即時擴展，毋需容量規劃即可吸收難以預測的週五提交尖峰，沒有伺服器或容器需要管理，且原生跨多個 Availability Zone 達成高可用。E 將提交資料存入 Amazon S3（耐久、可無限擴展、高可用），再以 Athena + QuickSight 產生每月報表；依據 AWS 文件，Athena 為無伺服器服務，'no infrastructure to set up or manage' 並且 'scales automatically'，最適合低頻率的每月批次報表且營運負擔最低。C 與 E 合起來構成端到端的無伺服器方案。B 技術上可行，但帶來較高營運負擔（需管理 ECS 叢集/容器），且依賴需要預測容量的『排程』擴展來應付僅為大概值（'多數在週五'）的負載；而無伺服器可被動即時吸收尖峰。D（Redshift）為佈建型資料倉儲叢集，需要調整與管理，對小量每週工時資料寫入加每月報表而言過度。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"EC2 On-Demand with scheduled Auto Scaling has the highest operational overhead (instance provisioning, OS patching) and scheduled scaling must guess capacity for an approximate Friday spike, failing the 'minimize operational overhead' qualifier.","why_zh":"EC2 On-Demand 搭配排程 Auto Scaling 營運負擔最高（需佈建執行個體、修補作業系統），且排程擴展必須猜測週五尖峰的容量，無法滿足『最小化營運負擔』的限定條件。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"ECS still requires managing a cluster, task definitions, and containers, and scheduled Service Auto Scaling pre-provisions a fixed capacity based on a prediction of an approximate ('most on Friday') load. The fully serverless C scales reactively with less overhead, so C beats B on the decisive 'minimize operational overhead' qualifier.","why_zh":"ECS 仍需管理叢集、任務定義與容器，且排程式 Service Auto Scaling 會依據對大概負載（'多數在週五'）的預測預先佈建固定容量。完全無伺服器的 C 可被動擴展且負擔更低，因此在決定性的『最小化營運負擔』限定條件上 C 勝過 B。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Redshift is a provisioned data-warehouse cluster that requires node sizing, scaling, and management overhead; it is overkill for ingesting small weekly timesheet records and running only monthly reports, losing to the serverless S3+Athena option E.","why_zh":"Amazon Redshift 為佈建型資料倉儲叢集，需要節點規模調整、擴展與管理負擔；對於每週寫入少量工時記錄並僅需每月報表而言過度，敗給無伺服器的 S3+Athena（E）方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/set-up-lambda-proxy-integrations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-apigateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/when-should-i-use-ate.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識・複選"},{"id":197,"question_en":"A company is storing sensitive data in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company must log all activities for objects in the S3 bucket and must keep the logs for 5 years. The company's security team also must receive an email notification every time there is an attempt to delete data in the S3 bucket. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司将敏感数据存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。公司必须记录 S3 存储桶中对象的所有活动，并且必须将日志保留 5 年。每次尝试 删除 S3 存储桶中的数据时，公司的安全团队还必须收到电子邮件通知。 哪种步骤组合能够最经济有效地满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS CloudTrail to log S3 data events.","B":"Configure S3 server access logging for the S3 bucket.","C":"Configure Amazon S3 to send object deletion events to Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES).","D":"Configure Amazon S3 to send object deletion events to an Amazon EventBridge event bus that publishes to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic.","E":"Configure Amazon S3 to send the logs to Amazon Timestream with data storage tiering.","F":"Configure a new S3 bucket to store the logs with an S3 Lifecycle policy."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS CloudTrail 以记录 S3 数据事件。","B":"为 S3 存储桶配置 S3 服务器访问日志记录。","C":"配置 Amazon S3 以将对象删除事件发送到 Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES)。","D":"配置 Amazon S3 以将对象删除事件发送到 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线，该事件总线发布到 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 主题。","E":"配置 Amazon S3 以将日志发送到具有数据存储分层的 Amazon Timestream。","F":"配置新的 S3 存储桶以使用 S3 生命周期策略存储日志。"},"answer":["A","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ADF":60,"BDF":39},"tags":["Storage","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・複選"},{"id":198,"question_en":"A company is building a hybrid environment that includes servers in an on-premises data center and in the AWS Cloud. The company has deployed Amazon EC2 instances in three VPCs. Each VPC is in a different AWS Region. The company has established an AWS Direct. Connect connection to the data center from the Region that is closest to the data center. The company needs the servers in the on-premises data center to have access to the EC2 instances in all three VPCs. The servers in the on- premises data center also must have access to AWS public services. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST cost? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在构建一个混合环境，其中包括本地数据中心和 AWS 云中的服务器。该公司已在三个 VPC 中部署了 Amazon EC2 实例。 每个 VPC 位于不同的 AWS 区域。该公司已建立 AWS Direct。从距离数据中心最近的区域连接到数据中心。 该公司需要本地数据中心的服务器能够访问所有三个 VPC 中的 EC2 实例。本地数据中心的服务器也必须能够访问AWS公共服务。 哪种步骤组合能够以最少的成本满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a Direct Connect gateway in the Region that is closest to the data center. Attach the Direct Connect connection to the Direct Connect gateway. Use the Direct Connect gateway to connect the VPCs in the other two Regions.","B":"Set up additional Direct Connect connections from the on-premises data center to the other two Regions.","C":"Create a private VIF. Establish an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection over the private VIF to the VPCs in the other two Regions.","D":"Create a public VIF. Establish an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection over the public VIF to the VPCs in the other two Regions.","E":"Use VPC peering to establish a connection between the VPCs across the Regions Create a private VIF with the existing Direct Connect connection to connect to the peered VPCs."},"options_zh":{"A":"在距离数据中心最近的区域创建专线网关。将 Direct Connect 连接附加到 Direct Connect 网关。使用专线网关连接另外两个 Region的VPC。","B":"设置从本地数据中心到其他两个区域的额外 Direct Connect 连接。","C":"创建私有 VIF。通过私有 VIF 与其他两个区域中的 VPC 建立 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 连接。","D":"创建公共 VIF。通过公共 VIF 与其他两个区域中的 VPC 建立 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 连接。","E":"使用 VPC 对等在跨区域的 VPC 之间建立连接 使用现有 Direct Connect 连接创建私有 VIF 以连接到对等 VPC。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AD":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":199,"question_en":"A company is using an organization in AWS Organizations to manage hundreds of AWS accounts. A solutions architect is working on a solution to provide baseline protection for the Open Web Application Security Project (OWASP) top 10 web application vulnerabilities. The solutions architect is using AWS WAF for all existing and new Amazon CloudFront distributions that are deployed within the organization. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect take to provide the baseline protection? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS Organizations 中的组织来管理数百个 AWS 账户。解决方案架构师正在开发一种解决方案，为开放 Web 应用 程序安全项目 (OWASP) 十大 Web 应用程序漏洞提供基线保护。解决方案架构师将 AWS WAF 用于组织内部署的所有现有和新的 Amazon CloudFront 发行版。 解决方案架构师应采取哪些步骤组合来提供基线保护？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Enable AWS Config in all accounts","B":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty in all accounts","C":"Enable all features for the organization","D":"Use AWS Firewall Manager to deploy AWS WAF rules in all accounts for all CloudFront distributions","E":"Use AWS Shield Advanced to deploy AWS WAF rules in all accounts for all CloudFront distributions","F":"Use AWS Security Hub to deploy AWS WAF rules in all accounts for all CloudFront distributions"},"options_zh":{"A":"在所有账户中启用 AWS Config","B":"在所有账户中启用 Amazon GuardDuty","C":"启用组织的所有功能","D":"使用 AWS Firewall Manager 在所有 CloudFront 分配的所有账户中部署 AWS WAF 规则","E":"使用 AWS Shield Advanced 在所有 CloudFront 分配的所有账户中部署 AWS WAF 规则","F":"使用 AWS Security Hub 在所有 CloudFront 分配的所有账户中部署 AWS WAF 规则"},"answer":["C","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ACD":72},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The goal is to deploy AWS WAF rules (OWASP Top 10 baseline) centrally across all existing and new CloudFront distributions in hundreds of accounts in an AWS Organization. AWS Firewall Manager is the purpose-built service for centrally deploying and enforcing WAF web ACLs across all member accounts, including automatically protecting new resources (D). Firewall Manager has two hard, documented prerequisites: (1) the organization must be enabled for 'all features' in AWS Organizations (C), and (2) AWS Config must be enabled in every member account and Region so Firewall Manager can detect resources and monitor policy compliance; for WAF policies you must enable Config for the CloudFront Distribution resource type (A). Therefore A, C, and D are all required. Shield Advanced (E) provides DDoS protection and managing WAF via Shield Advanced still relies on Firewall Manager for org-wide deployment, and it is not the mechanism for org-wide WAF distribution here. Security Hub (F) aggregates security findings and does not deploy WAF rules. GuardDuty (B) is a threat-detection service and plays no role in deploying WAF baseline protection.","explanation_zh":"目標是在 AWS Organization 中數百個帳戶的所有現有與新建 CloudFront distribution 上集中部署 AWS WAF 規則（OWASP Top 10 基線防護）。AWS Firewall Manager 是專為跨所有成員帳戶集中部署與強制套用 WAF web ACL 而設計的服務，並能自動保護新建的資源（D）。Firewall Manager 有兩個明文記載的必要前置條件：(1) 組織必須在 AWS Organizations 中啟用 'all features'（C）；(2) 每個成員帳戶與區域都必須啟用 AWS Config，Firewall Manager 才能偵測資源並監控政策合規狀態；對於 WAF policy，必須為 CloudFront Distribution 資源類型啟用 Config（A）。因此 A、C、D 三者皆為必需。Shield Advanced（E）提供 DDoS 防護，透過 Shield Advanced 管理 WAF 仍依賴 Firewall Manager 進行組織範圍的部署，並非此處組織範圍 WAF 部署的機制。Security Hub（F）彙整安全發現項，並不部署 WAF 規則。GuardDuty（B）為威脅偵測服務，與部署 WAF 基線防護無關。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon GuardDuty is a threat-detection service that analyzes logs for malicious activity; it does not deploy or manage AWS WAF rules and is not a Firewall Manager prerequisite.","why_zh":"Amazon GuardDuty 是分析日誌偵測惡意活動的威脅偵測服務；它不部署或管理 AWS WAF 規則，也非 Firewall Manager 的前置條件。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"AWS Shield Advanced provides DDoS protection. It does not itself deploy WAF rules across an organization's CloudFront distributions; org-wide WAF rule deployment is done via Firewall Manager.","why_zh":"AWS Shield Advanced 提供 DDoS 防護，本身不會跨組織的 CloudFront distribution 部署 WAF 規則；組織範圍的 WAF 規則部署是透過 Firewall Manager 完成。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"AWS Security Hub aggregates and prioritizes security findings against standards; it cannot deploy or push AWS WAF rules to accounts. This is the option the ExamTopics dump wrongly chose instead of A.","why_zh":"AWS Security Hub 彙整並依標準排序安全發現項；它無法部署或推送 AWS WAF 規則到各帳戶。這正是 ExamTopics dump 誤選用以取代 A 的選項。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/fms-prereq.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/join-aws-orgs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/enable-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/aws-config-firewall-manager-findings.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_org_support-all-features.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・複選"},{"id":200,"question_en":"A solutions architect has implemented a SAML 2.0 federated identity solution with their company's on-premises identity provider (IdP) to authenticate users' access to the AWS environment. When the solutions architect tests authentication through the federated identity web portal, access to the AWS environment is granted. However, when test users attempt to authenticate through the federated identity web portal, they are not able to access the AWS environment. Which items should the solutions architect check to ensure identity federation is properly configured? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"解决方案架构师与其公司的本地身份提供商 (IdP) 实施了 SAML 2.0 联合身份解决方案，以验证用户对 AWS 环境的访问权限。当解决 方案架构师通过联合身份 Web 门户测试身份验证时，将授予对 AWS 环境的访问权限。但是，当测试用户尝试通过联合身份 Web 门 户进行身份验证时，他们无法访问 AWS 环境。 解决方案架构师应检查哪些项目以确保身份联合配置正确？（选择三项。） 答： IAM 用户的权限策略允许该用户使用 SAML 联合。","options_en":{"A":"The IAM user's permissions policy has allowed the use of SAML federation for that user.","B":"Test users are not in the AWSFederatedUsers group in the company's IdP.","C":"The web portal calls the AWS STS AssumeRoleWithSAML API with the ARN of the SAML provider, the ARN of the IAM role, and the SAML assertion from IdP.","D":"The on-premises IdP's DNS hostname is reachable from the AWS environment VPCs.","E":"The company's IdP defines SAML assertions that properly map users or groups. In the company to IAM roles with appropriate permissions."},"options_zh":{"B":"测试用户不在公司 IdP 的 AWSFederatedUsers 组中。","C":"Web 门户使用 SAML 提供商的 ARN、IAM 角色的 ARN 以及来自 IdP 的 SAML 断言调用 AWS STS AssumeRoleWithSAML API。","D":"本地 IdP 的 DNS 主机名可从 AWS 环境 VPC 访问。","E":"公司的 IdP 定义了正确映射用户或组的 SAML 断言。在公司中给IAM角色赋予适当的权限。"},"answer":["B","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BCE":71},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"This is SAML 2.0 federation, which uses IAM roles (not IAM users) and STS AssumeRoleWithSAML. The architect's own login succeeds while test users fail, so the items to check are the legitimate federation-configuration components plus the user-mapping that differs between the architect and the test users. C is verbatim from the AWS docs: the client/web portal calls sts:AssumeRoleWithSAML passing the ARN of the SAML provider, the ARN of the IAM role, and the SAML assertion from the IdP. E is also directly from the configuration steps: in the IdP you define SAML assertions (the https://aws.amazon.com/SAML/Attributes/Role attribute) that map users or groups to IAM roles with appropriate permissions. B is the failure-mode check: the architect maps to a role because of their IdP group membership, but the test users are not in the IdP group that grants the AWS role mapping, so their assertion contains no usable Role attribute and assume-role fails. A is wrong because SAML federation does not involve IAM users or an 'IAM user permissions policy allowing SAML federation.' D is wrong because AWS/STS never reaches out to the on-premises IdP over DNS; the IdP authenticates the user and the client passes the signed assertion to STS, so VPC reachability to the IdP is irrelevant. The dump's BDF answer is invalid (no option F exists and D is technically false).","explanation_zh":"本題情境為 SAML 2.0 federation，使用的是 IAM role（而非 IAM user）與 STS AssumeRoleWithSAML。架構師本人登入成功但測試使用者失敗，因此要檢查的是合法的 federation 設定元件，以及架構師與測試使用者之間不同的使用者對應。C 幾乎是 AWS 文件原文：用戶端/入口網站呼叫 sts:AssumeRoleWithSAML，傳入 SAML provider 的 ARN、IAM role 的 ARN，以及來自 IdP 的 SAML assertion。E 同樣出自設定步驟：在 IdP 中定義 SAML assertion（https://aws.amazon.com/SAML/Attributes/Role 屬性），將使用者或群組對應到具備適當權限的 IAM role。B 是失敗成因的檢查點：架構師因其 IdP 群組成員身分而對應到 role，但測試使用者不在能授予 AWS role 對應的 IdP 群組中，因此其 assertion 中沒有可用的 Role 屬性，導致 assume-role 失敗。A 錯誤，因為 SAML federation 不涉及 IAM user，也沒有所謂『允許 SAML federation 的 IAM user 權限政策』。D 錯誤，因為 AWS/STS 從不透過 DNS 連向地端 IdP；IdP 驗證使用者後由用戶端把已簽署的 assertion 傳給 STS，因此 VPC 對 IdP 的網路可達性無關緊要。Dump 的 BDF 答案無效（不存在 F 選項，且 D 在技術上是錯的）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SAML 2.0 federation does not use IAM users at all; the design goal is to avoid creating an IAM user per person. There is no 'IAM user permissions policy that allows SAML federation' - federated access is granted via an IAM role trust policy and AssumeRoleWithSAML, not via an IAM user policy.","why_zh":"SAML 2.0 federation 完全不使用 IAM user；其設計目的就是避免為每個人建立 IAM user。並不存在『允許 SAML federation 的 IAM user 權限政策』——federated 存取是透過 IAM role 的 trust policy 與 AssumeRoleWithSAML 授予，而非透過 IAM user policy。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS STS never connects to the on-premises IdP. Per the AWS flow, the IdP authenticates the user and builds the SAML assertion, then the client passes that signed assertion to STS AssumeRoleWithSAML. AWS validates it with the uploaded IdP metadata certificate, so DNS/network reachability from AWS VPCs to the IdP is not required and is irrelevant to federation working.","why_zh":"AWS STS 從不連向地端 IdP。依 AWS 流程，IdP 先驗證使用者並建立 SAML assertion，接著由用戶端把已簽署的 assertion 傳給 STS AssumeRoleWithSAML。AWS 以上傳的 IdP metadata 憑證驗證，因此 AWS VPC 到 IdP 的 DNS/網路可達性並非必要，也與 federation 是否運作無關。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_providers_saml.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_providers_create_saml_assertions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/STS/latest/APIReference/API_AssumeRoleWithSAML.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・複選"},{"id":201,"question_en":"A solutions architect needs to improve an application that is hosted in the AWS Cloud. The application uses an Amazon Aurora MySQL DB instance that is experiencing overloaded connections. Most of the application’s operations insert records into the database. The application currently stores credentials in a text-based configuration file. The solutions architect needs to implement a solution so that the application can handle the current connection load. The solution must keep the credentials secure and must provide the ability to rotate the credentials automatically on a regular basis. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师需要改进托管在 AWS 云中的应用程序。该应用程序使用连接过载的 Amazon Aurora MySQL 数据库实例。大多数应用 程序的操作都会将记录插入数据库。该应用程序当前将凭据存储在基于文本的配置文件中。 解决方案架构师需要实现一个解决方案，以便应用程序可以处理当前的连接负载。该解决方案必须保证凭证的安全，并且必须提供 定期自动轮换凭证的能力。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an Amazon RDS Proxy layer. In front of the DB instance. Store the connection credentials as a secret in AWS Secrets Manager.","B":"Deploy an Amazon RDS Proxy layer in front of the DB instance. Store the connection credentials in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store","C":"Create an Aurora Replica. Store the connection credentials as a secret in AWS Secrets Manager","D":"Create an Aurora Replica. Store the connection credentials in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署 Amazon RDS 代理层。在数据库实例前面。将连接凭证作为密钥存储在 AWS Secrets Manager 中。","B":"在数据库实例前面部署 Amazon RDS 代理层。将连接凭证存储在 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store 中","C":"创建 Aurora 副本。将连接凭证作为密钥存储在 AWS Secrets Manager 中","D":"创建 Aurora 副本。将连接凭证存储在 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store 中。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":202,"question_en":"A company needs to build a disaster recovery (DR) solution for its ecommerce website. The web application is hosted on a ­eet of t3.large Amazon EC2 instances and uses an Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance. The EC2 instances are in an Auto Scaling group that extends across multiple Availability Zones. In the event of a disaster, the web application must fail over to the secondary environment with an RPO of 30 seconds and an RTO of 10 minutes. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司需要为其电子商务网站构建灾难恢复 (DR) 解决方案。该 Web 应用程序托管在一组 t3.large Amazon EC2 实例上，并使用 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库实例。EC2 实例位于跨多个可用区的 Auto Scaling 组中。 如果发生灾难，Web 应用程序必须故障转移到辅助环境，RPO 为 30 秒，RTO 为 10 分钟。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use infrastructure as code (IaC) to provision the new infrastructure in the DR Region. Create a cross-Region read replica for the DB instance. Set up a backup plan in AWS Backup to create cross-Region backups for the EC2 instances and the DB instance. Create a cron expression to back up the EC2 instances and the DB instance every 30 seconds to the DR Region. Recover the EC2 instances from the latest EC2 backup. Use an Amazon Route 53 geolocation routing policy to automatically fail over to the DR Region in the event of a disaster.","B":"Use infrastructure as code (IaC) to provision the new infrastructure in the DR Region. Create a cross-Region read replica for the DB instance. Set up AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery to continuously replicate the EC2 instances to the DR Region. Run the EC2 instances at the minimum capacity in the DR Region. Use an Amazon Route 53 failover routing policy to automatically fail over to the DR Region in the event of a disaster. Increase the desired capacity of the Auto Scaling group.","C":"Set up a backup plan in AWS Backup to create cross-Region backups for the EC2 instances and the DB instance. Create a cron expression to back up the EC2 instances and the DB instance every 30 seconds to the DR Region. Use infrastructure as code (IaC) to provision the new infrastructure in the DR Region. Manually restore the backed-up data on new instances. Use an Amazon Route 53 simple routing policy to automatically fail over to the DR Region in the event of a disaster.","D":"Use infrastructure as code (IaC) to provision the new infrastructure in the DR Region. Create an Amazon Aurora global database. Set up AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery to continuously replicate the EC2 instances to the DR Region. Run the Auto Scaling group of EC2 instances at full capacity in the DR Region. Use an Amazon Route 53 failover routing policy to automatically fail over to the DR Region in the event of a disaster."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用基础设施即代码 (IaC) 在 DR 区域配置新的基础设施。为数据库实例创建跨区域只读副本。在 AWS Backup 中设置备份计 划，为 EC2 实例和数据库实例创建跨区域备份。创建一个 cron 表达式，每 30 秒将 EC2 实例和数据库实例备份到 DR 区域。从最 新的 EC2 备份恢复 EC2 实例。使用 Amazon Route 53 地理位置路由策略在发生灾难时自动故障转移到 DR 区域。","B":"使用基础设施即代码 (IaC) 在 DR 区域配置新的基础设施。为数据库实例创建跨区域只读副本。设置 AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery 以将 EC2 实例持续复制到灾难恢复区域。在 DR 区域中以最小容量运行 EC2 实例。使用 Amazon Route 53 故障转移路由 策略在发生灾难时自动故障转移到 DR 区域。增加 Auto Scaling 组的所需容量。","C":"在 AWS Backup 中设置备份计划，为 EC2 实例和数据库实例创建跨区域备份。创建一个 cron 表达式，每 30 秒将 EC2 实例和数 据库实例备份到 DR 区域。使用基础设施即代码 (IaC) 在灾难恢复区域中配置新的基础设施。在新实例上手动恢复备份数据。使 用 Amazon Route 53 简单路由策略在发生灾难时自动故障转移到 DR 区域。","D":"使用基础设施即代码 (IaC) 在 DR 区域配置新的基础设施。创建 Amazon Aurora 全局数据库。设置 AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery 以将 EC2 实例持续复制到灾难恢复区域。在 DR 区域中以满负荷运行 EC2 实例的 Auto Scaling 组。使用 Amazon Route 53 故障转移 路由策略在发生灾难时自动故障转移到 DR 区域。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":89},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":203,"question_en":"A company is planning a one-time migration of an on-premises MySQL database to Amazon Aurora MySQL in the us-east-1 Region. The company's current internet connection has limited bandwidth. The on-premises MySQL database is 60 TB in size. The company estimates that it will take a month to transfer the data to AWS over the current internet connection. The company needs a migration solution that will migrate the database more quickly. Which solution will migrate the database in the LEAST amount of time?","question_zh":"一家公司正计划将本地 MySQL 数据库一次性迁移到 us-east-1 区域的 Amazon Aurora MySQL。该公司当前的互联网连接带宽有限。本 地MySQL数据库大小为60 TB。该公司估计，通过当前的互联网连接将数据传输到 AWS 需要一个月的时间。该公司需要一个能够更快 地迁移数据库的迁移解决方案。 哪种解决方案将在最短的时间内迁移数据库？","options_en":{"A":"Request a 1 Gbps AWS Direct Connect connection between the on-premises data center and AWS. Use AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to migrate the on-premises MySQL database to Aurora MySQL.","B":"Use AWS DataSync with the current internet connection to accelerate the data transfer between the on-premises data center and AWS. Use AWS Application Migration Service to migrate the on-premises MySQL database to Aurora MySQL.","C":"Order an AWS Snowball Edge device. Load the data into an Amazon S3 bucket by using the S3 interface. Use AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to migrate the data from Amazon S3 to Aurora MySQL.","D":"Order an AWS Snowball device. Load the data into an Amazon S3 bucket by using the S3 Adapter for Snowball. Use AWS Application Migration Service to migrate the data from Amazon S3 to Aurora MySQL."},"options_zh":{"A":"请求本地数据中心和 AWS 之间的 1 Gbps AWS Direct Connect 连接。使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 将本地 MySQL 数据库迁移到 Aurora MySQL。","B":"在当前互联网连接下使用 AWS DataSync 来加速本地数据中心和 AWS 之间的数据传输。使用 AWS Application Migration Service 将本地 MySQL 数据库迁移到 Aurora MySQL。","C":"订购 AWS Snowball Edge 设备。使用 S3 接口将数据加载到 Amazon S3 存储桶中。使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 将数据从 Amazon S3 迁移到 Aurora MySQL。","D":"订购 AWS Snowball 设备。使用适用于 Snowball 的 S3 适配器将数据加载到 Amazon S3 存储桶中。使用 AWS Application Migration Service 将数据从 Amazon S3 迁移到 Aurora MySQL。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":97},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":204,"question_en":"A company has an application in the AWS Cloud. The application runs on a ­eet of 20 Amazon EC2 instances. The EC2 instances are persistent and store data on multiple attached Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes. The company must maintain backups in a separate AWS Region. The company must be able to recover the EC2 instances and their configuration within 1 business day, with loss of no more than 1 day's worth of data. The company has limited staff and needs a backup solution that optimizes operational e®ciency and cost. The company already has created an AWS CloudFormation template that can deploy the required network configuration in a secondary Region. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 云中拥有一个应用程序。该应用程序在由 20 个 Amazon EC2 实例组成的队列上运行。EC2 实例是持久性的，并将数 据存储在多个附加的 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 卷上。 公司必须在单独的 AWS 区域维护备份。公司必须能够在 1 个工作日内恢复 EC2 实例及其配置，并且丢失的数据不超过 1 天。该公司 人员有限，需要一个能够优化运营效率和成本的备份解决方案。该公司已经创建了一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，可以在辅助区域 中部署所需的网络配置。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a second CloudFormation template that can recreate the EC2 instances in the secondary Region. Run daily multivolume snapshots by using AWS Systems Manager Automation runbooks. Copy the snapshots to the secondary Region. In the event of a failure launch the CloudFormation templates, restore the EBS volumes from snapshots, and transfer usage to the secondary Region.","B":"Use Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager (Amazon DLM) to create daily multivolume snapshots of the EBS volumes. In the event of a failure, launch the CloudFormation template and use Amazon DLM to restore the EBS volumes and transfer usage to the secondary Region.","C":"Use AWS Backup to create a scheduled daily backup plan for the EC2 instances. Configure the backup task to copy the backups to a vault in the secondary Region. In the event of a failure, launch the CloudFormation template, restore the instance volumes and configurations from the backup vault, and transfer usage to the secondary Region.","D":"Deploy EC2 instances of the same size and configuration to the secondary Region. Configure AWS DataSync daily to copy data from the primary Region to the secondary Region. In the event of a failure, launch the CloudFormation template and transfer usage to the secondary Region."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建第二个 CloudFormation 模板，该模板可以在辅助区域中重新创建 EC2 实例。使用 AWS Systems Manager Automation Runbook 运行每日多卷快照。将快照复制到辅助区域。如果发生故障，启动 CloudFormation 模板，从快照恢复 EBS 卷，并将使用 情况转移到辅助区域。","B":"使用 Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager (Amazon DLM) 创建 EBS 卷的每日多卷快照。如果发生故障，启动 CloudFormation 模板并使 用 Amazon DLM 恢复 EBS 卷并将使用情况转移到辅助区域。","C":"使用 AWS Backup 为 EC2 实例创建计划的每日备份计划。配置备份任务以将备份复制到次要区域中的保管库。如果发生故障， 启动 CloudFormation 模板，从备份保管库恢复实例卷和配置，并将使用情况转移到辅助区域。","D":"将相同大小和配置的 EC2 实例部署到辅助区域。每天配置 AWS DataSync 以将数据从主要区域复制到次要区域。如果发生故 障，启动 CloudFormation 模板并将使用转移到辅助区域。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":84,"B":16},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":205,"question_en":"A company is designing a new website that hosts static content. The website will give users the ability to upload and download large files. According to company requirements, all data must be encrypted in transit and at rest. A solutions architect is building the solution by using Amazon S3 and Amazon CloudFront. Which combination of steps will meet the encryption requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在设计一个托管静态内容的新网站。该网站将使用户能够上传和下载大文件。根据公司要求，所有数据在传输和静态时 都必须加密。解决方案架构师正在使用 Amazon S3 和 Amazon CloudFront 构建解决方案。 哪种步骤组合可以满足加密要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Turn on S3 server-side encryption for the S3 bucket that the web application uses.","B":"Add a policy attribute of \"aws:SecureTransport\": \"true\" for read and write operations in the S3 ACLs.","C":"Create a bucket policy that denies any unencrypted operations in the S3 bucket that the web application uses.","D":"Configure encryption at rest on CloudFront by using server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS).","E":"Configure redirection of HTTP requests to HTTPS requests in CloudFront.","F":"Use the RequireSSL option in the creation of presigned URLs for the S3 bucket that the web application uses."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 Web 应用程序使用的 S3 存储桶启用 S3 服务器端加密。","B":"在 S3 ACL 中为读写操作添加策略属性“aws:SecureTransport”:“true”。","C":"创建存储桶策略，拒绝 Web 应用程序使用的 S3 存储桶中的任何未加密操作。","D":"通过使用带有 AWS KMS 密钥的服务器端加密 (SSE-KMS) 在 CloudFront 上配置静态加密。","E":"在 CloudFront 中配置 HTTP 请求到 HTTPS 请求的重定向。","F":"在为 Web 应用程序使用的 S3 存储桶创建预签名 URL 时使用 RequireSSL 选项。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ACE":94},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":206,"question_en":"A company is implementing a serverless architecture by using AWS Lambda functions that need to access a Microsoft SQL Server DB instance on Amazon RDS. The company has separate environments for development and production, including a clone of the database system. The company's developers are allowed to access the credentials for the development database. However, the credentials for the production database must be encrypted with a key that only members of the IT security team's IAM user group can access. This key must be rotated on a regular basis. What should a solutions architect do in the production environment to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用需要访问 Amazon RDS 上的 Microsoft SQL Server 数据库实例的 AWS Lambda 函数来实施无服务器架构。该公司拥有 独立的开发和生产环境，包括数据库系统的克隆。 该公司的开发人员可以访问开发数据库的凭据。但是，生产数据库的凭证必须使用只有 IT 安全团队的 IAM 用户组成员才能访问的密 钥进行加密。该密钥必须定期轮换。 解决方案架构师应该在生产环境中做什么来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Store the database credentials in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store by using a SecureString parameter that is encrypted by an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key. Attach a role to each Lambda function to provide access to the SecureString parameter. Restrict access to the SecureString parameter and the customer managed key so that only the IT security team can access the parameter and the key.","B":"Encrypt the database credentials by using the AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) default Lambda key. Store the credentials in the environment variables of each Lambda function. Load the credentials from the environment variables in the Lambda code. Restrict access to the KMS key so that only the IT security team can access the key.","C":"Store the database credentials in the environment variables of each Lambda function. Encrypt the environment variables by using an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key. Restrict access to the customer managed key so that only the IT security team can access the key.","D":"Store the database credentials in AWS Secrets Manager as a secret that is associated with an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key. Attach a role to each Lambda function to provide access to the secret. Restrict access to the secret and the customer managed key so that only the IT security team can access the secret and the key."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用由 AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) 客户管理密钥加密的 SecureString 参数将数据库凭证存储在 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store 中。将角色附加到每个 Lambda 函数以提供对 SecureString 参数的访问。限制对 SecureString 参数和客户 管理密钥的访问，以便只有 IT 安全团队才能访问该参数和密钥。","B":"使用 AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) 默认 Lambda 密钥加密数据库凭证。将凭证存储在每个 Lambda 函数的环境变量 中。从 Lambda 代码中的环境变量加载凭证。限制对 KMS 密钥的访问，以便只有 IT 安全团队才能访问该密钥。","C":"将数据库凭证存储在每个 Lambda 函数的环境变量中。使用 AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) 客户托管密钥加密环境变 量。限制对客户管理密钥的访问，以便只有 IT 安全团队才能访问该密钥。","D":"将数据库凭证作为与 AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) 客户托管密钥关联的密钥存储在 AWS Secrets Manager 中。将角色 附加到每个 Lambda 函数以提供对密钥的访问。限制对机密和客户管理密钥的访问，以便只有 IT 安全团队才能访问机密和密 钥。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":76,"A":24},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":207,"question_en":"An online retail company is migrating its legacy on-premises .NET application to AWS. The application runs on load-balanced frontend web servers, load-balanced application servers, and a Microsoft SQL Server database. The company wants to use AWS managed services where possible and does not want to rewrite the application. A solutions architect needs to implement a solution to resolve scaling issues and minimize licensing costs as the application scales. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家在线零售公司正在将其遗留的本地 .NET 应用程序迁移到 AWS。该应用程序在负载平衡的前端 Web 服务器、负载平衡的应用程 序服务器和 Microsoft SQL Server 数据库上运行。 该公司希望尽可能使用 AWS 托管服务，并且不想重写应用程序。解决方案架构师需要实施一个解决方案来解决扩展问题并在应用程 序扩展时最大限度地降低许可成本。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer for the web tier and for the application tier. Use Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL with Babelfish turned on to replatform the SQL Server database.","B":"Create images of all the servers by using AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS). Deploy Amazon EC2 instances that are based on the on-premises imports. Deploy the instances in an Auto Scaling group behind a Network Load Balancer for the web tier and for the application tier. Use Amazon DynamoDB as the database tier.","C":"Containerize the web frontend tier and the application tier. Provision an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster. Create an Auto Scaling group behind a Network Load Balancer for the web tier and for the application tier. Use Amazon RDS for SQL Server to host the database.","D":"Separate the application functions into AWS Lambda functions. Use Amazon API Gateway for the web frontend tier and the application tier. Migrate the data to Amazon S3. Use Amazon Athena to query the data."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Web 层和应用程序层的应用程序负载均衡器后面的 Auto Scaling 组中部署 Amazon EC2 实例。使用启用 Babelfish 的 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL 来重构 SQL Server 数据库的平台。","B":"使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 创建所有服务器的映像。部署基于本地导入的 Amazon EC2 实例。在 Web 层和 应用程序层的网络负载均衡器后面的 Auto Scaling 组中部署实例。使用 Amazon DynamoDB 作为数据库层。","C":"将 Web 前端层和应用程序层容器化。预置 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 集群。在网络负载均衡器后面为 Web 层和应用程序层创建 Auto Scaling 组。使用 Amazon RDS for SQL Server 托管数据库。","D":"将应用程序函数分离为 AWS Lambda 函数。将 Amazon API Gateway 用于 Web 前端层和应用程序层。将数据迁移到 Amazon S3。 使用 Amazon Athena 查询数据。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":85,"C":15},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Analytics","Containers"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":208,"question_en":"A software-as-a-service (SaaS) provider exposes APIs through an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The ALB connects to an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster that is deployed in the us-east-1 Region. The exposed APIs contain usage of a few non-standard REST methods: LINK, UNLINK, LOCK, and UNLOCK. Users outside the United States are reporting long and inconsistent response times for these APIs. A solutions architect needs to resolve this problem with a solution that minimizes operational overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"软件即服务 (SaaS) 提供商通过应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 公开 API。ALB 连接到部署在 us-east-1 区域中的 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 集群。公开的 API 包含一些非标准 REST 方法的使用：LINK、UNLINK、LOCK 和 UNLOCK。 美国境外的用户报告这些 API 的响应时间长且不一致。解决方案架构师需要通过最小化运营开销的解决方案来解决此问题。 哪种解决方案满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add an Amazon CloudFront distribution. Configure the ALB as the origin.","B":"Add an Amazon API Gateway edge-optimized API endpoint to expose the APIs. Configure the ALB as the target.","C":"Add an accelerator in AWS Global Accelerator. Configure the ALB as the origin.","D":"Deploy the APIs to two additional AWS Regions: eu-west-1 and ap-southeast-2. Add latency-based routing records in Amazon Route 53."},"options_zh":{"A":"添加 Amazon CloudFront 分配。将 ALB 配置为源。","B":"添加 Amazon API Gateway 边缘优化的 API 终端节点以公开 API。将 ALB 配置为目标。","C":"在 AWS Global Accelerator 中添加加速器。将 ALB 配置为源。","D":"将 API 部署到另外两个 AWS 区域：eu-west-1 和 ap-southeast-2。在 Amazon Route 53 中添加基于延迟的路由记录。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":72,"B":22},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":209,"question_en":"A company runs an IoT application in the AWS Cloud. The company has millions of sensors that collect data from houses in the United States. The sensors use the MQTT protocol to connect and send data to a custom MQTT broker. The MQTT broker stores the data on a single Amazon EC2 instance. The sensors connect to the broker through the domain named iot.example.com. The company uses Amazon Route 53 as its DNS service. The company stores the data in Amazon DynamoDB. On several occasions, the amount of data has overloaded the MQTT broker and has resulted in lost sensor data. The company must improve the reliability of the solution. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 云中运行 IoT 应用程序。该公司拥有数百万个传感器，从美国的房屋收集数据。传感器使用 MQTT 协议连接并向自 定义 MQTT 代理发送数据。MQTT 代理将数据存储在单个 Amazon EC2 实例上。传感器通过名为 iot.example.com 的域连接到代理。该 公司使用 Amazon Route 53 作为其 DNS 服务。该公司将数据存储在 Amazon DynamoDB 中。 在某些情况下，数据量使 MQTT 代理超载并导致传感器数据丢失。公司必须提高解决方案的可靠性。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and an Auto Scaling group for the MQTT broker. Use the Auto Scaling group as the target for the ALB. Update the DNS record in Route 53 to an alias record. Point the alias record to the ALB. Use the MQTT broker to store the data.","B":"Set up AWS IoT Core to receive the sensor data. Create and configure a custom domain to connect to AWS IoT Core. Update the DNS record in Route 53 to point to the AWS IoT Core Data-ATS endpoint. Configure an AWS IoT rule to store the data.","C":"Create a Network Load Balancer (NLB). Set the MQTT broker as the target. Create an AWS Global Accelerator accelerator. Set the NLB as the endpoint for the accelerator. Update the DNS record in Route 53 to a multivalue answer record. Set the Global Accelerator IP addresses as values. Use the MQTT broker to store the data.","D":"Set up AWS IoT Greengrass to receive the sensor data. Update the DNS record in Route 53 to point to the AWS IoT Greengrass endpoint. Configure an AWS IoT rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to store the data."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 MQTT 代理创建应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 和 Auto Scaling 组。使用 Auto Scaling 组作为 ALB 的目标。将 Route 53 中的 DNS 记录更新为别名记录。将别名记录指向 ALB。使用 MQTT 代理来存储数据。","B":"设置 AWS IoT Core 以接收传感器数据。创建并配置自定义域以连接到 AWS IoT Core。更新 Route 53 中的 DNS 记录以指向 AWS IoT Core Data-ATS 终端节点。配置 AWS IoT 规则来存储数据。","C":"创建网络负载均衡器 (NLB)。将 MQTT 代理设置为目标。创建 AWS Global Accelerator 加速器。将 NLB 设置为加速器的端点。将 Route 53 中的 DNS 记录更新为多值应答记录。将全局加速器 IP 地址设置为值。使用 MQTT 代理来存储数据。","D":"设置 AWS IoT Greengrass 以接收传感器数据。更新 Route 53 中的 DNS 记录以指向 AWS IoT Greengrass 终端节点。配置 AWS IoT 规则以调用 AWS Lambda 函数来存储数据。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The root cause is a single self-managed MQTT broker on one EC2 instance that gets overloaded and loses data. Option B replaces this fragile component with AWS IoT Core, a fully managed service that natively handles MQTT and scales to millions of concurrent device connections, eliminating the single-instance bottleneck. AWS IoT Core supports a customer-managed (custom) domain configuration, so the company can keep its brand identity at iot.example.com and point the Route 53 record to the AWS IoT Core Data-ATS endpoint via the custom domain, requiring no device-side URL change. An AWS IoT rule action can write incoming MQTT messages directly to DynamoDB. This is the only option that addresses the actual reliability problem.","explanation_zh":"問題根因是單一自管的 MQTT broker 跑在一台 EC2 instance 上,流量過載導致感測器資料遺失。選項 B 以 AWS IoT Core 取代此脆弱元件,AWS IoT Core 是全託管服務,原生支援 MQTT 並可擴展到數百萬個並行裝置連線,徹底消除單一 instance 瓶頸。AWS IoT Core 支援 customer-managed(custom)domain configuration,公司可保留 iot.example.com 的品牌識別,並透過 custom domain 將 Route 53 記錄指向 AWS IoT Core Data-ATS endpoint,裝置端無需更改 URL。AWS IoT rule action 可將進入的 MQTT 訊息直接寫入 DynamoDB。這是唯一真正解決可靠性問題的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An Application Load Balancer is a Layer 7 HTTP/HTTPS load balancer and cannot load balance raw MQTT, which runs over TCP; MQTT requires a Network Load Balancer. It also keeps the self-managed broker and does not solve per-instance overload reliably.","why_zh":"Application Load Balancer 是 Layer 7 的 HTTP/HTTPS 負載平衡器,無法負載平衡走 TCP 的原生 MQTT;MQTT 需要 Network Load Balancer。且它仍保留自管 broker,無法可靠解決單機過載。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"NLB and Global Accelerator only improve network routing and availability, but the data is still stored on a single EC2 MQTT broker, which is the exact component being overloaded. The root cause of lost data remains unaddressed.","why_zh":"NLB 與 Global Accelerator 只改善網路路由與可用性,但資料仍儲存在單一 EC2 MQTT broker 上,而這正是過載的元件。資料遺失的根因並未被解決。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS IoT Greengrass is an edge/local runtime that runs on devices at the edge to process data locally; it is not a cloud-side MQTT ingestion endpoint that millions of distributed home sensors connect to over the internet via DNS. There is no Greengrass DNS endpoint for fleet ingestion, so this does not fit the architecture.","why_zh":"AWS IoT Greengrass 是在邊緣裝置上執行、進行本地端資料處理的邊緣執行階段,並非數百萬分散家庭感測器透過 DNS 連線的雲端 MQTT 接收 endpoint。Greengrass 沒有供整個 fleet 接收資料的 DNS endpoint,因此不符合此架構。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/iot-domain-configuration-what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/iot-custom-endpoints-configurable-custom.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/dynamodb-rule-action.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/mqtt.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/greengrass/v2/developerguide/what-is-iot-greengrass.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":210,"question_en":"A company has Linux-based Amazon EC2 instances. Users must access the instances by using SSH with EC2 SSH key pairs. Each machine requires a unique EC2 key pair. The company wants to implement a key rotation policy that will, upon request, automatically rotate all the EC2 key pairs and keep the keys in a securely encrypted place. The company will accept less than 1 minute of downtime during key rotation. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有基于 Linux 的 Amazon EC2 实例。用户必须使用 SSH 和 EC2 SSH 密钥对来访问实例。每台机器都需要唯一的 EC2 密钥 对。 该公司希望实施密钥轮换策略，该策略将根据请求自动轮换所有 EC2 密钥对并将密钥保存在安全加密的位置。公司将接受密钥轮换 期间少于 1 分钟的停机时间。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Store all the keys in AWS Secrets Manager. Define a Secrets Manager rotation schedule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to generate new key pairs. Replace public keys on EC2 instances. Update the private keys in Secrets Manager.","B":"Store all the keys in Parameter Store, a capability of AWS Systems Manager, as a string. Define a Systems Manager maintenance window to invoke an AWS Lambda function to generate new key pairs. Replace public keys on EC2 instances. Update the private keys in Parameter Store.","C":"Import the EC2 key pairs into AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS). Configure automatic key rotation for these key pairs. Create an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to initiate the key rotation in AWS KMS.","D":"Add all the EC2 instances to Fleet Manager, a capability of AWS Systems Manager. Define a Systems Manager maintenance window to issue a Systems Manager Run Command document to generate new key pairs and to rotate public keys to all the instances in Fleet Manager."},"options_zh":{"A":"将所有密钥存储在 AWS Secrets Manager 中。定义 Secrets Manager 轮换计划以调用 AWS Lambda 函数来生成新的密钥对。替换 EC2 实例上的公钥。更新 Secrets Manager 中的私钥。","B":"将所有密钥存储在 Parameter Store（AWS Systems Manager 的一项功能）中作为字符串。定义 Systems Manager 维护时段以调 用 AWS Lambda 函数来生成新的密钥对。替换 EC2 实例上的公钥。更新 Parameter Store 中的私钥。","C":"将 EC2 密钥对导入 AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS)。为这些密钥对配置自动密钥轮换。创建 Amazon EventBridge 计划 规则以调用 AWS Lambda 函数以启动 AWS KMS 中的密钥轮换。","D":"将所有 EC2 实例添加到 Fleet Manager（AW​S Systems Manager 的一项功能）。定义 Systems Manager 维护时段以发出 Systems Manager 运行命令文档以生成新的密钥对并将公钥轮换到 Fleet Manager 中的所有实例。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":81,"D":19},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":211,"question_en":"A company wants to migrate to AWS. The company is running thousands of VMs in a VMware ESXi environment. The company has no configuration management database and has little knowledge about the utilization of the VMware portfolio. A solutions architect must provide the company with an accurate inventory so that the company can plan for a cost-effective migration. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司想要迁移到 AWS。该公司在 VMware ESXi 环境中运行数千台虚拟机。该公司没有配置管理数据库，并且对 VMware 产品组 合的利用知之甚少。 解决方案架构师必须为公司提供准确的清单，以便公司能够规划经济高效的迁移。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager to deploy Migration Evaluator to each VM. Review the collected data in Amazon QuickSight. Identify servers that have high utilization. Remove the servers that have high utilization from the migration list. Import the data to AWS Migration Hub.","B":"Export the VMware portfolio to a .csv file. Check the disk utilization for each server. Remove servers that have high utilization. Export the data to AWS Application Migration Service. Use AWS Server Migration Service (AWS SMS) to migrate the remaining servers.","C":"Deploy the Migration Evaluator agentless collector to the ESXi hypervisor. Review the collected data in Migration Evaluator. Identify inactive servers. Remove the inactive servers from the migration list. Import the data to AWS Migration Hub.","D":"Deploy the AWS Application Migration Service Agent to each VM. When the data is collected, use Amazon Redshift to import and analyze the data. Use Amazon QuickSight for data visualization."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager 将 Migration Evaluator 部署到每个虚拟机。在 Amazon QuickSight 中查看收集的数据。 识别利用率高的服务器。从迁移列表中删除利用率较高的服务器。将数据导入到 AWS Migration Hub。","B":"将 VMware 产品组合导出到 .csv 文件。检查每个服务器的磁盘利用率。删除利用率高的服务器。将数据导出到 AWS Application Migration Service。使用 AWS Server Migration Service (AWS SMS) 迁移其余服务器。","C":"将 Migration Evaluator 无代理收集器部署到 ESXi 管理程序。在迁移评估器中查看收集的数据。识别不活动的服务器。从迁移列 表中删除不活动的服务器。将数据导入到 AWS Migration Hub。","D":"将 AWS Application Migration Service Agent 部署到每个虚拟机。收集数据后，使用 Amazon Redshift 导入并分析数据。使用 Amazon QuickSight 进行数据可视化。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Migration","Database","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":212,"question_en":"A company runs a microservice as an AWS Lambda function. The microservice writes data to an on-premises SQL database that supports a limited number of concurrent connections. When the number of Lambda function invocations is too high, the database crashes and causes application downtime. The company has an AWS Direct Connect connection between the company's VPC and the on-premises data center. The company wants to protect the database from crashes. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司将微服务作为 AWS Lambda 函数运行。微服务将数据写入支持有限数量并发连接的本地 SQL 数据库。当Lambda函数调用次 数过多时，数据库崩溃并导致应用程序停机。该公司在其 VPC 和本地数据中心之间建立了 AWS Direct Connect 连接。该公司希望保 护数据库免遭崩溃。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Write the data to an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Configure the Lambda function to read from the queue and write to the existing database. Set a reserved concurrency limit on the Lambda function that is less than the number of connections that the database supports.","B":"Create a new Amazon Aurora Serverless DB cluster. Use AWS DataSync to migrate the data from the existing database to Aurora Serverless. Reconfigure the Lambda function to write to Aurora.","C":"Create an Amazon RDS Proxy DB instance. Attach the RDS Proxy DB instance to the Amazon RDS DB instance. Reconfigure the Lambda function to write to the RDS Proxy DB instance.","D":"Write the data to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Invoke the Lambda function to write to the existing database when the topic receives new messages. Configure provisioned concurrency for the Lambda function to be equal to the number of connections that the database supports."},"options_zh":{"A":"将数据写入 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列。配置 Lambda 函数以从队列中读取数据并将其写入现有数据库。 对 Lambda 函数设置保留并发限制，该限制小于数据库支持的连接数。","B":"创建新的 Amazon Aurora Serverless 数据库集群。使用 AWS DataSync 将数据从现有数据库迁移到 Aurora Serverless。重新配置 Lambda 函数以写入 Aurora。","C":"创建 Amazon RDS 代理数据库实例。将 RDS 代理数据库实例附加到 Amazon RDS 数据库实例。重新配置 Lambda 函数以写入 RDS 代理数据库实例。","D":"将数据写入 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 主题。当主题收到新消息时，调用 Lambda 函数写入现有数据库。 将 Lambda 函数的预置并发配置为等于数据库支持的连接数。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":93},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The database has a limited number of concurrent connections and crashes when too many Lambda invocations hit it at once. The fix must decouple the spike and cap concurrent writers. Option A does both: SQS buffers/decouples the incoming traffic so messages are not lost during spikes, and a reserved concurrency limit set below the database's connection limit guarantees Lambda never opens more concurrent connections than the database can handle. AWS Lambda documentation explicitly states reserved concurrency 'can be used for limiting concurrency to prevent overwhelming downstream resources, like database connections' and that it acts as an upper bound. This is the canonical pattern for throttling Lambda against a connection-limited backend, and it keeps the existing on-premises database (reachable over Direct Connect) without migration or unsupported services.","explanation_zh":"該資料庫支援的並行連線數有限,當 Lambda 同時呼叫過多時就會崩潰造成停機。正確解法必須同時做到兩件事:吸收突發流量並限制同時寫入的數量。選項 A 兩者皆達成:Amazon SQS 作為緩衝佇列解耦傳入流量,確保突發期間訊息不會遺失;在 Lambda 上設定低於資料庫連線上限的 reserved concurrency,可保證 Lambda 開啟的並行連線數永遠不會超過資料庫能承受的範圍。AWS Lambda 官方文件明確指出 reserved concurrency 'can be used for limiting concurrency to prevent overwhelming downstream resources, like database connections',且其同時作為並行數的上限。這是針對連線受限後端節流 Lambda 的標準模式,並且保留既有的地端資料庫(透過 Direct Connect 連線),無須遷移或使用不支援的服務。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Migrating to Aurora Serverless is a heavy, unnecessary re-architecture that abandons the on-premises database; the requirement is to protect the existing database, not replace it. Also, AWS DataSync is for file/object data transfer (NFS, SMB, S3), not for migrating relational SQL database data.","why_zh":"遷移到 Aurora Serverless 是過度且不必要的重構,放棄了既有地端資料庫;需求是保護現有資料庫而非替換它。此外,AWS DataSync 用於檔案/物件資料傳輸(NFS、SMB、S3),並非用於遷移關聯式 SQL 資料庫資料。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"RDS Proxy only works with Amazon RDS and Amazon Aurora database instances. The database here is an on-premises SQL database, so it cannot be attached to RDS Proxy at all; the option even references 'the Amazon RDS DB instance' which does not exist in this scenario.","why_zh":"RDS Proxy 僅支援 Amazon RDS 與 Amazon Aurora 資料庫執行個體。本題的資料庫是地端 SQL 資料庫,根本無法掛載到 RDS Proxy;該選項甚至提到本情境中不存在的 'Amazon RDS DB instance'。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SNS is pub/sub and does not buffer/queue messages for delayed throttled processing; it fans out immediately, so it cannot smooth spikes. Provisioned concurrency pre-initializes environments to reduce cold starts but does NOT cap maximum concurrency, so Lambda can still scale past the connection limit and crash the database. Setting it equal to the connection count also leaves zero headroom.","why_zh":"SNS 屬於發布/訂閱模式,不會緩衝或排隊訊息以進行延遲節流處理;它會立即扇出,無法平滑突發流量。Provisioned concurrency 是預先初始化執行環境以減少冷啟動,並不會限制最大並行數,因此 Lambda 仍可能超過連線上限而使資料庫崩潰。將其設為等於連線數也完全沒有保留餘裕。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-concurrency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/lambda-concurrency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/rds-proxy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-sqs.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":213,"question_en":"A company uses a Grafana data visualization solution that runs on a single Amazon EC2 instance to monitor the health of the company's AWS workloads. The company has invested time and effort to create dashboards that the company wants to preserve. The dashboards need to be highly available and cannot be down for longer than 10 minutes. The company needs to minimize ongoing maintenance. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司使用在单个 Amazon EC2 实例上运行的 Grafana 数据可视化解决方案来监控公司 AWS 工作负载的运行状况。该公司投入了 时间和精力来创建公司希望保留的仪表板。仪表板需要具有高可用性，并且停机时间不能超过 10 分钟。公司需要最大限度地减少持 续维护。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate to Amazon CloudWatch dashboards. Recreate the dashboards to match the existing Grafana dashboards. Use automatic dashboards where possible.","B":"Create an Amazon Managed Grafana workspace. Configure a new Amazon CloudWatch data source. Export dashboards from the existing Grafana instance. Import the dashboards into the new workspace.","C":"Create an AMI that has Grafana pre-installed. Store the existing dashboards in Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS). Create an Auto Scaling group that uses the new AMI. Set the Auto Scaling group's minimum, desired, and maximum number of instances to one. Create an Application Load Balancer that serves at least two Availability Zones.","D":"Configure AWS Backup to back up the EC2 instance that runs Grafana once each hour. Restore the EC2 instance from the most recent snapshot in an alternate Availability Zone when required."},"options_zh":{"A":"迁移到 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板。重新创建仪表板以匹配现有的 Grafana 仪表板。尽可能使用自动仪表板。","B":"创建 Amazon Managed Grafana 工作区。配置新的 Amazon CloudWatch 数据源。从现有 Grafana 实例导出仪表板。将仪表板导入 新工作区。","C":"创建预安装 Grafana 的 AMI。将现有控制面板存储在 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 中。创建使用新 AMI 的 Auto Scaling 组。将 Auto Scaling 组的最小实例数、所需实例数和最大实例数设置为 1。创建至少为两个可用区提供服务的应用程序负 载均衡器。","D":"配置 AWS Backup 以每小时备份一次运行 Grafana 的 EC2 实例。需要时，从备用可用区中的最新快照还原 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":94},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":214,"question_en":"A company needs to migrate its customer transactions database from on premises to AWS. The database resides on an Oracle DB instance that runs on a Linux server. According to a new security requirement, the company must rotate the database password each year. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司需要将其客户交易数据库从本地迁移到 AWS。该数据库驻留在 Linux 服务器上运行的 Oracle 数据库实例上。根据新的安全 要求，该公司必须每年轮换数据库密码。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Convert the database to Amazon DynamoDB by using the AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT). Store the password in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to invoke an AWS Lambda function for yearly passtard rotation.","B":"Migrate the database to Amazon RDS for Oracle. Store the password in AWS Secrets Manager. Turn on automatic rotation. Configure a yearly rotation schedule.","C":"Migrate the database to an Amazon EC2 instance. Use AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store to keep and rotate the connection string by using an AWS Lambda function on a yearly schedule.","D":"Migrate the database to Amazon Neptune by using the AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT). Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to invoke an AWS Lambda function for yearly password rotation."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) 将数据库转换为 Amazon DynamoDB。将密码存储在 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store 中。创建 Amazon CloudWatch 警报以调用 AWS Lambda 函数以进行每年密码轮换。","B":"将数据库迁移到 Amazon RDS for Oracle。将密码存储在 AWS Secrets Manager 中。开启自动旋转。配置年度轮换计划。","C":"将数据库迁移到 Amazon EC2 实例。使用 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store 通过使用 AWS Lambda 函数按年度计划保留和 轮换连接字符串。","D":"使用 AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) 将数据库迁移到 Amazon Neptune。创建 Amazon CloudWatch 警报以调用 AWS Lambda 函数以进行每年的密码轮换。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Migration","Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The customer transactions database is a relational Oracle workload. Migrating it to Amazon RDS for Oracle is a like-to-like, fully managed move that requires no schema conversion, and RDS handles patching, backups, and HA. Storing the credential in AWS Secrets Manager and turning on automatic rotation with a yearly schedule satisfies the annual password-rotation requirement with the least operational overhead because Secrets Manager natively integrates with RDS to rotate the credential in both the secret and the database without any custom code to maintain. The other options either re-architect a relational database into the wrong engine (DynamoDB key-value, Neptune graph) or self-manage Oracle on EC2 with custom Lambda rotation, all of which add significant operational burden.","explanation_zh":"客戶交易資料庫是關聯式 Oracle 工作負載。將其遷移至 Amazon RDS for Oracle 是同質、全託管的遷移，不需要結構轉換，且 RDS 會負責修補、備份與高可用性。將憑證存放於 AWS Secrets Manager 並開啟自動輪替（設定為每年一次）即可以最低營運負擔滿足每年輪替密碼的需求，因為 Secrets Manager 與 RDS 原生整合，會同時更新 secret 與資料庫中的憑證，且無需維護任何自訂程式碼。其他選項不是把關聯式資料庫改造成錯誤的引擎（DynamoDB 鍵值、Neptune 圖形），就是在 EC2 上自管 Oracle 並用自訂 Lambda 輪替，皆會大幅增加營運負擔。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Converting a relational transactions database to Amazon DynamoDB (key-value/NoSQL) is a major re-architecture, not least overhead, and Parameter Store with a custom CloudWatch-triggered Lambda is hand-built rotation. CloudWatch alarms are not a scheduling/rotation mechanism for credentials.","why_zh":"將關聯式交易資料庫轉換為 Amazon DynamoDB（鍵值/NoSQL）是重大架構改造，營運負擔最高；Parameter Store 搭配自訂 CloudWatch 觸發的 Lambda 是手工輪替，且 CloudWatch 警報並非憑證排程或輪替機制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Running Oracle on an EC2 instance is fully self-managed (OS/DB patching, backups, HA all manual), the highest operational overhead. Parameter Store has no native database-credential rotation, so a custom Lambda must be built and maintained.","why_zh":"在 EC2 上執行 Oracle 為完全自管（作業系統/資料庫修補、備份、高可用性皆需手動），營運負擔最高。Parameter Store 沒有原生的資料庫憑證輪替功能，必須自行建置與維護 Lambda。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Neptune is a graph database and is the wrong engine for a relational transactions workload; AWS SCT does not target Neptune. A CloudWatch alarm plus custom Lambda for password rotation is hand-built and not least overhead.","why_zh":"Amazon Neptune 是圖形資料庫，對關聯式交易工作負載而言是錯誤引擎；AWS SCT 也不支援轉換至 Neptune。以 CloudWatch 警報加自訂 Lambda 進行密碼輪替屬手工方案，並非最低營運負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/rotating-secrets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/intro.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/database-authentication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/auth-and-access.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":215,"question_en":"A solutions architect is designing an AWS account structure for a company that consists of multiple teams. All the teams will work in the same AWS Region. The company needs a VPC that is connected to the on-premises network. The company expects less than 50 Mbps of total tra®c to and from the on-premises network. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"解决方案架构师正在为一家由多个团队组成的公司设计 AWS 账户结构。所有团队都将在同一 AWS 区域工作。公司需要一个连接到 本地网络的VPC。该公司预计进出本地网络的总流量将低于 50 Mbps。 哪种步骤组合能够最经济有效地满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template that provisions a VPC and the required subnets. Deploy the template to each AWS account.","B":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template that provisions a VPC and the required subnets. Deploy the template to a shared services account. Share the subnets by using AWS Resource Access Manager.","C":"Use AWS Transit Gateway along with an AWS Site-to-Site VPN for connectivity to the on-premises network. Share the transit gateway by using AWS Resource Access Manager.","D":"Use AWS Site-to-Site VPN for connectivity to the on-premises network.","E":"Use AWS Direct Connect for connectivity to the on-premises network."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板来预置 VPC 和所需的子网。将模板部署到每个 AWS 账户。","B":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板来预置 VPC 和所需的子网。将模板部署到共享服务帐户。使用 AWS Resource Access Manager 共享子网。","C":"使用 AWS Transit Gateway 和 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 连接到本地网络。使用 AWS Resource Access Manager 共享中转网关。","D":"使用 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 连接到本地网络。","E":"使用 AWS Direct Connect 连接到本地网络。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BD":70,"BC":20},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The two dimensions are the account/VPC structure for multiple teams and the on-premises connectivity, and the qualifier is MOST cost-effective. For structure, Option B (provision one VPC in a shared services account and share its subnets via AWS Resource Access Manager) is the documented cost-effective pattern: it reduces the number of VPCs to create and manage, lets every team launch resources into one centrally managed VPC while keeping separate accounts for billing and access control, and crucially requires only ONE on-premises connection. For connectivity, Option D (AWS Site-to-Site VPN) is the cheapest option and its standard tunnels deliver up to 1.25 Gbps per tunnel, far exceeding the required <50 Mbps. Option A (a VPC per account) is not cost-effective because it creates VPC sprawl and would need either multiple VPN connections or a Transit Gateway to reach on-premises from each VPC. Option C (Transit Gateway + VPN) adds per-attachment hourly and per-GB data-processing charges that are unnecessary for a single shared VPC at low bandwidth, and Option E (Direct Connect) carries expensive dedicated port fees and a physical cross-connect that are massive overkill for <50 Mbps. Thus B+D is the most cost-effective combination.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個面向：多團隊的帳號/VPC 架構，以及與地端網路的連線；限定條件是「最具成本效益」。在架構面，選項 B（在 shared services 帳號建立一個 VPC，並透過 AWS Resource Access Manager 分享子網路）是官方文件記載的成本效益模式：可減少需建立與管理的 VPC 數量，讓各團隊在同一個集中管理的 VPC 內部署資源，同時以不同帳號維持帳單與存取控制，最關鍵的是只需要「一條」地端連線。在連線面，選項 D（AWS Site-to-Site VPN）是最便宜的方案，標準通道每條可達 1.25 Gbps，遠超過所需的 <50 Mbps。選項 A（每個帳號各建一個 VPC）不具成本效益，因為會造成 VPC 氾濫，且每個 VPC 需各自的 VPN 連線或需 Transit Gateway 才能連到地端。選項 C（Transit Gateway + VPN）會增加每個 attachment 的時數費用與每 GB 的資料處理費，對單一共享 VPC 的低頻寬情境是多餘的；選項 E（Direct Connect）需昂貴的專用埠費用與實體 cross-connect，對 <50 Mbps 而言過度設計。因此 B+D 為最具成本效益的組合。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Deploying a separate VPC to each account creates VPC sprawl and would require either one VPN per VPC or a Transit Gateway to connect each VPC to on-premises, which is more costly to build and operate than a single shared VPC.","why_zh":"為每個帳號各部署一個 VPC 會造成 VPC 氾濫，且每個 VPC 需各自的 VPN 或需 Transit Gateway 才能連到地端，建置與營運成本都高於單一共享 VPC。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Transit Gateway adds per-attachment hourly charges plus per-GB data-processing fees; it is only justified when you must interconnect many separate VPCs, not for a single shared VPC carrying <50 Mbps, so it is not the most cost-effective.","why_zh":"Transit Gateway 會增加每個 attachment 的時數費用與每 GB 資料處理費；只有在需要連接多個獨立 VPC 時才合理，對承載 <50 Mbps 的單一共享 VPC 並非最具成本效益。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Direct Connect requires a dedicated physical port (recurring port-hour fees) and a cross-connect; it is built for high, consistent bandwidth and is far too expensive for less than 50 Mbps of traffic.","why_zh":"Direct Connect 需要專用實體埠（持續的埠時費用）與 cross-connect，是為高且穩定的頻寬設計，對少於 50 Mbps 的流量過於昂貴。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-sharing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ram/latest/userguide/getting-started-sharing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/s2svpn/VPNTunnels.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/s2svpn/VPC_VPN.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/what-is-transit-gateway.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・複選"},{"id":216,"question_en":"A solutions architect at a large company needs to set up network security for outbound tra®c to the internet from all AWS accounts within an organization in AWS Organizations. The organization has more than 100 AWS accounts, and the accounts route to each other by using a centralized AWS Transit Gateway. Each account has both an internet gateway and a NAT gateway for outbound tra®c to the internet. The company deploys resources only into a single AWS Region. The company needs the ability to add centrally managed rule-based filtering on all outbound tra®c to the internet for all AWS accounts in the organization. The peak load of outbound tra®c will not exceed 25 Gbps in each Availability Zone. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家大公司的解决方案架构师需要为 AWS Organizations 中组织内的所有 AWS 账户到 Internet 的出站流量设置网络安全。该组织拥有 100 多个 AWS 账户，这些账户通过使用集中式 AWS Transit Gateway 相互路由。每个帐户都有一个 Internet 网关和一个 NAT 网关，用 于发送到 Internet 的出站流量。该公司仅将资源部署到单个 AWS 区域。 该公司需要能够对组织中所有 AWS 账户的所有互联网出站流量添加集中管理的基于规则的过滤。每个可用区的出站流量峰值负载不 会超过 25 Gbps。 哪种解决方案满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new VPC for outbound tra®c to the internet. Connect the existing transit gateway to the new VPC. Configure a new NAT gateway. Create an Auto Scaling group of Amazon EC2 instances that run an open-source internet proxy for rule-based filtering across all Availability Zones in the Region. Modify all default routes to point to the proxy's Auto Scaling group.","B":"Create a new VPC for outbound tra®c to the internet. Connect the existing transit gateway to the new VPC. Configure a new NAT gateway. Use an AWS Network Firewall firewall for rule-based filtering. Create Network Firewall endpoints in each Availability Zone. Modify all default routes to point to the Network Firewall endpoints.","C":"Create an AWS Network Firewall firewall for rule-based filtering in each AWS account. Modify all default routes to point to the Network Firewall firewalls in each account.","D":"In each AWS account, create an Auto Scaling group of network-optimized Amazon EC2 instances that run an open-source internet proxy for rule-based filtering. Modify all default routes to point to the proxy's Auto Scaling group."},"options_zh":{"A":"为互联网的出站流量创建一个新的 VPC。将现有中转网关连接到新 VPC。配置新的 NAT 网关。创建一个由 Amazon EC2 实例组 成的 Auto Scaling 组，该实例运行开源 Internet 代理，以便在该区域的所有可用区中进行基于规则的过滤。修改所有默认路由以 指向代理的 Auto Scaling 组。","B":"为互联网的出站流量创建一个新的 VPC。将现有中转网关连接到新 VPC。配置新的 NAT 网关。使用 AWS Network Firewall 防火 墙进行基于规则的过滤。在每个可用区中创建网络防火墙端点。修改所有默认路由以指向网络防火墙端点。","C":"在每个 AWS 账户中创建 AWS Network Firewall 防火墙以进行基于规则的过滤。修改所有默认路由以指向每个帐户中的网络防火 墙防火墙。","D":"在每个 AWS 账户中，创建一个由网络优化的 Amazon EC2 实例组成的 Auto Scaling 组，这些实例运行开源互联网代理以进行基 于规则的过滤。修改所有默认路由以指向代理的 Auto Scaling 组。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is centrally managed, rule-based filtering of outbound internet traffic for 100+ accounts that already route through a centralized Transit Gateway, with peak load up to 25 Gbps per Availability Zone. Option B is the AWS-documented reference architecture for centralized IPv4 egress with inspection: create a dedicated egress (inspection) VPC, attach it to the existing Transit Gateway, place an AWS Network Firewall endpoint in each AZ, route default traffic from the TGW attachment subnets to the firewall endpoints for stateful/Suricata-based rule filtering, then to a NAT gateway. AWS Network Firewall is a managed service that auto-scales and supports up to 100 Gbps of throughput per Availability Zone, comfortably exceeding the 25 Gbps peak, and it integrates with AWS Firewall Manager for central rule management across an Organization. Option D is wrong because it deploys a self-managed EC2 proxy fleet in every one of the 100+ accounts, which is not centrally managed and is high operational overhead; Option C deploys a separate Network Firewall in each account (not centralized and far costlier); Option A uses an open-source EC2 proxy Auto Scaling group instead of the managed, centrally-manageable Network Firewall, adding operational burden and lacking native central rule management.","explanation_zh":"需求是為超過 100 個 AWS 帳戶提供集中管理、以規則為基礎的出站網際網路流量過濾,這些帳戶已透過集中式 Transit Gateway 路由,每個可用區峰值流量最高 25 Gbps。選項 B 正是 AWS 文件中針對「具檢測的集中式 IPv4 egress」的參考架構:建立專用的 egress(inspection)VPC,連接到既有的 Transit Gateway,在每個可用區放置一個 AWS Network Firewall endpoint,將 TGW attachment 子網的預設路由指向 firewall endpoints 進行 stateful/Suricata 規則過濾,再送往 NAT gateway。AWS Network Firewall 是受管服務,可自動擴展並支援每個可用區最高 100 Gbps 的吞吐量,遠超 25 Gbps 峰值需求,並可整合 AWS Firewall Manager 在 Organization 範圍內集中管理規則。選項 D 錯誤,因為它在 100 多個帳戶的每一個中部署自管的 EC2 proxy 機群,並非集中管理且維運負擔極高;選項 C 在每個帳戶各部署一個 Network Firewall(非集中且成本高昂);選項 A 使用開源 EC2 proxy Auto Scaling group 而非受管且可集中管理的 Network Firewall,增加維運負擔且缺乏原生集中規則管理。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses a self-managed open-source EC2 proxy Auto Scaling group for filtering instead of the managed AWS Network Firewall. This adds significant operational overhead (patching, scaling, HA, rule tooling) and lacks native central rule management across the Organization, even though it centralizes egress in one VPC.","why_zh":"使用自管的開源 EC2 proxy Auto Scaling group 過濾,而非受管的 AWS Network Firewall。即使在單一 VPC 集中化,仍帶來大量維運負擔(修補、擴展、HA、規則工具)且缺乏跨 Organization 的原生集中規則管理。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Deploys a separate Network Firewall in every account, which is the opposite of a centralized solution. It multiplies cost (100+ firewalls) and management effort, and does not leverage the existing centralized Transit Gateway egress design.","why_zh":"在每個帳戶各部署一個 Network Firewall,與集中化方案背道而馳。它使成本(100 多個 firewall)與管理工作倍增,且未利用既有的集中式 Transit Gateway egress 設計。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Deploys a self-managed EC2 proxy Auto Scaling group in each of the 100+ accounts. This is neither centrally managed nor low overhead, and managing consistent rules across so many distributed fleets is impractical compared to a single managed Network Firewall in a central egress VPC.","why_zh":"在 100 多個帳戶的每一個中部署自管的 EC2 proxy Auto Scaling group。這既非集中管理也非低負擔,相較於在單一集中式 egress VPC 中部署一個受管的 Network Firewall,跨眾多分散機群維持一致規則並不實際。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/building-scalable-secure-multi-vpc-network-infrastructure/using-nat-gateway-with-firewall.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/network-firewall/latest/developerguide/vpc-config-subnets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/network-firewall.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/network-firewall/latest/developerguide/what-is-aws-network-firewall.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":217,"question_en":"A company uses a load balancer to distribute tra®c to Amazon EC2 instances in a single Availability Zone. The company is concerned about security and wants a solutions architect to re-architect the solution to meet the following requirements: • Inbound requests must be filtered for common vulnerability attacks. • Rejected requests must be sent to a third-party auditing application. • All resources should be highly available. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用负载均衡器将流量分配到单个可用区中的 Amazon EC2 实例。该公司关注安全性，希望解决方案架构师重新构建解决 方案以满足以下要求： • 必须过滤入站请求以防止常见漏洞攻击。 • 被拒绝的请求必须发送至第三方审核应用程序。 • 所有资源都应该高度可用。 哪种解决方案满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a Multi-AZ Auto Scaling group using the application's AMI. Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and select the previously created Auto Scaling group as the target. Use Amazon Inspector to monitor tra®c to the ALB and EC2 instances. Create a web ACL in WAF. Create an AWS WAF using the web ACL and ALB. Use an AWS Lambda function to frequently push the Amazon Inspector report to the third-party auditing application.","B":"Configure an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and add the EC2 instances as targets. Create a web ACL in WAF. Create an AWS WAF using the web ACL and ALB name and enable logging with Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Use an AWS Lambda function to frequently push the logs to the third-party auditing application.","C":"Configure an Application Load Balancer (ALB) along with a target group adding the EC2 instances as targets. Create an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose with the destination of the third-party auditing application. Create a web ACL in WAF. Create an AWS WAF using the web ACL and ALB then enable logging by selecting the Kinesis Data Firehose as the destination. Subscribe to AWS Managed Rules in AWS Marketplace, choosing the WAF as the subscriber.","D":"Configure a Multi-AZ Auto Scaling group using the application's AMI. Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and select the previously created Auto Scaling group as the target. Create an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose with a destination of the third-party auditing application. Create a web ACL in WAF. Create an AWS WAF using the WebACL and ALB then enable logging by selecting the Kinesis Data Firehose as the destination. Subscribe to AWS Managed Rules in AWS Marketplace, choosing the WAF as the subscriber."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用应用程序的 AMI 配置多可用区 Auto Scaling 组。创建应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 并选择之前创建的 Auto Scaling 组作为目 标。使用 Amazon Inspector 监控 ALB 和 EC2 实例的流量。在WAF中创建Web ACL。使用 Web ACL 和 ALB 创建 AWS WAF。使用 AWS Lambda 函数频繁地将 Amazon Inspector 报告推送到第三方审核应用程序。","B":"配置应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 并将 EC2 实例添加为目标。在WAF中创建Web ACL。使用 Web ACL 和 ALB 名称创建 AWS WAF， 并使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 启用日志记录。使用 AWS Lambda 函数频繁地将日志推送到第三方审核应用程序。","C":"配置应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 以及将 EC2 实例添加为目标的目标组。使用第三方审核应用程序的目标创建 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose。在WAF中创建Web ACL。使用 Web ACL 和 ALB 创建 AWS WAF，然后通过选择 Kinesis Data Firehose 作为目标来启用 日志记录。在 AWS Marketplace 中订阅 AWS 托管规则，选择 WAF 作为订阅者。","D":"使用应用程序的 AMI 配置多可用区 Auto Scaling 组。创建应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 并选择之前创建的 Auto Scaling 组作为目 标。创建具有第三方审核应用程序目标的 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose。在WAF中创建Web ACL。使用 WebACL 和 ALB 创建 AWS WAF，然后通过选择 Kinesis Data Firehose 作为目标来启用日志记录。在 AWS Marketplace 中订阅 AWS 托管规则，选择 WAF 作为 订阅者。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":88},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Three requirements must all be met: (1) filter inbound requests for common vulnerability attacks, (2) send rejected requests to a third-party auditing application, and (3) all resources highly available. The original deployment is single-AZ, so high availability requires a Multi-AZ Auto Scaling group behind the ALB. Only options A and D add a Multi-AZ Auto Scaling group; B and C leave EC2 instances as direct ALB targets in a single AZ and therefore fail the HA requirement. Option A uses Amazon Inspector, which is a vulnerability/exposure assessment service for instances and does NOT filter inbound HTTP requests, so it fails requirement 1. Option D correctly uses AWS WAF with a web ACL subscribed to AWS Marketplace managed rule groups to filter common attacks, and enables WAF logging directly to an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose stream whose destination is the third-party auditing application. AWS WAF natively supports Amazon Data (Kinesis) Firehose as a logging destination, and Firehose can deliver to HTTP-endpoint third-party destinations, so no Lambda glue is needed. D therefore satisfies all three requirements.","explanation_zh":"三項需求都必須滿足：(1) 過濾針對常見漏洞攻擊的入站請求,(2) 將被拒絕的請求送到第三方稽核應用程式,(3) 所有資源都需高可用。原始部署為單一可用區,因此高可用需要在 ALB 後方使用 Multi-AZ Auto Scaling group。只有 A 與 D 加入了 Multi-AZ Auto Scaling group;B 與 C 仍將 EC2 instances 直接作為 ALB 目標且位於單一 AZ,因此不符合高可用需求。選項 A 使用 Amazon Inspector,但它是針對執行個體的漏洞/暴露評估服務,並不會過濾入站 HTTP 請求,因此不符合需求 1。選項 D 正確地使用 AWS WAF 搭配訂閱 AWS Marketplace managed rule groups 的 web ACL 來過濾常見攻擊,並將 WAF logging 直接啟用至以第三方稽核應用程式為目的地的 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose stream。AWS WAF 原生支援 Amazon Data (Kinesis) Firehose 作為 logging 目的地,Firehose 可投遞到 HTTP-endpoint 等第三方目的地,因此不需要 Lambda 介接。D 滿足全部三項需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Inspector performs vulnerability assessment of EC2 instances and network exposure; it does not filter inbound web requests for common attacks (that is WAF's job). It also relies on Lambda to push Inspector reports rather than streaming rejected-request logs, so it does not properly capture WAF-rejected requests.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 對 EC2 instances 進行漏洞與網路暴露評估,並不會過濾入站 Web 請求中的常見攻擊(那是 WAF 的工作)。它還依賴 Lambda 推送 Inspector 報告,而非串流被拒絕的請求日誌,因此無法正確擷取 WAF 拒絕的請求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"It adds EC2 instances directly as ALB targets with no Multi-AZ Auto Scaling group, leaving compute in a single AZ, so it fails the high-availability requirement. Using CloudWatch Logs plus a Lambda to push logs is also more operational overhead than native Firehose delivery.","why_zh":"它將 EC2 instances 直接作為 ALB 目標,沒有 Multi-AZ Auto Scaling group,運算仍在單一 AZ,因此不符合高可用需求。使用 CloudWatch Logs 再加 Lambda 推送日誌也比原生 Firehose 投遞更高的營運負擔。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The WAF/Firehose/Marketplace-rules logging design is correct, but it only registers EC2 instances in a target group without a Multi-AZ Auto Scaling group, so resources remain in a single AZ and the high-availability requirement is not met.","why_zh":"WAF/Firehose/Marketplace 規則的日誌設計正確,但它僅將 EC2 instances 註冊到目標群組,沒有 Multi-AZ Auto Scaling group,因此資源仍在單一 AZ,不符合高可用需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/marketplace-rule-groups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/aws-managed-rule-groups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/create-destination.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":218,"question_en":"A company is running an application in the AWS Cloud. The application consists of microservices that run on a ­eet of Amazon EC2 instances in multiple Availability Zones behind an Application Load Balancer. The company recently added a new REST API that was implemented in Amazon API Gateway. Some of the older microservices that run on EC2 instances need to call this new API. The company does not want the API to be accessible from the public internet and does not want proprietary data to traverse the public internet. What should a solutions architect do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 云中运行应用程序。该应用程序由微服务组成，这些微服务在应用程序负载均衡器后面的多个可用区中的一组 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。该公司最近添加了一个在 Amazon API Gateway 中实施的新 REST API。一些在 EC2 实例上运行的旧微服务需 要调用这个新 API。 该公司不希望可以从公共互联网访问 API，也不希望专有数据遍历公共互联网。 解决方案架构师应该怎样做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection between the VPC and the API Gateway. Use API Gateway to generate a unique API Key for each microservice. Configure the API methods to require the key.","B":"Create an interface VPC endpoint for API Gateway, and set an endpoint policy to only allow access to the specific API. Add a resource policy to API Gateway to only allow access from the VPC endpoint. Change the API Gateway endpoint type to private.","C":"Modify the API Gateway to use IAM authentication. Update the IAM policy for the IAM role that is assigned to the EC2 instances to allow access to the API Gateway. Move the API Gateway into a new VPDeploy a transit gateway and connect the VPCs.","D":"Create an accelerator in AWS Global Accelerator, and connect the accelerator to the API Gateway. Update the route table for all VPC subnets with a route to the created Global Accelerator endpoint IP address. Add an API key for each service to use for authentication."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 VPC 和 API Gateway 之间创建 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 连接。使用 API Gateway 为每个微服务生成唯一的 API Key。配置 API 方法 以需要密钥。","B":"为 API Gateway 创建接口 VPC 终端节点，并设置终端节点策略仅允许访问特定 API。向 API Gateway 添加资源策略，仅允许来 自 VPC 终端节点的访问。将 API 网关端点类型更改为私有。","C":"修改 API Gateway 以使用 IAM 身份验证。更新分配给 EC2 实例的 IAM 角色的 IAM 策略以允许访问 API Gateway。将 API 网关移 至新的 VP 部署中转网关并连接 VPC。","D":"在AWS Global Accelerator 中创建加速器，并将加速器连接到API Gateway。使用到创建的 Global Accelerator 终端节点 IP 地址的 路由更新所有 VPC 子网的路由表。为每个服务添加一个 API 密钥以用于身份验证。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is that the new API Gateway REST API must not be reachable from the public internet and that proprietary data must not traverse the public internet. AWS's documented mechanism for this is a private REST API: you create an interface VPC endpoint (powered by AWS PrivateLink) for the execute-api service, set the API's endpoint type to Private, attach a VPC endpoint policy to restrict access to the specific API, and attach an API Gateway resource policy that allows access only from the VPC endpoint (aws:SourceVpce). Traffic then stays entirely within the AWS network and never leaves it, exactly as the official 'Create a private API' procedure describes. Option B is the only choice that implements this end to end.","explanation_zh":"需求是新的 API Gateway REST API 不可從公網存取，且專屬資料不可經過公網傳輸。AWS 文件記載的做法就是建立 private REST API：為 execute-api 服務建立 interface VPC endpoint（由 AWS PrivateLink 提供），將 API 的 endpoint type 設為 Private，套用 VPC endpoint policy 以限制只能存取特定 API，並在 API Gateway 上加上 resource policy 只允許來自該 VPC endpoint（aws:SourceVpce）的存取。如此流量完全留在 AWS 網路內、絕不經過公網，正是官方『Create a private API』程序所述。選項 B 是唯一完整實作此方案的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Site-to-Site VPN connects a VPC to an on-premises/customer network, not to a managed service like API Gateway; you cannot create a VPN 'between a VPC and API Gateway'. API keys are for usage plans and throttling identification, not for keeping traffic off the public internet, so this does not satisfy the privacy requirement.","why_zh":"AWS Site-to-Site VPN 是連接 VPC 與地端/客戶網路，並非連到 API Gateway 這類受管服務；無法在『VPC 與 API Gateway 之間』建立 VPN。API key 用於 usage plan 與限流識別，不能讓流量不經公網，因此無法滿足隱私需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it is technically incoherent: API Gateway is a regional managed service and does not run inside a VPC, so you cannot 'move API Gateway into a new VPC' nor reach it via a transit gateway connecting VPCs. IAM authentication only controls who may call the API; a public regional/edge endpoint remains reachable from the internet, so data could still traverse the public internet.","why_zh":"這是 dump 的建議答案，但技術上不成立：API Gateway 是區域性受管服務，不在 VPC 內運行，因此無法『把 API Gateway 移入新的 VPC』，也無法透過連接 VPC 的 transit gateway 觸及它。IAM 驗證只控制誰可呼叫 API；公開的 regional/edge endpoint 仍可從網際網路存取，資料仍可能經過公網。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Global Accelerator does not support API Gateway as a backend endpoint, and it provides public anycast IP addresses for internet-facing acceleration, which is the opposite of keeping the API off the public internet. Adding API keys does not provide network privacy.","why_zh":"AWS Global Accelerator 不支援以 API Gateway 作為後端 endpoint，且其提供的是面向網際網路的公用 anycast IP，與『不讓 API 暴露於公網』正好相反。加上 API key 也無法提供網路層級的隱私。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-private-apis.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-private-api-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-vpc-endpoint-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/api-gateway-api-endpoint-types.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":219,"question_en":"A company has set up its entire infrastructure on AWS. The company uses Amazon EC2 instances to host its ecommerce website and uses Amazon S3 to store static data. Three engineers at the company handle the cloud administration and development through one AWS account. Occasionally, an engineer alters an EC2 security group configuration of another engineer and causes noncompliance issues in the environment. A solutions architect must set up a system that tracks changes that the engineers make. The system must send alerts when the engineers make noncompliant changes to the security settings for the EC2 instances. What is the FASTEST way for the solutions architect to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司已在 AWS 上建立了整个基础设施。该公司使用 Amazon EC2 实例托管其电子商务网站，并使用 Amazon S3 存储静态数据。 该公司的三名工程师通过一个 AWS 账户负责云管理和开发。有时，工程师会更改另一位工程师的 EC2 安全组配置，并导致环境中出 现不合规问题。 解决方案架构师必须建立一个系统来跟踪工程师所做的更改。当工程师对 EC2 实例的安全设置进行不合规的更改时，系统必须发送 警报。 解决方案架构师满足这些要求的最快方法是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Set up AWS Organizations for the company. Apply SCPs to govern and track noncompliant security group changes that are made to the AWS account.","B":"Enable AWS CloudTrail to capture the changes to EC2 security groups. Enable Amazon CloudWatch rules to provide alerts when noncompliant security settings are detected.","C":"Enable SCPs on the AWS account to provide alerts when noncompliant security group changes are made to the environment.","D":"Enable AWS Config on the EC2 security groups to track any noncompliant changes. Send the changes as alerts through an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"为公司设置 AWS Organizations。应用 SCP 来管理和跟踪对 AWS 账户进行的不合规安全组更改。","B":"启用 AWS CloudTrail 以捕获对 EC2 安全组的更改。启用 Amazon CloudWatch 规则，以便在检测到不合规的安全设置时提供警 报。","C":"启用 AWS 账户上的 SCP，以便在对环境进行不合规的安全组更改时提供警报。","D":"在 EC2 安全组上启用 AWS Config 以跟踪任何不合规的更改。通过 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 主题将更改 作为警报发送。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":85,"B":15},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to track security group changes AND send alerts specifically when engineers make NONCOMPLIANT changes. AWS Config is purpose-built for this: it records configuration changes to AWS::EC2::SecurityGroup resources and provides managed rules (e.g., restricted-common-ports / RESTRICTED_INCOMING_TRAFFIC and restricted-ssh) that evaluate security groups on every configuration change and flag them as NON_COMPLIANT. AWS Config then streams compliance-state change notifications to an Amazon SNS topic, so engineers receive alerts on noncompliant changes out of the box. This is the FASTEST path because it requires only turning on Config, enabling a managed rule, and wiring an SNS topic, with no custom evaluation logic. Option B (CloudTrail + CloudWatch/EventBridge rules) only captures the API call; it has no native notion of 'compliant vs noncompliant,' so you would have to author custom event-pattern logic to decide which changes violate policy, making it slower and a poor fit for the explicit 'noncompliant' requirement.","explanation_zh":"需求是追蹤 security group 變更，並在工程師做出「不合規 (noncompliant)」變更時發出警示。AWS Config 正是為此設計：它記錄 AWS::EC2::SecurityGroup 資源的組態變更，並提供受管規則 (例如 restricted-common-ports / RESTRICTED_INCOMING_TRAFFIC 與 restricted-ssh)，每次組態變更時評估 security group，並將違規者標記為 NON_COMPLIANT。AWS Config 接著會把合規狀態變更通知透過 Amazon SNS topic 串流送出，工程師即可開箱即用地收到不合規變更的警示。這是最快的方式，因為只需啟用 Config、開啟受管規則並接上 SNS topic，無需自行撰寫評估邏輯。選項 B (CloudTrail + CloudWatch/EventBridge rules) 只能擷取 API 呼叫，本身沒有「合規 vs 不合規」的概念，必須自行撰寫 event pattern 邏輯來判斷哪些變更違規，因此較慢且不符合題目明確的 noncompliant 要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SCPs are guardrails applied via AWS Organizations to restrict permissions; they do not track changes or send alerts. They are preventive, not detective, and would require setting up Organizations, which is overhead and not aligned with tracking/alerting on noncompliant changes.","why_zh":"SCP 是透過 AWS Organizations 套用的權限護欄，用於限制權限，並不會追蹤變更或發出警示。它是預防性而非偵測性的，且需先建立 Organizations，屬於額外負擔，也不符合追蹤/警示不合規變更的需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudTrail records the API call and CloudWatch/EventBridge can match events, but neither has a native compliance evaluation engine. Determining whether a security-group change is 'noncompliant' would require custom event-pattern or Lambda logic, so it is neither the fastest nor a natural fit for the stated noncompliance requirement.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 記錄 API 呼叫，CloudWatch/EventBridge 可比對事件，但兩者皆無原生合規評估引擎。要判斷 security group 變更是否「不合規」需自行撰寫 event pattern 或 Lambda 邏輯，因此既非最快，也不符合題目所述的不合規評估需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"SCPs do not generate alerts and cannot be 'enabled on an AWS account' to provide notifications; they require AWS Organizations and only restrict permissions. This option misrepresents what SCPs do.","why_zh":"SCP 無法產生警示，也無法「在單一 AWS 帳戶上啟用」來提供通知；它需要 AWS Organizations 且僅限制權限。此選項錯誤描述了 SCP 的功能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/WhatIsConfig.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/notifications-for-AWS-Config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/restricted-common-ports.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/restricted-ssh.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":220,"question_en":"A company has IoT sensors that monitor tra®c patterns throughout a large city. The company wants to read and collect data from the sensors and perform aggregations on the data. A solutions architect designs a solution in which the IoT devices are streaming to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams. Several applications are reading from the stream. However, several consumers are experiencing throttling and are periodically encountering a ReadProvisionedThroughputExceeded error. Which actions should the solutions architect take to resolve this issue? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司拥有物联网传感器，可以监控整个大城市的交通模式。该公司希望从传感器读取和收集数据并对数据进行聚合。 解决方案架构师设计了一个解决方案，其中 IoT 设备流式传输到 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams。多个应用程序正在从流中读取数据。 但是，一些使用者遇到了限制，并且定期遇到 ReadProvisionedThroughputExceeded 错误。 解决方案架构师应采取哪些措施来解决此问题？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Reshard the stream to increase the number of shards in the stream.","B":"Use the Kinesis Producer Library (KPL). Adjust the polling frequency.","C":"Use consumers with the enhanced fan-out feature.","D":"Reshard the stream to reduce the number of shards in the stream.","E":"Use an error retry and exponential backoff mechanism in the consumer logic.","F":"Configure the stream to use dynamic partitioning."},"options_zh":{"A":"对流重新分片以增加流中的分片数量。","B":"使用 Kinesis Producer Library (KPL)。调整轮询频率。","C":"使用具有增强扇出功能的消费者。","D":"对流进行重新分片以减少流中的分片数量。","E":"在消费者逻辑中使用错误重试和指数退避机制。","F":"配置流以使用动态分区。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ACE":100},"tags":["Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":221,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts. The company needs a list of all its Amazon EC2 instances that have underutilized CPU or memory usage. The company also needs recommendations for how to downsize these underutilized instances. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST effort?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理其 AWS 账户。该公司需要一份 CPU 或内存使用率未充分利用的所有 Amazon EC2 实例的列 表。该公司还需要有关如何缩小这些未充分利用的实例的建议。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Install a CPU and memory monitoring tool from AWS Marketplace on all the EC2 instances. Store the findings in Amazon S3. Implement a Python script to identify underutilized instances. Reference EC2 instance pricing information for recommendations about downsizing options.","B":"Install the Amazon CloudWatch agent on all the EC2 instances by using AWS Systems Manager. Retrieve the resource optimization recommendations from AWS Cost Explorer in the organization’s management account. Use the recommendations to downsize underutilized instances in all accounts of the organization.","C":"Install the Amazon CloudWatch agent on all the EC2 instances by using AWS Systems Manager. Retrieve the resource optimization recommendations from AWS Cost Explorer in each account of the organization. Use the recommendations to downsize underutilized instances in all accounts of the organization.","D":"Install the Amazon CloudWatch agent on all the EC2 instances by using AWS Systems Manager. Create an AWS Lambda function to extract CPU and memory usage from all the EC2 instances. Store the findings as files in Amazon S3. Use Amazon Athena to find underutilized instances. Reference EC2 instance pricing information for recommendations about downsizing options."},"options_zh":{"A":"在所有 EC2 实例上安装来自 AWS Marketplace 的 CPU 和内存监控工具。将结果存储在 Amazon S3 中。实施 Python 脚本来识别 未充分利用的实例。请参考 EC2 实例定价信息，获取有关缩减规模选项的建议。","B":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 在所有 EC2 实例上安装 Amazon CloudWatch 代理。从组织管理账户中的 AWS Cost Explorer 检索资源 优化建议。使用这些建议来缩小组织所有账户中未充分利用的实例的规模。","C":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 在所有 EC2 实例上安装 Amazon CloudWatch 代理。从组织的每个账户中的 AWS Cost Explorer 检索资 源优化建议。使用这些建议来缩小组织所有账户中未充分利用的实例的规模。","D":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 在所有 EC2 实例上安装 Amazon CloudWatch 代理。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数以从所有 EC2 实例中 提取 CPU 和内存使用情况。将结果存储为 Amazon S3 中的文件。使用 Amazon Athena 查找未充分利用的实例。请参考 EC2 实例 定价信息，获取有关缩减规模选项的建议。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":222,"question_en":"A company wants to run a custom network analysis software package to inspect tra®c as tra®c leaves and enters a VPC. The company has deployed the solution by using AWS CloudFormation on three Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group. All network routing has been established to direct tra®c to the EC2 instances. Whenever the analysis software stops working, the Auto Scaling group replaces an instance. The network routes are not updated when the instance replacement occurs. Which combination of steps will resolve this issue? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司希望运行自定义网络分析软件包来检查流量离开和进入 VPC 时的流量。该公司已在 Auto Scaling 组中的三个 Amazon EC2 实 例上使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署该解决方案。所有网络路由均已建立，以将流量引导至 EC2 实例。 每当分析软件停止工作时，Auto Scaling 组就会替换实例。发生实例替换时，网络路由不会更新。 哪种步骤组合可以解决此问题？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create alarms based on EC2 status check metrics that will cause the Auto Scaling group to replace the failed instance.","B":"Update the CloudFormation template to install the Amazon CloudWatch agent on the EC2 instances. Configure the CloudWatch agent to send process metrics for the application.","C":"Update the CloudFormation template to install AWS Systems Manager Agent on the EC2 instances. Configure Systems Manager Agent to send process metrics for the application.","D":"Create an alarm for the custom metric in Amazon CloudWatch for the failure scenarios. Configure the alarm to publish a message to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic.","E":"Create an AWS Lambda function that responds to the Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) message to take the instance out of service. Update the network routes to point to the replacement instance.","F":"In the CloudFormation template, write a condition that updates the network routes when a replacement instance is launched."},"options_zh":{"A":"根据 EC2 状态检查指标创建警报，这将导致 Auto Scaling 组替换故障实例。","B":"更新 CloudFormation 模板以在 EC2 实例上安装 Amazon CloudWatch 代理。配置 CloudWatch 代理以发送应用程序的进程指标。","C":"更新 CloudFormation 模板以在 EC2 实例上安装 AWS Systems Manager 代理。配置 Systems Manager 代理以发送应用程序的进程 指标。","D":"在 Amazon CloudWatch 中为故障场景的自定义指标创建警报。配置警报以将消息发布到 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 主题。","E":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来响应 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 消息以使实例停止服务。更新网络路由以指 向替换实例。","F":"在 CloudFormation 模板中，编写一个在启动替换实例时更新网络路由的条件。"},"answer":["A","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BDE":100},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Two problems must be solved: detecting that the custom network-analysis process has stopped (EC2/ASG health checks won't catch an app-level failure), and updating the VPC route tables to point at the replacement instance after ASG swaps it. B installs the CloudWatch agent with the procstat plugin, which collects per-process metrics and is the supported way to detect that the specific application process is no longer running. D creates a CloudWatch alarm on that custom metric and publishes to an SNS topic when the failure scenario occurs. E subscribes a Lambda function to the SNS topic; the function takes the failed instance out of service and updates the network routes to point to the healthy replacement instance. This event-driven chain (custom metric -> alarm -> SNS -> Lambda remediation) is the canonical AWS automation pattern, the same model used with ASG lifecycle hooks and EventBridge.","explanation_zh":"需要解決兩個問題：偵測自訂網路分析程序已停止(EC2/ASG 的 status check 與健康檢查無法偵測應用層級的程序失敗)，以及在 ASG 替換實例後更新 VPC route table 指向新實例。B 安裝 CloudWatch agent 並使用 procstat plugin 收集個別程序指標，這是偵測特定應用程序是否仍在執行的支援方式。D 針對該自訂指標建立 CloudWatch alarm，當失敗情境發生時發布訊息到 SNS topic。E 讓 Lambda function 訂閱該 SNS topic，將失敗實例下線並更新網路路由指向健康的替換實例。此事件驅動鏈(自訂指標 -> alarm -> SNS -> Lambda 修復)是 AWS 的標準自動化模式，與 ASG lifecycle hooks 及 EventBridge 採用相同模型。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"EC2 status check metrics (StatusCheckFailed_System/_Instance) detect host hardware, hypervisor, and OS-level network reachability problems, not a stopped custom application process. A healthy instance whose analysis software crashed would not trip a status check, so this does not detect the actual failure scenario.","why_zh":"EC2 status check 指標(StatusCheckFailed_System/_Instance)偵測主機硬體、hypervisor 與 OS 層級的網路可達性問題，無法偵測自訂應用程序停止。實例本身健康但分析軟體當機時並不會觸發 status check，因此無法偵測真正的失敗情境。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Systems Manager Agent is for instance management (Run Command, State Manager, Session Manager, patching) and does not send application process metrics to CloudWatch. The procstat process-metrics capability belongs to the CloudWatch agent, not the SSM Agent, making this a wrong-agent distractor of B.","why_zh":"AWS Systems Manager Agent 用於實例管理(Run Command、State Manager、Session Manager、修補)，並不會將應用程序指標傳送到 CloudWatch。procstat 程序指標功能屬於 CloudWatch agent 而非 SSM Agent，因此這是 B 的錯誤代理混淆選項。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"A CloudFormation condition is evaluated at stack create/update time, not in response to runtime ASG events. ASG instance replacement happens outside CloudFormation, which has no knowledge of which new instance was launched, so a CFN condition cannot dynamically update route tables when a replacement instance launches.","why_zh":"CloudFormation condition 在堆疊建立/更新時評估，而非回應執行階段的 ASG 事件。ASG 的實例替換發生在 CloudFormation 之外，CFN 不知道啟動了哪個新實例，因此 CFN condition 無法在替換實例啟動時動態更新 route table。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch-Agent-procstat-process-metrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Install-CloudWatch-Agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/lifecycle-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/tutorial-lifecycle-hook-lambda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/monitoring-system-instance-status-check.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":223,"question_en":"A company is developing a new on-demand video application that is based on microservices. The application will have 5 million users at launch and will have 30 million users after 6 months. The company has deployed the application on Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) on AWS Fargate. The company developed the application by using ECS services that use the HTTPS protocol. A solutions architect needs to implement updates to the application by using blue/green deployments. The solution must distribute tra®c to each ECS service through a load balancer. The application must automatically adjust the number of tasks in response to an Amazon CloudWatch alarm. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在开发一种基于微服务的新点播视频应用程序。该应用程序在发布时将拥有 500 万用户，6 个月后将拥有 3000 万用户。 该公司已将该应用程序部署在 AWS Fargate 上的 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 上。该公司通过使用 HTTPS 协议的 ECS 服务开发了该应用程序。 解决方案架构师需要使用蓝/绿部署来实施应用程序更新。该解决方案必须通过负载均衡器将流量分配到每个 ECS 服务。应用程序必 须自动调整任务数量以响应 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the ECS services to use the blue/green deployment type and a Network Load Balancer. Request increases to the service quota for tasks per service to meet the demand.","B":"Configure the ECS services to use the blue/green deployment type and a Network Load Balancer. Implement Auto Scaling group for each ECS service by using the Cluster Autoscaler.","C":"Configure the ECS services to use the blue/green deployment type and an Application Load Balancer. Implement an Auto Scaling group for each ECS service by using the Cluster Autoscaler.","D":"Configure the ECS services to use the blue/green deployment type and an Application Load Balancer. Implement Service Auto Scaling for each ECS service."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 ECS 服务以使用蓝/绿部署类型和网络负载均衡器。请求增加每个服务任务的服务配额以满足需求。","B":"配置 ECS 服务以使用蓝/绿部署类型和网络负载均衡器。使用 Cluster Autoscaler 为每个 ECS 服务实现 Auto Scaling 组。","C":"配置 ECS 服务以使用蓝/绿部署类型和应用程序负载均衡器。使用 Cluster Autoscaler 为每个 ECS 服务实现 Auto Scaling 组。","D":"配置 ECS 服务以使用蓝/绿部署类型和应用程序负载均衡器。为每个ECS服务实现服务自动伸缩。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":91},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"All three requirements point to option D. (1) Blue/green deployment that distributes traffic to each ECS service through a load balancer is implemented with an Application Load Balancer, which uses two target groups (blue and green) and supports the HTTP/HTTPS protocol the application uses; ALB is the documented load balancer for ECS blue/green deployments. (2) The requirement to automatically adjust the number of tasks in response to a CloudWatch alarm is met by Service Auto Scaling (Application Auto Scaling), which increases or decreases the desired task count using CloudWatch-based target tracking or step scaling policies. (3) Cluster Autoscaler is a Kubernetes/EKS construct that scales worker nodes, not ECS tasks, so options B and C are technically invalid for ECS/Fargate. Option A uses a Network Load Balancer (Layer 4, not the standard choice for an HTTPS microservice blue/green) and, critically, raising the tasks-per-service quota only lifts a static ceiling, it does not auto-scale tasks in response to a CloudWatch alarm. Therefore D is the only solution meeting every requirement.","explanation_zh":"三項需求都指向選項 D。(1) 透過 load balancer 將流量分送給每個 ECS service 的 blue/green 部署，需使用 Application Load Balancer（ALB），它使用兩個 target group（blue 與 green）並支援應用程式採用的 HTTP/HTTPS 協定；ALB 是 ECS blue/green 部署的標準 load balancer。(2)「依 CloudWatch alarm 自動調整 task 數量」由 Service Auto Scaling（Application Auto Scaling）達成，可用 target tracking 或 step scaling 政策依 CloudWatch 指標增減 desired task count。(3) Cluster Autoscaler 是 Kubernetes/EKS 的概念，用於擴縮 worker node 而非 ECS task，故 B、C 對 ECS/Fargate 在技術上無效。選項 A 使用 Network Load Balancer（L4，非 HTTPS 微服務 blue/green 的標準選擇），而且調高 tasks-per-service quota 只是提高靜態上限，並不會依 CloudWatch alarm 自動擴縮 task。因此只有 D 滿足所有需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Network Load Balancer is Layer 4 and not the standard choice for an HTTPS microservice; more importantly, requesting a service-quota increase for tasks per service only raises a static limit and does not automatically scale tasks in response to a CloudWatch alarm.","why_zh":"Network Load Balancer 屬 L4，非 HTTPS 微服務的標準選擇；更關鍵的是，提高 tasks-per-service 的 service quota 只是抬高靜態上限，無法依 CloudWatch alarm 自動擴縮 task。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Cluster Autoscaler is a Kubernetes/EKS component that scales nodes, not ECS tasks, and ECS on Fargate has no node Auto Scaling group; it also uses NLB instead of the HTTPS-appropriate ALB.","why_zh":"Cluster Autoscaler 是 Kubernetes/EKS 元件，用於擴縮 node 而非 ECS task，且 ECS on Fargate 沒有 node 的 Auto Scaling group；此外它用 NLB 而非適合 HTTPS 的 ALB。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Uses ALB correctly, but Cluster Autoscaler does not apply to ECS/Fargate (it scales Kubernetes nodes, not ECS tasks), so it cannot adjust the number of ECS tasks from a CloudWatch alarm.","why_zh":"ALB 選擇正確，但 Cluster Autoscaler 不適用於 ECS/Fargate（它擴縮 Kubernetes node 而非 ECS task），無法依 CloudWatch alarm 調整 ECS task 數量。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/target-tracking-create-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/alb-resources-for-blue-green.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/deployment-type-blue-green.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/service-auto-scaling.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":224,"question_en":"A company is running a containerized application in the AWS Cloud. The application is running by using Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) on a set of Amazon EC2 instances. The EC2 instances run in an Auto Scaling group. The company uses Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) to store its container images. When a new image version is uploaded, the new image version receives a unique tag. The company needs a solution that inspects new image versions for common vulnerabilities and exposures. The solution must automatically delete new image tags that have Critical or High severity findings. The solution also must notify the development team when such a deletion occurs. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 云中运行容器化应用程序。该应用程序通过使用 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 在一组 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。EC2 实例在 Auto Scaling 组中运行。 该公司使用 Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) 来存储其容器映像。当上传新的图像版本时，新的图像版本会收到一个唯 一的标签。 该公司需要一种解决方案来检查新映像版本是否存在常见漏洞和暴露情况。该解决方案必须自动删除具有“严重”或“高”严重性结果的 新图像标签。当发生此类删除时，解决方案还必须通知开发团队。 哪种解决方案满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure scan on push on the repository. Use Amazon EventBridge to invoke an AWS Step Functions state machine when a scan is complete for images that have Critical or High severity findings. Use the Step Functions state machine to delete the image tag for those images and to notify the development team through Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS).","B":"Configure scan on push on the repository. Configure scan results to be pushed to an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Invoke an AWS Lambda function when a new message is added to the SQS queue. Use the Lambda function to delete the image tag for images that have Critical or High severity findings. Notify the development team by using Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES).","C":"Schedule an AWS Lambda function to start a manual image scan every hour. Configure Amazon EventBridge to invoke another Lambda function when a scan is complete. Use the second Lambda function to delete the image tag for images that have Critical or High severity findings. Notify the development team by using Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS).","D":"Configure periodic image scan on the repository. Configure scan results to be added to an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Invoke an AWS Step Functions state machine when a new message is added to the SQS queue. Use the Step Functions state machine to delete the image tag for images that have Critical or High severity findings. Notify the development team by using Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES)."},"options_zh":{"A":"在存储库上配置推送时扫描。当对具有“严重”或“高”严重性结果的图像完成扫描时，使用 Amazon EventBridge 调用 AWS Step Functions 状态机。使用 Step Functions 状态机删除这些图像的图像标签，并通过 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 通知开发团队。","B":"在存储库上配置推送时扫描。配置要推送到 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列的扫描结果。当新消息添加到 SQS 队列时调用 AWS Lambda 函数。使用 Lambda 函数删除具有“严重”或“高”严重性结果的图像的图像标签。使用 Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) 通知开发团队。","C":"安排 AWS Lambda 函数每小时启动一次手动图像扫描。配置 Amazon EventBridge 以在扫描完成时调用另一个 Lambda 函数。使 用第二个 Lambda 函数删除具有“严重”或“高”严重性结果的图像的图像标签。使用 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 通知开发团队。","D":"在存储库上配置定期图像扫描。配置要添加到 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列的扫描结果。将新消息添加到 SQS 队列时调用 AWS Step Functions 状态机。使用 Step Functions 状态机删除具有“严重”或“高”严重性结果的图像的图像标签。使 用 Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) 通知开发团队。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Amazon ECR basic scan-on-push automatically scans each new image when it is pushed and, on completion, emits an 'ECR Image Scan' EventBridge event whose detail includes 'scan-status: COMPLETE' and a 'finding-severity-counts' map (e.g. CRITICAL, HIGH). An EventBridge rule can pattern-match on those severity counts and trigger a supported target. AWS docs explicitly list 'Activating an AWS Step Functions state machine' as a valid EventBridge target, so a Step Functions state machine can delete the offending image tag (BatchDeleteImage) and publish to Amazon SNS to notify the team. This is the only fully native, event-driven design that inspects images on upload. Option A is correct.","explanation_zh":"Amazon ECR 的 basic scan-on-push 會在每個新映像被推送時自動掃描，完成後發出一個 'ECR Image Scan' 的 EventBridge 事件，其 detail 內含 'scan-status: COMPLETE' 以及 'finding-severity-counts' 對應表（例如 CRITICAL、HIGH）。EventBridge 規則可針對這些嚴重性計數做事件模式比對並觸發目標。AWS 文件明確將「Activating an AWS Step Functions state machine」列為合法的 EventBridge 目標，因此 Step Functions 狀態機可刪除有問題的映像標籤（BatchDeleteImage）並透過 Amazon SNS 通知團隊。這是唯一在上傳時即檢查、且完全原生且事件驅動的設計，所以選項 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"ECR has no native capability to 'push scan results to an SQS queue.' Scan completion is surfaced via EventBridge, not by configuring ECR to deliver findings into SQS. This step is fictional, so the option fails regardless of the otherwise-reasonable Lambda/SES handling.","why_zh":"ECR 沒有原生「將掃描結果推送到 SQS 佇列」的功能。掃描完成是透過 EventBridge 發布，而非設定 ECR 直接把結果送進 SQS。此步驟並不存在，因此即使後續 Lambda/SES 處理合理，整個選項仍不成立。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Scheduling an hourly manual scan ignores native scan-on-push, delays detection of newly uploaded tags, adds operational overhead, and conflicts with the requirement to inspect new image versions as they are pushed. Basic scanning also limits manual scans to once per image per 24 hours. This is the dump's suggested answer but is technically inferior and wrong.","why_zh":"排程每小時手動掃描忽略原生的 scan-on-push，會延遲對新上傳標籤的偵測、增加維運負擔，且與「在映像推送時即檢查新版本」的需求衝突。basic scanning 對同一映像的手動掃描也限制為每 24 小時一次。這是題庫建議答案，但技術上較差且錯誤。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same non-existent 'scan results to SQS' assumption as B, and 'periodic' (continuous/scheduled) scanning rather than scan-on-push does not inspect each new version promptly at upload time as required.","why_zh":"與 B 相同地假設了不存在的「掃描結果送到 SQS」功能，且使用 periodic（持續/排程）掃描而非 scan-on-push，無法依需求在上傳當下即時檢查每個新版本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/ecr-eventbridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-basic-enabling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-enhanced-events.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":225,"question_en":"A company runs many workloads on AWS and uses AWS Organizations to manage its accounts. The workloads are hosted on Amazon EC2. AWS Fargate. and AWS Lambda. Some of the workloads have unpredictable demand. Accounts record high usage in some months and low usage in other months. The company wants to optimize its compute costs over the next 3 years. A solutions architect obtains a 6-month average for each of the accounts across the organization to calculate usage. Which solution will provide the MOST cost savings for all the organization's compute usage?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上运行许多工作负载并使用 AWS Organizations 来管理其账户。工作负载托管在 Amazon EC2 上。AWS Fargate。和 AWS Lambda。有些工作负载的需求是不可预测的。帐户在某些月份记录高使用率，而在其他月份记录低使用率。 该公司希望在未来 3 年内优化其计算成本。解决方案架构师获取整个组织中每个帐户 6 个月的平均值来计算使用情况。 哪种解决方案将为组织的所有计算使用提供最大程度的成本节省？","options_en":{"A":"Purchase Reserved Instances for the organization to match the size and number of the most common EC2 instances from the member accounts.","B":"Purchase a Compute Savings Plan for the organization from the management account by using the recommendation at the management account level.","C":"Purchase Reserved Instances for each member account that had high EC2 usage according to the data from the last 6 months.","D":"Purchase an EC2 Instance Savings Plan for each member account from the management account based on EC2 usage data from the last 6 months."},"options_zh":{"A":"为组织购买预留实例，以匹配成员账户中最常见 EC2 实例的大小和数量。","B":"使用管理账户级别的建议从管理账户为组织购买计算储蓄计划。","C":"根据过去 6 个月的数据，为 EC2 使用率较高的每个会员账户购买预留实例。","D":"根据过去 6 个月的 EC2 使用数据，从管理账户为每个成员账户购买 EC2 实例节省计划。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Cost Optimization","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":226,"question_en":"A company has hundreds of AWS accounts. The company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage all the accounts. The company has turned on all features. A finance team has allocated a daily budget for AWS costs. The finance team must receive an email notification if the organization's AWS costs exceed 80% of the allocated budget. A solutions architect needs to implement a solution to track the costs and deliver the notifications. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有数百个 AWS 账户。该公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的组织来管理所有账户。该公司已启用所有功能。 财务团队已为 AWS 成本分配每日预算。如果组织的 AWS 成本超过分配预算的 80%，财务团队必须收到电子邮件通知。解决方案架构 师需要实施一个解决方案来跟踪成本并发送通知。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？ 答： 在组织的管理账户中，使用 AWS Budgets 创建具有每日周期的预算。添加警报阈值并将值设置为 80%。使用 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 通知财务团队。","options_en":{"A":"In the organization's management account, use AWS Budgets to create a budget that has a daily period. Add an alert threshold and set the value to 80%. Use Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to notify the finance team.","B":"In the organization’s management account, set up the organizational view feature for AWS Trusted Advisor. Create an organizational view report for cost optimization. Set an alert threshold of 80%. Configure notification preferences. Add the email addresses of the finance team.","C":"Register the organization with AWS Control Tower. Activate the optional cost control (guardrail). Set a control (guardrail) parameter of 80%. Configure control (guardrail) notification preferences. Use Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to notify the finance team.","D":"Configure the member accounts to save a daily AWS Cost and Usage Report to an Amazon S3 bucket in the organization's management account. Use Amazon EventBridge to schedule a daily Amazon Athena query to calculate the organization’s costs. Configure Athena to send an Amazon CloudWatch alert if the total costs are more than 80% of the allocated budget. Use Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to notify the finance team."},"options_zh":{"B":"在组织的管理账户中，设置 AWS Trusted Advisor 的组织视图功能。创建组织视图报告以优化成本。将警报阈值设置为 80%。配 置通知首选项。添加财务团队的电子邮件地址。","C":"向 AWS Control Tower 注册组织。激活可选的成本控制（护栏）。将控制（护栏）参数设置为 80%。配置控制（护栏）通知首 选项。使用 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 通知财务团队。","D":"配置成员账户以将每日 AWS 成本和使用情况报告保存到组织管理账户中的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。使用 Amazon EventBridge 安 排每日 Amazon Athena 查询以计算组织的成本。配置 Athena 在总成本超过分配预算的 80% 时发送 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。使 用 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 通知财务团队。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":227,"question_en":"A company provides auction services for artwork and has users across North America and Europe. The company hosts its application in Amazon EC2 instances in the us-east-1 Region. Artists upload photos of their work as large-size. high-resolution image files from their mobile phones to a centralized Amazon S3 bucket created in the us-east-1 Region. The users in Europe are reporting slow performance for their image uploads. How can a solutions architect improve the performance of the image upload process?","question_zh":"一家公司提供艺术品拍卖服务，其用户遍布北美和欧洲。该公司将其应用程序托管在 us-east-1 区域的 Amazon EC2 实例中。艺术家 上传他们的大尺寸作品照片。将高分辨率图像文件从手机传输到在 us-east-1 区域创建的集中式 Amazon S3 存储桶。欧洲用户报告图 像上传速度缓慢。 解决方案架构师如何提高图像上传过程的性能？","options_en":{"A":"Redeploy the application to use S3 multipart uploads.","B":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution and point to the application as a custom origin.","C":"Configure the buckets to use S3 Transfer Acceleration.","D":"Create an Auto Scaling group for the EC2 instances and create a scaling policy."},"options_zh":{"A":"重新部署应用程序以使用 S3 分段上传。","B":"创建 Amazon CloudFront 分配并指向应用程序作为自定义源。","C":"配置存储桶以使用 S3 传输加速。","D":"为 EC2 实例创建 Auto Scaling 组并创建扩展策略。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":94},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":228,"question_en":"A company wants to containerize a multi-tier web application and move the application from an on-premises data center to AWS. The application includes web. application, and database tiers. The company needs to make the application fault tolerant and scalable. Some frequently accessed data must always be available across application servers. Frontend web servers need session persistence and must scale to meet increases in tra®c. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST ongoing operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司希望对多层 Web 应用程序进行容器化，并将该应用程序从本地数据中心迁移到 AWS。该应用程序包括网络。应用层和数据 库层。公司需要使应用程序具有容错性和可扩展性。一些经常访问的数据必须始终跨应用程序服务器可用。前端 Web 服务器需要会 话持久性，并且必须进行扩展以满足流量的增长。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的持续运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Run the application on Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) on AWS Fargate. Use Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) for data that is frequently accessed between the web and application tiers. Store the frontend web server session data in Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS).","B":"Run the application on Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) on Amazon EC2. Use Amazon ElastiCache for Redis to cache frontend web server session data. Use Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) with Multi-Attach on EC2 instances that are distributed across multiple Availability Zones.","C":"Run the application on Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS). Configure Amazon EKS to use managed node groups. Use ReplicaSets to run the web servers and applications. Create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. Mount the EFS file system across all EKS pods to store frontend web server session data.","D":"Deploy the application on Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS). Configure Amazon EKS to use managed node groups. Run the web servers and application as Kubernetes deployments in the EKS cluster. Store the frontend web server session data in an Amazon DynamoDB table. Create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) volume that all applications will mount at the time of deployment."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS Fargate 上的 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 上运行应用程序。将 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 用于在 Web 层和应用程序层之间频繁访问的数据。将前端 Web 服务器会话数据存储在 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 中。","B":"在 Amazon EC2 上的 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 上运行应用程序。使用 Amazon ElastiCache for Redis 缓存前 端 Web 服务器会话数据。在分布于多个可用区的 EC2 实例上将 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 与多重附加结合使用。","C":"在 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 上运行应用程序。配置 Amazon EKS 以使用托管节点组。使用 ReplicaSets 运 行 Web 服务器和应用程序。创建 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统。在所有 EKS Pod 上挂载 EFS 文件系统以存储 前端 Web 服务器会话数据。","D":"在 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 上部署应用程序。配置 Amazon EKS 以使用托管节点组。将 Web 服务器和应 用程序作为 EKS 集群中的 Kubernetes 部署运行。将前端 Web 服务器会话数据存储在 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。创建一个 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 卷，所有应用程序将在部署时挂载该卷。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":86},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The qualifier is LEAST ongoing operational overhead for a fault-tolerant, scalable, multi-tier containerized app where some frequently accessed data must be shared across app servers and frontend web servers need session persistence while scaling. Option D uses EKS with managed node groups (managed control plane and node lifecycle), runs the tiers as Kubernetes deployments, stores frontend session data in DynamoDB, and uses EFS as a shared file system for frequently accessed data. DynamoDB is a fully managed, horizontally scalable, distributed session store decoupled from any instance, which is the recommended pattern for session persistence that survives scaling and instance failure. EFS provides a fully managed, multi-AZ shared file system that all pods can mount concurrently for the frequently accessed data. Option B is the dump's suggested answer but is technically invalid: EBS Multi-Attach only attaches a single io1/io2 volume to instances in the SAME Availability Zone, so distributing the instances across multiple AZs is impossible, and standard file systems require a clustered file system for concurrent multi-server access, adding overhead.","explanation_zh":"本題的限定條件是在容錯、可擴展的多層容器化應用中，以最少的持續營運負擔達成需求：部分常用資料必須在應用伺服器間共享，且前端網頁伺服器在擴展時需要工作階段持久性。選項 D 使用 Amazon EKS 搭配 managed node groups（受管控制平面與節點生命週期），將各層以 Kubernetes deployments 執行，將前端工作階段資料存於 DynamoDB，並以 EFS 作為共享檔案系統存放常用資料。DynamoDB 是完全受管、可水平擴展且與任何實例解耦的分散式工作階段儲存，是工作階段持久性的建議模式，能在擴展與實例故障後仍保留資料。EFS 提供完全受管、跨多可用區的共享檔案系統，所有 pod 可同時掛載。選項 B 是題庫建議答案但技術上不可行：EBS Multi-Attach 只能將單一 io1/io2 磁碟區掛載到同一可用區內的實例，無法跨多可用區分散實例，且標準檔案系統需要叢集檔案系統才能多伺服器同時存取，反而增加營運負擔。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Fargate plus EFS is the lowest-overhead compute and shared-storage combination, but storing frontend session data in Amazon SQS is wrong: SQS is a message queue, not a session store, and cannot provide key-based session lookup/persistence across scaling web servers.","why_zh":"Fargate 加 EFS 是最低營運負擔的運算與共享儲存組合，但將前端工作階段資料存於 Amazon SQS 是錯誤的：SQS 是訊息佇列而非工作階段儲存，無法在擴展的網頁伺服器間提供以鍵值查找的工作階段持久性。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"EBS Multi-Attach attaches a single io1/io2 volume only to instances in the SAME Availability Zone, so 'distributed across multiple Availability Zones' is impossible. Standard file systems also need a clustered file system for safe concurrent multi-server access, and ECS on EC2 adds node-management overhead.","why_zh":"EBS Multi-Attach 只能將單一 io1/io2 磁碟區掛載到同一可用區內的實例，因此「跨多個可用區分散」根本不可行。標準檔案系統還需要叢集檔案系統才能安全地多伺服器同時存取，且 ECS on EC2 增加節點管理負擔。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EKS with EFS for shared data is valid, but using a shared NFS/EFS file system to store frontend web session data is not the recommended session-persistence pattern; it conflates shared data with session state and is inferior to a purpose-built distributed session store like DynamoDB.","why_zh":"EKS 搭配 EFS 存放共享資料可行，但用共享 NFS/EFS 檔案系統存放前端網頁工作階段資料並非建議的工作階段持久性模式；它將共享資料與工作階段狀態混為一談，劣於 DynamoDB 這類專用的分散式工作階段儲存。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ebs/latest/userguide/ebs-volumes-multi.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdk-for-php/v3/developer-guide/service_dynamodb-session-handler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/microservices-on-aws/data-store.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/mounting-fs.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":229,"question_en":"A solutions architect is planning to migrate critical Microsoft SQL Server databases to AWS. Because the databases are legacy systems, the solutions architect will move the databases to a modern data architecture. The solutions architect must migrate the databases with near-zero downtime. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师正计划将关键的 Microsoft SQL Server 数据库迁移到 AWS。由于数据库是遗留系统，解决方案架构师会将数据库迁移 到现代数据架构。解决方案架构师必须在近乎零停机的情况下迁移数据库。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Application Migration Service and the AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT). Perform an in-place upgrade before the migration. Export the migrated data to Amazon Aurora Serverless after cutover. Repoint the applications to Amazon Aurora.","B":"Use AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to rehost the database. Set Amazon S3 as a target. Set up change data capture (CDC) replication. When the source and destination are fully synchronized, load the data from Amazon S3 into an Amazon RDS for Microsoft SQL Server DB instance.","C":"Use native database high availability tools. Connect the source system to an Amazon RDS for Microsoft SQL Server DB instance. Configure replication accordingly. When data replication is finished, transition the workload to an Amazon RDS for Microsoft SQL Server DB instance.","D":"Use AWS Application Migration Service. Rehost the database server on Amazon EC2. When data replication is finished, detach the database and move the database to an Amazon RDS for Microsoft SQL Server DB instance. Reattach the database and then cut over all networking."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Application Migration Service 和 AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT)。在迁移之前执行就地升级。切换后将迁移的 数据导出到 Amazon Aurora Serverless。将应用程序重新指向 Amazon Aurora。","B":"使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 重新托管数据库。将 Amazon S3 设置为目标。设置变更数据捕获 (CDC) 复制。 当源和目标完全同步后，将数据从 Amazon S3 加载到 Amazon RDS for Microsoft SQL Server 数据库实例中。","C":"使用本机数据库高可用性工具。将源系统连接到 Amazon RDS for Microsoft SQL Server 数据库实例。相应地配置复制。数据复制 完成后，将工作负载转移到 Amazon RDS for Microsoft SQL Server 数据库实例。","D":"使用 AWS Application Migration Service。在 Amazon EC2 上重新托管数据库服务器。数据复制完成后，分离数据库并将数据库移 动到 Amazon RDS for Microsoft SQL Server 数据库实例。重新连接数据库，然后切断所有网络。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":49,"B":47},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識"},{"id":230,"question_en":"A company's solutions architect is analyzing costs of a multi-application environment. The environment is deployed across multiple Availability Zones in a single AWS Region. After a recent acquisition, the company manages two organizations in AWS Organizations. The company has created multiple service provider applications as AWS PrivateLink-powered VPC endpoint services in one organization. The company has created multiple service consumer applications in the other organization. Data transfer charges are much higher than the company expected, and the solutions architect needs to reduce the costs. The solutions architect must recommend guidelines for developers to follow when they deploy services. These guidelines must minimize data transfer charges for the whole environment. Which guidelines meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司的解决方案架构师正在分析多应用程序环境的成本。该环境跨单个 AWS 区域中的多个可用区部署。最近进行收购后，该公 司管理着 AWS Organizations 中的两个组织。该公司在一个组织中创建了多个服务提供商应用程序作为 AWS PrivateLink 支持的 VPC 终 端节点服务。该公司已在其他组织中创建了多个服务使用者应用程序。 数据传输费用远高于公司预期，解决方案架构师需要降低成本。解决方案架构师必须向开发人员推荐在部署服务时应遵循的指南。 这些准则必须最大限度地减少整个环境的数据传输费用。 哪些指南满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Resource Access Manager to share the subnets that host the service provider applications with other accounts in the organization.","B":"Place the service provider applications and the service consumer applications in AWS accounts in the same organization.","C":"Turn off cross-zone load balancing for the Network Load Balancer in all service provider application deployments.","D":"Ensure that service consumer compute resources use the Availability Zone-specific endpoint service by using the endpoint's local DNS name.","E":"Create a Savings Plan that provides adequate coverage for the organization's planned inter-Availability Zone data transfer usage."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Resource Access Manager 与组织中的其他账户共享托管服务提供商应用程序的子网。","B":"将服务提供商应用程序和服务使用者应用程序放置在同一组织的 AWS 账户中。","C":"在所有服务提供商应用程序部署中关闭网络负载均衡器的跨区域负载均衡。","D":"确保服务使用者计算资源通过使用端点的本地 DNS 名称来使用特定于可用区的端点服务。","E":"创建一个节省计划，为组织计划的可用区间数据传输使用提供足够的保障。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{"CD":41,"BD":38,"AD":18},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The cost driver is inter-Availability Zone (inter-AZ) data transfer within a single Region, which AWS meters as Region-DataTransfer-Regional-Bytes and charges on BOTH the inbound and outbound side. The guidelines must keep PrivateLink traffic within the same AZ on both the consumer and provider ends. Option D is correct: AWS PrivateLink generates both Regional and zonal (AZ-specific) endpoint DNS names, and AWS documentation explicitly states the zonal DNS name lets you 'reduce regional data transfer costs' by keeping traffic in the same AZ; if consumer compute uses the Regional DNS name, requests can land on an endpoint network interface in another AZ and incur inter-AZ charges. Option C is correct on the provider side: by default NLB cross-zone load balancing is off, so each NLB node only sends traffic to targets in its own AZ; turning it ON would make every node distribute to targets in all AZs, generating cross-AZ traffic and charges. Keeping cross-zone load balancing off (the guideline) preserves same-AZ traffic from the NLB node to its backend target. Together, C (provider side) and D (consumer side) minimize inter-AZ data transfer end to end. The dump's A/B answer is wrong: RAM subnet sharing does not work across two separate organizations and does not change data transfer pricing, and organization membership is purely a billing/governance grouping with zero effect on inter-AZ data transfer charges.","explanation_zh":"成本主因是單一 Region 內跨可用區 (inter-AZ) 的資料傳輸，AWS 以 Region-DataTransfer-Regional-Bytes 計費，且進出兩端都收費。因此指引必須讓 PrivateLink 流量在消費端與提供端都維持在同一個 AZ。選項 D 正確：AWS PrivateLink 會同時產生 Regional 與 zonal（特定 AZ）的端點 DNS 名稱，AWS 文件明確指出使用 zonal DNS 名稱可『降低 regional 資料傳輸成本』，因為流量會留在同一 AZ；若消費端使用 Regional DNS 名稱，請求可能命中位於其他 AZ 的端點網路介面而產生跨 AZ 費用。選項 C 在提供端正確：NLB 的 cross-zone load balancing 預設為關閉，每個 NLB 節點只將流量送往自己 AZ 內的目標；若開啟，每個節點會分送到所有 AZ 的目標而產生跨 AZ 流量與費用。維持關閉（此指引）可保持 NLB 節點到後端目標的同 AZ 流量。C（提供端）與 D（消費端）合起來可端到端最小化跨 AZ 資料傳輸。Dump 的 A/B 答案錯誤：RAM 子網共享無法跨兩個獨立 organization，也不改變資料傳輸定價；而 organization 歸屬純粹是計費/治理分組，對跨 AZ 資料傳輸費用毫無影響。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM) shares resources within a single organization (or to specific accounts), not across two separate organizations as described. Sharing subnets also does not change data transfer pricing; PrivateLink already provides the cross-org connectivity, so this neither applies nor reduces inter-AZ charges.","why_zh":"AWS RAM 是在單一 organization 內（或指定帳戶間）共享資源，無法用於題目描述的兩個獨立 organization。共享子網也不會改變資料傳輸定價；PrivateLink 已提供跨 org 連線，因此此選項既不適用也不能降低跨 AZ 費用。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Whether the provider and consumer accounts sit in the same AWS Organization is purely a billing/governance grouping and has no effect on inter-AZ data transfer rates. Consolidating organizations does not minimize data transfer charges and is also impractical guidance for ongoing service deployment.","why_zh":"提供端與消費端帳戶是否位於同一個 AWS Organization 純屬計費/治理分組，對跨 AZ 資料傳輸費率毫無影響。整併 organization 不會降低資料傳輸費用，作為持續部署的指引也不切實際。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Savings Plans cover compute usage (EC2, Fargate, Lambda) only; they do NOT cover data transfer charges, including inter-AZ data transfer. This option is based on a false premise and cannot reduce the data transfer costs.","why_zh":"Savings Plans 只涵蓋運算用量（EC2、Fargate、Lambda），不涵蓋任何資料傳輸費用，包含跨 AZ 資料傳輸。此選項建立在錯誤前提上，無法降低資料傳輸成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/neptune-analytics/latest/userguide/gettingStarted-connecting-private-link-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/network/network-load-balancers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cur/latest/userguide/cur-data-transfers-charges.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/concepts.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識・多選項拉鋸・複選"},{"id":231,"question_en":"A company has an on-premises Microsoft SQL Server database that writes a nightly 200 GB export to a local drive. The company wants to move the backups to more robust cloud storage on Amazon S3. The company has set up a 10 Gbps AWS Direct Connect connection between the on-premises data center and AWS. Which solution meets these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个本地 Microsoft SQL Server 数据库，该数据库每晚将 200 GB 导出数据写入本地驱动器。该公司希望将备份转移到 Amazon S3 上更强大的云存储中。该公司已在本地数据中心和 AWS 之间建立了 10 Gbps AWS Direct Connect 连接。 哪种解决方案最经济高效地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new S3 bucket. Deploy an AWS Storage Gateway file gateway within the VPC that is connected to the Direct Connect connection. Create a new SMB file share. Write nightly database exports to the new SMB file share.","B":"Create an Amazon FSx for Windows File Server Single-AZ file system within the VPC that is connected to the Direct Connect connection. Create a new SMB file share. Write nightly database exports to an SMB file share on the Amazon FSx file system. Enable nightly backups.","C":"Create an Amazon FSx for Windows File Server Multi-AZ file system within the VPC that is connected to the Direct Connect connection. Create a new SMB file share. Write nightly database exports to an SMB file share on the Amazon FSx file system. Enable nightly backups.","D":"Create a new S3 bucket. Deploy an AWS Storage Gateway volume gateway within the VPC that is connected to the Direct Connect connection. Create a new SMB file share. Write nightly database exports to the new SMB file share on the volume gateway, and automate copies of this data to an S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的 S3 存储桶。在连接到 Direct Connect 连接的 VPC 内部署 AWS Storage Gateway 文件网关。创建新的 SMB 文件共 享。将夜间数据库导出写入新的 SMB 文件共享。","B":"在连接到 Direct Connect 连接的 VPC 内创建 Amazon FSx for Windows File Server 单可用区文件系统。创建新的 SMB 文件共享。 将夜间数据库导出写入 Amazon FSx 文件系统上的 SMB 文件共享。启用夜间备份。","C":"在连接到 Direct Connect 连接的 VPC 中创建 Amazon FSx for Windows File Server 多可用区文件系统。创建新的 SMB 文件共享。 将夜间数据库导出写入 Amazon FSx 文件系统上的 SMB 文件共享。启用夜间备份。","D":"创建一个新的 S3 存储桶。在连接到 Direct Connect 连接的 VPC 中部署 AWS Storage Gateway 卷网关。创建新的 SMB 文件共享。 将夜间数据库导出写入卷网关上的新 SMB 文件共享，并自动将此数据复制到 S3 存储桶。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":95},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Database","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":232,"question_en":"A company needs to establish a connection from its on-premises data center to AWS. The company needs to connect all of its VPCs that are located in different AWS Regions with transitive routing capabilities between VPC networks. The company also must reduce network outbound tra®c costs, increase bandwidth throughput, and provide a consistent network experience for end users. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要建立从其本地数据中心到 AWS 的连接。该公司需要通过 VPC 网络之间的传递路由功能连接位于不同 AWS 区域的所有 VPC。该公司还必须降低网络出站流量成本，提高带宽吞吐量，并为最终用户提供一致的网络体验。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection between the on-premises data center and a new central VPC. Create VPC peering connections that initiate from the central VPC to all other VPCs.","B":"Create an AWS Direct Connect connection between the on-premises data center and AWS. Provision a transit VIF, and connect it to a Direct Connect gateway. Connect the Direct Connect gateway to all the other VPCs by using a transit gateway in each Region.","C":"Create an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection between the on-premises data center and a new central VPUse a transit gateway with dynamic routing. Connect the transit gateway to all other VPCs.","D":"Create an AWS Direct Connect connection between the on-premises data center and AWS. Establish an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection between all VPCs in each Region. Create VPC peering connections that initiate from the central VPC to all other VPCs."},"options_zh":{"A":"在本地数据中心和新的中央 VPC 之间创建 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 连接。创建从中央 VPC 发起到所有其他 VPC 的 VPC 对等连接。","B":"在本地数据中心和 AWS 之间创建 AWS Direct Connect 连接。配置中转 VIF，并将其连接到 Direct Connect 网关。使用每个区域中 的中转网关将 Direct Connect 网关连接到所有其他 VPC。","C":"在本地数据中心和新的中央 VP 之间创建 AWS 站点到站点 VPN 连接使用具有动态路由的中转网关。将中转网关连接到所有其 他 VPC。","D":"在本地数据中心和 AWS 之间创建 AWS Direct Connect 连接。在每个区域的所有 VPC 之间建立 AWS 站点到站点 VPN 连接。创建 从中央 VPC 发起到所有其他 VPC 的 VPC 对等连接。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":233,"question_en":"A company is migrating its development and production workloads to a new organization in AWS Organizations. The company has created a separate member account for development and a separate member account for production. Consolidated billing is linked to the management account. In the management account, a solutions architect needs to create an IAM user that can stop or terminate resources in both member accounts. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司正在将其开发和生产工作负载迁移到 AWS Organizations 中的新组织。该公司创建了一个用于开发的单独的会员帐户和一个 用于生产的单独的会员帐户。合并账单链接到管理帐户。在管理账户中，解决方案架构师需要创建一个 IAM 用户，该用户可以停止 或终止两个成员账户中的资源。 哪种解决方案可以满足这个要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM user and a cross-account role in the management account. Configure the cross-account role with least privilege access to the member accounts.","B":"Create an IAM user in each member account. In the management account, create a cross-account role that has least privilege access. Grant the IAM users access to the cross-account role by using a trust policy.","C":"Create an IAM user in the management account. In the member accounts, create an IAM group that has least privilege access. Add the IAM user from the management account to each IAM group in the member accounts.","D":"Create an IAM user in the management account. In the member accounts, create cross-account roles that have least privilege access. Grant the IAM user access to the roles by using a trust policy."},"options_zh":{"A":"在管理账户中创建 IAM 用户和跨账户角色。配置对成员账户具有最小权限访问权限的跨账户角色。","B":"在每个成员账户中创建一个 IAM 用户。在管理账户中，创建具有最小权限访问权限的跨账户角色。使用信任策略授予 IAM 用 户对跨账户角色的访问权限。","C":"在管理账户中创建 IAM 用户。在成员账户中，创建具有最小权限访问权限的 IAM 组。将 IAM 用户从管理账户添加到成员账户 中的每个 IAM 组。","D":"在管理账户中创建 IAM 用户。在成员账户中，创建具有最小权限访问权限的跨账户角色。使用信任策略授予 IAM 用户对角色 的访问权限。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":234,"question_en":"A company wants to use AWS for disaster recovery for an on-premises application. The company has hundreds of Windows-based servers that run the application. All the servers mount a common share. The company has an RTO of 15 minutes and an RPO of 5 minutes. The solution must support native failover and fallback capabilities. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司希望使用 AWS 为本地应用程序进行灾难恢复。该公司拥有数百台运行该应用程序的基于 Windows 的服务器。所有服务器都 安装一个公共共享。 该公司的 RTO 为 15 分钟，RPO 为 5 分钟。该解决方案必须支持本机故障转移和回退功能。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Storage Gateway File Gateway. Schedule daily Windows server backups. Save the data to Amazon S3. During a disaster, recover the on-premises servers from the backup. During tailback, run the on-premises servers on Amazon EC2 instances.","B":"Create a set of AWS CloudFormation templates to create infrastructure. Replicate all data to Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) by using AWS DataSync. During a disaster, use AWS CodePipeline to deploy the templates to restore the on-premises servers. Fail back the data by using DataSync.","C":"Create an AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK) pipeline to stand up a multi-site active-active environment on AWS. Replicate data into Amazon S3 by using the s3 sync command. During a disaster, swap DNS endpoints to point to AWS. Fail back the data by using the s3 sync command.","D":"Use AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery to replicate the on-premises servers. Replicate data to an Amazon FSx for Windows File Server file system by using AWS DataSync. Mount the file system to AWS servers. During a disaster, fail over the on-premises servers to AWS. Fail back to new or existing servers by using Elastic Disaster Recovery."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 AWS Storage Gateway 文件网关。安排每日 Windows 服务器备份。将数据保存到 Amazon S3。在灾难期间，从备份恢复本 地服务器。在 tailback 期间，在 Amazon EC2 实例上运行本地服务器。","B":"创建一组 AWS CloudFormation 模板来创建基础设施。使用 AWS DataSync 将所有数据复制到 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)。在灾难期间，使用 AWS CodePipeline 部署模板以恢复本地服务器。使用 DataSync 对数据进行故障回复。","C":"创建 AWS 云开发工具包 (AWS CDK) 管道以在 AWS 上建立多站点主动-主动环境。使用 s3sync 命令将数据复制到 Amazon S3。在 灾难期间，交换 DNS 终端节点以指向 AWS。使用 s3 同步命令对数据进行故障回复。","D":"使用 AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery 复制本地服务器。使用 AWS DataSync 将数据复制到 Amazon FSx for Windows File Server 文件 系统。将文件系统挂载到AWS服务器。在灾难期间，将本地服务器故障转移到 AWS。使用弹性灾难恢复故障恢复到新的或现有的 服务器。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery (DRS) is the purpose-built DR service for replicating on-premises servers. It performs continuous, block-level (Continuous Data Protection) replication that achieves sub-second RPO and an RTO of minutes, comfortably meeting the RPO of 5 minutes and RTO of 15 minutes for hundreds of Windows servers. DRS provides native failover (launching recovery EC2 instances) and native failback (via the Failback Client ISO / DRS Failback automation back to new or existing source servers), exactly the 'native failover and fallback' requirement. The common SMB share is correctly handled by Amazon FSx for Windows File Server (a managed Windows-native SMB file system) populated by AWS DataSync, since Windows servers must mount an SMB share. This is the most cost-effective design that still meets the aggressive RTO/RPO because DRS uses low-cost staging storage and minimal compute until failover. Option B (dump answer) is wrong: it relies on scheduled DataSync plus CloudFormation/CodePipeline redeploy (a backup/restore pattern with no native failover/failback) and targets Amazon EFS, which is NFS/Linux and cannot serve as the Windows SMB common share, and re-provisioning hundreds of servers via a pipeline cannot meet a 15-minute RTO.","explanation_zh":"AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery (DRS) 是專為複製地端伺服器而設計的災難復原服務。它執行持續的區塊層級複製 (Continuous Data Protection)，可達到接近秒級的 RPO 與數分鐘的 RTO，能輕鬆滿足數百台 Windows 伺服器 5 分鐘 RPO 與 15 分鐘 RTO 的需求。DRS 提供原生 failover（啟動復原 EC2 執行個體）與原生 failback（透過 Failback Client ISO / DRS Failback 自動化回到新的或既有來源伺服器），完全符合題目對「native failover and fallback」的要求。共用 SMB 檔案分享則正確地由 Amazon FSx for Windows File Server（Windows 原生受管 SMB 檔案系統）承載，並以 AWS DataSync 複製資料，因為 Windows 伺服器必須掛載 SMB 分享。由於 DRS 在故障切換前僅使用低成本暫存儲存與最少運算資源，這是同時滿足嚴格 RTO/RPO 又最具成本效益的設計。選項 B（dump 答案）錯誤：它依賴排程式 DataSync 加上 CloudFormation/CodePipeline 重新部署（屬於 backup/restore 模式，無原生 failover/failback），且目標為 Amazon EFS（NFS/Linux，無法作為 Windows SMB 共用分享），透過 pipeline 重新佈建數百台伺服器也無法達到 15 分鐘 RTO。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Daily Windows server backups to S3 via File Gateway yield an RPO of up to 24 hours, grossly violating the 5-minute RPO; restore-from-backup also cannot meet a 15-minute RTO and offers no native failover/failback.","why_zh":"透過 File Gateway 每日備份 Windows 伺服器至 S3，RPO 最多達 24 小時，嚴重違反 5 分鐘 RPO；從備份還原也無法達到 15 分鐘 RTO，且無原生 failover/failback。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"This is a backup/restore IaC pattern with no native failover/failback. CodePipeline redeploying CloudFormation for hundreds of servers cannot meet a 15-minute RTO, scheduled DataSync does not give a 5-minute RPO, and Amazon EFS is NFS/Linux so Windows servers cannot mount it as the common SMB share.","why_zh":"這是 backup/restore 的 IaC 模式，沒有原生 failover/failback。透過 CodePipeline 為數百台伺服器重新部署 CloudFormation 無法達到 15 分鐘 RTO，排程式 DataSync 也達不到 5 分鐘 RPO，且 Amazon EFS 為 NFS/Linux，Windows 伺服器無法將其掛載為共用 SMB 分享。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Multi-site active-active is the most expensive DR strategy (a full duplicate running environment) and therefore fails the 'MOST cost-effective' qualifier; standing up active-active for hundreds of stateful Windows servers via CDK is also impractical and overkill for DR.","why_zh":"Multi-site active-active 是成本最高的災難復原策略（需要完整重複的運行環境），因此不符合「MOST cost-effective」的要求；透過 CDK 為數百台有狀態 Windows 伺服器建立 active-active 也不切實際，對於災難復原而言過度設計。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/what-is-drs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/failback.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/WindowsGuide/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/WindowsGuide/migrate-files-fsx.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/disaster-recovery-workloads-on-aws/disaster-recovery-options-in-the-cloud.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":235,"question_en":"A company has built a high performance computing (HPC) cluster in AWS for a tightly coupled workload that generates a large number of shared files stored in Amazon EFS. The cluster was performing well when the number of Amazon EC2 instances in the cluster was 100. However, when the company increased the cluster size to 1.000 EC2 instances, overall performance was well below expectations. Which collection of design choices should a solutions architect make to achieve the maximum performance from the HPC cluster? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 中构建了一个高性能计算 (HPC) 集群，用于紧密耦合的工作负载，该工作负载会生成存储在 Amazon EFS 中的大量 共享文件。当集群中的 Amazon EC2 实例数量为 100 时，集群性能良好。但是，当公司将集群规模增加到 1000 个 EC2 实例时，整体 性能远低于预期。 解决方案架构师应该做出哪些设计选择才能实现 HPC 集群的最大性能？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Ensure the HPC cluster is launched within a single Availability Zone.","B":"Launch the EC2 instances and attach elastic network interfaces in multiples of four.","C":"Select EC2 instance types with an Elastic Fabric Adapter (EFA) enabled.","D":"Ensure the cluster is launched across multiple Availability Zones.","E":"Replace Amazon EFS with multiple Amazon EBS volumes in a RAID array.","F":"Replace Amazon EFS with Amazon FSx for Lustre."},"options_zh":{"A":"确保 HPC 集群在单个可用区内启动。","B":"启动 EC2 实例并附加四个弹性网络接口。","C":"选择启用了 Elastic Fabric Adapter (EFA) 的 EC2 实例类型。","D":"确保集群跨多个可用区启动。","E":"将 Amazon EFS 替换为 RAID 阵列中的多个 Amazon EBS 卷。","F":"将 Amazon EFS 替换为 Amazon FSx for Lustre。"},"answer":["A","C","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ACF":91},"tags":["Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":236,"question_en":"A company is designing an AWS Organizations structure. The company wants to standardize a process to apply tags across the entire organization. The company will require tags with specific values when a user creates a new resource. Each of the company's OUs will have unique tag values. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在设计 AWS Organizations 结构。该公司希望标准化在整个组织中应用标签的流程。当用户创建新资源时，公司将要求具 有特定值的标签。公司的每个 OU 都将具有唯一的标签值。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use an SCP to deny the creation of resources that do not have the required tags. Create a tag policy that includes the tag values that the company has assigned to each OU. Attach the tag policies to the OUs.","B":"Use an SCP to deny the creation of resources that do not have the required tags. Create a tag policy that includes the tag values that the company has assigned to each OU. Attach the tag policies to the organization's management account.","C":"Use an SCP to allow the creation of resources only when the resources have the required tags. Create a tag policy that includes the tag values that the company has assigned to each OU. Attach the tag policies to the OUs.","D":"Use an SCP to deny the creation of resources that do not have the required tags. Define the list of tags. Attach the SCP to the OUs."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 SCP 拒绝创建不具有所需标签的资源。创建一个标签策略，其中包含公司分配给每个 OU 的标签值。将标签策略附加到 OU。","B":"使用 SCP 拒绝创建不具有所需标签的资源。创建一个标签策略，其中包含公司分配给每个 OU 的标签值。将标签策略附加到组 织的管理帐户。","C":"仅当资源具有所需标签时，才使用 SCP 允许创建资源。创建一个标签策略，其中包含公司分配给每个 OU 的标签值。将标签策 略附加到 OU。","D":"使用 SCP 拒绝创建不具有所需标签的资源。定义标签列表。将 SCP 连接到 OU。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":83,"B":17},"tags":["Organizations/Governance"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement has two parts that need two different AWS Organizations features. First, tag policies cannot block the creation of untagged resources: AWS docs state that basic compliance rules 'do not enforce tag compliance on resources that are created without tags' and 'You cannot use this capability to ensure that required or mandatory tag keys are configured at resource creation. Use SCPs to prevent IAM users and roles in target accounts from creating certain resource types if the request doesn't include the specified tags.' So an SCP that denies resource creation when the required tags are absent (using aws:RequestTag/aws:TagKeys conditions) is needed to make tags mandatory at creation. Second, because each OU has unique tag values, the tag policy that defines those compliant values must be attached at the OU level so each OU gets its own value set. AWS's recommended SCP strategy is the deny-list model (FullAWSAccess plus explicit Deny guardrails), so a Deny SCP is the correct construct. Option A combines a Deny SCP with per-OU tag policies, matching the documented pattern exactly.","explanation_zh":"此需求有兩個部分，需要 AWS Organizations 的兩種不同功能。第一，Tag policies 無法阻止建立未加標籤的資源：AWS 文件明確指出 basic compliance rules「不會對建立時未加標籤的資源強制執行標籤合規」，且「無法用此功能確保資源建立時設定了必要或強制的 tag key。請使用 SCP 來阻止目標帳戶中的 IAM 使用者和角色，在請求未包含指定標籤時建立特定資源類型」。因此需要一個 SCP（使用 aws:RequestTag/aws:TagKeys condition）在缺少必要標籤時拒絕資源建立，才能讓標籤在建立時成為強制要求。第二，由於每個 OU 有各自獨特的 tag 值，定義合規值的 tag policy 必須附加在 OU 層級，使每個 OU 取得自己的值集。AWS 推薦的 SCP 策略是 deny-list 模型（FullAWSAccess 加上明確的 Deny 護欄），因此 Deny SCP 才是正確做法。選項 A 將 Deny SCP 與每個 OU 的 tag policies 結合，完全符合文件記載的模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Attaching the tag policies to the management account does not deliver per-OU unique values and does not flow down to member accounts the way an OU-level attachment does; the management account itself is also not constrained by policies in the way OU members are. The per-OU value requirement demands attachment at each OU.","why_zh":"將 tag policies 附加到 management account 無法提供每個 OU 各自獨特的值，也不會像附加在 OU 層級那樣向下套用到成員帳戶；management account 本身也不會像 OU 成員那樣被政策約束。每個 OU 的獨特值需求要求附加在各個 OU 上。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Using an Allow SCP that permits creation 'only when resources have the required tags' is the wrong construct. SCPs operate on a deny-by-default, deny-list model on top of FullAWSAccess; an Allow SCP scoped narrowly to tagged-resource creation would implicitly deny all other actions not listed, breaking normal operations. AWS recommends Deny guardrails, making A's deny approach correct over C's allow approach. This is the dump's suggested answer and it is wrong.","why_zh":"使用 Allow SCP 來「僅在資源具有必要標籤時允許建立」是錯誤的做法。SCP 採用 deny-by-default、在 FullAWSAccess 之上的 deny-list 模型；範圍僅限於加標籤資源建立的 Allow SCP 會隱含地拒絕所有未列出的其他動作，破壞正常運作。AWS 推薦使用 Deny 護欄，因此 A 的 deny 做法優於 C 的 allow 做法。這是 dump 建議答案，但它是錯的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An SCP alone cannot define a structured list of compliant tag values per OU the way a tag policy can, and it provides no standardized organization-wide tag value definition. SCPs enforce presence via conditions but the requirement to standardize and define specific compliant values per OU is precisely the job of tag policies, which D omits entirely.","why_zh":"單獨的 SCP 無法像 tag policy 那樣為每個 OU 定義結構化的合規標籤值清單，也無法提供標準化的組織範圍標籤值定義。SCP 透過 condition 強制標籤存在，但標準化並為每個 OU 定義特定合規值正是 tag policies 的職責，而 D 完全省略了 tag policies。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-enforcement.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_example-tag-policies.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":237,"question_en":"A company has more than 10,000 sensors that send data to an on-premises Apache Kafka server by using the Message Queuing Telemetry Transport (MQTT) protocol. The on-premises Kafka server transforms the data and then stores the results as objects in an Amazon S3 bucket. Recently, the Kafka server crashed. The company lost sensor data while the server was being restored. A solutions architect must create a new design on AWS that is highly available and scalable to prevent a similar occurrence. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有 10,000 多个传感器，这些传感器使用消息队列遥测传输 (MQTT) 协议将数据发送到本地 Apache Kafka 服务器。本地 Kafka 服务器转换数据，然后将结果作为对象存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。 最近，Kafka服务器崩溃了。该公司在恢复服务器时丢失了传感器数据。解决方案架构师必须在 AWS 上创建高度可用且可扩展的新 设计，以防止类似情况发生。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Launch two Amazon EC2 instances to host the Kafka server in an active/standby configuration across two Availability Zones. Create a domain name in Amazon Route 53. Create a Route 53 failover policy. Route the sensors to send the data to the domain name.","B":"Migrate the on-premises Kafka server to Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK). Create a Network Load Balancer (NLB) that points to the Amazon MSK broker. Enable NLB health checks. Route the sensors to send the data to the NLB.","C":"Deploy AWS IoT Core, and connect it to an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream. Use an AWS Lambda function to handle data transformation. Route the sensors to send the data to AWS IoT Core.","D":"Deploy AWS IoT Core, and launch an Amazon EC2 instance to host the Kafka server. Configure AWS IoT Core to send the data to the EC2 instance. Route the sensors to send the data to AWS IoT Core."},"options_zh":{"A":"启动两个 Amazon EC2 实例，以跨两个可用区的主动/备用配置托管 Kafka 服务器。在 Amazon Route 53 中创建域名。创建 Route 53 故障转移策略。路由传感器以将数据发送到域名。","B":"将本地 Kafka 服务器迁移到 Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK)。创建指向 Amazon MSK 代理的网络负载 均衡器 (NLB)。启用 NLB 运行状况检查。路由传感器以将数据发送到 NLB。","C":"部署 AWS IoT Core，并将其连接到 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 传输流。使用 AWS Lambda 函数处理数据转换。路由传感器以 将数据发送到 AWS IoT Core。","D":"部署 AWS IoT Core，并启动 Amazon EC2 实例来托管 Kafka 服务器。配置 AWS IoT Core 以将数据发送到 EC2 实例。路由传感器 以将数据发送到 AWS IoT Core。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":87},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is a highly available, scalable design that eliminates the single self-managed server that crashed and caused data loss. The sensors speak MQTT, so the ingestion layer must natively accept MQTT. AWS IoT Core is a fully managed, serverless message broker that natively supports MQTT (and MQTT over WSS) and scales elastically to billions of messages with no servers to operate or fail. The IoT Core rules engine has a native 'firehose' rule action that sends messages to a Kinesis Data Firehose (Amazon Data Firehose) delivery stream, and Firehose supports an AWS Lambda function for data transformation before durably delivering objects to Amazon S3. This end-to-end pipeline (IoT Core -> Firehose -> Lambda transform -> S3) is fully managed, highly available, and scalable, which directly prevents a recurrence of the server-crash data loss. Option C matches this exactly.","explanation_zh":"需求是一個高可用、可擴展的設計，移除導致資料遺失的單一自管伺服器。感測器使用 MQTT，因此擷取層必須原生支援 MQTT。AWS IoT Core 是全託管、無伺服器的訊息代理，原生支援 MQTT（及 MQTT over WSS），可彈性擴展至數十億則訊息，沒有需要維運或會當機的伺服器。IoT Core 的規則引擎具有原生的 'firehose' 規則動作，可將訊息送至 Kinesis Data Firehose（Amazon Data Firehose）傳遞串流，而 Firehose 支援以 AWS Lambda 函數進行資料轉換後，再持久地將物件交付到 Amazon S3。此端到端管線（IoT Core -> Firehose -> Lambda 轉換 -> S3）為全託管、高可用且可擴展，直接避免伺服器當機造成的資料遺失再次發生。選項 C 完全符合。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Two EC2 instances running Kafka in active/standby with Route 53 failover is still a self-managed Kafka cluster with only one active node. It does not scale elastically, and Route 53 failover relies on DNS TTL and health-check delays during which sensor data is lost - the same failure mode that caused the original outage. High operational overhead and not truly highly available.","why_zh":"兩台 EC2 以主備模式執行 Kafka 並用 Route 53 故障轉移，仍是自管 Kafka 且只有一個活躍節點。無法彈性擴展，且 Route 53 故障轉移依賴 DNS TTL 與健康檢查延遲，期間感測器資料仍會遺失，正是原始故障模式。維運負擔高且非真正高可用。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon MSK and Kafka use the Kafka wire protocol, not MQTT. Placing a Network Load Balancer in front of MSK does not translate the sensors' MQTT traffic into the Kafka protocol, so the 10,000 MQTT sensors cannot publish to MSK this way. It also does not address the transformation/storage pipeline. Fundamental protocol mismatch.","why_zh":"Amazon MSK 與 Kafka 使用 Kafka 線路協定，而非 MQTT。在 MSK 前放置 Network Load Balancer 並不會將感測器的 MQTT 流量轉換為 Kafka 協定，因此 10,000 個 MQTT 感測器無法以此方式發佈到 MSK。也未處理轉換／儲存管線。屬於根本性的協定不相符。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Using IoT Core to feed a single EC2-hosted Kafka server reintroduces the exact single point of failure (one self-managed EC2 Kafka instance) that crashed and caused the data loss. It is neither highly available nor scalable.","why_zh":"用 IoT Core 將資料送至單一 EC2 上的 Kafka 伺服器，重新引入正是當機並導致資料遺失的單點故障（單一自管 EC2 Kafka 執行個體）。既非高可用也不可擴展。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/what-is-aws-iot.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/mqtt.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/iot-rule-actions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/kinesis-firehose-rule-action.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/data-transformation.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":238,"question_en":"A company recently started hosting new application workloads in the AWS Cloud. The company is using Amazon EC2 instances. Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file systems, and Amazon RDS DB instances. To meet regulatory and business requirements, the company must make the following changes for data backups: • Backups must be retained based on custom daily, weekly, and monthly requirements. • Backups must be replicated to at least one other AWS Region immediately after capture. • The backup solution must provide a single source of backup status across the AWS environment. • The backup solution must send immediate notifications upon failure of any resource backup. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST amount of operational overhead? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司最近开始在 AWS 云中托管新的应用程序工作负载。该公司正在使用 Amazon EC2 实例。Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统和 Amazon RDS 数据库实例。 为了满足法规和业务要求，公司必须对数据备份进行以下更改： • 必须根据自定义的每日、每周和每月要求保留备份。 • 备份必须在捕获后立即复制到至少一个其他AWS 区域。 • 备份解决方案必须在整个AWS 环境中提供单一备份状态源。 • 备份解决方案必须在任何资源备份失败时立即发送通知。 哪种步骤组合能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Backup plan with a backup rule for each of the retention requirements.","B":"Configure an AWS Backup plan to copy backups to another Region.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function to replicate backups to another Region and send notification if a failure occurs.","D":"Add an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to the backup plan to send a notification for finished jobs that have any status except BACKUP_JOB_COMPLETED.","E":"Create an Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager (Amazon DLM) snapshot lifecycle policy for each of the retention requirements.","F":"Set up RDS snapshots on each database."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Backup 计划，其中包含满足每个保留要求的备份规则。","B":"配置 AWS Backup 计划以将备份复制到另一个区域。","C":"创建 AWS Lambda 函数以将备份复制到另一个区域并在发生故障时发送通知。","D":"将 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 主题添加到备份计划，以发送具有除 BACKUP_JOB_COMPLETED 之外的任何 状态的已完成作业的通知。","E":"为每个保留要求创建 Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager (Amazon DLM) 快照生命周期策略。","F":"在每个数据库上设置 RDS 快照。"},"answer":["A","B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ABD":100},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":239,"question_en":"A company is developing a gene reporting device that will collect genomic information to assist researchers with collecting large samples of data from a diverse population. The device will push 8 KB of genomic data every second to a data platform that will need to process and analyze the data and provide information back to researchers. The data platform must meet the following requirements: • Provide near-real-time analytics of the inbound genomic data • Ensure the data is ­exible, parallel, and durable • Deliver results of processing to a data warehouse Which strategy should a solutions architect use to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在开发一种基因报告设备，该设备将收集基因组信息，以帮助研究人员从不同人群中收集大量数据样本。该设备每秒将 8 KB 的基因组数据推送到需要处理和分析数据并向研究人员提供信息的数据平台。数据平台必须满足以下要求： • 提供入站基因组数据的近实时分析 • 确保数据灵活、并行和持久 • 将处理结果交付到数据仓库 解决方案架构师应该使用哪种策略来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to collect the inbound sensor data, analyze the data with Kinesis clients, and save the results to an Amazon RDS instance.","B":"Use Amazon Kinesis Data Streams to collect the inbound sensor data, analyze the data with Kinesis clients, and save the results to an Amazon Redshift cluster using Amazon EMR.","C":"Use Amazon S3 to collect the inbound device data, analyze the data from Amazon SQS with Kinesis, and save the results to an Amazon Redshift cluster.","D":"Use an Amazon API Gateway to put requests into an Amazon SQS queue, analyze the data with an AWS Lambda function, and save the results to an Amazon Redshift cluster using Amazon EMR."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 收集入站传感器数据，使用 Kinesis 客户端分析数据，并将结果保存到 Amazon RDS 实例。","B":"使用 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams 收集入站传感器数据，使用 Kinesis 客户端分析数据，并使用 Amazon EMR 将结果保存到 Amazon Redshift 集群。","C":"使用 Amazon S3 收集入站设备数据，通过 Kinesis 分析来自 Amazon SQS 的数据，并将结果保存到 Amazon Redshift 集群。","D":"使用 Amazon API Gateway 将请求放入 Amazon SQS 队列，使用 AWS Lambda 函数分析数据，并使用 Amazon EMR 将结果保存到 Amazon Redshift 集群。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":95},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":240,"question_en":"A solutions architect needs to define a reference architecture for a solution for three-tier applications with web. application, and NoSQL data layers. The reference architecture must meet the following requirements: • High availability within an AWS Region • Able to fail over in 1 minute to another AWS Region for disaster recovery • Provide the most e®cient solution while minimizing the impact on the user experience Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"解决方案架构师需要为带有 Web 的三层应用程序的解决方案定义参考架构。应用程序层和 NoSQL 数据层。参考架构必须满足以下要 求： • AWS 区域内的高可用性 • 能够在 1 分钟内故障转移到另一个 AWS 区域以进行灾难恢复 • 提供最高效的解决方案，同时尽量减少对用户体验的影响 哪些步骤组合将满足这些要求吗？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use an Amazon Route 53 weighted routing policy set to 100/0 across the two selected Regions. Set Time to Live (TTL) to 1 hour.","B":"Use an Amazon Route 53 failover routing policy for failover from the primary Region to the disaster recovery Region. Set Time to Live (TTL) to 30 seconds.","C":"Use a global table within Amazon DynamoDB so data can be accessed in the two selected Regions.","D":"Back up data from an Amazon DynamoDB table in the primary Region every 60 minutes and then write the data to Amazon S3. Use S3 cross-Region replication to copy the data from the primary Region to the disaster recovery Region. Have a script import the data into DynamoDB in a disaster recovery scenario.","E":"Implement a hot standby model using Auto Scaling groups for the web and application layers across multiple Availability Zones in the Regions. Use zonal Reserved Instances for the minimum number of servers and On-Demand Instances for any additional resources.","F":"Use Auto Scaling groups for the web and application layers across multiple Availability Zones in the Regions. Use Spot Instances for the required resources."},"options_zh":{"A":"在两个选定区域中使用设置为 100/0 的 Amazon Route 53 加权路由策略。将生存时间 (TTL) 设置为 1 小时。","B":"使用 Amazon Route 53 故障转移路由策略从主区域故障转移到灾难恢复区域。将生存时间 (TTL) 设置为 30 秒。","C":"在 Amazon DynamoDB 中使用全局表，以便可以在两个选定区域中访问数据。","D":"每 60 分钟备份一次主要区域中的 Amazon DynamoDB 表中的数据，然后将数据写入 Amazon S3。使用S3跨Region复制将数据从 主Region复制到灾备Region。让脚本在灾难恢复场景中将数据导入 DynamoDB。","E":"使用 Auto Scaling 组在区域中的多个可用区的 Web 和应用程序层实施热备用模型。对最少数量的服务器使用区域预留实例，对 任何其他资源使用按需实例。","F":"对区域中多个可用区的 Web 和应用程序层使用 Auto Scaling 组。使用 Spot 实例来获取所需的资源。"},"answer":["D","E","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BCE":94},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirements are: HA within a Region (multi-AZ), fail over to a second Region in under 1 minute, and the most efficient solution that minimizes user-experience impact. (B) A Route 53 failover routing policy with health checks is the canonical active-passive cross-Region DR pattern, and a 30-second TTL lets resolvers re-query quickly so failover completes within ~1 minute; a 100/0 weighted policy with a 1-hour TTL (A) caches stale answers for up to an hour and cannot meet the 1-minute target. (C) A DynamoDB global table gives multi-active, multi-Region replication where any replica serves reads/writes with low/zero RPO, so the NoSQL data is already present and current in the DR Region. (E) Running the web and application tiers as a hot standby across multiple AZs means the DR Region is already up, enabling near-instant failover, while Reserved Instances cover the steady-state minimum (lowest cost) and On-Demand absorbs bursts. The dump's D/E/F is wrong: D backs up only every 60 minutes and requires a script import on failover, giving an RPO/RTO far beyond 1 minute, and F uses Spot Instances, which AWS can reclaim with a 2-minute warning and are unsuitable for HA/DR production tiers that must minimize user impact.","explanation_zh":"需求為：Region 內高可用 (跨多個 AZ)、能在 1 分鐘內切換到第二個 Region 做災難復原、且要在最小化使用者體驗影響下提供最有效率的方案。(B) Route 53 failover 路由政策搭配健康檢查是標準的跨 Region active-passive DR 模式，將 TTL 設為 30 秒可讓 resolver 快速重新查詢，使切換在約 1 分鐘內完成；而 (A) 的 100/0 weighted 政策搭配 1 小時 TTL 會快取舊答案長達一小時，無法達成 1 分鐘目標。(C) DynamoDB global table 提供 multi-active、多 Region 複寫，任一 replica 都可讀寫且 RPO 低或為零，因此 NoSQL 資料在 DR Region 已是最新且可立即使用。(E) 以 hot standby 方式在多個 AZ 運行 web 與 application 層，代表 DR Region 已在運行可近乎即時切換；用 Reserved Instances 涵蓋穩態最低數量 (成本最低)、再以 On-Demand 處理突發負載。Dump 的 D/E/F 不正確：D 每 60 分鐘才備份且切換時還需腳本匯入，RPO/RTO 遠超過 1 分鐘；F 使用 Spot Instances，AWS 可在 2 分鐘預警後回收，不適合必須最小化使用者影響的 HA/DR 正式環境層。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A 1-hour TTL means DNS resolvers cache the answer for up to an hour, so failover cannot complete in 1 minute; a static 100/0 weighted policy also does not automatically shift traffic on failure.","why_zh":"1 小時 TTL 代表 DNS resolver 會快取答案長達一小時，無法在 1 分鐘內完成切換；靜態 100/0 weighted 政策也不會在故障時自動轉移流量。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Backing up DynamoDB only every 60 minutes to S3 and importing via a script during DR gives an RPO of up to an hour and a slow RTO, violating the 1-minute failover and harming the user experience.","why_zh":"每 60 分鐘才備份 DynamoDB 到 S3、且 DR 時要靠腳本匯入，RPO 最長達一小時、RTO 也很慢，違反 1 分鐘切換要求並損害使用者體驗。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Spot Instances can be reclaimed by AWS with a 2-minute notice, making them unreliable for HA/DR production web and application tiers that must minimize impact on user experience.","why_zh":"Spot Instances 可被 AWS 在 2 分鐘預警後回收，對於必須最小化使用者體驗影響的 HA/DR 正式 web 與 application 層而言並不可靠。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/GlobalTables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/disaster-recovery-workloads-on-aws/disaster-recovery-options-in-the-cloud.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":241,"question_en":"A company manufactures smart vehicles. The company uses a custom application to collect vehicle data. The vehicles use the MQTT protocol to connect to the application. The company processes the data in 5-minute intervals. The company then copies vehicle telematics data to on- premises storage. Custom applications analyze this data to detect anomalies. The number of vehicles that send data grows constantly. Newer vehicles generate high volumes of data. The on-premises storage solution is not able to scale for peak tra®c, which results in data loss. The company must modernize the solution and migrate the solution to AWS to resolve the scaling challenges. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司生产智能汽车。该公司使用定制应用程序来收集车辆数据。车辆使用 MQTT 协议连接到应用程序。该公司每 5 分钟处理一 次数据。然后，该公司将车辆远程信息处理数据复制到本地存储。自定义应用程序分析这些数据以检测异常情况。 发送数据的车辆数量不断增长。较新的车辆会产生大量数据。本地存储解决方案无法针对峰值流量进行扩展，从而导致数据丢失。 公司必须对解决方案进行现代化改造并将解决方案迁移到 AWS 以解决扩展挑战。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS IoT Greengrass to send the vehicle data to Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK). Create an Apache Kafka application to store the data in Amazon S3. Use a pretrained model in Amazon SageMaker to detect anomalies.","B":"Use AWS IoT Core to receive the vehicle data. Configure rules to route data to an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream that stores the data in Amazon S3. Create an Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics application that reads from the delivery stream to detect anomalies.","C":"Use AWS IoT FleetWise to collect the vehicle data. Send the data to an Amazon Kinesis data stream. Use an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream to store the data in Amazon S3. Use the built-in machine learning transforms in AWS Glue to detect anomalies.","D":"Use Amazon MQ for RabbitMQ to collect the vehicle data. Send the data to an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream to store the data in Amazon S3. Use Amazon Lookout for Metrics to detect anomalies."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS IoT Greengrass 将车辆数据发送到 Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK)。创建 Apache Kafka 应用 程序以将数据存储在 Amazon S3 中。使用 Amazon SageMaker 中的预训练模型来检测异常。","B":"使用 AWS IoT Core 接收车辆数据。配置规则以将数据路由到将数据存储在 Amazon S3 中的 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 传输 流。创建一个 Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics 应用程序，该应用程序从传输流中读取数据以检测异常。","C":"使用 AWS IoT FleetWise 收集车辆数据。将数据发送到 Amazon Kinesis 数据流。使用 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 传输流将数据 存储在 Amazon S3 中。使用 AWS Glue 中的内置机器学习转换来检测异常。","D":"使用 Amazon MQ for RabbitMQ 收集车辆数据。将数据发送到 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 传输流以将数据存储在 Amazon S3 中。使用 Amazon Lookout for Metrics 检测异常。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":85},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The vehicles already speak MQTT to a custom application, so AWS IoT Core is the natural fully managed MQTT ingestion endpoint. An IoT rule can route messages directly to a Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream, which is serverless and auto-scales to absorb peak traffic before landing data in Amazon S3, eliminating the on-premises scaling/data-loss problem. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics (for SQL) provides a built-in RANDOM_CUT_FOREST function purpose-built to assign anomaly scores to streaming records, so the entire pipeline is managed with no servers to operate. This gives the LEAST operational overhead. Option C fails technically: AWS IoT FleetWise's DataDestinationConfig only supports an MQTT topic, Amazon S3, or Amazon Timestream as destinations (not a Kinesis data stream), FleetWise also requires CAN-bus/OBD signal catalogs and decoder manifests rather than ingesting a generic custom MQTT feed, and AWS Glue ML transforms are FindMatches (record matching/deduplication), not anomaly detection.","explanation_zh":"車輛已透過 MQTT 連接到自訂應用程式，因此 AWS IoT Core 是天然的全代管 MQTT 接收端點。IoT rule 可直接將訊息路由到 Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream，它是無伺服器且自動擴展的，能在資料落地到 Amazon S3 前吸收尖峰流量，解決地端無法擴展與資料遺失的問題。Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics (SQL) 內建 RANDOM_CUT_FOREST 函式，專門用來為串流記錄計算異常分數，因此整條管線皆為代管、無需維運伺服器，達到最低營運負擔。選項 C 技術上不成立：AWS IoT FleetWise 的 DataDestinationConfig 只支援 MQTT topic、Amazon S3 或 Amazon Timestream 作為目的地（不支援 Kinesis data stream），且 FleetWise 需要 CAN-bus/OBD 的 signal catalog 與 decoder manifest，而非接收一般自訂 MQTT 資料流；此外 AWS Glue 的 ML transform 是 FindMatches（記錄比對/去重），並非異常偵測。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS IoT Greengrass is an edge runtime for local devices, not a cloud MQTT ingestion endpoint for fleet vehicles, and self-managing an Amazon MSK cluster plus writing/operating a custom Apache Kafka application to land data in S3 is far higher operational overhead than a managed Firehose-to-S3 pipeline.","why_zh":"AWS IoT Greengrass 是邊緣裝置的本地執行環境，而非車隊雲端 MQTT 接收端點；自行管理 Amazon MSK 叢集並撰寫/維運自訂 Apache Kafka 應用程式把資料寫入 S3，營運負擔遠高於代管的 Firehose-to-S3 管線。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS IoT FleetWise DataDestinationConfig only supports MQTT topic, Amazon S3, or Amazon Timestream as destinations (not a Kinesis data stream as stated), it requires CAN/OBD signal catalogs and decoder manifests rather than a generic custom MQTT feed, and AWS Glue ML transforms are FindMatches for record matching/deduplication, not anomaly detection.","why_zh":"AWS IoT FleetWise 的 DataDestinationConfig 只支援 MQTT topic、Amazon S3 或 Amazon Timestream（並非選項所述的 Kinesis data stream），且需要 CAN/OBD signal catalog 與 decoder manifest 而非一般自訂 MQTT 資料流；AWS Glue 的 ML transform 是用於記錄比對/去重的 FindMatches，並非異常偵測。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon MQ for RabbitMQ is a managed message broker but not a managed IoT/MQTT device gateway and you must size/operate broker instances (more overhead). Amazon Lookout for Metrics is being discontinued/retired and is oriented to business metrics rather than this telematics anomaly use case, making the design weaker than the IoT-native Option B.","why_zh":"Amazon MQ for RabbitMQ 是代管訊息代理但非代管 IoT/MQTT 裝置閘道，且需自行調整/維運 broker 執行個體（負擔較高）。Amazon Lookout for Metrics 已停止服務/退役，且偏向商業指標而非此車載遙測異常情境，整體設計弱於 IoT 原生的選項 B。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/aws-iot-how-it-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/data-transformation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/app-anomaly-detection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot-fleetwise/latest/APIReference/API_DataDestinationConfig.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/console-machine-learning-transforms.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":242,"question_en":"During an audit, a security team discovered that a development team was putting IAM user secret access keys in their code and then committing it to an AWS CodeCommit repository. The security team wants to automatically find and remediate instances of this security vulnerability. Which solution will ensure that the credentials are appropriately secured automatically?","question_zh":"在审核过程中，安全团队发现开发团队将 IAM 用户秘密访问密钥放入其代码中，然后将其提交到 AWS CodeCommit 存储库。安全团 队希望自动查找并修复此安全漏洞的实例。 哪种解决方案将确保凭证自动得到适当保护？","options_en":{"A":"Run a script nightly using AWS Systems Manager Run Command to search for credentials on the development instances. If found, use AWS Secrets Manager to rotate the credentials","B":"Use a scheduled AWS Lambda function to download and scan the application code from CodeCommit. If credentials are found, generate new credentials and store them in AWS KMS.","C":"Configure Amazon Macie to scan for credentials in CodeCommit repositories. If credentials are found, trigger an AWS Lambda function to disable the credentials and notify the user.","D":"Configure a CodeCommit trigger to invoke an AWS Lambda function to scan new code submissions for credentials. If credentials are found, disable them in AWS IAM and notify the user."},"options_zh":{"A":"每晚使用 AWS Systems Manager Run Command 运行脚本以搜索开发实例上的凭证。如果找到，请使用 AWS Secrets Manager 轮 换凭证","B":"使用计划的 AWS Lambda 函数从 CodeCommit 下载并扫描应用程序代码。如果找到凭证，则生成新凭证并将其存储在 AWS KMS 中。","C":"配置 Amazon Macie 以扫描 CodeCommit 存储库中的凭证。如果找到凭证，则触发 AWS Lambda 函数以禁用凭证并通知用户。","D":"配置 CodeCommit 触发器以调用 AWS Lambda 函数来扫描新提交的代码以获取凭证。如果找到凭证，请在 AWS IAM 中禁用它们 并通知用户。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":93},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The secret access keys are committed into a CodeCommit repository, so the remediation must act on CodeCommit push events. CodeCommit natively supports triggers that invoke an AWS Lambda function on code pushes (up to 10 triggers per repo). The Lambda can scan each new submission for credentials and, if found, disable the exposed IAM keys (the AWS-recommended response to compromised credentials is to deactivate/disable them) and notify the user. This is fully automatic and event-driven, exactly what the question asks. Option A is wrong because the keys live in the repository, not on development instances, and rotating via Secrets Manager does not address keys already exposed in source. Option B incorrectly proposes storing generated credentials in AWS KMS (KMS manages encryption keys, not arbitrary secrets) and relies on slower scheduled scanning. Option C is wrong because Amazon Macie only discovers sensitive data in Amazon S3 buckets and cannot scan CodeCommit repositories.","explanation_zh":"secret access keys 被提交進了 CodeCommit repository，因此修復動作必須針對 CodeCommit 的 push 事件。CodeCommit 原生支援 triggers，可在程式碼推送時呼叫 AWS Lambda function（每個 repo 最多 10 個 trigger）。Lambda 可掃描每次新提交是否含憑證，若找到則停用（disable）外洩的 IAM keys（AWS 建議對遭洩漏憑證的處置是停用而非僅輪替）並通知使用者，完全自動且為事件驅動，正符合題意。選項 A 錯誤，因為金鑰存在於 repository 而非開發實例上，且用 Secrets Manager 輪替無法處理已暴露在原始碼中的金鑰。選項 B 錯誤地把產生的憑證存到 AWS KMS（KMS 管理加密金鑰，而非任意 secrets），且採用較慢的排程掃描。選項 C 錯誤，因為 Amazon Macie 僅能在 Amazon S3 buckets 中發現敏感資料，無法掃描 CodeCommit repositories。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The credentials are in a CodeCommit repository, not on development instances, so Systems Manager Run Command scans the wrong location. Rotating keys via Secrets Manager also does not remediate keys already committed in source code.","why_zh":"憑證在 CodeCommit repository 中，而非開發實例上，因此用 Systems Manager Run Command 掃描的是錯誤位置。透過 Secrets Manager 輪替金鑰也無法處理已提交在原始碼中的金鑰。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS KMS stores and manages encryption keys, not arbitrary credentials/secrets, so storing new credentials in KMS is technically incorrect. A scheduled scan is also less timely than an event-driven CodeCommit trigger.","why_zh":"AWS KMS 用於儲存與管理加密金鑰，而非任意憑證/secrets，因此把新憑證存到 KMS 在技術上錯誤。排程掃描也不如 CodeCommit trigger 的事件驅動方式即時。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Macie only discovers and scans sensitive data within Amazon S3 buckets; it cannot scan CodeCommit repositories, so the trigger condition can never fire.","why_zh":"Amazon Macie 只能發現並掃描 Amazon S3 buckets 內的敏感資料，無法掃描 CodeCommit repositories，因此觸發條件根本不會成立。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/how-to-notify.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/how-to-notify-lambda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/what-is-macie.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":243,"question_en":"A company has a data lake in Amazon S3 that needs to be accessed by hundreds of applications across many AWS accounts. The company's information security policy states that the S3 bucket must not be accessed over the public internet and that each application should have the minimum permissions necessary to function. To meet these requirements, a solutions architect plans to use an S3 access point that is restricted to specific VPCs for each application. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect take to implement this solution? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司在 Amazon S3 中拥有一个数据湖，多个 AWS 账户中的数百个应用程序需要访问该数据湖。该公司的信息安全政策规定，不 得通过公共互联网访问 S3 存储桶，并且每个应用程序都应拥有运行所需的最低权限。 为了满足这些要求，解决方案架构师计划使用仅限于每个应用程序的特定 VPC 的 S3 接入点。 解决方案架构师应采取哪些步骤组合来实施该解决方案？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an S3 access point for each application in the AWS account that owns the S3 bucket. Configure each access point to be accessible only from the application’s VPC. Update the bucket policy to require access from an access point.","B":"Create an interface endpoint for Amazon S3 in each application's VPC. Configure the endpoint policy to allow access to an S3 access point. Create a VPC gateway attachment for the S3 endpoint.","C":"Create a gateway endpoint for Amazon S3 in each application's VPConfigure the endpoint policy to allow access to an S3 access point. Specify the route table that is used to access the access point.","D":"Create an S3 access point for each application in each AWS account and attach the access points to the S3 bucket. Configure each access point to be accessible only from the application's VPC. Update the bucket policy to require access from an access point.","E":"Create a gateway endpoint for Amazon S3 in the data lake's VPC. Attach an endpoint policy to allow access to the S3 bucket. Specify the route table that is used to access the bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"为拥有 S3 存储桶的 AWS 账户中的每个应用程序创建一个 S3 访问点。将每个访问点配置为只能从应用程序的 VPC 访问。更新 存储桶策略以要求从接入点进行访问。","B":"在每个应用程序的 VPC 中为 Amazon S3 创建接口终端节点。配置端点策略以允许访问 S3 访问点。为 S3 终端节点创建 VPC 网 关连接。","C":"在每个应用程序的 VP 中为 Amazon S3 创建网关终端节点，配置终端节点策略以允许访问 S3 访问点。指定用于访问接入点的 路由表。","D":"为每个 AWS 账户中的每个应用程序创建一个 S3 访问点，并将访问点附加到 S3 存储桶。将每个访问点配置为只能从应用程序 的 VPC 访问。更新存储桶策略以要求从接入点进行访问。","E":"在数据湖的 VPC 中为 Amazon S3 创建网关终端节点。附加端点策略以允许访问 S3 存储桶。指定用于访问存储桶的路由表。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AC":68,"AB":20},"tags":["Storage","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is private (non-internet) S3 access for hundreds of applications across many accounts, each with least privilege, using VPC-restricted S3 access points. Per AWS docs, S3 access points are created in the account that OWNS the bucket (the create-access-point CLI uses the bucket owner's --account-id), are restricted to a single VPC via VpcConfiguration (network origin = VPC), and the bucket policy can be updated to delegate/require access through access points. That is exactly Option A. To actually reach the access point privately from each consumer VPC, you create an S3 VPC endpoint in that application's VPC and grant the access point in the endpoint policy. A gateway endpoint (Option C) is added to the VPC route table, supports an endpoint policy, keeps traffic on the AWS network (off the public internet), and is free, so it is the correct and simplest choice. Option B describes an interface endpoint but tacks on a fabricated step, 'Create a VPC gateway attachment for the S3 endpoint,' which is not a real action (interface endpoints use ENIs and security groups, not gateway attachments), so B is invalid even though interface endpoints can otherwise work.","explanation_zh":"需求是讓數百個跨帳號的應用程式以私有方式(非公網)存取資料湖中的 S3,並使用限制到特定 VPC 的 S3 access point、各自最小權限。依 AWS 文件,S3 access point 必須建立在「擁有該 bucket 的帳號」中(create-access-point CLI 使用 bucket owner 的 --account-id),透過 VpcConfiguration 限制為單一 VPC(network origin = VPC),並可更新 bucket policy 要求只能透過 access point 存取,這正是選項 A。要從每個消費端 VPC 私有地連到 access point,需在該應用程式的 VPC 中建立 S3 VPC endpoint,並在 endpoint policy 中允許該 access point。Gateway endpoint(選項 C)會加入 VPC route table、支援 endpoint policy、流量留在 AWS 網路(不經公網)且免費,因此是正確且最簡單的選擇。選項 B 描述 interface endpoint,但加上虛構步驟「Create a VPC gateway attachment for the S3 endpoint」,此動作不存在(interface endpoint 使用 ENI 與 security group,而非 gateway attachment),故 B 無效,即使 interface endpoint 本身也能運作。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Interface endpoints do work with access points, but the step 'Create a VPC gateway attachment for the S3 endpoint' is fabricated and incorrect. Interface endpoints are realized as ENIs with security groups via PrivateLink; there is no 'VPC gateway attachment' action for them. The extra cost and complexity are also unnecessary here since no on-premises or cross-Region access is required.","why_zh":"Interface endpoint 確實可搭配 access point,但步驟「Create a VPC gateway attachment for the S3 endpoint」是虛構且錯誤的。Interface endpoint 透過 PrivateLink 以 ENI 加 security group 實作,並無所謂「VPC gateway attachment」動作。此處不需要地端或跨區存取,interface endpoint 的額外費用與複雜度也不必要。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Incorrect because S3 access points are created in the account that owns the bucket, not 'in each AWS account.' You do not create per-account access points in the consumer accounts and 'attach' them to the bucket. The ownership/creation model in this option contradicts AWS documentation.","why_zh":"錯誤,因為 S3 access point 是建立在擁有 bucket 的帳號中,而非「在每個 AWS 帳號」中建立。你不會在各消費端帳號建立各自的 access point 再「附加」到 bucket。此選項的擁有/建立模型與 AWS 文件相違背。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Wrong direction: it puts the gateway endpoint in the data lake's VPC and points it at the bucket. The endpoint must live in each application's (consumer) VPC so those VPCs can reach S3 privately. A single endpoint in the data lake's VPC does nothing for the hundreds of consumer VPCs, and it ignores access points entirely.","why_zh":"方向錯誤:它把 gateway endpoint 放在資料湖的 VPC 並指向 bucket。endpoint 必須位於每個應用程式(消費端)的 VPC,才能讓這些 VPC 私有地連到 S3。把單一 endpoint 放在資料湖 VPC 對數百個消費端 VPC 毫無作用,且完全忽略 access point。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/access-points.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/access-points-vpc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/vpc-endpoints-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/privatelink-interface-endpoints.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・複選"},{"id":244,"question_en":"A company has developed a hybrid solution between its data center and AWS. The company uses Amazon VPC and Amazon EC2 instances that send application logs to Amazon CloudWatch. The EC2 instances read data from multiple relational databases that are hosted on premises. The company wants to monitor which EC2 instances are connected to the databases in near-real time. The company already has a monitoring solution that uses Splunk on premises. A solutions architect needs to determine how to send networking tra®c to Splunk. How should the solutions architect meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司开发了其数据中心和 AWS 之间的混合解决方案。该公司使用 Amazon VPC 和 Amazon EC2 实例将应用程序日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch。EC2 实例从本地托管的多个关系数据库读取数据。 该公司希望近乎实时地监控哪些 EC2 实例连接到数据库。该公司已经拥有在本地使用 Splunk 的监控解决方案。解决方案架构师需要 确定如何将网络流量发送到 Splunk。 解决方案架构师应该如何满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable VPC ­ows logs, and send them to CloudWatch. Create an AWS Lambda function to periodically export the CloudWatch logs to an Amazon S3 bucket by using the pre-defined export function. Generate ACCESS_KEY and SECRET_KEY AWS credentials. Configure Splunk to pull the logs from the S3 bucket by using those credentials.","B":"Create an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream with Splunk as the destination. Configure a pre-processing AWS Lambda function with a Kinesis Data Firehose stream processor that extracts individual log events from records sent by CloudWatch Logs subscription filters. Enable VPC ­ows logs, and send them to CloudWatch. Create a CloudWatch Logs subscription that sends log events to the Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream.","C":"Ask the company to log every request that is made to the databases along with the EC2 instance IP address. Export the CloudWatch logs to an Amazon S3 bucket. Use Amazon Athena to query the logs grouped by database name. Export Athena results to another S3 bucket. Invoke an AWS Lambda function to automatically send any new file that is put in the S3 bucket to Splunk.","D":"Send the CloudWatch logs to an Amazon Kinesis data stream with Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for SQL Applications. Configure a 1- minute sliding window to collect the events. Create a SQL query that uses the anomaly detection template to monitor any networking tra®c anomalies in near-real time. Send the result to an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream with Splunk as the destination."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 VPC 流日志，并将其发送到 CloudWatch。创建 AWS Lambda 函数，以使用预定义的导出函数定期将 CloudWatch 日志导出 到 Amazon S3 存储桶。生成 ACCESS_KEY 和 SECRET_KEY AWS 凭证。配置 Splunk 以使用这些凭据从 S3 存储桶中提取日志。","B":"创建 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 传输流，并将 Splunk 作为目标。使用 Kinesis Data Firehose 流处理器配置预处理 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数从 CloudWatch Logs 订阅筛选器发送的记录中提取各个日志事件。启用 VPC 流日志，并将其发送到 CloudWatch。创 建将日志事件发送到 Kinesis Data Firehose 传输流的 CloudWatch Logs 订阅。","C":"要求公司记录向数据库发出的每个请求以及 EC2 实例 IP 地址。将 CloudWatch 日志导出到 Amazon S3 存储桶。使用 Amazon Athena 查询按数据库名称分组的日志。将 Athena 结果导出到另一个 S3 存储桶。调用 AWS Lambda 函数以自动将放入 S3 存储桶 中的任何新文件发送到 Splunk。","D":"使用 Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for SQL 应用程序将 CloudWatch 日志发送到 Amazon Kinesis 数据流。配置 1 分钟滑动窗口来 收集事件。创建一个使用异常检测模板的 SQL 查询来近乎实时地监控任何网络流量异常。将结果发送到 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 传输流，并以 Splunk 作为目标。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is near-real-time visibility into which EC2 instances connect to the on-premises databases, streamed to an existing on-prem Splunk monitor. VPC Flow Logs capture the IP traffic (source/destination IPs, ports) needed to identify which instances talk to the databases, and they can be published to CloudWatch Logs. To stream CloudWatch Logs to Splunk in near real time, the AWS-native pattern is a CloudWatch Logs subscription filter delivering log events to an Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream that has Splunk as a destination. CloudWatch Logs subscription records are base64-encoded, gzip-compressed, and wrapped with metadata containing multiple logEvents per record; AWS documentation explicitly states that for a Splunk destination you must extract the individual message/log-event fields (via decompression + message extraction or, equivalently, a Firehose data-transformation Lambda) so Splunk can parse the data. Option B describes exactly this end-to-end pipeline (Firehose to Splunk + pre-processing Lambda processor that extracts individual log events from CloudWatch Logs subscription records + VPC Flow Logs to CloudWatch + subscription filter to Firehose), making it the correct, fully managed near-real-time solution.","explanation_zh":"需求是近即時掌握哪些 EC2 instance 連到地端資料庫,並把網路流量送到既有的地端 Splunk 監控。VPC Flow Logs 可擷取 IP 流量(來源/目的 IP、連接埠),用以辨識哪些 instance 與資料庫通訊,並可發佈到 CloudWatch Logs。要近即時把 CloudWatch Logs 串流到 Splunk,AWS 原生模式是用 CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 將 log events 送到以 Splunk 為目的地的 Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream。CloudWatch Logs subscription 記錄是 base64 編碼、gzip 壓縮,並包覆每筆含多個 logEvents 的中繼資料;AWS 文件明確指出,送到 Splunk 目的地時必須抽取出個別的 message/log-event 欄位(透過解壓縮 + message extraction,或等效的 Firehose data-transformation Lambda),Splunk 才能解析資料。選項 B 正好描述這條完整管線(Firehose 到 Splunk + 預處理 Lambda 抽取 CloudWatch Logs subscription 記錄中的個別 log events + VPC Flow Logs 送 CloudWatch + subscription filter 送 Firehose),因此是正確且全託管的近即時方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it is wrong: a Lambda periodically exporting CloudWatch Logs to S3 and Splunk pulling on a schedule is batch, not near-real-time, and the CreateExportTask API is explicitly intended for bulk export (can take up to 12 hours), not streaming. It also relies on long-lived static ACCESS_KEY/SECRET_KEY credentials, an insecure anti-pattern AWS discourages.","why_zh":"這是 dump 建議答案,但是錯的:用 Lambda 定期把 CloudWatch Logs 匯出到 S3、Splunk 再排程拉取屬於批次而非近即時;CreateExportTask 是大量匯出用途(最長可達 12 小時),不適合串流。且依賴長期靜態 ACCESS_KEY/SECRET_KEY 憑證,屬於 AWS 不建議的不安全反模式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Requiring the application to log every database request plus running Athena queries over S3 exports and triggering Lambda on new files is a batch, high-overhead analytics workflow, not near-real-time network monitoring. It also changes the application and does not use the natural VPC Flow Logs network-traffic source the question implies.","why_zh":"要求應用程式記錄每筆資料庫請求,再用 Athena 查 S3 匯出檔、對新檔觸發 Lambda,屬於批次、高負擔的分析流程,而非近即時網路監控。它還需改動應用程式,也未使用題目暗示的 VPC Flow Logs 網路流量來源。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Kinesis Data Analytics with an anomaly-detection (RANDOM_CUT_FOREST) SQL template detects traffic anomalies, but the requirement is to monitor which EC2 instances connect to the databases, not to flag anomalies. The added analytics layer over-engineers the solution and discards the connection records Splunk needs to see.","why_zh":"Kinesis Data Analytics 搭配異常偵測(RANDOM_CUT_FOREST)SQL 範本是偵測流量異常,但需求是監控哪些 EC2 instance 連到資料庫,而非標記異常。多加的分析層過度設計,且會丟失 Splunk 需要看到的連線記錄。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/Message_extraction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/writing-with-cloudwatch-logs-decompression.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/flow-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/flow-logs-cwl.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":245,"question_en":"A company has five development teams that have each created five AWS accounts to develop and host applications. To track spending, the development teams log in to each account every month, record the current cost from the AWS Billing and Cost Management console, and provide the information to the company's finance team. The company has strict compliance requirements and needs to ensure that resources are created only in AWS Regions in the United States. However, some resources have been created in other Regions. A solutions architect needs to implement a solution that gives the finance team the ability to track and consolidate expenditures for all the accounts. The solution also must ensure that the company can create resources only in Regions in the United States. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally e®cient way? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司有五个开发团队，每个团队创建了五个 AWS 账户来开发和托管应用程序。为了跟踪支出，开发团队每月登录每个账户，从 AWS 账单和成本管理控制台记录当前成本，并将信息提供给公司的财务团队。 该公司有严格的合规性要求，需要确保仅在美国的 AWS 区域创建资源。然而，其他区域已经创建了一些资源。 解决方案架构师需要实施一个解决方案，使财务团队能够跟踪和合并所有账户的支出。该解决方案还必须确保公司只能在美国的地 区创建资源。 哪种步骤组合能够以最高效的方式满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a new account to serve as a management account. Create an Amazon S3 bucket for the finance team. Use AWS Cost and Usage Reports to create monthly reports and to store the data in the finance team's S3 bucket.","B":"Create a new account to serve as a management account. Deploy an organization in AWS Organizations with all features enabled. Invite all the existing accounts to the organization. Ensure that each account accepts the invitation.","C":"Create an OU that includes all the development teams. Create an SCP that allows the creation of resources only in Regions that are in the United States. Apply the SCP to the OU.","D":"Create an OU that includes all the development teams. Create an SCP that denies the creation of resources in Regions that are outside the United States. Apply the SCP to the OU.","E":"Create an IAM role in the management account. Attach a policy that includes permissions to view the Billing and Cost Management console. Allow the finance team users to assume the role. Use AWS Cost Explorer and the Billing and Cost Management console to analyze cost.","F":"Create an IAM role in each AWS account. Attach a policy that includes permissions to view the Billing and Cost Management console. Allow the finance team users to assume the role."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新帐户作为管理帐户。为财务团队创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。使用 AWS 成本和使用情况报告创建月度报告并将数 据存储在财务团队的 S3 存储桶中。","B":"创建一个新帐户作为管理帐户。在 AWS Organizations 中部署组织并启用所有功能。邀请所有现有帐户加入组织。确保每个帐 户都接受邀请。","C":"创建一个包含所有开发团队的 OU。创建一个 SCP，仅允许在美国的区域中创建资源。将 SCP 应用到 OU。","D":"创建一个包含所有开发团队的 OU。创建一个 SCP，拒绝在美国以外的区域创建资源。将 SCP 应用到 OU。","E":"在管理账户中创建 IAM 角色。附加包含查看计费和成本管理控制台的权限的策略。允许财务团队用户承担该角色。使用 AWS Cost Explorer 以及账单和成本管理控制台来分析成本。","F":"在每个 AWS 账户中创建 IAM 角色。附加包含查看计费和成本管理控制台的权限的策略。允许财务团队用户承担该角色。"},"answer":["A","C","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BDE":87},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The finance team needs consolidated cost visibility across all 25 accounts, and resource creation must be limited to US Regions. (B) Creating a management account and deploying AWS Organizations with all features enabled is required: SCPs are only available with all features enabled, not consolidated-billing-only, and Organizations is what enables consolidated billing. (D) An SCP that DENIES actions in non-US Regions is the correct, recommended pattern (AWS Control Tower's Region deny control uses exactly this deny strategy). An SCP never grants permissions, so an 'allow only US Regions' SCP (option C) is the wrong construct and is operationally fragile because it would block global/IAM/STS/CloudFront-style actions that route through us-east-1 and require explicit NotAction exceptions. (E) Because the management account has full access to ALL Billing and Cost Management data for both management and member accounts via consolidated billing, a single IAM role in the management account lets the finance team use Cost Explorer and the Billing console to see consolidated spend - the most operationally efficient approach. Option F (a role in each of the 25 accounts, logging into each) reproduces the exact manual per-account process the company wants to eliminate, and option A (Cost and Usage Reports to S3) is more setup than the simpler Cost Explorer access and still requires the org from B. The dump answer A/C/F is wrong on all three counts.","explanation_zh":"財務團隊需要跨全部 25 個帳戶的合併成本可視性，且資源建立必須限制在美國 Regions。(B) 必須建立管理帳戶並部署啟用所有功能 (all features enabled) 的 AWS Organizations：SCP 只有在啟用所有功能時才可用，僅啟用合併帳單 (consolidated billing only) 時無法使用；而且 Organizations 才能啟用合併帳單。(D) 使用「拒絕 (deny) 非美國 Regions 動作」的 SCP 才是正確且建議的做法 (AWS Control Tower 的 Region deny control 正是採用此拒絕策略)。SCP 永遠不會授予權限，因此「只允許美國 Regions」的 SCP (選項 C) 是錯誤的構造，而且在運維上很脆弱，因為它會阻擋透過 us-east-1 路由的全域/IAM/STS/CloudFront 類動作，需要明確的 NotAction 例外。(E) 由於管理帳戶透過合併帳單對管理帳戶與成員帳戶的全部 Billing and Cost Management 資料都有完整存取權，在管理帳戶建立單一 IAM role 即可讓財務團隊使用 Cost Explorer 與 Billing console 查看合併支出，這是運維上最有效率的方式。選項 F (在 25 個帳戶各建立 role 並逐一登入) 重現了公司想消除的逐帳戶手動流程；選項 A (Cost and Usage Reports 存到 S3) 設定比單純的 Cost Explorer 存取更繁瑣，且仍需 B 的組織。Dump 答案 A/C/F 三項皆錯。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Cost and Usage Reports to an S3 bucket is more setup-heavy than simply granting the finance team Cost Explorer/Billing console access in the management account, and it still depends on an organization existing (B). It is the less operationally efficient way to give the finance team consolidated tracking.","why_zh":"將 Cost and Usage Reports 輸出到 S3 bucket 比單純在管理帳戶授予財務團隊 Cost Explorer/Billing console 存取更繁瑣，且仍需先有組織 (B)。對於提供合併追蹤而言運維效率較低。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An SCP never grants permissions; an 'allow only US Regions' allow-list SCP is the wrong construct and is fragile because it blocks global services (IAM, STS, CloudFront, Organizations) that operate via us-east-1, requiring complex NotAction carve-outs. The deny-based SCP in D is the AWS-recommended Region-restriction pattern.","why_zh":"SCP 永遠不授予權限；「只允許美國 Regions」的允許清單式 SCP 是錯誤構造且脆弱，因為它會阻擋透過 us-east-1 運作的全域服務 (IAM、STS、CloudFront、Organizations)，需要複雜的 NotAction 例外。D 的拒絕式 SCP 才是 AWS 建議的 Region 限制做法。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Creating an IAM role in every one of the 25 accounts and assuming each one to view billing reproduces the manual per-account login process the company wants to eliminate. The management account already has full consolidated cost data for all member accounts, so a single role there (E) is far more operationally efficient.","why_zh":"在全部 25 個帳戶各建立 IAM role 並逐一切換查看帳單，正好重現公司想消除的逐帳戶手動登入流程。管理帳戶已擁有所有成員帳戶的完整合併成本資料，因此在那裡建立單一 role (E) 運維效率高得多。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/ou-region-deny.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/consolidated-billing.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・複選"},{"id":246,"question_en":"A company needs to create and manage multiple AWS accounts for a number of departments from a central location. The security team requires read-only access to all accounts from its own AWS account. The company is using AWS Organizations and created an account for the security team. How should a solutions architect meet these requirements?","question_zh":"公司需要从一个中心位置为多个部门创建和管理多个 AWS 账户。安全团队需要从其自己的 AWS 账户对所有账户进行只读访问。该 公司正在使用 AWS Organizations 并为安全团队创建了一个账户。 解决方案架构师应该如何满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use the OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM role to create a new IAM policy with read-only access in each member account. Establish a trust relationship between the IAM policy in each member account and the security account. Ask the security team to use the IAM policy to gain access.","B":"Use the OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM role to create a new IAM role with read-only access in each member account. Establish a trust relationship between the IAM role in each member account and the security account. Ask the security team to use the IAM role to gain access.","C":"Ask the security team to use AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) to call the AssumeRole API for the OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM role in the management account from the security account. Use the generated temporary credentials to gain access.","D":"Ask the security team to use AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) to call the AssumeRole API for the OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM role in the member account from the security account. Use the generated temporary credentials to gain access."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM 角色在每个成员账户中创建具有只读访问权限的新 IAM 策略。在每个成员账户中的 IAM策略和安全账户之间建立信任关系。要求安全团队使用 IAM 策略来获取访问权限。","B":"使用 OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM 角色在每个成员账户中创建一个具有只读访问权限的新 IAM 角色。在每个成员账户中 的IAM角色和安全账户之间建立信任关系。要求安全团队使用 IAM 角色来获取访问权限。","C":"要求安全团队使用 AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) 从安全账户中调用管理账户中 OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM 角色 的 AssumeRole API。使用生成的临时凭据来获取访问权限。","D":"要求安全团队使用 AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) 从安全账户中调用成员账户中 OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM 角色 的 AssumeRole API。使用生成的临时凭据来获取访问权限。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":247,"question_en":"A large company runs workloads in VPCs that are deployed across hundreds of AWS accounts. Each VPC consists of public subnets and private subnets that span across multiple Availability Zones. NAT gateways are deployed in the public subnets and allow outbound connectivity to the internet from the private subnets. A solutions architect is working on a hub-and-spoke design. All private subnets in the spoke VPCs must route tra®c to the internet through an egress VPC. The solutions architect already has deployed a NAT gateway in an egress VPC in a central AWS account. Which set of additional steps should the solutions architect take to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家大公司在跨数百个 AWS 账户部署的 VPC 中运行工作负载。每个 VPC 均由跨多个可用区的公有子网和私有子网组成。NAT 网关 部署在公共子网中，并允许从私有子网到 Internet 的出站连接。 解决方案架构师正在研究中心辐射型设计。分支 VPC 中的所有私有子网必须通过出口 VPC 将流量路由到互联网。解决方案架构师已 在中央 AWS 账户的出口 VPC 中部署了 NAT 网关。 解决方案架构师应采取哪一组附加步骤来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create peering connections between the egress VPC and the spoke VPCs. Configure the required routing to allow access to the internet.","B":"Create a transit gateway, and share it with the existing AWS accounts. Attach existing VPCs to the transit gateway. Configure the required routing to allow access to the internet.","C":"Create a transit gateway in every account. Attach the NAT gateway to the transit gateways. Configure the required routing to allow access to the internet.","D":"Create an AWS PrivateLink connection between the egress VPC and the spoke VPCs. Configure the required routing to allow access to the internet."},"options_zh":{"A":"在出口 VPC 和分支 VPC 之间创建对等连接。配置所需的路由以允许访问互联网。","B":"创建中转网关，并将其与现有 AWS 账户共享。将现有 VPC 连接到中转网关。配置所需的路由以允许访问互联网。","C":"在每个账户中创建一个中转网关。将 NAT 网关连接到中转网关。配置所需的路由以允许访问互联网。","D":"在出口 VPC 和分支 VPC 之间创建 AWS PrivateLink 连接。配置所需的路由以允许访问互联网。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":94},"tags":["Networking/DNS"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The scenario is the textbook AWS centralized-egress pattern: NAT gateways live in a central egress VPC and all spoke VPCs route internet-bound traffic to it. The AWS whitepaper 'Building a Scalable and Secure Multi-VPC AWS Network Infrastructure' states that to centralize, you create an egress VPC, deploy NAT gateways there, and route all egress traffic from spoke VPCs to those NAT gateways using Transit Gateway (or Cloud WAN). With hundreds of accounts/VPCs, you create a Transit Gateway and share it via AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM) with the existing accounts, attach the VPCs, and configure routing (spoke route tables point 0.0.0.0/0 to the TGW; the egress VPC's TGW route table sends internet traffic to the NAT gateway, then the IGW). Transit Gateway is the AWS-recommended hub-and-spoke model precisely because it scales to thousands of VPCs and avoids the unmanageable many-to-many mesh. Therefore B is correct.","explanation_zh":"此情境正是 AWS 標準的集中式出口 (centralized egress) 架構: NAT gateway 部署在中央 egress VPC, 所有 spoke VPC 將前往網際網路的流量導向該處。AWS 白皮書《Building a Scalable and Secure Multi-VPC AWS Network Infrastructure》明確指出, 要集中化就是建立 egress VPC、在其中部署 NAT gateway, 並透過 Transit Gateway (或 Cloud WAN) 將所有 spoke VPC 的出口流量導向這些 NAT gateway。面對數百個帳戶與 VPC, 做法是建立一個 Transit Gateway, 透過 AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM) 分享給既有帳戶, 將 VPC 附加 (attach) 上去, 並設定路由 (spoke 路由表將 0.0.0.0/0 指向 TGW; egress VPC 的 TGW 路由表將網際網路流量送往 NAT gateway, 再到 IGW)。Transit Gateway 正是 AWS 建議的 hub-and-spoke 模型, 因為它能擴展到數千個 VPC 並避免難以維護的多對多網狀連線。因此 B 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"VPC peering does not support transitive routing and cannot scale to hundreds of VPCs. You would need a full mesh of point-to-point peerings, and peering cannot route spoke traffic THROUGH the egress VPC's NAT gateway to the internet (non-transitive). AWS Well-Architected explicitly lists 'using VPC peering to connect more than two VPCs' as an anti-pattern.","why_zh":"VPC peering 不支援遞移式 (transitive) 路由, 無法擴展到數百個 VPC。會需要全網狀的點對點 peering, 且 peering 無法讓 spoke 流量「穿過」egress VPC 的 NAT gateway 到網際網路 (非遞移)。AWS Well-Architected 明確將「用 VPC peering 連接超過兩個 VPC」列為反模式 (anti-pattern)。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Creating a Transit Gateway in every account defeats the purpose of a central hub and is enormous operational overhead; you would still need to interconnect them. Also you cannot 'attach a NAT gateway to a transit gateway' — TGW attachments are VPCs, VPNs, Direct Connect, or peering, not NAT gateways. Technically invalid.","why_zh":"在每個帳戶都建立 Transit Gateway 違背中央 hub 的目的, 且營運負擔極大, 仍須彼此互連。此外無法「將 NAT gateway 附加到 transit gateway」—TGW 的 attachment 是 VPC、VPN、Direct Connect 或 peering, 而非 NAT gateway。技術上不成立。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS PrivateLink exposes a specific service endpoint (one-way, service-oriented) and is not designed for general routed internet egress. It cannot carry arbitrary outbound internet traffic from private subnets through a NAT gateway. Wrong tool for centralized egress.","why_zh":"AWS PrivateLink 公開的是特定服務端點 (單向、面向服務), 並非為一般可路由的網際網路出口而設計。它無法將私有子網的任意出站網際網路流量透過 NAT gateway 傳送。用於集中式出口是錯誤的工具。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/building-scalable-secure-multi-vpc-network-infrastructure/using-nat-gateway-for-centralized-egress.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_planning_network_topology_prefer_hub_and_spoke.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/what-is-transit-gateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/peering/vpc-peering-basics.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":248,"question_en":"An education company is running a web application used by college students around the world. The application runs in an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster in an Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). A system administrator detects a weekly spike in the number of failed login attempts, which overwhelm the application's authentication service. All the failed login attempts originate from about 500 different IP addresses that change each week. A solutions architect must prevent the failed login attempts from overwhelming the authentication service. Which solution meets these requirements with the MOST operational e®ciency?","question_zh":"一家教育公司正在运行一个供世界各地大学生使用的网络应用程序。该应用程序在应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面的 Auto Scaling 组 中的 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 集群中运行。系统管理员检测到每周失败的登录尝试次数激增，这导致应用程序 的身份验证服务不堪重负。所有失败的登录尝试均来自大约 500 个每周都会变化的不同 IP 地址。解决方案架构师必须防止失败的登 录尝试淹没身份验证服务。 哪种解决方案能够以最高的运营效率满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Firewall Manager to create a security group and security group policy to deny access from the IP addresses.","B":"Create an AWS WAF web ACL with a rate-based rule, and set the rule action to Block. Connect the web ACL to the ALB.","C":"Use AWS Firewall Manager to create a security group and security group policy to allow access only to specific CIDR ranges.","D":"Create an AWS WAF web ACL with an IP set match rule, and set the rule action to Block. Connect the web ACL to the ALB."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Firewall Manager 创建安全组和安全组策略以拒绝来自 IP 地址的访问。","B":"使用基于速率的规则创建 AWS WAF Web ACL，并将规则操作设置为阻止。将 Web ACL 连接到 ALB。","C":"使用 AWS Firewall Manager 创建安全组和安全组策略，以仅允许访问特定 CIDR 范围。","D":"使用 IP 集匹配规则创建 AWS WAF Web ACL，并将规则操作设置为阻止。将 Web ACL 连接到 ALB。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":249,"question_en":"A company operates an on-premises software-as-a-service (SaaS) solution that ingests several files daily. The company provides multiple public SFTP endpoints to its customers to facilitate the file transfers. The customers add the SFTP endpoint IP addresses to their firewall allow list for outbound tra®c. Changes to the SFTP endpoint IP addresses are not permitted. The company wants to migrate the SaaS solution to AWS and decrease the operational overhead of the file transfer service. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司运营一个本地软件即服务 (SaaS) 解决方案，每天都会摄取多个文件。该公司向客户提供多个公共 SFTP 端点以促进文件传 输。客户将 SFTP 端点 IP 地址添加到出站流量的防火墙允许列表中。不允许更改 SFTP 端点 IP 地址。 该公司希望将 SaaS 解决方案迁移到 AWS 并减少文件传输服务的运营开销。 哪种解决方案满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Register the customer-owned block of IP addresses in the company's AWS account. Create Elastic IP addresses from the address pool and assign them to an AWS Transfer for SFTP endpoint. Use AWS Transfer to store the files in Amazon S3.","B":"Add a subnet containing the customer-owned block of IP addresses to a VPC. Create Elastic IP addresses from the address pool and assign them to an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Launch EC2 instances hosting FTP services in an Auto Scaling group behind the ALStore the files in attached Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes.","C":"Register the customer-owned block of IP addresses with Amazon Route 53. Create alias records in Route 53 that point to a Network Load Balancer (NLB). Launch EC2 instances hosting FTP services in an Auto Scaling group behind the NLB. Store the files in Amazon S3.","D":"Register the customer-owned block of IP addresses in the company’s AWS account. Create Elastic IP addresses from the address pool and assign them to an Amazon S3 VPC endpoint. Enable SFTP support on the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"在公司的 AWS 账户中注册客户拥有的 IP 地址块。从地址池创建弹性 IP 地址并将其分配给 AWS Transfer for SFTP 终端节点。使 用 AWS Transfer 将文件存储在 Amazon S3 中。","B":"将包含客户拥有的 IP 地址块的子网添加到 VPC。从地址池中创建弹性 IP 地址并将其分配给应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB)。在 AL 后面的 Auto Scaling 组中启动托管 FTP 服务的 EC2 实例将文件存储在附加的 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 卷中。","C":"将客户拥有的 IP 地址块注册到 Amazon Route 53。在 Route 53 中创建指向网络负载均衡器 (NLB) 的别名记录。在 NLB 后面的 Auto Scaling 组中启动托管 FTP 服务的 EC2 实例。将文件存储在 Amazon S3 中。","D":"在公司的 AWS 账户中注册客户拥有的 IP 地址块。从地址池创建弹性 IP 地址并将其分配给 Amazon S3 VPC 终端节点。在 S3 存 储桶上启用 SFTP 支持。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to migrate a self-managed on-premises SFTP service to AWS, keep the exact same public IP addresses (customers have allow-listed them and changes are not permitted), and reduce operational overhead. AWS Transfer Family is a fully managed SFTP service that writes directly to Amazon S3, which removes the burden of running servers (least operational overhead). To preserve the fixed IPs, the company registers its customer-owned IPv4 block in its AWS account using Bring Your Own IP (BYOIP), creates Elastic IP addresses from that pool, and attaches them to the Transfer Family server's VPC (internet-facing) endpoint. The AWS Transfer Family endpoint-type matrix explicitly states that for a VPC internet-facing endpoint 'You can attach Elastic IP addresses to the endpoint. These can be AWS-owned IP addresses or your own IP addresses (Bring your own IP addresses). Elastic IP addresses attached to the endpoint don't change.' Option A is the only choice that combines BYOIP-derived Elastic IPs, a managed SFTP service, and S3 storage, so it uniquely satisfies all constraints.","explanation_zh":"需求是把本地自管的 SFTP 服務遷移到 AWS、保留完全相同的對外 IP 位址(客戶已將其加入防火牆白名單且不允許變更),並降低運維負擔。AWS Transfer Family 是全託管的 SFTP 服務,可直接寫入 Amazon S3,免去自行維運伺服器(運維負擔最低)。為保留固定 IP,公司可用 Bring Your Own IP (BYOIP) 將自有 IPv4 區塊註冊到其 AWS 帳戶,從該位址池建立 Elastic IP,並掛載到 Transfer Family 伺服器的 VPC(對外)端點。AWS Transfer Family 端點類型對照表明確指出,對於 VPC internet-facing 端點:『可將 Elastic IP 掛載到端點,可以是 AWS 擁有的 IP 或你自己的 IP(BYOIP),掛載到端點的 Elastic IP 不會改變。』選項 A 是唯一同時結合 BYOIP 取得的 Elastic IP、託管 SFTP 服務與 S3 儲存的方案,因此唯一滿足所有限制條件。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"An Application Load Balancer operates at Layer 7 (HTTP/HTTPS) and cannot front SFTP/FTP TCP traffic. Running an EC2 Auto Scaling fleet of FTP servers with EBS storage is self-managed and increases operational overhead, the opposite of the requirement.","why_zh":"Application Load Balancer 在第七層(HTTP/HTTPS)運作,無法承載 SFTP/FTP 的 TCP 流量。以 EC2 Auto Scaling 自管 FTP 伺服器叢集並用 EBS 儲存屬自行維運,反而增加運維負擔,與需求相反。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"You cannot 'register a block of IP addresses with Route 53' - Route 53 is a DNS service, not an IP registry. Alias records to an NLB resolve to the NLB's IPs, not to the customer-owned fixed IPs. It also relies on a self-managed EC2 FTP fleet, raising operational overhead.","why_zh":"無法『把 IP 區塊註冊到 Route 53』——Route 53 是 DNS 服務而非 IP 註冊處。指向 NLB 的別名記錄解析到 NLB 的 IP,而非客戶自有的固定 IP。此外仍依賴自管 EC2 FTP 叢集,提升運維負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is fabricated and technically impossible: Amazon S3 has no native SFTP support, you cannot 'enable SFTP on an S3 bucket', and you cannot assign Elastic IP addresses to an S3 (gateway or interface) VPC endpoint. SFTP access to S3 is provided by AWS Transfer Family, not by the bucket itself. This is the dump's suggested answer and it is wrong.","why_zh":"此選項屬虛構且技術上不可行:Amazon S3 沒有原生 SFTP 支援,無法『在 S3 儲存貯體上啟用 SFTP』,也無法把 Elastic IP 指派給 S3(gateway 或 interface)VPC 端點。對 S3 的 SFTP 存取是由 AWS Transfer Family 提供,而非儲存貯體本身。這是題庫建議答案,但它是錯的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transfer/latest/userguide/sftp-for-transfer-family.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transfer/latest/APIReference/API_EndpointDetails.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/ec2-byoip.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/byoip-working-with.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transfer/latest/userguide/what-is-aws-transfer-family.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":250,"question_en":"A company has a new application that needs to run on five Amazon EC2 instances in a single AWS Region. The application requires high- throughput, low-latency network connections between all of the EC2 instances where the application will run. There is no requirement for the application to be fault tolerant. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个新应用程序，需要在单个 AWS 区域中的五个 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。该应用程序需要在运行该应用程序的所有 EC2 实例之间建立高吞吐量、低延迟的网络连接。应用程序不要求具有容错能力。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Launch five new EC2 instances into a cluster placement group. Ensure that the EC2 instance type supports enhanced networking.","B":"Launch five new EC2 instances into an Auto Scaling group in the same Availability Zone. Attach an extra elastic network interface to each EC2 instance.","C":"Launch five new EC2 instances into a partition placement group. Ensure that the EC2 instance type supports enhanced networking.","D":"Launch five new EC2 instances into a spread placement group. Attach an extra elastic network interface to each EC2 instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"在集群置放群组中启动五个新的 EC2 实例。确保 EC2 实例类型支持增强联网。","B":"在同一可用区的 Auto Scaling 组中启动五个新的 EC2 实例。将额外的弹性网络接口附加到每个 EC2 实例。","C":"在分区置放群组中启动五个新的 EC2 实例。确保 EC2 实例类型支持增强联网。","D":"将五个新的 EC2 实例启动到分散置放组中。将额外的弹性网络接口附加到每个 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":251,"question_en":"A company is creating a REST API to share information with six of its partners based in the United States. The company has created an Amazon API Gateway Regional endpoint. Each of the six partners will access the API once per day to post daily sales figures. After initial deployment, the company observes 1,000 requests per second originating from 500 different IP addresses around the world. The company believes this tra®c is originating from a botnet and wants to secure its API while minimizing cost. Which approach should the company take to secure its API?","question_zh":"一家公司正在创建 REST API，以便与位于美国的六个合作伙​伴共享信息。该公司创建了一个 Amazon API Gateway 区域终端节点。六 个合作伙​伴中的每一个每天都会访问 API 一次，以发布每日销售数据。 初始部署后，该公司观察到每秒来自全球 500 个不同 IP 地址的 1,000 个请求。该公司认为此流量源自僵尸网络，并希望保护其 API，同时最大限度地降低成本。 公司应采取哪种方法来保护其 API 安全？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution with the API as the origin. Create an AWS WAF web ACL with a rule to block clients that submit more than five requests per day. Associate the web ACL with the CloudFront distribution. Configure CloudFront with an origin access identity (OAI) and associate it with the distribution. Configure API Gateway to ensure only the OAI can run the POST method.","B":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution with the API as the origin. Create an AWS WAF web ACL with a rule to block clients that submit more than five requests per day. Associate the web ACL with the CloudFront distribution. Add a custom header to the CloudFront distribution populated with an API key. Configure the API to require an API key on the POST method.","C":"Create an AWS WAF web ACL with a rule to allow access to the IP addresses used by the six partners. Associate the web ACL with the API. Create a resource policy with a request limit and associate it with the API. Configure the API to require an API key on the POST method.","D":"Create an AWS WAF web ACL with a rule to allow access to the IP addresses used by the six partners. Associate the web ACL with the API. Create a usage plan with a request limit and associate it with the API. Create an API key and add it to the usage plan."},"options_zh":{"A":"以 API 作为源创建 Amazon CloudFront 分配。创建一个 AWS WAF Web ACL，其中包含阻止每天提交超过 5 个请求的客户端的规 则。将 Web ACL 与 CloudFront 分配关联。使用源访问身份 (OAI) 配置 CloudFront 并将其与分配关联。配置 API Gateway 以确保只 有 OAI 可以运行 POST 方法。","B":"以 API 作为源创建 Amazon CloudFront 分配。创建一个 AWS WAF Web ACL，其中包含阻止每天提交超过 5 个请求的客户端的规 则。将 Web ACL 与 CloudFront 分配关联。将自定义标头添加到填充有 API 密钥的 CloudFront 分配。将 API 配置为在 POST 方法上 需要 API 密钥。","C":"创建一个 AWS WAF Web ACL，其中包含一条允许访问六个合作伙​伴使用的 IP 地址的规则。将 Web ACL 与 API 关联。创建具有 请求限制的资源策略并将其与 API 关联。将 API 配置为在 POST 方法上需要 API 密钥。","D":"创建一个 AWS WAF Web ACL，其中包含一条允许访问六个合作伙​伴使用的 IP 地址的规则。将 Web ACL 与 API 关联。创建具有 请求限制的使用计划并将其与 API 关联。创建 API 密钥并将其添加到使用计划中。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":97},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The qualifier is 'secure its API while minimizing cost,' so the chosen approach must be both technically valid and avoid unnecessary services. AWS WAF web ACLs can be associated directly with a Regional API Gateway stage (apigateway-control-access-aws-waf.html), so options A and B's CloudFront distribution is an unnecessary added cost and complexity. The decisive distinction between the two remaining options (C and D) is the request-limit mechanism: API Gateway resource policies only allow/deny access based on AWS account roles (SigV4), source IP ranges, or VPC/VPC-endpoint (apigateway-resource-policies-examples.html) — they have NO 'request limit' capability, so option C is technically invalid. Request rate limits and quotas in API Gateway are enforced via usage plans tied to API keys (api-gateway-api-usage-plans.html). Option D correctly combines a WAF web ACL that allow-lists the six partner IP addresses (directly on the API), a usage plan with a request limit, and an API key added to that usage plan, all at the lowest cost. Therefore D is the only fully correct and cost-minimizing answer.","explanation_zh":"題目限定條件為「在最小化成本的前提下保護 API」，因此選定方案必須技術上可行且不引入不必要的服務。AWS WAF web ACL 可直接關聯到 Regional API Gateway 的 stage（apigateway-control-access-aws-waf.html），所以 A 與 B 額外建立 CloudFront distribution 屬於不必要的成本與複雜度。剩下 C 與 D 的關鍵差異在於「請求限制」的實作方式：API Gateway resource policy 只能依 AWS 帳號角色（SigV4）、來源 IP 範圍或 VPC/VPC endpoint 進行 allow/deny（apigateway-resource-policies-examples.html），並無設定 request limit 的能力，因此 C 在技術上無效。API Gateway 的請求速率限制與配額是透過綁定 API key 的 usage plan 來實作（api-gateway-api-usage-plans.html）。D 正確地結合了直接關聯到 API 的 WAF web ACL（允許六個合作夥伴 IP）、含 request limit 的 usage plan，以及加入該 usage plan 的 API key，且成本最低，因此 D 是唯一完全正確且成本最小化的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Adds a CloudFront distribution that is unnecessary because WAF can attach directly to a Regional API stage, increasing cost against the 'minimize cost' goal. CloudFront origin access identity (OAI) is for restricting access to S3 origins, not API Gateway custom origins. WAF rate-based rules also count over a trailing 5-minute window, not 'per day,' so 'five requests per day' is not implementable as stated.","why_zh":"額外加入 CloudFront distribution 不必要，因為 WAF 可直接關聯到 Regional API stage，違反「最小化成本」目標。CloudFront 的 origin access identity (OAI) 用於限制 S3 來源的存取，並不適用於 API Gateway 自訂來源。此外 WAF rate-based rule 是以滾動的 5 分鐘窗口計數，而非「每日」，故「每日五次請求」無法如題述實作。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Also adds an unnecessary CloudFront distribution, raising cost. WAF can be associated directly with the Regional API. The custom-header-plus-API-key pattern works, but the extra CloudFront layer violates the cost-minimization qualifier, and WAF rate-based rules cannot express a true 'five requests per day' limit (5-minute trailing window only).","why_zh":"同樣加入不必要的 CloudFront distribution，增加成本。WAF 可直接關聯到 Regional API。自訂標頭加 API key 的模式雖可行，但多出的 CloudFront 層違反成本最小化的限定條件，且 WAF rate-based rule 無法表達真正的「每日五次請求」限制（僅有 5 分鐘滾動窗口）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Technically invalid: API Gateway resource policies only support allow/deny by AWS account role, source IP range, or VPC/VPC-endpoint — there is no 'request limit' option in a resource policy. Request limits/quotas in API Gateway are provided by usage plans, not resource policies, so 'Create a resource policy with a request limit' cannot be done. This is the dump's suggested answer and is wrong.","why_zh":"技術上無效：API Gateway resource policy 僅支援依 AWS 帳號角色、來源 IP 範圍或 VPC/VPC endpoint 進行 allow/deny，resource policy 本身並無「request limit」選項。API Gateway 的請求限制／配額是由 usage plan 提供，而非 resource policy，因此「建立含 request limit 的 resource policy」根本無法實作。這是題庫的建議答案，但其實是錯的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/api-gateway-api-usage-plans.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-resource-policies-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-control-access-aws-waf.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-rate-based-request-limiting.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":252,"question_en":"A company uses an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster for applications in a single AWS Region. The company's database team must monitor all data activity on all the databases. Which solution will achieve this goal?","question_zh":"一家公司将 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群用于单个 AWS 区域中的应用程序。公司的数据库团队必须监控所有数据库上的所 有数据活动。 哪种解决方案将实现这一目标？","options_en":{"A":"Set up an AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) change data capture (CDC) task. Specify the Aurora DB cluster as the source. Specify Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose as the target. Use Kinesis Data Firehose to upload the data into an Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster for further analysis.","B":"Start a database activity stream on the Aurora DB cluster to capture the activity stream in Amazon EventBridge. Define an AWS Lambda function as a target for EventBridge. Program the Lambda function to decrypt the messages from EventBridge and to publish all database activity to Amazon S3 for further analysis.","C":"Start a database activity stream on the Aurora DB cluster to push the activity stream to an Amazon Kinesis data stream. Configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to consume the Kinesis data stream and to deliver the data to Amazon S3 for further analysis.","D":"Set up an AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) change data capture (CDC) task. Specify the Aurora DB cluster as the source. Specify Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose as the target. Use Kinesis Data Firehose to upload the data into an Amazon Redshift cluster. Run queries on the Amazon Redshift data to determine database activities on the Aurora database."},"options_zh":{"A":"设置 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 更改数据捕获 (CDC) 任务。指定 Aurora 数据库集群作为源。指定 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 作为目标。使用 Kinesis Data Firehose 将数据上传到 Amazon OpenSearch Service 集群以进行进一步分析。","B":"在 Aurora 数据库集群上启动数据库活动流以捕获 Amazon EventBridge 中的活动流。将 AWS Lambda 函数定义为 EventBridge 的 目标。对 Lambda 函数进行编程，以解密来自 EventBridge 的消息并将所有数据库活动发布到 Amazon S3 以供进一步分析。","C":"在 Aurora 数据库集群上启动数据库活动流，以将活动流推送到 Amazon Kinesis 数据流。配置 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 以 使用 Kinesis 数据流并将数据传输到 Amazon S3 进行进一步分析。","D":"设置 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 更改数据捕获 (CDC) 任务。指定 Aurora 数据库集群作为源。指定 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 作为目标。使用 Kinesis Data Firehose 将数据上传到 Amazon Redshift 集群。对 Amazon Redshift 数据运行查 询以确定 Aurora 数据库上的数据库活动。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to monitor ALL data activity on all databases in an Aurora PostgreSQL cluster. The purpose-built feature for this is Database Activity Streams (DAS), which captures a near real-time, auditable stream of all database activity (SQL statements, connections, etc.) at the cluster level for every DB instance. Per AWS docs, 'Your Aurora DB cluster pushes activities to an Amazon Kinesis data stream in near real time. The Kinesis stream is created automatically. From Kinesis, you can configure AWS services such as Amazon Data Firehose and AWS Lambda to consume the stream and store the data.' Option C is the exact documented pattern: start a DAS, the cluster pushes to a Kinesis data stream, and Kinesis Data Firehose consumes that stream and delivers records to Amazon S3 for analysis. DMS CDC (options A and D) only captures committed row-level data changes for replication, not full database activity (logins, SELECTs, DDL, admin actions, failed queries), so it cannot satisfy 'monitor all data activity.' Option B is technically impossible because a database activity stream pushes to Kinesis Data Streams, not to Amazon EventBridge.","explanation_zh":"需求是監控 Aurora PostgreSQL 叢集中所有資料庫的「所有資料活動」。針對此需求的專屬功能是 Database Activity Streams (DAS)，它在叢集層級為每個 DB 執行個體擷取近即時、可稽核的所有資料庫活動串流（SQL 陳述式、連線等）。根據 AWS 文件：『Your Aurora DB cluster pushes activities to an Amazon Kinesis data stream in near real time. The Kinesis stream is created automatically. From Kinesis, you can configure AWS services such as Amazon Data Firehose and AWS Lambda to consume the stream and store the data.』選項 C 正是文件記載的標準模式：啟動 DAS，叢集推送至 Kinesis data stream，再由 Kinesis Data Firehose 消費該串流並將資料送至 Amazon S3 供分析。DMS CDC（選項 A 與 D）僅擷取已提交的列層級資料變更以供複寫，無法擷取完整的資料庫活動（登入、SELECT、DDL、管理操作、失敗查詢），因此無法滿足『監控所有資料活動』。選項 B 在技術上不可能，因為 database activity stream 推送至 Kinesis Data Streams，而非 Amazon EventBridge。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"DMS CDC only captures committed row-level data changes (inserts/updates/deletes) for migration/replication. It does not capture full database activity such as logins, SELECT queries, DDL, or administrative actions, so it cannot 'monitor all data activity.' OpenSearch as a target adds extra components without solving the core capture gap.","why_zh":"DMS CDC 僅擷取已提交的列層級資料變更（插入/更新/刪除）以供遷移或複寫，無法擷取登入、SELECT 查詢、DDL 或管理操作等完整資料庫活動，因此無法『監控所有資料活動』。以 OpenSearch 作為目標只增加元件，並未解決核心擷取缺口。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Technically impossible: Aurora Database Activity Streams push to an Amazon Kinesis data stream, not to Amazon EventBridge. There is no native path that captures the activity stream directly in EventBridge, so this architecture does not work.","why_zh":"技術上不可行：Aurora Database Activity Streams 推送至 Amazon Kinesis data stream，而非 Amazon EventBridge。沒有原生路徑能直接在 EventBridge 擷取活動串流，因此此架構無法運作。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same fundamental flaw as A: DMS CDC captures only data changes, not full database activity, so it fails the 'all data activity' requirement. Loading into Redshift and querying adds operational overhead without addressing the gap.","why_zh":"與 A 相同的根本缺陷：DMS CDC 僅擷取資料變更，而非完整資料庫活動，因此無法滿足『所有資料活動』需求。載入 Redshift 再查詢只增加營運負擔，並未解決問題。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/DBActivityStreams.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/using-other-services-aurora.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/DBActivityStreams.KinesisAccess.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/DBActivityStreams.Monitoring.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":253,"question_en":"An entertainment company recently launched a new game. To ensure a good experience for players during the launch period, the company deployed a static quantity of 12 r6g.16xlarge (memory optimized) Amazon EC2 instances behind a Network Load Balancer. The company's operations team used the Amazon CloudWatch agent and a custom metric to include memory utilization in its monitoring strategy. Analysis of the CloudWatch metrics from the launch period showed consumption at about one quarter of the CPU and memory that the company expected. Initial demand for the game has subsided and has become more variable. The company decides to use an Auto Scaling group that monitors the CPU and memory consumption to dynamically scale the instance ­eet. A solutions architect needs to configure the Auto Scaling group to meet demand in the most cost-effective way. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家娱乐公司最近推出了一款新游戏。为了确保玩家在发布期间获得良好的体验，该公司在网络负载均衡器后面部署了静态数量的 12 个 r6g.16xlarge（内存优化）Amazon EC2 实例。该公司的运营团队使用 Amazon CloudWatch 代理和自定义指标将内存利用率纳入 其监控策略。 对发布期间的 CloudWatch 指标的分析显示，CPU 和内存消耗量约为公司预期的四分之一。最初对游戏的需求已经减弱，并且变得更 加多变。该公司决定使用 Auto Scaling 组来监控 CPU 和内存消耗，以动态扩展实例队列。解决方案架构师需要配置 Auto Scaling 组， 以便以最具成本效益的方式满足需求。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the Auto Scaling group to deploy c6g.4xlarge (compute optimized) instances. Configure a minimum capacity of 3, a desired capacity of 3, and a maximum capacity of 12.","B":"Configure the Auto Scaling group to deploy m6g.4xlarge (general purpose) instances. Configure a minimum capacity of 3, a desired capacity of 3, and a maximum capacity of 12.","C":"Configure the Auto Scaling group to deploy r6g.4xlarge (memory optimized) instances. Configure a minimum capacity of 3, a desired capacity of 3, and a maximum capacity of 12.","D":"Configure the Auto Scaling group to deploy r6g.8xlarge (memory optimized) instances. Configure a minimum capacity of 2, a desired capacity of 2, and a maximum capacity of 6."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 Auto Scaling 组以部署 c6g.4xlarge（计算优化）实例。配置最小容量为 3、所需容量为 3、最大容量为 12。","B":"配置 Auto Scaling 组以部署 m6g.4xlarge（通用）实例。配置最小容量为 3、所需容量为 3、最大容量为 12。","C":"配置 Auto Scaling 组以部署 r6g.4xlarge（内存优化）实例。配置最小容量为 3、所需容量为 3、最大容量为 12。","D":"配置 Auto Scaling 组以部署 r6g.8xlarge（内存优化）实例。配置最小容量为 2、所需容量为 2、最大容量为 6。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":96},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The workload is memory-intensive game servers, so AWS right-sizing guidance (PERF02-BP04) says to keep the memory-optimized R family (r6g), which has an 8:1 GiB-per-vCPU ratio. During launch, both CPU and memory ran at about one quarter of the provisioned 12 x r6g.16xlarge fleet. Original capacity = 768 vCPU / 6144 GiB; observed peak demand = ~1/4 = 192 vCPU / 1536 GiB. r6g.4xlarge = 16 vCPU / 128 GiB, so a max of 12 instances = 192 vCPU / 1536 GiB, exactly matching the observed peak, while a desired/min of 3 gives a low, cost-efficient baseline (384 GiB). Option C keeps the correct family, sizes max to true peak demand, and uses small instances for fine-grained scaling that tracks the now-variable demand without over-provisioning. Option D (r6g.8xlarge, 2/2/6) reaches the same 1536 GiB ceiling but with a higher baseline floor (2 x 256 GiB = 512 GiB) and coarser 256 GiB scaling steps, making it less cost-effective for variable demand. C is therefore the most cost-effective.","explanation_zh":"此工作負載是記憶體密集型的遊戲伺服器，因此依據 AWS right-sizing 指引 (PERF02-BP04)，應維持 memory optimized 的 R 系列 (r6g)，其每 vCPU 為 8 GiB 記憶體的比例。啟動期間 CPU 與記憶體都只用到原配置 12 台 r6g.16xlarge 的約四分之一。原始容量 = 768 vCPU / 6144 GiB；觀察到的尖峰需求約為 1/4 = 192 vCPU / 1536 GiB。r6g.4xlarge = 16 vCPU / 128 GiB，因此 maximum 設 12 台 = 192 vCPU / 1536 GiB，正好對應實際尖峰，而 desired/min 設 3 提供較低且符合成本效益的基準 (384 GiB)。選項 C 保留正確的執行個體系列、將上限設為真實尖峰需求，並使用較小執行個體以細緻地擴展，貼合現在已變得多變的需求且不會過度佈建。選項 D (r6g.8xlarge, 2/2/6) 雖達到相同 1536 GiB 上限，但基準較高 (2 x 256 GiB = 512 GiB) 且擴展粒度較粗 (每步 256 GiB)，對多變需求較不符合成本效益。因此 C 最具成本效益。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"c6g.4xlarge is compute optimized (2:1 GiB/vCPU). For a memory-intensive workload this is the wrong family; you would run out of memory long before CPU. Meeting the 1536 GiB peak would need 48 c6g.4xlarge instances, far beyond the max of 12, so it cannot satisfy demand.","why_zh":"c6g.4xlarge 是 compute optimized (每 vCPU 2 GiB)。對記憶體密集型工作負載而言這是錯誤系列；記憶體會遠早於 CPU 耗盡。要達到 1536 GiB 尖峰需 48 台 c6g.4xlarge，遠超過上限 12 台，無法滿足需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"m6g.4xlarge is general purpose (4:1 GiB/vCPU), only half the memory ratio of r6g. The workload is explicitly memory-intensive, so this under-provisions memory; reaching 1536 GiB would need 24 instances, beyond the max of 12. Wrong family for a memory-bound game server.","why_zh":"m6g.4xlarge 是 general purpose (每 vCPU 4 GiB)，記憶體比例僅為 r6g 的一半。工作負載明確為記憶體密集型，因此記憶體配置不足；要達到 1536 GiB 需 24 台，超過上限 12 台。對記憶體受限的遊戲伺服器是錯誤系列。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"r6g.8xlarge (2/2/6) is the correct family and reaches the same 1536 GiB peak at max, but its baseline floor (2 x 256 GiB = 512 GiB) is higher than C's (3 x 128 GiB = 384 GiB) and it scales in coarse 256 GiB steps. Since r6g.4xlarge is exactly half the price/capacity of r6g.8xlarge, per-GiB cost is identical, so C's lower floor and finer scaling granularity make it cheaper for the now-variable demand. D is the ExamTopics suggested answer but is less cost-effective.","why_zh":"r6g.8xlarge (2/2/6) 系列正確且在上限同樣達到 1536 GiB，但其基準下限 (2 x 256 GiB = 512 GiB) 高於 C 的 (3 x 128 GiB = 384 GiB)，且以較粗的 256 GiB 為步進擴展。由於 r6g.4xlarge 的價格/容量恰為 r6g.8xlarge 的一半，每 GiB 成本相同，因此 C 較低的下限與更細的擴展粒度使其對現在多變的需求更便宜。D 是 ExamTopics 建議答案但較不具成本效益。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/2023-04-10/framework/perf_select_compute_right_sizing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ec2/latest/instancetypes/mo.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/performance-efficiency-pillar/perf_compute_hardware_configure_and_right_size_compute_resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/as-scaling-target-tracking.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":254,"question_en":"A financial services company loaded millions of historical stock trades into an Amazon DynamoDB table. The table uses on-demand capacity mode. Once each day at midnight, a few million new records are loaded into the table. Application read activity against the table happens in bursts throughout the day. and a limited set of keys are repeatedly looked up. The company needs to reduce costs associated with DynamoDB. Which strategy should a solutions architect recommend to meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家金融服务公司将数百万条历史股票交易加载到 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。该表采用按需扩容模式。每天午夜一次，数百万条新记 录会加载到表中。针对表的应用程序读取活动全天突然发生。并且重复查找一组有限的键。该公司需要降低与 DynamoDB 相关的成 本。 解决方案架构师应该推荐哪种策略来满足此要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an Amazon ElastiCache cluster in front of the DynamoDB table","B":"Deploy DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX). Configure DynamoDB auto scaling. Purchase Savings Plans in Cost Explorer.","C":"Use provisioned capacity mode. Purchase Savings Plans in Cost Explorer.","D":"Deploy DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX). Use provisioned capacity mode. Configure DynamoDB auto scaling."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 DynamoDB 表前面部署 Amazon ElastiCache 集群","B":"部署 DynamoDB 加速器 (DAX)。配置 DynamoDB 自动扩展。在 Cost Explorer 中购买 Savings Plans。","C":"使用预置容量模式。在 Cost Explorer 中购买 Savings Plans。","D":"部署 DynamoDB 加速器 (DAX)。使用预配置容量模式。配置 DynamoDB 自动扩展。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":86},"tags":["Compute","Database","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The workload is a high read-to-write pattern with a limited set of keys repeatedly looked up in bursts, plus a fully predictable daily bulk load at midnight. This matches DAX's documented sweet spot: 'minimize repeated reads of the same data,' 'caching common queries,' and 'bursty traffic patterns,' where a high cache hit rate makes the reduced table read cost exceed the DAX cluster cost, yielding net savings. Because the load is predictable, provisioned capacity mode is cheaper than on-demand, and DynamoDB auto scaling absorbs the read bursts so you do not over-provision. Option D combines all three valid DynamoDB cost levers (DAX caching + provisioned mode + auto scaling) with no invalid references. Critically, options B and C both say 'Purchase Savings Plans in Cost Explorer,' but DynamoDB is NOT covered by Savings Plans (those apply only to EC2/Fargate/Lambda/SageMaker); DynamoDB uses Reserved Capacity instead, so B and C are technically wrong. Option A (ElastiCache only) adds a side cache with extra application-managed cache-coherency logic and does nothing about the dominant cost lever (capacity mode), making it less effective and higher overhead than the purpose-built DAX in D.","explanation_zh":"此工作負載屬於高讀寫比模式，少量固定的 key 在一天中以突發方式被重複查詢，加上每天午夜完全可預測的批次載入。這正好符合 DAX 的適用情境文件所述：減少對相同資料的重複讀取、快取常見查詢、以及突發流量模式；在高快取命中率下，減少的資料表讀取成本會超過 DAX 叢集成本，產生淨節省。由於負載可預測，provisioned capacity mode 比 on-demand 更便宜，而 DynamoDB auto scaling 可吸收讀取突發以避免過度佈建。選項 D 結合三個有效的 DynamoDB 成本控制手段（DAX 快取 + provisioned mode + auto scaling），且無無效引用。關鍵在於選項 B 與 C 都提到「在 Cost Explorer 購買 Savings Plans」，但 DynamoDB 並不適用 Savings Plans（Savings Plans 僅涵蓋 EC2/Fargate/Lambda/SageMaker），DynamoDB 改用 Reserved Capacity，因此 B 與 C 技術上錯誤。選項 A（僅用 ElastiCache）需自行管理快取一致性邏輯，且未處理主要成本來源（capacity mode），效果較差且維運負擔較高，不如 D 中專為 DynamoDB 設計的 DAX。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"ElastiCache only adds a side cache requiring custom application-managed cache-coherency code and does not address the main cost lever (on-demand vs provisioned capacity). DAX is the purpose-built, write-through, lower-overhead caching layer for DynamoDB, and A leaves write/capacity costs unoptimized.","why_zh":"僅用 ElastiCache 需自行撰寫快取一致性邏輯，且未處理主要成本來源（on-demand 與 provisioned 的選擇）。DAX 才是 DynamoDB 專用、write-through、維運負擔較低的快取層；A 也未優化寫入與容量成本。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"It says 'Purchase Savings Plans in Cost Explorer,' but DynamoDB is not eligible for Savings Plans (those cover only EC2, Fargate, Lambda, and SageMaker). DynamoDB cost commitments use Reserved Capacity, so this option is technically invalid.","why_zh":"它提到「在 Cost Explorer 購買 Savings Plans」，但 DynamoDB 不適用 Savings Plans（僅涵蓋 EC2、Fargate、Lambda、SageMaker）。DynamoDB 的承諾折扣使用 Reserved Capacity，因此此選項技術上無效。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Provisioned mode is reasonable, but the 'Purchase Savings Plans in Cost Explorer' clause is invalid for DynamoDB (it would be Reserved Capacity). It also ignores the repeated-read caching opportunity that DAX provides for further cost reduction.","why_zh":"Provisioned mode 合理，但「在 Cost Explorer 購買 Savings Plans」對 DynamoDB 無效（應為 Reserved Capacity）。它也忽略了 DAX 對重複讀取所能帶來的進一步成本降低機會。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/evaluate-dax-suitability.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/DAX.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/serverless-applications-lens/capacity.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/reserved-capacity.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/provisioned-capacity-mode.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/AutoScaling.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":255,"question_en":"A company is creating a centralized logging service running on Amazon EC2 that will receive and analyze logs from hundreds of AWS accounts. AWS PrivateLink is being used to provide connectivity between the client services and the logging service. In each AWS account with a client, an interface endpoint has been created for the logging service and is available. The logging service running on EC2 instances with a Network Load Balancer (NLB) are deployed in different subnets. The clients are unable to submit logs using the VPC endpoint. Which combination of steps should a solutions architect take to resolve this issue? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在创建在 Amazon EC2 上运行的集中式日志记录服务，该服务将接收和分析来自数百个 AWS 账户的日志。AWS PrivateLink 用于提供客户端服务和日志记录服务之间的连接。 在每个具有客户端的 AWS 账户中，已为日志记录服务创建了一个接口终端节点并且可用。在具有网络负载均衡器 (NLB) 的 EC2 实例 上运行的日志记录服务部署在不同的子网中。客户端无法使用 VPC 终端节点提交日志。 解决方案架构师应采取哪些步骤组合来解决此问题？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Check that the NACL is attached to the logging service subnet to allow communications to and from the NLB subnets. Check that the NACL is attached to the NLB subnet to allow communications to and from the logging service subnets running on EC2 instances.","B":"Check that the NACL is attached to the logging service subnets to allow communications to and from the interface endpoint subnets. Check that the NACL is attached to the interface endpoint subnet to allow communications to and from the logging service subnets running on EC2 instances.","C":"Check the security group for the logging service running on the EC2 instances to ensure it allows ingress from the NLB subnets.","D":"Check the security group for the logging service running on EC2 instances to ensure it allows ingress from the clients.","E":"Check the security group for the NLB to ensure it allows ingress from the interface endpoint subnets."},"options_zh":{"A":"检查 NACL 是否已连接到日志记录服务子网，以允许与 NLB 子网之间的通信。检查 NACL 是否已附加到 NLB 子网，以允许与 EC2 实例上运行的日志服务子网之间进行通信。","B":"检查 NACL 是否已附加到日志记录服务子网，以允许与接口端点子网之间的通信。检查 NACL 是否已附加到接口终端节点子 网，以允许与 EC2 实例上运行的日志服务子网之间进行通信。","C":"检查 EC2 实例上运行的日志服务的安全组，以确保它允许来自 NLB 子网的入口。","D":"检查 EC2 实例上运行的日志服务的安全组，以确保它允许来自客户端的入口。","E":"检查 NLB 的安全组，确保它允许从接口端点子网进入。"},"answer":["A","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AC":64,"BD":23},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・複選"},{"id":256,"question_en":"A company has millions of objects in an Amazon S3 bucket. The objects are in the S3 Standard storage class. All the S3 objects are accessed frequently. The number of users and applications that access the objects is increasing rapidly. The objects are encrypted with server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS). A solutions architect reviews the company’s monthly AWS invoice and notices that AWS KMS costs are increasing because of the high number of requests from Amazon S3. The solutions architect needs to optimize costs with minimal changes to the application. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司的 Amazon S3 存储桶中有数百万个对象。这些对象属于 S3 标准存储类。所有 S3 对象都会被频繁访问。访问对象的用户和 应用程序的数量正在迅速增加。这些对象通过使用 AWS KMS 密钥 (SSE-KMS) 的服务器端加密进行加密。 解决方案架构师检查了公司的每月 AWS 发票，并注意到由于来自 Amazon S3 的大量请求，AWS KMS 成本正在增加。解决方案架构师 需要通过对应用程序进行最小的更改来优化成本。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new S3 bucket that has server-side encryption with customer-provided keys (SSE-C) as the encryption type. Copy the existing objects to the new S3 bucket. Specify SSE-C.","B":"Create a new S3 bucket that has server-side encryption with Amazon S3 managed keys (SSE-S3) as the encryption type. Use S3 Batch Operations to copy the existing objects to the new S3 bucket. Specify SSE-S3.","C":"Use AWS CloudHSM to store the encryption keys. Create a new S3 bucket. Use S3 Batch Operations to copy the existing objects to the new S3 bucket. Encrypt the objects by using the keys from CloudHSM.","D":"Use the S3 Intelligent-Tiering storage class for the S3 bucket. Create an S3 Intelligent-Tiering archive configuration to transition objects that are not accessed for 90 days to S3 Glacier Deep Archive."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的 S3 存储桶，该存储桶具有服务器端加密，并使用客户提供的密钥 (SSE-C) 作为加密类型。将现有对象复制到新 的 S3 存储桶。指定 SSE-C。","B":"创建一个新的 S3 存储桶，该存储桶采用 Amazon S3 托管密钥 (SSE-S3) 作为加密类型进行服务器端加密。使用 S3 批量操作将现 有对象复制到新的 S3 存储桶。指定 SSE-S3。","C":"使用 AWS CloudHSM 存储加密密钥。创建一个新的 S3 存储桶。使用 S3 批量操作将现有对象复制到新的 S3 存储桶。使用 CloudHSM 中的密钥加密对象。","D":"对 S3 存储桶使用 S3 智能分层存储类别。创建 S3 智能分层存档配置，将 90 天内未访问的对象过渡到 S3 Glacier Deep Archive。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The KMS cost driver is that with SSE-KMS and no S3 Bucket Key, Amazon S3 calls AWS KMS (GenerateDataKey/Decrypt) on every object request, so rapidly growing access multiplies KMS request charges. Among the offered options, switching to SSE-S3 eliminates these per-request KMS calls entirely, and SSE-S3 carries no additional fees. SSE-S3 encryption is fully transparent server-side, so it requires no changes to how the application reads/writes objects (minimal application change). Using S3 Batch Operations to copy the millions of existing objects re-encrypts them at scale with the least operational overhead, versus scripting your own copy. Note the ideal real-world fix (enable S3 Bucket Keys, up to ~99% KMS request reduction with no client changes) is not offered, making B the best available choice.","explanation_zh":"KMS 成本上升的根本原因是：在 SSE-KMS 且未啟用 S3 Bucket Key 的情況下，每次存取物件時 Amazon S3 都會呼叫 AWS KMS（GenerateDataKey/Decrypt），因此存取量快速增加會使 KMS 請求費用倍增。在所提供的選項中，改用 SSE-S3 可完全消除這些逐請求的 KMS 呼叫，且 SSE-S3 不收取額外費用。SSE-S3 在伺服器端完全透明，應用程式讀寫物件的方式無需更動（變更最少）。使用 S3 Batch Operations 來複製數百萬個既有物件可大規模重新加密，營運負擔最低，優於自行撰寫複製腳本。注意：實務上最理想的修法（啟用 S3 Bucket Keys，可在不更動用戶端的情況下將 KMS 請求降低約 99%）並未列入選項，因此 B 是現有選項中的最佳答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SSE-C requires the client to generate, store, and supply the encryption key in required headers on EVERY PUT/GET/COPY/HEAD request. S3 does not store the key, so this forces major application changes and heavy key-management operational overhead, directly contradicting 'minimal changes' and 'LEAST operational overhead.'","why_zh":"SSE-C 要求用戶端自行產生、保管，並在每次 PUT/GET/COPY/HEAD 請求的必填標頭中提供金鑰；S3 不會保存該金鑰，因此需大幅改動應用程式並承擔沉重的金鑰管理負擔，與「變更最少」「營運負擔最低」直接抵觸。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Using AWS CloudHSM and encrypting objects with HSM keys means operating an HSM cluster and building custom encryption integration, the highest operational overhead of all options and far from minimal application change.","why_zh":"使用 AWS CloudHSM 並以 HSM 金鑰加密物件，意味著要維運 HSM 叢集並建立自訂加密整合，是所有選項中營運負擔最高者，遠非變更最少。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Intelligent-Tiering plus Glacier Deep Archive optimizes STORAGE cost, not KMS REQUEST cost. The objects remain SSE-KMS encrypted, so KMS calls per access continue. Also the objects are accessed frequently, so they would not transition to colder tiers; this does not solve the stated problem.","why_zh":"Intelligent-Tiering 加 Glacier Deep Archive 優化的是「儲存」成本，而非「KMS 請求」成本。物件仍為 SSE-KMS 加密，每次存取仍會呼叫 KMS。且物件被頻繁存取，不會轉入較冷層級，無法解決題目所述問題。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/UsingServerSideEncryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/bucket-key.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/UsingKMSEncryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/ServerSideEncryptionCustomerKeys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/batch-ops-update-encryption.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":257,"question_en":"A media storage application uploads user photos to Amazon S3 for processing by AWS Lambda functions. Application state is stored in Amazon DynamoDB tables. Users are reporting that some uploaded photos are not being processed properly. The application developers trace the logs and find that Lambda is experiencing photo processing issues when thousands of users upload photos simultaneously. The issues are the result of Lambda concurrency limits and the performance of DynamoDB when data is saved. Which combination of actions should a solutions architect take to increase the performance and reliability of the application? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"媒体存储应用程序将用户照片上传到 Amazon S3 以供 AWS Lambda 函数处理。应用程序状态存储在 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。用户报 告称，某些上传的照片未得到正确处理。应用程序开发人员跟踪日志发现，当数千个用户同时上传照片时，Lambda 遇到照片处理问 题。这些问题是由于 Lambda 并发限制和保存数据时 DynamoDB 的性能造成的。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪种操作组合来提高应用程序的性能和可靠性？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Evaluate and adjust the RCUs for the DynamoDB tables.","B":"Evaluate and adjust the WCUs for the DynamoDB tables.","C":"Add an Amazon ElastiCache layer to increase the performance of Lambda functions.","D":"Add an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue and reprocessing logic between Amazon S3 and the Lambda functions.","E":"Use S3 Transfer Acceleration to provide lower latency to users."},"options_zh":{"A":"评估并调整 DynamoDB 表的 RCU。","B":"评估并调整 DynamoDB 表的 WCU。","C":"添加 Amazon ElastiCache 层以提高 Lambda 函数的性能。","D":"在 Amazon S3 和 Lambda 函数之间添加 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列和重新处理逻辑。","E":"使用 S3 传输加速为用户提供更低的延迟。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BD":100},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":258,"question_en":"A company runs an application in an on-premises data center. The application gives users the ability to upload media files. The files persist in a file server. The web application has many users. The application server is overutilized, which causes data uploads to fail occasionally. The company frequently adds new storage to the file server. The company wants to resolve these challenges by migrating the application to AWS. Users from across the United States and Canada access the application. Only authenticated users should have the ability to access the application to upload files. The company will consider a solution that refactors the application, and the company needs to accelerate application development. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司在本地数据中心运行应用程序。该应用程序使用户能够上传媒体文件。文件保留在文件服务器中。Web 应用程序有很多用 户。应用服务器利用率过高，偶尔会导致数据上传失败。该公司经常向文件服务器添加新存储。该公司希望通过将应用程序迁移到 AWS 来解决这些挑战。 来自美国和加拿大各地的用户访问该应用程序。只有经过身份验证的用户才能够访问应用程序来上传文件。公司会考虑重构应用程 序的解决方案，公司需要加速应用程序开发。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Application Migration Service to migrate the application server to Amazon EC2 instances. Create an Auto Scaling group for the EC2 instances. Use an Application Load Balancer to distribute the requests. Modify the application to use Amazon S3 to persist the files. Use Amazon Cognito to authenticate users.","B":"Use AWS Application Migration Service to migrate the application server to Amazon EC2 instances. Create an Auto Scaling group for the EC2 instances. Use an Application Load Balancer to distribute the requests. Set up AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) to give users the ability to sign in to the application. Modify the application to use Amazon S3 to persist the files.","C":"Create a static website for uploads of media files. Store the static assets in Amazon S3. Use AWS AppSync to create an API. Use AWS Lambda resolvers to upload the media files to Amazon S3. Use Amazon Cognito to authenticate users.","D":"Use AWS Amplify to create a static website for uploads of media files. Use Amplify Hosting to serve the website through Amazon CloudFront. Use Amazon S3 to store the uploaded media files. Use Amazon Cognito to authenticate users."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Application Migration Service 将应用程序服务器迁移到 Amazon EC2 实例。为 EC2 实例创建 Auto Scaling 组。使用应用 程序负载均衡器来分发请求。修改应用程序以使用 Amazon S3 来保留文件。使用 Amazon Cognito 对用户进行身份验证。","B":"使用 AWS Application Migration Service 将应用程序服务器迁移到 Amazon EC2 实例。为 EC2 实例创建 Auto Scaling 组。使用应用 程序负载均衡器来分发请求。设置 AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On)，使用户能够登录应用程序。修改应用程序以使用 Amazon S3 来保留文件。","C":"创建一个用于上传媒体文件的静态网站。将静态资产存储在 Amazon S3 中。使用 AWS AppSync 创建 API。使用 AWS Lambda 解 析器将媒体文件上传到 Amazon S3。使用 Amazon Cognito 对用户进行身份验证。","D":"使用 AWS Amplify 创建用于上传媒体文件的静态网站。使用 Amplify Hosting 通过 Amazon CloudFront 为网站提供服务。使用 Amazon S3 存储上传的媒体文件。使用 Amazon Cognito 对用户进行身份验证。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":94},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifiers are 'refactor the application,' 'accelerate application development,' and 'LEAST operational overhead,' with public end users in the US/Canada who must be authenticated before uploading. AWS Amplify is purpose-built to accelerate full-stack development: Amplify Hosting serves the static frontend through Amazon CloudFront, the Amplify Storage module performs direct browser-to-S3 uploads, and Amplify integrates Amazon Cognito for end-user authentication out of the box. This removes the overutilized server and the need to keep adding storage, scales automatically, and requires the least code and least ongoing management. Option D satisfies every requirement in a single managed framework.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定詞是「重構應用程式」、「加速應用程式開發」與「最少維運負擔」，並且美國/加拿大的公開終端使用者必須先通過驗證才能上傳檔案。AWS Amplify 正是為加速全端開發而設計：Amplify Hosting 透過 Amazon CloudFront 提供靜態前端，Amplify 的 Storage 模組可直接從瀏覽器上傳至 S3，並內建整合 Amazon Cognito 進行終端使用者驗證。這消除了過載的伺服器與不斷擴充儲存的需求、可自動擴展，且所需程式碼與持續維運最少。選項 D 以單一受管框架滿足所有需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) is a rehost/lift-and-shift tool; it migrates the existing application server to EC2 rather than refactoring it, and it does not accelerate application development. Managing EC2 Auto Scaling, an ALB, OS patching, and the application itself is far higher operational overhead than a managed Amplify stack.","why_zh":"AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) 是重新託管（lift-and-shift）工具；它將既有應用伺服器遷移到 EC2，並非重構，也無法加速開發。需自行管理 EC2 Auto Scaling、ALB、作業系統修補與應用程式本身，維運負擔遠高於受管的 Amplify 架構。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same rehost-to-EC2 high-overhead problem as A and no refactor. Worse, it uses AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS SSO), which is intended for workforce/internal user single sign-on, not for authenticating large numbers of public external application end users across the US and Canada; Amazon Cognito is the correct service for customer-facing auth.","why_zh":"與 A 相同的「遷移到 EC2、高維運負擔且未重構」問題。更糟的是它採用 AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS SSO)，那是給員工/內部使用者單一登入用的，並不適合驗證跨美加的大量公開外部終端使用者；面向客戶的驗證應使用 Amazon Cognito。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Serverless and does refactor, but it requires you to design and maintain an AWS AppSync GraphQL API plus write/operate custom Lambda resolvers and separately wire up hosting. Routing media file uploads through Lambda resolvers is also an anti-pattern (Lambda payload limits). This is more development effort and more operational overhead than Amplify, which bundles hosting, direct S3 uploads, and Cognito auth.","why_zh":"屬於無伺服器且有重構，但需自行設計與維護 AWS AppSync GraphQL API，並撰寫/維運自訂 Lambda resolver，還要另外串接代管。透過 Lambda resolver 傳輸媒體檔案上傳也是反模式（Lambda 酬載大小限制）。相較於整合了代管、直接 S3 上傳與 Cognito 驗證的 Amplify，這需要更多開發工作與維運負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/hands-on/latest/build-react-app-amplify-graphql/build-react-app-amplify-graphql.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/API/browser-based-uploads-aws-amplify.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amplify/latest/userguide/server-side-rendering-amplify.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/patterns/create-a-react-app-by-using-aws-amplify-and-add-authentication-with-amazon-cognito.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":259,"question_en":"A company has an application that is deployed on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The instances are part of an Auto Scaling group. The application has unpredictable workloads and frequently scales out and in. The company’s development team wants to analyze application logs to find ways to improve the application's performance. However, the logs are no longer available after instances scale in. Which solution will give the development team the ability to view the application logs after a scale-in event?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个应用程序部署在应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面的 Amazon EC2 实例上。这些实例是 Auto Scaling 组的一部分。该应 用程序具有不可预测的工作负载，并且频繁地横向扩展和收缩。该公司的开发团队希望分析应用程序日志，以找到提高应用程序性 能的方法。但是，在实例缩减后，日志将不再可用。 哪种解决方案将使开发团队能够在缩减事件后查看应用程序日志？","options_en":{"A":"Enable access logs for the ALB. Store the logs in an Amazon S3 bucket.","B":"Configure the EC2 instances to publish logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs by using the unified CloudWatch agent.","C":"Modify the Auto Scaling group to use a step scaling policy.","D":"Instrument the application with AWS X-Ray tracing."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 ALB 的访问日志。将日志存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。","B":"配置 EC2 实例以使用统一 CloudWatch 代理将日志发布到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。","C":"修改 Auto Scaling 组以使用步进扩展策略。","D":"使用 AWS X-Ray 跟踪检测应用程序。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":260,"question_en":"A company runs an unauthenticated static website (www.example.com) that includes a registration form for users. The website uses Amazon S3 for hosting and uses Amazon CloudFront as the content delivery network with AWS WAF configured. When the registration form is submitted, the website calls an Amazon API Gateway API endpoint that invokes an AWS Lambda function to process the payload and forward the payload to an external API call. During testing, a solutions architect encounters a cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) error. The solutions architect confirms that the CloudFront distribution origin has the Access-Control-Allow-Origin header set to www.example.com. What should the solutions architect do to resolve the error?","question_zh":"一家公司运行一个未经身份验证的静态网站 (www.example.com)，其中包含用户注册表单。该网站使用 Amazon S3 进行托管，并使用 Amazon CloudFront 作为配置了 AWS WAF 的内容交付网络。提交注册表单后，网站会调用 Amazon API Gateway API 终端节点，该终端 节点会调用 AWS Lambda 函数来处理负载并将负载转发到外部 API 调用。 在测试期间，解决方案架构师遇到跨源资源共享 (CORS) 错误。解决方案架构师确认 CloudFront 分发源的 Access-Control-Allow-Origin 标头设置为 www.example.com。 解决方案架构师应该如何解决该错误？","options_en":{"A":"Change the CORS configuration on the S3 bucket. Add rules for CORS to the AllowedOrigin element for www.example.com.","B":"Enable the CORS setting in AWS WAF. Create a web ACL rule in which the Access-Control-Allow-Origin header is set to www.example.com.","C":"Enable the CORS setting on the API Gateway API endpoint. Ensure that the API endpoint is configured to return all responses that have the Access-Control-Allow-Origin header set to www.example.com.","D":"Enable the CORS setting on the Lambda function. Ensure that the return code of the function has the Access-Control-Allow-Origin header set to www.example.com."},"options_zh":{"A":"更改 S3 存储桶上的 CORS 配置。将 CORS 规则添加到 www.example.com 的AllowedOrigin 元素。","B":"在 AWS WAF 中启用 CORS 设置。创建一个 Web ACL 规则，其中 Access-Control-Allow-Origin 标头设置为 www.example.com。","C":"在 API Gateway API 端点上启用 CORS 设置。确保 API 端点配置为返回 Access-Control-Allow-Origin 标头设置为 www.example.com 的所有响应。","D":"在 Lambda 函数上启用 CORS 设置。确保函数的返回代码的 Access-Control-Allow-Origin 标头设置为 www.example.com。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":95},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The CORS error occurs on the request the browser makes from www.example.com (served via CloudFront) to the API Gateway endpoint, which is a different origin (different domain). CORS is enforced by the browser, and the cross-origin response must come from the server that actually handles the request. The form POST is processed by API Gateway invoking Lambda, so API Gateway must return the Access-Control-Allow-Origin header (and respond to the OPTIONS preflight) for the matching origin. The clue that the CloudFront origin already has Access-Control-Allow-Origin set to www.example.com is a distractor: that header on the static site's own origin does nothing for the separate request to the API Gateway endpoint. AWS API Gateway provides built-in CORS enablement that creates an OPTIONS method and adds the Access-Control-Allow-Origin header to method responses, which is exactly what is needed.","explanation_zh":"CORS 錯誤發生在瀏覽器從 www.example.com（透過 CloudFront 提供）向 API Gateway 端點發出的請求上，而該端點屬於不同來源（不同網域）。CORS 由瀏覽器強制執行，跨來源的回應必須來自實際處理該請求的伺服器。表單 POST 由 API Gateway 呼叫 Lambda 處理，因此 API Gateway 必須針對相符的來源回傳 Access-Control-Allow-Origin 標頭（並回應 OPTIONS 預檢請求）。題目提到 CloudFront origin 已將 Access-Control-Allow-Origin 設為 www.example.com 是干擾項：該標頭設在靜態網站自己的來源上，對於另一個對 API Gateway 端點的請求毫無幫助。API Gateway 內建啟用 CORS 的功能，會建立 OPTIONS 方法並在方法回應中加入 Access-Control-Allow-Origin 標頭，這正是本題所需。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"S3 bucket CORS only affects requests made directly to the S3 origin for static assets. The CORS error is on the call to the API Gateway endpoint, not to S3, so changing S3 CORS does not resolve it.","why_zh":"S3 bucket 的 CORS 只影響直接對 S3 來源請求靜態資產的情況。CORS 錯誤發生在對 API Gateway 端點的呼叫上，而非 S3，因此修改 S3 CORS 無法解決問題。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS WAF is a web application firewall that inspects and blocks/allows requests based on rules; it has no feature to set CORS response headers like Access-Control-Allow-Origin. There is no 'CORS setting' in WAF.","why_zh":"AWS WAF 是依規則檢查並允許/封鎖請求的網頁應用程式防火牆，沒有設定 Access-Control-Allow-Origin 等 CORS 回應標頭的功能。WAF 中並不存在所謂的「CORS 設定」。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"There is no 'CORS setting' to enable on a Lambda function itself for an API Gateway proxy/non-proxy REST integration in this design; CORS must be handled at API Gateway, which manages the OPTIONS preflight method. Even with Lambda proxy integration the standard, AWS-documented fix here is enabling CORS on the API Gateway resource (which creates the OPTIONS method); the question explicitly points to enabling the CORS setting on the API endpoint. Returning a header from Lambda alone does not satisfy the preflight handled by API Gateway.","why_zh":"在此設計中，Lambda 函式本身並沒有可啟用的「CORS 設定」；CORS 必須在 API Gateway 處理，由其管理 OPTIONS 預檢方法。AWS 文件記載的標準做法是在 API Gateway 資源上啟用 CORS（會建立 OPTIONS 方法），題目也明確指向在 API 端點啟用 CORS 設定。僅由 Lambda 回傳標頭無法滿足由 API Gateway 處理的預檢請求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/how-to-cors.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/how-to-cors-console.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-test-cors.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":261,"question_en":"A company has many separate AWS accounts and uses no central billing or management. Each AWS account hosts services for different departments in the company. The company has a Microsoft Azure Active Directory that is deployed. A solutions architect needs to centralize billing and management of the company’s AWS accounts. The company wants to start using identity federation instead of manual user management. The company also wants to use temporary credentials instead of long-lived access keys. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司拥有许多独立的 AWS 账户，并且不使用集中计费或管理。每个 AWS 账户都为公司的不同部门托管服务。该公司已部署 Microsoft Azure Active Directory。 解决方案架构师需要集中公司 AWS 账户的计费和管理。该公司希望开始使用身份联合而不是手动用户管理。该公司还希望使用临时 凭证而不是长期访问密钥。 哪种步骤组合可以满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a new AWS account to serve as a management account. Deploy an organization in AWS Organizations. Invite each existing AWS account to join the organization. Ensure that each account accepts the invitation.","B":"Configure each AWS account's email address to be aws+@example.com so that account management email messages and invoices are sent to the same place.","C":"Deploy AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) in the management account. Connect IAM Identity Center to the Azure Active Directory. Configure IAM Identity Center for automatic synchronization of users and groups.","D":"Deploy an AWS Managed Microsoft AD directory in the management account. Share the directory with all other accounts in the organization by using AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM).","E":"Create AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) permission sets. Attach the permission sets to the appropriate IAM Identity Center groups and AWS accounts.","F":"Configure AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) in each AWS account to use AWS Managed Microsoft AD for authentication and authorization."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的 AWS 账户作为管理账户。在 AWS Organizations 中部署组织。邀请每个现有 AWS 账户加入该组织。确保每个帐户 都接受邀请。","B":"将每个AWS账户的电子邮件地址配置为aws+@example.com，以便将帐户管理电子邮件和发票发送到同一位置。","C":"在管理账户中部署 AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On)。将 IAM 身份中心连接到 Azure Active Directory。配置 IAM Identity Center 以自动同步用户和组。","D":"在管理账户中部署 AWS Managed Microsoft AD 目录。使用 AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) 与组织中的所有其他账户共 享目录。","E":"创建 AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) 权限集。将权限集附加到适当的 IAM Identity Center 组和 AWS 账户。","F":"在每个 AWS 账户中配置 AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM)，以使用 AWS Managed Microsoft AD 进行身份验证和授权。"},"answer":["C","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ACE":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The three requirements are: centralize billing/management, use identity federation with the existing Azure AD instead of manual user management, and use temporary credentials. (A) Creating a management account, deploying AWS Organizations, and inviting existing accounts is the foundation that centralizes consolidated billing and management; it is also a prerequisite because IAM Identity Center multi-account permission sets are available only for an organization instance of IAM Identity Center. (C) Deploying IAM Identity Center in the management account, connecting it to Azure Active Directory via SAML 2.0, and enabling SCIM gives one point of federation with automatic synchronization of users and groups, replacing manual user management. (E) Creating permission sets and attaching them to IAM Identity Center groups and accounts grants access; when a permission set is assigned, IAM Identity Center provisions IAM roles that users assume, which inherently provides short-lived temporary credentials instead of long-lived access keys. The dump answer (C, D, E) is wrong because it omits A (no Organizations means no management account, no consolidated billing, and no organization instance for cross-account permission sets) and includes D, which is unnecessary since the company already has Azure AD as its IdP.","explanation_zh":"本題有三個需求：集中帳單與管理、使用既有 Azure AD 做身分聯合 (federation) 取代手動管理使用者、以及使用臨時憑證。(A) 建立 management account、部署 AWS Organizations 並邀請現有帳號加入，是集中合併帳單 (consolidated billing) 與管理的基礎；同時也是必要前提，因為 IAM Identity Center 的多帳號 permission sets 僅在 organization instance 的 IAM Identity Center 中可用。(C) 在 management account 部署 IAM Identity Center，透過 SAML 2.0 連接 Azure Active Directory，並啟用 SCIM 自動同步使用者與群組，提供單一聯合點並取代手動使用者管理。(E) 建立 permission sets 並指派給 IAM Identity Center 的群組與帳號；指派 permission set 時，IAM Identity Center 會佈建供使用者擔任 (assume) 的 IAM roles，本質上提供短期臨時憑證，取代長效 access keys。Dump 答案 (C, D, E) 有誤，因為它遺漏 A（沒有 Organizations 就沒有 management account、沒有合併帳單、也沒有可做跨帳號 permission sets 的 organization instance），且納入了 D，而公司已有 Azure AD 作為 IdP，部署 AWS Managed Microsoft AD 是多餘的。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Configuring a shared catch-all email alias for account messages and invoices is a minor convenience, not a required step for centralizing billing; consolidated billing is achieved through AWS Organizations (A), not via email aliasing.","why_zh":"為帳號訊息與發票設定共用的 catch-all 電子郵件別名只是次要便利做法，並非集中帳單的必要步驟；合併帳單是透過 AWS Organizations (A) 達成，而非靠電子郵件別名。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Deploying AWS Managed Microsoft AD and sharing it via AWS RAM is unnecessary because the company already has Azure AD as its identity provider; you federate IAM Identity Center directly to Azure AD via SAML/SCIM rather than standing up and RAM-sharing a separate directory.","why_zh":"部署 AWS Managed Microsoft AD 並透過 AWS RAM 分享是多餘的，因為公司已有 Azure AD 作為身分提供者；應透過 SAML/SCIM 直接將 IAM Identity Center 與 Azure AD 聯合，而非另建並用 RAM 分享一個獨立目錄。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"IAM does not authenticate users against AWS Managed Microsoft AD per account in this manner, and configuring each account individually contradicts the centralization goal and the use of the existing Azure AD as the federation source.","why_zh":"IAM 並不會以這種方式在每個帳號中對 AWS Managed Microsoft AD 進行驗證，且逐一設定每個帳號違背了集中化目標，也未使用既有的 Azure AD 作為聯合來源。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/manage-your-identity-source-idp.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/provision-automatically.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/permissionsetsconcept.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_invite-account.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":262,"question_en":"A company wants to manage the costs associated with a group of 20 applications that are infrequently used, but are still business-critical, by migrating to AWS. The applications are a mix of Java and Node.js spread across different instance clusters. The company wants to minimize costs while standardizing by using a single deployment methodology. Most of the applications are part of month-end processing routines with a small number of concurrent users, but they are occasionally run at other times. Average application memory consumption is less than 1 GB. though some applications use as much as 2.5 GB of memory during peak processing. The most important application in the group is a billing report written in Java that accesses multiple data sources and often runs for several hours. Which is the MOST cost-effective solution?","question_zh":"一家公司希望通过迁移到 AWS 来管理与 20 个不常用但仍对业务至关重要的应用程序组相关的成本。这些应用程序是 Java 和 Node.js 的混合体，分布在不同的实例集群中。该公司希望通过使用单一部署方法来实现标准化，同时最大限度地降低成本。 大多数应用程序是具有少量并发用户的月末处理例程的一部分，但它们偶尔会在其他时间运行。平均应用程序内存消耗小于 1 GB。 尽管某些应用程序在高峰处理期间使用多达 2.5 GB 的内存。该组中最重要的应用程序是用 Java 编写的计费报告，它访问多个数据 源并且通常运行几个小时。 哪个是最具成本效益的解决方案？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy a separate AWS Lambda function for each application. Use AWS CloudTrail logs and Amazon CloudWatch alarms to verify completion of critical jobs.","B":"Deploy Amazon ECS containers on Amazon EC2 with Auto Scaling configured for memory utilization of 75%. Deploy an ECS task for each application being migrated with ECS task scaling. Monitor services and hosts by using Amazon CloudWatch.","C":"Deploy AWS Elastic Beanstalk for each application with Auto Scaling to ensure that all requests have su®cient resources. Monitor each AWS Elastic Beanstalk deployment by using CloudWatch alarms.","D":"Deploy a new Amazon EC2 instance cluster that co-hosts all applications by using EC2 Auto Scaling and Application Load Balancers. Scale cluster size based on a custom metric set on instance memory utilization. Purchase 3-year Reserved Instance reservations equal to the GroupMaxSize parameter of the Auto Scaling group."},"options_zh":{"A":"为每个应用程序部署单独的 AWS Lambda 函数。使用 AWS CloudTrail 日志和 Amazon CloudWatch 警报来验证关键作业的完成情 况。","B":"在 Amazon EC2 上部署 Amazon ECS 容器，并将 Auto Scaling 配置为内存利用率为 75%。为通过 ECS 任务扩展迁移的每个应用程 序部署一个 ECS 任务。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 监控服务和主机。","C":"使用 Auto Scaling 为每个应用程序部署 AWS Elastic Beanstalk，以确保所有请求都有足够的资源。使用 CloudWatch 警报监控每 个 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 部署。","D":"使用 EC2 Auto Scaling 和 Application Load Balancer 部署一个新的 Amazon EC2 实例集群，该集群共同托管所有应用程序。根据 实例内存利用率设置的自定义指标来扩展集群大小。购买等于 Auto Scaling 组的 GroupMaxSize 参数的 3 年预留实例预留。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":86},"tags":["Compute","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":263,"question_en":"A solutions architect needs to review the design of an Amazon EMR cluster that is using the EMR File System (EMRFS). The cluster performs tasks that are critical to business needs. The cluster is running Amazon EC2 On-Demand Instances at all times for all task, primary, and core nodes. The EMR tasks run each morning, starting at 1:00 AM. and take 6 hours to finish running. The amount of time to complete the processing is not a priority because the data is not referenced until late in the day. The solutions architect must review the architecture and suggest a solution to minimize the compute costs. Which solution should the solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师需要检查使用 EMR 文件系统 (EMRFS) 的 Amazon EMR 集群的设计。集群执行对业务需求至关重要的任务。该集群始 终为所有任务、主节点和核心节点运行 Amazon EC2 按需实例。EMR 任务每天早上从凌晨 1:00 开始运行。并需要6个小时才能完成运 行。完成处理的时间量不是优先考虑的问题，因为直到当天晚些时候才会引用数据。 解决方案架构师必须审查架构并提出解决方案以最大限度地降低计算成本。 解决方案架构师应该推荐哪种解决方案来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Launch all task, primary, and core nodes on Spot Instances in an instance ­eet. Terminate the cluster, including all instances, when the processing is completed.","B":"Launch the primary and core nodes on On-Demand Instances. Launch the task nodes on Spot Instances in an instance ­eet. Terminate the cluster, including all instances, when the processing is completed. Purchase Compute Savings Plans to cover the On-Demand Instance usage.","C":"Continue to launch all nodes on On-Demand Instances. Terminate the cluster, including all instances, when the processing is completed. Purchase Compute Savings Plans to cover the On-Demand Instance usage.","D":"Launch the primary and core nodes on On-Demand Instances. Launch the task nodes on Spot Instances in an instance ­eet. Terminate only the task node instances when the processing is completed. Purchase Compute Savings Plans to cover the On-Demand Instance usage."},"options_zh":{"A":"在实例队列中的 Spot 实例上启动所有任务、主节点和核心节点。处理完成后，终止集群，包括所有实例。","B":"在按需实例上启动主节点和核心节点。在实例队列中的 Spot 实例上启动任务节点。处理完成后，终止集群，包括所有实例。 购买计算节省计划来满足按需实例的使用。","C":"继续启动按需实例上的所有节点。处理完成后，终止集群，包括所有实例。购买计算节省计划来满足按需实例的使用。","D":"在按需实例上启动主节点和核心节点。在实例队列中的 Spot 实例上启动任务节点。处理完成后仅终止任务节点实例。购买计 算节省计划来满足按需实例的使用。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":62,"B":37},"tags":["Compute","Cost Optimization","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The cluster runs business-critical jobs for only 6 hours each morning. Per AWS EMR guidance, task nodes do not store HDFS data, so terminating them (e.g., Spot interruption) causes no data loss and minimal cluster impact, making task nodes the recommended Spot use case. Primary and core nodes must stay reliable: terminating the primary ends the whole cluster, and core nodes hold HDFS data, so AWS warns to use Spot for them only when sudden termination or partial HDFS data loss is tolerable, which is unacceptable for business-critical work. So the architecture should keep primary/core on On-Demand and put only task nodes on Spot (rules out A). Because the job finishes each morning and data isn't read until late in the day, the cluster (all instances) should be terminated after processing to stop incurring compute charges during the ~18 idle hours. Option B does exactly this; Option D wrongly terminates only the task instances, leaving On-Demand primary/core running idle all day, which costs far more. Option C keeps all nodes On-Demand with no Spot savings. The Compute Savings Plans clause is suboptimal for a 6-hour/day workload, but B is the only choice that both uses Spot correctly for task nodes AND terminates the entire cluster to eliminate idle cost, making it the most cost-effective valid answer.","explanation_zh":"此叢集每天早上只執行 6 小時的關鍵業務工作。根據 AWS EMR 指南,task 節點不儲存 HDFS 資料,因此被終止(例如 Spot 中斷)不會造成資料遺失,對叢集影響最小,是建議的 Spot 使用情境。Primary 與 core 節點必須維持可靠:終止 primary 會結束整個叢集,而 core 節點保存 HDFS 資料,AWS 警告只有在可接受突然終止或部分 HDFS 資料遺失時才在這些節點使用 Spot,而關鍵業務工作無法接受,因此排除 A。架構應將 primary/core 保留為 On-Demand,只把 task 節點放在 Spot。由於工作每天早上完成且資料到當天稍晚才被讀取,處理完成後應終止整個叢集(所有執行個體),以避免約 18 小時閒置期間繼續產生運算費用。選項 B 正是如此;選項 D 只終止 task 執行個體,讓 On-Demand 的 primary/core 整天閒置運行,成本高得多。選項 C 全部使用 On-Demand,沒有任何 Spot 節省。Compute Savings Plans 對於每天僅 6 小時的工作並非最佳,但 B 是唯一同時正確地對 task 節點使用 Spot 並終止整個叢集以消除閒置成本的選項,因此是最具成本效益的有效答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Launching primary and core nodes on Spot risks ending the entire cluster (primary) and HDFS data loss (core). AWS docs say to use Spot for primary/core only when sudden termination or partial data loss is tolerable, which is unacceptable for business-critical tasks.","why_zh":"將 primary 與 core 節點放在 Spot 會有結束整個叢集(primary)及 HDFS 資料遺失(core)的風險。AWS 文件指出只有在可接受突然終止或部分資料遺失時才對 primary/core 使用 Spot,這對關鍵業務工作不可接受。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Keeping all nodes On-Demand forgoes the large Spot savings available for task nodes, which carry no data-loss risk. It is the least cost-optimized of the valid options that terminate the cluster.","why_zh":"所有節點維持 On-Demand 放棄了 task 節點可用的大幅 Spot 節省,而 task 節點並無資料遺失風險。在會終止叢集的有效選項中,這是成本最未最佳化的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Terminating only the task (Spot) instances leaves the On-Demand primary and core nodes running 24/7 even though the job finishes each morning, paying for ~18 idle hours daily. This is far more expensive than terminating the whole cluster as in B.","why_zh":"只終止 task(Spot)執行個體會讓 On-Demand 的 primary 與 core 節點全天 24 小時運行,即使工作每天早上就完成,每天仍為約 18 小時的閒置時間付費。這比 B 終止整個叢集昂貴得多。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/emr/latest/ManagementGuide/emr-plan-instances-guidelines.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/emr/latest/ManagementGuide/emr-master-core-task-nodes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/savingsplans/latest/userguide/what-is-savings-plans.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":264,"question_en":"A company has migrated a legacy application to the AWS Cloud. The application runs on three Amazon EC2 instances that are spread across three Availability Zones. One EC2 instance is in each Availability Zone. The EC2 instances are running in three private subnets of the VPC and are set up as targets for an Application Load Balancer (ALB) that is associated with three public subnets. The application needs to communicate with on-premises systems. Only tra®c from IP addresses in the company's IP address range are allowed to access the on-premises systems. The company’s security team is bringing only one IP address from its internal IP address range to the cloud. The company has added this IP address to the allow list for the company firewall. The company also has created an Elastic IP address for this IP address. A solutions architect needs to create a solution that gives the application the ability to communicate with the on-premises systems. The solution also must be able to mitigate failures automatically. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司已将旧应用程序迁移到 AWS 云。该应用程序在分布于三个可用区的三个 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。每个可用区中有一个 EC2 实例。EC2 实例在 VPC 的三个私有子网中运行，并设置为与三个公有子网关联的应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 的目标。 应用程序需要与本地系统通信。仅允许来自公司IP地址范围内的IP地址的流量访问本地系统。该公司的安全团队仅将其内部 IP 地址 范围中的一个 IP 地址引入到云端。公司已将此 IP 地址添加到公司防火墙的允许列表中。该公司还为此IP地址创建了一个弹性IP地 址。 解决方案架构师需要创建一个解决方案，使应用程序能够与本地系统进行通信。该解决方案还必须能够自动缓解故障。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy three NAT gateways, one in each public subnet. Assign the Elastic IP address to the NAT gateways. Turn on health checks for the NAT gateways. If a NAT gateway fails a health check, recreate the NAT gateway and assign the Elastic IP address to the new NAT gateway.","B":"Replace the ALB with a Network Load Balancer (NLB). Assign the Elastic IP address to the NLTurn on health checks for the NLIn the case of a failed health check, redeploy the NLB in different subnets.","C":"Deploy a single NAT gateway in a public subnet. Assign the Elastic IP address to the NAT gateway. Use Amazon CloudWatch with a custom metric to monitor the NAT gateway. If the NAT gateway is unhealthy, invoke an AWS Lambda function to create a new NAT gateway in a different subnet. Assign the Elastic IP address to the new NAT gateway.","D":"Assign the Elastic IP address to the ALB. Create an Amazon Route 53 simple record with the Elastic IP address as the value. Create a Route 53 health check. In the case of a failed health check, recreate the ALB in different subnets."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署三个 NAT 网关，每个公有子网各一个。将弹性 IP 地址分配给 NAT 网关。打开 NAT 网关的运行状况检查。如果NAT网关健 康检查失败，请重新创建NAT网关并将弹性IP地址分配给新的NAT网关。","B":"将 ALB 替换为网络负载均衡器 (NLB)。为 NLT 分配弹性 IP 地址打开 NL 的运行状况检查。如果运行状况检查失败，请在不同子 网中重新部署 NLB。","C":"在公有子网中部署单个 NAT 网关。将弹性 IP 地址分配给 NAT 网关。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 和自定义指标来监控 NAT 网关。 如果 NAT 网关运行状况不佳，请调用 AWS Lambda 函数在不同的子网中创建新的 NAT 网关。将弹性 IP 地址分配给新的 NAT 网 关。","D":"将弹性 IP 地址分配给 ALB。使用弹性 IP 地址作为值创建 Amazon Route 53 简单记录。创建 Route 53 运行状况检查。如果运行 状况检查失败，请在不同子网中重新创建 ALB。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is that private-subnet EC2 instances reach on-premises systems using a single allow-listed source IP, and the design must automatically mitigate failures. The company has exactly ONE Elastic IP. A public NAT gateway preserves the instances' outbound source IP as its associated Elastic IP, and each public NAT gateway must have an Elastic IP associated at creation. Critically, an Elastic IP can be associated with only ONE NAT gateway at a time, so you cannot assign the single EIP to three NAT gateways simultaneously (option A is impossible, and NAT gateways have no 'turn on health checks' feature). Option C deploys one NAT gateway holding the single EIP, monitors it with a CloudWatch custom metric, and uses a Lambda function to recreate the NAT gateway in a different subnet/AZ and re-associate the same EIP if it becomes unhealthy. That is the only design that respects the one-EIP constraint, keeps the source IP fixed and allow-listed, and automatically mitigates AZ/NAT failures.","explanation_zh":"需求是讓私有子網的 EC2 instances 以單一被允許清單的來源 IP 連到地端系統，且設計需自動緩解故障。公司只有一個 Elastic IP。Public NAT gateway 會把 instances 的對外來源 IP 轉換成其關聯的 Elastic IP，且每個 public NAT gateway 在建立時都必須關聯一個 Elastic IP。關鍵在於：一個 Elastic IP 同一時間只能關聯到一個 NAT gateway，因此無法把唯一的 EIP 同時指派給三個 NAT gateway（選項 A 不可行，且 NAT gateway 也沒有可開啟的 health check 功能）。選項 C 部署一個持有該唯一 EIP 的 NAT gateway，用 CloudWatch 自訂指標監控，並在不健康時以 Lambda 在不同子網/AZ 重建 NAT gateway 並重新關聯同一個 EIP。這是唯一同時符合單一 EIP 限制、維持固定且被允許的來源 IP，並能自動緩解 AZ/NAT 故障的設計。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Technically impossible: a single Elastic IP cannot be associated with three NAT gateways at the same time, and the company only has one allow-listed EIP. NAT gateways also have no native 'health check' feature you can turn on. The design contradicts how EIPs and NAT gateways work.","why_zh":"技術上不可行：一個 Elastic IP 無法同時關聯到三個 NAT gateway，而公司只有一個被允許的 EIP。NAT gateway 也沒有可開啟的原生 health check 功能，此設計與 EIP/NAT gateway 的運作方式相矛盾。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"An NLB is the inbound load balancer; its Elastic IP is the destination for inbound clients, not the source IP of the EC2 instances' outbound traffic to on-premises. Replacing the ALB with an NLB does nothing to make outbound traffic originate from the allow-listed EIP.","why_zh":"NLB 是入站負載平衡器，其 Elastic IP 是入站客戶端的目的地，並非 EC2 instances 對外去地端流量的來源 IP。把 ALB 換成 NLB 完全無法讓對外流量以被允許的 EIP 作為來源。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Application Load Balancers do not support assigning Elastic IP addresses (only NLBs do), and an ALB is for inbound traffic. Assigning an EIP to the ALB and using Route 53 does not control the source IP of the instances' outbound connections to on-premises.","why_zh":"Application Load Balancer 不支援指派 Elastic IP（只有 NLB 支援），且 ALB 是處理入站流量。把 EIP 指派給 ALB 並用 Route 53 並無法控制 instances 對外連到地端的來源 IP。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-nat-gateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/nat-gateway-basics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/nat-gateway-scenarios.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":265,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage more than 1,000 AWS accounts. The company has created a new developer organization. There are 540 developer member accounts that must be moved to the new developer organization. All accounts are set up with all the required information so that each account can be operated as a standalone account. Which combination of steps should a solutions architect take to move all of the developer accounts to the new developer organization? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 管理 1,000 多个 AWS 账户。该公司创建了一个新的开发者组织。有 540 个开发者成员帐户必须迁移 到新的开发者组织。所有帐户均设置有所有必需的信息，以便每个帐户都可以作为独立帐户进行操作。 解决方案架构师应采取哪些步骤组合将所有开发人员帐户移至新的开发人员组织？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Call the MoveAccount operation in the Organizations API from the old organization's management account to migrate the developer accounts to the new developer organization.","B":"From the management account, remove each developer account from the old organization using the RemoveAccountFromOrganization operation in the Organizations API.","C":"From each developer account, remove the account from the old organization using the RemoveAccountFromOrganization operation in the Organizations API.","D":"Sign in to the new developer organization's management account and create a placeholder member account that acts as a target for the developer account migration.","E":"Call the InviteAccountToOrganization operation in the Organizations API from the new developer organization's management account to send invitations to the developer accounts.","F":"Have each developer sign in to their account and confirm to join the new developer organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"从​旧组织的管理账户调用 Organizations API 中的 MoveAccount 操作，将开发者账户迁移到新的开发者组织。","B":"在管理帐户中，使用组织 API 中的 RemoveAccountFromOrganization 操作从旧组织中删除每个开发人员帐户。","C":"在每个开发者帐户中，使用组织 API 中的 RemoveAccountFromOrganization 操作从旧组织中删除该帐户。","D":"登录新开发者组织的管理帐户并创建一个占位成员帐户，作为开发者帐户迁移的目标。","E":"从新开发者组织的管理账户调用 Organizations API 中的 InviteAccountToOrganization 操作，向开发者账户发送邀请。","F":"让每个开发者登录他们的帐户并确认加入新的开发者组织。"},"answer":["C","E","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BEF":89},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Migration"],"research":{"verdict":["B","E","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Moving accounts between AWS Organizations is done by the destination organization's management account inviting each account (InviteAccountToOrganization), the account accepting/confirming the invitation, and the source organization releasing the account. AWS docs state migration 'requires you to send an invite from the management account of the new organization, and to use the invited account to accept the invite to join the new organization' (E and F). For the release from the old org, RemoveAccountFromOrganization is a MANAGEMENT-ACCOUNT operation that removes a specified member account; a member account itself instead uses LeaveOrganization. Therefore B (management account calls RemoveAccountFromOrganization) is correct and C (each developer account calls RemoveAccountFromOrganization) is wrong because that API cannot be invoked by the member on itself. RemoveAccountFromOrganization additionally requires that the account already has standalone-account information (support plan, contact info, payment method), which the question explicitly states is true, confirming B as the intended path rather than the member-side leave flow.","explanation_zh":"在 AWS Organizations 之間移動帳戶的流程是：由目標組織的 management account 對每個帳戶發出邀請（InviteAccountToOrganization），帳戶接受/確認邀請加入新組織，並由原組織釋出該帳戶。AWS 文件指出遷移『需要由新組織的 management account 發送邀請，並由受邀帳戶接受邀請以加入新組織』（對應 E 與 F）。至於從舊組織釋出帳戶，RemoveAccountFromOrganization 是 management account 的操作，用於移除指定的成員帳戶；成員帳戶本身則改用 LeaveOrganization。因此 B（management account 呼叫 RemoveAccountFromOrganization）正確，而 C（由每個 developer 帳戶呼叫 RemoveAccountFromOrganization）錯誤，因為成員帳戶無法對自己呼叫該 API。RemoveAccountFromOrganization 還要求該帳戶已具備可作為獨立帳戶運作的資訊（support plan、聯絡資訊、付款方式），題目明確說明此條件已滿足，進一步確認 B 為正解。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"MoveAccount only relocates accounts within the SAME organization (root to OU, OU to OU). It cannot move accounts across two different organizations, so it cannot migrate developer accounts to the new organization.","why_zh":"MoveAccount 只能在『同一個』組織內移動帳戶（root 與 OU 之間、OU 與 OU 之間），無法跨兩個不同組織移動帳戶，因此無法把 developer 帳戶遷移到新組織。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"RemoveAccountFromOrganization is a management-account API used to remove a specified member account; a member account cannot call it on itself. To leave from the member side you use LeaveOrganization. So removing 'from each developer account' via RemoveAccountFromOrganization is technically invalid.","why_zh":"RemoveAccountFromOrganization 是 management account 用來移除指定成員帳戶的 API；成員帳戶不能對自己呼叫它。成員端離開應使用 LeaveOrganization。因此『從每個 developer 帳戶』呼叫 RemoveAccountFromOrganization 在技術上不成立。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"No placeholder/target member account is needed. Migration moves the actual existing account itself via invite-and-accept; there is no concept of a placeholder migration target in AWS Organizations.","why_zh":"不需要建立佔位用的目標成員帳戶。遷移是透過『邀請並接受』直接移動既有的實際帳戶，AWS Organizations 沒有佔位遷移目標的概念。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_account_migration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_remove.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_leave-as-member.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/move_account_to_ou.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・複選"},{"id":266,"question_en":"A company’s interactive web application uses an Amazon CloudFront distribution to serve images from an Amazon S3 bucket. Occasionally, third-party tools ingest corrupted images into the S3 bucket. This image corruption causes a poor user experience in the application later. The company has successfully implemented and tested Python logic to detect corrupt images. A solutions architect must recommend a solution to integrate the detection logic with minimal latency between the ingestion and serving. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的交互式 Web 应用程序使用 Amazon CloudFront 发行版来提供来自 Amazon S3 存储桶的图像。有时，第三方工具会将损坏 的图像提取到 S3 存储桶中。此图像损坏会导致稍后应用程序中的用户体验不佳。该公司已成功实施并测试了 Python 逻辑来检测损 坏的图像。 解决方案架构师必须推荐一种解决方案来集成检测逻辑，并在摄取和服务之间实现最小延迟。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use a Lambda@Edge function that is invoked by a viewer-response event.","B":"Use a Lambda@Edge function that is invoked by an origin-response event.","C":"Use an S3 event notification that invokes an AWS Lambda function.","D":"Use an S3 event notification that invokes an AWS Step Functions state machine."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用由查看者响应事件调用的 Lambda@Edge 函数。","B":"使用由源响应事件调用的 Lambda@Edge 函数。","C":"使用调用 AWS Lambda 函数的 S3 事件通知。","D":"使用调用 AWS Step Functions 状态机的 S3 事件通知。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to integrate the corruption-detection Python logic with minimal latency between ingestion and serving, meaning corrupt images should be caught as soon as they are written so they are never served. An S3 event notification (ObjectCreated) invokes the Lambda function asynchronously and immediately at ingestion time (typically delivered within seconds), running the detection off the serving path. This catches and remediates corrupt images right after third-party tools upload them, before any viewer request, and keeps CloudFront delivery fast. Option B (Lambda@Edge origin-response) only runs when CloudFront fetches an object from the S3 origin on a cache miss in response to a viewer request, so detection is deferred to serving time, executes on the critical latency path for every cache miss, and never acts at ingestion at all, which directly contradicts 'minimal latency between the ingestion and serving.' Therefore the S3-event-driven Lambda is the correct integration point.","explanation_zh":"需求是把腐損偵測的 Python 邏輯整合進來，並讓「攝入(ingestion)到提供服務(serving)」之間的延遲最小，亦即腐損影像應在寫入後立即被偵測，使其不會被送達使用者。S3 事件通知 (ObjectCreated) 會在物件被建立（攝入）的當下，以非同步方式立即觸發 Lambda 函式（通常數秒內送達），偵測邏輯在提供服務路徑之外執行。如此可在第三方工具上傳後、任何使用者請求之前就抓出並處理腐損影像，同時保持 CloudFront 傳遞快速。選項 B（Lambda@Edge origin-response）只有在 CloudFront 因快取未命中而向 S3 原始來源抓取物件時才執行，因此偵測被延後到服務時間、在每次快取未命中的關鍵延遲路徑上執行，且完全不會在攝入時觸發，這與「攝入到服務之間延遲最小」直接矛盾。因此由 S3 事件驅動的 Lambda 才是正確的整合點。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A viewer-response Lambda@Edge runs at the very last moment before returning the response to the viewer, on the serving critical path, and only on viewer requests. It does nothing at ingestion and adds latency to delivery; viewer-response events also cannot read or modify the body.","why_zh":"viewer-response 的 Lambda@Edge 在回應送回使用者前的最後一刻執行，位於服務關鍵路徑且僅於使用者請求時觸發。它在攝入時不做任何事且會增加傳遞延遲；viewer-response 事件也無法讀取或修改回應主體。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Origin-response Lambda@Edge only fires when CloudFront fetches from the S3 origin on a cache miss triggered by a viewer request. Detection is deferred to serving time, runs on the latency path for every miss, and never executes at ingestion, contradicting 'minimal latency between ingestion and serving.' This is the dump's suggested answer but it is technically wrong.","why_zh":"origin-response 的 Lambda@Edge 只有在使用者請求造成快取未命中、CloudFront 向 S3 原始來源抓取時才觸發。偵測被延後到服務時間、在每次未命中的延遲路徑上執行，且不會在攝入時執行，與「攝入到服務之間延遲最小」矛盾。這是題庫建議答案，但技術上是錯的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An S3 event notification to a Step Functions state machine would also act at ingestion, but Step Functions adds an unnecessary orchestration layer and operational overhead for a single, self-contained Python detection step. With one simple detection function, invoking Lambda directly is the more appropriate and lower-latency choice.","why_zh":"由 S3 事件通知觸發 Step Functions 狀態機同樣會在攝入時動作，但對單一、獨立的 Python 偵測步驟而言，Step Functions 增加了不必要的編排層與營運負擔。當只有一個簡單偵測函式時，直接觸發 Lambda 才是更恰當且延遲更低的選擇。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/EventNotifications.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/lambda-edge-event-request-response.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/lambda-event-structure.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":267,"question_en":"A company has an application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances in an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group. The company uses AWS CodePipeline to deploy the application. The instances that run in the Auto Scaling group are constantly changing because of scaling events. When the company deploys new application code versions, the company installs the AWS CodeDeploy agent on any new target EC2 instances and associates the instances with the CodeDeploy deployment group. The application is set to go live within the next 24 hours. What should a solutions architect recommend to automate the application deployment process with the LEAST amount of operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个在 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 组中的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行的应用程序。该公司使用 AWS CodePipeline 来部署应用程 序。Auto Scaling 组中运行的实例会因伸缩事件而不断变化。 当公司部署新的应用程序代码版本时，公司会在任何新的目标 EC2 实例上安装 AWS CodeDeploy 代理，并将这些实例与 CodeDeploy 部署组关联。该应用程序将在未来 24 小时内上线。 解决方案架构师应该建议什么来以最少的运营开销实现应用程序部署过程的自动化？","options_en":{"A":"Configure Amazon EventBridge to invoke an AWS Lambda function when a new EC2 instance is launched into the Auto Scaling group. Code the Lambda function to associate the EC2 instances with the CodeDeploy deployment group.","B":"Write a script to suspend Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling operations before the deployment of new code. When the deployment is complete, create a new AMI and configure the Auto Scaling group's launch template to use the new AMI for new launches. Resume Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling operations.","C":"Create a new AWS CodeBuild project that creates a new AMI that contains the new code. Configure CodeBuild to update the Auto Scaling group’s launch template to the new AMI. Run an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling instance refresh operation.","D":"Create a new AMI that has the CodeDeploy agent installed. Configure the Auto Scaling group’s launch template to use the new AMI. Associate the CodeDeploy deployment group with the Auto Scaling group instead of the EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 Amazon EventBridge 配置为在 Auto Scaling 组中启动新的 EC2 实例时调用 AWS Lambda 函数。对 Lambda 函数进行编码以将 EC2 实例与 CodeDeploy 部署组关联。","B":"编写一个脚本以在部署新代码之前暂停 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 操作。部署完成后，创建新的 AMI 并配置 Auto Scaling 组的启 动模板以使用新的 AMI 进行新启动。恢复 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 操作。","C":"创建一个新的 AWS CodeBuild 项目，该项目将创建一个包含新代码的新 AMI。配置 CodeBuild 以将 Auto Scaling 组的启动模板更 新为新的 AMI。运行 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 实例刷新操作。","D":"创建安装了 CodeDeploy 代理的新 AMI。配置 Auto Scaling 组的启动模板以使用新的 AMI。将 CodeDeploy 部署组与 Auto Scaling 组（而不是 EC2 实例）关联。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":95},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":268,"question_en":"A company has a website that runs on four Amazon EC2 instances that are behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). When the ALB detects that an EC2 instance is no longer available, an Amazon CloudWatch alarm enters the ALARM state. A member of the company's operations team then manually adds a new EC2 instance behind the ALB. A solutions architect needs to design a highly available solution that automatically handles the replacement of EC2 instances. The company needs to minimize downtime during the switch to the new solution. Which set of steps should the solutions architect take to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的网站在应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面的四个 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。当 ALB 检测到 EC2 实例不再可用时，Amazon CloudWatch 警报将进入 ALARM 状态。然后，公司运营团队的一名成员在 ALB 后面手动添加一个新的 EC2 实例。 解决方案架构师需要设计一个高度可用的解决方案，自动处理 EC2 实例的更换。该公司需要最大限度地减少改用新解决方案期间的 停机时间。 解决方案架构师应采取哪组步骤来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Delete the existing ALB. Create an Auto Scaling group that is configured to handle the web application tra®c. Attach a new launch template to the Auto Scaling group. Create a new ALB. Attach the Auto Scaling group to the new ALB. Attach the existing EC2 instances to the Auto Scaling group.","B":"Create an Auto Scaling group that is configured to handle the web application tra®c. Attach a new launch template to the Auto Scaling group. Attach the Auto Scaling group to the existing ALAttach the existing EC2 instances to the Auto Scaling group.","C":"Delete the existing ALB and the EC2 instances. Create an Auto Scaling group that is configured to handle the web application tra®c. Attach a new launch template to the Auto Scaling group. Create a new ALB. Attach the Auto Scaling group to the new ALB. Wait for the Auto Scaling group to launch the minimum number of EC2 instances.","D":"Create an Auto Scaling group that is configured to handle the web application tra®c. Attach a new launch template to the Auto Scaling group. Attach the Auto Scaling group to the existing ALB. Wait for the existing ALB to register the existing EC2 instances with the Auto Scaling group."},"options_zh":{"A":"删除现有的 ALB。创建一个配置为处理 Web 应用程序流量的 Auto Scaling 组。将新的启动模板附加到 Auto Scaling 组。创建一 个新的 ALB。将 Auto Scaling 组附加到新的 ALB。将现有 EC2 实例附加到 Auto Scaling 组。","B":"创建一个配置为处理 Web 应用程序流量的 Auto Scaling 组。将新的启动模板附加到 Auto Scaling 组。将 Auto Scaling 组附加到 现有 ALA 将现有 EC2 实例附加到 Auto Scaling 组。","C":"删除现有 ALB 和 EC2 实例。创建一个配置为处理 Web 应用程序流量的 Auto Scaling 组。将新的启动模板附加到 Auto Scaling 组。创建一个新的 ALB。将 Auto Scaling 组附加到新的 ALB。等待 Auto Scaling 组启动最小数量的 EC2 实例。","D":"创建一个配置为处理 Web 应用程序流量的 Auto Scaling 组。将新的启动模板附加到 Auto Scaling 组。将 Auto Scaling 组附加到现 有 ALB。等待现有 ALB 将现有 EC2 实例注册到 Auto Scaling 组。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":91},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is a highly available solution that auto-replaces EC2 instances while minimizing downtime during the cutover. Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling lets you attach an existing load balancer (its target group) to an Auto Scaling group either at creation or afterward, so the ALB does not need to be deleted/recreated and the endpoint stays the same. EC2 Auto Scaling also supports attaching existing running instances to a group (the instance must be running, its AMI must still exist, not already in another ASG, in a defined AZ, and same VPC); once attached to an ASG that has a load balancer, the instances are automatically registered with that load balancer. Option B performs exactly this no-disruption path: create the ASG with a launch template, attach it to the existing ALB, and attach the four existing instances - giving automatic replacement going forward with essentially zero downtime. Options A and C delete and recreate the ALB (and C also deletes the instances), causing downtime; D describes a non-existent mechanism (the ALB does not 'register existing EC2 instances with the Auto Scaling group' - the ASG registers instances with the ALB, and standalone instances must be explicitly attached to the ASG).","explanation_zh":"需求是建立高可用方案，自動替換 EC2 執行個體，並在切換時將停機時間降到最低。Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 允許在建立 Auto Scaling group 時或建立後，將既有的 load balancer（其 target group）附加到 Auto Scaling group，因此不需要刪除/重建 ALB，端點維持不變。EC2 Auto Scaling 也支援將既有正在執行的執行個體附加到群組（執行個體須為 running 狀態、其 AMI 仍存在、不屬於其他 ASG、位於已定義的 AZ、且同一 VPC）；一旦附加到帶有 load balancer 的 ASG，這些執行個體會自動註冊到該 load balancer。選項 B 正是這條無中斷路徑：使用 launch template 建立 ASG、附加到既有 ALB、再附加四台既有執行個體，往後即可自動替換且幾乎零停機。選項 A 與 C 刪除並重建 ALB（C 還刪除執行個體），會造成停機；D 描述了不存在的機制（ALB 不會『把既有 EC2 執行個體註冊到 Auto Scaling group』 - 是 ASG 把執行個體註冊到 ALB，而獨立執行個體必須明確附加到 ASG）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Deleting the existing ALB and creating a new one is unnecessary and causes downtime plus endpoint/DNS changes; you can attach the existing ALB's target group to a new ASG directly.","why_zh":"刪除既有 ALB 再建立新的並無必要，會造成停機與端點/DNS 變更；可直接將既有 ALB 的 target group 附加到新的 ASG。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it deletes both the ALB and all EC2 instances, then waits for new ones to launch - the maximum-downtime option, directly contradicting 'minimize downtime.'","why_zh":"這是 dump 建議答案，但它同時刪除 ALB 與所有 EC2 執行個體，再等待新執行個體啟動，是停機時間最長的選項，直接違反『最小化停機時間』。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Describes a non-existent mechanism: an ALB does not register existing standalone instances into an Auto Scaling group. The ASG registers its instances with the ALB; existing instances must be explicitly attached to the ASG, so waiting on the ALB to do it would never bring the four instances under management.","why_zh":"描述了不存在的機制：ALB 不會把既有獨立執行個體註冊進 Auto Scaling group。是 ASG 把其執行個體註冊到 ALB；既有執行個體必須明確附加到 ASG，等待 ALB 去做永遠不會讓那四台執行個體納入管理。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/attach-load-balancer-asg.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-auto-scaling-detach-attach-instances.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/autoscaling-load-balancer.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":269,"question_en":"A company wants to optimize AWS data-transfer costs and compute costs across developer accounts within the company's organization in AWS Organizations. Developers can configure VPCs and launch Amazon EC2 instances in a single AWS Region. The EC2 instances retrieve approximately 1 TB of data each day from Amazon S3. The developer activity leads to excessive monthly data-transfer charges and NAT gateway processing charges between EC2 instances and S3 buckets, along with high compute costs. The company wants to proactively enforce approved architectural patterns for any EC2 instance and VPC infrastructure that developers deploy within the AWS accounts. The company does not want this enforcement to negatively affect the speed at which the developers can perform their tasks. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司希望优化 AWS Organizations 中该公司组织内开发人员账户之间的 AWS 数据传输成本和计算成本。开发人员可以在单个 AWS 区域中配置 VPC 并启动 Amazon EC2 实例。EC2 实例每天从 Amazon S3 检索大约 1 TB 的数据。 开发人员的活动导致 EC2 实例和 S3 存储桶之间每月产生过高的数据传输费用和 NAT 网关处理费用，以及高昂的计算成本。该公司 希望为开发人员在 AWS 账户中部署的任何 EC2 实例和 VPC 基础设施主动实施经批准的架构模式。该公司不希望这种强制执行对开 发人员执行任务的速度产生负面影响。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create SCPs to prevent developers from launching unapproved EC2 instance types. Provide the developers with an AWS CloudFormation template to deploy an approved VPC configuration with S3 interface endpoints. Scope the developers' IAM permissions so that the developers can launch VPC resources only with CloudFormation.","B":"Create a daily forecasted budget with AWS Budgets to monitor EC2 compute costs and S3 data-transfer costs across the developer accounts. When the forecasted cost is 75% of the actual budget cost, send an alert to the developer teams. If the actual budget cost is 100%, create a budget action to terminate the developers' EC2 instances and VPC infrastructure.","C":"Create an AWS Service Catalog portfolio that users can use to create an approved VPC configuration with S3 gateway endpoints and approved EC2 instances. Share the portfolio with the developer accounts. Configure an AWS Service Catalog launch constraint to use an approved IAM role. Scope the developers' IAM permissions to allow access only to AWS Service Catalog.","D":"Create and deploy AWS Config rules to monitor the compliance of EC2 and VPC resources in the developer AWS accounts. If developers launch unapproved EC2 instances or if developers create VPCs without S3 gateway endpoints, perform a remediation action to terminate the unapproved resources."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 SCP 以防止开发人员启动未经批准的 EC2 实例类型。为开发人员提供 AWS CloudFormation 模板，以使用 S3 接口终端节点 部署经过批准的 VPC 配置。限制开发人员的 IAM 权限范围，以便开发人员只能使用 CloudFormation 启动 VPC 资源。","B":"使用 AWS Budgets 创建每日预测预算，以监控跨开发人员帐户的 EC2 计算成本和 S3 数据传输成本。当预测成本为实际预算成 本的75%时，向开发团队发送警报。如果实际预算成本为 100%，则创建预算操作以终止开发人员的 EC2 实例和 VPC 基础设施。","C":"创建一个 AWS Service Catalog 组合，用户可以使用该组合来创建具有 S3 网关终端节点和批准的 EC2 实例的批准的 VPC 配置。 与开发者帐户共享产品组合。配置 AWS Service Catalog 启动约束以使用已批准的 IAM 角色。将开发人员的 IAM 权限范围限制为 仅允许访问 AWS Service Catalog。","D":"创建并部署 AWS Config 规则以监控开发人员 AWS 账户中 EC2 和 VPC 资源的合规性。如果开发人员启动未经批准的 EC2 实例， 或者开发人员创建没有 S3 网关端点的 VPC，请执行修复操作以终止未经批准的资源。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":270,"question_en":"A company is expanding. The company plans to separate its resources into hundreds of different AWS accounts in multiple AWS Regions. A solutions architect must recommend a solution that denies access to any operations outside of specifically designated Regions. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在扩张。该公司计划将其资源划分到多个 AWS 区域的数百个不同的 AWS 账户中。解决方案架构师必须推荐一种拒绝访 问特定指定区域之外的任何操作的解决方案。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create IAM roles for each account. Create IAM policies with conditional allow permissions that include only approved Regions for the accounts.","B":"Create an organization in AWS Organizations. Create IAM users for each account. Attach a policy to each user to block access to Regions where an account cannot deploy infrastructure.","C":"Launch an AWS Control Tower landing zone. Create OUs and attach SCPs that deny access to run services outside of the approved Regions.","D":"Enable AWS Security Hub in each account. Create controls to specify the Regions where an account can deploy infrastructure."},"options_zh":{"A":"为每个账户创建 IAM 角色。创建具有条件允许权限的 IAM 策略，其中仅包含账户的批准区域。","B":"在 AWS Organizations 中创建组织。为每个账户创建 IAM 用户。为每个用户附加一个策略，以阻止访问帐户无法部署基础设施 的区域。","C":"启动 AWS Control Tower 登陆区。创建 OU 并附加 SCP，拒绝访问批准区域之外的运行服务。","D":"在每个账户中启用 AWS Security Hub。创建控件以指定帐户可以部署基础设施的区域。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to deny access to any operations outside specifically designated Regions across hundreds of accounts in an organization. Only a Service Control Policy (SCP) can enforce a preventive deny boundary across many accounts, because SCPs set the maximum available permissions for all IAM users and roles in member accounts. AWS Control Tower provides the purpose-built, managed implementation of this: the OU Region deny control (CT.MULTISERVICE.PV.1), which is a preventive SCP that 'disallows access to unlisted operations in global and regional AWS services, outside of the specified Regions for an organizational unit (OU)' using the aws:RequestedRegion condition key. Launching a Control Tower landing zone, creating OUs, and attaching Region-deny SCPs (option C) is exactly this best-practice pattern and scales cleanly to hundreds of accounts. Option B fails because attaching policies to IAM users does not create an enforceable organization-wide deny: IAM user/identity policies only constrain those users, are bypassable by account admins and do not affect the root user, and SCPs (not user policies) are the mechanism to 'block' Regions across accounts.","explanation_zh":"需求是在組織中數百個帳戶內拒絕對指定 Region 以外任何操作的存取。只有 Service Control Policy (SCP) 能在眾多帳戶間強制執行預防性的 deny 邊界，因為 SCP 為成員帳戶中所有 IAM 使用者與角色設定可用權限的上限。AWS Control Tower 提供了專為此情境打造的受管實作：OU Region deny control (CT.MULTISERVICE.PV.1)，它是一個預防性 SCP，使用 aws:RequestedRegion 條件鍵『拒絕對組織單位 (OU) 指定 Region 以外的全域與區域 AWS 服務之未列出操作的存取』。啟動 Control Tower landing zone、建立 OU 並附加 Region-deny SCP（選項 C）正是此最佳實務模式，並能乾淨地擴展到數百個帳戶。選項 B 錯誤，因為將政策附加到 IAM 使用者無法建立可強制執行的組織範圍 deny：IAM 使用者／身分政策僅約束這些使用者，可被帳戶管理員繞過且不影響 root 使用者，跨帳戶『封鎖』Region 的機制是 SCP 而非使用者政策。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Conditional allow IAM policies attached per account/role do not form a deny boundary; they only grant scoped access and can be overridden or supplemented by other identity policies, and they do not scale to centrally enforce Region restrictions across hundreds of accounts. They cannot deny operations the way the requirement demands.","why_zh":"逐帳戶／角色附加的條件式 allow IAM 政策不構成 deny 邊界；它們僅授予範圍化存取，可被其他身分政策覆寫或補充，也無法集中地擴展至數百個帳戶強制執行 Region 限制，無法如需求所要求般拒絕操作。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Although it creates an Organization, it relies on attaching policies to IAM users to 'block' Regions. IAM user/identity-based policies do not enforce an organization-wide guardrail, are bypassable by account admins, do not affect the root user, and do not scale to hundreds of accounts. The blocking mechanism for Region denial must be an SCP, not a per-user policy.","why_zh":"雖然建立了 Organization，卻依賴將政策附加到 IAM 使用者來『封鎖』Region。IAM 使用者／身分型政策無法強制執行組織範圍的防護欄，可被帳戶管理員繞過，不影響 root 使用者，且無法擴展至數百個帳戶。Region 拒絕的封鎖機制必須是 SCP，而非個別使用者政策。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Security Hub is a detective/security-posture aggregation service. It can detect and report on configurations but cannot preventively deny or block API operations in unapproved Regions. It does not meet the 'deny access to any operations' requirement.","why_zh":"AWS Security Hub 是偵測型／安全態勢彙整服務。它能偵測並回報組態，但無法預防性地拒絕或封鎖未核准 Region 中的 API 操作，無法滿足『拒絕任何操作存取』的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/ou-region-deny.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/what-is-control-tower.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":271,"question_en":"A company wants to refactor its retail ordering web application that currently has a load-balanced Amazon EC2 instance ­eet for web hosting, database API services, and business logic. The company needs to create a decoupled, scalable architecture with a mechanism for retaining failed orders while also minimizing operational costs. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望重构其零售订购 Web 应用程序，该应用程序当前拥有用于 Web 托管、数据库 API 服务和业务逻辑的负载平衡 Amazon EC2 实例队列。该公司需要创建一个解耦、可扩展的架构，并具有保留失败订单的机制，同时最大限度地降低运营成本。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon S3 for web hosting with Amazon API Gateway for database API services. Use Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) for order queuing. Use Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) for business logic with Amazon SQS long polling for retaining failed orders.","B":"Use AWS Elastic Beanstalk for web hosting with Amazon API Gateway for database API services. Use Amazon MQ for order queuing. Use AWS Step Functions for business logic with Amazon S3 Glacier Deep Archive for retaining failed orders.","C":"Use Amazon S3 for web hosting with AWS AppSync for database API services. Use Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) for order queuing. Use AWS Lambda for business logic with an Amazon SQS dead-letter queue for retaining failed orders.","D":"Use Amazon Lightsail for web hosting with AWS AppSync for database API services. Use Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) for order queuing. Use Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) for business logic with Amazon OpenSearch Service for retaining failed orders."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon S3 进行 Web 托管，并使用 Amazon API Gateway 进行数据库 API 服务。使用 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 进行订单排队。使用 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 实现业务逻辑，并通过 Amazon SQS 长轮询保留失败的订 单。","B":"使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 进行 Web 托管，并使用 Amazon API Gateway 进行数据库 API 服务。使用 Amazon MQ 进行订单排 队。使用 AWS Step Functions 实现业务逻辑，并使用 Amazon S3 Glacier Deep Archive 来保留失败的订单。","C":"使用 Amazon S3 进行 Web 托管，并使用 AWS AppSync 进行数据库 API 服务。使用 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 进 行订单排队。使用 AWS Lambda 实现业务逻辑，并使用 Amazon SQS 死信队列来保留失败的订单。","D":"使用 Amazon Lightsail 进行 Web 托管，并使用 AWS AppSync 进行数据库 API 服务。使用 Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) 进行订单排队。使用 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 实现业务逻辑，并使用 Amazon OpenSearch Service 保留 失败的订单。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":84,"A":16},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is a decoupled, scalable architecture with a mechanism for RETAINING FAILED ORDERS while minimizing operational cost. Option C does this correctly: Amazon S3 hosts the static web tier (fully managed, lowest cost), AWS AppSync provides managed GraphQL database API services, Amazon SQS decouples order intake, and AWS Lambda runs business logic serverlessly (no servers to manage = least operational cost). Critically, it uses an Amazon SQS dead-letter queue (DLQ) to retain failed orders. Per AWS docs, a DLQ is the purpose-built feature for 'messages that are not processed successfully,' isolating unconsumed/poison messages via a redrive policy and maxReceiveCount. Option A is nearly identical but fatally states 'Amazon SQS long polling for retaining failed orders' - long polling is only a message-receiving/cost-optimization technique (reduces empty ReceiveMessage responses); it does NOT retain or capture failed messages, so A fails the core requirement. That single phrase is the decisive differentiator between A and C.","explanation_zh":"需求是建立解耦、可擴展的架構，並具備「保留失敗訂單」的機制，同時將營運成本降到最低。選項 C 正確達成此目標：Amazon S3 託管靜態 Web 層（全託管、成本最低），AWS AppSync 提供託管的 GraphQL database API 服務，Amazon SQS 解耦訂單接收，AWS Lambda 以無伺服器方式執行 business logic（無需管理伺服器＝營運成本最低）。關鍵在於它使用 Amazon SQS dead-letter queue (DLQ) 來保留失敗訂單。根據 AWS 文件，DLQ 正是為「未成功處理的訊息」設計的功能，透過 redrive policy 與 maxReceiveCount 隔離無法消費的（poison）訊息。選項 A 幾乎相同，但致命地寫成「Amazon SQS long polling 用於保留失敗訂單」——long polling 僅是接收訊息／成本最佳化的技術（減少空的 ReceiveMessage 回應），並不會保留或捕捉失敗訊息，因此 A 無法滿足核心需求。這一句正是 A 與 C 之間的決定性差異。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses 'SQS long polling for retaining failed orders' - long polling only reduces empty ReceiveMessage responses to lower cost; it does not capture or retain failed messages. The correct mechanism for retaining failed orders is a dead-letter queue, so A fails the core requirement despite otherwise sound S3/API Gateway/SQS/ECS choices. ECS is also slightly more operational overhead than Lambda for pure business logic.","why_zh":"使用「SQS long polling 來保留失敗訂單」——long polling 僅減少空的 ReceiveMessage 回應以降低成本，並不會捕捉或保留失敗訊息。保留失敗訂單的正確機制是 dead-letter queue，因此 A 無法滿足核心需求。此外 ECS 用於純 business logic 的營運負擔也略高於 Lambda。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Elastic Beanstalk for web hosting reintroduces managed EC2 (more operational overhead and cost than S3 static hosting). Amazon MQ is a managed broker requiring instance provisioning/sizing (higher cost than SQS). S3 Glacier Deep Archive is cold archival storage with hours-long retrieval - wholly unsuited as a near-term retry/inspection store for failed orders.","why_zh":"Elastic Beanstalk 託管 Web 又重新引入受管 EC2（營運負擔與成本均高於 S3 靜態託管）。Amazon MQ 是需佈建/調整實例的受管 broker（成本高於 SQS）。S3 Glacier Deep Archive 屬冷封存儲存、取回需數小時，完全不適合作為失敗訂單的近期重試/檢視儲存。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Lightsail is VM-based hosting (more operational overhead than S3). Amazon SES is an email service, not a message queue, so it cannot serve as order queuing. EKS adds significant cluster operational overhead versus Lambda. OpenSearch is a search/analytics engine, not a failed-order retention/redrive mechanism.","why_zh":"Amazon Lightsail 是以 VM 為基礎的託管（營運負擔高於 S3）。Amazon SES 是電子郵件服務而非訊息佇列，無法作為訂單佇列。EKS 相較 Lambda 增加大量叢集營運負擔。OpenSearch 是搜尋／分析引擎，並非保留失敗訂單或 redrive 的機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-dead-letter-queues.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-short-and-long-polling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/appsync/latest/devguide/designing-a-graphql-api.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/WebsiteHosting.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":272,"question_en":"A company hosts a web application on AWS in the us-east-1 Region. The application servers are distributed across three Availability Zones behind an Application Load Balancer. The database is hosted in a MySQL database on an Amazon EC2 instance. A solutions architect needs to design a cross-Region data recovery solution using AWS services with an RTO of less than 5 minutes and an RPO of less than 1 minute. The solutions architect is deploying application servers in us-west-2, and has configured Amazon Route 53 health checks and DNS failover to us- west-2. Which additional step should the solutions architect take?","question_zh":"一家公司在 us-east-1 区域的 AWS 上托管 Web 应用程序。应用程序服务器分布在应用程序负载均衡器后面的三个可用区中。该数据 库托管在 Amazon EC2 实例上的 MySQL 数据库中。解决方案架构师需要使用 AWS 服务设计跨区域数据恢复解决方案，RTO 小于 5 分 钟，RPO 小于 1 分钟。解决方案架构师正在 us-west-2 中部署应用程序服务器，并已配置 Amazon Route 53 运行状况检查和 DNS 故障 转移到 us-west-2。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪些额外步骤？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate the database to an Amazon RDS for MySQL instance with a cross-Region read replica in us-west-2.","B":"Migrate the database to an Amazon Aurora global database with the primary in us-east-1 and the secondary in us-west-2.","C":"Migrate the database to an Amazon RDS for MySQL instance with a Multi-AZ deployment.","D":"Create a MySQL standby database on an Amazon EC2 instance in us-west-2."},"options_zh":{"A":"将数据库迁移到 us-west-2 中具有跨区域只读副本的 Amazon RDS for MySQL 实例。","B":"将数据库迁移到 Amazon Aurora 全局数据库，其中主数据库位于 us-east-1，辅助数据库位于 us-west-2。","C":"将数据库迁移到具有多可用区部署的 Amazon RDS for MySQL 实例。","D":"在 us-west-2 中的 Amazon EC2 实例上创建 MySQL 备用数据库。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":94},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirements are cross-Region DR (us-east-1 to us-west-2) with RTO < 5 minutes and RPO < 1 minute, using AWS services. Amazon Aurora Global Database is purpose-built for exactly this: AWS documentation states replication latency is 'typically under a second,' RPO is 'typically measured in seconds,' and RTO 'can be in the order of minutes.' Replication uses dedicated storage-layer infrastructure (not the database engine), so the secondary in us-west-2 stays within sub-second lag and can be promoted quickly via cross-Region failover, satisfying both the <1 min RPO and <5 min RTO. With Route 53 health checks and DNS failover already configured, migrating the EC2 MySQL database to an Aurora global database (primary in us-east-1, secondary in us-west-2) is the additional step that completes the design.","explanation_zh":"需求為跨區域災難復原（us-east-1 到 us-west-2），RTO < 5 分鐘且 RPO < 1 分鐘，並使用 AWS 服務。Amazon Aurora Global Database 正是為此設計：AWS 文件指出複寫延遲『通常低於一秒』、RPO『通常以秒計算』、RTO『可在數分鐘等級』。其複寫使用專屬的儲存層基礎設施（而非資料庫引擎），因此 us-west-2 的次要叢集維持次秒級延遲，並可透過跨區域 failover 快速升級為主要叢集，同時滿足 <1 分鐘 RPO 與 <5 分鐘 RTO。由於 Route 53 健康檢查與 DNS failover 已設定完成，將 EC2 上的 MySQL 資料庫遷移至 Aurora global database（主要在 us-east-1、次要在 us-west-2）即為完成此架構所需的額外步驟。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"RDS for MySQL cross-Region read replicas use engine-based asynchronous binlog replication, whose lag is variable and frequently exceeds 60 seconds under write load, so RPO < 1 minute cannot be reliably guaranteed. AWS positions Aurora Global Database (storage-layer replication) precisely because standard RDS cross-Region replicas cannot meet such tight RPO/RTO targets.","why_zh":"RDS for MySQL 跨區域唯讀複本使用引擎層的非同步 binlog 複寫，延遲不穩定且在寫入負載下常超過 60 秒，無法可靠保證 RPO < 1 分鐘。AWS 之所以推出 Aurora Global Database（儲存層複寫），正是因為標準 RDS 跨區域複本無法達到如此嚴格的 RPO/RTO 目標。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Multi-AZ is single-Region high availability only; it replicates within Availability Zones in one Region and provides no cross-Region disaster recovery, which is the explicit requirement here.","why_zh":"Multi-AZ 僅提供單一區域內的高可用性，只在同一區域的可用區之間複寫，完全無法提供本題明確要求的跨區域災難復原。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it is a fully self-managed MySQL standby on EC2: no managed automated cross-Region failover, manual promotion, and high operational overhead, making a reliable < 5 min RTO impractical. The question asks for an AWS-services DR design, and AWS best practice for these tight objectives is Aurora Global Database, not a hand-rolled EC2 standby.","why_zh":"這是題庫建議答案，但它是在 EC2 上完全自管的 MySQL 待命資料庫：沒有受管的自動跨區域 failover、需手動升級、營運負擔高，難以可靠達成 < 5 分鐘 RTO。題目要求以 AWS 服務設計災難復原，而 AWS 對此類嚴格目標的最佳實務是 Aurora Global Database，而非自行搭建的 EC2 待命資料庫。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database-disaster-recovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_ReadRepl.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":273,"question_en":"A company is using AWS Organizations to manage multiple accounts. Due to regulatory requirements, the company wants to restrict specific member accounts to certain AWS Regions, where they are permitted to deploy resources. The resources in the accounts must be tagged, enforced based on a group standard, and centrally managed with minimal configuration. What should a solutions architect do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS Organizations 来管理多个账户。由于监管要求，该公司希望将特定成员账户限制在某些允许部署资源的 AWS 区域。帐户中的资源必须被标记、基于组标准强制实施，并以最少的配置进行集中管理。 解决方案架构师应该怎样做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Config rule in the specific member accounts to limit Regions and apply a tag policy.","B":"From the AWS Billing and Cost Management console, in the management account, disable Regions for the specific member accounts and apply a tag policy on the root.","C":"Associate the specific member accounts with the root. Apply a tag policy and an SCP using conditions to limit Regions.","D":"Associate the specific member accounts with a new OU. Apply a tag policy and an SCP using conditions to limit Regions."},"options_zh":{"A":"在特定成员账户中创建 AWS Config 规则以限制区域并应用标签策略。","B":"在 AWS Billing and Cost Management 控制台的管理账户中，禁用特定成员账户的区域并在根账户上应用标签策略。","C":"将特定成员帐户与 root 关联。使用条件来应用标签策略和 SCP 来限制区域。","D":"将特定成员帐户与新 OU 关联。使用条件来应用标签策略和 SCP 来限制区域。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirements are: restrict specific member accounts to certain Regions, enforce a group-standard tagging policy, and manage centrally with minimal configuration. AWS Organizations provides exactly two native tools for this: a Service Control Policy (SCP) with a condition (aws:RequestedRegion in a Deny statement) to limit which Regions principals can act in, and a tag policy to enforce the tagging standard. To target only SPECIFIC member accounts, you group those accounts into a dedicated organizational unit (OU) and attach both policies to that OU, so inheritance applies only to those accounts. AWS explicitly recommends NOT attaching SCPs to the organization root and instead creating an OU and moving accounts into it, which is precisely what option D does. Option C attaches to the root, which would affect every account in the organization (not just the specific ones) and is contrary to AWS guidance.","explanation_zh":"需求為：將特定成員帳戶限制在某些 Region、依群組標準強制執行標籤政策,並以最少設定集中管理。AWS Organizations 為此提供兩項原生工具:使用 SCP(在 Deny 陳述式中搭配 aws:RequestedRegion 條件)限制可操作的 Region,以及使用 tag policy 強制標籤標準。若只想針對「特定」成員帳戶,應將這些帳戶歸入一個專屬的 organizational unit(OU),並將兩項政策附加到該 OU,讓繼承只套用到這些帳戶。AWS 明確建議「不要」把 SCP 附加到組織 root,而應建立 OU 並把帳戶移入,這正是選項 D 的做法。選項 C 附加到 root 會影響組織內所有帳戶(而非僅特定帳戶),違反 AWS 指引。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Config rules are detective/reactive (they evaluate resources after the fact) and cannot proactively restrict which Regions an account may deploy into; only an SCP can prevent actions in non-permitted Regions. Config rules are also configured per-account, which is the opposite of centrally managed with minimal configuration. This is the dump's suggested answer and it is technically wrong.","why_zh":"AWS Config 規則屬於偵測/事後反應性質(對既有資源做評估),無法主動限制帳戶可在哪些 Region 部署;只有 SCP 能阻止在不允許 Region 的操作。Config 規則也是逐帳戶設定,與「集中管理、最少設定」相反。這是 dump 的建議答案,但技術上錯誤。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Region 'enable/disable' in Billing only applies to a small set of opt-in Regions (e.g. certain newer Regions) and cannot disable the default-enabled Regions; it is also not a granular regulatory deployment guardrail. It does not enforce a tagging standard the way a tag policy plus SCP combination does for the specific accounts.","why_zh":"Billing 中的 Region 啟用/停用僅適用於少數需選擇加入(opt-in)的 Region,無法停用預設啟用的 Region,也不是細緻的法規部署護欄。它無法像 tag policy 加 SCP 組合那樣對特定帳戶強制標籤標準。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Attaching the tag policy and SCP at the root applies them to EVERY account in the organization, not just the specific member accounts required, and AWS explicitly advises against attaching SCPs to the root without isolating accounts in an OU first. This violates the 'specific member accounts' requirement.","why_zh":"在 root 附加 tag policy 與 SCP 會套用到組織中所有帳戶,而非僅需要的特定成員帳戶,且 AWS 明確建議不要在未先用 OU 隔離帳戶前把 SCP 附加到 root。這違反「特定成員帳戶」的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_ous.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":274,"question_en":"A company has an application that generates reports and stores them in an Amazon S3 bucket. When a user accesses their report, the application generates a signed URL to allow the user to download the report. The company's security team has discovered that the files are public and that anyone can download them without authentication. The company has suspended the generation of new reports until the problem is resolved. Which set of actions will immediately remediate the security issue without impacting the application's normal work­ow?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个应用程序，可以生成报告并将其存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。当用户访问其报告时，应用程序会生成一个签名 URL 以允许用户下载报告。该公司的安全团队发现这些文件是公开的，任何人都可以在未经身份验证的情况下下载它们。该公司已暂停 生成新报告，直到问题得到解决。 哪组操作将立即修复安全问题而不影响应用程序的正常工作流程？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function that applies a deny all policy for users who are not authenticated. Create a scheduled event to invoke the Lambda function.","B":"Review the AWS Trusted Advisor bucket permissions check and implement the recommended actions.","C":"Run a script that puts a private ACL on all of the objects in the bucket.","D":"Use the Block Public Access feature in Amazon S3 to set the IgnorePublicAcIs option to TRUE on the bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，为未经身份验证的用户应用拒绝所有策略。创建计划事件以调用 Lambda 函数。","B":"查看 AWS Trusted Advisor 存储桶权限检查并实施建议的操作。","C":"运行一个脚本，将私有 ACL 应用于存储桶中的所有对象。","D":"使用 Amazon S3 中的阻止公共访问功能将存储桶上的 IgnorePublicAcIs 选项设置为 TRUE。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":85,"C":15},"tags":["Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The reports are public because of public ACLs on the objects, while the application's normal workflow uses presigned (signed) URLs. Setting the S3 Block Public Access option IgnorePublicAcls to TRUE causes Amazon S3 to ignore all public ACLs on the bucket and any objects it contains, so anonymous downloads stop immediately. Presigned URLs are unaffected because they are authorized by the IAM credentials of the principal that generated them, not by object ACLs, so the application keeps working. This is a single account/bucket-level configuration change that takes effect immediately and is the cleanest fix. IgnorePublicAcls is the specific BPA flag that neutralizes existing public ACLs (BlockPublicAcls only blocks setting new public ACLs and does not affect existing ones).","explanation_zh":"報告之所以公開，是因為物件上存在公開的 ACL，而應用程式的正常流程是使用 presigned（簽章）URL。將 S3 Block Public Access 的 IgnorePublicAcls 設為 TRUE，會讓 Amazon S3 忽略該 bucket 及其所含所有物件上的公開 ACL，因此匿名下載會立即停止。presigned URL 不受影響，因為它是以產生 URL 的 IAM 主體憑證進行授權，而非依賴物件 ACL，所以應用程式仍可正常運作。這是單一帳戶／bucket 層級的設定變更，會立即生效，是最乾淨的補救方式。IgnorePublicAcls 正是用來使既有公開 ACL 失效的 BPA 旗標（BlockPublicAcls 只會阻擋新設定的公開 ACL，不會影響既有 ACL）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A Lambda 'deny all' policy invoked on a schedule is not how anonymous S3 object access is controlled, is not immediate, and would not reliably block public ACL-based access. It is an invented, non-functional remediation.","why_zh":"以排程觸發 Lambda 套用『拒絕全部』政策並非控制 S3 匿名物件存取的方式，既非立即生效，也無法可靠阻擋基於公開 ACL 的存取，屬於虛構且無效的補救方法。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Trusted Advisor's bucket permissions check only detects and reports public buckets; it does not itself remediate. Reviewing recommendations is not an immediate, decisive fix and adds manual steps.","why_zh":"AWS Trusted Advisor 的 bucket 權限檢查僅能偵測並回報公開 bucket，本身不會進行補救。檢視建議並非立即且決定性的修復，且需手動步驟。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Scripting a private ACL on every object can work but is not immediate (must iterate all objects, error-prone at scale) and does not prevent new objects from getting public ACLs. Block Public Access (D) is the cleaner, instantaneous account/bucket-level guardrail.","why_zh":"以腳本對每個物件套用私有 ACL 雖可行，但並非立即生效（需逐一處理所有物件、大規模時易出錯），也無法防止新物件再次被設為公開 ACL。Block Public Access（D）是更乾淨且即時的帳戶／bucket 層級防護。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/API/API_control_PublicAccessBlockConfiguration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/access-control-block-public-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/using-presigned-url.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":275,"question_en":"A company is planning to migrate an Amazon RDS for Oracle database to an RDS for PostgreSQL DB instance in another AWS account. A solutions architect needs to design a migration strategy that will require no downtime and that will minimize the amount of time necessary to complete the migration. The migration strategy must replicate all existing data and any new data that is created during the migration. The target database must be identical to the source database at completion of the migration process. All applications currently use an Amazon Route 53 CNAME record as their endpoint for communication with the RDS for Oracle DB instance. The RDS for Oracle DB instance is in a private subnet. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司计划将 Amazon RDS for Oracle 数据库迁移到另一个 AWS 账户中的 RDS for PostgreSQL 数据库实例。解决方案架构师需要设 计一种无需停机并最大限度地减少完成迁移所需时间的迁移策略。迁移策略必须复制所有现有数据以及迁移期间创建的任何新数 据。迁移过程完成时，目标数据库必须与源数据库相同。 目前，所有应用程序都使用 Amazon Route 53 CNAME 记录作为与 RDS for Oracle 数据库实例进行通信的终端节点。RDS for Oracle 数据 库实例位于私有子网中。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a new RDS for PostgreSQL DB instance in the target account. Use the AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) to migrate the database schema from the source database to the target database.","B":"Use the AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) to create a new RDS for PostgreSQL DB instance in the target account with the schema and initial data from the source database.","C":"Configure VPC peering between the VPCs in the two AWS accounts to provide connectivity to both DB instances from the target account. Configure the security groups that are attached to each DB instance to allow tra®c on the database port from the VPC in the target account.","D":"Temporarily allow the source DB instance to be publicly accessible to provide connectivity from the VPC in the target account. Configure the security groups that are attached to each DB instance to allow tra®c on the database port from the VPC in the target account.","E":"Use AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) in the target account to perform a full load plus change data capture (CDC) migration from the source database to the target database. When the migration is complete, change the CNAME record to point to the target DB instance endpoint.","F":"Use AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) in the target account to perform a change data capture (CDC) migration from the source database to the target database. When the migration is complete, change the CNAME record to point to the target DB instance endpoint."},"options_zh":{"A":"在目标账户中创建新的 RDS for PostgreSQL 数据库实例。使用 AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) 将数据库架构从源数据库 迁移到目标数据库。","B":"使用 AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) 在目标账户中使用源数据库中的架构和初始数据创建新的 RDS for PostgreSQL 数据 库实例。","C":"在两个 AWS 账户中的 VPC 之间配置 VPC 对等互连，以提供从目标账户到两个数据库实例的连接。配置附加到每个数据库实例 的安全组，以允许来自目标账户中的 VPC 的数据库端口上的流量。","D":"暂时允许源数据库实例可公开访问，以提供来自目标账户中的 VPC 的连接。配置附加到每个数据库实例的安全组，以允许来 自目标账户中的 VPC 的数据库端口上的流量。","E":"在目标账户中使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 执行从源数据库到目标数据库的完整加载加更改数据捕获 (CDC) 迁移。迁移完成后，更改 CNAME 记录以指向目标数据库实例终端节点。","F":"在目标账户中使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 执行从源数据库到目标数据库的变更数据捕获 (CDC) 迁移。迁移 完成后，更改 CNAME 记录以指向目标数据库实例终端节点。"},"answer":["C","E","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ACE":96},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"This is a heterogeneous, cross-account migration (RDS for Oracle to RDS for PostgreSQL) requiring no downtime, minimal migration time, replication of all existing AND new data, and an identical target. The canonical AWS pattern is: AWS SCT converts the schema to the target engine, and AWS DMS migrates the data. (A) is correct: you create the new RDS for PostgreSQL instance and use AWS SCT to convert/migrate the schema. AWS SCT only converts schema/code; it does NOT provision RDS instances and does NOT load table data, which is why B is wrong on both counts. (C) is correct: the source Oracle DB is in a private subnet, so VPC peering between the two accounts' VPCs (plus security groups allowing the DB port) is the secure way to give the target-account DMS connectivity to both instances. (E) is correct: a DMS full load plus CDC task loads all existing data and continuously applies new changes during the migration, keeping source and target in sync; cutover is done by repointing the Route 53 CNAME, achieving no downtime. (F) is wrong because CDC-only replication starts from a change point and does NOT copy the pre-existing data, so the target would not contain all existing data and would not be identical. The dump answer C,E,F is internally inconsistent (both E and F change the CNAME) and fails the 'replicate all existing data' requirement; the community answer A,C,E is technically correct.","explanation_zh":"這是一個異質、跨帳號的資料庫遷移（RDS for Oracle 遷移到 RDS for PostgreSQL），要求零停機、最短遷移時間、複製所有既有資料與遷移期間的新資料，且目標需與來源完全相同。AWS 的標準模式是：AWS SCT 轉換 schema 到目標引擎，AWS DMS 負責遷移資料。(A) 正確：你需建立新的 RDS for PostgreSQL 執行個體，並用 AWS SCT 轉換/遷移 schema。AWS SCT 只轉換 schema 與程式碼，它不會佈建 RDS 執行個體，也不會載入資料表的資料，因此 B 在這兩點上都錯。(C) 正確：來源 Oracle 在 private subnet，因此在兩個帳號的 VPC 之間建立 VPC peering（並設定 security group 允許資料庫連接埠）是讓目標帳號的 DMS 安全連線到兩個執行個體的方式。(E) 正確：DMS full load 加上 CDC 任務會載入所有既有資料，並在遷移期間持續套用新變更，維持來源與目標同步；最後透過修改 Route 53 CNAME 完成切換以達零停機。(F) 錯誤，因為只做 CDC 的複製是從某個變更起點開始，不會複製先前既有的資料，目標就不會包含所有既有資料，也不會完全相同。Dump 答案 C,E,F 本身矛盾（E 與 F 都在改 CNAME），且不符合『複製所有既有資料』的要求；社群答案 A,C,E 才是技術上正確的。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS SCT does not provision/create RDS DB instances and does not migrate initial table data. SCT only converts the schema and code objects; data loading is performed by AWS DMS (full load). This makes B incorrect on two counts and is the alternative to the correct option A.","why_zh":"AWS SCT 不會佈建/建立 RDS 執行個體，也不會遷移初始的資料表資料。SCT 只轉換 schema 與程式碼物件；資料載入是由 AWS DMS（full load）執行。因此 B 在兩點上都錯誤，是正確選項 A 的對照陷阱。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Making the source RDS instance publicly accessible is an insecure, unnecessary anti-pattern. The source is in a private subnet; secure cross-account connectivity is achieved with VPC peering (option C), not by exposing the database to the internet.","why_zh":"將來源 RDS 執行個體設為公開存取是不安全且不必要的反模式。來源位於 private subnet；安全的跨帳號連線應透過 VPC peering（選項 C）達成，而不是把資料庫暴露到網際網路。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"CDC-only replication captures changes from a start point onward and does NOT copy the pre-existing data already in the source. The requirement is to replicate ALL existing data plus new data and to make the target identical, so a full load plus CDC (option E) is required, not CDC alone.","why_zh":"只做 CDC 的複製是從某個起點開始捕捉變更，並不會複製來源中既有的資料。題目要求複製所有既有資料加上新資料並使目標完全相同，因此需要 full load 加 CDC（選項 E），而非僅 CDC。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/dms/latest/sbs/chap-rdsoracle2postgresql.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/SchemaConversionTool/latest/userguide/CHAP_Welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/patterns/migrate-amazon-rds-for-oracle-to-amazon-rds-for-postgresql-in-ssl-mode-by-using-aws-dms.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/dms/latest/userguide/CHAP_Task.CDC.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/patterns/migrate-an-amazon-rds-db-instance-to-another-vpc-or-account.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":276,"question_en":"A company has implemented an ordering system using an event-driven architecture. During initial testing, the system stopped processing orders. Further log analysis revealed that one order message in an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) standard queue was causing an error on the backend and blocking all subsequent order messages. The visibility timeout of the queue is set to 30 seconds, and the backend processing timeout is set to 10 seconds. A solutions architect needs to analyze faulty order messages and ensure that the system continues to process subsequent messages. Which step should the solutions architect take to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用事件驱动架构实现了订购系统。在初始测试期间，系统停止处理订单。进一步的日志分析显示，Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 标准队列中的一条订单消息导致后端出现错误并阻止所有后续订单消息。队列的可见性超时设置为30秒，后端 处理超时设置为10秒。解决方案架构师需要分析错误的订单消息并确保系统继续处理后续消息。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪一步来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Increase the backend processing timeout to 30 seconds to match the visibility timeout.","B":"Reduce the visibility timeout of the queue to automatically remove the faulty message.","C":"Configure a new SQS FIFO queue as a dead-letter queue to isolate the faulty messages.","D":"Configure a new SQS standard queue as a dead-letter queue to isolate the faulty messages."},"options_zh":{"A":"将后端处理超时增加到 30 秒以匹配可见性超时。","B":"减少队列的可见性超时以自动移除错误消息。","C":"配置一个新的SQS FIFO 队列作为死信队列，以隔离故障消息。","D":"配置一个新的SQS标准队列作为死信队列来隔离故障消息。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":87},"tags":["Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The source queue is an Amazon SQS standard queue. AWS requires that a dead-letter queue (DLQ) be the same type as its source queue: a standard queue can only use a standard DLQ, and a FIFO queue can only use a FIFO DLQ. A DLQ isolates the poison-pill message after it exceeds maxReceiveCount, which unblocks subsequent messages and lets the architect analyze the faulty order message. Therefore the correct action is to configure a new SQS standard DLQ (D). Option C is technically invalid because a FIFO DLQ cannot be attached to a standard source queue. Tuning the visibility/processing timeouts (A) or shortening visibility (B) does not isolate the bad message or stop it from repeatedly blocking the queue.","explanation_zh":"來源佇列是 Amazon SQS standard queue。AWS 規定 dead-letter queue (DLQ) 必須與其來源佇列的類型相同：standard queue 只能使用 standard DLQ，FIFO queue 只能使用 FIFO DLQ。當訊息超過 maxReceiveCount 後，DLQ 會將該毒丸 (poison-pill) 訊息隔離出來，解除對後續訊息的阻塞，並讓架構師可以分析有問題的訂單訊息。因此正確做法是建立新的 SQS standard DLQ (選項 D)。選項 C 在技術上無效，因為 FIFO DLQ 無法附加到 standard 來源佇列。調整 visibility/processing timeout (A) 或縮短 visibility (B) 都無法隔離壞訊息，也無法阻止它反覆卡住整個佇列。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Increasing the processing timeout to match visibility does not isolate the faulty message; the poison-pill message would still be redelivered and keep blocking the queue. It also worsens throughput by holding messages invisible longer.","why_zh":"把 processing timeout 提高到與 visibility 相同並不能隔離有問題的訊息；毒丸訊息仍會被重新投遞並持續阻塞佇列，且讓訊息維持不可見更久反而降低吞吐。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Reducing the visibility timeout does NOT automatically delete a message. Messages are only removed when explicitly deleted by a consumer or after the retention period; a shorter visibility timeout actually causes faster, more frequent redelivery of the faulty message.","why_zh":"縮短 visibility timeout 並不會自動刪除訊息。訊息只有在消費者明確刪除或保留期到期後才會移除；更短的 visibility timeout 反而會讓壞訊息更快、更頻繁地被重新投遞。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A FIFO DLQ cannot be attached to a standard source queue. AWS requires the DLQ type to match the source queue type, so a standard queue must use a standard DLQ. This configuration would be rejected.","why_zh":"FIFO DLQ 無法附加到 standard 來源佇列。AWS 要求 DLQ 類型必須與來源佇列類型相符，因此 standard queue 必須使用 standard DLQ；此設定會被拒絕。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-configure-dead-letter-queue.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-dead-letter-queues.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-visibility-timeout.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":277,"question_en":"A company has automated the nightly retraining of its machine learning models by using AWS Step Functions. The work­ow consists of multiple steps that use AWS Lambda. Each step can fail for various reasons, and any failure causes a failure of the overall work­ow. A review reveals that the retraining has failed multiple nights in a row without the company noticing the failure. A solutions architect needs to improve the work­ow so that notifications are sent for all types of failures in the retraining process. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Step Functions 自动化了其机器学习模型的夜间重新训练。该工作流程由使用 AWS Lambda 的多个步骤组成。每个 步骤都可能因各种原因而失败，任何失败都会导致整个工作流程的失败。 审查显示，再培训连续多个晚上都失败了，而公司却没有注意到这一失败。解决方案架构师需要改进工作流程，以便针对再培训过 程中的所有类型的故障发送通知。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic with a subscription of type \"Email\" that targets the team's mailing list.","B":"Create a task named \"Email\" that forwards the input arguments to the SNS topic.","C":"Add a Catch field to all Task, Map, and Parallel states that have a statement of \"ErrorEquals\": [ \"States.ALL\" ] and \"Next”: \"Email\".","D":"Add a new email address to Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES). Verify the email address.","E":"Create a task named \"Email\" that forwards the input arguments to the SES email address.","F":"Add a Catch field to all Task, Map, and Parallel states that have a statement of \"ErrorEquals\": [ \"States.Runtime\" ] and \"Next\": \"Email\"."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 主题，其中包含针对团队邮件列表的“电子邮件”类型的订阅。","B":"创建一个名为“Email”的任务，将输入参数转发到 SNS 主题。","C":"将 Catch 字段添加到具有“ErrorEquals”：[“States.ALL”] 和“Next”：“Email”语句的所有任务、映射和并行状态。","D":"将新电子邮件地址添加到 Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES)。验证电子邮件地址。","E":"创建一个名为“Email”的任务，将输入参数转发到 SES 电子邮件地址。","F":"将 Catch 字段添加到具有“ErrorEquals”：[“States.Runtime”] 和“Next”：“Email”语句的所有任务、映射和并行状态。"},"answer":["B","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ABC":88},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The native, complete solution is SNS-based. (A) Create an SNS topic with an Email subscription to the team's mailing list. (B) Create an Email task that publishes the failure input to that SNS topic - Amazon SNS is an optimized Step Functions service integration (arn:aws:states:::sns:publish), so a Task can forward arguments to it directly. (C) Add a Catch field with ErrorEquals: [\"States.ALL\"] and Next: \"Email\" to all Task, Map, and Parallel states - per AWS docs, catchers are available only for Task, Parallel, and Map states, and States.ALL is the wildcard that matches any known error name, ensuring all failure types route to the Email/notification task. The dump answer BDE is wrong: it omits the Catch field entirely, so no failure is ever routed to a notification (the core requirement is unmet), and it mixes SNS (B) with SES (D, E) inconsistently. Option F is wrong because States.Runtime is non-retriable and represents only one narrow error class; AWS docs explicitly state a catch on States.ALL won't catch States.Runtime, so catching only States.Runtime would miss almost all failures.","explanation_zh":"原生且完整的解法以 SNS 為核心。(A) 建立 SNS topic 並以 Email 訂閱團隊郵件清單。(B) 建立一個 Email task，將失敗輸入發佈到該 SNS topic - Amazon SNS 是 Step Functions 的 optimized 服務整合（arn:aws:states:::sns:publish），因此 Task 可直接轉送參數。(C) 在所有 Task、Map 與 Parallel state 加上 Catch 欄位，ErrorEquals 為 [\"States.ALL\"] 且 Next 為 \"Email\" - 依 AWS 文件，catcher 僅 Task、Parallel、Map state 支援，而 States.ALL 是可比對任何已知錯誤名稱的萬用字元，確保所有失敗類型都導向 Email 通知任務。Dump 答案 BDE 錯誤：它完全省略 Catch 欄位，因此沒有任何失敗會被導向通知（核心需求未達成），且不一致地混用 SNS（B）與 SES（D、E）。選項 F 錯誤，因為 States.Runtime 不可重試且僅代表一類狹義錯誤；AWS 文件明確說明 States.ALL 的 catch 無法捕捉 States.Runtime，因此僅捕捉 States.Runtime 會漏掉幾乎所有失敗。","distractors":[{"letter":"D","why_en":"Verifying an SES email address is unnecessary for this solution; the failure notification path is built with SNS (A+B). SES is not an optimized Step Functions integration and adds nothing the SNS email subscription doesn't already provide.","why_zh":"驗證 SES email 對此解法非必要；失敗通知路徑以 SNS（A+B）建立。SES 不是 Step Functions 的 optimized 整合，且無法提供 SNS email 訂閱已涵蓋的功能。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"There is no clean Task that 'forwards input arguments to an SES email address.' SES is only reachable via the generic AWS SDK integration and requires structured SendEmail parameters, not a simple address target. The SNS publish task (B) is the native, correct mechanism.","why_zh":"沒有可直接『將輸入參數轉送到 SES email 位址』的乾淨 Task。SES 僅能透過通用 AWS SDK 整合呼叫，且需要結構化的 SendEmail 參數，而非單純的位址目標。SNS publish task（B）才是原生且正確的機制。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"ErrorEquals: [\"States.Runtime\"] catches only non-retriable runtime errors (e.g., null InputPath), a narrow class. AWS docs state States.Runtime is not retriable and a catch on States.ALL won't catch it. Catching only States.Runtime would miss Lambda task failures and most error types, failing the 'all types of failures' requirement.","why_zh":"ErrorEquals: [\"States.Runtime\"] 只捕捉不可重試的 runtime 錯誤（例如對 null 套用 InputPath），屬狹義類別。AWS 文件指出 States.Runtime 不可重試且 States.ALL 的 catch 無法捕捉它。僅捕捉 States.Runtime 會漏掉 Lambda task 失敗及大多數錯誤類型，無法滿足『所有失敗類型』的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/concepts-error-handling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/integrate-optimized.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/connect-sns.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/state-parallel.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・複選"},{"id":278,"question_en":"A company plans to deploy a new private intranet service on Amazon EC2 instances inside a VPC. An AWS Site-to-Site VPN connects the VPC to the company's on-premises network. The new service must communicate with existing on-premises services. The on-premises services are accessible through the use of hostnames that reside in the company.example DNS zone. This DNS zone is wholly hosted on premises and is available only on the company's private network. A solutions architect must ensure that the new service can resolve hostnames on the company.example domain to integrate with existing services. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司计划在 VPC 内的 Amazon EC2 实例上部署新的私有 Intranet 服务。AWS 站点到站点 VPN 将 VPC 连接到公司的本地网络。新 服务必须与现有的本地服务进行通信。可通过使用驻留在 company.example DNS 区域中的主机名来访问本地服务。该 DNS 区域完全 托管在本地，并且仅在公司的专用网络上可用。 解决方案架构师必须确保新服务可以解析 company.example 域上的主机名，以与现有服务集成。 哪种解决方案满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an empty private zone in Amazon Route 53 for company.example. Add an additional NS record to the company's on-premises company.example zone that points to the authoritative name servers for the new private zone in Route 53.","B":"Turn on DNS hostnames for the VPC. Configure a new outbound endpoint with Amazon Route 53 Resolver. Create a Resolver rule to forward requests for company.example to the on-premises name servers.","C":"Turn on DNS hostnames for the VPConfigure a new inbound resolver endpoint with Amazon Route 53 Resolver. Configur&the on- premises DNS server to forward requests for company.example to the new resolver.","D":"Use AWS Systems Manager to configure a run document that will install a hosts file that contains any required hostnames. Use an Amazon EventBridge rule to run the document when an instance is entering the running state."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon Route 53 中为 company.example 创建一个空的私有区域。将额外的 NS 记录添加到公司的本地 company.example 区 域，该区域指向 Route 53 中新私有区域的权威名称服务器。","B":"为 VPC 打开 DNS 主机名。使用 Amazon Route 53 Resolver 配置新的出站终端节点。创建解析程序规则以将对 company.example 的请求转发到本地名称服务器。","C":"打开 VP 的 DNS 主机名使用 Amazon Route 53 解析器配置新的入站解析器终端节点。配置本地 DNS 服务器，将对 company.example 的请求转发到新解析器。","D":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 配置运行文档，该文档将安装包含任何所需主机名的主机文件。当实例进入运行状态时，使用 Amazon EventBridge 规则运行文档。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is for new EC2 instances inside a VPC to resolve hostnames in the company.example zone that is hosted entirely on-premises. This is an outbound DNS flow: queries originate in the VPC and must be forwarded to the on-premises authoritative DNS servers. Amazon Route 53 Resolver supports exactly this with an OUTBOUND endpoint plus a conditional forwarding rule. Per AWS docs, 'Outbound Resolver endpoints allow DNS queries from your VPC to your on-premises network,' and a Resolver forwarding rule specifies the domain (company.example) and the on-premises resolver IP addresses, then is associated with the VPC. Turning on DNS hostnames/resolution and creating the outbound endpoint with a forward rule to the on-premises name servers is the native, low-overhead solution that matches the documented outbound example precisely.","explanation_zh":"需求是讓 VPC 內新的 EC2 執行個體能解析完全託管在地端的 company.example 區域中的主機名稱。這是一個「出站(outbound)」DNS 流程:查詢源自 VPC,必須轉發到地端的權威 DNS 伺服器。Amazon Route 53 Resolver 正是透過「outbound endpoint」加上條件式轉發規則(conditional forwarding rule)來支援此情境。根據 AWS 文件,『Outbound Resolver endpoints 允許 DNS 查詢從你的 VPC 送往地端網路』,而 Resolver 轉發規則會指定網域(company.example)與地端解析器的 IP 位址,並關聯到該 VPC。開啟 DNS hostnames、建立 outbound endpoint 並設定轉發規則指向地端 name server,正是原生、低營運負擔且完全符合官方出站範例的解法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Adding an NS delegation record on-premises pointing to an empty Route 53 private zone is backwards. The company.example zone data lives entirely on-premises and is private; an empty Route 53 zone has no records and cannot serve the real hostnames. NS delegation would direct queries to Route 53 (which has nothing), not to the on-premises authoritative servers, so resolution fails.","why_zh":"在地端加入 NS 委派記錄指向一個空的 Route 53 私有區域方向完全相反。company.example 的資料完全存在於地端且為私有;空的 Route 53 區域沒有任何記錄,無法提供真正的主機名稱。NS 委派會把查詢導向 Route 53(裡面什麼都沒有),而非地端的權威伺服器,因此解析會失敗。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An INBOUND endpoint handles the opposite direction: it lets on-premises (or other VPC) clients resolve names hosted in AWS. Here the EC2 instances need to reach on-premises names, so an inbound endpoint plus forwarding from the on-prem DNS server to it does not let VPC instances query on-premises. Wrong endpoint type for the required flow.","why_zh":"INBOUND endpoint 處理的是相反方向:它讓地端(或其他 VPC)用戶端解析託管在 AWS 的名稱。本題是 EC2 執行個體需要存取地端名稱,因此 inbound endpoint 加上地端 DNS 轉發到它,無法讓 VPC 執行個體查詢地端。對於所需流程而言是錯誤的端點類型。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Maintaining static hosts files pushed via Systems Manager run documents on instance launch is brittle and high operational overhead. It does not perform real DNS resolution, breaks when on-prem records change, and does not scale. It is an anti-pattern compared to native Route 53 Resolver conditional forwarding.","why_zh":"透過 Systems Manager run document 在執行個體啟動時推送靜態 hosts 檔案既脆弱又營運負擔高。它並非真正的 DNS 解析,當地端記錄變更時即失效,且無法擴展。相較於原生 Route 53 Resolver 條件式轉發,這是反模式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/resolver.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/resolver-overview-forward-vpc-to-network.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/resolver-rules-managing.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":279,"question_en":"A company uses AWS CloudFormation to deploy applications within multiple VPCs that are all attached to a transit gateway. Each VPC that sends tra®c to the public internet must send the tra®c through a shared services VPC. Each subnet within a VPC uses the default VPC route table, and the tra®c is routed to the transit gateway. The transit gateway uses its default route table for any VPC attachment. A security audit reveals that an Amazon EC2 instance that is deployed within a VPC can communicate with an EC2 instance that is deployed in any of the company's other VPCs. A solutions architect needs to limit the tra®c between the VPCs. Each VPC must be able to communicate only with a predefined, limited set of authorized VPCs. What should the solutions architect do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS CloudFormation 在多个 VPC 中部署应用程序，这些 VPC 全部连接到一个中转网关。将流量发送到公共互联网的每 个 VPC 必须通过共享服务 VPC 发送流量。VPC 内的每个子网都使用默认 VPC 路由表，并且流量将路由到中转网关。中转网关将其默 认路由表用于任何 VPC 连接。 安全审核显示，部署在 VPC 内的 Amazon EC2 实例可以与部署在公司任何其他 VPC 中的 EC2 实例进行通信。解决方案架构师需要限 制 VPC 之间的流量。每个 VPC 必须只能与一组预定义的、有限的授权 VPC 进行通信。 解决方案架构师应该怎样做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Update the network ACL of each subnet within a VPC to allow outbound tra®c only to the authorized VPCs. Remove all deny rules except the default deny rule.","B":"Update all the security groups that are used within a VPC to deny outbound tra®c to security groups that are used within the unauthorized VPCs.","C":"Create a dedicated transit gateway route table for each VPC attachment. Route tra®c only to the authorized VPCs.","D":"Update the main route table of each VPC to route tra®c only to the authorized VPCs through the transit gateway."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新 VPC 内每个子网的网络 ACL，以仅允许出站流量流向授权的 VPC。删除除默认拒绝规则之外的所有拒绝规则。","B":"更新 VPC 内使用的所有安全组，以拒绝流向未经授权的 VPC 内使用的安全组的出站流量。","C":"为每个 VPC 连接创建专用中转网关路由表。仅将流量路由到授权的 VPC。","D":"更新每个 VPC 的主路由表，以通过中转网关仅将流量路由到授权的 VPC。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":280,"question_en":"A company has a Windows-based desktop application that is packaged and deployed to the users' Windows machines. The company recently acquired another company that has employees who primarily use machines with a Linux operating system. The acquiring company has decided to migrate and rehost the Windows-based desktop application to AWS. All employees must be authenticated before they use the application. The acquiring company uses Active Directory on premises but wants a simplified way to manage access to the application on AWS for all the employees. Which solution will rehost the application on AWS with the LEAST development effort?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个基于 Windows 的桌面应用程序，该应用程序被打包并部署到用户的 Windows 计算机上。该公司最近收购了另一家公 司，该公司的员工主要使用装有 Linux 操作系统的机器。收购公司已决定将基于 Windows 的桌面应用程序迁移并重新托管到 AWS。 所有员工在使用该应用程序之前都必须经过身份验证。收购公司在本地使用 Active Directory，但希望采用一种简化的方式来管理所 有员工对 AWS 上应用程序的访问。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的开发工作在 AWS 上重新托管应用程序？","options_en":{"A":"Set up and provision an Amazon Workspaces virtual desktop for every employee. Implement authentication by using Amazon Cognito identity pools. Instruct employees to run the application from their provisioned Workspaces virtual desktops.","B":"Create an Auto Scaling group of Windows-based Amazon EC2 instances. Join each EC2 instance to the company’s Active Directory domain. Implement authentication by using the Active Directory that is running on premises. Instruct employees to run the application by using a Windows remote desktop.","C":"Use an Amazon AppStream 2.0 image builder to create an image that includes the application and the required configurations. Provision an AppStream 2.0 On-Demand ­eet with dynamic Fleet Auto Scaling policies for running the image. Implement authentication by using AppStream 2.0 user pools. Instruct the employees to access the application by starting browser-based AppStream 2.0 streaming sessions.","D":"Refactor and containerize the application to run as a web-based application. Run the application in Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) on AWS Fargate with step scaling policies. Implement authentication by using Amazon Cognito user pools. Instruct the employees to run the application from their browsers."},"options_zh":{"A":"为每位员工设置并配置 Amazon Workspaces 虚拟桌面。使用 Amazon Cognito 身份池实施身份验证。指导员工从其配置的 Workspaces 虚拟桌面运行应用程序。","B":"创建基于 Windows 的 Amazon EC2 实例的 Auto Scaling 组。将每个 EC2 实例加入公司的 Active Directory 域。使用本地运行的 Active Directory 实施身份验证。指导员工使用 Windows 远程桌面运行应用程序。","C":"使用 Amazon AppStream 2.0 映像生成器创建包含应用程序和所需配置的映像。使用动态队列 Auto Scaling 策略配置 AppStream 2.0 按需队列以运行映像。使用 AppStream 2.0 用户池实施身份验证。指导员工通过启动基于浏览器的 AppStream 2.0 流会话来访 问应用程序。","D":"重构应用程序并将其容器化以作为基于 Web 的应用程序运行。使用逐步扩展策略在 AWS Fargate 上的 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 中运行应用程序。使用 Amazon Cognito 用户池实施身份验证。指导员工从浏览器运行应用程序。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":94},"tags":["Migration","Security/IAM","Compute","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is 'LEAST development effort' to REHOST an existing Windows-based desktop application. Rehost (lift-and-shift) means moving the app as-is without changing its code. Amazon AppStream 2.0 (now WorkSpaces Applications) is a fully managed application streaming service that lets you take an existing Windows desktop application, capture it in an image via the image builder, and stream it to any user through an HTML5 web browser. Linux users can access it because the client is just a browser, so the platform mismatch is solved. AppStream 2.0 also offers built-in user pools for simplified authentication that does not require joining a domain, satisfying the 'simplified way to manage access for all employees.' An On-Demand fleet with Fleet Auto Scaling handles scaling. This requires essentially zero application development. Option D requires refactoring and containerizing the application into a web app, which is the very opposite of 'rehost with least development effort' (that is a refactor/re-architect migration with maximum development work). Therefore C is correct and the dump's suggested answer D is wrong.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定詞是『最少開發工作量(LEAST development effort)』來『重新託管(rehost)』一個既有的 Windows 桌面應用程式。Rehost(直接搬遷)意味著原封不動地將應用程式遷移,不修改其程式碼。Amazon AppStream 2.0(現更名為 WorkSpaces Applications)是一項全託管的應用程式串流服務,可透過 image builder 將既有的 Windows 桌面應用程式擷取成映像,並透過 HTML5 瀏覽器串流給任何使用者。由於用戶端只是瀏覽器,Linux 使用者也能存取,解決了作業系統不相容的問題。AppStream 2.0 還提供內建的 user pools 來簡化驗證,不需要加入網域,滿足『為所有員工簡化存取管理』的需求。On-Demand fleet 搭配 Fleet Auto Scaling 處理擴展。這幾乎不需要任何應用程式開發。選項 D 需要重構並容器化應用程式成為 Web 應用,這恰好與『以最少開發工作量重新託管』相反(那是 refactor/re-architect 遷移,開發量最大)。因此 C 正確,題庫建議答案 D 是錯的。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon WorkSpaces provisions a full persistent virtual desktop per employee, which is heavier and more costly than streaming a single application, and is overkill for delivering one app. More importantly, Cognito identity pools provide AWS credentials/authorization for AWS resources, not end-user sign-in to a WorkSpaces desktop; WorkSpaces uses a directory (Managed AD / AD Connector / Simple AD), so the described authentication mechanism does not fit. It is not the least-effort rehost for a single application.","why_zh":"Amazon WorkSpaces 為每位員工配置一個完整的持久化虛擬桌面,比串流單一應用程式更笨重、成本更高,對於只交付一個應用程式而言過度設計。更重要的是,Cognito identity pools 提供存取 AWS 資源的 AWS 憑證/授權,而非讓終端使用者登入 WorkSpaces 桌面;WorkSpaces 使用目錄(Managed AD / AD Connector / Simple AD),因此所描述的驗證機制並不相符。對於單一應用程式而言,這不是最省力的 rehost。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Running Windows EC2 instances joined to the on-premises Active Directory and having employees connect via Windows remote desktop creates high operational overhead (patching, scaling, domain join, RDP licensing/CALs) and does not give Linux users a clean experience. It relies on extending on-prem AD rather than a simplified managed access model, and a remote desktop to a Windows server is not the simplified approach the question asks for.","why_zh":"執行加入內部部署 Active Directory 的 Windows EC2 執行個體,並讓員工透過 Windows 遠端桌面連線,會產生高營運負擔(修補、擴展、加入網域、RDP 授權/CAL),且無法為 Linux 使用者提供乾淨的體驗。它依賴延伸內部部署 AD,而非簡化的託管存取模型,連到 Windows 伺服器的遠端桌面也不是題目所要求的簡化方式。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This requires refactoring and containerizing the desktop application into a web-based application running on ECS/Fargate. Rewriting a Windows desktop app into a web app is a major re-architect effort, which is the maximum development effort, directly contradicting the 'LEAST development effort' and 'rehost' requirements. This is the dump's suggested answer but it is technically wrong for this qualifier.","why_zh":"此選項需要將桌面應用程式重構並容器化為在 ECS/Fargate 上執行的 Web 應用程式。將 Windows 桌面應用程式改寫為 Web 應用是重大的重新架構工作,屬於最大的開發工作量,直接違反『最少開發工作量』與『rehost』的要求。這是題庫建議的答案,但就此限定詞而言在技術上是錯的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/appstream2/latest/developerguide/what-is-appstream.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/appstream2/latest/developerguide/use-web-browser-start-streaming-session-user-pool.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/appstream2/latest/developerguide/use-client-start-streaming-session.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/best-practices-for-deploying-amazon-appstream-2/best-practices-for-deploying-amazon-appstream-2.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":281,"question_en":"A company is collecting a large amount of data from a ­eet of IoT devices. Data is stored as Optimized Row Columnar (ORC) files in the Hadoop Distributed File System (HDFS) on a persistent Amazon EMR cluster. The company's data analytics team queries the data by using SQL in Apache Presto deployed on the same EMR cluster. Queries scan large amounts of data, always run for less than 15 minutes, and run only between 5 PM and 10 PM. The company is concerned about the high cost associated with the current solution. A solutions architect must propose the most cost- effective solution that will allow SQL data queries. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在从一组物联网设备收集大量数据。数据作为优化行列式 (ORC) 文件存储在持久 Amazon EMR 集群上的 Hadoop 分布式文 件系统 (HDFS) 中。该公司的数据分析团队使用部署在同一 EMR 集群上的 Apache Presto 中的 SQL 查询数据。查询会扫描大量数据， 运行时间始终少于 15 分钟，并且仅在下午 5 点到晚上 10 点之间运行。 该公司担心当前解决方案的高成本。解决方案架构师必须提出最具成本效益的解决方案，以允许 SQL 数据查询。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Store data in Amazon S3. Use Amazon Redshift Spectrum to query data.","B":"Store data in Amazon S3. Use the AWS Glue Data Catalog and Amazon Athena to query data.","C":"Store data in EMR File System (EMRFS). Use Presto in Amazon EMR to query data.","D":"Store data in Amazon Redshift. Use Amazon Redshift to query data."},"options_zh":{"A":"将数据存储在 Amazon S3 中。使用 Amazon Redshift Spectrum 查询数据。","B":"将数据存储在 Amazon S3 中。使用 AWS Glue 数据目录和 Amazon Athena 查询数据。","C":"将数据存储在 EMR 文件系统 (EMRFS) 中。在 Amazon EMR 中使用 Presto 查询数据。","D":"将数据存储在 Amazon Redshift 中。使用 Amazon Redshift 查询数据。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":96},"tags":["Storage","Database","Cost Optimization","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is MOST cost-effective for SQL queries that run only 5 hours/day (5-10 PM) and always finish in under 15 minutes. Amazon Athena is serverless: there is no cluster or infrastructure to provision, and you pay only per query based on the amount of data scanned. Because the data is stored as ORC (a columnar format), Athena scans far less data, minimizing cost, and the AWS Glue Data Catalog supplies the persistent metadata store so the existing Hive/Presto schemas map directly. Storing the data in S3 and querying with Athena eliminates the always-on EMR cluster cost while still allowing standard SQL. Redshift Spectrum (A) and Redshift (D) both require a provisioned, continuously running Redshift cluster, and EMRFS with Presto (C) keeps the same persistent EMR cluster running - all incur idle compute cost during the 19 hours/day when no queries run, so none is the most cost-effective.","explanation_zh":"決定性的條件是「最具成本效益」，而查詢每天只在 5-10 PM 共約 5 小時執行、且每次都在 15 分鐘內完成。Amazon Athena 是無伺服器服務：不需佈建或管理任何叢集或基礎設施，僅依每次查詢掃描的資料量計費。由於資料以 ORC（欄式格式）儲存，Athena 掃描的資料量大幅降低，成本最省；而 AWS Glue Data Catalog 提供持久的中繼資料存放區，現有的 Hive/Presto 結構描述可直接對應。將資料放在 S3 並用 Athena 查詢，可消除常駐 EMR 叢集的成本，同時仍支援標準 SQL。Redshift Spectrum (A) 與 Redshift (D) 都需要一個持續運行的佈建式 Redshift 叢集，而 EMRFS 搭配 Presto (C) 仍維持原本的持久 EMR 叢集 - 這三者在每天約 19 小時沒有查詢時都會產生閒置運算成本，因此都不是最具成本效益的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Redshift Spectrum requires a provisioned, always-on Amazon Redshift cluster (the Spectrum layer is invoked from the cluster, and an IAM role must be associated with that cluster). Paying for a running cluster for queries that only run 5 hours a day is not the most cost-effective option.","why_zh":"Redshift Spectrum 需要一個佈建且持續運行的 Amazon Redshift 叢集（Spectrum 層由叢集呼叫，且必須將 IAM 角色關聯到該叢集）。為每天只執行 5 小時的查詢支付常駐叢集費用並非最具成本效益。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EMRFS still requires keeping the persistent EMR cluster with Presto running. This retains exactly the always-on compute cost the company wants to eliminate, so it is not cost-effective.","why_zh":"EMRFS 仍需保持搭載 Presto 的持久 EMR 叢集持續運行，等於保留了公司想消除的常駐運算成本，因此不具成本效益。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Loading data into Amazon Redshift requires a provisioned data warehouse running continuously, plus ingest/storage in the warehouse. This is the highest-cost option and is over-engineered for short ad hoc queries that run only a few hours per day; Redshift is best for complex joins over highly structured warehouse data, not this scenario.","why_zh":"將資料載入 Amazon Redshift 需要一個持續運行的佈建式資料倉儲，加上倉儲內的匯入與儲存成本。這是成本最高的選項，對每天僅執行數小時的短暫臨時查詢而言過度設計；Redshift 適用於高度結構化倉儲資料的複雜聯結，而非此情境。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/when-should-i-use-ate.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/performance-tuning-data-optimization-techniques.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/redshift/latest/dg/c-using-spectrum.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/redshift/latest/dg/c-getting-started-using-spectrum.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":282,"question_en":"A large company recently experienced an unexpected increase in Amazon RDS and Amazon DynamoDB costs. The company needs to increase visibility into details of AWS Billing and Cost Management. There are various accounts associated with AWS Organizations, including many development and production accounts. There is no consistent tagging strategy across the organization, but there are guidelines in place that require all infrastructure to be deployed using AWS CloudFormation with consistent tagging. Management requires cost center numbers and project ID numbers for all existing and future DynamoDB tables and RDS instances. Which strategy should the solutions architect provide to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家大公司最近遇到 Amazon RDS 和 Amazon DynamoDB 成本意外增加的情况。该公司需要提高 AWS 计费和成本管理详细信息的可见 性。有多种与 AWS Organizations 关联的账户，包括许多开发和生产账户。整个组织没有一致的标记策略，但有指导方针要求所有基 础设施都使用具有一致标记的 AWS CloudFormation 进行部署。管理层需要所有现有和未来的 DynamoDB 表和 RDS 实例的成本中心编 号和项目 ID 编号。 解决方案架构师应该提供哪种策略来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Tag Editor to tag existing resources. Create cost allocation tags to define the cost center and project ID and allow 24 hours for tags to propagate to existing resources.","B":"Use an AWS Config rule to alert the finance team of untagged resources. Create a centralized AWS Lambda based solution to tag untagged RDS databases and DynamoDB resources every hour using a cross-account role.","C":"Use Tag Editor to tag existing resources. Create cost allocation tags to define the cost center and project ID. Use SCPs to restrict resource creation that do not have the cost center and project ID on the resource.","D":"Create cost allocation tags to define the cost center and project ID and allow 24 hours for tags to propagate to existing resources. Update existing federated roles to restrict privileges to provision resources that do not include the cost center and project ID on the resource."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用标签编辑器来标记现有资源。创建成本分配标签来定义成本中心和项目 ID，并允许标签在 24 小时内传播到现有资源。","B":"使用 AWS Config 规则向财务团队发出未标记资源的警报。创建基于 AWS Lambda 的集中式解决方案，使用跨账户角色每小时标 记未标记的 RDS 数据库和 DynamoDB 资源。","C":"使用标签编辑器来标记现有资源。创建成本分配标签以定义成本中心和项目 ID。使用 SCP 限制资源上没有成本中心和项目 ID 的资源创建。","D":"创建成本分配标签来定义成本中心和项目 ID，并允许标签在 24 小时内传播到现有资源。更新现有联合角色以限制配置不包含 资源成本中心和项目 ID 的资源的权限。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":89},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to apply cost center and project ID tags to ALL existing and FUTURE DynamoDB tables and RDS instances, and to gain billing visibility. Option C does all three: Tag Editor backfills tags on existing resources (cost allocation tags do not apply to resources created before the tag existed, so existing resources must be tagged manually); creating cost allocation tags activates those tag keys so the cost center and project ID appear in Cost Explorer and the Cost and Usage Report; and an SCP using the aws:RequestTag condition denies creation of DynamoDB and RDS resources that lack the required tags, enforcing compliance for all future resources organization-wide. AWS explicitly recommends this pattern: tag policies report noncompliance but cannot prevent untagged resource creation, so 'consider creating an SCP to set guardrails around resource creation requests.' RDS and DynamoDB both support tag-on-create with aws:RequestTag, making the SCP enforceable.","explanation_zh":"需求是要為所有現有及未來的 DynamoDB 資料表與 RDS 執行個體套用 cost center 與 project ID 標籤，並提升帳單可見度。選項 C 同時滿足三點：用 Tag Editor 為現有資源補上標籤（cost allocation tags 不會套用到標籤建立之前就存在的資源，因此現有資源必須手動標記）；建立 cost allocation tags 會啟用這些標籤鍵，使 cost center 與 project ID 顯示在 Cost Explorer 與 Cost and Usage Report 中；再以使用 aws:RequestTag 條件的 SCP 拒絕缺少必要標籤的 DynamoDB 與 RDS 資源建立，於整個組織層級強制未來資源合規。AWS 官方明確建議此模式：tag policies 只能回報不合規，無法阻止未標記資源的建立，因此「考慮建立 SCP 對資源建立請求設定護欄」。RDS 與 DynamoDB 皆支援建立時標記（tag-on-create）並可被 aws:RequestTag 約束，使 SCP 可被強制執行。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Tag Editor plus cost allocation tags handles existing resources and billing visibility, but provides nothing to enforce tags on FUTURE resources, which is an explicit requirement. The phrase 'allow 24 hours for tags to propagate to existing resources' is also a misconception: cost allocation tag activation does not propagate tag values onto resources.","why_zh":"Tag Editor 加 cost allocation tags 可處理現有資源與帳單可見度，但對「未來資源」的標籤強制毫無作為，而這是明確需求。「等待 24 小時讓標籤傳播到現有資源」也是誤解：啟用 cost allocation tag 並不會把標籤值傳播到資源上。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Config alerting is only detective, and an hourly cross-account Lambda that auto-tags resources is reactive, high operational overhead, and fragile. It cannot guarantee the required cost center/project ID values and does not prevent untagged creation; it merely patches after the fact. This is the dump's suggested answer and is technically inferior.","why_zh":"AWS Config 警示僅屬偵測性，每小時跨帳戶執行的 Lambda 自動標記屬被動補救、營運負擔高且脆弱。它無法保證正確的 cost center/project ID 值，也無法阻止未標記資源建立，只是在事後修補。此為題庫建議答案，技術上較差。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"It repeats the false 'tags propagate to existing resources' claim and uses no Tag Editor to backfill existing resources. Restricting only federated roles leaves gaps (IAM users, other roles, cross-account principals, root), whereas an SCP applies org-wide. It is both technically inaccurate and incomplete in coverage.","why_zh":"重複了錯誤的「標籤會傳播到現有資源」說法，也未用 Tag Editor 為現有資源補標籤。僅限制 federated roles 會留下漏洞（IAM 使用者、其他角色、跨帳戶主體、root），而 SCP 可在整個組織生效。此選項既技術不準確、涵蓋面也不完整。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/custom-tags.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/security_iam_id-based-policy-examples-grant-permissions-tags-on-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_tags.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":283,"question_en":"A company wants to send data from its on-premises systems to Amazon S3 buckets. The company created the S3 buckets in three different accounts. The company must send the data privately without the data traveling across the internet. The company has no existing dedicated connectivity to AWS. Which combination of steps should a solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司希望将数据从其本地系统发送到 Amazon S3 存储桶。该公司在三个不同的账户中创建了 S3 存储桶。公司必须私下发送数 据，而不能通过互联网传输数据。该公司目前没有与 AWS 的专用连接。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Establish a networking account in the AWS Cloud. Create a private VPC in the networking account. Set up an AWS Direct Connect connection with a private VIF between the on-premises environment and the private VPC.","B":"Establish a networking account in the AWS Cloud. Create a private VPC in the networking account. Set up an AWS Direct Connect connection with a public VIF between the on-premises environment and the private VPC.","C":"Create an Amazon S3 interface endpoint in the networking account.","D":"Create an Amazon S3 gateway endpoint in the networking account.","E":"Establish a networking account in the AWS Cloud. Create a private VPC in the networking account. Peer VPCs from the accounts that host the S3 buckets with the VPC in the network account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS 云中建立网络帐户。在网络帐户中创建私有 VPC。在本地环境和私有 VPC 之间设置具有私有 VIF 的 AWS Direct Connect 连接。","B":"在 AWS 云中建立网络帐户。在网络帐户中创建私有 VPC。在本地环境和私有 VPC 之间设置具有公共 VIF 的 AWS Direct Connect 连接。","C":"在网络帐户中创建 Amazon S3 接口终端节点。","D":"在网络帐户中创建 Amazon S3 网关终端节点。","E":"在 AWS 云中建立网络帐户。在网络帐户中创建私有 VPC。来自托管 S3 存储桶的账户的对等 VPC 与网络账户中的 VPC。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AC":84},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is private (no-internet) connectivity from on-premises to S3 buckets in three accounts, with no existing dedicated link. Step 1 is to build the private path: a Direct Connect connection with a PRIVATE VIF (Option A) connects the on-premises network to a VPC using private IP addresses. Step 2 is to make S3 reachable privately from that VPC and on-premises: an S3 INTERFACE endpoint (Option C, AWS PrivateLink) provides private IP ENIs that, per the S3 PrivateLink docs, are 'directly accessible from applications that are on premises over VPN and Direct Connect.' A gateway endpoint (Option D) is wrong because AWS docs explicitly state gateway endpoints 'do not allow access from on premises' — they only add route-table entries for traffic originating inside the VPC. A public VIF (Option B) reaches AWS PUBLIC service endpoints over public IPs, not a private VPC, so the wording is contradictory and would not be a private VPC path. Because S3 is a regional service accessed via the regional endpoint, a single interface endpoint serves buckets in all three accounts (subject to endpoint/bucket policies); there is no VPC 'hosting' an S3 bucket to peer, so Option E is irrelevant. The correct combination is A and C.","explanation_zh":"需求是從地端私有地（不經網際網路）連線到三個帳戶中的 S3 儲存貯體，且目前沒有既有的專線連線。第一步是建立私有路徑：使用 PRIVATE VIF 的 AWS Direct Connect 連線（選項 A）以私有 IP 位址將地端網路連到 VPC。第二步是讓 S3 可從該 VPC 與地端私有地存取：S3 INTERFACE endpoint（選項 C，AWS PrivateLink）提供私有 IP 的 ENI，依 S3 PrivateLink 文件所述，'可由地端應用程式透過 VPN 與 Direct Connect 直接存取'。gateway endpoint（選項 D）錯誤，因為 AWS 文件明確指出 gateway endpoints『不允許來自地端的存取』——它只在路由表中加入項目，僅服務 VPC 內部發起的流量。public VIF（選項 B）連到的是 AWS 公有服務端點（公有 IP），而非私有 VPC，敘述自相矛盾且不是私有 VPC 路徑。由於 S3 是區域型服務、透過區域端點存取，單一 interface endpoint 即可服務三個帳戶的儲存貯體（受端點/貯體政策約束）；S3 儲存貯體並非由 VPC『承載』，沒有可對等互連的對象，故選項 E 無關。正確組合為 A 與 C。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A public VIF accesses AWS public service endpoints over public IP addresses, not a private VPC. The statement 'public VIF between on-premises and the private VPC' is contradictory, and routing S3 traffic via the public endpoint does not provide the private VPC-based path the design needs.","why_zh":"public VIF 以公有 IP 存取 AWS 公有服務端點，而非私有 VPC。『public VIF 連到 private VPC』的敘述自相矛盾，且經公有端點存取 S3 並非設計所需的私有 VPC 路徑。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 gateway endpoints use route-table entries with AWS-managed prefix lists and only serve traffic originating inside the VPC. AWS documentation explicitly states gateway endpoints 'do not allow access from on premises,' so traffic arriving over Direct Connect cannot use them.","why_zh":"S3 gateway endpoint 使用路由表項目與 AWS 託管的字首清單，僅服務 VPC 內部發起的流量。AWS 文件明確指出 gateway endpoints『不允許來自地端的存取』，故經 Direct Connect 進入的流量無法使用。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"S3 is a regional service, not a resource inside a VPC, so there are no 'VPCs that host the S3 buckets' to peer. VPC peering does not provide a private path to S3; a single interface endpoint already reaches the regional S3 service for all three accounts.","why_zh":"S3 是區域型服務，並非位於 VPC 內的資源，因此沒有『承載 S3 儲存貯體的 VPC』可供對等互連。VPC peering 無法提供存取 S3 的私有路徑；單一 interface endpoint 即可為三個帳戶觸及區域型 S3 服務。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/privatelink-interface-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/gateway-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directconnect/latest/UserGuide/WorkingWithVirtualInterfaces.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/create-interface-endpoint.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・複選"},{"id":284,"question_en":"A company operates quick-service restaurants. The restaurants follow a predictable model with high sales tra®c for 4 hours daily. Sales tra®c is lower outside of those peak hours. The point of sale and management platform is deployed in the AWS Cloud and has a backend that is based on Amazon DynamoDB. The database table uses provisioned throughput mode with 100,000 RCUs and 80,000 WCUs to match known peak resource consumption. The company wants to reduce its DynamoDB cost and minimize the operational overhead for the IT staff. Which solution meets these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司经营快餐店。这些餐厅遵循可预测的模式，每天 4 小时的客流量很高。高峰时段之外的销售流量较低。 销售点和管理平台部署在 AWS 云中，并具有基于 Amazon DynamoDB 的后端。数据库表使用具有 100,000 个 RCU 和 80,000 个 WCU 的 预配置吞吐量模式，以匹配已知的峰值资源消耗。 该公司希望降低 DynamoDB 成本并最大限度地减少 IT 员工的运营开销。 哪种解决方案最经济高效地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Reduce the provisioned RCUs and WCUs.","B":"Change the DynamoDB table to use on-demand capacity.","C":"Enable Dynamo DB auto scaling for the table.","D":"Purchase 1-year reserved capacity that is su®cient to cover the peak load for 4 hours each day."},"options_zh":{"A":"减少配置的 RCU 和 WCU。","B":"更改 DynamoDB 表以使用按需容量。","C":"为表启用 Dynamo DB 自动缩放。","D":"购买1年预留容量，足以满足每天4小时的高峰负载。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":70,"B":22},"tags":["Compute","Database","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The workload is explicitly predictable and cyclical: high traffic for 4 hours daily and low traffic the rest of the time. The table is provisioned at peak (100,000 RCU / 80,000 WCU) 24/7, so it pays for ~20 hours of unused capacity every day. DynamoDB auto scaling (option C) is purpose-built for exactly this cyclical pattern - the AWS docs describe a workload 'active during daytime hours' with no need for the same throughput at night, and auto scaling uses Application Auto Scaling with target tracking to raise capacity for the peak and lower it afterward so 'you don't pay for unused provisioned capacity.' Because it is a managed AWS feature, it also minimizes operational overhead for IT staff. The decision is really between B (on-demand) and C: both cut cost versus the current 24/7 over-provisioning, but for a HIGH-VOLUME, PREDICTABLE workload on-demand's pay-per-request pricing (roughly 6-7x the provisioned hourly rate) is more expensive than provisioned-with-auto-scaling, which keeps the cheaper provisioned pricing during the known peak while shedding capacity off-peak. Therefore C is the MOST cost-effective with low operational overhead.","explanation_zh":"此工作負載明確是可預測且週期性的：每天有 4 小時高流量，其餘時間流量低。資料表全天候依尖峰值佈建（100,000 RCU / 80,000 WCU），因此每天約有 20 小時在為未使用的容量付費。DynamoDB auto scaling（選項 C）正是為這種週期性模式設計的——AWS 文件描述了一個「白天活躍」、夜間不需相同吞吐量的工作負載，auto scaling 透過 Application Auto Scaling 的 target tracking 在尖峰時調高容量、之後調低，讓您「不必為未使用的佈建容量付費」。由於這是 AWS 託管功能，也能將 IT 人員的營運負擔降到最低。真正的取捨在 B（on-demand）與 C 之間：兩者都比目前全天候過度佈建省錢，但對於高流量且可預測的工作負載，on-demand 的按請求計費（約為佈建小時費率的 6-7 倍）比佈建加 auto scaling 更貴；後者在已知尖峰期間維持較便宜的佈建定價，並在離峰時釋放容量。因此 C 最具成本效益且營運負擔低。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A flat, manual reduction of RCUs/WCUs would under-provision during the 4-hour peak and cause throttling; to avoid throttling you must keep capacity at peak, which yields no savings. Continually adjusting it by hand also adds operational overhead, contradicting the requirement to minimize it.","why_zh":"一次性手動調低 RCU/WCU 會在 4 小時尖峰時容量不足而造成限流；要避免限流就得維持在尖峰值，無法省錢。持續手動調整也增加營運負擔，違反最小化營運負擔的要求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"On-demand minimizes operational overhead but is designed for unpredictable/spiky/unknown workloads. For this high-volume, predictable peak, per-request pricing (~6-7x the provisioned hourly rate) makes it more expensive than provisioned-with-auto-scaling, so it is not the MOST cost-effective.","why_zh":"On-demand 能最小化營運負擔，但設計給不可預測／突發／未知的工作負載。對此高流量且可預測的尖峰，按請求計費（約佈建小時費率的 6-7 倍）比佈建加 auto scaling 更貴，因此不是最具成本效益。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"DynamoDB reserved capacity is a 1-year/3-year billing commitment that discounts continuously provisioned throughput; it is not a time-windowed purchase for '4 hours a day,' and it does not reduce the cost of the idle 20 hours unless paired with scaling. It also requires capacity forecasting and a long-term commitment, adding overhead and risk.","why_zh":"DynamoDB reserved capacity 是 1 年／3 年的計費承諾，對持續佈建的吞吐量提供折扣；它並非針對「每天 4 小時」的時段性購買，且若不搭配縮放，也無法降低閒置 20 小時的成本。它還需要容量預測與長期承諾，增加負擔與風險。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/AutoScaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/provisioned-capacity-mode.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/on-demand-capacity-mode.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/HowItWorks.ReadWriteCapacityMode.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":285,"question_en":"A company hosts a blog post application on AWS using Amazon API Gateway, Amazon DynamoDB, and AWS Lambda. The application currently does not use API keys to authorize requests. The API model is as follows: GET /posts/{postId}: to get post details GET /users/{userId}: to get user details GET /comments/{commentId}: to get comments details The company has noticed users are actively discussing topics in the comments section, and the company wants to increase user engagement by making the comments appear in real time. Which design should be used to reduce comment latency and improve user experience?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 Amazon API Gateway、Amazon DynamoDB 和 AWS Lambda 在 AWS 上托管博客文章应用程序。该应用程序当前不使用 API 密钥来授权请求​。API 模型如下： GET /posts/{postId}：获取帖子详情 GET /users/{userId}：获取用户详情 GET /comments/{commentId}：获取评论详情 公司注意到用户活跃在评论部分讨论主题，该公司希望通过实时显示评论来提高用户参与度。 应该采用哪种设计来减少评论延迟并提高用户体验？","options_en":{"A":"Use edge-optimized API with Amazon CloudFront to cache API responses.","B":"Modify the blog application code to request GET/comments/{commentId} every 10 seconds.","C":"Use AWS AppSync and leverage WebSockets to deliver comments.","D":"Change the concurrency limit of the Lambda functions to lower the API response time."},"options_zh":{"A":"将边缘优化的 API 与 Amazon CloudFront 结合使用来缓存 API 响应。","B":"修改博客应用代码，每 10 秒请求一次 GET/comments/{commentId}。","C":"使用 AWS AppSync 并利用 WebSockets 来提供评论。","D":"更改 Lambda 函数的并发限制以降低 API 响应时间。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":286,"question_en":"A company manages hundreds of AWS accounts centrally in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company recently started to allow product teams to create and manage their own S3 access points in their accounts. The S3 access points can be accessed only within VPCs, not on the internet. What is the MOST operationally e®cient way to enforce this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Organizations 的组织中集中管理数百个 AWS 账户。该公司最近开始允许产品团队在其帐户中创建和管理自己的 S3 访问点。S3 接入点只能在 VPC 内访问，不能在 Internet 上访问。 执行此要求最有效的操作方法是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Set the S3 access point resource policy to deny the s3:CreateAccessPoint action unless the s3:AccessPointNetworkOrigin condition key evaluates to VPC.","B":"Create an SCP at the root level in the organization to deny the s3:CreateAccessPoint action unless the s3:AccessPointNetworkOrigin condition key evaluates to VPC.","C":"Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to create a new IAM policy in each AWS account that allows the s3:CreateAccessPoint action only if the s3:AccessPointNetworkOrigin condition key evaluates to VPC.","D":"Set the S3 bucket policy to deny the s3:CreateAccessPoint action unless the s3:AccessPointNetworkOrigin condition key evaluates to VPC."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 S3 接入点资源策略设置为拒绝 s3:CreateAccessPoint 操作，除非 s3:AccessPointNetworkOrigin 条件键的计算结果为 VPC。","B":"在组织中的根级别创建 SCP 以拒绝 s3:CreateAccessPoint 操作，除非 s3:AccessPointNetworkOrigin 条件键计算结果为 VPC。","C":"使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 在每个 AWS 账户中创建新的 IAM 策略，仅当 s3:AccessPointNetworkOrigin 条件键计算结果为 VPC 时才允许 s3:CreateAccessPoint 操作。","D":"将 S3 存储桶策略设置为拒绝 s3:CreateAccessPoint 操作，除非 s3:AccessPointNetworkOrigin 条件键的计算结果为 VPC。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":95},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to enforce VPC-only S3 access points across hundreds of accounts in an AWS Organization, while product teams create and manage their own access points. The most operationally efficient enforcement is a preventive guardrail applied once at the organization level. AWS's official S3 documentation 'Configuring IAM policies for using access points' shows this exact pattern in 'Example 4 - Service control policy': a Deny on s3:CreateAccessPoint with StringNotEquals on s3:AccessPointNetworkOrigin = VPC, stating it 'requires all new access points to be created with a virtual private cloud (VPC) network origin' so 'users in your organization can't create new access points that are accessible from the internet.' This matches option B precisely. An SCP automatically applies to all current and future member accounts and cannot be overridden by the teams, requiring no per-account deployment or ongoing maintenance.","explanation_zh":"需求是在 AWS Organizations 的數百個帳戶中強制 S3 access points 僅限 VPC，同時讓產品團隊自行建立與管理 access points。最具運維效率的做法是在組織層級套用一次性的預防性護欄。AWS 官方 S3 文件「Configuring IAM policies for using access points」在「Example 4 - Service control policy」中正是這個模式：對 s3:CreateAccessPoint 使用 Deny，並以 StringNotEquals 條件判斷 s3:AccessPointNetworkOrigin 是否為 VPC，文件明確說明此政策「要求所有新的 access points 必須以 VPC 網路來源建立」，使「組織中的使用者無法建立可從網際網路存取的新 access points」。這正好對應選項 B。SCP 會自動套用到所有現有與未來的成員帳戶，且團隊無法繞過，無需逐帳戶部署或持續維護。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An S3 access point resource policy governs object operations (GetObject/PutObject) made THROUGH an existing access point. It cannot control the s3:CreateAccessPoint control-plane action because at creation time the access point and its resource policy do not yet exist. It also would not apply org-wide; this is a category error.","why_zh":"S3 access point 資源政策管制的是透過既有 access point 進行的物件操作（GetObject/PutObject）。它無法管制 s3:CreateAccessPoint 這個控制平面動作，因為建立當下 access point 與其資源政策尚不存在，且無法套用至整個組織，屬於概念錯置。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Deploying an IAM Allow-only policy via CloudFormation StackSets does not prevent teams from creating internet-origin access points; an Allow grant does not remove other permissions, and only an explicit Deny (or SCP) prevents the action. It also requires deploying and maintaining policies in hundreds of accounts, far more operational overhead than a single SCP.","why_zh":"透過 CloudFormation StackSets 部署僅含 Allow 的 IAM 政策無法阻止團隊建立網際網路來源的 access point；Allow 授權不會移除其他權限，只有明確 Deny（或 SCP）才能阻擋該動作。此外還需在數百個帳戶部署與維護政策，運維負擔遠高於單一 SCP。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A bucket policy controls operations on the bucket and its objects, not the s3:CreateAccessPoint control-plane action, and applies only to one bucket in one account rather than enforcing the requirement across the entire organization.","why_zh":"儲存貯體政策管制的是對該貯體與其物件的操作，而非 s3:CreateAccessPoint 控制平面動作，且僅適用於單一帳戶中的單一貯體，無法在整個組織強制執行此需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/access-points-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/access-points.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/s3-access-point-in-vpc-only.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/service-authorization/latest/reference/list_amazons3.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":287,"question_en":"A solutions architect must update an application environment within AWS Elastic Beanstalk using a blue/green deployment methodology. The solutions architect creates an environment that is identical to the existing application environment and deploys the application to the new environment. What should be done next to complete the update?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师必须使用蓝/绿部署方法更新 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 中的应用程序环境。解决方案架构师创建一个与现有应用程序环 境相同的环境，并将应用程序部署到新环境。 接下来应该做什么来完成更新？","options_en":{"A":"Redirect to the new environment using Amazon Route 53.","B":"Select the Swap Environment URLs option.","C":"Replace the Auto Scaling launch configuration.","D":"Update the DNS records to point to the green environment."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Route 53 重定向到新环境。","B":"选择交换环境 URL 选项。","C":"替换 Auto Scaling 启动配置。","D":"更新 DNS 记录以指向绿色环境。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"AWS Elastic Beanstalk has a native blue/green deployment feature built on CNAME swapping. The official procedure is: (1) clone or launch a new identical environment, (2) deploy the new application version to it, (3) test it, then (4) on the environment overview page choose Actions and select 'Swap environment URLs', selecting the current (production) environment. Elastic Beanstalk then swaps the CNAME records of the two environments, redirecting traffic to the new version instantly with no downtime. Because the question explicitly frames this as the Elastic Beanstalk blue/green methodology and states the new environment is already created and deployed, the documented next step is the Swap Environment URLs option (B).","explanation_zh":"AWS Elastic Beanstalk 內建以 CNAME 交換為基礎的 blue/green 部署功能。官方流程為:(1) 複製或啟動一個全新且相同的 environment,(2) 將新版應用程式部署到該 environment,(3) 進行測試,然後 (4) 在 environment 總覽頁面選擇 Actions 並點選 'Swap environment URLs',再選取目前的(正式)environment。Elastic Beanstalk 接著會交換兩個 environment 的 CNAME 記錄,瞬間把流量導向新版本且不中斷服務。由於題目明確以 Elastic Beanstalk 的 blue/green 方法為情境,且新 environment 已建立並部署完成,文件記載的下一步就是 Swap Environment URLs 選項(B)。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Redirecting via Amazon Route 53 is not the Elastic Beanstalk-native blue/green mechanism. Beanstalk's built-in feature is the CNAME swap (Swap Environment URLs), which it performs internally and instantly. Route 53 is unnecessary and is not the documented step for completing a Beanstalk blue/green deployment.","why_zh":"透過 Amazon Route 53 重新導向並非 Elastic Beanstalk 原生的 blue/green 機制。Beanstalk 的內建功能是 CNAME 交換(Swap Environment URLs),由其內部即時執行。Route 53 並非必要,也不是完成 Beanstalk blue/green 部署的文件步驟。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Replacing the Auto Scaling launch configuration has nothing to do with switching traffic between two environments. It does not redirect users to the new (green) environment and is irrelevant to completing a blue/green cutover.","why_zh":"更換 Auto Scaling launch configuration 與在兩個 environment 之間切換流量完全無關。它無法把使用者導向新的(green)environment,與完成 blue/green 切換無關。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Manually updating DNS records to point to the green environment is not how Elastic Beanstalk completes a blue/green deployment. Beanstalk handles the redirection internally by swapping CNAMEs via the Swap Environment URLs action; manual DNS edits are not the documented or intended step.","why_zh":"手動更新 DNS 記錄指向 green environment 並非 Elastic Beanstalk 完成 blue/green 部署的方式。Beanstalk 透過 Swap Environment URLs 動作在內部交換 CNAME 來處理導向;手動編輯 DNS 並非文件所載或預期的步驟。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.CNAMESwap.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.deploy-existing-version.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":288,"question_en":"A company is building an image service on the web that will allow users to upload and search random photos. At peak usage, up to 10,000 users worldwide will upload their images. The will then overlay text on the uploaded images, which will then be published on the company website. Which design should a solutions architect implement?","question_zh":"一家公司正在网络上构建图像服务，允许用户上传和搜索随机照片。在使用高峰期，全球多达 10,000 名用户将上传他们的图像。然 后，将在上传的图像上覆盖文本，然后将其发布在公司网站上。 解决方案架构师应该实施哪种设计？","options_en":{"A":"Store the uploaded images in Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS). Send application log information about each image to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Create a ­eet of Amazon EC2 instances that use CloudWatch Logs to determine which images need to be processed. Place processed images in another directory in Amazon EFS. Enable Amazon CloudFront and configure the origin to be the one of the EC2 instances in the ­eet.","B":"Store the uploaded images in an Amazon S3 bucket and configure an S3 bucket event notification to send a message to Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS). Create a ­eet of Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) to pull messages from Amazon SNS to process the images and place them in Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS). Use Amazon CloudWatch metrics for the SNS message volume to scale out EC2 instances. Enable Amazon CloudFront and configure the origin to be the ALB in front of the EC2 instances.","C":"Store the uploaded images in an Amazon S3 bucket and configure an S3 bucket event notification to send a message to the Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Create a ­eet of Amazon EC2 instances to pull messages from the SQS queue to process the images and place them in another S3 bucket. Use Amazon CloudWatch metrics for queue depth to scale out EC2 instances. Enable Amazon CloudFront and configure the origin to be the S3 bucket that contains the processed images.","D":"Store the uploaded images on a shared Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume mounted to a ­eet of Amazon EC2 Spot instances. Create an Amazon DynamoDB table that contains information about each uploaded image and whether it has been processed. Use an Amazon EventBridge rule to scale out EC2 instances. Enable Amazon CloudFront and configure the origin to reference an Elastic Load Balancer in front of the ­eet of EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"将上传的图像存储在 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 中。将有关每个图像的应用程序日志信息发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。创建一组 Amazon EC2 实例，这些实例使用 CloudWatch Logs 来确定需要处理哪些图像。将处理后的图像放置 在 Amazon EFS 中的另一个目录中。启用 Amazon CloudFront 并将源配置为队列中的 EC2 实例之一。","B":"将上传的图像存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中，并配置 S3 存储桶事件通知以将消息发送到 Amazon Simple notification Service (Amazon SNS)。在 Application Load Balancer (ALB) 后面创建一组 Amazon EC2 实例，以从 Amazon SNS 拉取消息来处理图像并将其 放置在 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 中。使用 SNS 消息量的 Amazon CloudWatch 指标来扩展 EC2 实例。启用 Amazon CloudFront 并将源配置为 EC2 实例前面的 ALB。","C":"将上传的图像存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中，并配置 S3 存储桶事件通知以将消息发送到 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列。创建一组 Amazon EC2 实例以从 SQS 队列中提取消息来处理图像并将它们放入另一个 S3 存储桶中。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 队列深度指标来扩展 EC2 实例。启用 Amazon CloudFront 并将源配置为包含已处理图像的 S3 存储桶。","D":"将上传的图像存储在安装到 Amazon EC2 Spot 实例队列的共享 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 卷上。创建一个 Amazon DynamoDB 表，其中包含有关每个上传图像及其是否已处理的信息。使用 Amazon EventBridge 规则扩展 EC2 实例。启用 Amazon CloudFront 并配置源以引用 EC2 实例队列前面的弹性负载均衡器。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Option C is the canonical AWS decoupled image-processing pattern that AWS documents almost verbatim. Users upload images to S3, an S3 event notification places a message on an SQS queue, a fleet of EC2 instances pulls messages from SQS to process (overlay text), and processed images go to a second S3 bucket served by CloudFront. SQS provides durable, decoupled buffering of work items so spikes from up to 10,000 worldwide users do not overwhelm the processing fleet, and the Auto Scaling group scales on the SQS queue-depth (backlog-per-instance) CloudWatch metric. CloudFront with an S3 origin is the standard, scalable, low-cost way to globally serve the static processed images. The AWS EC2 Auto Scaling guide explicitly uses this exact scenario (web app where users upload images that must be resized/encoded before publishing, with the app placing image data on an SQS queue and scaling on queue length).","explanation_zh":"選項 C 是 AWS 官方文件幾乎逐字描述的標準解耦影像處理架構。使用者將影像上傳到 S3，S3 事件通知將訊息送入 SQS 佇列，一組 EC2 執行個體從 SQS 拉取訊息進行處理（疊加文字），處理後的影像放入第二個 S3 儲存貯體並由 CloudFront 對外提供。SQS 提供持久且解耦的工作緩衝，使全球多達 10,000 名使用者的尖峰上傳不會壓垮處理機群，Auto Scaling 群組依 SQS 佇列深度（每執行個體積壓量）的 CloudWatch 指標進行擴展。CloudFront 以 S3 為來源是全球提供靜態處理後影像的標準、可擴展且低成本方式。AWS EC2 Auto Scaling 指南正是以此情境為例（使用者上傳需先調整大小/編碼再發佈的影像，應用程式將影像資料放入 SQS 佇列並依佇列長度擴展）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Using CloudWatch Logs to determine which images need processing is an anti-pattern; logs are for observability, not as a reliable work queue. EFS shared across the fleet plus EC2 as a CloudFront origin is operationally heavy and far less scalable/cheap than S3+SQS. CloudFront pointing at a single EC2 instance is a single point of failure.","why_zh":"用 CloudWatch Logs 來判斷哪些影像需要處理是反模式；Logs 用於可觀測性，而非可靠的工作佇列。整個機群共用 EFS 並以 EC2 作為 CloudFront 來源在運維上沉重，且遠不如 S3+SQS 可擴展或便宜。CloudFront 指向單一 EC2 執行個體形成單點故障。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"EC2 instances cannot 'pull' messages from Amazon SNS; SNS is push-based pub/sub, so a fleet behind an ALB polling SNS is technically invalid. SNS lacks durable buffering/backlog for batch workers, and serving images from EFS via an ALB/EC2 origin is needlessly complex and costly versus an S3 origin.","why_zh":"EC2 執行個體無法從 Amazon SNS『拉取』訊息；SNS 是以推送為基礎的發佈/訂閱機制，因此 ALB 後的機群輪詢 SNS 在技術上不成立。SNS 缺乏供批次工作者使用的持久緩衝/積壓，且透過 ALB/EC2 來源由 EFS 提供影像，相較 S3 來源既複雜又昂貴。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it is wrong: EBS volumes cannot be reliably shared read-write across a fleet of many EC2 instances (io2 Multi-Attach is limited to a small number of instances and requires a cluster-aware filesystem). Using a DynamoDB table plus EventBridge as the work-tracking/scaling mechanism is a brittle custom build versus SQS+queue-depth scaling, and serving images through an ELB/EC2 origin is costlier and less scalable than an S3/CloudFront origin.","why_zh":"這是題庫建議答案，但它是錯的：EBS 磁碟區無法可靠地在眾多 EC2 執行個體間共享讀寫（io2 Multi-Attach 僅支援少量執行個體且需具叢集感知的檔案系統）。用 DynamoDB 表加 EventBridge 作為工作追蹤/擴展機制是脆弱的自製方案，遠不如 SQS 加佇列深度擴展；透過 ELB/EC2 來源提供影像也比 S3/CloudFront 來源更貴且更不可擴展。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/as-using-sqs-queue.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/scale-sqs-queue-cli.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/example_s3_Scenario_ProcessS3EventNotification_section.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/private-content-restricting-access-to-s3.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":289,"question_en":"A company has deployed its database on an Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance in the us-east-1 Region. The company needs to make its data available to customers in Europe. The customers in Europe must have access to the same data as customers in the United States (US) and will not tolerate high application latency or stale data. The customers in Europe and the customers in the US need to write to the database. Both groups of customers need to see updates from the other group in real time. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司已将其数据库部署在 us-east-1 区域的 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库实例上。该公司需要向欧洲客户提供其数据。欧洲客户 必须能够访问与美国 (US) 客户相同的数据，并且不能容忍高应用程序延迟或过时的数据。欧洲的客户和美国的客户需要写入数据 库。两组客户都需要实时查看另一组的更新。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Aurora MySQL replica of the RDS for MySQL DB instance. Pause application writes to the RDS DB instance. Promote the Aurora Replica to a standalone DB cluster. Reconfigure the application to use the Aurora database and resume writes. Add eu-west-1 as a secondary Region to the DB cluster. Enable write forwarding on the DB cluster. Deploy the application in eu-west-1. Configure the application to use the Aurora MySQL endpoint in eu-west-1.","B":"Add a cross-Region replica in eu-west-1 for the RDS for MySQL DB instance. Configure the replica to replicate write queries back to the primary DB instance. Deploy the application in eu-west-1. Configure the application to use the RDS for MySQL endpoint in eu-west-1.","C":"Copy the most recent snapshot from the RDS for MySQL DB instance to eu-west-1. Create a new RDS for MySQL DB instance in eu-west- 1 from the snapshot. Configure MySQL logical replication from us-east-1 to eu-west-1. Enable write forwarding on the DB cluster. Deploy the application in eu-wes&1. Configure the application to use the RDS for MySQL endpoint in eu-west-1.","D":"Convert the RDS for MySQL DB instance to an Amazon Aurora MySQL DB cluster. Add eu-west-1 as a secondary Region to the DB cluster. Enable write forwarding on the DB cluster. Deploy the application in eu-west-1. Configure the application to use the Aurora MySQL endpoint in eu-west-1."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 RDS for MySQL 数据库实例的 Amazon Aurora MySQL 副本。暂停应用程序写入 RDS 数据库实例。将 Aurora 副本提升为独立 数据库集群。重新配置应用程序以使用 Aurora 数据库并恢复写入。将 eu-west-1 作为辅助区域添加到数据库集群。在数据库集群 上启用写转发。在 eu-west-1 中部署应用程序。配置应用程序以使用 eu-west-1 中的 Aurora MySQL 终端节点。","B":"在 eu-west-1 中为 RDS for MySQL 数据库实例添加跨区域副本。配置副本以将写入查询复制回主数据库实例。在 eu-west-1 中部 署应用程序。配置应用程序以使用 eu-west-1 中的 RDS for MySQL 端点。","C":"将最新快照从 RDS for MySQL 数据库实例复制到 eu-west-1。从快照在 eu-west-1 中创建新的 RDS for MySQL 数据库实例。配置从 us-east-1 到 eu-west-1 的 MySQL 逻辑复制。在数据库集群上启用写转发。在 eu-wes&1 中部署应用程序。配置应用程序以使用 eu- west-1 中的 RDS for MySQL 端点。","D":"将 RDS for MySQL 数据库实例转换为 Amazon Aurora MySQL 数据库集群。将 eu-west-1 作为辅助区域添加到数据库集群。在数据 库集群上启用写转发。在 eu-west-1 中部署应用程序。配置应用程序以使用 eu-west-1 中的 Aurora MySQL 终端节点。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":68,"D":32},"tags":["Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirements demand a single, consistent dataset that both US (us-east-1) and EU (eu-west-1) customers can write to, with each group seeing the other's updates in real time and without stale reads. Only an Amazon Aurora MySQL global database with write forwarding satisfies this: secondary-Region clusters forward write SQL to the single primary cluster (the source of truth), which then replicates changes back, avoiding multi-master write conflicts and stale data. Both A and D end in this same Aurora global database + write forwarding architecture, but A is genuinely correct because it describes the actual AWS-documented migration path: create an Aurora MySQL read replica of the RDS for MySQL instance, wait for replica lag to reach 0, pause writes, promote the Aurora Replica to a standalone Aurora DB cluster, repoint the application, then add eu-west-1 as a secondary Region and enable write forwarding. Option D's 'Convert the RDS for MySQL DB instance to an Amazon Aurora MySQL DB cluster' is not a real one-step operation - there is no in-place convert action - so A is the more accurate description of the supported procedure. The dump's suggested answer B is technically impossible: RDS for MySQL cross-Region read replicas are read-only and cannot replicate writes back to the primary, and RDS for MySQL has no write-forwarding feature.","explanation_zh":"需求要求美國 (us-east-1) 與歐洲 (eu-west-1) 客戶都能寫入同一份一致的資料，且雙方需即時看到對方的更新、不可有過期讀取。只有 Amazon Aurora MySQL global database 搭配 write forwarding 能滿足此需求：次要區域叢集會把寫入 SQL 轉發到唯一的主要叢集（資料的單一真實來源），再由主要叢集把變更複製回各區域，避免多主寫入衝突與過期資料。選項 A 與 D 最終都是相同的 Aurora global database + write forwarding 架構，但 A 才是真正正確的，因為它描述了 AWS 官方文件記載的遷移路徑：先為 RDS for MySQL 建立 Aurora MySQL read replica，待 replica lag 歸零後暫停寫入，將 Aurora Replica 提升 (promote) 為獨立 Aurora DB cluster，重新指向應用程式，再把 eu-west-1 加為次要區域並啟用 write forwarding。選項 D 的『Convert the RDS for MySQL DB instance to an Amazon Aurora MySQL DB cluster』並非真正的單步操作（不存在就地轉換的動作），因此 A 更準確描述受支援的程序。題庫建議答案 B 在技術上不可行：RDS for MySQL 的跨區域 read replica 為唯讀，無法把寫入複製回主要執行個體，且 RDS for MySQL 沒有 write forwarding 功能。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"RDS for MySQL cross-Region read replicas are read-only; you cannot 'configure the replica to replicate write queries back to the primary.' RDS for MySQL has no write-forwarding capability (only Aurora global databases do), so EU customers cannot write through this replica. This is technically impossible.","why_zh":"RDS for MySQL 的跨區域 read replica 為唯讀；無法『設定該 replica 將寫入查詢複製回主要執行個體』。RDS for MySQL 不具備 write forwarding 功能（僅 Aurora global database 有），因此歐洲客戶無法透過此 replica 寫入，技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This keeps two standalone RDS for MySQL instances and tries to 'Enable write forwarding on the DB cluster,' but there is no Aurora DB cluster here and RDS for MySQL does not support write forwarding. MySQL logical replication is one-directional and would not provide real-time bidirectional, conflict-free writes from both Regions.","why_zh":"此方案維持兩個獨立的 RDS for MySQL 執行個體，並嘗試『在 DB cluster 上啟用 write forwarding』，但此處並無 Aurora DB cluster，且 RDS for MySQL 不支援 write forwarding。MySQL logical replication 為單向，無法提供兩區域即時、無衝突的雙向寫入。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The end-state architecture (Aurora global database + write forwarding) is correct, but 'Convert the RDS for MySQL DB instance to an Amazon Aurora MySQL DB cluster' is not a real single operation - there is no in-place convert. The supported, accurately described migration (create Aurora read replica, pause writes, promote, then add the secondary Region) is what option A states, making A the more precise and correct choice.","why_zh":"最終架構（Aurora global database + write forwarding）正確，但『Convert the RDS for MySQL DB instance to an Amazon Aurora MySQL DB cluster』並非真正的單步操作——不存在就地轉換。受支援且描述準確的遷移（建立 Aurora read replica、暫停寫入、提升、再新增次要區域）正是選項 A 所述，故 A 更精確且正確。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database-write-forwarding.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database-write-forwarding-ams.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/AuroraMySQL.Migrating.RDSMySQL.Replica.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_ReadRepl.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":290,"question_en":"A company is serving files to its customers through an SFTP server that is accessible over the internet. The SFTP server is running on a single Amazon EC2 instance with an Elastic IP address attached. Customers connect to the SFTP server through its Elastic IP address and use SSH for authentication. The EC2 instance also has an attached security group that allows access from all customer IP addresses. A solutions architect must implement a solution to improve availability, minimize the complexity of infrastructure management, and minimize the disruption to customers who access files. The solution must not change the way customers connect. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司通过可通过互联网访问的 SFTP 服务器向其客户提供文件。SFTP 服务器在附加了弹性 IP 地址的单个 Amazon EC2 实例上运 行。客户通过其弹性IP地址连接到SFTP服务器并使用SSH进行身份验证。EC2 实例还具有一个附加的安全组，允许从所有客户 IP 地 址进行访问。 解决方案架构师必须实施一个解决方案来提高可用性、最大限度地降低基础设施管理的复杂性，并最大限度地减少对访问文件的客 户的干扰。该解决方案不得改变客户的连接方式。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Disassociate the Elastic IP address from the EC2 instance. Create an Amazon S3 bucket to be used for SFTP file hosting. Create an AWS Transfer Family server. Configure the Transfer Family server with a publicly accessible endpoint. Associate the SFTP Elastic IP address with the new endpoint. Point the Transfer Family server to the S3 bucket. Sync all files from the SFTP server to the S3 bucket.","B":"Disassociate the Elastic IP address from the EC2 instance. Create an Amazon S3 bucket to be used for SFTP file hosting. Create an AWS Transfer Family server. Configure the Transfer Family server with a VPC-hosted, internet-facing endpoint. Associate the SFTP Elastic IP address with the new endpoint. Attach the security group with customer IP addresses to the new endpoint. Point the Transfer Family server to the S3 bucket. Sync all files from the SFTP server to the S3 bucket.","C":"Disassociate the Elastic IP address from the EC2 instance. Create a new Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system to be used for SFTP file hosting. Create an AWS Fargate task definition to run an SFTP server. Specify the EFS file system as a mount in the task definition. Create a Fargate service by using the task definition, and place a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in front of the service. When configuring the service, attach the security group with customer IP addresses to the tasks that run the SFTP server. Associate the Elastic IP address with the NLB. Sync all files from the SFTP server to the S3 bucket.","D":"Disassociate the Elastic IP address from the EC2 instance. Create a multi-attach Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume to be used for SFTP file hosting. Create a Network Load Balancer (NLB) with the Elastic IP address attached. Create an Auto Scaling group with EC2 instances that run an SFTP server. Define in the Auto Scaling group that instances that are launched should attach the new multi- attach EBS volume. Configure the Auto Scaling group to automatically add instances behind the NLB. Configure the Auto Scaling group to use the security group that allows customer IP addresses for the EC2 instances that the Auto Scaling group launches. Sync all files from the SFTP server to the new multi-attach EBS volume."},"options_zh":{"A":"解除弹性 IP 地址与 EC2 实例的关联。创建用于 SFTP 文件托管的 Amazon S3 存储桶。创建 AWS Transfer Family 服务器。使用可 公开访问的端点配置 Transfer Family 服务器。将 SFTP 弹性 IP 地址与新端点关联。将 Transfer Family 服务器指向 S3 存储桶。将所 有文件从 SFTP 服务器同步到 S3 存储桶。","B":"解除弹性 IP 地址与 EC2 实例的关联。创建用于 SFTP 文件托管的 Amazon S3 存储桶。创建 AWS Transfer Family 服务器。使用 VPC 托管、面向 Internet 的终端节点配置 Transfer Family 服务器。将 SFTP 弹性 IP 地址与新端点关联。将具有客户 IP 地址的安全 组附加到新端点。将 Transfer Family 服务器指向 S3 存储桶。将所有文件从 SFTP 服务器同步到 S3 存储桶。 C。 取消弹性 IP 地址与 EC2 实例的关联。创建一个新的 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统以用于 SFTP 文件托 管。创建 AWS Fargate 任务定义以运行 SFTP 服务器。在任务定义中指定 EFS 文件系统作为挂载。使用任务定义创建 Fargate 服 务，并将网络负载均衡器 (NLB) 放置在该服务前面。配置服务时，将具有客户 IP 地址的安全组附加到运行 SFTP 服务器的任务。 将弹性 IP 地址与 NLB 关联。将所有文件从 SFTP 服务器同步到 S3 存储桶。 D . 取消弹性 IP 地址与 EC2 实例的关联。创建用于 SFTP 文件托管的多附加 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 卷。创建附加 弹性 IP 地址的网络负载均衡器 (NLB)。使用运行 SFTP 服务器的 EC2 实例创建 Auto Scaling 组。在 Auto Scaling 组中定义启动的实 例应附加新的多附加 EBS 卷。配置 Auto Scaling 组以自动在 NLB 后面添加实例。配置 Auto Scaling 组以使用允许 Auto Scaling 组启 动的 EC2 实例的客户 IP 地址的安全组。将 SFTP 服务器中的所有文件同步到新的多附加 EBS 卷。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":91},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirements are: improve availability, minimize infrastructure management complexity (favoring a managed service), minimize disruption, and NOT change how customers connect (they must keep using the same Elastic IP for SSH/SFTP and keep their source-IP restrictions). AWS Transfer Family is a fully managed SFTP service backed by S3, which satisfies availability and low management overhead. The deciding factor is the endpoint type matrix: only the VPC-hosted internet-facing endpoint (EndpointType=VPC, internet-facing) can attach Elastic IP addresses AND use security groups to allow access by customer source IP addresses. Option B does exactly this, preserving the existing Elastic IP and the customer-IP security group, so customers connect identically. Therefore B is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求為：提升可用性、降低基礎設施管理複雜度（偏好受管服務）、降低中斷，且不可改變客戶連線方式（客戶必須沿用相同的 Elastic IP 進行 SSH/SFTP，並維持來源 IP 限制）。AWS Transfer Family 是以 S3 為後端的全受管 SFTP 服務，可同時滿足可用性與低管理負擔。關鍵的決定因素在於 endpoint 類型矩陣：只有 VPC 託管的 internet-facing endpoint（EndpointType=VPC、internet-facing）才能附掛 Elastic IP，並可使用 security group 依客戶來源 IP 允許存取。選項 B 正是如此，保留既有的 Elastic IP 與客戶 IP 的 security group，客戶連線方式完全不變，因此 B 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The Public endpoint type cannot attach a static/Elastic IP (AWS assigns IPs that change) and does not support source-IP allow lists via security groups. Associating the existing Elastic IP and preserving customer-IP restrictions is impossible with a public endpoint, so customers' connection method would break.","why_zh":"Public endpoint 類型無法附掛靜態/Elastic IP（AWS 指派的 IP 會變動），也不支援以 security group 設定來源 IP 允許清單。無法套用既有 Elastic IP 或保留客戶 IP 限制，會破壞客戶的連線方式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Running a self-managed SFTP server on Fargate with EFS plus an NLB greatly increases infrastructure management complexity, contradicting the 'minimize complexity' requirement when a fully managed Transfer Family service exists. It also references syncing files to an S3 bucket that was never created (it uses EFS), and an NLB masks the real client source IP, complicating IP-based access control. This is the dump's suggested answer but is technically inferior and internally inconsistent.","why_zh":"在 Fargate 上以 EFS 自管 SFTP 伺服器並加上 NLB，會大幅提高基礎設施管理複雜度，與『降低複雜度』需求相違，尤其已有全受管的 Transfer Family。該選項還提到同步檔案到從未建立的 S3 bucket（實際用的是 EFS），且 NLB 會遮蔽真實客戶來源 IP，使以 IP 為基礎的存取控制更複雜。這是題庫建議答案，但技術上較差且自相矛盾。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Multi-attach EBS volumes (io1/io2) attached to multiple EC2 instances do not provide a shared file system unless you run a cluster-aware file system; you cannot simply mount one volume read-write across Auto Scaling instances for SFTP hosting safely. This is also fully self-managed with the highest operational overhead, violating the minimize-complexity requirement.","why_zh":"Multi-attach EBS 磁碟區（io1/io2）掛載到多個 EC2 並不會提供共用檔案系統，除非執行叢集感知的檔案系統；無法在 Auto Scaling 多台實例間安全地以讀寫方式掛載同一磁碟區來提供 SFTP。此方案完全自管、營運負擔最高，違反降低複雜度的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transfer/latest/userguide/sftp-for-transfer-family.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transfer/latest/userguide/create-server-in-vpc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transfer/latest/userguide/what-is-aws-transfer-family.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":291,"question_en":"A company ingests and processes streaming market data. The data rate is constant. A nightly process that calculates aggregate statistics takes 4 hours to complete. The statistical analysis is not critical to the business, and data points are processed during the next iteration if a particular run fails. The current architecture uses a pool of Amazon EC2 Reserved Instances with 1-year reservations. These EC2 instances run full time to ingest and store the streaming data in attached Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes. A scheduled script launches EC2 On-Demand Instances each night to perform the nightly processing. The instances access the stored data from NFS shares on the ingestion servers. The script terminates the instances when the processing is complete. The Reserved Instance reservations are expiring. The company needs to determine whether to purchase new reservations or implement a new design. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司摄取并处理流市场数据。数据速率是恒定的。每晚计算汇总统计数据的过程需要 4 小时才能完成。统计分析对于业务来说 并不重要，如果特定运行失败，数据点将在下一次迭代期间进行处理。 当前架构使用具有 1 年预留的 Amazon EC2 预留实例池。这些 EC2 实例全职运行，以提取流数据并将其存储在附加的 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 卷中。计划脚本每晚启动 EC2 按需实例来执行夜间处理。实例从摄取服务器上的 NFS 共享访问存储的数 据。处理完成后，脚本将终止实例。 预留实例预留即将到期。公司需要确定是否购买新的预订或实施新的设计。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Update the ingestion process to use Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to save data to Amazon S3. Use a scheduled script to launch a ­eet of EC2 On-Demand Instances each night to perform the batch processing of the S3 data. Configure the script to terminate the instances when the processing is complete.","B":"Update the ingestion process to use Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to save data to Amazon S3. Use AWS Batch with Spot Instances to perform nightly processing with a maximum Spot price that is 50% of the On-Demand price.","C":"Update the ingestion process to use a ­eet of EC2 Reserved Instances with 3-year reservations behind a Network LoadBalancer. Use AWS Batch with Spot Instances to perform nightly processing with a maximum Spot price that is 50% of the On-Demand price.","D":"Update the ingestion process to use Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to save data to Amazon Redshift. Use Amazon EventBridge to schedule an AWS Lambda function to run nightly to query Amazon Redshift to generate the daily statistics."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新提取流程以使用 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 将数据保存到 Amazon S3。使用计划脚本每晚启动一组 EC2 按需实例来执行 S3 数据的批处理。配置脚本以在处理完成时终止实例。","B":"更新提取流程以使用 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 将数据保存到 Amazon S3。将 AWS Batch 与 Spot 实例结合使用可每晚执行处 理，最高 Spot 价格为按需价格的 50%。","C":"更新摄取流程，以在网络负载均衡器后面使用一组具有 3 年预留的 EC2 预留实例。将 AWS Batch 与 Spot 实例结合使用可每晚 执行处理，最高 Spot 价格为按需价格的 50%。","D":"更新提取流程以使用 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 将数据保存到 Amazon Redshift。使用 Amazon EventBridge 安排 AWS Lambda 函数每晚运行以查询 Amazon Redshift 以生成每日统计数据。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":95},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is MOST cost-effective for a workload that is explicitly fault-tolerant: the nightly statistical analysis is non-critical and any failed run is simply reprocessed in the next iteration. That tolerance for interruption and rescheduling is the textbook criterion for EC2 Spot Instances, which run fault-tolerant workloads for up to 90% off On-Demand. Both A and B replace the always-on EC2 ingestion fleet (plus EBS volumes and NFS shares) with Kinesis Data Firehose delivering to S3, which removes the largest cost (full-time Reserved Instances) and the operational burden. The differentiator is the nightly compute: Option A uses On-Demand Instances at full price, while Option B uses AWS Batch with Spot Instances capped at 50% of On-Demand, and AWS Batch automatically provisions and terminates capacity. Because the job tolerates interruption, Spot is cheaper than On-Demand with no real downside, so B is strictly more cost-effective than A. The 4-hour runtime is longer than the 30-minute Spot sweet spot, but AWS Batch guidance explicitly says Spot is appropriate when you can tolerate interruptions and job rescheduling, which this workload can.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定詞是「最具成本效益」，而此工作負載明確具備容錯特性：每晚的統計分析並非關鍵業務，任何失敗的執行只會在下一次迭代重新處理。這種可容忍中斷與重新排程的特性，正是使用 EC2 Spot Instances 的教科書條件，Spot 可讓容錯工作負載相較 On-Demand 節省最高達 90%。選項 A 與 B 都以 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 將資料寫入 S3 來取代全時運行的 EC2 擷取機隊（以及 EBS 磁碟區與 NFS 共享），消除了最大的成本（全時 Reserved Instances）與營運負擔。差別在於每晚的運算：選項 A 以全價 On-Demand Instances 執行，選項 B 則使用 AWS Batch 搭配 Spot Instances 並將上限設為 On-Demand 價格的 50%，且 AWS Batch 會自動佈建與終止運算容量。由於此作業可容忍中斷，Spot 比 On-Demand 更便宜且無實質缺點，因此 B 嚴格優於 A。雖然 4 小時的執行時間長於 Spot 約 30 分鐘的最佳範圍，但 AWS Batch 指引明確指出：只要能容忍中斷與重新排程，Spot 即為適用，此工作負載正符合此條件。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Functionally correct (Firehose to S3, scheduled fleet that self-terminates) but uses On-Demand Instances for the nightly job. Since the workload is fault-tolerant, Spot via AWS Batch (Option B) does the same work for roughly half the price, making A less cost-effective than B.","why_zh":"功能上可行（Firehose 至 S3、排程機隊自動終止），但每晚作業使用 On-Demand Instances。由於工作負載具容錯性，透過 AWS Batch 使用 Spot（選項 B）能以約一半價格完成相同工作，因此 A 的成本效益不如 B。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Keeps an expensive always-on ingestion tier by committing to 3-year Reserved Instances behind a Network Load Balancer, instead of moving ingestion to serverless Firehose/S3. Retaining a full-time RI fleet plus an NLB is far costlier than the Firehose-to-S3 approach, so it is not the most cost-effective.","why_zh":"藉由承諾 3 年期 Reserved Instances 並置於 Network Load Balancer 之後，保留昂貴的全時擷取層，而非將擷取轉為無伺服器的 Firehose/S3。維持全時 RI 機隊加上 NLB 遠比 Firehose 至 S3 的方案昂貴，故非最具成本效益。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Technically broken: AWS Lambda has a hard 15-minute maximum timeout and cannot run a 4-hour aggregation job. It also requires a continuously running Amazon Redshift cluster, which is expensive for a once-nightly batch use case, so it neither works nor is cost-effective.","why_zh":"技術上不可行：AWS Lambda 有 15 分鐘的硬性執行上限，無法執行長達 4 小時的彙總作業。此外它需要持續運行的 Amazon Redshift 叢集，對每晚僅執行一次的批次用途而言成本高昂，因此既不可行也不具成本效益。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/batch/latest/userguide/bestpractice5.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/batch/latest/userguide/bestpractice6.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/cost-optimization-leveraging-ec2-spot-instances/when-to-use-spot-instances.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/create-destination.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/gettingstarted-limits.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":292,"question_en":"A company needs to migrate an on-premises SFTP site to AWS. The SFTP site currently runs on a Linux VM. Uploaded files are made available to downstream applications through an NFS share. As part of the migration to AWS, a solutions architect must implement high availability. The solution must provide external vendors with a set of static public IP addresses that the vendors can allow. The company has set up an AWS Direct Connect connection between its on-premises data center and its VPC. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司需要将本地 SFTP 站点迁移到 AWS。SFTP 站点当前在 Linux VM 上运行。上传的文件可通过 NFS 共享供下游应用程序使用。 作为迁移到 AWS 的一部分，解决方案架构师必须实现高可用性。该解决方案必须向外部供应商提供一组供应商允许的静态公共IP 地 址。该公司已在其本地数据中心与其 VPC 之间建立了 AWS Direct Connect 连接。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Transfer Family server. Configure an internet-facing VPC endpoint for the Transfer Family server. Specify an Elastic IP address for each subnet. Configure the Transfer Family server to place files into an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system that is deployed across multiple Availability Zones. Modify the configuration on the downstream applications that access the existing NFS share to mount the EFS endpoint instead.","B":"Create an AWS Transfer Family server. Configure a publicly accessible endpoint for the Transfer Family server. Configure the Transfer Family server to place files into an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system that is deployed across multiple Availability Zones. Modify the configuration on the downstream applications that access the existing NFS share to mount the EFS endpoint instead.","C":"Use AWS Application Migration Service to migrate the existing Linux VM to an Amazon EC2 instance. Assign an Elastic IP address to the EC2 instance. Mount an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system to the EC2 instance. Configure the SFTP server to place files in the EFS file system. Modify the configuration on the downstream applications that access the existing NFS share to mount the EFS endpoint instead.","D":"Use AWS Application Migration Service to migrate the existing Linux VM to an AWS Transfer Family server. Configure a publicly accessible endpoint for the Transfer Family server. Configure the Transfer Family server to place files into an Amazon FSx for Lustre file system that is deployed across multiple Availability Zones. Modify the configuration on the downstream applications that access the existing NFS share to mount the FSx for Lustre endpoint instead."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 AWS Transfer Family 服务器。为 Transfer Family 服务器配置面向互联网的 VPC 终端节点。为每个子网指定弹性 IP 地址。 配置 Transfer Family 服务器以将文件放入跨多个可用区部署的 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统中。修改访问现 有 NFS 共享的下游应用程序的配置以挂载 EFS 端点。","B":"创建 AWS Transfer Family 服务器。为 Transfer Family 服务器配置可公开访问的端点。配置 Transfer Family 服务器以将文件放入 跨多个可用区部署的 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统中。修改访问现有 NFS 共享的下游应用程序的配置以挂载 EFS 端点。","C":"使用 AWS Application Migration Service 将现有 Linux VM 迁移到 Amazon EC2 实例。为 EC2 实例分配弹性 IP 地址。将 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统挂载到 EC2 实例。配置SFTP服务器以将文件放置在EFS文件系统中。修改访问现有 NFS 共享的下游应用程序的配置以挂载 EFS 端点。","D":"使用 AWS Application Migration Service 将现有 Linux VM 迁移到 AWS Transfer Family 服务器。为 Transfer Family 服务器配置可公 开访问的端点。配置 Transfer Family 服务器以将文件放入跨多个可用区部署的 Amazon FSx for Lustre 文件系统中。修改访问现有 NFS 共享的下游应用程序上的配置以挂载 FSx for Lustre 端点。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement set is: high availability, a set of STATIC public IP addresses that external vendors can allowlist, an NFS-compatible share for downstream apps, and the LEAST operational overhead. The AWS Transfer Family endpoint type matrix is decisive: a 'Public' endpoint states 'You can't attach a static IP address. AWS provides IP addresses that are subject to change,' while a 'VPC - Internet' (internet-facing VPC-hosted) endpoint lets you 'attach Elastic IP addresses to the endpoint... Elastic IP addresses attached to the endpoint don't change.' Only Option A uses an internet-facing VPC endpoint with an Elastic IP per subnet, delivering the static, allowlistable IPs the vendors require. Amazon EFS is a multi-AZ, NFSv4 file system, so it provides built-in HA and can be mounted by the downstream apps in place of the existing NFS share, and Transfer Family is fully managed, giving the lowest operational overhead. Options B and D use publicly accessible endpoints whose IPs change, failing the static-IP requirement, and D is also infeasible because Application Migration Service cannot migrate a VM into a managed Transfer Family server and FSx for Lustre is not an NFS share. Option C lift-and-shifts to a single EC2 instance, which is neither highly available nor low-overhead.","explanation_zh":"需求為：高可用性、提供一組外部廠商可加入允許清單的「靜態」公用 IP、供下游應用使用的 NFS 相容共享，以及最少的營運負擔。AWS Transfer Family 的 endpoint type matrix 為關鍵依據：'Public' 端點明確說明『無法附加靜態 IP，AWS 提供的 IP 會變動』；而 'VPC - Internet'（面向網際網路的 VPC 託管）端點可『附加 Elastic IP，且附加的 Elastic IP 不會變動』。只有選項 A 採用面向網際網路的 VPC 端點，並為每個子網路指定一個 Elastic IP，提供廠商所需的靜態且可加入允許清單的 IP。Amazon EFS 是跨多個可用區的 NFSv4 檔案系統，因此內建 HA，且下游應用可掛載它以取代既有的 NFS 共享；Transfer Family 為全託管服務，營運負擔最低。選項 B 與 D 使用公用端點，其 IP 會變動，無法滿足靜態 IP 需求；D 還不可行，因為 Application Migration Service 無法將 VM 遷移成為託管的 Transfer Family 伺服器，且 FSx for Lustre 並非 NFS 共享。選項 C 將 VM lift-and-shift 至單一 EC2 執行個體，既非高可用，也非低營運負擔。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A publicly accessible (PUBLIC) Transfer Family endpoint cannot have static IPs attached; per AWS docs the IPs 'are subject to change,' so vendors cannot reliably allowlist them. This violates the static public IP requirement.","why_zh":"公開可存取（PUBLIC）的 Transfer Family 端點無法附加靜態 IP；依 AWS 文件其 IP『會變動』，廠商無法可靠地加入允許清單，違反靜態公用 IP 需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Migrating the Linux VM to a single EC2 instance with one Elastic IP provides no high availability and carries high operational overhead (self-managing, patching, and scaling the SFTP server). It fails both the HA and least-overhead goals.","why_zh":"將 Linux VM 遷移至單一 EC2 執行個體並配一個 Elastic IP，不具高可用性，且需自行管理、修補與擴展 SFTP 伺服器，營運負擔高，違反 HA 與最少營運負擔兩項目標。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Application Migration Service migrates VMs to EC2, not into a managed AWS Transfer Family server, so this step is technically impossible. It also uses a public endpoint (changing IPs) and FSx for Lustre, which is a high-performance compute file system, not an NFS share replacement.","why_zh":"Application Migration Service 是把 VM 遷移到 EC2，無法遷移成託管的 AWS Transfer Family 伺服器，此步驟在技術上不可行；且使用公用端點（IP 會變動）與 FSx for Lustre（高效能運算檔案系統，非 NFS 共享替代品）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transfer/latest/userguide/sftp-for-transfer-family.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transfer/latest/userguide/create-server-in-vpc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transfer/latest/userguide/what-is-aws-transfer-family.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":293,"question_en":"A solutions architect has an operational workload deployed on Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group. The VPC architecture spans two Availability Zones (AZ) with a subnet in each that the Auto Scaling group is targeting. The VPC is connected to an on-premises environment and connectivity cannot be interrupted. The maximum size of the Auto Scaling group is 20 instances in service. The VPC IPv4 addressing is as follows: VPC CIDR: 10.0.0.0/23 - AZ1 subnet CIDR: 10.0.0.0/24 - AZ2 subnet CIDR: 10.0.1.0/24 - Since deployment, a third AZ has become available in the Region. The solutions architect wants to adopt the new AZ without adding additional IPv4 address space and without service downtime. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师在 Auto Scaling 组中的 Amazon EC2 实例上部署了操作工作负载。VPC 架构跨越两个可用区 (AZ)，每个可用区都有一 个 Auto Scaling 组所针对的子网。VPC与本地环境连接，且连接不中断。Auto Scaling 组的最大大小为 20 个正在服务的实例。VPC IPv4 寻址如下： VPC CIDR：10.0.0.0/23 - AZ1 子网 CIDR：10.0.0.0/24 - AZ2 子网 CIDR：10.0.1.0/24 - 自部署以来，该区域已提供第三个可用区。解决方案架构师希望采用新的可用区，而无需添加额外的 IPv4 地址空间，也不会造成服 务停机。哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？ A。 更新 Auto Scaling 组以仅使用 AZ2 子网。使用先前地址空间的一半删除并重新创建 AZ1 子网。调整 Auto Scaling 组以也使用 新的 AZ1 子网。当实例运行状况良好时，将 Auto Scaling 组调整为仅使用 AZ1 子网。删除当前的 AZ2 子网。使用原始 AZ1 子网的 后半部分地址空间创建新的 AZ2 子网。使用一半的原始 AZ2 子网地址空间创建新的 AZ3 子网，然后更新 Auto Scaling 组以定位所 有三个新子网。","options_en":{"A":"Update the Auto Scaling group to use the AZ2 subnet only. Delete and re-create the AZ1 subnet using half the previous address space. Adjust the Auto Scaling group to also use the new AZ1 subnet. When the instances are healthy, adjust the Auto Scaling group to use the AZ1 subnet only. Remove the current AZ2 subnet. Create a new AZ2 subnet using the second half of the address space from the original AZ1 subnet. Create a new AZ3 subnet using half the original AZ2 subnet address space, then update the Auto Scaling group to target all three new subnets.","B":"Terminate the EC2 instances in the AZ1 subnet. Delete and re-create the AZ1 subnet using half the address space. Update the Auto Scaling group to use this new subnet. Repeat this for the second AZ. Define a new subnet in AZ3, then update the Auto Scaling group to target all three new subnets.","C":"Create a new VPC with the same IPv4 address space and define three subnets, with one for each AZ. Update the existing Auto Scaling group to target the new subnets in the new VPC.","D":"Update the Auto Scaling group to use the AZ2 subnet only. Update the AZ1 subnet to have half the previous address space. Adjust the Auto Scaling group to also use the AZ1 subnet again. When the instances are healthy, adjust the Auto Scaling group to use the AZ1 subnet only. Update the current AZ2 subnet and assign the second half of the address space from the original AZ1 subnet. Create a new AZ3 subnet using half the original AZ2 subnet address space, then update the Auto Scaling group to target all three new subnets."},"options_zh":{"B":"终止 AZ1 子网中的 EC2 实例。使用一半的地址空间删除并重新创建 AZ1 子网。更新 Auto Scaling 组以使用此新子网。对第二个 AZ 重复此操作。在 AZ3 中定义一个新子网，然后更新 Auto Scaling 组以定位所有三个新子网。","C":"创建一个具有相同 IPv4 地址空间的新 VPC，并定义三个子网，每个可用区一个子网。更新现有 Auto Scaling 组以定位新 VPC 中的新子网。","D":"更新 Auto Scaling 组以仅使用 AZ2 子网。更新 AZ1 子网以拥有先前地址空间的一半。调整 Auto Scaling 组以再次使用 AZ1 子 网。当实例运行状况良好时，将 Auto Scaling 组调整为仅使用 AZ1 子网。更新当前 AZ2 子网并分配原始 AZ1 子网的后半部分地址 空间。使用一半的原始 AZ2 子网地址空间创建新的 AZ3 子网，然后更新 Auto Scaling 组以定位所有三个新子网。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":93},"tags":["Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive technical constraint is that a subnet's IPv4 CIDR block cannot be modified or resized in place. AWS provides no API to change an existing subnet's CIDR; to change the addressing you must delete the subnet and create a new one, and a subnet can only be deleted after all instances/network interfaces in it are removed (the freed CIDR then returns to the VPC pool). Option A is the only choice that respects this: it drains an AZ by re-targeting the Auto Scaling group to the other AZ, deletes and re-creates the subnet with half the address space, then repeats, finally carving an AZ3 subnet out of freed space. By always keeping at least one AZ with healthy instances in service and never deleting the VPC, it avoids service downtime and never interrupts the on-premises (VGW/DX) connectivity, which lives at the VPC level. The math also works: the /23 VPC (512 IPs) is re-divided into three /25 subnets (128 IPs each, ~123 usable), easily covering the max 20 instances, with no additional address space added.","explanation_zh":"決定性的技術限制是：subnet 的 IPv4 CIDR 區塊無法就地修改或重新調整大小。AWS 沒有提供更改既有 subnet CIDR 的 API；若要更改定址，必須刪除 subnet 再建立新的，而且只有在移除 subnet 內所有執行個體/網路介面後才能刪除（釋放的 CIDR 會回到 VPC 位址池）。Option A 是唯一符合此限制的做法：先把 Auto Scaling group 重新指向另一個 AZ 以排空某 AZ，刪除並以一半位址空間重建 subnet，再重複此流程，最後從釋放出的空間切出 AZ3 的 subnet。由於整個過程中至少保有一個 AZ 維持健康執行個體在服務、且從未刪除 VPC，因此不會造成服務中斷，也不會中斷位於 VPC 層級的地端 (VGW/DX) 連線。位址數學也成立：/23 VPC（512 個 IP）重新切成三個 /25 subnet（各 128 個 IP、約 123 可用），足以涵蓋最多 20 台執行個體，且未新增任何位址空間。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"B abruptly terminates the EC2 instances in AZ1 without first re-targeting the Auto Scaling group to keep capacity in the other AZ, risking reduced/zero in-service capacity and service downtime. It is a cruder version of A that does not orchestrate the drain to preserve availability, so it does not meet the 'no service downtime' requirement.","why_zh":"B 在未先將 Auto Scaling group 重新指向另一 AZ 以維持容量的情況下，直接終止 AZ1 的 EC2 執行個體，可能造成服務容量降低或歸零而中斷服務。它是 A 的粗糙版本，未編排排空流程以維持可用性，因此不符合「無服務停機」的要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An Auto Scaling group can only reference subnets within a single VPC; you cannot point an existing ASG at subnets in a new VPC. A new VPC with the same CIDR also cannot connect to the same on-premises Direct Connect/VPN without overlapping routes, which would interrupt the required connectivity.","why_zh":"Auto Scaling group 只能參照同一個 VPC 內的 subnet，無法將既有 ASG 指向新 VPC 的 subnet。具有相同 CIDR 的新 VPC 也無法在不發生路由重疊的情況下連到同一條地端 Direct Connect/VPN，會中斷所要求的連線。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"D relies on 'updating' (resizing) the AZ1 and AZ2 subnets to half/reassigned address space in place. AWS does not support modifying an existing subnet's CIDR block; the only way is delete-and-recreate. This step is technically impossible, so D cannot work despite being the dump's suggested answer.","why_zh":"D 仰賴就地『更新』（重新調整大小）AZ1 與 AZ2 subnet 為一半／重新指派的位址空間。AWS 不支援修改既有 subnet 的 CIDR 區塊，唯一方式是刪除後重建。此步驟在技術上不可行，因此即使 D 是題庫建議答案，仍無法成立。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/subnet-deleting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/subnet-sizing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/configure-subnets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/as-add-az-console.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":294,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage the company's AWS accounts. The company uses AWS CloudFormation to deploy all infrastructure. A finance team wants to build a chargeback model. The finance team asked each business unit to tag resources by using a predefined list of project values. When the finance team used the AWS Cost and Usage Report in AWS Cost Explorer and filtered based on project, the team noticed noncompliant project values. The company wants to enforce the use of project tags for new resources. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST effort?","question_zh":"公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的组织来管理公司的 AWS 账户。该公司使用 AWS CloudFormation 来部署所有基础设施。财务团队想要 构建退款模型。财务团队要求每个业务部门使用预定义的项目值列表来标记资源。 当财务团队在 AWS Cost Explorer 中使用 AWS 成本和使用情况报告并根据项目进行筛选时，团队注意到不合规的项目值。该公司希望 强制对新资源使用项目标签。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a tag policy that contains the allowed project tag values in the organization's management account. Create an SCP that denies the cloudformation:CreateStack API operation unless a project tag is added. Attach the SCP to each OU.","B":"Create a tag policy that contains the allowed project tag values in each OU. Create an SCP that denies the cloudformation:CreateStack API operation unless a project tag is added. Attach the SCP to each OU.","C":"Create a tag policy that contains the allowed project tag values in the AWS management account. Create an IAM policy that denies the cloudformation:CreateStack API operation unless a project tag is added. Assign the policy to each user.","D":"Use AWS Service Catalog to manage the CloudFormation stacks as products. Use a TagOptions library to control project tag values. Share the portfolio with all OUs that are in the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建标签策略，其中包含组织管理帐户中允许的项目标签值。创建一个拒绝 cloudformation:CreateStack API 操作的 SCP，除非 添加项目标签。将 SCP 连接到每个 OU。","B":"创建一个标签策略，其中包含每个 OU 中允许的项目标签值。创建一个拒绝 cloudformation:CreateStack API 操作的 SCP，除非 添加项目标签。将 SCP 连接到每个 OU。","C":"创建包含 AWS 管理账户中允许的项目标签值的标签策略。创建拒绝 cloudformation:CreateStack API 操作的 IAM 策略，除非添加 项目标签。将策略分配给每个用户。","D":"使用 AWS Service Catalog 将 CloudFormation 堆栈作为产品进行管理。使用 TagOptions 库来控制项目标签值。与组织中的所有 OU 共享产品组合。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"AWS Organizations tag policies are created and managed in the organization's management account, where you author them and then attach them to organization entities (OUs/accounts) to standardize allowed tag values. However, tag policies alone do NOT prevent the creation of untagged resources: AWS documentation explicitly states that resources which never had tags attached don't show as noncompliant and that account administrators can still create untagged resources. AWS therefore recommends pairing tag policies with a service control policy (SCP) to 'set guardrails around resource creation requests.' Option A does exactly this combination at the org level with least effort: the tag policy in the management account constrains the allowed project values (fixing the noncompliant values the finance team saw), and an SCP that denies cloudformation:CreateStack unless a project tag is present (using aws:RequestTag/aws:TagKeys conditions) forces the tag on new stacks; the SCP is attached to each OU and centrally affects all member accounts. Option B is wrong/more effort because tag policies are authored in the management account, not 'in each OU,' so duplicating them per OU is unnecessary work. Option C scales poorly and is far more effort (an IAM deny policy assigned to every user in every account, with no central org enforcement), and tag policies are an Organizations construct, not enforced via per-user IAM. Option D forces all infrastructure through AWS Service Catalog products and a TagOptions library, a large operational/migration change that is not the least-effort path for a company already deploying directly with CloudFormation.","explanation_zh":"AWS Organizations 的 tag policy 是在組織的 management account 中建立與管理的,你在該帳戶撰寫後再附加到組織實體(OU/帳戶)以標準化允許的 tag 值。但是,tag policy 本身並無法阻止建立未加標籤的資源:AWS 文件明確指出,從未附加過標籤的資源不會顯示為不合規,且帳戶管理員仍可建立未加標籤的資源。因此 AWS 建議搭配 service control policy(SCP)來『對資源建立請求設立防護機制』。選項 A 正是以最少工作量在組織層級結合這兩者:在 management account 的 tag policy 限制允許的 project 值(修正財務團隊看到的不合規值),而 SCP 透過 aws:RequestTag/aws:TagKeys 條件拒絕未帶 project tag 的 cloudformation:CreateStack,強制新堆疊帶上標籤;此 SCP 附加到每個 OU 並集中影響所有成員帳戶。選項 B 錯誤且更費工,因為 tag policy 是在 management account 撰寫,而非『在每個 OU』建立,逐個 OU 重複建立是多餘的。選項 C 擴展性差且工作量大很多(對每個帳戶的每個使用者指派 IAM 拒絕政策,缺乏集中式組織強制),且 tag policy 屬於 Organizations 構件,並非透過個別 IAM 強制。選項 D 強迫所有基礎設施走 AWS Service Catalog 產品與 TagOptions 函式庫,對於已直接以 CloudFormation 部署的公司而言是大規模的營運/遷移變更,並非最少工作量的途徑。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Tag policies are authored in the management account, not 'in each OU.' Creating a separate tag policy in every OU is redundant duplication and more effort; you create centrally and attach to OUs.","why_zh":"Tag policy 是在 management account 撰寫,而非『在每個 OU』建立。在每個 OU 各建一份是多餘的重複且更費工;應集中建立後再附加到各 OU。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Assigning an IAM deny policy to each user across every account is high-effort, brittle, and not centrally enforced; it doesn't cover roles or new users. Tag policies are an Organizations feature, not enforced via per-user IAM, making this the wrong tool for org-wide enforcement.","why_zh":"對每個帳戶的每位使用者指派 IAM 拒絕政策工作量大、易遺漏且非集中強制;無法涵蓋角色或新使用者。Tag policy 屬於 Organizations 功能,並非以個別使用者 IAM 強制,對於全組織強制而言是錯誤工具。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Forcing all CloudFormation deployments through Service Catalog products with a TagOptions library is a major operational/migration change, not the least-effort solution for a company already deploying directly with CloudFormation.","why_zh":"強迫所有 CloudFormation 部署改走 Service Catalog 產品並使用 TagOptions 函式庫是重大的營運/遷移變更,對於已直接以 CloudFormation 部署的公司並非最少工作量的方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_example-tag-policies.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":295,"question_en":"An application is deployed on Amazon EC2 instances that run in an Auto Scaling group. The Auto Scaling group configuration uses only one type of instance. CPU and memory utilization metrics show that the instances are underutilized. A solutions architect needs to implement a solution to permanently reduce the EC2 cost and increase the utilization. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST number of configuration changes in the future?","question_zh":"应用程序部署在 Auto Scaling 组中运行的 Amazon EC2 实例上。Auto Scaling 组配置仅使用一种类型的实例。 CPU 和内存利用率指标显示实例未得到充分利用。解决方案架构师需要实施一个解决方案来永久降低 EC2 成本并提高利用率。 未来哪种解决方案能够以最少的配置更改来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"List instance types that have properties that are similar to the properties that the current instances have. Modify the Auto Scaling group's launch template configuration to use multiple instance types from the list.","B":"Use the information about the application's CPU and memory utilization to select an instance type that matches the requirements. Modify the Auto Scaling group's configuration by adding the new instance type. Remove the current instance type from the configuration.","C":"Use the information about the application's CPU and memory utilization to specify CPU and memory requirements in a new revision of the Auto Scaling group's launch template. Remove the current instance type from the configuration.","D":"Create a script that selects the appropriate instance types from the AWS Price List Bulk API. Use the selected instance types to create a new revision of the Auto Scaling group's launch template."},"options_zh":{"A":"列出具有与当前实例具有的属性相似的属性的实例类型。修改 Auto Scaling 组的启动模板配置以使用列表中的多种实例类型。","B":"根据应用程序的CPU和内存利用率信息选择符合要求的实例类型。通过添加新实例类型来修改 Auto Scaling 组的配置。从配置 中删除当前实例类型。","C":"使用有关应用程序的 CPU 和内存利用率的信息在 Auto Scaling 组启动模板的新版本中指定 CPU 和内存要求。从配置中删除当 前实例类型。","D":"创建一个脚本，从 AWS Price List Bulk API 选择适当的实例类型。使用选定的实例类型创建 Auto Scaling 组启动模板的新修订 版。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":68,"B":31},"tags":["Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The key qualifier is 'LEAST number of configuration changes in the future.' Option C uses EC2 Auto Scaling attribute-based instance type selection: instead of naming a specific instance type, you specify CPU and memory requirements (e.g., min/max vCPUs and memory) in the launch template's InstanceRequirements. Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling then automatically picks matching instance types, and per the AWS docs it will 'automatically use newer generation instance types as they're released' whenever they match the stated requirements. This right-sizes the fleet (fixing underutilization), permanently reduces cost, and requires no future config changes when AWS launches better/cheaper instance types. Option B fixes a single new static instance type, so any future right-sizing or new-generation adoption requires another manual change, which directly fails the 'least number of future changes' qualifier. C is the only choice that is both attribute-driven and future-proof.","explanation_zh":"關鍵限定詞是「未來最少的組態變更」。選項 C 使用 EC2 Auto Scaling 的 attribute-based instance type selection（屬性式執行個體類型選擇）：不指定特定執行個體類型，而是在 launch template 的 InstanceRequirements 中指定 CPU 與記憶體需求（例如 vCPU 與記憶體的上下限）。Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 會自動挑選符合條件的執行個體類型，且根據 AWS 文件，當 AWS 推出符合需求的新世代執行個體類型時會『自動採用』。這能正確調整規模（解決使用率過低）、永久降低成本，且未來 AWS 推出更佳或更便宜的執行個體類型時無需再變更組態。選項 B 只是固定換成另一個單一靜態執行個體類型，未來若要再調整規模或採用新世代類型仍須手動變更，直接違反『未來最少變更』的限定詞。C 是唯一同時兼具屬性驅動與面向未來的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Listing similar instance types and hardcoding multiple types into the launch template still requires manual research and future updates as new instance generations appear; it adds diversity but not automatic right-sizing or future-proofing via requirements.","why_zh":"列出相似類型並把多個類型硬編進 launch template，仍需人工研究，未來出現新世代執行個體時還要再更新；它增加了多樣性，卻無法透過需求達到自動調整規模與面向未來。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Selecting one new static instance type fixes utilization once, but any future re-sizing or adoption of newer/cheaper generations requires another manual configuration change, violating the 'least number of future changes' qualifier.","why_zh":"換成一個新的靜態執行個體類型只能一次性解決使用率問題，未來要重新調整規模或採用更新/更便宜的世代仍需再次手動變更組態，違反『未來最少變更』的限定詞。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Building a custom script against the Price List Bulk API to pick types and then revising the launch template is high operational overhead and still produces a static list that must be re-run and re-applied over time; it is not the attribute-based, self-updating mechanism.","why_zh":"自行撰寫腳本呼叫 Price List Bulk API 來挑選類型再修改 launch template，營運負擔高，且仍產生一份需要定期重跑與重新套用的靜態清單；並非屬性式、可自我更新的機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/create-mixed-instances-group-attribute-based-instance-type-selection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-ec2-launchtemplate-instancerequirements.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/APIReference/API_InstanceRequirements.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":296,"question_en":"A company implements a containerized application by using Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) and Amazon API Gateway The application data is stored in Amazon Aurora databases and Amazon DynamoDB databases. The company automates infrastructure provisioning by using AWS CloudFormation. The company automates application deployment by using AWS CodePipeline. A solutions architect needs to implement a disaster recovery (DR) strategy that meets an RPO of 2 hours and an RTO of 4 hours. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 和 Amazon API Gateway 实施容器化应用程序。应用程序数据存储在 Amazon Aurora 数据库和 Amazon DynamoDB 数据库中。该公司使用 AWS CloudFormation 自动化基础设施配置。该公司使用 AWS CodePipeline 自动化应用程序部署。 解决方案架构师需要实施满足 2 小时 RPO 和 4 小时 RTO 的灾难恢复 (DR) 策略。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up an Aurora global database and DynamoDB global tables to replicate the databases to a secondary AWS Region. In the primary Region and in the secondary Region, configure an API Gateway API with a Regional endpoint. Implement Amazon CloudFront with origin failover to route tra®c to the secondary Region during a DR scenario.","B":"Use AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS), Amazon EventBridge, and AWS Lambda to replicate the Aurora databases to a secondary AWS Region. Use DynamoDB Streams, EventBridge. and Lambda to replicate the DynamoDB databases to the secondary Region. In the primary Region and in the secondary Region, configure an API Gateway API with a Regional endpoint. Implement Amazon Route 53 failover routing to switch tra®c from the primary Region to the secondary Region.","C":"Use AWS Backup to create backups of the Aurora databases and the DynamoDB databases in a secondary AWS Region. In the primary Region and in the secondary Region, configure an API Gateway API with a Regional endpoint. Implement Amazon Route 53 failover routing to switch tra®c from the primary Region to the secondary Region.","D":"Set up an Aurora global database and DynamoDB global tables to replicate the databases to a secondary AWS Region. In the primary Region and in the secondary Region, configure an API Gateway API with a Regional endpoint. Implement Amazon Route 53 failover routing to switch tra®c from the primary Region to the secondary Region."},"options_zh":{"A":"设置 Aurora 全局数据库和 DynamoDB 全局表以将数据库复制到辅助 AWS 区域。在主要区域和次要区域中，使用区域终端节点 配置 API Gateway API。实施具有源故障转移功能的 Amazon CloudFront，以在灾难恢复场景期间将流量路由到次要区域。","B":"使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS)、Amazon EventBridge 和 AWS Lambda 将 Aurora 数据库复制到辅助 AWS 区域。 使用 DynamoDB 流、EventBridge。Lambda 将 DynamoDB 数据库复制到辅助区域。在主要区域和次要区域中，使用区域终端节点 配置 API Gateway API。实施 Amazon Route 53 故障转移路由，将流量从主要区域切换到次要区域。","C":"使用 AWS Backup 在辅助 AWS 区域中创建 Aurora 数据库和 DynamoDB 数据库的备份。在主要区域和次要区域中，使用区域终端 节点配置 API Gateway API。实施 Amazon Route 53 故障转移路由，将流量从主要区域切换到次要区域。","D":"设置 Aurora 全局数据库和 DynamoDB 全局表以将数据库复制到辅助 AWS 区域。在主要区域和次要区域中，使用区域终端节点 配置 API Gateway API。实施 Amazon Route 53 故障转移路由，将流量从主要区域切换到次要区域。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":59,"D":36},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is MOST cost-effective for a relaxed RPO of 2 hours and RTO of 4 hours. Because the recovery objectives are measured in hours (not seconds/minutes), a Backup and Restore strategy is sufficient and is the lowest-cost DR approach per AWS's DR whitepaper. AWS Backup supports scheduled cross-Region copies of both Aurora and DynamoDB; setting backup frequency to 2 hours or less meets the 2-hour RPO, and because the company already uses CloudFormation (infrastructure as code) and CodePipeline (application deployment), the recovery Region can be rebuilt and data restored well within the 4-hour RTO. The DR Region stores only backups (no continuously running standby databases), making it far cheaper than the global-database designs. Options A and D set up Aurora Global Database plus DynamoDB Global Tables, which deliver RPO in seconds and RTO in minutes - massively over-engineering the 2h/4h targets while incurring ongoing cost for a continuously running secondary cluster and continuous global-table replication, so neither is the MOST cost-effective. Between A and D, Route 53 failover routing (D) is the correct cross-Region traffic-switching mechanism, whereas CloudFront origin failover (A) only retries on specific HTTP errors/timeouts per request and is not a true DR routing tool, which is why the dump's suggested answer A is wrong. C is the cost-effective fit for the stated objectives.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定詞是「MOST cost-effective」，且 RPO 為 2 小時、RTO 為 4 小時這種較寬鬆的目標。由於復原目標以小時計（而非秒/分鐘），採用 Backup and Restore 策略已足夠，且依 AWS DR 白皮書，這是成本最低的災難復原方法。AWS Backup 支援對 Aurora 與 DynamoDB 進行排程的跨區域複製；將備份頻率設為 2 小時或更短即可達成 2 小時 RPO，加上公司已使用 CloudFormation（基礎設施即程式碼）與 CodePipeline（應用程式部署），可在 4 小時 RTO 內於復原區域重建環境並還原資料。災難復原區域僅存放備份（沒有持續執行的待命資料庫），因此遠比 global database 設計便宜。選項 A 與 D 建立 Aurora Global Database 與 DynamoDB Global Tables，可達到秒級 RPO 與分鐘級 RTO，對 2h/4h 目標而言嚴重過度設計，且需持續支付待命叢集與 global table 持續複製的費用，因此都不是最具成本效益的。在 A 與 D 之間，Route 53 failover routing（D）才是正確的跨區域流量切換機制；而 CloudFront origin failover（A）只在特定 HTTP 錯誤或逾時時對單一請求重試，並非真正的 DR 路由工具，這正是 dump 建議答案 A 錯誤之處。C 才是符合所述目標且最具成本效益的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Aurora Global Database + DynamoDB Global Tables over-deliver (seconds RPO, minutes RTO) and cost more than needed for a 2h/4h target. CloudFront origin failover only retries to a secondary origin on specific HTTP error status codes or connection timeouts per request; it is not a proper cross-Region DR traffic-switching mechanism and adds an unnecessary CloudFront layer/cost. This is the dump's wrong suggested answer.","why_zh":"Aurora Global Database + DynamoDB Global Tables 過度滿足需求（秒級 RPO、分鐘級 RTO），對 2h/4h 目標而言成本過高。CloudFront origin failover 只在特定 HTTP 錯誤狀態碼或連線逾時時對單一請求改連次要來源，並非真正的跨區域 DR 流量切換機制，且增加多餘的 CloudFront 層與成本。此為 dump 的錯誤建議答案。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Building custom replication with DMS, DynamoDB Streams, EventBridge, and Lambda for both databases is the highest operational-overhead and complexity option, and is not the most cost-effective. Native features (global database or AWS Backup) replace this custom plumbing entirely.","why_zh":"用 DMS、DynamoDB Streams、EventBridge 與 Lambda 為兩種資料庫自建複製，是營運負擔與複雜度最高的選項，並非最具成本效益。原生功能（global database 或 AWS Backup）可完全取代這些自建管線。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Technically valid and uses the correct Route 53 failover routing, but Aurora Global Database plus DynamoDB Global Tables run a continuously provisioned secondary cluster and continuous cross-Region replication, costing far more than necessary for a relaxed 2h/4h objective. It loses to C strictly on the MOST cost-effective qualifier.","why_zh":"技術上可行且使用正確的 Route 53 failover routing，但 Aurora Global Database 加 DynamoDB Global Tables 會持續佈建次要叢集並進行持續的跨區域複製，對寬鬆的 2h/4h 目標而言成本遠高於所需。在「最具成本效益」這個限定詞下，輸給 C。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/disaster-recovery-workloads-on-aws/disaster-recovery-options-in-the-cloud.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/point-in-time-recovery-copying.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/whatisbackup.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database-disaster-recovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/high_availability_origin_failover.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":297,"question_en":"A company has a complex web application that leverages Amazon CloudFront for global scalability and performance. Over time, users report that the web application is slowing down. The company's operations team reports that the CloudFront cache hit ratio has been dropping steadily. The cache metrics report indicates that query strings on some URLs are inconsistently ordered and are specified sometimes in mixed-case letters and sometimes in lowercase letters. Which set of actions should the solutions architect take to increase the cache hit ratio as quickly as possible?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个复杂的 Web 应用程序，该应用程序利用 Amazon CloudFront 实现全球可扩展性和性能。随着时间的推移，用户报 告 Web 应用程序速度变慢。 该公司的运营团队报告称，CloudFront 缓存命中率一直在稳步下降。缓存指标报告表明某些 URL 上的查询字符串排序不一致，并且 有时以混合大小写字母指定，有时以小写字母指定。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪组操作来尽快提高缓存命中率？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy a Lambda@Edge function to sort parameters by name and force them to be lowercase. Select the CloudFront viewer request trigger to invoke the function.","B":"Update the CloudFront distribution to disable caching based on query string parameters.","C":"Deploy a reverse proxy after the load balancer to post-process the emitted URLs in the application to force the URL strings to be lowercase.","D":"Update the CloudFront distribution to specify casing-insensitive query string processing."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署 Lambda@Edge 函数以按名称对参数进行排序并强制它们为小写。选择 CloudFront 查看器请求触发器以调用该函数。","B":"更新 CloudFront 发行版以根据查询字符串参数禁用缓存。","C":"在负载均衡器之后部署反向代理，以对应用程序中发出的 URL 进行后处理，以强制 URL 字符串为小写。","D":"更新 CloudFront 发行版以指定不区分大小写的查询字符串处理。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":92},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":298,"question_en":"A company runs an ecommerce application in a single AWS Region. The application uses a five-node Amazon Aurora MySQL DB cluster to store information about customers and their recent orders. The DB cluster experiences a large number of write transactions throughout the day. The company needs to replicate the data in the Aurora database to another Region to meet disaster recovery requirements. The company has an RPO of 1 hour. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LOWEST cost?","question_zh":"一家公司在单个 AWS 区域中运行电子商务应用程序。该应用程序使用五节点 Amazon Aurora MySQL 数据库集群来存储有关客户及其 最近订单的信息。数据库集群全天经历大量写入事务。 公司需要将Aurora数据库中的数据复制到另一个Region以满足容灾需求。该公司的 RPO 为 1 小时。 哪种解决方案能够以最低的成本满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Modify the Aurora database to be an Aurora global database. Create a second Aurora database in another Region.","B":"Enable the Backtrack feature for the Aurora database. Create an AWS Lambda function that runs daily to copy the snapshots of the database to a backup Region.","C":"Use AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS). Create a DMS change data capture (CDC) task that replicates the ongoing changes from the Aurora database to an Amazon S3 bucket in another Region.","D":"Turn off automated Aurora backups. Configure Aurora backups with a backup frequency of 1 hour. Specify another Region as the destination Region. Select the Aurora database as the resource assignment."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 Aurora 数据库修改为 Aurora 全局数据库。在另一个区域创建第二个 Aurora 数据库。","B":"启用 Aurora 数据库的 Backtrack 功能。创建每天运行的 AWS Lambda 函数，将数据库快照复制到备份区域。","C":"使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS)。创建 DMS 更改数据捕获 (CDC) 任务，将正在进行的更改从 Aurora 数据库复制 到另一个区域中的 Amazon S3 存储桶。","D":"关闭自动 Aurora 备份。配置 Aurora 备份，备份频率为 1 小时。指定另一个区域作为目标区域。选择 Aurora 数据库作为资源分 配。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":61,"A":29},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":299,"question_en":"A company's solutions architect is evaluating an AWS workload that was deployed several years ago. The application tier is stateless and runs on a single large Amazon EC2 instance that was launched from an AMI. The application stores data in a MySQL database that runs on a single EC2 instance. The CPU utilization on the application server EC2 instance often reaches 100% and causes the application to stop responding. The company manually installs patches on the instances. Patching has caused downtime in the past. The company needs to make the application highly available. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST development me?","question_zh":"一家公司的解决方案架构师正在评估几年前部署的 AWS 工作负载。应用程序层是无状态的，并在从 AMI 启动的单个大型 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。该应用程序将数据存储在在单个 EC2 实例上运行的 MySQL 数据库中。 应用服务器EC2实例上的CPU利用率经常达到100%并导致应用程序停止响应。公司在实例上手动安装补丁。过去，修补程序曾导致停 机。公司需要使应用程序具有高可用性。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的开发满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Move the application tier to AWS Lambda functions in the existing VPC. Create an Application Load Balancer to distribute tra®c across the Lambda functions. Use Amazon GuardDuty to scan the Lambda functions. Migrate the database to Amazon DocumentDB (with MongoDB compatibility.","B":"Change the EC2 instance type to a smaller Graviton powered instance type. Use the existing AMI to create a launch template for an Auto Scaling group. Create an Application Load Balancer to distribute tra®c across the instances in the Auto Scaling group. Set the Auto Scaling group to scale based on CPU utilization. Migrate the database to Amazon DynamoDB.","C":"Move the application tier to containers by using Docker. Run the containers on Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) with EC2 instances. Create an Application Load Balancer to distribute tra®c across the ECS cluster. Configure the ECS cluster to scale based on CPU utilization. Migrate the database to Amazon Neptune.","D":"Create a now AMI that is configured with AWS Systems Manager Agent (SSM Agent). Use the new AMI to create a launch template for an Auto Scaling group. Use smaller instances in the Auto Scaling group. Create an Application Load Balancer to distribute tra®c across the instances in the Auto Scaling group. Set the Auto Scaling group to scale based on CPU utilization. Migrate the database to Amazon Aurora MySQL."},"options_zh":{"A":"将应用程序层移至现有 VPC 中的 AWS Lambda 函数。创建应用程序负载均衡器以跨 Lambda 函数分配流量。使用 Amazon GuardDuty 扫描 Lambda 函数。将数据库迁移到 Amazon DocumentDB（与 MongoDB 兼容）。","B":"将 EC2 实例类型更改为较小的 Graviton 支持的实例类型。使用现有 AMI 为 Auto Scaling 组创建启动模板。创建应用程序负载均 衡器以在 Auto Scaling 组中的实例之间分配流量。将 Auto Scaling 组设置为根据 CPU 利用率进行扩展。将数据库迁移到 Amazon DynamoDB。","C":"使用 Docker 将应用层移至容器。使用 EC2 实例在 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 上运行容器。创建应用程序负 载均衡器以跨 ECS 集群分配流量。配置 ECS 集群以根据 CPU 利用率进行扩展。将数据库迁移到 Amazon Neptune。","D":"现在创建一个配置有 AWS Systems Manager 代理（SSM 代理）的 AMI。使用新的 AMI 为 Auto Scaling 组创建启动模板。在 Auto Scaling 组中使用较小的实例。创建应用程序负载均衡器以在 Auto Scaling 组中的实例之间分配流量。将 Auto Scaling 组设置为根 据 CPU 利用率进行扩展。将数据库迁移到 Amazon Aurora MySQL。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":300,"question_en":"A company is planning to migrate several applications to AWS. The company does not have a good understanding of its entire application estate. The estate consists of a mixture of physical machines and VMs. One application that the company will migrate has many dependencies that are sensitive to latency. The company is unsure what all the dependencies are. However the company knows that the low-latency communications use a custom IP-based protocol that runs on port 1000. The company wants to migrate the application and these dependencies together to move all the low-latency interfaces to AWS at the same time. The company has installed the AWS Application Discovery Agent and has been collecting data for several months. What should the company do to identify the dependencies that need to be migrated in the same phase as the application?","question_zh":"一家公司正计划将多个应用程序迁移到 AWS。该公司对其整个应用领域并没有很好的了解。该资产由物理机和虚拟机混合组成。 公司将迁移的一款应用程序具有许多对延迟敏感的依赖项。该公司不确定所有依赖项是什么。然而，该公司知道低延迟通信使用在 端口 1000 上运行的基于 IP 的自定义协议。该公司希望将应用程序和这些依赖项一起迁移，以同时将所有低延迟接口迁移到 AWS。 该公司已安装 AWS Application Discovery Agent，并已收集数据数月。 公司应该如何识别需要与应用程序同一阶段迁移的依赖项？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Migration Hub and select the servers that host the application. Visualize the network graph to find servers that interact with the application. Turn on data exploration in Amazon Athena. Query the data that is transferred between the servers to identify the servers that communicate on port 1000. Return to Migration Hub. Create a move group that is based on the findings from the Athena queries.","B":"Use AWS Application Migration Service and select the servers that host the application. Visualize the network graph to find servers that interact with the application. Configure Application Migration Service to launch test instances for all the servers that interact with the application. Perform acceptance tests on the test instances. If no issues are identified, create a move group that is based on the tested servers.","C":"Use AWS Migration Hub and select the servers that host the application. Turn on data exploration in Network Access Analyzer. Use the Network Access Analyzer console to select the servers that host the application. Select a Network Access Scope of port 1000 and note the matching servers. Return to Migration Hub. Create a move group that is based on the findings from Network Access Analyzer.","D":"Use AWS Migration Hub and select the servers that host the application. Push the Amazon CloudWalch agent to the identified servers by using the AWS Application Discovery Agent. Export the CloudWatch logs that the agents collect to Amazon S3. Use Amazon Athena to query the logs to find servers that communicate on port 1000. Return to Migration Hub Create a move group that is based on the findings from the Athena queries."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Migration Hub 并选择托管应用程序的服务器。可视化网络图以查找与应用程序交互的服务器。在 Amazon Athena 中 启用数据探索。查询服务器之间传输的数据，以识别在端口 1000 上通信的服务器。返回到 Migration Hub。根据 Athena 查询的结 果创建一个移动组。","B":"使用 AWS Application Migration Service 并选择托管应用程序的服务器。可视化网络图以查找与应用程序交互的服务器。配置应 用程序迁移服务以启动与应用程序交互的所有服务器的测试实例。对测试实例执行验收测试。如果未发现任何问题，请创建基 于已测试服务器的移动组。","C":"使用 AWS Migration Hub 并选择托管应用程序的服务器。在网络访问分析器中打开数据探索。使用网络访问分析器控制台选择 托管应用程序的服务器。选择端口 1000 的网络访问范围并记下匹配的服务器。返回迁移中心。根据网络访问分析器的结果创建 移动组。","D":"使用 AWS Migration Hub 并选择托管应用程序的服务器。使用 AWS Application Discovery Agent 将 Amazon CloudWalch 代理推送到 已识别的服务器。将代理收集的 CloudWatch 日志导出到 Amazon S3。使用 Amazon Athena 查询日志以查找在端口 1000 上通信的 服务器。 返回 Migration Hub 根据 Athena 查询的结果创建移动组。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":95},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":301,"question_en":"A company is building an application that will run on an AWS Lambda function. Hundreds of customers will use the application. The company wants to give each customer a quota of requests for a specific time period. The quotas must match customer usage patterns. Some customers must receive a higher quota for a shorter time period. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在构建将在 AWS Lambda 函数上运行的应用程序。数百名客户将使用该应用程序。该公司希望为每个客户提供特定时间 段内的请求配额。配额必须符合客户的使用模式。一些客户必须在更短的时间内获得更高的配额。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon API Gateway REST API with a proxy integration to invoke the Lambda function. For each customer, configure an API Gateway usage plan that includes an appropriate request quota. Create an API key from the usage plan for each user that the customer needs.","B":"Create an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API with a proxy integration to invoke the Lambda function. For each customer configure an API Gateway usage plan that includes an appropriate request quota Configure route-level throttling for each usage plan. Create an API Key from the usage plan for each user that the customer needs.","C":"Create a Lambda function alias for each customer. Include a concurrency limit with an appropriate request quota. Create a Lambda function URL for each function alias. Share the Lambda function URL for each alias with the relevant customer.","D":"Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in a VPC. Configure the Lambda function as a target for the ALB. Configure an AWS WAF web ACL for the ALB. For each customer configure a rale-based rule that includes an appropriate request quota."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建具有代理集成的 Amazon API Gateway REST API 以调用 Lambda 函数。为每个客户配置一个包含适当请求配额的 API Gateway 使用计划。根据使用计划为客户需要的每个用户创建 API 密钥。","B":"创建具有代理集成的 Amazon API Gateway HTTP API 以调用 Lambda 函数。为每个客户配置一个 API Gateway 使用计划，其中包 括适当的请求配额 为每个使用计划配置路由级限制。根据使用计划为客户需要的每个用户创建 API 密钥。","C":"为每个客户创建 Lambda 函数别名。包括具有适当请求配额的并发限制。为每个函数别名创建 Lambda 函数 URL。与相关客户 共享每个别名的 Lambda 函数 URL。","D":"在 VPC 中创建应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB)。将 Lambda 函数配置为 ALB 的目标。为 ALB 配置 AWS WAF Web ACL。为每个客户配 置基于规则的规则，其中包括适当的请求配额。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":86},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":302,"question_en":"A company is planning to migrate its on-premises VMware cluster of 120 VMs to AWS. The VMs have many different operating systems and many custom software packages installed. The company also has an on-premises NFS server that is 10 TB in size. The company has set up a 10 Gbps AWS Direct Connect connection to AWS for the migration. Which solution will complete the migration to AWS in the LEAST amount of time?","question_zh":"一家公司计划将其包含 120 个虚拟机的本地 VMware 集群迁移到 AWS。虚拟机安装了许多不同的操作系统和许多自定义软件包。该 公司还有一个大小为 10 TB 的本地 NFS 服务器。该公司已建立与 AWS 的 10 Gbps AWS Direct Connect 连接以进行迁移。 哪种解决方案能够在最短的时间内完成到 AWS 的迁移？","options_en":{"A":"Export the on-premises VMs and copy them to an Amazon S3 bucket. Use VM Import/Export to create AMIs from the VM images that are stored in Amazon S3. Order an AWS Snowball Edge device. Copy the NFS server data to the device. Restore the NFS server data to an Amazon EC2 instance that has NFS configured.","B":"Configure AWS Application Migration Service with a connection to the VMware cluster. Create a replication job for the VMS. Create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. Configure AWS DataSync to copy the NFS server data to the EFS file system over the Direct Connect connection.","C":"Recreate the VMs on AWS as Amazon EC2 instances. Install all the required software packages. Create an Amazon FSx for Lustre file system. Configure AWS DataSync to copy the NFS server data to the FSx for Lustre file system over the Direct Connect connection.","D":"Order two AWS Snowball Edge devices. Copy the VMs and the NFS server data to the devices. Run VM Import/Export after the data from the devices is loaded to an Amazon S3 bucket. Create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. Copy the NFS server data from Amazon S3 to the EFS file system."},"options_zh":{"A":"导出本地 VM 并将其复制到 Amazon S3 存储桶。使用 VM Import/Export 从存储在 Amazon S3 中的 VM 映像创建 AMI。订购 AWS Snowball Edge 设备。将 NFS 服务器数据复制到设备。将 NFS 服务器数据恢复到配置了 NFS 的 Amazon EC2 实例。","B":"配置 AWS Application Migration Service 并连接到 VMware 集群。为 VMS 创建复制作业。创建 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统。配置 AWS DataSync 以通过 Direct Connect 连接将 NFS 服务器数据复制到 EFS 文件系统。","C":"在 AWS 上将虚拟机重新创建为 Amazon EC2 实例。安装所有必需的软件包。创建 Amazon FSx for Lustre 文件系统。配置 AWS DataSync 以通过 Direct Connect 连接将 NFS 服务器数据复制到 FSx for Lustre 文件系统。","D":"订购两个 AWS Snowball Edge 设备。将虚拟机和 NFS 服务器数据复制到设备。将设备中的数据加载到 Amazon S3 存储桶后运行 VM Import/Export。创建 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统。将 NFS 服务器数据从 Amazon S3 复制到 EFS 文件系 统。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":93},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":303,"question_en":"An online survey company runs its application in the AWS Cloud. The application is distributed and consists of microservices that run in an automatically scaled Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster. The ECS cluster is a target for an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The ALB is a custom origin for an Amazon CloudFront distribution. The company has a survey that contains sensitive data. The sensitive data must be encrypted when it moves through the application. The application's data-handling microservice is the only microservice that should be able to decrypt the data Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家在线调查公司在 AWS 云中运行其应用程序。该应用程序是分布式的，由在自动扩展的 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 集群中运行的微服务组成。ECS 集群是应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 的目标。ALB 是 Amazon CloudFront 分配的自定义源。 该公司有一项包含敏感数据的调查。敏感数据在应用程序中移动时必须进行加密。应用程序的数据处理微服务是唯一能够解密数据 的微服务 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a symmetric AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key that is dedicated to the data-handling microservice. Create a field- level encryption profile and a configuration. Associate the KMS key and the configuration with the CloudFront cache behavior.","B":"Create an RSA key pair that is dedicated to the data-handing microservice. Upload the public key to the CloudFront distribution. Create a field-level encryption profile and a configuration. Add the configuration to the CloudFront cache behavior.","C":"Create a symmetric AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key that is dedicated to the data-handling microservice. Create a Lambda@Edge function. Program the function to use the KMS key to encrypt the sensitive data.","D":"Create an RSA key pair that is dedicated to the data-handling microservice. Create a Lambda@Edge function. Program the function to use the private key of the RSA key pair to encrypt the sensitive data."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建专用于数据处理微服务的对称 AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) 密钥。创建字段级加密配置文件和配置。将 KMS 密 钥和配置与 CloudFront 缓存行为关联。","B":"创建专用于数据处理微服务的 RSA 密钥对。将公钥上传到 CloudFront 分配。创建字段级加密配置文件和配置。将配置添加到 CloudFront 缓存行为。","C":"创建专用于数据处理微服务的对称 AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) 密钥。创建 Lambda@Edge 函数。对函数进行编程 以使用 KMS 密钥加密敏感数据。","D":"创建专用于数据处理微服务的 RSA 密钥对。创建 Lambda@Edge 函数。对该函数进行编程，以使用 RSA 密钥对的私钥来加密敏 感数据。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":86},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":304,"question_en":"A solutions architect is determining the DNS strategy for an existing VPC. The VPC is provisioned to use the 10.24.34.0/24 CIDR block. The VPC also uses Amazon Route 53 Resolver for DNS. New requirements mandate that DNS queries must use private hosted zones. Additionally instances that have public IP addresses must receive corresponding public hostnames Which solution will meet these requirements to ensure that the domain names are correctly resolved within the VPC?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师正在确定现有 VPC 的 DNS 策略。VPC 配置为使用 10.24.34.0/24 CIDR 块。VPC 还使用 Amazon Route 53 Resolver 作为 DNS。新要求强制 DNS 查询必须使用私有托管区域。此外，具有公共 IP 地址的实例必须接收相应的公共主机名。 哪种解决方案将满足这些要求，以确保域名在 VPC 内正确解析？","options_en":{"A":"Create a private hosted zone. Activate the enableDnsSupport attribute and the enableDnsHostnames attribute for the VPC. Update the VPC DHCP options set to include domain-name-servers=10.24.34.2.","B":"Create a private hosted zone Associate the private hosted zone with the VPC. Activate the enableDnsSupport attribute and the enableDnsHostnames attribute for the VPC. Create a new VPC DHCP options set, and configure domain-name- servers=AmazonProvidedDNS. Associate the new DHCP options set with the VPC.","C":"Deactivate the enableDnsSupport attribute for the VPActivate the enableDnsHostnames attribute for the VPCreate a new VPC DHCP options set, and configure doman-name-servers=10.24.34.2. Associate the new DHCP options set with the VPC.","D":"Create a private hosted zone. Associate the private hosted zone with the VPC. Activate the enableDnsSupport attribute for the VPC. Deactivate the enableDnsHostnames attribute for the VPC. Update the VPC DHCP options set to include domain-name- servers=AmazonProvidedDNS."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建私有托管区域。激活VPC的enableDnsSupport属性和enableDnsHostnames属性。更新 VPC DHCP 选项集以包括domain-name- servers=10.24.34.2。","B":"创建私有托管区 将私有托管区与VPC 关联。激活VPC的enableDnsSupport属性和enableDnsHostnames属性。创建新的 VPC DHCP 选项集，并配置domain-name-servers=AmazonProvidedDNS。将新的 DHCP 选项集与 VPC 关联。","C":"停用 VP 的enableDnsSupport 属性激活VP 的enableDnsHostnames 属性创建新的VPC DHCP 选项集，并配置doman-name- servers=10.24.34.2。将新的 DHCP 选项集与 VPC 关联。","D":"创建私有托管区域。将私有托管区域与 VPC 关联。激活VPC的enableDnsSupport属性。停用 VPC 的enableDnsHostnames 属性。 更新 VPC DHCP 选项集以包括domain-name-servers=AmazonProvidedDNS。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":305,"question_en":"A data analytics company has an Amazon Redshift cluster that consists of several reserved nodes. The cluster is experiencing unexpected bursts of usage because a team of employees is compiling a deep audit analysis report. The queries to generate the report are complex read queries and are CPU intensive. Business requirements dictate that the cluster must be able to service read and write queries at all times. A solutions architect must devise a solution that accommodates the bursts of usage. Which solution meets these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家数据分析公司拥有一个由多个保留节点组成的 Amazon Redshift 集群。由于员工团队正在编写深入的审计分析报告，因此集群正 在经历意外的使用激增。生成报告的查询是复杂的读取查询，并且是 CPU 密集型的。 业务需求决定集群必须能够始终为读写查询提供服务。解决方案架构师必须设计一种能够适应突发使用的解决方案。 哪种解决方案最经济高效地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Provision an Amazon EMR cluster O¯oad the complex data processing tasks.","B":"Deploy an AWS Lambda function to add capacity to the Amazon Redshift cluster by using a classic resize operation when the cluster’s CPU metrics in Amazon CloudWatch reach 80%.","C":"Deploy an AWS Lambda function to add capacity to the Amazon Redshift cluster by using an elastic resize operation when the cluster’s CPU metrics in Amazon CloudWatch reach 80%.","D":"Turn on the Concurrency Scaling feature for the Amazon Redshift cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 Amazon EMR 集群 减轻复杂的数据处理任务。","B":"当 Amazon CloudWatch 中集群的 CPU 指标达到 80% 时，部署 AWS Lambda 函数以使用经典的调整大小操作向 Amazon Redshift 集群添加容量。","C":"部署 AWS Lambda 函数，以便在 Amazon CloudWatch 中的集群 CPU 指标达到 80% 时，使用弹性调整大小操作向 Amazon Redshift 集群添加容量。","D":"打开 Amazon Redshift 集群的并发扩展功能。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":306,"question_en":"A research center is migrating to the AWS Cloud and has moved its on-premises 1 PB object storage to an Amazon S3 bucket. One hundred scientists are using this object storage to store their work-related documents. Each scientist has a personal folder on the object store. All the scientists are members of a single IAM user group. The research center's compliance o®cer is worried that scientists will be able to access each other's work. The research center has a strict obligation to report on which scientist accesses which documents. The team that is responsible for these reports has little AWS experience and wants a ready-to-use solution that minimizes operational overhead. Which combination of actions should a solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家研究中心正在迁移到 AWS 云，并将其本地 1 PB 对象存储迁移到 Amazon S3 存储桶。一百名科学家正在使用此对象存储来存储 他们的工作相关文档。每个科学家在对象存储上都有一个个人文件夹。所有科学家都是同一个 IAM 用户组的成员。 该研究中心的合规官员担心科学家们将能够访问彼此的工作成果。研究中心有严格的义务报告哪些科学家访问了哪些文件。负责这 些报告的团队几乎没有 AWS 经验，并且需要一个现成的解决方案来最大限度地减少运营开销。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪些操作组合来满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an identity policy that grants the user read and write access. Add a condition that specifies that the S3 paths must be prefixed with $(aws:username). Apply the policy on the scientists’ IAM user group.","B":"Configure a trail with AWS CloudTrail to capture all object-level events in the S3 bucket. Store the trail output in another S3 bucket. Use Amazon Athena to query the logs and generate reports.","C":"Enable S3 server access logging. Configure another S3 bucket as the target for log delivery. Use Amazon Athena to query the logs and generate reports.","D":"Create an S3 bucket policy that grants read and write access to users in the scientists’ IAM user group.","E":"Configure a trail with AWS CloudTrail to capture all object-level events in the S3 bucket and write the events to Amazon CloudWatch. Use the Amazon Athena CloudWatch connector to query the logs and generate reports."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建授予用户读写访问权限的身份策略。添加一个条件，指定 S3 路径必须以 $(aws:username) 为前缀。将策略应用于科学家 的 IAM 用户组。","B":"使用 AWS CloudTrail 配置跟踪以捕获 S3 存储桶中的所有对象级事件。将跟踪输出存储在另一个 S3 存储桶中。使用 Amazon Athena 查询日志并生成报告。","C":"启用 S3 服务器访问日志记录。配置另一个S3存储桶作为日志传送的目标。使用 Amazon Athena 查询日志并生成报告。","D":"创建一个 S3 存储桶策略，向科学家的 IAM 用户组中的用户授予读写访问权限。","E":"使用 AWS CloudTrail 配置跟踪以捕获 S3 存储桶中的所有对象级事件并将这些事件写入 Amazon CloudWatch。使用 Amazon Athena CloudWatch 连接器查询日志并生成报告。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AB":74,"AC":16},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・複選"},{"id":307,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage a multi-account structure. The company has hundreds of AWS accounts and expects the number of accounts to increase. The company is building a new application that uses Docker images. The company will push the Docker images to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). Only accounts that are within the company’s organization should have access to the images. The company has a CI/CD process that runs frequently. The company wants to retain all the tagged images. However, the company wants to retain only the five most recent untagged images. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理多账户结构。该公司拥有数百个 AWS 账户，预计账户数量还会增加。该公司正在构建一个使 用 Docker 镜像的新应用程序。该公司将把 Docker 镜像推送到 Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR)。只有公司组织内的帐 户才有权访问这些图像。 该公司有一个频繁运行的 CI/CD 流程。该公司希望保留所有标记的图像。然而，该公司希望只保留最近的五张未标记的图像。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a private repository in Amazon ECR. Create a permissions policy for the repository that allows only required ECR operations. Include a condition to allow the ECR operations if the value of the aws:PrincipalOrglD condition key is equal to the ID of the company’s organization. Add a lifecycle rule to the ECR repository that deletes all untagged images over the count of five","B":"Create a public repository in Amazon ECR. Create an IAM role in the ECR account. Set permissions so that any account can assume the role if the value of the aws:PrincipalOrglD condition key is equal to the ID of the company’s organization. Add a lifecycle rule to the ECR repository that deletes all untagged images over the count of five.","C":"Create a private repository in Amazon ECR. Create a permissions policy for the repository that includes only required ECR operations. Include a condition to allow the ECR operations for all account IDs in the organization Schedule a daily Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function that deletes all untagged images over the count of five.","D":"Create a public repository in Amazon ECR. Configure Amazon ECR to use an interface VPC endpoint with an endpoint policy that includes the required permissions for images that the company needs to pull. Include a condition to allow the ECR operations for all account IDs in the company’s organization. Schedule a daily Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function that deletes all untagged images over the count of five."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon ECR 中创建私有存储库。为存储库创建仅允许所需的 ECR 操作的权限策略。如果 aws:PrincipalOrglD 条件键的值等于 公司组织的 ID，请包括允许 ECR 操作的条件。向 ECR 存储库添加生命周期规则，删除超过 5 个的所有未标记图像","B":"在 Amazon ECR 中创建公共存储库。在 ECR 账户中创建 IAM 角色。设置权限，以便在 aws:PrincipalOrglD 条件键的值等于公司 组织的 ID 时任何账户都可以代入该角色。将生命周期规则添加到 ECR 存储库，删除超过 5 个的所有未标记图像。","C":"在 Amazon ECR 中创建私有存储库。为存储库创建仅包含所需 ECR 操作的权限策略。包含一个条件以允许对组织中的所有账户 ID 进行 ECR 操作 安排每日 Amazon EventBridge 规则来调用 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数将删除超过 5 个的所有未标记图像。","D":"在 Amazon ECR 中创建公共存储库。配置 Amazon ECR 以使用接口 VPC 终端节点以及终端节点策略，其中包含公司需要拉取的 映像所需的权限。包括允许对公司组织中的所有账户 ID 进行 ECR 操作的条件。安排每日 Amazon EventBridge 规则来调用 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数将删除超过 5 个的所有未标记图像。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":308,"question_en":"A solutions architect is reviewing a company's process for taking snapshots of Amazon RDS DB instances. The company takes automatic snapshots every day and retains the snapshots for 7 days. The solutions architect needs to recommend a solution that takes snapshots every 6 hours and retains the snapshots for 30 days. The company uses AWS Organizations to manage all of its AWS accounts. The company needs a consolidated view of the health of the RDS snapshots. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师正在审查公司拍摄 Amazon RDS 数据库实例快照的流程。公司每天自动进行快照，快照保留7天。 解决方案架构师需要推荐一种每 6 小时拍摄一次快照并将快照保留 30 天的解决方案。该公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理其所有 AWS 账户。该公司需要 RDS 快照运行状况的综合视图。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Turn on the cross-account management feature in AWS Backup. Create a backup plan that specifies the frequency and retention requirements. Add a tag to the DB instances. Apply the backup plan by using tags. Use AWS Backup to monitor the status of the backups.","B":"Turn on the cross-account management feature in Amazon RDS. Create a snapshot global policy that specifies the frequency and retention requirements. Use the RDS console in the management account to monitor the status of the backups.","C":"Turn on the cross-account management feature in AWS CloudFormation. From the management account, deploy a CloudFormation stack set that contains a backup plan from AWS Backup that specifies the frequency and retention requirements. Create an AWS Lambda function in the management account to monitor the status of the backups. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule in each account to run the Lambda function on a schedule.","D":"Configure AWS Backup in each account. Create an Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager lifecycle policy that specifies the frequency and retention requirements. Specify the DB instances as the target resource Use the Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager console in each member account to monitor the status of the backups."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS Backup 中打开跨账户管理功能。创建指定频率和保留要求的备份计划。向数据库实例添加标签。使用标签应用备份计 划。使用 AWS Backup 监控备份的状态。","B":"在 Amazon RDS 中打开跨账户管理功能。创建指定频率和保留要求的快照全局策略。使用管理帐户中的 RDS 控制台监控备份的 状态。","C":"在 AWS CloudFormation 中打开跨账户管理功能。从管理账户中，部署一个 CloudFormation 堆栈集，其中包含 AWS Backup 中指 定频率和保留要求的备份计划。在管理账户中创建 AWS Lambda 函数来监控备份的状态。在每个账户中创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则以按计划运行 Lambda 函数。","D":"在每个账户中配置 AWS Backup。创建指定频率和保留要求的 Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager 生命周期策略。将数据库实例指定 为目标资源 使用每个成员账户中的 Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager 控制台来监控备份的状态。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":309,"question_en":"A company is using AWS Organizations with a multi-account architecture. The company's current security configuration for the account architecture includes SCPs, resource-based policies, identity-based policies, trust policies, and session policies. A solutions architect needs to allow an IAM user in Account A to assume a role in Account B. Which combination of steps must the solutions architect take to meet this requirement? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用具有多账户架构的 AWS Organizations。公司当前账户架构的安全配置包括SCP、基于资源的策略、基于身份的策 略、信任策略和会话策略。 解决方案架构师需要允许账户 A 中的 IAM 用户承担账户 B 中的角色。 解决方案架构师必须采取哪些步骤组合才能满足此要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure the SCP for Account A to allow the action.","B":"Configure the resource-based policies to allow the action.","C":"Configure the identity-based policy on the user in Account A to allow the action.","D":"Configure the identity-based policy on the user in Account B to allow the action.","E":"Configure the trust policy on the target role in Account B to allow the action.","F":"Configure the session policy to allow the action and to be passed programmatically by the GetSessionToken API operation."},"options_zh":{"A":"为账户 A 配置 SCP 以允许该操作。","B":"配置基于资源的策略以允许该操作。","C":"在账户 A 中的用户上配置基于身份的策略以允许该操作。","D":"在账户 B 中的用户上配置基于身份的策略以允许该操作。","E":"在账户 B 中的目标角色上配置信任策略以允许该操作。","F":"配置会话策略以允许该操作并由 GetSessionToken API 操作以编程方式传递。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ACE":56,"BCE":26},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・複選"},{"id":310,"question_en":"A company wants to use Amazon S3 to back up its on-premises file storage solution. The company’s on-premises file storage solution supports NFS, and the company wants its new solution to support NFS. The company wants to archive the backup files after 5 days. If the company needs archived files for disaster recovery, the company is willing to wait a few days for the retrieval of those files. Which solution meets these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司希望使用 Amazon S3 来备份其本地文件存储解决方案。该公司的本地文件存储解决方案支持 NFS，并且该公司希望其新解 决方案支持 NFS。该公司希望在 5 天后归档备份文件。如果公司需要归档文件进行灾难恢复，公司愿意等待几天来检索这些文件。 哪种解决方案最经济高效地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an AWS Storage Gateway file gateway that is associated with an S3 bucket. Move the files from the on-premises file storage solution to the file gateway. Create an S3 Lifecycle rule to move the files to S3 Standard-Infrequent Access (S3 Standard-IA) after 5 days.","B":"Deploy an AWS Storage Gateway volume gateway that is associated with an S3 bucket. Move the files from the on-premises file storage solution to the volume gateway. Create an S3 Lifecycle rule to move the files to S3 Glacier Deep Archive after 5 days.","C":"Deploy an AWS Storage Gateway tape gateway that is associated with an S3 bucket. Move the files from the on-premises file storage solution to the tape gateway. Create an S3 Lifecycle rule to move the files to S3 Standard-Infrequent Access (S3 Standard-IA) after 5 days.","D":"Deploy an AWS Storage Gateway file gateway that is associated with an S3 bucket. Move the files from the on-premises file storage solution to the file gateway. Create an S3 Lifecycle rule to move the files to S3 Glacier Deep Archive after 5 days."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署与 S3 存储桶关联的 AWS Storage Gateway 文件网关。将文件从本地文件存储解决方案移动到文件网关。创建 S3 生命周期 规则以在 5 天后将文件移至 S3 标准-不频繁访问 (S3 标准-IA)。","B":"部署与 S3 存储桶关联的 AWS Storage Gateway 卷网关。将文件从本地文件存储解决方案移动到卷网关。创建 S3 生命周期规则 以在 5 天后将文件移至 S3 Glacier Deep Archive。","C":"部署与 S3 存储桶关联的 AWS Storage Gateway 磁带网关。将文件从本地文件存储解决方案移动到磁带网关。创建 S3 生命周期 规则以在 5 天后将文件移至 S3 标准-不频繁访问 (S3 标准-IA)。","D":"部署与 S3 存储桶关联的 AWS Storage Gateway 文件网关。将文件从本地文件存储解决方案移动到文件网关。创建 S3 生命周期 规则以在 5 天后将文件移至 S3 Glacier Deep Archive。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":311,"question_en":"A company runs its application on Amazon EC2 instances and AWS Lambda functions. The EC2 instances experience a continuous and stable load. The Lambda functions experience a varied and unpredictable load. The application includes a caching layer that uses an Amazon MemoryDB for Redis cluster. A solutions architect must recommend a solution to minimize the company's overall monthly costs. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 Amazon EC2 实例和 AWS Lambda 函数上运行其应用程序。EC2 实例承受持续稳定的负载。Lambda 函数会经历变化且不 可预测的负载。该应用程序包括一个使用 Amazon MemoryDB for Redis 集群的缓存层。 解决方案架构师必须推荐一种解决方案，以最大限度地降低公司的每月总体成本。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Purchase an EC2 instance Savings Plan to cover the EC2 instances. Purchase a Compute Savings Plan for Lambda to cover the minimum expected consumption of the Lambda functions. Purchase reserved nodes to cover the MemoryDB cache nodes.","B":"Purchase a Compute Savings Plan to cover the EC2 instances. Purchase Lambda reserved concurrency to cover the expected Lambda usage. Purchase reserved nodes to cover the MemoryDB cache nodes.","C":"Purchase a Compute Savings Plan to cover the entire expected cost of the EC2 instances, Lambda functions, and MemoryDB cache nodes.","D":"Purchase a Compute Savings Plan to cover the EC2 instances and the MemoryDB cache nodes. Purchase Lambda reserved concurrency to cover the expected Lambda usage."},"options_zh":{"A":"购买 EC2 实例 Savings Plan 以涵盖 EC2 实例。购买 Lambda 计算节省计划以满足 Lambda 函数的最低预期消耗。购买预留节点 来覆盖MemoryDB缓存节点。","B":"购买计算节省计划以涵盖 EC2 实例。购买 Lambda 预留并发以满足预期的 Lambda 使用量。购买预留节点来覆盖MemoryDB缓 存节点。","C":"购买计算节省计划以涵盖 EC2 实例、Lambda 函数和 MemoryDB 缓存节点的全部预期成本。","D":"购买计算节省计划以涵盖 EC2 实例和 MemoryDB 缓存节点。购买 Lambda 预留并发以满足预期的 Lambda 使用量。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":88},"tags":["Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The workload has three distinct components, each needing a different cost-optimization mechanism. (1) EC2 has a continuous, stable load, so an EC2 Instance Savings Plan delivers the deepest discount (up to 72% off On-Demand) for a committed instance family/Region. (2) Lambda has varied, unpredictable load; a Compute Savings Plan covering only the minimum expected (baseline) consumption guarantees savings on usage you will always incur, while the unpredictable spikes stay on On-Demand. (3) MemoryDB for Redis is NOT eligible for any Savings Plan (Compute Savings Plans cover only EC2, Fargate, and Lambda; Database Savings Plans cover ElastiCache but not MemoryDB), so the correct discount mechanism is MemoryDB reserved nodes. Option A combines all three correctly. Option C is technically impossible because a Compute Savings Plan cannot apply to MemoryDB. Options B and D both rely on Lambda reserved concurrency, which only reserves concurrency capacity and provides no billing discount, so they fail to minimize cost.","explanation_zh":"此工作負載有三個不同元件，各需不同的成本最佳化機制。(1) EC2 為持續且穩定的負載，因此 EC2 Instance Savings Plan 可提供最深折扣（相較 On-Demand 最高 72%），承諾特定執行個體系列/區域即可。(2) Lambda 負載多變且不可預測；以 Compute Savings Plan 僅涵蓋最低預期（基線）用量，可保證對一定會產生的用量取得折扣，而不可預測的尖峰仍維持 On-Demand。(3) MemoryDB for Redis 不符合任何 Savings Plan 資格（Compute Savings Plans 僅涵蓋 EC2、Fargate、Lambda；Database Savings Plans 涵蓋 ElastiCache 但不含 MemoryDB），因此正確的折扣機制是 MemoryDB reserved nodes。選項 A 正確結合三者。選項 C 技術上不可能，因為 Compute Savings Plan 無法套用於 MemoryDB。選項 B 與 D 都依賴 Lambda reserved concurrency，但它只是預留並行容量、不提供任何帳單折扣，因此無法將成本降到最低。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Lambda reserved concurrency only reserves concurrency capacity for predictable invocation; it does not lower the price of Lambda usage, so it provides no cost savings. A Compute Savings Plan on the minimum Lambda consumption (as in A) is the actual cost mechanism.","why_zh":"Lambda reserved concurrency 只是為可預測的呼叫預留並行容量，並不會降低 Lambda 使用價格，因此無成本節省。針對 Lambda 最低用量購買 Compute Savings Plan（如 A）才是真正的省錢機制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Technically impossible: a Compute Savings Plan applies only to EC2, Fargate, and Lambda. It cannot cover MemoryDB cache nodes at all, so this option cannot meet the requirement. This is the dump's suggested answer and it is wrong.","why_zh":"技術上不可能：Compute Savings Plan 僅適用於 EC2、Fargate、Lambda，完全無法涵蓋 MemoryDB 快取節點，故無法滿足需求。此為題庫建議答案，且為錯誤。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Two flaws: a Compute Savings Plan cannot be applied to MemoryDB cache nodes (only reserved nodes can), and Lambda reserved concurrency gives no billing discount. Both errors mean it does not minimize cost.","why_zh":"兩處錯誤：Compute Savings Plan 無法套用於 MemoryDB 快取節點（僅 reserved nodes 可），且 Lambda reserved concurrency 不提供帳單折扣。兩者皆使其無法將成本降到最低。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/savingsplans/latest/userguide/plan-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/savingsplans/latest/userguide/what-is-savings-plans.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/memorydb/latest/devguide/nodes.reservednodes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/savingsplans/latest/userguide/sp-applying.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":312,"question_en":"A company is launching a new online game on Amazon EC2 instances. The game must be available globally. The company plans to run the game in three AWS Regions us-east-1, eu-west-1, and ap-southeast-1. The game's leaderboards, player inventory and event status must be available across Regions. A solutions architect must design a solution that will give any Region the ability to scale to handle the load of all Regions. Additionally, users must automatically connect to the Region that provides the least latency. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 Amazon EC2 实例上推出一款新的在线游戏。该游戏必须在全球范围内发售。该公司计划在三个 AWS 区域 us-east-1、 eu-west-1 和 ap-southeast-1 运行该游戏。游戏的排行榜、玩家库存和活动状态必须跨区域可用。 解决方案架构师必须设计一个解决方案，使任何区域都能够扩展以处理所有区域的负载。此外，用户必须自动连接到提供最少延迟 的区域。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an EC2 Spot Fleet. Attach the Spot Fleet to a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in each Region. Create an AWS Global Accelerator IP address that points to the NLB. Create an Amazon Route 53 latency-based routing entry for the Global Accelerator IP address. Save the game metadata to an Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance in each Region. Set up a read replica in the other Regions.","B":"Create an Auto Scaling group for the EC2 instances Attach the Auto Scaling group to a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in each Region. For each Region, create an Amazon Route 53 entry that uses geoproximity routing and points to the NLB in that Region. Save the game metadata to MySQL databases on EC2 instances in each Region. Set up replication between the database EC2 instances in each Region.","C":"Create an Auto Scaling group for the EC2 instances. Attach the Auto Scaling group to a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in each Region. For each Region, create an Amazon Route 53 entry that uses latency-based routing and points to the NLB in that Region. Save the game metadata to an Amazon DynamoDB global table.","D":"Use EC2 Global View. Deploy the EC2 instances to each Region. Attach the instances to a Network Load Balancer (NLB). Deploy a DNS server on an EC2 instance in each Region. Set up custom logic on each DNS server to redirect the user to the Region that provides the lowest latency. Save the game metadata to an Amazon Aurora global database."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 EC2 Spot 队列。将 Spot 队列附加到每个区域中的网络负载均衡器 (NLB)。创建指向 NLB 的 AWS Global Accelerator IP 地 址。为 Global Accelerator IP 地址创建 Amazon Route 53 基于延迟的路由条目。将游戏元数据保存到每个区域中的 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库实例。在其他区域设置只读副本。","B":"为 EC2 实例创建 Auto Scaling 组 将 Auto Scaling 组附加到每个区域中的网络负载均衡器 (NLB)。对于每个区域，创建一个使用 地理位置邻近路由并指向该区域中的 NLB 的 Amazon Route 53 条目。将游戏元数据保存到每个区域的 EC2 实例上的 MySQL 数据 库。在每个区域中的数据库 EC2 实例之间设置复制。","C":"为 EC2 实例创建 Auto Scaling 组。将 Auto Scaling 组附加到每个区域中的网络负载均衡器 (NLB)。对于每个区域，创建一个 Amazon Route 53 条目，该条目使用基于延迟的路由并指向该区域中的 NLB。将游戏元数据保存到 Amazon DynamoDB 全局表。","D":"使用 EC2 全局视图。将 EC2 实例部署到每个区域。将实例附加到网络负载均衡器 (NLB)。在每个区域的 EC2 实例上部署 DNS 服务器。在每个 DNS 服务器上设置自定义逻辑，将用户重定向到提供最低延迟的区域。将游戏元数据保存到 Amazon Aurora 全局 数据库。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":313,"question_en":"A company is deploying a third-party firewall appliance solution from AWS Marketplace to monitor and protect tra®c that leaves the company's AWS environments. The company wants to deploy this appliance into a shared services VPC and route all outbound internet-bound tra®c through the appliances. A solutions architect needs to recommend a deployment method that prioritizes reliability and minimizes failover time between firewall appliances within a single AWS Region. The company has set up routing from the shared services VPC to other VPCs. Which steps should the solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在部署 AWS Marketplace 中的第三方防火墙设备解决方案，以监控和保护离开该公司 AWS 环境的流量。该公司希望将此 设备部署到共享服务 VPC 中，并通过这些设备路由所有出站互联网流量。 解决方案架构师需要推荐一种部署方法，该方法优先考虑可靠性并最大限度地减少单个 AWS 区域内防火墙设备之间的故障转移时 间。该公司已设置从共享服务 VPC 到其他 VPC 的路由。 解决方案架构师应该建议采取哪些步骤来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Deploy two firewall appliances into the shared services VPC, each in a separate Availability Zone.","B":"Create a new Network Load Balancer in the shared services VPC. Create a new target group, and attach it to the new Network Load Balancer. Add each of the firewall appliance instances to the target group.","C":"Create a new Gateway Load Balancer in the shared services VPCreate a new target group, and attach it to the new Gateway Load Balancer Add each of the firewall appliance instances to the target group.","D":"Create a VPC interface endpoint. Add a route to the route table in the shared services VPC. Designate the new endpoint as the next hop for tra®c that enters the shared services VPC from other VPCs.","E":"Deploy two firewall appliances into the shared services VPC, each in the same Availability Zone.","F":"Create a VPC Gateway Load Balancer endpoint. Add a route to the route table in the shared services VPC. Designate the new endpoint as the next hop for tra®c that enters the shared services VPC from other VPCs."},"options_zh":{"A":"将两个防火墙设备部署到共享服务 VPC 中，每个设备位于单独的可用区中。","B":"在共享服务 VPC 中创建新的网络负载均衡器。创建新的目标组，并将其附加到新的网络负载均衡器。将每个防火墙设备实例 添加到目标组。","C":"在共享服务 VP 中创建新的网关负载均衡器 创建新的目标组，并将其附加到新的网关负载均衡器 将每个防火墙设备实例添加 到目标组。","D":"创建 VPC 接口终端节点。将路由添加到共享服务 VPC 中的路由表。将新终端节点指定为从其他 VPC 进入共享服务 VPC 的流量 的下一跃点。","E":"将两个防火墙设备部署到共享服务 VPC 中，每个设备位于同一可用区。","F":"创建 VPC 网关负载均衡器终端节点。将路由添加到共享服务 VPC 中的路由表。将新终端节点指定为从其他 VPC 进入共享服务 VPC 的流量的下一跃点。"},"answer":["A","C","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ACF":89},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・複選"},{"id":314,"question_en":"A solutions architect needs to migrate an on-premises legacy application to AWS. The application runs on two servers behind a load balancer. The application requires a license file that is associated with the MAC address of the server's network adapter It takes the software vendor 12 hours to send new license files. The application also uses configuration files with a static IP address to access a database server, host names are not supported. Given these requirements, which combination of steps should be taken to implement highly available architecture for the application servers in AWS? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"解决方案架构师需要将本地旧应用程序迁移到 AWS。该应用程序在负载平衡器后面的两台服务器上运行。该应用程序需要与服务器 网络适配器的 MAC 地址关联的许可证文件。软件供应商需要 12 小时才能发送新的许可证文件。该应用程序还使用具有静态IP地址 的配置文件来访问数据库服务器，不支持主机名。 考虑到这些要求，应该采取哪些步骤组合来为 AWS 中的应用程序服务器实现高可用架构？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a pool of ENIs. Request license files from the vendor for the pool, and store the license files in Amazon S3. Create a bootstrap automation script to download a license file and attach the corresponding ENI to an Amazon EC2 instance.","B":"Create a pool of ENIs. Request license files from the vendor for the pool, store the license files on an Amazon EC2 instance. Create an AMI from the instance and use this AMI for all future EC2 instances.","C":"Create a bootstrap automation script to request a new license file from the vendor .When the response is received, apply the license file to an Amazon EC2 instance.","D":"Edit the bootstrap automation script to read the database server IP address from the AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store, and inject the value into the local configuration files.","E":"Edit an Amazon EC2 instance to include the database server IP address in the configuration files and re-create the AMI to use for all future EC2 stances."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 ENI 池。向池供应商请求许可证文件，并将许可证文件存储在 Amazon S3 中。创建引导自动化脚本以下载许可证文件并将 相应的 ENI 附加到 Amazon EC2 实例。","B":"创建 ENI 池。向池供应商请求许可证文件，将许可证文件存储在 Amazon EC2 实例上。从实例创建 AMI 并将此 AMI 用于所有未 来的 EC2 实例。","C":"创建引导自动化脚本以向供应商请求新的许可证文件。收到响应后，将许可证文件应用到 Amazon EC2 实例。","D":"编辑引导自动化脚本以从 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store 读取数据库服务器 IP 地址，并将该值注入到本地配置文件中。","E":"编辑 Amazon EC2 实例以将数据库服务器 IP 地址包含在配置文件中，并重新创建 AMI 以用于未来的所有 EC2 立场。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AD":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":315,"question_en":"A company runs its sales reporting application in an AWS Region in the United States. The application uses an Amazon API Gateway Regional API and AWS Lambda functions to generate on-demand reports from data in an Amazon RDS for MySQL database. The frontend of the application is hosted on Amazon S3 and is accessed by users through an Amazon CloudFront distribution. The company is using Amazon Route 53 as the DNS service for the domain. Route 53 is configured with a simple routing policy to route tra®c to the API Gateway API. In the next 6 months, the company plans to expand operations to Europe. More than 90% of the database tra®c is read-only tra®c. The company has already deployed an API Gateway API and Lambda functions in the new Region. A solutions architect must design a solution that minimizes latency for users who download reports. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在美国的 AWS 区域运行其销售报告应用程序。该应用程序使用 Amazon API Gateway Regional API 和 AWS Lambda 函数根据 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库中的数据生成按需报告。该应用程序的前端托管在 Amazon S3 上，用户可以通过 Amazon CloudFront 发 行版进行访问。该公司使用 Amazon Route 53 作为域的 DNS 服务。Route 53 配置了一个简单的路由策略，用于将流量路由到 API Gateway API。 未来6个月内，该公司计划将业务扩展至欧洲。超过90%的数据库流量是只读流量。该公司已经在新区域部署了 API Gateway API 和 Lambda 函数。 解决方案架构师必须设计一种解决方案，最大限度地减少下载报告的用户的延迟。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use an AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) task with full load to replicate the primary database in the original Region to the database in the new Region. Change the Route 53 record to latency-based routing to connect to the API Gateway API.","B":"Use an AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) task with full load plus change data capture (CDC) to replicate the primary database in the original Region to the database in the new Region. Change the Route 53 record to geolocation routing to connect to the API Gateway API.","C":"Configure a cross-Region read replica for the RDS database in the new Region Change the Route 53 record to latency-based routing to connect to the API Gateway API.","D":"Configure a cross-Region read replica for the RDS database in the new Region. Change the Route 53 record to geolocation routing to connect to the API Gateway API."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用满负载的 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 任务将原始区域中的主数据库复制到新区域中的数据库。将 Route 53 记录更改为基于延迟的路由以连接到 API Gateway API。","B":"使用具有完全加载和更改数据捕获 (CDC) 功能的 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 任务将原始区域中的主数据库复制 到新区域中的数据库。将 Route 53 记录更改为地理位置路由以连接到 API Gateway API。","C":"在新区域中为 RDS 数据库配置跨区域只读副本 将 Route 53 记录更改为基于延迟的路由以连接到 API Gateway API。","D":"在新Region中为RDS数据库配置跨Region只读副本。将 Route 53 记录更改为地理位置路由以连接到 API Gateway API。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":96},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Two decisions drive this answer. First, more than 90% of database traffic is read-only, so an RDS for MySQL cross-Region read replica is the purpose-built, low-overhead way to serve reads from the new European Region; AWS describes read replicas as the feature for elastically scaling out read-heavy workloads with built-in asynchronous replication. AWS DMS full-load only (A) makes a one-time copy with no ongoing sync, so reports go stale, and DMS full-load+CDC (B) is far more operationally complex than a native read replica and is intended for migrations, not as a permanent read-scaling architecture. Second, the requirement is to minimize latency for users downloading reports. Route 53 latency-based routing explicitly directs each DNS query to the AWS Region that provides the lowest network latency, which is exactly the stated goal. Geolocation routing routes by the user's geographic location and is intended for content localization and compliance, not latency optimization, and a geographically nearer Region is not always the lowest-latency one. Therefore the correct combination is cross-Region read replica plus latency-based routing (C). The dump's suggested D pairs the right database choice with the wrong routing policy.","explanation_zh":"兩個關鍵決策決定了答案。第一，超過 90% 的資料庫流量是唯讀，因此 RDS for MySQL 的跨區域 read replica 是專為此設計、低維運負擔的方式，可在新的歐洲區域提供讀取服務；AWS 將 read replica 定義為以內建非同步複寫來彈性擴展讀取密集型工作負載的功能。AWS DMS 僅 full load（A）只做一次性複製、沒有持續同步，報表會過時；DMS full load+CDC（B）相較原生 read replica 維運複雜許多，且 DMS 是為遷移而設計，並非作為長期讀取擴展架構。第二，需求是為下載報表的使用者降低延遲。Route 53 latency-based routing 明確會把每個 DNS 查詢導向提供最低網路延遲的 AWS 區域，正好符合需求。Geolocation routing 是依使用者地理位置路由，用於內容在地化與合規，而非延遲最佳化，而且地理上較近的區域不一定延遲最低。因此正確組合是跨區域 read replica 加上 latency-based routing（C）。題庫建議的 D 把正確的資料庫選擇配上錯誤的路由策略。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"DMS full-load only performs a one-time copy with no change data capture, so the European database never receives ongoing updates and reports become stale; a native read replica is also far simpler for continuous read scaling. (Routing policy is correct, but the data layer is wrong.)","why_zh":"DMS 僅 full load 只做一次性複製、無 CDC，歐洲資料庫不會持續更新，報表會過時；原生 read replica 對持續讀取擴展也更簡單。（路由策略正確，但資料層錯誤。）"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Both parts are wrong for this scenario: DMS full-load+CDC adds unnecessary operational complexity versus a native RDS cross-Region read replica for a homogeneous MySQL read-scaling use case, and geolocation routing optimizes by user location rather than lowest latency.","why_zh":"兩部分都不適合：對同質 MySQL 讀取擴展案例，DMS full-load+CDC 相較原生 RDS 跨區域 read replica 增加不必要的維運複雜度；而 geolocation routing 依使用者位置最佳化，而非最低延遲。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The cross-Region read replica is correct, but geolocation routing routes by geographic location (for localization/compliance), not by lowest network latency. The requirement explicitly is to minimize latency, which is what latency-based routing delivers; a nearer Region is not guaranteed to be the lowest-latency one.","why_zh":"跨區域 read replica 正確，但 geolocation routing 是依地理位置路由（用於在地化/合規），而非最低網路延遲。需求明確是要降低延遲，這正是 latency-based routing 的功能；較近的區域不保證延遲最低。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-latency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-geo.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_ReadRepl.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_ReadRepl.XRgn.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":316,"question_en":"A software company needs to create short-lived test environments to test pull requests as part of its development process. Each test environment consists of a single Amazon EC2 instance that is in an Auto Scaling group. The test environments must be able to communicate with a central server to report test results. The central server is located in an on- premises data center. A solutions architect must implement a solution so that the company can create and delete test environments without any manual intervention. The company has created a transit gateway with a VPN attachment to the on-premises network. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"软件公司需要创建短期测试环境来测试拉取请求，作为其开发过程的一部分。每个测试环境均包含 Auto Scaling 组中的单个 Amazon EC2 实例。 测试环境必须能够与中央服务器通信以报告测试结果。中央服务器位于本地数据中心。解决方案架构师必须实施解决方案，以便公 司无需任何手动干预即可创建和删除测试环境。该公司创建了一个中转网关，其中包含连接到本地网络的 VPN 连接。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template that contains a transit gateway attachment and related routing configurations. Create a CloudFormation stack set that includes this template. Use CloudFormation StackSets to deploy a new stack for each VPC in the account. Deploy a new VPC for each test environment.","B":"Create a single VPC for the test environments. Include a transit gateway attachment and related routing configurations. Use AWS CloudFormation to deploy all test environments into the VPC.","C":"Create a new OU in AWS Organizations for testing. Create an AWS CioudFormation template that contains a VPC, necessary networking resources, a transit gateway attachment, and related routing configurations. Create a CloudFormation stack set that includes this template. Use CloudFormation StackSets for deployments into each account under the testing OU. Create a new account for each test environment.","D":"Convert the test environment EC2 instances into Docker images. Use AWS CloudFormation to configure an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster in a new VPC, create a transit gateway attachment, and create related routing configurations. Use Kubernetes to manage the deployment and lifecycle of the test environments."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，其中包含中转网关附件和相关路由配置。创建包含此模板的 CloudFormation 堆栈集。使 用 CloudFormation StackSets 为账户中的每个 VPC 部署新堆栈。为每个测试环境部署新的 VPC。","B":"为测试环境创建单个 VPC。包括中转网关连接和相关路由配置。使用 AWS CloudFormation 将所有测试环境部署到 VPC 中。","C":"在 AWS Organizations 中创建新的 OU 进行测试。创建一个 AWS CioudFormation 模板，其中包含 VPC、必要的网络资源、中转网 关附件和相关路由配置。创建包含此模板的 CloudFormation 堆栈集。使用 CloudFormation StackSets 部署到测试 OU 下的每个账 户。为每个测试环境创建一个新帐户。","D":"将测试环境 EC2 实例转换为 Docker 镜像。使用 AWS CloudFormation 在新 VPC 中配置 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 集群、创建中转网关附件并创建相关路由配置。使用 Kubernetes 管理测试环境的部署和生命周期。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":83,"A":17},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":317,"question_en":"A company is deploying a new API to AWS. The API uses Amazon API Gateway with a Regional API endpoint and an AWS Lambda function for hosting. The API retrieves data from an external vendor API, stores data in an Amazon DynamoDB global table, and retrieves data from the DynamoDB global table The API key for the vendor's API is stored in AWS Secrets Manager and is encrypted with a customer managed key in AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS). The company has deployed its own API into a single AWS Region. A solutions architect needs to change the API components of the company’s API to ensure that the components can run across multiple Regions in an active-active configuration. Which combination of changes will meet this requirement with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在向 AWS 部署新的 API。该 API 使用 Amazon API Gateway 以及区域 API 终端节点和 AWS Lambda 函数进行托管。API 从外 部供应商 API 检索数据，将数据存储在 Amazon DynamoDB 全局表中，并从 DynamoDB 全局表检索数据 供应商 API 的 API 密钥存储在 AWS Secrets Manager 中，并使用 AWS 中的客户托管密钥进行加密密钥管理服务 (AWS KMS)。该公司已将自己的 API 部署到单个 AWS 区域中。 解决方案架构师需要更改公司API的API组件，以确保组件能够以双活配置跨多个Region运行。 哪种变更组合能够以最少的运营开销满足这一要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the API to multiple Regions. Configure Amazon Route 53 with custom domain names that route tra®c to each Regional API endpoint. Implement a Route 53 multivalue answer routing policy.","B":"Create a new KMS multi-Region customer managed key. Create a new KMS customer managed replica key in each in-scope Region.","C":"Replicate the existing Secrets Manager secret to other Regions. For each in-scope Region's replicated secret, select the appropriate KMS key.","D":"Create a new AWS managed KMS key in each in-scope Region. Convert an existing key to a multiRegion key. Use the multi-Region key in other Regions.","E":"Create a new Secrets Manager secret in each in-scope Region. Copy the secret value from the existing Region to the new secret in each in-scope Region.","F":"Modify the deployment process for the Lambda function to repeat the deployment across in-scope Regions. Turn on the multi-Region option for the existing API. Select the Lambda function that is deployed in each Region as the backend for the multi-Region API."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 API 部署到多个区域。使用自定义域名配置 Amazon Route 53，将流量路由到每个区域 API 终端节点。实施 Route 53 多值应 答路由策略。","B":"创建新的 KMS 多区域客户管理密钥。在每个范围内区域创建新的 KMS 客户管理副本密钥。","C":"将现有 Secrets Manager 密钥复制到其他区域。对于每个范围内区域的复制密钥，选择适当的 KMS 密钥。","D":"在每个范围内区域创建新的 AWS 托管 KMS 密钥。将现有密钥转换为多区域密钥。在其他区域使用多区域密钥。","E":"在每个范围内区域创建新的 Secrets Manager 密钥。将密钥值从现有区域复制到每个范围内区域中的新密钥。","F":"修改 Lambda 函数的部署过程以跨范围内的区域重复部署。为现有 API 启用多区域选项。选择部署在每个区域中的 Lambda 函 数作为多区域 API 的后端。"},"answer":["A","B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ABC":79,"BCF":21},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・複選"},{"id":318,"question_en":"An online retail company hosts its stateful web-based application and MySQL database in an on-premises data center on a single server. The company wants to increase its customer base by conducting more marketing campaigns and promotions. In preparation, the company wants to migrate its application and database to AWS to increase the reliability of its architecture. Which solution should provide the HIGHEST level of reliability?","question_zh":"一家在线零售公司将其基于 Web 的状态应用程序和 MySQL 数据库托管在单个服务器上的本地数据中心中。该公司希望通过开展更 多营销活动和促销活动来扩大客户群。在准备过程中，该公司希望将其应用程序和数据库迁移到 AWS，以提高其架构的可靠性。 哪种解决方案应提供最高级别的可靠性？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate the database to an Amazon RDS MySQL Multi-AZ DB instance. Deploy the application in an Auto Scaling group on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer. Store sessions in Amazon Neptune","B":"Migrate the database to Amazon Aurora MySQL. Deploy the application in an Auto Scaling group on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer. Store sessions in an Amazon ElastiCache for Redis replication group.","C":"Migrate the database to Amazon DocumentDB (with MongoDB compatibility). Deploy the application in an Auto Scaling group on Amazon EC2 instances behind a Network Load Balancer Store sessions in Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose.","D":"Migrate the database to an Amazon RDS MariaDB Multi-AZ DB instance. Deploy the application in an Auto Scaling group on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer. Store sessions in Amazon ElastiCache for Memcached."},"options_zh":{"A":"将数据库迁移到 Amazon RDS MySQL 多可用区数据库实例。将应用程序部署在应用程序负载均衡器后面的 Amazon EC2 实例上 的 Auto Scaling 组中。Amazon Neptune 中的存储会话","B":"将数据库迁移到 Amazon Aurora MySQL。将应用程序部署在应用程序负载均衡器后面的 Amazon EC2 实例上的 Auto Scaling 组 中。将会话存储在 Amazon ElastiCache for Redis 复制组中。","C":"将数据库迁移到 Amazon DocumentDB（兼容 MongoDB）。将应用程序部署在 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 中网络负载均衡器存 储会话后面的 Amazon EC2 实例上的 Auto Scaling 组中。","D":"将数据库迁移到 Amazon RDS MariaDB 多可用区数据库实例。将应用程序部署在应用程序负载均衡器后面的 Amazon EC2 实例上 的 Auto Scaling 组中。将会话存储在 Amazon ElastiCache for Memcached 中。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":319,"question_en":"A company’s solutions architect needs to provide secure Remote Desktop connectivity to users for Amazon EC2 Windows instances that are hosted in a VPC. The solution must integrate centralized user management with the company's on-premises Active Directory. Connectivity to the VPC is through the internet. The company has hardware that can be used to establish an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"公司的解决方案架构师需要为 VPC 中托管的 Amazon EC2 Windows 实例的用户提供安全的远程桌面连接。该解决方案必须将集中式 用户管理与公司的本地 Active Directory 集成。与 VPC 的连接是通过互联网进行的。该公司拥有可用于建立 AWS 站点到站点 VPN 连 接的硬件。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy a managed Active Directory by using AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory. Establish a trust with the on-premises Active Directory. Deploy an EC2 instance as a bastion host in the VPC. Ensure that the EC2 instance is joined to the domain. Use the bastion host to access the target instances through RDP.","B":"Configure AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) to integrate with the on-premises Active Directory by using the AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory AD Connector. Configure permission sets against user groups for access to AWS Systems Manager. Use Systems Manager Fleet Manager to access the target instances through RDP.","C":"Implement a VPN between the on-premises environment and the target VPEnsure that the target instances are joined to the on- premises Active Directory domain over the VPN connection. Configure RDP access through the VPN. Connect from the company’s network to the target instances.","D":"Deploy a managed Active Directory by using AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory. Establish a trust with the on-premises Active Directory. Deploy a Remote Desktop Gateway on AWS by using an AWS Quick Start. Ensure that the Remote Desktop Gateway is joined to the domain. Use the Remote Desktop Gateway to access the target instances through RDP."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory 部署托管 Active Directory。与本地 Active Directory 建立信任。在 VPC 中 部署 EC2 实例作为堡垒主机。确保 EC2 实例已加入域。使用堡垒主机通过RDP访问目标实例。","B":"使用 AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory AD Connector 将 AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) 配置为与本 地 Active Directory 集成。针对用户组配置权限集以访问 AWS Systems Manager。使用 Systems Manager Fleet Manager 通过 RDP 访 问目标实例。","C":"在本地环境和目标 VP 之间实施 VPN 确保目标实例通过 VPN 连接加入本地 Active Directory 域。通过 VPN 配置 RDP 访问。从公 司网络连接到目标实例。","D":"使用 AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory 部署托管 Active Directory。与本地 Active Directory 建立信任。使用 AWS 快速入门在 AWS 上部署远程桌面网关。确保远程桌面网关已加入域。使用远程桌面网关通过 RDP 访问目标实例。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":49,"C":47},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The deciding qualifier is MOST cost-effective, and all options must deliver secure RDP, centralized user management tied to on-premises AD, and internet-based connectivity. Option B is cheapest because it uses AD Connector, a lightweight directory gateway that proxies authentication to on-premises AD without hosting any AD instances in the cloud (far cheaper than AWS Managed Microsoft AD, which both A and D require). IAM Identity Center connects to a self-managed Active Directory through AD Connector for centralized identity and permission-set assignment. Systems Manager Fleet Manager Remote Desktop (GUI Connect, powered by Amazon DCV) provides secure RDP over the SSM channel through the internet with no inbound ports opened, no bastion or RD Gateway EC2 instance to run, and no Site-to-Site VPN to maintain; Fleet Manager RDP itself carries no extra charge. Options A and D both incur the cost of AWS Managed Microsoft AD plus a continuously running EC2 host and a forest trust, and Option C requires a 24/7 VPN tunnel plus managing domain joins and RDP exposure over it, all of which cost more or add operational overhead than the AD Connector + Fleet Manager approach.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定條件是 MOST cost-effective（最具成本效益）。所有選項都必須提供安全的 RDP、與地端 AD 整合的集中式使用者管理，以及透過網際網路的連線。選項 B 最便宜，因為它使用 AD Connector——一個輕量的目錄閘道，將驗證請求代理回地端 AD，而不在雲端託管任何 AD 執行個體（比 A 與 D 都需要的 AWS Managed Microsoft AD 便宜許多）。IAM Identity Center 透過 AD Connector 連接自管的 Active Directory，達成集中式身分與權限集（permission set）指派。Systems Manager Fleet Manager Remote Desktop（GUI Connect，由 Amazon DCV 提供）透過 SSM 通道在網際網路上提供安全 RDP，不需開放任何入站連接埠、不需運行 bastion 或 RD Gateway EC2 執行個體，也不需維護 Site-to-Site VPN；Fleet Manager RDP 本身不額外收費。選項 A 與 D 都需承擔 AWS Managed Microsoft AD 加上持續運行的 EC2 主機與樹系信任的成本；選項 C 需要 24/7 的 VPN 通道並管理網域加入與 RDP 暴露，這些都比 AD Connector + Fleet Manager 方案成本更高或維運負擔更重。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Requires AWS Managed Microsoft AD (a paid managed directory) plus a forest trust and a continuously running bastion-host EC2 instance. The Managed Microsoft AD plus always-on bastion makes this notably more expensive than AD Connector with Fleet Manager.","why_zh":"需要 AWS Managed Microsoft AD（付費的受管目錄）、樹系信任，以及持續運行的 bastion 主機 EC2 執行個體。Managed Microsoft AD 加上常駐 bastion 使其明顯比 AD Connector + Fleet Manager 昂貴。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Technically works but is not the most cost-effective: it requires the Site-to-Site VPN tunnel running 24/7 (hourly + data-transfer charges), managing domain joins over the VPN, and exposing/managing RDP. This is the dump's suggested answer but carries more cost and operational overhead than B.","why_zh":"技術上可行，但並非最具成本效益：需要 24/7 運行的 Site-to-Site VPN 通道（按小時計費加資料傳輸費）、透過 VPN 管理網域加入，以及暴露與管理 RDP。這是題庫建議答案，但成本與維運負擔都高於 B。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Like A, it requires the paid AWS Managed Microsoft AD plus a forest trust and a dedicated, always-on Remote Desktop Gateway EC2 instance deployed via Quick Start. The Managed AD plus standing RD Gateway host make it more costly than B.","why_zh":"與 A 相同，需要付費的 AWS Managed Microsoft AD、樹系信任，以及透過 Quick Start 部署的專用常駐 Remote Desktop Gateway EC2 執行個體。Managed AD 加上常駐 RD Gateway 主機使其成本高於 B。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/fleet-manager-remote-desktop-connections.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/connect-rdp-fleet-manager.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directoryservice/latest/admin-guide/directory_ad_connector.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/manage-your-identity-source-ad.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":320,"question_en":"A company's compliance audit reveals that some Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes that were created in an AWS account were not encrypted. A solutions architect must implement a solution to encrypt all new EBS volumes at rest. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST effort?","question_zh":"一家公司的合规性审计显示，在 AWS 账户中创建的一些 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 卷未加密。解决方案架构师必须实 施一个解决方案来加密所有新的静态 EBS 卷。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的努力满足此要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to detect the creation of unencrypted EBS volumes. Invoke an AWS Lambda function to delete noncompliant volumes.","B":"Use AWS Audit Manager with data encryption.","C":"Create an AWS Config rule to detect the creation of a new EBS volume. Encrypt the volume by using AWS Systems Manager Automation.","D":"Turn on EBS encryption by default in all AWS Regions."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则来检测未加密的 EBS 卷的创建。调用 AWS Lambda 函数来删除不合规的卷。","B":"使用 AWS Audit Manager 进行数据加密。","C":"创建 AWS Config 规则来检测新 EBS 卷的创建。使用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 加密卷。","D":"在所有 AWS 区域中默认启用 EBS 加密。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":78,"C":22},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":321,"question_en":"A research company is running daily simulations in the AWS Cloud to meet high demand. The simulations run on several hundred Amazon EC2 instances that are based on Amazon Linux 2. Occasionally, a simulation gets stuck and requires a cloud operations engineer to solve the problem by connecting to an EC2 instance through SSH. Company policy states that no EC2 instance can use the same SSH key and that all connections must be logged in AWS CloudTrail. How can a solutions architect meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家研究公司正在 AWS 云中运行日常模拟以满足高需求。模拟在数百个基于 Amazon Linux 2 的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。偶尔，模 拟会陷入困境，需要云运维工程师通过 SSH 连接到 EC2 实例来解决问题。 公司政策规定，任何 EC2 实例都不能使用相同的 SSH 密钥，并且所有连接都必须记录在 AWS CloudTrail 中。 解决方案架构师如何满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Launch new EC2 instances, and generate an individual SSH key for each instance. Store the SSH key in AWS Secrets Manager. Create a new IAM policy, and attach it to the engineers’ IAM role with an Allow statement for the GetSecretValue action. Instruct the engineers to fetch the SSH key from Secrets Manager when they connect through any SSH client.","B":"Create an AWS Systems Manager document to run commands on EC2 instances to set a new unique SSH key. Create a new IAM policy, and attach it to the engineers’ IAM role with an Allow statement to run Systems Manager documents. Instruct the engineers to run the document to set an SSH key and to connect through any SSH client.","C":"Launch new EC2 instances without setting up any SSH key for the instances. Set up EC2 Instance Connect on each instance. Create a new IAM policy, and attach it to the engineers’ IAM role with an Allow statement for the SendSSHPublicKey action. Instruct the engineers to connect to the instance by using a browser-based SSH client from the EC2 console.","D":"Set up AWS Secrets Manager to store the EC2 SSH key. Create a new AWS Lambda function to create a new SSH key and to call AWS Systems Manager Session Manager to set the SSH key on the EC2 instance. Configure Secrets Manager to use the Lambda function for automatic rotation once daily. Instruct the engineers to fetch the SSH key from Secrets Manager when they connect through any SSH client."},"options_zh":{"A":"启动新的 EC2 实例，并为每个实例生成单独的 SSH 密钥。将 SSH 密钥存储在 AWS Secrets Manager 中。创建新的 IAM 策略，并 使用 GetSecretValue 操作的允许语句将其附加到工程师的 IAM 角色。指示工程师在通过任何 SSH 客户端连接时从 Secrets Manager 获取 SSH 密钥。","B":"创建 AWS Systems Manager 文档以在 EC2 实例上运行命令以设置新的唯一 SSH 密钥。创建新的 IAM 策略，并使用允许运行 Systems Manager 文档的语句将其附加到工程师的 IAM 角色。指导工程师运行该文档来设置 SSH 密钥并通过任何 SSH 客户端进行 连接。","C":"启动新的 EC2 实例，无需为实例设置任何 SSH 密钥。在每个实例上设置 EC2 Instance Connect。创建新的 IAM 策略，并使用 SendSSHPublicKey 操作的允许语句将其附加到工程师的 IAM 角色。指导工程师通过 EC2 控制台使用基于浏览器的 SSH 客户端连 接到实例。","D":"设置 AWS Secrets Manager 以存储 EC2 SSH 密钥。创建新的 AWS Lambda 函数以创建新的 SSH 密钥并调用 AWS Systems Manager 会话管理器以在 EC2 实例上设置 SSH 密钥。配置 Secrets Manager 以使用 Lambda 函数每天自动轮换一次。指示工程师在通过任 何 SSH 客户端连接时从 Secrets Manager 获取 SSH 密钥。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":322,"question_en":"A company is migrating mobile banking applications to run on Amazon EC2 instances in a VPC. Backend service applications run in an on- premises data center. The data center has an AWS Direct Connect connection into AWS. The applications that run in the VPC need to resolve DNS requests to an on-premises Active Directory domain that runs in the data center. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST administrative overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在迁移移动银行应用程序以在 VPC 中的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。后端服务应用程序在本地数据中心运行。数据中心具 有与 AWS 的 AWS Direct Connect 连接。在 VPC 中运行的应用程序需要将 DNS 请求解析到在数据中心运行的本地 Active Directory 域。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的管理开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Provision a set of EC2 instances across two Availability Zones in the VPC as caching DNS servers to resolve DNS queries from the application servers within the VPC.","B":"Provision an Amazon Route 53 private hosted zone. Configure NS records that point to on-premises DNS servers.","C":"Create DNS endpoints by using Amazon Route 53 Resolver. Add conditional forwarding rules to resolve DNS namespaces between the on-premises data center and the VPC.","D":"Provision a new Active Directory domain controller in the VPC with a bidirectional trust between this new domain and the on-premises Active Directory domain."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 VPC 中的两个可用区中配置一组 EC2 实例作为缓存 DNS 服务器，以解析来自 VPC 内的应用程序服务器的 DNS 查询。","B":"配置 Amazon Route 53 私有托管区域。配置指向本地 DNS 服务器的 NS 记录。","C":"使用 Amazon Route 53 Resolver 创建 DNS 终端节点。添加条件转发规则以解析本地数据中心和VPC之间的DNS命名空间。","D":"在 VPC 中配置一个新的 Active Directory 域控制器，并在该新域和本地 Active Directory 域之间建立双向信任。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":323,"question_en":"A company processes environmental data. The company has set up sensors to provide a continuous stream of data from different areas in a city. The data is available in JSON format. The company wants to use an AWS solution to send the data to a database that does not require fixed schemas for storage. The data must be sent in real time. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司处理环境数据。该公司设置了传感器来提供来自城市不同区域的连续数据流。数据以 JSON 格式提供。 该公司希望使用 AWS 解决方案将数据发送到不需要固定架构存储的数据库。数据必须实时发送。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to send the data to Amazon Redshift.","B":"Use Amazon Kinesis Data Streams to send the data to Amazon DynamoDB.","C":"Use Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK) to send the data to Amazon Aurora.","D":"Use Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to send the data to Amazon Keyspaces (for Apache Cassandra)."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 将数据发送到 Amazon Redshift。","B":"使用 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams 将数据发送到 Amazon DynamoDB。","C":"使用 Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK) 将数据发送到 Amazon Aurora。","D":"使用 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 将数据发送到 Amazon Keyspaces（适用于 Apache Cassandra）。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":92},"tags":["Database","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirements are: real-time delivery, JSON data, and a database that does NOT require a fixed schema (a NoSQL/schemaless store). Amazon DynamoDB is a NoSQL key-value/document database that requires only the primary key to be defined; other attributes vary freely per item, so it does not require a fixed schema. Amazon Kinesis Data Streams provides true real-time streaming, and a consumer (e.g., a Lambda function via an event source mapping) writes records to DynamoDB in real time. Option A fails because Amazon Redshift is a relational data warehouse that requires fixed table schemas, and Firehose loads it via S3 + COPY micro-batches rather than true real time. Option C fails because Aurora is a relational engine requiring fixed schemas. Option D is technically impossible because Amazon Data Firehose does not support Amazon Keyspaces as a delivery destination (supported destinations are S3, Redshift, OpenSearch, Splunk, Apache Iceberg Tables, and HTTP endpoints), and Keyspaces still requires defined table schemas. Therefore B is the only solution meeting all three requirements, and the dump's suggested answer A is wrong.","explanation_zh":"需求為：即時傳送、JSON 資料，以及一個「不需要固定 schema」的資料庫（即 NoSQL/無 schema 的儲存）。Amazon DynamoDB 是 NoSQL 鍵值/文件型資料庫，只需定義主鍵，其他屬性可逐項自由變化，因此不需要固定 schema。Amazon Kinesis Data Streams 提供真正的即時串流，消費端（例如透過 event source mapping 觸發的 Lambda 函式）可即時將紀錄寫入 DynamoDB。選項 A 不成立，因為 Amazon Redshift 是需要固定資料表 schema 的關聯式資料倉儲，且 Firehose 是透過 S3 + COPY 的微批次載入，並非真正即時。選項 C 不成立，因為 Aurora 是需要固定 schema 的關聯式引擎。選項 D 在技術上不可行，因為 Amazon Data Firehose 不支援將 Amazon Keyspaces 作為傳送目的地（支援的目的地為 S3、Redshift、OpenSearch、Splunk、Apache Iceberg Tables 與 HTTP endpoints），且 Keyspaces 仍需要定義資料表 schema。因此 B 是唯一同時滿足三項需求的方案，dump 建議答案 A 是錯的。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Redshift is a relational data warehouse that REQUIRES fixed table schemas (CREATE TABLE with defined columns), directly violating the 'no fixed schema' requirement. Firehose also loads Redshift via S3 staging plus a COPY command in micro-batches, which is not true real-time delivery.","why_zh":"Amazon Redshift 是關聯式資料倉儲，需要固定資料表 schema（CREATE TABLE 須定義欄位），直接違反「不需固定 schema」的需求。Firehose 也是透過 S3 暫存加上 COPY 指令以微批次方式載入 Redshift，並非真正的即時傳送。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Aurora is a relational database (MySQL/PostgreSQL-compatible) that requires fixed schemas, so it violates the 'no fixed schema' requirement. MSK is a valid streaming layer, but the chosen destination is wrong.","why_zh":"Amazon Aurora 是關聯式資料庫（相容 MySQL/PostgreSQL），需要固定 schema，違反「不需固定 schema」的需求。MSK 雖是有效的串流層，但所選目的地錯誤。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Data Firehose does NOT support Amazon Keyspaces as a delivery destination (supported destinations are S3, Redshift, OpenSearch Service/Serverless, Splunk, Apache Iceberg Tables, and HTTP endpoints), so this integration cannot be configured. Additionally, Keyspaces (Cassandra) requires defined table schemas with column definitions.","why_zh":"Amazon Data Firehose 不支援將 Amazon Keyspaces 作為傳送目的地（支援目的地為 S3、Redshift、OpenSearch Service/Serverless、Splunk、Apache Iceberg Tables 與 HTTP endpoints），因此此整合無法設定。此外 Keyspaces（Cassandra）需要定義含欄位的資料表 schema。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/create-destination.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/bp-general-nosql-design.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/SQLtoNoSQL.WhyDynamoDB.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-kinesis-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/keyspaces/latest/devguide/cql.ddl.table.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":324,"question_en":"A company is migrating a legacy application from an on-premises data center to AWS. The application uses MongoDB as a key-value database. According to the company's technical guidelines, all Amazon EC2 instances must be hosted in a private subnet without an internet connection. In addition, all connectivity between applications and databases must be encrypted. The database must be able to scale based on demand. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在将旧应用程序从本地数据中心迁移到 AWS。该应用程序使用 MongoDB 作为键值数据库。根据该公司的技术指南，所有 Amazon EC2 实例都必须托管在没有互联网连接的私有子网中。此外，应用程序和数据库之间的所有连接都必须加密。数据库必须能 够根据需求进行扩展。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create new Amazon DocumentDB (with MongoDB compatibility) tables for the application with Provisioned IOPS volumes. Use the instance endpoint to connect to Amazon DocumentDB.","B":"Create new Amazon DynamoDB tables for the application with on-demand capacity. Use a gateway VPC endpoint for DynamoDB to connect to the DynamoDB tables.","C":"Create new Amazon DynamoDB tables for the application with on-demand capacity. Use an interface VPC endpoint for DynamoDB to connect to the DynamoDB tables.","D":"Create new Amazon DocumentDB (with MongoDB compatibility) tables for the application with Provisioned IOPS volumes. Use the cluster endpoint to connect to Amazon DocumentDB."},"options_zh":{"A":"为具有预配置 IOPS 卷的应用程序创建新的 Amazon DocumentDB（与 MongoDB 兼容）表。使用实例终端节点连接到 Amazon DocumentDB。","B":"为具有按需容量的应用程序创建新的 Amazon DynamoDB 表。使用 DynamoDB 的网关 VPC 终端节点连接到 DynamoDB 表。","C":"为具有按需容量的应用程序创建新的 Amazon DynamoDB 表。使用 DynamoDB 的接口 VPC 终端节点连接到 DynamoDB 表。","D":"为具有预配置 IOPS 卷的应用程序创建新的 Amazon DocumentDB（与 MongoDB 兼容）表。使用集群终端节点连接到 Amazon DocumentDB。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":48,"D":42},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirements are: EC2 in a private subnet with no internet, all connectivity encrypted, and the database must scale based on demand. DynamoDB with on-demand capacity natively scales based on demand (its core serverless characteristic), and DynamoDB traffic is sent over HTTPS/TLS so it is encrypted in transit. For an EC2 instance inside a private subnet (same region, no internet) to reach DynamoDB privately, the canonical and recommended mechanism is a gateway VPC endpoint, which keeps traffic on the AWS network and is not billed. The AWS docs state that interface (PrivateLink) endpoints for DynamoDB exist specifically to extend access from on-premises (Direct Connect/VPN) or from another AWS Region (VPC peering/Transit Gateway) and are billed — capabilities not needed here, where the application runs in the same VPC. Options A and D use Amazon DocumentDB with Provisioned IOPS, which does not scale compute on demand (read scaling requires manually adding up to 15 replicas; write scaling requires manually changing instance classes), and they incorrectly refer to DocumentDB 'tables' (DocumentDB uses collections). Therefore B is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求為:EC2 位於沒有網際網路的 private subnet、所有連線必須加密、且資料庫須能依需求擴展。DynamoDB 搭配 on-demand 容量可原生依需求自動擴展(這是其 serverless 的核心特性),且 DynamoDB 流量透過 HTTPS/TLS 傳輸,因此傳輸中已加密。對於位於 private subnet(同區域、無網際網路)的 EC2 私有存取 DynamoDB,標準且建議的機制是 gateway VPC endpoint,流量保留在 AWS 網路內且不收費。AWS 文件指出 DynamoDB 的 interface (PrivateLink) endpoint 主要用於擴展自地端(Direct Connect/VPN)或跨區域(VPC peering/Transit Gateway)的存取,且會計費 — 在此情境(應用程式位於同一 VPC)並不需要。選項 A 與 D 使用 Amazon DocumentDB 搭配 Provisioned IOPS,無法依需求自動擴展運算(讀取擴展需手動新增最多 15 個 replica;寫入擴展需手動變更 instance class),且錯誤地稱 DocumentDB 為 'tables'(DocumentDB 使用 collections)。因此正確答案為 B。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"DocumentDB with Provisioned IOPS does not scale on demand (compute scaling is manual via replicas/instance classes), and it uses an instance endpoint, which targets a single instance rather than the cluster; also 'DocumentDB tables' is wrong terminology (DocumentDB uses collections).","why_zh":"DocumentDB 搭配 Provisioned IOPS 無法依需求自動擴展(運算擴展需透過 replica/instance class 手動進行),且使用指向單一執行個體的 instance endpoint;另外 'DocumentDB tables' 為錯誤用語(DocumentDB 使用 collections)。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An interface (PrivateLink) endpoint for DynamoDB technically works but is intended for on-premises (Direct Connect/VPN) or cross-Region access and incurs hourly plus data-processing charges. For EC2 in the same VPC/Region the gateway endpoint is the recommended, free, canonical choice, so this is not the best answer.","why_zh":"DynamoDB 的 interface (PrivateLink) endpoint 技術上可行,但其用途是地端(Direct Connect/VPN)或跨區域存取,且需按小時與資料處理計費。對於同一 VPC/區域內的 EC2,gateway endpoint 才是建議、免費且標準的選擇,因此這不是最佳答案。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"DocumentDB with Provisioned IOPS does not scale based on demand (storage auto-scales but compute scaling is manual). The cluster endpoint is correct over instance endpoint, but the provisioned model fails the 'scale based on demand' requirement, and 'tables' is incorrect terminology.","why_zh":"DocumentDB 搭配 Provisioned IOPS 無法依需求擴展(儲存可自動擴展,但運算擴展為手動)。雖然 cluster endpoint 比 instance endpoint 正確,但 provisioned 模式不符合『依需求擴展』的需求,且 'tables' 為錯誤用語。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/privatelink-interface-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/vpc-endpoints-dynamodb.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/devguide/db-cluster-manage-performance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/HowItWorks.ReadWriteCapacityMode.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識"},{"id":325,"question_en":"A company is running an application on Amazon EC2 instances in the AWS Cloud. The application is using a MongoDB database with a replica set as its data tier. The MongoDB database is installed on systems in the company’s on-premises data center and is accessible through an AWS Direct Connect connection to the data center environment. A solutions architect must migrate the on-premises MongoDB database to Amazon DocumentDB (with MongoDB compatibility). Which strategy should the solutions architect choose to perform this migration?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 云中的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行应用程序。该应用程序使用 MongoDB 数据库，并将副本集作为其数据层。 MongoDB 数据库安装在公司本地数据中心的系统上，可通过与数据中心环境的 AWS Direct Connect 连接进行访问。 解决方案架构师必须将本地 MongoDB 数据库迁移到 Amazon DocumentDB（与 MongoDB 兼容）。 解决方案架构师应该选择哪种策略来执行此迁移？","options_en":{"A":"Create a ­eet of EC2 instances. Install MongoDB Community Edition on the EC2 instances, and create a database. Configure continuous synchronous replication with the database that is running in the on-premises data center.","B":"Create an AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) replication instance. Create a source endpoint for the on-premises MongoDB database by using change data capture (CDC). Create a target endpoint for the Amazon DocumentDB database. Create and run a DMS migration task.","C":"Create a data migration pipeline by using AWS Data Pipeline. Define data nodes for the on-premises MongoDB database and the Amazon DocumentDB database. Create a scheduled task to run the data pipeline.","D":"Create a source endpoint for the on-premises MongoDB database by using AWS Glue crawlers. Configure continuous asynchronous replication between the MongoDB database and the Amazon DocumentDB database."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 EC2 实例队列。在 EC2 实例上安装 MongoDB Community Edition，并创建数据库。配置与本地数据中心运行的数据库的连 续同步复制。","B":"创建 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 复制实例。使用更改数据捕获 (CDC) 为本地 MongoDB 数据库创建源终端节点。 为 Amazon DocumentDB 数据库创建目标终端节点。创建并运行DMS迁移任务。","C":"使用 AWS Data Pipeline 创建数据迁移管道。为本地 MongoDB 数据库和 Amazon DocumentDB 数据库定义数据节点。创建计划任 务来运行数据管道。","D":"使用 AWS Glue 爬网程序为本地 MongoDB 数据库创建源终端节点。配置 MongoDB 数据库和 Amazon DocumentDB 数据库之间的 连续异步复制。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Compute","Database","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":326,"question_en":"A company is rearchitecting its applications to run on AWS. The company’s infrastructure includes multiple Amazon EC2 instances. The company's development team needs different levels of access. The company wants to implement a policy that requires all Windows EC2 instances to be joined to an Active Directory domain on AWS. The company also wants to implement enhanced security processes such as multi-factor authentication (MFA). The company wants to use managed AWS services wherever possible. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在重新构建其应用程序以在 AWS 上运行。该公司的基础设施包括多个 Amazon EC2 实例。公司的开发团队需要不同级别 的访问权限。该公司希望实施一项策略，要求所有 Windows EC2 实例加入 AWS 上的 Active Directory 域。该公司还希望实施增强的安 全流程，例如多重身份验证 (MFA)。该公司希望尽可能使用托管 AWS 服务。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory implementation. Launch an Amazon Workspace. Connect to and use the Workspace for domain security configuration tasks.","B":"Create an AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory implementation. Launch an EC2 instance. Connect to and use the EC2 instance for domain security configuration tasks.","C":"Create an AWS Directory Service Simple AD implementation. Launch an EC2 instance. Connect to and use the EC2 instance for domain security configuration tasks.","D":"Create an AWS Directory Service Simple AD implementation. Launch an Amazon Workspace. Connect to and use the Workspace for domain security configuration tasks."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 Microsoft Active Directory 实施创建 AWS Directory Service。启动 Amazon 工作区。连接到工作区并使用工作区执行域安全配置 任务。","B":"为 Microsoft Active Directory 实施创建 AWS Directory Service。启动 EC2 实例。连接到 EC2 实例并使用它来执行域安全配置任 务。","C":"创建 AWS Directory Service Simple AD 实施。启动 EC2 实例。连接到 EC2 实例并使用它来执行域安全配置任务。","D":"创建 AWS Directory Service Simple AD 实施。启动 Amazon 工作区。连接到工作区并使用工作区执行域安全配置任务。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":60,"A":40},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement explicitly demands multi-factor authentication (MFA). AWS Directory Service Simple AD (a Samba 4-based directory) does NOT support MFA, so options C and D are eliminated outright. Only AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory (AWS Managed Microsoft AD) supports MFA, domain joining of Windows EC2 instances, and is the managed service requested. Between A and B, both use AWS Managed Microsoft AD; the difference is using an Amazon WorkSpace versus an EC2 instance to perform domain security configuration tasks. The AWS-documented method for administering the managed AD (installing the Active Directory Domain Services / AD LDS RSAT tools and managing users, groups, and group policies) is to launch and domain-join an EC2 Windows Server instance, where you install the administration tools and run domain configuration. AWS even provides a directory administration EC2 instance with these tools pre-installed. A WorkSpace is an end-user DaaS virtual desktop, not the prescribed administrative configuration host. Therefore B is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求明確要求多重要素驗證 (MFA)。AWS Directory Service Simple AD (以 Samba 4 為基礎的目錄) 不支援 MFA，因此選項 C 與 D 直接排除。只有 AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory (AWS Managed Microsoft AD) 同時支援 MFA、將 Windows EC2 執行個體加入網域，且是題目要求的受管服務。A 與 B 都使用 AWS Managed Microsoft AD，差別在於使用 Amazon WorkSpace 還是 EC2 執行個體執行網域安全設定工作。AWS 文件所記載的受管 AD 管理方式 (安裝 Active Directory Domain Services / AD LDS RSAT 工具，並管理使用者、群組與群組原則) 是啟動並將 EC2 Windows Server 執行個體加入網域，在其上安裝管理工具並進行網域設定；AWS 甚至提供已預裝這些工具的目錄管理 EC2 執行個體。WorkSpace 是面向終端使用者的 DaaS 虛擬桌面，並非規範用於管理設定的主機。因此正確答案為 B。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses the correct directory (AWS Managed Microsoft AD), but a WorkSpace is an end-user virtual desktop (DaaS), not the AWS-documented host for performing domain security configuration. AWS prescribes launching/joining an EC2 Windows Server instance to install the AD administration (RSAT) tools and manage the domain.","why_zh":"使用了正確的目錄 (AWS Managed Microsoft AD)，但 WorkSpace 是面向終端使用者的虛擬桌面 (DaaS)，並非 AWS 文件記載用於執行網域安全設定的主機。AWS 規範的做法是啟動並加入 EC2 Windows Server 執行個體以安裝 AD 管理 (RSAT) 工具並管理網域。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Simple AD does not support MFA, which is an explicit requirement; it also lacks PowerShell, trusts, and AD Administrative Center. Eliminated regardless of the EC2 admin host.","why_zh":"Simple AD 不支援 MFA，而 MFA 是明確要求；它也不支援 PowerShell、信任關係與 AD 系統管理中心。無論管理主機為何皆被排除。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same fatal flaw as C: Simple AD does not support MFA. Using a WorkSpace as the admin host is also not the prescribed approach.","why_zh":"與 C 相同的致命缺陷：Simple AD 不支援 MFA。以 WorkSpace 作為管理主機也非規範做法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directoryservice/latest/admin-guide/directory_simple_ad.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directoryservice/latest/admin-guide/directory_microsoft_ad.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directoryservice/latest/admin-guide/ms_ad_install_ad_tools.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directoryservice/latest/admin-guide/launching_instance.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":327,"question_en":"A company wants to migrate its on-premises application to AWS. The database for the application stores structured product data and temporary user session data. The company needs to decouple the product data from the user session data. The company also needs to implement replication in another AWS Region for disaster recovery. Which solution will meet these requirements with the HIGHEST performance?","question_zh":"一家公司希望将其本地应用程序迁移到 AWS。应用程序的数据库存储结构化产品数据和临时用户会话数据。公司需要将产品数据与 用户会话数据解耦。该公司还需要在另一个 AWS 区域实施复制以实现灾难恢复。 哪种解决方案能够以最高的性能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon RDS DB instance with separate schemas to host the product data and the user session data. Configure a read replica for the DB instance in another Region.","B":"Create an Amazon RDS DB instance to host the product data. Configure a read replica for the DB instance in another Region. Create a global datastore in Amazon ElastiCache for Memcached to host the user session data.","C":"Create two Amazon DynamoDB global tables. Use one global table to host the product data. Use the other global table to host the user session data. Use DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) for caching.","D":"Create an Amazon RDS DB instance to host the product data. Configure a read replica for the DB instance in another Region. Create an Amazon DynamoDB global table to host the user session data."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建具有单独架构的 Amazon RDS 数据库实例来托管产品数据和用户会话数据。为另一个区域中的数据库实例配置只读副本。","B":"创建 Amazon RDS 数据库实例来托管产品数据。为另一个区域中的数据库实例配置只读副本。在 Amazon ElastiCache for Memcached 中创建全局数据存储以托管用户会话数据。","C":"创建两个 Amazon DynamoDB 全局表。使用一张全局表来托管产品数据。使用另一个全局表来托管用户会话数据。使用 DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) 进行缓存。","D":"创建 Amazon RDS 数据库实例来托管产品数据。为另一个区域中的数据库实例配置只读副本。创建 Amazon DynamoDB 全局表 来托管用户会话数据。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":51,"C":31,"B":18},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Database"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識・多選項拉鋸"},{"id":328,"question_en":"A company orchestrates a multi-account structure on AWS by using AWS Control Tower. The company is using AWS Organizations, AWS Config, and AWS Trusted Advisor. The company has a specific OU for development accounts that developers use to experiment on AWS. The company has hundreds of developers, and each developer has an individual development account. The company wants to optimize costs in these development accounts. Amazon EC2 instances and Amazon RDS instances in these accounts must be burstable. The company wants to disallow the use of other services that are not relevant. What should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Control Tower 在 AWS 上协调多账户结构。该公司正在使用 AWS Organizations、AWS Config 和 AWS Trusted Advisor。该公司有一个用于开发帐户的特定 OU，开发人员可以使用该 OU 在 AWS 上进行实验。公司拥有数百名开发者，每个开发者 都有一个单独的开发账户。 该公司希望优化这些开发账户的成本。这些账户中的 Amazon EC2 实例和 Amazon RDS 实例必须是可突发的。该公司希望禁止使用其 他不相关的服务。 解决方案架构师应该建议什么来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a custom SCP in AWS Organizations to allow the deployment of only burstable instances and to disallow services that are not relevant. Apply the SCP to the development OU.","B":"Create a custom detective control (guardrail) in AWS Control Tower. Configure the control (guardrail) to allow the deployment of only burstable instances and to disallow services that are not relevant. Apply the control (guardrail) to the development OU.","C":"Create a custom preventive control (guardrail) in AWS Control Tower. Configure the control (guardrail) to allow the deployment of only burstable instances and to disallow services that are not relevant. Apply the control (guardrail) to the development OU.","D":"Create an AWS Config rule in the AWS Control Tower account. Configure the AWS Config rule to allow the deployment of only burstable instances and to disallow services that are not relevant. Deploy the AWS Config rule to the development OU by using AWS CloudFormation StackSets."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS Organizations 中创建自定义 SCP，以仅允许部署可突发实例并禁止不相关的服务。将 SCP 应用到开发 OU。","B":"在 AWS Control Tower 中创建自定义检测控制（护栏）。配置控制（护栏）以仅允许部署可突发实例并禁止不相关的服务。将 控制（护栏）应用到开发 OU。","C":"在 AWS Control Tower 中创建自定义预防控制（护栏）。配置控制（护栏）以仅允许部署可突发实例并禁止不相关的服务。将 控制（护栏）应用到开发 OU。","D":"在 AWS Control Tower 账户中创建 AWS Config 规则。配置 AWS Config 规则以仅允许部署可突发实例并禁止不相关的服务。使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 将 AWS Config 规则部署到开发 OU。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":58,"C":42},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":329,"question_en":"A financial services company runs a complex, multi-tier application on Amazon EC2 instances and AWS Lambda functions. The application stores temporary data in Amazon S3. The S3 objects are valid for only 45 minutes and are deleted after 24 hours. The company deploys each version of the application by launching an AWS CloudFormation stack. The stack creates all resources that are required to run the application. When the company deploys and validates a new application version, the company deletes the CloudFormation stack of the old version. The company recently tried to delete the CloudFormation stack of an old application version, but the operation failed. An analysis shows that CloudFormation failed to delete an existing S3 bucket. A solutions architect needs to resolve this issue without making major changes to the application's architecture. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家金融服务公司在 Amazon EC2 实例和 AWS Lambda 函数上运行复杂的多层应用程序。该应用程序将临时数据存储在 Amazon S3 中。S3 对象的有效期仅为 45 分钟，24 小时后将被删除。 该公司通过启动 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈来部署应用程序的每个版本。该堆栈创建运行应用程序所需的所有资源。当公司部署并验 证新的应用程序版本时，公司会删除旧版本的 CloudFormation 堆栈。 该公司最近尝试删除旧应用程序版本的CloudFormation堆栈，但操作失败。分析表明，CloudFormation 无法删除现有的 S3 存储桶。 解决方案架构师需要在不对应用程序架构进行重大更改的情况下解决此问题。 哪种解决方案满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Implement a Lambda function that deletes all files from a given S3 bucket. Integrate this Lambda function as a custom resource into the CloudFormation stack. Ensure that the custom resource has a DependsOn attribute that points to the S3 bucket's resource.","B":"Modify the CloudFormation template to provision an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system to store the temporary files there instead of in Amazon S3. Configure the Lambda functions to run in the same VPC as the file system. Mount the file system to the EC2 instances and Lambda functions.","C":"Modify the CloudF ormation stack to create an S3 Lifecycle rule that expires all objects 45 minutes after creation. Add a DependsOn attribute that points to the S3 bucket’s resource.","D":"Modify the CloudFormation stack to attach a DeletionPolicy attribute with a value of Delete to the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"实现一个 Lambda 函数，从给定的 S3 存储桶中删除所有文件。将此 Lambda 函数作为自定义资源集成到 CloudFormation 堆栈 中。确保自定义资源具有指向 S3 存储桶资源的 DependsOn 属性。","B":"修改 CloudFormation 模板以预置 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统，以将临时文件存储在其中而不是存储在 Amazon S3 中。将 Lambda 函数配置为在与文件系统相同的 VPC 中运行。将文件系统挂载到 EC2 实例和 Lambda 函数。","C":"修改 CloudFormation 堆栈以创建一条 S3 生命周期规则，该规则使所有对象在创建 45 分钟后过期。添加指向 S3 存储桶资源的 DependsOn 属性。","D":"修改 CloudFormation 堆栈，将值为“Delete”的 DeletionPolicy 属性附加到 S3 存储桶。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":93},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The stack deletion failed because CloudFormation can only delete empty S3 buckets. The AWS::S3::Bucket docs state: 'You can only delete empty buckets. Deletion fails for buckets that have contents,' and the DeletionPolicy 'Delete' option states: 'For Amazon S3 buckets, you must delete all objects in the bucket for deletion to succeed.' Because objects live up to 24 hours and new ones can be written until the moment of teardown, the bucket is generally not empty when the stack is deleted. The standard, minimal-change AWS pattern is a Lambda-backed custom resource that empties the bucket: on stack delete, CloudFormation sends a Delete event to the custom resource, and with DependsOn pointing to the bucket, CloudFormation deletes the custom resource BEFORE the bucket (reverse dependency order), so the Lambda empties the bucket first and the subsequent bucket deletion succeeds. This requires no architectural change to the application.","explanation_zh":"Stack 刪除失敗是因為 CloudFormation 只能刪除空的 S3 bucket。AWS::S3::Bucket 文件明確說明：『You can only delete empty buckets. Deletion fails for buckets that have contents』，而 DeletionPolicy 的 Delete 選項也說：『For Amazon S3 buckets, you must delete all objects in the bucket for deletion to succeed』。由於物件可存活達 24 小時、且在刪除當下仍可能寫入新物件，刪除 stack 時 bucket 通常不是空的。標準且改動最小的 AWS 做法是使用 Lambda 支援的 custom resource 來清空 bucket：刪除 stack 時 CloudFormation 會送 Delete 事件給 custom resource，而 DependsOn 指向 bucket 會讓 CloudFormation 以相反相依順序先刪除 custom resource、再刪除 bucket，因此 Lambda 會先清空 bucket，後續的 bucket 刪除即可成功。此方案不需更動應用程式架構。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Replacing S3 with Amazon EFS, putting Lambda in a VPC, and mounting the file system to EC2 and Lambda is a major architectural change, which directly violates the requirement to resolve the issue 'without making major changes to the application's architecture.' This is the dump's suggested answer and is wrong.","why_zh":"把 S3 換成 Amazon EFS、將 Lambda 放進 VPC、並把檔案系統掛載到 EC2 與 Lambda，是重大的架構變更，直接違反『不大幅變更應用程式架構』的要求。這是 dump 的建議答案，但是錯的。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An S3 Lifecycle rule expiring objects 45 minutes after creation runs asynchronously (expiration is batch-processed, often with delays of many hours), so it cannot guarantee the bucket is empty at the instant of stack deletion. Objects written shortly before teardown would still be present, so the bucket deletion can still fail. DependsOn on a lifecycle rule also does not affect this. It does not reliably resolve the failure.","why_zh":"設定 45 分鐘後過期的 S3 Lifecycle 規則是非同步執行（過期動作以批次處理，常延遲數小時），無法保證刪除 stack 當下 bucket 已清空。刪除前不久寫入的物件仍會存在，bucket 刪除仍可能失敗。在 lifecycle 規則上加 DependsOn 也無濟於事，無法可靠解決問題。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"DeletionPolicy: Delete is already the default behavior when no policy is set, so it changes nothing. The docs explicitly state that even with Delete, 'you must delete all objects in the bucket for deletion to succeed' — it does not empty the bucket. The deletion would still fail.","why_zh":"未設定政策時 DeletionPolicy: Delete 本就是預設行為，等於沒有改變。文件明確指出即使設為 Delete，『you must delete all objects in the bucket for deletion to succeed』——它不會清空 bucket，因此刪除仍會失敗。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-properties-s3-bucket.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-attribute-deletionpolicy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-resource-cfn-customresource.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-attribute-dependson.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":330,"question_en":"A company has developed a mobile game. The backend for the game runs on several virtual machines located in an on-premises data center. The business logic is exposed using a REST API with multiple functions. Player session data is stored in central file storage. Backend services use different API keys for throttling and to distinguish between live and test tra®c. The load on the game backend varies throughout the day. During peak hours, the server capacity is not su®cient. There are also latency issues when fetching player session data. Management has asked a solutions architect to present a cloud architecture that can handle the game’s varying load and provide low-latency data access. The API model should not be changed. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司开发了一款手机游戏。游戏的后端在位于本地数据中心的多个虚拟机上运行。业务逻辑使用具有多种功能的 REST API 公 开。玩家会话数据存储在中央文件存储中。后端服务使用不同的 API 密钥进行限制并区分实时流量和测试流量。 游戏后端的负载全天都在变化。高峰时段，服务器容量不足。获取玩家会话数据时也存在延迟问题。管理层要求解决方案架构师提 供一个云架构，该架构可以处理游戏的变化负载并提供低延迟的数据访问。API 模型不应更改。 哪种解决方案满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Implement the REST API using a Network Load Balancer (NLB). Run the business logic on an Amazon EC2 instance behind the NLB. Store player session data in Amazon Aurora Serverless.","B":"Implement the REST API using an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Run the business logic in AWS Lambda. Store player session data in Amazon DynamoDB with on-demand capacity.","C":"Implement the REST API using Amazon API Gateway. Run the business logic in AWS Lambda. Store player session data in Amazon DynamoDB with on-demand capacity.","D":"Implement the REST API using AWS AppSync. Run the business logic in AWS Lambda. Store player session data in Amazon Aurora Serverless."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用网络负载均衡器 (NLB) 实施 REST API。在 NLB 后面的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行业务逻辑。将玩家会话数据存储在 Amazon Aurora Serverless 中。","B":"使用应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 实施 REST API。在 AWS Lambda 中运行业务逻辑。将玩家会话数据存储在具有按需容量的 Amazon DynamoDB 中。","C":"使用 Amazon API Gateway 实施 REST API。在 AWS Lambda 中运行业务逻辑。将玩家会话数据存储在具有按需容量的 Amazon DynamoDB 中。","D":"使用 AWS AppSync 实施 REST API。在 AWS Lambda 中运行业务逻辑。将玩家会话数据存储在 Amazon Aurora Serverless 中。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifiers are (1) the backend exposes a REST API that 'should not be changed', and (2) it uses 'different API keys for throttling and to distinguish between live and test traffic'. Amazon API Gateway natively builds REST APIs and provides usage plans and API keys, which throttle requests and identify clients per stage (a 'live' stage and a 'test' stage map directly to different API keys). AWS Lambda runs the business logic serverlessly and scales automatically with the varying load, and DynamoDB with on-demand capacity delivers single-digit-millisecond latency while auto-scaling read/write capacity to match peaks. This combination satisfies every requirement: unchanged REST model, API-key throttling/segmentation, automatic scaling, and low-latency session access. Option D (AppSync) is GraphQL, which would change the API model, and Aurora Serverless (especially v1) has scaling lag that is not ideal for low-latency key-value session lookups.","explanation_zh":"決定性條件有兩個：(1) 後端公開的是 REST API，且要求「API 模型不應改變」；(2) 使用「不同的 API key 進行節流並區分正式與測試流量」。Amazon API Gateway 原生支援建立 REST API，並提供 usage plans 與 API keys，可依 stage 對請求節流並識別用戶端（live stage 與 test stage 直接對應不同 API key）。AWS Lambda 以無伺服器方式執行商業邏輯並隨負載自動擴展，DynamoDB 搭配 on-demand 容量提供個位數毫秒延遲，同時自動擴展讀寫容量以因應尖峰。此組合滿足所有需求：保留 REST 模型、API key 節流/區分、自動擴展、低延遲 session 存取。選項 D 的 AppSync 是 GraphQL，會改變 API 模型；而 Aurora Serverless（尤其 v1）有擴展延遲，不適合低延遲的鍵值 session 查詢。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A Network Load Balancer operates at Layer 4 and is not a REST API management service; it does not natively provide API keys, usage plans, or request throttling to distinguish live/test traffic. Running business logic on a single EC2 instance behind the NLB also reintroduces capacity/scaling management instead of handling the varying load automatically.","why_zh":"Network Load Balancer 在第 4 層運作，並非 REST API 管理服務，無法原生提供 API key、usage plans 或節流以區分正式/測試流量。將商業邏輯放在 NLB 後的單一 EC2 執行個體也重新引入容量/擴展管理，無法自動因應負載變化。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"An Application Load Balancer can invoke Lambda, but it is not a REST API gateway and does not provide usage plans or API keys for throttling and live/test traffic separation. The requirement to distinguish traffic via API keys and to throttle per key cannot be met by ALB, making API Gateway the necessary front end.","why_zh":"Application Load Balancer 可呼叫 Lambda，但它不是 REST API 閘道，無法提供 usage plans 或 API key 來進行節流及區分正式/測試流量。以 API key 區分流量並依 key 節流的需求 ALB 無法滿足，因此必須使用 API Gateway 作為前端。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS AppSync is a GraphQL service, so adopting it would change the API model, directly violating the 'API model should not be changed' constraint for an existing REST API. Aurora Serverless (v1 in particular) has scaling latency and is a relational engine that is less suited than DynamoDB for low-latency, high-throughput player session lookups. This is the dump's suggested answer but it is wrong on the REST-vs-GraphQL distinction.","why_zh":"AWS AppSync 是 GraphQL 服務，採用它會改變 API 模型，直接違反現有 REST API「API 模型不應改變」的限制。Aurora Serverless（尤其 v1）有擴展延遲，且為關聯式引擎，相較 DynamoDB 較不適合低延遲、高吞吐的玩家 session 查詢。這是題庫建議答案，但在 REST 與 GraphQL 的區別上是錯誤的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/api-gateway-api-usage-plans.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/on-demand-capacity-mode.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/Introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/appsync/latest/devguide/graphql-types.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":331,"question_en":"A company is migrating an application to the AWS Cloud. The application runs in an on-premises data center and writes thousands of images into a mounted NFS file system each night. After the company migrates the application, the company will host the application on an Amazon EC2 instance with a mounted Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. The company has established an AWS Direct Connect connection to AWS. Before the migration cutover, a solutions architect must build a process that will replicate the newly created on-premises images to the EFS file system. What is the MOST operationally e®cient way to replicate the images?","question_zh":"一家公司正在将应用程序迁移到 AWS 云。该应用程序在本地数据中心运行，每晚将数千个图像写入已安装的 NFS 文件系统中。在公 司迁移应用程序后，公司将在安装有 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统的 Amazon EC2 实例上托管该应用程序。 该公司已建立与 AWS 的 AWS Direct Connect 连接。在迁移转换之前，解决方案架构师必须构建一个流程，将新创建的本地映像复制 到 EFS 文件系统。 复制图像最有效的操作方法是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a periodic process to run the aws s3 sync command from the on-premises file system to Amazon S3. Configure an AWS Lambda function to process event notifications from Amazon S3 and copy the images from Amazon S3 to the EFS file system.","B":"Deploy an AWS Storage Gateway file gateway with an NFS mount point. Mount the file gateway file system on the on-premises server. Configure a process to periodically copy the images to the mount point.","C":"Deploy an AWS DataSync agent to an on-premises server that has access to the NFS file system. Send data over the Direct Connect connection to an S3 bucket by using a public VIF. Configure an AWS Lambda function to process event notifications from Amazon S3 and copy the images from Amazon S3 to the EFS file system.","D":"Deploy an AWS DataSync agent to an on-premises server that has access to the NFS file system. Send data over the Direct Connect connection to an AWS PrivateLink interface VPC endpoint for Amazon EFS by using a private VIF. Configure a DataSync scheduled task to send the images to the EFS file system every 24 hours."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置定期进程以运行从本地文件系统到 Amazon S3 的 aws s3sync 命令。配置 AWS Lambda 函数以处理来自 Amazon S3 的事件通 知并将图像从 Amazon S3 复制到 EFS 文件系统。","B":"使用 NFS 挂载点部署 AWS Storage Gateway 文件网关。在本地服务器上挂载文件网关文件系统。配置进程以定期将映像复制到 挂载点。","C":"将 AWS DataSync 代理部署到有权访问 NFS 文件系统的本地服务器。使用公共 VIF 通过 Direct Connect 连接将数据发送到 S3 存 储桶。配置 AWS Lambda 函数以处理来自 Amazon S3 的事件通知并将图像从 Amazon S3 复制到 EFS 文件系统。","D":"将 AWS DataSync 代理部署到有权访问 NFS 文件系统的本地服务器。使用私有 VIF 通过 Direct Connect 连接将数据发送到 Amazon EFS 的 AWS PrivateLink 接口 VPC 终端节点。配置 DataSync 计划任务以每 24 小时将映像发送到 EFS 文件系统。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"AWS DataSync natively supports Amazon EFS as a transfer destination and can copy directly from an on-premises NFS source location to an EFS destination location, with a scheduled task to run periodically (e.g., every 24 hours). Sending traffic over Direct Connect via a private VIF to a private VPC endpoint (the EFS file system's elastic network interfaces in the VPC) is the AWS-documented architecture for DataSync transfers to a file system over Direct Connect. This single managed service handles incremental detection, scheduling, retries, encryption, and data integrity verification, so it is the MOST operationally efficient option. Option C is needlessly complex and incorrect: it routes DataSync to S3 and then bolts on a Lambda function to copy objects from S3 into EFS, adding an intermediate store, custom event-processing code, and extra failure points when DataSync can write to EFS directly. Therefore D is the lowest-overhead, fully native solution.","explanation_zh":"AWS DataSync 原生支援以 Amazon EFS 作為傳輸目的地，可直接從地端 NFS 來源 location 複製到 EFS 目的地 location，並以排程任務定期執行（例如每 24 小時）。透過 private VIF 經由 Direct Connect 將流量送到 VPC 內 EFS 檔案系統的私有 VPC endpoint（elastic network interface），正是 AWS 官方文件所描述、經由 Direct Connect 進行 DataSync 檔案系統傳輸的架構。此單一受管服務即可處理增量偵測、排程、重試、加密與資料完整性驗證，因此是「最具運維效率」的選項。選項 C 不必要地複雜且不正確：它先讓 DataSync 傳到 S3，再加掛一個 Lambda 函式把物件從 S3 複製到 EFS，憑空增加中介儲存、自訂事件處理程式與更多故障點，而 DataSync 本可直接寫入 EFS。因此 D 是運維負擔最低、完全原生的解法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Using aws s3 sync plus an S3 event-driven Lambda to land files in EFS is a hand-built multi-stage pipeline (S3 staging bucket, custom Lambda code, event notifications) with far more operational overhead than DataSync's native NFS-to-EFS transfer, and it does not leverage the existing Direct Connect link efficiently.","why_zh":"用 aws s3 sync 加上 S3 事件觸發的 Lambda 把檔案落到 EFS，是自行打造的多階段管線（S3 暫存桶、自訂 Lambda 程式、事件通知），運維負擔遠高於 DataSync 原生 NFS 到 EFS 的傳輸，且未有效利用既有的 Direct Connect 連線。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Storage Gateway file gateway backs an NFS/SMB mount with Amazon S3, not EFS. It would not place images into the target EFS file system, and you would still need an additional process to move data from S3 into EFS, so it does not meet the requirement efficiently.","why_zh":"AWS Storage Gateway file gateway 是以 Amazon S3 為後端支撐 NFS/SMB 掛載，而非 EFS。它無法將影像放入目標 EFS 檔案系統，仍需額外流程把資料從 S3 搬到 EFS，因此無法有效滿足需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it is technically inferior: DataSync can write directly to EFS, so routing through an S3 bucket (public VIF) and then adding a Lambda function to copy S3 objects into EFS introduces an unnecessary intermediate store, custom code, and more moving parts, increasing operational overhead rather than minimizing it.","why_zh":"這是題庫建議答案，但技術上較差：DataSync 本可直接寫入 EFS，因此先經由 S3 桶（public VIF）再加上 Lambda 把 S3 物件複製到 EFS，憑空增加中介儲存、自訂程式與更多元件，提高而非降低運維負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datasync/latest/userguide/direct-connect-architecture.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datasync/latest/userguide/what-is-datasync.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datasync/latest/userguide/create-nfs-location.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datasync/latest/userguide/networking-datasync.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/how-it-works.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":332,"question_en":"A company recently migrated a web application from an on-premises data center to the AWS Cloud. The web application infrastructure consists of an Amazon CloudFront distribution that routes to an Application Load Balancer (ALB), with Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) to process requests. A recent security audit revealed that the web application is accessible by using both CloudFront and ALB endpoints. However, the company requires that the web application must be accessible only by using the CloudFront endpoint. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST amount of effort?","question_zh":"一家公司最近将 Web 应用程序从本地数据中心迁移到 AWS 云。Web 应用程序基础设施由 Amazon CloudFront 分配组成，该分配路由 到应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB)，并使用 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 来处理请求。最近的安全审核显示，可以使用 CloudFront 和 ALB 端点访问该 Web 应用程序。但是，该公司要求只能使用 CloudFront 端点访问 Web 应用程序。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的努力满足此要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new security group and attach it to the CloudFront distribution. Update the ALB security group ingress to allow access only from the CloudFront security group.","B":"Update ALB security group ingress to allow access only from the com.amazonaws.global.cloudfront.origin-facing CloudFront managed prefix list.","C":"Create a com.amazonaws.region.elasticloadbalancing VPC interface endpoint for Elastic Load Balancing. Update the ALB scheme from internet-facing to internal.","D":"Extract CloudFront IPs from the AWS provided ip-ranges.json document. Update ALB security group ingress to allow access only from CloudFront IPs."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的安全组并将其附加到 CloudFront 分配。更新 ALB 安全组入口以仅允许从 CloudFront 安全组进行访问。","B":"更新 ALB 安全组入口，以仅允许从面向 com.amazonaws.global.cloudfront.origin 的 CloudFront 托管前缀列表进行访问。","C":"为 Elastic Load Balancing 创建 com.amazonaws.region.elasticloadbalancing VPC 接口终端节点。将 ALB 方案从面向互联网更新为 内部。","D":"从 AWS 提供的 ip-ranges.json 文档中提取 CloudFront IP。更新 ALB 安全组入口以仅允许从 CloudFront IP 进行访问。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to make the web application reachable only through CloudFront, with the LEAST effort, while keeping the internet-facing ALB. AWS publishes a CloudFront-managed prefix list, com.amazonaws.global.cloudfront.origin-facing, that contains the IP ranges of all CloudFront origin-facing servers. By updating the ALB security group ingress to allow traffic only from this prefix list (and removing other inbound rules), all non-CloudFront traffic is blocked. CloudFront keeps the list current automatically, so there is no ongoing maintenance, making this a single, low-effort change. The AWS 'Restrict access to Application Load Balancers' and 'Locations and IP address ranges of CloudFront edge servers' pages explicitly document this exact approach.","explanation_zh":"需求是讓 web application 只能透過 CloudFront 存取,且要用最少的工作量,同時保留 internet-facing 的 ALB。AWS 提供一個由 CloudFront 維護的 managed prefix list:com.amazonaws.global.cloudfront.origin-facing,內含所有 CloudFront origin-facing 伺服器的 IP 範圍。只要把 ALB security group 的 ingress 改成僅允許此 prefix list 的流量(並移除其他 inbound 規則),即可阻擋所有非 CloudFront 的流量。CloudFront 會自動維護此清單,無須持續維運,因此這是單一且低工作量的變更。AWS 的 'Restrict access to Application Load Balancers' 與 'Locations and IP address ranges of CloudFront edge servers' 文件明確記載了此做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"You cannot attach a security group to a CloudFront distribution, and an ALB security group cannot reference a CloudFront distribution as a source. CloudFront is a global edge service, not a VPC resource, so security-group-to-security-group referencing is not possible here. This option is technically impossible.","why_zh":"無法將 security group 掛到 CloudFront distribution 上,ALB 的 security group 也無法把 CloudFront distribution 當作來源來引用。CloudFront 是全球邊緣服務而非 VPC 資源,因此無法用 security group 互相引用,此選項在技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Changing the ALB to internal would break CloudFront's ability to reach it via a public DNS name (unless using VPC origins, which is a different architecture not described). A com.amazonaws.region.elasticloadbalancing VPC interface endpoint is for the ELB management API, not the data path, so it does not route viewer traffic. This is a major re-architecture and does not meet the goal with least effort.","why_zh":"把 ALB 改為 internal 會讓 CloudFront 無法透過公開 DNS 名稱連到它(除非改用 VPC origins,但那是另一種未被描述的架構)。com.amazonaws.region.elasticloadbalancing VPC interface endpoint 是給 ELB 管理 API 用的,不是資料路徑,無法路由觀眾流量。這是大幅度的重新架構,且無法以最少工作量達成目標。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Extracting CloudFront IPs from ip-ranges.json technically works but requires ongoing manual updates whenever the IP ranges change. AWS explicitly recommends the managed prefix list precisely so you do not need to read or maintain the IP list yourself, so D involves substantially more effort than B.","why_zh":"從 ip-ranges.json 取出 CloudFront IP 技術上可行,但每當 IP 範圍變動時都需手動更新。AWS 明確建議使用 managed prefix list,正是為了讓你不必自行讀取或維護 IP 清單,因此 D 的工作量遠高於 B。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/LocationsOfEdgeServers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/restrict-access-to-load-balancer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/working-with-aws-managed-prefix-lists.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":333,"question_en":"A company hosts a community forum site using an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and a Docker application hosted in an Amazon ECS cluster. The site data is stored in Amazon RDS for MySQL and the container image is stored in ECR. The company needs to provide their customers with a disaster recovery SLA with an RTO of no more than 24 hours and RPO of no more than 8 hours. Which of the following solutions is the MOST cost-effective way to meet the requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 和 Amazon ECS 集群中托管的 Docker 应用程序托管社区论坛网站。站点数据存储在 Amazon RDS for MySQL 中，容器映像存储在 ECR 中。该公司需要为其客户提供灾难恢复 SLA，其中 RTO 不超过 24 小时，RPO 不超过 8 小 时。 以下哪种解决方案是满足要求的最具成本效益的方法？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudFormation to deploy identical ALB, EC2, ECS and RDS resources in two regions. Schedule RDS snapshots every 8 hours. Use RDS multi-region replication to update the secondary region's copy of the database. In the event of a failure, restore from the latest snapshot, and use an Amazon Route 53 DNS failover policy to automatically redirect customers to the ALB in the secondary region.","B":"Store the Docker image in ECR in two regions. Schedule RDS snapshots every 8 hours with snapshots copied to the secondary region. In the event of a failure, use AWS CloudFormation to deploy the ALB, EC2, ECS and RDS resources in the secondary region, restore from the latest snapshot, and update the DNS record to point to the ALB in the secondary region.","C":"Use AWS CloudFormation to deploy identical ALB, EC2, ECS, and RDS resources in a secondary region. Schedule hourly RDS MySQL backups to Amazon S3 and use cross-region replication to replicate data to a bucket in the secondary region. In the event of a failure, import the latest Docker image to Amazon ECR in the secondary region, deploy to the EC2 instance, restore the latest MySQL backup, and update the DNS record to point to the ALB in the secondary region.","D":"Deploy a pilot light environment in a secondary region with an ALB and a minimal resource EC2 deployment for Docker in an AWS Auto Scaling group with a scaling policy to increase instance size and number of nodes. Create a cross-region read replica of the RDS data. In the event of a failure, promote the replica to primary, and update the DNS record to point to the ALB in the secondary region."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 在两个区域部署相同的 ALB、EC2、ECS 和 RDS 资源。每 8 小时安排一次 RDS 快照。使用 RDS 多区域 复制来更新辅助区域的数据库副本。如果发生故障，请从最新快照恢复，并使用 Amazon Route 53 DNS 故障转移策略自动将客户 重定向到次要区域中的 ALB。","B":"将 Docker 镜像存储在两个区域的 ECR 中。每 8 小时计划一次 RDS 快照，并将快照复制到次要区域。如果发生故障，请使用 AWS CloudFormation 在次要区域中部署 ALB、EC2、ECS 和 RDS 资源，从最新快照进行恢复，并更新 DNS 记录以指向次要区域中 的 ALB。","C":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 在次要区域中部署相同的 ALB、EC2、ECS 和 RDS 资源。安排每小时 RDS MySQL 备份到 Amazon S3， 并使用跨区域复制将数据复制到次要区域中的存储桶。如果出现故障，请将最新的 Docker 映像导入到次要区域中的 Amazon ECR，部署到 EC2 实例，恢复最新的 MySQL 备份，并更新 DNS 记录以指向次要区域中的 ALB。","D":"在次要区域中部署一个试点环境，其中包含 ALB 和 AWS Auto Scaling 组中 Docker 的最小资源 EC2 部署，并采用扩展策略来增 加实例大小和节点数量。创建RDS数据的跨区域只读副本。如果出现故障，请将副本提升为主要副本，并更新 DNS 记录以指向次 要区域中的 ALB。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":91},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":334,"question_en":"A company is migrating its infrastructure to the AWS Cloud. The company must comply with a variety of regulatory standards for different projects. The company needs a multi-account environment. A solutions architect needs to prepare the baseline infrastructure. The solution must provide a consistent baseline of management and security, but it must allow ­exibility for different compliance requirements within various AWS accounts. The solution also needs to integrate with the existing on-premises Active Directory Federation Services (AD FS) server. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST amount of operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在将其基础设施迁移到 AWS 云。公司必须遵守针对不同项目的各种监管标准。公司需要一个多帐户环境。 解决方案架构师需要准备基线基础设施。该解决方案必须提供一致的管理和安全基线，但必须能够灵活地满足各种 AWS 账户内的不 同合规性要求。该解决方案还需要与现有的本地 Active Directory 联合身份验证服务 (AD FS) 服务器集成。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an organization in AWS Organizations. Create a single SCP for least privilege access across all accounts. Create a single OU for all accounts. Configure an IAM identity provider for federation with the on-premises AD FS server. Configure a central logging account with a defined process for log generating services to send log events to the central account. Enable AWS Config in the central account with conformance packs for all accounts.","B":"Create an organization in AWS Organizations. Enable AWS Control Tower on the organization. Review included controls (guardrails) for SCPs. Check AWS Config for areas that require additions. Add OUs as necessary. Connect AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) to the on-premises AD FS server.","C":"Create an organization in AWS Organizations. Create SCPs for least privilege access. Create an OU structure, and use it to group AWS accounts. Connect AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) to the on-premises AD FS server. Configure a central logging account with a defined process for log generating services to send log events to the central account. Enable AWS Config in the central account with aggregators and conformance packs.","D":"Create an organization in AWS Organizations. Enable AWS Control Tower on the organization. Review included controls (guardrails) for SCPs. Check AWS Config for areas that require additions. Configure an IAM identity provider for federation with the on-premises AD FS server."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS Organizations 中创建一个组织。创建单个 SCP 以实现所有帐户的最低权限访问。为所有帐户创建一个 OU。配置 IAM 身 份提供商以与本地 AD FS 服务器联合。使用定义的日志生成服务流程配置中央日志记录帐户，以将日志事件发送到中央帐户。在 中央账户中启用 AWS Config，并为所有账户提供一致性包。","B":"在 AWS Organizations 中创建组织。在组织上启用 AWS Control Tower。审查包括 SCP 的控制（护栏）。检查 AWS Config 是否有 需要添加的区域。根据需要添加 OU。将 AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) 连接到本地 AD FS 服务器。","C":"在 AWS Organizations 中创建组织。创建 SCP 以实现最低权限访问。创建 OU 结构，并使用它对 AWS 账户进行分组。将 AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) 连接到本地 AD FS 服务器。使用定义的日志生成服务流程配置中央日志记录帐户，以将日 志事件发送到中央帐户。使用聚合器和一致性包在中央账户中启用 AWS Config。","D":"在 AWS Organizations 中创建组织。在组织上启用 AWS Control Tower。审查包括 SCP 的控制（护栏）。检查 AWS Config 是否有 需要添加的区域。配置 IAM 身份提供商以与本地 AD FS 服务器联合。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The qualifier is LEAST operational overhead. AWS Control Tower is a managed service that orchestrates AWS Organizations, AWS Config, AWS Service Catalog, and AWS IAM Identity Center to stand up a well-architected multi-account landing zone in under an hour, automatically creating a security/audit account, a centralized log archive account, an OU structure, and preventive/detective controls (guardrails implemented as SCPs and Config rules). This delivers the required consistent baseline of management and security while letting you add OUs and elective controls for differing compliance needs - all as managed infrastructure rather than hand-built SCPs, aggregators, and logging pipelines. For the AD FS integration, AD FS is a SAML 2.0 IdP, and the lowest-overhead, AWS-recommended approach is to connect IAM Identity Center (which Control Tower already deploys and uses as its access layer) to the external SAML IdP once, centrally. Option B does exactly this. Option D is identical to B on the Control Tower side but configures a classic per-account IAM identity provider (IAM SAML federation), which works against Control Tower's IAM Identity Center design and requires per-account setup - higher overhead. Options A and C build the entire baseline (custom SCPs, OUs, central logging, Config aggregators and conformance packs) manually, which is far more operational overhead than the managed Control Tower landing zone.","explanation_zh":"本題限定條件為「最少維運負擔（LEAST operational overhead）」。AWS Control Tower 是受管服務，會自動編排 AWS Organizations、AWS Config、AWS Service Catalog 與 AWS IAM Identity Center，在一小時內建立符合 Well-Architected 的多帳戶 landing zone，並自動建立 security/audit 帳戶、集中式 log archive 帳戶、OU 結構，以及預防性/偵測性 controls（以 SCP 和 Config rules 實作的 guardrails）。這提供了所需的一致管理與安全基線，同時可再新增 OU 與選用 controls 以滿足不同的合規需求，且全部為受管基礎設施，而非手動建構 SCP、aggregator 與日誌管線。至於 AD FS 整合，AD FS 屬於 SAML 2.0 IdP，最低負擔且 AWS 建議的做法是將 Control Tower 已部署並作為存取層的 IAM Identity Center 一次性集中連接到外部 SAML IdP。選項 B 正是如此。選項 D 在 Control Tower 部分與 B 相同，但改用傳統的逐帳戶 IAM identity provider（IAM SAML 聯合），與 Control Tower 的 IAM Identity Center 設計相違，且需逐帳戶設定，負擔較高。選項 A 與 C 則手動建構整個基線（自訂 SCP、OU、集中日誌、Config aggregator 與 conformance packs），維運負擔遠高於受管的 Control Tower landing zone。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Manually builds everything (single SCP, single OU, custom central logging, Config conformance packs) and uses per-account IAM SAML federation. A single OU and single SCP cannot provide flexibility for different compliance requirements, and the all-manual baseline is far more operational overhead than Control Tower.","why_zh":"全手動建構（單一 SCP、單一 OU、自訂集中日誌、Config conformance packs）並採用逐帳戶 IAM SAML 聯合。單一 OU 與單一 SCP 無法為不同合規需求提供彈性，且全手動基線的維運負擔遠高於 Control Tower。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Uses IAM Identity Center for AD FS (good) but manually constructs SCPs, OU structure, a central logging account, and Config aggregators/conformance packs. This duplicates what Control Tower delivers as managed infrastructure, so it has significantly higher operational overhead.","why_zh":"AD FS 部分使用 IAM Identity Center（正確），但手動建構 SCP、OU 結構、集中日誌帳戶及 Config aggregator/conformance packs。這等於重做 Control Tower 已受管交付的內容，維運負擔明顯更高。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Identical Control Tower setup to B, but federates via a classic per-account IAM identity provider instead of IAM Identity Center. Control Tower already provisions and integrates IAM Identity Center as its access layer; configuring separate IAM SAML providers per account adds overhead and conflicts with the managed design, so it is not the LEAST overhead.","why_zh":"Control Tower 設定與 B 相同，但改以傳統逐帳戶 IAM identity provider 而非 IAM Identity Center 進行聯合。Control Tower 已佈建並整合 IAM Identity Center 作為存取層；逐帳戶設定 IAM SAML provider 會增加負擔並與受管設計衝突，故非最少負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/what-is-control-tower.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/aws-multi-account-landing-zone.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/how-to-connect-idp.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_providers.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":335,"question_en":"An online magazine will launch its latest edition this month. This edition will be the first to be distributed globally. The magazine's dynamic website currently uses an Application Load Balancer in front of the web tier, a ­eet of Amazon EC2 instances for web and application servers, and Amazon Aurora MySQL. Portions of the website include static content and almost all tra®c is read-only. The magazine is expecting a significant spike in internet tra®c when the new edition is launched. Optimal performance is a top priority for the week following the launch. Which combination of steps should a solutions architect take to reduce system response times for a global audience? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一本在线杂志将于本月推出最新一期。该版本将是第一个在全球发行的版本。该杂志的动态网站目前在 Web 层前面使用应用程序负 载均衡器、一组用于 Web 和应用程序服务器的 Amazon EC2 实例以及 Amazon Aurora MySQL。该网站的部分内容包含静态内容，几乎 所有流量都是只读的。 该杂志预计新版本推出后互联网流量将大幅增加。最佳性能是发布后一周的首要任务。 解决方案架构师应采取哪些步骤组合来减少全球受众的系统响应时间？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Use logical cross-Region replication to replicate the Aurora MySQL database to a secondary Region. Replace the web servers with Amazon S3. Deploy S3 buckets in cross-Region replication mode.","B":"Ensure the web and application tiers are each in Auto Scaling groups. Introduce an AWS Direct Connect connection. Deploy the web and application tiers in Regions across the world.","C":"Migrate the database from Amazon Aurora to Amazon RDS for MySQL. Ensure all three of the application tiers – web, application, and database – are in private subnets.","D":"Use an Aurora global database for physical cross-Region replication. Use Amazon S3 with cross-Region replication for static content and resources. Deploy the web and application tiers in Regions across the world.","E":"Introduce Amazon Route 53 with latency-based routing and Amazon CloudFront distributions. Ensure the web and application tiers are each in Auto Scaling groups."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用逻辑跨区域复制将 Aurora MySQL 数据库复制到辅助区域。将 Web 服务器替换为 Amazon S3。以跨区域复制模式部署S3存 储桶。","B":"确保 Web 层和应用程序层均位于 Auto Scaling 组中。引入 AWS Direct Connect 连接。在世界各地的区域部署 Web 和应用程序 层。","C":"将数据库从 Amazon Aurora 迁移到 Amazon RDS for MySQL。确保所有三个应用程序层（Web、应用程序和数据库）均位于私有 子网中。","D":"使用 Aurora 全局数据库进行物理跨区域复制。使用 Amazon S3 进行静态内容和资源的跨区域复制。在世界各地的区域部署 Web 和应用程序层。","E":"引入具有基于延迟的路由和 Amazon CloudFront 发行版的 Amazon Route 53。确保 Web 层和应用程序层均位于 Auto Scaling 组 中。"},"answer":["D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"DE":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":336,"question_en":"An online gaming company needs to optimize the cost of its workloads on AWS. The company uses a dedicated account to host the production environment for its online gaming application and an analytics application. Amazon EC2 instances host the gaming application and must always be available. The EC2 instances run all year. The analytics application uses data that is stored in Amazon S3. The analytics application can be interrupted and resumed without issue. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家在线游戏公司需要优化 AWS 上的工作负载成本。该公司使用专用帐户来托管其在线游戏应用程序和分析应用程序的生产环境。 Amazon EC2 实例托管游戏应用程序并且必须始终可用。EC2 实例全年运行。分析应用程序使用存储在 Amazon S3 中的数据。分析应 用程序可以毫无问题地中断和恢复。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Purchase an EC2 Instance Savings Plan for the online gaming application instances. Use On-Demand Instances for the analytics application.","B":"Purchase an EC2 Instance Savings Plan for the online gaming application instances. Use Spot Instances for the analytics application.","C":"Use Spot Instances for the online gaming application and the analytics application. Set up a catalog in AWS Service Catalog to provision services at a discount.","D":"Use On-Demand Instances for the online gaming application. Use Spot Instances for the analytics application. Set up a catalog in AWS Service Catalog to provision services at a discount."},"options_zh":{"A":"为在线游戏应用程序实例购买 EC2 Instance Savings Plan。将按需实例用于分析应用程序。","B":"为在线游戏应用程序实例购买 EC2 Instance Savings Plan。将 Spot 实例用于分析应用程序。","C":"将 Spot 实例用于在线游戏应用程序和分析应用程序。在 AWS Service Catalog 中设置目录以折扣方式预置服务。","D":"对在线游戏应用程序使用按需实例。将 Spot 实例用于分析应用程序。在 AWS Service Catalog 中设置目录以折扣方式预置服 务。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":337,"question_en":"A company runs applications in hundreds of production AWS accounts. The company uses AWS Organizations with all features enabled and has a centralized backup operation that uses AWS Backup. The company is concerned about ransomware attacks. To address this concern, the company has created a new policy that all backups must be resilient to breaches of privileged-user credentials in any production account. Which combination of steps will meet this new requirement? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在数百个生产 AWS 账户中运行应用程序。该公司使用启用了所有功能的 AWS Organizations，并使用 AWS Backup 进行集中 备份操作。 该公司担心勒索软件攻击。为了解决这个问题，该公司制定了一项新政策，即所有备份都必须能够抵御任何生产帐户中特权用户凭 据的泄露。 哪种步骤组合可以满足这一新要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Implement cross-account backup with AWS Backup vaults in designated non-production accounts.","B":"Add an SCP that restricts the modification of AWS Backup vaults.","C":"Implement least privilege access for the IAM service role that is assigned to AWS Backup.","D":"Configure the backup frequency, lifecycle, and retention period to ensure that at least one backup always exists in the cold tier.","E":"Configure AWS Backup to write all backups to an Amazon S3 bucket in a designated non-production account. Ensure that the S3 bucket has S3 Object Lock enabled."},"options_zh":{"A":"在指定的非生产账户中使用 AWS Backup 文件库实施跨账户备份。","B":"添加限制修改 AWS Backup 文件库的 SCP。","C":"为分配给 AWS Backup 的 IAM 服务角色实施最低权限访问。","D":"配置备份频率、生命周期和保留期限，确保冷层中始终存在至少一份备份。","E":"配置 AWS Backup 以将所有备份写入指定非生产账户中的 Amazon S3 存储桶。确保 S3 存储桶启用了 S3 对象锁定。"},"answer":["A","C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ABC":54,"ACD":31,"ACE":15},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B","C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The threat model is a breach of privileged-user (admin/root) credentials in any production account, so the controls must keep backups out of reach of, or non-modifiable by, those credentials. (A) Cross-account backup to designated non-production accounts physically isolates the backup copies in separate AWS accounts; a privileged credential compromised in a production account has no authority in the backup destination account, so it cannot delete or alter those copies. (B) An SCP that restricts modification of AWS Backup vaults is an organization-level guardrail that even the member account root user cannot override, so privileged users in production accounts are prevented from tampering with vaults. (C) Implementing least privilege for the AWS Backup IAM service role reduces the blast radius and is a defense-in-depth layer that complements A and B. The remaining options are technically inadequate: D (keeping a copy in the cold tier) is a cost/storage class choice that provides no immutability and does not stop a privileged user from deleting it, and E is invalid because AWS Backup writes recovery points to backup vaults, not to a customer-specified Amazon S3 bucket with Object Lock. The dump's ['A','C','D'] is wrong because D adds no resilience against credential breaches, whereas an SCP (B) is the org-wide guardrail that does.","explanation_zh":"威脅模型是任何 production 帳戶中特權使用者（admin/root）憑證遭到入侵，因此控制措施必須讓備份脫離這些憑證的控制範圍或使其無法被修改。(A) 跨帳戶備份到指定的 non-production 帳戶，將備份副本實體隔離在獨立的 AWS 帳戶中；在 production 帳戶中被盜用的特權憑證在備份目的帳戶中沒有任何權限，因此無法刪除或變更這些副本。(B) 限制修改 AWS Backup vault 的 SCP 是組織層級的護欄，連成員帳戶的 root 使用者都無法繞過，因此可防止 production 帳戶中的特權使用者竄改 vault。(C) 為 AWS Backup IAM service role 實施最小權限可縮小受影響範圍，是與 A、B 互補的縱深防禦層。其餘選項在技術上不充分：D（在 cold tier 保留一份副本）只是成本/儲存類別的選擇，不提供不可變性，也無法阻止特權使用者刪除它；E 不成立，因為 AWS Backup 是將 recovery point 寫入 backup vault，而非寫入客戶指定且啟用 Object Lock 的 Amazon S3 bucket。Dump 的 ['A','C','D'] 是錯的，因為 D 對憑證入侵不增加任何韌性，而 SCP（B）才是組織層級的有效護欄。","distractors":[{"letter":"D","why_en":"Keeping at least one backup in the cold tier is a storage-class/cost choice (e.g., 90-day minimum). Cold storage provides no immutability or WORM protection and does not prevent a privileged user from deleting the recovery point, so it adds no resilience to a credential breach.","why_zh":"在 cold tier 保留至少一份備份只是儲存類別/成本的選擇（例如最少 90 天）。冷儲存不提供不可變性或 WORM 保護，也無法阻止特權使用者刪除 recovery point，因此對憑證入侵毫無韌性。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"AWS Backup writes recovery points to AWS Backup vaults, not to an arbitrary customer-specified Amazon S3 bucket. You cannot configure AWS Backup to write all backups to an S3 bucket with Object Lock, so this option is not how the service works.","why_zh":"AWS Backup 是將 recovery point 寫入 AWS Backup vault，而非寫入任意客戶指定的 Amazon S3 bucket。無法設定 AWS Backup 將所有備份寫入啟用 Object Lock 的 S3 bucket，因此此選項不符合服務的運作方式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/create-cross-account-backup.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/vault-lock.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/create-a-vault-access-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/security-best-practices/safeguard.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識・多選項拉鋸・複選・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":338,"question_en":"A company needs to aggregate Amazon CloudWatch logs from its AWS accounts into one central logging account. The collected logs must remain in the AWS Region of creation. The central logging account will then process the logs, normalize the logs into standard output format, and stream the output logs to a security tool for more processing. A solutions architect must design a solution that can handle a large volume of logging data that needs to be ingested. Less logging will occur outside normal business hours than during normal business hours. The logging solution must scale with the anticipated load. The solutions architect has decided to use an AWS Control Tower design to handle the multi-account logging process. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect take to meet the requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司需要将其 AWS 账户中的 Amazon CloudWatch 日志聚合到一个中央日志记录账户中。收集的日志必须保留在创建的 AWS 区域 中。然后，中央日志记录帐户将处理日志，将日志标准化为标准输出格式，并将输出日志流式传输到安全工具以进行更多处理。 解决方案架构师必须设计一个能够处理需要摄取的大量日志记录数据的解决方案。正常工作时间之外发生的日志记录比正常工作时 间内发生的日志记录要少。日志记录解决方案必须根据预期负载进行扩展。解决方案架构师决定使用 AWS Control Tower 设计来处理 多账户日志记录过程。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪些步骤组合来满足要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a destination Amazon Kinesis data stream in the central logging account.","B":"Create a destination Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue in the central logging account.","C":"Create an IAM role that grants Amazon CloudWatch Logs the permission to add data to the Amazon Kinesis data stream. Create a trust policy. Specify the trust policy in the IAM role. In each member account, create a subscription filter for each log group to send data to the Kinesis data stream.","D":"Create an IAM role that grants Amazon CloudWatch Logs the permission to add data to the Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Create a trust policy. Specify the trust policy in the IAM role. In each member account, create a single subscription filter for all log groups to send data to the SQS queue.","E":"Create an AWS Lambda function. Program the Lambda function to normalize the logs in the central logging account and to write the logs to the security tool.","F":"Create an AWS Lambda function. Program the Lambda function to normalize the logs in the member accounts and to write the logs to the security tool."},"options_zh":{"A":"在中央日志记录账户中创建目标 Amazon Kinesis 数据流。","B":"在中央日志记录账户中创建目标 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列。","C":"创建一个 IAM 角色，向 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 授予将数据添加到 Amazon Kinesis 数据流的权限。制定信托政策。指定 IAM 角色中的信任策略。在每个成员账户中，为每个日志组创建订阅筛选器以将数据发送到 Kinesis 数据流。","D":"创建一个 IAM 角色，向 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 授予将数据添加到 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列的权限。制 定信托政策。指定 IAM 角色中的信任策略。在每个成员帐户中，为所有日志组创建单个订阅过滤器，以将数据发送到 SQS 队 列。","E":"创建 AWS Lambda 函数。对 Lambda 函数进行编程，以规范中央日志记录帐户中的日志并将日志写入安全工具。","F":"创建 AWS Lambda 函数。对 Lambda 函数进行编程，以规范成员帐户中的日志并将日志写入安全工具。"},"answer":["B","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ACE":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"CloudWatch Logs subscription filters can only deliver to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, AWS Lambda, Amazon Data Firehose, or Amazon OpenSearch Service - SQS is not a supported subscription-filter destination, which eliminates options B and D. The documented cross-account centralization pattern is: (A) create a destination Kinesis Data Stream in the central/recipient account; (C) create an IAM role with a trust policy that lets CloudWatch Logs (logs.amazonaws.com) put records into the stream, then in each member account create a subscription filter per log group pointing at the destination. The log group and its destination must be in the same Region, so logs remain in the Region of creation. Kinesis Data Streams scales with the anticipated variable load (on-demand mode 'instantly accommodates your workloads as they ramp up or down'), satisfying the business-hours-vs-off-hours scaling requirement. (E) The requirement explicitly states the CENTRAL logging account processes and normalizes the logs and streams them to the security tool, so the Lambda must run in the central account, not the member accounts (which rules out F).","explanation_zh":"CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 只能將資料傳送到 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams、AWS Lambda、Amazon Data Firehose 或 Amazon OpenSearch Service，SQS 並非支援的 subscription filter 目的地，因此排除選項 B 與 D。官方記載的跨帳號集中化模式為：(A) 在中央/接收帳號建立目的地 Kinesis Data Stream；(C) 建立一個含信任政策（trust policy，主體為 logs.amazonaws.com）的 IAM role 授權 CloudWatch Logs 將紀錄寫入該 stream，並在每個成員帳號針對各 log group 建立 subscription filter 指向該 destination。log group 與其 destination 必須位於同一個 Region，因此日誌會保留在建立時的 Region。Kinesis Data Streams 可隨預期的變動負載擴展（on-demand 模式可即時因應負載上升或下降），滿足正常上班時間與非上班時間的擴展需求。(E) 題目明確指出由中央日誌帳號處理、標準化日誌並串流至安全工具，因此 Lambda 必須在中央帳號執行，而非成員帳號（故排除 F）。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon SQS is not a valid destination for CloudWatch Logs subscription filters; only Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda, Firehose, and OpenSearch are supported. SQS also cannot natively keep logs Region-scoped via the subscription-filter mechanism in the documented pattern.","why_zh":"Amazon SQS 不是 CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 的有效目的地；只支援 Kinesis Data Streams、Lambda、Firehose 與 OpenSearch。SQS 也無法以官方記載的 subscription filter 機制原生承接日誌。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same fatal flaw as B: SQS cannot receive CloudWatch Logs via subscription filters. Additionally a 'single subscription filter for all log groups' is not how it works - account-level filters exist but the standard pattern uses per-log-group filters, and the destination type here (SQS) is invalid regardless.","why_zh":"與 B 同樣致命：SQS 無法透過 subscription filter 接收 CloudWatch Logs。此外『單一 subscription filter 涵蓋所有 log group』並非運作方式，且此處的目的地類型（SQS）本身就無效。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"The requirement explicitly states the CENTRAL logging account processes, normalizes, and streams logs to the security tool. Running normalization in each member account contradicts the centralized-processing requirement and would duplicate logic across accounts.","why_zh":"題目明確指出由中央日誌帳號處理、標準化並串流日誌至安全工具。在每個成員帳號執行標準化違反集中處理需求，且會在各帳號重複邏輯。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CreateDestination.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CrossAccountSubscriptions-Kinesis-Account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CreateSubscriptionFilter.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":339,"question_en":"A company is migrating a legacy application from an on-premises data center to AWS. The application consists of a single application server and a Microsoft SQL Server database server. Each server is deployed on a VMware VM that consumes 500 TB of data across multiple attached volumes. The company has established a 10 Gbps AWS Direct Connect connection from the closest AWS Region to its on-premises data center. The Direct Connect connection is not currently in use by other services. Which combination of steps should a solutions architect take to migrate the application with the LEAST amount of downtime? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在将旧应用程序从本地数据中心迁移到 AWS。该应用程序由单个应用程序服务器和 Microsoft SQL Server 数据库服务器组 成。每台服务器都部署在 VMware VM 上，该 VM 跨多个附加卷消耗 500 TB 的数据。 该公司已在最近的 AWS 区域与其本地数据中心之间建立了 10 Gbps AWS Direct Connect 连接。Direct Connect 连接当前未被其他服务使 用。 解决方案架构师应采取哪种步骤组合来以最短的停机时间迁移应用程序？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Use an AWS Server Migration Service (AWS SMS) replication job to migrate the database server VM to AWS.","B":"Use VM Import/Export to import the application server VM.","C":"Export the VM images to an AWS Snowball Edge Storage Optimized device.","D":"Use an AWS Server Migration Service (AWS SMS) replication job to migrate the application server VM to AWS.","E":"Use an AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) replication instance to migrate the database to an Amazon RDS DB instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Server Migration Service (AWS SMS) 复制作业将数据库服务器虚拟机迁移到 AWS。","B":"使用VM Import/Export 导入应用服务器VM。","C":"将 VM 映像导出到 AWS Snowball Edge Storage Optimized 设备。","D":"使用 AWS Server Migration Service (AWS SMS) 复制作业将应用程序服务器虚拟机迁移到 AWS。","E":"使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 复制实例将数据库迁移到 Amazon RDS 数据库实例。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"DE":59,"AD":31},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The application has two distinct components, so one step addresses the stateless application server and one addresses the SQL Server database. For LEAST downtime, the application server VM is best migrated with an AWS SMS replication job (D): SMS performs an initial full replication followed by scheduled incremental delta replications, keeping the AWS AMI continuously updated so cutover requires only a final small delta sync and a switch-over. For the live SQL Server database, AWS DMS with a replication instance (E) is the least-downtime path: DMS performs a full load while the source stays online and then uses change data capture (CDC) ongoing replication to keep the Amazon RDS target continuously in sync, allowing a near-zero cutover. The decisive qualifier is LEAST downtime: DMS CDC keeps the database serving traffic throughout, whereas replicating the database VM via SMS (A) snapshots an active SQL Server's data files (not transaction-consistent) and still needs the VM stopped for a clean final delta, yielding more downtime. The 10 Gbps Direct Connect makes online replication over the wire feasible for the 500 TB volumes, so an offline Snowball export is unnecessary.","explanation_zh":"此應用程式由兩個獨立元件組成，因此一個步驟處理無狀態的 application server，另一個處理 SQL Server 資料庫。為達到最少停機時間，application server VM 最適合用 AWS SMS replication job (D) 遷移：SMS 先做一次完整複寫，接著依排程進行增量 (delta) 複寫，使 AWS 上的 AMI 持續保持最新，切換時只需最後一次小幅 delta 同步即可切換。對於線上運行的 SQL Server 資料庫，使用 AWS DMS 與 replication instance (E) 是停機最少的途徑：DMS 在來源持續上線的情況下執行 full load，再透過 change data capture (CDC) 持續複寫，使 Amazon RDS 目標持續同步，達到近乎零停機的切換。決定性條件是『最少停機』：DMS CDC 讓資料庫全程持續服務，而用 SMS 複寫資料庫 VM (A) 是對運行中的 SQL Server 資料檔做快照（非交易一致），最終仍須停機取得乾淨的 delta，停機時間更長。10 Gbps Direct Connect 使 500 TB 的線上複寫可行，因此不需要離線 Snowball 匯出。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Using AWS SMS to replicate the SQL Server database VM snapshots an active database's data files at the VM level, which is not transactionally consistent and still requires stopping the VM for a clean final delta, producing more downtime than DMS CDC. AWS guidance is to migrate live databases with DMS, not VM replication.","why_zh":"用 AWS SMS 複寫 SQL Server 資料庫 VM，是在 VM 層級對運行中資料庫的資料檔做快照，無交易一致性，且最終仍須停機取得乾淨的 delta，停機時間比 DMS CDC 長。AWS 建議用 DMS 遷移線上資料庫，而非 VM 複寫。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"VM Import/Export is a one-time bulk import with no ongoing incremental delta replication, so the application VM must be exported/stopped and the long import completes before cutover, causing significantly more downtime than an SMS replication job.","why_zh":"VM Import/Export 是一次性大量匯入，無持續增量 delta 複寫，應用程式 VM 必須匯出/停止且需等漫長匯入完成才能切換，停機時間遠多於 SMS replication job。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Exporting VM images to Snowball Edge is an offline, physical-shipment transfer that addresses only data movement, not low-downtime cutover, and is unnecessary because the unused 10 Gbps Direct Connect can carry the data online while replication keeps targets in sync.","why_zh":"將 VM 映像匯出至 Snowball Edge 是離線、實體運送的傳輸方式，只處理資料搬移而非低停機切換，且因未使用的 10 Gbps Direct Connect 可線上傳輸並由複寫保持目標同步，故無必要。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/dms/latest/userguide/CHAP_Task.CDC.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/dms/latest/userguide/Welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/dms/latest/userguide/CHAP_BestPractices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/migration-sql-server/ec2-sql.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・複選"},{"id":340,"question_en":"A company operates a ­eet of servers on premises and operates a ­eet of Amazon EC2 instances in its organization in AWS Organizations. The company's AWS accounts contain hundreds of VPCs. The company wants to connect its AWS accounts to its on-premises network. AWS Site-to-Site VPN connections are already established to a single AWS account. The company wants to control which VPCs can communicate with other VPCs. Which combination of steps will achieve this level of control with the LEAST operational effort? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在本地运营一组服务器，并在其位于 AWS Organizations 的组织中运营一组 Amazon EC2 实例。该公司的 AWS 账户包含数百 个 VPC。该公司希望将其 AWS 账户连接到其本地网络。已与单个 AWS 账户建立 AWS 站点到站点 VPN 连接。该公司希望控制哪些 VPC 可以与其他 VPC 通信。 哪种步骤组合能够以最少的操作工作量实现这种级别的控制？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a transit gateway in an AWS account. Share the transit gateway across accounts by using AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM).","B":"Configure attachments to all VPCs and VPNs.","C":"Setup transit gateway route tables. Associate the VPCs and VPNs with the route tables.","D":"Configure VPC peering between the VPCs.","E":"Configure attachments between the VPCs and VPNs.","F":"Setup route tables on the VPCs and VPNs."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS 账户中创建中转网关。使用 AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) 跨账户共享中转网关。","B":"配置所有 VPC 和 VPN 的连接。","C":"设置中转网关路由表。将 VPC 和 VPN 与路由表关联。","D":"配置 VPC 之间的 VPC 对等互连。","E":"配置VPC 和VPN 之间的连接。","F":"在VPC和VPN上设置路由表。"},"answer":["C","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ABC":73,"ACE":27},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"With hundreds of VPCs across multiple Organizations accounts plus an existing Site-to-Site VPN, AWS Transit Gateway is the scalable hub and gives the LEAST operational effort. (A) Create a transit gateway and share it across the organization accounts with AWS RAM so all accounts can attach to the central hub. (B) Configure attachments to all the VPCs and the VPN connections so they connect to the transit gateway (attachments are between the TGW and each resource). (C) Set up multiple transit gateway route tables and associate the VPC and VPN attachments with them; per AWS docs each attachment is associated with exactly one route table, and TGW route tables 'direct how your network traffic is routed between your VPCs and VPNs.' Using separate TGW route tables/associations is exactly how you segment and control which VPCs can communicate with which other VPCs. The wrong options are VPC peering (D) which is full-mesh, non-transitive, and does not scale to hundreds of VPCs; (E) which describes attaching VPCs directly to VPNs, which is not a valid TGW attachment model; and (F) which uses VPC/VPN subnet route tables rather than the transit gateway route tables that actually enforce inter-VPC isolation.","explanation_zh":"面對橫跨 Organizations 多個帳戶的數百個 VPC 並已有 Site-to-Site VPN，AWS Transit Gateway 是可擴展的中樞，且營運負擔最低。(A) 建立 transit gateway 並透過 AWS RAM 跨組織帳戶共享，讓所有帳戶都能連到中央中樞。(B) 為所有 VPC 與 VPN 連線設定 attachments，使其連到 transit gateway（attachment 是介於 TGW 與各資源之間）。(C) 建立多個 transit gateway route tables 並將 VPC 與 VPN 的 attachments 關聯到這些 route tables；依 AWS 文件，每個 attachment 僅關聯到一個 route table，而 TGW route tables 用來「決定流量如何在你的 VPC 與 VPN 之間路由」。使用不同的 TGW route table/關聯正是用來分段並控制哪些 VPC 可彼此通訊的方式。錯誤選項：VPC peering (D) 為全網狀、不可轉遞，無法擴展到數百個 VPC；(E) 描述把 VPC 直接連到 VPN，並非有效的 TGW attachment 模型；(F) 使用 VPC/VPN 子網路的 route table，而非真正用來實施 VPC 間隔離的 transit gateway route tables。","distractors":[{"letter":"D","why_en":"VPC peering creates a non-transitive full mesh; for hundreds of VPCs this means thousands of peering connections and route entries, which is the highest operational effort, not the least.","why_zh":"VPC peering 屬不可轉遞的全網狀連線；面對數百個 VPC 將產生成千上萬條 peering 與路由項目，是最高而非最低的營運負擔。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Transit gateway attachments are between the TGW and a resource (a VPC or a VPN), not 'between the VPCs and VPNs.' You attach VPCs and VPNs to the gateway, so option B is the correct phrasing and E is a misleading distractor.","why_zh":"Transit gateway 的 attachment 是介於 TGW 與資源（VPC 或 VPN）之間，而非『VPC 與 VPN 之間』。應將 VPC 與 VPN attach 到 gateway，故 B 的說法正確，E 為誤導性干擾項。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Controlling which VPCs communicate is done with transit gateway route tables (option C), not VPC/VPN subnet route tables. VPN connections do not have user-managed 'route tables' in this sense; this conflates subnet route tables with TGW route tables.","why_zh":"控制哪些 VPC 可通訊是靠 transit gateway route tables（選項 C），而非 VPC/VPN 子網路 route table。VPN 連線本身並無此種使用者管理的『route table』；此選項混淆了子網路 route table 與 TGW route table。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/what-is-transit-gateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/how-transit-gateways-work.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/tgw-route-tables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/tgw-transit-gateways.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/share-accept-tgw.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・複選"},{"id":341,"question_en":"A company needs to optimize the cost of its application on AWS. The application uses AWS Lambda functions and Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) containers that run on AWS Fargate. The application is write-heavy and stores data in an Amazon Aurora MySQL database. The load on the application is not consistent. The application experiences long periods of no usage, followed by sudden and significant increases and decreases in tra®c. The database runs on a memory optimized DB instance that cannot handle the load. A solutions architect must design a solution that can scale to handle the changes in tra®c. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司需要优化其在 AWS 上的应用程序的成本。该应用程序使用 AWS Lambda 函数和在 AWS Fargate 上运行的 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 容器。该应用程序写入量大，并将数据存储在 Amazon Aurora MySQL 数据库中。 应用程序的负载不一致。该应用程序经历了长时间未使用，然后流量突然显着增加和减少。数据库在无法处理负载的内存优化数据 库实例上运行。 解决方案架构师必须设计一个可以扩展以处理流量变化的解决方案。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add additional read replicas to the database. Purchase Instance Savings Plans and RDS Reserved Instances.","B":"Migrate the database to an Aurora DB cluster that has multiple writer instances. Purchase Instance Savings Plans.","C":"Migrate the database to an Aurora global database. Purchase Compute Savings Plans and RDS Reserved instances.","D":"Migrate the database to Aurora Serverless v1. Purchase Compute Savings Plans."},"options_zh":{"A":"将其他只读副本添加到数据库。购买实例节省计划和 RDS 预留实例。","B":"将数据库迁移到具有多个写入器实例的 Aurora 数据库集群。购买实例节省计划。","C":"将数据库迁移到 Aurora 全局数据库。购买计算节省计划和 RDS 预留实例。","D":"将数据库迁移到 Aurora Serverless v1。购买计算节省计划。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Migration","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The workload has long idle periods punctuated by sudden, large traffic swings, and the current fixed-size memory-optimized instance cannot keep up. Aurora Serverless automatically scales database capacity up and down to match unpredictable demand and can scale down (auto-pause) during the long no-usage periods so you pay only for storage when idle. AWS documentation lists exactly this scenario ('Variable workloads ... sudden and unpredictable increases in activity ... scales back down when the surge is over ... no longer need to provision for peak or average capacity') as the primary Aurora Serverless use case. Compute Savings Plans are the correct compute commitment because they apply to EC2, AWS Fargate, AND AWS Lambda usage (the application's compute tier), giving cost coverage across both Lambda and ECS-on-Fargate. Option D therefore matches both the database scaling need and the compute cost optimization most cost-effectively.","explanation_zh":"此工作負載有長時間閒置期,並夾雜突發的大幅流量起伏,而目前固定大小的 memory-optimized 執行個體無法負荷。Aurora Serverless 會自動依需求向上或向下調整資料庫容量,並可在長時間無使用期間縮減(auto-pause),閒置時只需支付儲存費用。AWS 文件正是把這種情境(可變工作負載、突發且無法預測的流量增加、活動結束後自動縮減、不再需要為尖峰或平均容量預先佈建)列為 Aurora Serverless 的主要使用案例。Compute Savings Plans 是正確的運算承諾,因為它同時適用於 EC2、AWS Fargate 與 AWS Lambda 用量(應用程式的運算層),可同時涵蓋 Lambda 與 ECS-on-Fargate 的成本。因此選項 D 最符合資料庫擴展需求與運算成本最佳化,且最具成本效益。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The application is write-heavy, so read replicas do not relieve the write bottleneck. RDS Reserved Instances and Instance Savings Plans commit to always-on provisioned capacity, which is wasteful during the long periods of no usage, so this is neither effective nor most cost-effective.","why_zh":"應用程式是寫入密集型,read replicas 無法緩解寫入瓶頸。RDS Reserved Instances 與 Instance Savings Plans 承諾持續運行的佈建容量,在長時間無使用期間造成浪費,既無效也非最具成本效益。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Aurora multiple-writer (multi-master) clusters are provisioned instances that run and bill continuously, so they do not address the long no-usage idle cost; they target sustained high-availability write workloads, not intermittent ones. Pairing with Instance Savings Plans is also misaligned because EC2 Instance Savings Plans do not cover Lambda or Fargate. This is the dump's suggested answer but it is technically wrong.","why_zh":"Aurora 多寫入(multi-master)叢集是持續運行並計費的佈建執行個體,無法解決長時間閒置的成本;它針對的是持續高可用的寫入工作負載,而非間歇性負載。搭配 Instance Savings Plans 也不對,因為 EC2 Instance Savings Plans 不涵蓋 Lambda 或 Fargate。這是題庫建議答案,但技術上是錯的。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Aurora global database is designed for cross-region disaster recovery and low-latency global reads, not for cost optimization of an intermittent single-region workload. It adds a continuously running secondary cluster cost and does not provide scale-to-near-zero during idle periods.","why_zh":"Aurora global database 用於跨區域災難復原與低延遲全球讀取,並非用來最佳化單一區域間歇性工作負載的成本。它會增加持續運行的次要叢集成本,且無法在閒置期間縮減至接近零。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-serverless-v2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-serverless-v2-auto-pause.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/savingsplans/latest/userguide/plan-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/cost-optimization-reservation-models/savings-plans.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":342,"question_en":"A company migrated an application to the AWS Cloud. The application runs on two Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Application data is stored in a MySQL database that runs on an additional EC2 instance. The application's use of the database is read-heavy. The application loads static content from Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes that are attached to each EC2 instance. The static content is updated frequently and must be copied to each EBS volume. The load on the application changes throughout the day. During peak hours, the application cannot handle all the incoming requests. Trace data shows that the database cannot handle the read load during peak hours. Which solution will improve the reliability of the application?","question_zh":"一家公司将应用程序迁移到 AWS 云。该应用程序在应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面的两个 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。 应用程序数据存储在另一个 EC2 实例上运行的 MySQL 数据库中。应用程序对数据库的使用是大量读取的。 该应用程序从附加到每个 EC2 实例的 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 卷加载静态内容。静态内容经常更新，必须复制到每个 EBS 卷。 应用程序的负载全天都在变化。在高峰时段，应用程序无法处理所有传入请求。跟踪数据显示数据库无法处理高峰时段的读取负 载。 哪种解决方案将提高应用程序的可靠性？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate the application to a set of AWS Lambda functions. Set the Lambda functions as targets for the ALB. Create a new single EBS volume for the static content. Configure the Lambda functions to read from the new EBS volume. Migrate the database to an Amazon RDS for MySQL Multi-AZ DB cluster.","B":"Migrate the application to a set of AWS Step Functions state machines. Set the state machines as targets for the ALCreate an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system for the static content. Configure the state machines to read from the EFS file system. Migrate the database to Amazon Aurora MySQL Serverless v2 with a reader DB instance.","C":"Containerize the application. Migrate the application to an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster. Use the AWS Fargate launch type for the tasks that host the application. Create a new single EBS volume for the static content. Mount the new EBS volume on the ECS cluster. Configure AWS Application Auto Scaling on the ECS cluster. Set the ECS service as a target for the ALB. Migrate the database to an Amazon RDS for MySQL Multi-AZ DB cluster.","D":"Containerize the application. Migrate the application to an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster. Use the AWS Fargate launch type for the tasks that host the application. Create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system for the static content. Mount the EFS file system to each container. Configure AWS Application Auto Scaling on the ECS cluster. Set the ECS service as a target for the ALB. Migrate the database to Amazon Aurora MySQL Serverless v2 with a reader DB instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"将应用程序迁移到一组 AWS Lambda 函数。将 Lambda 函数设置为 ALB 的目标。为静态内容创建一个新的单个 EBS 卷。配置 Lambda 函数以从新的 EBS 卷读取。将数据库迁移到 Amazon RDS for MySQL 多可用区数据库集群。","B":"将应用程序迁移到一组 AWS Step Functions 状态机。将状态机设置为 AL 的目标为静态内容创建 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统。配置状态机以从 EFS 文件系统读取。使用读取器数据库实例将数据库迁移到 Amazon Aurora MySQL Serverless v2。","C":"将应用程序容器化。将应用程序迁移到 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 集群。对托管应用程序的任务使用 AWS Fargate 启动类型。为静态内容创建一个新的单个 EBS 卷。在 ECS 集群上挂载新的 EBS 卷。在 ECS 集群上配置 AWS Application Auto Scaling。将 ECS 服务设置为 ALB 的目标。将数据库迁移到 Amazon RDS for MySQL 多可用区数据库集群。","D":"将应用程序容器化。将应用程序迁移到 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 集群。对托管应用程序的任务使用 AWS Fargate 启动类型。为静态内容创建 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统。将 EFS 文件系统挂载到每个容器。在 ECS 集群上配置 AWS Application Auto Scaling。将 ECS 服务设置为 ALB 的目标。使用读取器数据库实例将数据库迁移到 Amazon Aurora MySQL Serverless v2。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":89},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The scenario has three pain points: (1) the read-heavy MySQL database cannot handle the read load at peak, (2) static content must be redundantly copied to each EBS volume (a shared-storage problem), and (3) load varies through the day so the compute tier must scale. Option D solves all three: Amazon Aurora MySQL Serverless v2 with a reader DB instance offloads and scales the read traffic; an Amazon EFS file system mounted to each container gives a single shared, concurrently writable file system so static content is updated once and seen by every container (no per-volume copying); and ECS Fargate with AWS Application Auto Scaling behind the ALB scales the application with the daily load. EFS is the only option that supports concurrent shared mounting across many tasks - per the ECS docs an EBS volume is attached 'one EBS volume per task' and cannot be a single shared volume across tasks, so Options A and C fail on the storage design (and Lambda cannot read from an EBS volume at all). Option B is architecturally invalid because AWS Step Functions state machines cannot be registered as ALB targets (ALB targets are instances, IPs, or Lambda functions).","explanation_zh":"情境有三個痛點:(1) 讀取繁重的 MySQL 資料庫在尖峰無法承受讀取負載,(2) 靜態內容必須重複複製到每個 EBS volume(共享儲存問題),(3) 負載一天中變動,運算層必須能擴展。選項 D 同時解決三者:Amazon Aurora MySQL Serverless v2 加上 reader DB instance 可卸載並擴展讀取流量;掛載到每個 container 的 Amazon EFS file system 提供單一、可同時寫入的共享檔案系統,靜態內容只需更新一次即可被所有 container 看見(免去逐個 volume 複製);而 ECS Fargate 搭配 AWS Application Auto Scaling 置於 ALB 後可隨每日負載擴展。EFS 是唯一支援跨多個 task 同時共享掛載的選項 - 依 ECS 文件,EBS volume 是『每個 task 一個 EBS volume』,無法作為跨 task 的單一共享 volume,因此選項 A 與 C 在儲存設計上失敗(且 Lambda 根本無法讀取 EBS volume)。選項 B 在架構上無效,因為 AWS Step Functions 狀態機無法註冊為 ALB target(ALB target 只能是 instance、IP 或 Lambda function)。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Lambda cannot mount or read from an Amazon EBS volume - Lambda only supports Amazon EFS for shared file storage. Configuring Lambda functions to read from an EBS volume is technically impossible, so this design is invalid regardless of the otherwise-valid RDS Multi-AZ DB cluster.","why_zh":"AWS Lambda 無法掛載或讀取 Amazon EBS volume - Lambda 的共享檔案儲存只支援 Amazon EFS。設定 Lambda function 從 EBS volume 讀取在技術上不可行,因此即使 RDS Multi-AZ DB cluster 部分有效,此設計仍無效。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Step Functions state machines cannot be set as Application Load Balancer targets. ALB target types are limited to EC2 instances, IP addresses, and Lambda functions; Step Functions is an orchestration service, not a synchronous HTTP request handler, so this architecture cannot serve the application's web traffic.","why_zh":"AWS Step Functions 狀態機無法被設為 Application Load Balancer 的 target。ALB target 類型僅限於 EC2 instance、IP 位址與 Lambda function;Step Functions 是編排服務,不是同步 HTTP 請求處理器,因此此架構無法服務應用程式的網路流量。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A single EBS volume cannot be mounted as shared storage across multiple Fargate tasks. ECS attaches one EBS volume per task (block storage is AZ-bound and not concurrently shareable for Fargate), so it fails to solve the frequently-updated shared static-content requirement, even though the RDS Multi-AZ DB cluster read scaling is acceptable.","why_zh":"單一 EBS volume 無法作為共享儲存掛載到多個 Fargate task。ECS 是每個 task 掛載一個 EBS volume(區塊儲存綁定可用區且 Fargate 無法同時共享),因此無法解決頻繁更新的共享靜態內容需求,即使 RDS Multi-AZ DB cluster 的讀取擴展可接受。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/ebs-volumes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/specify-efs-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-serverless-v2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Managing.Performance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-target-groups.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":343,"question_en":"A solutions architect wants to make sure that only AWS users or roles with suitable permissions can access a new Amazon API Gateway endpoint. The solutions architect wants an end-to-end view of each request to analyze the latency of the request and create service maps. How can the solutions architect design the API Gateway access control and perform request inspections?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师希望确保只有具有适当权限的 AWS 用户或角色才能访问新的 Amazon API Gateway 终端节点。解决方案架构师希望获 得每个请求的端到端视图，以分析请求的延迟并创建服务映射。 解决方案架构师如何设计 API 网关访问控制并执行请求检查？","options_en":{"A":"For the API Gateway method, set the authorization to AWS_IAM. Then, give the IAM user or role execute-api:Invoke permission on the REST API resource. Enable the API caller to sign requests with AWS Signature when accessing the endpoint. Use AWS X-Ray to trace and analyze user requests to API Gateway.","B":"For the API Gateway resource, set CORS to enabled and only return the company's domain in Access-Control-Allow-Origin headers. Then, give the IAM user or role execute-api:Invoke permission on the REST API resource. Use Amazon CloudWatch to trace and analyze user requests to API Gateway.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function as the custom authorizer, ask the API client to pass the key and secret when making the call, and then use Lambda to validate the key/secret pair against the IAM system. Use AWS X-Ray to trace and analyze user requests to API Gateway.","D":"Create a client certificate for API Gateway. Distribute the certificate to the AWS users and roles that need to access the endpoint. Enable the API caller to pass the client certificate when accessing the endpoint. Use Amazon CloudWatch to trace and analyze user requests to API Gateway."},"options_zh":{"A":"对于 API Gateway 方法，将授权设置为 AWS_IAM。然后，向 IAM 用户或角色授予对 REST API 资源的execute-api:Invoke 权限。允 许 API 调用者在访问终端节点时使用 AWS 签名对请求进行签名。使用 AWS X-Ray 跟踪和分析对 API Gateway 的用户请求。","B":"对于 API 网关资源，将 CORS 设置为启用，并且仅在 Access-Control-Allow-Origin 标头中返回公司的域。然后，向 IAM 用户或角 色授予对 REST API 资源的execute-api:Invoke 权限。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 跟踪和分析对 API Gateway 的用户请求。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数作为自定义授权方，要求 API 客户端在进行调用时传递密钥和密钥，然后使用 Lambda 根据 IAM 系 统验证密钥/密钥对。使用 AWS X-Ray 跟踪和分析对 API Gateway 的用户请求。","D":"为 API Gateway 创建客户端证书。将证书分发给需要访问终端节点的 AWS 用户和角色。允许 API 调用者在访问端点时传递客户 端证书。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 跟踪和分析对 API Gateway 的用户请求。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":344,"question_en":"A company is using AWS CodePipeline for the CI/CD of an application to an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group. All AWS resources are defined in AWS CloudFormation templates. The application artifacts are stored in an Amazon S3 bucket and deployed to the Auto Scaling group using instance user data scripts. As the application has become more complex, recent resource changes in the CloudFormation templates have caused unplanned downtime. How should a solutions architect improve the CI/CD pipeline to reduce the likelihood that changes in the templates will cause downtime?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS CodePipeline 将应用程序 CI/CD 发送到 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 组。所有 AWS 资源均在 AWS CloudFormation 模板中定义。应用程序项目存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中，并使用实例用户数据脚本部署到 Auto Scaling 组。随着应用程序变得更加 复杂，CloudFormation 模板中最近的资源更改导致了计划外停机。 解决方案架构师应如何改进 CI/CD 管道，以减少模板更改导致停机的可能性？","options_en":{"A":"Adapt the deployment scripts to detect and report CloudFormation error conditions when performing deployments. Write test plans for a testing team to run in a non-production environment before approving the change for production.","B":"Implement automated testing using AWS CodeBuild in a test environment. Use CloudFormation change sets to evaluate changes before deployment. Use AWS CodeDeploy to leverage blue/green deployment patterns to allow evaluations and the ability to revert changes, if needed.","C":"Use plugins for the integrated development environment (IDE) to check the templates for errors, and use the AWS CLI to validate that the templates are correct. Adapt the deployment code to check for error conditions and generate notifications on errors. Deploy to a test environment and run a manual test plan before approving the change for production.","D":"Use AWS CodeDeploy and a blue/green deployment pattern with CloudFormation to replace the user data deployment scripts. Have the operators log in to running instances and go through a manual test plan to verify the application is running as expected."},"options_zh":{"A":"调整部署脚本以在执行部署时检测并报告 CloudFormation 错误情况。在批准生产更改之前，为测试团队编写测试计划以在非 生产环境中运行。","B":"在测试环境中使用 AWS CodeBuild 实施自动化测试。在部署之前使用 CloudFormation 更改集评估更改。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 来利用蓝/绿部署模式来进行评估并能够在需要时恢复更改。","C":"使用集成开发环境 (IDE) 的插件检查模板是否有错误，并使用 AWS CLI 验证模板是否正确。调整部署代码以检查错误情况并生 成错误通知。在批准生产更改之前，部署到测试环境并运行手动测试计划。","D":"使用 AWS CodeDeploy 和蓝/绿部署模式与 CloudFormation 来替换用户数据部署脚本。让操作员登录到正在运行的实例并执行手 动测试计划以验证应用程序是否按预期运行。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The goal is to improve the CI/CD pipeline so that CloudFormation template changes are far less likely to cause downtime. Option B layers three complementary, automated, AWS-native controls that each target a distinct failure mode: (1) automated testing with AWS CodeBuild in a test environment catches application and configuration defects before they ever reach production; (2) CloudFormation change sets let you preview exactly which resources will be added, modified, replaced, or deleted - the docs state change sets 'preview how proposed changes to a stack might impact your running resources... whether your changes will delete or replace any critical resources' - which directly surfaces the destructive infrastructure changes causing the downtime; and (3) AWS CodeDeploy blue/green deployment provides a safe evaluation step and the ability to revert/roll back, which the CodeDeploy docs explicitly describe as minimizing downtime and supporting stop-and-roll-back. Together this is automated, repeatable, and scalable, matching CI/CD and CloudFormation best practices.","explanation_zh":"目標是改善 CI/CD 管線, 使 CloudFormation 範本變更不易造成停機。選項 B 疊加三層互補且自動化的 AWS 原生控制, 各自針對不同的失敗點: (1) 在測試環境使用 AWS CodeBuild 進行自動化測試, 可在缺陷進入生產前攔截應用程式與設定問題; (2) CloudFormation change sets 可預覽哪些資源將被新增、修改、取代或刪除 - 文件明確指出 change sets 可預覽變更對執行中資源的影響, 包含是否會刪除或取代關鍵資源 - 直接揭露造成停機的破壞性基礎設施變更; (3) AWS CodeDeploy blue/green 部署提供安全的評估步驟與還原/回滾能力, CodeDeploy 文件明確稱其可將停機降至最低並支援停止與回滾。三者結合即為自動化、可重複、可擴充, 符合 CI/CD 與 CloudFormation 最佳實務。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Relies on custom deployment scripts to detect errors and a manual testing team running test plans. It is manual, error-prone, and does not use CloudFormation change sets to preview destructive template changes, nor blue/green deployment for safe rollback. It does not meaningfully reduce downtime risk through automation.","why_zh":"依賴自訂部署腳本偵測錯誤及測試團隊手動執行測試計畫。屬手動且易出錯, 未使用 CloudFormation change sets 預覽破壞性範本變更, 也無 blue/green 安全回滾, 無法透過自動化有效降低停機風險。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"IDE plugins plus 'aws cloudformation validate-template' only check syntax/structure, not the runtime impact on running resources; validate-template does not reveal which resources will be replaced or deleted (only change sets do). It still depends on a manual test plan and lacks blue/green rollback, so it does not reliably reduce downtime.","why_zh":"IDE 外掛加上 validate-template 僅檢查語法與結構, 無法揭示對執行中資源的實際影響; validate-template 不會顯示哪些資源會被取代或刪除 (只有 change sets 可以)。仍依賴手動測試計畫且缺乏 blue/green 回滾, 無法可靠降低停機。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but is inferior. While it adds CodeDeploy blue/green, it requires operators to log into running instances and run a MANUAL test plan to verify the app - manual, unscalable, and contrary to CI/CD best practice. It omits automated CodeBuild testing and CloudFormation change sets, the key mechanism for previewing the very template changes that cause downtime, so it does not minimize the likelihood of failure as effectively as B.","why_zh":"此為題庫建議答案但較差。雖加入 CodeDeploy blue/green, 卻要求操作人員登入執行中執行個體手動執行測試計畫驗證應用 - 手動、不可擴充, 違反 CI/CD 最佳實務。缺少自動化 CodeBuild 測試與 CloudFormation change sets (預覽造成停機之範本變更的關鍵機制), 因此降低失敗可能性的效果不及 B。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-updating-stacks-changesets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/how-to-create-pipeline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/integrations-aws-auto-scaling.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":345,"question_en":"A North American company with headquarters on the East Coast is deploying a new web application running on Amazon EC2 in the us-east-1 Region. The application should dynamically scale to meet user demand and maintain resiliency. Additionally, the application must have disaster recovery capabilities in an active-passive configuration with the us-west-1 Region. Which steps should a solutions architect take after creating a VPC in the us-east-1 Region?","question_zh":"一家总部位于东海岸的北美公司正在 us-east-1 区域部署一个在 Amazon EC2 上运行的新 Web 应用程序。应用程序应动态扩展以满足 用户需求并保持弹性。此外，应用程序必须在 us-west-1 区域的主动-被动配置中具有灾难恢复功能。 在 us-east-1 区域创建 VPC 后，解决方案架构师应采取哪些步骤？","options_en":{"A":"Create a VPC in the us-west-1 Region. Use inter-Region VPC peering to connect both VPCs. Deploy an Application Load Balancer (ALB) spanning multiple Availability Zones (AZs) to the VPC in the us-east-1 Region. Deploy EC2 instances across multiple AZs in each Region as part of an Auto Scaling group spanning both VPCs and served by the ALB.","B":"Deploy an Application Load Balancer (ALB) spanning multiple Availability Zones (AZs) to the VPC in the us-east-1 Region. Deploy EC2 instances across multiple AZs as part of an Auto Scaling group served by the ALDeploy the same solution to the us-west-1 Region. Create an Amazon Route 53 record set with a failover routing policy and health checks enabled to provide high availability across both Regions.","C":"Create a VPC in the us-west-1 Region. Use inter-Region VPC peering to connect both VPCs. Deploy an Application Load Balancer (ALB) that spans both VPCs. Deploy EC2 instances across multiple Availability Zones as part of an Auto Scaling group in each VPC served by the ALB. Create an Amazon Route 53 record that points to the ALB.","D":"Deploy an Application Load Balancer (ALB) spanning multiple Availability Zones (AZs) to the VPC in the us-east-1 Region. Deploy EC2 instances across multiple AZs as part of an Auto Scaling group served by the ALB. Deploy the same solution to the us-west-1 Region. Create separate Amazon Route 53 records in each Region that point to the ALB in the Region. Use Route 53 health checks to provide high availability across both Regions."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 us-west-1 区域创建 VPC。使用区域间 VPC 对等互连来连接两个 VPC。将跨多个可用区 (AZ) 的应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 部 署到 us-east-1 区域中的 VPC。跨每个区域的多个可用区部署 EC2 实例，作为跨越两个 VPC 并由 ALB 提供服务的 Auto Scaling 组 的一部分。","B":"将跨多个可用区 (AZ) 的应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 部署到 us-east-1 区域中的 VPC。跨多个可用区部署 EC2 实例，作为 AL 提供 服务的 Auto Scaling 组的一部分将相同的解决方案部署到 us-west-1 区域。创建一个 Amazon Route 53 记录集，并启用故障转移路 由策略和运行状况检查，以提供跨两个区域的高可用性。","C":"在 us-west-1 区域创建 VPC。使用区域间 VPC 对等互连来连接两个 VPC。部署跨两个 VPC 的应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB)。跨多 个可用区部署 EC2 实例，作为 ALB 服务的每个 VPC 中 Auto Scaling 组的一部分。创建指向 ALB 的 Amazon Route 53 记录。","D":"将跨多个可用区 (AZ) 的应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 部署到 us-east-1 区域中的 VPC。跨多个可用区部署 EC2 实例，作为 ALB 提 供服务的 Auto Scaling 组的一部分。将相同的解决方案部署到 us-west-1 区域。在每个区域中创建指向该区域中的 ALB 的单独 Amazon Route 53 记录。使用 Route 53 运行状况检查在两个区域之间提供高可用性。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is dynamic scaling/resiliency in the active us-east-1 Region plus an active-passive disaster recovery configuration in the passive us-west-1 Region. An EC2 Auto Scaling group and an Application Load Balancer are both Regional (and VPC-scoped) constructs: an ASG cannot span multiple VPCs or Regions, and an ALB only routes to targets in its own Region. Therefore the correct pattern is to build a complete, independent stack (ALB across multiple AZs + ASG across multiple AZs) in each Region, then implement active-passive failover at the DNS layer. AWS documents that active-passive failover is configured using the Route 53 failover routing policy combined with health checks, where Route 53 returns the primary (us-east-1) resources while healthy and only switches to the secondary (us-west-1) resources when the primary becomes unhealthy. Option B is the only choice that builds duplicate Regional stacks and uses a Route 53 failover routing policy with health checks, exactly matching the active-passive DR requirement.","explanation_zh":"需求是在主用 us-east-1 區域提供動態擴展與韌性，並在備用 us-west-1 區域以 active-passive 方式做災難復原。EC2 Auto Scaling group 與 Application Load Balancer 都是區域型（且綁定 VPC）的資源：ASG 無法跨多個 VPC 或跨區域，ALB 也只能將流量導向同一區域內的目標。因此正確做法是在每個區域各自建立完整且獨立的堆疊（跨多個 AZ 的 ALB 加上跨多個 AZ 的 ASG），再於 DNS 層實作 active-passive 故障切換。AWS 文件指出 active-passive 故障切換要使用 Route 53 failover routing policy 搭配 health checks：當主要資源（us-east-1）健康時 Route 53 回應主要資源，僅在主要資源不健康時才切換到次要資源（us-west-1）。選項 B 是唯一在每個區域建立重複堆疊並使用 Route 53 failover routing policy 加 health checks 的答案，完全符合 active-passive 災難復原需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Technically impossible: an Auto Scaling group cannot span two VPCs/Regions and a single ALB cannot serve EC2 instances located in another Region. Inter-Region VPC peering does not let one ASG/ALB stretch across Regions, and it provides no failover/DR mechanism.","why_zh":"技術上不可行：Auto Scaling group 無法跨兩個 VPC/區域，單一 ALB 也無法服務位於另一區域的 EC2 執行個體。跨區域 VPC peering 並不會讓一個 ASG/ALB 延伸至多個區域，也沒有提供任何故障切換/災難復原機制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An ALB cannot span two VPCs across Regions, so 'an ALB that spans both VPCs' is invalid. It also uses a single Route 53 record pointing to the ALB with no failover routing policy or health checks, so it provides no active-passive DR.","why_zh":"ALB 無法跨兩個區域的 VPC，所以「橫跨兩個 VPC 的 ALB」不成立。而且只用單一 Route 53 記錄指向 ALB，沒有 failover routing policy 或 health checks，無法達成 active-passive 災難復原。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Builds duplicate Regional stacks correctly, but Route 53 is a global service; you do not create 'separate records in each Region.' Creating independent records pointing to each Region's ALB without a single failover (primary/secondary) routing policy does not yield a coordinated active-passive failover, so the DNS design is incorrect.","why_zh":"雖然在每個區域正確地建立了重複堆疊，但 Route 53 是全域服務，並不會「在每個區域分別建立記錄」。各自獨立、分別指向各區域 ALB 的記錄，若沒有單一的 failover（primary/secondary）routing policy，無法達成協調的 active-passive 故障切換，因此其 DNS 設計是錯誤的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-configuring.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/auto-scaling-groups.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":346,"question_en":"A company has a legacy application that runs on multiple NET Framework components. The components share the same Microsoft SQL Server database and communicate with each other asynchronously by using Microsoft Message Queueing (MSMQ). The company is starting a migration to containerized .NET Core components and wants to refactor the application to run on AWS. The .NET Core components require complex orchestration. The company must have full control over networking and host configuration. The application's database model is strongly relational. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个在多个 NET Framework 组件上运行的遗留应用程序。这些组件共享相同的 Microsoft SQL Server 数据库，并使用 Microsoft 消息队列 (MSMQ) 相互异步通信。 该公司正在开始迁移到容器化 .NET Core 组件，并希望重构应用程序以在 AWS 上运行。.NET Core 组件需要复杂的编排。公司必须完 全控制网络和主机配置。应用程序的数据库模型是强相关的。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Host the INET Core components on AWS App Runner. Host the database on Amazon RDS for SQL Server. Use Amazon EventBiridge for asynchronous messaging.","B":"Host the .NET Core components on Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) with the AWS Fargate launch type. Host the database on Amazon DynamoDUse Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) for asynchronous messaging.","C":"Host the .NET Core components on AWS Elastic Beanstalk. Host the database on Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL Serverless v2. Use Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK) for asynchronous messaging.","D":"Host the NET Core components on Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) with the Amazon EC2 launch type. Host the database on Amazon Aurora MySQL Serverless v2. Use Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) for asynchronous messaging."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS App Runner 上托管 INET Core 组件。在 Amazon RDS for SQL Server 上托管数据库。使用 Amazon EventBiridge 进行异步消 息传递。","B":"使用 AWS Fargate 启动类型在 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 上托管 .NET Core 组件。在 Amazon Dynamo 上托管 数据库使用 Amazon Simple notification Service (Amazon SNS) 进行异步消息传递。","C":"在 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 上托管 .NET Core 组件。在 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL Serverless v2 上托管数据库。使用 Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK) 进行异步消息传递。","D":"使用 Amazon EC2 启动类型在 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 上托管 NET Core 组件。在 Amazon Aurora MySQL Serverless v2 上托管数据库。使用 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 进行异步消息传递。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":96},"tags":["Migration","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Analytics","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is 'complex orchestration' plus 'full control over networking and host configuration.' Only Amazon ECS with the EC2 launch type satisfies both: ECS provides full container orchestration, and the EC2 launch type means you manage the underlying EC2 container instances, giving you complete control over networking (e.g., bridge/host/awsvpc network modes, security groups, subnets) and host configuration (instance type, AMI, kernel/OS tuning, agents). Fargate (B) is serverless and removes host-level control; App Runner (A) is fully managed and offers neither complex orchestration nor host control; Elastic Beanstalk (C) abstracts the host away. The database model is 'strongly relational,' so the database must stay relational — Aurora MySQL Serverless v2 in D is relational, while DynamoDB in B is NoSQL and is disqualified. For asynchronous messaging replacing MSMQ (a point-to-point queue), Amazon SQS is the direct managed-queue equivalent; EventBridge (A) is event-bus/routing, SNS (B) is pub/sub fan-out, and MSK (C) is a streaming platform with high operational overhead. Only option D meets every requirement, making it correct; the ExamTopics suggested answer A is wrong because App Runner cannot provide complex orchestration or host/network control.","explanation_zh":"決定性的關鍵字是「複雜的編排 (complex orchestration)」加上「對網路與主機組態的完全控制」。只有採用 EC2 啟動類型 (launch type) 的 Amazon ECS 同時滿足這兩點：ECS 提供完整的容器編排，而 EC2 啟動類型代表您管理底層的 EC2 容器執行個體，因此能完全控制網路（如 bridge/host/awsvpc 網路模式、安全群組、子網路）以及主機組態（執行個體類型、AMI、核心/OS 調校、代理程式）。Fargate（B）是無伺服器，會移除主機層級的控制；App Runner（A）為全託管，既無複雜編排也無主機控制；Elastic Beanstalk（C）則將主機抽象化。資料庫模型屬「強關聯式 (strongly relational)」，因此必須維持關聯式資料庫——D 的 Aurora MySQL Serverless v2 為關聯式，而 B 的 DynamoDB 是 NoSQL，因此被排除。對於取代 MSMQ（點對點佇列）的非同步訊息傳遞，Amazon SQS 是最直接對應的託管佇列；EventBridge（A）是事件匯流排/路由，SNS（B）是發布/訂閱扇出，MSK（C）是串流平台且維運負擔高。只有 D 同時滿足所有需求，因此為正確答案；ExamTopics 建議答案 A 錯誤，因為 App Runner 無法提供複雜編排或主機/網路控制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"App Runner is a fully managed service that hides the host and network layer, so it provides neither 'complex orchestration' nor 'full control over networking and host configuration.' EventBridge is an event bus for routing/fan-out, not a direct point-to-point queue replacement for MSMQ. RDS for SQL Server is relational and fine, but the compute and messaging choices fail the requirements.","why_zh":"App Runner 是全託管服務，隱藏了主機與網路層，因此既無法提供「複雜編排」也無法提供「對網路與主機組態的完全控制」。EventBridge 是用於路由/扇出的事件匯流排，並非取代 MSMQ 點對點佇列的直接對應。RDS for SQL Server 雖為關聯式且可行，但運算與訊息傳遞的選擇不符合需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Two failures: Fargate is serverless and gives no control over the host/host configuration, violating the requirement; DynamoDB is a NoSQL key-value/document store and cannot serve a 'strongly relational' database model. SNS is pub/sub fan-out rather than a queue replacing MSMQ.","why_zh":"兩個失敗點：Fargate 為無伺服器，無法控制主機/主機組態，違反需求；DynamoDB 是 NoSQL 鍵值/文件儲存，無法支援「強關聯式」資料庫模型。SNS 是發布/訂閱扇出，而非取代 MSMQ 的佇列。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Elastic Beanstalk abstracts away host/networking management (it provisions and manages the underlying resources for you), so it does not satisfy 'full control over networking and host configuration' nor 'complex orchestration.' Amazon MSK (managed Kafka) is a streaming platform with significant operational overhead and is overkill versus a simple MSMQ-style queue; SQS is the better fit. Aurora PostgreSQL is relational, but the compute and messaging choices fail.","why_zh":"Elastic Beanstalk 將主機/網路管理抽象化（它會替您佈建並管理底層資源），因此不滿足「對網路與主機組態的完全控制」也不滿足「複雜編排」。Amazon MSK（託管 Kafka）是串流平台，維運負擔大，相對於簡單的 MSMQ 式佇列屬過度設計；SQS 才是較佳選擇。Aurora PostgreSQL 雖為關聯式，但運算與訊息傳遞選擇不符。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/launch-type-ec2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/AWS_Fargate.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/task-networking.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/patterns/migrate-a-messaging-queue-from-microsoft-azure-service-bus-to-amazon-sqs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdk-for-net/v3/developer-guide/sqs-apis-intro.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":347,"question_en":"A solutions architect has launched multiple Amazon EC2 instances in a placement group within a single Availability Zone. Because of additional load on the system, the solutions architect attempts to add new instances to the placement group. However, the solutions architect receives an insu®cient capacity error. What should the solutions architect do to troubleshoot this issue?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师已在单个可用区内的置放群组中启动了多个 Amazon EC2 实例。由于系统上有额外负载，解决方案架构师尝试将新 实例添加到置放群组中。然而，解决方案架构师收到容量不足的错误。 解决方案架构师应该如何解决这个问题？","options_en":{"A":"Use a spread placement group. Set a minimum of eight instances for each Availability Zone.","B":"Stop and start all the instances in the placement group. Try the launch again.","C":"Create a new placement group. Merge the new placement group with the original placement group.","D":"Launch the additional instances as Dedicated Hosts in the placement groups."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用分散安置组。为每个可用区至少设置八个实例。","B":"停止并启动置放群组中的所有实例。再次尝试启动。","C":"创建一个新的置放群组。将新置放群组与原始置放群组合并。","D":"在置放群组中启动其他实例作为专用主机。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":88},"tags":["Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The scenario describes a cluster placement group (instances launched into a placement group within a single Availability Zone for additional load/HPC-style packing). The official EC2 documentation on placement strategies gives the exact remediation for this scenario: 'If you receive a capacity error when launching an instance in a placement group that already has running instances, stop and start all of the instances in the placement group, and try the launch again. Starting the instances may migrate them to hardware that has capacity for all of the requested instances.' This is verbatim option B. The same docs explicitly state 'You can't merge placement groups' (eliminating C) and 'You can't launch Dedicated Hosts in placement groups' (eliminating D). Option A misstates spread placement group limits (max seven running instances per AZ, not a minimum of eight) and does not resolve a cluster placement group insufficient-capacity error. Therefore B is the documented, correct troubleshooting step.","explanation_zh":"情境描述的是一個 cluster placement group(在單一可用區內為了額外負載/HPC 緊密排列而啟動的執行個體)。EC2 placement strategies 官方文件給出此情境的確切解法:『如果在已有執行中執行個體的 placement group 啟動執行個體時收到容量錯誤,請停止並重新啟動 placement group 中的所有執行個體,然後再試一次啟動。重新啟動執行個體可能會將它們遷移到具有足夠容量可容納所有請求執行個體的硬體上。』這與選項 B 完全一致。同一份文件明確指出『You can't merge placement groups』(排除 C),以及『You can't launch Dedicated Hosts in placement groups』(排除 D)。選項 A 對 spread placement group 限制描述錯誤(每個 AZ 最多七個執行中執行個體,而非最少八個),且無法解決 cluster placement group 的容量不足錯誤。因此 B 是文件記載的正確排查步驟。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Spread placement groups support a maximum of seven running instances per Availability Zone, not a minimum of eight; this is technically impossible and does not address the cluster placement group capacity error in the scenario.","why_zh":"Spread placement group 每個可用區最多支援七個執行中執行個體,而非最少八個;此設定技術上不可能,且無法解決情境中 cluster placement group 的容量錯誤。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS documentation explicitly states 'You can't merge placement groups,' so creating a new group and merging it is not possible.","why_zh":"AWS 文件明確指出『You can't merge placement groups』,因此建立新群組再合併的做法不可行。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS documentation explicitly states 'You can't launch Dedicated Hosts in placement groups,' so this option is invalid.","why_zh":"AWS 文件明確指出『You can't launch Dedicated Hosts in placement groups』,因此此選項無效。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/placement-strategies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/placement-groups.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":348,"question_en":"A company has used infrastructure as code (IaC) to provision a set of two Amazon EC2 instances. The instances have remained the same for several years. The company's business has grown rapidly in the past few months. In response, the company’s operations team has implemented an Auto Scaling group to manage the sudden increases in tra®c. Company policy requires a monthly installation of security updates on all operating systems that are running. The most recent security update required a reboot. As a result, the Auto Scaling group terminated the instances and replaced them with new, unpatched instances. Which combination of steps should a solutions architect recommend to avoid a recurrence of this issue? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用基础设施即代码 (IaC) 来配置一组两个 Amazon EC2 实例。这些实例多年来一直保持不变。 过去几个月，该公司的业务增长迅速。作为应对措施，该公司的运营团队实施了 Auto Scaling 组来管理突然增加的流量。公司政策 要求每月在所有正在运行的操作系统上安装安全更新。 最新的安全更新需要重新启动。因此，Auto Scaling 组终止了这些实例，并将其替换为新的、未修补的实例。 解决方案架构师应该建议采取哪些步骤组合来避免再次出现此问题？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Modify the Auto Scaling group by setting the Update policy to target the oldest launch configuration for replacement.","B":"Create a new Auto Scaling group before the next patch maintenance. During the maintenance window, patch both groups and reboot the instances.","C":"Create an Elastic Load Balancer in front of the Auto Scaling group. Configure monitoring to ensure that target group health checks return healthy after the Auto Scaling group replaces the terminated instances.","D":"Create automation scripts to patch an AMI, update the launch configuration, and invoke an Auto Scaling instance refresh.","E":"Create an Elastic Load Balancer in front of the Auto Scaling group. Configure termination protection on the instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"通过设置更新策略来修改 Auto Scaling 组，以将最旧的启动配置作为替换目标。","B":"在下次补丁维护之前创建一个新的 Auto Scaling 组。在维护时段期间，修补两个组并重新启动实例。","C":"在 Auto Scaling 组前面创建一个 Elastic Load Balancer。配置监控以确保目标组运行状况检查在 Auto Scaling 组替换已终止的实 例后恢复正常。","D":"创建自动化脚本来修补 AMI、更新启动配置并调用 Auto Scaling 实例刷新。","E":"在 Auto Scaling 组前面创建一个 Elastic Load Balancer。在实例上配置终止保护。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"CD":44,"AD":32,"AC":21},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The root cause is that patches were applied to running instances only; when Auto Scaling replaced an instance (after the reboot was detected as unhealthy), the new instance was launched from the unpatched launch configuration/AMI, so the patch was lost. The durable fix is to bake the patch into a new AMI, update the launch template/launch configuration, and run an instance refresh (or replace instances) so all current and future instances are patched (D) - this is exactly the use case AWS documents for instance refresh ('Applying security patches or software updates'). Putting an Elastic Load Balancer in front of the group and using its health checks ensures that when instances are replaced during the rolling update, the replacement (now patched) instances are validated as healthy before they serve traffic, preventing an uncontrolled, traffic-impacting replacement cycle (C). Together C and D both address the recurrence: D makes replacements patched, and C makes the replacement process health-aware and safe.","explanation_zh":"問題根因是只在執行中的執行個體上套用了修補程式；當 Auto Scaling 因重新開機被判定為不健康而替換執行個體時，新執行個體是從未修補的 launch configuration/AMI 啟動，導致修補遺失。持久的解法是把修補烘焙進新的 AMI、更新 launch template/launch configuration，並執行 instance refresh（D）- 這正是 AWS 文件記載的 instance refresh 使用情境（套用安全修補或軟體更新）。在 Auto Scaling group 前放置 Elastic Load Balancer 並使用其 health checks，可確保在滾動更新替換執行個體時，新的（已修補的）執行個體先被驗證為健康才接收流量，避免不受控、影響流量的替換循環（C）。C 與 D 共同解決問題重現：D 讓替換後的執行個體已修補，C 讓替換過程具健康狀態感知且安全。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Setting the update/termination policy to target the oldest launch configuration only chooses WHICH instances are terminated; it does nothing to bake patches into the AMI or launch config, so newly launched replacement instances remain unpatched. It does not address the root cause.","why_zh":"將 update/termination 政策設為針對最舊的 launch configuration 只是決定要終止哪些執行個體，並不會把修補烘焙進 AMI 或 launch config，因此新啟動的替換執行個體仍未修補，無法解決根本問題。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Creating a second Auto Scaling group and patching running instances in both groups is high operational overhead and still leaves the launch configuration unpatched, so any future instance launch is again unpatched. It does not prevent recurrence.","why_zh":"建立第二個 Auto Scaling group 並修補兩組執行中的執行個體，操作成本高，且 launch configuration 仍未修補，未來啟動的執行個體又會是未修補狀態，無法防止問題重現。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Termination protection (and even Auto Scaling scale-in protection) does NOT prevent Auto Scaling from terminating/replacing an instance that fails its health checks; AWS docs state scale-in protection does not protect against health-check-based replacement, and EC2 termination protection is ignored by Auto Scaling. So this would not stop the replacement, and it does not patch the launch config.","why_zh":"Termination protection（甚至 Auto Scaling 的 scale-in protection）並不能阻止 Auto Scaling 終止/替換健康檢查失敗的執行個體；AWS 文件指出 scale-in protection 無法防止基於健康檢查的替換，而 EC2 termination protection 會被 Auto Scaling 忽略。因此無法阻止替換，也未修補 launch config。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/asg-instance-refresh.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/instance-refresh-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/health-checks-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-auto-scaling-instance-protection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/blue-green-deployments/update-auto-scaling-group-launch-configurations.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識・多選項拉鋸・複選"},{"id":349,"question_en":"A team of data scientists is using Amazon SageMaker instances and SageMaker APIs to train machine learning (ML) models. The SageMaker instances are deployed in a VPC that does not have access to or from the internet. Datasets for ML model training are stored in an Amazon S3 bucket. Interface VPC endpoints provide access to Amazon S3 and the SageMaker APIs. Occasionally, the data scientists require access to the Python Package Index (PyPI) repository to update Python packages that they use as part of their work­ow. A solutions architect must provide access to the PyPI repository while ensuring that the SageMaker instances remain isolated from the internet. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"数据科学家团队正在使用 Amazon SageMaker 实例和 SageMaker API 来训练机器学习 (ML) 模型。SageMaker 实例部署在无法访问互联 网或从互联网访问的 VPC 中。用于 ML 模型训练的数据集存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。接口 VPC 终端节点提供对 Amazon S3 和 SageMaker API 的访问。 有时，数据科学家需要访问 Python 包索引 (PyPI) 存储库来更新他们在工作流程中使用的 Python 包。解决方案架构师必须提供对 PyPI 存储库的访问，同时确保 SageMaker 实例与互联网保持隔离。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CodeCommit repository for each package that the data scientists need to access. Configure code synchronization between the PyPI repository and the CodeCommit repository. Create a VPC endpoint for CodeCommit.","B":"Create a NAT gateway in the VPC. Configure VPC routes to allow access to the internet with a network ACL that allows access to only the PyPI repository endpoint.","C":"Create a NAT instance in the VPConfigure VPC routes to allow access to the internet. Configure SageMaker notebook instance firewall rules that allow access to only the PyPI repository endpoint.","D":"Create an AWS CodeArtifact domain and repository. Add an external connection for public:pypi to the CodeArtifact repository. Configure the Python client to use the CodeArtifact repository. Create a VPC endpoint for CodeArtifact."},"options_zh":{"A":"为数据科学家需要访问的每个包创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 存储库。配置 PyPI 存储库和 CodeCommit 存储库之间的代码同步。 为 CodeCommit 创建 VPC 终端节点。","B":"在VPC内创建NAT网关。配置 VPC 路由以允许使用仅允许访问 PyPI 存储库端点的网络 ACL 访问互联网。","C":"在VP中创建NAT实例配置VPC路由以允许访问Internet。配置 SageMaker 笔记本实例防火墙规则，仅允许访问 PyPI 存储库端 点。","D":"创建 AWS CodeArtifact 域和存储库。将 public:pypi 的外部连接添加到 CodeArtifact 存储库。配置 Python 客户端以使用 CodeArtifact 存储库。为 CodeArtifact 创建 VPC 终端节点。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"AWS CodeArtifact natively supports a public:pypi external connection (the pypi-store connected to the Python Packaging Authority), so the CodeArtifact repository proxies and caches packages from the real PyPI without the SageMaker instances ever touching the internet. CodeArtifact is reachable privately through AWS PrivateLink interface VPC endpoints, and the Python client (pip) is configured to point at the CodeArtifact repository. AWS's own SageMaker documentation prescribes exactly this pattern for VPCs with no internet access: create a private PyPI repository in CodeArtifact, create CodeArtifact VPC endpoints (plus an S3 gateway endpoint for package assets), and run 'aws codeartifact login --tool pip' against the endpoint. This keeps the instances fully isolated while still providing up-to-date PyPI packages with minimal operational overhead. Option C (the dump's suggested answer) is wrong because a NAT instance gives the instances outbound internet access, violating the hard requirement that they remain isolated from the internet.","explanation_zh":"AWS CodeArtifact 原生支援 public:pypi 外部連線（pypi-store 連接到 Python Packaging Authority），因此 CodeArtifact repository 會代理並快取真實 PyPI 的套件，而 SageMaker 執行個體完全不需接觸網際網路。CodeArtifact 可透過 AWS PrivateLink 介面 VPC endpoint 進行私有存取，並設定 Python client（pip）指向 CodeArtifact repository。AWS 的 SageMaker 官方文件針對無網際網路存取的 VPC 正好建議此模式：在 CodeArtifact 建立私有 PyPI repository、建立 CodeArtifact VPC endpoint（再加上用於套件資產的 S3 gateway endpoint），並執行 'aws codeartifact login --tool pip'。這讓執行個體保持完全隔離，同時仍能取得最新的 PyPI 套件，且維運負擔最低。選項 C（dump 建議答案）錯誤，因為 NAT instance 會讓執行個體取得對外網際網路存取，違反必須與網際網路隔離的硬性需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CodeCommit is a Git source-control repository, not a Python package index; there is no native PyPI synchronization feature, so building and maintaining per-package CodeCommit repos with custom sync is not a real or supported pip workflow and carries enormous operational overhead. CodeCommit is also closed to new customers.","why_zh":"CodeCommit 是 Git 原始碼控管儲存庫，並非 Python 套件索引；沒有原生 PyPI 同步功能，因此為每個套件建立 CodeCommit repo 並自訂同步並非真實或受支援的 pip 工作流程，且維運負擔極大。CodeCommit 也已不對新客戶開放。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A NAT gateway provides the instances with outbound internet access, which directly violates the requirement that the SageMaker instances remain isolated from the internet. A network ACL cannot reliably restrict traffic to 'only the PyPI endpoint' because PyPI/CDN uses many changing IPs, and NACLs filter by IP/port, not by hostname.","why_zh":"NAT gateway 會讓執行個體取得對外網際網路存取，直接違反 SageMaker 執行個體必須與網際網路隔離的需求。Network ACL 也無法可靠地將流量限制為「僅 PyPI endpoint」，因為 PyPI/CDN 使用許多會變動的 IP，而 NACL 是依 IP/port 過濾而非主機名稱。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A NAT instance still grants outbound internet connectivity to the instances, breaking the isolation requirement. SageMaker notebook 'firewall rules' restricting to a single PyPI endpoint is not a real feature, and PyPI resolves to many CDN IPs, so host-based allow-listing is not practical or compliant with the no-internet mandate.","why_zh":"NAT instance 仍會讓執行個體取得對外網際網路連線，破壞隔離需求。SageMaker notebook 限制為單一 PyPI endpoint 的「防火牆規則」並非實際存在的功能，且 PyPI 會解析到許多 CDN IP，因此以主機為基礎的允許清單不切實際，也不符合無網際網路的要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/train-remote-decorator-private.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/external-connection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/create-vpc-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/using-python.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":350,"question_en":"A solutions architect works for a government agency that has strict disaster recovery requirements. All Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) snapshots are required to be saved in at least two additional AWS Regions. The agency also is required to maintain the lowest possible operational overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师为具有严格灾难恢复要求的政府机构工作。所有 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 快照都需要保存在至少两个 额外的 AWS 区域中。该机构还需要保持尽可能低的运营费用。 哪种解决方案满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a policy in Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager (Amazon DLM) to run once daily to copy the EBS snapshots to the additional Regions.","B":"Use Amazon EventBridge to schedule an AWS Lambda function to copy the EBS snapshots to the additional Regions.","C":"Setup AWS Backup to create the EBS snapshots. Configure Amazon S3 Cross-Region Replication to copy the EBS snapshots to the additional Regions.","D":"Schedule Amazon EC2 Image Builder to run once daily to create an AMI and copy the AMI to the additional Regions."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager (Amazon DLM) 中配置策略以每天运行一次，以将 EBS 快照复制到其他区域。","B":"使用 Amazon EventBridge 安排 AWS Lambda 函数将 EBS 快照复制到其他区域。","C":"设置 AWS Backup 以创建 EBS 快照。配置 Amazon S3 跨区域复制以将 EBS 快照复制到其他区域。","D":"安排 Amazon EC2 Image Builder 每天运行一次以创建 AMI 并将 AMI 复制到其他区域。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":88},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":351,"question_en":"A company has a project that is launching Amazon EC2 instances that are larger than required. The project's account cannot be part of the company's organization in AWS Organizations due to policy restrictions to keep this activity outside of corporate IT. The company wants to allow only the launch of t3.small EC2 instances by developers in the project's account. These EC2 instances must be restricted to the us-east- 2 Region. What should a solutions architect do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的一个项目正在启动大于所需的 Amazon EC2 实例。由于政策限制，该项目的账户不能成为 AWS Organizations 中公司组织 的一部分，以将此活动保留在公司 IT 之外。该公司希望仅允许开发人员在项目帐户中启动 t3.small EC2 实例。这些 EC2 实例必须限 制在 us-east-2 区域。 解决方案架构师应该怎样做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new developer account. Move all EC2 instances, users, and assets into us-east-2. Add the account to the company's organization in AWS Organizations. Enforce a tagging policy that denotes Region a®nity.","B":"Create an SCP that denies the launch of all EC2 instances except t3.small EC2 instances in us-east-2. Attach the SCP to the project's account.","C":"Create and purchase a t3.small EC2 Reserved Instance for each developer in us-east-2. Assign each developer a specific EC2 instance with their name as the tag.","D":"Create an IAM policy than allows the launch of only t3.small EC2 instances in us-east-2. Attach the policy to the roles and groups that the developers use in the project's account."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的开发者帐户。将所有 EC2 实例、用户和资产移至 us-east-2。将账户添加到 AWS Organizations 中的公司组织。实 施表示区域关联性的标记策略。","B":"创建一个 SCP，拒绝启动 us-east-2 中除 t3.small EC2 实例之外的所有 EC2 实例。将 SCP 附加到项目的帐户。","C":"为 us-east-2 中的每个开发人员创建并购买一个 t3.small EC2 预留实例。为每个开发人员分配一个特定的 EC2 实例，并以其名称 作为标签。","D":"创建一个 IAM 策略，仅允许在 us-east-2 中启动 t3.small EC2 实例。将策略附加到开发人员在项目帐户中使用的角色和组。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":91},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive constraint is that the project's account CANNOT be part of the company's AWS Organizations organization. Service Control Policies (SCPs) are an AWS Organizations feature that only apply to member accounts within an organization that has all features enabled; you cannot attach an SCP to a standalone account outside the organization. Therefore Option B is technically impossible to implement given the stated restriction. Option D works entirely within the standalone project account: an IAM identity-based policy attached to the developers' roles and groups can allow ec2:RunInstances only when the ec2:InstanceType condition key equals t3.small and the aws:RequestedRegion (or ec2:Region) condition key equals us-east-2, denying everything else. This meets both the instance-type and Region restrictions without any dependency on Organizations.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限制條件是該專案帳戶「無法」成為公司 AWS Organizations 組織的一部分。Service Control Policies (SCP) 是 AWS Organizations 的功能，只能套用到已啟用全部功能 (all features) 之組織中的成員帳戶；你無法將 SCP 附加到組織外的獨立帳戶。因此在此限制下，選項 B 在技術上根本無法實作。選項 D 完全在獨立的專案帳戶內運作：將 IAM 身分型政策附加到開發人員使用的角色與群組，僅當 ec2:InstanceType 條件鍵等於 t3.small 且 aws:RequestedRegion (或 ec2:Region) 條件鍵等於 us-east-2 時才允許 ec2:RunInstances，其餘一律拒絕。這同時滿足執行個體類型與區域的限制，且不依賴 AWS Organizations。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creating a new account and adding it to AWS Organizations directly violates the explicit requirement that the account cannot be part of the organization. It is also massively over-engineered, and a tagging policy does not enforce/prevent instance launches.","why_zh":"建立新帳戶並加入 AWS Organizations 直接違反帳戶不得加入組織的明確要求。此做法也過度設計，且標籤政策無法強制阻擋執行個體的啟動。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"SCPs are an AWS Organizations feature and can only be attached to member accounts within an organization. Since the project's account cannot be part of the organization, an SCP cannot be attached to it, so this is technically impossible.","why_zh":"SCP 是 AWS Organizations 的功能，只能附加到組織內的成員帳戶。由於該專案帳戶不能加入組織，SCP 無法附加到它，因此技術上無法實作。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Reserved Instances are a billing/pricing construct for cost savings; they do not restrict which instance types or Regions developers can launch. Developers could still launch larger on-demand instances, so this does not enforce the requirement.","why_zh":"Reserved Instances 是用於節省成本的計費/定價結構，並不會限制開發人員能啟動的執行個體類型或區域。開發人員仍可啟動更大的隨需執行個體，因此無法達成需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_condition-keys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_elements_condition.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/ExamplePolicies_EC2.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":352,"question_en":"A scientific company needs to process text and image data from an Amazon S3 bucket. The data is collected from several radar stations during a live, time-critical phase of a deep space mission. The radar stations upload the data to the source S3 bucket. The data is prefixed by radar station identification number. The company created a destination S3 bucket in a second account. Data must be copied from the source S3 bucket to the destination S3 bucket to meet a compliance objective. This replication occurs through the use of an S3 replication rule to cover all objects in the source S3 bucket. One specific radar station is identified as having the most accurate data. Data replication at this radar station must be monitored for completion within 30 minutes after the radar station uploads the objects to the source S3 bucket. What should a solutions architect do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家科学公司需要处理来自 Amazon S3 存储桶的文本和图像数据。这些数据是在深空任务的实时、时间关键阶段从多个雷达站收集 的。雷达站将数据上传到源S3存储桶。数据以雷达站识别号为前缀。 该公司在第二个帐户中创建了目标 S3 存储桶。必须将数据从源 S3 存储桶复制到目标 S3 存储桶才能满足合规性目标。此复制通过使 用 S3 复制规则来覆盖源 S3 存储桶中的所有对象来进行。 一个特定的雷达站被认为拥有最准确的数据。必须监控该雷达站的数据复制是否在雷达站将对象上传到源 S3 存储桶后 30 分钟内完 成。 解决方案架构师应该怎样做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Setup an AWS DataSync agent to replicate the prefixed data from the source S3 bucket to the destination S3 bucket. Select to use all available bandwidth on the task, and monitor the task to ensure that itis in the TRANSFERRING status. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to initiate an alert if this status changes.","B":"In the second account, create another S3 bucket to receive data from the radar station with the most accurate data. Set up a new replication rule for this new S3 bucket to separate the replication from the other radar stations. Monitor the maximum replication time to the destination. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to initiate an alert when the time exceeds the desired threshold.","C":"Enable Amazon S3 Transfer Acceleration on the source S3 bucket, and configure the radar station with the most accurate data to use the new endpoint. Monitor the S3 destination bucket's TotalRequestLatency metric. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to initiate an alert if this status changes.","D":"Create a new S3 replication rule on the source S3 bucket that filters for the keys that use the prefix of the radar station with the most accurate data. Enable S3 Replication Time Control (S3 RTC). Monitor the maximum replication time to the destination. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to initiate an alert when the time exceeds the desired threshold."},"options_zh":{"A":"设置 AWS DataSync 代理以将带前缀的数据从源 S3 存储桶复制到目标 S3 存储桶。选择使用任务上的所有可用带宽，并监视任 务以确保其处于 TRANSFERRING 状态。创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以便在此状态发生变化时启动警报。","B":"在第二个账户中，创建另一个 S3 存储桶，用于接收来自数据最准确的雷达站的数据。为这个新的 S3 存储桶设置新的复制规 则，以将复制与其他雷达站分开。监视到目标的最大复制时间。创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则以在时间超过所需阈值时启动警 报。","C":"在源 S3 存储桶上启用 Amazon S3 Transfer Acceleration，并使用最准确的数据配置雷达站以使用新终端节点。监控 S3 目标存储 桶的 TotalRequestLatency 指标。创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以便在此状态发生变化时启动警报。","D":"在源 S3 存储桶上创建新的 S3 复制规则，以筛选使用数据最准确的雷达站前缀的键。启用 S3 复制时间控制 (S3 RTC)。监视到 目标的最大复制时间。创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则以在时间超过所需阈值时启动警报。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to monitor that replication of one specific radar station's prefix completes within 30 minutes of upload, with an alert if it exceeds the threshold. S3 Replication Time Control (S3 RTC) is the purpose-built feature for this: it replicates 99.9% of objects within a 15-minute SLA (well inside the 30-minute window) and automatically publishes S3 Replication metrics to CloudWatch, including the Replication Latency metric (the maximum number of seconds the destination is behind the source). Creating a new replication rule on the source bucket filtered by the prefix of the most-accurate radar station isolates that dataset, enables RTC only where it is needed, and lets you alarm via an EventBridge rule when the maximum replication time exceeds the desired threshold. This matches option D exactly. Option C is wrong because S3 Transfer Acceleration only speeds uploads INTO S3 over long distances and TotalRequestLatency measures per-API-call latency, neither of which tracks cross-account replication completion.","explanation_zh":"需求是監控某個特定雷達站 prefix 的資料在上傳後 30 分鐘內完成複製,並在超過門檻時發出警報。S3 Replication Time Control (S3 RTC) 正是為此設計的功能:它以 15 分鐘的 SLA 複製 99.9% 的物件(遠在 30 分鐘範圍內),並自動將 S3 Replication 指標發佈到 CloudWatch,包括 Replication Latency 指標(目的端落後來源端的最大秒數)。在來源 bucket 上建立一條以該最準確雷達站 prefix 過濾的新複製規則,可隔離此資料集、僅在需要處啟用 RTC,並透過 EventBridge 規則在最大複製時間超過門檻時發警報,完全對應選項 D。選項 C 錯誤,因為 S3 Transfer Acceleration 只是加速跨遠距離上傳到 S3,而 TotalRequestLatency 衡量的是單一 API 呼叫延遲,兩者都無法追蹤跨帳戶複製是否完成。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS DataSync is for migrating/transferring data on schedules or on demand, not for continuous replication with a per-object completion SLA. Monitoring a TRANSFERRING status and 'use all available bandwidth' does not measure whether each object replicated within 30 minutes, and the requirement already mandates an S3 replication rule, not DataSync.","why_zh":"AWS DataSync 用於排程或按需的資料遷移/傳輸,而非提供每個物件完成 SLA 的持續複製。監控 TRANSFERRING 狀態與『使用所有可用頻寬』無法衡量每個物件是否在 30 分鐘內完成複製,且需求已明定使用 S3 複製規則而非 DataSync。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Creating a second destination bucket and a separate rule could isolate the dataset, but without enabling S3 RTC there is no SLA and S3 only publishes the Replication Latency / maximum replication time metric when replication metrics (which RTC turns on) are enabled. The option vaguely says 'monitor the maximum replication time' but provides no mechanism (RTC/metrics) to actually produce that metric, so it does not reliably meet the timed-completion monitoring requirement. It also adds an unnecessary extra bucket.","why_zh":"建立第二個目的端 bucket 與獨立規則雖能隔離資料集,但若未啟用 S3 RTC 就沒有 SLA,且只有在啟用複製指標(由 RTC 開啟)時 S3 才會發佈 Replication Latency / 最大複製時間指標。此選項僅含糊地說『監控最大複製時間』卻沒有提供實際產生該指標的機制(RTC/指標),因此無法可靠達成限時完成監控需求,還多建立了不必要的 bucket。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but is technically wrong. S3 Transfer Acceleration only accelerates uploads INTO an S3 bucket over long network distances; it has nothing to do with replication between buckets in different accounts. TotalRequestLatency measures the elapsed time of individual S3 API requests, not whether replication of an object completed within a 30-minute window, so it cannot satisfy the compliance/monitoring requirement.","why_zh":"這是題庫建議答案,但技術上錯誤。S3 Transfer Acceleration 只是透過長距離網路加速上傳到 S3 bucket,與跨帳戶 bucket 之間的複製毫無關係。TotalRequestLatency 衡量的是個別 S3 API 請求的耗時,而非物件複製是否在 30 分鐘內完成,因此無法滿足合規/監控需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication-time-control.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/repl-metrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication-metrics-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/API/API_control_ReplicationRuleFilter.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":353,"question_en":"A company wants to migrate its on-premises data center to the AWS Cloud. This includes thousands of virtualized Linux and Microsoft Windows servers, SAN storage, Java and PHP applications with MySQL, and Oracle databases. There are many dependent services hosted either in the same data center or externally. The technical documentation is incomplete and outdated. A solutions architect needs to understand the current environment and estimate the cloud resource costs after the migration. Which tools or services should the solutions architect use to plan the cloud migration? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司希望将其本地数据中心迁移到 AWS 云。其中包括数千个虚拟化 Linux 和 Microsoft Windows 服务器、SAN 存储、带有 MySQL 的 Java 和 PHP 应用程序以及 Oracle 数据库。有许多依赖服务托管在同一数据中心或外部。技术文档不完整且过时。解决方案架构 师需要了解当前环境并估算迁移后的云资源成本。 解决方案架构师应该使用哪些工具或服务来规划云迁移？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"AWS Application Discovery Service","B":"AWS SMS","C":"AWS X-Ray","D":"AWS Cloud Adoption Readiness Tool (CART)","E":"Amazon Inspector","F":"AWS Migration Hub"},"options_zh":{"A":"AWS 应用程序发现服务 B.AWS SMS C.AWS X 射线","D":"AWS 云采用准备工具 (CART)","E":"亚马逊检查员 F.AWS 迁移中心"},"answer":["D","E","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ADF":76},"tags":["Migration","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The task has two needs: understand the current (poorly documented) environment and estimate post-migration cloud costs. AWS Application Discovery Service (A) collects configuration, performance/utilization data, and the network connections/dependencies between thousands of on-prem Linux/Windows servers and databases, and its exported utilization data feeds a cost model and Migration Hub EC2 recommendations. AWS Migration Hub (F) aggregates that discovery data into a single console and provides Amazon EC2 instance recommendations that explicitly estimate the least-expensive EC2 instance and per-hour cost of running existing servers in AWS. AWS Cloud Adoption Readiness Tool / CART (D) is the migration-planning assessment that gauges organizational/technical readiness and produces a readiness report to plan the migration. The dump answer DEF wrongly includes Amazon Inspector (a security vulnerability scanner, not a discovery or cost tool) and wrongly drops Application Discovery Service, the core environment-discovery service. By technical merit and elimination of B (SMS executes migration), C (X-Ray traces apps already in AWS), and E (Inspector security), the three planning tools are A, D, and F.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個需求：了解目前(文件不全)的環境，以及估算遷移後的雲端資源成本。AWS Application Discovery Service (A) 會蒐集上千台地端 Linux/Windows 伺服器與資料庫的組態、效能/使用率資料，以及伺服器之間的網路連線/相依性，且其匯出的使用率資料可餵入成本模型與 Migration Hub 的 EC2 建議。AWS Migration Hub (F) 將探索資料彙整於單一主控台，並提供 Amazon EC2 instance recommendations，明確估算最省成本的 EC2 執行個體與每小時費用，亦即估算雲端資源成本。AWS Cloud Adoption Readiness Tool / CART (D) 是遷移規劃用的就緒度評估工具，產出就緒度報告以規劃遷移。題庫答案 DEF 錯誤地納入 Amazon Inspector(安全弱點掃描，非探索或成本工具)，並錯誤排除核心的環境探索服務 Application Discovery Service。依技術正確性並排除 B(SMS 執行遷移)、C(X-Ray 追蹤已在 AWS 的應用)、E(Inspector 安全)，三個規劃工具為 A、D、F。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS SMS (Server Migration Service) executes migration by replicating on-prem VMs into AMIs; it neither discovers the environment nor estimates cloud costs. The task is to plan, not migrate.","why_zh":"AWS SMS(Server Migration Service)透過將地端 VM 複製為 AMI 來執行遷移；它既不探索環境也不估算雲端成本。本題是規劃而非執行遷移。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS X-Ray is for tracing and debugging distributed applications already running on AWS. It does not discover on-prem environments or estimate migration costs.","why_zh":"AWS X-Ray 用於追蹤與除錯已運行在 AWS 上的分散式應用，無法探索地端環境或估算遷移成本。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Amazon Inspector performs security vulnerability assessments of AWS workloads. It plays no role in discovering the on-prem environment or estimating cloud resource costs, so the dump's inclusion of it is wrong.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 對 AWS 工作負載進行安全弱點評估，與探索地端環境或估算雲端資源成本無關，因此題庫納入它是錯誤的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/what-is-appdiscovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/migrationhub/latest/ug/ec2-recommendations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/migration-tools/discovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/migration-readiness/welcome.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・複選"},{"id":354,"question_en":"A solutions architect is reviewing an application's resilience before launch. The application runs on an Amazon EC2 instance that is deployed in a private subnet of a VPC. The EC2 instance is provisioned by an Auto Scaling group that has a minimum capacity of 1 and a maximum capacity of 1. The application stores data on an Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance. The VPC has subnets configured in three Availability Zones and is configured with a single NAT gateway. The solutions architect needs to recommend a solution to ensure that the application will operate across multiple Availability Zones. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"解决方案架构师正在应用程序启动前审查其弹性。该应用程序在部署在 VPC 的私有子网中的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。EC2 实例由 Auto Scaling 组预置，该组的最小容量为 1，最大容量为 1。该应用程序将数据存储在 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库实例上。VPC 在 三个可用区中配置了子网，并配置了单个 NAT 网关。 解决方案架构师需要推荐一个解决方案，以确保应用程序能够跨多个可用区运行。 哪种解决方案可以满足这个要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an additional NAT gateway in the other Availability Zones. Update the route tables with appropriate routes. Modify the RDS for MySQL DB instance to a Multi-AZ configuration. Configure the Auto Scaling group to launch the instances across Availability Zones. Set the minimum capacity and maximum capacity of the Auto Scaling group to 3.","B":"Replace the NAT gateway with a virtual private gateway. Replace the RDS for MySQL DB instance with an Amazon Aurora MySQL DB cluster. Configure the Auto Scaling group to launch instances across all subnets in the VPC. Set the minimum capacity and maximum capacity of the Auto Scaling group to 3.","C":"Replace the NAT gateway with a NAT instance. Migrate the RDS for MySQL DB instance to an RDS for PostgreSQL DB instance. Launch a new EC2 instance in the other Availability Zones.","D":"Deploy an additional NAT gateway in the other Availability Zones. Update the route tables with appropriate routes. Modify the RDS for MySQL DB instance to turn on automatic backups and retain the backups for 7 days. Configure the Auto Scaling group to launch instances across all subnets in the VPC. Keep the minimum capacity and the maximum capacity of the Auto Scaling group at 1."},"options_zh":{"A":"在其他可用区中部署额外的 NAT 网关。使用适当的路由更新路由表。将 RDS for MySQL 数据库实例修改为多可用区配置。配置 Auto Scaling 组以跨可用区启动实例。设置Auto Scaling组的最小容量和最大容量为3。","B":"将 NAT 网关替换为虚拟专用网关。将 RDS for MySQL 数据库实例替换为 Amazon Aurora MySQL 数据库集群。配置 Auto Scaling 组以跨 VPC 中的所有子网启动实例。设置Auto Scaling组的最小容量和最大容量为3。","C":"将 NAT 网关替换为 NAT 实例。将 RDS for MySQL 数据库实例迁移到 RDS for PostgreSQL 数据库实例。在其他可用区启动新的 EC2 实例。","D":"在其他可用区部署额外的 NAT 网关。使用适当的路由更新路由表。修改RDS for MySQL实例开启自动备份，并保留备份7天。配 置 Auto Scaling 组以跨 VPC 中的所有子网启动实例。Auto Scaling组的最小容量和最大容量保持为1。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is full multi-AZ operation across all three layers: compute, NAT egress, and database. Option A is the only solution that correctly addresses every layer. AWS VPC documentation explicitly states that if resources in multiple AZs share one NAT gateway and that gateway's AZ fails, resources in other AZs lose internet access, so the recommendation is to create a NAT gateway in each Availability Zone and configure routing so resources use the NAT gateway in the same AZ - exactly what A does (additional NAT gateways plus route table updates). Converting the RDS for MySQL DB instance to Multi-AZ provides synchronous standby and automatic failover across AZs. Setting the Auto Scaling group to launch across AZs with min=max=3 places one instance per AZ so the app runs in all three zones simultaneously. The other options each break at least one layer.","explanation_zh":"需求是讓應用在三個層面都能跨多個 Availability Zone 運作:運算、NAT 對外連線、資料庫。只有 Option A 正確處理了每一層。AWS VPC 文件明確指出,若多個 AZ 的資源共用一個 NAT gateway,而該 gateway 所在 AZ 故障,其他 AZ 的資源就會失去網際網路存取;因此建議在每個 Availability Zone 各建立一個 NAT gateway,並設定路由讓資源使用同一 AZ 的 NAT gateway,這正是 A 所做的(新增 NAT gateway 並更新 route table)。將 RDS for MySQL 改為 Multi-AZ 提供跨 AZ 的同步備援與自動容錯移轉。將 Auto Scaling group 設定為跨 AZ 啟動且 min=max=3,讓每個 AZ 各有一個執行個體,使應用同時在三個區域運作。其他選項至少在某一層上有缺陷。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Replacing the NAT gateway with a virtual private gateway is wrong. A VGW is the VPN endpoint for connectivity to on-premises networks; it does not provide internet egress for private subnet instances, so outbound internet access for the application would break. Aurora would satisfy the DB layer, but the NAT change is fatal.","why_zh":"用 virtual private gateway 取代 NAT gateway 是錯的。VGW 是連到地端網路的 VPN 端點,不提供私有子網路執行個體的網際網路對外連線,會導致應用無法對外上網。Aurora 雖能滿足資料庫層,但 NAT 變更是致命缺陷。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but is wrong on every component. A single NAT instance is a single point of failure in one AZ and is legacy/less resilient than NAT gateways. Migrating MySQL to PostgreSQL is an irrelevant engine change that does nothing for AZ resilience and breaks the application/data. Manually launching EC2 instances bypasses the Auto Scaling group (still min/max=1), giving no managed, self-healing multi-AZ deployment.","why_zh":"這是 dump 建議的答案,但每個元件都錯。單一 NAT instance 是單一 AZ 的單點故障,且比 NAT gateway 更舊、更不具韌性。把 MySQL 遷移到 PostgreSQL 是與 AZ 韌性無關的引擎變更,還會破壞應用與資料。手動啟動 EC2 繞過了 Auto Scaling group(仍維持 min/max=1),無法提供受管、自我修復的多 AZ 部署。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Per-AZ NAT gateways are correct, but turning on automatic backups with 7-day retention provides point-in-time recovery, not high availability - a backup does not keep the database running across an AZ failure. Keeping the Auto Scaling group at min=max=1 means only one instance ever runs; the app does not operate across multiple AZs concurrently and there is downtime while a replacement relaunches. The database is not Multi-AZ. Fails the requirement.","why_zh":"每個 AZ 各放 NAT gateway 是對的,但開啟自動備份並保留 7 天提供的是時間點還原,而非高可用性 - 備份無法在 AZ 故障時讓資料庫持續運作。把 Auto Scaling group 維持在 min=max=1 代表永遠只有一個執行個體在執行;應用不會同時跨多個 AZ 運作,替換重啟期間也會有停機。資料庫並非 Multi-AZ。不符合需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/nat-gateway-basics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-nat-gateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/Concepts.MultiAZ.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/Concepts.MultiAZSingleStandby.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":355,"question_en":"A company is planning to migrate its on-premises transaction-processing application to AWS. The application runs inside Docker containers that are hosted on VMs in the company's data center. The Docker containers have shared storage where the application records transaction data. The transactions are time sensitive. The volume of transactions inside the application is unpredictable. The company must implement a low- latency storage solution that will automatically scale throughput to meet increased demand. The company cannot develop the application further and cannot continue to administer the Docker hosting environment. How should the company migrate the application to AWS to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正计划将其本地事务处理应用程序迁移到 AWS。该应用程序在托管在公司数据中心的虚拟机上的 Docker 容器内运行。 Docker 容器具有共享存储，应用程序在其中记录事务数据。 交易对时间敏感。应用程序内的交易量是不可预测的。该公司必须实施一种低延迟存储解决方案，该解决方案将自动扩展吞吐量以 满足不断增长的需求。该公司无法进一步开发该应用程序，也无法继续管理 Docker 托管环境。 公司应该如何将应用程序迁移到AWS来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate the containers that run the application to Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS). Use Amazon S3 to store the transaction data that the containers share.","B":"Migrate the containers that run the application to AWS Fargate for Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS). Create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. Create a Fargate task definition. Add a volume to the task definition to point to the EFS file system.","C":"Migrate the containers that run the application to AWS Fargate for Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS). Create an Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume. Create a Fargate task definition. Attach the EBS volume to each running task.","D":"Launch Amazon EC2 instances. Install Docker on the EC2 instances. Migrate the containers to the EC2 instances. Create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. Add a mount point to the EC2 instances for the EFS file system."},"options_zh":{"A":"将运行应用程序的容器迁移到 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS)。使用 Amazon S3 存储容器共享的事务数据。","B":"将运行应用程序的容器迁移到 AWS Fargate for Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS)。创建 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统。创建 Fargate 任务定义。将卷添加到任务定义以指向 EFS 文件系统。","C":"将运行应用程序的容器迁移到 AWS Fargate for Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS)。创建 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 卷。创建 Fargate 任务定义。将 EBS 卷附加到每个正在运行的任务。","D":"启动 Amazon EC2 实例。在 EC2 实例上安装 Docker。将容器迁移到 EC2 实例。创建 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文 件系统。将 EFS 文件系统的挂载点添加到 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Compute","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirements are: shared storage across containers, low latency for time-sensitive transactions, throughput that automatically scales to meet unpredictable demand, no further application development, and no continued administration of the Docker hosting environment. AWS Fargate for Amazon ECS is serverless and removes the need to administer the container host environment. Amazon EFS is a POSIX shared file system that multiple containers/tasks can mount concurrently (Fargate explicitly supports EFS volumes via the task definition volumes parameter). EFS Elastic throughput is the default mode and 'performance automatically scales up or down to meet the needs of your workload activity,' delivering ~1 ms read / ~2.7 ms write latency, which satisfies both the auto-scaling-throughput and low-latency requirements. Because the app already writes to shared file storage and cannot be modified, EFS lets it run unchanged, whereas S3 would require rewriting to object APIs. Option B is the only choice meeting every constraint.","explanation_zh":"需求為：容器間共用儲存、對時間敏感交易需低延遲、能自動隨不可預測需求擴展吞吐量、不可再開發應用程式、不可繼續管理 Docker 主機環境。AWS Fargate for Amazon ECS 為無伺服器服務，免除管理容器主機環境的需求。Amazon EFS 是 POSIX 共用檔案系統，多個容器/任務可同時掛載（Fargate 透過 task definition 的 volumes 參數明確支援 EFS volume）。EFS 的 Elastic throughput 為預設模式，效能會「自動上下擴展以符合工作負載需求」，並提供約 1 ms 讀取 / 2.7 ms 寫入的延遲，同時滿足自動擴展吞吐量與低延遲的需求。由於應用程式已使用共用檔案儲存且不可修改，EFS 可讓其原樣運行；而 S3 則需改寫為物件 API。選項 B 是唯一同時滿足所有限制的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon EKS still requires administering the Kubernetes/cluster environment (violates 'cannot continue to administer the Docker hosting environment'), and Amazon S3 is object storage, not a mountable POSIX shared file system; the existing app writes transaction data to shared file storage and cannot be modified to use S3 APIs.","why_zh":"Amazon EKS 仍需管理 Kubernetes/叢集環境（違反『不可繼續管理 Docker 主機環境』），且 Amazon S3 為物件儲存，並非可掛載的 POSIX 共用檔案系統；既有應用程式將交易資料寫入共用檔案儲存且不可改用 S3 API。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon EBS volumes attached to Fargate tasks are provisioned per task and are single-attach block storage; they cannot be shared concurrently across the multiple containers/tasks that the application requires, and EBS does not provide a shared file system or auto-scaling file throughput.","why_zh":"附加到 Fargate 任務的 Amazon EBS volume 為每任務各自配置且為單一附加的區塊儲存，無法在應用程式所需的多個容器/任務間同時共用，且 EBS 不提供共用檔案系統或自動擴展的檔案吞吐量。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Launching EC2 instances and installing Docker means the company must continue to manage and administer the Docker hosting environment, directly violating the stated requirement.","why_zh":"啟動 EC2 執行個體並安裝 Docker，意味著公司必須繼續管理與維護 Docker 主機環境，直接違反題目明確要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/managing-throughput.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/performance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/specify-efs-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/task_definition_parameters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/AWS_Fargate.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":356,"question_en":"A company is planning to migrate to the AWS Cloud. The company hosts many applications on Windows servers and Linux servers. Some of the servers are physical, and some of the servers are virtual. The company uses several types of databases in its on-premises environment. The company does not have an accurate inventory of its on-premises servers and applications. The company wants to rightsize its resources during migration. A solutions architect needs to obtain information about the network connections and the application relationships. The solutions architect must assess the company’s current environment and develop a migration plan. Which solution will provide the solutions architect with the required information to develop the migration plan?","question_zh":"一家公司正计划迁移到 AWS 云。该公司在 Windows 服务器和 Linux 服务器上托管许多应用程序。有些服务器是物理服务器，有些服 务器是虚拟服务器。该公司在其本地环境中使用多种类型的数据库。该公司没有其本地服务器和应用程序的准确清单。 该公司希望在迁移过程中调整其资源规模。解决方案架构师需要获取有关网络连接和应用程序关系的信息。解决方案架构师必须评 估公司当前的环境并制定迁移计划。 哪种解决方案将为解决方案架构师提供制定迁移计划所需的信息？","options_en":{"A":"Use Migration Evaluator to request an evaluation of the environment from AWS. Use the AWS Application Discovery Service Agentless Collector to import the details into a Migration Evaluator Quick Insights report.","B":"Use AWS Migration Hub and install the AWS Application Discovery Agent on the servers. Deploy the Migration Hub Strategy Recommendations application data collector. Generate a report by using Migration Hub Strategy Recommendations.","C":"Use AWS Migration Hub and run the AWS Application Discovery Service Agentless Collector on the servers. Group the servers and databases by using AWS Application Migration Service. Generate a report by using Migration Hub Strategy Recommendations.","D":"Use the AWS Migration Hub import tool to load the details of the company’s on-premises environment. Generate a report by using Migration Hub Strategy Recommendations."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Migration Evaluator 请求 AWS 对环境进行评估。使用 AWS Application Discovery Service Agentless Collector 将详细信息导入 到 Migration Evaluator Quick Insights 报告中。","B":"使用 AWS Migration Hub 并在服务器上安装 AWS Application Discovery Agent。部署迁移中心策略建议应用程序数据收集器。使用 迁移中心策略建议生成报告。","C":"使用 AWS Migration Hub 并在服务器上运行 AWS Application Discovery Service Agentless Collector。使用 AWS Application Migration Service 对服务器和数据库进行分组。使用迁移中心策略建议生成报告。","D":"使用 AWS Migration Hub 导入工具加载公司本地环境的详细信息。使用迁移中心策略建议生成报告。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Migration"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The company has no accurate inventory and needs to discover network connections and application relationships across Windows/Linux servers that are both physical and virtual, plus rightsizing data. Of the Application Discovery Service collection methods, only the AWS Application Discovery Agent supports physical servers AND captures inbound/outbound network connections, running processes, and time-series performance/utilization data needed for dependency mapping and rightsizing (the Agentless Collector is a VMware vCenter OVA that does not support physical servers and, in the vCenter module, cannot see processes or network connections). Migration Hub Strategy Recommendations explicitly consumes Application Discovery Service data and can use the Discovery Agent as its source; you then deploy the Strategy Recommendations application data collector to analyze applications/databases and generate the migration strategy report. Option D (Migration Hub import) only ingests whatever inventory you already provide and discovers nothing, so it cannot obtain network connections or application relationships for a company that lacks an inventory. Thus B is the only solution that actually discovers the required information.","explanation_zh":"公司沒有準確的清單，需要在實體與虛擬的 Windows/Linux 伺服器上探索網路連線與應用程式關聯，並取得 rightsizing 所需資料。在 Application Discovery Service 的收集方法中，只有 AWS Application Discovery Agent 同時支援實體伺服器，並能擷取進出站網路連線、執行中的處理程序，以及做相依性對應與 rightsizing 所需的時間序列效能/使用率資料（Agentless Collector 是部署在 VMware vCenter 的 OVA，不支援實體伺服器，且 vCenter 模組看不到處理程序或網路連線）。Migration Hub Strategy Recommendations 明確使用 Application Discovery Service 的資料，並可採用 Discovery Agent 作為來源；接著部署 Strategy Recommendations application data collector 來分析應用程式/資料庫並產生遷移策略報告。選項 D（Migration Hub import）只會匯入你已提供的清單，本身不做任何探索，因此無法為缺乏清單的公司取得網路連線或應用程式關聯。故 B 是唯一能真正探索所需資訊的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Migration Evaluator (formerly TSO Logic) produces a directional business case and cost estimate for migration; it does not map network connections or application relationships. Importing Agentless Collector data into a 'Quick Insights' report does not deliver dependency/relationship discovery, and Agentless Collector also omits physical servers.","why_zh":"Migration Evaluator（前身 TSO Logic）產生的是方向性的商業論證與成本估算，並不會對應網路連線或應用程式關聯。把 Agentless Collector 資料匯入 Quick Insights 報告無法提供相依性/關聯探索，而且 Agentless Collector 也不涵蓋實體伺服器。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) is the rehost execution/cutover tool; you cannot 'group servers and databases' with it. The Agentless Collector is a VMware vCenter appliance that does not support physical servers and (in the vCenter module) does not capture processes or network connections, so the required dependency data is missing.","why_zh":"AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) 是 rehost 的執行/切換工具，無法用它來『分組伺服器與資料庫』。Agentless Collector 是 VMware vCenter 設備，不支援實體伺服器，且（在 vCenter 模組中）不擷取處理程序或網路連線，因此缺少所需的相依性資料。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The Migration Hub import tool only ingests inventory data you supply via a CSV template and performs no discovery ('the data ingested is dependent on the data provided'). Since the company explicitly has no accurate inventory, import cannot obtain network connections or application relationships. This is the dump's suggested answer but it is technically wrong.","why_zh":"Migration Hub import 工具只會匯入你透過 CSV 範本提供的清單資料，本身不做探索（『匯入的資料取決於提供的資料』）。由於公司明確沒有準確清單，import 無法取得網路連線或應用程式關聯。這是題庫建議答案，但技術上是錯的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/what-is-appdiscovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/discovery-agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/migrationhub-strategy/latest/userguide/getting-started-prerequisites.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/migrationhub-strategy/latest/userguide/application-data-collector.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/discovery-import.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":357,"question_en":"A financial services company sells its software-as-a-service (SaaS) platform for application compliance to large global banks. The SaaS platform runs on AWS and uses multiple AWS accounts that are managed in an organization in AWS Organizations. The SaaS platform uses many AWS resources globally. For regulatory compliance, all API calls to AWS resources must be audited, tracked for changes, and stored in a durable and secure data store. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家金融服务公司向大型跨国银行出售其用于应用程序合规性的软件即服务 (SaaS) 平台。SaaS 平台在 AWS 上运行，并使用在 AWS Organizations 中的组织中管理的多个 AWS 账户。SaaS 平台使用全球许多 AWS 资源。 为了遵守法规，对 AWS 资源的所有 API 调用都必须经过审核、跟踪更改并存储在持久且安全的数据存储中。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new AWS CloudTrail trail. Use an existing Amazon S3 bucket in the organization's management account to store the logs. Deploy the trail to all AWS Regions. Enable MFA delete and encryption on the S3 bucket.","B":"Create a new AWS CloudTrail trail in each member account of the organization. Create new Amazon S3 buckets to store the logs. Deploy the trail to all AWS Regions. Enable MFA delete and encryption on the S3 buckets.","C":"Create a new AWS CloudTrail trail in the organization's management account. Create a new Amazon S3 bucket with versioning turned on to store the logs. Deploy the trail for all accounts in the organization. Enable MFA delete and encryption on the S3 bucket.","D":"Create a new AWS CloudTrail trail in the organization's management account. Create a new Amazon S3 bucket to store the logs. Configure Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to send log-file delivery notifications to an external management system that will track the logs. Enable MFA delete and encryption on the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建新的 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪。使用组织管理账户中的现有 Amazon S3 存储桶来存储日志。将跟踪部署到所有 AWS 区域。在 S3 存储桶上启用 MFA 删除和加密。","B":"在组织的每个成员账户中创建新的 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪。创建新的 Amazon S3 存储桶来存储日志。将跟踪部署到所有 AWS 区 域。在 S3 存储桶上启用 MFA 删除和加密。","C":"在组织的管理账户中创建新的 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪。创建一个启用版本控制的新 Amazon S3 存储桶来存储日志。为组织中的所 有帐户部署跟踪。在 S3 存储桶上启用 MFA 删除和加密。","D":"在组织的管理账户中创建新的 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪。创建新的 Amazon S3 存储桶来存储日志。配置 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 以将日志文件传送通知发送到将跟踪日志的外部管理系统。在 S3 存储桶上启用 MFA 删除和加密。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":94},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":358,"question_en":"A company is deploying a distributed in-memory database on a ­eet of Amazon EC2 instances. The ­eet consists of a primary node and eight worker nodes. The primary node is responsible for monitoring cluster health, accepting user requests, distributing user requests to worker nodes, and sending an aggregate response back to a client. Worker nodes communicate with each other to replicate data partitions. The company requires the lowest possible networking latency to achieve maximum performance. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在一组 Amazon EC2 实例上部署分布式内存数据库。该队列由一个主节点和八个工作节点组成。主节点负责监控集群健 康状况、接受用户请求、将用户请求分发到工作节点以及将聚合响应发送回客户端。工作节点相互通信以复制数据分区。 该公司需要尽可能低的网络延迟才能实现最佳性能。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Launch memory optimized EC2 instances in a partition placement group.","B":"Launch compute optimized EC2 instances in a partition placement group.","C":"Launch memory optimized EC2 instances in a cluster placement group.","D":"Launch compute optimized EC2 instances in a spread placement group."},"options_zh":{"A":"在分区置放组中启动内存优化的 EC2 实例。","B":"在分区置放群组中启动计算优化的 EC2 实例。","C":"在集群置放群组中启动内存优化的 EC2 实例。","D":"在分散放置组中启动计算优化的 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":359,"question_en":"A company maintains information on premises in approximately 1 million.csv files that are hosted on a VM. The data initially is 10 TB in size and grows at a rate of 1 TB each week. The company needs to automate backups of the data to the AWS Cloud. Backups of the data must occur daily. The company needs a solution that applies custom filters to back up only a subset of the data that is located in designated source directories. The company has set up an AWS Direct Connect connection. Which solution will meet the backup requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司在虚拟机上托管的大约 100 万个 .csv 文件中维护本地信息。数据最初大小为 10 TB，并以每周 1 TB 的速度增长。该公司需 要自动将数据备份到 AWS 云。 数据备份必须每天进行。该公司需要一种应用自定义过滤器来仅备份位于指定源目录中的数据子集的解决方案。该公司已建立 AWS Direct Connect 连接。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足备份要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use the Amazon S3 CopyObject API operation with multipart upload to copy the existing data to Amazon S3. Use the CopyObject API operation to replicate new data to Amazon S3 daily.","B":"Create a backup plan in AWS Backup to back up the data to Amazon S3. Schedule the backup plan to run daily.","C":"Install the AWS DataSync agent as a VM that runs on the on-premises hypervisor. Configure a DataSync task to replicate the data to Amazon S3 daily.","D":"Use an AWS Snowball Edge device for the initial backup. Use AWS DataSync for incremental backups to Amazon S3 daily."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon S3 CopyObject API 操作和分段上传将现有数据复制到 Amazon S3。使用 CopyObject API 操作每天将新数据复制到 Amazon S3。","B":"在 AWS Backup 中创建备份计划以将数据备份到 Amazon S3。安排备份计划每天运行。","C":"将 AWS DataSync 代理安装为在本地虚拟机管理程序上运行的虚拟机。配置 DataSync 任务以每天将数据复制到 Amazon S3。","D":"使用 AWS Snowball Edge 设备进行初始备份。每天使用 AWS DataSync 增量备份到 Amazon S3。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":82,"B":18},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is LEAST operational overhead combined with the hard requirement to apply custom filters that back up only a subset of data in designated source directories. AWS DataSync is purpose-built for this: you deploy a DataSync agent as a VM on the on-premises hypervisor, create a task to Amazon S3, schedule it to run daily, and use DataSync FilterRule (SIMPLE_PATTERN include/exclude, e.g. /folder1|/folder2) to transfer only the designated directories. DataSync also does incremental, multi-threaded, managed transfers over the existing AWS Direct Connect connection and scales easily to ~1M files and growing TBs, all with no custom code. Option D adds a Snowball Edge device for the initial seed, which is unnecessary operational overhead because a Direct Connect link already exists and 10 TB transfers fine over it, so it is not the LEAST-overhead choice. Therefore C is correct.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定詞是「LEAST operational overhead（最少維運負擔）」加上必須套用自訂篩選、只備份指定來源目錄子集的硬性需求。AWS DataSync 正是為此而生：在地端 hypervisor 上以 VM 部署 DataSync agent，建立傳輸到 Amazon S3 的 task，排程每日執行，並使用 DataSync FilterRule（SIMPLE_PATTERN 的 include/exclude，例如 /folder1|/folder2）只傳輸指定目錄。DataSync 還能透過既有的 AWS Direct Connect 進行增量、多執行緒、全代管傳輸，輕鬆擴展到約 100 萬個檔案與持續增長的 TB 級資料，且完全不需自訂程式碼。選項 D 為初始備份加入 Snowball Edge 裝置，但因為已有 Direct Connect 連線、10 TB 透過它傳輸並無問題，這個實體裝置只是多餘的維運負擔，因此並非最少負擔的方案。故正確答案為 C。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Building and maintaining custom CopyObject/multipart-upload scripts for ~1M files with daily change detection and directory filtering is high operational overhead and is not a managed solution.","why_zh":"為約 100 萬個檔案自行撰寫並維護 CopyObject/multipart 上傳腳本，還要每日偵測變更與做目錄篩選，維運負擔很高，且非代管方案。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Backup protects supported AWS service resources (EFS, FSx, EC2, RDS, S3, etc.) and VMware via Backup Gateway; it cannot natively back up arbitrary .csv files on a generic on-premises VM, and it offers no per-directory include/exclude file filters as required.","why_zh":"AWS Backup 保護的是受支援的 AWS 服務資源（EFS、FSx、EC2、RDS、S3 等）與透過 Backup Gateway 的 VMware，無法原生備份一般地端 VM 上的任意 .csv 檔案，也不提供題目所需的逐目錄 include/exclude 檔案篩選。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A Snowball Edge for the initial 10 TB seed is unnecessary because AWS Direct Connect already exists and easily handles the transfer; shipping/managing a physical device adds operational overhead, so this is not the LEAST-overhead option. DataSync alone already covers both initial and incremental transfers.","why_zh":"用 Snowball Edge 做 10 TB 初始播種並無必要，因為已有 AWS Direct Connect 可輕鬆傳輸；訂購/管理實體裝置增加維運負擔，故非最少負擔方案。單用 DataSync 即可涵蓋初始與增量傳輸。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datasync/latest/apireference/API_FilterRule.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datasync/latest/userguide/deploy-agents.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datasync/latest/userguide/what-is-datasync.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datasync/latest/userguide/create-s3-location.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/whatisbackup.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":360,"question_en":"A financial services company has an asset management product that thousands of customers use around the world. The customers provide feedback about the product through surveys. The company is building a new analytical solution that runs on Amazon EMR to analyze the data from these surveys. The following user personas need to access the analytical solution to perform different actions: • Administrator: Provisions the EMR cluster for the analytics team based on the team’s requirements • Data engineer: Runs ETL scripts to process, transform, and enrich the datasets • Data analyst: Runs SQL and Hive queries on the data A solutions architect must ensure that all the user personas have least privilege access to only the resources that they need. The user personas must be able to launch only applications that are approved and authorized. The solution also must ensure tagging for all resources that the user personas create. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家金融服务公司拥有一款资产管理产品，全世界数以千计的客户都在使用。客户通过调查提供有关产品的反馈。该公司正在构建 一个在 Amazon EMR 上运行的新分析解决方案，以分析这些调查的数据。以下用户角色需要访问分析解决方案以执行不同的操作： • 管理员：根据分析团队的需求为分析团队配置 EMR 集群 • 数据工程师：运行 ETL 脚本来处理、转换和丰富数据集 • 数据分析师：对数据运行 SQL 和 Hive 查询 解决方案架构师必须确保所有用户角色仅对他们所需的资源具有最低权限访问权限。用户角色必须能够仅启动经过批准和授权的应 用程序。该解决方案还必须确保对用户角色创建的所有资源进行标记。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create IAM roles for each user persona. Attach identity-based policies to define which actions the user who assumes the role can perform. Create an AWS Config rule to check for noncompliant resources. Configure the rule to notify the administrator to remediate the noncompliant resources.","B":"Setup Kerberos-based authentication for EMR clusters upon launch. Specify a Kerberos security configuration along with cluster-specific Kerberos options.","C":"Use AWS Service Catalog to control the Amazon EMR versions available for deployment, the cluster configuration, and the permissions for each user persona.","D":"Launch the EMR cluster by using AWS CloudFormation, Attach resource-based policies to the EMR cluster during cluster creation. Create an AWS. Config rule to check for noncompliant clusters and noncompliant Amazon S3 buckets. Configure the rule to notify the administrator to remediate the noncompliant resources."},"options_zh":{"A":"为每个用户角色创建 IAM 角色。附加基于身份的策略来定义担任该角色的用户可以执行哪些操作。创建 AWS Config 规则来检 查不合规的资源。配置规则以通知管理员修复不合规的资源。","B":"在启动时为 EMR 集群设置基于 Kerberos 的身份验证。指定 Kerberos 安全配置以及特定于集群的 Kerberos 选项。","C":"使用 AWS Service Catalog 控制可用于部署的 Amazon EMR 版本、集群配置以及每个用户角色的权限。","D":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 启动 EMR 集群，在集群创建期间将基于资源的策略附加到 EMR 集群。创建 AWS。配置规则以检查不 合规的集群和不合规的 Amazon S3 存储桶。配置规则以通知管理员修复不合规的资源。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":83,"A":17},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"AWS Service Catalog is purpose-built for exactly these requirements. Administrators package approved EMR deployments as CloudFormation-based products, organize them into per-persona portfolios, and grant least-privilege access via IAM users/groups/roles so each persona (administrator, data engineer, data analyst) only sees and launches the products they are authorized to use. Template and launch constraints restrict the EMR release versions, instance types, and cluster configuration, ensuring users can launch only approved and authorized applications. Versioning controls which EMR versions are available. The TagOption Library enforces a consistent tagging taxonomy on every provisioned product, satisfying the requirement that all resources users create are tagged. This is proactive, preventive governance applied at provisioning time. Option A (IAM roles + AWS Config) is detective/reactive: identity-based policies alone cannot restrict which EMR versions/applications users launch, and AWS Config only flags noncompliant resources after creation and then relies on manual remediation, so it neither limits users to approved applications nor enforces tagging at creation.","explanation_zh":"AWS Service Catalog 正是為這些需求設計的。管理員將核准的 EMR 部署封裝為以 CloudFormation 為基礎的 product，依不同人物角色組織成各自的 portfolio，並透過 IAM 使用者/群組/角色授予最小權限存取，使每個角色（administrator、data engineer、data analyst）只能看到並啟動其被授權使用的 product。Template constraint 與 launch constraint 可限制 EMR release 版本、執行個體類型與叢集組態，確保使用者只能啟動經核准與授權的應用程式；versioning 控制可用的 EMR 版本。TagOption Library 對每個 provisioned product 強制套用一致的標籤分類，滿足「所有使用者建立的資源都需標籤」的需求。這是在佈建當下套用的主動式預防治理。選項 A（IAM 角色 + AWS Config）屬於偵測式/被動式：僅靠 identity-based policy 無法限制使用者啟動哪些 EMR 版本/應用程式，而 AWS Config 只在資源建立後標記不合規並依賴人工補救，因此既無法限定核准應用程式，也無法在建立時強制標籤。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"IAM identity-based policies grant/deny API actions but cannot constrain which EMR release versions, applications, or cluster configurations a user launches, so they do not guarantee only approved/authorized applications. AWS Config is detective and reactive, flagging noncompliant resources only after creation and relying on manual remediation; it does not enforce tagging or approved configurations at provisioning time, so it fails least-privilege-to-approved-resources and proactive tagging.","why_zh":"IAM identity-based policy 只能允許/拒絕 API 動作，無法限制使用者啟動哪些 EMR release 版本、應用程式或叢集組態，因此無法保證只啟動經核准/授權的應用程式。AWS Config 屬偵測式且被動，僅在資源建立後標記不合規並依賴人工補救，無法在佈建當下強制標籤或核准組態，因此無法達成對核准資源的最小權限與主動標籤。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Kerberos security configurations provide authentication for users connecting to applications on the EMR cluster (e.g., big-data app principals). They do not provision clusters per persona, restrict which approved EMR versions/applications can be launched, enforce least-privilege AWS permissions, or enforce resource tagging. It addresses none of the stated governance requirements.","why_zh":"Kerberos 安全組態提供使用者連線到 EMR 叢集應用程式時的驗證（例如大數據應用主體），並不能依角色佈建叢集、限制可啟動的核准 EMR 版本/應用程式、強制 AWS 最小權限或強制資源標籤，無法滿足任何治理需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon EMR does not support resource-based policies attached to the cluster, so 'attach resource-based policies to the EMR cluster during creation' is not a valid mechanism. Using CloudFormation plus AWS Config is again detective and does not prevent users from launching unapproved EMR versions/applications or proactively enforce tagging, relying on after-the-fact manual remediation.","why_zh":"Amazon EMR 並不支援將 resource-based policy 附加到叢集，因此「在叢集建立時附加 resource-based policy」並非有效機制。CloudFormation 搭配 AWS Config 同樣是偵測式，無法阻止使用者啟動未核准的 EMR 版本/應用程式，也無法主動強制標籤，僅能事後人工補救。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/what-is_concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/tagoptions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/studio-notebooks-set-up-emr-templates.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/emr/latest/ManagementGuide/emr-kerberos.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":361,"question_en":"A software as a service (SaaS) company uses AWS to host a service that is powered by AWS PrivateLink. The service consists of proprietary software that runs on three Amazon EC2 instances behind a Network Load Balancer (NLB). The instances are in private subnets in multiple Availability Zones in the eu-west-2 Region. All the company's customers are in eu-west-2. However, the company now acquires a new customer in the us-east-1 Region. The company creates a new VPC and new subnets in us-east-1. The company establishes inter-Region VPC peering between the VPCs in the two Regions. The company wants to give the new customer access to the SaaS service, but the company does not want to immediately deploy new EC2 resources in us-east-1. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家软件即服务 (SaaS) 公司使用 AWS 托管由 AWS PrivateLink 提供支持的服务。该服务由专有软件组成，该软件在网络负载均衡器 (NLB) 后面的三个 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。这些实例位于 eu-west-2 区域的多个可用区的私有子网中。该公司的所有客户均位于 eu- west-2。 然而，该公司现在在 us-east-1 区域获得了一个新客户。该公司在 us-east-1 中创建了一个新的 VPC 和新的子网。公司在两个区域的 VPC 之间建立区域间 VPC 对等互连。 该公司希望让新客户能够访问 SaaS 服务，但公司不希望立即在 us-east-1 中部署新的 EC2 资源。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a PrivateLink endpoint service in us-east-1 to use the existing NLB that is in eu-west-2. Grant specific AWS accounts access to connect to the SaaS service.","B":"Create an NLB in us-east-1. Create an IP target group that uses the IP addresses of the company's instances in eu-west-2 that host the SaaS service. Configure a PrivateLink endpoint service that uses the NLB that is in us-east-1. Grant specific AWS accounts access to connect to the SaaS service.","C":"Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in front of the EC2 instances in eu-west-2. Create an NLB in us-east-1. Associate the NLB that is in us-east-1 with an ALB target group that uses the ALB that is in eu-west-2. Configure a PrivateLink endpoint service that uses the NLB that is in us-east-1. Grant specific AWS accounts access to connect to the SaaS service.","D":"Use AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) to share the EC2 instances that are in eu-west-2. In us-east-1, create an NLB and an instance target group that includes the shared EC2 instances from eu-west-2. Configure a PrivateLink endpoint service that uses the NLB that is in us-east-1. Grant specific AWS accounts access to connect to the SaaS service."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 us-east-1 中配置 PrivateLink 端点服务以使用 eu-west-2 中的现有 NLB。授予特定 AWS 账户访问权限以连接到 SaaS 服务。","B":"在 us-east-1 中创建 NLB。创建一个 IP 目标组，该组使用 eu-west-2 中托管 SaaS 服务的公司实例的 IP 地址。配置使用 us-east-1 中的 NLB 的 PrivateLink 端点服务。授予特定 AWS 账户访问权限以连接到 SaaS 服务。","C":"在 eu-west-2 中的 EC2 实例前面创建应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB)。在 us-east-1 中创建 NLB。将 us-east-1 中的 NLB 与使用 eu- west-2 中的 ALB 的 ALB 目标组关联。配置使用 us-east-1 中的 NLB 的 PrivateLink 端点服务。授予特定 AWS 账户访问权限以连接到 SaaS 服务。","D":"使用 AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) 共享 eu-west-2 中的 EC2 实例。在 us-east-1 中，创建一个 NLB 和一个实例目标 组，其中包括来自 eu-west-2 的共享 EC2 实例。配置使用 us-east-1 中的 NLB 的 PrivateLink 端点服务。授予特定 AWS 账户访问权 限以连接到 SaaS 服务。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":58,"B":42},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"A PrivateLink endpoint service is a Regional construct, and the load balancer specified when creating an endpoint service must reside in the same Region (and account) as the service. So you must build an NLB in us-east-1 and attach the endpoint service to it. The eu-west-2 instances cannot be reached as instance-ID targets cross-Region, but an NLB IP target group accepts any reachable private IP from RFC 1918 / 100.64.0.0/10 CIDR blocks (the same mechanism used for on-premises targets over Direct Connect/VPN). Because inter-Region VPC peering is already established between the two VPCs, the us-east-1 NLB can register the eu-west-2 instances' private IPs as ip targets and route to them over the peering connection, with no new EC2 resources deployed in us-east-1. This is exactly Option B. The community top vote (A) is the closest distractor but is technically impossible: you cannot point a us-east-1 endpoint service at an NLB located in eu-west-2.","explanation_zh":"PrivateLink endpoint service 是區域性資源；建立 endpoint service 時所指定的 load balancer 必須與該服務位於同一個 Region（與帳號）。因此必須在 us-east-1 建立一個 NLB，並把 endpoint service 綁定到它。eu-west-2 的執行個體無法以 instance-ID（instance 目標類型）跨 Region 註冊，但 NLB 的 IP 目標群組可接受 RFC 1918 / 100.64.0.0/10 私有 CIDR 範圍內任何可達的私有 IP（與 Direct Connect/VPN 連線的地端目標所用機制相同）。由於兩個 VPC 之間已建立跨 Region VPC peering，us-east-1 的 NLB 可將 eu-west-2 執行個體的私有 IP 註冊為 ip 目標，並透過 peering 連線轉送流量，且不需在 us-east-1 部署任何新的 EC2 資源。這正是選項 B。社群最高票（A）是最接近的干擾項，但技術上不可行：你無法讓 us-east-1 的 endpoint service 指向位於 eu-west-2 的 NLB。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An endpoint service and its load balancer are Regional and must be co-located. You cannot create a PrivateLink endpoint service in us-east-1 that references an existing NLB located in eu-west-2; the NLB must be in the same Region as the endpoint service.","why_zh":"endpoint service 與其 load balancer 都是區域性的，必須位於同一 Region。你無法在 us-east-1 建立一個指向位於 eu-west-2 既有 NLB 的 PrivateLink endpoint service；該 NLB 必須與 endpoint service 同 Region。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Registering an ALB as a target of an NLB requires both load balancers to be in the same VPC within the same account (per AWS docs), so an eu-west-2 ALB cannot be a target of a us-east-1 NLB. It also adds an unnecessary ALB layer.","why_zh":"把 ALB 註冊為 NLB 的目標時，依 AWS 文件規定兩個 load balancer 必須在同一帳號的同一 VPC 內，因此 eu-west-2 的 ALB 不能作為 us-east-1NLB 的目標；而且還多加了不必要的 ALB 層。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS RAM does not share EC2 instances in a way that lets them be registered by instance ID in another Region's NLB. The instance target type requires targets in the same VPC/Region as the load balancer, so shared cross-Region instances cannot be added to a us-east-1 instance target group. This is the dump's suggested answer but is infeasible.","why_zh":"AWS RAM 無法以可讓另一 Region 的 NLB 透過 instance ID 註冊的方式來分享 EC2 執行個體。instance 目標類型要求目標與 load balancer 在同一 VPC/Region，因此跨 Region 分享的執行個體無法加入 us-east-1 的 instance 目標群組。這是題庫建議答案，但技術上不可行。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/network/load-balancer-target-groups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/network/application-load-balancer-target.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/network/target-group-register-targets.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":362,"question_en":"A company needs to monitor a growing number of Amazon S3 buckets across two AWS Regions. The company also needs to track the percentage of objects that are encrypted in Amazon S3. The company needs a dashboard to display this information for internal compliance teams. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司需要监控两个 AWS 区域中越来越多的 Amazon S3 存储桶。该公司还需要跟踪 Amazon S3 中加密对象的百分比。该公司需要 一个仪表板来为内部合规团队显示这些信息。 哪种解决方案能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new 3 Storage Lens dashboard in each Region to track bucket and encryption metrics. Aggregate data from both Region dashboards into a single dashboard in Amazon QuickSight for the compliance teams.","B":"Deploy an AWS Lambda function in each Region to list the number of buckets and the encryption status of objects. Store this data in Amazon S3. Use Amazon Athena queries to display the data on a custom dashboard in Amazon QuickSight for the compliance teams.","C":"Use the S3 Storage Lens default dashboard to track bucket and encryption metrics. Give the compliance teams access to the dashboard directly in the S3 console.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to detect AWS CloudTrail events for S3 object creation. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to record encryption metrics in Amazon DynamoDB. Use Amazon QuickSight to display the metrics in a dashboard for the compliance teams."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个区域中创建一个新的 3 Storage Lens 仪表板来跟踪存储桶和加密指标。将两个区域控制面板中的数据聚合到 Amazon QuickSight 中的单个控制面板中，供合规团队使用。","B":"在每个区域部署 AWS Lambda 函数，列出存储桶的数量和对象的加密状态。将此数据存储在 Amazon S3 中。使用 Amazon Athena 查询在 Amazon QuickSight 的自定义仪表板上为合规团队显示数据。","C":"使用 S3 Storage Lens 默认仪表板来跟踪存储桶和加密指标。让合规团队可以直接在 S3 控制台中访问仪表板。","D":"创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则以检测 S3 对象创建的 AWS CloudTrail 事件。配置规则以调用 AWS Lambda 函数以记录 Amazon DynamoDB 中的加密指标。使用 Amazon QuickSight 在仪表板中为合规团队显示指标。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":76},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The qualifier is LEAST operational overhead. Amazon S3 Storage Lens automatically provides a preconfigured default dashboard (default-account-dashboard) that summarizes insights for the entire account across ALL AWS Regions and updates daily, with drill-down by Region, bucket, prefix, etc. Its free-tier metrics include the Data protection metric '% encrypted objects' (Percentage of objects that are encrypted), which directly satisfies the requirement to track the encryption percentage. Compliance teams can be given access to this dashboard directly in the S3 console, so no dashboard creation, no ETL, and no separate analytics service is required, and newly added buckets are picked up automatically. Options A, B, and D all build or maintain extra infrastructure (per-Region dashboards plus QuickSight, custom Lambda/Athena pipelines, or EventBridge/CloudTrail/Lambda/DynamoDB), which is strictly more operational overhead than using the built-in default dashboard. Therefore C is correct; the dump's suggested answer B is wrong.","explanation_zh":"題目限定條件是 LEAST operational overhead（最少維運負擔）。Amazon S3 Storage Lens 會自動提供一個預先設定好的 default dashboard（default-account-dashboard），它會彙總整個帳戶、橫跨所有 AWS Region 的洞察並每日更新，並可依 Region、bucket、prefix 等下鑽。其免費層指標已包含 Data protection 類別的『% encrypted objects』（加密物件百分比），正好滿足追蹤加密比例的需求。只要把此 dashboard 在 S3 主控台中授權給合規團隊即可，無需建立 dashboard、無需 ETL、也不需另外的分析服務，且新增的 bucket 會自動被納入。選項 A、B、D 都需要額外建置或維護基礎設施（每個 Region 各建 dashboard 再加 QuickSight、自訂 Lambda/Athena 管線、或 EventBridge/CloudTrail/Lambda/DynamoDB），維運負擔都比直接使用內建 default dashboard 大。因此正解是 C；dump 建議答案 B 錯誤。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creating new Storage Lens dashboards in each Region and then aggregating into QuickSight adds setup and ongoing maintenance. Storage Lens already aggregates account-wide across Regions, so the per-Region dashboards plus a QuickSight pipeline are unnecessary and add overhead compared to the default dashboard.","why_zh":"在每個 Region 新建 Storage Lens dashboard 再彙整到 QuickSight，會增加建置與持續維護工作。Storage Lens 本身已可跨 Region 在帳戶層級彙總，故每個 Region 各建 dashboard 加 QuickSight 管線是多餘的，比起 default dashboard 維運負擔更高。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but is the highest-overhead option: building and maintaining per-Region Lambda functions, storing to S3, writing Athena queries, and building a custom QuickSight dashboard. Storage Lens natively reports the encryption percentage, so this fully custom pipeline is unnecessary and contradicts the LEAST-overhead requirement.","why_zh":"這是 dump 建議答案，卻是維運負擔最高的方案：要建置並維護各 Region 的 Lambda、存到 S3、撰寫 Athena 查詢，再建自訂 QuickSight dashboard。Storage Lens 原生即可報告加密百分比，故此完全自訂的管線並無必要，且與最少維運負擔的要求相違。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An EventBridge + CloudTrail + Lambda + DynamoDB + QuickSight pipeline is also fully custom and high-overhead. It only records encryption status for objects created after deployment (no baseline for existing objects) and requires building/maintaining multiple components, far more than using the managed default dashboard.","why_zh":"EventBridge + CloudTrail + Lambda + DynamoDB + QuickSight 的管線同樣完全自訂且維運負擔高。它只會記錄部署之後新建物件的加密狀態（無法涵蓋既有物件的基準），且需建置與維護多個元件，遠多於直接使用受管的 default dashboard。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/storage_lens_basics_metrics_recommendations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/storage_lens_metrics_glossary.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/metrics-dimensions.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":363,"question_en":"A company’s CISO has asked a solutions architect to re-engineer the company's current CI/CD practices to make sure patch deployments to its application can happen as quickly as possible with minimal downtime if vulnerabilities are discovered. The company must also be able to quickly roll back a change in case of errors. The web application is deployed in a ­eet of Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer. The company is currently using GitHub to host the application source code, and has configured an AWS CodeBuild project to build the application. The company also intends to use AWS CodePipeline to trigger builds from GitHub commits using the existing CodeBuild project. What CI/CD configuration meets all of the requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的 CISO 已要求解决方案架构师重新设计该公司当前的 CI/CD 实践，以确保在发现漏洞时尽快对其应用程序进行补丁部署， 同时将停机时间降至最低。公司还必须能够在出现错误时快速回滚更改。 Web 应用程序部署在应用程序负载均衡器后面的一组 Amazon EC2 实例中。该公司目前使用 GitHub 托管应用程序源代码，并配置了 AWS CodeBuild 项目来构建应用程序。该公司还打算使用 AWS CodePipeline 来触发使用现有 CodeBuild 项目的 GitHub 提交的构建。 什么样的 CI/CD 配置可以满足所有要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure CodePipeline with a deploy stage using AWS CodeDeploy configured for in-place deployment. Monitor the newly deployed code, and, if there are any issues, push another code update","B":"Configure CodePipeline with a deploy stage using AWS CodeDeploy configured for blue/green deployments. Monitor the newly deployed code, and, if there are any issues, trigger a manual rollback using CodeDeploy.","C":"Configure CodePipeline with a deploy stage using AWS CloudFormation to create a pipeline for test and production stacks. Monitor the newly deployed code, and, if there are any issues, push another code update.","D":"Configure the CodePipeline with a deploy stage using AWS OpsWorks and in-place deployments. Monitor the newly deployed code, and, if there are any issues, push another code update."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用配置为就地部署的 AWS CodeDeploy 通过部署阶段配置 CodePipeline。监控新部署的代码，如果有任何问题，推送另一个 代码更新","B":"使用为蓝/绿部署配置的 AWS CodeDeploy 通过部署阶段配置 CodePipeline。监视新部署的代码，如果存在任何问题，请使用 CodeDeploy 触发手动回滚。","C":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 配置 CodePipeline 的部署阶段，为测试和生产堆栈创建管道。监视新部署的代码，如果存在任何问 题，则推送另一个代码更新。","D":"使用 AWS OpsWorks 和就地部署通过部署阶段配置 CodePipeline。监视新部署的代码，如果存在任何问题，则推送另一个代码 更新。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirements are fast patch deployment with minimal downtime AND quick rollback on errors, for an EC2 fleet behind an ALB with existing GitHub/CodeBuild/CodePipeline. AWS CodeDeploy blue/green deployment provisions a replacement (green) environment, registers it behind the ALB, and shifts production traffic to it only after the new revision is healthy, so there is minimal downtime. Because the original (blue) instances are kept available, rollback is fast: CodeDeploy can automatically or manually roll back by rerouting traffic back to the original environment (or redeploying the last known good revision), which is far quicker than rebuilding and redeploying. Option B is the only choice that pairs blue/green (minimal downtime) with a true CodeDeploy rollback, making it the correct answer. The exam dump's suggested answer C is wrong because CloudFormation test/prod stacks with 'push another code update' provide no rapid rollback and add overhead.","explanation_zh":"需求是以最快速度部署修補且停機時間最短，並且在發生錯誤時能快速回復，環境為 ALB 後方的 EC2 機群，並已有 GitHub/CodeBuild/CodePipeline。AWS CodeDeploy 的 blue/green 部署會建立一組替換（green）環境，將其註冊到 ALB 後方，只有在新版本健康後才把正式流量切換過去，因此停機時間最短。由於原本的（blue）執行個體仍保留可用，回復速度很快：CodeDeploy 可自動或手動回復，將流量切回原環境（或重新部署上一個正常版本），遠比重新建置並重新部署更快。選項 B 是唯一同時提供 blue/green（最短停機）與真正 CodeDeploy 回復機制的答案，故為正解。考古題建議答案 C 是錯的，因為用 CloudFormation 建立 test/prod 堆疊並『再推送一次程式更新』無法快速回復，且增加運維負擔。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CodeDeploy in-place deployment takes instances offline during the rolling update, risking downtime, and 'push another code update' as rollback requires a full new build/deploy cycle rather than a fast traffic reroute, so it fails both the minimal-downtime and quick-rollback requirements.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy 就地（in-place）部署在滾動更新時會將執行個體下線，有停機風險；而以『再推送一次程式更新』作為回復需要完整的重新建置與部署週期，並非快速的流量切換，因此同時不符合最短停機與快速回復的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Using CloudFormation to build test/production stacks does not provide a rapid rollback mechanism; 'push another code update' means a slow rebuild/redeploy, and managing stacks adds operational complexity without the fast traffic-shift rollback that blue/green provides.","why_zh":"使用 CloudFormation 建立 test/production 堆疊並未提供快速回復機制；『再推送一次程式更新』代表緩慢的重新建置與重新部署，且管理堆疊增加運維複雜度，缺乏 blue/green 那種快速流量切換的回復能力。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS OpsWorks with in-place deployments is the wrong fit: in-place causes downtime, OpsWorks does not naturally integrate with the existing CodePipeline/CodeBuild GitHub toolchain for blue/green, and 'push another code update' is not a fast rollback.","why_zh":"AWS OpsWorks 搭配就地部署並不合適：就地部署會造成停機，OpsWorks 也無法自然地與既有的 CodePipeline/CodeBuild/GitHub 工具鏈整合做 blue/green，而『再推送一次程式更新』也非快速回復。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployments-rollback-and-redeploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/overview-deployment-options/bluegreen-deployments.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":364,"question_en":"A company is managing many AWS accounts by using an organization in AWS Organizations. Different business units in the company run applications on Amazon EC2 instances. All the EC2 instances must have a BusinessUnit tag so that the company can track the cost for each business unit. A recent audit revealed that some instances were missing this tag. The company manually added the missing tag to the instances. What should a solutions architect do to enforce the tagging requirement in the future?","question_zh":"一家公司通过使用 AWS Organizations 中的组织来管理许多 AWS 账户。公司中的不同业务部门在 Amazon EC2 实例上运行应用程序。 所有 EC2 实例都必须具有 BusinessUnit 标签，以便公司可以跟踪每个业务部门的成本。 最近的审计显示，某些实例缺少此标签。该公司手动将丢失的标签添加到实例中。 解决方案架构师应该做什么来强制执行未来的标记要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable tag policies in the organization. Create a tag policy for the BusinessUnit tag. Ensure that compliance with tag key capitalization is turned off. Implement the tag policy for the ec2:instance resource type. Attach the tag policy to the root of the organization.","B":"Enable tag policies in the organization. Create a tag policy for the BusinessUnit tag. Ensure that compliance with tag key capitalization is turned on. Implement the tag policy for the ec2:instance resource type. Attach the tag policy to the organization's management account.","C":"Create an SCP and attach the SCP to the root of the organization. Include the following statement in the SCP:","D":"Create an SCP and attach the SCP to the organization’s management account. Include the following statement in the SCP:"},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织中启用标签策略。为 BusinessUnit 标签创建标签策略。确保关闭标签键大写合规性。实施 ec2:instance 资源类型的标签 策略。将标签策略附加到组织的根目录。","B":"在组织中启用标签策略。为 BusinessUnit 标签创建标签策略。确保启用标签键大写合规性。实施 ec2:instance 资源类型的标签 策略。将标签策略附加到组织的管理帐户。","C":"创建 SCP 并将 SCP 附加到组织的根目录。在 SCP 中包含以下声明：","D":"创建 SCP 并将 SCP 附加到组织的管理帐户。在 SCP 中包含以下声明："},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":70,"B":21},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to PREVENT EC2 instances from being created without the BusinessUnit tag. Tag policies (options A and B) cannot do this: per AWS docs, 'Untagged resources or tags that aren't defined in the tag policy aren't evaluated for compliance' and 'Resources that have never had tags attached to them don't show as noncompliant... Account administrators can still create untagged resources.' Tag policy enforcement (enforced_for) only blocks noncompliant tagging operations (wrong case/value) on tags that ARE applied; it never forces a tag to exist. The AWS-recommended way to mandate a tag at creation time is an SCP that denies the create action when the required tag key is absent (Deny with a Null condition on aws:RequestTag/BusinessUnit). The SCP must be attached to the organization root (or the OUs containing the member accounts) so it applies to all member accounts where the business units run their instances. This makes C correct. D fails because, per the docs, 'SCPs don't affect users or roles in the management account. They affect only the member accounts'; attaching the SCP only to the management account enforces nothing on the member accounts that actually run the EC2 instances.","explanation_zh":"需求是要「防止」EC2 instances 在缺少 BusinessUnit 標籤的情況下被建立。Tag policies（選項 A 與 B）做不到：根據 AWS 文件，未加標籤的資源或未在 tag policy 中定義的標籤不會被評估合規性，而且「從未加過標籤的資源不會顯示為不合規……帳戶管理員仍可建立未加標籤的資源」。Tag policy 的 enforced_for 強制只會阻擋已套用標籤上的「不合規標籤操作」（錯誤的大小寫或值），絕不會強制標籤必須存在。AWS 建議用來在建立時強制加標籤的做法是 SCP：當必要標籤鍵不存在時 Deny 建立動作（搭配對 aws:RequestTag/BusinessUnit 的 Null 條件）。此 SCP 必須附加到 organization root（或包含成員帳戶的 OU），才能套用到所有實際執行 instances 的成員帳戶，因此 C 正確。D 錯誤的原因是文件明載「SCP 不影響 management account 的使用者或角色，只影響成員帳戶」；僅將 SCP 附加到 management account 對實際執行 EC2 instances 的成員帳戶毫無強制效果。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Tag policies do not prevent creation of untagged resources; untagged resources are not evaluated for compliance, so an EC2 instance can still be launched with no BusinessUnit tag. The requirement (enforce/prevent missing tags) is unmet. Also turning capitalization compliance off is irrelevant to requiring the tag's existence.","why_zh":"Tag policies 無法阻止建立未加標籤的資源；未加標籤的資源不會被評估合規性，因此仍可啟動沒有 BusinessUnit 標籤的 EC2 instance，無法滿足需求。而且關閉大小寫合規與「要求標籤存在」無關。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same core flaw as A: tag policies cannot force a tag to be present at creation, so missing tags are not prevented. Additionally, attaching to the management account is wrong; tag policies should be attached to OUs/root to apply to member accounts. This is the dump's suggested answer and it is technically incorrect.","why_zh":"與 A 的核心缺陷相同：tag policies 無法在建立時強制標籤存在，因此無法防止缺漏標籤。此外附加到 management account 也不對；tag policies 應附加到 OU/root 才能作用於成員帳戶。這是 dump 建議答案，但技術上錯誤。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An SCP is the right mechanism, but SCPs do not affect users or roles in the management account; they only affect member accounts. Attaching the SCP solely to the management account would not enforce the tag requirement on the member accounts where the business units launch instances, so the audit gap remains.","why_zh":"SCP 是正確機制，但 SCP 不影響 management account 的使用者或角色，只影響成員帳戶。僅附加到 management account 無法對實際啟動 instances 的成員帳戶強制標籤需求，稽核漏洞仍存在。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_example-tag-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":365,"question_en":"A company is running a workload that consists of thousands of Amazon EC2 instances. The workload is running in a VPC that contains several public subnets and private subnets. The public subnets have a route for 0.0.0.0/0 to an existing internet gateway. The private subnets have a route for 0.0.0.0/0 to an existing NAT gateway. A solutions architect needs to migrate the entire ­eet of EC2 instances to use IPv6. The EC2 instances that are in private subnets must not be accessible from the public internet. What should the solutions architect do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在运行由数千个 Amazon EC2 实例组成的工作负载。工作负载在包含多个公有子网和私有子网的 VPC 中运行。公有子网 有一条从 0.0.0.0/0 到现有 Internet 网关的路由。私有子网有一条从 0.0.0.0/0 到现有 NAT 网关的路由。 解决方案架构师需要迁移整个 EC2 实例队列以使用 IPv6。私有子网中的 EC2 实例不得从公共互联网访问。 解决方案架构师应该怎样做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Update the existing VPC, and associate a custom IPv6 CIDR block with the VPC and all subnets. Update all the VPC route tables, and add a route for ::/0 to the internet gateway.","B":"Update the existing VPC, and associate an Amazon-provided IPv6 CIDR block with the VPC and all subnets. Update the VPC route tables for all private subnets, and add a route for ::/0 to the NAT gateway.","C":"Update the existing VPC, and associate an Amazon-provided IPv6 CIDR block with the VPC and all subnets. Create an egress-only internet gateway. Update the VPC route tables for all private subnets, and add a route for ::/0 to the egress-only internet gateway.","D":"Update the existing VPC, and associate a custom IPV6 CIDR block with the VPC and all subnets. Create a new NAT gateway, and enable IPV6 support. Update the VPC route tables for all private subnets, and add a route for ::/0 to the IPv6-enabled NAT gateway."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新现有 VPC，并将自定义 IPv6 CIDR 块与 VPC 和所有子网关联。更新所有 VPC 路由表，并将 ::/0 的路由添加到 Internet 网 关。","B":"更新现有 VPC，并将 Amazon 提供的 IPv6 CIDR 块与 VPC 和所有子网关联。更新所有私有子网的 VPC 路由表，并将 ::/0 的路由 添加到 NAT 网关。","C":"更新现有 VPC，并将 Amazon 提供的 IPv6 CIDR 块与 VPC 和所有子网关联。创建仅出口的互联网网关。更新所有私有子网的 VPC 路由表，并将 ::/0 的路由添加到仅出口互联网网关。","D":"更新现有 VPC，并将自定义 IPV6 CIDR 块与 VPC 和所有子网关联。创建新的 NAT 网关，并启用 IPV6 支持。更新所有私有子网 的 VPC 路由表，并将 ::/0 的路由添加到启用 IPv6 的 NAT 网关。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":92},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":366,"question_en":"A company is using Amazon API Gateway to deploy a private REST API that will provide access to sensitive data. The API must be accessible only from an application that is deployed in a VPC. The company deploys the API successfully. However, the API is not accessible from an Amazon EC2 instance that is deployed in the VPC. Which solution will provide connectivity between the EC2 instance and the API?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 Amazon API Gateway 部署私有 REST API，以提供对敏感数据的访问。该 API 必须只能从部署在 VPC 中的应用程序 访问。该公司成功部署了 API。但是，无法从部署在 VPC 中的 Amazon EC2 实例访问该 API。 哪种解决方案将提供 EC2 实例和 API 之间的连接？","options_en":{"A":"Create an interface VPC endpoint for API Gateway. Attach an endpoint policy that allows apigateway:* actions. Disable private DNS naming for the VPC endpoint. Configure an API resource policy that allows access from the VPC. Use the VPC endpoint's DNS name to access the API.","B":"Create an interface VPC endpoint for API Gateway. Attach an endpoint policy that allows the execute-api:Invoke action. Enable private DNS naming for the VPC endpoint. Configure an API resource policy that allows access from the VPC endpoint. Use the API endpoint’s DNS names to access the API.","C":"Create a Network Load Balancer (NLB) and a VPC link. Configure private integration between API Gateway and the NLB. Use the API endpoint’s DNS names to access the API.","D":"Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and a VPC Link. Configure private integration between API Gateway and the ALB. Use the ALB endpoint’s DNS name to access the API."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 API Gateway 创建接口 VPC 终端节点。附加允许 apigateway:* 操作的端点策略。禁用 VPC 终端节点的私有 DNS 命名。配置 允许VPC访问的API资源策略。使用 VPC 终端节点的 DNS 名称访问 API。","B":"为 API Gateway 创建接口 VPC 终端节点。附加允许执行 api:Invoke 操作的端点策略。为 VPC 终端节点启用私有 DNS 命名。配置 允许从 VPC 终端节点访问的 API 资源策略。使用 API 端点的 DNS 名称来访问 API。","C":"创建网络负载均衡器 (NLB) 和 VPC 链路。配置 API Gateway 和 NLB 之间的私有集成。使用 API 端点的 DNS 名称来访问 API。","D":"创建应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 和 VPC 链接。配置 API Gateway 和 ALB 之间的私有集成。使用 ALB 端点的 DNS 名称来访问 API。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"A private REST API in API Gateway is reachable from a VPC only through an interface VPC endpoint for the execute-api service, combined with an API resource policy that permits the VPC/VPC endpoint and an endpoint policy that allows the data-plane action execute-api:Invoke. Option B does exactly this: it creates the interface endpoint, attaches an endpoint policy allowing execute-api:Invoke, enables private DNS naming, configures an API resource policy that allows access from the VPC endpoint, and uses the API endpoint's DNS names. Enabling private DNS lets the EC2 instance resolve and call the standard https://{restapi-id}.execute-api.{region}.amazonaws.com/{stage} URL without adding Host or x-apigw-api-id headers, which is the recommended access method. The dump's suggested answer D (ALB + VPC Link private integration) is wrong because VPC Link/private integration is for the opposite direction (letting a public/regional API reach resources inside a VPC), not for letting a VPC client reach a private API.","explanation_zh":"API Gateway 的 private REST API 只能透過針對 execute-api 服務建立的 interface VPC endpoint，再搭配允許該 VPC/VPC endpoint 的 API resource policy，以及允許資料平面動作 execute-api:Invoke 的 endpoint policy 才能從 VPC 內被存取。選項 B 正是如此：建立 interface endpoint、附加允許 execute-api:Invoke 的 endpoint policy、啟用 private DNS naming、設定允許從 VPC endpoint 存取的 API resource policy，並使用 API endpoint 的 DNS 名稱。啟用 private DNS 後，EC2 執行個體即可解析並呼叫標準的 https://{restapi-id}.execute-api.{region}.amazonaws.com/{stage} URL，毋須加上 Host 或 x-apigw-api-id 標頭，這是建議的存取方式。Dump 建議答案 D（ALB + VPC Link 私有整合）是錯的，因為 VPC Link/private integration 是相反方向的用途（讓公開/區域型 API 連到 VPC 內的資源），而非讓 VPC 內的用戶端連到 private API。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses the wrong endpoint-policy action (apigateway:* is the management/control-plane permission, not the data-plane execute-api:Invoke needed to call the API), and disabling private DNS plus relying on the VPC endpoint's DNS name is the harder, non-recommended path that requires overriding headers; combined these break clean connectivity.","why_zh":"使用錯誤的 endpoint-policy 動作（apigateway:* 是管理/控制平面權限，而非呼叫 API 所需的資料平面 execute-api:Invoke），且關閉 private DNS 並改用 VPC endpoint DNS 名稱屬於較困難且非建議的做法，需覆寫標頭；兩者合併會破壞正常連線。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"NLB + VPC Link private integration is used to let an API Gateway API reach private resources inside a VPC (backend integration), not to let a VPC client reach a private REST API; it does not provide the missing inbound connectivity to the private API.","why_zh":"NLB + VPC Link 私有整合是讓 API Gateway API 連到 VPC 內私有資源（後端整合）之用，而非讓 VPC 內用戶端連到 private REST API；無法提供連到 private API 所缺的入站連線。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same fundamental error as C and is the dump's wrong suggested answer: ALB + VPC Link private integration is for exposing VPC resources behind an API as a private integration target, not for a VPC client to invoke a private API. It addresses the opposite traffic direction.","why_zh":"與 C 同樣的根本錯誤，也是 dump 的錯誤建議答案：ALB + VPC Link 私有整合是把 VPC 資源作為 API 的私有整合後端，而非讓 VPC 用戶端呼叫 private API，方向相反。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-private-apis.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-private-api-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-private-api-test-invoke-url.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-vpc-endpoint-policies.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":367,"question_en":"A large payroll company recently merged with a small sta®ng company. The unified company now has multiple business units, each with its own existing AWS account. A solutions architect must ensure that the company can centrally manage the billing and access policies for all the AWS accounts. The solutions architect configures AWS Organizations by sending an invitation to all member accounts of the company from a centralized management account. What should the solutions architect do next to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家大型薪资公司最近与一家小型人力资源公司合并。合并后的公司现在拥​有多个业务部门，每个部门都有自己的现有 AWS 账户。 解决方案架构师必须确保公司可以集中管理所有 AWS 账户的计费和访问策略。解决方案架构师通过从集中管理账户向公司的所有成 员账户发送邀请来配置 AWS Organizations。 解决方案架构师接下来应该做什么来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create the OrganizationAccountAccess IAM group in each member account. Include the necessary IAM roles for each administrator.","B":"Create the OrganizationAccountAccessPolicy IAM policy in each member account. Connect the member accounts to the management account by using cross-account access.","C":"Create the OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM role in each member account. Grant permission to the management account to assume the IAM role.","D":"Create the OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM role in the management account. Attach the AdministratorAccess AWS managed policy to the IAM role. Assign the IAM role to the administrators in each member account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个成员账户中创建 OrganizationAccountAccess IAM 组。包括每个管理员必需的 IAM 角色。","B":"在每个成员账户中创建 OrganizationAccountAccessPolicy IAM 策略。使用跨账户访问将成员账户连接到管理账户。","C":"在每个成员账户中创建 OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM 角色。向管理账户授予承担 IAM 角色的权限。","D":"在管理账户中创建 OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM 角色。将 AdministratorAccess AWS 托管策略附加到 IAM 角色。将 IAM 角 色分配给每个成员账户中的管理员。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":91},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"When member accounts are INVITED to join an AWS Organization (as opposed to being created by the organization), AWS does NOT automatically create the cross-account administrator role. The official AWS Organizations documentation explicitly states this and provides the exact remediation: in each invited member account, manually create an IAM role (recommended name OrganizationAccountAccessRole) with a trust policy that grants the management account permission to assume it, and attach the AdministratorAccess managed policy. Users/groups in the management account are then given sts:AssumeRole permission so they can centrally administer each member account. Option C captures this exactly: create the OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM role in each member account and grant the management account permission to assume it. Combined with consolidated billing (automatic in Organizations), this satisfies the requirement to centrally manage billing and access policies.","explanation_zh":"當成員帳戶被「邀請」加入 AWS Organization（而非由組織建立）時，AWS 不會自動建立跨帳戶管理員角色。官方 AWS Organizations 文件明確說明此情況並提供確切做法：在每個被邀請的成員帳戶中手動建立 IAM 角色（建議命名為 OrganizationAccountAccessRole），其信任政策授予管理帳戶 (management account) 假設此角色的權限，並附加 AdministratorAccess 受管政策。接著在管理帳戶中為使用者或群組授予 sts:AssumeRole 權限，即可集中管理各成員帳戶。選項 C 正是如此：在每個成員帳戶建立 OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM 角色，並授予管理帳戶假設該角色的權限。配合 Organizations 自動提供的合併帳單，即可滿足集中管理帳單與存取政策的需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Cross-account administration uses an IAM ROLE assumed via STS, not an IAM GROUP. Groups are containers for IAM users within a single account and cannot be assumed cross-account, so creating 'OrganizationAccountAccessGroup' in each member account does not enable the management account to access them.","why_zh":"跨帳戶管理是透過 STS 假設 IAM 角色 (role)，而非 IAM 群組 (group)。群組只是單一帳戶內 IAM 使用者的容器，無法被跨帳戶假設，因此在每個成員帳戶建立群組無法讓管理帳戶存取它們。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but is wrong. There is no 'OrganizationAccountAccessPolicy' IAM policy; the mechanism is a ROLE, not a standalone policy. A policy alone, without a role and trust relationship, does not establish cross-account access. The vague 'connect via cross-account access' restates the goal without the actual mechanism (the AssumeRole role).","why_zh":"這是 dump 建議答案但是錯誤的。並不存在名為 'OrganizationAccountAccessPolicy' 的 IAM 政策；正確機制是「角色」而非單獨的政策。僅有政策、沒有角色與信任關係，無法建立跨帳戶存取。'透過跨帳戶存取連接' 只是重述目標，並未說明真正的機制（AssumeRole 角色）。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The role must be created in each MEMBER account (the account being administered), not in the management account. The trust must point at the management account, and AdministratorAccess grants permissions WITHIN the member account. Creating the role in the management account and 'assigning it to administrators in each member account' inverts the trust direction and does not let the management account administer the members.","why_zh":"角色必須建立在每個「成員帳戶」（被管理的帳戶）中，而非管理帳戶中。信任關係應指向管理帳戶，AdministratorAccess 是授予在成員帳戶內的權限。在管理帳戶建立角色並 '指派給各成員帳戶的管理員' 顛倒了信任方向，無法讓管理帳戶管理成員帳戶。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_create-cross-account-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_access-cross-account-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_access.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":368,"question_en":"A company has application services that have been containerized and deployed on multiple Amazon EC2 instances with public IPs. An Apache Kafka cluster has been deployed to the EC2 instances. A PostgreSQL database has been migrated to Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL. The company expects a significant increase of orders on its platform when a new version of its ­agship product is released. What changes to the current architecture will reduce operational overhead and support the product release?","question_zh":"一家公司的应用程序服务已容器化并部署在具有公共 IP 的多个 Amazon EC2 实例上。Apache Kafka 集群已部署到 EC2 实例。 PostgreSQL 数据库已迁移到 Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL。该公司预计，当其旗舰产品新版本发布时，其平台上的订单将大幅增加。 当前架构的哪些变化将减少运营开销并支持产品发布？","options_en":{"A":"Create an EC2 Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer. Create additional read replicas for the DB instance. Create Amazon Kinesis data streams and configure the application services to use the data streams. Store and serve static content directly from Amazon S3.","B":"Create an EC2 Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer. Deploy the DB instance in Multi-AZ mode and enable storage auto scaling. Create Amazon Kinesis data streams and configure the application services to use the data streams. Store and serve static content directly from Amazon S3.","C":"Deploy the application on a Kubernetes cluster created on the EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer. Deploy the DB instance in Multi-AZ mode and enable storage auto scaling. Create an Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka cluster and configure the application services to use the cluster. Store static content in Amazon S3 behind an Amazon CloudFront distribution.","D":"Deploy the application on Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) with AWS Fargate and enable auto scaling behind an Application Load Balancer. Create additional read replicas for the DB instance. Create an Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka cluster and configure the application services to use the cluster. Store static content in Amazon S3 behind an Amazon CloudFront distribution."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Application Load Balancer 后面创建一个 EC2 Auto Scaling 组。为数据库实例创建额外的只读副本。创建 Amazon Kinesis 数据 流并配置应用程序服务以使用数据流。直接从 Amazon S3 存储和提供静态内容。","B":"在 Application Load Balancer 后面创建一个 EC2 Auto Scaling 组。以多可用区模式部署数据库实例并启用存储自动伸缩。创建 Amazon Kinesis 数据流并配置应用程序服务以使用数据流。直接从 Amazon S3 存储和提供静态内容。","C":"在应用程序负载均衡器后面的 EC2 实例上创建的 Kubernetes 集群上部署应用程序。以多可用区模式部署数据库实例并启用存 储自动伸缩。创建 Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka 集群并配置应用程序服务以使用该集群。将静态内容存储在 Amazon CloudFront 分配后面的 Amazon S3 中。","D":"使用 AWS Fargate 在 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 上部署应用程序，并在 Application Load Balancer 后面启用 自动扩展。为数据库实例创建额外的只读副本。创建 Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka 集群并配置应用程序服务以使 用该集群。将静态内容存储在 Amazon CloudFront 分配后面的 Amazon S3 中。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":91},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Analytics","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The qualifier is reduce operational overhead while supporting a product-launch traffic surge. Option D minimizes overhead across every layer without re-architecting the app: EKS with AWS Fargate gives a fully managed Kubernetes control plane plus serverless data plane, removing all EC2/node patching and capacity management (AWS docs: EKS lets you 'deploy applications faster with less operational overhead'); Amazon MSK is a fully managed, drop-in Kafka replacement so the existing Kafka-based services need no code changes (AWS docs: 'existing applications, tooling, and plugins... supported without requiring changes to application code'); RDS read replicas absorb the read-heavy order surge; and S3 behind CloudFront delivers and caches static content at scale. Options A and B force a Kafka-to-Kinesis rewrite (the opposite of reducing overhead and contradicting reuse of existing services) and keep raw EC2 management, while Option C runs self-managed Kubernetes on EC2, where you must operate the control plane and nodes yourself (high overhead). Only D reduces operational overhead on all fronts and supports the release.","explanation_zh":"本題關鍵限定詞是「降低運維負擔」並支撐新版產品上線帶來的流量暴增。選項 D 在不需重構應用程式的前提下,於各層級都把運維負擔降到最低:Amazon EKS 搭配 AWS Fargate 提供全託管的 Kubernetes 控制平面與無伺服器資料平面,免除所有 EC2/節點修補與容量管理(AWS 文件:EKS 讓你「以更少的運維負擔更快部署應用」);Amazon MSK 是全託管、可直接替換的 Kafka,既有以 Kafka 為基礎的服務無需修改程式碼(AWS 文件:「既有應用、工具與外掛...無需修改程式碼即可支援」);RDS read replicas 可吸收訂單暴增帶來的大量讀取;S3 搭配 CloudFront 可大規模交付並快取靜態內容。選項 A、B 強迫把 Kafka 改寫成 Kinesis(這反而增加負擔且與沿用既有服務相矛盾)且仍維持原始 EC2 管理;選項 C 在 EC2 上自管 Kubernetes,需自行運維控制平面與節點(運維負擔高)。只有 D 在所有層面都降低運維負擔並支撐上線。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Keeps containers on raw EC2 (manual orchestration/patching) and replaces Apache Kafka with Kinesis Data Streams, which requires re-writing the application's streaming code -- that increases, not reduces, operational overhead. Read replicas alone provide no HA failover and there is no storage auto scaling or CloudFront.","why_zh":"容器仍跑在原始 EC2 上(需手動編排與修補),且把 Apache Kafka 換成 Kinesis Data Streams 需重寫串流程式碼,反而增加運維負擔。僅有 read replicas 無法提供高可用故障轉移,也沒有儲存自動擴展或 CloudFront。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same fundamental flaw as A: forces a Kafka-to-Kinesis application rewrite and keeps self-managed EC2 for containers. Although Multi-AZ and storage auto scaling improve the DB, it still lacks CloudFront and does not reduce the compute/streaming operational overhead.","why_zh":"與 A 同樣的根本缺陷:強迫把 Kafka 改寫為 Kinesis,且容器仍由自管 EC2 承載。雖然 Multi-AZ 與儲存自動擴展改善了資料庫,但仍缺 CloudFront,且未降低運算/串流層的運維負擔。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Self-managed Kubernetes on EC2 means the company operates the control plane, master/worker nodes, and upgrades itself -- high operational overhead, the opposite of the goal. MSK and S3+CloudFront are good, but the compute layer choice disqualifies it versus managed EKS+Fargate.","why_zh":"在 EC2 上自管 Kubernetes 代表公司要自行運維控制平面、主/工作節點與升級,運維負擔高,與目標相反。MSK 與 S3+CloudFront 雖佳,但運算層的選擇使其不如全託管的 EKS+Fargate。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/what-is-eks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/msk/latest/developerguide/what-is-msk.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/fargate.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":369,"question_en":"A company hosts a VPN in an on-premises data center. Employees currently connect to the VPN to access files in their Windows home directories. Recently, there has been a large growth in the number of employees who work remotely. As a result, bandwidth usage for connections into the data center has begun to reach 100% during business hours. The company must design a solution on AWS that will support the growth of the company's remote workforce, reduce the bandwidth usage for connections into the data center, and reduce operational overhead. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司在本地数据中心托管 VPN。员工当前连接到 VPN 以访问其 Windows 主目录中的文件。最近，远程工作的员工数量大幅增 长。因此，在工作时间内连接到数据中心的带宽使用率已开始达到 100%。 该公司必须在 AWS 上设计一个解决方案，以支持公司远程员工的增长，减少连接数据中心的带宽使用量，并降低运营开销。 哪种步骤组合能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Storage Gateway Volume Gateway. Mount a volume from the Volume Gateway to the on-premises file server.","B":"Migrate the home directories to Amazon FSx for Windows File Server.","C":"Migrate the home directories to Amazon FSx for Lustre.","D":"Migrate remote users to AWS Client VPN.","E":"Create an AWS Direct Connect connection from the on-premises data center to AWS."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 AWS Storage Gateway 卷网关。将卷从卷网关装载到本地文件服务器。","B":"将主目录迁移到 Amazon FSx for Windows File Server。","C":"将主目录迁移到 Amazon FSx for Lustre。","D":"将远程用户迁移到 AWS 客户端 VPN。","E":"创建从本地数据中心到 AWS 的 AWS Direct Connect 连接。"},"answer":["B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BD":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The bandwidth bottleneck exists because Windows home directories live in the on-premises data center and every remote employee tunnels through the on-premises VPN to reach them. The fix is to remove the data center from the file-access path entirely. Option B migrates the home directories to Amazon FSx for Windows File Server, a fully managed native Windows/SMB file service with Active Directory integration that AWS docs explicitly list 'home directories' as an ideal use case for; this relocates the files into AWS so traffic no longer flows into the data center. Option D moves remote users to AWS Client VPN, a fully managed, elastically scaling client VPN that terminates in the VPC where FSx resides, so remote-user file access goes user -> Client VPN -> FSx and never touches the data center. Together B+D meet all goals (scale, reduced data-center bandwidth, least operational overhead) because both services are fully managed. Option E (Direct Connect) is wrong: a dedicated circuit from the data center to AWS does not help remote users (who connect over the internet/VPN), takes weeks to provision and adds operational/physical overhead, and once files are in FSx the data center is no longer in the path, so DX solves nothing. The dump's B+E pairing is internally inconsistent.","explanation_zh":"頻寬瓶頸的根因是 Windows home directories 存放在地端資料中心，所有遠端員工都透過地端 VPN 連入存取，因而塞滿進入資料中心的頻寬。正解是把資料中心徹底移出檔案存取路徑。選項 B 將 home directories 遷移到 Amazon FSx for Windows File Server，這是完全受管、原生 Windows/SMB、整合 Active Directory 的檔案服務，AWS 文件明確將 'home directories' 列為其理想使用情境；檔案搬到 AWS 後，流量就不再進入地端資料中心。選項 D 將遠端使用者改用 AWS Client VPN，這是完全受管、可彈性自動擴展的用戶端 VPN，終結點位於 FSx 所在的 VPC，遠端存取路徑變成 使用者 -> Client VPN -> FSx，完全不經過資料中心。B+D 同時滿足擴展性、降低資料中心頻寬與最低營運負擔，因為兩者都是完全受管服務。選項 E（Direct Connect）錯誤：從資料中心到 AWS 的專線對透過網際網路/VPN 連線的遠端使用者毫無幫助，佈建需數週並增加營運與實體負擔；且檔案搬到 FSx 後資料中心已不在路徑上，DX 無法解決問題。Dump 的 B+E 組合在邏輯上自相矛盾。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Storage Gateway Volume Gateway provides iSCSI block volumes backed by S3 to an on-premises server; it keeps the file server in the data center, so remote users still tunnel through the on-prem VPN and the data-center bandwidth problem is unchanged. It is also not native Windows/SMB home-directory storage.","why_zh":"Storage Gateway Volume Gateway 提供以 S3 為後端的 iSCSI 區塊磁碟給地端伺服器；檔案伺服器仍留在資料中心，遠端使用者仍需經地端 VPN，資料中心頻寬問題未解。它也不是原生 Windows/SMB 的 home directory 儲存。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon FSx for Lustre is a high-performance file system for HPC/ML/analytics workloads using the Lustre/POSIX interface, not SMB. It does not natively serve Windows home directories or integrate with AD for SMB shares, so it is the wrong FSx variant.","why_zh":"Amazon FSx for Lustre 是供 HPC/ML/分析等高效能工作負載使用的 Lustre/POSIX 檔案系統，而非 SMB。它無法原生提供 Windows home directories 或整合 AD 的 SMB 共用，因此是錯誤的 FSx 類型。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Direct Connect is a dedicated link from the data center to AWS; it does nothing for remote users who connect over the internet, requires weeks of provisioning and adds physical/operational overhead. After files move to FSx the data center is out of the path, so DX neither reduces data-center bandwidth for remote users nor lowers operational overhead.","why_zh":"Direct Connect 是資料中心到 AWS 的專線；對透過網際網路連線的遠端使用者毫無作用，佈建需數週並增加實體與營運負擔。檔案搬到 FSx 後資料中心已不在路徑上，DX 既無法為遠端使用者降低資料中心頻寬，也無法降低營運負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/WindowsGuide/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/WindowsGuide/migrate-files-fsx.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":370,"question_en":"A company has multiple AWS accounts. The company recently had a security audit that revealed many unencrypted Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes attached to Amazon EC2 instances. A solutions architect must encrypt the unencrypted volumes and ensure that unencrypted volumes will be detected automatically in the future. Additionally, the company wants a solution that can centrally manage multiple AWS accounts with a focus on compliance and security. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司拥有多个 AWS 账户。该公司最近进行了一次安全审计，发现许多附加到 Amazon EC2 实例的未加密 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 卷。 解决方案架构师必须对未加密的卷进行加密，并确保将来能够自动检测到未加密的卷。此外，该公司希望有一个解决方案能够集中 管理多个 AWS 账户，并重点关注合规性和安全性。 解决方案架构师应该采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an organization in AWS Organizations. Set up AWS Control Tower, and turn on the strongly recommended controls (guardrails). Join all accounts to the organization. Categorize the AWS accounts into OUs.","B":"Use the AWS CLI to list all the unencrypted volumes in all the AWS accounts. Run a script to encrypt all the unencrypted volumes in place.","C":"Create a snapshot of each unencrypted volume. Create a new encrypted volume from the unencrypted snapshot. Detach the existing volume, and replace it with the encrypted volume.","D":"Create an organization in AWS Organizations. Set up AWS Control Tower, and turn on the mandatory controls (guardrails). Join all accounts to the organization. Categorize the AWS accounts into OUs.","E":"Turn on AWS CloudTrail. Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to detect and automatically encrypt unencrypted volumes."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS Organizations 中创建一个组织。设置 AWS Control Tower，并打开强烈推荐的控件（护栏）。将所有帐户加入组织。将 AWS 账户分类为 OU。","B":"使用 AWS CLI 列出所有 AWS 账户中的所有未加密卷。运行脚本以加密所有未加密的卷。","C":"创建每个未加密卷的快照。从未加密的快照创建新的加密卷。分离现有卷，并将其替换为加密卷。","D":"在 AWS Organizations 中创建组织。设置 AWS Control Tower，并启用强制控制（护栏）。将所有帐户加入组织。将 AWS 账户分 类为 OU。","E":"打开 AWS CloudTrail。配置 Amazon EventBridge 规则以检测并自动加密未加密的卷。"},"answer":["C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AC":83,"AE":17},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Two requirements must both be met: (1) encrypt the existing unencrypted EBS volumes, and (2) automatically detect unencrypted volumes in the future while centrally governing multiple accounts. For (1), AWS EBS documentation is explicit: 'You can't directly encrypt existing unencrypted volumes or snapshots. To encrypt an unencrypted volume, create a snapshot of that volume, and then use the snapshot to create a new encrypted volume.' That is exactly Option C (snapshot the volume, create an encrypted volume from the snapshot, detach and replace). For (2), AWS Control Tower provides the central multi-account governance with a compliance/security focus, and the control that detects unencrypted attached EBS volumes is 'Detect Whether Encryption is Enabled for Amazon EBS Volumes Attached to Amazon EC2 Instances' (backed by the ENCRYPTED_VOLUMES Config rule). AWS documentation classifies this as a detective control with STRONGLY RECOMMENDED guidance that is not enabled by default, so Option A (turn on the strongly recommended controls) is required. Option D is wrong because mandatory controls only protect Control Tower's own resources (CloudTrail config/log buckets, Config recorder, SNS) and cannot be deactivated; they do NOT include EBS encryption detection. Thus the correct pair is A + C.","explanation_zh":"本題需同時滿足兩項需求:(1) 加密既有未加密的 EBS volumes,(2) 未來能自動偵測未加密 volumes,並以合規與安全為重點集中管理多個帳戶。對於 (1),AWS EBS 文件明確指出:無法直接就地加密既有的未加密 volume 或 snapshot,必須先對 volume 建立 snapshot,再用該 snapshot 建立新的加密 volume,然後卸載並替換原 volume,這正是選項 C。對於 (2),AWS Control Tower 提供以合規與安全為重點的多帳戶集中治理,而偵測未加密附掛 EBS volume 的控制項為 'Detect Whether Encryption is Enabled for Amazon EBS Volumes Attached to Amazon EC2 Instances'(以 ENCRYPTED_VOLUMES Config rule 實作)。AWS 文件將其歸類為具 STRONGLY RECOMMENDED(強烈建議)指引的偵測型控制項,且預設未啟用,因此需要選項 A(開啟強烈建議的控制項)。選項 D 錯誤,因為 mandatory(強制)控制項僅保護 Control Tower 自身資源(CloudTrail/Config/log buckets、Config recorder、SNS)且無法停用,並不包含 EBS 加密偵測。故正確組合為 A + C。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS explicitly states you cannot encrypt an existing EBS volume in place: 'You can't directly encrypt existing unencrypted volumes or snapshots.' There is no API to encrypt a volume in place, so a script that 'encrypts unencrypted volumes in place' is technically impossible.","why_zh":"AWS 明確指出無法就地加密既有 EBS volume:『You can't directly encrypt existing unencrypted volumes or snapshots.』並無就地加密 volume 的 API,故『就地加密』的腳本在技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Mandatory controls in Control Tower only protect Control Tower's own resources (CloudTrail, Config recorder, log S3 buckets, SNS) and cannot be deactivated. The EBS-volume-encryption detection control is classified as a STRONGLY RECOMMENDED detective control, not a mandatory one, so turning on mandatory controls does not detect unencrypted EBS volumes.","why_zh":"Control Tower 的 mandatory 控制項僅保護 Control Tower 自身資源(CloudTrail、Config recorder、log S3 buckets、SNS)且無法停用。偵測 EBS volume 加密的控制項被歸類為 STRONGLY RECOMMENDED 偵測型控制項,而非 mandatory,故開啟 mandatory 控制項無法偵測未加密的 EBS volume。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"CloudTrail + an EventBridge rule does not provide a managed, multi-account compliance dashboard, and there is no clean event signal for 'volume is unencrypted'; building auto-encryption via EventBridge is custom, high-overhead, and does not deliver the central multi-account governance the question requires. AWS Control Tower (with the strongly recommended controls) is the intended managed solution.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 加 EventBridge 規則無法提供受管的多帳戶合規儀表板,且沒有乾淨的『volume 未加密』事件訊號;以 EventBridge 自建自動加密屬於高維運負擔的客製方案,也無法達成題目要求的多帳戶集中治理。AWS Control Tower(搭配強烈建議控制項)才是預期的受管解決方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ebs/latest/userguide/ebs-encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/strongly-recommended-detective-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/detective-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/mandatory-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/what-is-control-tower.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・複選"},{"id":371,"question_en":"A company hosts an intranet web application on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Currently, users authenticate to the application against an internal user database. The company needs to authenticate users to the application by using an existing AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory directory. All users with accounts in the directory must have access to the application. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面的 Amazon EC2 实例上托管一个 Intranet Web 应用程序。目前，用户根据内部用户数据库 向应用程序进行身份验证。 该公司需要使用现有的 AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory 目录对应用程序的用户进行身份验证。目录中拥有帐户的所 有用户都必须有权访问该应用程序。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new app client in the directory. Create a listener rule for the ALB. Specify the authenticate-oidc action for the listener rule. Configure the listener rule with the appropriate issuer, client ID and secret, and endpoint details for the Active Directory service. Configure the new app client with the callback URL that the ALB provides.","B":"Configure an Amazon Cognito user pool. Configure the user pool with a federated identity provider (ldP) that has metadata from the directory. Create an app client. Associate the app client with the user pool. Create a listener rule for the ALSpecify the authenticate- cognito action for the listener rule. Configure the listener rule to use the user pool and app client.","C":"Add the directory as a new IAM identity provider (ldP). Create a new IAM role that has an entity type of SAML 2.0 federation. Configure a role policy that allows access to the ALB. Configure the new role as the default authenticated user role for the ldP. Create a listener rule for the ALB. Specify the authenticate-oidc action for the listener rule.","D":"Enable AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On). Configure the directory as an external identity provider (ldP) that uses SAML. Use the automatic provisioning method. Create a new IAM role that has an entity type of SAML 2.0 federation. Configure a role policy that allows access to the ALB. Attach the new role to all groups. Create a listener rule for the ALB. Specify the authenticate-cognito action for the listener rule."},"options_zh":{"A":"在目录中创建一个新的应用程序客户端。为 ALB 创建侦听器规则。为侦听器规则指定authenticate-oidc 操作。使用适当的颁发 者、客户端 ID 和密钥以及 Active Directory 服务的端点详细信息配置侦听器规则。使用 ALB 提供的回调 URL 配置新的应用程序客 户端。","B":"配置 Amazon Cognito 用户池。使用具有目录中元数据的联合身份提供程序 (ldP) 配置用户池。创建应用程序客户端。将应用程 序客户端与用户池关联。为 AL 创建侦听器规则为侦听器规则指定authenticate-cognito 操作。配置侦听器规则以使用用户池和应 用程序客户端。","C":"添加目录作为新的 IAM 身份提供商 (ldP)。创建一个具有 SAML 2.0 联合实体类型的新 IAM 角色。配置允许访问 ALB 的角色策 略。将新角色配置为 ldP 的默认经过身份验证的用户角色。为 ALB 创建侦听器规则。为侦听器规则指定authenticate-oidc 操作。","D":"启用 AWS IAM Identity Center（AW​S 单点登录）。将目录配置为使用 SAML 的外部身份提供商 (ldP)。使用自动配置方法。创建 一个具有 SAML 2.0 联合实体类型的新 IAM 角色。配置允许访问 ALB 的角色策略。将新角色附加到所有组。为 ALB 创建侦听器规 则。指定侦听器规则的authenticate-cognito 操作。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":61,"D":31},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"An Application Load Balancer can natively authenticate users with only two listener actions: authenticate-oidc (for a directly OIDC-compliant IdP) and authenticate-cognito (for an Amazon Cognito user pool). The AWS ALB user-authentication documentation explicitly lists the supported use case: 'Authenticate users through corporate identities, using SAML, OpenID Connect (OIDC), or OAuth, through the user pools supported by Amazon Cognito.' AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory is not itself an OIDC provider, so it cannot be wired directly to the ALB. The documented pattern is to create a Cognito user pool, configure the directory as a federated SAML identity provider (using the directory's SAML metadata, typically via AD FS or IAM Identity Center as the SAML IdP), create an app client, and then use the authenticate-cognito action on the ALB listener rule pointing at that user pool and app client. That is exactly Option B, so all directory users gain access to the intranet app.","explanation_zh":"Application Load Balancer 原生只支援兩種驗證 listener action：authenticate-oidc（用於直接符合 OIDC 的 IdP）與 authenticate-cognito（用於 Amazon Cognito user pool）。AWS ALB 使用者驗證文件明確列出支援情境：透過 Amazon Cognito user pool，使用 SAML、OIDC 或 OAuth 來驗證企業身分。AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory 本身不是 OIDC 供應商，無法直接接到 ALB。文件化的正確做法是：建立 Cognito user pool，將該目錄設定為 federated SAML identity provider（使用目錄的 SAML metadata，通常經由 AD FS 或 IAM Identity Center 作為 SAML IdP），建立 app client，然後在 ALB listener rule 上使用 authenticate-cognito action 指向該 user pool 與 app client。這正是選項 B，因此目錄中所有使用者皆可存取此 intranet 應用程式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory is not an OIDC provider. You cannot create an 'app client in the directory' with an OIDC issuer, client ID/secret and authorization/token/userinfo endpoints. authenticate-oidc requires a publicly resolvable, OIDC-compliant IdP, which AD does not expose directly; a Cognito user pool is needed to bridge SAML AD to the ALB.","why_zh":"AWS Managed Microsoft AD 不是 OIDC 供應商，無法在目錄中建立帶有 OIDC issuer、client ID/secret 及 authorization/token/userinfo 端點的 app client。authenticate-oidc 需要可公開解析且符合 OIDC 的 IdP，而 AD 並不直接提供，需要 Cognito user pool 作為橋接。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"IAM SAML identity providers and IAM roles (entity type SAML 2.0 federation) grant federated access to AWS APIs/console resources, not to an intranet web application behind an ALB. ALB does not authenticate end users via IAM IdPs or IAM roles, and authenticate-oidc cannot reference an IAM identity provider. The components do not fit ALB user authentication.","why_zh":"IAM SAML identity provider 與 IAM role（SAML 2.0 federation 實體類型）是授予對 AWS API/主控台資源的聯合存取，並非對 ALB 後方的 intranet 網頁應用。ALB 不會透過 IAM IdP 或 IAM role 驗證終端使用者，且 authenticate-oidc 無法參照 IAM identity provider，元件不適用於 ALB 使用者驗證。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This option mixes IAM Identity Center SAML federation with IAM roles for AWS resource access (not application user auth) and then incorrectly specifies authenticate-cognito without ever creating a Cognito user pool or app client for the listener to reference. The pieces are internally inconsistent and do not enable ALB-based user authentication for the web app.","why_zh":"此選項混用 IAM Identity Center SAML 聯合與 IAM role（用於 AWS 資源存取，而非應用程式使用者驗證），又錯誤地指定 authenticate-cognito 卻完全沒有建立 Cognito user pool 或 app client 供 listener 參照。各元件彼此矛盾，無法為網頁應用啟用以 ALB 為基礎的使用者驗證。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/listener-authenticate-users.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/cognito-user-pools-saml-idp.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/cognito-user-pools-managing-saml-idp.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":372,"question_en":"A company has a website that serves many visitors. The company deploys a backend service for the website in a primary AWS Region and a disaster recovery (DR) Region. A single Amazon CloudFront distribution is deployed for the website. The company creates an Amazon Route 53 record set with health checks and a failover routing policy for the primary Region’s backend service. The company configures the Route 53 record set as an origin for the CloudFront distribution. The company configures another record set that points to the backend service's endpoint in the DR Region as a secondary failover record type. The TTL for both record sets is 60 seconds. Currently, failover takes more than 1 minute. A solutions architect must design a solution that will provide the fastest failover time. Which solution will achieve this goal?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个为许多访问者提供服务的网站。该公司在主要 AWS 区域和灾难恢复 (DR) 区域中为网站部署了后端服务。 为网站部署了单个 Amazon CloudFront 发行版。该公司创建了一个 Amazon Route 53 记录集，其中包含主要区域后端服务的运行状况 检查和故障转移路由策略。该公司将 Route 53 记录集配置为 CloudFront 分配的源。该公司配置了另一个记录集，该记录集指向 DR 区域中的后端服务端点作为辅助故障转移记录类型。两个记录集的 TTL 均为 60 秒。 目前，故障转移需要 1 分钟以上。解决方案架构师必须设计一个能够提供最快故障转移时间的解决方案。 哪种解决方案将实现这一目标？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an additional CloudFront distribution. Create a new Route 53 failover record set with health checks for both CloudFront distributions.","B":"Set the TTL to 4 second for the existing Route 53 record sets that are used for the backend service in each Region.","C":"Create new record sets for the backend services by using a latency routing policy. Use the record sets as an origin in the CloudFront distribution.","D":"Create a CloudFront origin group that includes two origins, one for each backend service Region. Configure origin failover as a cache behavior for the CloudFront distribution."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署额外的 CloudFront 发行版。创建一个新的 Route 53 故障转移记录集，并对两个 CloudFront 分配进行运行状况检查。","B":"将每个区域中用于后端服务的现有 Route 53 记录集的 TTL 设置为 4 秒。","C":"使用延迟路由策略为后端服务创建新的记录集。使用记录集作为 CloudFront 分配中的源。","D":"创建一个 CloudFront 源组，其中包含两个源，每个后端服务区域一个。将源故障转移配置为 CloudFront 分配的缓存行为。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The fastest failover is achieved by using CloudFront's native origin failover. You create a distribution with two origins (one per backend Region), group them into an origin group with a primary and secondary, and assign that origin group to a cache behavior. CloudFront then fails over per request, entirely at the edge: when the primary origin returns a configured failure status code, fails to connect, or times out, CloudFront immediately routes the request to the secondary origin. This avoids DNS-based detection latency altogether. Crucially, this approach eliminates the dependency on Route 53 health checks and DNS TTL propagation, both of which add minutes to failover. Origin connection timeout (1-10s) and connection attempts (1-3) are tunable, so failover can occur within seconds. Option B (lowering TTL) is wrong because failover time is dominated by Route 53 health-check detection latency (health-check interval times the failure threshold, minimum ~30s for fast 10-second checks times 3), not just TTL, and Route 53 does not honor an arbitrarily tiny 4-second TTL for this design; lowering TTL alone cannot beat the inherent DNS health-check detection delay.","explanation_zh":"最快的故障轉移是透過 CloudFront 原生的 origin failover 達成。建立一個含有兩個 origin（每個後端 Region 各一個）的 distribution，將兩者組成一個 origin group 並指定主要與次要 origin，再把該 origin group 指派給某個 cache behavior。CloudFront 會在 edge 端以每個請求為單位進行故障轉移：當主要 origin 回傳已設定的失敗狀態碼、連線失敗或逾時時，CloudFront 會立即將請求路由至次要 origin，完全避免 DNS 偵測延遲。這個方法消除了對 Route 53 health check 與 DNS TTL 傳播的依賴，而這兩者都會使故障轉移延遲數分鐘。Origin connection timeout（1-10 秒）與 connection attempts（1-3 次）皆可調整，因此故障轉移可在數秒內完成。選項 B（降低 TTL）錯誤，因為故障轉移時間主要由 Route 53 health check 的偵測延遲決定（health check 間隔乘以失敗門檻，使用快速 10 秒檢查時最少約為 30 秒乘以 3 次），而非僅僅是 TTL；且 Route 53 並不會對此設計採用任意極小的 4 秒 TTL，僅降低 TTL 無法克服 DNS health check 固有的偵測延遲。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Two CloudFront distributions with a Route 53 failover record between them still relies on DNS health-check detection plus TTL propagation, which is exactly the slow mechanism the question wants to replace; it adds complexity without reducing failover time.","why_zh":"兩個 CloudFront distribution 之間以 Route 53 failover 紀錄切換，仍依賴 DNS health check 偵測加上 TTL 傳播，正是題目想取代的慢速機制；它只增加複雜度而未縮短故障轉移時間。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Lowering TTL does not address the dominant delay, which is Route 53 health-check detection latency (interval times failure threshold). Failover would still exceed a minute, and Route 53 does not effectively honor a 4-second TTL for this failover-over-CloudFront design.","why_zh":"降低 TTL 並未解決主要延遲來源，即 Route 53 health check 偵測延遲（間隔乘以失敗門檻）。故障轉移仍會超過一分鐘，且 Route 53 對此種透過 CloudFront 的故障轉移設計不會真正採用 4 秒 TTL。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Latency routing policy chooses the lowest-latency Region for performance; it is not a failover mechanism and would not provide faster, deterministic disaster-recovery failover. It also still relies on DNS resolution and TTL.","why_zh":"Latency 路由政策是為了效能選擇延遲最低的 Region，並非故障轉移機制，無法提供更快且確定性的災難復原切換。它同樣仍依賴 DNS 解析與 TTL。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/high_availability_origin_failover.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":373,"question_en":"A company is using multiple AWS accounts and has multiple DevOps teams running production and non-production workloads in these accounts. The company would like to centrally-restrict access to some of the AWS services that the DevOps teams do not use. The company decided to use AWS Organizations and successfully invited all AWS accounts into the Organization. They would like to allow access to services that are currently in-use and deny a few specific services. Also they would like to administer multiple accounts together as a single unit. What combination of steps should the solutions architect take to satisfy these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用多个 AWS 账户，并拥有多个开发运营团队在这些账户中运行生产和非生产工作负载。该公司希望集中限制对 DevOps 团队不使用的一些 AWS 服务的访问。该公司决定使用 AWS Organizations 并成功邀请所有 AWS 账户加入该组织。他们希望允许访问 当前正在使用的服务并拒绝一些特定服务。他们还希望将多个帐户作为一个整体进行管理。 解决方案架构师应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use a Deny list strategy.","B":"Review the Access Advisor in AWS IAM to determine services recently used","C":"Review the AWS Trusted Advisor report to determine services recently used.","D":"Remove the default FullAWSAccess SCP.","E":"Define organizational units (OUs) and place the member accounts in the OUs.","F":"Remove the default DenyAWSAccess SCP."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用拒绝列表策略。","B":"查看 AWS IAM 中的访问顾问以确定最近使用的服务","C":"查看 AWS Trusted Advisor 报告以确定最近使用的服务。","D":"删除默认的 FullAWSAccess SCP。","E":"定义组织单位 (OU) 并将成员帐户放置在 OU 中。","F":"删除默认的 DenyAWSAccess SCP。"},"answer":["C","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ABE":93},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The company wants to keep all currently-used services working while denying a few specific services, identify which services are actually used, and administer multiple accounts as a single unit. (A) A Deny list strategy is correct: you keep the default FullAWSAccess SCP (which allows everything) and add explicit Deny statements only for the few unwanted services, so all in-use services keep working with minimal effort. (B) IAM Access Advisor (service last accessed data) is the official tool AWS recommends to determine which services have recently been used so you can refine SCPs. (E) Organizational units (OUs) let you group member accounts and administer them together as a single unit by attaching policies at the OU level. The dump answer C/D/F is wrong: AWS Trusted Advisor reports cost/security/performance/limits, not which services were recently used; removing FullAWSAccess (D) is the start of an allow-list strategy and would break all currently-used services (deny-by-default), contradicting the requirement; and there is no default 'DenyAWSAccess' SCP (F is fabricated).","explanation_zh":"公司希望保持目前正在使用的所有服務正常運作、僅拒絕少數特定服務、找出實際使用的服務，並將多個帳戶當作單一單元一起管理。(A) Deny list 策略正確：保留預設的 FullAWSAccess SCP（允許所有服務），僅針對少數不需要的服務加入明確的 Deny 陳述，因此所有使用中的服務都能持續運作且工作量最少。(B) IAM Access Advisor（service last accessed data）是 AWS 官方建議用來判斷近期使用了哪些服務以便調整 SCP 的工具。(E) Organizational units (OUs) 可將成員帳戶分組，並在 OU 層級附加政策，把多個帳戶當作單一單元一起管理。題庫答案 C/D/F 錯誤：AWS Trusted Advisor 報告的是成本/安全/效能/配額，而非近期使用了哪些服務；移除 FullAWSAccess (D) 是 allow-list 策略的起點，會因 deny-by-default 而封鎖所有使用中的服務，與需求矛盾；且根本不存在預設的 'DenyAWSAccess' SCP（F 為虛構）。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Trusted Advisor provides cost optimization, security, performance, fault tolerance, and service-limit checks. It does NOT report which AWS services have recently been used. IAM Access Advisor / service last accessed data is the correct tool for that.","why_zh":"AWS Trusted Advisor 提供成本最佳化、安全、效能、容錯與服務配額檢查，並不會報告近期使用了哪些 AWS 服務。要查近期使用的服務應使用 IAM Access Advisor / service last accessed data。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Removing the default FullAWSAccess SCP is the first step of an allow-list strategy. Because SCPs are deny-by-default, removing it without replacement blocks all actions, breaking the currently-used services the company wants to keep. A deny-list strategy keeps FullAWSAccess and adds Deny statements.","why_zh":"移除預設的 FullAWSAccess SCP 是 allow-list 策略的第一步。由於 SCP 採 deny-by-default，移除後若不替換會封鎖所有動作，破壞公司想保留的使用中服務。Deny list 策略應保留 FullAWSAccess 並加入 Deny 陳述。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"There is no default 'DenyAWSAccess' SCP in AWS Organizations. The only AWS-managed default SCP is FullAWSAccess. This option is fabricated.","why_zh":"AWS Organizations 中並不存在預設的 'DenyAWSAccess' SCP。唯一的 AWS 受管預設 SCP 是 FullAWSAccess。此選項為虛構。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_access-advisor.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_last-accessed-view-data-orgs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_ous.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":374,"question_en":"A live-events company is designing a scaling solution for its ticket application on AWS. The application has high peaks of utilization during sale events. Each sale event is a one-time event that is scheduled. The application runs on Amazon EC2 instances that are in an Auto Scaling group. The application uses PostgreSQL for the database layer. The company needs a scaling solution to maximize availability during the sale events. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家现场活动公司正在为其 AWS 上的门票应用程序设计扩展解决方案。该应用程序在促销活动期间的利用率很高。每个销售活动都 是预定的一次性活动。该应用程序在 Auto Scaling 组中的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。该应用程序使用 PostgreSQL 作为数据库层。 该公司需要一个扩展解决方案，以最大限度地提高销售活动期间的可用性。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use a predictive scaling policy for the EC2 instances. Host the database on an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL Serverless v2 Multi-AZ DB instance with automatically scaling read replicas. Create an AWS Step Functions state machine to run parallel AWS Lambda functions to pre-warm the database before a sale event. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the state machine.","B":"Use a scheduled scaling policy for the EC2 instances. Host the database on an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL Mulli-AZ DB instance with automatically scaling read replicas. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes an AWS Lambda function to create a larger read replica before a sale event. Fail over to the larger read replica. Create another EventBridge rule that invokes another Lambda function to scale down the read replica after the sale event.","C":"Use a predictive scaling policy for the EC2 instances. Host the database on an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL MultiAZ DB instance with automatically scaling read replicas. Create an AWS Step Functions state machine to run parallel AWS Lambda functions to pre-warm the database before a sale event. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the state machine.","D":"Use a scheduled scaling policy for the EC2 instances. Host the database on an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL Multi-AZ DB cluster. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes an AWS Lambda function to create a larger Aurora Replica before a sale event. Fail over to the larger Aurora Replica. Create another EventBridge rule that invokes another Lambda function to scale down the Aurora Replica after the sale event."},"options_zh":{"A":"对 EC2 实例使用预测扩展策略。将数据库托管在具有自动扩展只读副本功能的 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL Serverless v2 多可用 区数据库实例上。创建 AWS Step Functions 状态机来运行并行 AWS Lambda 函数，以便在销售活动之前预热数据库。创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则以调用状态机。","B":"对 EC2 实例使用计划的扩展策略。将数据库托管在具有自动扩展只读副本功能的 Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL 多可用区数据库 实例上。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则调用 AWS Lambda 函数以在促销活动之前创建更大的只读副本。故障转移到 更大的只读副本。创建另一个 EventBridge 规则，该规则调用另一个 Lambda 函数以在销售事件后缩减只读副本。","C":"对 EC2 实例使用预测扩展策略。将数据库托管在 Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL 多可用区数据库实例上，并自动扩展只读副本。 创建 AWS Step Functions 状态机来运行并行 AWS Lambda 函数，以便在销售活动之前预热数据库。创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则 以调用状态机。","D":"对 EC2 实例使用计划的扩展策略。将数据库托管在 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL 多可用区数据库集群上。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则调用 AWS Lambda 函数以在促销活动之前创建更大的 Aurora 副本。故障转移到更大的 Aurora 副本。创 建另一个 EventBridge 规则，该规则调用另一个 Lambda 函数以在促销活动结束后缩小 Aurora 副本的规模。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Two qualifiers decide this: the events are one-time scheduled events, and the goal is to maximize availability. Predictive scaling needs at least 24 hours of history and only works for workloads with recurring day-of-week/time-of-day patterns, so it cannot forecast a one-time event; this eliminates A and C. Scheduled scaling is the documented method for when you know exactly when to add capacity, so B and D are the candidates. The database tiebreaker favors D: Aurora Replicas share a single cluster storage volume with sub-100ms replica lag, and failover to a larger Aurora Replica (promoting a reader to writer) is a clean, fast, lossless operation built for high availability. In B, RDS for PostgreSQL read replicas use asynchronous native PostgreSQL replication; 'failing over' to one actually requires promotion, which the docs state is irreversible and stops WAL replication from the source, creating a split-brain/orphaned-writer situation rather than a clean failover. Therefore D (scheduled scaling + Aurora Multi-AZ cluster with a pre-created larger Aurora Replica) best maximizes availability.","explanation_zh":"兩個關鍵限定詞決定答案：銷售活動是一次性且已排程的事件，且目標是在活動期間最大化可用性。Predictive scaling 需要至少 24 小時的歷史資料，且僅適用於具有每週/每日重複模式的工作負載，無法預測一次性事件，因此排除 A 與 C。Scheduled scaling 是當你確切知道何時需要增加容量時的官方建議方法，所以 B 與 D 為候選。資料庫層面由 D 勝出：Aurora Replicas 共用單一叢集儲存磁碟區，replica lag 通常小於 100 毫秒，且故障轉移到較大的 Aurora Replica（將 reader 提升為 writer）是專為高可用性設計的乾淨、快速且不丟失資料的操作。在 B 中，RDS for PostgreSQL read replica 使用非同步的 PostgreSQL 原生複製；對其進行所謂的「故障轉移」實際上需要 promote，而官方文件指出此操作不可逆且會停止從來源接收 WAL，造成 split-brain／孤立 writer，而非乾淨的故障轉移。因此 D（scheduled scaling + Aurora Multi-AZ 叢集搭配預先建立的較大 Aurora Replica）最能最大化可用性。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses predictive scaling, which requires 24+ hours of history and recurring day/time load patterns; a one-time scheduled sale event has no recurring pattern, so predictive scaling cannot forecast it. The Aurora Serverless v2 'Multi-AZ DB instance' wording is also imprecise (Aurora is a cluster), and pre-warming via parallel Lambda is unnecessary overhead.","why_zh":"使用 predictive scaling，需要 24 小時以上的歷史資料與重複的每日/時段負載模式；一次性排程的銷售活動沒有重複模式，predictive scaling 無法預測。Aurora Serverless v2「Multi-AZ DB instance」用詞也不精確（Aurora 是 cluster），且以平行 Lambda 預熱屬於不必要的額外負擔。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Scheduled scaling is correct, but 'fail over to the larger read replica' in RDS for PostgreSQL actually means promoting the replica, which per AWS docs is irreversible and stops WAL replication from the source. This breaks replication and creates an orphaned/split writer rather than a clean HA failover, and RDS native replication is asynchronous with lag, so it does not maximize availability.","why_zh":"Scheduled scaling 正確，但在 RDS for PostgreSQL 中「故障轉移到較大的 read replica」實際上是 promote replica，根據 AWS 文件此操作不可逆且會停止從來源接收 WAL。這會中斷複製並產生孤立／分裂的 writer，而非乾淨的高可用故障轉移，加上 RDS 原生複製為非同步且有延遲，無法最大化可用性。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Same predictive-scaling problem as A: a one-time scheduled event lacks the recurring pattern and historical data predictive scaling needs. Also uses RDS for PostgreSQL rather than Aurora's shared-storage fast failover, making it weaker for maximizing availability.","why_zh":"與 A 相同的 predictive scaling 問題：一次性排程事件缺乏 predictive scaling 所需的重複模式與歷史資料。同時使用 RDS for PostgreSQL 而非 Aurora 的共用儲存快速故障轉移，較不利於最大化可用性。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/predictive-scaling-policy-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/scaling-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-failover.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_PostgreSQL.Replication.ReadReplicas.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":375,"question_en":"A company runs an intranet application on premises. The company wants to configure a cloud backup of the application. The company has selected AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery for this solution. The company requires that replication tra®c does not travel through the public internet. The application also must not be accessible from the internet. The company does not want this solution to consume all available network bandwidth because other applications require bandwidth. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在本地运行 Intranet 应用程序。该公司想要配置应用程序的云备份。该公司为此解决方案选择了 AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery。 该公司要求复制流量不通过公共互联网传输。该应用程序也不能通过互联网访问。该公司不希望该解决方案消耗所有可用的网络带 宽，因为其他应用程序需要带宽。 哪种步骤组合可以满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a VPC that has at least two private subnets, two NAT gateways, and a virtual private gateway.","B":"Create a VPC that has at least two public subnets, a virtual private gateway, and an internet gateway.","C":"Create an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection between the on-premises network and the target AWS network.","D":"Create an AWS Direct Connect connection and a Direct Connect gateway between the on-premises network and the target AWS network.","E":"During configuration of the replication servers, select the option to use private IP addresses for data replication.","F":"During configuration of the launch settings for the target servers, select the option to ensure that the Recovery instance’s private IP address matches the source server's private IP address."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个至少具有两个私有子网、两个 NAT 网关和一个虚拟私有网关的 VPC。","B":"创建一个至少具有两个公有子网、一个虚拟专用网关和一个互联网网关的 VPC。","C":"在本地网络和目标 AWS 网络之间创建 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 连接。","D":"在本地网络和目标 AWS 网络之间创建 AWS Direct Connect 连接和 Direct Connect 网关。","E":"在配置复制服务器期间，选择使用专用 IP 地址进行数据复制的选项。","F":"在配置目标服务器的启动设置期间，选择该选项以确保恢复实例的私有 IP 地址与源服务器的私有 IP 地址匹配。"},"answer":["A","E","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ADE":65,"DEF":19},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery (and MGN, which shares the same replication architecture) by default sends replication traffic from source servers to the staging-area replication servers over the public internet using public IPv4 addresses assigned to the replication servers, and by default it uses ALL available network bandwidth with five concurrent connections. To meet the three requirements: (E) In the replication settings you must enable 'Use private IP for data replication', which routes replicated data over an existing private connection (VPN, Direct Connect, or VPC peering) instead of the public internet; the docs note this option also lets you 'allocate a dedicated bandwidth for replication'. (D) A truly private path that does NOT traverse the public internet requires AWS Direct Connect plus a Direct Connect gateway — a dedicated, private connection that also gives predictable, dedicated bandwidth so replication does not starve other applications. A Site-to-Site VPN (C) is encrypted but its packets still ride the public internet, so it does not fully satisfy 'traffic does not travel through the public internet' and gives no dedicated bandwidth guarantee. (A) The VPC needs private subnets (so neither the replication servers nor recovery instances are internet-reachable) and a virtual private gateway to terminate/route the on-premises private connection; NAT gateways provide outbound-only access without exposing instances to inbound internet traffic. The dump answer AEF is wrong because it includes no private connection at all (neither C nor D) — yet 'Use private IP' (E) explicitly requires a pre-existing VPN/Direct Connect/VPC peering, so AEF leaves no private path. F is a launch setting (match recovery instance private IP to source) used for failover convenience and is irrelevant to keeping replication off the internet, blocking inbound internet access, or limiting bandwidth.","explanation_zh":"AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery（與共用相同複寫架構的 MGN）預設會使用指派給複寫伺服器的 public IPv4 位址，將來源伺服器的複寫流量透過公網傳送到 staging area 的複寫伺服器，且預設會以五條並行連線用盡所有可用頻寬。要滿足三項需求：（E）必須在 replication settings 啟用『Use private IP for data replication』，讓複寫資料改走既有的私有連線（VPN、Direct Connect 或 VPC peering）而非公網；官方文件也指出此選項可『為複寫配置專用頻寬』。（D）真正不經過公網的私有路徑需要 AWS Direct Connect 加上 Direct Connect gateway，這是專屬的私有連線，並提供可預期的專用頻寬，使複寫不會搶用其他應用的頻寬。Site-to-Site VPN（C）雖加密，但封包仍走公網，無法完全符合『流量不經公網』，且無專用頻寬保證。（A）VPC 需要 private subnets（使複寫伺服器與 recovery instance 都不可由網際網路存取）以及 virtual private gateway 來終結／路由地端私有連線；NAT gateway 僅提供對外輸出，不會暴露 inbound 網際網路存取。dump 答案 AEF 不正確，因為完全沒有私有連線（C 與 D 皆無），而『Use private IP』（E）明確要求事先存在 VPN／Direct Connect／VPC peering，故 AEF 沒有任何私有路徑。F 是 launch setting（讓 recovery instance 私有 IP 與來源相符），用於 failover 便利性，與『讓複寫不經公網』『阻擋 inbound 網際網路存取』或『限制頻寬』皆無關。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Public subnets plus an internet gateway would expose the replication servers and recovery instances to the internet, violating the requirement that the application must not be accessible from the internet. The correct VPC design uses private subnets (option A).","why_zh":"Public subnets 加 internet gateway 會讓複寫伺服器與 recovery instance 暴露於網際網路，違反『應用程式不可由網際網路存取』的需求。正確的 VPC 設計應使用 private subnets（選項 A）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A Site-to-Site VPN is encrypted but its packets still transit the public internet and it offers no dedicated bandwidth, so it does not fully meet 'traffic does not travel through the public internet' nor the bandwidth-isolation requirement. Direct Connect (D) is the dedicated, fully private option.","why_zh":"Site-to-Site VPN 雖加密但封包仍走公網，且無專用頻寬，無法完全符合『流量不經公網』與頻寬隔離需求。Direct Connect（D）才是專屬且完全私有的選項。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Making the recovery instance's private IP match the source server is a target launch setting useful for failover/cutover IP continuity. It does nothing to keep replication off the public internet, to block inbound internet access, or to limit bandwidth, so it does not address any of the three stated requirements.","why_zh":"讓 recovery instance 的私有 IP 與來源伺服器相符是 target launch setting，用於 failover／cutover 的 IP 延續性。它無助於讓複寫不經公網、阻擋 inbound 網際網路存取或限制頻寬，因此未對應任何一項需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/individual-replication-settings.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/mgn/latest/ug/replication-server-settings.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/drs-at-scale.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpn-connections.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/aws-vpc-connectivity-options/aws-direct-connect.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・複選"},{"id":376,"question_en":"A company that provides image storage services wants to deploy a customer-facing solution to AWS. Millions of individual customers will use the solution. The solution will receive batches of large image files, resize the files, and store the files in an Amazon S3 bucket for up to 6 months. The solution must handle significant variance in demand. The solution must also be reliable at enterprise scale and have the ability to rerun processing jobs in the event of failure. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家提供图像存储服务的公司希望将面向客户的解决方案部署到 AWS。数百万个人客户将使用该解决方案。该解决方案将接收批量 大型图像文件，调整文件大小，并将文件存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中长达 6 个月。 该解决方案必须能够处理需求的显着变化。该解决方案还必须在企业规模上可靠，并且能够在发生故障时重新运行处理作业。 哪种解决方案能够最具成本效益地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Step Functions to process the S3 event that occurs when a user stores an image. Run an AWS Lambda function that resizes the image in place and replaces the original file in the S3 bucket. Create an S3 Lifecycle expiration policy to expire all stored images after 6 months.","B":"Use Amazon EventBridge to process the S3 event that occurs when a user uploads an image. Run an AWS Lambda function that resizes the image in place and replaces the original file in the S3 bucket. Create an S3 Lifecycle expiration policy to expire all stored images after 6 months.","C":"Use S3 Event Notifications to invoke an AWS Lambda function when a user stores an image. Use the Lambda function to resize the image in place and to store the original file in the S3 bucket. Create an S3 Lifecycle policy to move all stored images to S3 Standard- Infrequent Access (S3 Standard-IA) after 6 months.","D":"Use Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) to process the S3 event that occurs when a user stores an image. Run an AWS Lambda function that resizes the image and stores the resized file in an S3 bucket that uses S3 Standard-Infrequent Access (S3 Standard- IA). Create an S3 Lifecycle policy to move all stored images to S3 Glacier Deep Archive after 6 months."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Step Functions 处理用户存储图像时发生的 S3 事件。运行 AWS Lambda 函数，调整图像大小并替换 S3 存储桶中的原 始文件。创建 S3 生命周期过期策略，使所有存储的图像在 6 个月后过期。","B":"使用 Amazon EventBridge 处理用户上传图像时发生的 S3 事件。运行 AWS Lambda 函数，调整图像大小并替换 S3 存储桶中的原 始文件。创建 S3 生命周期过期策略，使所有存储的图像在 6 个月后过期。","C":"当用户存储图像时，使用 S3 事件通知调用 AWS Lambda 函数。使用 Lambda 函数就地调整图像大小并将原始文件存储在 S3 存 储桶中。创建 S3 生命周期策略，以在 6 个月后将所有存储的图像移至 S3 标准-不频繁访问 (S3 标准-IA)。","D":"使用 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 处理用户存储图像时发生的 S3 事件。运行 AWS Lambda 函数来调整图像大小 并将调整后的文件存储在使用 S3 标准-不频繁访问 (S3 标准-IA) 的 S3 存储桶中。创建 S3 生命周期策略，以在 6 个月后将所有存 储的图像移至 S3 Glacier Deep Archive。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":41,"D":28,"A":26},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The question stacks reliability requirements: handle significant variance in demand, be reliable at enterprise scale, and (critically) have the ability to rerun processing jobs in the event of failure, all most cost-effectively. Amazon SQS is the canonical AWS pattern for these needs: S3 can publish events directly to an SQS queue, which durably buffers bursts (load leveling for demand spikes) and, via the Lambda SQS event source mapping, redelivers messages after the visibility timeout if processing fails, with a DLQ capturing repeated failures. That precisely satisfies 'rerun processing jobs in the event of failure' and 'reliable at enterprise scale.' Option D also stores the resized files in S3 Standard-IA and transitions to S3 Glacier Deep Archive after 6 months, the cheapest long-term tier, making it the most cost-effective storage path. The other options rely on asynchronous Lambda invocation (S3 direct or via EventBridge), where AWS docs warn that overloaded events can age out and be silently discarded, so they do not durably buffer demand variance or guarantee reprocessing.","explanation_zh":"此題疊加多項可靠性需求:需吸收顯著的需求波動、在企業規模下保持可靠,且關鍵在於具備失敗時重新執行處理工作的能力,同時要最具成本效益。Amazon SQS 正是 AWS 處理這些需求的標準模式:S3 可直接將事件發布到 SQS 佇列,佇列能持久地緩衝突發流量(對需求高峰做負載平準),並透過 Lambda 的 SQS event source mapping 在處理失敗時於 visibility timeout 後重新投遞訊息,並以 DLQ 捕捉反覆失敗的訊息。這精準符合『失敗時重新執行處理工作』與『企業規模下的可靠性』。選項 D 還將縮放後的檔案存於 S3 Standard-IA,並在 6 個月後轉移到 S3 Glacier Deep Archive,即最便宜的長期儲存層,因此是最具成本效益的儲存路徑。其餘選項依賴 Lambda 的非同步呼叫(S3 直接或經由 EventBridge),AWS 文件警告事件過載時可能逾期並被靜默丟棄,無法持久緩衝需求波動或保證重新處理。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"S3 events cannot natively trigger Step Functions (they would need EventBridge in between), Step Functions adds unnecessary orchestration cost for a single resize, and resizing 'in place' to replace the original destroys the source file. It does not provide a durable work queue for reprocessing.","why_zh":"S3 事件無法原生觸發 Step Functions(中間需 EventBridge),為單一縮放動作引入 Step Functions 增加不必要的編排成本,而且『就地縮放並取代原檔』會破壞原始檔案,亦無持久工作佇列可供重新處理。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"EventBridge to Lambda is still an asynchronous invocation. AWS docs state overloaded async events can age out and be discarded, so it does not durably buffer significant demand variance nor reliably rerun failed processing jobs the way an SQS queue does. 'Expire after 6 months' also deletes the images rather than retaining them cheaply.","why_zh":"EventBridge 轉 Lambda 仍是非同步呼叫。AWS 文件指出過載的非同步事件可能逾期而被丟棄,因此無法像 SQS 佇列那樣持久緩衝顯著的需求波動或可靠地重新執行失敗的處理工作。『6 個月後到期』還會刪除影像而非以低成本保留。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Direct S3-to-Lambda async invocation is the weakest reliability/rerun story (events can be silently discarded under load). 'Resize in place' destroys the original, and moving to Standard-IA only after 6 months gives far less cost savings than archiving cold data to Glacier Deep Archive.","why_zh":"S3 直接非同步觸發 Lambda 的可靠性與重試能力最弱(過載時事件可能被靜默丟棄)。『就地縮放』會破壞原檔,且僅在 6 個月後才轉到 Standard-IA,成本節省遠不及將冷資料封存至 Glacier Deep Archive。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-sqs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/invocation-async-error-handling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/EventNotifications.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/glacier-storage-classes.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識・多選項拉鋸"},{"id":377,"question_en":"A company has an organization in AWS Organizations that includes a separate AWS account for each of the company’s departments. Application teams from different departments develop and deploy solutions independently. The company wants to reduce compute costs and manage costs appropriately across departments. The company also wants to improve visibility into billing for individual departments. The company does not want to lose operational ­exibility when the company selects compute resources. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Organizations 中拥有一个组织，其中包含公司每个部门的单独 AWS 账户。不同部门的应用团队独立开发和部署解决 方案。 该公司希望降低计算成本并适当管理跨部门的成本。该公司还希望提高各个部门计费的可见性。公司不希望在选择计算资源时失去 运营灵活性。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Budgets for each department. Use Tag Editor to apply tags to appropriate resources. Purchase EC2 Instance Savings Plans.","B":"Configure AWS Organizations to use consolidated billing. Implement a tagging strategy that identifies departments. Use SCPs to apply tags to appropriate resources. Purchase EC2 Instance Savings Plans.","C":"Configure AWS Organizations to use consolidated billing. Implement a tagging strategy that identifies departments. Use Tag Editor to apply tags to appropriate resources. Purchase Compute Savings Plans.","D":"Use AWS Budgets for each department. Use SCPs to apply tags to appropriate resources. Purchase Compute Savings Plans."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用每个部门的 AWS 预算。使用标签编辑器将标签应用到适当的资源。购买 EC2 实例节省计划。","B":"配置 AWS Organizations 以使用合并账单。实施识别部门的标记策略。使用 SCP 将标签应用到适当的资源。购买 EC2 实例节省 计划。","C":"配置 AWS Organizations 以使用合并账单。实施识别部门的标记策略。使用标签编辑器将标签应用到适当的资源。购买计算节 省计划。","D":"使用每个部门的 AWS 预算。使用 SCP 将标签应用到适当的资源。购买计算节省计划。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":87},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":378,"question_en":"A company has a web application that securely uploads pictures and videos to an Amazon S3 bucket. The company requires that only authenticated users are allowed to post content. The application generates a presigned URL that is used to upload objects through a browser interface. Most users are reporting slow upload times for objects larger than 100 MB. What can a solutions architect do to improve the performance of these uploads while ensuring only authenticated users are allowed to post content?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个 Web 应用程序，可以将图片和视频安全上传到 Amazon S3 存储桶。该公司要求只有经过身份验证的用户才可以发布 内容。该应用程序生成一个预签名 URL，用于通过浏览器界面上传对象。大多数用户报告大于 100 MB 的对象上传速度缓慢。 解决方案架构师可以采取哪些措施来提高这些上传的性能，同时确保只允许经过身份验证的用户发布内容？","options_en":{"A":"Set up an Amazon API Gateway with an edge-optimized API endpoint that has a resource as an S3 service proxy. Configure the PUT method for this resource to expose the S3 PutObject operation. Secure the API Gateway using a COGNITO_USER_POOLS authorizer. Have the browser interface use API Gateway instead of the presigned URL to upload objects.","B":"Set up an Amazon API Gateway with a regional API endpoint that has a resource as an S3 service proxy. Configure the PUT method for this resource to expose the S3 PutObject operation. Secure the API Gateway using an AWS Lambda authorizer. Have the browser interface use API Gateway instead of the presigned URL to upload objects.","C":"Enable an S3 Transfer Acceleration endpoint on the S3 bucket. Use the endpoint when generating the presigned URL. Have the browser interface upload the objects to this URL using the S3 multipart upload API.","D":"Configure an Amazon CloudFront distribution for the destination S3 bucket. Enable PUT and POST methods for the CloudFront cache behavior. Update the CloudFront origin to use an origin access identity (OAI). Give the OAI user 3: PutObject permissions in the bucket policy. Have the browser interface upload objects using the CloudFront distribution."},"options_zh":{"A":"设置具有边缘优化 API 终端节点的 Amazon API Gateway，该终端节点具有作为 S3 服务代理的资源。配置此资源的 PUT 方法以 公开 S3 PutObject 操作。使用 COGNITO_USER_POOLS 授权者保护 API 网关。让浏览器界面使用 API Gateway 而不是预签名 URL 来 上传对象。","B":"设置具有区域 API 终端节点的 Amazon API Gateway，该终端节点具有作为 S3 服务代理的资源。配置此资源的 PUT 方法以公开 S3 PutObject 操作。使用 AWS Lambda 授权者保护 API Gateway。让浏览器界面使用 API Gateway 而不是预签名 URL 来上传对象。","C":"在 S3 存储桶上启用 S3 传输加速端点。生成预签名 URL 时使用端点。让浏览器界面使用 S3 分段上传 API 将对象上传到此 URL。","D":"为目标 S3 存储桶配置 Amazon CloudFront 分配。为 CloudFront 缓存行为启用 PUT 和 POST 方法。更新 CloudFront 源以使用源访 问身份 (OAI)。在存储桶策略中为 OAI 用户授予 3: PutObject 权限。让浏览器界面使用 CloudFront 分配上传对象。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":78,"A":17},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The application already uses a presigned URL, which satisfies the 'only authenticated users' requirement because the server generates the signed URL only for authenticated users. The slowness is from uploading large (>100 MB) objects over long internet distances. Option C addresses this directly: enabling S3 Transfer Acceleration routes the upload through the nearest CloudFront edge location over AWS's optimized backbone, and using the multipart upload API for objects >=100 MB (AWS's own recommended threshold) parallelizes the transfer. Transfer Acceleration works with presigned URLs simply by generating them against the s3-accelerate endpoint, so authentication is fully preserved with minimal change. Options A and B are technically broken because API Gateway has a hard 10 MB payload-size quota that cannot be increased, so any object over 10 MB (let alone 100 MB) would fail through an S3 service proxy regardless of whether a COGNITO_USER_POOLS or Lambda authorizer is used.","explanation_zh":"此應用程式已使用 presigned URL，這已滿足「只有經過驗證的使用者才能上傳」的需求，因為伺服器只會為已驗證的使用者產生簽署過的 URL。上傳緩慢的原因是大型物件（>100 MB）需經由長距離網際網路傳輸。選項 C 直接解決此問題：啟用 S3 Transfer Acceleration 會將上傳透過最近的 CloudFront 邊緣節點，經由 AWS 最佳化的骨幹網路傳送；並對 >=100 MB 的物件使用 multipart upload API（這正是 AWS 建議的門檻），可平行化傳輸。Transfer Acceleration 只需以 s3-accelerate 端點產生 presigned URL 即可搭配使用，因此完全保留驗證機制且改動極小。選項 A 與 B 在技術上行不通，因為 API Gateway 的 payload 大小配額硬性限制為 10 MB 且無法調高，因此任何超過 10 MB（更遑論 100 MB）的物件透過 S3 service proxy 都會失敗，無論使用 COGNITO_USER_POOLS 或 Lambda authorizer 都一樣。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Routing uploads through an API Gateway S3 service proxy hits API Gateway's hard 10 MB payload-size quota (cannot be increased), so objects >100 MB fail outright. A Cognito authorizer secures auth but does nothing for the size/performance problem.","why_zh":"將上傳透過 API Gateway S3 service proxy 會撞上 API Gateway 硬性的 10 MB payload 大小配額（無法調高），因此 >100 MB 的物件會直接失敗。Cognito authorizer 雖能處理驗證，但完全無法解決大小與效能問題。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same fatal flaw as A: the API Gateway 10 MB payload limit makes >100 MB uploads impossible through an S3 proxy. Swapping a Lambda authorizer for Cognito does not change this; it is the dump's suggested answer but is technically infeasible.","why_zh":"與 A 相同的致命缺陷：API Gateway 的 10 MB payload 限制使得透過 S3 proxy 上傳 >100 MB 物件不可能。把 authorizer 換成 Lambda 並不會改變這點；這雖是題庫的建議答案，但技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudFront with an OAI is designed to restrict GET access to an S3 origin, not to perform authenticated PUT uploads. Granting the OAI s3:PutObject would let anyone reaching the distribution write to the bucket, breaking the 'only authenticated users' requirement, and CloudFront does not improve large upload performance the way Transfer Acceleration/multipart does.","why_zh":"使用 OAI 的 CloudFront 是設計用來限制對 S3 origin 的 GET 存取，而非執行已驗證的 PUT 上傳。給 OAI s3:PutObject 權限會讓任何能存取此 distribution 的人都能寫入 bucket，破壞「只有經過驗證的使用者」需求，且 CloudFront 也無法像 Transfer Acceleration/multipart 那樣改善大型上傳效能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/transfer-acceleration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/qfacts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/mpuoverview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/PresignedUrlUploadObject.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/api-gateway-execution-service-limits-table.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":379,"question_en":"A large company is migrating its entire IT portfolio to AWS. Each business unit in the company has a standalone AWS account that supports both development and test environments. New accounts to support production workloads will be needed soon. The finance department requires a centralized method for payment but must maintain visibility into each group's spending to allocate costs. The security team requires a centralized mechanism to control IAM usage in all the company’s accounts. What combination of the following options meets the company’s needs with the LEAST effort? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家大公司正在将其整个 IT 产品组合迁移到 AWS。公司的每个业务部门都有一个独立的AWS账户，支持开发和测试环境。很快将需 要新帐户来支持生产工作负载。 财务部门需要一种集中的付款方式，但必须保持对每个组的支出的可见性以分配成本。 安全团队需要一个集中机制来控制公司所有账户中的 IAM 使用情况。 以下选项的哪种组合能够以最少的努力满足公司的需求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Use a collection of parameterized AWS CloudFormation templates defining common IAM permissions that are launched into each account. Require all new and existing accounts to launch the appropriate stacks to enforce the least privilege model.","B":"Use AWS Organizations to create a new organization from a chosen payer account and define an organizational unit hierarchy. Invite the existing accounts to join the organization and create new accounts using Organizations.","C":"Require each business unit to use its own AWS accounts. Tag each AWS account appropriately and enable Cost Explorer to administer chargebacks.","D":"Enable all features of AWS Organizations and establish appropriate service control policies that filter IAM permissions for sub-accounts.","E":"Consolidate all of the company's AWS accounts into a single AWS account. Use tags for billing purposes and the IAM’s Access Advisor feature to enforce the least privilege model."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用一组参数化的 AWS CloudFormation 模板来定义在每个账户中启动的常见 IAM 权限。要求所有新帐户和现有帐户启动适当 的堆栈以强制执行最小权限模型​。","B":"使用 AWS Organizations 从所选付款人账户创建新组织并定义组织单位层次结构。邀请现有帐户加入组织并使用组织创建新帐 户。","C":"要求每个业务部门使用自己的AWS账户。适当标记每个 AWS 账户并启用 Cost Explorer 管理退款。","D":"启用 AWS Organizations 的所有功能并建立适当的服务控制策略来筛选子账户的 IAM 权限。","E":"将公司的所有 AWS 账户合并到一个 AWS 账户中。使用标签进行计费，并使用 IAM 的访问顾问功能来强制执行最小权限模型​。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BD":65,"BC":35},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The company needs two things: (1) a centralized payment method that still gives the finance team visibility into each business unit's spending for cost allocation, and (2) a centralized mechanism for the security team to control IAM usage across all accounts. Option B sets up AWS Organizations from a chosen payer (management) account, builds an OU hierarchy, invites the existing standalone accounts, and creates new production accounts directly in Organizations. This delivers consolidated billing (one centralized payment) while the management account retains per-account cost visibility via Cost Explorer/cost allocation, satisfying finance with the least effort. Option D enables ALL FEATURES of AWS Organizations and applies Service Control Policies (SCPs); per AWS docs, SCPs are the central guardrail that limits the maximum IAM permissions for users and roles in member accounts, and SCPs are available ONLY when all features are enabled (not in consolidated-billing-only mode). Together B+D give centralized billing with visibility plus centralized IAM control with the least operational effort, because everything is managed natively in Organizations rather than per-account.","explanation_zh":"公司需要兩件事：(1) 集中的付款方式，同時讓財務團隊仍能看見每個業務單位的支出以進行成本分攤；(2) 讓安全團隊在所有帳戶集中控管 IAM 使用的機制。選項 B 從指定的付款（管理）帳戶建立 AWS Organizations、建立 OU 階層、邀請現有的獨立帳戶加入，並直接透過 Organizations 建立新的生產帳戶。這提供了合併帳單（consolidated billing，單一集中付款），同時管理帳戶可透過 Cost Explorer/成本分攤標籤保有逐帳戶的成本可見性，以最少的工作量滿足財務需求。選項 D 啟用 AWS Organizations 的「所有功能（all features）」並套用 Service Control Policies（SCP）；根據 AWS 文件，SCP 是集中的防護欄，限制成員帳戶中使用者與角色的最大 IAM 權限，且 SCP 只有在啟用所有功能時才可使用（在僅合併帳單模式下無法使用）。B+D 合起來以最少的維運工作量同時達成具可見性的集中帳單與集中 IAM 控管，因為一切都在 Organizations 中原生管理，而非逐帳戶處理。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Launching parameterized CloudFormation stacks of IAM permissions into every account is high-effort, decentralized, and not a true centralized control mechanism. It does nothing for centralized billing/cost visibility, and it relies on each account complying rather than enforcing a guardrail centrally. SCPs (via Organizations) achieve centralized IAM control with far less effort.","why_zh":"把參數化的 IAM 權限 CloudFormation 堆疊部署到每個帳戶，工作量大、分散，且非真正的集中控管機制。它對集中帳單/成本可見性毫無幫助，且依賴各帳戶自行遵循而非集中強制護欄。透過 Organizations 的 SCP 能以更少工作量達成集中 IAM 控管。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Keeping each business unit on its own separate AWS accounts with per-account tagging and Cost Explorer does NOT provide a centralized payment method (each account still pays its own bill) and provides no centralized IAM control mechanism. It fails both core requirements.","why_zh":"讓每個業務單位維持各自獨立的 AWS 帳戶並逐帳戶加標籤與使用 Cost Explorer，無法提供集中付款方式（每個帳戶仍各自付款），也沒有集中 IAM 控管機制。兩項核心需求都無法滿足。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Consolidating everything into a single AWS account destroys account-level isolation between business units and environments (dev/test/prod), makes per-group cost allocation crude (tags only), and IAM Access Advisor only reports last-accessed data; it is not a centralized enforcement mechanism. Merging accounts is also enormous effort, the opposite of 'least effort'.","why_zh":"把所有東西併入單一 AWS 帳戶會破壞業務單位與環境（dev/test/prod）之間的帳戶層級隔離，使各群組成本分攤變得粗糙（僅靠標籤），而 IAM Access Advisor 只提供最後存取資料，並非集中強制機制。合併帳戶工作量也極大，與「最少工作量」背道而馳。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_getting-started_concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/consolidated-billing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_org_support-all-features.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・複選"},{"id":380,"question_en":"A company has a solution that analyzes weather data from thousands of weather stations. The weather stations send the data over an Amazon API Gateway REST API that has an AWS Lambda function integration. The Lambda function calls a third-party service for data pre- processing. The third-party service gets overloaded and fails the pre-processing, causing a loss of data. A solutions architect must improve the resiliency of the solution. The solutions architect must ensure that no data is lost and that data can be processed later if failures occur. What should the solutions architect do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个解决方案可以分析来自数千个气象站的天气数据。气象站通过集成了 AWS Lambda 函数的 Amazon API Gateway REST API 发送数据。Lambda函数调用第三方服务进行数据预处理。第三方服务过载，预处理失败，导致数据丢失。 解决方案架构师必须提高解决方案的弹性。解决方案架构师必须确保不会丢失任何数据，并且在发生故障时可以稍后处理数据。 解决方案架构师应该怎样做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Configure the queue as the dead-letter queue for the API.","B":"Create two Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queues: a primary queue and a secondary queue. Configure the secondary queue as the dead-letter queue for the primary queue. Update the API to use a new integration to the primary queue. Configure the Lambda function as the invocation target for the primary queue.","C":"Create two Amazon EventBridge event buses: a primary event bus and a secondary event bus. Update the API to use a new integration to the primary event bus. Configure an EventBridge rule to react to all events on the primary event bus. Specify the Lambda function as the target of the rule. Configure the secondary event bus as the failure destination for the Lambda function.","D":"Create a custom Amazon EventBridge event bus. Configure the event bus as the failure destination for the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列。将队列配置为 API 的死信队列。","B":"创建两个 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列：主队列和辅助队列。将辅助队列配置为主队列的死信队列。更新 API 以使用与主队列的新集成。将 Lambda 函数配置为主队列的调用目标。","C":"创建两个 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线：主事件总线和辅助事件总线。更新 API 以使用与主事件总线的新集成。配置 EventBridge 规则以对主事件总线上的所有事件做出反应。将 Lambda 函数指定为规则的目标。将辅助事件总线配置为 Lambda 函 数的故障目标。","D":"创建自定义 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线。将事件总线配置为 Lambda 函数的故障目标。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":94},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":381,"question_en":"A company built an ecommerce website on AWS using a three-tier web architecture. The application is Java-based and composed of an Amazon CloudFront distribution, an Apache web server layer of Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group, and a backend Amazon Aurora MySQL database. Last month, during a promotional sales event, users reported errors and timeouts while adding items to their shopping carts. The operations team recovered the logs created by the web servers and reviewed Aurora DB cluster performance metrics. Some of the web servers were terminated before logs could be collected and the Aurora metrics were not su®cient for query performance analysis. Which combination of steps must the solutions architect take to improve application performance visibility during peak tra®c events? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用三层 Web 架构在 AWS 上构建了一个电子商务网站。该应用程序基于 Java，由 Amazon CloudFront 发行版、Auto Scaling 组中 Amazon EC2 实例的 Apache Web 服务器层以及后端 Amazon Aurora MySQL 数据库组成。 上个月，在促销活动期间，用户报告在将商品添加到购物车时出现错误和超时。运营团队恢复了 Web 服务器创建的日志并审查了 Aurora 数据库集群性能指标。一些 Web 服务器在收集日志之前被终止，并且 Aurora 指标不足以进行查询性能分析。 解决方案架构师必须采取哪些步骤组合来提高高峰流量事件期间的应用程序性能可见性？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure the Aurora MySQL DB cluster to publish slow query and error logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs.","B":"Implement the AWS X-Ray SDK to trace incoming HTTP requests on the EC2 instances and implement tracing of SQL queries with the X- Ray SDK for Java.","C":"Configure the Aurora MySQL DB cluster to stream slow query and error logs to Amazon Kinesis.","D":"Install and configure an Amazon CloudWatch Logs agent on the EC2 instances to send the Apache logs to CloudWatch Logs.","E":"Enable and configure AWS CloudTrail to collect and analyze application activity from Amazon EC2 and Aurora","F":"Enable Aurora MySQL DB cluster performance benchmarking and publish the stream to AWS X-Ray."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 Aurora MySQL 数据库集群以将慢速查询和错误日志发布到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。","B":"实施 AWS X-Ray 开发工具包以跟踪 EC2 实例上的传入 HTTP 请求，并使用适用于 Java 的 X-Ray 开发工具包实施 SQL 查询跟 踪。","C":"配置 Aurora MySQL 数据库集群以将慢速查询和错误日志流式传输到 Amazon Kinesis。","D":"在 EC2 实例上安装并配置 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 代理，以将 Apache 日志发送到 CloudWatch Logs。","E":"启用并配置 AWS CloudTrail 以收集和分析来自 Amazon EC2 和 Aurora 的应用程序活动","F":"启用 Aurora MySQL 数据库集群性能基准测试并将流发布到 AWS X-Ray。"},"answer":["A","E","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ABD":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The scenario has two visibility gaps. First, web server (Apache) logs were lost because Auto Scaling terminated instances before logs were collected; installing the CloudWatch Logs agent on the EC2 instances ships Apache logs off-instance to CloudWatch Logs so they survive termination (D). Second, the Aurora metrics were insufficient for query performance analysis; configuring the Aurora MySQL cluster to publish slow query and error logs to CloudWatch Logs surfaces the slow/erroring queries needed for tuning (A). To get true end-to-end application performance visibility, the AWS X-Ray SDK for Java instruments incoming HTTP requests via a servlet filter and traces downstream SQL queries through the SQL connector, pinpointing where the add-to-cart latency/errors originate (B). CloudTrail (E) records control-plane API activity, not application or query performance; and 'Aurora performance benchmarking published to X-Ray' (F) is not a real feature, while streaming Aurora logs to Kinesis (C) is not the native, lowest-overhead path (Aurora publishes to CloudWatch Logs).","explanation_zh":"情境中有兩個可見度缺口。第一,Web 伺服器(Apache)日誌因 Auto Scaling 在收集前終止執行個體而遺失;在 EC2 上安裝 CloudWatch Logs agent 可將 Apache 日誌傳送到 CloudWatch Logs,即使執行個體被終止也能保留(D)。第二,Aurora 指標不足以進行查詢效能分析;將 Aurora MySQL 叢集設定為將 slow query 與 error logs 發布到 CloudWatch Logs,可呈現需要調校的緩慢/錯誤查詢(A)。為取得真正的端到端應用程式效能可見度,AWS X-Ray SDK for Java 透過 servlet filter 對傳入的 HTTP 請求進行儀器化,並透過 SQL connector 追蹤下游 SQL 查詢,定位加入購物車延遲/錯誤的來源(B)。CloudTrail(E)記錄的是控制平面 API 活動,而非應用程式或查詢效能;『Aurora 效能基準測試發布到 X-Ray』(F)並非真實功能;而將 Aurora 日誌串流到 Kinesis(C)並非原生且最低負擔的路徑(Aurora 原生發布到 CloudWatch Logs)。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"Aurora MySQL natively publishes slow query and error logs to CloudWatch Logs, not directly to Kinesis; routing them to Kinesis adds unnecessary pipeline overhead and is not the intended log-export path. Option A is the correct native mechanism.","why_zh":"Aurora MySQL 原生將 slow query 與 error logs 發布到 CloudWatch Logs,而非直接到 Kinesis;導向 Kinesis 增加不必要的管線負擔,不是預期的日誌匯出路徑。A 才是正確的原生機制。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"CloudTrail captures management/control-plane API calls and account activity, not application data-plane behavior, SQL query performance, or shopping-cart errors. It does nothing to improve application or query performance visibility.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 擷取的是管理/控制平面 API 呼叫與帳戶活動,而非應用程式資料平面行為、SQL 查詢效能或購物車錯誤。它無助於改善應用程式或查詢效能可見度。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"There is no Aurora MySQL feature called 'performance benchmarking', and X-Ray does not ingest a database benchmarking stream. This option is fabricated and technically impossible.","why_zh":"Aurora MySQL 並無所謂『performance benchmarking』功能,X-Ray 也不會接收資料庫基準測試串流。此選項為虛構且技術上不可行。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-mysql-troubleshooting-logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/xray/latest/devguide/xray-sdk-java.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/xray/latest/devguide/xray-sdk-java-filters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/install-CloudWatch-Agent-on-EC2-Instance.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":382,"question_en":"A company that provisions job boards for a seasonal workforce is seeing an increase in tra®c and usage. The backend services run on a pair of Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer with Amazon DynamoDB as the datastore. Application read and write tra®c is slow during peak seasons. Which option provides a scalable application architecture to handle peak seasons with the LEAST development effort?","question_zh":"一家为季节性劳动力提供招聘网站的公司的流量和使用量都在增加。后端服务在应用程序负载均衡器后面的一对 Amazon EC2 实例 上运行，并以 Amazon DynamoDB 作为数据存储。旺季应用读写流量较慢。 哪个选项提供可扩展的应用程序架构，以最少的开发工作来应对旺季？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate the backend services to AWS Lambda. Increase the read and write capacity of DynamoDB.","B":"Migrate the backend services to AWS Lambda. Configure DynamoDB to use global tables.","C":"Use Auto Scaling groups for the backend services. Use DynamoDB auto scaling.","D":"Use Auto Scaling groups for the backend services. Use Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) and an AWS Lambda function to write to DynamoDB."},"options_zh":{"A":"将后端服务迁移到AWS Lambda。增加DynamoDB的读写能力。","B":"将后端服务迁移到AWS Lambda。配置 DynamoDB 以使用全局表。","C":"将 Auto Scaling 组用于后端服务。使用 DynamoDB 自动缩放。","D":"将 Auto Scaling 组用于后端服务。使用 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 和 AWS Lambda 函数写入 DynamoDB。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The scenario is cyclical/seasonal traffic causing slow reads and writes on EC2 instances behind an ALB with DynamoDB. The lowest-effort scalable fix keeps the existing architecture and adds automatic scaling at both tiers: EC2 Auto Scaling groups (with target tracking) automatically add/remove instances behind the ALB, and DynamoDB auto scaling (Application Auto Scaling) dynamically adjusts provisioned read and write capacity in response to actual traffic. AWS documentation explicitly cites cyclical/seasonal workloads as the ideal use case for DynamoDB auto scaling, which scales both read and write capacity without manual intervention. This requires no code changes, so it satisfies the LEAST development effort qualifier. Option B is wrong because DynamoDB global tables provide multi-active, multi-Region replication for availability/latency, not single-region throughput scaling, and migrating backend services to Lambda is a major re-architecture (high development effort).","explanation_zh":"情境是週期性/季節性流量造成 ALB 後方 EC2 與 DynamoDB 的讀寫變慢。開發成本最低且可擴展的做法是維持現有架構，並在兩層都加入自動擴展：EC2 Auto Scaling groups（搭配 target tracking）自動在 ALB 後方增減執行個體，而 DynamoDB auto scaling（Application Auto Scaling）依實際流量動態調整佈建的讀取與寫入容量。AWS 官方文件明確將週期性/季節性工作負載列為 DynamoDB auto scaling 的理想使用情境，可同時擴展讀寫容量且無需人工介入。此方案不需修改程式碼，符合「最少開發成本」的限定條件。選項 B 錯誤，因為 DynamoDB global tables 是多活、多區域複寫（用於可用性/延遲），並非單一區域的吞吐量擴展；且將後端服務遷移至 Lambda 屬於重大重構（開發成本高）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Migrating backend services to Lambda is a major re-architecture (high development effort), and merely increasing DynamoDB read/write capacity sets a static higher provisioning that does not adapt to peak vs off-peak seasons, leading to throttling at peaks or wasted spend off-peak.","why_zh":"將後端服務遷移至 Lambda 屬重大重構（開發成本高），而僅提高 DynamoDB 讀寫容量只是設定一個較高的靜態值，無法因應旺季與淡季的差異，旺季仍會節流、淡季則浪費費用。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"DynamoDB global tables provide multi-active, multi-Region replication for high availability and lower cross-region latency, not throughput scaling within a region; they do not fix slow peak-season reads/writes. Migrating to Lambda is also high development effort.","why_zh":"DynamoDB global tables 提供多活、多區域複寫以達高可用性與降低跨區延遲，並非區域內的吞吐量擴展，無法解決旺季讀寫變慢；且遷移至 Lambda 也屬高開發成本。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Adding SQS plus a Lambda writer introduces new components and code (more development effort) and only decouples/buffers writes; it does nothing for the slow read traffic, and write decoupling adds eventual-consistency complexity that is unnecessary here.","why_zh":"加入 SQS 與寫入用 Lambda 會引入新元件與程式碼（開發成本較高），且僅能解耦/緩衝寫入，對讀取變慢毫無幫助；寫入解耦還帶來最終一致性的額外複雜度，在此並無必要。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/AutoScaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/application/userguide/services-that-can-integrate-dynamodb.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/as-scaling-target-tracking.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/autoscaling-load-balancer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/GlobalTables.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":383,"question_en":"A company is migrating to the cloud. It wants to evaluate the configurations of virtual machines in its existing data center environment to ensure that it can size new Amazon EC2 instances accurately. The company wants to collect metrics, such as CPU, memory, and disk utilization, and it needs an inventory of what processes are running on each instance. The company would also like to monitor network connections to map communications between servers. Which would enable the collection of this data MOST cost effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司正在迁移到云。它希望评估现有数据中心环境中虚拟机的配置，以确保能够准确调整新 Amazon EC2 实例的大小。该公司 希望收集 CPU、内存和磁盘利用率等指标，并且需要列出每个实例上运行的进程的清单。该公司还希望监控网络连接以映射服务器 之间的通信。 哪种方式能够最经济有效地收集这些数据？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Application Discovery Service and deploy the data collection agent to each virtual machine in the data center.","B":"Configure the Amazon CloudWatch agent on all servers within the local environment and publish metrics to Amazon CloudWatch Logs.","C":"Use AWS Application Discovery Service and enable agentless discovery in the existing virtualization environment.","D":"Enable AWS Application Discovery Service in the AWS Management Console and configure the corporate firewall to allow scans over a VPN."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Application Discovery Service 并将数据收集代理部署到数据中心中的每个虚拟机。","B":"在本地环境中的所有服务器上配置 Amazon CloudWatch 代理，并将指标发布到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。","C":"使用 AWS Application Discovery Service 并在现有虚拟化环境中启用无代理发现。","D":"在 AWS 管理控制台中启用 AWS Application Discovery Service 并配置公司防火墙以允许通过 VPN 进行扫描。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":90},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirements include three distinct data sets: (1) utilization metrics (CPU, memory, disk), (2) an inventory of running processes on each instance, and (3) network connections to map server-to-server communications. Only the AWS Application Discovery Agent (Discovery Agent), installed on each VM, collects all three. AWS docs state the agent captures 'static configuration data, detailed time-series system-performance information, inbound and outbound network connections, and processes that are running' (CPU usage %, free RAM, disk metrics, cmdLine/process IDs, and source/destination IP and ports for TCP connections). This is exactly Option A. The 'MOST cost effectively' qualifier is a tiebreaker between options that work, but here the agentless option simply cannot meet the requirement: the docs explicitly say the Agentless Collector 'cannot \"look inside\" each of the VMs, and as such, cannot figure out what processes are running on each VM nor what network connections exist.' So Option C is disqualified on capability, not just cost. Option A is the only choice that collects processes and network connections, making it correct.","explanation_zh":"需求包含三類資料: (1) 使用率指標 (CPU、記憶體、磁碟), (2) 每台執行個體上執行中程序的清單, (3) 網路連線以對應伺服器之間的通訊。只有安裝在每台 VM 上的 AWS Application Discovery Agent (Discovery Agent) 能收集全部三類。AWS 文件指出該 agent 會擷取「靜態組態資料、詳細的時間序列系統效能資訊、進出站網路連線, 以及執行中的程序」(CPU 使用率、可用 RAM、磁碟指標、cmdLine/程序 ID, 以及 TCP 連線的來源/目的 IP 與連接埠)。這正是選項 A。「MOST cost effectively」這個限定詞通常用來在都可行的選項間做取捨, 但這裡 agentless 選項根本無法滿足需求: 文件明確說明 Agentless Collector「無法『看進』每台 VM 內部, 因此無法得知每台 VM 上執行哪些程序, 也無法得知存在哪些網路連線」。所以選項 C 是因能力不足而被排除, 而非僅因成本。選項 A 是唯一能收集程序與網路連線的選項, 故為正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The CloudWatch agent can collect CPU/memory/disk and even per-process metrics via procstat, but it does not build an inventory of all running processes automatically, and it does not map TCP network connections between servers for dependency analysis. It is also not the migration-assessment/right-sizing tool AWS intends here; publishing custom metrics from many on-prem servers to CloudWatch is more operationally and cost-heavy than ADS.","why_zh":"CloudWatch agent 可透過 procstat 收集 CPU/記憶體/磁碟甚至個別程序指標, 但它不會自動建立所有執行中程序的清單, 也無法對應伺服器之間的 TCP 網路連線以做相依性分析。它也不是 AWS 針對遷移評估/規模調整所設計的工具; 從大量地端伺服器發佈自訂指標到 CloudWatch, 在維運與成本上都比 ADS 更重。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Agentless discovery (Agentless Collector via vCenter) collects CPU/RAM/Disk utilization and static config, but AWS docs explicitly state it cannot determine what processes are running on each VM nor what network connections exist. It therefore fails two of the three stated requirements (process inventory and network connection mapping), regardless of cost.","why_zh":"Agentless discovery (透過 vCenter 的 Agentless Collector) 會收集 CPU/RAM/磁碟使用率與靜態組態, 但 AWS 文件明確指出它無法判定每台 VM 上執行哪些程序, 也無法判定存在哪些網路連線。因此無論成本如何, 它都無法滿足三項需求中的兩項 (程序清單與網路連線對應)。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"There is no Application Discovery Service mode that simply scans the data center over a VPN through the corporate firewall from the AWS console. ADS uses either the Discovery Agent, the vCenter Agentless Collector, or file import. This option describes a mechanism that does not exist, which is why it is wrong despite being the dump's suggested answer.","why_zh":"Application Discovery Service 並沒有一種模式是單純從 AWS 主控台透過 VPN 經由企業防火牆掃描資料中心。ADS 使用的是 Discovery Agent、vCenter Agentless Collector 或檔案匯入。此選項描述的機制並不存在, 因此即使它是 dump 的建議答案, 仍然是錯的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/what-is-appdiscovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/discovery-agent.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":384,"question_en":"A company provides a software as a service (SaaS) application that runs in the AWS Cloud. The application runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind a Network Load Balancer (NLB). The instances are in an Auto Scaling group and are distributed across three Availability Zones in a single AWS Region. The company is deploying the application into additional Regions. The company must provide static IP addresses for the application to customers so that the customers can add the IP addresses to allow lists. The solution must automatically route customers to the Region that is geographically closest to them. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司提供在 AWS 云中运行的软件即服务 (SaaS) 应用程序。该应用程序在网络负载均衡器 (NLB) 后面的 Amazon EC2 实例上运 行。这些实例位于 Auto Scaling 组中，分布在单个 AWS 区域的三个可用区中。 该公司正在将该应用程序部署到其他区域。公司必须向客户提供应用程序的静态 IP 地址，以便客户可以将 IP 地址添加到允许列表 中。该解决方案必须自动将客户路由到地理位置最接近他们的区域。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution. Create a CloudFront origin group. Add the NLB for each additional Region to the origin group. Provide customers with the IP address ranges of the distribution’s edge locations.","B":"Create an AWS Global Accelerator standard accelerator. Create a standard accelerator endpoint for the NLB in each additional Region. Provide customers with the Global Accelerator IP address.","C":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution. Create a custom origin for the NLB in each additional Region. Provide customers with the IP address ranges of the distribution’s edge locations.","D":"Create an AWS Global Accelerator custom routing accelerator. Create a listener for the custom routing accelerator. Add the IP address and ports for the NLB in each additional Region. Provide customers with the Global Accelerator IP address."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 Amazon CloudFront 分配。创建 CloudFront 源组。将每个附加区域的 NLB 添加到原始组。为客户提供分发边缘站点的 IP 地 址范围。","B":"创建 AWS Global Accelerator 标准加速器。在每个附加区域中为 NLB 创建标准加速器端点。为客户提供全球加速器 IP 地址。","C":"创建 Amazon CloudFront 分配。在每个附加区域中为 NLB 创建自定义源。为客户提供分发边缘站点的 IP 地址范围。","D":"创建 AWS Global Accelerator 自定义路由加速器。为自定义路由加速器创建侦听器。在每个附加区域中添加 NLB 的 IP 地址和端 口。为客户提供全球加速器 IP 地址。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":92},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"An AWS Global Accelerator standard accelerator meets both requirements directly. It provides a fixed set of static anycast IP addresses (two static IPv4 by default) that remain assigned for the life of the accelerator, so customers can add them to allow lists. For standard accelerators, Global Accelerator routes traffic over the AWS global network to the optimal regional endpoint based on client location and health, so it automatically sends customers to the geographically closest Region. Endpoints for standard accelerators can be Network Load Balancers in one or multiple Regions, which fits this NLB-backed multi-Region application. This is option B.","explanation_zh":"AWS Global Accelerator standard accelerator 直接滿足兩項需求。它提供一組固定的 static anycast IP 位址（預設兩個 static IPv4），這些位址在 accelerator 存在期間維持不變，因此客戶可加入允許清單（allow list）。對於 standard accelerator，Global Accelerator 會透過 AWS 全球網路依用戶端位置與健康狀態將流量導向最佳的區域端點，因此會自動將客戶導向地理上最近的 Region。Standard accelerator 的端點可以是位於單一或多個 Region 的 Network Load Balancer，正好符合此以 NLB 為後端的多 Region 應用。此為選項 B。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudFront does not give customers a small set of static IPs to allow-list; its edge server IP ranges are large, shared across all AWS customers, and change over time (published in ip-ranges.json). A CloudFront origin group provides primary/secondary failover, not automatic routing to the geographically closest Region. CloudFront also fronts HTTP(S) origins, not Layer 4 NLB-style traffic.","why_zh":"CloudFront 不會提供一小組可加入允許清單的 static IP；其 edge server IP 範圍龐大、為所有 AWS 客戶共用且會隨時間變動（發布於 ip-ranges.json）。CloudFront origin group 提供主/備容錯移轉，而非自動導向地理上最近的 Region。CloudFront 也是面向 HTTP(S) 來源，而非第 4 層的 NLB 流量。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it is wrong. CloudFront edge IP ranges are not static, dedicated allow-list addresses; they are large, shared, and dynamic. CloudFront routes viewers to the nearest edge location for caching, but it does not provide a static IP allow-list nor geographic routing to the closest origin Region (origins are selected by failover/cache behavior, not client geography).","why_zh":"這是題庫建議答案，但其錯誤。CloudFront 的 edge IP 範圍並非可供允許清單使用的固定專用位址；它們龐大、共用且會動態變動。CloudFront 會將觀眾導向最近的 edge location 以做快取，但不提供 static IP 允許清單，也不會依客戶地理位置將流量導向最近的來源 Region。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Custom routing accelerators only support Amazon VPC subnet endpoint types and route to private IP addresses within those subnets; they cannot use NLB endpoints. They are designed to deterministically map specific users to specific destinations (e.g., gaming, VoIP, media sessions) rather than to perform health-aware, geography-based routing to the closest Region.","why_zh":"Custom routing accelerator 僅支援 Amazon VPC subnet 端點類型，並將流量導向該 subnet 內的私有 IP；無法使用 NLB 端點。它的設計是將特定使用者確定性地對應到特定目的地（例如遊戲、VoIP、媒體連線），而非執行依健康狀態與地理位置導向最近 Region 的路由。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/global-accelerator/latest/dg/what-is-global-accelerator.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/global-accelerator/latest/dg/about-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/LocationsOfEdgeServers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/high_availability_origin_failover.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":385,"question_en":"A company is running multiple workloads in the AWS Cloud. The company has separate units for software development. The company uses AWS Organizations and federation with SAML to give permissions to developers to manage resources in their AWS accounts. The development units each deploy their production workloads into a common production account. Recently, an incident occurred in the production account in which members of a development unit terminated an EC2 instance that belonged to a different development unit. A solutions architect must create a solution that prevents a similar incident from happening in the future. The solution also must allow developers the possibility to manage the instances used for their workloads. Which strategy will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 云中运行多个工作负载。该公司拥有独立的软件开发部门。该公司使用 AWS Organizations 和 SAML 联合来向开发人 员授予管理其 AWS 账户中资源的权限。每个开发单元都将其生产工作负载部署到一个公共生产帐户中。 最近，生产账户中发生了一起事件，其中开发单元的成员终止了属于不同开发单元的 EC2 实例。解决方案架构师必须创建一个解决 方案，以防止将来发生类似事件。该解决方案还必须允许开发人员能够管理用于其工作负载的实例。 哪种策略可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create separate OUs in AWS Organizations for each development unit. Assign the created OUs to the company AWS accounts. Create separate SCP with a deny action and a StringNotEquals condition for the DevelopmentUnit resource tag that matches the development unit name. Assign the SCP to the corresponding OU.","B":"Pass an attribute for DevelopmentUnit as an AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) session tag during SAML federation. Update the IAM policy for the developers’ assumed IAM role with a deny action and a StringNotEquals condition for the DevelopmentUnit resource tag and aws:PrincipalTag/DevelopmentUnit.","C":"Pass an attribute for DevelopmentUnit as an AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) session tag during SAML federation. Create an SCP with an allow action and a StringEquals condition for the DevelopmentUnit resource tag and aws:PrincipalTag/DevelopmentUnit. Assign the SCP to the root OU.","D":"Create separate IAM policies for each development unit. For every IAM policy, add an allow action and a StringEquals condition for the DevelopmentUnit resource tag and the development unit name. During SAML federation, use AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) to assign the IAM policy and match the development unit name to the assumed IAM role."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS Organizations 中为每个开发单元创建单独的 OU。将创建的 OU 分配给公司 AWS 账户。使用拒绝操作和 StringNotEquals 条件为与开发单元名称匹配的 DevelopmentUnit 资源标记创建单独的 SCP。将 SCP 分配给相应的 OU。","B":"在 SAML 联合期间将 DevelopmentUnit 的属性作为 AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) 会话标签传递。使用 DevelopmentUnit 资 源标签和 aws:PrincipalTag/DevelopmentUnit 的拒绝操作和 StringNotEquals 条件更新开发人员假定的 IAM 角色的 IAM 策略。","C":"在 SAML 联合期间将 DevelopmentUnit 的属性作为 AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) 会话标签传递。为 DevelopmentUnit 资源 标签和 aws:PrincipalTag/DevelopmentUnit 创建一个具有允许操作和 StringEquals 条件的 SCP。将 SCP 分配给根 OU。","D":"为每个开发单元创建单独的 IAM 策略。对于每个 IAM 策略，为 DevelopmentUnit 资源标签和开发单元名称添加允许操作和 StringEquals 条件。在 SAML 联合期间，使用 AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) 分配 IAM 策略并将开发单元名称与假定的 IAM 角色相匹配。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":86},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":386,"question_en":"An enterprise company is building an infrastructure services platform for its users. The company has the following requirements: • Provide least privilege access to users when launching AWS infrastructure so users cannot provision unapproved services. • Use a central account to manage the creation of infrastructure services. • Provide the ability to distribute infrastructure services to multiple accounts in AWS Organizations. • Provide the ability to enforce tags on any infrastructure that is started by users. Which combination of actions using AWS services will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家企业公司正在为其用户构建基础设施服务平台。该公司有以下要求： • 在启动AWS 基础设施时向用户提供最低权限访问权限，以便用户无法配置未经批准的服务。 • 使用中央帐户来管理基础设施服务的创建。 • 提供将基础设施服务分发到AWS Organizations 中的多个账户的能力。 • 提供在用户启动的任何基础设施上强制执行标签的能力。 使用 AWS 服务的哪种操作组合可以满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Develop infrastructure services using AWS CloudFormation templates. Add the templates to a central Amazon S3 bucket and add the IAM roles or users that require access to the S3 bucket policy.","B":"Develop infrastructure services using AWS CloudFormation templates. Upload each template as an AWS Service Catalog product to portfolios created in a central AWS account. Share these portfolios with the Organizations structure created for the company.","C":"Allow user IAM roles to have AWSCloudFormationFullAccess and AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess permissions. Add an Organizations SCP at the AWS account root user level to deny all services except AWS CloudFormation and Amazon S3.","D":"Allow user IAM roles to have ServiceCatalogEndUserAccess permissions only. Use an automation script to import the central portfolios to local AWS accounts, copy the TagOption, assign users access, and apply launch constraints.","E":"Use the AWS Service Catalog TagOption Library to maintain a list of tags required by the company. Apply the TagOption to AWS Service Catalog products or portfolios.","F":"Use the AWS CloudFormation Resource Tags property to enforce the application of tags to any CloudFormation templates that will be created for users."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 模板开发基础设施服务。将模板添加到中央 Amazon S3 存储桶，并添加需要访问 S3 存储桶策略的 IAM 角色或用户。","B":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 模板开发基础设施服务。将每个模板作为 AWS Service Catalog 产品上传到在中央 AWS 账户中创建的 产品组合。与为公司创建的组织结构共享这些投资组合。","C":"允许用户 IAM 角色拥有 AWSCloudFormationFullAccess 和 AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess 权限。在 AWS 账户根用户级别添加组织 SCP 以拒绝除 AWS CloudFormation 和 Amazon S3 之外的所有服务。","D":"允许用户 IAM 角色仅具有 ServiceCatalogEndUserAccess 权限。使用自动化脚本将中央产品组合导入本地 AWS 账户、复制 TagOption、分配用户访问权限并应用启动限制。","E":"使用 AWS Service Catalog TagOption 库维护公司所需的标签列表。将 TagOption 应用于 AWS Service Catalog 产品或产品组合。","F":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 资源标签属性强制将标签应用到将为用户创建的任何 CloudFormation 模板。"},"answer":["B","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BDE":93},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":387,"question_en":"A company deploys a new web application. As part of the setup, the company configures AWS WAF to log to Amazon S3 through Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose. The company develops an Amazon Athena query that runs once daily to return AWS WAF log data from the previous 24 hours. The volume of daily logs is constant. However, over time, the same query is taking more time to run. A solutions architect needs to design a solution to prevent the query time from continuing to increase. The solution must minimize operational overhead. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司部署了一个新的 Web 应用程序。作为设置的一部分，该公司将 AWS WAF 配置为通过 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 登录到 Amazon S3。该公司开发了一个 Amazon Athena 查询，该查询每天运行一次，以返回过去 24 小时内的 AWS WAF 日志数据。每日日志 量是恒定的。然而，随着时间的推移，相同的查询将花费更多的时间来运行。 解决方案架构师需要设计一个解决方案来防止查询时间继续增加。该解决方案必须最大限度地减少运营开销。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function that consolidates each day's AWS WAF logs into one log file.","B":"Reduce the amount of data scanned by configuring AWS WAF to send logs to a different S3 bucket each day.","C":"Update the Kinesis Data Firehose configuration to partition the data in Amazon S3 by date and time. Create external tables for Amazon Redshift. Configure Amazon Redshift Spectrum to query the data source.","D":"Modify the Kinesis Data Firehose configuration and Athena table definition to partition the data by date and time. Change the Athena query to view the relevant partitions."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将每天的 AWS WAF 日志合并到一个日志文件中。","B":"通过配置 AWS WAF 每天将日志发送到不同的 S3 存储桶，减少扫描的数据量。","C":"更新 Kinesis Data Firehose 配置以按日期和时间对 Amazon S3 中的数据进行分区。为 Amazon Redshift 创建外部表。配置 Amazon Redshift Spectrum 以查询数据源。","D":"修改 Kinesis Data Firehose 配置和 Athena 表定义，以按日期和时间对数据进行分区。更改 Athena 查询以查看相关分区。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":388,"question_en":"A company is developing a web application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group behind a public-facing Application Load Balancer (ALB). Only users from a specific country are allowed to access the application. The company needs the ability to log the access requests that have been blocked. The solution should require the least possible maintenance. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在开发一个 Web 应用程序，该应用程序在面向公众的应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面的 Auto Scaling 组中的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。仅允许来自特定国家/地区的用户访问该应用程序。公司需要能够记录已被阻止的访问请求。该解决方案需要尽可能少 的维护。 哪种解决方案满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an IPSet containing a list of IP ranges that belong to the specified country. Create an AWS WAF web ACL. Configure a rule to block any requests that do not originate from an IP range in the IPSet. Associate the rule with the web ACL. Associate the web ACL with the ALB.","B":"Create an AWS WAF web ACL. Configure a rule to block any requests that do not originate from the specified country. Associate the rule with the web ACL. Associate the web ACL with the ALB.","C":"Configure AWS Shield to block any requests that do not originate from the specified country. Associate AWS Shield with the ALB.","D":"Create a security group rule that allows ports 80 and 443 from IP ranges that belong to the specified country. Associate the security group with the ALB."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 IPSet，其中包含属于指定国家/地区的 IP 范围列表。创建 AWS WAF Web ACL。配置规则以阻止并非源自 IPSet 中的 IP 范围的任何请求。将规则与 Web ACL 关联。将 Web ACL 与 ALB 关联。","B":"创建 AWS WAF Web ACL。配置规则以阻止任何并非源自指定国家/地区的请求。将规则与 Web ACL 关联。将 Web ACL 与 ALB 关 联。","C":"配置 AWS Shield 以阻止并非来自指定国家/地区的任何请求。将 AWS Shield 与 ALB 关联。","D":"创建安全组规则，允许属于指定国家/地区的 IP 范围的端口 80 和 443。将安全组与 ALB 关联。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"AWS WAF supports a geographic (geo) match rule statement that manages web requests based on the country of origin. AWS WAF determines a request's country from its IP address using the MaxMind GeoIP database, so you do not have to build or maintain any list of IP ranges. You associate a web ACL containing a geo match rule (configured to block requests not from the allowed country) with the ALB, and AWS WAF logging captures all evaluated requests, including those that are blocked. Because the GeoIP database is managed by AWS, this is the least-maintenance solution that both enforces country-based access and logs blocked requests. Option A also uses WAF but requires you to build and continuously maintain an IPSet of the country's IP ranges, which is far higher maintenance. Shield does not perform country/geo filtering, and security groups cannot log blocked (denied) requests and would require manual IP-range upkeep.","explanation_zh":"AWS WAF 提供地理 (geo) match rule statement，可依據請求的來源國家管理 web 請求。AWS WAF 透過 MaxMind GeoIP 資料庫從請求的 IP 位址判斷來源國家，因此不需要自行建立或維護任何 IP 範圍清單。將包含 geo match rule（設定為封鎖非允許國家的請求）的 web ACL 關聯到 ALB，且 AWS WAF logging 會記錄所有經過評估的請求，包括被封鎖的請求。由於 GeoIP 資料庫由 AWS 管理，這是同時能依國家強制存取控制並記錄被封鎖請求、且維護量最低的方案。選項 A 同樣使用 WAF，但需自行建立並持續維護該國家 IP 範圍的 IPSet，維護成本高出許多。Shield 不提供國家/地理過濾功能；security group 無法記錄被封鎖（拒絕）的請求，且需手動維護 IP 範圍。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Technically works with WAF but requires you to build and continuously maintain an IPSet of all IP ranges for the country, which is high maintenance and error-prone. A geo match statement (option B) achieves the same result with no list to maintain.","why_zh":"技術上可用 WAF 達成，但需自行建立並持續維護該國家所有 IP 範圍的 IPSet，維護量高且易出錯。geo match statement（選項 B）可在無需維護清單的情況下達成相同結果。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Shield is a DDoS protection service. It does not perform country-based (geo) request filtering and cannot block requests by country of origin; that capability belongs to AWS WAF.","why_zh":"AWS Shield 是 DDoS 防護服務，不提供以國家為基礎 (geo) 的請求過濾，無法依來源國家封鎖請求；該功能屬於 AWS WAF。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Security groups cannot filter by country and cannot log blocked/denied requests (security groups have no deny logging). You would also have to manually maintain the country's IP ranges, which is high maintenance and fails the logging requirement.","why_zh":"Security group 無法依國家過濾，也無法記錄被封鎖/拒絕的請求（security group 無拒絕記錄功能）。此外仍需手動維護該國家的 IP 範圍，維護量高且不滿足記錄需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-geo-match.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/web-acl.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":389,"question_en":"A company is migrating an application from on-premises infrastructure to the AWS Cloud. During migration design meetings, the company expressed concerns about the availability and recovery options for its legacy Windows file server. The file server contains sensitive business- critical data that cannot be recreated in the event of data corruption or data loss. According to compliance requirements, the data must not travel across the public internet. The company wants to move to AWS managed services where possible. The company decides to store the data in an Amazon FSx for Windows File Server file system. A solutions architect must design a solution that copies the data to another AWS Region for disaster recovery (DR) purposes. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在将应用程序从本地基础设施迁移到 AWS 云。在迁移设计会议期间，该公司对其旧版 Windows 文件服务器的可用性和恢 复选项表示担忧。文件服务器包含敏感的关键业务数据，这些数据在数据损坏或丢失时无法重新创建。根据合规要求，数据不得通 过公共互联网传输。该公司希望尽可能转向 AWS 托管服务。 该公司决定将数据存储在 Amazon FSx for Windows File Server 文件系统中。解决方案架构师必须设计一种解决方案，将数据复制到另 一个 AWS 区域以实现灾难恢复 (DR) 目的。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a destination Amazon S3 bucket in the DR Region. Establish connectivity between the FSx for Windows File Server file system in the primary Region and the S3 bucket in the DR Region by using Amazon FSx File Gateway. Configure the S3 bucket as a continuous backup source in FSx File Gateway.","B":"Create an FSx for Windows File Server file system in the DR Region. Establish connectivity between the VPC the primary Region and the VPC in the DR Region by using AWS Site-to-Site VPN. Configure AWS DataSync to communicate by using VPN endpoints.","C":"Create an FSx for Windows File Server file system in the DR Region. Establish connectivity between the VPC in the primary Region and the VPC in the DR Region by using VPC peering. Configure AWS DataSync to communicate by using interface VPC endpoints with AWS PrivateLink.","D":"Create an FSx for Windows File Server file system in the DR Region. Establish connectivity between the VPC in the primary Region and the VPC in the DR Region by using AWS Transit Gateway in each Region. Use AWS Transfer Family to copy files between the FSx for Windows File Server file system in the primary Region and the FSx for Windows File Server file system in the DR Region over the private AWS backbone network."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 DR 区域中创建目标 Amazon S3 存储桶。使用 Amazon FSx File Gateway 在主区域中的 FSx for Windows File Server 文件系统与 DR 区域中的 S3 存储桶之间建立连接。将 S3 存储桶配置为 FSx 文件网关中的连续备份源。","B":"在 DR 区域中创建 FSx for Windows 文件服务器文件系统。使用 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 在主要区域的 VPC 与 DR 区域中的 VPC 之间 建立连接。配置 AWS DataSync 以使用 VPN 终端节点进行通信。","C":"在 DR 区域中创建 FSx for Windows 文件服务器文件系统。通过使用 VPC 对等互连在主区域中的 VPC 和 DR 区域中的 VPC 之间 建立连接。将 AWS DataSync 配置为使用接口 VPC 终端节点与 AWS PrivateLink 进行通信。","D":"在 DR 区域中创建 FSx for Windows 文件服务器文件系统。使用每个区域中的 AWS Transit Gateway 在主要区域中的 VPC 与 DR 区 域中的 VPC 之间建立连接。使用 AWS Transfer Family 通过私有 AWS 主干网络在主要区域中的 FSx for Windows File Server 文件系统 和 DR 区域中的 FSx for Windows File Server 文件系统之间复制文件。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":82,"A":18},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":390,"question_en":"A company is currently in the design phase of an application that will need an RPO of less than 5 minutes and an RTO of less than 10 minutes. The solutions architecture team is forecasting that the database will store approximately 10 TB of data. As part of the design, they are looking for a database solution that will provide the company with the ability to fail over to a secondary Region. Which solution will meet these business requirements at the LOWEST cost?","question_zh":"一家公司目前正处于应用程序的设计阶段，该应用程序需要少于 5 分钟的 RPO 和少于 10 分钟的 RTO。解决方案架构团队预测该数 据库将存储大约 10 TB 的数据。作为设计的一部分，他们正在寻找一种数据库解决方案，该解决方案将为公司提供故障转移到辅助 区域的能力。 哪种解决方案能够以最低的成本满足这些业务需求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an Amazon Aurora DB cluster and take snapshots of the cluster every 5 minutes. Once a snapshot is complete, copy the snapshot to a secondary Region to serve as a backup in the event of a failure.","B":"Deploy an Amazon RDS instance with a cross-Region read replica in a secondary Region. In the event of a failure, promote the read replica to become the primary.","C":"Deploy an Amazon Aurora DB cluster in the primary Region and another in a secondary Region. Use AWS DMS to keep the secondary Region in sync.","D":"Deploy an Amazon RDS instance with a read replica in the same Region. In the event of a failure, promote the read replica to become the primary."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署 Amazon Aurora 数据库集群并每 5 分钟拍摄一次集群快照。快照完成后，将快照复制到辅助区域，以在出现故障时作为备 份。","B":"在辅助区域中部署具有跨区域只读副本的 Amazon RDS 实例。如果发生故障，请将只读副本提升为主副本。","C":"在主要区域中部署一个 Amazon Aurora 数据库集群，在次要区域中部署另一个 Amazon Aurora 数据库集群。使用 AWS DMS 使次 要区域保持同步。","D":"在同一区域中部署具有只读副本的 Amazon RDS 实例。如果发生故障，请将只读副本提升为主副本。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":86},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Database","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":391,"question_en":"A financial company needs to create a separate AWS account for a new digital wallet application. The company uses AWS Organizations to manage its accounts. A solutions architect uses the IAM user Support1 from the management account to create a new member account with finance1@example.com as the email address. What should the solutions architect do to create IAM users in the new member account?","question_zh":"一家金融公司需要为新的数字钱包应用程序创建单独的 AWS 账户。该公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理其账户。解决方案架构师使 用管理账户中的 IAM 用户 Support1 创建一个新的成员账户，并将Finance1@example.com作为电子邮件地址。 解决方案架构师应该如何在新成员账户中创建 IAM 用户？","options_en":{"A":"Sign in to the AWS Management Console with AWS account root user credentials by using the 64-character password from the initial AWS Organizations email sent to finance1@example.com. Set up the IAM users as required.","B":"From the management account, switch roles to assume the OrganizationAccountAccessRole role with the account ID of the new member account. Set up the IAM users as required.","C":"Go to the AWS Management Console sign-in page. Choose “Sign in using root account credentials.” Sign in in by using the email address finance 1@example.com and the management account's root password. Set up the IAM users as required.","D":"Go to the AWS Management Console sign-in page. Sign in by using the account ID of the new member account and the Support1 IAM credentials. Set up the IAM users as required."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用发送到Finance1@example.com的初始 AWS Organizations 电子邮件中的 64 个字符的密码，通过 AWS 账户根用户凭证登录 AWS 管理控制台。根据需要设置 IAM 用户。","B":"从管理帐户中，切换角色以使用新成员帐户的帐户 ID 承担 OrganizationAccountAccessRole 角色。根据需要设置 IAM 用户。","C":"转到 AWS 管理控制台登录页面。选择“使用根帐户凭据登录”。使用电子邮件地址 Finance 1@example.com和管理帐户的 root 密 码登录。根据需要设置 IAM 用户。","D":"转到 AWS 管理控制台登录页面。使用新成员账户的账户 ID 和 Support1 IAM 凭证登录。根据需要设置 IAM 用户。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":81,"D":19},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"When AWS Organizations creates a member account, it automatically provisions the IAM role OrganizationAccountAccessRole in that account, granting full administrative control to principals in the management account. The documented way to administer the new account (including creating IAM users) is to sign in to the management account and switch roles / assume OrganizationAccountAccessRole using the new member account's account ID. Option A is technically false: Organizations does not email a '64-character root password' for created member accounts; the root user has no password set and would require the password-reset flow, and AWS recommends against using root. Option C is wrong because the management account's root password cannot authenticate the member account's separate root user (finance1@example.com). Option D is wrong because the Support1 IAM user exists only in the management account; IAM users are account-scoped and cannot sign in directly to a different account—cross-account access requires assuming a role, which is exactly what B does.","explanation_zh":"當 AWS Organizations 建立成員帳戶時，會自動在該帳戶中建立 IAM 角色 OrganizationAccountAccessRole，授予 management account 中的主體完整管理控制權。對新帳戶進行管理（包括建立 IAM users）的官方做法，是以 management account 登入後使用新成員帳戶的 account ID 切換角色（assume OrganizationAccountAccessRole）。選項 A 在技術上是錯誤的：Organizations 不會以電子郵件寄送『64 字元 root 密碼』給所建立的成員帳戶；該 root user 並未設定密碼，需走密碼重設流程，且 AWS 建議避免使用 root。選項 C 錯誤，因為 management account 的 root 密碼無法驗證成員帳戶獨立的 root user（finance1@example.com）。選項 D 錯誤，因為 Support1 IAM user 只存在於 management account；IAM users 是帳戶範圍的，無法直接登入另一個帳戶，跨帳戶存取必須透過 assume role，這正是 B 所描述的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Organizations does not send a '64-character root password' in the account-creation email. For accounts created via Organizations, the root user password is not set; you would need the password-reset (forgot password) flow, and AWS explicitly recommends not using root for daily tasks.","why_zh":"AWS Organizations 不會在帳戶建立電子郵件中寄送『64 字元 root 密碼』。透過 Organizations 建立的帳戶其 root user 未設定密碼，需走密碼重設流程；且 AWS 明確建議勿用 root 進行日常工作。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The management account's root password cannot authenticate the member account's root user. Each AWS account has its own independent root credentials tied to its unique email address.","why_zh":"management account 的 root 密碼無法驗證成員帳戶的 root user。每個 AWS 帳戶都有與其唯一電子郵件繫結的獨立 root 憑證。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The Support1 IAM user exists only in the management account. IAM users are account-scoped, so its credentials cannot sign in directly to the new member account; cross-account administration is achieved by assuming OrganizationAccountAccessRole (option B), not by entering management-account IAM credentials at the member-account sign-in.","why_zh":"Support1 IAM user 只存在於 management account。IAM users 屬帳戶範圍，其憑證無法直接登入新成員帳戶；跨帳戶管理是透過 assume OrganizationAccountAccessRole（選項 B）達成，而非在成員帳戶登入頁輸入 management account 的 IAM 憑證。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_access-cross-account-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_access.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":392,"question_en":"A car rental company has built a serverless REST API to provide data to its mobile app. The app consists of an Amazon API Gateway API with a Regional endpoint, AWS Lambda functions, and an Amazon Aurora MySQL Serverless DB cluster. The company recently opened the API to mobile apps of partners. A significant increase in the number of requests resulted, causing sporadic database memory errors. Analysis of the API tra®c indicates that clients are making multiple HTTP GET requests for the same queries in a short period of time. Tra®c is concentrated during business hours, with spikes around holidays and other events. The company needs to improve its ability to support the additional usage while minimizing the increase in costs associated with the solution. Which strategy meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家汽车租赁公司构建了一个无服务器 REST API 来为其移动应用程序提供数据。该应用程序由具有区域终端节点的 Amazon API Gateway API、AWS Lambda 函数和 Amazon Aurora MySQL Serverless 数据库集群组成。该公司最近向合作伙伴的移动应用程序开放了 API。结果请求数量显着增加，导致偶发的数据库内存错误。 对 API 流量的分析表明，客户端在短时间内对同一查询发出多个 HTTP GET 请求。流量集中在工作时间，节假日和其他活动期间流量 高峰。 该公司需要提高支持额外使用的能力，同时最大限度地减少与解决方案相关的成本增加。 哪种策略可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Convert the API Gateway Regional endpoint to an edge-optimized endpoint. Enable caching in the production stage.","B":"Implement an Amazon ElastiCache for Redis cache to store the results of the database calls. Modify the Lambda functions to use the cache.","C":"Modify the Aurora Serverless DB cluster configuration to increase the maximum amount of available memory.","D":"Enable throttling in the API Gateway production stage. Set the rate and burst values to limit the incoming calls."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 API Gateway 区域终端节点转换为边缘优化终端节点。在生产阶段启用缓存。","B":"实施 Amazon ElastiCache for Redis 缓存来存储数据库调用的结果。修改 Lambda 函数以使用缓存。","C":"修改 Aurora Serverless 数据库集群配置以增加最大可用内存量。","D":"在 API Gateway 生产阶段启用节流。设置速率和突发值以限制来电。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":55,"A":45},"tags":["Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The symptom is clients making repeated HTTP GET requests for the same queries, causing redundant load that exhausts Aurora memory. The requirement is to support more usage while minimizing added cost. Amazon API Gateway stage caching is purpose-built for this: when enabled on a stage, only GET methods are cached by default, and API Gateway serves the cached response instead of invoking the backend, eliminating the duplicate Lambda-to-Aurora calls before they reach the database. It is a configuration toggle (no code changes), charged hourly by cache size, making it the lowest-effort and lowest-cost fit. The 'convert to edge-optimized' clause in option A is technically unnecessary (stage caching also works on Regional endpoints) but is benign and the load-bearing action 'Enable caching in the production stage' is correct. Option B (ElastiCache for Redis) also solves the problem but requires running a dedicated cluster 24/7, rewriting Lambda code, and managing cache logic, which is more operationally heavy and costlier, so it loses on the 'minimize cost' qualifier.","explanation_zh":"問題症狀是用戶端在短時間內對相同查詢重複發出 HTTP GET 請求，造成冗餘負載並耗盡 Aurora 記憶體。需求是在最小化成本增加的前提下支援更多用量。Amazon API Gateway 階段快取正是為此設計：在 stage 啟用快取後，預設只有 GET 方法被快取，API Gateway 會直接回傳快取結果而不呼叫後端，從而在請求到達資料庫之前就消除重複的 Lambda 到 Aurora 呼叫。這是一個設定切換（無需改程式碼），按快取容量每小時計費，是最省工、最省成本的方案。選項 A 中「轉為 edge-optimized」一句技術上並非必要（Regional 端點同樣支援階段快取），但無害，而真正關鍵的動作「在 production stage 啟用快取」是正確的。選項 B（ElastiCache for Redis）雖也能解決問題，但需 24/7 運行專用叢集、改寫 Lambda 程式碼並管理快取邏輯，營運負擔與成本更高，在「最小化成本」這個限定條件下落敗。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"ElastiCache for Redis solves the duplicate-query problem but requires provisioning a dedicated cluster running continuously, modifying Lambda code to read/write the cache, managing TTL/invalidation, and VPC networking. This is the most operationally heavy and costliest option, conflicting with the 'minimize increase in costs' requirement; native API Gateway GET caching intercepts duplicates even earlier (before Lambda runs) with zero code changes.","why_zh":"ElastiCache for Redis 雖能解決重複查詢問題，但需佈建一個持續運行的專用叢集、改寫 Lambda 程式碼以讀寫快取、管理 TTL 與失效、並處理 VPC 網路。這是營運負擔與成本最高的選項，與「最小化成本增加」需求衝突；原生的 API Gateway GET 快取能更早（在 Lambda 執行前）攔截重複請求且無需改程式碼。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Increasing Aurora Serverless maximum memory/capacity treats the symptom by throwing more expensive compute at redundant identical queries. It directly increases cost (the opposite of the requirement) and never addresses the root cause of duplicate GET requests. This is the dump's suggested answer and is wrong.","why_zh":"提高 Aurora Serverless 最大記憶體/容量只是用更昂貴的運算去硬撐冗餘的相同查詢。它直接增加成本（與需求相反），且完全沒有解決重複 GET 請求的根本原因。這是題庫建議答案，但是錯的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Enabling throttling rejects or limits legitimate partner requests, degrading the very service the company just opened to partners rather than supporting the additional usage. It does not reduce database load from cacheable repeated queries; it merely drops traffic, failing the 'support additional usage' goal.","why_zh":"啟用節流會拒絕或限制合法的合作夥伴請求，等於削弱公司剛開放給夥伴的服務，而非支援額外用量。它無法降低可快取重複查詢造成的資料庫負載，只是丟棄流量，無法達成「支援額外用量」的目標。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/api-gateway-caching.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/api-gateway-api-endpoint-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/set-up-stages.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":393,"question_en":"A company is migrating an on-premises application and a MySQL database to AWS. The application processes highly sensitive data, and new data is constantly updated in the database. The data must not be transferred over the internet. The company also must encrypt the data in transit and at rest. The database is 5 TB in size. The company already has created the database schema in an Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance. The company has set up a 1 Gbps AWS Direct Connect connection to AWS. The company also has set up a public VIF and a private VIF. A solutions architect needs to design a solution that will migrate the data to AWS with the least possible downtime. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在将本地应用程序和 MySQL 数据库迁移到 AWS。应用程序处理高度敏感的数据，新数据在数据库中不断更新。数据不得 通过互联网传输。公司还必须对传输中和静态的数据进行加密。 该数据库大小为 5 TB。该公司已在 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库实例中创建了数据库架构。该公司已建立与 AWS 的 1 Gbps AWS Direct Connect 连接。该公司还设立了公共 VIF 和私人 VIF。解决方案架构师需要设计一种解决方案，以尽可能少的停机时间将数据 迁移到 AWS。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Perform a database backup. Copy the backup files to an AWS Snowball Edge Storage Optimized device. Import the backup to Amazon S3. Use server-side encryption with Amazon S3 managed encryption keys (SSE-S3) for encryption at rest. Use TLS for encryption in transit. Import the data from Amazon S3 to the DB instance.","B":"Use AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to migrate the data to AWS. Create a DMS replication instance in a private subnet. Create VPC endpoints for AWS DMS. Configure a DMS task to copy data from the on-premises database to the DB instance by using full load plus change data capture (CDC). Use the AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) default key for encryption at rest. Use TLS for encryption in transit.","C":"Perform a database backup. Use AWS DataSync to transfer the backup files to Amazon S3. Use server-side encryption with Amazon S3 managed encryption keys (SSE-S3) for encryption at rest. Use TLS for encryption in transit. Import the data from Amazon S3 to the DB instance.","D":"Use Amazon S3 File Gateway. Set up a private connection to Amazon S3 by using AWS PrivateLink. Perform a database backup. Copy the backup files to Amazon S3. Use server-side encryption with Amazon S3 managed encryption keys (SSE-S3) for encryption at rest. Use TLS for encryption in transit. Import the data from Amazon S3 to the DB instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"执行数据库备份。将备份文件复制到 AWS Snowball Edge Storage Optimized 设备。将备份导入到 Amazon S3。使用服务器端加密 和 Amazon S3 托管加密密钥 (SSE-S3) 进行静态加密。使用 TLS 进行传输加密。将数据从 Amazon S3 导入到数据库实例。","B":"使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 将数据迁移到 AWS。在私有子网中创建 DMS 复制实例。为 AWS DMS 创建 VPC 终端节点。配置 DMS 任务以使用完全加载加更改数据捕获 (CDC) 将数据从本地数据库复制到数据库实例。使用 AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) 默认密钥进行静态加密。使用 TLS 进行传输加密。","C":"执行数据库备份。使用 AWS DataSync 将备份文件传输到 Amazon S3。使用服务器端加密和 Amazon S3 托管加密密钥 (SSE-S3) 进行静态加密。使用 TLS 进行传输加密。将数据从 Amazon S3 导入到数据库实例。","D":"使用 Amazon S3 文件网关。使用 AWS PrivateLink 设置与 Amazon S3 的私有连接。执行数据库备份。将备份文件复制到 Amazon S3。使用服务器端加密和 Amazon S3 托管加密密钥 (SSE-S3) 进行静态加密。使用 TLS 进行传输加密。将数据从 Amazon S3 导入到 数据库实例。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Security/IAM","Storage","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifiers are 'least possible downtime' combined with 'new data is constantly updated' and 'data must not be transferred over the internet.' Only AWS DMS with full load plus change data capture (CDC) keeps the source database online and continuously replicates ongoing changes, so the cutover can occur with near-zero downtime. By placing the DMS replication instance in a private subnet and using VPC endpoints together with the existing Direct Connect private VIF, all traffic stays off the public internet. DMS satisfies the encryption requirements: AWS KMS provides encryption at rest and SSL/TLS provides encryption in transit (AWS Config even has a managed rule, dms-endpoint-ssl-configured, that enforces SSL/TLS on endpoints). Options A, C, and D all rely on a one-time static database backup, which freezes data at backup time; transferring and importing 5 TB takes a long time, during which constantly updated data would be lost or would require extended downtime to keep the source quiesced, so they cannot meet the minimal-downtime requirement.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定條件是「儘可能最短的停機時間」加上「資料持續更新」以及「資料不得透過網際網路傳輸」。只有 AWS DMS 搭配 full load plus change data capture (CDC) 才能讓來源資料庫保持上線並持續複製進行中的變更，因此切換時可達到接近零停機。將 DMS replication instance 放在 private subnet 並使用 VPC endpoints，再搭配既有的 Direct Connect private VIF，所有流量都不會經過公共網際網路。DMS 也滿足加密需求：AWS KMS 提供靜態加密，SSL/TLS 提供傳輸中加密（AWS Config 甚至有 dms-endpoint-ssl-configured 管理規則強制 endpoint 使用 SSL/TLS）。選項 A、C、D 都依賴一次性的靜態資料庫備份，會在備份當下凍結資料；傳輸與匯入 5 TB 需要很長時間，期間持續更新的資料將遺失，或需要長時間凍結來源以避免遺失，因此無法滿足最短停機需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Snowball Edge plus a one-time backup freezes data at a point in time and offers no mechanism to capture changes made while the 5 TB is shipped, imported, and loaded, so constantly updated data is lost and downtime is large; it also defeats the purpose of the already-provisioned Direct Connect link.","why_zh":"Snowball Edge 加一次性備份會在某一時間點凍結資料，無法捕捉在 5 TB 運送、匯入與載入期間發生的變更，因此持續更新的資料會遺失且停機時間很長；同時也未利用已建置的 Direct Connect 連線。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but is wrong: DataSync transferring a static backup is still a one-time copy with no CDC, so ongoing updates are lost and the cutover requires the source to stay frozen during the lengthy transfer/import of 5 TB, failing the least-downtime requirement.","why_zh":"這是題庫建議答案但錯誤：DataSync 傳輸靜態備份仍是一次性複製且無 CDC，進行中的更新會遺失，且切換需要在漫長的 5 TB 傳輸/匯入期間凍結來源，無法滿足最短停機需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 File Gateway with PrivateLink plus a one-time backup is again a static snapshot with no ongoing change capture; the lengthy transfer and import of 5 TB means constantly updated data is lost or requires extended downtime, so it does not minimize downtime.","why_zh":"S3 File Gateway 搭配 PrivateLink 加一次性備份同樣是靜態快照，無法持續捕捉變更；5 TB 的漫長傳輸與匯入意味著持續更新的資料會遺失或需要長時間停機，因此無法將停機降到最低。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/dms/latest/userguide/dm-network.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/dms/latest/userguide/CHAP_VPC_Endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/dms/latest/userguide/CHAP_BestPractices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/dms-endpoint-ssl-configured.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":394,"question_en":"Accompany is deploying a new cluster for big data analytics on AWS. The cluster will run across many Linux Amazon EC2 instances that are spread across multiple Availability Zones. All of the nodes in the cluster must have read and write access to common underlying file storage. The file storage must be highly available, must be resilient, must be compatible with the Portable Operating System Interface (POSIX), and must accommodate high levels of throughput. Which storage solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"Accompany 正在 AWS 上部署一个用于大数据分析的新集群。该集群将在分布于多个可用区的许多 Linux Amazon EC2 实例上运行。 集群中的所有节点都必须具有对公共底层文件存储的读写访问权限。文件存储必须具有高可用性、必须具有弹性、必须与便携式操 作系统接口 (POSIX) 兼容，并且必须适应高水平的吞吐量。 哪种存储解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Provision an AWS Storage Gateway file gateway NFS file share that is attached to an Amazon S3 bucket. Mount the NFS file share on each EC2 instance in the cluster.","B":"Provision a new Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system that uses General Purpose performance mode. Mount the EFS file system on each EC2 instance in the cluster.","C":"Provision a new Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume that uses the io2 volume type. Attach the EBS volume to all of the EC2 instances in the cluster.","D":"Provision a new Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system that uses Max I/O performance mode. Mount the EFS file system on each EC2 instance in the cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置附加到 Amazon S3 存储桶的 AWS Storage Gateway 文件网关 NFS 文件共享。在集群中的每个 EC2 实例上挂载 NFS 文件共 享。","B":"预置一个使用通用性能模式的新 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统。在集群中的每个 EC2 实例上挂载 EFS 文件 系统。","C":"配置一个使用 io2 卷类型的新 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 卷。将 EBS 卷附加到集群中的所有 EC2 实例。","D":"预置一个使用最大 I/O 性能模式的新 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统。在集群中的每个 EC2 实例上挂载 EFS 文件系统。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":71,"B":28},"tags":["Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":395,"question_en":"A company hosts a software as a service (SaaS) solution on AWS. The solution has an Amazon API Gateway API that serves an HTTPS endpoint. The API uses AWS Lambda functions for compute. The Lambda functions store data in an Amazon Aurora Serverless v1 database. The company used the AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) to deploy the solution. The solution extends across multiple Availability Zones and has no disaster recovery (DR) plan. A solutions architect must design a DR strategy that can recover the solution in another AWS Region. The solution has an RTO of 5 minutes and an RPO of 1 minute. What should the solutions architect do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上托管软件即服务 (SaaS) 解决方案。该解决方案有一个为 HTTPS 终端节点提供服务的 Amazon API Gateway API。该 API 使用 AWS Lambda 函数进行计算。Lambda 函数将数据存储在 Amazon Aurora Serverless v1 数据库中。 该公司使用 AWS 无服务器应用程序模型 (AWS SAM) 来部署该解决方案。该解决方案跨越多个可用区，并且没有灾难恢复 (DR) 计划。 解决方案架构师必须设计一个可以在另一个 AWS 区域恢复解决方案的灾难恢复策略。该解决方案的 RTO 为 5 分钟，RPO 为 1 分钟。 解决方案架构师应该怎样做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a read replica of the Aurora Serverless v1 database in the target Region. Use AWS SAM to create a runbook to deploy the solution to the target Region. Promote the read replica to primary in case of disaster.","B":"Change the Aurora Serverless v1 database to a standard Aurora MySQL global database that extends across the source Region and the target Region. Use AWS SAM to create a runbook to deploy the solution to the target Region.","C":"Create an Aurora Serverless v1 DB cluster that has multiple writer instances in the target Region. Launch the solution in the target Region. Configure the two Regional solutions to work in an active-passive configuration.","D":"Change the Aurora Serverless v1 database to a standard Aurora MySQL global database that extends across the source Region and the target Region. Launch the solution in the target Region. Configure the two Regional solutions to work in an active-passive configuration."},"options_zh":{"A":"在目标区域中创建 Aurora Serverless v1 数据库的只读副本。使用 AWS SAM 创建 Runbook 以将解决方案部署到目标区域。在发 生灾难时将只读副本提升为主副本。","B":"将 Aurora Serverless v1 数据库更改为跨源区域和目标区域的标准 Aurora MySQL 全局数据库。使用 AWS SAM 创建 Runbook 以将 解决方案部署到目标区域。","C":"创建一个在目标区域中具有多个写入器实例的 Aurora Serverless v1 数据库集群。在目标区域启动解决方案。将两个区域解决方 案配置为在主动-被动配置中工作。","D":"将 Aurora Serverless v1 数据库更改为跨源区域和目标区域延伸的标准 Aurora MySQL 全局数据库。在目标区域启动解决方案。 将两个区域解决方案配置为在主动-被动配置中工作。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":93},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The RTO is 5 minutes and RPO is 1 minute, recovering in another Region. Aurora Serverless v1 cannot have cross-Region read replicas and is not compatible with Aurora Global Database, which is exactly why both surviving options (B and D) convert the database to a standard Aurora MySQL global database. An Aurora global database replicates with sub-second latency, giving an RPO measured in seconds and an RTO in minutes, comfortably satisfying RPO 1 min. The deciding factor between B and D is the application (API Gateway + Lambda) recovery approach. Option B only stores a SAM runbook and deploys the application to the target Region at disaster time; deploying a SAM/CloudFormation stack is a control-plane operation that takes time and, per the AWS DR whitepaper, this deploy-on-demand (backup-and-restore) model leads to increased recovery times that may exceed the RTO. Option D pre-launches the solution in the target Region in an active-passive (warm standby) configuration, so failover is just promoting the global database secondary and shifting traffic, achieving an RTO well within 5 minutes. Therefore D is the only option that reliably meets both the 5-minute RTO and 1-minute RPO.","explanation_zh":"需求為 RTO 5 分鐘、RPO 1 分鐘，並要在另一個 Region 復原。Aurora Serverless v1 無法建立跨 Region 唯讀複本，也不相容於 Aurora Global Database，這正是 B 與 D 兩個選項都要把資料庫改成標準 Aurora MySQL global database 的原因。Aurora global database 以低於一秒的延遲複寫，RPO 以秒計、RTO 以分鐘計，足以滿足 1 分鐘 RPO。B 與 D 的關鍵差異在於應用層（API Gateway + Lambda）的復原方式。B 只保存 SAM runbook，等災難發生時才把應用部署到目標 Region；部署 SAM/CloudFormation 堆疊屬於 control-plane 操作且需要時間，依 AWS DR 白皮書，此種按需部署（backup-and-restore）模式會拉長復原時間，可能超出 RTO。D 事先在目標 Region 以 active-passive（warm standby）方式啟動方案，故障轉移時只需提升 global database 的 secondary 並切換流量，RTO 可穩定落在 5 分鐘內。因此只有 D 能可靠地同時滿足 5 分鐘 RTO 與 1 分鐘 RPO。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Aurora Serverless v1 does not support cross-Region read replicas, so creating one in the target Region is not possible. It also relies on a SAM runbook deployed only at disaster time, which is a backup-and-restore model that risks exceeding the 5-minute RTO.","why_zh":"Aurora Serverless v1 不支援跨 Region 唯讀複本，因此無法在目標 Region 建立複本。它也只在災難時才用 SAM runbook 部署，屬 backup-and-restore 模式，恐超出 5 分鐘 RTO。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Aurora Serverless v1 does not support multiple writer instances (no multi-master), and Serverless v1 cannot span Regions or be made cross-Region. The configuration described is technically impossible.","why_zh":"Aurora Serverless v1 不支援多個 writer 實例（無 multi-master），且 Serverless v1 無法跨 Region。所述配置在技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"It correctly converts to an Aurora MySQL global database (good RPO), but the application is only deployed via a SAM runbook at disaster time. Deploying a SAM/CloudFormation stack is a slow control-plane operation; this deploy-on-demand approach risks exceeding the strict 5-minute RTO, unlike a pre-launched active-passive standby.","why_zh":"它正確地改用 Aurora MySQL global database（RPO 良好），但應用只在災難時透過 SAM runbook 部署。部署 SAM/CloudFormation 堆疊屬較慢的 control-plane 操作；此按需部署方式恐超出嚴格的 5 分鐘 RTO，不如事先啟動的 active-passive standby。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database-disaster-recovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/disaster-recovery-workloads-on-aws/disaster-recovery-options-in-the-cloud.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/reliability-pillar/plan-for-disaster-recovery-dr.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":396,"question_en":"A company owns a chain of travel agencies and is running an application in the AWS Cloud. Company employees use the application to search for information about travel destinations. Destination content is updated four times each year. Two fixed Amazon EC2 instances serve the application. The company uses an Amazon Route 53 public hosted zone with a multivalue record of travel.example.com that returns the Elastic IP addresses for the EC2 instances. The application uses Amazon DynamoDB as its primary data store. The company uses a self-hosted Redis instance as a caching solution. During content updates, the load on the EC2 instances and the caching solution increases drastically. This increased load has led to downtime on several occasions. A solutions architect must update the application so that the application is highly available and can handle the load that is generated by the content updates. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一系列旅行社，并在 AWS 云中运行一个应用程序。公司员工使用该应用程序搜索有关旅行目的地的信息。目的地内容 每年更新四次。 两个固定的 Amazon EC2 实例为该应用程序提供服务。该公司使用 Amazon Route 53 公共托管区域，该区域具有 Travel.example.com 的多值记录，该记录返回 EC2 实例的弹性 IP 地址。该应用程序使用 Amazon DynamoDB 作为其主要数据存储。该公司使用自托管的 Redis 实例作为缓存解决方案。 在内容更新期间，EC2 实例和缓存解决方案的负载急剧增加。负载的增加多次导致停机。解决方案架构师必须更新应用程序，以便 应用程序具有高可用性，并且可以处理内容更新生成的负载。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) as in-memory cache. Update the application to use DAX. Create an Auto Scaling group for the EC2 instances. Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Set the Auto Scaling group as a target for the ALB. Update the Route 53 record to use a simple routing policy that targets the ALB's DNS alias. Configure scheduled scaling for the EC2 instances before the content updates.","B":"Set up Amazon ElastiCache for Redis. Update the application to use ElastiCache. Create an Auto Scaling group for the EC2 instances. Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution, and set the Auto Scaling group as an origin for the distribution. Update the Route 53 record to use a simple routing policy that targets the CloudFront distribution’s DNS alias. Manually scale up EC2 instances before the content updates.","C":"Set up Amazon ElastiCache for Memcached. Update the application to use ElastiCache. Create an Auto Scaling group for the EC2 instances. Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Set the Auto Scaling group as a target for the ALB. Update the Route 53 record to use a simple routing policy that targets the ALB's DNS alias. Configure scheduled scaling for the application before the content updates.","D":"Set up DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) as in-memory cache. Update the application to use DAX. Create an Auto Scaling group for the EC2 instances. Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution, and set the Auto Scaling group as an origin for the distribution. Update the Route 53 record to use a simple routing policy that targets the CloudFront distribution's DNS alias. Manually scale up EC2 instances before the content updates."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) 设置为内存缓存。更新应用程序以使用 DAX。为 EC2 实例创建 Auto Scaling 组。创建应用程序负 载均衡器 (ALB)。将 Auto Scaling 组设置为 ALB 的目标。更新 Route 53 记录以使用针对 ALB 的 DNS 别名的简单路由策略。在内容 更新之前配置 EC2 实例的计划扩展。","B":"设置适用于 Redis 的 Amazon ElastiCache。更新应用程序以使用 ElastiCache。为 EC2 实例创建 Auto Scaling 组。创建 Amazon CloudFront 分配，并将 Auto Scaling 组设置为分配的源。更新 Route 53 记录以使用针对 CloudFront 分配的 DNS 别名的简单路由策 略。在内容更新之前手动扩展 EC2 实例。","C":"为 Memcached 设置 Amazon ElastiCache。更新应用程序以使用 ElastiCache。为 EC2 实例创建 Auto Scaling 组。创建应用程序负 载均衡器 (ALB)。将 Auto Scaling 组设置为 ALB 的目标。更新 Route 53 记录以使用针对 ALB 的 DNS 别名的简单路由策略。在内容 更新之前配置应用程序的计划缩放。","D":"将 DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) 设置为内存缓存。更新应用程序以使用 DAX。为 EC2 实例创建 Auto Scaling 组。创建 Amazon CloudFront 分配，并将 Auto Scaling 组设置为分配的源。更新 Route 53 记录以使用针对 CloudFront 分配的 DNS 别名的简单路由策 略。在内容更新之前手动扩展 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":98},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The app stores data in DynamoDB and fronts it with a self-hosted Redis cache; loads spike during predictable, scheduled content updates (4x/year) and must be highly available. DAX is the purpose-built, fully managed, Multi-AZ, DynamoDB-API-compatible in-memory cache, ideal for read-heavy/bursty workloads and requiring minimal application changes, so it directly replaces the self-hosted Redis tier. An Application Load Balancer with the Auto Scaling group as its target is the correct HA front door for an EC2 web tier, and a Route 53 simple alias to the ALB replaces the brittle multivalue Elastic IP record. Because content updates occur on a known schedule, scheduled scaling is the AWS-recommended mechanism for predictable, time-based load changes, ensuring capacity is in place before the spike. Option A is the only choice combining all three best practices (DAX + ALB + scheduled scaling).","explanation_zh":"應用程式以 DynamoDB 為主要資料儲存，前面放一個自架 Redis 快取；在可預測、排程式的內容更新（每年 4 次）期間負載暴增，且必須具備高可用性。DAX 是專為 DynamoDB 打造、全託管、Multi-AZ、與 DynamoDB API 相容的記憶體內快取，適合讀取密集／突發性工作負載，且只需極少的應用程式變更，能直接取代自架 Redis。以 Auto Scaling group 為目標的 Application Load Balancer 是 EC2 Web 層正確的高可用入口，再用 Route 53 simple alias 指向 ALB，取代脆弱的 multivalue Elastic IP 記錄。由於內容更新發生在已知時程，scheduled scaling 是 AWS 建議用於可預測、時間性負載變化的機制，可在尖峰前先備妥容量。選項 A 是唯一同時結合三項最佳實務（DAX + ALB + scheduled scaling）的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"ElastiCache for Redis is a valid managed Redis replacement, but B fronts the ASG with a CloudFront distribution using the Auto Scaling group as an origin (CloudFront is a CDN, not an HA load distributor to EC2; an ALB is the correct origin/front door) and uses manual scaling instead of scheduled scaling for predictable updates, making it operationally inferior and not properly HA at the web tier.","why_zh":"ElastiCache for Redis 雖是有效的託管 Redis 替代方案，但 B 用 CloudFront 以 Auto Scaling group 為來源放在前面（CloudFront 是 CDN，不是對 EC2 的高可用負載分配；正確的來源/入口應是 ALB），且對可預測更新使用手動擴展而非 scheduled scaling，在 Web 層運維上較差且未真正達到高可用。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"ALB and scheduled scaling are correct, but ElastiCache for Memcached has no replication, no Multi-AZ failover, and no persistence, so it is not highly available on its own and is a downgrade from the existing Redis cache; it fails the high-availability requirement for the caching tier.","why_zh":"ALB 與 scheduled scaling 是對的，但 ElastiCache for Memcached 沒有複寫、沒有 Multi-AZ 故障轉移、也沒有持久化，本身並非高可用，且是比現有 Redis 快取的退步；無法滿足快取層的高可用需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"DAX is the right cache, but D uses CloudFront with the Auto Scaling group as an origin (wrong front door for an EC2 HA web tier; an ALB is required) and manual scaling instead of scheduled scaling for predictable content updates, making it both architecturally and operationally inferior to A.","why_zh":"DAX 是正確的快取，但 D 用 CloudFront 以 Auto Scaling group 為來源（對 EC2 高可用 Web 層而言是錯誤入口，應使用 ALB），且對可預測的內容更新採用手動擴展而非 scheduled scaling，在架構與運維上都不如 A。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/DAX.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-auto-scaling-scheduled-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/attach-load-balancer-asg.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonElastiCache/latest/dg/SelectEngine.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":397,"question_en":"A company needs to store and process image data that will be uploaded from mobile devices using a custom mobile app. Usage peaks between 8 AM and 5 PM on weekdays, with thousands of uploads per minute. The app is rarely used at any other time. A user is notified when image processing is complete. Which combination of actions should a solutions architect take to ensure image processing can scale to handle the load? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"公司需要存储和处理将使用自定义移动应用程序从移动设备上传的图像数据。使用高峰期为工作日上午 8 点至下午 5 点，每分钟上 传数千次。该应用程序在其他时间很少使用。当图像处理完成时，用户会收到通知。 解决方案架构师应采取哪种操作组合来确保图像处理可以扩展以处理负载？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Upload files from the mobile software directly to Amazon S3. Use S3 event notifications to create a message in an Amazon MQ queue.","B":"Upload files from the mobile software directly to Amazon S3. Use S3 event notifications to create a message in an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) standard queue.","C":"Invoke an AWS Lambda function to perform image processing when a message is available in the queue.","D":"Invoke an S3 Batch Operations job to perform image processing when a message is available in the queue.","E":"Send a push notification to the mobile app by using Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) when processing is complete.","F":"Send a push notification to the mobile app by using Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) when processing is complete."},"options_zh":{"A":"将文件从移动软件直接上传到 Amazon S3。使用 S3 事件通知在 Amazon MQ 队列中创建消息。","B":"将文件从移动软件直接上传到 Amazon S3。使用 S3 事件通知在 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 标准队列中创建消 息。","C":"当队列中存在可用消息时，调用 AWS Lambda 函数来执行图像处理。","D":"当队列中有可用消息时，调用 S3 批量操作作业来执行图像处理。","E":"处理完成后，使用 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 向移动应用程序发送推送通知。","F":"处理完成后，使用 Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) 向移动应用程序发送推送通知。"},"answer":["A","C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BCE":93},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is building a decoupled, auto-scaling serverless pipeline. S3 Event Notifications support only SNS, SQS, Lambda, and EventBridge as destinations - Amazon MQ is NOT a valid destination, so A is wrong and B (S3 -> SQS standard queue) is correct. A standard SQS queue absorbs the bursty thousands-of-uploads-per-minute load and decouples ingestion from processing. C is correct because Lambda has a native SQS event source mapping that polls the queue and scales out automatically with concurrency, perfectly matching the weekday 8 AM-5 PM peak with near-idle off-hours. D is wrong: S3 Batch Operations performs bulk operations across many existing objects driven by a manifest, and cannot be invoked per-message from a queue. For user notification, E is correct because Amazon SNS natively delivers mobile push notifications to the app via platform application endpoints and device tokens. F is wrong because Amazon SES sends email, not mobile push notifications.","explanation_zh":"決定性條件是建立一個解耦且自動擴展的無伺服器處理管線。S3 Event Notifications 僅支援 SNS、SQS、Lambda 與 EventBridge 作為目的地,Amazon MQ 並不是有效目的地,因此 A 錯誤,而 B(S3 -> SQS standard queue)正確。Standard SQS queue 能吸收每分鐘數千次上傳的尖峰負載,並將擷取與處理解耦。C 正確,因為 Lambda 具備原生的 SQS event source mapping,可輪詢佇列並依並行數自動擴展,完美對應平日上午 8 點至下午 5 點的尖峰以及離峰時段近乎閒置的情況。D 錯誤:S3 Batch Operations 是依 manifest 對大量既有物件執行批次操作,無法依佇列逐則訊息觸發。針對使用者通知,E 正確,因為 Amazon SNS 可透過 platform application endpoints 與 device tokens 原生地將 mobile push notifications 傳送至 app。F 錯誤,因為 Amazon SES 是發送 email,而非 mobile push notifications。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon MQ is not a supported destination for S3 Event Notifications. S3 can only publish to SNS, SQS, Lambda, or EventBridge.","why_zh":"Amazon MQ 不是 S3 Event Notifications 支援的目的地。S3 只能發布到 SNS、SQS、Lambda 或 EventBridge。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 Batch Operations runs manifest-driven bulk jobs over existing objects; it cannot be invoked per-message when a message arrives in a queue, so it does not fit a real-time, scalable processing pipeline.","why_zh":"S3 Batch Operations 是依 manifest 對既有物件執行批次作業,無法在佇列收到訊息時逐則觸發,不適合即時可擴展的處理管線。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Amazon SES is an email-sending service and cannot send mobile push notifications to an app; Amazon SNS is the correct service for push notifications.","why_zh":"Amazon SES 是寄送 email 的服務,無法向 app 發送 mobile push notifications;Amazon SNS 才是推播通知的正確服務。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/EventNotifications.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-sqs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-sqs-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/sns-mobile-application-as-subscriber.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":398,"question_en":"A company is building an application on AWS. The application sends logs to an Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster for analysis. All data must be stored within a VPC. Some of the company’s developers work from home. Other developers work from three different company o®ce locations. The developers need to access OpenSearch Service to analyze and visualize logs directly from their local development machines. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 上构建应用程序。该应用程序将日志发送到 Amazon OpenSearch Service 集群进行分析。所有数据必须存储在 VPC 内。 该公司的一些开发人员在家工作。其他开发人员在三个不同的公司办公地点工作。开发人员需要访问 OpenSearch 服务来直接从本地 开发计算机分析和可视化日志。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure and set up an AWS Client VPN endpoint. Associate the Client VPN endpoint with a subnet in the VPC. Configure a Client VPN self-service portal. Instruct the developers to connect by using the client for Client VPN.","B":"Create a transit gateway, and connect it to the VPC. Create an AWS Site-to-Site VPN. Create an attachment to the transit gateway. Instruct the developers to connect by using an OpenVPN client.","C":"Create a transit gateway, and connect it to the VPOrder an AWS Direct Connect connection. Set up a public VIF on the Direct Connect connection. Associate the public VIF with the transit gateway. Instruct the developers to connect to the Direct Connect connection.","D":"Create and configure a bastion host in a public subnet of the VPC. Configure the bastion host security group to allow SSH access from the company CIDR ranges. Instruct the developers to connect by using SSH."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置并设置 AWS 客户端 VPN 终端节点。将客户端 VPN 终端节点与 VPC 中的子网关联。配置客户端 VPN 自助服务门户。指导 开发人员使用客户端 VPN 进行连接。","B":"创建中转网关，并将其连接到 VPC。创建 AWS 站点到站点 VPN。创建到中转网关的附件。指导开发人员使用 OpenVPN 客户端 进行连接。","C":"创建中转网关，并将其连接到 VPOrder AWS Direct Connect 连接。在 Direct Connect 连接上设置公共 VIF。将公共 VIF 与中转网 关关联。指导开发人员连接到 Direct Connect 连接。","D":"在 VPC 的公有子网中创建并配置堡垒主机。配置堡垒主机安全组以允许从公司 CIDR 范围进行 SSH 访问。指导开发人员使用 SSH进行连接。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The OpenSearch cluster lives in a VPC (all data must stay private), and developers need to reach it directly from their local machines whether they work from home or from any of three offices. AWS Client VPN is a managed client-based VPN: each developer installs the OpenVPN-based AWS VPN client, connects from any location, and gets secure private network access into the VPC. Associating the Client VPN endpoint with a VPC subnet places the connected clients inside the VPC so they can open OpenSearch Dashboards over HTTPS, and the self-service portal lets users download their client/configuration. This satisfies both the work-from-home and office-based developers with a single managed solution. Option D (bastion + SSH) is wrong because SSH does not provide browser/HTTP access to OpenSearch Dashboards for visualization (it would require manual tunneling), and an SSH security group keyed to fixed company CIDR ranges cannot cover work-from-home developers whose home IPs are dynamic/unknown.","explanation_zh":"OpenSearch 叢集部署在 VPC 內（所有資料必須保留在私有網路），開發人員無論是在家或在三個辦公室，都需要從本機直接存取它。AWS Client VPN 是受管的用戶端式 VPN：每位開發人員安裝以 OpenVPN 為基礎的 AWS VPN 用戶端，從任何位置連線，即可安全地進入 VPC 私有網路。將 Client VPN endpoint 關聯到 VPC 子網路，會讓已連線的用戶端處於 VPC 之內，因而可透過 HTTPS 開啟 OpenSearch Dashboards 進行分析與視覺化；self-service portal 讓使用者下載用戶端與設定檔。此方案以單一受管服務同時滿足在家與辦公室的開發人員。選項 D（bastion + SSH）錯誤：SSH 無法提供瀏覽器/HTTP 方式存取 OpenSearch Dashboards 做視覺化（需手動建立通道），且以固定公司 CIDR 範圍鎖定的 SSH 安全群組無法涵蓋在家工作、IP 為動態/未知的開發人員。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Site-to-Site VPN connects whole networks (the office sites) to the VPC; it does not provide connectivity for individual work-from-home developers' laptops, which have no site/customer gateway to attach. The 'OpenVPN client' detail is also wrong for Site-to-Site VPN.","why_zh":"Site-to-Site VPN 連接的是整個網路（辦公室站點）與 VPC，無法為在家工作的個別開發人員筆電提供連線，因為他們沒有可掛載的站點/客戶閘道。且 Site-to-Site VPN 也不使用 'OpenVPN client'。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Direct Connect with a public VIF reaches AWS public service endpoints over the AWS backbone, not private VPC resources, and individual home developers cannot 'connect to a Direct Connect connection.' It is also enormously expensive and slow to provision for this use case.","why_zh":"搭配 public VIF 的 Direct Connect 是透過 AWS 骨幹存取 AWS 公有服務端點，而非私有 VPC 資源，且在家的個別開發人員無法『連線到 Direct Connect 連線』。對此情境而言成本極高、佈建緩慢。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A bastion with SSH gives shell access, not browser/HTTP access to OpenSearch Dashboards for analysis and visualization (would need manual port-forwarding). Worse, the security group is restricted to fixed company CIDR ranges, which cannot accommodate work-from-home developers with dynamic/unknown home IPs.","why_zh":"bastion 搭配 SSH 提供的是 shell 存取，而非以瀏覽器/HTTP 存取 OpenSearch Dashboards 做分析與視覺化（需手動 port-forwarding）。更嚴重的是安全群組僅限固定公司 CIDR 範圍，無法涵蓋在家工作、IP 為動態/未知的開發人員。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/cvpn-getting-started.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/cvpn-self-service-portal.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opensearch-service/latest/developerguide/dashboards.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":399,"question_en":"A company wants to migrate its website from an on-premises data center onto AWS. At the same time, it wants to migrate the website to a containerized microservice-based architecture to improve the availability and cost e®ciency. The company’s security policy states that privileges and network permissions must be configured according to best practice, using least privilege. A solutions architect must create a containerized architecture that meets the security requirements and has deployed the application to an Amazon ECS cluster. What steps are required after the deployment to meet the requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司希望将其网站从本地数据中心迁移到 AWS。同时，希望将网站迁移到基于容器化微服务的架构，以提高可用性和成本效 率。该公司的安全策略规定，必须根据最佳实践，使用最小权限来配置权限和网络权限。 解决方案架构师必须创建一个满足安全要求的容器化架构，并将应用程序部署到 Amazon ECS 集群。 部署后需要采取哪些步骤才能满足要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create tasks using the bridge network mode.","B":"Create tasks using the awsvpc network mode.","C":"Apply security groups to Amazon EC2 instances, and use IAM roles for EC2 instances to access other resources.","D":"Apply security groups to the tasks, and pass IAM credentials into the container at launch time to access other resources.","E":"Apply security groups to the tasks, and use IAM roles for tasks to access other resources."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用桥接网络模式创建任务。","B":"使用 awsvpc 网络模式创建任务。","C":"将安全组应用到 Amazon EC2 实例，并使用 EC2 实例的 IAM 角色来访问其他资源。","D":"将安全组应用于任务，并在启动时将 IAM 凭证传递到容器中以访问其他资源。","E":"将安全组应用于任务，并使用任务的 IAM 角色来访问其他资源。"},"answer":["C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BE":100},"tags":["Migration","Security/IAM","Compute","Cost Optimization","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The security policy requires least privilege for both network permissions and IAM privileges, applied at the granularity of the workload (the tasks/microservices). Option B (awsvpc network mode) is correct because awsvpc is the only ECS network mode that gives each task its own elastic network interface (ENI) with its own security groups, enabling least-privilege network rules scoped to each individual task/microservice rather than to the shared EC2 host. The AWS docs state awsvpc 'provides greater security for your containers by allowing you to use security groups... at a more granular level within your tasks.' Option E (IAM roles for tasks) is correct because the docs explicitly state that assigning each task its own task IAM role 'aligns with the principle of least privileged access and allows for greater granular control over actions and resources,' giving each microservice only the permissions it needs. Together B and E apply least privilege at the task level for both networking and IAM. The qualifier that decides this is 'least privilege at the task/microservice granularity.'","explanation_zh":"安全政策要求網路權限與 IAM 權限都採用最小權限原則,並且要落實到工作負載(任務/微服務)的粒度。選項 B(awsvpc network mode)正確,因為 awsvpc 是 ECS 中唯一能讓每個 task 擁有自己的 elastic network interface (ENI) 及其專屬 security groups 的網路模式,可將最小權限的網路規則套用到個別 task/微服務,而非共用的 EC2 主機。AWS 文件指出 awsvpc 『藉由讓你在 task 層級更細緻地使用 security groups,為容器提供更高的安全性』。選項 E(IAM roles for tasks)正確,因為文件明確指出為每個 task 指派專屬的 task IAM role 『符合最小權限原則,並可對動作與資源有更細緻的控制』,讓每個微服務只取得所需權限。B 與 E 一起在 task 層級對網路與 IAM 都落實最小權限。決定關鍵的限定詞是『在 task/微服務粒度的最小權限』。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Bridge network mode does not allow attaching security groups to individual tasks; containers share the host's networking, so security groups apply at the EC2 instance level, not per task. This violates the least-privilege-per-microservice requirement.","why_zh":"Bridge network mode 無法將 security groups 附加到個別 task;容器共用主機網路,security groups 只能套用在 EC2 instance 層級,而非每個 task,違反每個微服務最小權限的要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Applying security groups and IAM roles at the EC2 instance level means all tasks/containers on that instance share the same network and IAM permissions. This is coarse-grained and violates least privilege at the task/microservice level; a compromised container would inherit the instance's broad permissions.","why_zh":"在 EC2 instance 層級套用 security groups 與 IAM roles,代表該 instance 上所有 task/容器共用相同的網路與 IAM 權限。這種粗粒度做法違反 task/微服務層級的最小權限;若某容器被入侵,將繼承 instance 的廣泛權限。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Passing long-lived IAM credentials into the container at launch time is an anti-pattern: static credentials are hard to rotate, can be leaked, and contradict AWS best practice. IAM roles for tasks (temporary, auto-rotated credentials) are the recommended approach instead.","why_zh":"在啟動時將長期 IAM 憑證傳入容器是反模式:靜態憑證難以輪替、容易外洩,且違反 AWS 最佳實務。應改用 IAM roles for tasks(臨時、自動輪替的憑證)。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/task-networking-awsvpc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/security-iam-roles.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/task-iam-roles.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/security-network.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":400,"question_en":"A company is running a serverless application that consists of several AWS Lambda functions and Amazon DynamoDB tables. The company has created new functionality that requires the Lambda functions to access an Amazon Neptune DB cluster. The Neptune DB cluster is located in three subnets in a VPC. Which of the possible solutions will allow the Lambda functions to access the Neptune DB cluster and DynamoDB tables? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在執行一個無伺服器應用程式，該應用程式由多個 AWS Lambda 函式和 Amazon DynamoDB 資料表組成。該公司建立了新功能，需要讓 Lambda 函式存取 Amazon Neptune DB 叢集。Neptune DB 叢集位於 VPC 中的三個子網路內。下列哪些可能的解決方案可讓 Lambda 函式存取 Neptune DB 叢集和 DynamoDB 資料表？（選擇兩項。）","options_en":{"A":"Create three public subnets in the Neptune VPC, and route tra®c through an internet gateway. Host the Lambda functions in the three new public subnets.","B":"Create three private subnets in the Neptune VPC, and route internet tra®c through a NAT gateway. Host the Lambda functions in the three new private subnets.","C":"Host the Lambda functions outside the VPUpdate the Neptune security group to allow access from the IP ranges of the Lambda functions.","D":"Host the Lambda functions outside the VPC. Create a VPC endpoint for the Neptune database, and have the Lambda functions access Neptune over the VPC endpoint.","E":"Create three private subnets in the Neptune VPC. Host the Lambda functions in the three new isolated subnets. Create a VPC endpoint for DynamoDB, and route DynamoDB tra®c to the VPC endpoint."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Neptune VPC 中建立三個公有子網路，並透過網際網路閘道路由流量。將 Lambda 函式部署在這三個新的公有子網路中。","B":"在 Neptune VPC 中建立三個私有子網路，並透過 NAT 閘道路由網際網路流量。將 Lambda 函式部署在這三個新的私有子網路中。","C":"將 Lambda 函式部署在 VPC 之外。更新 Neptune 安全群組，允許來自 Lambda 函式 IP 範圍的存取。","D":"將 Lambda 函式部署在 VPC 之外。為 Neptune 資料庫建立 VPC endpoint，並讓 Lambda 函式透過該 VPC endpoint 存取 Neptune。","E":"在 Neptune VPC 中建立三個私有子網路。將 Lambda 函式部署在這三個新的隔離子網路中。為 DynamoDB 建立 VPC endpoint，並將 DynamoDB 流量路由至該 VPC endpoint。"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BE":91},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Neptune has no public endpoint and is reachable only via private IPs inside its VPC, so the Lambda functions must be attached to that VPC (eliminating C and D, which host Lambda outside the VPC; D also invents a non-existent 'VPC endpoint for the Neptune database'). Both B and E place the functions in subnets of the Neptune VPC, giving them in-VPC connectivity to Neptune, and both provide a working path to DynamoDB: B routes DynamoDB traffic out through a NAT gateway, while E uses a DynamoDB gateway VPC endpoint (no NAT/IGW needed, no cost). Option A is wrong because a VPC-attached Lambda function gets a Hyperplane ENI with only a private IP - the AWS Lambda docs state plainly that 'Connecting a function to a public subnet doesn't give it internet access,' so placing Lambda in a public subnet behind an internet gateway provides no route to DynamoDB's public endpoint. Therefore the dump's suggested 'A,E' is incorrect on A, and the community answer B,E is the technically correct pair.","explanation_zh":"Neptune 沒有公開端點，只能透過其所在 VPC 內的私有 IP 連線，因此 Lambda 函式必須掛載到該 VPC（排除 C 和 D，這兩者都把 Lambda 放在 VPC 之外；D 還虛構了不存在的『Neptune 資料庫 VPC endpoint』）。B 與 E 都把函式放在 Neptune VPC 的子網中，因此都能在 VPC 內連到 Neptune，並且都提供可行的 DynamoDB 存取路徑：B 透過 NAT gateway 將 DynamoDB 流量導向公開端點，E 則使用 DynamoDB 的 gateway VPC endpoint（不需 NAT/IGW，且免費）。選項 A 錯誤，因為掛載到 VPC 的 Lambda 取得的 Hyperplane ENI 只有私有 IP；AWS Lambda 文件明確指出『將函式連到 public subnet 並不會給它網際網路存取』，所以把 Lambda 放在 public subnet 加 internet gateway 並無法連到 DynamoDB 的公開端點。因此 dump 建議的 'A,E' 在 A 上是錯的，社群的 B,E 才是技術上正確的組合。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A VPC-attached Lambda function only has a private IP on its Hyperplane ENI. AWS docs state 'Connecting a function to a public subnet doesn't give it internet access' - an internet gateway alone provides no DynamoDB connectivity for Lambda, so this fails the DynamoDB requirement.","why_zh":"掛載到 VPC 的 Lambda 的 Hyperplane ENI 只有私有 IP。AWS 文件指出『將函式連到 public subnet 不會給它網際網路存取』，僅有 internet gateway 無法讓 Lambda 連到 DynamoDB，因此不符合 DynamoDB 需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Hosting Lambda outside the VPC means it cannot reach Neptune's private IPs (Neptune has no public endpoint), and Lambda has no fixed IP ranges to allowlist in a security group.","why_zh":"把 Lambda 放在 VPC 之外就無法連到 Neptune 的私有 IP（Neptune 無公開端點），而且 Lambda 沒有固定 IP 範圍可加入安全群組允許清單。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"There is no VPC endpoint (PrivateLink) service for connecting to a Neptune database; Neptune is accessed via private IPs inside its VPC. Lambda outside the VPC cannot reach it this way.","why_zh":"並不存在用於連線 Neptune 資料庫的 VPC endpoint (PrivateLink) 服務；Neptune 是透過其 VPC 內的私有 IP 存取。位於 VPC 外的 Lambda 無法用此方式連線。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-vpc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-vpc-internet.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/vpc-endpoints-ddb.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":401,"question_en":"A company wants to design a disaster recovery (DR) solution for an application that runs in the company’s data center. The application writes to an SMB file share and creates a copy on a second file share. Both file shares are in the data center. The application uses two types of files: metadata files and image files. The company wants to store the copy on AWS. The company needs the ability to use SMB to access the data from either the data center or AWS if a disaster occurs. The copy of the data is rarely accessed but must be available within 5 minutes.","question_zh":"一家公司想要為在其資料中心執行的應用程式設計災難復原 (DR) 解決方案。該應用程式會寫入一個 SMB 檔案共用，並在第二個檔案共用上建立副本。這兩個檔案共用都位於資料中心內。該應用程式使用兩種類型的檔案：中繼資料檔案和影像檔案。該公司希望將副本儲存在 AWS 上。若發生災難，該公司需要能夠透過 SMB 從資料中心或 AWS 存取資料。這份資料副本很少被存取，但必須在 5 分鐘內可供使用。","options_en":{"A":"Deploy AWS Outposts with Amazon S3 storage. Configure a Windows Amazon EC2 instance on Outposts as a file server.","B":"Deploy an Amazon FSx File Gateway. Configure an Amazon FSx for Windows File Server Multi-AZ file system that uses SSD storage.","C":"Deploy an Amazon S3 File Gateway. Configure the S3 File Gateway to use Amazon S3 Standard-Infrequent Access (S3 Standard-IA) for the metadata files and to use S3 Glacier Deep Archive for the image files.","D":"Deploy an Amazon S3 File Gateway. Configure the S3 File Gateway to use Amazon S3 Standard-Infrequent Access (S3 Standard-IA) for the metadata files and image files."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署具有 Amazon S3 儲存體的 AWS Outposts。在 Outposts 上設定一個 Windows Amazon EC2 執行個體作為檔案伺服器。","B":"部署 Amazon FSx File Gateway。設定使用 SSD 儲存體的 Amazon FSx for Windows File Server 多可用區檔案系統。","C":"部署 Amazon S3 File Gateway。將 S3 File Gateway 設定為對中繼資料檔案使用 Amazon S3 Standard-Infrequent Access (S3 Standard-IA)，並對影像檔案使用 S3 Glacier Deep Archive。","D":"部署 Amazon S3 File Gateway。將 S3 File Gateway 設定為對中繼資料檔案和影像檔案都使用 Amazon S3 Standard-Infrequent Access (S3 Standard-IA)。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":74,"B":26},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":402,"question_en":"A company is creating a solution that can move 400 employees into a remote working environment in the event of an unexpected disaster. The user desktops have a mix of Windows and Linux operating systems. Multiple types of software, such as web browsers and mail clients, are installed on each desktop. A solutions architect needs to implement a solution that can be integrated with the company’s on-premises Active Directory to allow employees to use their existing identity credentials. The solution must provide multifactor authentication (MFA) and must replicate the user experience from the existing desktops. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在建立一個解決方案，以便在發生意外災難時，能將 400 名員工轉移到遠端工作環境。使用者桌面混合使用 Windows 與 Linux 作業系統，且每台桌面都安裝了多種軟體，例如網頁瀏覽器和郵件用戶端。解決方案架構師需要實作一個可與該公司內部部署的 Active Directory 整合的解決方案，讓員工能夠使用現有的身分憑證。該解決方案必須提供多因素驗證 (MFA)，並且必須重現現有桌面的使用者體驗。哪個解決方案可滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon WorkSpaces for the cloud desktop service. Set up a VPN connection to the on-premises network. Create an AD Connector, and connect to the on-premises Active Directory. Activate MFA for Amazon WorkSpaces by using the AWS Management Console.","B":"Use Amazon AppStream 2.0 as an application streaming service. Configure Desktop View for the employees. Set up a VPN connection to the on-premises network. Set up Active Directory Federation Services (AD FS) on premises. Connect the VPC network to AD FS through the VPN connection.","C":"Use Amazon WorkSpaces for the cloud desktop service. Set up a VPN connection to the on-premises network. Create an AD Connector, and connect to the on-premises Active Directory. Configure a RADIUS server for MFA.","D":"Use Amazon AppStream 2.0 as an application streaming service. Set up Active Directory Federation Services on premises. Configure MFA to grant users access on AppStream 2.0."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon WorkSpaces 作為雲端桌面服務。建立一個連接至內部部署網路的 VPN 連線。建立一個 AD Connector 並連接到內部部署的 Active Directory。透過 AWS Management Console 為 Amazon WorkSpaces 啟用 MFA。","B":"使用 Amazon AppStream 2.0 作為應用程式串流服務。為員工設定 Desktop View。建立一個連接至內部部署網路的 VPN 連線。在內部部署環境中設定 Active Directory Federation Services (AD FS)。透過該 VPN 連線將 VPC 網路連接至 AD FS。","C":"使用 Amazon WorkSpaces 作為雲端桌面服務。建立一個連接至內部部署網路的 VPN 連線。建立一個 AD Connector 並連接到內部部署的 Active Directory。設定 RADIUS 伺服器以支援 MFA。","D":"使用 Amazon AppStream 2.0 作為應用程式串流服務。在內部部署環境中設定 Active Directory Federation Services。設定 MFA 以授予使用者在 AppStream 2.0 上的存取權。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":86},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":403,"question_en":"A company has deployed an Amazon Connect contact center. Contact center agents are reporting large numbers of computer-generated calls. The company is concerned about the cost and productivity effects of these calls. The company wants a solution that will allow agents to ­ag the call as spam and automatically block the numbers from going to an agent in the future. What is the MOST operationally e®cient solution to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司已部署 Amazon Connect 聯絡中心。聯絡中心的客服人員回報大量電腦自動撥打的來電。該公司擔心這些來電對成本與生產力造成的影響。該公司希望有一個解決方案，讓客服人員能夠將來電標記為垃圾來電，並在未來自動封鎖這些號碼、不再轉接給客服人員。下列哪個解決方案在營運上最有效率，可滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Customize the Contact Control Panel (CCP) by adding a ­ag call button that will invoke an AWS Lambda function that calls the UpdateContactAttributes API. Use an Amazon DynamoDB table to store the spam numbers. Modify the contact ­ows to look for the updated attribute and to use a Lambda function to read and write to the DynamoDB table.","B":"Use a Contact Lens for Amazon Connect rule that will look for spam calls. Use an Amazon DynamoDB table to store the spam numbers. Modify the contact ­ows to look for the rule and to invoke an AWS Lambda function to read and write to the DynamoDB table.","C":"Use an Amazon DynamoDB table to store the spam numbers. Create a quick connect that the agents can transfer the spam call to from the Contact Control Panel (CCP). Modify the quick connect contact ­ow to invoke an AWS Lambda function to write to the DynamoDB table.","D":"Modify the initial contact ­ow to ask for caller input. If the agent does not receive input, the agent should mark the caller as spam. Use an Amazon DynamoDB table to store the spam numbers. Use an AWS Lambda function to read and write to the DynamoDB table."},"options_zh":{"A":"自訂 Contact Control Panel (CCP)，新增一個標記來電按鈕，觸發呼叫 UpdateContactAttributes API 的 AWS Lambda 函式。使用 Amazon DynamoDB 資料表儲存垃圾來電號碼。修改聯絡流程 (contact flow)，使其檢查更新後的屬性，並使用 Lambda 函式讀寫該 DynamoDB 資料表。","B":"使用 Contact Lens for Amazon Connect 規則來偵測垃圾來電。使用 Amazon DynamoDB 資料表儲存垃圾來電號碼。修改聯絡流程，使其檢查該規則，並觸發 AWS Lambda 函式讀寫該 DynamoDB 資料表。","C":"使用 Amazon DynamoDB 資料表儲存垃圾來電號碼。建立一個 quick connect，讓客服人員可以從 Contact Control Panel (CCP) 將垃圾來電轉接至該處。修改 quick connect 的聯絡流程，觸發 AWS Lambda 函式寫入該 DynamoDB 資料表。","D":"修改初始聯絡流程，要求來電者輸入資訊。如果客服人員未收到輸入，客服人員應將該來電者標記為垃圾來電。使用 Amazon DynamoDB 資料表儲存垃圾來電號碼。使用 AWS Lambda 函式讀寫該 DynamoDB 資料表。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":87},"tags":["Compute","Database","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement has two parts: agents must be able to MANUALLY flag a call as spam, and matching numbers must be AUTOMATICALLY blocked from reaching an agent in the future. Option A satisfies both directly and is the documented, supported pattern. The Amazon Connect CCP can be embedded/customized with the Amazon Connect Streams API, so you can add a custom 'flag call' button; that button invokes a Lambda that calls the UpdateContactAttributes API and writes the caller number to a DynamoDB table. The inbound contact flow then invokes a Lambda at the start to look up the caller's number in DynamoDB and route known spam numbers away from agents (e.g., disconnect) before they ever reach a queue. This achieves agent-initiated flagging plus automatic future blocking with minimal moving parts. Option B is wrong because Contact Lens performs natural-language analysis of the conversation transcript (sentiment, keyword/phrase detection, issue detection, categorization) - it acts on what is said, not on a caller's phone number and not on an agent pressing a flag button, so it cannot reliably identify computer-generated calls nor capture the agent's manual spam designation.","explanation_zh":"需求有兩部分：客服人員必須能夠手動將來電標記為垃圾來電，且符合的號碼未來必須被自動阻擋、不再轉接到客服。選項 A 直接滿足這兩點，且是官方支援的標準做法。Amazon Connect 的 CCP 可透過 Amazon Connect Streams API 嵌入與自訂，因此可加上自訂的『標記來電』按鈕；該按鈕觸發 Lambda 呼叫 UpdateContactAttributes API，並將來電號碼寫入 DynamoDB 資料表。之後 inbound contact flow 在流程開頭呼叫 Lambda，比對 DynamoDB 中的來電號碼，於進入佇列前將已知垃圾號碼導離客服（例如直接掛斷）。如此即可同時達成客服手動標記與未來自動阻擋，且元件最少。選項 B 錯誤，因為 Contact Lens 是對對話逐字稿做自然語言分析（情緒、關鍵字/片語偵測、問題偵測、分類），它依據『說了什麼』運作，無法依來電者電話號碼或客服按下標記按鈕運作，因此既無法可靠辨識電腦自動撥打的來電，也無法捕捉客服的手動垃圾標記。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Contact Lens rules analyze the conversation transcript (sentiment, keywords/phrases, issues, categorization), not the caller's phone number and not an agent's manual flag action. Computer-generated/robocalls would not reliably utter detectable spam keywords, and there is no rule that maps an agent button press to blocking a number, so it fails the 'agents flag the call' requirement.","why_zh":"Contact Lens 規則分析的是對話逐字稿（情緒、關鍵字/片語、問題、分類），而非來電者電話號碼，也非客服的手動標記動作。電腦自動撥打的來電不會可靠地說出可偵測的垃圾關鍵字，且沒有任何規則能把客服按鈕動作對應到阻擋號碼，因此無法滿足『客服標記來電』的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Quick connects are a transfer mechanism (to a queue, agent, or flow). Forcing agents to transfer a spam call to a quick-connect flow to log the number is a misuse of the feature, adds steps, and does not cleanly capture the current contact's caller ID for future automatic blocking. Less operationally efficient than a custom CCP flag button.","why_zh":"Quick connect 是轉接機制（轉到佇列、客服或流程）。逼客服把垃圾來電轉到 quick-connect 流程以記錄號碼是濫用此功能、增加步驟，且無法乾淨地擷取當前聯絡的來電號碼供未來自動阻擋。比自訂 CCP 標記按鈕更不具運作效率。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Gating on IVR caller input and having the agent mark callers as spam based on lack of input degrades the experience for all legitimate callers, conflates IVR logic with manual flagging, and does not match the 'agents flag the call' requirement cleanly. It is a brittle, less efficient design.","why_zh":"以 IVR 來電者輸入做閘控、再由客服依『沒有輸入』判定為垃圾來電，會傷害所有正常來電者的體驗，把 IVR 邏輯與手動標記混為一談，也不符合『客服標記來電』的需求。設計脆弱且效率較低。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/connect/latest/adminguide/use-attribs-ccp.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/connect/latest/devguide/contact-actions-updatecontactattributes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/connect/latest/adminguide/analyze-conversations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/connect/latest/adminguide/amazon-connect-contact-control-panel.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":404,"question_en":"A company has mounted sensors to collect information about environmental parameters such as humidity and light throughout all the company's factories. The company needs to stream and analyze the data in the AWS Cloud in real time. If any of the parameters fall out of acceptable ranges, the factory operations team must receive a notification immediately. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在其所有工廠中安裝了感測器，用於收集濕度和光線等環境參數資訊。該公司需要在 AWS 雲端中即時串流並分析這些資料。如果任何參數超出可接受範圍，工廠營運團隊必須立即收到通知。哪個解決方案可滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Stream the data to an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream. Use AWS Step Functions to consume and analyze the data in the Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream. Use Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to notify the operations team.","B":"Stream the data to an Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK) cluster. Set up a trigger in Amazon MSK to invoke an AWS Fargate task to analyze the data. Use Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) to notify the operations team.","C":"Stream the data to an Amazon Kinesis data stream. Create an AWS Lambda function to consume the Kinesis data stream and to analyze the data. Use Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to notify the operations team.","D":"Stream the data to an Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics application. Use an automatically scaled and containerized service in Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) to consume and analyze the data. Use Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) to notify the operations team."},"options_zh":{"A":"將資料串流至 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 傳送串流 (delivery stream)。使用 AWS Step Functions 消費並分析 Kinesis Data Firehose 傳送串流中的資料。使用 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 通知營運團隊。","B":"將資料串流至 Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK) 叢集。在 Amazon MSK 中設定觸發器 (trigger)，以叫用 AWS Fargate 任務來分析資料。使用 Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) 通知營運團隊。","C":"將資料串流至 Amazon Kinesis 資料串流 (data stream)。建立一個 AWS Lambda 函式來消費該 Kinesis 資料串流並分析資料。使用 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 通知營運團隊。","D":"將資料串流至一個 Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics 應用程式。使用 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 中一個可自動擴展的容器化服務來消費並分析資料。使用 Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) 通知營運團隊。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":93},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Analytics","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to stream and analyze sensor data in real time and notify the operations team immediately. Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is purpose-built for real-time data collection and processing (records are available for consumption within seconds). AWS Lambda has a native, fully supported event source mapping for Kinesis Data Streams, allowing it to consume and analyze each batch of records as it arrives and then publish to Amazon SNS, which pushes immediate notifications (SMS, email, mobile push) to the operations team. This is the canonical AWS pattern for real-time IoT/sensor alerting. The other options either rely on near-real-time delivery (Firehose buffers data before delivery) or describe service integrations that do not exist (an MSK 'trigger' that invokes Fargate; Step Functions 'consuming' a Firehose stream; Kinesis Data Analytics plus ECS both analyzing).","explanation_zh":"需求是即時串流並分析感測器資料，並立即通知工廠營運團隊。Amazon Kinesis Data Streams 專為即時資料收集與處理而設計（記錄在數秒內即可被消費）。AWS Lambda 對 Kinesis Data Streams 具有原生且完整支援的 event source mapping，可在每批記錄到達時消費並分析，然後發布到 Amazon SNS，由 SNS 立即推播通知（SMS、電子郵件、行動推播）給營運團隊。這是 AWS 即時 IoT/感測器告警的標準架構。其他選項要不是依賴近即時傳輸（Firehose 在傳輸前會緩衝資料），就是描述了不存在的服務整合（MSK 觸發 Fargate 任務的 trigger、Step Functions 消費 Firehose stream、Kinesis Data Analytics 再加 ECS 重複分析）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Kinesis Data Firehose is near-real-time, not real-time: it buffers records by size/interval (typically a 60+ second buffer) before delivering to destinations, so it cannot meet 'real time / immediately.' Moreover, AWS Step Functions has no native integration to 'consume and analyze data in a Firehose delivery stream'; Firehose delivers only to destinations like S3, Redshift, OpenSearch, HTTP endpoints, and Splunk.","why_zh":"Kinesis Data Firehose 是近即時而非即時：它會依大小/時間間隔（通常為 60 秒以上的緩衝）緩衝記錄後才傳送到目的地，因此無法滿足『即時 / 立即』。此外 Step Functions 並無原生整合可『消費並分析 Firehose delivery stream 中的資料』；Firehose 僅能傳送到 S3、Redshift、OpenSearch、HTTP 端點與 Splunk 等目的地。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"There is no native Amazon MSK feature to 'set up a trigger in MSK to invoke a Fargate task.' MSK can act as an event source for Lambda, but not as a trigger for Fargate tasks. This adds heavy operational overhead (managing a Kafka cluster) and describes a non-existent integration. SES is for transactional/bulk email, not the best fit for immediate operational alerts compared with SNS.","why_zh":"Amazon MSK 並沒有『在 MSK 中設定 trigger 以叫用 Fargate 任務』的原生功能。MSK 可作為 Lambda 的 event source，但無法作為觸發 Fargate 任務的觸發器。此方案增加大量營運負擔（須管理 Kafka 叢集），且描述了不存在的整合。SES 用於交易型/批量電子郵件，相較 SNS 不適合用於即時營運告警。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is architecturally contradictory: Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics (now Managed Service for Apache Flink) already performs the stream analysis, so streaming to it and then having ECS 'consume and analyze the data' is redundant and not how the service is designed to be consumed. It adds unnecessary complexity, and SES is again less suited than SNS for immediate notifications.","why_zh":"此架構自相矛盾：Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics（現為 Managed Service for Apache Flink）本身已執行串流分析，因此先串流到它再讓 ECS『消費並分析資料』是多餘的，也不是該服務的設計使用方式。這增加了不必要的複雜度，且 SES 同樣不如 SNS 適合用於即時通知。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-kinesis.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-kinesis-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-deliver.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":405,"question_en":"A company is preparing to deploy an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster for a workload. The company expects the cluster to support an unpredictable number of stateless pods. Many of the pods will be created during a short time period as the workload automatically scales the number of replicas that the workload uses. Which solution will MAXIMIZE node resilience?","question_zh":"一家公司準備為某個工作負載部署 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 叢集。該公司預期此叢集需要支援數量不可預測的無狀態 Pod。當該工作負載自動擴展所使用的複本數量時，許多 Pod 會在短時間內被建立。哪個解決方案能將節點的復原能力最大化？","options_en":{"A":"Use a separate launch template to deploy the EKS control plane into a second cluster that is separate from the workload node groups.","B":"Update the workload node groups. Use a smaller number of node groups and larger instances in the node groups.","C":"Configure the Kubernetes Cluster Autoscaler to ensure that the compute capacity of the workload node groups stays underprovisioned.","D":"Configure the workload to use topology spread constraints that are based on Availability Zone."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用獨立的啟動範本 (launch template)，將 EKS 控制平面部署到與工作負載節點群組分開的第二個叢集中。","B":"更新工作負載節點群組，改用數量較少的節點群組，並在節點群組中使用較大型的執行個體。","C":"設定 Kubernetes Cluster Autoscaler，確保工作負載節點群組的運算容量維持在配置不足 (underprovisioned) 的狀態。","D":"設定工作負載使用以可用區為基礎的拓撲擴散限制 (topology spread constraints)。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":91},"tags":["Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":406,"question_en":"A company needs to implement a disaster recovery (DR) plan for a web application. The application runs in a single AWS Region. The application uses microservices that run in containers. The containers are hosted on AWS Fargate in Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS). The application has an Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance as its data layer and uses Amazon Route 53 for DNS resolution. An Amazon CloudWatch alarm invokes an Amazon EventBridge rule if the application experiences a failure. A solutions architect must design a DR solution to provide application recovery to a separate Region. The solution must minimize the time that is necessary to recover from a failure. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要為一個網頁應用程式實作災難復原 (DR) 計畫。該應用程式在單一 AWS 區域中執行。該應用程式使用在容器中執行的微服務。這些容器由 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 上的 AWS Fargate 託管。該應用程式使用 Amazon RDS for MySQL 資料庫執行個體作為其資料層，並使用 Amazon Route 53 進行 DNS 解析。如果應用程式發生故障，Amazon CloudWatch 警示會叫用一個 Amazon EventBridge 規則。解決方案架構師必須設計一個 DR 解決方案，以提供應用程式復原到另一個獨立的區域。此解決方案必須將故障復原所需的時間降到最低。哪個解決方案可滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Setup a second ECS cluster and ECS service on Fargate in the separate Region. Create an AWS Lambda function to perform the following actions: take a snapshot of the RDS DB instance, copy the snapshot to the separate Region, create a new RDS DB instance from the snapshot, and update Route 53 to route tra®c to the second ECS cluster. Update the EventBridge rule to add a target that will invoke the Lambda function.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function that creates a second ECS cluster and ECS service in the separate Region. Configure the Lambda function to perform the following actions: take a snapshot of the RDS DB instance, copy the snapshot to the separate Region, create a new RDS DB instance from the snapshot, and update Route 53 to route tra®c to the second ECS cluster. Update the EventBridge rule to add a target that will invoke the Lambda function.","C":"Setup a second ECS cluster and ECS service on Fargate in the separate Region. Create a cross-Region read replica of the RDS DB instance in the separate Region. Create an AWS Lambda function to promote the read replica to the primary database. Configure the Lambda function to update Route 53 to route tra®c to the second ECS cluster. Update the EventBridge rule to add a target that will invoke the Lambda function.","D":"Setup a second ECS cluster and ECS service on Fargate in the separate Region. Take a snapshot of the RDS DB instance. Convert the snapshot to an Amazon DynamoDB global table. Create an AWS Lambda function to update Route 53 to route tra®c to the second ECS cluster. Update the EventBridge rule to add a target that will invoke the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"在另一個獨立區域中設定第二個以 Fargate 執行的 ECS 叢集和 ECS 服務。建立一個 AWS Lambda 函式，執行以下動作：對 RDS 資料庫執行個體建立快照 (snapshot)、將該快照複製到獨立區域、從該快照建立一個新的 RDS 資料庫執行個體，並更新 Route 53 將流量路由至第二個 ECS 叢集。更新 EventBridge 規則，新增一個會叫用該 Lambda 函式的目標 (target)。","B":"建立一個 AWS Lambda 函式，用於在獨立區域中建立第二個 ECS 叢集和 ECS 服務。設定該 Lambda 函式執行以下動作：對 RDS 資料庫執行個體建立快照、將該快照複製到獨立區域、從該快照建立一個新的 RDS 資料庫執行個體，並更新 Route 53 將流量路由至第二個 ECS 叢集。更新 EventBridge 規則，新增一個會叫用該 Lambda 函式的目標。","C":"在另一個獨立區域中設定第二個以 Fargate 執行的 ECS 叢集和 ECS 服務。在該獨立區域中為 RDS 資料庫執行個體建立跨區域讀取複本 (read replica)。建立一個 AWS Lambda 函式，將該讀取複本升級 (promote) 為主要資料庫。設定該 Lambda 函式更新 Route 53，將流量路由至第二個 ECS 叢集。更新 EventBridge 規則，新增一個會叫用該 Lambda 函式的目標。","D":"在另一個獨立區域中設定第二個以 Fargate 執行的 ECS 叢集和 ECS 服務。對 RDS 資料庫執行個體建立快照。將該快照轉換為 Amazon DynamoDB global table。建立一個 AWS Lambda 函式來更新 Route 53，將流量路由至第二個 ECS 叢集。更新 EventBridge 規則，新增一個會叫用該 Lambda 函式的目標。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is 'minimize the time necessary to recover from a failure' (lowest RTO/RPO). Option C uses a cross-Region read replica that continuously and asynchronously replicates the RDS for MySQL data into the DR Region. On failure, the Lambda function only needs to promote the already-warm replica to a standalone primary (a fast operation) and update Route 53 to point at the pre-provisioned second ECS/Fargate cluster. The RDS User Guide explicitly lists 'Implementing disaster recovery. You can promote a read replica to a standalone instance as a disaster recovery solution if the primary DB instance fails' as a core use case, and this matches the AWS Pilot Light DR pattern where data is always replicated and infrastructure is pre-provisioned. Options A and B follow the slow Backup-and-Restore pattern (take a snapshot at failure time, copy it cross-Region, then restore a new instance), which can take many minutes to hours and may fail entirely if the primary is already down; B is worse because it also creates the ECS cluster at failure time via a control-plane operation. Option D is technically invalid because an RDS for MySQL snapshot cannot be converted into a DynamoDB global table (different engines and data models).","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定條件是『盡量縮短從故障中恢復所需的時間』（最低的 RTO/RPO）。選項 C 使用跨區域 read replica，持續且非同步地將 RDS for MySQL 資料複製到 DR 區域。發生故障時，Lambda 函數只需將已經處於熱備狀態的 replica 提升 (promote) 為獨立 primary（這是快速操作），並更新 Route 53 指向已預先佈建好的第二個 ECS/Fargate 叢集。RDS User Guide 明確將『實作災難復原。當 primary DB instance 故障時，可將 read replica 提升為獨立 instance 作為災難復原解決方案』列為核心使用情境，這對應到 AWS 的 Pilot Light DR 模式：資料持續複製、基礎架構預先佈建。選項 A 與 B 走的是緩慢的 Backup-and-Restore 模式（故障時才拍 snapshot、跨區域複製、再還原新 instance），可能需要數十分鐘到數小時，且若 primary 已經當機甚至可能完全失敗；B 更糟，因為它還在故障時才透過 control-plane 操作建立 ECS 叢集。選項 D 技術上不成立，因為 RDS for MySQL snapshot 無法被『轉換』成 DynamoDB global table（引擎與資料模型完全不同）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"This is the slow Backup-and-Restore pattern: it takes an RDS snapshot only after the failure occurs, copies it cross-Region, and then restores a brand-new DB instance. Cross-Region snapshot copy plus restore can take tens of minutes to hours, directly contradicting the 'minimize recovery time' requirement, and snapshotting an already-failed primary may be impossible or capture stale/corrupt data.","why_zh":"這是緩慢的 Backup-and-Restore 模式：故障發生後才拍 RDS snapshot、跨區域複製、再還原全新的 DB instance。跨區域 snapshot 複製加上還原可能需要數十分鐘到數小時，直接違反『縮短恢復時間』的要求；而且對已經故障的 primary 拍 snapshot 可能無法執行或只擷取到過時/損壞的資料。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Even slower and more fragile than A: in addition to the snapshot-copy-restore chain, it creates the second ECS cluster and service from scratch via Lambda at failure time. Provisioning control-plane resources during a disaster increases RTO and risk; the cluster should be pre-provisioned.","why_zh":"比 A 更慢且更脆弱：除了 snapshot 複製還原的流程外，它還在故障時透過 Lambda 從頭建立第二個 ECS 叢集與服務。在災難期間佈建 control-plane 資源會增加 RTO 與風險；叢集應該預先佈建好。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Technically impossible: a relational RDS for MySQL snapshot cannot be 'converted' to an Amazon DynamoDB global table. They are entirely different engines and data models, so this option does not provide a working data layer in the DR Region at all.","why_zh":"技術上不可能：關聯式的 RDS for MySQL snapshot 無法被『轉換』成 Amazon DynamoDB global table。兩者是完全不同的引擎與資料模型，因此此選項根本無法在 DR 區域提供可運作的資料層。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_ReadRepl.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_ReadRepl.XRgn.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_ReadRepl.Promote.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/disaster-recovery-workloads-on-aws/disaster-recovery-options-in-the-cloud.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":407,"question_en":"A company has AWS accounts that are in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company wants to track Amazon EC2 usage as a metric. The company’s architecture team must receive a daily alert if the EC2 usage is more than 10% higher the average EC2 usage from the last 30 days. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司擁有多個位於 AWS Organizations 組織中的 AWS 帳戶。該公司希望將 Amazon EC2 使用量作為指標進行追蹤。如果 EC2 使用量比過去 30 天的平均 EC2 使用量高出超過 10%，該公司的架構團隊必須每天收到警示。哪個解決方案可滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS Budgets in the organization's management account. Specify a usage type of EC2 running hours. Specify a daily period. Set the budget amount to be 10% more than the reported average usage for the last 30 days from AWS Cost Explorer. Configure an alert to notify the architecture team if the usage threshold is met","B":"Configure AWS Cost Anomaly Detection in the organization's management account. Configure a monitor type of AWS Service. Apply a filter of Amazon EC2. Configure an alert subscription to notify the architecture team if the usage is 10% more than the average usage for the last 30 days.","C":"Enable AWS Trusted Advisor in the organization's management account. Configure a cost optimization advisory alert to notify the architecture team if the EC2 usage is 10% more than the reported average usage for the last 30 days.","D":"Configure Amazon Detective in the organization's management account. Configure an EC2 usage anomaly alert to notify the architecture team if Detective identifies a usage anomaly of more than 10%."},"options_zh":{"A":"在組織的管理帳戶中設定 AWS Budgets。指定使用量類型 (usage type) 為 EC2 執行小時數。指定每日 (daily) 期間。將預算金額設定為 AWS Cost Explorer 報告的過去 30 天平均使用量再加 10%。設定警示，若達到使用量門檻則通知架構團隊。","B":"在組織的管理帳戶中設定 AWS Cost Anomaly Detection。設定監控器類型 (monitor type) 為 AWS Service。套用 Amazon EC2 篩選條件。設定警示訂閱 (alert subscription)，若使用量比過去 30 天平均使用量高出 10%，則通知架構團隊。","C":"在組織的管理帳戶中啟用 AWS Trusted Advisor。設定成本最佳化建議警示，若 EC2 使用量比報告的過去 30 天平均使用量高出 10%，則通知架構團隊。","D":"在組織的管理帳戶中設定 Amazon Detective。設定 EC2 使用量異常警示，若 Detective 偵測到超過 10% 的使用量異常，則通知架構團隊。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":76,"B":24},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"AWS Budgets supports usage budgets that track the usage of a specific service. You can create a budget with a usage type of EC2 running hours, set a daily time period, and define a fixed usage amount. Per the AWS docs, a usage budget lets you 'establish usage limits for one or more services and get notified when usage approaches or exceeds your set threshold.' By querying Cost Explorer for the average EC2 usage over the last 30 days and setting the budget amount to 110% of that average, the architecture team receives a daily alert (via SNS/email) whenever EC2 usage is more than 10% higher than the 30-day average. This directly satisfies the requirement of tracking EC2 usage as a metric and alerting daily on the threshold. AWS Cost Anomaly Detection (B) only detects anomalous SPEND (net unblended cost) using ML models; it does not let you set a user-defined '10% over the 30-day average usage' threshold, and it monitors cost, not usage as a metric. Trusted Advisor (C) and Amazon Detective (D) have no such EC2-usage-versus-average alerting capability (Detective is a security investigation service).","explanation_zh":"AWS Budgets 支援 usage budgets（使用量預算），可追蹤特定服務的使用量。你可以建立一個 usage type 為 EC2 running hours 的預算，設定每日（daily）週期，並指定固定的使用量金額。根據 AWS 文件，usage budget 可『為一個或多個服務設定使用量上限，並在使用量接近或超過設定門檻時收到通知』。先用 Cost Explorer 查出過去 30 天的平均 EC2 使用量，再把預算金額設為該平均值的 110%，架構團隊就能在 EC2 使用量超過 30 天平均值 10% 時，每日透過 SNS/email 收到警示。這正好符合『以使用量為指標追蹤 EC2 並每日警示』的需求。AWS Cost Anomaly Detection（B）只用 ML 偵測異常的『花費』（net unblended cost），無法讓使用者自訂『比 30 天平均使用量高 10%』的門檻，且它監控的是成本而非使用量指標。Trusted Advisor（C）與 Amazon Detective（D）都沒有此類 EC2 使用量對比平均值的警示功能（Detective 是安全調查服務）。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Cost Anomaly Detection monitors anomalous SPEND (net unblended cost) via ML models; its alert subscriptions are based on the dollar/percentage impact of an ML-detected anomaly, not a user-defined '10% over the 30-day average usage' threshold. It tracks cost, not usage as a metric, so the described configuration does not exist.","why_zh":"Cost Anomaly Detection 透過 ML 監控異常『花費』（net unblended cost）；其 alert subscription 門檻是依 ML 偵測出的異常金額/百分比影響，而非使用者自訂的『比 30 天平均使用量高 10%』。它追蹤的是成本而非使用量指標，因此題目描述的設定方式並不存在。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Trusted Advisor cost optimization checks identify idle/underutilized resources and savings opportunities; there is no configurable 'cost optimization advisory alert' that fires when EC2 usage exceeds the 30-day average by 10%.","why_zh":"Trusted Advisor 的成本最佳化檢查是找出閒置/低使用率資源與節省機會；並沒有可設定的『成本最佳化建議警示』能在 EC2 使用量超過 30 天平均 10% 時觸發。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Detective is a security investigation service (analyzes CloudTrail, VPC Flow Logs, and GuardDuty findings). It has no EC2 'usage anomaly alert' feature; this option describes functionality the service does not have.","why_zh":"Amazon Detective 是安全調查服務（分析 CloudTrail、VPC Flow Logs 與 GuardDuty 發現項目）。它沒有 EC2『使用量異常警示』功能；此選項描述的是該服務不具備的能力。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-managing-costs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/manage-ad.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":408,"question_en":"An e-commerce company is revamping its IT infrastructure and is planning to use AWS services. The company’s CIO has asked a solutions architect to design a simple, highly available, and loosely coupled order processing application. The application is responsible for receiving and processing orders before storing them in an Amazon DynamoDB table. The application has a sporadic tra®c pattern and should be able to scale during marketing campaigns to process the orders with minimal delays. Which of the following is the MOST reliable approach to meet the requirements?","question_zh":"一家電子商務公司正在翻新其 IT 基礎設施，並計畫使用 AWS 服務。該公司的 CIO 要求解決方案架構師設計一個簡單、高可用且鬆耦合的訂單處理應用程式。該應用程式負責接收並處理訂單，然後將其儲存到 Amazon DynamoDB 資料表中。該應用程式的流量模式屬於零星型，且應能在行銷活動期間擴展，以最小延遲處理訂單。下列哪一項是滿足這些需求最可靠的做法？","options_en":{"A":"Receive the orders in an Amazon EC2-hosted database and use EC2 instances to process them.","B":"Receive the orders in an Amazon SQS queue and invoke an AWS Lambda function to process them.","C":"Receive the orders using the AWS Step Functions program and launch an Amazon ECS container to process them.","D":"Receive the orders in Amazon Kinesis Data Streams and use Amazon EC2 instances to process them."},"options_zh":{"A":"在一個 Amazon EC2 託管的資料庫中接收訂單，並使用 EC2 執行個體處理這些訂單。","B":"在一個 Amazon SQS 佇列中接收訂單，並叫用 AWS Lambda 函式處理這些訂單。","C":"使用 AWS Step Functions 程式接收訂單，並啟動一個 Amazon ECS 容器來處理這些訂單。","D":"在 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams 中接收訂單，並使用 Amazon EC2 執行個體處理這些訂單。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":83,"C":17},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirements are: simple, highly available, loosely coupled, sporadic/bursty traffic, must scale during marketing campaigns with minimal delay, and store results in DynamoDB. Receiving orders in an Amazon SQS queue and invoking an AWS Lambda function (Option B) is the canonical AWS serverless decoupling pattern. SQS is a fully managed, durable, highly available queue that decouples order ingestion from processing, and Lambda automatically scales event pollers based on message volume (starting at 5 concurrent invokes and ramping up by 300 concurrent invokes per minute to as many as 1,250), making it ideal for sporadic bursts with no servers to manage. This delivers the simplest, most reliable, fully serverless solution that writes to DynamoDB. Option C (Step Functions to 'receive' orders + ECS) is wrong because Step Functions is a workflow orchestrator, not an order-ingestion endpoint, and managing ECS containers adds significant operational complexity that contradicts the 'simple' requirement.","explanation_zh":"需求為:簡單、高可用、鬆耦合、流量零星且突發、行銷活動期間需快速擴展且延遲最小、並將結果存入 DynamoDB。將訂單接收到 Amazon SQS 佇列並觸發 AWS Lambda 函式(選項 B)是 AWS 標準的無伺服器解耦模式。SQS 是全託管、持久、高可用的佇列,將訂單接收與處理解耦;Lambda 會依訊息量自動擴展事件輪詢器(從 5 個並行調用開始,每分鐘增加 300 個並行調用,最高可達 1,250),非常適合零星突發流量且無需管理伺服器。此方案最簡單、最可靠、完全無伺服器並可寫入 DynamoDB。選項 C(用 Step Functions「接收」訂單 + ECS)是錯的,因為 Step Functions 是工作流程編排服務,而非訂單接收端點,且管理 ECS 容器會大幅增加營運複雜度,與「簡單」需求相牴觸。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An EC2-hosted database plus EC2 processing is not loosely coupled, not highly available by default, requires server/patch management, and does not auto-scale simply for bursty traffic. It fails the simple, HA, and decoupling requirements.","why_zh":"EC2 自架資料庫加 EC2 處理並非鬆耦合,預設也非高可用,需自行管理伺服器與修補,且無法簡單地針對突發流量自動擴展。不符合簡單、高可用與解耦的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but is wrong: AWS Step Functions is a workflow orchestrator, not an order-receiving/ingestion endpoint, and launching/managing ECS containers adds operational overhead that contradicts the 'simple' requirement. It is over-engineered for a simple receive-and-store flow.","why_zh":"這是題庫建議答案但錯誤:Step Functions 是工作流程編排服務,並非訂單接收端點,且啟動與管理 ECS 容器會增加營運負擔,與「簡單」需求相違背。對於單純的接收並儲存流程屬於過度設計。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Kinesis Data Streams targets ordered, high-throughput streaming/analytics and requires shard capacity planning; pairing it with EC2 processing adds management overhead and does not scale as effortlessly or simply as SQS + Lambda for sporadic order decoupling.","why_zh":"Kinesis Data Streams 適用於有序、高吞吐的串流/分析,且需規劃分片容量;搭配 EC2 處理會增加管理負擔,對於零星訂單解耦不如 SQS + Lambda 那樣輕鬆且簡單地擴展。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-sqs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-sqs-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/invocation-eventsourcemapping.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-configure-lambda-function-trigger.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":409,"question_en":"A company is deploying AWS Lambda functions that access an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database. The company needs to launch the Lambda functions in a QA environment and in a production environment. The company must not expose credentials within application code and must rotate passwords automatically. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在部署會存取 Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL 資料庫的 AWS Lambda 函式。該公司需要在 QA 環境和生產環境中啟動這些 Lambda 函式。該公司不得在應用程式碼中暴露憑證，且必須自動輪替密碼。哪個解決方案可滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Store the database credentials for both environments in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Encrypt the credentials by using an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key. Within the application code of the Lambda functions, pull the credentials from the Parameter Store parameter by using the AWS SDK for Python (Boto3). Add a role to the Lambda functions to provide access to the Parameter Store parameter.","B":"Store the database credentials for both environments in AWS Secrets Manager with distinct key entry for the QA environment and the production environment. Turn on rotation. Provide a reference to the Secrets Manager key as an environment variable for the Lambda functions.","C":"Store the database credentials for both environments in AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS). Turn on rotation. Provide a reference to the credentials that are stored in AWS KMS as an environment variable for the Lambda functions.","D":"Create separate S3 buckets for the QA environment and the production environment. Turn on server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS) for the S3 buckets. Use an object naming pattern that gives each Lambda function’s application code the ability to pull the correct credentials for the function's corresponding environment. Grant each Lambda function's execution role access to Amazon S3."},"options_zh":{"A":"將這兩個環境的資料庫憑證儲存在 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store 中。使用 AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) 金鑰加密這些憑證。在 Lambda 函式的應用程式碼中，使用 AWS SDK for Python (Boto3) 從 Parameter Store 參數提取憑證。為 Lambda 函式新增一個角色，以提供對該 Parameter Store 參數的存取權。","B":"將這兩個環境的資料庫憑證儲存在 AWS Secrets Manager 中，並為 QA 環境和生產環境分別建立不同的金鑰項目 (key entry)。開啟輪替 (rotation) 功能。將 Secrets Manager 金鑰的參照以環境變數的形式提供給 Lambda 函式。","C":"將這兩個環境的資料庫憑證儲存在 AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) 中。開啟輪替功能。將儲存在 AWS KMS 中的憑證參照以環境變數的形式提供給 Lambda 函式。","D":"為 QA 環境和生產環境分別建立獨立的 S3 儲存貯體。為這些 S3 儲存貯體開啟以 AWS KMS 金鑰進行的伺服器端加密 (SSE-KMS)。使用一種物件命名模式，讓每個 Lambda 函式的應用程式碼能夠提取該函式對應環境的正確憑證。授予每個 Lambda 函式的執行角色對 Amazon S3 的存取權。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The two hard requirements are (1) credentials must not be exposed in application code and (2) passwords must rotate automatically. AWS Secrets Manager is purpose-built for exactly this: it stores database credentials and provides native automatic rotation for Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL (managed rotation or a rotation Lambda that updates both the secret and the database). Storing distinct secrets for QA and production, turning on rotation, and passing the secret reference (ARN/name) as a Lambda environment variable keeps the actual credentials out of code while satisfying automatic rotation. Option A (Parameter Store) is the dump's suggested answer but is wrong because Parameter Store has no built-in automatic credential rotation; it only stores encrypted parameters. The decisive qualifier 'must rotate passwords automatically' eliminates A, C, and D and points to Secrets Manager.","explanation_zh":"兩個硬性需求是 (1) 憑證不可暴露在應用程式碼中，以及 (2) 密碼必須自動輪替。AWS Secrets Manager 正是為此而生：它儲存資料庫憑證，並為 Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL 提供原生的自動輪替（managed rotation 或輪替 Lambda，會同時更新 secret 與資料庫）。為 QA 與 production 各建立不同的 secret、開啟 rotation，並將 secret 參照（ARN 或名稱）以環境變數傳給 Lambda，既讓真正的憑證不出現在程式碼中，又滿足自動輪替。選項 A（Parameter Store）是 dump 建議答案但錯誤，因為 Parameter Store 沒有內建的自動憑證輪替，它只儲存加密參數。決定性條件『必須自動輪替密碼』排除了 A、C、D，指向 Secrets Manager。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Systems Manager Parameter Store can store encrypted credentials and serve them via the SDK, but it has NO native automatic password rotation. It fails the 'rotate passwords automatically' requirement, so it is technically incorrect despite being the dump's suggested answer.","why_zh":"Systems Manager Parameter Store 可儲存加密憑證並透過 SDK 提供，但它沒有原生的自動密碼輪替功能，無法滿足『自動輪替密碼』需求，因此即使是 dump 建議答案也技術上錯誤。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS KMS is a key-management service, not a credential store. You cannot store database credentials in KMS, and KMS key rotation rotates encryption key material, not database passwords. Invalid.","why_zh":"AWS KMS 是金鑰管理服務，不是憑證儲存庫。無法將資料庫憑證儲存於 KMS，且 KMS 金鑰輪替輪的是加密金鑰材料，而非資料庫密碼。不成立。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 with SSE-KMS encrypts objects at rest but provides no mechanism to automatically rotate database passwords. It also adds operational overhead with naming patterns and offers no integration with RDS rotation. Fails the rotation requirement.","why_zh":"S3 加上 SSE-KMS 可加密靜態物件，但沒有自動輪替資料庫密碼的機制，且命名模式增加運維負擔，也無 RDS 輪替整合。無法滿足輪替需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/rotating-secrets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/intro.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-parameter-store.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":410,"question_en":"A company is using AWS Control Tower to manage AWS accounts in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company has an OU that contains accounts. The company must prevent any new or existing Amazon EC2 instances in the OU's accounts from gaining a public IP address. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Control Tower 來管理 AWS Organizations 組織中的 AWS 帳戶。該公司有一個包含多個帳戶的 OU。該公司必須防止該 OU 內帳戶中任何新的或既有的 Amazon EC2 執行個體取得公有 IP 位址。哪個解決方案可滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure all instances in each account in the OU to use AWS Systems Manager. Use a Systems Manager Automation runbook to prevent public IP addresses from being attached to the instances.","B":"Implement the AWS Control Tower proactive control to check whether instances in the OU's accounts have a public IP address. Set the AssociatePublicIpAddress property to False. Attach the proactive control to the OU.","C":"Create an SCP that prevents the launch of instances that have a public IP address. Additionally, configure the SCP to prevent the attachment of a public IP address to existing instances. Attach the SCP to the OU.","D":"Create an AWS Config custom rule that detects instances that have a public IP address. Configure a remediation action that uses an AWS Lambda function to detach the public IP addresses from the instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"設定該 OU 中每個帳戶的所有執行個體使用 AWS Systems Manager。使用 Systems Manager Automation runbook 防止公有 IP 位址被關聯到這些執行個體。","B":"實作 AWS Control Tower 主動式控制 (proactive control)，檢查該 OU 內帳戶中的執行個體是否具有公有 IP 位址。將 AssociatePublicIpAddress 屬性設定為 False。將該主動式控制附加到該 OU。","C":"建立一個 SCP，防止啟動具有公有 IP 位址的執行個體。此外，將該 SCP 設定為防止將公有 IP 位址關聯到既有的執行個體。將該 SCP 附加到該 OU。","D":"建立一個 AWS Config 自訂規則，偵測具有公有 IP 位址的執行個體。設定一個補救動作 (remediation action)，使用 AWS Lambda 函式將公有 IP 位址從這些執行個體中分離。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":55,"B":45},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to PREVENT any new or existing EC2 instances across an OU's accounts from gaining a public IP address. A Service Control Policy is the correct preventive, organization-wide guardrail. AWS documentation (EKS Auto Mode organization controls) explicitly shows the exact SCP: Deny ec2:RunInstances on the network-interface resource when the ec2:AssociatePublicIpAddress condition key is true, which blocks launching instances with auto-assigned public IPs regardless of subnet auto-assign settings. SCPs apply to every principal and every access path (console, CLI, SDK, CloudFormation) and to all accounts in the OU including future accounts, and they also let you deny the association of an Elastic/public IP (ec2:AssociateAddress) to existing instances. Option D (AWS Config custom rule + Lambda) is only detective/reactive: the instance must first launch with a public IP, and there is no API to detach an auto-assigned public IPv4 address from a running instance, so the 'detach via Lambda' premise is technically unsound and it does not PREVENT the condition. Therefore C is the only option that truly prevents the behavior with low operational overhead.","explanation_zh":"需求是要「預防」OU 內各帳戶中任何新的或既有的 EC2 執行個體取得公有 IP 位址。Service Control Policy (SCP) 是正確的、跨組織的預防性護欄。AWS 官方文件（EKS Auto Mode 的組織控制）明確示範了正確的 SCP：當 ec2:AssociatePublicIpAddress 條件鍵為 true 時，對 network-interface 資源 Deny ec2:RunInstances，無論子網路的自動指派設定為何，都能阻止以自動指派公有 IP 的方式啟動執行個體。SCP 套用於所有 principal、所有存取路徑（console、CLI、SDK、CloudFormation）以及 OU 內所有帳戶（含未來加入的帳戶），同時也能 Deny 對既有執行個體關聯 Elastic/公有 IP 的動作（ec2:AssociateAddress）。選項 D（AWS Config 自訂規則 + Lambda）僅屬偵測/事後補救：執行個體必須先以公有 IP 啟動，且並不存在可從執行中執行個體「分離」自動指派公有 IPv4 的 API，因此「用 Lambda 分離公有 IP」在技術上不成立，且無法「預防」此情況。故 C 是唯一能真正預防且維運負擔低的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Systems Manager Automation runbooks are reactive operational automation that requires every instance to be SSM-managed; there is no runbook that prevents a public IP from being assigned, and it provides no organization-wide preventive guardrail.","why_zh":"Systems Manager Automation runbook 是事後的維運自動化，需要每台執行個體都受 SSM 管理；並無可預防公有 IP 被指派的 runbook，也無法提供跨組織的預防性護欄。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Control Tower proactive controls are implemented as CloudFormation preCreate/preUpdate hooks; AWS docs state they may not affect requests made directly through the console, APIs, or SDKs, and they do nothing for existing instances. The described single 'set AssociatePublicIpAddress to False' control also does not match the actual EC2 proactive controls (PR.8/PR.9/PR.11), so it fails the 'any new or existing' requirement.","why_zh":"Control Tower proactive control 以 CloudFormation 的 preCreate/preUpdate hook 實作；AWS 文件指出它可能不會影響直接透過 console、API 或 SDK 發出的請求，且對既有執行個體完全無作用。題目描述的單一『設定 AssociatePublicIpAddress 為 False』控制也與實際的 EC2 proactive control（PR.8/PR.9/PR.11）不符，因此無法滿足『任何新的或既有』的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Config custom rule + Lambda is detective and reactive: the instance must first launch with a public IP before Config evaluates it, so it does not PREVENT the condition. Moreover, there is no API to detach an auto-assigned public IPv4 address from a running instance, making the Lambda remediation technically unworkable. This is the ExamTopics suggested answer but it is wrong.","why_zh":"AWS Config 自訂規則 + Lambda 屬偵測與事後補救：執行個體必須先以公有 IP 啟動，Config 才會評估，因此無法『預防』此情況。再者，並無 API 可從執行中執行個體分離自動指派的公有 IPv4，使得 Lambda 補救在技術上不可行。這是 ExamTopics 的建議答案，但其為錯誤答案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/auto-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/proactive-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/ec2-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/service-authorization/latest/reference/list_amazonec2.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":411,"question_en":"A company is deploying a third-party web application on AWS. The application is packaged as a Docker image. The company has deployed the Docker image as an AWS Fargate service in Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS). An Application Load Balancer (ALB) directs tra®c to the application. The company needs to give only a specific list of users the ability to access the application from the internet. The company cannot change the application and cannot integrate the application with an identity provider. All users must be authenticated through multi-factor authentication (MFA). Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 上部署一個第三方網頁應用程式。該應用程式已封裝為 Docker 映像檔。該公司已將此 Docker 映像檔部署為 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 上的 AWS Fargate 服務。一個 Application Load Balancer (ALB) 將流量導向該應用程式。該公司需要只讓特定名單中的使用者能夠從網際網路存取該應用程式。該公司無法變更該應用程式，也無法將該應用程式與身分提供者整合。所有使用者都必須透過多因素驗證 (MFA) 進行驗證。哪個解決方案可滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a user pool in Amazon Cognito. Configure the pool for the application. Populate the pool with the required users. Configure the pool to require MFConfigure a listener rule on the ALB to require authentication through the Amazon Cognito hosted UI.","B":"Configure the users in AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM). Attach a resource policy to the Fargate service to require users to use MFA. Configure a listener rule on the ALB to require authentication through IAM.","C":"Configure the users in AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM). Enable AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On). Configure resource protection for the ALB. Create a resource protection rule to require users to use MFA.","D":"Create a user pool in AWS Amplify. Configure the pool for the application. Populate the pool with the required users. Configure the pool to require MFA. Configure a listener rule on the ALB to require authentication through the Amplify hosted UI."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon Cognito 中建立一個使用者集區 (user pool)。為該應用程式設定該使用者集區。將所需的使用者加入該使用者集區。設定該使用者集區要求 MFA。在 ALB 上設定一個接聽程式規則 (listener rule)，要求透過 Amazon Cognito 託管 UI 進行驗證。","B":"在 AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) 中設定這些使用者。將一個資源政策附加到 Fargate 服務，要求使用者使用 MFA。在 ALB 上設定一個接聽程式規則，要求透過 IAM 進行驗證。","C":"在 AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) 中設定這些使用者。啟用 AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On)。為 ALB 設定資源保護 (resource protection)。建立一個資源保護規則，要求使用者使用 MFA。","D":"在 AWS Amplify 中建立一個使用者集區。為該應用程式設定該使用者集區。將所需的使用者加入該使用者集區。設定該使用者集區要求 MFA。在 ALB 上設定一個接聽程式規則，要求透過 Amplify 託管 UI 進行驗證。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":93},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":412,"question_en":"A solutions architect is preparing to deploy a new security tool into several previously unused AWS Regions. The solutions architect will deploy the tool by using an AWS CloudFormation stack set. The stack set's template contains an IAM role that has a custom name. Upon creation of the stack set, no stack instances are created successfully. What should the solutions architect do to deploy the stacks successfully?","question_zh":"某解決方案架構師準備將一項新的安全工具部署到多個先前未使用過的 AWS 區域。該解決方案架構師將使用 AWS CloudFormation stack set 來部署此工具。該 stack set 的範本中包含一個具有自訂名稱的 IAM role。建立該 stack set 後，沒有任何 stack instance 成功建立。該解決方案架構師應該怎麼做，才能成功部署這些堆疊？","options_en":{"A":"Enable the new Regions in all relevant accounts. Specify the CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM capability during the creation of the stack set.","B":"Use the Service Quotas console to request a quota increase for the number of CloudFormation stacks in each new Region in all relevant accounts. Specify the CAPABILITY_IAM capability during the creation of the stack set.","C":"Specify the CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM capability and the SELF_MANAGED permissions model during the creation of the stack set.","D":"Specify an administration role ARN and the CAPABILITY_IAM capability during the creation of the stack set."},"options_zh":{"A":"在所有相關帳戶中啟用這些新區域。在建立 stack set 時指定 CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM 功能 (capability)。","B":"使用 Service Quotas 主控台，為所有相關帳戶中每個新區域的 CloudFormation 堆疊數量請求配額提升。在建立 stack set 時指定 CAPABILITY_IAM 功能。","C":"在建立 stack set 時指定 CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM 功能，並使用 SELF_MANAGED 權限模型。","D":"在建立 stack set 時指定一個管理角色 (administration role) 的 ARN，並指定 CAPABILITY_IAM 功能。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":93},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Two distinct failure causes must both be fixed for the stacks to deploy. First, the template defines an IAM role with a custom name; per the CreateStackSet API, IAM resources with custom names require the CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM capability (CAPABILITY_IAM alone causes an InsufficientCapabilities error). Second, the question stresses 'previously unused AWS Regions': Regions introduced after March 20, 2019 are disabled by default and must be enabled in the relevant accounts before stack instances can be created, because the target account must reside in a Region that is currently enabled for that account (and the administrator/management account must have the same Region enabled). Only option A addresses both root causes by enabling the new Regions in all relevant accounts and specifying CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM. The dump's suggested answer C correctly uses CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM but completely ignores the disabled-Region requirement, so deployment would still fail.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個必須同時解決的失敗原因。第一,範本定義了具有自訂名稱的 IAM role;依據 CreateStackSet API,帶有自訂名稱的 IAM 資源必須指定 CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM(僅用 CAPABILITY_IAM 會產生 InsufficientCapabilities 錯誤)。第二,題目強調是「先前未使用的 AWS Region」:2019 年 3 月 20 日之後推出的 Region 預設為停用 (disabled by default),必須先在相關帳戶中啟用,才能建立 stack instance,因為 target account 必須位於對該帳戶目前已啟用的 Region(且 administrator/management 帳戶也須啟用相同 Region)。只有選項 A 同時處理這兩個根本原因:在所有相關帳戶啟用新 Region,並指定 CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM。dump 建議的答案 C 雖然正確使用了 CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM,卻完全忽略停用 Region 的需求,因此部署仍會失敗。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A quota increase for the number of CloudFormation stacks is not the problem (deploying to a few new Regions does not hit stack quotas), and CAPABILITY_IAM is insufficient for a custom-named IAM role, which requires CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM.","why_zh":"增加 CloudFormation stack 數量配額並非問題所在(部署到少數新 Region 不會觸及 stack 配額),而且 CAPABILITY_IAM 不足以涵蓋自訂名稱的 IAM role,後者需要 CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM is correct, but choosing the SELF_MANAGED permissions model does nothing to enable the previously unused (disabled-by-default) Regions. SELF_MANAGED is also the default model, so this option leaves the Region-enablement root cause unresolved and instances would still fail.","why_zh":"CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM 正確,但選擇 SELF_MANAGED 權限模型對啟用先前未使用(預設停用)的 Region 毫無幫助。SELF_MANAGED 本來就是預設模型,因此此選項未解決 Region 啟用這個根本原因,instance 仍會失敗。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Specifying an administration role ARN addresses cross-account trust, not Region enablement, and CAPABILITY_IAM is insufficient for a custom-named IAM role (CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM is required). It fixes neither root cause.","why_zh":"指定 administration role ARN 處理的是跨帳戶信任關係,而非 Region 啟用,且 CAPABILITY_IAM 不足以涵蓋自訂名稱的 IAM role(需 CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM)。兩個根本原因都未解決。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-opt-in-regions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/APIReference/API_CreateStackSet.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/control-access-with-iam.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/accounts/latest/reference/manage-acct-regions.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":413,"question_en":"A company has an application that uses an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster for the application's database. The DB cluster contains one small primary instance and three larger replica instances. The application runs on an AWS Lambda function. The application makes many short-lived connections to the database's replica instances to perform read-only operations. During periods of high tra®c, the application becomes unreliable and the database reports that too many connections are being established. The frequency of high-tra®c periods is unpredictable. Which solution will improve the reliability of the application?","question_zh":"一家公司有一個應用程式，使用 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL 資料庫叢集作為該應用程式的資料庫。此資料庫叢集包含一個小型的主要執行個體 (primary instance) 和三個較大型的複本執行個體 (replica instance)。該應用程式在一個 AWS Lambda 函式上執行。該應用程式會對資料庫的複本執行個體建立大量短暫連線，以執行唯讀操作。在流量高峰期間，該應用程式變得不穩定，且資料庫回報建立的連線數過多。流量高峰期發生的頻率是不可預測的。哪個解決方案可提升該應用程式的可靠性？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon RDS Proxy to create a proxy for the DB cluster. Configure a read-only endpoint for the proxy. Update the Lambda function to connect to the proxy endpoint.","B":"Increase the max_connections setting on the DB cluster's parameter group. Reboot all the instances in the DB cluster. Update the Lambda function to connect to the DB cluster endpoint.","C":"Configure instance scaling for the DB cluster to occur when the DatabaseConnections metric is close to the max connections setting. Update the Lambda function to connect to the Aurora reader endpoint.","D":"Use Amazon RDS Proxy to create a proxy for the DB cluster. Configure a read-only endpoint for the Aurora Data API on the proxy. Update the Lambda function to connect to the proxy endpoint."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon RDS Proxy 為該資料庫叢集建立一個代理 (proxy)。為該代理設定一個唯讀端點。更新該 Lambda 函式，使其連接到該代理端點。","B":"提高該資料庫叢集參數群組 (parameter group) 中的 max_connections 設定。重新啟動該資料庫叢集中的所有執行個體。更新該 Lambda 函式，使其連接到資料庫叢集端點。","C":"設定當 DatabaseConnections 指標接近 max connections 設定時，該資料庫叢集即進行執行個體擴展。更新該 Lambda 函式，使其連接到 Aurora 讀取端點 (reader endpoint)。","D":"使用 Amazon RDS Proxy 為該資料庫叢集建立一個代理。在該代理上為 Aurora Data API 設定一個唯讀端點。更新該 Lambda 函式，使其連接到該代理端點。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The scenario is the canonical use case for Amazon RDS Proxy: a Lambda function opening many short-lived connections that exhausts the database during unpredictable traffic surges. AWS Lambda documentation explicitly recommends RDS Proxy for functions that make frequent short database connections or open and close large numbers of connections, because the proxy pools and shares connections, handles surges, and queues/throttles instead of failing. Configuring a read-only (READ_ONLY target role) proxy endpoint makes the proxy distribute read-only connections across the Aurora reader instances, which matches the application's read-only workload against the three replicas. This fixes the root cause (connection churn/oversubscription) with minimal code change, so A is correct.","explanation_zh":"此情境是 Amazon RDS Proxy 的典型使用案例：Lambda 函式建立大量短暫連線，在不可預測的流量高峰期間耗盡資料庫連線。AWS Lambda 官方文件明確建議，對於頻繁建立短暫連線、或大量開關連線的函式應使用 RDS Proxy，因為 Proxy 會集中並共用連線、處理流量突增，並以排隊/節流取代直接失敗。設定唯讀 (READ_ONLY target role) 的 Proxy 端點後，Proxy 會將唯讀連線分散到 Aurora 的多個讀取副本實例，正好對應此應用程式對三個副本的唯讀工作負載。這直接解決根本原因（連線頻繁建立/過度訂閱），且程式碼變更最少，因此 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Raising max_connections requires rebooting all instances (downtime), consumes more DB memory per connection, and does not address the root cause of rapid connection churn from short-lived Lambda connections. It is brittle for unpredictable surges and high operational overhead.","why_zh":"提高 max_connections 需重啟所有實例（造成停機），每條連線耗用更多資料庫記憶體，且無法解決 Lambda 短暫連線快速建立的根本問題。對不可預測的高峰非常脆弱，且營運負擔高。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Aurora has no native feature that adds provisioned replica instances automatically triggered by the DatabaseConnections metric approaching max_connections. Aurora Replica Auto Scaling adds instances reactively and slowly, and adding instances does not reduce the per-instance connection storm caused by short-lived Lambda connections. It does not solve connection exhaustion for unpredictable bursts.","why_zh":"Aurora 沒有可在 DatabaseConnections 接近 max_connections 時自動新增佈建副本實例的原生機制。Aurora Replica Auto Scaling 反應慢且為被動式，且新增實例無法降低 Lambda 短暫連線在單一實例上造成的連線風暴，無法解決不可預測突增下的連線耗盡問題。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"RDS Proxy and the Aurora Data API are separate, mutually exclusive interfaces. You cannot configure a Data API read-only endpoint on an RDS Proxy; the Data API is a connectionless HTTPS interface and is not layered onto a proxy endpoint. The wording is technically invalid.","why_zh":"RDS Proxy 與 Aurora Data API 是各自獨立、互斥的介面。無法在 RDS Proxy 上設定 Data API 的唯讀端點；Data API 是無連線的 HTTPS 介面，並非疊加在 Proxy 端點之上。此選項描述在技術上不成立。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-rds.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/rds-proxy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/rds-proxy-endpoints.CreatingEndpoint.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/rds-proxy-endpoints.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":414,"question_en":"A retail company is mounting IoT sensors in all of its stores worldwide. During the manufacturing of each sensor, the company’s private certificate authority (CA) issues an X.509 certificate that contains a unique serial number. The company then deploys each certificate to its respective sensor. A solutions architect needs to give the sensors the ability to send data to AWS after they are installed. Sensors must not be able to send data to AWS until they are installed. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家零售公司正在其全球所有門市中安裝 IoT 感測器。在每個感測器的製造過程中，該公司的私有憑證授權單位 (CA) 會發布一張包含唯一序號的 X.509 憑證。該公司隨後將每張憑證部署到對應的感測器上。解決方案架構師需要讓感測器在安裝完成後具備將資料傳送到 AWS 的能力。在感測器安裝完成之前，不得將資料傳送到 AWS。哪個解決方案可滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function that can validate the serial number. Create an AWS IoT Core provisioning template. Include the SerialNumber parameter in the Parameters section. Add the Lambda function as a pre-provisioning hook. During manufacturing, call the RegisterThing API operation and specify the template and parameters.","B":"Create an AWS Step Functions state machine that can validate the serial number. Create an AWS IoT Core provisioning template. Include the SerialNumber parameter in the Parameters section. Specify the Step Functions state machine to validate parameters. Call the StartThingRegistrationTask API operation during installation.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function that can validate the serial number. Create an AWS IoT Core provisioning template. Include the SerialNumber parameter in the Parameters section. Add the Lambda function as a pre-provisioning hook. Register the CA with AWS IoT Core, specify the provisioning template, and set the allow-auto-registration parameter.","D":"Create an AWS IoT Core provisioning template. Include the SerialNumber parameter in the Parameters section. Include parameter validation in the template. Provision a claim certificate and a private key for each device that uses the CA. Grant AWS IoT Core service permissions to update AWS IoT things during provisioning."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個可驗證序號的 AWS Lambda 函式。建立一個 AWS IoT Core 佈建範本 (provisioning template)。在 Parameters 區段中包含 SerialNumber 參數。將該 Lambda 函式新增為預先佈建掛鉤 (pre-provisioning hook)。在製造過程中，呼叫 RegisterThing API 操作並指定該範本與參數。","B":"建立一個可驗證序號的 AWS Step Functions 狀態機。建立一個 AWS IoT Core 佈建範本。在 Parameters 區段中包含 SerialNumber 參數。指定該 Step Functions 狀態機來驗證參數。在安裝過程中呼叫 StartThingRegistrationTask API 操作。","C":"建立一個可驗證序號的 AWS Lambda 函式。建立一個 AWS IoT Core 佈建範本。在 Parameters 區段中包含 SerialNumber 參數。將該 Lambda 函式新增為預先佈建掛鉤。向 AWS IoT Core 註冊該 CA，指定佈建範本，並設定 allow-auto-registration 參數。","D":"建立一個 AWS IoT Core 佈建範本。在 Parameters 區段中包含 SerialNumber 參數。在該範本中加入參數驗證。為每台使用該 CA 的裝置佈建一張聲明憑證 (claim certificate) 及一個私密金鑰。授予 AWS IoT Core 服務在佈建期間更新 AWS IoT things 的權限。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":91},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":415,"question_en":"A startup company recently migrated a large ecommerce website to AWS. The website has experienced a 70% increase in sales. Software engineers are using a private GitHub repository to manage code. The DevOps team is using Jenkins for builds and unit testing. The engineers need to receive notifications for bad builds and zero downtime during deployments. The engineers also need to ensure any changes to production are seamless for users and can be rolled back in the event of a major issue. The software engineers have decided to use AWS CodePipeline to manage their build and deployment process. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家新創公司最近將其大型電子商務網站遷移到 AWS。該網站的銷售額增加了 70%。軟體工程師使用私有的 GitHub 儲存庫來管理程式碼。DevOps 團隊使用 Jenkins 進行建置與單元測試。工程師需要在建置失敗時收到通知，並且在部署期間實現零停機。工程師還需要確保對生產環境的任何變更對使用者而言都是無縫的，並且在發生重大問題時可以復原 (roll back)。這些軟體工程師已決定使用 AWS CodePipeline 來管理其建置與部署流程。哪個解決方案可滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Use GitHub websockets to trigger the CodePipeline pipeline. Use the Jenkins plugin for AWS CodeBuild to conduct unit testing. Send alerts to an Amazon SNS topic for any bad builds. Deploy in an in-place, all-at-once deployment configuration using AWS CodeDeploy.","B":"Use GitHub webhooks to trigger the CodePipeline pipeline. Use the Jenkins plugin for AWS CodeBuild to conduct unit testing. Send alerts to an Amazon SNS topic for any bad builds. Deploy in a blue/green deployment using AWS CodeDeploy.","C":"Use GitHub websockets to trigger the CodePipeline pipeline. Use AWS X-Ray for unit testing and static code analysis. Send alerts to an Amazon SNS topic for any bad builds. Deploy in a blue/green deployment using AWS CodeDeploy.","D":"Use GitHub webhooks to trigger the CodePipeline pipeline. Use AWS X-Ray for unit testing and static code analysis. Send alerts to an Amazon SNS topic for any bad builds. Deploy in an in-place, all-at-once deployment configuration using AWS CodeDeploy."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 GitHub websocket 觸發 CodePipeline 管道 (pipeline)。使用適用於 AWS CodeBuild 的 Jenkins 外掛程式來執行單元測試。針對任何建置失敗，將警示傳送到一個 Amazon SNS 主題 (topic)。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 以就地 (in-place)、一次全部 (all-at-once) 的部署設定進行部署。","B":"使用 GitHub webhook 觸發 CodePipeline 管道。使用適用於 AWS CodeBuild 的 Jenkins 外掛程式來執行單元測試。針對任何建置失敗，將警示傳送到一個 Amazon SNS 主題。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 以藍綠 (blue/green) 部署方式進行部署。","C":"使用 GitHub websocket 觸發 CodePipeline 管道。使用 AWS X-Ray 進行單元測試與靜態程式碼分析。針對任何建置失敗，將警示傳送到一個 Amazon SNS 主題。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 以藍綠部署方式進行部署。","D":"使用 GitHub webhook 觸發 CodePipeline 管道。使用 AWS X-Ray 進行單元測試與靜態程式碼分析。針對任何建置失敗，將警示傳送到一個 Amazon SNS 主題。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 以就地、一次全部的部署設定進行部署。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":416,"question_en":"A software as a service (SaaS) company has developed a multi-tenant environment. The company uses Amazon DynamoDB tables that the tenants share for the storage layer. The company uses AWS Lambda functions for the application services. The company wants to offer a tiered subscription model that is based on resource consumption by each tenant. Each tenant is identified by a unique tenant ID that is sent as part of each request to the Lambda functions. The company has created an AWS Cost and Usage Report (AWS CUR) in an AWS account. The company wants to allocate the DynamoDB costs to each tenant to match that tenant's resource consumption. Which solution will provide a granular view of the DynamoDB cost for each tenant with the LEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"一家軟體即服務 (SaaS) 公司開發了一個多租戶環境。該公司使用租戶共用的 Amazon DynamoDB 資料表作為儲存層。該公司使用 AWS Lambda 函式提供應用程式服務。該公司希望依據每個租戶的資源消耗量，提供分層的訂閱模式。每個租戶都由一個唯一的租戶 ID (tenant ID) 識別，該 ID 會隨每個請求一起傳送給 Lambda 函式。該公司已在一個 AWS 帳戶中建立了 AWS Cost and Usage Report (AWS CUR)。該公司希望將 DynamoDB 成本依各租戶的資源消耗量分配給每個租戶。哪個解決方案能以最少的操作負擔，提供每個租戶精細的 DynamoDB 成本檢視？","options_en":{"A":"Associate a new tag that is named tenant ID with each table in DynamoDB. Activate the tag as a cost allocation tag in the AWS Billing and Cost Management console. Deploy new Lambda function code to log the tenant ID in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Use the AWS CUR to separate DynamoDB consumption cost for each tenant ID.","B":"Configure the Lambda functions to log the tenant ID and the number of RCUs and WCUs consumed from DynamoDB for each transaction to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Deploy another Lambda function to calculate the tenant costs by using the logged capacity units and the overall DynamoDB cost from the AWS Cost Explorer API. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the calculation Lambda function on a schedule.","C":"Create a new partition key that associates DynamoDB items with individual tenants. Deploy a Lambda function to populate the new column as part of each transaction. Deploy another Lambda function to calculate the tenant costs by using Amazon Athena to calculate the number of tenant items from DynamoDB and the overall DynamoDB cost from the AWS CUR. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the calculation Lambda function on a schedule.","D":"Deploy a Lambda function to log the tenant ID, the size of each response, and the duration of the transaction call as custom metrics to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Use CloudWatch Logs Insights to query the custom metrics for each tenant. Use AWS Pricing Calculator to obtain the overall DynamoDB costs and to calculate the tenant costs."},"options_zh":{"A":"為 DynamoDB 中的每張資料表關聯一個名為 tenant ID 的新標籤。在 AWS Billing and Cost Management 主控台中將該標籤啟用為成本分配標籤 (cost allocation tag)。部署新的 Lambda 函式程式碼，將租戶 ID 記錄到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中。使用 AWS CUR 依各租戶 ID 分拆 DynamoDB 消耗成本。","B":"設定這些 Lambda 函式，將每筆交易的租戶 ID，以及從 DynamoDB 消耗的 RCU 與 WCU 數量記錄到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中。部署另一個 Lambda 函式，使用記錄下來的容量單位以及從 AWS Cost Explorer API 取得的整體 DynamoDB 成本，計算各租戶成本。建立一個 Amazon EventBridge 規則，定期排程叫用這個計算用的 Lambda 函式。","C":"建立一個新的分割區索引鍵 (partition key)，將 DynamoDB 項目與個別租戶關聯。部署一個 Lambda 函式，在每筆交易中填入這個新的欄位。部署另一個 Lambda 函式，使用 Amazon Athena 計算 DynamoDB 中各租戶的項目數量，並搭配 AWS CUR 取得的整體 DynamoDB 成本，計算各租戶成本。建立一個 Amazon EventBridge 規則，定期排程叫用這個計算用的 Lambda 函式。","D":"部署一個 Lambda 函式，將租戶 ID、每個回應的大小，以及交易呼叫的持續時間，以自訂指標 (custom metric) 的形式記錄到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中。使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查詢各租戶的自訂指標。使用 AWS Pricing Calculator 取得整體 DynamoDB 成本並計算各租戶成本。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The tenants SHARE the DynamoDB tables (a pooled multi-tenant storage model), and DynamoDB cost allocation tags are applied at the table/resource level. Because each tag key can hold only one value per table, you cannot tag a shared table with a per-tenant ID, so tags can only break costs down per table, not per tenant. DynamoDB throughput is billed by consumed capacity (RCU/WCU or read/write request units), so the AWS-recommended SaaS metering pattern is to capture the ConsumedCapacity that DynamoDB returns on each request, attribute it to the tenant ID, and then proportionally allocate the overall DynamoDB cost across tenants by their share of consumed capacity. Option B does exactly this: it logs tenant ID plus RCUs/WCUs per transaction to CloudWatch Logs and runs a scheduled Lambda to apportion the total DynamoDB cost (from Cost Explorer) by each tenant's consumption. This is the only choice that both maps to the actual DynamoDB billing dimension and matches each tenant's resource consumption, with the least operational effort.","explanation_zh":"各租戶共用同一批 DynamoDB 資料表（pooled 多租戶儲存模型），而 DynamoDB 的成本分配標籤（cost allocation tags）是套用在資料表/資源層級。由於每個標籤鍵在一張表上只能有一個值，無法以每位租戶的 tenant ID 對共用表加標籤，因此標籤只能將成本拆分到「每張表」，而非「每位租戶」。DynamoDB 的吞吐量是依消耗的容量（RCU/WCU 或 read/write request units）計費，所以 AWS 建議的 SaaS 計量做法是擷取 DynamoDB 在每次請求回傳的 ConsumedCapacity，對應到 tenant ID，再依各租戶的消耗占比按比例分攤整體 DynamoDB 成本。選項 B 正是如此：將 tenant ID 與每筆交易的 RCU/WCU 記錄到 CloudWatch Logs，並以排程的 Lambda 依各租戶消耗量（搭配 Cost Explorer 取得的總成本）分攤。這是唯一既對應 DynamoDB 實際計費維度、又能精準對應各租戶資源消耗，且操作負擔最低的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Cost allocation tags are applied at the DynamoDB table (resource) level, and tenants share the tables. A shared table cannot carry a distinct per-tenant tag value, so the CUR can only attribute cost per table, never per tenant. Logging the tenant ID to CloudWatch Logs is not joined to the CUR, so this gives no granular per-tenant DynamoDB cost.","why_zh":"成本分配標籤套用在 DynamoDB 資料表（資源）層級，而租戶共用資料表。共用表無法帶有區分各租戶的標籤值，CUR 只能把成本歸到「每張表」而非「每位租戶」。將 tenant ID 寫入 CloudWatch Logs 也未與 CUR 關聯，因此無法產生細緻的每租戶 DynamoDB 成本。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Counting tenant items via Athena does not reflect DynamoDB throughput billing, which is based on consumed RCUs/WCUs, not item counts; a read-heavy small tenant could cost far more than item count implies. It also requires schema changes (new partition key, populating a column) and Athena setup, which is inaccurate and higher operational effort.","why_zh":"用 Athena 計算租戶項目數量無法反映 DynamoDB 以消耗 RCU/WCU 計費的本質（與項目數無關）；讀取量大的小租戶成本可能遠高於項目數所暗示。此外還需變更結構（新分割鍵、填欄位）與設定 Athena，既不準確又增加操作負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Response size and transaction duration do not map to DynamoDB billing (RCU/WCU). It also uses the AWS Pricing Calculator, which produces forward-looking estimates rather than actual incurred costs, so the resulting per-tenant figures are inaccurate.","why_zh":"回應大小與交易時長無法對應 DynamoDB 的計費維度（RCU/WCU）。此外它使用 AWS Pricing Calculator，產生的是預估值而非實際發生的成本，因此各租戶成本數字並不準確。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/Tagging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/cost-alloc-tags.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/bp-understanding-billing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/saas-lens/tenant-activity-and-consumption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/capacity-mode.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":417,"question_en":"A company has an application that stores data in a single Amazon S3 bucket. The company must keep all data for 1 year. The company’s security team is concerned that an attacker could gain access to the AWS account through leaked long-term credentials. Which solution will ensure that existing and future objects in the S3 bucket are protected?","question_zh":"一家公司有一個應用程式，將資料儲存在單一個 Amazon S3 儲存貯體中。該公司必須將所有資料保留 1 年。該公司的安全團隊擔心攻擊者可能透過洩漏的長期憑證取得該 AWS 帳戶的存取權。哪個解決方案可確保該 S3 儲存貯體中現有及未來的物件都受到保護？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new AWS account that is accessible only to the security team through an assumed role. Create an S3 bucket in the new account. Enable S3 Versioning and S3 Object Lock. Configure a default retention period of 1 year. Set up replication from the existing S3 bucket to the new S3 bucket. Create an S3 Batch Replication job to copy all existing data.","B":"Use the s3-bucket-versioning-enabled AWS Config managed rule. Configure an automatic remediation action that uses an AWS Lambda function to enable S3 Versioning and MFA Delete on noncompliant resources. Add an S3 Lifecycle rule to delete objects after 1 year.","C":"Explicitly deny bucket creation from all users and roles except for an AWS Service Catalog launch constraint role. Define a Service Catalog product for the creation of the S3 bucket to force S3 Versioning and MFA Delete to be enabled. Authorize users to launch the product when they need to create an S3 bucket.","D":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty with the S3 protection feature for the account and the AWS Region. Add an S3 Lifecycle rule to delete objects after 1 year."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個新的 AWS 帳戶，僅允許安全團隊透過擔任角色 (assumed role) 存取。在該新帳戶中建立一個 S3 儲存貯體。啟用 S3 Versioning 和 S3 Object Lock。設定 1 年的預設保留期。設定從現有 S3 儲存貯體到新 S3 儲存貯體的複寫 (replication)。建立一個 S3 Batch Replication 任務，複製所有現有資料。","B":"使用 s3-bucket-versioning-enabled 這個 AWS Config 受管規則 (managed rule)。設定一個自動補救動作，使用 AWS Lambda 函式為不合規資源啟用 S3 Versioning 和 MFA Delete。新增一個 S3 生命週期規則 (Lifecycle rule)，在 1 年後刪除物件。","C":"明確拒絕除 AWS Service Catalog 啟動限制角色 (launch constraint role) 以外的所有使用者和角色建立儲存貯體。定義一個用於建立 S3 儲存貯體的 Service Catalog 產品，強制啟用 S3 Versioning 和 MFA Delete。授權使用者在需要建立 S3 儲存貯體時啟動該產品。","D":"為該帳戶及該 AWS 區域啟用具備 S3 保護功能的 Amazon GuardDuty。新增一個 S3 生命週期規則，在 1 年後刪除物件。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":79,"D":21},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The threat is an attacker with leaked long-term credentials in the AWS account, and the requirement is to PROTECT (prevent destruction of) both existing and future objects while retaining data for 1 year. Option A delivers genuine prevention: it places the data in a separate, isolated AWS account that the compromised source-account credentials cannot reach, enables S3 Versioning + S3 Object Lock with a 1-year default retention (WORM model that prevents deletion/overwrite of locked versions per the S3 Object Lock docs), replicates future objects via S3 Replication, and copies all existing objects with an S3 Batch Replication job. This covers existing AND future objects and is resilient even against an account-root-level attacker in the original account. Option D (GuardDuty S3 Protection) is only a DETECTION control: per the GuardDuty docs it monitors CloudTrail data events and generates findings for suspicious access/destruction, but it does not block or prevent any delete operation; additionally its Lifecycle rule deletes objects after 1 year, which permits rather than prevents data loss. Therefore A is the only option that actually ensures protection against credential-based deletion.","explanation_zh":"威脅情境是攻擊者取得帳戶內外洩的長期憑證，需求是要「保護」(防止破壞) 現有與未來的物件，並保留資料 1 年。選項 A 提供真正的防護：將資料放入一個獨立隔離的 AWS 帳戶，使受損的來源帳戶憑證無法觸及；啟用 S3 Versioning + S3 Object Lock 並設定 1 年預設保留期 (WORM 模型，依 S3 Object Lock 文件可防止已鎖定版本被刪除或覆寫)；透過 S3 Replication 複寫未來物件，並以 S3 Batch Replication job 複製所有現有物件。這同時涵蓋現有與未來物件，即使攻擊者在原帳戶擁有 root 等級權限也無法刪除受保護的複本。選項 D (GuardDuty S3 Protection) 只是「偵測」控制：依 GuardDuty 文件，它監控 CloudTrail data events 並對可疑存取/破壞產生 findings，但無法阻擋或防止任何刪除操作；且其 Lifecycle rule 在 1 年後刪除物件，反而允許資料遺失。因此 A 是唯一真正能確保防止憑證導致刪除的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Config + Lambda remediation only reacts after noncompliance is detected and merely enables Versioning and MFA Delete; MFA Delete protects against version deletion but does not stop an attacker with valid console/CLI access plus a TOTP-less programmatic path in the same account, and it does not protect existing object versions retroactively against an account-level compromise. It also relies on the same account that is compromised.","why_zh":"AWS Config + Lambda 補救僅在偵測到不合規後才反應，只啟用 Versioning 與 MFA Delete；MFA Delete 雖能防止版本刪除，但無法抵禦同一個 (已受損) 帳戶內具有效存取權的攻擊者，且無法對現有物件版本提供溯及性的帳戶級保護，仍依賴遭入侵的同一帳戶。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Using Service Catalog to force Versioning + MFA Delete only governs how NEW buckets are created going forward; it does nothing to protect the existing bucket and its existing objects, and it does not isolate data from credentials compromised in the same account.","why_zh":"使用 Service Catalog 強制 Versioning + MFA Delete 只約束未來「新建」儲存貯體的建立方式，完全無法保護現有儲存貯體與其現有物件，也未將資料與同帳戶內遭外洩的憑證隔離。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"GuardDuty S3 Protection is detection-only: it monitors CloudTrail S3 data events and raises findings but cannot prevent an attacker from deleting objects. The added Lifecycle rule deletes objects after 1 year, enabling data loss rather than enforcing immutability. It provides no WORM/Object Lock protection for existing or future objects.","why_zh":"GuardDuty S3 Protection 只能偵測：它監控 CloudTrail S3 data events 並產生 findings，但無法阻止攻擊者刪除物件。額外的 Lifecycle rule 在 1 年後刪除物件，反而促成資料遺失，而非強制不可變性。它對現有或未來物件都未提供 WORM/Object Lock 保護。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lock.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lock-configure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/s3-batch-replication-batch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/s3-protection.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":418,"question_en":"A company needs to improve the security of its web-based application on AWS. The application uses Amazon CloudFront with two custom origins. The first custom origin routes requests to an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API. The second custom origin routes tra®c to an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The application integrates with an OpenID Connect (OIDC) identity provider (IdP) for user management. A security audit shows that a JSON Web Token (JWT) authorizer provides access to the API. The security audit also shows that the ALB accepts requests from unauthenticated users. A solutions architect must design a solution to ensure that all backend services respond to only authenticated users. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司需要提升其在 AWS 上網頁應用程式的安全性。該應用程式使用具有兩個自訂來源 (custom origin) 的 Amazon CloudFront。第一個自訂來源將請求路由到一個 Amazon API Gateway HTTP API。第二個自訂來源將流量路由到一個 Application Load Balancer (ALB)。該應用程式與一個 OpenID Connect (OIDC) 身分提供者 (IdP) 整合，以管理使用者。安全稽核顯示，有一個 JSON Web Token (JWT) 授權者 (authorizer) 提供對該 API 的存取權。安全稽核還顯示，該 ALB 接受來自未經驗證使用者的請求。解決方案架構師必須設計一個解決方案，確保所有後端服務只回應已驗證的使用者。哪個解決方案可滿足此需求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the ALB to enforce authentication and authorization by integrating the ALB with the IdP. Allow only authenticated users to access the backend services.","B":"Modify the CloudFront configuration to use signed URLs. Implement a permissive signing policy that allows any request to access the backend services.","C":"Create an AWS WAF web ACL that filters out unauthenticated requests at the ALB level. Allow only authenticated tra®c to reach the backend services.","D":"Enable AWS CloudTrail to log all requests that come to the ALB. Create an AWS Lambda function to analyze the logs and block any requests that come from unauthenticated users."},"options_zh":{"A":"設定該 ALB 與該 IdP 整合，以強制執行驗證與授權。僅允許已驗證的使用者存取後端服務。","B":"修改 CloudFront 設定以使用簽署 URL (signed URL)。實作一個寬鬆的簽署政策 (signing policy)，允許任何請求存取後端服務。","C":"建立一個 AWS WAF web ACL，在 ALB 層級篩除未經驗證的請求。僅允許已驗證的流量到達後端服務。","D":"啟用 AWS CloudTrail，記錄所有傳送到該 ALB 的請求。建立一個 AWS Lambda 函式來分析這些日誌，並封鎖所有來自未經驗證使用者的請求。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The Application Load Balancer has a native feature to authenticate users by integrating directly with an OIDC-compliant identity provider. The ALB can offload the work of authenticating users so backend services only receive authenticated requests, and it issues/validates session cookies and JWT claims. AWS documentation even provides a dedicated 'Prepare to use Amazon CloudFront' section for exactly this architecture (CloudFront in front of an ALB with OIDC authentication), which matches the question's setup. Since the API Gateway HTTP API already uses a JWT authorizer tied to the same OIDC IdP, configuring the ALB to enforce OIDC authentication brings the ALB to parity, ensuring all backend services respond only to authenticated users. This is the purpose-built, lowest-overhead solution.","explanation_zh":"Application Load Balancer 內建可直接與符合 OIDC 的身分提供者 (IdP) 整合來驗證使用者的功能。ALB 可以將驗證使用者的工作卸載到負載平衡器，使後端服務只接收已驗證的請求，並負責簽發/驗證 session cookie 與 JWT claims。AWS 文件甚至提供專門的「Prepare to use Amazon CloudFront」章節，正是針對這個架構（CloudFront 位於 ALB 前方並使用 OIDC 驗證），完全符合題目情境。由於 API Gateway HTTP API 已經使用綁定相同 OIDC IdP 的 JWT authorizer，將 ALB 設定為強制執行 OIDC 驗證可使 ALB 達到相同水準，確保所有後端服務只回應已驗證的使用者。這是專為此用途設計、營運負擔最低的解決方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Signed URLs only verify that a request was signed by the distribution owner; they do not authenticate end users against an OIDC IdP. A 'permissive signing policy that allows any request' explicitly defeats the goal of restricting access to authenticated users.","why_zh":"Signed URL 僅驗證請求是否由發佈擁有者簽署，並不會針對 OIDC IdP 驗證終端使用者。題目所述「允許任何請求的寬鬆簽署政策」更是直接違背了僅限已驗證使用者存取的目標。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS WAF inspects request attributes (IP, headers, rate, patterns) but has no built-in concept of OIDC user authentication; it cannot determine whether a user has a valid IdP session. WAF cannot perform the OAuth2/OIDC login flow that distinguishes authenticated from unauthenticated users.","why_zh":"AWS WAF 檢查請求屬性（IP、標頭、速率、樣式），但沒有內建的 OIDC 使用者驗證概念，無法判斷使用者是否擁有有效的 IdP 工作階段。WAF 無法執行用以區分已驗證與未驗證使用者的 OAuth2/OIDC 登入流程。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but is wrong. CloudTrail logs AWS API/management activity, not ALB data-plane user requests, and ALB does not natively emit per-request user traffic to CloudTrail. Analyzing logs and blocking after the fact is reactive (requests already reached the backend), high-overhead, and cannot enforce authentication in real time.","why_zh":"這是題庫建議的答案，但是錯誤的。CloudTrail 記錄的是 AWS API/管理活動，而非 ALB 資料層的使用者請求，ALB 不會原生地將每筆使用者流量送往 CloudTrail。事後分析日誌再封鎖屬於被動式（請求早已到達後端）、營運負擔高，且無法即時強制執行驗證。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/listener-authenticate-users.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/http-api-jwt-authorizer.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":419,"question_en":"A company creates an AWS Control Tower landing zone to manage and govern a multi-account AWS environment. The company's security team will deploy preventive controls and detective controls to monitor AWS services across all the accounts. The security team needs a centralized view of the security state of all the accounts. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司建立了一個 AWS Control Tower 登陸區 (landing zone)，用於管理與治理一個多帳戶的 AWS 環境。該公司的安全團隊將部署預防性控制 (preventive control) 和偵測性控制 (detective control)，以監控所有帳戶中的 AWS 服務。該安全團隊需要一個集中式檢視，以查看所有帳戶的安全狀態。哪個解決方案可滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"From the AWS Control Tower management account, use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy an AWS Config conformance pack to all accounts in the organization.","B":"Enable Amazon Detective for the organization in AWS Organizations. Designate one AWS account as the delegated administrator for Detective.","C":"From the AWS Control Tower management account, deploy an AWS CloudFormation stack set that uses the automatic deployment option to enable Amazon Detective for the organization.","D":"Enable AWS Security Hub for the organization in AWS Organizations. Designate one AWS account as the delegated administrator for Security Hub."},"options_zh":{"A":"從 AWS Control Tower 管理帳戶中，使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets，將一個 AWS Config conformance pack 部署到組織中的所有帳戶。","B":"在 AWS Organizations 中為該組織啟用 Amazon Detective。指定一個 AWS 帳戶作為 Detective 的委派管理員 (delegated administrator)。","C":"從 AWS Control Tower 管理帳戶中，部署一個使用自動部署選項的 AWS CloudFormation stack set，為該組織啟用 Amazon Detective。","D":"在 AWS Organizations 中為該組織啟用 AWS Security Hub。指定一個 AWS 帳戶作為 Security Hub 的委派管理員。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is a centralized view of the security state across all accounts, with detective and preventive controls already feeding findings. AWS Security Hub is purpose-built for this: it provides a comprehensive view of your security state, aggregates findings across all AWS accounts, and acts as a single pane of glass that ingests findings from GuardDuty, Inspector, Macie, AWS Config, and Control Tower controls. Integrating Security Hub with AWS Organizations and designating a delegated administrator automatically enrolls member accounts and centralizes findings with the least operational overhead. Option A (Config conformance pack via StackSets) only delivers Config compliance data, not a centralized security-state dashboard, and is more operationally complex. Amazon Detective (B and C) is for deep root-cause investigation of specific GuardDuty findings, not a centralized security-state view.","explanation_zh":"需求是跨所有帳戶的集中式安全狀態檢視，且偵測性與預防性控制已在產生 findings。AWS Security Hub 正是為此設計：它提供完整的安全狀態檢視、彙整所有 AWS 帳戶的 findings，並作為單一管理面板，吸收來自 GuardDuty、Inspector、Macie、AWS Config 與 Control Tower 控制的 findings。將 Security Hub 與 AWS Organizations 整合並指定一個委派管理員 (delegated administrator)，可自動納入成員帳戶並集中彙整 findings，營運負擔最低。選項 A（透過 StackSets 部署 Config conformance pack）僅提供 Config 合規資料，並非集中式安全狀態儀表板，且營運上更複雜。Amazon Detective（B 與 C）用於針對特定 GuardDuty findings 進行深入根因調查，而非集中式安全狀態檢視。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A Config conformance pack deployed via StackSets only provides AWS Config rule compliance status, not a unified security-state view that aggregates findings from multiple security services. It also requires more setup and ongoing management than the native Security Hub Organizations integration.","why_zh":"透過 StackSets 部署的 Config conformance pack 只提供 AWS Config 規則的合規狀態，並非彙整多個安全服務 findings 的統一安全狀態檢視。相較於原生的 Security Hub Organizations 整合，它也需要更多設定與持續管理。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Detective is an investigation tool that visualizes and finds root causes of specific GuardDuty/security findings using a behavior graph. It does not provide a centralized security-state dashboard across all accounts, so it does not meet the stated requirement.","why_zh":"Amazon Detective 是調查工具，使用行為圖視覺化並找出特定 GuardDuty/安全 findings 的根因。它不提供跨所有帳戶的集中式安全狀態儀表板，故不符合需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Same wrong service as B—Detective is for investigation, not a centralized security-state view. Detective also has native AWS Organizations integration with a delegated administrator, so using a CloudFormation StackSet to enable it is both the wrong tool and an unnecessarily complex method.","why_zh":"與 B 同樣選錯服務—Detective 用於調查，並非集中式安全狀態檢視。Detective 也具備原生的 AWS Organizations 整合與委派管理員，因此用 CloudFormation StackSet 啟用既選錯工具，方法也過於複雜。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/what-is-securityhub.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/designate-orgs-admin-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/detective/latest/userguide/what-is-detective.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":420,"question_en":"A company that develops consumer electronics with o®ces in Europe and Asia has 60 TB of software images stored on premises in Europe. The company wants to transfer the images to an Amazon S3 bucket in the ap-northeast-1 Region. New software images are created daily and must be encrypted in transit. The company needs a solution that does not require custom development to automatically transfer all existing and new software images to Amazon S3. What is the next step in the transfer process?","question_zh":"一家在歐洲和亞洲設有辦事處的消費電子產品開發公司，在歐洲的本地端儲存了 60 TB 的軟體映像檔。該公司希望將這些映像檔傳輸到 ap-northeast-1 區域中的 Amazon S3 儲存桶。新的軟體映像檔每天都會產生，且必須在傳輸過程中進行加密。該公司需要一種不需要自訂開發即可自動將所有現有及新增軟體映像檔傳輸到 Amazon S3 的解決方案。傳輸過程的下一步應該是什麼？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an AWS DataSync agent and configure a task to transfer the images to the S3 bucket.","B":"Configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transfer the images using S3 Transfer Acceleration.","C":"Use an AWS Snowball device to transfer the images with the S3 bucket as the target.","D":"Transfer the images over a Site-to-Site VPN connection using the S3 API with multipart upload."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署 AWS DataSync 代理程式，並設定任務以將映像檔傳輸到 S3 儲存桶。","B":"設定 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose，使用 S3 Transfer Acceleration 來傳輸映像檔。","C":"使用 AWS Snowball 裝置，以 S3 儲存桶作為目標來傳輸映像檔。","D":"透過 Site-to-Site VPN 連線，使用 S3 API 的多部分上傳功能來傳輸映像檔。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Security/IAM","Storage","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":421,"question_en":"A company has a web application that uses Amazon API Gateway. AWS Lambda, and Amazon DynamoDB. A recent marketing campaign has increased demand. Monitoring software reports that many requests have significantly longer response times than before the marketing campaign. A solutions architect enabled Amazon CloudWatch Logs for API Gateway and noticed that errors are occurring on 20% of the requests. In CloudWatch, the Lambda function Throttles metric represents 1% of the requests and the Errors metric represents 10% of the requests. Application logs indicate that, when errors occur, there is a call to DynamoDB. What change should the solutions architect make to improve the current response times as the web application becomes more popular?","question_zh":"一家公司有一個使用 Amazon API Gateway、AWS Lambda 和 Amazon DynamoDB 的 Web 應用程式。最近的行銷活動使需求增加。監控軟體回報，許多請求的回應時間比行銷活動之前明顯延長。解決方案架構師為 API Gateway 啟用了 Amazon CloudWatch Logs，並注意到 20% 的請求發生錯誤。在 CloudWatch 中，Lambda 函數的 Throttles 指標佔請求的 1%，Errors 指標則佔請求的 10%。應用程式日誌顯示，發生錯誤時都會呼叫 DynamoDB。隨著 Web 應用程式越來越受歡迎，解決方案架構師應該進行哪項變更以改善目前的回應時間？","options_en":{"A":"Increase the concurrency limit of the Lambda function.","B":"Implement DynamoDB auto scaling on the table.","C":"Increase the API Gateway throttle limit.","D":"Re-create the DynamoDB table with a better-partitioned primary index."},"options_zh":{"A":"提高 Lambda 函數的並行限制。","B":"在該表格上實作 DynamoDB 自動擴展。","C":"提高 API Gateway 的限流限制。","D":"使用分區更佳的主索引重新建立 DynamoDB 表格。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":422,"question_en":"A company has an application that has a web frontend. The application runs in the company's on-premises data center and requires access to file storage for critical data. The application runs on three Linux VMs for redundancy. The architecture includes a load balancer with HTTP request-based routing. The company needs to migrate the application to AWS as quickly as possible. The architecture on AWS must be highly available. Which solution will meet these requirements with the FEWEST changes to the architecture?","question_zh":"一家公司有一個具備 Web 前端的應用程式。該應用程式在公司的本地端資料中心運行，需要存取檔案儲存體來處理關鍵資料。為提供備援，該應用程式在三台 Linux VM 上運行。此架構包含一個以 HTTP 請求為基礎進行路由的負載平衡器。該公司需要盡快將應用程式遷移到 AWS。AWS 上的架構必須具備高可用性。哪種解決方案能以對架構的最少變更來滿足這些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate the application to Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) containers that use the Fargate launch type in three Availability Zones. Use Amazon S3 to provide file storage for all three containers. Use a Network Load Balancer to direct tra®c to the containers.","B":"Migrate the application to Amazon EC2 instances in three Availability Zones. Use Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) for file storage. Mount the file storage on all three EC2 instances. Use an Application Load Balancer to direct tra®c to the EC2 instances.","C":"Migrate the application to Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) containers that use the Fargate launch type in three Availability Zones. Use Amazon FSx for Lustre to provide file storage for all three containers. Use a Network Load Balancer to direct tra®c to the containers.","D":"Migrate the application to Amazon EC2 instances in three AWS Regions. Use Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) for file storage. Enable Cross-Region Replication (CRR) for all three EC2 instances. Use an Application Load Balancer to direct tra®c to the EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"將應用程式遷移到三個可用區域中使用 Fargate 啟動類型的 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 容器。使用 Amazon S3 為所有三個容器提供檔案儲存體。使用 Network Load Balancer 將流量導向這些容器。","B":"將應用程式遷移到三個可用區域中的 Amazon EC2 執行個體。使用 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 作為檔案儲存體。將檔案儲存體掛載到所有三個 EC2 執行個體上。使用 Application Load Balancer 將流量導向這些 EC2 執行個體。","C":"將應用程式遷移到三個可用區域中使用 Fargate 啟動類型的 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 容器。使用 Amazon FSx for Lustre 為所有三個容器提供檔案儲存體。使用 Network Load Balancer 將流量導向這些容器。","D":"將應用程式遷移到三個 AWS 區域中的 Amazon EC2 執行個體。使用 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 作為檔案儲存體。為所有三個 EC2 執行個體啟用跨區域複寫 (CRR)。使用 Application Load Balancer 將流量導向這些 EC2 執行個體。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":423,"question_en":"A company is planning to migrate an on-premises data center to AWS. The company currently hosts the data center on Linux-based VMware VMs. A solutions architect must collect information about network dependencies between the VMs. The information must be in the form of a diagram that details host IP addresses, hostnames, and network connection information. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司計劃將本地端資料中心遷移到 AWS。該公司目前在以 Linux 為基礎的 VMware VM 上託管資料中心。解決方案架構師必須收集 VM 之間網路相依性的相關資訊。這些資訊必須以圖表形式呈現，詳細列出主機 IP 位址、主機名稱和網路連線資訊。哪種解決方案能滿足這些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Application Discovery Service. Select an AWS Migration Hub home AWS Region. Install the AWS Application Discovery Agent on the on-premises servers for data collection. Grant permissions to Application Discovery Service to use the Migration Hub network diagrams.","B":"Use the AWS Application Discovery Service Agentless Collector for server data collection. Export the network diagrams from the AWS Migration Hub in .png format.","C":"Install the AWS Application Migration Service agent on the on-premises servers for data collection. Use AWS Migration Hub data in Workload Discovery on AWS to generate network diagrams.","D":"Install the AWS Application Migration Service agent on the on-premises servers for data collection. Export data from AWS Migration Hub in .csv format into an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard to generate network diagrams."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Application Discovery Service。選擇一個 AWS Migration Hub 主要 AWS 區域。在本地端伺服器上安裝 AWS Application Discovery Agent 以收集資料。授予 Application Discovery Service 使用 Migration Hub 網路圖表的權限。","B":"使用 AWS Application Discovery Service Agentless Collector 來收集伺服器資料。以 .png 格式從 AWS Migration Hub 匯出網路圖表。","C":"在本地端伺服器上安裝 AWS Application Migration Service 代理程式以收集資料。使用 AWS Migration Hub 資料，在 Workload Discovery on AWS 中產生網路圖表。","D":"在本地端伺服器上安裝 AWS Application Migration Service 代理程式以收集資料。以 .csv 格式從 AWS Migration Hub 匯出資料到 Amazon CloudWatch 儀表板中以產生網路圖表。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":88},"tags":["Migration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is a diagram of network dependencies between on-premises Linux VMware VMs showing host IP addresses, hostnames, and network connection information. The AWS Migration Hub network diagram is exactly this feature: it visualizes server dependencies, detailed server info (IP, hostname), and network connection information between servers. Its documented prerequisite is that the AWS Application Discovery Service Discovery Agent must be running on all on-premises servers to be mapped, and you must first choose a Migration Hub home Region before deploying the agent. The Discovery Agent collects hostName, ipAddress, sourceIp/destinationIp, and TCP network connections. Accessing the network diagram also requires the discovery:GetNetworkConnectionGraph IAM permission. Option A captures all of these steps (home Region, Discovery Agent install, and granting permission to use the network diagram), making it the only correct solution.","explanation_zh":"需求是要產生一張呈現地端 Linux VMware VM 之間網路相依關係的圖,並包含主機 IP 位址、主機名稱與網路連線資訊。AWS Migration Hub 的 network diagram 正好就是這個功能:它能視覺化伺服器相依性、顯示伺服器詳細資訊(IP、hostname),以及伺服器之間的網路連線資訊。其文件明載的先決條件是:必須在所有要繪製的地端伺服器上執行 AWS Application Discovery Service 的 Discovery Agent,且部署 agent 前必須先選擇 Migration Hub home Region。Discovery Agent 會收集 hostName、ipAddress、sourceIp/destinationIp 與 TCP 網路連線。存取 network diagram 還需要 discovery:GetNetworkConnectionGraph 這個 IAM 權限。選項 A 涵蓋了上述所有步驟(選 home Region、安裝 Discovery Agent、授予使用 network diagram 的權限),是唯一正確的解法。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The Migration Hub network diagram explicitly requires the Application Discovery Service Discovery Agent on each server; the Agentless Collector does not feed the network diagram. Also 'export network diagrams in .png' is not the documented workflow.","why_zh":"Migration Hub network diagram 明確要求每台伺服器安裝 Application Discovery Service Discovery Agent;Agentless Collector 無法產生 network diagram。且文件中沒有「以 .png 匯出網路圖」這種流程。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) agent is for replicating/migrating servers, not for discovering network dependencies. Workload Discovery on AWS visualizes resources already inside an AWS account, not on-premises VM network dependencies.","why_zh":"AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) 的 agent 是用來複寫/遷移伺服器,並非用於探索網路相依性。Workload Discovery on AWS 是視覺化 AWS 帳戶內既有資源,而非地端 VM 的網路相依關係。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but is wrong: the MGN agent does not collect dependency data, and an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard cannot generate network dependency diagrams from a .csv export. Migration Hub does not export to CloudWatch for this purpose.","why_zh":"這是題庫建議答案但錯誤:MGN agent 不收集相依性資料,且 Amazon CloudWatch dashboard 無法由 .csv 匯出產生網路相依圖。Migration Hub 也不會為此匯出到 CloudWatch。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/migrationhub/latest/ug/network-diagram.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/migrationhub/latest/ug/network-diagram-prerequisites.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/migrationhub/latest/ug/network-diagram-troubleshooting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/discovery-agent.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":424,"question_en":"A company runs a software-as-a-service (SaaS) application on AWS. The application consists of AWS Lambda functions and an Amazon RDS for MySQL Multi-AZ database. During market events, the application has a much higher workload than normal. Users notice slow response times during the peak periods because of many database connections. The company needs to improve the scalable performance and availability of the database. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上運行一個軟體即服務 (SaaS) 應用程式。該應用程式由 AWS Lambda 函數和一個 Amazon RDS for MySQL 多可用區資料庫組成。在市場活動期間，該應用程式的工作負載遠高於正常水準。由於大量的資料庫連線，使用者在高峰時段會注意到回應時間變慢。該公司需要改善資料庫的可擴展效能和可用性。哪種解決方案能滿足這些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm action that triggers a Lambda function to add an Amazon RDS for MySQL read replica when resource utilization hits a threshold.","B":"Migrate the database to Amazon Aurora, and add a read replica. Add a database connection pool outside of the Lambda handler function.","C":"Migrate the database to Amazon Aurora, and add a read replica. Use Amazon Route 53 weighted records.","D":"Migrate the database to Amazon Aurora, and add an Aurora Replica. Configure Amazon RDS Proxy to manage database connection pools."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個 Amazon CloudWatch 警示動作，當資源使用率達到門檻值時觸發 Lambda 函數以新增 Amazon RDS for MySQL 讀取複本。","B":"將資料庫遷移到 Amazon Aurora，並新增一個讀取複本。在 Lambda 處理函數之外新增一個資料庫連線池。","C":"將資料庫遷移到 Amazon Aurora，並新增一個讀取複本。使用 Amazon Route 53 加權記錄。","D":"將資料庫遷移到 Amazon Aurora，並新增一個 Aurora 複本。設定 Amazon RDS Proxy 來管理資料庫連線池。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":425,"question_en":"A company is planning to migrate an application from on premises to the AWS Cloud. The company will begin the migration by moving the application’s underlying data storage to AWS. The application data is stored on a shared file system on premises, and the application servers connect to the shared file system through SMB. A solutions architect must implement a solution that uses an Amazon S3 bucket for shared storage. Until the application is fully migrated and code is rewritten to use native Amazon S3 APIs, the application must continue to have access to the data through SMB. The solutions architect must migrate the application data to AWS to its new location while still allowing the on-premises application to access the data. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司計劃將應用程式從本地端遷移到 AWS Cloud。該公司將先把應用程式的基礎資料儲存體遷移到 AWS，以此展開遷移工作。應用程式資料儲存在本地端的共用檔案系統上，應用程式伺服器透過 SMB 連接到該共用檔案系統。解決方案架構師必須實作一個使用 Amazon S3 儲存桶作為共用儲存體的解決方案。在應用程式完全遷移並重寫程式碼以使用原生 Amazon S3 API 之前，該應用程式必須繼續透過 SMB 存取資料。解決方案架構師必須將應用程式資料遷移到 AWS 上的新位置，同時仍允許本地端應用程式存取這些資料。哪種解決方案能滿足這些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new Amazon FSx for Windows File Server file system. Configure AWS DataSync with one location for the on-premises file share and one location for the new Amazon FSx file system. Create a new DataSync task to copy the data from the on-premises file share location to the Amazon FSx file system.","B":"Create an S3 bucket for the application. Copy the data from the on-premises storage to the S3 bucket.","C":"Deploy an AWS Server Migration Service (AWS SMS) VM to the on-premises environment. Use AWS SMS to migrate the file storage server from on premises to an Amazon EC2 instance.","D":"Create an S3 bucket for the application. Deploy a new AWS Storage Gateway file gateway on an on-premises VM. Create a new file share that stores data in the S3 bucket and is associated with the file gateway. Copy the data from the on-premises storage to the new file gateway endpoint."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個新的 Amazon FSx for Windows File Server 檔案系統。設定 AWS DataSync，其中一個位置為本地端檔案共用，另一個位置為新的 Amazon FSx 檔案系統。建立一個新的 DataSync 任務，將資料從本地端檔案共用位置複製到 Amazon FSx 檔案系統。","B":"為應用程式建立一個 S3 儲存桶。將資料從本地端儲存體複製到 S3 儲存桶。","C":"在本地端環境中部署一個 AWS Server Migration Service (AWS SMS) VM。使用 AWS SMS 將檔案儲存伺服器從本地端遷移到 Amazon EC2 執行個體。","D":"為應用程式建立一個 S3 儲存桶。在本地端 VM 上部署一個新的 AWS Storage Gateway 檔案閘道。建立一個新的檔案共用，將資料儲存在 S3 儲存桶中，並與該檔案閘道建立關聯。將資料從本地端儲存體複製到新的檔案閘道端點。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":93},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirements are explicit: shared storage must be an Amazon S3 bucket, AND the on-premises application must continue to access that data via SMB until the code is rewritten to use native S3 APIs. Only AWS Storage Gateway S3 File Gateway satisfies both conditions simultaneously. An S3 File Gateway is deployed on premises as a VM and presents an SMB (or NFS) file share whose objects are stored directly in an S3 bucket; per AWS docs, it lets you 'store and retrieve objects in Amazon S3 using industry-standard file protocols such as NFS and SMB' and acts as a file system mount on Amazon S3. Copying the on-premises data to the file gateway endpoint writes it into the target S3 bucket while the application keeps SMB access. Option A (FSx for Windows + DataSync) stores data in an FSx file system, NOT in an S3 bucket, so it fails the core S3-bucket requirement. The marked dump answer (A) is therefore wrong.","explanation_zh":"需求很明確：共享儲存必須是 Amazon S3 bucket，而且在程式碼改寫為使用原生 S3 API 之前，地端應用程式必須持續透過 SMB 存取資料。只有 AWS Storage Gateway 的 S3 File Gateway 能同時滿足這兩個條件。S3 File Gateway 以 VM 形式部署在地端，提供 SMB（或 NFS）檔案共享，而其物件直接儲存在 S3 bucket 中；根據 AWS 文件，它可讓你『使用 NFS、SMB 等業界標準檔案協定在 Amazon S3 中存取物件』，等同於掛載在 S3 上的檔案系統。將地端資料複製到 file gateway 端點即會寫入目標 S3 bucket，同時應用程式仍維持 SMB 存取。選項 A（FSx for Windows + DataSync）將資料儲存在 FSx 檔案系統，而非 S3 bucket，因此不符合核心的 S3-bucket 需求。故 dump 標記答案 A 是錯的。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"FSx for Windows File Server stores data in an FSx file system, not in an S3 bucket. The requirement explicitly mandates an S3 bucket for shared storage, so DataSync-to-FSx fails the core requirement even though it does provide SMB access.","why_zh":"FSx for Windows File Server 將資料儲存在 FSx 檔案系統，而非 S3 bucket。需求明確要求以 S3 bucket 作為共享儲存，所以 DataSync 到 FSx 雖能提供 SMB 存取，仍不符合核心需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Simply copying data into an S3 bucket meets the storage target but provides no SMB interface, so the on-premises application can no longer access the data until the code is rewritten. It breaks the continued-SMB-access requirement.","why_zh":"單純把資料複製到 S3 bucket 雖達成儲存目標，但沒有 SMB 介面，地端應用程式在程式碼改寫前無法存取資料，違反持續 SMB 存取的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS SMS (now part of MGN) migrates the entire server as an EC2 instance; data ends up on EBS in EC2, not in an S3 bucket, and it does not address on-premises SMB access to S3 data. It is a server lift-and-shift, not the requested data-storage migration to S3.","why_zh":"AWS SMS（現屬 MGN）是將整台伺服器遷移為 EC2 執行個體，資料最終落在 EC2 的 EBS，而非 S3 bucket，也未解決地端透過 SMB 存取 S3 資料的需求。這是伺服器搬遷，並非題目要求的 S3 資料儲存遷移。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/filegateway/latest/files3/what-is-file-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/filegateway/latest/files3/CreatingAnSMBFileShare.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/filegateway/latest/files3/using-smb-fileshare.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":426,"question_en":"A global company has a mobile app that displays ticket barcodes. Customers use the tickets on the mobile app to attend live events. Event scanners read the ticket barcodes and call a backend API to validate the barcode data against data in a database. After the barcode is scanned, the backend logic writes to the database's single table to mark the barcode as used. The company needs to deploy the app on AWS with a DNS name of api.example.com. The company will host the database in three AWS Regions around the world. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LOWEST latency?","question_zh":"一家全球性公司有一個顯示票券條碼的行動應用程式。客戶使用行動應用程式上的票券參加現場活動。活動掃描器讀取票券條碼，並呼叫後端 API 將條碼資料與資料庫中的資料進行驗證。條碼掃描後，後端邏輯會寫入資料庫的單一表格，將該條碼標記為已使用。該公司需要在 AWS 上部署此應用程式，並使用 api.example.com 作為 DNS 名稱。該公司將在全球三個 AWS 區域中託管資料庫。哪種解決方案能以最低延遲滿足這些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Host the database on Amazon Aurora global database clusters. Host the backend on three Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) clusters that are in the same Regions as the database. Create an accelerator in AWS Global Accelerator to route requests to the nearest ECS cluster. Create an Amazon Route 53 record that maps api.example.com to the accelerator endpoint","B":"Host the database on Amazon Aurora global database clusters. Host the backend on three Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) clusters that are in the same Regions as the database. Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution with the three clusters as origins. Route requests to the nearest EKS cluster. Create an Amazon Route 53 record that maps api.example.com to the CloudFront distribution.","C":"Host the database on Amazon DynamoDB global tables. Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution. Associate the CloudFront distribution with a CloudFront function that contains the backend logic to validate the barcodes. Create an Amazon Route 53 record that maps api.example.com to the CloudFront distribution.","D":"Host the database on Amazon DynamoDB global tables. Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution. Associate the CloudFront distribution with a Lambda@Edge function that contains the backend logic to validate the barcodes. Create an Amazon Route 53 record that maps api.example.com to the CloudFront distribution."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon Aurora 全球資料庫叢集上託管資料庫。在與資料庫相同區域的三個 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 叢集上託管後端。在 AWS Global Accelerator 中建立一個加速器，將請求路由到最近的 ECS 叢集。建立一個 Amazon Route 53 記錄，將 api.example.com 對應到該加速器端點。","B":"在 Amazon Aurora 全球資料庫叢集上託管資料庫。在與資料庫相同區域的三個 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 叢集上託管後端。建立一個以這三個叢集作為來源的 Amazon CloudFront 發佈。將請求路由到最近的 EKS 叢集。建立一個 Amazon Route 53 記錄，將 api.example.com 對應到該 CloudFront 發佈。","C":"在 Amazon DynamoDB 全球表格上託管資料庫。建立一個 Amazon CloudFront 發佈。將該 CloudFront 發佈與一個包含驗證條碼後端邏輯的 CloudFront function 建立關聯。建立一個 Amazon Route 53 記錄，將 api.example.com 對應到該 CloudFront 發佈。","D":"在 Amazon DynamoDB 全球表格上託管資料庫。建立一個 Amazon CloudFront 發佈。將該 CloudFront 發佈與一個包含驗證條碼後端邏輯的 Lambda@Edge 函數建立關聯。建立一個 Amazon Route 53 記錄，將 api.example.com 對應到該 CloudFront 發佈。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The backend must read DynamoDB to validate a barcode and then write to the single table to mark it used. That requires network access and the AWS SDK to call DynamoDB. Per the AWS 'Differences between CloudFront Functions and Lambda@Edge' page, CloudFront Functions have NO network access, no AWS SDK, a 10 KB restricted JavaScript runtime, and can only reach CloudFront KeyValueStore (not DynamoDB) - they are limited to cache-key normalization, header manipulation, redirects, and JWT checks. Therefore Option C is technically impossible. Lambda@Edge explicitly supports network access and the AWS SDK 'for integration with other AWS services,' runs at the CloudFront edge for lowest viewer latency, and pairs with DynamoDB global tables, which are multi-active and provide local low-latency reads AND writes in every Region (the write-to-mark-used pattern). Option D therefore meets the requirement with the lowest latency. The Aurora options (A, B) are worse for latency because Aurora global database has a single primary writer Region, so writes from the other two Regions must cross Regions, and routing to a regional ECS/EKS cluster adds a hop versus executing at the edge.","explanation_zh":"後端必須讀取 DynamoDB 來驗證條碼，然後寫入單一資料表將條碼標記為已使用。這需要網路存取與 AWS SDK 才能呼叫 DynamoDB。根據 AWS『Differences between CloudFront Functions and Lambda@Edge』文件，CloudFront Functions 沒有網路存取能力、無法使用 AWS SDK、執行受限的 10 KB JavaScript 執行環境，且只能存取 CloudFront KeyValueStore（無法存取 DynamoDB），僅適用於 cache key 正規化、標頭處理、重新導向與 JWT 驗證。因此選項 C 在技術上不可行。Lambda@Edge 明確支援網路存取與 AWS SDK『以整合其他 AWS 服務』，在 CloudFront 邊緣執行以取得對檢視者最低的延遲，並可搭配 DynamoDB global tables（multi-active，在每個 Region 提供低延遲的本地讀取與寫入，正符合標記已使用的寫入模式）。因此選項 D 以最低延遲滿足需求。Aurora 選項（A、B）延遲較差，因為 Aurora global database 只有單一主要寫入 Region，另外兩個 Region 的寫入必須跨 Region，且路由到區域 ECS/EKS 叢集相較邊緣執行又多了一個跳轉。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Aurora global database has a single primary writer Region; writes to mark barcodes used from the other two Regions must traverse to that primary, adding cross-Region write latency. Global Accelerator routes to a regional ECS cluster rather than running compute at the edge, so it is not the lowest-latency option.","why_zh":"Aurora global database 只有單一主要寫入 Region，另外兩個 Region 標記條碼為已使用的寫入必須跨到該主要 Region，增加跨 Region 寫入延遲。Global Accelerator 路由到區域 ECS 叢集而非在邊緣執行運算，因此不是最低延遲方案。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same Aurora single-writer cross-Region write-latency problem. CloudFront does not load-balance across multiple custom origins by lowest latency the way described; it would still forward to a regional EKS cluster. More hops and higher write latency than edge compute with a multi-active database.","why_zh":"同樣有 Aurora 單一寫入者的跨 Region 寫入延遲問題。CloudFront 並非如描述般以最低延遲在多個自訂來源間負載平衡，仍會轉送到區域 EKS 叢集。相較邊緣運算搭配 multi-active 資料庫，跳轉更多、寫入延遲更高。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Technically impossible: CloudFront Functions have no network access and no AWS SDK, so they cannot read from or write to DynamoDB. The restricted runtime is only for cache-key normalization, header manipulation, redirects/rewrites, and token validation - it cannot run the barcode validate-and-mark-used database logic. This is the AWS-dump 'suggested' answer but it is wrong.","why_zh":"技術上不可行：CloudFront Functions 沒有網路存取能力，也無 AWS SDK，因此無法讀取或寫入 DynamoDB。其受限執行環境僅用於 cache key 正規化、標頭處理、重新導向/改寫與權杖驗證，無法執行條碼驗證並標記已使用的資料庫邏輯。這是 dump 的『建議』答案，但它是錯的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/edge-functions-choosing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/cloudfront-function-restrictions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/lambda-at-edge-function-restrictions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/GlobalTables.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":427,"question_en":"A medical company is running a REST API on a set of Amazon EC2 instances. The EC2 instances run in an Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The ALB runs in three public subnets, and the EC2 instances run in three private subnets. The company has deployed an Amazon CloudFront distribution that has the ALB as the only origin. Which solution should a solutions architect recommend to enhance the origin security?","question_zh":"一家醫療公司在一組 Amazon EC2 執行個體上運行 REST API。這些 EC2 執行個體在 Application Load Balancer (ALB) 後面的一個 Auto Scaling 群組中運行。ALB 運行在三個公有子網路中，而 EC2 執行個體則運行在三個私有子網路中。該公司已部署一個 Amazon CloudFront 發佈，並將該 ALB 設為唯一的來源。解決方案架構師應建議哪種解決方案來增強來源的安全性？","options_en":{"A":"Store a random string in AWS Secrets Manager. Create an AWS Lambda function for automatic secret rotation. Configure CloudFront to inject the random string as a custom HTTP header for the origin request. Create an AWS WAF web ACL rule with a string match rule for the custom header. Associate the web ACL with the ALB.","B":"Create an AWS WAF web ACL rule with an IP match condition of the CloudFront service IP address ranges. Associate the web ACL with the ALMove the ALB into the three private subnets.","C":"Store a random string in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Configure Parameter Store automatic rotation for the string. Configure CloudFront to inject the random string as a custom HTTP header for the origin request. Inspect the value of the custom HTTP header, and block access in the ALB.","D":"Configure AWS Shield Advanced Create a security group policy to allow connections from CloudFront service IP address ranges. Add the policy to AWS Shield Advanced, and attach the policy to the ALB."},"options_zh":{"A":"將一個隨機字串儲存在 AWS Secrets Manager 中。建立一個 AWS Lambda 函數以自動輪替密鑰。設定 CloudFront，將該隨機字串作為自訂 HTTP 標頭注入來源請求中。建立一個 AWS WAF web ACL 規則，對該自訂標頭進行字串比對。將該 web ACL 與 ALB 建立關聯。","B":"建立一個 AWS WAF web ACL 規則，設定 IP 比對條件為 CloudFront 服務的 IP 位址範圍。將該 web ACL 與 ALB 建立關聯。將 ALB 移到這三個私有子網路中。","C":"將一個隨機字串儲存在 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store 中。為該字串設定 Parameter Store 自動輪替。設定 CloudFront，將該隨機字串作為自訂 HTTP 標頭注入來源請求中。檢查該自訂 HTTP 標頭的值，並在 ALB 中封鎖存取。","D":"設定 AWS Shield Advanced。建立一個安全群組政策，允許來自 CloudFront 服務 IP 位址範圍的連線。將該政策新增到 AWS Shield Advanced 中，並將該政策附加到 ALB。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The AWS-recommended pattern to ensure only CloudFront can reach an internet-facing ALB is to have CloudFront inject a secret custom HTTP header on origin requests, then validate that header at the edge of the ALB and block requests that lack it. AWS WAF associated with the ALB performs this validation with a string-match rule on the custom header, dropping any direct requests that do not carry the secret. Because the security relies entirely on the header value staying secret, AWS docs explicitly recommend rotating the header value periodically; storing it in Secrets Manager with a Lambda rotation function and updating CloudFront/WAF automatically is exactly the reference solution AWS published in 'How to enhance Amazon CloudFront origin security with AWS WAF and AWS Secrets Manager,' which the AWS DDoS Resiliency whitepaper cites. Option A implements this full pattern, so it is correct.","explanation_zh":"AWS 建議用來確保只有 CloudFront 能存取對外的 ALB 的標準做法是：讓 CloudFront 在 origin request 中注入一個秘密的自訂 HTTP header，然後在 ALB 前緣驗證該 header,並封鎖沒有帶此 header 的請求。將 AWS WAF web ACL 關聯到 ALB,以 string match rule 比對該自訂 header,即可丟棄任何直接送達且不帶秘密值的請求。由於整套安全機制完全仰賴 header 值保密,AWS 文件明確建議定期輪替該 header 值;將其存放於 Secrets Manager 並以 Lambda 旋轉函式自動輪替、同步更新 CloudFront 與 WAF,正是 AWS 在『How to enhance Amazon CloudFront origin security with AWS WAF and AWS Secrets Manager』部落格所發表、且被 AWS DDoS Resiliency 白皮書引用的參考解決方案。選項 A 完整實作了此模式,故為正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The dump's suggested answer is technically flawed. CloudFront does not provide a stable, small set of service IP ranges suitable for a WAF IP-match rule; AWS provides a managed prefix list for security groups, not a fixed list for WAF IP conditions, and ranges change frequently. Worse, an internet-facing ALB used as a CloudFront origin must remain publicly reachable (it needs a public/routable front end); moving it into private subnets breaks CloudFront's ability to reach it over the internet unless you switch to VPC origins, which the option does not configure. The phrasing is also garbled ('ALMove').","why_zh":"Dump 建議答案在技術上有缺陷。CloudFront 並未提供適合 WAF IP-match 規則的穩定、少量服務 IP 範圍;AWS 提供的是給 security group 用的 managed prefix list,而非給 WAF IP 條件的固定清單,且範圍經常變動。更嚴重的是,作為 CloudFront origin 的對外 ALB 必須維持公開可達;將其移入 private subnet 會使 CloudFront 無法透過網際網路連到它(除非改用 VPC origins,而此選項並未設定)。敘述本身也有拼字錯誤('ALMove')。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Systems Manager Parameter Store does not have a built-in automatic rotation feature for parameters (rotation is a Secrets Manager capability), so 'Configure Parameter Store automatic rotation' is not a real feature. Also 'inspect the value of the custom HTTP header, and block access in the ALB' is vague; the ALB blocks via listener rules or WAF, not by arbitrary inspection, and without an automated rotation mechanism the secret-header approach is weaker than option A.","why_zh":"Systems Manager Parameter Store 並沒有內建的參數自動輪替功能(輪替是 Secrets Manager 的能力),因此『設定 Parameter Store 自動輪替』並非真實功能。此外『檢視自訂 HTTP header 的值並在 ALB 封鎖存取』含糊不清;ALB 是透過 listener rule 或 WAF 封鎖,而非任意檢視,且缺乏自動輪替機制使此秘密 header 方案弱於選項 A。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Shield Advanced is a DDoS protection service; it does not work by attaching a security-group policy that allows CloudFront IP ranges. There is no 'security group policy added to Shield Advanced.' This conflates Shield with Firewall Manager/security groups and does not implement the secret-header origin-restriction pattern, so it does not enhance origin access control in the intended way.","why_zh":"AWS Shield Advanced 是 DDoS 防護服務,並非透過附加允許 CloudFront IP 範圍的 security-group 政策運作。並不存在『加入 Shield Advanced 的 security group 政策』。此選項把 Shield 與 Firewall Manager/security group 混為一談,也未實作秘密 header 的 origin 限制模式,因此無法以預期方式強化 origin 存取控制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/restrict-access-to-load-balancer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/aws-best-practices-ddos-resiliency/protecting-your-origin-bp1-bp5.html","https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/security/how-to-enhance-amazon-cloudfront-origin-security-with-aws-waf-and-aws-secrets-manager/","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/rotating-secrets.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":428,"question_en":"To abide by industry regulations, a solutions architect must design a solution that will store a company's critical data in multiple public AWS Regions, including in the United States, where the company's headquarters is located. The solutions architect is required to provide access to the data stored in AWS to the company’s global WAN network. The security team mandates that no tra®c accessing this data should traverse the public internet. How should the solutions architect design a highly available solution that meets the requirements and is cost-effective?","question_zh":"為遵守產業法規，解決方案架構師必須設計一個解決方案，將公司的關鍵資料儲存在多個公有 AWS 區域中，包括公司總部所在的美國。解決方案架構師必須讓公司的全球 WAN 網路能夠存取儲存在 AWS 中的資料。安全團隊要求存取此資料的所有流量都不得經過公有網際網路。解決方案架構師應如何設計一個既滿足這些要求又具成本效益的高可用性解決方案？","options_en":{"A":"Establish AWS Direct Connect connections from the company headquarters to all AWS Regions in use. Use the company WAN to send tra®c over to the headquarters and then to the respective DX connection to access the data.","B":"Establish two AWS Direct Connect connections from the company headquarters to an AWS Region. Use the company WAN to send tra®c over a DX connection. Use inter-region VPC peering to access the data in other AWS Regions.","C":"Establish two AWS Direct Connect connections from the company headquarters to an AWS Region. Use the company WAN to send tra®c over a DX connection. Use an AWS transit VPC solution to access data in other AWS Regions.","D":"Establish two AWS Direct Connect connections from the company headquarters to an AWS Region. Use the company WAN to send tra®c over a DX connection. Use Direct Connect Gateway to access data in other AWS Regions."},"options_zh":{"A":"從公司總部建立 AWS Direct Connect 連線到所有使用中的 AWS 區域。使用公司 WAN 將流量傳送到總部，然後透過對應的 DX 連線存取資料。","B":"從公司總部建立兩條 AWS Direct Connect 連線到某個 AWS 區域。使用公司 WAN 透過 DX 連線傳送流量。使用跨區域 VPC 對等連線來存取其他 AWS 區域中的資料。","C":"從公司總部建立兩條 AWS Direct Connect 連線到某個 AWS 區域。使用公司 WAN 透過 DX 連線傳送流量。使用 AWS 傳輸 VPC 解決方案來存取其他 AWS 區域中的資料。","D":"從公司總部建立兩條 AWS Direct Connect 連線到某個 AWS 區域。使用公司 WAN 透過 DX 連線傳送流量。使用 Direct Connect Gateway 來存取其他 AWS 區域中的資料。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":90},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":429,"question_en":"A company has developed an application that is running Windows Server on VMware vSphere VMs that the company hosts on premises. The application data is stored in a proprietary format that must be read through the application. The company manually provisioned the servers and the application. As part of its disaster recovery plan, the company wants the ability to host its application on AWS temporarily if the company's on-premises environment becomes unavailable. The company wants the application to return to on-premises hosting after a disaster recovery event is complete. The RPO is 5 minutes. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST amount of operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司開發了一個應用程式，該應用程式在該公司本地端託管的 VMware vSphere VM 上運行 Windows Server。應用程式資料以一種必須透過該應用程式讀取的專有格式儲存。該公司以手動方式配置了伺服器和應用程式。作為災難復原計劃的一部分，該公司希望在本地端環境無法使用時，能夠暫時在 AWS 上託管其應用程式。該公司希望在災難復原事件結束後，將應用程式恢復到本地端託管。RPO 為 5 分鐘。哪種解決方案能以最少的運營開銷滿足這些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS DataSync. Replicate the data to Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes. When the on-premises environment is unavailable, use AWS CloudFormation templates to provision Amazon EC2 instances and attach the EBS volumes.","B":"Configure AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery. Replicate the data to replication Amazon EC2 instances that are attached to Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes. When the on-premises environment is unavailable, use Elastic Disaster Recovery to launch EC2 instances that use the replicated volumes.","C":"Provision an AWS Storage Gateway file gateway. Replicate the data to an Amazon S3 bucket. When the on-premises environment is unavailable, use AWS Backup to restore the data to Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes and launch Amazon EC2 instances from these EBS volumes.","D":"Provision an Amazon FSx for Windows File Server file system on AWS. Replicate the data to the file system. When the on-premises environment is unavailable, use AWS CloudFormation templates to provision Amazon EC2 instances and use AWS::CloudFormation::Init commands to mount the Amazon FSx file shares."},"options_zh":{"A":"設定 AWS DataSync。將資料複寫到 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 磁碟區。當本地端環境無法使用時，使用 AWS CloudFormation 範本配置 Amazon EC2 執行個體並附加這些 EBS 磁碟區。","B":"設定 AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery。將資料複寫到附加了 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 磁碟區的複寫用 Amazon EC2 執行個體。當本地端環境無法使用時，使用 Elastic Disaster Recovery 啟動使用這些複寫磁碟區的 EC2 執行個體。","C":"配置一個 AWS Storage Gateway 檔案閘道。將資料複寫到 Amazon S3 儲存桶。當本地端環境無法使用時，使用 AWS Backup 將資料還原到 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 磁碟區，並從這些 EBS 磁碟區啟動 Amazon EC2 執行個體。","D":"在 AWS 上配置一個 Amazon FSx for Windows File Server 檔案系統。將資料複寫到該檔案系統。當本地端環境無法使用時，使用 AWS CloudFormation 範本配置 Amazon EC2 執行個體，並使用 AWS::CloudFormation::Init 命令掛載 Amazon FSx 檔案共用。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":93},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":430,"question_en":"A company runs a highly available data collection application on Amazon EC2 in the eu-north-1 Region. The application collects data from end-user devices and writes records to an Amazon Kinesis data stream and a set of AWS Lambda functions that process the records. The company persists the output of the record processing to an Amazon S3 bucket in eu-north-1. The company uses the data in the S3 bucket as a data source for Amazon Athena. The company wants to increase its global presence. A solutions architect must launch the data collection capabilities in the sa-east-1 and ap- northeast-1 Regions. The solutions architect deploys the application, the Kinesis data stream, and the Lambda functions in the two new Regions. The solutions architect keeps the S3 bucket in eu-north-1 to meet a requirement to centralize the data analysis. During testing of the new setup, the solutions architect notices a significant lag on the arrival of data from the new Regions to the S3 bucket. Which solution will improve this lag time the MOST?","question_zh":"一家公司在 eu-north-1 區域的 Amazon EC2 上運行一個高可用性的資料收集應用程式。該應用程式從終端使用者裝置收集資料，並將記錄寫入 Amazon Kinesis 資料串流以及一組處理這些記錄的 AWS Lambda 函數。該公司將記錄處理的輸出保存到 eu-north-1 中的 Amazon S3 儲存桶。該公司使用 S3 儲存桶中的資料作為 Amazon Athena 的資料來源。該公司希望擴大其全球業務範圍。解決方案架構師必須在 sa-east-1 和 ap-northeast-1 區域中啟動資料收集功能。解決方案架構師在這兩個新區域中部署了應用程式、Kinesis 資料串流和 Lambda 函數。解決方案架構師將 S3 儲存桶保留在 eu-north-1 中，以滿足集中式資料分析的要求。在測試新架構時，解決方案架構師注意到資料從新區域抵達 S3 儲存桶時出現明顯的延遲。哪種解決方案最能改善這種延遲時間？","options_en":{"A":"In each of the two new Regions, set up the Lambda functions to run in a VPC. Set up an S3 gateway endpoint in that VPC.","B":"Turn on S3 Transfer Acceleration on the S3 bucket in eu-north-1. Change the application to use the new S3 accelerated endpoint when the application uploads data to the S3 bucket.","C":"Create an S3 bucket in each of the two new Regions. Set the application in each new Region to upload to its respective S3 bucket. Set up S3 Cross-Region Replication to replicate data to the S3 bucket in eu-north-1.","D":"Increase the memory requirements of the Lambda functions to ensure that they have multiple cores available. Use the multipart upload feature when the application uploads data to Amazon S3 from Lambda."},"options_zh":{"A":"在這兩個新區域中，分別設定 Lambda 函數在 VPC 中運行。在該 VPC 中設定一個 S3 閘道端點。","B":"在 eu-north-1 的 S3 儲存桶上開啟 S3 Transfer Acceleration。變更應用程式，使其在上傳資料到 S3 儲存桶時使用新的 S3 加速端點。","C":"在這兩個新區域中分別建立一個 S3 儲存桶。設定每個新區域中的應用程式上傳到其各自的 S3 儲存桶。設定 S3 跨區域複寫，將資料複寫到 eu-north-1 中的 S3 儲存桶。","D":"提高 Lambda 函數的記憶體需求，以確保它們擁有多個可用核心。當應用程式從 Lambda 上傳資料到 Amazon S3 時，使用多部分上傳功能。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":69,"B":31},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":431,"question_en":"A company provides a centralized Amazon EC2 application hosted in a single shared VPC. The centralized application must be accessible from client applications running in the VPCs of other business units. The centralized application front end is configured with a Network Load Balancer (NLB) for scalability. Up to 10 business unit VPCs will need to be connected to the shared VPC. Some of the business unit VPC CIDR blocks overlap with the shared VPC, and some overlap with each other Network connectivity to the centralized application in the shared VPC should be allowed from authorized business unit VPCs only. Which network configuration should a solutions architect use to provide connectivity from the client applications in the business unit VPCs to the centralized application in the shared VPC?","question_zh":"一家公司提供一個託管在單一共用 VPC 中的集中式 Amazon EC2 應用程式。該集中式應用程式必須能讓運行在其他業務單位 VPC 中的客戶端應用程式存取。該集中式應用程式的前端設定了一個 Network Load Balancer (NLB) 以提高可擴展性。最多將有 10 個業務單位 VPC 需要連接到該共用 VPC。部分業務單位 VPC 的 CIDR 區塊與共用 VPC 重疊，部分則彼此重疊。對共用 VPC 中集中式應用程式的網路連線，只能允許來自經授權的業務單位 VPC。解決方案架構師應使用哪種網路設定，以提供業務單位 VPC 中的客戶端應用程式與共用 VPC 中集中式應用程式之間的連線？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Transit Gateway. Attach the shared VPC and the authorized business unit VPCs to the transit gateway. Create a single transit gateway route table and associate it with all of the attached VPCs. Allow automatic propagation of routes from the attachments into the route table. Configure VPC routing tables to send tra®c to the transit gateway.","B":"Create a VPC endpoint service using the centralized application NLB and enable the option to require endpoint acceptance. Create a VPC endpoint in each of the business unit VPCs using the service name of the endpoint service. Accept authorized endpoint requests from the endpoint service console.","C":"Create a VPC peering connection from each business unit VPC to the shared VPAccept the VPC peering connections from the shared VPC console. Configure VPC routing tables to send tra®c to the VPC peering connection.","D":"Configure a virtual private gateway for the shared VPC and create customer gateways for each of the authorized business unit VPCs. Establish a Site-to-Site VPN connection from the business unit VPCs to the shared VPC. Configure VPC routing tables to send tra®c to the VPN connection."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個 AWS Transit Gateway。將共用 VPC 和經授權的業務單位 VPC 附加到該傳輸閘道。建立一個單一的傳輸閘道路由表，並將其與所有附加的 VPC 建立關聯。允許路由從附件自動傳播到路由表中。設定 VPC 路由表，將流量傳送到該傳輸閘道。","B":"使用該集中式應用程式的 NLB 建立一個 VPC 端點服務，並啟用需要端點接受的選項。在每個業務單位 VPC 中，使用該端點服務的服務名稱建立一個 VPC 端點。從端點服務主控台接受經授權的端點請求。","C":"從每個業務單位 VPC 建立一個到共用 VPC 的 VPC 對等連線。從共用 VPC 主控台接受這些 VPC 對等連線。設定 VPC 路由表，將流量傳送到該 VPC 對等連線。","D":"為共用 VPC 設定一個虛擬私有閘道，並為每個經授權的業務單位 VPC 建立客戶閘道。從業務單位 VPC 建立到共用 VPC 的 Site-to-Site VPN 連線。設定 VPC 路由表，將流量傳送到該 VPN 連線。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive constraint is that some business unit VPC CIDRs overlap with the shared VPC and with each other, while access must be one-directional (clients reach a centralized NLB-fronted application) and restricted to authorized VPCs. AWS PrivateLink (a VPC endpoint service backed by the NLB, consumed via interface VPC endpoints) is purpose-built for this: each consumer creates an interface endpoint that materializes as elastic network interfaces with local private IPs inside its own VPC and uses DNS resolution rather than CIDR routing, so overlapping CIDRs are irrelevant. Enabling 'require acceptance' on the endpoint service and accepting only authorized endpoint connection requests restricts connectivity to authorized business unit VPCs only. Transit Gateway (A) is explicitly unsupported here because AWS docs state a transit gateway does not support routing between VPCs with identical or overlapping CIDRs and will not propagate the overlapping routes. VPC peering (C) likewise cannot be established or routed between VPCs with overlapping CIDRs, and Site-to-Site VPN with a virtual private gateway/customer gateways (D) is a hybrid/on-premises construct that is operationally heavy, route-based (so overlap-sensitive), and not the appropriate VPC-to-VPC pattern.","explanation_zh":"決定性條件是部分業務單位 VPC 的 CIDR 與 shared VPC 以及彼此之間重疊，且存取為單向（用戶端連到 NLB 前端的集中式應用程式）並只允許授權的 VPC。AWS PrivateLink（以 NLB 為後端建立 VPC endpoint service，消費端透過 interface VPC endpoint 連入）正是為此設計：每個消費端在自己的 VPC 內建立 interface endpoint，會在當地子網建立具本地私有 IP 的 elastic network interface，並以 DNS 解析而非 CIDR 路由，因此 CIDR 重疊完全不影響。在 endpoint service 上啟用 require acceptance 並只接受授權的連線請求，即可將連線限制在授權的業務單位 VPC。Transit Gateway（A）在此明確不可行，AWS 文件指出 transit gateway 不支援在 CIDR 相同或重疊的 VPC 之間路由，重疊的路由不會被傳播。VPC peering（C）同樣無法在 CIDR 重疊的 VPC 之間建立或路由。使用 virtual private gateway/customer gateway 的 Site-to-Site VPN（D）屬於混合/地端連線構件，營運負擔大、以路由為基礎（同樣對重疊敏感），並非適當的 VPC 對 VPC 模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS docs explicitly state a transit gateway does not support routing between VPCs with identical or overlapping CIDRs; the overlapping VPC routes will not be propagated to the TGW route table, so connectivity to the centralized app would fail. A single shared route table with auto-propagation also does not restrict to authorized VPCs cleanly.","why_zh":"AWS 文件明確指出 transit gateway 不支援 CIDR 相同或重疊的 VPC 之間路由，重疊 VPC 的路由不會被傳播到 TGW route table，導致連線失敗。單一共用 route table 加自動傳播也無法乾淨地限制為授權 VPC。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"VPC peering cannot be created or routed between VPCs whose CIDR blocks overlap. Since some business unit CIDRs overlap with the shared VPC, peering is not viable.","why_zh":"VPC peering 無法在 CIDR 區塊重疊的 VPC 之間建立或路由。由於部分業務單位 CIDR 與 shared VPC 重疊，peering 不可行。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Virtual private gateway, customer gateways, and Site-to-Site VPN are intended for hybrid/on-premises connectivity, not VPC-to-VPC. This approach is high operational overhead, route-based (so overlapping CIDRs remain a problem), and is the wrong architectural construct for exposing an internal NLB-fronted app to other VPCs.","why_zh":"virtual private gateway、customer gateway 與 Site-to-Site VPN 是為混合/地端連線設計，而非 VPC 對 VPC。此做法營運負擔高、以路由為基礎（重疊 CIDR 仍是問題），且不是將內部 NLB 前端應用程式公開給其他 VPC 的正確架構。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/tgw-vpc-attachments.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/endpoint-services-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-peering.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":432,"question_en":"A company wants to migrate its website to AWS. The website uses microservices and runs on containers that are deployed in an on-premises, self-managed Kubernetes cluster. All the manifests that define the deployments for the containers in the Kubernetes deployment are in source control. All data for the website is stored in a PostgreSQL database. An open source container image repository runs alongside the on-premises environment. A solutions architect needs to determine the architecture that the company will use for the website on AWS. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST effort to migrate?","question_zh":"一家公司希望將其網站遷移到 AWS。該網站使用微服務架構，並運行在部署於本地端自行管理的 Kubernetes 叢集中的容器上。定義 Kubernetes 部署中容器部署的所有清單檔案都存放在原始碼控管中。該網站的所有資料都儲存在一個 PostgreSQL 資料庫中。本地端環境中還運行著一個開放原始碼的容器映像檔儲存庫。解決方案架構師需要決定該公司在 AWS 上用於此網站的架構。哪種解決方案能以最少的遷移工作滿足這些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS App Runner service. Connect the App Runner service to the open source container image repository. Deploy the manifests from on premises to the App Runner service. Create an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database.","B":"Create an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster that has managed node groups. Copy the application containers to a new Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. Deploy the manifests from on premises to the EKS cluster. Create an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster.","C":"Create an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster that has an Amazon EC2 capacity pool. Copy the application containers to a new Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. Register each container image as a new task definition. Configure ECS services for each task definition to match the original Kubernetes deployments. Create an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster.","D":"Rebuild the on-premises Kubernetes cluster by hosting the cluster on Amazon EC2 instances. Migrate the open source container image repository to the EC2 instances. Deploy the manifests from on premises to the new cluster on AWS. Deploy an open source PostgreSQL database on the new cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個 AWS App Runner 服務。將該 App Runner 服務連接到開放原始碼容器映像檔儲存庫。將本地端的清單檔案部署到該 App Runner 服務。建立一個 Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL 資料庫。","B":"建立一個具有受管節點群組的 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 叢集。將應用程式容器複製到一個新的 Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) 儲存庫。將本地端的清單檔案部署到該 EKS 叢集。建立一個 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL 資料庫叢集。","C":"建立一個具有 Amazon EC2 容量池的 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 叢集。將應用程式容器複製到一個新的 Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) 儲存庫。將每個容器映像檔註冊為新的任務定義。為每個任務定義設定對應的 ECS 服務，以符合原始的 Kubernetes 部署。建立一個 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL 資料庫叢集。","D":"透過在 Amazon EC2 執行個體上託管叢集，重新建置本地端的 Kubernetes 叢集。將開放原始碼容器映像檔儲存庫遷移到這些 EC2 執行個體上。將本地端的清單檔案部署到 AWS 上的新叢集。在該新叢集上部署一個開放原始碼的 PostgreSQL 資料庫。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Migration","Compute","Database","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The workload already runs on Kubernetes with all deployment manifests stored in source control, so the lowest-effort migration is to a managed Kubernetes service that consumes those manifests unchanged. Amazon EKS runs upstream Kubernetes, so the existing manifests deploy directly via kubectl/CI-CD with little or no modification, while AWS manages the control plane (less operational effort than self-managing). Container images are copied into Amazon ECR, and Aurora PostgreSQL provides a managed, PostgreSQL-compatible database for the website data. Option D (self-managed Kubernetes on EC2 with a self-hosted image repo and self-hosted PostgreSQL) would also run the manifests but is essentially a lift-and-shift that keeps every operational burden the company already had on premises - the MOST effort, not the least. Option A (App Runner) is invalid because App Runner is a single-image PaaS that does not consume Kubernetes manifests and only supports Amazon ECR / ECR Public as image sources (not an arbitrary open source repository), and Option C (ECS) requires rewriting every Kubernetes deployment into ECS task definitions and services, which is significant migration effort.","explanation_zh":"此工作負載已經在 Kubernetes 上運行，且所有部署 manifest 都存放在原始碼控制中，因此最省力的遷移方式是移轉到能直接沿用這些 manifest 的受管 Kubernetes 服務。Amazon EKS 執行的是上游標準 Kubernetes，現有 manifest 可透過 kubectl/CI-CD 幾乎不需修改即可直接部署，同時由 AWS 管理控制平面（比自行管理省力）。容器映像複製到 Amazon ECR，Aurora PostgreSQL 則提供受管且相容 PostgreSQL 的資料庫來存放網站資料。選項 D（在 EC2 上自管 Kubernetes，並自行託管映像庫與 PostgreSQL）雖然也能執行 manifest，但本質上是 lift-and-shift，把地端原有的所有營運負擔全部搬到雲端，是最費力而非最省力的做法。選項 A（App Runner）不成立，因為 App Runner 是單一映像的 PaaS，不會解析 Kubernetes manifest，且映像來源僅支援 Amazon ECR / ECR Public（無法連到任意開源映像庫）；選項 C（ECS）則需把每個 Kubernetes deployment 改寫成 ECS task definition 與 service，遷移工作量很大。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"App Runner is a single-container PaaS that runs one provided image per service and does not consume Kubernetes manifests, so 'deploy the manifests to the App Runner service' is not possible. It also supports only Amazon ECR and ECR Public as image sources, not an arbitrary open source repository, and is closed to new customers.","why_zh":"App Runner 是單一容器的 PaaS，每個服務執行一個提供的映像，並不會解析 Kubernetes manifest，所以『把 manifest 部署到 App Runner』根本做不到。它的映像來源僅支援 Amazon ECR 與 ECR Public，無法連到任意開源映像庫，且已不開放新客戶。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"ECS does not understand Kubernetes manifests. Migrating would require rewriting every Kubernetes deployment as an ECS task definition and service, which is substantial conversion effort and contradicts the LEAST-effort requirement.","why_zh":"ECS 不認識 Kubernetes manifest。遷移時必須把每個 Kubernetes deployment 重寫成 ECS task definition 與 service，是大量的轉換工作，違反『最省力』的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Self-managing a Kubernetes cluster on EC2 plus a self-hosted image repository and self-hosted PostgreSQL is essentially a lift-and-shift that retains all the on-premises operational burden (control plane, etcd, patching, upgrades, DB admin). This is the MOST effort, not the least, and ignores AWS managed services like EKS, ECR, and Aurora.","why_zh":"在 EC2 上自管 Kubernetes 叢集，再自行託管映像庫與 PostgreSQL，本質上是 lift-and-shift，保留了地端所有營運負擔（控制平面、etcd、修補、升級、資料庫維運）。這是最費力而非最省力的做法，且忽略了 EKS、ECR、Aurora 等 AWS 受管服務。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/what-is-eks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/managed-node-groups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apprunner/latest/dg/service-source-image.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/docker-push-ecr-image.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":433,"question_en":"A company uses a mobile app on AWS to run online contests. The company selects a winner at random at the end of each contest. The contests run for variable lengths of time. The company does not need to retain any data from a contest after the contest is finished. The company uses custom code that is hosted on Amazon EC2 instances to process the contest data and select a winner. The EC2 instances run behind an Application Load Balancer and store contest entries on Amazon RDS DB instances. The company must design a new architecture to reduce the cost of running the contests. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上使用一個行動應用程式來舉辦線上競賽。該公司在每次競賽結束時隨機選出一名獲勝者。競賽的持續時間並不固定。競賽結束後，該公司不需要保留該競賽的任何資料。該公司使用託管在 Amazon EC2 執行個體上的自訂程式碼來處理競賽資料並選出獲勝者。這些 EC2 執行個體在 Application Load Balancer 後面運行，並將競賽參賽項目儲存在 Amazon RDS 資料庫執行個體中。該公司必須設計一個新架構，以降低舉辦競賽的成本。哪種解決方案能以最具成本效益的方式滿足這些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate storage of the contest entries to Amazon DynamoDB. Create a DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster. Rewrite the code to run as Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) containers that use the Fargate launch type. At the end of the contest, delete the DynamoDB table.","B":"Migrate the storage of the contest entries to Amazon Redshift. Rewrite the code as AWS Lambda functions. At the end of the contest, delete the Redshift cluster.","C":"Add an Amazon ElastiCache for Redis cluster in front of the RDS DB instances to cache the contest entries. Rewrite the code to run as Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) containers that use the Fargate launch type. Set the ElastiCache TTL attribute on each entry to expire each entry at the end of the contest.","D":"Migrate the storage of the contest entries to Amazon DynamoDB. Rewrite the code as AWS Lambda functions. Set the DynamoDB TTL attribute on each entry to expire each entry at the end of the contest."},"options_zh":{"A":"將競賽參賽項目的儲存遷移到 Amazon DynamoDB。建立一個 DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) 叢集。重寫程式碼，使其以使用 Fargate 啟動類型的 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 容器方式運行。競賽結束時，刪除該 DynamoDB 表格。","B":"將競賽參賽項目的儲存遷移到 Amazon Redshift。將程式碼重寫為 AWS Lambda 函數。競賽結束時，刪除該 Redshift 叢集。","C":"在 RDS 資料庫執行個體前面新增一個 Amazon ElastiCache for Redis 叢集，以快取競賽參賽項目。重寫程式碼，使其以使用 Fargate 啟動類型的 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 容器方式運行。在每個項目上設定 ElastiCache TTL 屬性，使每個項目在競賽結束時到期。","D":"將競賽參賽項目的儲存遷移到 Amazon DynamoDB。將程式碼重寫為 AWS Lambda 函數。在每個項目上設定 DynamoDB TTL 屬性，使每個項目在競賽結束時到期。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":60,"A":40},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The qualifier is MOST cost-effective for an intermittent workload (contests of variable length) whose data is discarded when the contest ends. Option D replaces always-on EC2/RDS with fully serverless components: AWS Lambda bills only while code runs (scaling cost in line with usage per Well-Architected COST05-BP05), DynamoDB on-demand scales toward zero between contests, and DynamoDB TTL is explicitly documented as 'a cost-effective method for deleting items that are no longer relevant' that 'automatically deletes expired items within a few days of their expiration time, without consuming write throughput.' Setting a per-item TTL to expire entries at contest end matches the no-retention requirement at no deletion cost. Option C is the dump's suggested answer but is actually the most expensive: it KEEPS the RDS DB instances (the original cost driver) and ADDS a continuously billed ElastiCache for Redis cluster plus Fargate; a Redis TTL only evicts cache entries, not the underlying RDS data, so it increases rather than reduces cost.","explanation_zh":"本題限定詞是針對「間歇性工作負載」(比賽長度不固定、結束後資料不需保留) 找出 MOST cost-effective 的方案。選項 D 以全無伺服器元件取代常駐的 EC2/RDS：AWS Lambda 只在程式執行時計費 (符合 Well-Architected COST05-BP05 成本隨用量縮放),DynamoDB 隨需容量在比賽之間可趨近於零,而 DynamoDB TTL 官方文件明確描述為『刪除不再需要項目的具成本效益方法』,且『會在到期後數天內自動刪除過期項目,且不消耗寫入吞吐量』。將每筆項目的 TTL 設為比賽結束時到期,完全符合不需保留資料的需求,且刪除不額外計費。選項 C 是題庫建議答案,但實際上最昂貴:它仍保留 RDS 資料庫執行個體 (原本的成本來源),又額外加入持續計費的 ElastiCache for Redis 叢集與 Fargate;Redis TTL 只會清除快取項目,並不會刪除底層 RDS 資料,因此成本不降反升。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Migrating to DynamoDB is good, but adding a DAX cluster (continuously billed nodes used for read acceleration) is unnecessary for a short-lived write-heavy contest, and Fargate containers cost more than Lambda for intermittent bursts. Deleting the table works but the DAX + Fargate combination is not the MOST cost-effective.","why_zh":"遷移到 DynamoDB 不錯,但加入 DAX 叢集 (持續計費、用於讀取加速的節點) 對於短暫且寫入為主的比賽並無必要,且 Fargate 容器對間歇性突發負載比 Lambda 昂貴。雖然刪除資料表可行,但 DAX 加 Fargate 的組合並非最具成本效益。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Redshift is a data warehouse built for analytic queries over large datasets, not for transactional contest entry storage. It is expensive to run, and spinning up then deleting a Redshift cluster per contest is heavy-handed and far from cost-effective.","why_zh":"Amazon Redshift 是針對大型資料集分析查詢設計的資料倉儲,並不適合用於交易型的比賽參賽資料儲存。它的運行成本高,每場比賽建立再刪除 Redshift 叢集既笨重又遠非具成本效益。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer and is wrong: it RETAINS the RDS DB instances (the original cost) and ADDS a continuously billed ElastiCache for Redis cluster plus Fargate. A Redis TTL only expires cached copies, not the underlying RDS data, so this raises cost instead of reducing it.","why_zh":"這是題庫建議答案,但其實是錯的:它仍保留 RDS 資料庫執行個體 (原始成本),又額外加上持續計費的 ElastiCache for Redis 叢集與 Fargate。Redis TTL 只會讓快取副本過期,並不會刪除底層 RDS 資料,因此成本不減反增。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/TTL.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/time-to-live-ttl-before-you-start.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/2023-04-10/framework/cost_select_service_select_for_cost.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":434,"question_en":"A company has implemented a new security requirement. According to the new requirement, the company must scan all tra®c from corporate AWS instances in the company's VPC for violations of the company's security policies. As a result of these scans, the company can block access to and from specific IP addresses. To meet the new requirement, the company deploys a set of Amazon EC2 instances in private subnets to serve as transparent proxies. The company installs approved proxy server software on these EC2 instances. The company modifies the route tables on all subnets to use the corresponding EC2 instances with proxy software as the default route. The company also creates security groups that are compliant with the security policies and assigns these security groups to the EC2 instances. Despite these configurations, the tra®c of the EC2 instances in their private subnets is not being properly forwarded to the internet. What should a solutions architect do to resolve this issue?","question_zh":"一家公司實施了一項新的安全要求。根據該新要求，該公司必須掃描來自公司 VPC 中企業 AWS 執行個體的所有流量，以檢查是否違反公司的安全政策。根據這些掃描結果，該公司可以封鎖與特定 IP 位址之間的存取。為滿足此新要求，該公司在私有子網路中部署了一組 Amazon EC2 執行個體作為透明代理伺服器。該公司在這些 EC2 執行個體上安裝了經核准的代理伺服器軟體。該公司修改了所有子網路的路由表，將搭載代理軟體的對應 EC2 執行個體設為預設路由。該公司還建立了符合安全政策的安全群組，並將這些安全群組指派給這些 EC2 執行個體。儘管完成了這些設定，私有子網路中 EC2 執行個體的流量卻無法正確轉發到網際網路。解決方案架構師應該怎麼做才能解決這個問題？","options_en":{"A":"Disable source/destination checks on the EC2 instances that run the proxy software.","B":"Add a rule to the security group that is assigned to the proxy EC2 instances to allow all tra®c between instances that have this security group. Assign this security group to all EC2 instances in the VPC.","C":"Change the VPCs DHCP options set. Set the DNS server options to point to the addresses of the proxy EC2 instances.","D":"Assign one additional elastic network interface to each proxy EC2 instance. Ensure that one of these network interfaces has a route to the private subnets. Ensure that the other network interface has a route to the internet."},"options_zh":{"A":"停用運行代理伺服器軟體的 EC2 執行個體上的來源/目的地檢查。","B":"在指派給代理 EC2 執行個體的安全群組中新增一條規則，允許擁有此安全群組的執行個體之間的所有流量。將此安全群組指派給 VPC 中的所有 EC2 執行個體。","C":"變更 VPC 的 DHCP 選項集。將 DNS 伺服器選項設定為指向代理 EC2 執行個體的位址。","D":"為每個代理 EC2 執行個體額外指派一個彈性網路介面。確保其中一個網路介面具有通往私有子網路的路由。確保另一個網路介面具有通往網際網路的路由。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":83,"D":17},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":435,"question_en":"A company is running its solution on AWS in a manually created VPC. The company is using AWS CloudFormation to provision other parts of the infrastructure. According to a new requirement, the company must manage all infrastructure in an automatic way. What should the company do to meet this new requirement with the LEAST effort?","question_zh":"一家公司在以手動方式建立的 VPC 中於 AWS 上運行其解決方案。該公司使用 AWS CloudFormation 來配置其他部分的基礎設施。根據新的要求，該公司必須以自動化方式管理所有基礎設施。該公司應該怎麼做才能以最少的工作量滿足這項新要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK) stack that strictly provisions the existing VPC resources and configuration. Use AWS CDK to import the VPC into the stack and to manage the VPC.","B":"Create a CloudFormation stack set that creates the VPC. Use the stack set to import the VPC into the stack.","C":"Create a new CloudFormation template that strictly provisions the existing VPC resources and configuration. From the CloudFormation console, create a new stack by importing the Existing resources.","D":"Create a new CloudFormation template that creates the VPC. Use the AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) CLI to import the VPC."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個新的 AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK) 堆疊，嚴格按照現有 VPC 資源與設定進行配置。使用 AWS CDK 將該 VPC 匯入堆疊並進行管理。","B":"建立一個用於建立該 VPC 的 CloudFormation 堆疊集。使用該堆疊集將該 VPC 匯入堆疊中。","C":"建立一個新的 CloudFormation 範本，嚴格按照現有 VPC 資源與設定進行配置。從 CloudFormation 主控台，透過匯入現有資源來建立一個新堆疊。","D":"建立一個用於建立該 VPC 的新 CloudFormation 範本。使用 AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) CLI 來匯入該 VPC。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":79,"B":18},"tags":["Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"CloudFormation provides a native resource import feature specifically for bringing existing, manually-created resources (such as a VPC) under IaC management without deleting and recreating them. The documented workflow is exactly option C: author a template that describes the existing VPC resources and their current configuration (each with a DeletionPolicy and a resource identifier), then from the CloudFormation console choose Create stack > With existing resources (import resources) to create a new stack from those resources. Since the company already uses CloudFormation for other infrastructure, this reuses existing tooling and skills, which is the LEAST effort. Option D is wrong because the AWS SAM CLI is a serverless framework transform and has no command to import an existing VPC. Option B is wrong because StackSets deploy stacks across multiple accounts/Regions and have no resource-import capability. Option A (CDK) would mean adopting a new framework that just synthesizes to CloudFormation anyway, which is more effort, not less.","explanation_zh":"CloudFormation 提供原生的 resource import 功能，專門用於將既有、手動建立的資源（例如 VPC）納入 IaC 管理，而不需刪除並重建。官方文件描述的流程正是選項 C：撰寫一個描述既有 VPC 資源及其目前組態的範本（每個資源需包含 DeletionPolicy 與資源識別碼），然後在 CloudFormation 主控台選擇 Create stack > With existing resources (import resources)，以這些既有資源建立新的 stack。由於公司其他基礎架構已使用 CloudFormation，沿用既有工具與技能即為「最少工作量」。選項 D 錯誤，因為 AWS SAM CLI 是無伺服器框架的 transform，並沒有匯入既有 VPC 的指令。選項 B 錯誤，因為 StackSets 用於跨多帳號/區域部署 stack，並無 resource import 能力。選項 A（CDK）等於導入一個新框架，且最終仍是合成成 CloudFormation，工作量更大而非更少。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CDK can adopt resources but synthesizes to CloudFormation under the hood; introducing a new framework when the company already standardizes on CloudFormation is more effort, not the least.","why_zh":"CDK 雖能納管資源，但底層仍合成為 CloudFormation；在公司已採用 CloudFormation 的情況下再導入新框架反而更費工，並非最少工作量。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"StackSets are for deploying the same stack across multiple accounts/Regions; they do not provide a feature to import an existing resource into a stack.","why_zh":"StackSets 用於跨多個帳號/區域部署相同 stack，並不提供將既有資源匯入 stack 的功能。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The AWS SAM CLI is a serverless application transform/tooling layer and has no command or capability to import an existing VPC; this option is technically invalid.","why_zh":"AWS SAM CLI 是無伺服器應用的 transform/工具層，沒有任何指令或能力可匯入既有 VPC；此選項在技術上不成立。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/import-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/resource-import-new-stack.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/import-resources-manually.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":436,"question_en":"A company has developed a new release of a popular video game and wants to make it available for public download. The new release package is approximately 5 GB in size. The company provides downloads for existing releases from a Linux-based, publicly facing FTP site hosted in an on-premises data center. The company expects the new release will be downloaded by users worldwide. The company wants a solution that provides improved download performance and low transfer costs, regardless of a user's location.","question_zh":"一家公司開發了一款熱門電玩遊戲的新版本，並希望公開提供下載。這個新版本套件的大小約為 5 GB。該公司目前透過一個位於本地端資料中心、以 Linux 為基礎且對外公開的 FTP 站點，提供現有版本的下載。該公司預期這個新版本將被全球各地的使用者下載。該公司希望有一種解決方案，無論使用者位於何處，都能提供更好的下載效能並降低傳輸成本。","options_en":{"A":"Store the game files on Amazon EBS volumes mounted on Amazon EC2 instances within an Auto Scaling group. Configure an FTP service on the EC2 instances. Use an Application Load Balancer in front of the Auto Scaling group. Publish the game download URL for users to download the package.","B":"Store the game files on Amazon EFS volumes that are attached to Amazon EC2 instances within an Auto Scaling group. Configure an FTP service on each of the EC2 instances. Use an Application Load Balancer in front of the Auto Scaling group. Publish the game download URL for users to download the package.","C":"Configure Amazon Route 53 and an Amazon S3 bucket for website hosting. Upload the game files to the S3 bucket. Use Amazon CloudFront for the website. Publish the game download URL for users to download the package.","D":"Configure Amazon Route 53 and an Amazon S3 bucket for website hosting. Upload the game files to the S3 bucket. Set Requester Pays for the S3 bucket. Publish the game download URL for users to download the package."},"options_zh":{"A":"將遊戲檔案儲存在掛載於 Auto Scaling 群組中 Amazon EC2 執行個體上的 Amazon EBS 磁碟區。在這些 EC2 執行個體上設定 FTP 服務。在該 Auto Scaling 群組前面使用一個 Application Load Balancer。發布遊戲下載 URL，供使用者下載該套件。","B":"將遊戲檔案儲存在附加於 Auto Scaling 群組中 Amazon EC2 執行個體的 Amazon EFS 磁碟區。在每個 EC2 執行個體上設定 FTP 服務。在該 Auto Scaling 群組前面使用一個 Application Load Balancer。發布遊戲下載 URL，供使用者下載該套件。","C":"設定 Amazon Route 53 和一個用於網站託管的 Amazon S3 儲存桶。將遊戲檔案上傳到該 S3 儲存桶。為該網站使用 Amazon CloudFront。發布遊戲下載 URL，供使用者下載該套件。","D":"設定 Amazon Route 53 和一個用於網站託管的 Amazon S3 儲存桶。將遊戲檔案上傳到該 S3 儲存桶。為該 S3 儲存桶設定「請求者付費」。發布遊戲下載 URL，供使用者下載該套件。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":437,"question_en":"A company runs an application in the cloud that consists of a database and a website. Users can post data to the website, have the data processed, and have the data sent back to them in an email. Data is stored in a MySQL database running on an Amazon EC2 instance. The database is running in a VPC with two private subnets. The website is running on Apache Tomcat in a single EC2 instance in a different VPC with one public subnet. There is a single VPC peering connection between the database and website VPC. The website has suffered several outages during the last month due to high tra®c. Which actions should a solutions architect take to increase the reliability of the application? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在雲端運行一個由資料庫和網站組成的應用程式。使用者可以將資料發布到該網站，經過處理後，資料會透過電子郵件寄回給他們。資料儲存在運行於 Amazon EC2 執行個體上的 MySQL 資料庫中。該資料庫運行在具有兩個私有子網路的 VPC 中。該網站運行在另一個具有一個公有子網路的 VPC 中，於單一 EC2 執行個體上的 Apache Tomcat 上運作。資料庫 VPC 與網站 VPC 之間只有一條 VPC 對等連線。上個月由於流量過高，該網站發生了多次中斷。解決方案架構師應採取哪些行動來提高該應用程式的可靠性？（選擇三項。）","options_en":{"A":"Place the Tomcat server in an Auto Scaling group with multiple EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer.","B":"Provision an additional VPC peering connection.","C":"Migrate the MySQL database to Amazon Aurora with one Aurora Replica.","D":"Provision two NAT gateways in the database VPC.","E":"Move the Tomcat server to the database VPC.","F":"Create an additional public subnet in a different Availability Zone in the website VPC."},"options_zh":{"A":"將 Tomcat 伺服器放置在一個 Auto Scaling 群組中，該群組在 Application Load Balancer 後面擁有多個 EC2 執行個體。","B":"配置一條額外的 VPC 對等連線。","C":"將 MySQL 資料庫遷移到 Amazon Aurora，並搭配一個 Aurora 複本。","D":"在資料庫 VPC 中配置兩個 NAT 閘道。","E":"將 Tomcat 伺服器移到資料庫 VPC 中。","F":"在網站 VPC 中的另一個可用區域，建立一個額外的公有子網路。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"ACF":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"This is a 'Choose three' question and the genuinely correct set is A, C, and F. The website outages are caused by a single Tomcat EC2 instance in a single public subnet with no scaling. (A) Placing Tomcat in an Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer removes the single-instance SPOF and absorbs traffic spikes. (F) is mandatory because an ALB requires subnets in at least two Availability Zones and the website VPC currently has only one public subnet, so an additional public subnet in a different AZ is needed to make the multi-AZ ALB/ASG design work. (C) Migrating MySQL on a single EC2 instance to Amazon Aurora with an Aurora Replica removes the database SPOF and adds automatic multi-AZ failover. The dump's single answer 'A' is wrong because the question asks for three actions; the community answer 'ACF' is technically correct. The harness verdict schema only permits one letter, so A is recorded as the single most essential and universally-agreed action, but the true full answer is A, C, and F.","explanation_zh":"這是一題「選三個」的題目，真正正確的組合是 A、C、F。網站當機是因為單一 Tomcat EC2 實例位於單一公有子網且無法擴展所造成。(A) 將 Tomcat 放入 Auto Scaling group 並置於 Application Load Balancer 之後，可消除單一實例的單點故障並吸收流量尖峰。(F) 是必要的，因為 ALB 需要至少位於兩個 Availability Zone 的子網，而目前 website VPC 只有一個 public subnet，因此必須在不同 AZ 新增一個 public subnet，才能讓跨 AZ 的 ALB/ASG 架構成立。(C) 將單一 EC2 上的 MySQL 遷移到 Amazon Aurora 並搭配一個 Aurora Replica，可消除資料庫單點故障並提供自動跨 AZ 容錯切換。Dump 的單一答案「A」是錯的，因為題目要求三個動作；社群答案「ACF」在技術上正確。由於本系統的 verdict schema 僅允許一個字母，故記錄 A 作為最關鍵且雙方一致認同的動作，但真正完整答案為 A、C、F。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A single VPC peering connection is not a single point of failure or a throughput bottleneck within AWS; you cannot even create a second peering between the same two VPCs, and it does nothing for website scaling or DB HA.","why_zh":"單一 VPC peering 連線在 AWS 內並非單點故障或吞吐瓶頸，而且同兩個 VPC 之間無法再建立第二條 peering，對網站擴展或資料庫高可用毫無幫助。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"NAT gateways provide outbound internet access for private subnets. The database does not need outbound internet for this workload, so adding two NAT gateways does not improve reliability of the website or database.","why_zh":"NAT gateway 是供私有子網對外連網用。此工作負載的資料庫不需要對外連網，新增兩個 NAT gateway 無法提升網站或資料庫的可靠性。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Moving Tomcat into the database VPC is just a topology change. It does not add redundancy, scaling, or failover, so it does not address the high-traffic outages.","why_zh":"把 Tomcat 移到資料庫 VPC 只是改變網路拓撲，並未增加冗餘、擴展或容錯能力，無法解決高流量造成的當機。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-subnets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Concepts.AuroraHighAvailability.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Replication.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":438,"question_en":"A retail company is operating its ecommerce application on AWS. The application runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The company uses an Amazon RDS DB instance as the database backend. Amazon CloudFront is configured with one origin that points to the ALB. Static content is cached. Amazon Route 53 is used to host all public zones. After an update of the application, the ALB occasionally returns a 502 status code (Bad Gateway) error. The root cause is malformed HTTP headers that are returned to the ALB. The webpage returns successfully when a solutions architect reloads the webpage immediately after the error occurs. While the company is working on the problem, the solutions architect needs to provide a custom error page instead of the standard ALB error page to visitors. Which combination of steps will meet this requirement with the LEAST amount of operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家零售公司在 AWS 上運行其電子商務應用程式。該應用程式運行在 Application Load Balancer (ALB) 後面的 Amazon EC2 執行個體上。該公司使用 Amazon RDS 資料庫執行個體作為資料庫後端。Amazon CloudFront 設定了一個指向該 ALB 的來源。靜態內容會被快取。Amazon Route 53 用於託管所有公有區域。應用程式更新後，該 ALB 偶爾會傳回 502 狀態碼（Bad Gateway）錯誤。根本原因是傳回給 ALB 的 HTTP 標頭格式錯誤。當解決方案架構師在錯誤發生後立即重新載入網頁時，網頁便能成功載入。在該公司處理此問題期間，解決方案架構師需要為訪客提供自訂錯誤頁面，而非標準的 ALB 錯誤頁面。哪種步驟組合能以最少的運營開銷滿足此要求？（選擇兩項。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure the S3 bucket to host a static webpage. Upload the custom error pages to Amazon S3.","B":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to invoke an AWS Lambda function if the ALB health check response Target.FailedHealthChecks is greater than 0. Configure the Lambda function to modify the forwarding rule at the ALB to point to a publicly accessible web server.","C":"Modify the existing Amazon Route 53 records by adding health checks. Configure a fallback target if the health check fails. Modify DNS records to point to a publicly accessible webpage.","D":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to invoke an AWS Lambda function if the ALB health check response Elb.InternalError is greater than 0. Configure the Lambda function to modify the forwarding rule at the ALB to point to a public accessible web server.","E":"Add a custom error response by configuring a CloudFront custom error page. Modify DNS records to point to a publicly accessible web page."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個 Amazon S3 儲存桶。設定該 S3 儲存桶以託管靜態網頁。將自訂錯誤頁面上傳到 Amazon S3。","B":"建立一個 Amazon CloudWatch 警示，當 ALB 健康檢查回應 Target.FailedHealthChecks 大於 0 時，叫用一個 AWS Lambda 函數。設定該 Lambda 函數，修改 ALB 上的轉發規則，使其指向一個可公開存取的 Web 伺服器。","C":"透過新增健康檢查來修改現有的 Amazon Route 53 記錄。設定當健康檢查失敗時的備援目標。修改 DNS 記錄，使其指向一個可公開存取的網頁。","D":"建立一個 Amazon CloudWatch 警示，當 ALB 健康檢查回應 Elb.InternalError 大於 0 時，叫用一個 AWS Lambda 函數。設定該 Lambda 函數，修改 ALB 上的轉發規則，使其指向一個可公開存取的 Web 伺服器。","E":"透過設定 CloudFront 自訂錯誤頁面來新增自訂錯誤回應。修改 DNS 記錄，使其指向一個可公開存取的網頁。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"AE":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["E"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The genuinely correct combination is A + E. CloudFront already fronts the ALB as the single origin, so the lowest-overhead way to replace the standard ALB 502 page with a branded page is to use CloudFront's native custom error response feature. CloudFront can return a custom error page for origin-returned 5xx status codes including 502 (the docs explicitly list 500, 501, 502, 503, 504), and that custom error object (an HTML file) is typically hosted in an Amazon S3 bucket configured for static website hosting and added as an additional origin. So Option A creates and stores the custom page in S3, and Option E configures the CloudFront custom error response that intercepts the 502 from the ALB origin and serves the S3 page to viewers. This requires no new compute, no Lambda automation, and no DNS failover, satisfying the LEAST operational overhead qualifier. The schema forces a single letter; E is the load-bearing step because it is the mechanism that actually delivers the custom error page in place of the ALB error (A only stores the file). The phrase 'Modify DNS records' in E is extraneous/distractor wording, but E is still the only option that pairs with A to use CloudFront's edge custom error response.","explanation_zh":"真正正確的組合是 A + E。CloudFront 已經作為單一 origin 位於 ALB 前方，因此以最低營運負擔將標準 ALB 502 頁面換成自訂頁面的方式，就是使用 CloudFront 原生的 custom error response 功能。CloudFront 可針對 origin 回傳的 5xx 狀態碼（包含 502，文件明確列出 500、501、502、503、504）回傳自訂錯誤頁面，而該自訂錯誤物件（HTML 檔）通常存放在設定為靜態網站託管的 Amazon S3 bucket，並作為額外 origin 加入。因此 Option A 在 S3 建立並存放自訂頁面，Option E 設定 CloudFront custom error response，攔截來自 ALB origin 的 502 並把 S3 頁面送給檢視者。這不需要新的運算資源、Lambda 自動化或 DNS failover，符合 LEAST operational overhead 的條件。Schema 限制只能填一個字母；E 是關鍵步驟，因為它才是真正以自訂錯誤頁面取代 ALB 錯誤的機制（A 只負責存檔）。E 中的『Modify DNS records』屬於多餘的干擾字句，但 E 仍是唯一能與 A 搭配使用 CloudFront 邊緣 custom error response 的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A is actually a correct part of the real two-answer combination (it creates the S3 static site that stores the custom error page). It is only marked as a non-verdict here because the schema forces a single letter and E is the load-bearing mechanism; A alone does nothing without E.","why_zh":"A 其實是真正雙選答案組合的正確之一（建立存放自訂錯誤頁面的 S3 靜態網站）。此處未列入 verdict 僅因 schema 限制只能填一個字母，而 E 才是關鍵機制；A 單獨存在若無 E 則無作用。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Target.FailedHealthChecks is not a real ALB CloudWatch metric, and using a Lambda function to rewrite ALB forwarding rules to a public web server is high operational overhead and complex. Health checks would not reliably fire for intermittent 502s caused by malformed headers, since the targets are otherwise healthy.","why_zh":"Target.FailedHealthChecks 並非真正的 ALB CloudWatch 指標，且用 Lambda 改寫 ALB 轉送規則指向公開網頁伺服器營運負擔高且複雜。針對由格式錯誤標頭造成的間歇性 502，目標本身仍健康，健康檢查不會可靠觸發。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Route 53 health-check failover is DNS-based and routes ALL traffic to a fallback, not just failed requests; it cannot detect intermittent per-request 502s (the ALB endpoint stays healthy). High overhead and ineffective for transient malformed-header errors.","why_zh":"Route 53 健康檢查 failover 屬 DNS 層級，會把所有流量導向備援而非僅失敗請求；無法偵測逐請求的間歇性 502（ALB 端點仍健康）。對暫時性的格式錯誤標頭錯誤而言負擔高且無效。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Elb.InternalError is not a valid ALB CloudWatch metric name. Like B, the Lambda-based forwarding-rule rewrite adds significant automation complexity and operational overhead, far more than CloudFront's built-in custom error response.","why_zh":"Elb.InternalError 並非有效的 ALB CloudWatch 指標名稱。與 B 相同，以 Lambda 改寫轉送規則會增加大量自動化複雜度與營運負擔，遠高於 CloudFront 內建的 custom error response。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/GeneratingCustomErrorResponses.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/creating-custom-error-pages.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/DownloadDistValuesErrorPages.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/custom-error-pages-different-locations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-cloudwatch-metrics.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":439,"question_en":"A company wants to migrate an Amazon Aurora MySQL DB cluster from an existing AWS account to a new AWS account in the same AWS Region. Both accounts are members of the same organization in AWS Organizations. The company must minimize database service interruption before the company performs DNS cutover to the new database. Which migration strategy will meet this requirement? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司希望將一個 Amazon Aurora MySQL 資料庫叢集從現有的 AWS 帳戶遷移到同一 AWS 區域中的新 AWS 帳戶。這兩個帳戶都是 AWS Organizations 中同一組織的成員。在該公司對新資料庫執行 DNS 切換之前，必須盡量減少資料庫服務中斷的時間。哪種遷移策略能滿足此要求？（選擇兩項。）","options_en":{"A":"Take a snapshot of the existing Aurora database. Share the snapshot with the new AWS account. Create an Aurora DB cluster in the new account from the snapshot.","B":"Create an Aurora DB cluster in the new AWS account. Use AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to migrate data between the two Aurora DB clusters.","C":"Use AWS Backup to share an Aurora database backup from the existing AWS account to the new AWS account. Create an Aurora DB cluster in the new AWS account from the snapshot.","D":"Create an Aurora DB cluster in the new AWS account. Use AWS Application Migration Service to migrate data between the two Aurora DB clusters."},"options_zh":{"A":"為現有的 Aurora 資料庫建立一個快照。將該快照與新的 AWS 帳戶共用。從該快照在新帳戶中建立一個 Aurora 資料庫叢集。","B":"在新的 AWS 帳戶中建立一個 Aurora 資料庫叢集。使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 在這兩個 Aurora 資料庫叢集之間遷移資料。","C":"使用 AWS Backup 將現有 AWS 帳戶中的 Aurora 資料庫備份共用給新的 AWS 帳戶。從該快照在新的 AWS 帳戶中建立一個 Aurora 資料庫叢集。","D":"在新的 AWS 帳戶中建立一個 Aurora 資料庫叢集。使用 AWS Application Migration Service 在這兩個 Aurora 資料庫叢集之間遷移資料。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AB":67,"B":33},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Migration","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is to minimize database service interruption before DNS cutover when moving an Aurora MySQL cluster to another account in the same Region/Organization. Two valid native approaches exist. (A) Aurora supports sharing a manual DB cluster snapshot cross-account via ModifyDBClusterSnapshotAttribute and restoring a new cluster in the target account; the source keeps running the whole time, so there is no interruption to the live database until the DNS cutover. (B) AWS DMS supports Aurora MySQL as both source and target and, using ongoing replication / change data capture (CDC), keeps the new cluster continuously synchronized with the live source so the only interruption is the brief DNS cutover. D is wrong because AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) is a server lift-and-shift/rehost tool that performs block-level OS replication of physical, virtual, or cloud servers; it cannot migrate data between managed Aurora DB clusters (no OS/agent access on a managed service). The dump answer including D is therefore technically impossible. Between A and C, both are point-in-time copy mechanisms, but A is the canonical, directly documented native Aurora cross-account snapshot path, making A+B the intended pair.","explanation_zh":"需求是在 DNS cutover 之前，將 Aurora MySQL 叢集遷移到同一 Region/Organization 內的另一個帳號時，將資料庫服務中斷降到最低。有兩種有效的原生方法。(A) Aurora 支援透過 ModifyDBClusterSnapshotAttribute 跨帳號共用手動 DB cluster snapshot，並在目標帳號從該 snapshot 還原出新叢集；過程中來源資料庫持續運作，直到 DNS cutover 前都不會中斷。(B) AWS DMS 支援 Aurora MySQL 同時作為來源與目標，並可使用持續複寫 / change data capture (CDC) 讓新叢集與運作中的來源持續同步，因此唯一的中斷只是短暫的 DNS cutover。D 錯誤，因為 AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) 是伺服器 lift-and-shift/rehost 工具，對實體、虛擬或雲端伺服器執行區塊層級的 OS 複寫；它無法在受管理的 Aurora DB 叢集之間遷移資料（受管服務沒有 OS/agent 存取）。因此包含 D 的 dump 答案在技術上不可能成立。A 與 C 都是時間點複本機制，但 A 是經官方文件記載的原生 Aurora 跨帳號 snapshot 路徑，故 A+B 為正解組合。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Backup cross-account copy + restore is functionally a point-in-time copy, the same class of mechanism as A, but A is the canonical native Aurora cross-account snapshot path; in a choose-two it is the redundant/less-direct option versus the A+B pair.","why_zh":"AWS Backup 跨帳號複製 + 還原本質上是時間點複本，與 A 屬同一類機制，但 A 才是官方記載的原生 Aurora 跨帳號 snapshot 路徑；在二選的情境下，相較 A+B 組合它是較冗餘、較不直接的選項。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) is a server lift-and-shift/rehost service using block-level OS replication of physical/virtual/cloud servers; it cannot migrate data between managed Aurora DB clusters, so it does not apply at all.","why_zh":"AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) 是使用區塊層級 OS 複寫的伺服器 lift-and-shift/rehost 服務；它無法在受管理的 Aurora DB 叢集之間遷移資料，因此完全不適用。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/USER_CopyDBClusterSnapshot.CrossAccount.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/USER_DMS_migration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/dms/latest/userguide/CHAP_Source.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/dms/latest/userguide/CHAP_Source.MySQL.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/mgn/latest/ug/what-is-application-migration-service.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・複選・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":440,"question_en":"A software as a service (SaaS) company provides a media software solution to customers. The solution is hosted on 50 VPCs across various AWS Regions and AWS accounts. One of the VPCs is designated as a management VPC. The compute resources in the VPCs work independently. The company has developed a new feature that requires all 50 VPCs to be able to communicate with each other. The new feature also requires one-way access from each customer's VPC to the company's management VPC. The management VPC hosts a compute resource that validates licenses for the media software solution. The number of VPCs that the company will use to host the solution will continue to increase as the solution grows. Which combination of steps will provide the required VPC connectivity with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家軟體即服務 (SaaS) 公司為客戶提供媒體軟體解決方案。該解決方案託管在跨越多個 AWS 區域和 AWS 帳戶的 50 個 VPC 上。其中一個 VPC 被指定為管理 VPC。這些 VPC 中的運算資源各自獨立運作。該公司開發了一項新功能，需要讓所有 50 個 VPC 能夠彼此通訊。這項新功能還需要從每個客戶的 VPC 對公司的管理 VPC 進行單向存取。管理 VPC 上託管了一個負責驗證媒體軟體解決方案授權的運算資源。隨著解決方案的成長，公司用於託管該解決方案的 VPC 數量將持續增加。哪種步驟組合能以最少的營運開銷提供所需的 VPC 連線能力？（選擇兩項。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a transit gateway. Attach all the company's VPCs and relevant subnets to the transit gateway.","B":"Create VPC peering connections between all the company's VPCs.","C":"Create a Network Load Balancer (NLB) that points to the compute resource for license validation. Create an AWS PrivateLink endpoint service that is available to each customer's VPAssociate the endpoint service with the NLB.","D":"Create a VPN appliance in each customer's VPC. Connect the company's management VPC to each customer's VPC by using AWS Site- to-Site VPN.","E":"Create a VPC peering connection between the company's management VPC and each customer's VPC."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個 AWS Transit Gateway，並將公司所有的 VPC 與相關子網路連接至該 Transit Gateway。","B":"在公司所有的 VPC 之間建立 VPC 對等連線。","C":"建立一個指向授權驗證運算資源的 Network Load Balancer (NLB)。建立一個可供每個客戶 VPC 使用的 AWS PrivateLink 端點服務，並將該端點服務與 NLB 建立關聯。","D":"在每個客戶的 VPC 中建立一個 VPN 設備。使用 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 將公司的管理 VPC 連接到每個客戶的 VPC。","E":"在公司的管理 VPC 與每個客戶的 VPC 之間建立 VPC 對等連線。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"AC":67,"BC":25},"tags":["Networking/DNS"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The question states two distinct requirements: (1) all 50+ growing VPCs across multiple Regions and accounts must communicate with each other (any-to-any mesh), and (2) one-way access from each customer VPC to a single compute resource in the management VPC for license validation. Requirement 1 is best met by AWS Transit Gateway (A), a managed hub-and-spoke transit hub that interconnects VPCs across accounts (via RAM) and Regions (via inter-Region peering); adding new VPCs is a single attachment, giving the least operational overhead as the fleet grows. Requirement 2 is best met by AWS PrivateLink (C): an NLB-backed endpoint service exposes the license-validation compute resource privately to each customer's VPC, and PrivateLink is inherently unidirectional (consumers initiate connections to the provider; the provider cannot reach back into consumer VPCs), which exactly satisfies the 'one-way access' wording. Transit Gateway alone (the dump answer A) provides bidirectional routable connectivity, so enforcing one-way access would require additional route-table/security-group engineering and would not natively give the one-way guarantee the question explicitly calls out.","explanation_zh":"題目有兩個明確需求:(1) 跨多個 Region 與帳戶、且數量持續成長的 50+ 個 VPC 必須互相通訊(任意對任意的網狀連線);(2) 每個客戶 VPC 對 management VPC 中單一授權驗證 compute 資源的「單向」存取。需求 1 最適合用 AWS Transit Gateway (A) 滿足,它是受管的 hub-and-spoke 轉接中樞,可跨帳戶(透過 RAM)與跨 Region(透過 inter-Region peering)互連 VPC;新增 VPC 只需一個 attachment,隨著規模成長維運負擔最低。需求 2 最適合用 AWS PrivateLink (C):以 NLB 為後端的 endpoint service 將授權驗證資源私密地提供給每個客戶 VPC,而 PrivateLink 本質上是單向的(consumer 主動連向 provider,provider 無法反向連入 consumer VPC),正好符合「單向存取」的描述。僅用 Transit Gateway(dump 答案 A)提供的是雙向可路由連線,要達成單向限制需額外設計路由表/安全群組,且無法原生保證題目明確要求的單向特性。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Full-mesh VPC peering between 50 VPCs requires N(N-1)/2 = 1,225 connections, peering is non-transitive, and every new VPC needs peering to all existing ones - the highest operational overhead, the opposite of what is required. It also does not address the one-way license-validation requirement.","why_zh":"50 個 VPC 的全網狀 peering 需要 N(N-1)/2 = 1,225 條連線,peering 不具遞移性,且每新增一個 VPC 都要與所有現有 VPC 建立 peering,維運負擔最高,與需求相反。也未解決單向授權驗證需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Deploying self-managed VPN appliances in every customer VPC plus Site-to-Site VPN is high operational overhead (managing appliances, tunnels, BGP) and does not provide the any-to-any mesh across all 50 VPCs; it only links management to each customer.","why_zh":"在每個客戶 VPC 部署自管 VPN 設備並建立 Site-to-Site VPN,維運負擔高(需管理設備、隧道、BGP),且無法提供全部 50 個 VPC 間的任意對任意網狀連線;只連接 management 與各客戶。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Peering only the management VPC to each customer VPC creates one-way-ish hub connectivity for license validation but is bidirectional and routable, and crucially does NOT satisfy the requirement that all 50 VPCs communicate with each other (spokes cannot reach each other through a peering hub since peering is non-transitive).","why_zh":"僅將 management VPC 與每個客戶 VPC 建立 peering,雖能做到中樞式連線供授權驗證,但它是雙向可路由的,且關鍵在於無法滿足所有 50 個 VPC 互相通訊的需求(因為 peering 不具遞移性,spoke 之間無法透過 peering 中樞互通)。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/what-is-transit-gateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/building-scalable-secure-multi-vpc-network-infrastructure/transit-gateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/patterns/access-container-applications-privately-on-amazon-ecs-by-using-aws-privatelink-and-a-network-load-balancer.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":441,"question_en":"A company has multiple lines of business (LOBs) that roll up to the parent company. The company has asked its solutions architect to develop a solution with the following requirements: • Produce a single AWS invoice for all of the AWS accounts used by its LOBs. • The costs for each LOB account should be broken out on the invoice. • Provide the ability to restrict services and features in the LOB accounts, as defined by the company's governance policy. • Each LOB account should be delegated full administrator permissions, regardless of the governance policy. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司擁有多個業務部門 (LOB)，這些部門皆歸屬於母公司。該公司要求解決方案架構師設計一套滿足以下需求的解決方案：\n• 針對其各業務部門所使用的所有 AWS 帳戶，產生單一的 AWS 帳單。\n• 帳單上須列出每個業務部門帳戶各自的費用明細。\n• 能夠依照公司的治理政策，限制業務部門帳戶可使用的服務與功能。\n• 無論治理政策為何，每個業務部門帳戶都應獲得完整的管理員權限委派。\n解決方案架構師應採取哪兩項步驟組合來滿足這些需求？（選擇兩項。）","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Organizations to create an organization in the parent account for each LOB. Then invite each LOB account to the appropriate organization.","B":"Use AWS Organizations to create a single organization in the parent account. Then, invite each LOB's AWS account to join the organization.","C":"Implement service quotas to define the services and features that are permitted and apply the quotas to each LOB. as appropriate.","D":"Create an SCP that allows only approved services and features, then apply the policy to the LOB accounts.","E":"Enable consolidated billing in the parent account's billing console and link the LOB accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Organizations 在母公司帳戶中為每個業務部門建立一個組織。然後邀請每個業務部門帳戶加入相應的組織。","B":"使用 AWS Organizations 在母公司帳戶中建立單一組織。然後邀請每個業務部門的 AWS 帳戶加入該組織。","C":"實作服務配額 (service quotas) 來定義允許使用的服務與功能，並依需要將配額套用到每個業務部門。","D":"建立一個僅允許已核准服務與功能的 SCP，然後將此政策套用到各業務部門帳戶。","E":"在母公司帳戶的帳單主控台中啟用合併帳單，並連結各業務部門帳戶。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BD":51,"BE":44},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識・複選"},{"id":442,"question_en":"A solutions architect has deployed a web application that serves users across two AWS Regions under a custom domain. The application uses Amazon Route 53 latency-based routing. The solutions architect has associated weighted record sets with a pair of web servers in separate Availability Zones for each Region. The solutions architect runs a disaster recovery scenario. When all the web servers in one Region are stopped, Route 53 does not automatically redirect users to the other Region. Which of the following are possible root causes of this issue? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位解決方案架構師已部署一個 Web 應用程式，該應用程式在自訂網域下為跨兩個 AWS 區域的使用者提供服務。此應用程式使用 Amazon Route 53 的延遲基礎路由。解決方案架構師已將加權記錄集與每個區域中各自位於不同可用區的一對 Web 伺服器建立關聯。解決方案架構師執行了一次災難復原情境測試。當某個區域中的所有 Web 伺服器都停止運作時，Route 53 並未自動將使用者重新導向到另一個區域。以下哪些可能是造成此問題的根本原因？（選擇兩項。）","options_en":{"A":"The weight for the Region where the web servers were stopped is higher than the weight for the other Region.","B":"One of the web servers in the secondary Region did not pass its HTTP health check.","C":"Latency resource record sets cannot be used in combination with weighted resource record sets.","D":"The setting to evaluate target health is not turned on for the latency alias resource record set that is associated with the domain in the Region where the web servers were stopped.","E":"An HTTP health check has not been set up for one or more of the weighted resource record sets associated with the stopped web servers."},"options_zh":{"A":"已停止 Web 伺服器所在區域的權重高於另一個區域的權重。","B":"次要區域中的其中一台 Web 伺服器未通過其 HTTP 健康檢查。","C":"延遲資源記錄集無法與加權資源記錄集結合使用。","D":"與已停止 Web 伺服器所在區域網域相關聯的延遲別名資源記錄集，未啟用評估目標健康狀態的設定。","E":"與已停止的 Web 伺服器相關聯的一個或多個加權資源記錄集，尚未設定 HTTP 健康檢查。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"DE":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"This is the canonical Route 53 'complex configuration' described in the AWS docs: latency alias records at the top of the tree, each targeting a group of weighted (non-alias) records for EC2 instances in two Regions. For Route 53 to back out of a failed Region and redirect users to the other Region, two conditions must hold, and the question's symptom (no automatic redirect when a whole Region is stopped) maps directly to violations of them. (D) Evaluate Target Health must be set to Yes on the latency alias record. The docs state that if it is set to No, 'Route 53 continues to route traffic to the records that an alias record refers to even if health checks for those records are failing... Route 53 must choose one record in this branch instead of backing out of the branch and looking for a healthy record in the other region' — so failover never happens. (E) Every weighted (non-alias) record must have an HTTP health check; the docs say if you omit a health check, 'Route 53 has no way to know. Route 53 assumes that the resource is healthy and returns the applicable value,' so a stopped instance still gets returned and no failover occurs. The intended answer set is D and E (this harness allows only one letter, so D is given as the lead root cause, with E documented here as the co-correct option). The dump's suggestion (A) is wrong; the community answer (DE) is correct.","explanation_zh":"這是 AWS 文件中典型的 Route 53「複雜設定」：樹的頂端是 latency alias 記錄，各自指向兩個 Region 中對應 EC2 執行個體的一組 weighted（非 alias）記錄。要讓 Route 53 在某 Region 全部失效時退出該分支並把使用者導向另一個 Region，必須同時滿足兩個條件，而題目的症狀（整個 Region 停掉卻沒有自動轉址）正對應到違反這兩個條件。(D) latency alias 記錄上的 Evaluate Target Health 必須設為 Yes。文件指出若設為 No，『Route 53 會繼續把流量導向 alias 記錄所指的記錄，即使這些記錄的健康檢查正在失敗……Route 53 必須在此分支中選擇一筆記錄，而不是退出分支去尋找另一 Region 中健康的記錄』，因此永遠不會 failover。(E) 每一筆 weighted（非 alias）記錄都必須有 HTTP 健康檢查；文件指出若省略健康檢查，『Route 53 無從得知，會假設資源是健康的並回傳對應值』，因此被停掉的執行個體仍會被回傳，不會 failover。正確答案組合是 D 與 E（本系統只允許一個字母，故以 D 作為主因，E 在此一併記錄為共同正解）。Dump 建議的 A 是錯的；社群答案 DE 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Weight only governs how traffic is distributed among HEALTHY records within a Region; it never prevents failover. Once health checks mark every record in the stopped Region unhealthy, Route 53 ignores weight and backs out to the other Region. A higher weight in the failed Region does not stop redirection.","why_zh":"權重只決定流量如何分配給某 Region 內『健康』的記錄，永遠不會阻止 failover。一旦健康檢查把停掉 Region 的所有記錄標為不健康，Route 53 就會忽略權重並退出到另一 Region。失效 Region 權重較高並不會阻止轉址。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"If only one of the two secondary-Region servers failed its health check, the other secondary server is still healthy, so Route 53 would still successfully redirect traffic there. A single failed secondary check does not explain a total failure to redirect.","why_zh":"若次要 Region 兩台伺服器中只有一台健康檢查失敗，另一台仍健康，Route 53 仍能成功把流量導向那裡。單一次要伺服器檢查失敗無法解釋完全無法轉址。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"False. The AWS docs explicitly present latency alias records targeting weighted records as a standard 'complex configuration.' Latency and weighted record sets are designed to be combined in a decision tree.","why_zh":"錯誤。AWS 文件明確把 latency alias 記錄指向 weighted 記錄列為標準的『複雜設定』。latency 與 weighted 記錄就是設計用來在決策樹中組合使用的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-complex-configs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-simple-configs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-configuring.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-weighted.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":443,"question_en":"A ­ood monitoring agency has deployed more than 10,000 water-level monitoring sensors. Sensors send continuous data updates, and each update is less than 1 MB in size. The agency has a ­eet of on-premises application servers. These servers receive updates from the sensors, convert the raw data into a human readable format, and write the results to an on-premises relational database server. Data analysts then use simple SQL queries to monitor the data. The agency wants to increase overall application availability and reduce the effort that is required to perform maintenance tasks. These maintenance tasks, which include updates and patches to the application servers, cause downtime. While an application server is down, data is lost from sensors because the remaining servers cannot handle the entire workload. The agency wants a solution that optimizes operational overhead and costs. A solutions architect recommends the use of AWS IoT Core to collect the sensor data. What else should the solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家洪水監測機構已部署超過 10,000 個水位監測感測器。感測器持續傳送資料更新，每次更新的大小皆小於 1 MB。該機構擁有一批本地應用程式伺服器。這些伺服器接收來自感測器的更新，將原始資料轉換為人類可讀的格式，並將結果寫入本地的關聯式資料庫伺服器。資料分析師則使用簡單的 SQL 查詢來監控資料。該機構希望提高整體應用程式的可用性，並減少執行維護任務所需的工作量。這些維護任務（包括對應用程式伺服器的更新與修補）會導致停機。當某台應用程式伺服器停機時，由於其餘伺服器無法處理全部工作負載，會導致來自感測器的資料遺失。該機構希望採用一種能夠優化營運開銷與成本的解決方案。一位解決方案架構師建議使用 AWS IoT Core 來收集感測器資料。解決方案架構師還應建議什麼，才能滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Send the sensor data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose. Use an AWS Lambda function to read the Kinesis Data Firehose data, convert it to .csv format, and insert it into an Amazon Aurora MySQL DB instance. Instruct the data analysts to query the data directly from the DB instance.","B":"Send the sensor data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose. Use an AWS Lambda function to read the Kinesis Data Firehose data, convert it to Apache Parquet format, and save it to an Amazon S3 bucket. Instruct the data analysts to query the data by using Amazon Athena.","C":"Send the sensor data to an Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink (previously known as Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics) application to convert the data to .csv format and store it in an Amazon S3 bucket. Import the data into an Amazon Aurora MySQL DB instance. Instruct the data analysts to query the data directly from the DB instance.","D":"Send the sensor data to an Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink (previously known as Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics) application to convert the data to Apache Parquet format and store it in an Amazon S3 bucket. Instruct the data analysts to query the data by using Amazon Athena."},"options_zh":{"A":"將感測器資料傳送到 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose。使用 AWS Lambda 函數讀取 Kinesis Data Firehose 的資料，將其轉換為 .csv 格式，並插入到 Amazon Aurora MySQL 資料庫執行個體中。指示資料分析師直接從該資料庫執行個體查詢資料。","B":"將感測器資料傳送到 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose。使用 AWS Lambda 函數讀取 Kinesis Data Firehose 的資料，將其轉換為 Apache Parquet 格式，並儲存到 Amazon S3 儲存桶中。指示資料分析師使用 Amazon Athena 查詢資料。","C":"將感測器資料傳送到 Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink（先前稱為 Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics）應用程式，將資料轉換為 .csv 格式並儲存到 Amazon S3 儲存桶中。將資料匯入 Amazon Aurora MySQL 資料庫執行個體。指示資料分析師直接從該資料庫執行個體查詢資料。","D":"將感測器資料傳送到 Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink（先前稱為 Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics）應用程式，將資料轉換為 Apache Parquet 格式並儲存到 Amazon S3 儲存桶中。指示資料分析師使用 Amazon Athena 查詢資料。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":80},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The architect has already chosen AWS IoT Core. IoT Core's rules engine supports a 'firehose' rule action that sends messages directly to a Firehose delivery stream, but it has NO action that delivers data directly to an Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink application; Flink only ingests from Kinesis Data Streams or Amazon MSK, not from IoT Core directly. That makes options C and D architecturally invalid as written ('Send the sensor data to an Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink application'). Between the two valid IoT Core -> Firehose designs (A and B), the requirement is to increase availability and minimize maintenance/operational overhead and cost. Option B is fully serverless: Firehose with a Lambda transform converts the JSON to columnar Apache Parquet, lands it in S3 (cheap, durable, no patching), and analysts run simple SQL with Athena (pay-per-query, no servers). Option A loads every sub-1MB update into a provisioned Aurora MySQL instance that must run 24/7 and be patched/managed, which is higher operational overhead and cost. So B best meets the 'optimize operational overhead and costs' qualifier.","explanation_zh":"架構師已選定 AWS IoT Core。IoT Core 規則引擎支援 'firehose' 規則動作，可將訊息直接送入 Firehose 傳遞串流，但並沒有可直接將資料送入 Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink 應用程式的動作；Flink 只能從 Kinesis Data Streams 或 Amazon MSK 擷取資料，無法直接由 IoT Core 餵入。因此選項 C 與 D 所寫的「Send the sensor data to an Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink application」在架構上不成立。在兩個有效的 IoT Core -> Firehose 設計（A 與 B）之間，需求是提高可用性、降低維護/營運負擔與成本。選項 B 完全無伺服器：Firehose 搭配 Lambda 轉換將 JSON 轉成欄式 Apache Parquet 並存入 S3（便宜、耐久、免修補），分析師以 Amazon Athena 用簡單 SQL 查詢（按查詢計費、無伺服器）。選項 A 將每筆小於 1MB 的更新寫入需 24/7 運行且須修補管理的 Aurora MySQL 執行個體，營運負擔與成本較高。因此 B 最符合『optimize operational overhead and costs』的條件。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Technically works (IoT Core -> Firehose -> Lambda -> Aurora), but loading continuous sub-1MB updates from 10,000+ sensors into a provisioned Aurora MySQL instance that runs 24/7 and needs patching/scaling adds operational overhead and cost, contradicting the 'optimize operational overhead and costs' requirement that a serverless S3/Athena pattern satisfies.","why_zh":"技術上可行（IoT Core -> Firehose -> Lambda -> Aurora），但將 10,000 多個感測器持續產生的小型更新寫入需 24/7 運行並要修補/擴展的 Aurora MySQL 執行個體，增加營運負擔與成本，違反『optimize operational overhead and costs』需求，而無伺服器的 S3/Athena 模式較佳。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Architecturally invalid: IoT Core cannot send data directly to a Managed Service for Apache Flink application (no such rule action), and Flink ingests only from Kinesis Data Streams/MSK. Also adds the heavier Aurora layer, increasing cost/overhead.","why_zh":"架構不成立：IoT Core 無法將資料直接送至 Managed Service for Apache Flink 應用程式（無此規則動作），且 Flink 僅能從 Kinesis Data Streams/MSK 擷取。此外又加上較重的 Aurora 層，增加成本與負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but is wrong: IoT Core has no rule action to deliver data directly to a Managed Service for Apache Flink application, and Flink sources are Kinesis Data Streams/MSK only. Even ignoring that, a managed Flink application is more operational/cost overhead than Firehose's native (or Lambda-based) JSON-to-Parquet conversion for this simple convert-and-store use case.","why_zh":"這是題庫建議答案，但有誤：IoT Core 沒有可將資料直接送至 Managed Service for Apache Flink 應用程式的規則動作，且 Flink 的來源僅限 Kinesis Data Streams/MSK。即使忽略此點，對於這種單純的轉換並儲存情境，受管的 Flink 應用程式比 Firehose 原生（或基於 Lambda）的 JSON 轉 Parquet 帶來更高的營運與成本負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/iot-rule-actions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/kinesis-firehose-rule-action.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/record-format-conversion.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/data-transformation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/managed-flink/latest/java/how-sources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/what-is.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":444,"question_en":"A public retail web application uses an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in front of Amazon EC2 instances running across multiple Availability Zones (AZs) in a Region backed by an Amazon RDS MySQL Multi-AZ deployment. Target group health checks are configured to use HTTP and pointed at the product catalog page. Auto Scaling is configured to maintain the web ­eet size based on the ALB health check. Recently, the application experienced an outage. Auto Scaling continuously replaced the instances during the outage. A subsequent investigation determined that the web server metrics were within the normal range, but the database tier was experiencing high load, resulting in severely elevated query response times. Which of the following changes together would remediate these issues while improving monitoring capabilities for the availability and functionality of the entire application stack for future growth? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一個公開的零售 Web 應用程式在 Application Load Balancer (ALB) 後方使用跨越某個區域內多個可用區 (AZ) 執行的 Amazon EC2 執行個體，並以 Amazon RDS MySQL Multi-AZ 部署作為後端支援。目標群組的健康檢查已設定為使用 HTTP，並指向產品目錄頁面。Auto Scaling 已設定為根據 ALB 健康檢查來維持 Web 機群的大小。最近，該應用程式發生了一次中斷。在中斷期間，Auto Scaling 不斷地替換執行個體。後續調查發現，Web 伺服器的指標皆在正常範圍內，但資料庫層承受高負載，導致查詢回應時間嚴重延長。以下哪些變更組合可同時解決這些問題，並改善整個應用程式堆疊在未來成長時的可用性與功能監控能力？（選擇兩項。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure read replicas for Amazon RDS MySQL and use the single reader endpoint in the web application to reduce the load on the backend database tier.","B":"Configure the target group health check to point at a simple HTML page instead of a product catalog page and the Amazon Route 53 health check against the product page to evaluate full application functionality. Configure Amazon CloudWatch alarms to notify administrators when the site fails.","C":"Configure the target group health check to use a TCP check of the Amazon EC2 web server and the Amazon Route 53 health check against the product page to evaluate full application functionality. Configure Amazon CloudWatch alarms to notify administrators when the site fails.","D":"Configure an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for Amazon RDS with an action to recover a high-load, impaired RDS instance in the database tier.","E":"Configure an Amazon ElastiCache cluster and place it between the web application and RDS MySQL instances to reduce the load on the backend database tier."},"options_zh":{"A":"為 Amazon RDS MySQL 設定讀取複本，並在 Web 應用程式中使用單一讀取端點，以降低後端資料庫層的負載。","B":"將目標群組健康檢查改為指向一個簡單的 HTML 頁面，而非產品目錄頁面，並針對產品頁面設定 Amazon Route 53 健康檢查以評估完整的應用程式功能。設定 Amazon CloudWatch 警示，在網站發生故障時通知管理員。","C":"將目標群組健康檢查改為對 Amazon EC2 Web 伺服器使用 TCP 檢查，並針對產品頁面設定 Amazon Route 53 健康檢查以評估完整的應用程式功能。設定 Amazon CloudWatch 警示，在網站發生故障時通知管理員。","D":"為 Amazon RDS 設定 Amazon CloudWatch 警示，並配置動作以復原資料庫層中負載過高、狀態受損的 RDS 執行個體。","E":"設定一個 Amazon ElastiCache 叢集，並將其置於 Web 應用程式與 RDS MySQL 執行個體之間，以降低後端資料庫層的負載。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BE":68,"AB":17},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The outage cause was that the ALB target group health check pointed at the product catalog page, which queries the database. When the RDS tier was overloaded and slow, the health check failed even though the web servers were healthy, so Auto Scaling kept replacing perfectly good instances. The remediation must (1) stop the fleet from being churned by DB problems while still monitoring real functionality, and (2) reduce the read load on the database. Option B decouples the ASG/ALB health check from the DB by pointing it at a simple static HTML page (so the web tier is only judged on web health), and adds a Route 53 health check against the product page plus CloudWatch alarms to monitor and alert on full end-to-end application functionality and availability. Option E adds an ElastiCache cluster between the web app and RDS MySQL; AWS docs describe a database cache as supplementing the primary database by 'removing unnecessary pressure on it, typically in the form of frequently-accessed read data,' which is exactly the read-heavy retail catalog scenario and is the correct way to reduce load on an RDS MySQL backend. Together B and E fix the root cause and improve monitoring for future growth.","explanation_zh":"故障根因是 ALB target group 的 health check 指向會查詢資料庫的 product catalog 頁面。當 RDS 層過載且回應緩慢時，即使 web server 本身正常，health check 仍然失敗，導致 Auto Scaling 持續更換健康的執行個體。修復方案必須 (1) 讓 web 機隊不再因資料庫問題而被反覆汰換，同時仍能監控真正的功能；(2) 降低資料庫的讀取負載。選項 B 將 ASG/ALB health check 改指向一個簡單的靜態 HTML 頁面，使 web 層只依據 web 健康狀態判斷，並另外設定 Route 53 health check 針對 product 頁面以評估完整的端到端應用功能與可用性，再搭配 CloudWatch alarm 通知。選項 E 在 web 應用與 RDS MySQL 之間加入 ElastiCache cluster；AWS 文件指出資料庫快取可作為主資料庫的補充，移除其不必要的壓力，特別是頻繁讀取的資料，這正是讀取繁重的零售目錄情境，也是降低 RDS MySQL 後端負載的正確做法。B 與 E 共同修正根因並改善未來成長的監控能力。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"RDS MySQL read replicas do NOT provide a single 'reader endpoint' that load-balances across replicas. The single reader endpoint with DNS-based connection distribution is an Amazon Aurora feature; each RDS MySQL read replica has its own individual endpoint. The option's stated mechanism is technically false for RDS MySQL, so A cannot be a correct remediation as written.","why_zh":"RDS MySQL 的 read replica 並沒有一個能在多個副本間做負載平衡的單一 'reader endpoint'。具備 DNS 連線分配的單一 reader endpoint 是 Amazon Aurora 的功能；每個 RDS MySQL read replica 都有各自獨立的 endpoint。此選項描述的機制對 RDS MySQL 在技術上是錯誤的，因此 A 不能成為正確的修復方案。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A TCP health check only verifies the listener port is open; it does not confirm the web server returns a valid HTTP response, providing weaker functional monitoring than B's HTTP check against a simple page. While TCP would also decouple the check from the DB, the question explicitly asks to improve monitoring of availability and functionality, making B's HTTP-page + Route 53 approach superior.","why_zh":"TCP health check 僅驗證監聽埠是否開啟，並不能確認 web server 回傳有效的 HTTP 回應，其功能性監控弱於 B 中針對簡單頁面的 HTTP 檢查。雖然 TCP 同樣能讓檢查與資料庫脫鉤，但題目明確要求改善可用性與功能的監控，因此 B 的 HTTP 頁面加上 Route 53 的方式更佳。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"There is no CloudWatch alarm action to 'recover' an RDS instance. The recover (and stop/terminate/reboot) alarm actions apply only to Amazon EC2 per-instance metrics. RDS Multi-AZ already provides automatic failover for instance impairment, and 'high load' is not an instance impairment that recovery would fix, so D is invalid.","why_zh":"CloudWatch 並沒有可 'recover' RDS 執行個體的 alarm action。recover（以及 stop/terminate/reboot）等 alarm action 僅適用於 Amazon EC2 的單一執行個體指標。RDS Multi-AZ 本身已對執行個體損壞提供自動故障轉移，而 '高負載' 並非 recovery 能修復的執行個體損壞，因此 D 無效。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/UsingAlarmActions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Endpoints.Reader.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_MySQL.Replication.ReadReplicas.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/database-caching-strategies-using-redis/types-of-database-caching.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/target-group-health-checks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/welcome-health-checks.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・複選"},{"id":445,"question_en":"A company has an on-premises data center and is using Kubernetes to develop a new solution on AWS. The company uses Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) clusters for its development and test environments. The EKS control plane and data plane for production workloads must reside on premises. The company needs an AWS managed solution for Kubernetes management. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司擁有本地資料中心，並正在使用 Kubernetes 在 AWS 上開發一項新的解決方案。該公司在其開發與測試環境中使用 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 叢集。生產工作負載的 EKS 控制平面與資料平面必須位於本地端。該公司需要一套 AWS 受管的 Kubernetes 管理解決方案。哪種解決方案能以最少的營運開銷滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Install an AWS Outposts server in the on-premises data center. Deploy Amazon EKS by using a local cluster configuration on the Outposts server for the production workloads.","B":"Install Amazon EKS Anywhere on the company's hardware in the on-premises data center. Deploy the production workloads on an EKS Anywhere cluster.","C":"Install an AWS Outposts server in the on-premises data center. Deploy Amazon EKS by using an extended cluster configuration on the Outposts server for the production workloads.","D":"Install an AWS Outposts server in the on-premises data center. Install Amazon EKS Anywhere on the Outposts server. Deploy the production workloads on an EKS Anywhere cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"在本地資料中心安裝 AWS Outposts 伺服器。針對生產工作負載，在 Outposts 伺服器上使用本地叢集設定來部署 Amazon EKS。","B":"在本地資料中心的公司硬體上安裝 Amazon EKS Anywhere。將生產工作負載部署到 EKS Anywhere 叢集上。","C":"在本地資料中心安裝 AWS Outposts 伺服器。針對生產工作負載，在 Outposts 伺服器上使用延伸叢集設定來部署 Amazon EKS。","D":"在本地資料中心安裝 AWS Outposts 伺服器。在該 Outposts 伺服器上安裝 Amazon EKS Anywhere。將生產工作負載部署到 EKS Anywhere 叢集上。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":75,"B":17},"tags":["Compute","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirements are: (1) the EKS control plane AND data plane for production must reside on premises, and (2) the company needs an AWS-managed solution for Kubernetes management with the LEAST operational overhead. Amazon EKS local clusters on AWS Outposts run the ENTIRE Kubernetes cluster (both control plane and data plane) on the Outposts in the customer's data center, while AWS still manages the EKS control plane lifecycle. Per the AWS EKS deployment-options doc, for EKS on Outposts the control plane location can be 'AWS Regions or AWS Outposts' (the local-cluster option places it on premises) and control plane management is AWS-managed. EKS Anywhere (options B and D) is explicitly described by AWS as a CUSTOMER-MANAGED product where customers are responsible for cluster lifecycle operations and maintenance, so it is not an AWS-managed solution and carries higher operational overhead. The Outposts EXTENDED cluster (option C) keeps the control plane in the AWS Region with only worker nodes on Outposts, which violates the requirement that the control plane reside on premises. Therefore A (local cluster on Outposts) is the only option that keeps both control plane and data plane on premises while remaining AWS-managed with the least overhead.","explanation_zh":"需求為：(1) 生產環境的 EKS control plane 與 data plane 都必須位於地端；(2) 公司需要 AWS 託管 (AWS-managed) 的 Kubernetes 管理方案，且營運負擔最低。Amazon EKS local clusters on AWS Outposts 會把整個 Kubernetes cluster（control plane 與 data plane）都跑在客戶資料中心的 Outposts 上，同時 AWS 仍負責 EKS control plane 的生命週期管理。根據 AWS EKS 部署選項文件，EKS on Outposts 的 control plane 位置可為「AWS Regions 或 AWS Outposts」（local cluster 選項即放在地端），且 control plane management 為 AWS-managed。EKS Anywhere（選項 B、D）被 AWS 明確定義為 customer-managed 產品，客戶須自行負責 cluster 生命週期作業與維運，並非 AWS 託管方案且營運負擔較高。Outposts 的 extended cluster（選項 C）則把 control plane 留在 AWS Region，只有 worker node 在 Outposts，違反 control plane 必須位於地端的要求。因此只有 A（Outposts 上的 local cluster）能同時把 control plane 與 data plane 留在地端，且維持 AWS 託管、營運負擔最低。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"EKS Anywhere is explicitly a CUSTOMER-managed product; AWS docs state customers are responsible for cluster lifecycle operations and maintenance. It does not meet 'AWS managed solution' and adds operational overhead.","why_zh":"EKS Anywhere 被明確定義為 customer-managed 產品；AWS 文件指出客戶須自行負責 cluster 生命週期與維運，不符合「AWS 託管方案」且增加營運負擔。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An Outposts extended cluster keeps the EKS control plane in the AWS Region (only worker nodes run on Outposts), which violates the requirement that the production control plane reside on premises.","why_zh":"Outposts extended cluster 的 EKS control plane 仍留在 AWS Region（只有 worker node 在 Outposts），違反生產 control plane 必須位於地端的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Combines two wrong ideas: EKS Anywhere is customer-managed (not AWS-managed), and you do not install EKS Anywhere 'on an Outposts'; this adds unnecessary overhead and does not satisfy the AWS-managed requirement.","why_zh":"結合兩個錯誤：EKS Anywhere 為 customer-managed（非 AWS 託管），且不會把 EKS Anywhere 安裝『在 Outposts 上』；此做法增加不必要的負擔且不符合 AWS 託管的要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/eks-deployment-options.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/eks-outposts-local-cluster-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/eks-outposts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/aws-outposts-high-availability-design/eks-local-cluster.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":446,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage its development environment. Each development team at the company has its own AWS account. Each account has a single VPC and CIDR blocks that do not overlap. The company has an Amazon Aurora DB cluster in a shared services account. All the development teams need to work with live data from the DB cluster. Which solution will provide the required connectivity to the DB cluster with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 來管理其開發環境。公司的每個開發團隊都擁有自己的 AWS 帳戶。每個帳戶皆有一個 VPC，且各 VPC 的 CIDR 區塊互不重疊。該公司在一個共享服務帳戶中擁有一個 Amazon Aurora 資料庫叢集。所有開發團隊都需要使用該資料庫叢集中的即時資料。哪種解決方案能以最少的營運開銷提供所需的資料庫叢集連線能力？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) resource share for the DB cluster. Share the DB cluster with all the development accounts.","B":"Create a transit gateway in the shared services account. Create an AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) resource share for the transit gateway. Share the transit gateway with all the development accounts. Instruct the developers to accept the resource share. Configure networking.","C":"Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB) that points to the IP address of the DB cluster. Create an AWS PrivateLink endpoint service that uses the ALB. Add permissions to allow each development account to connect to the endpoint service.","D":"Create an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection in the shared services account. Configure networking. Use AWS Marketplace VPN software in each development account to connect to the Site-to-Site VPN connection."},"options_zh":{"A":"為該資料庫叢集建立一個 AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) 資源共用。將該資料庫叢集與所有開發帳戶共用。","B":"在共享服務帳戶中建立一個 transit gateway。為該 transit gateway 建立一個 AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) 資源共用。將該 transit gateway 與所有開發帳戶共用。指示開發人員接受該資源共用。設定網路連線。","C":"建立一個指向該資料庫叢集 IP 位址的 Application Load Balancer (ALB)。建立一個使用該 ALB 的 AWS PrivateLink 端點服務。新增權限，允許每個開發帳戶連接到該端點服務。","D":"在共享服務帳戶中建立一個 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 連線。設定網路連線。在每個開發帳戶中使用 AWS Marketplace 的 VPN 軟體連接到該 Site-to-Site VPN 連線。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":79,"A":19},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is network connectivity so all dev accounts can work with LIVE data in the running Aurora DB cluster, with the least operational overhead. Option B does exactly that: a transit gateway created in the shared services account and shared to all member accounts via AWS RAM acts as a regional network hub. Each VPC attaches to it, and because the VPC CIDRs do not overlap, routing works cleanly, giving every dev VPC private IP connectivity to the Aurora endpoints. This is the standard, low-overhead AWS multi-account hub-and-spoke pattern. Option A is the trap: AWS RAM sharing of an Aurora DB cluster (rds:Cluster) is ONLY for cross-account cloning, not for live network access. The official RAM 'Shareable resources' page states the use case is so 'multiple AWS accounts clone a shared, centrally managed DB cluster,' linking to the cross-account cloning guide. A clone is a separate, independent copy of the data, so it does not satisfy the 'live data' requirement.","explanation_zh":"需求是讓所有開發帳戶能透過網路連線存取共享服務帳戶中正在執行的 Aurora DB cluster 的「即時資料」(live data),且運維負擔最低。選項 B 正是如此:在共享服務帳戶建立 transit gateway,透過 AWS RAM 分享給組織內所有成員帳戶,作為區域層級的網路樞紐。各 VPC 將其附加 (attach) 上去,由於各 VPC 的 CIDR 不重疊,路由可正常運作,讓每個開發 VPC 透過私有 IP 連線至 Aurora 端點。這是 AWS 多帳戶 hub-and-spoke 的標準低負擔做法。選項 A 是陷阱:AWS RAM 對 Aurora DB cluster (rds:Cluster) 的分享「僅用於跨帳戶 cloning」,而非提供即時的網路存取。官方 RAM 'Shareable resources' 頁面明載其用途為讓「多個 AWS 帳戶 clone 一個共享、集中管理的 DB cluster」,並連結至跨帳戶 cloning 指南。clone 是資料的獨立副本,無法滿足「即時資料」需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"RAM sharing of an Aurora DB cluster (rds:Cluster) only enables cross-account CLONING, per the official RAM shareable resources page. Recipients create independent clone copies; they do not get network connectivity to query the live, running cluster, so the 'work with live data' requirement is not met.","why_zh":"依官方 RAM shareable resources 頁面,對 Aurora DB cluster (rds:Cluster) 的 RAM 分享僅啟用跨帳戶 CLONING。接收方建立的是獨立 clone 副本,並未取得連線至執行中 cluster 查詢即時資料的網路通道,因此不符合『存取即時資料』的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An ALB cannot front a stateful relational database connection (it does TCP/HTTP load balancing, not native MySQL/PostgreSQL protocol session proxying to a DB cluster), and building an ALB plus a PrivateLink endpoint service per consumer is far more operational overhead than a shared transit gateway. RDS Proxy / direct endpoints, not ALB+PrivateLink, would be the path, and even then this is over-engineered.","why_zh":"ALB 無法承載有狀態的關聯式資料庫連線(它做的是 TCP/HTTP 負載平衡,而非對 DB cluster 的原生 MySQL/PostgreSQL 通訊協定工作階段代理),且建立 ALB 加 PrivateLink endpoint service 的運維負擔遠高於共享 transit gateway。即使要私有連線,應走 RDS Proxy 或直接端點,而非 ALB+PrivateLink,且此方案過度設計。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Site-to-Site VPN plus third-party Marketplace VPN software in every dev account is intended for on-premises/hybrid connectivity, not for intra-AWS account-to-account connectivity within one Region. It adds the highest operational overhead (managing software appliances, tunnels, licensing per account) and is the wrong tool for VPC-to-VPC connectivity.","why_zh":"Site-to-Site VPN 加上每個開發帳戶安裝第三方 Marketplace VPN 軟體,是為地端/混合雲連線設計,而非用於單一區域內 AWS 帳戶間的連線。它帶來最高的運維負擔(需管理軟體設備、通道、各帳戶授權),對 VPC 對 VPC 連線而言是錯誤的工具。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ram/latest/userguide/shareable.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Managing.Clone.Cross-Account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/what-is-transit-gateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/share-accept-tgw.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/tgw/tgw-vpc-attachments.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":447,"question_en":"A company used AWS CloudFormation to create all new infrastructure in its AWS member accounts. The resources rarely change and are properly sized for the expected load. The monthly AWS bill is consistent. Occasionally, a developer creates a new resource for testing and forgets to remove the resource when the test is complete. Most of these tests last a few days before the resources are no longer needed. The company wants to automate the process of finding unused resources. A solutions architect needs to design a solution that determines whether the cost in the AWS bill is increasing. The solution must help identify resources that cause an increase in cost and must automatically notify the company's operations team. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS CloudFormation 在其 AWS 成員帳戶中建立所有新的基礎設施。這些資源很少變更，且其大小已針對預期的負載進行妥善調整。每月的 AWS 帳單金額相當穩定。偶爾會有開發人員建立新資源用於測試，卻在測試完成後忘記移除該資源。這些測試大多只會持續幾天，之後這些資源就不再需要。該公司希望自動化尋找未使用資源的流程。解決方案架構師需要設計一套解決方案，判斷 AWS 帳單中的費用是否正在增加。該解決方案必須能協助識別造成費用增加的資源，並自動通知公司的營運團隊。哪種解決方案能滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Turn on billing alerts. Use AWS Cost Explorer to determine the costs for the past month. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for total estimated charges. Specify a cost threshold that is higher than the costs that Cost Explorer determined. Add a notification to alert the operations team if the alarm threshold is breached.","B":"Turn on billing alerts. Use AWS Cost Explorer to determine the average monthly costs for the past 3 months. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for total estimated charges. Specify a cost threshold that is higher than the costs that Cost Explorer determined. Add a notification to alert the operations team if the alarm threshold is breached.","C":"Use AWS Cost Anomaly Detection to create a cost monitor that has a monitor type of Linked account. Create a subscription to send daily AWS cost summaries to the operations team. Specify a threshold for cost variance.","D":"Use AWS Cost Anomaly Detection to create a cost monitor that has a monitor type of AWS services. Create a subscription to send daily AWS cost summaries to the operations team. Specify a threshold for cost variance."},"options_zh":{"A":"啟用帳單警示。使用 AWS Cost Explorer 判斷上個月的費用。為總預估費用建立一個 Amazon CloudWatch 警示。指定一個高於 Cost Explorer 所判斷費用的成本閾值。新增通知，在警示閾值被突破時提醒營運團隊。","B":"啟用帳單警示。使用 AWS Cost Explorer 判斷過去 3 個月的平均月費用。為總預估費用建立一個 Amazon CloudWatch 警示。指定一個高於 Cost Explorer 所判斷費用的成本閾值。新增通知，在警示閾值被突破時提醒營運團隊。","C":"使用 AWS Cost Anomaly Detection 建立一個監控器類型為 Linked account（連結帳戶）的成本監控器。建立一個訂閱，每天將 AWS 費用摘要傳送給營運團隊。指定費用變動的閾值。","D":"使用 AWS Cost Anomaly Detection 建立一個監控器類型為 AWS services（AWS 服務）的成本監控器。建立一個訂閱，每天將 AWS 費用摘要傳送給營運團隊。指定費用變動的閾值。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":76,"C":24},"tags":["Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The requirements are: detect whether cost is increasing, identify the resources causing the increase, and automatically notify the operations team. AWS Cost Anomaly Detection uses ML to detect anomalous spend and provides root cause analysis ranked by dollar impact across AWS service, AWS account, Region, and usage type, then notifies via alert subscriptions (daily summaries to email/SNS) -- so it satisfies all three requirements. Options A and B use a CloudWatch billing alarm on EstimatedCharges with a static threshold set above prior costs; this only fires on total spend and never identifies which resource caused the increase, and a few-days test resource that adds modest cost will rarely breach a threshold set deliberately above normal spend, so both fail the 'identify resources' requirement. Between C and D, the scenario is explicitly built around multiple AWS member accounts where developers leave forgotten test resources; per the AWS Monitor types documentation, the Linked account monitor (C) automatically tracks spending patterns across all member accounts independently and automatically includes new accounts, so it isolates the specific account whose spend spiked (with root-cause drill-down to the service/usage type), most directly identifying the offending resource. An AWS services monitor (D) evaluates each service in aggregate, where a single small test resource in one of many member accounts is more easily diluted by the consistent combined baseline. Because the architecture centers on per-member-account isolation, the Linked account monitor type is the better-aligned answer.","explanation_zh":"需求為：偵測成本是否上升、找出造成成本上升的資源、並自動通知營運團隊。AWS Cost Anomaly Detection 使用機器學習偵測異常支出，並提供依金額影響排序的根本原因分析（橫跨 AWS service、AWS account、Region、usage type 四個維度），再透過 alert subscription（每日彙總寄送至 email/SNS）通知，因此三項需求皆能滿足。選項 A 與 B 採用 CloudWatch 對 EstimatedCharges 設定的靜態門檻警示（門檻設在過往成本之上）；這僅針對總支出觸發，完全無法指出是哪個資源造成上升，而且僅持續數天的測試資源所增加的成本不大，幾乎不會突破刻意設在正常支出之上的門檻，因此兩者皆無法滿足『找出資源』的要求。在 C 與 D 之間，情境明確圍繞多個 AWS member account、開發者遺留測試資源；依 AWS Monitor types 文件，Linked account 監視器（C）會自動且獨立地追蹤所有 member account 的支出模式，並自動納入新帳戶，因此能鎖定支出異常飆升的特定帳戶（再透過根本原因下鑽到 service/usage type），最直接地找出問題資源。AWS services 監視器（D）以彙總方式評估各服務，眾多 member account 合併後的穩定基線容易稀釋單一小型測試資源的影響。由於架構以各 member account 的隔離為核心，Linked account 監視器類型才是更貼合的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A CloudWatch billing alarm on EstimatedCharges with a static threshold above last month's cost only signals that total spend crossed a number; it never identifies which resource caused the increase, and a few-days test resource adds too little to breach a threshold set above normal spend. The threshold also needs manual updating as the bill changes.","why_zh":"對 EstimatedCharges 設定高於上月成本的靜態門檻警示，只能顯示總支出是否越過某數值，完全無法指出是哪個資源造成上升；僅數天的測試資源增加太少，無法突破設在正常支出之上的門檻，且門檻還需隨帳單變化手動更新。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same fundamental flaw as A -- a CloudWatch total-estimated-charges alarm with a static threshold (here based on a 3-month average) cannot identify the resource causing the increase and will likely miss a modest, short-lived test resource. Averaging over 3 months does not fix the inability to pinpoint root cause.","why_zh":"與 A 同樣的根本缺陷：對總估計費用設定靜態門檻（此處以三個月平均為基礎）的 CloudWatch 警示無法找出造成上升的資源，且很可能漏掉成本不大、存續短暫的測試資源。以三個月平均計算並無助於定位根本原因。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An AWS services monitor evaluates each AWS service in aggregate. The scenario centers on multiple member accounts each potentially holding a forgotten test resource; a single small test resource in one of many accounts is more easily diluted within the consistent combined per-service baseline, and this type does not isolate the offending account. The Linked account monitor is the architecturally aligned choice for per-member-account anomaly isolation.","why_zh":"AWS services 監視器以彙總方式評估各 AWS 服務。情境圍繞多個 member account，每個都可能遺留測試資源；單一小型測試資源在眾多帳戶的穩定合併服務基線中更容易被稀釋，且此類型無法鎖定出問題的帳戶。Linked account 監視器才是針對各 member account 異常隔離的架構契合選擇。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/manage-ad.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/getting-started-ad.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/monitor_estimated_charges_with_cloudwatch.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":448,"question_en":"A company is deploying a new web-based application and needs a storage solution for the Linux application servers. The company wants to create a single location for updates to application data for all instances. The active dataset will be up to 100 GB in size. A solutions architect has determined that peak operations will occur for 3 hours daily and will require a total of 225 MiBps of read throughput. The solutions architect must design a Multi-AZ solution that makes a copy of the data available in another AWS Region for disaster recovery (DR). The DR copy has an RPO of less than 1 hour. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在部署一個新的 Web 應用程式，需要為其 Linux 應用程式伺服器提供儲存解決方案。該公司希望建立一個單一位置，供所有執行個體更新應用程式資料。活動資料集的大小最高可達 100 GB。解決方案架構師已判定，尖峰作業將於每天發生 3 小時，並需要總計 225 MiBps 的讀取吞吐量。解決方案架構師必須設計一套 Multi-AZ 解決方案，將資料副本提供給另一個 AWS 區域，以進行災難復原 (DR)。該 DR 副本的 RPO 須小於 1 小時。哪種解決方案能滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy a new Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) Multi-AZ file system. Configure the file system for 75 MiBps of provisioned throughput. Implement replication to a file system in the DR Region.","B":"Deploy a new Amazon FSx for Lustre file system. Configure Bursting Throughput mode for the file system. Use AWS Backup to back up the file system to the DR Region.","C":"Deploy a General Purpose SSD (gp3) Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume with 225 MiBps of throughput. Enable Multi- Attach for the EBS volume. Use AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery to replicate the EBS volume to the DR Region.","D":"Deploy an Amazon FSx for OpenZFS file system in both the production Region and the DR Region. Create an AWS DataSync scheduled task to replicate the data from the production file system to the DR file system every 10 minutes."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署一個新的 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) Multi-AZ 檔案系統。將該檔案系統設定為 75 MiBps 的佈建吞吐量。實作到 DR 區域中檔案系統的複寫。","B":"部署一個新的 Amazon FSx for Lustre 檔案系統。將該檔案系統設定為 Bursting Throughput（爆發吞吐量）模式。使用 AWS Backup 將該檔案系統備份到 DR 區域。","C":"部署一個具有 225 MiBps 吞吐量的通用型 SSD (gp3) Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 磁碟區。為該 EBS 磁碟區啟用 Multi-Attach。使用 AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery 將該 EBS 磁碟區複寫到 DR 區域。","D":"在生產區域與 DR 區域中皆部署 Amazon FSx for OpenZFS 檔案系統。建立一個 AWS DataSync 排程任務，每 10 分鐘將資料從生產檔案系統複寫到 DR 檔案系統。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":64,"D":36},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The workload needs a single shared location for updates accessible by all Linux application servers, which calls for a managed NFS file system. Amazon EFS is natively Multi-AZ and provides one shared namespace for all instances. The decisive detail is throughput: EFS meters read requests at one-third the rate of other operations, so the Maximum Read Throughput equals three times the provisioned throughput. With 75 MiBps of provisioned throughput, EFS delivers 3 x 75 = 225 MiBps of read throughput, exactly matching the peak requirement. EFS cross-Region replication maintains a 15-minute RPO, which is well under the required RPO of less than 1 hour. Therefore Option A satisfies every requirement (shared storage, Multi-AZ, 225 MiBps read, and DR RPO < 1 hour).","explanation_zh":"此工作負載需要一個可供所有 Linux 應用伺服器存取的單一共用更新位置，因此需要受管的 NFS 檔案系統。Amazon EFS 原生即為 Multi-AZ，並為所有執行個體提供單一共用命名空間。決定性細節在於輸送量：EFS 對讀取請求的計量速率為其他操作的三分之一，因此 Maximum Read Throughput 等於 provisioned throughput 的三倍。設定 75 MiBps 的 provisioned throughput 時，EFS 可提供 3 x 75 = 225 MiBps 的讀取輸送量，恰好符合尖峰需求。EFS 跨區域 replication 維持 15 分鐘的 RPO，遠低於要求的 RPO 小於 1 小時。因此選項 A 滿足所有需求（共用儲存、Multi-AZ、225 MiBps 讀取，以及 DR RPO < 1 小時）。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"FSx for Lustre is an HPC/scratch-oriented file system, and AWS Backup is point-in-time scheduled backup, not continuous replication; its effective RPO depends on backup frequency and does not guarantee less than 1 hour. Bursting Throughput on a 100 GB file system yields baseline throughput proportional to capacity and cannot reliably sustain 225 MiBps for 3 hours.","why_zh":"FSx for Lustre 是偏向 HPC/scratch 的檔案系統，而 AWS Backup 是排程式時間點備份，並非持續性 replication；其實際 RPO 取決於備份頻率，無法保證小於 1 小時。對 100 GB 檔案系統使用 Bursting Throughput 的基準輸送量與容量成正比，無法可靠地持續提供 225 MiBps 達 3 小時。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EBS Multi-Attach only attaches volumes to instances in the same Availability Zone (not Multi-AZ), is supported only on io1/io2 (not gp3), and standard Linux file systems like XFS/EXT4 cannot be shared concurrently without a clustered file system. It is block storage, not a turnkey single shared location, and fails the Multi-AZ requirement.","why_zh":"EBS Multi-Attach 僅能將磁碟區掛載至同一個 Availability Zone 的執行個體（並非 Multi-AZ），且僅支援 io1/io2（不支援 gp3），而 XFS/EXT4 等標準 Linux 檔案系統若無叢集式檔案系統便無法同時共用。它屬於區塊儲存，並非開箱即用的單一共用位置，且不符合 Multi-AZ 需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"FSx for OpenZFS plus a custom DataSync task every 10 minutes can technically meet the RPO, but it adds significant operational overhead (managing two file systems and a scheduled replication task) and is not the native, recommended shared Linux storage path. EFS provides built-in Multi-AZ design and managed cross-Region replication with a 15-minute RPO with far less complexity, making A the better fit.","why_zh":"FSx for OpenZFS 搭配每 10 分鐘的自訂 DataSync 任務雖然技術上可達到 RPO，但會帶來顯著的維運負擔（需管理兩個檔案系統及排程 replication 任務），且不是原生、建議的共用 Linux 儲存方案。EFS 內建 Multi-AZ 設計與受管跨區域 replication（15 分鐘 RPO），複雜度低得多，因此 A 是更佳選擇。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/managing-throughput.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/efs-replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ebs/latest/userguide/ebs-volumes-multi.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/LustreGuide/what-is.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":449,"question_en":"A company needs to gather data from an experiment in a remote location that does not have internet connectivity. During the experiment, sensors that are connected to a local network will generate 6 TB of data in a proprietary format over the course of 1 week. The sensors can be configured to upload their data files to an FTP server periodically, but the sensors do not have their own FTP server. The sensors also do not support other protocols. The company needs to collect the data centrally and move the data to object storage in the AWS Cloud as soon as possible after the experiment. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要收集來自一個沒有網際網路連線的偏遠地點所進行實驗的資料。實驗期間，連接到本地網路的感測器將在 1 週內以專有格式產生 6 TB 的資料。這些感測器可設定為定期將其資料檔案上傳到 FTP 伺服器，但感測器本身並沒有內建 FTP 伺服器，也不支援其他通訊協定。該公司需要集中收集資料，並在實驗結束後盡快將資料移轉到 AWS Cloud 中的物件儲存體。哪種解決方案能滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Order an AWS Snowball Edge Compute Optimized device. Connect the device to the local network. Configure AWS DataSync with a target bucket name, and unload the data over NFS to the device. After the experiment, return the device to AWS so that the data can be loaded into Amazon S3.","B":"Order an AWS Snowcone device, including an Amazon Linux 2 AMI. Connect the device to the local network. Launch an Amazon EC2 instance on the device. Create a shell script that periodically downloads data from each sensor. After the experiment, return the device to AWS so that the data can be loaded as an Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume.","C":"Order an AWS Snowcone device, including an Amazon Linux 2 AMI. Connect the device to the local network. Launch an Amazon EC2 instance on the device. Install and configure an FTP server on the EC2 instance. Configure the sensors to upload data to the EC2 instance. After the experiment, return the device to AWS so that the data can be loaded into Amazon S3.","D":"Order an AWS Snowcone device. Connect the device to the local network. Configure the device to use Amazon FSx. Configure the sensors to upload data to the device. Configure AWS DataSync on the device to synchronize the uploaded data with an Amazon S3 bucket. Return the device to AWS so that the data can be loaded as an Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume."},"options_zh":{"A":"訂購一台 AWS Snowball Edge Compute Optimized 裝置。將該裝置連接到本地網路。設定 AWS DataSync 並指定目標儲存桶名稱，透過 NFS 將資料卸載到該裝置上。實驗結束後，將裝置寄回給 AWS，以便將資料載入 Amazon S3。","B":"訂購一台包含 Amazon Linux 2 AMI 的 AWS Snowcone 裝置。將該裝置連接到本地網路。在該裝置上啟動一個 Amazon EC2 執行個體。建立一個 shell 腳本，定期從每個感測器下載資料。實驗結束後，將裝置寄回給 AWS，以便將資料以 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 磁碟區的形式載入。","C":"訂購一台包含 Amazon Linux 2 AMI 的 AWS Snowcone 裝置。將該裝置連接到本地網路。在該裝置上啟動一個 Amazon EC2 執行個體。在該 EC2 執行個體上安裝並設定 FTP 伺服器。設定感測器將資料上傳到該 EC2 執行個體。實驗結束後，將裝置寄回給 AWS，以便將資料載入 Amazon S3。","D":"訂購一台 AWS Snowcone 裝置。將該裝置連接到本地網路。設定該裝置使用 Amazon FSx。設定感測器將資料上傳到該裝置。在該裝置上設定 AWS DataSync，將已上傳的資料同步到一個 Amazon S3 儲存桶。將裝置寄回給 AWS，以便將資料以 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 磁碟區的形式載入。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":450,"question_en":"A company that has multiple business units is using AWS Organizations with all features enabled. The company has implemented an account structure in which each business unit has its own AWS account. Administrators in each AWS account need to view detailed cost and utilization data for their account by using Amazon Athena. Each business unit can have access to only its own cost and utilization data. The IAM policies that govern the ability to set up AWS Cost and Usage Reports are in place. A central Cost and Usage Report that contains all data for the organization is already available in an Amazon S3 bucket. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational complexity?","question_zh":"一家擁有多個業務部門的公司正在使用已啟用所有功能的 AWS Organizations。該公司已實作一種帳戶結構，讓每個業務部門都擁有自己的 AWS 帳戶。每個 AWS 帳戶中的管理員都需要使用 Amazon Athena 查看其帳戶的詳細費用與使用率資料。每個業務部門只能存取自己的費用與使用率資料。用於管理 AWS Cost and Usage Report 設定權限的 IAM 政策已經到位。一份包含整個組織所有資料的中央 Cost and Usage Report 已存放在一個 Amazon S3 儲存桶中。哪種解決方案能以最低的營運複雜度滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"In the organization's management account, use AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) to share the Cost and Usage Report data with each member account.","B":"In the organization's management account, configure an S3 event to invoke an AWS Lambda function each time a new file arrives in the S3 bucket that contains the central Cost and Usage Report. Configure the Lambda function to extract each member account’s data and to place the data in Amazon S3 under a separate prefix. Modify the S3 bucket policy to allow each member account to access its own prefix.","C":"In each member account, access AWS Cost Explorer. Create a new report that contains relevant cost information for the account. Save the report in Cost Explorer. Provide instructions that the account administrators can use to access the saved report.","D":"In each member account, create a new S3 bucket to store Cost and Usage Report data. Set up a Cost and Usage Report to deliver the data to the new S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"在組織的管理帳戶中，使用 AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) 將 Cost and Usage Report 的資料與每個成員帳戶共用。","B":"在組織的管理帳戶中，設定一個 S3 事件，每當有新檔案送達存放中央 Cost and Usage Report 的 S3 儲存桶時，即呼叫一個 AWS Lambda 函數。設定該 Lambda 函數提取每個成員帳戶的資料，並將資料存放到 Amazon S3 中各自獨立的前綴下。修改 S3 儲存桶政策，允許每個成員帳戶存取其自己的前綴。","C":"在每個成員帳戶中，存取 AWS Cost Explorer。建立一份包含該帳戶相關費用資訊的新報表。將該報表儲存在 Cost Explorer 中。提供操作說明，讓帳戶管理員能夠存取已儲存的報表。","D":"在每個成員帳戶中，建立一個新的 S3 儲存桶來存放 Cost and Usage Report 資料。設定一份 Cost and Usage Report，將資料傳送到該新的 S3 儲存桶。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":57,"D":29},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The requirement is that each member account admin views detailed cost/utilization data for ONLY their own account via Amazon Athena, with the LEAST operational complexity, and IAM permissions to set up CUR are already in place. Per AWS docs, in AWS Organizations a member account can create a Cost and Usage Report for 'only the member account's cost and usage data,' and the account that creates the CUR must own the destination S3 bucket. The Athena CUR guide further recommends creating a new S3 bucket and a new CUR (Parquet) specifically for Athena. Option D does exactly this in each member account: it natively produces a report scoped to only that account's data, lands it in a bucket that account owns, and the account can query it directly with Athena. Data isolation is inherent (the report only contains that account's data) and there is no custom code to build or maintain. Option B works technically but requires building and maintaining a Lambda pipeline that parses the central CUR, splits per-account data, and manages S3 prefixes/bucket policies, which is far higher operational complexity. So neither the dump answer (A) nor the community answer (B) is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求是讓每個成員帳戶的管理員透過 Amazon Athena 只檢視自己帳戶的詳細成本與使用量資料，且要求「最少的營運複雜度」，並且設定 CUR 的 IAM 權限已經就緒。根據 AWS 文件，在 AWS Organizations 中，成員帳戶可以建立只包含「該成員帳戶自身成本與使用量資料」的 Cost and Usage Report，且建立 CUR 的帳戶必須擁有目的地 S3 儲存貯體。Athena CUR 指南更建議專門為 Athena 建立新的 S3 儲存貯體與新的 CUR（Parquet 格式）。選項 D 正是在每個成員帳戶中執行此操作：原生產生只含該帳戶資料的報告，存放於該帳戶自己擁有的儲存貯體，並可直接用 Athena 查詢。資料隔離是天然的（報告只含該帳戶資料），且無需建置或維護任何自訂程式碼。選項 B 技術上可行，但需建置並維護一個 Lambda 管線來解析中央 CUR、拆分各帳戶資料並管理 S3 前綴與儲存貯體政策，營運複雜度高得多。因此題庫答案（A）與社群答案（B）都不正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM) shares specific resource types such as subnets, Transit Gateways, Route 53 Resolver rules, and License Manager configurations. It cannot share Cost and Usage Report data or S3 objects, so this approach is technically invalid and cannot meet the requirement.","why_zh":"AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM) 用於分享特定資源類型（如子網路、Transit Gateway、Route 53 Resolver 規則、License Manager 設定）。它無法分享 Cost and Usage Report 資料或 S3 物件，因此此做法技術上不可行，無法滿足需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"It works but requires building, deploying, and maintaining a custom Lambda function to parse the central CUR (handling monthly column/schema changes and Parquet partitioning), split per-account data into prefixes, and manage bucket policies. That is substantially more operational complexity than the native member-account CUR in option D, so it fails the LEAST operational complexity qualifier.","why_zh":"此方案可行，但需建置、部署並維護自訂 Lambda 函式來解析中央 CUR（須處理每月欄位/結構變更與 Parquet 分割）、將各帳戶資料拆分至前綴並管理儲存貯體政策。相較於選項 D 使用原生的成員帳戶 CUR，營運複雜度高得多，因此不符合「最少營運複雜度」的限定條件。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The requirement explicitly states admins must use Amazon Athena. Cost Explorer is a separate visualization tool, not Athena-queryable line-item data, and member-account Cost Explorer access is often disabled by default in an organization. This does not satisfy the 'using Amazon Athena' requirement.","why_zh":"需求明確要求管理員須使用 Amazon Athena。Cost Explorer 是另一個視覺化工具，並非可由 Athena 查詢的明細資料，且組織中成員帳戶的 Cost Explorer 存取通常預設為停用。此方案不符合「使用 Amazon Athena」的要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cur/latest/userguide/cur-consolidated-billing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cur/latest/userguide/cur-query-athena.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cur/latest/userguide/cur-ate-manual.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cur/latest/userguide/what-is-cur.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":451,"question_en":"A company is designing an AWS environment for a manufacturing application. The application has been successful with customers, and the application's user base has increased. The company has connected the AWS environment to the company's on-premises data center through a 1 Gbps AWS Direct Connect connection. The company has configured BGP for the connection. The company must update the existing network connectivity solution to ensure that the solution is highly available, fault tolerant, and secure. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司正在為一款製造業應用程式設計 AWS 環境。該應用程式深受客戶青睞，其使用者群也持續增加。該公司已透過一條 1 Gbps 的 AWS Direct Connect 連線，將 AWS 環境與公司的本地資料中心連接起來，並已為該連線設定 BGP。該公司必須更新現有的網路連線解決方案，以確保該解決方案具備高可用性、容錯能力並且安全。哪種解決方案能以最具成本效益的方式滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Add a dynamic private IP AWS Site-to-Site VPN as a secondary path to secure data in transit and provide resilience for the Direct Connect connection. Configure MACsec to encrypt tra®c inside the Direct Connect connection.","B":"Provision another Direct Connect connection between the company's on-premises data center and AWS to increase the transfer speed and provide resilience. Configure MACsec to encrypt tra®c inside the Direct Connect connection.","C":"Configure multiple private VIFs. Load balance data across the VIFs between the on-premises data center and AWS to provide resilience.","D":"Add a static AWS Site-to-Site VPN as a secondary path to secure data in transit and to provide resilience for the Direct Connect connection."},"options_zh":{"A":"新增一個使用動態私有 IP 的 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 作為次要路徑，以保護傳輸中的資料並為 Direct Connect 連線提供復原能力。設定 MACsec 以加密 Direct Connect 連線內的流量。","B":"在公司的本地資料中心與 AWS 之間佈建另一條 Direct Connect 連線，以提高傳輸速度並提供復原能力。設定 MACsec 以加密 Direct Connect 連線內的流量。","C":"設定多個私有虛擬介面 (VIF)。在本地資料中心與 AWS 之間跨這些 VIF 對資料進行負載平衡，以提供復原能力。","D":"新增一個靜態的 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 作為次要路徑，以保護傳輸中的資料，並為 Direct Connect 連線提供復原能力。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":76,"A":24},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Security/IAM","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":452,"question_en":"A company needs to modernize an application and migrate the application to AWS. The application stores user profile data as text in a single table in an on-premises MySQL database. After the modernization, users will use the application to upload video files that are up to 4 GB in size. Other users must be able to download the video files from the application. The company needs a video storage solution that provides rapid scaling. The solution must not affect application performance. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要對某個應用程式進行現代化改造，並將其遷移到 AWS。該應用程式將使用者個人資料以文字形式儲存在本地 MySQL 資料庫的單一表格中。現代化改造完成後，使用者將透過該應用程式上傳最大 4 GB 的影片檔案，其他使用者則必須能夠從該應用程式下載這些影片檔案。該公司需要一套能夠快速擴充的影片儲存解決方案，且該解決方案不得影響應用程式效能。哪種解決方案能滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate the database to Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL by using AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS). Store the videos as base64- encoded strings in a TEXT column in the database.","B":"Migrate the database to Amazon DynamoDB by using AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) with the AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT). Store the videos as objects in Amazon S3. Store the S3 key in the corresponding DynamoDB item.","C":"Migrate the database to Amazon Keyspaces (for Apache Cassandra) by using AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) with the AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT). Store the videos as objects in Amazon S3. Store the S3 object identifier in the corresponding Amazon Keyspaces entry.","D":"Migrate the database to Amazon DynamoDB by using AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) with the AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT). Store the videos as base64-encoded strings in the corresponding DynamoDB item."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 將資料庫遷移到 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL。將影片以 base64 編碼字串的形式儲存在資料庫的 TEXT 資料欄中。","B":"搭配使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 與 AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT)，將資料庫遷移到 Amazon DynamoDB。將影片以物件形式儲存在 Amazon S3 中，並將 S3 金鑰儲存在對應的 DynamoDB 項目中。","C":"搭配使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 與 AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT)，將資料庫遷移到 Amazon Keyspaces (for Apache Cassandra)。將影片以物件形式儲存在 Amazon S3 中，並將 S3 物件識別碼儲存在對應的 Amazon Keyspaces 項目中。","D":"搭配使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 與 AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT)，將資料庫遷移到 Amazon DynamoDB。將影片以 base64 編碼字串的形式儲存在對應的 DynamoDB 項目中。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":453,"question_en":"A company stores and manages documents in an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. The file system is encrypted with an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key. The file system is mounted to an Amazon EC2 instance that runs proprietary software. The company has enabled automatic backups for the file system. The automatic backups use the AWS Backup default backup plan. A solutions architect must ensure that deleted documents can be recovered within an RPO of 100 minutes. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在一個 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 檔案系統中儲存並管理文件。該檔案系統使用 AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) 金鑰進行加密，並掛載到一個執行專有軟體的 Amazon EC2 執行個體上。該公司已為該檔案系統啟用自動備份，這些自動備份使用 AWS Backup 的預設備份計畫。解決方案架構師必須確保已刪除的文件能在 100 分鐘的 RPO 內復原。哪種解決方案能滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new IAM role. Create a new backup plan. Use the new IAM role to create backups. Update the KMS key policy to allow the new IAM role to use the key. Implement an hourly backup schedule for the file system.","B":"Create a new backup plan. Update the KMS key policy to allow the AWSServiceRoleForBackup IAM role to use the key. Implement a custom cron expression to run a backup of the file system every 30 minutes.","C":"Create a new IAM role. Use the existing backup plan. Update the KMS key policy to allow the new IAM role to use the key. Enable continuous backups for point-in-time recovery.","D":"Use the existing backup plan. Update the KMS key policy to allow the AWSServiceRoleForBackup IAM role to use the key. Enable Cross- Region Replication for the file system."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個新的 IAM 角色。建立一份新的備份計畫。使用該新的 IAM 角色來建立備份。更新 KMS 金鑰政策，允許該新的 IAM 角色使用該金鑰。為該檔案系統實作每小時的備份排程。","B":"建立一份新的備份計畫。更新 KMS 金鑰政策，允許 AWSServiceRoleForBackup IAM 角色使用該金鑰。實作一個自訂的 cron 表達式，每 30 分鐘對該檔案系統執行一次備份。","C":"建立一個新的 IAM 角色。使用現有的備份計畫。更新 KMS 金鑰政策，允許該新的 IAM 角色使用該金鑰。啟用持續備份以支援還原到某個時間點。","D":"使用現有的備份計畫。更新 KMS 金鑰政策，允許 AWSServiceRoleForBackup IAM 角色使用該金鑰。為該檔案系統啟用跨區域複寫。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":81},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is an RPO of 100 minutes for recovering deleted documents from a KMS-encrypted EFS file system. The default AWS Backup plan for EFS performs daily backups (~24h RPO), which is insufficient. A backup must run at least every 100 minutes. Option A schedules hourly backups (60-minute RPO, within the 100-minute target), creates a dedicated IAM role that AWS Backup uses to perform the backups, and updates the KMS key policy so that role can encrypt/decrypt the encrypted file system data. This is all supported and meets the RPO. The decisive technical fact is that AWS Backup snapshot backups can be scheduled 'as frequently as hourly' (per the Backup plan options doc) - hourly is the maximum supported frequency. That eliminates Option B, which proposes a 30-minute schedule that AWS Backup cannot honor. Continuous backups/PITR (Option C) are only supported for Amazon S3, Amazon RDS/Aurora, and SAP HANA on EC2 - not Amazon EFS - so PITR cannot be enabled for an EFS file system. Cross-Region Replication (Option D) mirrors the file system including deletions, providing disaster recovery but not recovery of individually deleted documents.","explanation_zh":"需求是針對以 KMS 加密的 EFS 檔案系統，要在 RPO 100 分鐘內復原被刪除的文件。EFS 的 AWS Backup 預設備份計畫為每日備份（RPO 約 24 小時），不足以滿足需求，備份必須至少每 100 分鐘執行一次。選項 A 設定每小時備份（RPO 60 分鐘，落在 100 分鐘目標內），建立專用的 IAM role 供 AWS Backup 執行備份，並更新 KMS key policy 讓該 role 能對加密的檔案系統資料進行加解密。這些都受支援且滿足 RPO。決定性的技術事實是：依據 Backup plan options 文件，AWS Backup 快照備份最頻繁只能設定為『每小時一次（hourly）』，每小時即為支援的最高頻率。這排除了選項 B，因為它提出每 30 分鐘的排程，AWS Backup 無法支援。連續備份/PITR（選項 C）僅支援 Amazon S3、Amazon RDS/Aurora 與 EC2 上的 SAP HANA，不支援 Amazon EFS，因此無法為 EFS 檔案系統啟用 PITR。Cross-Region Replication（選項 D）會連同刪除動作一起鏡像檔案系統，提供的是災難復原，而非個別已刪除文件的復原。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Backup snapshot backups can be scheduled 'as frequently as hourly' - 30-minute (sub-hourly) frequency is not supported, so a cron expression running every 30 minutes cannot be honored by AWS Backup. Also only one concurrent backup is allowed per EFS resource.","why_zh":"AWS Backup 快照備份最頻繁只能設為每小時一次，不支援每 30 分鐘（次小時）的頻率，因此 AWS Backup 無法執行每 30 分鐘的 cron 排程。此外每個 EFS 資源同時只允許一個備份作業。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Continuous backups and point-in-time recovery (PITR) in AWS Backup are only supported for Amazon S3, Amazon RDS/Aurora, and SAP HANA on EC2 - not Amazon EFS. PITR cannot be enabled for an EFS file system.","why_zh":"AWS Backup 的連續備份與時間點復原（PITR）僅支援 Amazon S3、Amazon RDS/Aurora 與 EC2 上的 SAP HANA，不支援 Amazon EFS，因此無法為 EFS 檔案系統啟用 PITR。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EFS Cross-Region Replication continuously mirrors the file system, including deletions, to another Region. It addresses regional disaster recovery but does not let you recover individually deleted documents, so it fails the requirement.","why_zh":"EFS Cross-Region Replication 會持續將檔案系統（含刪除動作）鏡像到另一個區域，解決的是區域災難復原，無法復原個別被刪除的文件，因此不符合需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/plan-options-and-configuration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/point-in-time-recovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/awsbackup.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/backup-replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/EFSKMS.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":454,"question_en":"A solutions architect must provide a secure way for a team of cloud engineers to use the AWS CLI to upload objects into an Amazon S3 bucket. Each cloud engineer has an IAM user, IAM access keys, and a virtual multi-factor authentication (MFA) device. The IAM users for the cloud engineers are in a group that is named S3-access. The cloud engineers must use MFA to perform any actions in Amazon S3. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"解決方案架構師必須為一組雲端工程師提供一種安全的方式，讓他們能夠使用 AWS CLI 將物件上傳到 Amazon S3 儲存桶。每位雲端工程師都擁有一個 IAM 使用者、IAM 存取金鑰以及一個虛擬多重要素驗證 (MFA) 裝置。這些雲端工程師的 IAM 使用者皆屬於一個名為 S3-access 的群組。雲端工程師在 Amazon S3 中執行任何操作時都必須使用 MFA。哪種解決方案能滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Attach a policy to the S3 bucket to prompt the IAM user for an MFA code when the IAM user performs actions on the S3 bucket. Use IAM access keys with the AWS CLI to call Amazon S3.","B":"Update the trust policy for the S3-access group to require principals to use MFA when principals assume the group. Use IAM access keys with the AWS CLI to call Amazon S3.","C":"Attach a policy to the S3-access group to deny all S3 actions unless MFA is present. Use IAM access keys with the AWS CLI to call Amazon S3.","D":"Attach a policy to the S3-access group to deny all S3 actions unless MFA is present. Request temporary credentials from AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS). Attach the temporary credentials in a profile that Amazon S3 will reference when the user performs actions in Amazon S3."},"options_zh":{"A":"將一個政策附加到該 S3 儲存桶，當 IAM 使用者對該 S3 儲存桶執行操作時，提示該使用者輸入 MFA 驗證碼。搭配 AWS CLI 使用 IAM 存取金鑰來呼叫 Amazon S3。","B":"更新 S3-access 群組的信任政策，要求主體在擔任該群組時必須使用 MFA。搭配 AWS CLI 使用 IAM 存取金鑰來呼叫 Amazon S3。","C":"將一個政策附加到 S3-access 群組，除非存在 MFA，否則拒絕所有 S3 操作。搭配 AWS CLI 使用 IAM 存取金鑰來呼叫 Amazon S3。","D":"將一個政策附加到 S3-access 群組，除非存在 MFA，否則拒絕所有 S3 操作。向 AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) 請求臨時憑證。將該臨時憑證附加到一個設定檔中，供使用者在 Amazon S3 中執行操作時參照使用。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":455,"question_en":"A company needs to migrate 60 on-premises legacy applications to AWS. The applications are based on the NET Framework and run on Windows. The company needs a solution that minimizes migration time and requires no application code changes. The company also does not want to manage the infrastructure. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要將 60 個本地舊版應用程式遷移到 AWS。這些應用程式皆以 .NET Framework 為基礎，並在 Windows 上執行。該公司需要一套能夠縮短遷移時間、且無需變更應用程式程式碼的解決方案。該公司也不希望自行管理基礎設施。哪種解決方案能滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Refactor the applications and containerize them by using AWS Toolkit for NET Refactoring. Use Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) with the Fargate launch type to host the containerized applications.","B":"Use the Windows Web Application Migration Assistant to migrate the applications to AWS Elastic Beanstalk. Use Elastic Beanstalk to deploy and manage the applications.","C":"Use the Windows Web Application Migration Assistant to migrate the applications to Amazon EC2 instances. Use the EC2 instances to deploy and manage the applications.","D":"Refactor the applications and containerize them by using AWS Toolkit for NET Refactoring. Use Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) with the Fargate launch type to host the containerized applications."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Toolkit for .NET Refactoring 重構這些應用程式並將其容器化。使用搭配 Fargate 啟動類型的 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 來託管容器化後的應用程式。","B":"使用 Windows Web Application Migration Assistant 將這些應用程式遷移到 AWS Elastic Beanstalk。使用 Elastic Beanstalk 來部署與管理這些應用程式。","C":"使用 Windows Web Application Migration Assistant 將這些應用程式遷移到 Amazon EC2 執行個體。使用這些 EC2 執行個體來部署與管理這些應用程式。","D":"使用 AWS Toolkit for .NET Refactoring 重構這些應用程式並將其容器化。使用搭配 Fargate 啟動類型的 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 來託管容器化後的應用程式。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":70,"A":30},"tags":["Migration","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":456,"question_en":"A company needs to run large batch-processing jobs on data that is stored in an Amazon S3 bucket. The jobs perform simulations. The results of the jobs are not time sensitive, and the process can withstand interruptions. Each job must process 15-20 GB of data when the data is stored in the S3 bucket. The company will store the output from the jobs in a different Amazon S3 bucket for further analysis. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司需要對存放在 Amazon S3 儲存桶中的資料執行大型批次處理作業。這些作業執行的是模擬工作。作業結果對時間並不敏感，且該流程可以承受中斷。當資料存放在 S3 儲存桶中時，每項作業必須處理 15-20 GB 的資料。該公司會將作業的輸出結果存放到另一個 Amazon S3 儲存桶中，以供進一步分析。哪種解決方案能以最具成本效益的方式滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a serverless data pipeline. Use AWS Step Functions for orchestration. Use AWS Lambda functions with provisioned capacity to process the data.","B":"Create an AWS Batch compute environment that includes Amazon EC2 Spot Instances. Specify the SPOT_CAPACITY_OPTIMIZED allocation strategy.","C":"Create an AWS Batch compute environment that includes Amazon EC2 On-Demand Instances and Spot Instances. Specify the SPOT_CAPACITY_OPTIMIZED allocation strategy for the Spot Instances.","D":"Use Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) to run the processing jobs. Use managed node groups that contain a combination of Amazon EC2 On-Demand Instances and Spot Instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個無伺服器資料管線。使用 AWS Step Functions 進行協調。使用具備佈建容量的 AWS Lambda 函數來處理資料。","B":"建立一個包含 Amazon EC2 Spot 執行個體的 AWS Batch 運算環境。指定 SPOT_CAPACITY_OPTIMIZED 配置策略。","C":"建立一個包含 Amazon EC2 隨需執行個體與 Spot 執行個體的 AWS Batch 運算環境。針對 Spot 執行個體指定 SPOT_CAPACITY_OPTIMIZED 配置策略。","D":"使用 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 來執行處理作業。使用同時包含 Amazon EC2 隨需執行個體與 Spot 執行個體的受管節點群組。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":457,"question_en":"A company has an application that analyzes and stores image data on premises. The application receives millions of new image files every day. Files are an average of 1 MB in size. The files are analyzed in batches of 1 GB. When the application analyzes a batch, the application zips the images together. The application then archives the images as a single file in an on-premises NFS server for long-term storage. The company has a Microsoft Hyper-V environment on premises and has compute capacity available. The company does not have storage capacity and wants to archive the images on AWS. The company needs the ability to retrieve archived data within 1 week of a request. The company has a 10 Gbps AWS Direct Connect connection between its on-premises data center and AWS. The company needs to set bandwidth limits and schedule archived images to be copied to AWS during non-business hours. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司擁有一個在本地分析並儲存影像資料的應用程式。該應用程式每天會接收數百萬個新的影像檔案，檔案平均大小為 1 MB。這些檔案會以 1 GB 為一批進行分析。應用程式在分析一批資料時，會將這些影像壓縮成一個 zip 檔案，然後將該檔案作為單一檔案封存到本地的 NFS 伺服器中，以進行長期儲存。該公司在本地擁有一套 Microsoft Hyper-V 環境，並有可用的運算容量，但沒有儲存容量，因此希望將影像封存到 AWS 上。該公司需要能夠在提出請求後 1 週內取回已封存的資料。該公司的本地資料中心與 AWS 之間有一條 10 Gbps 的 AWS Direct Connect 連線。該公司需要設定頻寬限制，並排定在非營業時間將封存的影像複製到 AWS。哪種解決方案能以最具成本效益的方式滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an AWS DataSync agent on a new GPU-based Amazon EC2 instance. Configure the DataSync agent to copy the batch of files from the NFS on-premises server to Amazon S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval. After the successful copy, delete the data from the on-premises storage.","B":"Deploy an AWS DataSync agent as a Hyper-V VM on premises. Configure the DataSync agent to copy the batch of files from the NFS on- premises server to Amazon S3 Glacier Deep Archive. After the successful copy, delete the data from the on-premises storage.","C":"Deploy an AWS DataSync agent on a new general purpose Amazon EC2 instance. Configure the DataSync agent to copy the batch of files from the NFS on-premises server to Amazon S3 Standard. After the successful copy, delete the data from the on-premises storage. Create an S3 Lifecycle rule to transition objects from S3 Standard to S3 Glacier Deep Archive after 1 day.","D":"Deploy an AWS Storage Gateway Tape Gateway on premises in the Hyper-V environment. Connect the Tape Gateway to AWS. Use automatic tape creation. Specify an Amazon S3 Glacier Deep Archive pool. Eject the tape after the batch of images is copied."},"options_zh":{"A":"在一個新的 GPU 型 Amazon EC2 執行個體上部署一個 AWS DataSync 代理程式。設定該 DataSync 代理程式，將這批檔案從本地的 NFS 伺服器複製到 Amazon S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval。複製成功後，刪除本地儲存體中的資料。","B":"在本地以 Hyper-V VM 的形式部署一個 AWS DataSync 代理程式。設定該 DataSync 代理程式，將這批檔案從本地的 NFS 伺服器複製到 Amazon S3 Glacier Deep Archive。複製成功後，刪除本地儲存體中的資料。","C":"在一個新的通用型 Amazon EC2 執行個體上部署一個 AWS DataSync 代理程式。設定該 DataSync 代理程式，將這批檔案從本地的 NFS 伺服器複製到 Amazon S3 Standard。複製成功後，刪除本地儲存體中的資料。建立一條 S3 生命週期規則，在 1 天後將物件從 S3 Standard 轉換到 S3 Glacier Deep Archive。","D":"在本地的 Hyper-V 環境中部署一個 AWS Storage Gateway Tape Gateway。將該 Tape Gateway 連接到 AWS。使用自動磁帶建立功能，並指定一個 Amazon S3 Glacier Deep Archive 磁帶儲存池。在這批影像複製完成後退出磁帶。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"DataSync can be deployed as a Hyper-V VM on premises, which leverages the company's existing Hyper-V environment and available compute (no EC2 cost), and DataSync natively supports bandwidth limits and scheduling for non-business-hours copies. The official DataSync S3 location documentation lists S3 Glacier Deep Archive as a destination storage class that DataSync transfers data directly into, so option C's extra step of landing in S3 Standard and adding a lifecycle rule is unnecessary and adds an EC2 agent cost plus lifecycle/request charges. Deep Archive offers the lowest storage cost and its 9-48 hour (up to 12 hours standard / 48 hours bulk) retrieval is well within the 1-week requirement. The DataSync small-object caveat (objects under 40 KB are placed in S3 Standard) does not apply because the application zips each batch into a single 1 GB archive file before copying. Therefore B is the most cost-effective solution.","explanation_zh":"DataSync agent 可以部署為地端的 Hyper-V VM，直接利用公司既有的 Hyper-V 環境與閒置運算資源（不需額外 EC2 費用），且 DataSync 原生支援頻寬限制與排程，可在非營業時間複製資料。官方 DataSync S3 location 文件明確列出 S3 Glacier Deep Archive 為 DataSync 可直接寫入的目的地 storage class，因此選項 C 先落地到 S3 Standard 再用 lifecycle rule 轉移的做法是多餘的，還會多出 EC2 agent 成本與 lifecycle/request 費用。Deep Archive 儲存成本最低，其 9 到 48 小時的取回時間（standard 約 12 小時、bulk 約 48 小時）遠在 1 週的要求範圍內。DataSync 對小物件的限制（小於 40 KB 的物件會被放到 S3 Standard）在此不適用，因為應用程式會先把每批影像壓縮成單一 1 GB 的封存檔再複製。因此 B 是最具成本效益的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A GPU-based EC2 instance is wasteful: DataSync does not need GPU and an EC2-hosted agent adds cost when the company already has Hyper-V compute. S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval also has far higher storage cost than Deep Archive while the 1-week retrieval window does not require millisecond access.","why_zh":"GPU 型 EC2 instance 是浪費：DataSync 不需要 GPU，且在公司已有 Hyper-V 運算資源時用 EC2 託管 agent 會增加成本。S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval 的儲存成本也遠高於 Deep Archive，而 1 週的取回需求並不需要毫秒級存取。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"DataSync supports writing directly to S3 Glacier Deep Archive, so first landing in S3 Standard and adding a lifecycle rule is unnecessary. It also runs the agent on a billed EC2 instance instead of free Hyper-V compute and incurs extra lifecycle transition and request charges, making it less cost-effective than B.","why_zh":"DataSync 支援直接寫入 S3 Glacier Deep Archive，因此先落地 S3 Standard 再加 lifecycle rule 是多餘的。它還把 agent 跑在需付費的 EC2 instance 上而非免費的 Hyper-V 運算資源，並產生額外的 lifecycle 轉移與 request 費用，成本效益不如 B。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Tape Gateway requires an iSCSI VTL with third-party backup software and tape eject/archive workflows, adding significant operational overhead. It is not the intended pattern for simply archiving already-zipped files and is less cost-effective and more complex than a direct DataSync-to-Deep-Archive copy.","why_zh":"Tape Gateway 需要 iSCSI VTL 搭配第三方備份軟體與磁帶 eject/archive 流程，增加可觀的營運負擔。對於只是封存已壓縮檔案的情境並非預期用法，比起直接用 DataSync 寫入 Deep Archive 更複雜也較不具成本效益。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datasync/latest/userguide/create-s3-location.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datasync/latest/userguide/deploy-agents.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datasync/latest/userguide/configure-bandwidth.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/glacier-storage-classes.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":458,"question_en":"A company wants to record key performance indicators (KPIs) from its application as part of a strategy to convert to a user-based licensing schema. The application is a multi-tier application with a web-based UI. The company saves all log files to Amazon CloudWatch by using the CloudWatch agent. All logins to the application are saved in a log file. As part of the new license schema, the company needs to find out how many unique users each client has on a daily basis, weekly basis, and monthly basis. Which solution will provide this information with the LEAST change to the application?","question_zh":"一家公司希望記錄其應用程式的關鍵績效指標 (KPI)，作為轉換為使用者授權計費模式策略的一部分。該應用程式是一個具備 Web 使用者介面的多層式應用程式。該公司使用 CloudWatch 代理程式，將所有日誌檔案儲存到 Amazon CloudWatch。應用程式的所有登入記錄都會儲存在一個日誌檔案中。作為新授權計費模式的一部分，該公司需要瞭解每個客戶每天、每週及每月各有多少不重複使用者。哪種解決方案能以對應用程式最少的變更提供這項資訊？","options_en":{"A":"Configure an Amazon CloudWatch Logs metric filter that saves each successful login as a metric. Configure the user name and client name as dimensions for the metric.","B":"Change the application logic to make each successful login generate a call to the AWS SDK to increment a custom metric that records user name and client name dimensions in CloudWatch.","C":"Configure the CloudWatch agent to extract successful login metrics from the logs. Additionally, configure the CloudWatch agent to save the successful login metrics as a custom metric that uses the user name and client name as dimensions for the metric.","D":"Configure an AWS Lambda function to consume an Amazon CloudWatch Logs stream of the application logs. Additionally, configure the Lambda function to increment a custom metric in CloudWatch that uses the user name and client name as dimensions for the metric."},"options_zh":{"A":"設定一個 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 指標篩選器，將每次成功登入儲存為一個指標。將使用者名稱與客戶名稱設定為該指標的維度。","B":"變更應用程式邏輯，讓每次成功登入都呼叫 AWS SDK，以增加在 CloudWatch 中記錄使用者名稱與客戶名稱維度的自訂指標。","C":"設定 CloudWatch 代理程式，從日誌中提取成功登入的指標。此外，設定 CloudWatch 代理程式，將成功登入的指標儲存為一個以使用者名稱與客戶名稱作為維度的自訂指標。","D":"設定一個 AWS Lambda 函數，以消費應用程式日誌的 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 串流。此外，設定該 Lambda 函數，增加一個在 CloudWatch 中以使用者名稱與客戶名稱作為維度的自訂指標。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":89},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":459,"question_en":"A company is using GitHub Actions to run a CI/CD pipeline that accesses resources on AWS. The company has an IAM user that uses a secret key in the pipeline to authenticate to AWS. An existing IAM role with an attached policy grants the required permissions to deploy resources. The company’s security team implements a new requirement that pipelines can no longer use long-lived secret keys. A solutions architect must replace the secret key with a short-lived solution. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 GitHub Actions 執行一套會存取 AWS 資源的 CI/CD 管線。該公司有一個 IAM 使用者，在該管線中使用密鑰來驗證身分以存取 AWS。一個現有的 IAM 角色（已附加相應政策）授予部署資源所需的權限。該公司的安全團隊實施了一項新規定，管線不得再使用長期有效的密鑰。解決方案架構師必須以短期有效的解決方案取代該密鑰。哪種解決方案能以最少的營運開銷滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM SAML 2.0 identity provider (IdP) in AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM). Create a new IAM role with the appropriate trust policy that allows the sts:AssumeRole API call. Attach the existing IAM policy to the new IAM role. Update GitHub to use SAML authentication for the pipeline.","B":"Create an IAM OpenID Connect (OIDC) identity provider (IdP) in AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM). Create a new IAM role with the appropriate trust policy that allows the sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity API call from the GitHub OIDC IdP. Update GitHub to assume the role for the pipeline.","C":"Create an Amazon Cognito identity pool. Configure the authentication provider to use GitHub. Create a new IAM role with the appropriate trust policy that allows the sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity API call from the GitHub authentication provider. Configure the pipeline to use Cognito as its authentication provider.","D":"Create a trust anchor to AWS Private Certificate Authority. Generate a client certificate to use with AWS IAM Roles Anywhere. Create a new IAM role with the appropriate trust policy that allows the sts:AssumeRole API call. Attach the existing IAM policy to the new IAM role. Configure the pipeline to use the credential helper tool and to reference the client certificate public key to assume the new IAM role."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) 中建立一個 IAM SAML 2.0 身分提供者 (IdP)。建立一個新的 IAM 角色，並設定適當的信任政策以允許呼叫 sts:AssumeRole API。將現有的 IAM 政策附加到該新的 IAM 角色。更新 GitHub，讓管線使用 SAML 驗證。","B":"在 AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) 中建立一個 IAM OpenID Connect (OIDC) 身分提供者 (IdP)。建立一個新的 IAM 角色，並設定適當的信任政策，允許來自 GitHub OIDC IdP 的 sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity API 呼叫。更新 GitHub，讓管線擔任該角色。","C":"建立一個 Amazon Cognito 身分集區。將驗證提供者設定為使用 GitHub。建立一個新的 IAM 角色，並設定適當的信任政策，允許來自 GitHub 驗證提供者的 sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity API 呼叫。設定管線使用 Cognito 作為其驗證提供者。","D":"建立一個連接到 AWS Private Certificate Authority 的信任錨點。產生一份用於 AWS IAM Roles Anywhere 的客戶端憑證。建立一個新的 IAM 角色，並設定適當的信任政策以允許呼叫 sts:AssumeRole API。將現有的 IAM 政策附加到該新的 IAM 角色。設定管線使用憑證輔助工具，並參照該客戶端憑證公鑰以擔任該新的 IAM 角色。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":460,"question_en":"A company is running a web-crawling process on a list of target URLs to obtain training documents for machine learning training algorithms. A ­eet of Amazon EC2 t2.micro instances pulls the target URLs from an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. The instances then write the result of the crawling algorithm as a .csv file to an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) volume. The EFS volume is mounted on all instances of the ­eet. A separate system adds the URLs to the SQS queue at infrequent rates. The instances crawl each URL in 10 seconds or less. Metrics indicate that some instances are idle when no URLs are in the SQS queue. A solutions architect needs to redesign the architecture to optimize costs. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在對一份目標 URL 清單執行網頁爬取程序，以取得機器學習訓練演算法所需的訓練文件。一組 Amazon EC2 t2.micro 執行個體從 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 佇列中提取目標 URL。這些執行個體會將爬取演算法的結果以 .csv 檔案的形式寫入 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 磁碟區。該 EFS 磁碟區已掛載到叢集中的所有執行個體上。另一個系統會以不定期的頻率將 URL 新增到 SQS 佇列中。這些執行個體在 10 秒或更短的時間內完成每個 URL 的爬取。指標顯示，當 SQS 佇列中沒有 URL 時，部分執行個體會處於閒置狀態。解決方案架構師需要重新設計架構以優化成本。哪種步驟組合能以最具成本效益的方式滿足這些需求？（請選擇兩項。）","options_en":{"A":"Use m5.8xlarge instances instead of t2.micro instances for the web-crawling process. Reduce the number of instances in the ­eet by 50%.","B":"Convert the web-crawling process into an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to pull URLs from the SQS queue.","C":"Modify the web-crawling process to store results in Amazon Neptune.","D":"Modify the web-crawling process to store results in an Amazon Aurora Serverless MySQL instance.","E":"Modify the web-crawling process to store results in Amazon S3."},"options_zh":{"A":"將網頁爬取程序使用的執行個體從 t2.micro 變更為 m5.8xlarge。將叢集中的執行個體數量減少 50%。","B":"將網頁爬取程序轉換為 AWS Lambda 函數。將該 Lambda 函數設定為從 SQS 佇列中提取 URL。","C":"修改網頁爬取程序，將結果儲存在 Amazon Neptune 中。","D":"修改網頁爬取程序，將結果儲存在 Amazon Aurora Serverless MySQL 執行個體中。","E":"修改網頁爬取程序，將結果儲存在 Amazon S3 中。"},"answer":["B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BE":100},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":461,"question_en":"A company needs to migrate its website from an on-premises data center to AWS. The website consists of a load balancer, a content management system (CMS) that runs on a Linux operating system, and a MySQL database. The CMS requires persistent NFS-compatible storage for a file system. The new solution on AWS must be able to scale from 2 Amazon EC2 instances to 30 EC2 instances in response to unpredictable tra®c increases. The new solution also must require no changes to the website and must prevent data loss. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要將其網站從內部部署資料中心遷移到 AWS。該網站包含一個負載平衡器、一套在 Linux 作業系統上執行的內容管理系統 (CMS)，以及一個 MySQL 資料庫。CMS 需要持久性且相容 NFS 的檔案系統儲存空間。AWS 上的新解決方案必須能夠因應無法預測的流量增加，從 2 個 Amazon EC2 執行個體擴展到 30 個 EC2 執行個體。新解決方案也不能對網站進行任何變更，並且必須防止資料遺失。哪種解決方案能滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. Deploy the CMS to AWS Elastic Beanstalk with an Application Load Balancer and an Auto Scaling group. Use .ebextensions to mount the EFS file system to the EC2 instances. Create an Amazon Aurora MySQL database that is separate from the Elastic Beanstalk environment.","B":"Create an Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) Multi-Attach volume. Deploy the CMS to AWS Elastic Beanstalk with a Network Load Balancer and an Auto Scaling group. Use .ebextensions to mount the EBS volume to the EC2 instances. Create an Amazon RDS for MySQL database in the Elastic Beanstalk environment.","C":"Create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. Create a launch template and an Auto Scaling group to launch EC2 instances to support the CMS. Create a Network Load Balancer to distribute tra®c. Create an Amazon Aurora MySQL database. Use an EC2 Auto Scaling scale-in lifecycle hook to mount the EFS file system to the EC2 instances.","D":"Create an Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) Multi-Attach volume. Create a launch template and an Auto Scaling group to launch EC2 instances to support the CMS. Create an Application Load Balancer to distribute tra®c. Create an Amazon ElastiCache for Redis cluster to support the MySQL database. Use EC2 user data to attach the EBS volume to the EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 檔案系統。將 CMS 部署到具有 Application Load Balancer 和 Auto Scaling 群組的 AWS Elastic Beanstalk。使用 .ebextensions 將 EFS 檔案系統掛載到 EC2 執行個體。建立一個獨立於 Elastic Beanstalk 環境的 Amazon Aurora MySQL 資料庫。","B":"建立一個 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 多重連接磁碟區。將 CMS 部署到具有 Network Load Balancer 和 Auto Scaling 群組的 AWS Elastic Beanstalk。使用 .ebextensions 將 EBS 磁碟區掛載到 EC2 執行個體。在 Elastic Beanstalk 環境中建立一個 Amazon RDS for MySQL 資料庫。","C":"建立一個 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 檔案系統。建立一個啟動範本和一個 Auto Scaling 群組，用以啟動支援 CMS 的 EC2 執行個體。建立一個 Network Load Balancer 來分配流量。建立一個 Amazon Aurora MySQL 資料庫。使用 EC2 Auto Scaling 縮減規模生命週期掛勾，將 EFS 檔案系統掛載到 EC2 執行個體。","D":"建立一個 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 多重連接磁碟區。建立一個啟動範本和一個 Auto Scaling 群組，用以啟動支援 CMS 的 EC2 執行個體。建立一個 Application Load Balancer 來分配流量。建立一個 Amazon ElastiCache for Redis 叢集來支援 MySQL 資料庫。使用 EC2 使用者資料將 EBS 磁碟區連接到 EC2 執行個體。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":93},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirements are NFS-compatible persistent shared storage, scaling from 2 to 30 EC2 instances, no website changes, and no data loss. Amazon EFS is a fully managed NFS file system that can be mounted concurrently by many instances across multiple Availability Zones with no practical instance-count limit, so it satisfies NFS compatibility, the 30-instance scale, and durability. Option A deploys the CMS on Elastic Beanstalk (managed ALB + Auto Scaling) and mounts EFS via .ebextensions, which is the AWS-documented pattern that lets you scale to multiple instances without changing application code, and uses a separate Aurora MySQL database that survives environment changes (no data loss). Option C also uses EFS but ties the mount to an EC2 Auto Scaling SCALE-IN lifecycle hook, which fires when instances are terminated rather than launched, so the file system would never be mounted on new instances; that makes C technically broken. Options B and D rely on EBS Multi-Attach, which is restricted to a maximum of 16 instances in a single Availability Zone, is not NFS, and requires a clustered file system to avoid corruption (standard XFS/EXT4 are not safe for simultaneous multi-server access), so they cannot scale to 30 instances and risk data loss; D additionally misuses ElastiCache for Redis as a substitute for the MySQL database.","explanation_zh":"需求為 NFS 相容的持久共享儲存、從 2 台擴展到 30 台 EC2、不需修改網站、且不能遺失資料。Amazon EFS 是全託管的 NFS 檔案系統，可被多個跨可用區的執行個體同時掛載，且實務上沒有執行個體數量上限，因此滿足 NFS 相容性、30 台規模與耐久性。選項 A 將 CMS 部署在 Elastic Beanstalk（受管 ALB 與 Auto Scaling），並透過 .ebextensions 掛載 EFS，這正是 AWS 官方文件記載的做法，可在不修改應用程式碼的情況下擴展到多個執行個體，並使用獨立的 Aurora MySQL 資料庫以避免資料遺失。選項 C 雖然也用 EFS，但把掛載綁在 EC2 Auto Scaling 的 SCALE-IN（縮減）生命週期掛鉤上，而 scale-in 是在執行個體終止時觸發、而非啟動時，因此新執行個體永遠不會掛載到檔案系統，技術上不可行。選項 B 與 D 使用 EBS Multi-Attach，其限制為單一可用區最多 16 個執行個體、非 NFS，且需要叢集感知檔案系統才能避免資料損毀（標準 XFS/EXT4 不適合多伺服器同時存取），故無法擴展到 30 台且有資料遺失風險；D 還誤把 ElastiCache for Redis 當作 MySQL 資料庫的替代品。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"EBS Multi-Attach supports at most 16 instances in a single Availability Zone and is not NFS; standard file systems like XFS/EXT4 are not designed for simultaneous multi-server access, so it cannot scale to 30 instances and risks data corruption/loss.","why_zh":"EBS Multi-Attach 在單一可用區最多支援 16 個執行個體且非 NFS；XFS/EXT4 等標準檔案系統不適合多伺服器同時存取，無法擴展到 30 台且有資料損毀/遺失風險。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Uses EFS correctly but mounts it via a SCALE-IN lifecycle hook, which fires on instance termination, not launch; new instances launched during scale-out would never mount the file system, so the CMS would fail. The mount should occur on launch/scale-out or via user data.","why_zh":"雖正確使用 EFS，但用 SCALE-IN（縮減）生命週期掛鉤掛載，該掛鉤在執行個體終止時觸發而非啟動時；擴展時新啟動的執行個體永遠不會掛載檔案系統，導致 CMS 失效。掛載應在啟動/擴展時或透過 user data 進行。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EBS Multi-Attach is capped at 16 instances per AZ, is not NFS, and needs a clustered file system; additionally it wrongly proposes ElastiCache for Redis to 'support the MySQL database', which is an in-memory cache, not a MySQL-compatible relational database.","why_zh":"EBS Multi-Attach 每個可用區上限 16 台、非 NFS 且需叢集檔案系統；此外錯誤地用 ElastiCache for Redis 來『支援 MySQL 資料庫』，Redis 是記憶體快取，並非 MySQL 相容的關聯式資料庫。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/services-efs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ebs/latest/userguide/ebs-volumes-multi.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/mounting-fs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.managing.as.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":462,"question_en":"A company needs to implement disaster recovery for a critical application that runs in a single AWS Region. The application's users interact with a web frontend that is hosted on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The application writes to an Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance. The application also outputs processed documents that are stored in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company’s finance team directly queries the database to run reports. During busy periods, these queries consume resources and negatively affect application performance. A solutions architect must design a solution that will provide resiliency during a disaster. The solution must minimize data loss and must resolve the performance problems that result from the finance team's queries. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要為一個在單一 AWS 區域中執行的關鍵應用程式實作災難復原機制。該應用程式的使用者透過位於 Application Load Balancer (ALB) 後方、在 Amazon EC2 執行個體上託管的網頁前端進行互動。該應用程式會寫入 Amazon RDS for MySQL 資料庫執行個體。應用程式也會輸出經處理的文件，並儲存在 Amazon S3 儲存貯體中。該公司的財務團隊會直接查詢資料庫以產生報表。在繁忙時段，這些查詢會消耗資源並對應用程式效能造成負面影響。解決方案架構師必須設計一套能在災難期間提供彈性的解決方案。該解決方案必須將資料遺失降到最低，並解決財務團隊查詢所造成的效能問題。哪種解決方案能滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate the database to Amazon DynamoDB and use DynamoDB global tables. Instruct the finance team to query a global table in a separate Region. Create an AWS Lambda function to periodically synchronize the contents of the original S3 bucket to a new S3 bucket in the separate Region. Launch EC2 instances and create an ALB in the separate Region. Configure the application to point to the new S3 bucket.","B":"Launch additional EC2 instances that host the application in a separate Region. Add the additional instances to the existing ALIn the separate Region, create a read replica of the RDS DB instance. Instruct the finance team to run queries against the read replica. Use S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) from the original S3 bucket to a new S3 bucket in the separate Region. During a disaster, promote the read replica to a standalone DB instance. Configure the application to point to the new S3 bucket and to the newly promoted read replica.","C":"Create a read replica of the RDS DB instance in a separate Region. Instruct the finance team to run queries against the read replica. Create AMIs of the EC2 instances that host the application frontend. Copy the AMIs to the separate Region. Use S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) from the original S3 bucket to a new S3 bucket in the separate Region. During a disaster, promote the read replica to a standalone DB instance. Launch EC2 instances from the AMIs and create an ALB to present the application to end users. Configure the application to point to the new S3 bucket.","D":"Create hourly snapshots of the RDS DB instance. Copy the snapshots to a separate Region. Add an Amazon ElastiCache cluster in front of the existing RDS database. Create AMIs of the EC2 instances that host the application frontend. Copy the AMIs to the separate Region. Use S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) from the original S3 bucket to a new S3 bucket in the separate Region. During a disaster, restore the database from the latest RDS snapshot. Launch EC2 instances from the AMIs and create an ALB to present the application to end users. Configure the application to point to the new S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"將資料庫遷移到 Amazon DynamoDB 並使用 DynamoDB 全域資料表。指示財務團隊在另一個區域查詢全域資料表。建立一個 AWS Lambda 函數，定期將原始 S3 儲存貯體的內容同步到另一個區域中的新 S3 儲存貯體。在另一個區域啟動 EC2 執行個體並建立 ALB。將應用程式設定為指向新的 S3 儲存貯體。","B":"在另一個區域啟動額外的 EC2 執行個體來託管應用程式。將這些額外的執行個體新增到現有的 ALB 中。在另一個區域建立 RDS 資料庫執行個體的讀取複本。指示財務團隊針對該讀取複本執行查詢。使用 S3 跨區域複寫 (CRR) 將原始 S3 儲存貯體的內容複寫到另一個區域中的新 S3 儲存貯體。發生災難時，將讀取複本升級為獨立的資料庫執行個體。將應用程式設定為指向新的 S3 儲存貯體以及新升級的讀取複本。","C":"在另一個區域建立 RDS 資料庫執行個體的讀取複本。指示財務團隊針對該讀取複本執行查詢。為託管應用程式前端的 EC2 執行個體建立 AMI。將這些 AMI 複製到另一個區域。使用 S3 跨區域複寫 (CRR) 將原始 S3 儲存貯體的內容複寫到另一個區域中的新 S3 儲存貯體。發生災難時，將讀取複本升級為獨立的資料庫執行個體。使用這些 AMI 啟動 EC2 執行個體，並建立 ALB 向終端使用者呈現應用程式。將應用程式設定為指向新的 S3 儲存貯體。","D":"每小時為 RDS 資料庫執行個體建立快照。將快照複製到另一個區域。在現有的 RDS 資料庫前方新增一個 Amazon ElastiCache 叢集。為託管應用程式前端的 EC2 執行個體建立 AMI。將這些 AMI 複製到另一個區域。使用 S3 跨區域複寫 (CRR) 將原始 S3 儲存貯體的內容複寫到另一個區域中的新 S3 儲存貯體。發生災難時，從最新的 RDS 快照還原資料庫。使用這些 AMI 啟動 EC2 執行個體，並建立 ALB 向終端使用者呈現應用程式。將應用程式設定為指向新的 S3 儲存貯體。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Option C is the only solution that cleanly satisfies both requirements with a coherent, valid architecture. A cross-Region RDS for MySQL read replica serves a dual purpose: the finance team runs reporting queries against the read replica (AWS explicitly lists 'business reporting/data warehousing' and 'disaster recovery' as canonical read-replica use cases), which offloads reporting load from the primary and fixes the performance problem; and during a disaster the replica is promoted to a standalone instance for recovery. Because RDS read replicas use continuous asynchronous replication, RPO is near-real-time, which minimizes data loss. The frontend is recoverable via AMIs copied to the DR Region (launch EC2 + a new ALB there), and S3 Cross-Region Replication continuously copies documents to a bucket in the DR Region. Every component lives in a self-contained DR Region, which is the correct pilot-light/warm-standby pattern.","explanation_zh":"選項 C 是唯一以正確且可行架構同時滿足兩項需求的方案。跨區域的 RDS for MySQL read replica 一舉兩得：財務團隊對 read replica 執行報表查詢（AWS 明確將「商業報表/資料倉儲」與「災難復原」列為 read replica 的標準使用情境），可將報表負載自主資料庫卸載，解決效能問題；發生災難時再將 replica 提升為獨立 DB instance 以進行復原。由於 RDS read replica 採用持續性的非同步複寫，RPO 接近即時，可將資料遺失降到最低。前端透過複製到 DR 區域的 AMI 復原（在當地啟動 EC2 並建立新的 ALB），S3 Cross-Region Replication 持續將文件複寫到 DR 區域的儲存桶。所有元件都位於一個獨立完整的 DR 區域，符合正確的 pilot-light/warm-standby 模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Migrating RDS for MySQL to DynamoDB is a drastic, unnecessary re-platforming from relational to NoSQL that breaks the finance team's SQL-based reporting and is enormously high-effort. A Lambda that 'periodically synchronizes' S3 is inferior to continuous CRR and increases RPO/data loss. It does not properly solve the query-contention problem either.","why_zh":"將 RDS for MySQL 遷移到 DynamoDB 是不必要的大規模重構（關聯式轉 NoSQL），會破壞財務團隊以 SQL 為基礎的報表，工作量極大。以 Lambda「定期同步」S3 不如持續性的 CRR，且會增加 RPO/資料遺失，也未真正解決查詢競爭問題。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"This is architecturally invalid: an Application Load Balancer is a single-Region resource and you cannot register EC2 instances that are launched in a separate Region into the existing ALB by instance ID, nor is fronting two Regions with one ALB a valid DR design (the ALB itself becomes a single point of failure). The frontend recovery story is incoherent even though the read-replica + promote and S3 CRR pieces are individually fine.","why_zh":"此架構不成立：Application Load Balancer 是單一區域資源，無法將在另一區域啟動的 EC2 以 instance ID 註冊到既有 ALB，且用單一 ALB 同時承載兩個區域並非有效的 DR 設計（ALB 本身會成為單點故障）。即使 read replica + 提升與 S3 CRR 部分各自可行，其前端復原方式仍不合理。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Fails both requirements. Hourly RDS snapshots give an RPO of up to ~1 hour, which is significant data loss and violates 'minimize data loss.' Adding an ElastiCache cluster in front of RDS does not solve the finance team's ad-hoc reporting query contention—those queries still hit the primary DB and are not naturally served by a cache.","why_zh":"兩項需求皆未達成。每小時 RDS 快照的 RPO 最高約 1 小時，屬重大資料遺失，違反「將資料遺失降到最低」。在 RDS 前面加上 ElastiCache 叢集無法解決財務團隊臨時報表查詢的競爭問題，這些查詢仍會打到主資料庫，且本質上無法由快取服務。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_ReadRepl.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_ReadRepl.XRgn.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_ReadRepl.Promote.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-target-groups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":463,"question_en":"A company has many services running in its on-premises data center. The data center is connected to AWS using AWS Direct Connect (DX) and an IPSec VPN. The service data is sensitive and connectivity cannot traverse the internet. The company wants to expand into a new market segment and begin offering its services to other companies that are using AWS. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在其內部部署資料中心中執行許多服務。該資料中心透過 AWS Direct Connect (DX) 與 IPSec VPN 連接到 AWS。服務資料屬於敏感資料，連線不能經過網際網路。該公司希望拓展到新的市場領域，開始向其他使用 AWS 的公司提供其服務。哪種解決方案能滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a VPC Endpoint Service that accepts TCP tra®c, host it behind a Network Load Balancer, and make the service available over DX.","B":"Create a VPC Endpoint Service that accepts HTTP or HTTPS tra®c, host it behind an Application Load Balancer, and make the service available over DX.","C":"Attach an internet gateway to the VPC, and ensure that network access control and security group rules allow the relevant inbound and outbound tra®c.","D":"Attach a NAT gateway to the VPC, and ensure that network access control and security group rules allow the relevant inbound and outbound tra®c."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個接受 TCP 流量的 VPC 端點服務，將其託管在 Network Load Balancer 後方，並透過 DX 提供該服務。","B":"建立一個接受 HTTP 或 HTTPS 流量的 VPC 端點服務，將其託管在 Application Load Balancer 後方，並透過 DX 提供該服務。","C":"將網際網路閘道連接到 VPC，並確保網路存取控制清單和安全群組規則允許相關的輸入和輸出流量。","D":"將 NAT 閘道連接到 VPC，並確保網路存取控制清單和安全群組規則允許相關的輸入和輸出流量。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":86},"tags":["Networking/DNS"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":464,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts. A solutions architect must design a solution in which only administrator roles are allowed to use IAM actions. However, the solutions architect does not have access to all the AWS accounts throughout the company. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 來管理其 AWS 帳戶。解決方案架構師必須設計一套解決方案，使只有管理員角色能夠使用 IAM 操作。然而，該解決方案架構師無法存取公司內所有的 AWS 帳戶。哪種解決方案能以最少的運維成本滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an SCP that applies to all the AWS accounts to allow IAM actions only for administrator roles. Apply the SCP to the root OU.","B":"Configure AWS CloudTrail to invoke an AWS Lambda function for each event that is related to IAM actions. Configure the function to deny the action if the user who invoked the action is not an administrator.","C":"Create an SCP that applies to all the AWS accounts to deny IAM actions for all users except for those with administrator roles. Apply the SCP to the root OU.","D":"Set an IAM permissions boundary that allows IAM actions. Attach the permissions boundary to every administrator role across all the AWS accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個適用於所有 AWS 帳戶的 SCP，只允許管理員角色使用 IAM 操作。將此 SCP 套用到根 OU。","B":"將 AWS CloudTrail 設定為針對每個與 IAM 操作相關的事件呼叫 AWS Lambda 函數。將該函數設定為在呼叫該操作的使用者不是管理員時拒絕該操作。","C":"建立一個適用於所有 AWS 帳戶的 SCP，拒絕除具有管理員角色的使用者之外所有使用者執行 IAM 操作。將此 SCP 套用到根 OU。","D":"設定一個允許 IAM 操作的 IAM 許可範圍界限。將此許可範圍界限連接到所有 AWS 帳戶中的每個管理員角色。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"SCPs are managed centrally from the AWS Organizations management account and automatically apply to every member account under the targeted OU, so the architect does NOT need direct access to each account - this gives the LEAST operational overhead and satisfies the 'no access to all accounts' constraint. The correct technique is a deny-list strategy: an SCP with an explicit Deny on all iam:* actions, combined with a condition (for example aws:PrincipalArn ArnNotLike the administrator role) so the deny does not apply to administrator roles. Because SCPs never grant permissions and an explicit Deny always wins in policy evaluation, this guardrail blocks IAM actions for every principal except the admin roles across all accounts. Option C describes exactly this deny-except-admin approach applied at the root OU.","explanation_zh":"SCP 由 AWS Organizations 的 management account 集中管理，並自動套用到目標 OU 底下的每一個 member account，因此架構師不需要直接存取每個帳戶，這符合「無法存取所有帳戶」的限制，也帶來最少的營運負擔。正確做法是 deny-list 策略：以 SCP 對所有 iam:* 動作設定明確的 Deny，再加上條件（例如 aws:PrincipalArn ArnNotLike 管理員角色），讓此 Deny 不套用於管理員角色。由於 SCP 從不授予權限，且明確 Deny 在政策評估中永遠優先，這道護欄會在所有帳戶中阻止除管理員角色外的所有主體執行 IAM 動作。選項 C 正是描述在 root OU 套用「拒絕除管理員外」的這種做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SCPs never grant permissions; an Allow-style SCP that 'allows IAM actions only for administrator roles' does not deny IAM for non-admins. To restrict access you need a deny-list (explicit Deny), not an allow statement. An allow-only SCP at root would also break all other (non-IAM) actions unless everything else is whitelisted.","why_zh":"SCP 從不授予權限；「只允許管理員角色執行 IAM 動作」的 Allow 型 SCP 並不會拒絕非管理員執行 IAM。要限制存取需用 deny-list（明確 Deny），而非 Allow 陳述。在 root 套用僅 Allow 的 SCP 還會中斷所有其他（非 IAM）動作，除非把其他全部列入白名單。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudTrail records events after they occur and cannot block an in-flight API call; a Lambda triggered by CloudTrail is reactive, not preventive. Building per-event Lambda logic across all accounts is high operational overhead and is not a real access-control mechanism.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 在事件發生後才記錄，無法即時阻擋進行中的 API 呼叫；由 CloudTrail 觸發的 Lambda 是事後反應而非事前預防。在所有帳戶建置逐事件的 Lambda 邏輯營運負擔極高，且並非真正的存取控制機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A permissions boundary must be attached to each IAM entity in each account, requiring access to every account (which the architect lacks) and high overhead. Worse, a boundary that 'allows IAM actions' attached to admin roles would cap those admins to ONLY IAM actions, breaking their broader administrative access.","why_zh":"權限邊界必須逐一附加到每個帳戶的每個 IAM 實體，需要存取所有帳戶（架構師並不具備）且負擔很高。更糟的是，把「允許 IAM 動作」的邊界附加到管理員角色，會把這些管理員限制成只能做 IAM 動作，破壞其更廣泛的管理權限。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_boundaries.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":465,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage multiple AWS accounts. The company hosts some applications in a VPC in the company's shared services account. The company has attached a transit gateway to the VPC in the shared services account. The company is developing a new capability and has created a development environment that requires access to the applications that are in the shared services account. The company intends to delete and recreate resources frequently in the development account. The company also wants to give a development team the ability to recreate the team's connection to the shared services account as required. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的一個組織來管理多個 AWS 帳戶。該公司在其共用服務帳戶的 VPC 中託管一些應用程式。該公司已將一個傳輸閘道連接到共用服務帳戶中的 VPC。該公司正在開發一項新功能，並已建立一個開發環境，該環境需要存取共用服務帳戶中的應用程式。該公司打算在開發帳戶中頻繁刪除並重新建立資源。該公司也希望讓開發團隊能夠根據需要重新建立其與共用服務帳戶的連線。哪種解決方案能滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a transit gateway in the development account. Create a transit gateway peering request to the shared services account. Configure the shared services transit gateway to automatically accept peering connections.","B":"Turn on automatic acceptance for the transit gateway in the shared services account. Use AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) to share the transit gateway resource in the shared services account with the development account. Accept the resource in the development account. Create a transit gateway attachment in the development account.","C":"Turn on automatic acceptance for the transit gateway in the shared services account. Create a VPC endpoint. Use the endpoint policy to grant permissions on the VPC endpoint for the development account. Configure the endpoint service to automatically accept connection requests. Provide the endpoint details to the development team.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function that accepts the transit gateway attachment when the development account makes an attachment request. Use AWS Network Manager to share the transit gateway in the shared services account with the development account. Accept the transit gateway in the development account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在開發帳戶中建立一個傳輸閘道。向共用服務帳戶建立一個傳輸閘道對等連線請求。將共用服務帳戶的傳輸閘道設定為自動接受對等連線。","B":"為共用服務帳戶中的傳輸閘道開啟自動接受功能。使用 AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) 將共用服務帳戶中的傳輸閘道資源與開發帳戶共用。在開發帳戶中接受該資源。在開發帳戶中建立一個傳輸閘道連接。","C":"為共用服務帳戶中的傳輸閘道開啟自動接受功能。建立一個 VPC 端點。使用端點政策為開發帳戶授予該 VPC 端點的許可。將端點服務設定為自動接受連線請求。將端點詳細資訊提供給開發團隊。","D":"建立一個 Amazon EventBridge 規則，在開發帳戶提出連接請求時呼叫 AWS Lambda 函數來接受該傳輸閘道連接。使用 AWS Network Manager 將共用服務帳戶中的傳輸閘道與開發帳戶共用。在開發帳戶中接受該傳輸閘道。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":466,"question_en":"A company wants to migrate virtual Microsoft workloads from an on-premises data center to AWS. The company has successfully tested a few sample workloads on AWS. The company also has created an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection to a VPC. A solutions architect needs to generate a total cost of ownership (TCO) report for the migration of all the workloads from the data center. Simple Network Management Protocol (SNMP) has been enabled on each VM in the data center. The company cannot add more VMs in the data center and cannot install additional software on the VMs. The discovery data must be automatically imported into AWS Migration Hub. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望將虛擬 Microsoft 工作負載從內部部署資料中心遷移到 AWS。該公司已成功在 AWS 上測試了幾個範例工作負載。該公司也已建立一個連接到 VPC 的 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 連線。解決方案架構師需要為資料中心所有工作負載的遷移產生總擁有成本 (TCO) 報告。資料中心內的每個虛擬機器都已啟用簡易網路管理通訊協定 (SNMP)。該公司無法在資料中心新增更多虛擬機器，也無法在虛擬機器上安裝額外的軟體。探索資料必須自動匯入 AWS Migration Hub。哪種解決方案能滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Use the AWS Application Migration Service agentless service and the AWS Migration Hub Strategy Recommendations to generate the TCO report.","B":"Launch a Windows Amazon EC2 instance. Install the Migration Evaluator agentless collector on the EC2 instance. Configure Migration Evaluator to generate the TCO report.","C":"Launch a Windows Amazon EC2 instance. Install the Migration Evaluator agentless collector on the EC2 instance. Configure Migration Hub to generate the TCO report.","D":"Use the AWS Migration Readiness Assessment tool inside the VPC. Configure Migration Evaluator to generate the TCO report."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Application Migration Service 的無代理服務以及 AWS Migration Hub 策略建議來產生 TCO 報告。","B":"啟動一個 Windows Amazon EC2 執行個體。在該 EC2 執行個體上安裝 Migration Evaluator 的無代理收集器。將 Migration Evaluator 設定為產生 TCO 報告。","C":"啟動一個 Windows Amazon EC2 執行個體。在該 EC2 執行個體上安裝 Migration Evaluator 的無代理收集器。將 Migration Hub 設定為產生 TCO 報告。","D":"在 VPC 內使用 AWS Migration Readiness Assessment 工具。將 Migration Evaluator 設定為產生 TCO 報告。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Migration Evaluator (formerly TSO Logic) is AWS's discovery and business-case tool whose explicit purpose is to generate a TCO assessment/business case. Its documented discovery method is 'Agentless - Uses protocols or interfaces such as SNMP or WMI,' which exactly matches the constraint that SNMP is enabled on each VM and that no software can be installed on the VMs and no new VMs can be added. The Migration Evaluator agentless collector is a software package that runs on a Windows host (here, a Windows EC2 instance reachable over the existing Site-to-Site VPN) and polls the on-premises VMs via SNMP/WMI; its discovery data is automatically surfaced 'through AWS Migration Hub' for visualization. Crucially, the TCO/business-case report is produced by Migration Evaluator itself, not by Migration Hub - Migration Hub is only a centralized tracking/visualization dashboard. Option B correctly installs the Migration Evaluator agentless collector on a Windows EC2 instance and configures Migration Evaluator to generate the TCO report.","explanation_zh":"Migration Evaluator(前身為 TSO Logic)是 AWS 的探索與商業案例分析工具,其明確用途就是產生 TCO 評估與商業案例。其官方文件記載的探索方式為「無代理程式 - 使用如 SNMP 或 WMI 等協定或介面」,這正好符合題目限制:每台 VM 已啟用 SNMP、無法在 VM 上安裝額外軟體、也無法在資料中心新增 VM。Migration Evaluator agentless collector 是安裝在 Windows 主機上的軟體(此處為可透過現有 Site-to-Site VPN 連線的 Windows EC2 instance),透過 SNMP/WMI 輪詢內部 VM;其探索資料會自動透過 AWS Migration Hub 呈現以供視覺化。關鍵在於:TCO/商業案例報告是由 Migration Evaluator 本身產生,而非由 Migration Hub 產生 - Migration Hub 僅是集中式追蹤/視覺化儀表板。選項 B 正確地在 Windows EC2 instance 上安裝 Migration Evaluator agentless collector,並設定 Migration Evaluator 來產生 TCO 報告。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) is a rehost/replication tool, not a TCO/business-case tool. Migration Hub Strategy Recommendations produces migration strategy recommendations (rehost/replatform/refactor), not a TCO report, and its collector requires SSH/WMI remote credentials setup. Neither produces a TCO report.","why_zh":"AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) 是 rehost/複寫工具,並非 TCO/商業案例工具。Migration Hub Strategy Recommendations 產生的是遷移策略建議(rehost/replatform/refactor),而非 TCO 報告,且其 collector 需要設定 SSH/WMI 遠端憑證。兩者都無法產生 TCO 報告。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The collector and instance setup are correct, but it says configure Migration Hub to generate the TCO report. Migration Hub is only a centralized tracking and visualization dashboard; it does not generate TCO/business-case reports. Migration Evaluator generates the TCO report. This single wrong clause makes C incorrect versus B.","why_zh":"collector 與 instance 的設定正確,但它寫的是設定 Migration Hub 來產生 TCO 報告。Migration Hub 僅是集中式追蹤與視覺化儀表板,並不會產生 TCO/商業案例報告。產生 TCO 報告的是 Migration Evaluator。這一個錯誤子句使 C 相對於 B 變成錯誤。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"There is no AWS software tool called 'AWS Migration Readiness Assessment tool' that you deploy inside a VPC; MRA is a partner-led assessment workshop/methodology, not a deployable discovery tool. The option is a fabricated combination.","why_zh":"並不存在可部署於 VPC 內、名為「AWS Migration Readiness Assessment tool」的 AWS 軟體工具;MRA 是由合作夥伴主導的評估工作坊/方法論,而非可部署的探索工具。此選項為虛構的組合。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/migration-tools/discovery-migration-evaluator.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/migration-tools/business-case-migration-evaluator.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/migrationhub/latest/ug/troubleshooting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/migrationhub-strategy/latest/userguide/getting-started.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":467,"question_en":"A company that is developing a mobile game is making game assets available in two AWS Regions. Game assets are served from a set of Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in each Region. The company requires game assets to be fetched from the closest Region. If game assets become unavailable in the closest Region, they should be fetched from the other Region. What should a solutions architect do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家正在開發行動遊戲的公司，將遊戲資源提供在兩個 AWS 區域中。遊戲資源由每個區域中位於 Application Load Balancer (ALB) 後方的一組 Amazon EC2 執行個體提供服務。該公司要求從最接近的區域擷取遊戲資源。如果最接近的區域中的遊戲資源無法使用，則應從另一個區域擷取。解決方案架構師應該怎麼做才能滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution. Create an origin group with one origin for each ALB. Set one of the origins as primary.","B":"Create an Amazon Route 53 health check for each ALCreate a Route 53 failover routing record pointing to the two ALBs. Set the Evaluate Target Health value to Yes.","C":"Create two Amazon CloudFront distributions, each with one ALB as the origin. Create an Amazon Route 53 failover routing record pointing to the two CloudFront distributions. Set the Evaluate Target Health value to Yes.","D":"Create an Amazon Route 53 health check for each ALB. Create a Route 53 latency alias record pointing to the two ALBs. Set the Evaluate Target Health value to Yes."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個 Amazon CloudFront 發佈。建立一個來源群組，為每個 ALB 各設定一個來源。將其中一個來源設定為主要來源。","B":"為每個 ALB 建立一個 Amazon Route 53 健康檢查。建立一個指向這兩個 ALB 的 Route 53 容錯移轉路由記錄。將「評估目標健康狀態」值設定為「是」。","C":"建立兩個 Amazon CloudFront 發佈，每個發佈分別以一個 ALB 作為來源。建立一個指向這兩個 CloudFront 發佈的 Amazon Route 53 容錯移轉路由記錄。將「評估目標健康狀態」值設定為「是」。","D":"為每個 ALB 建立一個 Amazon Route 53 健康檢查。建立一個指向這兩個 ALB 的 Route 53 延遲別名記錄。將「評估目標健康狀態」值設定為「是」。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":50,"A":44},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識"},{"id":468,"question_en":"A company deploys workloads in multiple AWS accounts. Each account has a VPC with VPC ­ow logs published in text log format to a centralized Amazon S3 bucket. Each log file is compressed with gzip compression. The company must retain the log files indefinitely. A security engineer occasionally analyzes the logs by using Amazon Athena to query the VPC ­ow logs. The query performance is degrading over time as the number of ingested logs is growing. A solutions architect must improve the performance of the log analysis and reduce the storage space that the VPC ­ow logs use. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LARGEST performance improvement?","question_zh":"一家公司在多個 AWS 帳戶中部署工作負載。每個帳戶都有一個 VPC，其 VPC 流量記錄以文字記錄格式發佈到一個集中的 Amazon S3 儲存貯體。每個記錄檔都以 gzip 壓縮方式壓縮。該公司必須無限期保留這些記錄檔。安全工程師偶爾會使用 Amazon Athena 查詢 VPC 流量記錄來進行分析。隨著匯入的記錄數量增加，查詢效能隨時間逐漸下降。解決方案架構師必須改善記錄分析的效能，並減少 VPC 流量記錄所使用的儲存空間。哪種解決方案能帶來最大幅度的效能改善，並滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function to decompress the gzip files and to compress the files with bzip2 compression. Subscribe the Lambda function to an s3:ObjectCreated:Put S3 event notification for the S3 bucket.","B":"Enable S3 Transfer Acceleration for the S3 bucket. Create an S3 Lifecycle configuration to move files to the S3 Intelligent-Tiering storage class as soon as the files are uploaded.","C":"Update the VPC ­ow log configuration to store the files in Apache Parquet format. Specify hourly partitions for the log files.","D":"Create a new Athena workgroup without data usage control limits. Use Athena engine version 2."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個 AWS Lambda 函數，用以解壓縮 gzip 檔案並以 bzip2 壓縮方式重新壓縮這些檔案。將此 Lambda 函數訂閱到該 S3 儲存貯體的 s3:ObjectCreated:Put S3 事件通知。","B":"為該 S3 儲存貯體啟用 S3 傳輸加速功能。建立一個 S3 生命週期設定，在檔案上傳後立即將其移動到 S3 Intelligent-Tiering 儲存類別。","C":"更新 VPC 流量記錄的設定，將檔案以 Apache Parquet 格式儲存。為記錄檔指定按小時分割的分區。","D":"建立一個沒有資料使用量控管限制的新 Athena 工作群組。使用 Athena 引擎版本 2。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":469,"question_en":"A company wants to establish a dedicated connection between its on-premises infrastructure and AWS. The company is setting up a 1 Gbps AWS Direct Connect connection to its account VPC. The architecture includes a transit gateway and a Direct Connect gateway to connect multiple VPCs and the on-premises infrastructure. The company must connect to VPC resources over a transit VIF by using the Direct Connect connection. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司希望在其內部部署基礎架構與 AWS 之間建立一條專用連線。該公司正在為其帳戶 VPC 設定一條 1 Gbps 的 AWS Direct Connect 連線。此架構包含一個傳輸閘道和一個 Direct Connect 閘道，用以連接多個 VPC 和內部部署基礎架構。該公司必須透過此 Direct Connect 連線，經由傳輸虛擬介面 (transit VIF) 連接到 VPC 資源。哪種步驟組合能滿足這些需求？（請選擇兩項。）","options_en":{"A":"Update the 1 Gbps Direct Connect connection to 10 Gbps.","B":"Advertise the on-premises network prefixes over the transit VIF.","C":"Advertise the VPC prefixes from the Direct Connect gateway to the on-premises network over the transit VIF.","D":"Update the Direct Connect connection's MACsec encryption mode attribute to must_encrypt.","E":"Associate a MACsec Connection Key Name/Connectivity Association Key (CKN/CAK) pair with the Direct Connect connection."},"options_zh":{"A":"將 1 Gbps 的 Direct Connect 連線升級為 10 Gbps。","B":"透過傳輸虛擬介面通告內部部署網路的前綴。","C":"透過傳輸虛擬介面，從 Direct Connect 閘道向內部部署網路通告 VPC 前綴。","D":"將該 Direct Connect 連線的 MACsec 加密模式屬性更新為 must_encrypt。","E":"將一組 MACsec 連線金鑰名稱/連線關聯金鑰 (CKN/CAK) 配對與該 Direct Connect 連線建立關聯。"},"answer":["B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BC":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":470,"question_en":"A company wants to use Amazon WorkSpaces in combination with thin client devices to replace aging desktops. Employees use the desktops to access applications that work with Clinical trial data. Corporate security policy states that access to the applications must be restricted to only company branch o®ce locations. The company is considering adding an additional branch o®ce in the next 6 months. Which solution meets these requirements with the MOST operational e®ciency?","question_zh":"一家公司希望結合使用 Amazon WorkSpaces 與精簡型客戶端裝置來取代老舊的桌上型電腦。員工使用這些桌上型電腦存取處理臨床試驗資料的應用程式。公司的安全政策規定，對這些應用程式的存取必須僅限於公司分公司所在地點。該公司正在考慮在未來 6 個月內新增一個分公司。哪種解決方案能以最高的運維效率滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an IP access control group rule with the list of public addresses from the branch o®ces. Associate the IP access control group with the WorkSpaces directory.","B":"Use AWS Firewall Manager to create a web ACL rule with an IPSet with the list of public addresses from the branch o®ce locations. Associate the web ACL with the WorkSpaces directory.","C":"Use AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) to issue trusted device certificates to the machines deployed in the branch o®ce locations. Enable restricted access on the WorkSpaces directory.","D":"Create a custom WorkSpace image with Windows Firewall configured to restrict access to the public addresses of the branch o®ces. Use the image to deploy the WorkSpaces."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用分公司的公有位址清單建立一條 IP 存取控制群組規則。將該 IP 存取控制群組與 WorkSpaces 目錄建立關聯。","B":"使用 AWS Firewall Manager 建立一條 Web ACL 規則，其中包含分公司地點公有位址清單的 IPSet。將該 Web ACL 與 WorkSpaces 目錄建立關聯。","C":"使用 AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) 向部署在分公司地點的機器發放受信任的裝置憑證。在 WorkSpaces 目錄上啟用受限存取功能。","D":"建立一個自訂 WorkSpace 映像檔，並設定 Windows 防火牆以將存取限制為分公司的公有位址。使用該映像檔部署 WorkSpaces。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":82,"B":18},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Amazon WorkSpaces provides IP access control groups, a native feature that acts as a virtual firewall controlling the source IP addresses from which users can connect their streaming sessions. You add CIDR rules containing the public IP addresses of each branch office and associate the IP access control group with the WorkSpaces directory, so users can connect only when on a trusted branch-office network. This directly satisfies the location-based corporate policy, and when the new branch office opens in 6 months you simply add one more rule (up to 30 rules per group) with no rebuild or redeployment, giving the MOST operational efficiency. Option B is technically invalid because AWS WAF/Firewall Manager web ACLs can only be associated with CloudFront, ALB, API Gateway, AppSync, Cognito, App Runner, or Verified Access resources, not a WorkSpaces directory. Option C (trusted-device certificates) restricts by device identity rather than location and requires an internal CA (not ACM) plus per-device certificate distribution and management, which is both off-requirement and higher overhead. Option D uses Windows Firewall inside the WorkSpace, which governs the WorkSpace OS network traffic, not the user's connecting location, and maintaining custom images is high operational overhead.","explanation_zh":"Amazon WorkSpaces 提供 IP access control groups，這是原生功能，扮演虛擬防火牆，控制使用者連線串流工作階段時的來源 IP。你只要將各分公司的公用 IP 以 CIDR 規則加入 IP access control group，並與 WorkSpaces directory 關聯，使用者就只能在受信任的分公司網路上連線，直接符合以地點為基礎的公司安全政策。當 6 個月後新分公司啟用時，只需再新增一條規則（每組最多 30 條），無需重建或重新部署，達到最高的營運效率。選項 B 在技術上不可行，因為 AWS WAF/Firewall Manager 的 web ACL 只能關聯到 CloudFront、ALB、API Gateway、AppSync、Cognito、App Runner 或 Verified Access 資源，無法關聯到 WorkSpaces directory。選項 C（trusted-device 憑證）是以裝置身分而非地點限制，且需要內部 CA（非 ACM）並逐一部署與管理裝置憑證，既不符合需求又增加負擔。選項 D 在 WorkSpace 內使用 Windows Firewall，只能管控 WorkSpace 作業系統的網路流量，無法限制使用者連入的地點，且維護自訂映像營運負擔高。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS WAF / Firewall Manager web ACLs can only be associated with CloudFront, ALB, API Gateway, AppSync, Cognito user pools, App Runner, or Verified Access resources. There is no mechanism to associate a web ACL or IPSet with a WorkSpaces directory, so this solution cannot be implemented.","why_zh":"AWS WAF／Firewall Manager 的 web ACL 只能關聯到 CloudFront、ALB、API Gateway、AppSync、Cognito user pool、App Runner 或 Verified Access。沒有任何方式可將 web ACL 或 IPSet 關聯到 WorkSpaces directory，因此此方案無法實作。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Trusted-device certificate authentication restricts access by device identity, not by physical/network location, so a trusted laptop could connect from anywhere, failing the location-based policy. It also requires an internal CA (not ACM) and per-device certificate deployment and lifecycle management via MDM/SCCM, which is higher operational overhead.","why_zh":"Trusted-device 憑證驗證是以裝置身分而非實體/網路地點限制，受信任的筆電在任何地方都能連線，無法滿足以地點為基礎的政策。且需要內部 CA（非 ACM），並透過 MDM/SCCM 逐一部署與管理裝置憑證，營運負擔較高。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Windows Firewall inside the WorkSpace controls the WorkSpace OS's own inbound/outbound traffic, not the source location from which the user connects the streaming session. It cannot enforce a branch-office connection restriction, and building/maintaining custom images plus redeploying WorkSpaces is high operational overhead.","why_zh":"WorkSpace 內的 Windows Firewall 控制的是 WorkSpace 作業系統本身的進出流量，而非使用者連入串流工作階段的來源地點，無法落實分公司連線限制；且建立與維護自訂映像並重新部署 WorkSpaces 的營運負擔很高。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/workspaces/latest/adminguide/amazon-workspaces-ip-access-control-groups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/workspaces/latest/adminguide/trusted-devices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/workspaces/latest/adminguide/control-device-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/web-acl-associating-aws-resource.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":471,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations. The company runs two firewall appliances in a centralized networking account. Each firewall appliance runs on a manually configured highly available Amazon EC2 instance. A transit gateway connects the VPC from the centralized networking account to VPCs of member accounts. Each firewall appliance uses a static private IP address that is then used to route tra®c from the member accounts to the internet. During a recent incident, a badly configured script initiated the termination of both firewall appliances. During the rebuild of the firewall appliances, the company wrote a new script to configure the firewall appliances at startup. The company wants to modernize the deployment of the firewall appliances. The firewall appliances need the ability to scale horizontally to handle increased tra®c when the network expands. The company must continue to use the firewall appliances to comply with company policy. The provider of the firewall appliances has confirmed that the latest version of the firewall code will work with all AWS services. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations。該公司在一個集中式網路帳戶中執行兩個防火牆應用裝置。每個防火牆應用裝置都在一個手動設定的高可用性 Amazon EC2 執行個體上執行。一個傳輸閘道將集中式網路帳戶的 VPC 連接到成員帳戶的多個 VPC。每個防火牆應用裝置使用一個靜態私有 IP 位址，該位址用於將流量從成員帳戶路由到網際網路。在最近一次事件中，一個設定錯誤的腳本啟動了對兩個防火牆應用裝置的終止操作。在重建防火牆應用裝置的過程中，該公司編寫了一個新腳本，用於在啟動時設定防火牆應用裝置。該公司希望將防火牆應用裝置的部署方式現代化。當網路擴展時，防火牆應用裝置需要具備水平擴展的能力來應對增加的流量。該公司必須依照公司政策繼續使用這些防火牆應用裝置。防火牆應用裝置的供應商已確認，最新版本的防火牆程式碼可與所有 AWS 服務相容。解決方案架構師應建議哪種步驟組合，以最具成本效益的方式滿足這些需求？（請選擇三項。）","options_en":{"A":"Deploy a Gateway Load Balancer in the centralized networking account. Set up an endpoint service that uses AWS PrivateLink.","B":"Deploy a Network Load Balancer in the centralized networking account. Set up an endpoint service that uses AWS PrivateLink.","C":"Create an Auto Scaling group and a launch template that uses the new script as user data to configure the firewall appliances. Create a target group that uses the instance target type.","D":"Create an Auto Scaling group. Configure an AWS Launch Wizard deployment that uses the new script as user data to configure the firewall appliances. Create a target group that uses the IP target type.","E":"Create VPC endpoints in each member account. Update the route tables to point to the VPC endpoints.","F":"Create VPC endpoints in the centralized networking account. Update the route tables in each member account to point to the VPC endpoints."},"options_zh":{"A":"在集中式網路帳戶中部署一個 Gateway Load Balancer。設定一個使用 AWS PrivateLink 的端點服務。","B":"在集中式網路帳戶中部署一個 Network Load Balancer。設定一個使用 AWS PrivateLink 的端點服務。","C":"建立一個 Auto Scaling 群組和一個啟動範本，將新腳本作為使用者資料來設定防火牆應用裝置。建立一個使用執行個體目標類型的目標群組。","D":"建立一個 Auto Scaling 群組。設定一個 AWS Launch Wizard 部署，將新腳本作為使用者資料來設定防火牆應用裝置。建立一個使用 IP 目標類型的目標群組。","E":"在每個成員帳戶中建立 VPC 端點。更新路由表以指向這些 VPC 端點。","F":"在集中式網路帳戶中建立 VPC 端點。更新每個成員帳戶中的路由表以指向這些 VPC 端點。"},"answer":["A","C","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ACF":56,"ACE":38},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・複選"},{"id":472,"question_en":"A solutions architect must implement a multi-Region architecture for an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database that supports a web application. The database launches from an AWS CloudFormation template that includes AWS services and features that are present in both the primary and secondary Regions. The database is configured for automated backups, and it has an RTO of 15 minutes and an RPO of 2 hours. The web application is configured to use an Amazon Route 53 record to route tra®c to the database. Which combination of steps will result in a highly available architecture that meets all the requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"解決方案架構師必須為支援某個網頁應用程式的 Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL 資料庫實作多區域架構。該資料庫是由一個 AWS CloudFormation 範本啟動的，其中包含主要區域和次要區域均具備的 AWS 服務和功能。該資料庫已設定自動備份，其 RTO 為 15 分鐘，RPO 為 2 小時。該網頁應用程式已設定使用 Amazon Route 53 記錄將流量路由到資料庫。哪種步驟組合能建構出一套滿足所有需求的高可用性架構？（請選擇兩項。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a cross-Region read replica of the database in the secondary Region. Configure an AWS Lambda function in the secondary Region to promote the read replica during a failover event.","B":"In the primary Region, create a health check on the database that will invoke an AWS Lambda function when a failure is detected. Program the Lambda function to recreate the database from the latest database snapshot in the secondary Region and update the Route 53 host records for the database.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function to copy the latest automated backup to the secondary Region every 2 hours.","D":"Create a failover routing policy in Route 53 for the database DNS record. Set the primary and secondary endpoints to the endpoints in each Region.","E":"Create a hot standby database in the secondary Region. Use an AWS Lambda function to restore the secondary database to the latest RDS automatic backup in the event that the primary database fails."},"options_zh":{"A":"在次要區域中為資料庫建立一個跨區域讀取複本。在次要區域中設定一個 AWS Lambda 函數，於容錯移轉事件發生時升級該讀取複本。","B":"在主要區域中為資料庫建立一個健康檢查，於偵測到故障時呼叫 AWS Lambda 函數。將該 Lambda 函數程式設計為使用最新的資料庫快照在次要區域中重新建立資料庫，並更新資料庫的 Route 53 主機記錄。","C":"建立一個 AWS Lambda 函數，每 2 小時將最新的自動備份複製到次要區域。","D":"在 Route 53 中為資料庫的 DNS 記錄建立一個容錯移轉路由政策。將主要端點和次要端點分別設定為各區域中的端點。","E":"在次要區域中建立一個熱備援資料庫。當主要資料庫發生故障時，使用 AWS Lambda 函數將次要資料庫還原至最新的 RDS 自動備份。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AD":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":473,"question_en":"An ecommerce company runs an application on AWS. The application has an Amazon API Gateway API that invokes an AWS Lambda function. The data is stored in an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL DB instance. During the company’s most recent ­ash sale, a sudden increase in API calls negatively affected the application's performance. A solutions architect reviewed the Amazon CloudWatch metrics during that time and noticed a significant increase in Lambda invocations and database connections. The CPU utilization also was high on the DB instance. What should the solutions architect recommend to optimize the application's performance?","question_zh":"一家電子商務公司在 AWS 上執行一個應用程式。該應用程式具有一個 Amazon API Gateway API，用於呼叫 AWS Lambda 函數。資料儲存在一個 Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL 資料庫執行個體中。在該公司最近一次限時促銷活動期間，API 呼叫量突然增加，對應用程式效能造成負面影響。解決方案架構師檢視了當時的 Amazon CloudWatch 指標，發現 Lambda 呼叫次數和資料庫連線數都大幅增加。該資料庫執行個體的 CPU 使用率也很高。解決方案架構師應建議採取什麼做法來優化應用程式效能？","options_en":{"A":"Increase the memory of the Lambda function. Modify the Lambda function to close the database connections when the data is retrieved.","B":"Add an Amazon ElastiCache for Redis cluster to store the frequently accessed data from the RDS database.","C":"Create an RDS proxy by using the Lambda console. Modify the Lambda function to use the proxy endpoint.","D":"Modify the Lambda function to connect to the database outside of the function's handler. Check for an existing database connection before creating a new connection."},"options_zh":{"A":"增加該 Lambda 函數的記憶體。修改該 Lambda 函數，使其在取得資料後關閉資料庫連線。","B":"新增一個 Amazon ElastiCache for Redis 叢集，用以儲存從 RDS 資料庫頻繁存取的資料。","C":"使用 Lambda 主控台建立一個 RDS 代理。修改該 Lambda 函數以使用該代理端點。","D":"修改該 Lambda 函數，使其在函數處理程式之外連接到資料庫。在建立新連線之前先檢查是否已有現有的資料庫連線。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":74,"D":26},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The symptoms are a flash-sale spike that drove a large increase in Lambda invocations AND database connections, with high DB CPU. The root cause is a connection storm: when Lambda scales out to many concurrent execution environments, each one opens its own RDS connection, oversubscribing the database and burning CPU on connection establishment. Amazon RDS Proxy is purpose-built for exactly this: it establishes a database connection pool and reuses/shares connections across the many Lambda instances, caps the number of database connections to protect against oversubscription, and queues or throttles excess requests instead of overwhelming the DB. AWS docs explicitly recommend RDS Proxy to handle unpredictable surges in database traffic from Lambda, and it can be enabled with no application code changes beyond pointing the function at the proxy endpoint. Option D (reuse a connection initialized outside the handler) is a valid best practice but only reuses one connection per warm environment; with hundreds of concurrent environments during a flash sale, total connection count and DB CPU still spike, so it does not solve the described problem at scale. Therefore C is the correct, decisive fix.","explanation_zh":"症狀是 flash sale 流量暴增導致 Lambda invocations 與 database connections 同時大幅上升，且 DB instance CPU 偏高。根本原因是 connection storm：當 Lambda 橫向擴展出大量並行的 execution environment 時，每一個都各自開啟自己的 RDS 連線，造成資料庫連線被超量訂閱，並在建立連線上消耗大量 CPU。Amazon RDS Proxy 正是為此而設計：它建立一個 database connection pool，在眾多 Lambda 實例之間重用與共享連線，限制資料庫連線數以防止超量訂閱，並對超出的請求進行排隊或節流而非壓垮資料庫。AWS 官方文件明確建議使用 RDS Proxy 來處理來自 Lambda 的不可預期流量暴增，且除了將函式指向 proxy endpoint 外幾乎不需修改程式碼。選項 D（在 handler 外初始化並重用連線）雖是有效的最佳實務，但每個 warm environment 只能重用一條連線；在 flash sale 時有數百個並行環境，總連線數與 DB CPU 仍會暴增，無法在規模上解決所述問題。因此 C 是正確且決定性的解法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Increasing memory does not address connection count, and closing the database connection after every retrieval forces a new connection on each invocation, which increases connection churn and CPU on the DB instance, making the problem worse.","why_zh":"增加記憶體無法解決連線數問題，而每次取資料後就關閉連線會迫使每次呼叫都重新建立連線，反而增加連線開銷與 DB CPU，使問題惡化。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"An ElastiCache for Redis cache can offload read-heavy hot data, but it requires significant application code changes and does not directly fix the connection storm or the high DatabaseConnections metric; uncached/write paths still open many direct DB connections. It is a larger architectural change than the purpose-built RDS Proxy.","why_zh":"ElastiCache for Redis 可分流讀取密集的熱門資料，但需大量改寫應用程式碼，且無法直接解決 connection storm 或高 DatabaseConnections 指標；未命中或寫入路徑仍會開大量直連。相較於專為此設計的 RDS Proxy，這是更大的架構變更。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Initializing the connection outside the handler and reusing it is a documented best practice, but it only reuses one connection per warm execution environment. During a flash sale Lambda scales to many concurrent environments, each holding its own connection, so total connections and DB CPU still spike. It does not pool/cap connections across instances the way RDS Proxy does.","why_zh":"在 handler 外初始化並重用連線是官方最佳實務，但每個 warm environment 只能重用一條連線。Flash sale 時 Lambda 會擴展出大量並行環境，各自持有連線，總連線數與 DB CPU 仍會暴增。它無法像 RDS Proxy 那樣跨實例做連線池化與上限控制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/rds-proxy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/ddb-rds-database-decision.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/lambda-rds-connect.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/rds-proxy-connections.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/best-practices.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":474,"question_en":"A retail company wants to improve its application architecture. The company's applications register new orders, handle returns of merchandise, and provide analytics. The applications store retail data in a MySQL database and an Oracle OLAP analytics database. All the applications and databases are hosted on Amazon EC2 instances. Each application consists of several components that handle different parts of the order process. These components use incoming data from different sources. A separate ETL job runs every week and copies data from each application to the analytics database. A solutions architect must redesign the architecture into an event-driven solution that uses serverless services. The solution must provide updated analytics in near real time. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家零售公司希望改善其應用程式架構。該公司的應用程式負責註冊新訂單、處理商品退貨以及提供分析功能。這些應用程式將零售資料儲存在一個 MySQL 資料庫和一個 Oracle OLAP 分析資料庫中。所有應用程式和資料庫都託管在 Amazon EC2 執行個體上。每個應用程式都由幾個負責訂單流程不同部分的元件組成。這些元件使用來自不同來源的輸入資料。另有一個獨立的 ETL 作業每週執行一次，將資料從每個應用程式複製到分析資料庫。解決方案架構師必須將架構重新設計為使用無伺服器服務的事件驅動解決方案。該解決方案必須提供近乎即時的最新分析結果。哪種解決方案能滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate the individual applications as microservices to Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) containers that use AWS Fargate. Keep the retail MySQL database on Amazon EC2. Move the analytics database to Amazon Neptune. Use Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) to send all the incoming data to the microservices and the analytics database.","B":"Create an Auto Scaling group for each application. Specify the necessary number of EC2 instances in each Auto Scaling group. Migrate the retail MySQL database and the analytics database to Amazon Aurora MySQL. Use Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to send all the incoming data to the correct EC2 instances and the analytics database.","C":"Migrate the individual applications as microservices to Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) containers that use AWS Fargate. Migrate the retail MySQL database to Amazon Aurora Serverless MySQL. Migrate the analytics database to Amazon Redshift Serverless. Use Amazon EventBridge to send all the incoming data to the microservices and the analytics database.","D":"Migrate the individual applications as microservices to Amazon AppStream 2.0. Migrate the retail MySQL database to Amazon Aurora MySQL. Migrate the analytics database to Amazon Redshift Serverless. Use AWS IoT Core to send all the incoming data to the microservices and the analytics database."},"options_zh":{"A":"將各個應用程式作為微服務遷移到使用 AWS Fargate 的 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 容器中。將零售 MySQL 資料庫保留在 Amazon EC2 上。將分析資料庫移轉到 Amazon Neptune。使用 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 將所有傳入資料傳送至微服務和分析資料庫。","B":"為每個應用程式建立一個 Auto Scaling 群組。在每個 Auto Scaling 群組中指定所需的 EC2 執行個體數量。將零售 MySQL 資料庫和分析資料庫遷移到 Amazon Aurora MySQL。使用 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 將所有傳入資料傳送到正確的 EC2 執行個體和分析資料庫。","C":"將各個應用程式作為微服務遷移到使用 AWS Fargate 的 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 容器中。將零售 MySQL 資料庫遷移到 Amazon Aurora Serverless MySQL。將分析資料庫遷移到 Amazon Redshift Serverless。使用 Amazon EventBridge 將所有傳入資料傳送至微服務和分析資料庫。","D":"將各個應用程式作為微服務遷移到 Amazon AppStream 2.0。將零售 MySQL 資料庫遷移到 Amazon Aurora MySQL。將分析資料庫遷移到 Amazon Redshift Serverless。使用 AWS IoT Core 將所有傳入資料傳送至微服務和分析資料庫。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Migration","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":475,"question_en":"A company is planning a migration from an on-premises data center to the AWS Cloud. The company plans to use multiple AWS accounts that are managed in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company will create a small number of accounts initially and will add accounts as needed. A solutions architect must design a solution that turns on AWS CloudTrail in all AWS accounts. What is the MOST operationally e®cient solution that meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在規劃從內部部署資料中心遷移到 AWS 雲端。該公司計劃使用多個由 AWS Organizations 中的一個組織所管理的 AWS 帳戶。該公司最初會建立少量帳戶，並根據需要新增更多帳戶。解決方案架構師必須設計一套解決方案，在所有 AWS 帳戶中開啟 AWS CloudTrail。哪種解決方案能以最高的運維效率滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function that creates a new CloudTrail trail in all AWS accounts in the organization. Invoke the Lambda function daily by using a scheduled action in Amazon EventBridge.","B":"Create a new CloudTrail trail in the organization's management account. Configure the trail to log all events for all AWS accounts in the organization.","C":"Create a new CloudTrail trail in all AWS accounts in the organization. Create new trails whenever a new account is created. Define an SCP that prevents deletion or modification of trails. Apply the SCP to the root OU.","D":"Create an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook that creates a CloudTrail trail in all AWS accounts in the organization. Invoke the automation by using Systems Manager State Manager."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個 AWS Lambda 函數，在組織中所有 AWS 帳戶中建立新的 CloudTrail 追蹤。使用 Amazon EventBridge 中的排程動作每天呼叫該 Lambda 函數。","B":"在組織的管理帳戶中建立一個新的 CloudTrail 追蹤。將該追蹤設定為記錄組織中所有 AWS 帳戶的所有事件。","C":"在組織中所有 AWS 帳戶中建立新的 CloudTrail 追蹤。每當建立新帳戶時就建立新的追蹤。定義一個防止刪除或修改追蹤的 SCP。將此 SCP 套用到根 OU。","D":"建立一個 AWS Systems Manager Automation 執行手冊，在組織中所有 AWS 帳戶中建立 CloudTrail 追蹤。使用 Systems Manager State Manager 呼叫此自動化。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Migration","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":476,"question_en":"A software development company has multiple engineers who are working remotely. The company is running Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) on an Amazon EC2 instance. The company's security policy states that all internal, nonpublic services that are deployed in a VPC must be accessible through a VPN. Multi-factor authentication (MFA) must be used for access to a VPN. What should a solutions architect do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家軟體開發公司有多位遠端工作的工程師。該公司在 Amazon EC2 執行個體上執行 Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS)。該公司的安全政策規定，部署在 VPC 中的所有內部、非公開服務都必須透過 VPN 才能存取。存取 VPN 時必須使用多因素驗證 (MFA)。解決方案架構師應該怎麼做才能滿足這些需求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection. Configure integration between a VPN and AD DS. Use an Amazon WorkSpaces client with MFA support enabled to establish a VPN connection.","B":"Create an AWS Client VPN endpoint. Create an AD Connector directory for integration with AD DS. Enable MFA for AD Connector. Use AWS Client VPN to establish a VPN connection.","C":"Create multiple AWS Site-to-Site VPN connections by using AWS VPN CloudHub. Configure integration between AWS VPN CloudHub and AD DS. Use AWS Copilot to establish a VPN connection.","D":"Create an Amazon WorkLink endpoint. Configure integration between Amazon WorkLink and AD DS. Enable MFA in Amazon WorkLink. Use AWS Client VPN to establish a VPN connection."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一個 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 連線。設定 VPN 與 AD DS 之間的整合。使用已啟用 MFA 支援的 Amazon WorkSpaces 客戶端建立 VPN 連線。","B":"建立一個 AWS Client VPN 端點。建立一個 AD Connector 目錄以與 AD DS 整合。為 AD Connector 啟用 MFA。使用 AWS Client VPN 建立 VPN 連線。","C":"使用 AWS VPN CloudHub 建立多個 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 連線。設定 AWS VPN CloudHub 與 AD DS 之間的整合。使用 AWS Copilot 建立 VPN 連線。","D":"建立一個 Amazon WorkLink 端點。設定 Amazon WorkLink 與 AD DS 之間的整合。在 Amazon WorkLink 中啟用 MFA。使用 AWS Client VPN 建立 VPN 連線。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":477,"question_en":"A company is running a three-tier web application in an on-premises data center. The frontend is served by an Apache web server, the middle tier is a monolithic Java application, and the storage tier is a PostgreSQL database. During a recent marketing promotion, customers could not place orders through the application because the application crashed. An analysis showed that all three tiers were overloaded. The application became unresponsive, and the database reached its capacity limit because of read operations. The company already has several similar promotions scheduled in the near future. A solutions architect must develop a plan for migration to AWS to resolve these issues. The solution must maximize scalability and must minimize operational effort Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在其內部部署資料中心中執行一個三層式網頁應用程式。前端由 Apache 網頁伺服器提供服務，中間層是一個單一龐大架構的 Java 應用程式，儲存層則是一個 PostgreSQL 資料庫。在最近一次行銷促銷活動中，客戶無法透過該應用程式下訂單，因為應用程式當機了。分析顯示，三層都出現超載情況。應用程式變得無回應，而資料庫因為讀取操作而達到其容量上限。該公司近期已排定幾次類似的促銷活動。解決方案架構師必須制定遷移到 AWS 的計畫，以解決這些問題。該解決方案必須最大化可擴縮性，並最小化運維工作量。哪種步驟組合能滿足這些需求？（請選擇三項。）","options_en":{"A":"Refactor the frontend so that static assets can be hosted on Amazon S3. Use Amazon CloudFront to serve the frontend to customers. Connect the frontend to the Java application.","B":"Rehost the Apache web server of the frontend on Amazon EC2 instances that are in an Auto Scaling group. Use a load balancer in front of the Auto Scaling group. Use Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) to host the static assets that the Apache web server needs.","C":"Rehost the Java application in an AWS Elastic Beanstalk environment that includes auto scaling.","D":"Refactor the Java application, Develop a Docker container to run the Java application. Use AWS Fargate to host the container.","E":"Use AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to replatform the PostgreSQL database to an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL database. Use Aurora Auto Scaling for read replicas.","F":"Rehost the PostgreSQL database on an Amazon EC2 instance that has twice as much memory as the on-premises server."},"options_zh":{"A":"重構前端，使靜態資源能夠託管在 Amazon S3 上。使用 Amazon CloudFront 向客戶提供前端服務。將前端連接到該 Java 應用程式。","B":"將前端的 Apache 網頁伺服器重新託管到位於 Auto Scaling 群組中的 Amazon EC2 執行個體上。在 Auto Scaling 群組前方使用一個負載平衡器。使用 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 來託管 Apache 網頁伺服器所需的靜態資源。","C":"將該 Java 應用程式重新託管到一個包含自動擴縮功能的 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 環境中。","D":"重構該 Java 應用程式。開發一個 Docker 容器來執行該 Java 應用程式。使用 AWS Fargate 託管該容器。","E":"使用 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 將該 PostgreSQL 資料庫轉換平台為 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL 資料庫。針對讀取複本使用 Aurora Auto Scaling。","F":"將該 PostgreSQL 資料庫重新託管到記憶體是內部部署伺服器兩倍的 Amazon EC2 執行個體上。"},"answer":["A","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ACE":79},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is 'maximize scalability AND minimize operational effort,' and the solution must cover all three tiers. Frontend (A): Refactoring static assets onto Amazon S3 and serving via CloudFront gives effectively unlimited, serverless scalability with the least operational effort, since there are no servers, Auto Scaling groups, or EFS file systems to manage. Middle tier (C): Rehosting the monolithic Java app in AWS Elastic Beanstalk with auto scaling is a lift-and-shift ('rehost') that automatically provisions an Auto Scaling group plus load balancer and handles capacity, health, and platform patching, requiring minimal effort. Storage tier (E): The database failed due to READ operations, so AWS DMS to Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL with Aurora Auto Scaling for read replicas directly and automatically scales read capacity; per AWS docs, Aurora Auto Scaling dynamically adds/removes Aurora Replicas to absorb workload spikes. Together A+C+E address all three tiers with managed/serverless services. The dump's choice D (refactor the Java app, build a Docker container, run on Fargate) explicitly REFACTORS and re-architects the monolith, which is far more operational/development effort than rehosting in Beanstalk, so it loses to C under the 'minimize operational effort' qualifier.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定條件是「最大化可擴展性且最小化營運投入」,且方案必須涵蓋全部三層。前端(A):將靜態資產重構至 Amazon S3 並透過 CloudFront 提供,可獲得近乎無限、無伺服器(serverless)的擴展能力,且營運投入最低,因為沒有伺服器、Auto Scaling group 或 EFS 檔案系統需要管理。中間層(C):將單體 Java 應用以 rehost(原樣搬遷)方式部署到含 auto scaling 的 AWS Elastic Beanstalk,Beanstalk 會自動建立 Auto Scaling group 與負載平衡器並處理容量、健康檢查與平台修補,投入最小。儲存層(E):資料庫因「讀取」操作而達到容量上限,因此用 AWS DMS 遷移到 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL 並啟用 Aurora Auto Scaling for read replicas,可直接且自動地擴展讀取容量;依 AWS 文件,Aurora Auto Scaling 會動態增減 Aurora Replicas 以吸收工作負載尖峰。A+C+E 以受管/無伺服器服務解決全部三層。題庫所選的 D(重構 Java 應用、建立 Docker 容器、於 Fargate 執行)明確地對單體進行重構與重新架構,其營運與開發投入遠高於在 Beanstalk 上 rehost,因此在「最小化營運投入」的限定下不如 C。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Rehosting Apache on an EC2 Auto Scaling group behind a load balancer and using EFS for static assets still requires managing EC2 fleets, AMIs, patching, and an EFS file system. That is more operational effort and less scalable than S3+CloudFront, so it loses to A under 'minimize operational effort + maximize scalability.'","why_zh":"把 Apache 搬到 EC2 Auto Scaling group 並用負載平衡器,再以 EFS 存放靜態資產,仍需管理 EC2 機群、AMI、修補與 EFS 檔案系統。相較 S3+CloudFront,營運投入更高且擴展性更差,因此在限定條件下輸給 A。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This option REFACTORS the monolithic Java app, builds a Docker container, and runs it on Fargate. Refactoring/containerizing a monolith is significant development and operational effort compared to a simple rehost in Elastic Beanstalk (C), which already provides managed auto scaling. It directly conflicts with the 'minimize operational effort' qualifier.","why_zh":"此選項對單體 Java 應用進行重構、建立 Docker 容器並於 Fargate 執行。將單體容器化屬大量的開發與營運投入,相較於在 Elastic Beanstalk 上單純 rehost(C,已內建受管 auto scaling)。這直接違背「最小化營運投入」的限定條件。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Rehosting PostgreSQL on a single EC2 instance with twice the memory is self-managed (you handle patching, backups, HA) and does NOT auto-scale reads. The failure was caused by read operations, which a single larger instance cannot elastically absorb; only Aurora read replicas with Auto Scaling (E) solve this.","why_zh":"把 PostgreSQL 搬到記憶體加倍的單一 EC2 執行個體屬自管(需自行處理修補、備份、高可用),且無法自動擴展讀取。故障是由讀取操作引起,單一更大執行個體無法彈性吸收;唯有 Aurora read replicas 搭配 Auto Scaling(E)能解決。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Integrating.AutoScaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.managing.as.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/AuroraPostgreSQL.Migrating.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/GettingStarted.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/HostingWebsiteOnS3Setup.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・複選"},{"id":478,"question_en":"A company is deploying a new application on AWS. The application consists of an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster and an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. The EKS cluster has an AWS managed node group. The company's security guidelines state that all resources on AWS must be continuously scanned for security vulnerabilities. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 上部署一個新的應用程式。該應用程式包含一個 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 叢集和一個 Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) 儲存庫。該 EKS 叢集具有一個 AWS 受管節點群組。該公司的安全準則規定，AWS 上的所有資源都必須持續掃描安全漏洞。哪種解決方案能以最少的運維成本滿足這項需求？","options_en":{"A":"Activate AWS Security Hub. Configure Security Hub to scan the EKS nodes and the ECR repository.","B":"Activate Amazon Inspector to scan the EKS nodes and the ECR repository.","C":"Launch a new Amazon EC2 instance and install a vulnerability scanning tool from AWS Marketplace. Configure the EC2 instance to scan the EKS nodes. Configure Amazon ECR to perform a basic scan on push.","D":"Install the Amazon CloudWatch agent on the EKS nodes. Configure the CloudWatch agent to scan continuously. Configure Amazon ECR to perform a basic scan on push."},"options_zh":{"A":"啟用 AWS Security Hub。將 Security Hub 設定為掃描 EKS 節點和 ECR 儲存庫。","B":"啟用 Amazon Inspector 來掃描 EKS 節點和 ECR 儲存庫。","C":"啟動一個新的 Amazon EC2 執行個體，並從 AWS Marketplace 安裝一個漏洞掃描工具。將該 EC2 執行個體設定為掃描 EKS 節點。將 Amazon ECR 設定為在推送時執行基本掃描。","D":"在 EKS 節點上安裝 Amazon CloudWatch 代理程式。將該 CloudWatch 代理程式設定為持續掃描。將 Amazon ECR 設定為在推送時執行基本掃描。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":85,"A":15},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":479,"question_en":"A company needs to improve the reliability of its ticketing application. The application runs on an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster. The company uses Amazon CloudFront to serve the application. A single ECS service of the ECS cluster is the CloudFront distribution’s origin. The application allows only a specific number of active users to enter a ticket purchasing ­ow. These users are identified by an encrypted attribute in their JSON Web Token (JWT). All other users are redirected to a waiting room module until there is available capacity for purchasing. The application is experiencing high loads. The waiting room module is working as designed, but load on the waiting room is disrupting the applications availability. This disruption is negatively affecting the application's ticket sale transactions. Which solution will provide the MOST reliability for ticket sale transactions during periods of high load?","question_zh":"一家公司需要改善其票務應用程式的可靠性。該應用程式在一個 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 叢集上執行。該公司使用 Amazon CloudFront 來提供該應用程式的服務。該 ECS 叢集中的單一 ECS 服務是 CloudFront 發佈的來源。該應用程式僅允許特定數量的活躍使用者進入購票流程。這些使用者是透過其 JSON Web Token (JWT) 中的一個加密屬性來識別的。所有其他使用者則會被重新導向到一個等候室模組，直到有可用的購買容量為止。該應用程式目前正承受高負載。等候室模組的運作方式符合預期設計，但等候室的負載正在干擾該應用程式的可用性。這種干擾對該應用程式的售票交易造成了負面影響。哪種解決方案能在高負載期間為售票交易提供最高的可靠性？","options_en":{"A":"Create a separate service in the ECS cluster for the waiting room. Use a separate scaling configuration. Ensure that the ticketing service uses the JWT information and appropriately forwards requests to the waiting room service.","B":"Move the application to an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster. Split the waiting room module into a pod that is separate from the ticketing pod. Make the ticketing pod part of a StatefulSet. Ensure that the ticketing pod uses the JWT information and appropriately forwards requests to the waiting room pod.","C":"Create a separate service in the ECS cluster for the waiting room. Use a separate scaling configuration. Create a CloudFront function that inspects the JWT information and appropriately forwards requests to the ticketing service or the waiting room service.","D":"Move the application to an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster. Split the waiting room module into a pod that is separate from the ticketing pod. Use AWS App Mesh by provisioning the App Mesh controller for Kubernetes. Enable mTLS authentication and service-to-service authentication for communication between the ticketing pod and the waiting room pod. Ensure that the ticketing pod uses the JWT information and appropriately forwards requests to the waiting room pod."},"options_zh":{"A":"在該 ECS 叢集中為等候室建立一個獨立的服務。使用獨立的擴縮設定。確保票務服務使用 JWT 資訊，並適當地將請求轉發到等候室服務。","B":"將該應用程式移轉到一個 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 叢集。將等候室模組拆分為一個與票務 Pod 分離的獨立 Pod。將票務 Pod 設為 StatefulSet 的一部分。確保票務 Pod 使用 JWT 資訊，並適當地將請求轉發到等候室 Pod。","C":"在該 ECS 叢集中為等候室建立一個獨立的服務。使用獨立的擴縮設定。建立一個 CloudFront 函數，用以檢查 JWT 資訊，並適當地將請求轉發到票務服務或等候室服務。","D":"將該應用程式移轉到一個 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 叢集。將等候室模組拆分為一個與票務 Pod 分離的獨立 Pod。透過佈建適用於 Kubernetes 的 App Mesh 控制器來使用 AWS App Mesh。為票務 Pod 與等候室 Pod 之間的通訊啟用 mTLS 驗證和服務對服務驗證。確保票務 Pod 使用 JWT 資訊，並適當地將請求轉發到等候室 Pod。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":480,"question_en":"A solutions architect is creating an AWS CloudFormation template from an existing manually created non-production AWS environment. The CloudFormation template can be destroyed and recreated as needed. The environment contains an Amazon EC2 instance. The EC2 instance has an instance profile that the EC2 instance uses to assume a role in a parent account. The solutions architect recreates the role in a CloudFormation template and uses the same role name. When the CloudFormation template is launched in the child account, the EC2 instance can no longer assume the role in the parent account because of insu®cient permissions What should the solutions architect do to resolve this issue?","question_zh":"一位解决方案架构师正在根据现有的手动创建的非生产 AWS 环境建立 AWS CloudFormation 模板。该 CloudFormation 模板可以根据需要销毁并重新创建。该环境包含一个 Amazon EC2 实例。该 EC2 实例具有一个实例配置文件，EC2 实例使用该配置文件在父账户中扮演一个角色。解决方案架构师在 CloudFormation 模板中重新创建了该角色，并使用相同的角色名称。当该 CloudFormation 模板在子账户中启动后，由于权限不足，EC2 实例无法再在父账户中扮演该角色。解决方案架构师应该怎么做才能解决此问题？","options_en":{"A":"In the parent account, edit the trust policy for the role that the EC2 instance needs to assume. Ensure that the target role ARN in the existing statement that allows the sts:AssumeRole action is correct. Save the trust policy.","B":"In the parent account, edit the trust policy for the role that the EC2 instance needs to assume. Add a statement that allows the sts:AssumeRole action for the root principal of the child account. Save the trust policy.","C":"Update the CloudFormation stack again. Specify only the CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM capability.","D":"Update the CloudFormation stack again. Specify the CAPABILITY_IAM capability and the CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM capability."},"options_zh":{"A":"在父账户中，编辑 EC2 实例需要扮演的角色的信任策略。确保允许 sts:AssumeRole 操作的现有语句中的目标角色 ARN 正确无误。保存信任策略。","B":"在父账户中，编辑 EC2 实例需要扮演的角色的信任策略。添加一条语句，允许子账户的根主体执行 sts:AssumeRole 操作。保存信任策略。","C":"再次更新 CloudFormation 堆栈，仅指定 CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM 功能。","D":"再次更新 CloudFormation 堆栈，同时指定 CAPABILITY_IAM 功能和 CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM 功能。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":64,"B":29},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"When an IAM role ARN is used in the Principal element of another role's trust policy, IAM transforms that ARN into the role's unique principal ID at save time (to prevent privilege escalation via delete/recreate). When the solutions architect recreated the child-account EC2 role via CloudFormation with the same name, the new role received a NEW unique principal ID. The parent account's trust policy still contained the OLD principal ID, so it no longer matched and AssumeRole failed with insufficient permissions. The documented fix is to edit the parent account's trust policy and re-save it with the correct (new) role ARN, which IAM then re-transforms into the new principal ID. Option A describes exactly this: edit the existing sts:AssumeRole statement so the target role ARN is correct and save the policy. AWS docs state explicitly: 'if you delete and recreate a role referenced in a trust policy's Principal element, you must edit the role in the policy to replace the principal ID with the correct ARN.'","explanation_zh":"當某個 IAM role 的 ARN 被用在另一個 role 的 trust policy 的 Principal 元素中時，IAM 在儲存時會把該 ARN 轉換成該 role 的唯一 principal ID（用以防止透過刪除/重建來提權）。當解決方案架構師使用 CloudFormation 以相同名稱重建 child account 的 EC2 role 時，新 role 取得了一個全新的唯一 principal ID。parent account 的 trust policy 中仍存著舊的 principal ID，因此不再相符，AssumeRole 便因權限不足而失敗。官方文件記載的修正方式是編輯 parent account 的 trust policy 並以正確（新的）role ARN 重新儲存，IAM 會再次將其轉換為新的 principal ID。選項 A 正是描述此操作：編輯既有的 sts:AssumeRole 陳述，確保目標 role ARN 正確並儲存 policy。AWS 文件明確指出：若刪除並重建 trust policy 之 Principal 元素中所引用的 role，必須編輯該 policy 並以正確的 ARN 取代 principal ID。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Adding the child account's root principal would over-broaden the trust (allowing any identity in the child account to be delegated) and is not the documented remedy for a broken principal-ID transformation. The original trust statement already targeted the specific role ARN; the only thing broken is the stale principal ID, which is fixed by re-saving the correct ARN. Granting the whole account root is unnecessary and weakens least privilege.","why_zh":"加入 child account 的 root principal 會把信任範圍過度放寬（允許 child account 中任何身分被委派），且這並非針對 principal ID 轉換失效的官方修正方式。原本的 trust 陳述已鎖定特定 role ARN，唯一壞掉的是過時的 principal ID，只需重新儲存正確的 ARN 即可修正。授予整個帳號 root 既無必要又削弱最小權限原則。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM only affects whether CloudFormation is permitted to create IAM resources with custom names during stack operations in the child account. The role was already created successfully; the failure is in the parent account's trust policy, which CloudFormation in the child account cannot influence. Re-running the stack with this capability does nothing to fix the stale principal ID.","why_zh":"CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM 只影響 CloudFormation 在 child account 進行堆疊操作時是否獲准建立具自訂名稱的 IAM 資源。該 role 已成功建立；失敗點在 parent account 的 trust policy，child account 的 CloudFormation 無法影響它。以此 capability 重跑堆疊完全無法修正過時的 principal ID。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same flaw as C: IAM capabilities (CAPABILITY_IAM / CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM) only authorize the stack to manage IAM resources within the deploying (child) account. They have no bearing on the parent account's trust policy where the broken principal-ID mapping lives. Re-deploying with both capabilities will not restore the cross-account trust.","why_zh":"與 C 相同的缺陷：IAM capabilities（CAPABILITY_IAM / CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM）只授權堆疊在部署的（child）帳號內管理 IAM 資源，與存放著失效 principal ID 對應的 parent account trust policy 毫無關係。以兩個 capability 重新部署並不會恢復跨帳號信任。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_elements_principal.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_update-role-trust-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_identifiers.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":481,"question_en":"A company's web application has reliability issues. The application serves customers globally. The application runs on a single Amazon EC2 instance and performs read-intensive operations on an Amazon RDS for MySQL database. During high load, the application becomes unresponsive and requires a manual restart of the EC2 instance. A solutions architect must improve the application's reliability. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST development effort?","question_zh":"一家公司的 Web 应用程序存在可靠性问题。该应用程序为全球客户提供服务。该应用程序在单个 Amazon EC2 实例上运行，并对 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库执行读密集型操作。在高负载期间，应用程序会变得无响应，需要手动重启 EC2 实例。解决方案架构师必须提高应用程序的可靠性。哪种解决方案能以最少的开发工作量满足此要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution. Specify the EC2 instance as the distribution’s origin. Configure a Multi-AZ deployment for the RDS for MySQL database. Use the standby DB instance for the read-intensive operations.","B":"Run the application on EC2 instances that are in an Auto Scaling group. Place the EC2 instances behind an Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) load balancer. Replace the database service with Amazon Aurora. Use Aurora Replicas for the read-intensive operations.","C":"Deploy AWS Global Accelerator. Configure a Multi-AZ deployment for the RDS for MySQL database. Use the standby DB instance for the read-intensive operations.","D":"Migrate the application to AWS Lambda functions. Create read replicas for the RDS for MySQL database. Use the read replicas for the read-intensive operations."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon CloudFront 分配，将 EC2 实例指定为该分配的源。为 RDS for MySQL 数据库配置多可用区部署，并使用备用数据库实例执行读密集型操作。","B":"在 Auto Scaling 组中的 EC2 实例上运行该应用程序，并将这些 EC2 实例放置在 Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) 负载均衡器之后。将数据库服务替换为 Amazon Aurora，并使用 Aurora 副本执行读密集型操作。","C":"部署 AWS Global Accelerator。为 RDS for MySQL 数据库配置多可用区部署，并使用备用数据库实例执行读密集型操作。","D":"将应用程序迁移到 AWS Lambda 函数。为 RDS for MySQL 数据库创建读取副本，并使用这些读取副本执行读密集型操作。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":77},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The application has two reliability problems: a single EC2 instance that becomes unresponsive under load (no horizontal scaling/self-healing), and a read-intensive RDS for MySQL database. Option B fixes both: an Auto Scaling group behind an ELB removes the single-instance failure mode (unhealthy instances are replaced automatically and capacity scales with load), and Amazon Aurora with Aurora Replicas provides valid read scaling via the reader endpoint plus automatic failover. This is the standard AWS reliability pattern and requires no application rewrite, satisfying the LEAST development effort qualifier. Options A and C are technically invalid because they propose using a standard RDS for MySQL Multi-AZ standby for the read-intensive operations; AWS docs state a Multi-AZ DB instance deployment's standby 'provides failover support, but doesn't serve read traffic.' A also leaves the single overloaded EC2 instance in place (CloudFront does not solve the compute overload), and D (rewriting the app as Lambda) is heavy re-architecture, the opposite of least development effort.","explanation_zh":"此應用有兩個可靠性問題：單一 EC2 instance 在高負載下會無回應（缺乏水平擴展與自我修復），以及讀取密集的 RDS for MySQL 資料庫。選項 B 同時解決兩者：Auto Scaling group 搭配 ELB 消除單一 instance 的故障點（不健康的 instance 會自動被替換，容量隨負載擴展），而 Amazon Aurora 搭配 Aurora Replicas 透過 reader endpoint 提供有效的讀取擴展並具備自動 failover。這是標準的 AWS 可靠性架構，且不需重寫應用程式，符合「最少開發工作」的條件。選項 A 與 C 在技術上不成立，因為它們提議用標準 RDS for MySQL Multi-AZ 的 standby 來處理讀取密集操作；AWS 文件明確指出 Multi-AZ DB instance 部署的 standby「提供 failover 支援，但不提供讀取流量」。A 同時還保留了單一過載的 EC2 instance（CloudFront 無法解決運算過載），而 D（將應用重寫為 Lambda）屬於大規模重新架構，與最少開發工作恰好相反。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A standard RDS for MySQL Multi-AZ (DB instance) standby does NOT serve read traffic per AWS docs, so the read-offload plan is invalid. It also keeps the single overloaded EC2 instance; CloudFront fronts/caches content but does not fix the compute overload causing unresponsiveness and manual restarts.","why_zh":"依 AWS 文件，標準 RDS for MySQL Multi-AZ（DB instance）的 standby 不提供讀取流量，因此讀取卸載方案無效。它也保留了單一過載的 EC2 instance；CloudFront 只負責前端/快取，無法解決導致無回應與手動重啟的運算過載。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Same fatal flaw as A on the database: a Multi-AZ DB instance standby cannot serve reads. Global Accelerator only improves global network routing and does nothing to add compute capacity or self-healing for the single EC2 instance, so the core reliability issue remains.","why_zh":"資料庫面與 A 有相同的致命缺陷：Multi-AZ DB instance 的 standby 無法提供讀取。Global Accelerator 只改善全球網路路由，無法為單一 EC2 instance 增加運算容量或自我修復，核心可靠性問題依舊存在。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Read replicas would offload reads correctly, but migrating the application to AWS Lambda requires substantial re-architecture and code changes to fit the serverless execution model. That contradicts the 'LEAST development effort' requirement.","why_zh":"read replicas 可正確卸載讀取，但將應用遷移到 AWS Lambda 需要大量重新架構與程式碼變更以符合無伺服器執行模型，違反「最少開發工作」的要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/Concepts.MultiAZ.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Integrating.AutoScaling.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":482,"question_en":"A company needs to use an AWS Transfer Family SFTP-enabled server with an Amazon S3 bucket to receive updates from a third-party data supplier. The data is encrypted with Pretty Good Privacy (PGP) encryption. The company needs a solution that will automatically decrypt the data after the company receives the data. A solutions architect will use a Transfer Family managed work­ow. The company has created an IAM service role by using an IAM policy that allows access to AWS Secrets Manager and the S3 bucket. The role’s trust relationship allows the transfer amazonaws.com service to assume the role. What should the solutions architect do next to complete the solution for automatic decryption?","question_zh":"一家公司需要使用启用了 SFTP 的 AWS Transfer Family 服务器和一个 Amazon S3 存储桶，以接收来自第三方数据供应商的更新数据。这些数据使用 Pretty Good Privacy (PGP) 加密。该公司需要一种解决方案，能够在收到数据后自动对其进行解密。解决方案架构师将使用 Transfer Family 托管工作流。该公司已通过一个允许访问 AWS Secrets Manager 和该 S3 存储桶的 IAM 策略创建了一个 IAM 服务角色。该角色的信任关系允许 transfer.amazonaws.com 服务扮演该角色。为了完成自动解密解决方案，解决方案架构师接下来应该做什么？","options_en":{"A":"Store the PGP public key in Secrets Manager. Add a nominal step in the Transfer Family managed work­ow to decrypt files. Configure PGP encryption parameters in the nominal step. Associate the work­ow with the Transfer Family server.","B":"Store the PGP private key in Secrets Manager. Add an exception-handling step in the Transfer Family managed work­ow to decrypt files. Configure PGP encryption parameters in the exception handler. Associate the work­ow with the SFTP user.","C":"Store the PGP private key in Secrets Manager. Add a nominal step in the Transfer Family managed work­ow to decrypt files. Configure PGP decryption parameters in the nominal step. Associate the work­ow with the Transfer Family server.","D":"Store the PGP public key in Secrets Manager. Add an exception-handling step in the Transfer Family managed work­ow to decrypt files. Configure PGP decryption parameters in the exception handler. Associate the work­ow with the SFTP user."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 PGP 公钥存储在 Secrets Manager 中。在 Transfer Family 托管工作流中添加一个常规步骤以解密文件。在该常规步骤中配置 PGP 加密参数。将该工作流与 Transfer Family 服务器关联。","B":"将 PGP 私钥存储在 Secrets Manager 中。在 Transfer Family 托管工作流中添加一个异常处理步骤以解密文件。在异常处理程序中配置 PGP 加密参数。将该工作流与 SFTP 用户关联。","C":"将 PGP 私钥存储在 Secrets Manager 中。在 Transfer Family 托管工作流中添加一个常规步骤以解密文件。在该常规步骤中配置 PGP 解密参数。将该工作流与 Transfer Family 服务器关联。","D":"将 PGP 公钥存储在 Secrets Manager 中。在 Transfer Family 托管工作流中添加一个异常处理步骤以解密文件。在异常处理程序中配置 PGP 解密参数。将该工作流与 SFTP 用户关联。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"AWS Transfer Family decrypts PGP-encrypted files using a managed workflow with a DECRYPT step placed in the Nominal steps section, and the PGP PRIVATE key (with passphrase) must be stored in AWS Secrets Manager. PGP encryption uses the recipient's public key to encrypt and the corresponding private key to decrypt, so decryption requires the private key, not the public key. The AWS tutorial explicitly stores the key as 'PGPPrivateKey' and warns that the value must contain only the private key. The decrypt step is a normal (nominal) processing step, not an exception-handling step (exception handlers run only when a nominal step fails). Finally, the managed workflow is associated with the Transfer Family server (as the 'Workflow for complete file uploads'), not with an individual SFTP user. Option C matches all of these facts: private key in Secrets Manager, nominal decrypt step with PGP decryption parameters, workflow associated with the server.","explanation_zh":"AWS Transfer Family 透過 managed workflow 中的 decrypt 步驟來解密 PGP 加密檔案，該步驟放在 Nominal steps（正常步驟）區段，並且必須將 PGP 私鑰（連同 passphrase）儲存在 AWS Secrets Manager 中。PGP 使用接收方的公鑰加密、對應的私鑰解密，因此解密需要的是私鑰而非公鑰。AWS 官方教學明確以 'PGPPrivateKey' 鍵名儲存，並警告值中只能包含私鑰。Decrypt 步驟屬於正常（nominal）處理步驟，而非例外處理（exception-handling）步驟（例外處理僅在 nominal 步驟失敗時才執行）。最後，managed workflow 是關聯到 Transfer Family server（設定為 'Workflow for complete file uploads'），而非個別 SFTP user。選項 C 完全符合：私鑰存於 Secrets Manager、nominal decrypt 步驟搭配 PGP 解密參數、workflow 關聯到 server。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Decryption requires the PGP PRIVATE key, not the public key. The public key is used only to encrypt; storing it would not allow Transfer Family to decrypt the incoming files. The nominal step and server association are otherwise correct, but the public key makes this wrong.","why_zh":"解密需要 PGP 私鑰而非公鑰。公鑰只用於加密，儲存公鑰無法讓 Transfer Family 解密接收到的檔案。雖然 nominal 步驟與關聯到 server 的部分正確，但使用公鑰使此選項錯誤。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The decrypt step is a nominal step, not an exception-handling step (exception handlers only run when a nominal step fails). It also incorrectly associates the workflow with the SFTP user instead of the Transfer Family server. The private key part is correct but the other two errors make it wrong.","why_zh":"Decrypt 步驟是 nominal 步驟，而非例外處理步驟（例外處理僅在 nominal 步驟失敗時執行）。且此選項錯誤地將 workflow 關聯到 SFTP user 而非 Transfer Family server。私鑰部分正確，但其餘兩處錯誤使其不成立。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it is wrong on three counts: it stores the public key (decryption needs the private key), it uses an exception-handling step (decrypt is a nominal step), and it associates the workflow with the SFTP user (the workflow is associated with the server).","why_zh":"這是 dump 建議的答案，但有三處錯誤：儲存公鑰（解密需要私鑰）、使用例外處理步驟（decrypt 為 nominal 步驟）、以及將 workflow 關聯到 SFTP user（workflow 應關聯到 server）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transfer/latest/userguide/workflow-decrypt-tutorial.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transfer/latest/userguide/manage-pgp-keys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transfer/latest/userguide/key-management.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":483,"question_en":"A company is migrating infrastructure for its massive multiplayer game to AWS. The game’s application features a leaderboard where players can see rankings in real time. The leaderboard requires microsecond reads and single-digit-millisecond write latencies. The datasets are single-digit terabytes in size and must be available to accept writes in less than a minute if a primary node failure occurs. The company needs a solution in which data can persist for further analytical processing through a data pipeline. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在将其大型多人游戏的基础设施迁移到 AWS。该游戏的应用程序具有一个排行榜功能，玩家可以借此实时查看排名。该排行榜要求读取延迟达到微秒级，写入延迟达到个位数毫秒级。数据集大小为个位数 TB 级别，并且在主节点发生故障时，必须能够在一分钟内恢复写入能力。该公司需要一种解决方案，使数据能够持久保存，以便通过数据管道进行进一步的分析处理。哪种解决方案能以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"B":"Create an Amazon ROS database with a read replica. Configure the application to point writes to the writer endpoint. Configure the application to point reads to the reader endpoint.","C":"Create an Amazon MemoryDB for Redis cluster in Muit-AZ mode Configure the application to interact with the primary node.","D":"Create multiple Redis nodes on Amazon EC2 instances that are spread across multiple Availability Zones. Configure backups to Amazon S3."},"options_zh":{"B":"创建一个带有读取副本的 Amazon RDS 数据库。将应用程序配置为将写入操作指向写入端点，将读取操作指向读取端点。","C":"以多可用区模式创建一个 Amazon MemoryDB for Redis 集群。将应用程序配置为与主节点进行交互。","D":"在跨多个可用区分布的 Amazon EC2 实例上创建多个 Redis 节点，并将备份配置为存储到 Amazon S3。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The deciding requirement is 'microsecond reads and single-digit-millisecond write latency' combined with durable persistence, automatic failover in under a minute, and least operational overhead. Amazon MemoryDB for Redis is the only fully managed AWS service that the documentation explicitly describes as delivering 'microsecond read and single-digit millisecond write latency' while storing data 'durably across multiple Availability Zones using a Multi-AZ transactional log.' In Multi-AZ mode, primary node failover to a consistent replica completes in 'just a few seconds' (well under one minute) with no data loss. Data also persists durably for downstream analytical processing via a data pipeline. Option C is therefore correct and lowest operational overhead because MemoryDB is fully managed (no node/backup management). The dump's suggested answer B is wrong: RDS is a disk-based relational database and cannot deliver microsecond reads. Option D requires self-managing Redis on EC2 with manual S3 backups, which fails the durability/in-minute-write guarantee and has the highest operational overhead.","explanation_zh":"決定性需求是『microsecond 讀取與個位數 millisecond 寫入延遲』，再加上資料持久化、主節點故障時一分鐘內可恢復寫入，且維運負擔最低。Amazon MemoryDB for Redis 是 AWS 文件中唯一明確描述能提供『microsecond read and single-digit millisecond write latency』，同時透過 Multi-AZ transactional log『跨多個 Availability Zones 持久化儲存資料』的全託管服務。在 Multi-AZ 模式下，主節點故障切換至一致的 replica 僅需『幾秒鐘』（遠低於一分鐘）且不會遺失資料。資料也能持久化，供後續資料管線進行分析處理。因此選項 C 正確且維運負擔最低，因為 MemoryDB 是全託管（無需管理節點或備份）。Dump 建議答案 B 錯誤：RDS 是磁碟型關聯式資料庫，無法提供 microsecond 讀取。選項 D 需自行在 EC2 上管理 Redis 並手動備份至 S3，無法滿足持久化/一分鐘內寫入的保證，且維運負擔最高。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon RDS is a disk-based relational database; it cannot deliver microsecond read latency. Read replicas serve eventually-consistent reads and do not provide the in-memory microsecond performance required by a real-time leaderboard.","why_zh":"Amazon RDS 是磁碟型關聯式資料庫，無法提供 microsecond 讀取延遲。Read replica 提供最終一致讀取，無法達到即時排行榜所需的記憶體內 microsecond 效能。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Self-managed Redis on EC2 with S3 backups places all operational burden (patching, scaling, failover orchestration, backup management) on the company. Restoring from S3 backups cannot guarantee resuming writes in under a minute, and it lacks the durable Multi-AZ transactional log that MemoryDB provides. Highest operational overhead.","why_zh":"在 EC2 上自管 Redis 並備份至 S3，會將所有維運負擔（修補、擴展、故障切換協調、備份管理）交給公司。從 S3 備份還原無法保證一分鐘內恢復寫入，且缺乏 MemoryDB 提供的持久化 Multi-AZ transactional log。維運負擔最高。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/memorydb/latest/devguide/what-is-memorydb.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/memorydb/latest/devguide/autofailover.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":484,"question_en":"A company is running several applications in the AWS Cloud. The applications are specific to separate business units in the company. The company is running the components of the applications in several AWS accounts that are in an organization in AWS Organizations. Every cloud resource in the company’s organization has a tag that is named BusinessUnit. Every tag already has the appropriate value of the business unit name. The company needs to allocate its cloud costs to different business units. The company also needs to visualize the cloud costs for each business unit. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 云中运行多个应用程序，这些应用程序分别对应公司内不同的业务部门。该公司在 AWS Organizations 组织中的多个 AWS 账户中运行这些应用程序的组件。该公司组织中的每个云资源都带有一个名为 BusinessUnit 的标签，且每个标签都已具有相应的业务部门名称值。该公司需要将其云成本分配给不同的业务部门，同时还需要将每个业务部门的云成本可视化。哪种解决方案能够满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"In the organization's management account, create a cost allocation tag that is named BusinessUnit. Also in the management account, create an Amazon S3 bucket and an AWS Cost and Usage Report (AWS CUR). Configure the S3 bucket as the destination for the AWS CUR. From the management account, query the AWS CUR data by using Amazon Athena. Use Amazon QuickSight for visualization.","B":"In each member account, create a cost allocation tag that is named BusinessUnit. In the organization’s management account, create an Amazon S3 bucket and an AWS Cost and Usage Report (AWS CUR). Configure the S3 bucket as the destination for the AWS CUR. Create an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard for visualization.","C":"In the organization's management account, create a cost allocation tag that is named BusinessUnit. In each member account, create an Amazon S3 bucket and an AWS Cost and Usage Report (AWS CUR). Configure each S3 bucket as the destination for its respective AWS CUR. In the management account, create an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard for visualization.","D":"In each member account, create a cost allocation tag that is named BusinessUnit. Also in each member account, create an Amazon S3 bucket and an AWS Cost and Usage Report (AWS CUR). Configure each S3 bucket as the destination for its respective AWS CUR. From the management account, query the AWS CUR data by using Amazon Athena. Use Amazon QuickSight for visualization."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织的管理账户中创建一个名为 BusinessUnit 的成本分配标签。同样在管理账户中创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶和一个 AWS Cost and Usage Report (AWS CUR)。将该 S3 存储桶配置为 AWS CUR 的目标位置。从管理账户中使用 Amazon Athena 查询 AWS CUR 数据，并使用 Amazon QuickSight 进行可视化。","B":"在每个成员账户中创建一个名为 BusinessUnit 的成本分配标签。在组织的管理账户中创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶和一个 AWS Cost and Usage Report (AWS CUR)，并将该 S3 存储桶配置为 AWS CUR 的目标位置。创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 仪表板进行可视化。","C":"在组织的管理账户中创建一个名为 BusinessUnit 的成本分配标签。在每个成员账户中创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶和一个 AWS Cost and Usage Report (AWS CUR)，并将每个 S3 存储桶配置为其对应 AWS CUR 的目标位置。在管理账户中创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 仪表板进行可视化。","D":"在每个成员账户中创建一个名为 BusinessUnit 的成本分配标签。同样在每个成员账户中创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶和一个 AWS Cost and Usage Report (AWS CUR)，并将每个 S3 存储桶配置为其对应 AWS CUR 的目标位置。从管理账户中使用 Amazon Athena 查询 AWS CUR 数据，并使用 Amazon QuickSight 进行可视化。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Cost allocation tags can only be created/activated by the organization's management account. AWS Billing docs state: 'Only a management account in an organization and single accounts that aren't members of an organization have access to the cost allocation tags manager in the Billing and Cost Management console.' This eliminates options B and D, which create the BusinessUnit cost allocation tag in each member account (member accounts cannot do this). Between A and C, a single AWS CUR in the management account already covers the entire organization through consolidated billing, so per-member-account CURs (option C) are unnecessary and fragmented. For visualization, CUR data delivered to S3 is queried with Amazon Athena and visualized with Amazon QuickSight; Amazon CloudWatch dashboards (options B and C) cannot visualize CUR billing data stored in S3. Option A correctly activates the tag in the management account, delivers a single org-wide CUR to an S3 bucket, queries it with Athena, and visualizes with QuickSight.","explanation_zh":"Cost allocation tags 只能由 organization 的 management account 建立與啟用。AWS Billing 文件明確指出:'Only a management account in an organization and single accounts that aren't members of an organization have access to the cost allocation tags manager in the Billing and Cost Management console.' 這直接排除 B 和 D,因為它們在各 member account 建立 BusinessUnit cost allocation tag(member account 無法執行此操作)。在 A 與 C 之間,management account 的單一 AWS CUR 已透過 consolidated billing 涵蓋整個 organization,所以在每個 member account 各建一份 CUR(選項 C)既多餘又分散。視覺化方面,交付到 S3 的 CUR 資料須以 Amazon Athena 查詢、以 Amazon QuickSight 視覺化;Amazon CloudWatch dashboard(選項 B 與 C)無法視覺化儲存在 S3 的 CUR 帳務資料。選項 A 正確地在 management account 啟用標籤、將單一全組織 CUR 交付至 S3 bucket、以 Athena 查詢、並以 QuickSight 視覺化。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Creates the cost allocation tag in each member account, but only the management account can access/activate cost allocation tags. Also uses a CloudWatch dashboard, which cannot visualize CUR data stored in S3.","why_zh":"在各 member account 建立 cost allocation tag,但只有 management account 能存取/啟用 cost allocation tags。且使用 CloudWatch dashboard,無法視覺化儲存於 S3 的 CUR 資料。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Activates the tag in the management account (correct), but creates a separate S3 bucket and CUR in each member account, which is unnecessary because a single management-account CUR already aggregates all member accounts via consolidated billing. It also uses a CloudWatch dashboard, which cannot visualize S3-based CUR data.","why_zh":"在 management account 啟用標籤(正確),但在每個 member account 各建 S3 bucket 與 CUR,屬多餘——單一 management account 的 CUR 已透過 consolidated billing 彙整所有 member account。且使用 CloudWatch dashboard,無法視覺化 S3 上的 CUR 資料。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creates the cost allocation tag in each member account, which is impossible since only the management account can manage cost allocation tags. Per-member-account CURs are also unnecessary given consolidated billing.","why_zh":"在各 member account 建立 cost allocation tag,屬不可行,因為僅 management account 能管理 cost allocation tags。鑑於 consolidated billing,每個 member account 各建 CUR 也屬多餘。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/custom-tags.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/activating-tags.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cur/latest/userguide/cur-query-athena.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cur/latest/userguide/what-is-cur.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":485,"question_en":"A utility company wants to collect usage data every 5 minutes from its smart meters to facilitate time-of-use metering. When a meter sends data to AWS, the data is sent to Amazon API Gateway, processed by an AWS Lambda function. and stored in an Amazon DynamoDB table. During the pilot phase, the Lambda functions took from 3 to 5 seconds to complete. As more smart meters are deployed, the engineers notice the Lambda functions are taking from 1 to 2 minutes to complete. The functions are also increasing in duration as new types of metrics are collected from the devices. There are many ProvisionedThroughputExceededException errors while performing PUT operations on DynamoDB, and there are also many TooManyRequestsException errors from Lambda. Which combination of changes will resolve these issues? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公用事业公司希望每 5 分钟从其智能电表收集一次用量数据，以支持分时电价计量。当电表将数据发送到 AWS 时，数据会被发送到 Amazon API Gateway，由一个 AWS Lambda 函数进行处理，并存储在一个 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。在试点阶段，Lambda 函数的完成时间为 3 到 5 秒。随着更多智能电表的部署，工程师们发现 Lambda 函数的完成时间增加到了 1 到 2 分钟。随着从设备收集的指标类型增多，函数的执行时长也在不断增加。在对 DynamoDB 执行 PUT 操作时出现了大量 ProvisionedThroughputExceededException 错误，Lambda 也出现了大量 TooManyRequestsException 错误。哪种组合变更能够解决这些问题？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Increase the write capacity units to the DynamoDB table.","B":"Increase the memory available to the Lambda functions.","C":"Increase the payload size from the smart meters to send more data.","D":"Stream the data into an Amazon Kinesis data stream from API Gateway and process the data in batches.","E":"Collect data in an Amazon SQS FIFO queue, which triggers a Lambda function to process each message"},"options_zh":{"A":"增加 DynamoDB 表的写入容量单位。","B":"增加 Lambda 函数可用的内存。","C":"增加智能电表发送数据的有效负载大小，以发送更多数据。","D":"将数据从 API Gateway 流式传输到 Amazon Kinesis 数据流中，并批量处理数据。","E":"将数据收集到一个 Amazon SQS FIFO 队列中，由该队列触发一个 Lambda 函数来处理每条消息。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AD":100},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"There are two distinct throttling symptoms. (1) ProvisionedThroughputExceededException on DynamoDB PUTs is a pure write-capacity throttle, fixed by increasing write capacity units (or enabling auto scaling/on-demand) - Option A. (2) TooManyRequestsException (HTTP 429) from Lambda is a concurrency throttle: the synchronous API Gateway->Lambda model invokes one function per meter, and because durations grew from 3-5s to 1-2min, concurrent executions (invocation rate x duration) exceed the account concurrency limit. Option D streams meter data into Kinesis and processes it with a stream event-source mapping, which invokes Lambda once per shard batch instead of once per request. This collapses the concurrent invocation count (eliminating the 429s) and lets the function batch/smooth writes (e.g., BatchWriteItem) to DynamoDB, while Kinesis buffers bursts and provides back-pressure. Together A+D resolve both errors. Option B (more memory) gives more CPU but does not raise Lambda's concurrency limit and does not decouple the per-request invocation model, so it does not resolve the TooManyRequestsException root cause and does nothing for the DynamoDB write rate; the dump's A+B therefore fails on the Lambda half.","explanation_zh":"題目有兩個不同的限流症狀。(1) DynamoDB PUT 的 ProvisionedThroughputExceededException 是純粹的寫入容量限流,解法是提高 write capacity units(或啟用 auto scaling/on-demand),即選項 A。(2) Lambda 的 TooManyRequestsException(HTTP 429)是並行(concurrency)限流:同步的 API Gateway->Lambda 模型每個電表觸發一個函數,而執行時間從 3-5 秒增加到 1-2 分鐘,使得並行執行數(呼叫率 x 執行時間)超過帳號 concurrency 上限。選項 D 將資料串流進 Kinesis Data Stream,改以 stream event source mapping 批次處理,Lambda 每個 shard batch 只呼叫一次而非每個請求一次,大幅降低並行呼叫數(消除 429),並可批次/平滑寫入 DynamoDB(如 BatchWriteItem),同時 Kinesis 提供緩衝與 back-pressure。A+D 同時解決兩個錯誤。選項 B(增加記憶體)只提供更多 CPU,並不會提高 Lambda concurrency 上限,也不會改變每請求一次的呼叫模型,因此無法解決 TooManyRequestsException 的根因,對 DynamoDB 寫入率也毫無幫助;dump 的 A+B 在 Lambda 這半邊失敗。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Increasing memory adds CPU and may slightly reduce duration, but it does not raise Lambda's concurrency limit nor decouple the one-invocation-per-request model, so it does not resolve the TooManyRequestsException concurrency throttle, and it does nothing for DynamoDB write throughput.","why_zh":"增加記憶體會提升 CPU 並可能略微縮短執行時間,但不會提高 Lambda 的 concurrency 上限,也不會解除每請求一次的呼叫模型,因此無法解決 TooManyRequestsException 的並行限流,對 DynamoDB 寫入吞吐量也無幫助。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Sending larger payloads increases per-invocation work and data written, making both Lambda durations and DynamoDB write pressure worse, not better.","why_zh":"傳送更大的 payload 會增加每次呼叫的處理量與寫入資料量,使 Lambda 執行時間與 DynamoDB 寫入壓力更糟,而非改善。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"SQS FIFO has a hard throughput cap (300 msg/s, 3,000 with batching per message group) unsuitable for high-volume telemetry, ordering is not required here, and triggering Lambda per message keeps the per-record invocation pattern that causes the throttling. A standard queue might help, but FIFO is the wrong tool and Kinesis batching (D) is the intended decoupling solution.","why_zh":"SQS FIFO 有硬性吞吐量上限(每秒 300 則,批次可達每訊息群組 3,000 則),不適合大量遙測資料,本情境也不需要排序,且每則訊息觸發一次 Lambda 仍維持造成限流的逐筆呼叫模式。標準佇列或許有幫助,但 FIFO 是錯誤工具,Kinesis 批次(D)才是預期的解耦方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/scaling-behavior.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-kinesis.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-kinesis-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/AutoScaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/botocore/latest/reference/services/dynamodb/client/exceptions/ProvisionedThroughputExceededException.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":486,"question_en":"A company recently completed a successful proof of concept of Amazon WorkSpaces. A solutions architect needs to make the solution highly available across two AWS Regions. Amazon WorkSpaces is deployed in a failover Region, and a hosted zone is deployed in Amazon Route 53. What should the solutions architect do to configure high availability for the solution?","question_zh":"一家公司最近成功完成了 Amazon WorkSpaces 的概念验证。解决方案架构师需要使该解决方案在两个 AWS 区域之间实现高可用性。Amazon WorkSpaces 已部署在故障转移区域中，并且已在 Amazon Route 53 中部署了一个托管区域。解决方案架构师应该怎样做才能为该解决方案配置高可用性？","options_en":{"A":"Create a connection alias in the primary Region and in the failover Region. Associate the connection aliases with a directory in each Region. Create a Route 53 failover routing policy. Set Evaluate Target Health to Yes.","B":"Create a connection alias in the primary Region and in the failover Region. Associate the connection aliases with a directory in the primary Region. Create a Route 53 multivalue answer routing policy.","C":"Create a connection alias in the primary Region. Associate the connection alias with a directory in the primary Region. Create a Route 53 weighted routing policy.","D":"Create a connection alias in the primary Region Associate the connection alias with a directory in the failover Region. Create a Route 53 failover routing policy. Set Evaluate Target Health to Yes."},"options_zh":{"A":"在主区域和故障转移区域中分别创建连接别名，并将这些连接别名与各自区域中的目录相关联。创建一个 Route 53 故障转移路由策略，并将 Evaluate Target Health 设置为 Yes。","B":"在主区域和故障转移区域中分别创建连接别名，并将这些连接别名与主区域中的目录相关联。创建一个 Route 53 多值应答路由策略。","C":"在主区域中创建一个连接别名，并将该连接别名与主区域中的目录相关联。创建一个 Route 53 加权路由策略。","D":"在主区域中创建一个连接别名，并将该连接别名与故障转移区域中的目录相关联。创建一个 Route 53 故障转移路由策略，并将 Evaluate Target Health 设置为 Yes。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":72,"D":28},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Amazon WorkSpaces cross-Region redirection is the feature that provides regional resiliency/HA. Per the AWS admin guide, you must (Step 1) create connection aliases in EACH primary and failover Region using the same AWS account, (Step 3) associate the SAME connection alias with a WorkSpaces directory in EACH Region (creating an association pair), and (Step 4) configure a Route 53 failover routing policy with a health check on the primary Region. Option A is the only choice that creates aliases in both Regions, associates them with a directory in each Region, and uses a failover routing policy, so it matches the documented procedure. Option D (the dump answer) is wrong because it creates the alias in only one Region and associates it only with the failover Region directory; a connection alias is a regional resource that must exist in, and be associated with a directory in, each Region for cross-Region redirection to work.","explanation_zh":"Amazon WorkSpaces 的跨區域重新導向 (cross-Region redirection) 功能才能提供區域韌性與高可用性。依官方管理員指南：步驟 1 必須以同一個 AWS 帳戶在「每個」主要與容錯移轉區域建立 connection alias；步驟 3 必須把「同一個」connection alias 與「每個」區域中的 WorkSpaces directory 建立關聯 (形成 association pair)；步驟 4 在 Route 53 設定 failover routing policy，並在主要區域設定 health check。選項 A 是唯一同時在兩個區域建立 alias、在每個區域關聯 directory、並使用 failover routing policy 的答案，完全符合文件流程。選項 D (dump 標示答案) 錯誤，因為它只在一個區域建立 alias 且只關聯到容錯移轉區域的 directory；connection alias 是區域性資源，必須在每個區域內存在並與該區域的 directory 關聯，跨區域重新導向才能運作。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A multivalue answer routing policy returns multiple healthy records randomly; it does not implement active-passive failover. Also it associates the aliases only with a directory in the primary Region, which leaves no failover association.","why_zh":"Multivalue answer routing policy 會隨機回傳多筆健康紀錄，無法實作主動-被動的容錯移轉；而且它只把 alias 關聯到主要區域的 directory，沒有容錯移轉區域的關聯。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"It only creates an alias and associates a directory in the primary Region with weighted routing, so there is no failover Region setup at all and no high availability across Regions.","why_zh":"它只在主要區域建立 alias 並關聯 directory、使用 weighted routing，完全沒有設定容錯移轉區域，無法達成跨區域高可用性。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Marked dump answer but wrong: it creates the connection alias in only the primary Region and associates it with a directory only in the failover Region. The docs require creating aliases in EACH Region and associating the same alias with a directory in EACH Region (primary and failover) to form the association pair.","why_zh":"Dump 標示答案但錯誤：它只在主要區域建立 connection alias，且只把它關聯到容錯移轉區域的 directory。文件要求在「每個」區域建立 alias，並把同一個 alias 關聯到「每個」區域 (主要與容錯移轉) 的 directory 以形成 association pair。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/workspaces/latest/adminguide/cross-region-redirection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy.html"]},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":487,"question_en":"A company plans to migrate many VMs from an on-premises environment to AWS. The company requires an initial assessment of the on- premises environment before the migration, a visualization of the dependencies between applications that run on the VMs, and a report that provides an assessment of the on-premises environment. To get this information, the company has initiated a Migration Evaluator assessment request. The company has the ability to install collector software in its on-premises environment without any constraints Which solution will provide the company with the required information with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司计划将许多虚拟机从本地环境迁移到 AWS。该公司在迁移之前需要对本地环境进行初步评估，需要可视化展示虚拟机上运行的应用程序之间的依赖关系，还需要一份提供本地环境评估结果的报告。为获取这些信息，该公司已发起了一个 Migration Evaluator 评估请求。该公司能够在其本地环境中不受任何限制地安装收集器软件。哪种解决方案能以最少的运营开销为该公司提供所需信息？","options_en":{"A":"Install the AWS Application Discovery Agent on each on-premises VM. After the data collection period ends, use AWS Migration Hub to view the application dependencies. Download the Quick insights assessment report from Migration Hub.","B":"Install the Migration Evaluator Collector on each on-premises VM. After the data collection period ends, use Migration Evaluator to view the application dependencies. Download and export the discovered server list from Migration Evaluator. Upload the list to Amazon QuickSight When the QuickSight report is generated, download the Quick Insights assessment report.","C":"Setup the AWS Application Discovery Service Agentless Collector in the on-premises environment. After the data collection period ends, use AWS Migration Hub to view the application dependencies. Export the discovered server list from Application Discovery Service. Upload the list to Migration Evaluator. When the Migration Evaluator report is generated, download the Quick Insights assessment.","D":"Set up the Migration Evaluator Collector in the on-premises environment. Install the AWS Application Discovery Agent on each VM. After the data collection period ends, use AWS Migration Hub to view the application dependencies. Download the Quick Insights assessment report from Migration Evaluator."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个本地虚拟机上安装 AWS Application Discovery Agent。数据收集周期结束后，使用 AWS Migration Hub 查看应用程序依赖关系，并从 Migration Hub 下载 Quick Insights 评估报告。","B":"在每个本地虚拟机上安装 Migration Evaluator Collector。数据收集周期结束后，使用 Migration Evaluator 查看应用程序依赖关系，从 Migration Evaluator 下载并导出已发现的服务器列表，然后将该列表上传到 Amazon QuickSight。生成 QuickSight 报告后，下载 Quick Insights 评估报告。","C":"在本地环境中设置 AWS Application Discovery Service Agentless Collector。数据收集周期结束后，使用 AWS Migration Hub 查看应用程序依赖关系，从 Application Discovery Service 导出已发现的服务器列表，然后将该列表上传到 Migration Evaluator。生成 Migration Evaluator 报告后，下载 Quick Insights 评估结果。","D":"在本地环境中设置 Migration Evaluator Collector，并在每个虚拟机上安装 AWS Application Discovery Agent。数据收集周期结束后，使用 AWS Migration Hub 查看应用程序依赖关系，并从 Migration Evaluator 下载 Quick Insights 评估报告。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":56,"A":44},"tags":["Migration","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The qualifier is LEAST operational overhead, and the answer must correctly attribute two deliverables: (1) application dependency visualization comes from AWS Migration Hub (the Application Discovery Service Agentless Collector's Network Data Collection module discovers server-to-server dependencies and gives visibility into how applications communicate, surfaced in Migration Hub), and (2) the 'Quick Insights' assessment report is a Migration Evaluator deliverable, not a Migration Hub artifact. Option C is the only internally consistent flow: deploy the agentless ADS collector (no per-VM agent = least overhead), view dependencies in Migration Hub, export the discovered server list into Migration Evaluator (already engaged), and download the Quick Insights assessment from Migration Evaluator. Option A is wrong because it requires installing the Discovery Agent on every VM (more overhead than agentless) and incorrectly claims to download the Quick Insights report from Migration Hub. Option B falsely states the Migration Evaluator Collector is installed on each VM (it is agentless), wrongly uses Migration Evaluator for dependency visualization, and invents a QuickSight step. Option D deploys BOTH the Migration Evaluator collector and an agent on every VM, which is the highest operational overhead, directly contradicting the qualifier.","explanation_zh":"本題限定詞是 LEAST operational overhead（最少維運負擔），且正確答案必須正確歸屬兩項產出：(1) 應用程式相依性視覺化來自 AWS Migration Hub（Application Discovery Service 的 Agentless Collector 的 Network Data Collection 模組會探索伺服器間相依性，呈現應用程式如何跨伺服器溝通，並在 Migration Hub 中檢視）；(2)『Quick Insights』評估報告是 Migration Evaluator 的產出，而非 Migration Hub 的產物。選項 C 是唯一邏輯一致的流程：部署無代理程式的 ADS Agentless Collector（不需在每台 VM 安裝代理程式，維運負擔最低），在 Migration Hub 檢視相依性，將探索到的伺服器清單匯出至已啟動的 Migration Evaluator，再由 Migration Evaluator 產生並下載 Quick Insights 評估。選項 A 錯誤，因為需在每台 VM 安裝 Discovery Agent（比無代理程式負擔更高），且錯誤宣稱可從 Migration Hub 下載 Quick Insights 報告。選項 B 錯誤聲稱 Migration Evaluator Collector 安裝在每台 VM（實際上是無代理程式），且錯誤用 Migration Evaluator 做相依性視覺化，並虛構 QuickSight 步驟。選項 D 同時部署 Migration Evaluator collector 與在每台 VM 安裝代理程式，維運負擔最高，直接違反限定詞。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Installing the Discovery Agent on every VM is more operational overhead than agentless collection, and the Quick Insights assessment report is a Migration Evaluator deliverable, not something downloaded from Migration Hub.","why_zh":"在每台 VM 安裝 Discovery Agent 比無代理程式蒐集負擔更高，且 Quick Insights 評估報告是 Migration Evaluator 的產出，並非從 Migration Hub 下載。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The Migration Evaluator Collector is agentless and is not installed on each VM; dependency visualization is provided by Migration Hub (not Migration Evaluator); and uploading the server list to QuickSight to generate Quick Insights is fabricated.","why_zh":"Migration Evaluator Collector 是無代理程式，不需安裝在每台 VM；相依性視覺化由 Migration Hub 提供（非 Migration Evaluator）；將伺服器清單上傳至 QuickSight 以產生 Quick Insights 為虛構流程。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Deploying both the Migration Evaluator Collector and the Discovery Agent on every VM is the highest operational overhead, directly contradicting the LEAST operational overhead requirement, even though it correctly attributes Quick Insights to Migration Evaluator.","why_zh":"同時部署 Migration Evaluator Collector 與在每台 VM 安裝 Discovery Agent 為最高維運負擔，直接違反『最少維運負擔』要求，即使其將 Quick Insights 正確歸屬於 Migration Evaluator。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/migration-tools/discovery-migration-evaluator.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/what-is-appdiscovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/agentless-collector-gs-network-data-collection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/discovery-agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/dashboard.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":488,"question_en":"A company hosts its primary API on AWS by using an Amazon API Gateway API and AWS Lambda functions that contain the logic for the API methods. The company’s internal applications use the API for core functionality and business logic. The company’s customers use the API to access data from their accounts. Several customers also have access to a legacy API that is running on a single standalone Amazon EC2 instance. The company wants to increase the security for these APIs to better prevent denial of service (DoS) attacks, check for vulnerabilities, and guard against common exploits. What should a solutions architect do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 Amazon API Gateway API 和包含 API 方法逻辑的 AWS Lambda 函数在 AWS 上托管其主要 API。该公司的内部应用程序使用该 API 来实现核心功能和业务逻辑。该公司的客户使用该 API 访问其账户中的数据。部分客户还可以访问运行在单个独立 Amazon EC2 实例上的旧版 API。该公司希望提高这些 API 的安全性，以更好地防止拒绝服务 (DoS) 攻击、检查漏洞，并防范常见的攻击利用手段。解决方案架构师应该怎么做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS WAF to protect both APIs. Configure Amazon Inspector to analyze the legacy API. Configure Amazon GuardDuty to monitor for malicious attempts to access the APIs.","B":"Use AWS WAF to protect the API Gateway API. Configure Amazon Inspector to analyze both APIs. Configure Amazon GuardDuty to block malicious attempts to access the APIs.","C":"Use AWS WAF to protect the API Gateway API. Configure Amazon Inspector to analyze the legacy API. Configure Amazon GuardDuty to monitor for malicious attempts to access the APIs.","D":"Use AWS WAF to protect the API Gateway AP! Configure Amazon Inspector to protect the legacy API. Configure Amazon GuardDuty to block malicious attempts to access the APIs."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS WAF 保护这两个 API。配置 Amazon Inspector 来分析旧版 API。配置 Amazon GuardDuty 来监控针对这些 API 的恶意访问尝试。","B":"使用 AWS WAF 保护 API Gateway API。配置 Amazon Inspector 来分析这两个 API。配置 Amazon GuardDuty 来阻止针对这些 API 的恶意访问尝试。","C":"使用 AWS WAF 保护 API Gateway API。配置 Amazon Inspector 来分析旧版 API。配置 Amazon GuardDuty 来监控针对这些 API 的恶意访问尝试。","D":"使用 AWS WAF 保护 API Gateway API。配置 Amazon Inspector 来保护旧版 API。配置 Amazon GuardDuty 来阻止针对这些 API 的恶意访问尝试。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":80,"A":20},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":489,"question_en":"A company is running a serverless ecommerce application on AWS. The application uses Amazon API Gateway to invoke AWS Lambda Java functions. The Lambda functions connect to an Amazon RDS for MySQL database to store data. During a recent sale event, a sudden increase in web tra®c resulted in poor API performance and database connection failures. The company needs to implement a solution to minimize the latency for the Lambda functions and to support bursts in tra®c. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST amount of change to the application?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上运行一个无服务器电子商务应用程序。该应用程序使用 Amazon API Gateway 调用 AWS Lambda Java 函数，这些 Lambda 函数连接到 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库以存储数据。在最近一次促销活动期间，Web 流量的突然增加导致 API 性能下降和数据库连接失败。该公司需要实施一种解决方案，以最大限度地降低 Lambda 函数的延迟并支持突发流量。哪种解决方案能以最少的应用程序改动量满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Update the code of the Lambda functions so that the Lambda functions open the database connection outside of the function handler. Increase the provisioned concurrency for the Lambda functions.","B":"Create an RDS Proxy endpoint for the database. Store database secrets in AWS Secrets Manager. Set up the required IAM permissions. Update the Lambda functions to connect to the RDS Proxy endpoint. Increase the provisioned concurrency for the Lambda functions.","C":"Create a custom parameter group. Increase the value of the max_connections parameter. Associate the custom parameter group with the RDS DB instance and schedule a reboot. Increase the reserved concurrency for the Lambda functions.","D":"Create an RDS Proxy endpoint for the database. Store database secrets in AWS Secrets Manager. Set up the required IAM permissions. Update the Lambda functions to connect to the RDS Proxy endpoint. Increase the reserved concurrency for the Lambda functions."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新 Lambda 函数的代码，使 Lambda 函数在函数处理程序之外打开数据库连接，并增加 Lambda 函数的预置并发量。","B":"为数据库创建一个 RDS Proxy 端点，将数据库凭据存储在 AWS Secrets Manager 中，并设置所需的 IAM 权限。更新 Lambda 函数以连接到该 RDS Proxy 端点，并增加 Lambda 函数的预置并发量。","C":"创建一个自定义参数组，增加 max_connections 参数的值，将该自定义参数组与 RDS 数据库实例关联并安排重启。增加 Lambda 函数的预留并发量。","D":"为数据库创建一个 RDS Proxy 端点，将数据库凭据存储在 AWS Secrets Manager 中，并设置所需的 IAM 权限。更新 Lambda 函数以连接到该 RDS Proxy 端点，并增加 Lambda 函数的预留并发量。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":54,"D":31,"A":15},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識・多選項拉鋸"},{"id":490,"question_en":"A company requires that all internal application connectivity use private IP addresses. To facilitate this policy, a solutions architect has created interface endpoints to connect to AWS Public services. Upon testing, the solutions architect notices that the service names are resolving to public IP addresses, and that internal services cannot connect to the interface endpoints. Which step should the solutions architect take to resolve this issue?","question_zh":"一家公司要求所有内部应用程序连接都必须使用私有 IP 地址。为实现该策略，解决方案架构师创建了接口端点以连接到 AWS 公共服务。测试时，解决方案架构师发现服务名称解析为公共 IP 地址，导致内部服务无法连接到这些接口端点。解决方案架构师应采取哪个步骤来解决此问题？","options_en":{"A":"Update the subnet route table with a route to the interface endpoint.","B":"Enable the private DNS option on the VPC attributes.","C":"Configure the security group on the interface endpoint to allow connectivity to the AWS services.","D":"Configure an Amazon Route 53 private hosted zone with a conditional forwarder for the internal application."},"options_zh":{"A":"在子网路由表中添加一条指向该接口端点的路由。","B":"在 VPC 属性中启用私有 DNS 选项。","C":"在接口端点上配置安全组，以允许连接到相应的 AWS 服务。","D":"为内部应用程序配置一个带有条件转发器的 Amazon Route 53 私有托管区域。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":491,"question_en":"A company is developing a latency-sensitive application. Part of the application includes several AWS Lambda functions that need to initialize as quickly as possible. The Lambda functions are written in Java and contain initialization code outside the handlers to load libraries, initialize classes, and generate unique IDs. Which solution will meet the startup performance requirement MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司正在开发一个对延迟敏感的应用程序。该应用程序的一部分包含若干 AWS Lambda 函数，这些函数需要尽可能快速地完成初始化。这些 Lambda 函数使用 Java 编写，并在处理程序之外包含用于加载库、初始化类和生成唯一 ID 的初始化代码。哪种解决方案能以最具成本效益的方式满足启动性能要求？","options_en":{"A":"Move all the initialization code to the handlers for each Lambda function. Activate Lambda SnapStart for each Lambda function. Configure SnapStart to reference the $LATEST version of each Lambda function.","B":"Publish a version of each Lambda function. Create an alias for each Lambda function. Configure each alias to point to its corresponding version. Set up a provisioned concurrency configuration for each Lambda function to point to the corresponding alias.","C":"Publish a version of each Lambda function. Set up a provisioned concurrency configuration for each Lambda function to point to the corresponding version. Activate Lambda SnapStar for the published versions of the Lambda functions.","D":"Update the Lambda functions to add a pre-snapshot hook. Move the code that generates unique IDs into the handlers. Publish a version of each Lambda function. Activate Lambda SnapStart for the published versions of the Lambda functions."},"options_zh":{"A":"将所有初始化代码移动到每个 Lambda 函数的处理程序中。为每个 Lambda 函数激活 Lambda SnapStart，并将 SnapStart 配置为引用每个 Lambda 函数的 $LATEST 版本。","B":"为每个 Lambda 函数发布一个版本，并为每个 Lambda 函数创建一个别名，将该别名配置为指向对应的版本。为每个 Lambda 函数设置预置并发配置，使其指向对应的别名。","C":"为每个 Lambda 函数发布一个版本，为每个 Lambda 函数设置预置并发配置，使其指向对应的版本，并为这些已发布版本的 Lambda 函数激活 Lambda SnapStart。","D":"更新 Lambda 函数以添加一个快照前挂钩 (pre-snapshot hook)。将生成唯一 ID 的代码移动到处理程序中，为每个 Lambda 函数发布一个版本，并为这些已发布版本的 Lambda 函数激活 Lambda SnapStart。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":62,"C":38},"tags":["Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"For Java managed runtimes, Lambda SnapStart has no additional cost, making it the most cost-effective way to reduce cold-start latency, whereas provisioned concurrency (options B and C) charges continuously to keep environments warm. SnapStart can only be enabled on published function versions or aliases pointing to versions, not on $LATEST, and it is mutually exclusive with provisioned concurrency. The function's expensive init code (loading libraries, initializing classes) should remain outside the handler so SnapStart can capture it in the Firecracker snapshot; only the unique-ID generation must be made snapshot-safe by moving it into the handler or using a runtime (pre-snapshot/after-restore) hook, per AWS uniqueness guidance. Option D does exactly this: adds a pre-snapshot hook, moves unique-ID generation into the handlers, publishes versions, and activates SnapStart on those published versions, satisfying the startup-performance requirement at no extra SnapStart cost.","explanation_zh":"對於 Java 受管 runtime，Lambda SnapStart 不收取額外費用，是降低冷啟動延遲最具成本效益的方式；而 provisioned concurrency（選項 B 和 C）會持續收費以維持環境暖機。SnapStart 只能在已發佈的 function 版本或指向版本的 alias 上啟用，無法用於 $LATEST，且與 provisioned concurrency 互斥。函式昂貴的初始化程式碼（載入函式庫、初始化類別）應保留在 handler 之外，讓 SnapStart 能在 Firecracker 快照中擷取；只有產生 unique ID 的部分需要做快照安全處理，依 AWS uniqueness 指引應移到 handler 內或使用 runtime（pre-snapshot/after-restore）hook。選項 D 正是如此：新增 pre-snapshot hook、把產生 unique ID 的程式碼移到 handler、發佈版本、並在已發佈版本上啟用 SnapStart，在不增加 SnapStart 費用的情況下滿足啟動效能需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SnapStart cannot be configured on $LATEST (only on published versions or aliases pointing to versions), so this is technically impossible. It also moves ALL init code into the handler, which defeats SnapStart's purpose since the library/class initialization is exactly what should stay in the init phase to be captured in the snapshot.","why_zh":"SnapStart 無法設定在 $LATEST 上（只能用於已發佈版本或指向版本的 alias），因此技術上不可行。它還把所有初始化程式碼移到 handler，反而失去 SnapStart 的效益，因為函式庫/類別初始化正是應該留在 init 階段被快照擷取的部分。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Provisioned concurrency works for performance but charges continuously to keep environments pre-initialized, so it is not the MOST cost-effective option when SnapStart for Java is free.","why_zh":"Provisioned concurrency 能達到效能要求，但會持續收費以維持環境預先初始化，因此在 Java SnapStart 免費的情況下，並非最具成本效益的選項。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"SnapStart does not support provisioned concurrency; the two features are mutually exclusive and cannot be configured together on the same version, making this combination invalid.","why_zh":"SnapStart 不支援 provisioned concurrency；兩項功能互斥，無法在同一版本上同時設定，因此這個組合無效。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/snapstart.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/snapstart-uniqueness.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/snapstart-runtime-hooks-java.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":492,"question_en":"A solutions architect is importing a VM from an on-premises environment by using the Amazon EC2 VM Import feature of AWS Import/Export. The solutions architect has created an AMI and has provisioned an Amazon EC2 instance that is based on that AMI. The EC2 instance runs inside a public subnet in a VPC and has a public IP address assigned. The EC2 instance does not appear as a managed instance in the AWS Systems Manager console. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect take to troubleshoot this issue? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位解决方案架构师正在使用 AWS Import/Export 的 Amazon EC2 VM Import 功能从本地环境导入一个虚拟机。该解决方案架构师已创建了一个 AMI，并基于该 AMI 配置了一个 Amazon EC2 实例。该 EC2 实例运行在 VPC 中的一个公有子网内，并分配了一个公有 IP 地址。该 EC2 实例未在 AWS Systems Manager 控制台中显示为受管实例。解决方案架构师应采取哪些步骤组合来排查此问题？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Verify that Systems Manager Agent is installed on the instance and is running.","B":"Verify that the instance is assigned an appropriate IAM role for Systems Manager.","C":"Verify the existence of a VPC endpoint on the VPC.","D":"Verity that the AWS Application Discovery Agent is configured.","E":"Verify the correct configuration of service-linked roles for Systems Manager."},"options_zh":{"A":"验证该实例上是否已安装 Systems Manager Agent 并且正在运行。","B":"验证该实例是否已分配适用于 Systems Manager 的适当 IAM 角色。","C":"验证该 VPC 上是否存在 VPC 端点。","D":"验证 AWS Application Discovery Agent 是否已配置。","E":"验证 Systems Manager 的服务相关角色是否配置正确。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AB":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"AWS documents three core requirements for an EC2 instance to appear as a Systems Manager managed node: (1) SSM Agent installed and running, (2) an IAM instance profile attached granting AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore permissions, and (3) connectivity to a Systems Manager service endpoint. The instance here was created from an AMI imported via VM Import, which does NOT preinstall SSM Agent (only AWS-provided/custom-prepared AMIs do), so verifying the agent is installed and running (A) is essential. An imported instance also will not automatically have an IAM instance profile with the required SSM permissions, so verifying the role (B) is the other essential step. Because the instance is in a public subnet with a public IP, it reaches the SSM endpoints over the internet through the internet gateway, so a VPC endpoint (C) is not needed. The dump's suggested answer of D is wrong: the AWS Application Discovery Agent belongs to Application Discovery Service / Migration Hub and has nothing to do with SSM managed-instance registration.","explanation_zh":"AWS 官方文件列出 EC2 instance 要成為 Systems Manager managed node 必須符合三項核心需求：(1) 已安裝並運行 SSM Agent；(2) 已附加授予 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 權限的 IAM instance profile；(3) 能連線到 Systems Manager 服務端點。本題的 instance 是用 VM Import 匯入後建立的 AMI，匯入的 VM 不會預先安裝 SSM Agent（只有 AWS 提供或自訂預裝的 AMI 才有），因此驗證 Agent 是否已安裝並運行 (A) 是關鍵步驟。匯入的 instance 也不會自動擁有具備 SSM 權限的 IAM instance profile，所以驗證 IAM role (B) 是另一個必要步驟。由於 instance 位於 public subnet 並擁有 public IP，它透過 internet gateway 經由網際網路即可連到 SSM 端點，因此不需要 VPC endpoint (C)。題庫建議答案 D 是錯的：AWS Application Discovery Agent 屬於 Application Discovery Service / Migration Hub，與 SSM managed instance 註冊毫無關係。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"A VPC endpoint is only required when an instance has no internet path to the SSM endpoints. This instance is in a public subnet with a public IP, so it reaches Systems Manager over the internet gateway; an interface VPC endpoint is not needed.","why_zh":"只有當 instance 沒有對外網路路徑到 SSM 端點時才需要 VPC endpoint。本 instance 位於 public subnet 且有 public IP，可透過 internet gateway 連到 Systems Manager，因此不需要 interface VPC endpoint。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The AWS Application Discovery Agent is part of AWS Application Discovery Service / Migration Hub used to inventory on-premises servers before migration. It is unrelated to whether an EC2 instance registers as an SSM managed node, so it cannot explain the missing managed instance.","why_zh":"AWS Application Discovery Agent 屬於 AWS Application Discovery Service / Migration Hub，用於遷移前盤點地端伺服器，與 EC2 instance 是否註冊為 SSM managed node 無關，無法解釋 managed instance 不出現的問題。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"What makes an EC2 instance a managed node is the IAM instance profile, not a service-linked role. Service-linked roles for Systems Manager support specific features (e.g., OpsCenter/Explorer/maintenance windows) but are not a prerequisite for an instance to appear as managed, so this is not a valid troubleshooting step here.","why_zh":"讓 EC2 instance 成為 managed node 的是 IAM instance profile，而非 service-linked role。Systems Manager 的 service-linked role 用於特定功能（如 OpsCenter/Explorer/maintenance window），並非 instance 顯示為 managed 的前提條件，因此不是有效的排錯步驟。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/fleet-manager-troubleshooting-managed-nodes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/ssm-agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/troubleshooting-ssm-agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/manually-install-ssm-agent-linux.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":493,"question_en":"A company is using AWS CloudFormation as its deployment tool for all applications. It stages all application binaries and templates within Amazon S3 buckets with versioning enabled. Developers have access to an Amazon EC2 instance that hosts the integrated development environment (IDE). The developers download the application binaries from Amazon S3 to the EC2 instance, make changes, and upload the binaries to an S3 bucket after running the unit tests locally. The developers want to improve the existing deployment mechanism and implement CI/CD using AWS CodePipeline. The developers have the following requirements: • Use AWS CodeCommit for source control. • Automate unit testing and security scanning. • Alert the developers when unit tests fail. • Turn application features on and off, and customize deployment dynamically as part of CI/CD. • Have the lead developer provide approval before deploying an application. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS CloudFormation 作为其所有应用程序的部署工具。该公司将所有应用程序二进制文件和模板存放在启用了版本控制的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。开发人员可以访问托管集成开发环境 (IDE) 的 Amazon EC2 实例。开发人员将应用程序二进制文件从 Amazon S3 下载到该 EC2 实例，进行修改，并在本地运行单元测试后将二进制文件上传到 S3 存储桶。开发人员希望改进现有的部署机制，并使用 AWS CodePipeline 实现 CI/CD。开发人员有以下要求：• 使用 AWS CodeCommit 进行源代码管理。• 自动化单元测试和安全扫描。• 在单元测试失败时向开发人员发出警报。• 作为 CI/CD 的一部分，能够启用和禁用应用程序功能，并动态自定义部署。• 在部署应用程序之前，需要由首席开发人员进行审批。哪种解决方案能够满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CodeBuild to run unit tests and security scans. Use an Amazon EventBridge rule to send Amazon SNS alerts to the developers when unit tests fail. Write AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK) constructs for different solution features, and use a manifest file to tum features on and off in the AWS CDK application. Use a manual approval stage in the pipeline to allow the lead developer to approve applications.","B":"Use AWS Lambda to run unit tests and security scans. Use Lambda in a subsequent stage in the pipeline to send Amazon SNS alerts to the developers when unit tests fail. Write AWS Amplify plugins for different solution features and utilize user prompts to tum features on and off. Use Amazon SES in the pipeline to allow the lead developer to approve applications.","C":"Use Jenkins to run unit tests and security scans. Use an Amazon EventBridge rule in the pipeline to send Amazon SES alerts to the developers when unit tests fail Use AWS CloudFormation nested stacks for different solution features and parameters to turn features on and off. Use AWS Lambda in the pipeline to allow the lead developer to approve applications.","D":"Use AWS CodeDeploy to run unit tests and security scans. Use an Amazon CloudWatch alarm in the pipeline to send Amazon SNS alerts to the developers when unit tests fail. Use Docker images for different solution features and the AWS CLI to turn features on and off. Use a manual approval stage in the pipeline to allow the lead developer to approve applications."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CodeBuild 运行单元测试和安全扫描。使用 Amazon EventBridge 规则在单元测试失败时向开发人员发送 Amazon SNS 警报。为不同的解决方案功能编写 AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK) 构造，并使用清单文件在 AWS CDK 应用程序中启用和禁用相应功能。在管道中使用手动审批阶段，让首席开发人员对应用程序进行审批。","B":"使用 AWS Lambda 运行单元测试和安全扫描。在管道的后续阶段使用 Lambda，在单元测试失败时向开发人员发送 Amazon SNS 警报。为不同的解决方案功能编写 AWS Amplify 插件，并利用用户提示来启用和禁用相应功能。在管道中使用 Amazon SES，让首席开发人员对应用程序进行审批。","C":"使用 Jenkins 运行单元测试和安全扫描。在管道中使用 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在单元测试失败时向开发人员发送 Amazon SES 警报。针对不同的解决方案功能使用 AWS CloudFormation 嵌套堆栈，并使用参数来启用和禁用相应功能。在管道中使用 AWS Lambda，让首席开发人员对应用程序进行审批。","D":"使用 AWS CodeDeploy 运行单元测试和安全扫描。在管道中使用 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，在单元测试失败时向开发人员发送 Amazon SNS 警报。针对不同的解决方案功能使用 Docker 镜像，并使用 AWS CLI 来启用和禁用相应功能。在管道中使用手动审批阶段，让首席开发人员对应用程序进行审批。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":494,"question_en":"A global ecommerce company has many data centers around the world. With the growth of its stored data, the company needs to set up a solution to provide scalable storage for legacy on-premises file applications. The company must be able to take point-in-time copies of volumes by using AWS Backup and must retain low-latency access to frequently accessed data. The company also needs to have storage volumes that can be mounted as Internet Small Computer System Interface (iSCSI) devices from the company’s on-premises application servers. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家全球性电子商务公司在世界各地拥有多个数据中心。随着存储数据量的增长，该公司需要建立一种解决方案，为旧版本地文件应用程序提供可扩展的存储空间。该公司必须能够使用 AWS Backup 对卷进行时间点复制，并且必须对经常访问的数据保持低延迟访问。该公司还需要能够从其本地应用程序服务器将存储卷挂载为 Internet Small Computer System Interface (iSCSI) 设备。哪种解决方案能够满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Provision an AWS Storage Gateway tape gateway. Configure the tape gateway to store data in an Amazon S3 bucket. Deploy AWS Backup to take point-in-time copies of the volumes.","B":"Provision an Amazon FSx File Gateway and an Amazon S3 File Gateway. Deploy AWS Backup to take point-in-time copies of the data.","C":"Provision an AWS Storage Gateway volume gateway in cache mode. Back up the on-premises Storage Gateway volumes with AWS Backup.","D":"Provision an AWS Storage Gateway file gateway in cache mode. Deploy AWS Backup to take point-in-time copies of the volumes."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个 AWS Storage Gateway 磁带网关，将该磁带网关设置为将数据存储在一个 Amazon S3 存储桶中，并部署 AWS Backup 对卷进行时间点复制。","B":"配置一个 Amazon FSx File Gateway 和一个 Amazon S3 File Gateway，并部署 AWS Backup 对数据进行时间点复制。","C":"以缓存模式配置一个 AWS Storage Gateway 卷网关，并使用 AWS Backup 对本地 Storage Gateway 卷进行备份。","D":"以缓存模式配置一个 AWS Storage Gateway 文件网关，并部署 AWS Backup 对卷进行时间点复制。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive requirement is the iSCSI mount: storage volumes must be mounted as iSCSI devices from on-premises application servers, with point-in-time copies via AWS Backup and low-latency access to frequently accessed data. Only the AWS Storage Gateway Volume Gateway exposes block storage volumes as iSCSI targets. In cached-volumes mode, S3 is the primary store while frequently accessed data is retained locally in the gateway cache for low-latency access, satisfying both the scalable-storage and low-latency requirements. AWS Backup supports Volume Gateway as a resource (it can back up gateway volumes and even restore snapshots back to a gateway volume via an iSCSI target), satisfying the point-in-time copy requirement. Option C matches all requirements exactly. The dump's suggested answer D fails because a File Gateway only exposes NFS/SMB file shares, not iSCSI devices, and AWS Backup does not take point-in-time copies of File Gateway 'volumes' (there are none).","explanation_zh":"決定性的需求是 iSCSI 掛載：儲存磁碟區必須能從地端應用伺服器以 iSCSI 裝置掛載，並透過 AWS Backup 取得時間點副本，同時對常用資料保有低延遲存取。只有 AWS Storage Gateway 的 Volume Gateway 會把區塊儲存磁碟區以 iSCSI 目標形式公開。在 cached volumes 模式下，S3 為主要儲存，而常用資料保留在本機閘道快取中以提供低延遲存取，同時滿足可擴充儲存與低延遲的需求。AWS Backup 支援 Volume Gateway 作為資源（可備份閘道磁碟區，甚至能透過 iSCSI 目標將快照還原回閘道磁碟區），滿足時間點副本需求。選項 C 完全符合所有需求。dump 建議答案 D 不成立，因為 File Gateway 只公開 NFS/SMB 檔案共用，並非 iSCSI 裝置，且 AWS Backup 不會對 File Gateway 的『磁碟區』取得時間點副本（File Gateway 根本沒有磁碟區）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Tape Gateway provides a virtual tape library (VTL) for backup archival to S3/Glacier, not live iSCSI block volumes for application data with low-latency cached access. It does not meet the iSCSI-mounted file-application storage requirement, and AWS Backup does not take point-in-time copies of tape gateway 'volumes'.","why_zh":"Tape Gateway 提供虛擬磁帶庫（VTL）將備份歸檔至 S3/Glacier，並非供應用資料使用、具低延遲快取的即時 iSCSI 區塊磁碟區。無法滿足以 iSCSI 掛載檔案應用儲存的需求，且 AWS Backup 不會對 tape gateway 的『磁碟區』取得時間點副本。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"FSx File Gateway and S3 File Gateway both expose only NFS/SMB file shares, never iSCSI block devices. The requirement to mount volumes as iSCSI devices cannot be met, and these gateways do not present 'volumes' for AWS Backup point-in-time copies.","why_zh":"FSx File Gateway 與 S3 File Gateway 都只公開 NFS/SMB 檔案共用，不提供 iSCSI 區塊裝置。無法滿足以 iSCSI 掛載磁碟區的需求，且這些閘道沒有可供 AWS Backup 取得時間點副本的『磁碟區』。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it is wrong: a File Gateway in cached mode serves NFS/SMB file shares, not iSCSI devices, so it cannot be mounted as iSCSI from application servers. It also has no block 'volumes' for AWS Backup to copy. Only Volume Gateway provides iSCSI volumes.","why_zh":"這是 dump 的建議答案，但它是錯的：cached 模式的 File Gateway 提供 NFS/SMB 檔案共用，並非 iSCSI 裝置，因此無法從應用伺服器以 iSCSI 掛載。它也沒有可供 AWS Backup 複製的區塊『磁碟區』。只有 Volume Gateway 提供 iSCSI 磁碟區。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/StorageGatewayConcepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/WhatIsStorageGateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/restoring-ebs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/filegateway/latest/files3/what-is-file-s3.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":495,"question_en":"A company has an application that uses AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) to encrypt and decrypt data. The application stores data in an Amazon S3 bucket in an AWS Region. Company security policies require the data to be encrypted before the data is placed into the S3 bucket. The application must decrypt the data when the application reads files from the S3 bucket. The company replicates the S3 bucket to other Regions. A solutions architect must design a solution so that the application can encrypt and decrypt data across Regions. The application must use the same key to decrypt the data in each Region. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个应用程序，使用 AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) 对数据进行加密和解密。该应用程序将数据存储在某个 AWS 区域中的一个 Amazon S3 存储桶中。公司的安全策略要求数据在放入该 S3 存储桶之前必须先进行加密。当应用程序从 S3 存储桶中读取文件时，必须对数据进行解密。该公司将该 S3 存储桶复制到其他区域。解决方案架构师必须设计一种解决方案，使应用程序能够跨区域对数据进行加密和解密，并且应用程序在每个区域中都必须使用相同的密钥来解密数据。哪种解决方案能够满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a KMS multi-Region primary key. Use the KMS multi-Region primary key to create a KMS multi-Region replica key in each additional Region where the application is running. Update the application code to use the specific replica key in each Region.","B":"Create a new customer managed KMS key in each additional Region where the application is running. Update the application code to use the specific KMS key in each Region.","C":"Use AWS Private Certificate Authority to create a new certificate authority (CA) in the primary Region. Issue a new private certificate from the CA for the application’s website URL. Share the CA with the additional Regions by using AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM). Update the application code to use the shared CA certificates in each Region.","D":"Use AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store to create a parameter in each additional Region where the application is running. Export the key material from the KMS key in the primary Region. Store the key material in the parameter in each Region. Update the application code to use the key data from the parameter in each Region."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 KMS 多区域主密钥，并使用该 KMS 多区域主密钥在应用程序运行的每个其他区域中创建一个 KMS 多区域副本密钥。更新应用程序代码，使其在每个区域中使用相应的副本密钥。","B":"在应用程序运行的每个其他区域中创建一个新的客户托管 KMS 密钥。更新应用程序代码，使其在每个区域中使用相应的 KMS 密钥。","C":"使用 AWS Private Certificate Authority 在主区域中创建一个新的证书颁发机构 (CA)，并从该 CA 为应用程序的网站 URL 签发一个新的私有证书。使用 AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) 将该 CA 共享给其他区域。更新应用程序代码，使其在每个区域中使用共享的 CA 证书。","D":"使用 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store 在应用程序运行的每个其他区域中创建一个参数。从主区域的 KMS 密钥中导出密钥材料，并将该密钥材料存储在每个区域的参数中。更新应用程序代码，使其在每个区域中使用参数中的密钥数据。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":496,"question_en":"A company hosts an application that uses several Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). During the initial startup of the EC2 instances, the EC2 instances run user data scripts to download critical content for the application from an Amazon S3 bucket. The EC2 instances are launching correctly. However, after a period of time, the EC2 instances are terminated with the following error message: “An instance was taken out of service in response to an ELB system health check failure.” EC2 instances continue to launch and be terminated because of Auto Scaling events in an endless loop. The only recent change to the deployment is that the company added a large amount of critical content to the S3 bucket. The company does not want to alter the user data scripts in production. What should a solutions architect do so that the production environment can deploy successfully?","question_zh":"一家公司托管着一个应用程序，该应用程序在 Application Load Balancer (ALB) 之后的 Auto Scaling 组中使用多个 Amazon EC2 实例。在 EC2 实例的初始启动过程中，这些 EC2 实例会运行用户数据脚本，从一个 Amazon S3 存储桶下载应用程序所需的关键内容。EC2 实例能够正确启动，但经过一段时间后，这些 EC2 实例会因以下错误消息而被终止：“An instance was taken out of service in response to an ELB system health check failure.”（实例因响应 ELB 系统健康检查失败而被下线。）由于 Auto Scaling 事件，EC2 实例不断启动又被终止，陷入无限循环。此次部署唯一的近期变更是该公司向 S3 存储桶中添加了大量关键内容。该公司不希望在生产环境中修改用户数据脚本。解决方案架构师应该怎么做，才能让生产环境成功部署？","options_en":{"A":"Increase the size of the EC2 instances.","B":"Increase the health check timeout for the ALB.","C":"Change the health check path for the ALB.","D":"Increase the health check grace period for the Auto Scaling group."},"options_zh":{"A":"增加 EC2 实例的规格。","B":"增加 ALB 的健康检查超时时间。","C":"更改 ALB 的健康检查路径。","D":"增加 Auto Scaling 组的健康检查宽限期。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The instances launch fine but then need extra time during initialization to download the now-larger S3 content via the user data script. They are registered with the ALB and enter the InService state before the download finishes, so they fail the ELB health checks and Auto Scaling terminates them, causing the endless launch/terminate loop. The Auto Scaling health check grace period is the minimum time to keep a newly launched InService instance before terminating it if it fails health checks; AWS docs state it 'prevents Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling from marking your newly launched instances Unhealthy and terminating them unnecessarily if they don't immediately pass these health checks after they enter the InService state.' Increasing the grace period gives the longer download time to complete without modifying the user data scripts, satisfying the constraint. The termination message ('taken out of service in response to an ELB system health check failure') is exactly the Auto Scaling action the grace period governs.","explanation_zh":"EC2 執行個體可以正常啟動，但因為 S3 內容變大，user data script 需要更多時間下載內容。執行個體在下載完成前就被註冊到 ALB 並進入 InService 狀態，因此無法通過 ELB health check，Auto Scaling 隨即將其終止，形成不斷啟動與終止的迴圈。Auto Scaling 的 health check grace period 是新啟動的 InService 執行個體在被視為不健康而終止前必須保留的最短時間；AWS 文件指出它可『避免 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 在新執行個體進入 InService 狀態後未立即通過 health check 時，就被錯誤地標記為 Unhealthy 並終止』。增加 grace period 可讓較長的下載時間完成，且無需修改 user data script，符合題目限制。終止訊息（'taken out of service in response to an ELB system health check failure'）正是 grace period 所管控的 Auto Scaling 行為。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A larger instance might download slightly faster but does not address the timing race between initialization and ELB health checks; the instance can still enter InService before the download completes and be terminated. It also adds cost without solving the root cause.","why_zh":"較大的執行個體下載可能稍快，但無法解決初始化與 ELB health check 之間的時間競賽；執行個體仍可能在下載完成前進入 InService 而被終止，且增加成本卻未解決根本原因。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The ALB health check timeout is the per-request wait time for a single health check response (default 5s). The instance is not responding slowly to a single probe; it is not ready at all because the download has not finished, so increasing the per-request timeout does not provide the needed startup window.","why_zh":"ALB 的 health check timeout 是單次 health check 回應的等待時間（預設 5 秒）。執行個體並非單次探測回應太慢，而是下載尚未完成、根本還沒就緒，因此延長單次 timeout 無法提供所需的啟動緩衝時間。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Changing the health check path does not help because the path is not the problem; the application is simply not ready yet while the S3 download runs. This is the dump's suggested answer and is technically wrong for this timing/initialization scenario.","why_zh":"更改 health check path 沒有幫助，因為問題不在路徑；應用程式只是在 S3 下載期間尚未就緒。這是 dump 的建議答案，但對此啟動/初始化時間問題在技術上是錯誤的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/health-check-grace-period.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/health-checks-overview.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":497,"question_en":"A company needs to move some on-premises Oracle databases to AWS. The company has chosen to keep some of the databases on premises for business compliance reasons. The on-premises databases contain spatial data and run cron jobs for maintenance. The company needs to connect to the on-premises systems directly from AWS to query data as a foreign table. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要将部分本地 Oracle 数据库迁移到 AWS。出于业务合规性原因，该公司选择将部分数据库保留在本地。这些本地数据库包含空间数据，并运行 cron 作业进行维护。该公司需要直接从 AWS 连接到这些本地系统，以外部表的形式查询数据。哪种解决方案能够满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create Amazon DynamoDB global tables with auto scaling enabled. Use the AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) and AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to move the data from on premises to DynamoDB. Create an AWS Lambda function to move the spatial data to Amazon S3. Query the data by using Amazon Athena. Use Amazon EventBridge to schedule jobs in DynamoDB for maintenance. Use Amazon API Gateway for foreign table support.","B":"Create an Amazon RDS for Microsoft SQL Server DB instance. Use native replication to move the data from on premises to the DB instance. Use the AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) to modify the SQL Server schema as needed after replication. Move the spatial data to Amazon Redshift. Use stored procedures for system maintenance. Create AWS Glue crawlers to connect to the on-premises Oracle databases for foreign table support.","C":"Launch Amazon EC2 instances to host the Oracle databases. Place the EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group. Use AWS Application Migration Service to move the data from on premises to the EC2 instances and for real-time bidirectional change data capture (CDC) synchronization. Use Oracle native spatial data support. Create an AWS Lambda function to run maintenance jobs as part of an AWS Step Functions work­ow. Create an internet gateway for foreign table support.","D":"Create an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL DB instance. Use the AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) and AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to move the data from on premises to the DB instance. Use PostgreSQL native spatial data support. Run cron jobs on the DB instance for maintenance. Use AWS Direct Connect to connect the DB instance to the on-premises environment for foreign table support."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建启用了自动扩展的 Amazon DynamoDB 全局表。使用 AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) 和 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 将数据从本地迁移到 DynamoDB。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数将空间数据移动到 Amazon S3，并使用 Amazon Athena 查询数据。使用 Amazon EventBridge 在 DynamoDB 中调度维护作业，并使用 Amazon API Gateway 支持外部表功能。","B":"创建一个 Amazon RDS for Microsoft SQL Server 数据库实例。使用原生复制将数据从本地迁移到该数据库实例。复制完成后，根据需要使用 AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) 修改 SQL Server 架构。将空间数据移动到 Amazon Redshift，使用存储过程进行系统维护，并创建 AWS Glue 爬虫连接到本地 Oracle 数据库以支持外部表功能。","C":"启动 Amazon EC2 实例来托管 Oracle 数据库，并将这些 EC2 实例放置在一个 Auto Scaling 组中。使用 AWS Application Migration Service 将数据从本地迁移到这些 EC2 实例，并实现实时双向变更数据捕获 (CDC) 同步。使用 Oracle 原生空间数据支持功能。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，作为 AWS Step Functions 工作流的一部分来运行维护作业，并创建一个互联网网关以支持外部表功能。","D":"创建一个 Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL 数据库实例。使用 AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) 和 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 将数据从本地迁移到该数据库实例。使用 PostgreSQL 原生空间数据支持功能，在该数据库实例上运行 cron 作业进行维护，并使用 AWS Direct Connect 将该数据库实例与本地环境连接，以支持外部表功能。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The decisive requirement is querying the retained on-premises Oracle database directly from AWS 'as a foreign table.' Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL natively supports the oracle_fdw foreign data wrapper, which lets you CREATE FOREIGN TABLE pointing at an Oracle database (CREATE SERVER ... FOREIGN DATA WRAPPER oracle_fdw; CREATE FOREIGN TABLE ... SERVER oradb). PostgreSQL also has native spatial support via the PostGIS extension on RDS, covering the spatial-data requirement. AWS SCT + AWS DMS is the standard heterogeneous (Oracle-to-PostgreSQL) migration path. AWS Direct Connect provides the private, direct network connectivity from the RDS VPC to the on-premises Oracle systems so oracle_fdw can reach them for foreign-table queries, and cron-style maintenance can run via the database. Every part of D maps to a real, supported AWS capability, so D is correct.","explanation_zh":"決定性需求是要從 AWS 直接以「foreign table」方式查詢仍保留在地端的 Oracle 資料庫。Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL 原生支援 oracle_fdw foreign data wrapper，可以建立指向 Oracle 的 foreign table（CREATE SERVER ... FOREIGN DATA WRAPPER oracle_fdw; CREATE FOREIGN TABLE ... SERVER oradb），正好滿足此需求。PostgreSQL 在 RDS 上也透過 PostGIS extension 原生支援空間資料。AWS SCT 加上 AWS DMS 是 Oracle 轉 PostgreSQL 的標準異質遷移路徑。AWS Direct Connect 提供 RDS VPC 與地端 Oracle 系統之間的私有直連網路，讓 oracle_fdw 能連到地端執行 foreign table 查詢；維護所需的 cron 工作可在資料庫上執行。D 的每個組成都對應到真實且受支援的 AWS 能力，因此 D 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"DynamoDB is a NoSQL key-value store with no relational/spatial data type and no foreign-table capability; Athena queries S3, not the live on-premises Oracle DB. 'API Gateway for foreign table support' is not a real mechanism. This fails the core foreign-table-to-Oracle requirement.","why_zh":"DynamoDB 是 NoSQL 鍵值儲存，沒有關聯式/空間資料型別，也沒有 foreign table 能力；Athena 查的是 S3 而非地端的即時 Oracle DB。「用 API Gateway 提供 foreign table」不是真實機制，無法滿足對 Oracle 的 foreign table 需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Moving to RDS for SQL Server via 'native replication' from Oracle is not a valid path, and SQL Server is not asked for. AWS Glue crawlers only catalog metadata for ETL/analytics; they do not create live foreign tables that query an on-premises Oracle DB. Redshift is not needed for spatial data here.","why_zh":"用「native replication」把 Oracle 搬到 RDS for SQL Server 並不成立，題目也沒要求 SQL Server。AWS Glue crawler 只是為 ETL/分析建立中繼資料目錄，無法建立可即時查詢地端 Oracle 的 foreign table。此處空間資料也不需要 Redshift。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but is wrong: 'create an internet gateway for foreign table support' is meaningless (an IGW only provides public internet egress, not a foreign-table mechanism). Application Migration Service (MGN) is for full-server lift-and-shift, not Oracle database CDC; AWS DMS provides CDC. Hosting Oracle on an EC2 Auto Scaling group does not give native foreign-table querying of the retained on-premises DB.","why_zh":"這是題庫建議答案但錯誤：「建立 internet gateway 以支援 foreign table」沒有意義（IGW 只提供對外網際網路出口，不是 foreign table 機制）。Application Migration Service (MGN) 用於整機 lift-and-shift，並非 Oracle 資料庫的 CDC；CDC 應由 AWS DMS 提供。把 Oracle 放在 EC2 Auto Scaling group 上也無法對保留在地端的 DB 提供原生 foreign table 查詢。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/postgresql-oracle-fdw.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/Appendix.PostgreSQL.CommonDBATasks.Extensions.foreign-data-wrappers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/Appendix.PostgreSQL.CommonDBATasks.PostGIS.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/dms/latest/sbs/CHAP_Oracle2PostgreSQL.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":498,"question_en":"Accompany runs an application on Amazon EC2 and AWS Lambda. The application stores temporary data in Amazon S3. The S3 objects are deleted after 24 hours. The company deploys new versions of the application by launching AWS CloudFormation stacks. The stacks create the required resources. After validating a new version, the company deletes the old stack. The deletion of an old development stack recently failed. A solutions architect needs to resolve this issue without major architecture changes. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 Amazon EC2 和 AWS Lambda 上运行一个应用程序。该应用程序将临时数据存储在 Amazon S3 中，这些 S3 对象会在 24 小时后被删除。该公司通过启动 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈来部署应用程序的新版本，堆栈会创建所需的资源。验证新版本后，该公司会删除旧的堆栈。最近一次旧开发堆栈的删除操作失败了。解决方案架构师需要在不进行重大架构变更的情况下解决此问题。哪种解决方案能够满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a Lambda function to delete objects from an S3 bucket. Add the Lambda function as a custom resource in the CloudFormation stack with a DependsOn attribute that points to the S3 bucket resource.","B":"Modify the CloudFormation stack to attach a DeletionPolicy attribute with a value of Delete to the S3 bucket.","C":"Update the CloudFormation stack to add a DeletionPolicy attribute with a value of Snapshot for the S3 bucket resource","D":"Update the CloudFormation template to create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system to store temporary files instead of Amazon S3. Configure the Lambda functions to run in the same VPC as the EFS file system."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Lambda 函数以删除 S3 存储桶中的对象。将该 Lambda 函数作为自定义资源添加到 CloudFormation 堆栈中，并使用 DependsOn 属性指向该 S3 存储桶资源。","B":"修改 CloudFormation 堆栈，为该 S3 存储桶附加一个值为 Delete 的 DeletionPolicy 属性。","C":"更新 CloudFormation 堆栈，为该 S3 存储桶资源添加一个值为 Snapshot 的 DeletionPolicy 属性。","D":"更新 CloudFormation 模板，创建一个 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统来存储临时文件，而不使用 Amazon S3。将 Lambda 函数配置为在与该 EFS 文件系统相同的 VPC 中运行。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":70,"B":20},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":499,"question_en":"A company has an application that stores user-uploaded videos in an Amazon S3 bucket that uses S3 Standard storage. Users access the videos frequently in the first 180 days after the videos are uploaded. Access after 180 days is rare. Named users and anonymous users access the videos. Most of the videos are more than 100 MB in size. Users often have poor internet connectivity when they upload videos, resulting in failed uploads. The company uses multipart uploads for the videos. A solutions architect needs to optimize the S3 costs of the application. Which combination of actions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司有一个应用程序，将用户上传的视频存储在使用 S3 Standard 存储类别的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。用户在视频上传后的前 180 天内经常访问这些视频，180 天后访问频率很低。具名用户和匿名用户都会访问这些视频。大多数视频的大小超过 100 MB。用户上传视频时通常网络连接状况不佳，导致上传失败。该公司对视频使用分段上传。解决方案架构师需要优化该应用程序的 S3 成本。哪种组合操作能够满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure the S3 bucket to be a Requester Pays bucket.","B":"Use S3 Transfer Acceleration to upload the videos to the S3 bucket.","C":"Create an S3 Lifecycle configuration o expire incomplete multipart uploads 7 days after initiation.","D":"Create an S3 Lifecycle configuration to transition objects to S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval after 1 day.","E":"Create an S3 Lifecycle configuration to transition objects to S3 Standard-infrequent Access (S3 Standard- IA) after 180 days."},"options_zh":{"A":"将该 S3 存储桶配置为请求者付费存储桶。","B":"使用 S3 Transfer Acceleration 将视频上传到该 S3 存储桶。","C":"创建一个 S3 生命周期配置，在分段上传发起 7 天后终止未完成的分段上传。","D":"创建一个 S3 生命周期配置，在对象存储 1 天后将其转换为 S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval 存储类别。","E":"创建一个 S3 生命周期配置，在对象存储 180 天后将其转换为 S3 Standard-Infrequent Access (S3 Standard-IA) 存储类别。"},"answer":["C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"CE":90},"tags":["Storage","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The scenario has two independent cost drivers to fix. First, users have poor connectivity and multipart uploads frequently fail, leaving incomplete multipart upload parts sitting in the bucket. AWS documentation states that after you initiate a multipart upload, Amazon S3 retains all uploaded parts until the upload is either completed or explicitly aborted -- these orphaned parts are billed as normal storage even though they never become a retrievable object. The documented fix is an S3 Lifecycle rule with the AbortIncompleteMultipartUpload action (option C), which automatically deletes incomplete upload parts after a specified number of days (7 days is a common, AWS-documented value); this action does not apply to completed objects and incurs no early-deletion charges, so it purely removes wasted storage cost from failed uploads with no risk to data. Second, videos are accessed frequently for the first 180 days and rarely after that, which is the textbook access pattern for transitioning to a cheaper infrequent-access tier once the 'frequent access' window closes. Option E creates a Lifecycle transition to S3 Standard-IA after 180 days, which matches the observed access pattern exactly and reduces per-GB storage cost for the long tail of rarely accessed videos while keeping millisecond retrieval available if a video is occasionally accessed after day 180. Option A (Requester Pays) shifts data transfer and request costs to whoever downloads the object, but the scenario includes anonymous users, and many use cases (including anonymous/public access scenarios) are incompatible with Requester Pays; more importantly, it does nothing to reduce the company's own S3 storage costs, which is what the question asks to optimize. Option B (S3 Transfer Acceleration) speeds up long-distance uploads over the AWS edge network and could help with failed uploads caused by high latency, but it is a performance feature that adds cost (Transfer Acceleration carries its own per-GB fee) rather than reducing it, and it does not address storage cost optimization at all. Option D transitions objects to S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval after only 1 day, which directly contradicts the requirement that videos are accessed frequently during the first 180 days: Glacier Instant Retrieval has a documented 90-day minimum storage duration charge and higher per-request/retrieval costs than S3 Standard, so moving frequently-accessed videos there after just 1 day would increase costs (via retrieval fees and the minimum-duration commitment) rather than reduce them.","explanation_zh":"此情境有兩個各自獨立、需要分別解決的成本問題。第一，使用者網路品質不佳，multipart upload 經常失敗，導致未完成的分段上傳資料殘留在 bucket 中。AWS 文件指出，一旦發起 multipart upload，Amazon S3 會保留所有已上傳的分段，直到該上傳被完成或明確中止為止——這些「孤兒」分段仍會依一般儲存費率計費，即使它們永遠不會成為可存取的物件。文件記載的解法是使用 S3 Lifecycle 規則中的 AbortIncompleteMultipartUpload 動作（選項 C），自動在指定天數後（7 天是常見且 AWS 文件建議的數值）刪除未完成的上傳分段；此動作不會影響已完成的物件，也不會產生提前刪除費用，因此可以純粹地消除失敗上傳所浪費的儲存成本，且不會有資料風險。第二，影片在上傳後前 180 天被頻繁存取，之後則極少被存取，這正是「頻繁存取期結束後轉移到較便宜的不常存取層」的教科書級使用模式。選項 E 建立 Lifecycle 轉換規則，在 180 天後將物件轉移到 S3 Standard-IA，正好對應觀察到的存取模式，能降低這批長尾、極少被存取影片的每 GB 儲存成本，同時如果偶爾在第 180 天之後仍被存取，依然能維持毫秒級的取回速度。選項 A（Requester Pays）會把資料傳輸與請求成本轉嫁給下載該物件的人，但題目情境包含匿名使用者，而許多情境（包括匿名／公開存取情境）與 Requester Pays 並不相容；更重要的是，這個選項完全無法降低公司自身的 S3 儲存成本，而這正是題目要求優化的目標。選項 B（S3 Transfer Acceleration）能加速透過 AWS edge network 進行的長距離上傳，或許有助於緩解因高延遲造成的上傳失敗，但這是一項會增加成本的效能功能（Transfer Acceleration 本身依每 GB 收費），而非降低成本，且完全沒有針對儲存成本優化。選項 D 在僅僅 1 天後就將物件轉移到 S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval，這直接違背「影片在前 180 天被頻繁存取」的需求：Glacier Instant Retrieval 文件記載有 90 天的最低儲存期間計費規定，且每次請求／取回的費用高於 S3 Standard，因此把仍被頻繁存取的影片在僅 1 天後就搬過去，反而會因取回費用與最低儲存期間承諾而增加成本，而不是降低成本。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Requester Pays shifts data transfer and request costs to the downloader, but it does not reduce the company's own S3 storage costs and is generally unsuitable for buckets accessed by anonymous users, which this application explicitly has.","why_zh":"Requester Pays 只是把資料傳輸與請求費用轉嫁給下載者，並不會降低公司自身的 S3 儲存成本，而且通常不適用於有匿名使用者存取的 bucket，而這個應用程式明確包含匿名使用者。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"S3 Transfer Acceleration can reduce upload failures caused by latency over long distances, but it is a performance feature that adds its own per-GB fee rather than reducing cost, and it does not address the storage-cost optimization that the question asks for.","why_zh":"S3 Transfer Acceleration 或許能減少因長距離高延遲造成的上傳失敗，但這是一項會額外收費（依 GB 計費）的效能功能，而非降低成本的手段，也完全沒有處理題目所要求的儲存成本優化。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Transitioning objects to S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval after just 1 day directly contradicts the fact that videos are accessed frequently for the first 180 days; Glacier Instant Retrieval carries a 90-day minimum storage duration charge and higher retrieval costs than S3 Standard, so this would increase costs rather than reduce them.","why_zh":"僅 1 天後就將物件轉移到 S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval，直接違背影片在前 180 天被頻繁存取的事實；Glacier Instant Retrieval 有 90 天最低儲存期間計費規定，且取回成本高於 S3 Standard，因此這樣做反而會增加成本，而非降低成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/mpu-abort-incomplete-mpu-lifecycle-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/lifecycle-configuration-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/storage-lens-optimize-storage.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/lifecycle-transition-general-considerations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/lifecycle-expire-general-considerations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/glacier-storage-classes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/transfer-acceleration.html"]}},{"id":500,"question_en":"A company runs an ecommerce web application on AWS. The web application is hosted as a static website on Amazon S3 with Amazon CloudFront for content delivery. An Amazon API Gateway API invokes AWS Lambda functions to handle user requests and order processing for the web application The Lambda functions store data in an Amazon ROS for MySQL DB cluster that uses On-Demand instances. The DB cluster usage has been consistent in the past 12 months. Recently, the website has experienced SQL injection and web exploit attempts. Customers also report that order processing time has increased during periods of peak usage. During these periods, the Lambda functions often have cold starts. As the company grows, the company needs to ensure scalability and low-latency access during tra®c peaks. The company also must optimize the database costs and add protection against the SQL injection and web exploit attempts. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上运行电子商务 Web 应用程序。该 Web 应用程序作为静态网站托管在 Amazon S3 上，并使用 Amazon CloudFront 进 行内容交付。Amazon API Gateway API 调用 AWS Lambda 函数来处理 Web 应用程序的用户请求和订单处理。Lambda 函数将数据存储在使用按需实例的 Amazon ROS for MySQL DB 集群中。过去 12 个月中，DB 集群的使用率一直保持稳定。 最近，该网站遭遇了 SQL 注入和 Web 漏洞攻击。客户还报告称，在使用高峰期，订单处理时间有所增加。在这些时段，Lambda 函 数经常出现冷启动。随着公司的发展，公司需要确保流量高峰期间的可扩展性和低延迟访问。公司还必须优化数据库成本并增加针 对 SQL 注入和 Web 漏洞攻击的保护。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the Lambda functions to have an increased timeout value during peak periods. Use RDS Reserved Instances for the database. Use CloudFront and subscribe to AWS Shield Advanced to protect against the SQL injection and web exploit attempts.","B":"Increase the memory of the Lambda functions, Transition to Amazon Redshift for the database. Integrate Amazon Inspector with CloudFront to protect against the SQL injection and web exploit attempts.","C":"Use Lambda functions with provisioned concurrency for compute during peak periods, Transition to Amazon Aurora Serverless for the database. Use CloudFront and subscribe to AWS Shield Advanced to protect against the SQL injection and web exploit attempts.","D":"Use Lambda functions with provisioned concurrency for compute during peak periods. Use RDS Reserved Instances for the database. Integrate AWS WAF with CloudFront to protect against the SQL injection and web exploit attempts."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 Lambda 函数以在高峰期增加超时值。对数据库使用 RDS 预留实例。使用 CloudFront 并订阅 AWS Shield Advanced 以防范 SQL 注入和 Web 漏洞攻击。","B":"增加 Lambda 函数的内存，将数据库转换到 Amazon Redshift。将 Amazon Inspector 与 CloudFront 集成，以防止 SQL 注入和 Web 漏洞攻击。","C":"在高峰期使用具有预置并发性的 Lambda 函数进行计算，将数据库转换到 Amazon Aurora Serverless。使用 CloudFront 并订阅 AWS Shield Advanced 以防止 SQL 注入和 Web 漏洞攻击。","D":"在高峰期使用具有预置并发性的 Lambda 函数进行计算。使用 RDS 预留实例作为数据库。将 AWS WAF 与 CloudFront 集成，以 防止 SQL 注入和 Web 漏洞攻击。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":88},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The question has three requirements, and two of them decisively select D over C. (1) Security: it asks specifically for protection against SQL injection and web exploit attempts. AWS docs state AWS WAF protects against common web exploits such as SQL injection and XSS at the application layer, while AWS Shield (Standard/Advanced) is a managed DDoS protection service. Therefore WAF integrated with CloudFront is the correct control, and the Shield-based options (A and C) do not address SQL injection/web exploits. (2) Database cost: usage has been consistent for 12 months (steady-state). Aurora Serverless is designed for highly variable and unpredictable workloads, so it is the wrong cost-optimization choice for a predictable, consistent workload; RDS Reserved Instances provide a significant committed discount over on-demand for steady-state usage, which is the cost-optimal fit. (3) Compute: provisioned concurrency pre-initializes Lambda execution environments to eliminate cold starts during peak periods. Only option D combines provisioned concurrency + RDS Reserved Instances + AWS WAF on CloudFront, satisfying all three requirements.","explanation_zh":"本題有三項需求，其中兩項可決定性地選出 D 而非 C。(1) 安全性：題目明確要求防護 SQL injection 與 web exploit 攻擊。AWS 文件指出 AWS WAF 在應用層防護常見 web exploits（如 SQL injection 與 XSS），而 AWS Shield（Standard/Advanced）是針對 DDoS 的代管防護服務。因此在 CloudFront 整合 AWS WAF 才是正確的控制，使用 Shield 的選項（A 與 C）並未處理 SQL injection/web exploit 需求。(2) 資料庫成本：使用量過去 12 個月維持一致（穩態）。Aurora Serverless 適用於高度變動且不可預測的工作負載，對可預測且一致的工作負載並非成本最佳選擇；對穩態使用而言，RDS Reserved Instances 透過承諾使用可獲得相較 On-Demand 的顯著折扣，才是成本最佳解。(3) 運算：provisioned concurrency 會預先初始化 Lambda 執行環境，消除尖峰期間的 cold start。只有選項 D 同時結合 provisioned concurrency + RDS Reserved Instances + CloudFront 上的 AWS WAF，滿足全部三項需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Increasing Lambda timeout does nothing to fix cold starts or peak latency (provisioned concurrency is the fix). RDS Reserved Instances are correct for cost, but Shield Advanced protects against DDoS, not SQL injection/web exploits, so the security requirement is unmet.","why_zh":"增加 Lambda timeout 無法解決 cold start 或尖峰延遲（正解是 provisioned concurrency）。RDS Reserved Instances 在成本上正確，但 Shield Advanced 防護 DDoS 而非 SQL injection/web exploit，故安全需求未被滿足。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Increasing memory does not reliably eliminate cold starts (provisioned concurrency does). Redshift is a data warehouse (OLAP), wrong for an ecommerce transactional/order-processing workload. Amazon Inspector is a vulnerability assessment service, not an inline web-exploit/SQL-injection filter, and it does not integrate with CloudFront for request filtering.","why_zh":"增加記憶體無法可靠消除 cold start（應用 provisioned concurrency）。Redshift 是資料倉儲（OLAP），不適合電商交易/訂單處理工作負載。Amazon Inspector 是弱點評估服務，並非即時過濾 web exploit/SQL injection 的機制，也不會整合到 CloudFront 進行請求過濾。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Provisioned concurrency is correct, but Aurora Serverless is optimized for variable/unpredictable workloads, not the stated consistent 12-month usage (Reserved Instances are more cost-optimal for steady-state). More importantly, Shield Advanced is DDoS protection and does not address the required SQL injection/web exploit defense, which is AWS WAF's role.","why_zh":"provisioned concurrency 正確，但 Aurora Serverless 適用於變動/不可預測的工作負載，而非題述一致的 12 個月使用量（穩態下 Reserved Instances 更具成本效益）。更關鍵的是 Shield Advanced 屬於 DDoS 防護，無法滿足所需的 SQL injection/web exploit 防護，那是 AWS WAF 的職責。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/decision-guides/latest/waf-or-shield/waf-or-shield.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/cloudfront-features.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/provisioned-concurrency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_WorkingWithReservedDBInstances.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-serverless-v2.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":501,"question_en":"A company runs a web application on a single Amazon EC2 instance. End users experience slow application performance during times of peak usage, when CPU utilization is consistently more than 95%. A user data script installs required custom packages on the EC2 instance. The process of launching the instance takes several minutes. The company is creating an Auto Scaling group that has mixed instance groups, varied CPUs, and a maximum capacity limit. The Auto Scaling group will use a launch template for various configuration options. The company needs to decrease application latency when new instances are launched during auto scaling. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在单个 Amazon EC2 实例上运行 Web 应用程序。在高峰使用时段，当 CPU 利用率持续超过 95% 时，最终用户会发现应用程 序性能缓慢。 用户数据脚本会在 EC2 实例上安装所需的自定义包。启动实例的过程需要几分钟。 该公司正在创建一个 Auto Scaling 组，该组具有混合实例组、不同的 CPU 和最大容量限制。Auto Scaling 组将使用启动模板来处理各 种配置选项。该公司需要在 Auto Scaling 期间启动新实例时降低应用程序延迟。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use a predictive scaling policy. Use an instance maintenance policy to run the user data script. Set the default instance warmup time to 0 seconds.","B":"Use a dynamic scaling policy. Use lifecycle hooks to run the user data script. Set the default instance warmup time to 0 seconds.","C":"Use a predictive scaling policy. Enable warm pools for the Auto Scaling group. Use an instance maintenance policy to run the user data script.","D":"Use a dynamic scaling policy. Enable warm pools for the Auto Scaling group. Use lifecycle hooks to run the user data script."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用预测扩展策略。使用实例维护策略运行用户数据脚本。将默认实例预热时间设置为 0 秒。","B":"使用动态扩展策略。使用生命周期钩子运行用户数据脚本。将默认实例预热时间设置为 0 秒。","C":"使用预测扩展策略。为 Auto Scaling 组启用热池。使用实例维护策略运行用户数据脚本。","D":"使用动态扩展策略。为 Auto Scaling 组启用热池。使用生命周期挂钩运行用户数据脚本。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The requirement is to reduce launch latency for new Auto Scaling instances whose startup is slow because a user data script must install custom packages before the instance can serve traffic. Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling warm pools are purpose-built for exactly this: AWS documentation titles the feature 'Decrease latency for applications with long boot times using warm pools' and describes a warm pool as a group of pre-initialized EC2 instances that sit ready (Stopped or Running) outside the Auto Scaling group so that, when a scale-out event occurs, the group pulls already-initialized instances from the pool instead of launching and initializing new ones from scratch. Lifecycle hooks are the documented mechanism for running the user data script during warm pool instance creation: a hook puts the instance into a wait state (Pending:Wait) so the initialization script can complete before the instance is marked Warmed and becomes eligible to enter the group, ensuring every warmed instance already has the custom packages installed. A dynamic scaling policy (here, target tracking or step scaling on CPU utilization) is the correct scaling type for this workload, because the trigger is CPU crossing a threshold in real time, not a predictable recurring pattern. This combination (D) directly eliminates the multi-minute delay from the user data script by moving that work out of the scale-out critical path. Options A and C both choose predictive scaling, which AWS documentation states requires at least 24 hours of historical data (with 2 full weeks recommended) to forecast a REPEATING daily/weekly load pattern; the scenario describes sustained CPU above 95% during undefined 'peak usage' times, not a documented cyclical pattern, so predictive scaling is not the appropriate policy type here and does not by itself reduce per-instance launch latency. A and C also pair predictive scaling (or, in A's case, no warm pool at all) with an 'instance maintenance policy,' which is an EC2 Auto Scaling feature that controls the order and batch size of instance replacement during instance refresh/health-check replacement -- it has no mechanism for running a user data script and is not a substitute for lifecycle hooks or warm pools. Option B sets default instance warmup to 0 seconds and uses lifecycle hooks, but with no warm pool enabled, every new instance still launches cold and must run the multi-minute user data script in the scale-out path; setting warmup to 0 only affects how quickly CloudWatch metrics and scaling policies treat the instance as contributing capacity, it does not speed up the instance's own boot/initialization time, so it fails to address the actual latency problem.","explanation_zh":"需求是縮短新 Auto Scaling 實例的啟動延遲，因為 user data script 必須先安裝自訂套件才能讓實例開始服務，導致啟動過程耗時數分鐘。Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 的 warm pool 正是為此設計：AWS 官方文件將此功能命名為「Decrease latency for applications with long boot times using warm pools」，說明 warm pool 是一群預先初始化好的 EC2 實例，維持在 Stopped 或 Running 狀態、置於 Auto Scaling group 之外待命；當發生擴容事件時，group 會直接從池子裡取用已初始化完成的實例，而不需要重新啟動並初始化全新的實例。Lifecycle hook 則是文件記載、用於在建立 warm pool 實例期間執行 user data script 的機制：hook 會讓實例進入等待狀態（Pending:Wait），確保初始化腳本執行完成後才將實例標記為 Warmed 並允許加入 group，這樣每個暖機實例都已經裝好自訂套件。Dynamic scaling policy（此情境下即 target tracking 或針對 CPU 使用率的 step scaling）是這個工作負載正確的擴縮類型，因為觸發條件是 CPU 即時超過閾值，而非可預測的週期性模式。這個組合（D）直接把 user data script 的耗時工作移出擴容的關鍵路徑，消除了數分鐘的延遲。選項 A 與 C 都選用 predictive scaling，但 AWS 文件明確指出 predictive scaling 需要至少 24 小時的歷史資料（建議完整兩週）才能預測「重複出現」的每日/每週負載模式；題目描述的是未明確定義的「尖峰時段」持續 CPU 超過 95%，並非文件所指的週期性模式，因此 predictive scaling 在此並非合適的擴縮策略類型，本身也無法降低單一實例的啟動延遲。A 與 C 還將 predictive scaling（A 甚至完全沒有啟用 warm pool）搭配「instance maintenance policy」，但這是 EC2 Auto Scaling 用來控管 instance refresh／健康檢查替換時的替換順序與批次大小的功能，並沒有執行 user data script 的機制，也不能取代 lifecycle hook 或 warm pool 的作用。選項 B 將 default instance warmup 設為 0 秒並使用 lifecycle hook，但因為沒有啟用 warm pool，每個新實例仍然是冷啟動，仍必須在擴容路徑中執行耗時數分鐘的 user data script；將 warmup 設為 0 秒只會影響 CloudWatch 指標與擴縮策略多快將該實例視為已貢獻容量，並不會加快實例本身的開機／初始化時間，因此無法解決真正的延遲問題。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Predictive scaling requires at least 24 hours (ideally two weeks) of historical load data to forecast a recurring daily/weekly pattern, which does not match the scenario's sustained high-CPU 'peak usage' description. It also pairs with an instance maintenance policy, which governs replacement batching/ordering during instance refresh and has no mechanism to run the user data script or pre-initialize instances, so launch latency is not reduced.","why_zh":"Predictive scaling 需要至少 24 小時（理想上兩週）的歷史負載資料才能預測重複出現的每日/每週模式，這與題目描述的持續高 CPU「尖峰時段」不符。此選項還搭配 instance maintenance policy，該功能只管理 instance refresh 時的替換批次與順序，並沒有執行 user data script 或預先初始化實例的機制，因此無法降低啟動延遲。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Without warm pools enabled, every new instance still launches cold and must run the multi-minute user data script during the scale-out event. Setting default instance warmup to 0 seconds only changes how quickly the instance is treated as contributing to scaling metrics; it does not accelerate the instance's actual boot or package-installation time, so the core latency problem remains unsolved.","why_zh":"沒有啟用 warm pool 的情況下，每個新實例仍是冷啟動，擴容時仍須執行耗時數分鐘的 user data script。將 default instance warmup 設為 0 秒只會改變該實例多快被視為對擴縮指標有貢獻，並不會加快實例真正的開機或套件安裝時間，因此核心的延遲問題並未解決。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Predictive scaling is mismatched to a sustained high-CPU workload without a documented recurring pattern, and it needs at least 24 hours of history before it can forecast anything. Instance maintenance policy again has no capability to run initialization scripts or pre-warm instances -- that role belongs to lifecycle hooks and warm pools, neither of which this option correctly combines.","why_zh":"Predictive scaling 不適合沒有明確週期性模式的持續高 CPU 工作負載，且需要至少 24 小時的歷史資料才能開始預測。Instance maintenance policy 同樣沒有執行初始化腳本或預熱實例的能力——這是 lifecycle hook 與 warm pool 的職責，而此選項並未正確搭配兩者。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-auto-scaling-warm-pools.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/warm-pool-instance-lifecycle.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/create-warm-pool.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/predictive-scaling-policy-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/plans/userguide/gs-create-scaling-plan.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/instance-maintenance-policy-overview-and-considerations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/as-scaling-target-tracking.html"]}},{"id":502,"question_en":"A company needs to migrate its on-premises database ­eet to Amazon RDS. The company is currently using a mixture of Microsoft SQL Server, MySQL, and Oracle databases. Some of the databases have custom schemas and stored procedures. Which combination of steps should the company take for the migration? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司需要将其本地数据库迁移到 Amazon RDS。该公司目前混合使用 Microsoft SQL Server、MySQL 和 Oracle 数据库。一些数据库 具有自定义架构和存储过程。 该公司应采取哪些步骤组合进行迁移？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Use Migration Evaluator Quick Insights to analyze the source databases and to identify the stored procedures that need to be migrated.","B":"Use AWS Application Migration Service to analyze the source databases and to identify the stored procedures that need to be migrated.","C":"Use the AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) to analyze the source databases for changes that are required","D":"Use AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to migrate the source databases to Amazon RDS.","E":"Use AWS DataSync to migrate the data from the source databases to Amazon RDS."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用迁移评估器快速洞察来分析源数据库并识别需要迁移的存储过程。","B":"使用 AWS 应用程序迁移服务分析源数据库并识别需要迁移的存储过程。","C":"使用 AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) 分析源数据库以查找所需的更改","D":"使用 AWS 数据库迁移服务 (AWS DMS) 将源数据库迁移到 Amazon RDS。","E":"使用 AWS DataSync 将数据从源数据库迁移到 Amazon RDS。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"CD":100},"tags":["Migration","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"This is a standard AWS heterogeneous database migration workflow. The source fleet (SQL Server, MySQL, Oracle) has custom schemas and stored procedures, so the company must first assess what code/objects need to change before moving data. The AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) is purpose-built to analyze source schemas, produce a database migration assessment report, and convert schema objects including stored procedures and functions that cannot be automatically converted, flagging the changes required (option C). After the schema is converted, AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) migrates the actual data from the source databases to Amazon RDS, supporting both full load and ongoing replication (option D). SCT + DMS is the canonical AWS pairing for migrations involving schema/stored-procedure conversion. The dump's suggested answer (B,D) is wrong because AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) is a lift-and-shift server rehosting tool that has no capability to analyze databases or identify stored procedures.","explanation_zh":"這是標準的 AWS 異質資料庫遷移流程。來源資料庫（SQL Server、MySQL、Oracle）含有自訂 schema 與 stored procedure，因此公司必須先評估哪些程式碼／物件需要變更，再搬移資料。AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) 專門用來分析來源 schema、產生資料庫遷移評估報告，並轉換包含 stored procedure 與函式在內的 schema 物件，標示出需要進行的變更（選項 C）。完成 schema 轉換後，再以 AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) 將實際資料從來源資料庫遷移到 Amazon RDS，支援 full load 與持續複寫（選項 D）。SCT 加 DMS 是 AWS 針對牽涉 schema／stored procedure 轉換的遷移所採用的標準組合。Dump 建議答案 (B,D) 錯誤，因為 AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) 是 lift-and-shift 的伺服器 rehost 工具，無法分析資料庫或辨識 stored procedure。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Migration Evaluator (formerly TSO Logic) provides high-level business cost/TCO and right-sizing insights for planning a migration; it does not analyze database schemas or identify stored procedures that need conversion.","why_zh":"Migration Evaluator（前身 TSO Logic）提供高階的商業成本／TCO 與規模優化洞察以供遷移規劃，並不會分析資料庫 schema 或辨識需轉換的 stored procedure。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) is a lift-and-shift agent-based server rehosting tool for migrating servers/applications block by block; it cannot analyze database engines or identify stored procedures for conversion.","why_zh":"AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) 是以代理程式進行 lift-and-shift 伺服器 rehost 的工具，用於整機搬移伺服器／應用程式，無法分析資料庫引擎或辨識需轉換的 stored procedure。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"AWS DataSync moves files and object storage between NFS/SMB/HDFS/S3-style locations; it is not a database migration tool and cannot load relational data with schema/stored-procedure semantics into Amazon RDS.","why_zh":"AWS DataSync 用於在 NFS／SMB／HDFS／S3 等檔案與物件儲存位置之間搬移資料，並非資料庫遷移工具，無法將具備 schema／stored procedure 語意的關聯式資料載入 Amazon RDS。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/SchemaConversionTool/latest/userguide/CHAP_Welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/SchemaConversionTool/latest/userguide/CHAP_GettingStarted.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/dms/latest/userguide/data-migrations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_DMS_migration.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":503,"question_en":"A company is migrating its blog platform to AWS. The company's on-premises servers connect to AWS through an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection. The blog content is updated several times a day by multiple authors and is served from a file share on a network-attached storage (NAS) server. The company needs to migrate the blog platform without delaying the content updates. The company has deployed Amazon EC2 instances across multiple Availability Zones to run the blog platform behind an Application Load Balancer. The company also needs to move 200 TB of archival data from its on-premises servers to Amazon S3 as soon as possible. Which combination of stops will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在将其博客平台迁移到 AWS。该公司的本地服务器通过 AWS 站点到站点 VPN 连接连接到 AWS。博客内容由多位作者每 天更新数次，并通过网络附加存储 (NAS) 服务器上的文件共享提供。 该公司需要迁移博客平台而不延迟内容更新。该公司已在多个可用区部署了 Amazon EC2 实例，以在应用程序负载均衡器后面运行 博客平台。该公司还需要尽快将 200 TB 的存档数据从其本地服务器移动到 Amazon S3。 哪些站点组合可以满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a weekly cron job in Amazon EventBridge. Use the cron job to invoke an AWS Lambda function to update the EC2 instances from the NAS server.","B":"Configure an Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) Multi-Attach volume for the EC2 instances to share for content access. Write code to synchronize the EBS volume with the NAS server weekly.","C":"Mount an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system to the on-premises servers to act as the NAS server. Copy the blog data to the EFS file system. Mount the EFS file system to the C2 instances to serve the content.","D":"Order an AWS Snowball Edge Storage Optimized device. Copy the static data artifacts to the device. Ship the device to AWS.","E":"Order an AWS Snowcons SSD device. Copy the static data artifacts to the device. Ship the device to AWS."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon EventBridge 中创建每周 cron 作业。使用 cron 作业调用 AWS Lambda 函数从 NAS 服务器更新 EC2 实例。","B":"配置 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) Multi-Attach 卷，供 EC2 实例共享内容访问。编​写代码每周将 EBS 卷与 NAS 服务 器同步。","C":"将 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统挂载到本地服务器以充当 NAS 服务器。将博客数据复制到 EFS 文件系统。 将 EFS 文件系统挂载到 C2 实例以提供内容。","D":"订购 AWS Snowball Edge Storage Optimized 设备。将静态数据工件复制到设备。将设备运送到 AWS。","E":"订购 AWS Snowcons SSD 设备。将静态数据工件复制到设备。将设备运送到 AWS。"},"answer":["B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{"CD":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Two distinct requirements drive the answer. (1) Migrate the frequently-updated NAS file share without delaying content updates: Amazon EFS (Option C) is a fully managed NFS file system that can be mounted simultaneously on the on-premises servers over the existing Site-to-Site VPN (AWS provides a dedicated 'Mounting with on-premises Linux clients' tutorial) and on the EC2 instances across multiple Availability Zones. Authors keep writing during the cutover and EC2 serves the same content, so no updates are delayed. (2) Move 200 TB to S3 as soon as possible: AWS Snowball Edge Storage Optimized (Option D) provides 210 TB of usable capacity, enough for the entire dataset in a single device, and physical shipment is far faster than transferring 200 TB over a VPN. Therefore C and D are correct. The dump's suggested B+C is wrong because EBS Multi-Attach is constrained to a single Availability Zone (the fleet spans multiple AZs), supports only io1/io2 volumes with a cluster-aware filesystem, and a weekly sync would delay content updated several times a day.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個獨立需求。(1) 在不延遲內容更新的情況下遷移頻繁更新的 NAS 檔案共享：Amazon EFS（選項 C）是全託管 NFS 檔案系統，可透過既有的 Site-to-Site VPN 同時掛載到地端伺服器（AWS 提供專門的『Mounting with on-premises Linux clients』教學），也可同時掛載到跨多個可用區的 EC2 instances。作者在切換期間仍可持續寫入，EC2 直接提供相同內容，因此不會延遲任何更新。(2) 盡快將 200 TB 移到 S3：AWS Snowball Edge Storage Optimized（選項 D）提供 210 TB 可用容量，單一裝置即可容納整個資料集，且實體寄送遠比透過 VPN 傳輸 200 TB 快。因此正確答案為 C 與 D。題庫建議的 B+C 是錯的，因為 EBS Multi-Attach 僅限單一可用區（本題機群跨多個 AZ）、只支援 io1/io2 並需叢集感知檔案系統，且每週同步會延遲每天多次更新的內容。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A weekly cron job to pull content from the NAS cannot keep pace with a blog updated several times a day, directly violating the 'without delaying the content updates' requirement.","why_zh":"每週執行的排程從 NAS 拉取內容，無法跟上每天多次更新的部落格，直接違反『不延遲內容更新』的要求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"EBS Multi-Attach is limited to a single Availability Zone (the EC2 fleet spans multiple AZs), supports only Provisioned IOPS io1/io2 volumes, and needs a cluster-aware filesystem; plus a weekly sync delays the frequent updates.","why_zh":"EBS Multi-Attach 僅限單一可用區（EC2 機群跨多個 AZ），只支援 io1/io2 Provisioned IOPS 卷且需叢集感知檔案系統；加上每週同步會延遲頻繁的更新。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"AWS Snowcone SSD holds only about 14 TB, far short of the 200 TB archival dataset, so it cannot move the data in one device.","why_zh":"AWS Snowcone SSD 僅約 14 TB 容量，遠不足以容納 200 TB 封存資料，無法以單一裝置完成搬移。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/snowball/latest/developer-guide/device-differences.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/mounting-fs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/mounting-fs-mount-helper-direct.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/ebs-volumes-multi.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":504,"question_en":"A company plans to migrate a legacy on-premises application to AWS. The application is a Java web application that runs on Apache Tomcat with a PostgreSQL database. The company does not have access to the source code but can deploy the application Java Archive (JAR) files. The application has increased tra®c at the end of each month. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司计划将一个传统的本地应用程序迁移到 AWS。该应用程序是一个 Java Web 应用程序，运行在带有 PostgreSQL 数据库的 Apache Tomcat 上。 该公司无法访问源代码，但可以部署应用程序 Java 存档 (JAR) 文件。该应用程序的流量在每个月底都会增加。 哪种解决方案可以以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Launch Amazon EC2 instances in multiple Availability Zones. Deploy Tomcat and PostgreSQL to all the instances by using Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) mount points. Use AWS Step Functions to deploy additional EC2 instances to scale for increased tra®c.","B":"Provision Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) in an Auto Scaling group across multiple AWS Regions. Deploy Tomcat and PostgreSQL in the container images. Use a Network Load Balancer to scale for increased tra®c.","C":"Refactor the Java application into Python-based containers. Use AWS Lambda functions for the application logic. Store application data in Amazon DynamoDB global tables. Use AWS Storage Gateway and Lambda concurrency to scale for increased tra®c.","D":"Use AWS Elastic Beanstalk to deploy the Tomcat servers with auto scaling in multiple Availability Zones. Store application data in an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database. Deploy Amazon CloudFront and an Application Load Balancer to scale for increased tra®c."},"options_zh":{"A":"在多个可用区中启动 Amazon EC2 实例。使用 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 挂载点将 Tomcat 和 PostgreSQL 部署到所 有实例。使用 AWS Step Functions 部署额外的 EC2 实例以扩展流量。","B":"在跨多个 AWS 区域的 Auto Scaling 组中配置 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS)。在容器映像中部署 Tomcat 和 PostgreSQL。使用网络负载均衡器扩展以应对增加的流量。","C":"将 Java 应用程序重构为基于 Python 的容器。使用 AWS Lambda 函数实现应用程序逻辑。将应用程序数据存储在 Amazon DynamoDB 全局表中。使用 AWS Storage Gateway 和 Lambda 并发来扩展以应对增加的流量。","D":"使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 在多个可用区部署具有自动扩展功能的 Tomcat 服务器。将应用程序数据存储在 Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL 数据库中。部署 Amazon CloudFront 和应用程序负载均衡器以扩展流量。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":505,"question_en":"A company is migrating its on-premises IoT platform to AWS. The platform consists of the following components: • A MongoDB cluster as a data store for all collected and processed IoT data. • An application that uses Message Queuing Telemetry Transport (MQTT) to connect to IoT devices every 5 minutes to collect data. • An application that runs jobs periodically to generate reports from the IoT data. The jobs take 120-600 seconds to finish running. • A web application that runs on a web server. End users use the web application to generate reports that are accessible to the general public. The company needs to migrate the platform to AWS to reduce operational overhead while maintaining performance. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在将其本地 IoT 平台迁移到 AWS。该平台由以下组件组成： • MongoDB 集群作为所有收集和处理的 IoT 数据的数据存储。 • 使用消息队列遥测传输 (MQTT) 每 5 分钟连接到 IoT 设备以收集数据的应用程序。 • 定期运行作业以根据 IoT 数据生成报告的应用程序。作业需要 120-600 秒才能完成运行。 • 在 Web 服务器上运行的 Web 应用程序。最终用户使用 Web 应用程序生成可供公众访问的报告。 公司需要将平台迁移到 AWS，以减少运营开销，同时保持性能。 哪些步骤组合可以以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？（选择三个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create AWS Step Functions state machines with AUS Lambda tasks to prepare the reports and to write the reports to Amazon S3. Configure an Amazon CloudFront distribution that has an S3 origin to serve the reports","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function. Program the Lambda function to connect to the IoT devices. process the data, and write the data to the data store. Configure a Lambda layer to temporarily store messages for processing.","C":"Configure an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster with Amazon EC2 instances to prepare the reports. Create an ingress controller on the EKS cluster to serve the reports.","D":"Connect the IoT devices to AWS IoT Core to publish messages. Create an AWS IoT rule that runs when a message is received. Configure the rule to call an AWS Lambda function. Program the Lambda function to parse, transform, and store device message data to the data store.","E":"Migrate the MongoDB cluster to Amazon DocumentDB (with MongoDB compatibility).","F":"Migrate the MongoDB cluster to Amazon EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AUS Lambda 任务创建 AWS Step Functions 状态机，以准备报告并将报告写入 Amazon S3。配置具有 S3 源的 Amazon CloudFront 分发以提供报告","B":"创建 AWS Lambda 函数。编写 Lambda 函数以连接到 IoT 设备。处理数据，并将数据写入数据存储。配置 Lambda 层以临时存 储消息以供处理。","C":"使用 Amazon EC2 实例配置 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 集群以准备报告。在 EKS 集群上创建入口控制器以 提供报告。","D":"将 IoT 设备连接到 AWS IoT Core 以发布消息。创建在收到消息时运行的 AWS IoT 规则。配置规则以调用 AWS Lambda 函数。对 Lambda 函数进行编程以解析、转换并将设备消息数据存储到数据存储中。","E":"将 MongoDB 集群迁移到 Amazon DocumentDB（与 MongoDB 兼容）。","F":"将 MongoDB 集群迁移到 Amazon EC2 实例。"},"answer":["A","B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ADE":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The four platform components map to fully managed/serverless AWS services for the LEAST operational overhead. (D) AWS IoT Core is the purpose-built, fully managed MQTT broker for IoT devices; an IoT rule triggers a Lambda to parse, transform, and store the data with no servers to manage. (E) Amazon DocumentDB is the fully managed, MongoDB-compatible data store, far less overhead than self-managing MongoDB on EC2. (A) Report jobs take 120-600 seconds, which fits inside Lambda's 900-second (15-minute) maximum timeout, so Step Functions orchestrating Lambda tasks that write reports to Amazon S3 is serverless and low-overhead, and a CloudFront distribution with an S3 origin serves the public reports with no server administration. Together A+D+E address all four components (ingestion, data store, report generation, and public delivery) with the least operational overhead.","explanation_zh":"四個平台元件對應到全託管/無伺服器的 AWS 服務以達到最低營運負擔。(D) AWS IoT Core 是專為 IoT 裝置設計的全託管 MQTT broker；IoT rule 觸發 Lambda 來解析、轉換並儲存資料，無需管理伺服器。(E) Amazon DocumentDB 是全託管且相容 MongoDB 的資料儲存，比在 EC2 上自行管理 MongoDB 的負擔低得多。(A) 報表工作需時 120-600 秒,在 Lambda 的 900 秒(15 分鐘)上限之內,因此用 Step Functions 編排 Lambda task 將報表寫入 Amazon S3 屬無伺服器且低負擔,再用 CloudFront 搭配 S3 origin 對外提供公開報表,無需伺服器管理。A+D+E 一併涵蓋擷取、資料儲存、報表產生與公開傳遞四個元件,且營運負擔最低。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Lambda cannot act as a persistent MQTT broker connecting to IoT devices, and 'configuring a Lambda layer to temporarily store messages' is invalid (layers ship code/dependencies, not message buffers). IoT Core (D) is the correct managed MQTT entry point.","why_zh":"Lambda 無法作為持續連線到 IoT 裝置的 MQTT broker,且『設定 Lambda layer 暫存訊息』在技術上無效(layer 用於程式碼/相依套件,而非訊息緩衝)。IoT Core(D)才是正確的託管 MQTT 進入點。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Running an EKS cluster on EC2 instances and managing an ingress controller is high operational overhead (node patching, scaling, cluster ops), which contradicts the LEAST-operational-overhead requirement; serverless Step Functions/Lambda/S3/CloudFront in A is lower overhead.","why_zh":"在 EC2 上運行 EKS 叢集並管理 ingress controller 屬高營運負擔(節點修補、擴展、叢集維運),與『最低營運負擔』需求相違;A 的無伺服器 Step Functions/Lambda/S3/CloudFront 負擔更低。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Migrating MongoDB to self-managed EC2 instances leaves the company responsible for OS patching, backups, replication, scaling, and failover, which is high operational overhead versus the fully managed Amazon DocumentDB in E.","why_zh":"將 MongoDB 遷移到自行管理的 EC2 instance,公司仍須負責 OS 修補、備份、複寫、擴展與容錯移轉,相較於 E 的全託管 Amazon DocumentDB 屬高營運負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/aws-iot-how-it-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/iot-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/devguide/docdb-migration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/documentdb/latest/devguide/compatibility.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-timeout.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/private-content-restricting-access-to-s3.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":506,"question_en":"A company creates an Amazon API Gateway API and shares the API with an external development team. The API uses AWS Lambda functions and is deployed to a stage that is named Production. The external development team is the sole consumer of the API. The API experiences sudden increases of usage at specific times, leading to concerns about increased costs. The company needs to limit cost and usage without reworking the Lambda functions. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司创建了一个 Amazon API Gateway API 并与外部开发团队共享该 API。该 API 使用 AWS Lambda 函数并部署到名为 Production 的阶段。 外部开发团队是该 API 的唯一消费者。该 API 在特定时间的使用量突然增加，导致人们担心成本增加。该公司需要在不重新设计 Lambda 函数的情况下限制成本和使用量。 哪种解决方案能够以最具成本效益的方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the API to send requests to Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queues instead of directly to the Lambda functions. Update the Lambda functions to consume messages from the queues and to process the requests. Set up the queues to invoke the Lambda functions when new messages arrive.","B":"Configure provisioned concurrency for each Lambda function. Use AWS Application Auto Scaling to register the Lambda functions as targets. Set up scaling schedules to increase and decrease capacity to match changes in API usage.","C":"Create an API Gateway API key and an AWS WAF Regional web ACL. Associate the web ACL with the Production stage. Add a rate-based rule to the web ACL. In the rule, specify the rate limit and a custom request aggregation that uses the X-API-Key header. Share the API key with the external development team.","D":"Create an API Gateway API Key and usage plan. Define throttling limits and quotas in the usage plan. Associate the usage plan with the Production stage and the API key. Share the API key with the external development team."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 API 以将请求发送到 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 队列，而不是直接发送到 Lambda 函数。更新 Lambda 函 数以使用队列中的消息并处理请求。设置队列以在新消息到达时调用 Lambda 函数。","B":"为每个 Lambda 函数配置预置并发。使用 AWS Application Auto Scaling 将 Lambda 函数注册为目标。设置扩展计划以增加和减 少容量，以匹配 API 使用情况的变化。","C":"创建 API 网关 API 密钥和 AWS WAF 区域 Web ACL。将 Web ACL 与生产阶段关联。向 Web ACL 添加基于速率的规则。在规则 中，指定速率限制和使用 X-API-Key 标头的自定义请求聚合。与外部开发团队共享 API 密钥。","D":"创建 API 网关 API 密钥和使用计划。在使用计划中定义限制和配额。将使用计划与生产阶段和 API 密钥关联。与外部开发团队 共享 API 密钥。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":507,"question_en":"An entertainment company hosts a ticketing service on a ­eet of Linux Amazon EC2 instances that are in an Auto Scaling group. The ticketing service uses a pricing file. The pricing file is stored in an Amazon S3 bucket that has S3 Standard storage. A central pricing solution that is hosted by a third party updates the pricing file. The pricing file is updated every 1-15 minutes and has several thousand line items. The pricing file is downloaded to each EC2 instance when the instance launches. The EC2 instances occasionally use outdated pricing information that can result in incorrect charges for customers. Which solution will resolve this problem MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家娱乐公司在 Auto Scaling 组中的一组 Linux Amazon EC2 实例上托管售票服务。售票服务使用定价文件。定价文件存储在具有 S3 标准存储的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。由第三方托管的中央定价解决方案会更新定价文件。 定价文件每 1-15 分钟更新一次，包含数千个项目。实例启动时，定价文件会下载到每个 EC2 实例。EC2 实例偶尔会使用过时的定价信息，这可能会导致向客户收取错误费用。 哪种解决方案可以最经济有效地解决此问题？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function to update an Amazon DynamoDB table with new prices each time the pricing file is updated. Update the ticketing service to use DynramoDB to look up pricing","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function to update an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file share with the pricing file each time the file is updated. Update the ticketing service to use Amazon EFS to access the pricing file.","C":"Load Mountpoint for Amazon S3 onto the AMI of the EC2 instances. Configure Mountpoint for Amazon S3 to mount the S3 bucket that contains the pricing file. Update the ticketing service to point to the mount point and path to access the $3 object,","D":"Create an Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume. Use EBS Multi-Attach to attach the volume to every EC2 instance. When a new EC2 instance launches, configure the new instance to update the pricing file on the EBS volume. Update the ticketing service to point to the new local source."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，以便在每次更新定价文件时使用新价格更新 Amazon DynamoDB 表。更新票务服务以使用 DynramoDB 查找定价","B":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，以便在每次更新定价文件时使用定价文件更新 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件共 享。更新票务服务以使用 Amazon EFS 访问定价文件。","C":"将 Amazon S3 的 Mountpoint 加载到 EC2 实例的 AMI 上。配置 Amazon S3 的 Mountpoint 以挂载包含定价文件的 S3 存储桶。更新 票务服务以指向访问 $3 对象的挂载点和路径，","D":"创建 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 卷。使用 EBS Multi-Attach 将卷附加到每个 EC2 实例。当新的 EC2 实例启动时，配 置新实例以更新 EBS 卷上的定价文件。更新票务服务以指向新的本地源。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":67,"A":33},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The root problem is that the pricing file is downloaded only once at instance launch, so instances serve outdated prices. Mountpoint for Amazon S3 mounts the S3 bucket as a local file system and translates each file read (open/read) directly into S3 GetObject API calls. Because caching in Mountpoint is opt-in (off by default) and S3 provides strong read-after-write consistency, every time the ticketing service reads the pricing file through the mount path it retrieves the current object, eliminating staleness. This is the MOST cost-effective option: it reuses the existing S3 Standard object (no new storage), requires no new always-on services, and adds only S3 GET request charges. Mountpoint runs on Linux (the instances are Linux) and is designed for read-heavy access to existing files, which matches a read-only pricing file perfectly.","explanation_zh":"問題根源在於定價檔案只在 EC2 instance 啟動時下載一次，因此 instance 會使用過時的定價。Mountpoint for Amazon S3 可將 S3 bucket 掛載為本機檔案系統，並把每次檔案讀取 (open/read) 直接轉換為 S3 GetObject API 呼叫。由於 Mountpoint 的快取為選用 (預設關閉)，加上 S3 提供強一致性 (strong read-after-write consistency)，ticketing service 每次透過掛載路徑讀取定價檔案時都會取得最新物件，徹底解決過時問題。這是最具成本效益的選項：沿用既有的 S3 Standard 物件 (無新增儲存)、不需任何常駐新服務，只增加 S3 GET 請求費用。Mountpoint 在 Linux 上執行 (本題 instance 為 Linux)，且專為對既有檔案的大量讀取設計，非常符合唯讀定價檔案的情境。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Lambda updating DynamoDB on every file change works and removes staleness, but it adds an always-on DynamoDB table (storage + read/write capacity for thousands of line items) plus a Lambda triggered every 1-15 minutes, and requires rewriting the app to do per-item key lookups. This is more costly and higher operational overhead than reading the file directly from S3, so it is not the MOST cost-effective.","why_zh":"用 Lambda 在每次檔案變更時更新 DynamoDB 雖可消除過時問題，但會新增常駐的 DynamoDB 表 (數千筆項目的儲存與讀寫容量) 與每 1-15 分鐘觸發的 Lambda，並需改寫應用程式以逐項查詢。相較直接從 S3 讀檔，成本與營運負擔更高，並非最具成本效益。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Copying the file into EFS via Lambda on every update duplicates the data into a per-GB-priced EFS file system (more expensive than S3) and adds a Lambda on every update. More cost and more moving parts than reading directly from the existing S3 object.","why_zh":"每次更新都用 Lambda 把檔案複製到 EFS，會把資料複製到按 GB 計費的 EFS 檔案系統 (比 S3 貴)，且每次更新都需執行 Lambda。比直接讀取既有 S3 物件成本更高、元件更多。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EBS Multi-Attach is supported only on io1/io2 volumes within a single Availability Zone and requires a cluster-aware file system to avoid corruption; an Auto Scaling group typically spans multiple AZs, so a single shared EBS volume cannot serve all instances. It is technically unsuitable and not cost-effective.","why_zh":"EBS Multi-Attach 僅支援 io1/io2 磁碟區且限於單一可用區，並需叢集感知檔案系統以避免資料損毀；Auto Scaling group 通常跨多個 AZ，單一共用 EBS 磁碟區無法服務所有 instance。技術上不適用且不具成本效益。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/mountpoint.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/mountpoint-usage.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/mountpoint-installation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/Welcome.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":508,"question_en":"A company has an application that uses Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group. The quality assurance (QA) department needs to launch a large number of short-lived environments to test the application. The application environments are currently launched by the manager of the department using an AWS CloudFormation template. To launch the stack, the manager uses a role with permission to use CloudFormation, EC2, and Auto Scaling APIs. The manager wants to allow testers to launch their own environments, but does not want to grant broad permissions to each user. Which set up would achieve these goals?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个应用程序，该应用程序使用 Auto Scaling 组中的 Amazon EC2 实例。质量保证 (QA) 部门需要启动大量短期环境来测试 该应用程序。应用程序环境目前由部门经理使用 AWS CloudFormation 模板启动。要启动堆栈，经理使用具有使用 CloudFormation、 EC2 和 Auto Scaling API 权限的角色。经理希望允许测试人员启动自己的环境，但不想向每个用户授予广泛的权限。 哪种设置可以实现这些目标？","options_en":{"A":"Upload the AWS CloudFormation template to Amazon S3. Give users in the QA department permission to assume the manager’s role and add a policy that restricts the permissions to the template and the resources it creates. Train users to launch the template from the CloudFormation console.","B":"Create an AWS Service Catalog product from the environment template. Add a launch constraint to the product with the existing role. Give users in the QA department permission to use AWS Service Catalog APIs only. Train users to launch the template from the AWS Service Catalog console.","C":"Upload the AWS CloudFormation template to Amazon S3. Give users in the QA department permission to use CloudFormation and S3 APIs, with conditions that restrict the permissions to the template and the resources it creates. Train users to launch the template from the CloudFormation console.","D":"Create an AWS Elastic Beanstalk application from the environment template. Give users in the QA department permission to use Elastic Beanstalk permissions only. Train users to launch Elastic Beanstalk environments with the Elastic Beanstalk CLI, passing the existing role to the environment as a service role."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 AWS CloudFormation 模板上传到 Amazon S3。授予 QA 部门的用户担任经理角色的权限，并添加限制模板及其所创建资源权 限的策略。培训用户从 CloudFormation 控制台启动模板。","B":"从环境模板创建 AWS Service Catalog 产品。使用现有角色向产品添加启动约束。授予 QA 部门用户仅使用 AWS Service Catalog API 的权限。培训用户从 AWS Service Catalog 控制台启动模板。","C":"将 AWS CloudFormation 模板上传到 Amazon S3。授予 QA 部门的用户使用 CloudFormation 和 S3 API 的权限，但要限制对模板及 其创建的资源的权限。培训用户从 CloudFormation 控制台启动模板。","D":"从环境模板创建 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 应用程序。仅授予 QA 部门的用户使用 Elastic Beanstalk 权限。培训用户使用 Elastic Beanstalk CLI 启动 Elastic Beanstalk 环境，将现有角色作为服务角色传递给环境。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":509,"question_en":"A company is using a single AWS Region for its ecommerce website. The website includes a web application that runs on several Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The website also includes an Amazon DynamoDB table. A custom domain name in Amazon Route 53 is linked to the ALB. The company created an SSL/TLS certificate in AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) and attached the certificate to the ALB. The company is not using a content delivery network as part of its design. The company wants to replicate its entire application stack in a second Region to provide disaster recovery, plan for future growth, and provide improved access time to users. A solutions architect needs to implement a solution that achieves these goals and minimizes administrative overhead. Which combination of steps should the solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在为其电子商务网站使用单个 AWS 区域。该网站包括一个 Web 应用程序，该应用程序在应用程序负载均衡器 (ALB) 后面 的多个 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。该网站还包括一个 Amazon DynamoDB 表。Amazon Route 53 中的自定义域名链接到 ALB。该公司在 AWS 证书管理器 (ACM) 中创建了一个 SSL/TLS 证书，并将该证书附加到 ALB。该公司未在其设计中使用内容交付网络。 该公司希望在第二个区域复制其整个应用程序堆栈，以提供灾难恢复、规划未来增长并为用户提供更好的访问时间。解决方案架构 师需要实施一个解决方案来实现这些目标并最大限度地减少管理开销。 解决方案架构师应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template for the current infrastructure design. Use parameters for important system values, including Region. Use the CloudFormation template to create the new infrastructure in the second Region.","B":"Use the AWS Management Console to document the existing infrastructure design in the first Region and to create the new infrastructure in the second Region.","C":"Update the Route 53 hosted zone record for the application to use weighted routing. Send 50% of the tra®c to the ALB in each Region.","D":"Update the Route 53 hosted zone record for the application to use latency-based routing. Send tra®c to the ALB in each Region.","E":"Update the configuration of the existing DynamoDB table by enabling DynamoDB Streams. Add the second Region to create a global table.","F":"Create a new DynamoDB table. Enable DynamoDB Streams for the new table. Add the second Region to create a global table. Copy the data from the existing DynamoDB table to the new table as a one-time operation."},"options_zh":{"A":"为当前基础设施设计创建 AWS CloudFormation 模板。使用参数来表示重要的系统值，包括 Region。使用 CloudFormation 模板 在第二个 Region 中创建新的基础设施。","B":"使用 AWS 管理控制台记录第一个区域中现有的基础设施设计，并在第二个区域中创建新的基础设施。","C":"更新应用程序的 Route 53 托管区域记录以使用加权路由。将 50% 的流量发送到每个区域的 ALB。","D":"更新应用程序的 Route 53 托管区域记录以使用基于延迟的路由。将流量发送到每个区域中的 ALB。","E":"通过启用 DynamoDB Streams 更新现有 DynamoDB 表的配置。添加第二个区域以创建全局表。","F":"创建新的 DynamoDB 表。为新表启用 DynamoDB Streams。添加第二个区域以创建全局表。将数据从现有 DynamoDB 表复制到新 表，作为一次性操作。"},"answer":["A","E","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ADE":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirements are disaster recovery, future growth, improved access time, and minimal administrative overhead. (A) Using a parameterized AWS CloudFormation template (with Region as a parameter) lets the architect reproduce the entire stack in the second Region as infrastructure-as-code, which is repeatable and lower overhead than manually documenting/recreating via the console (B). (D) Latency-based routing in Route 53 routes each user to the Region that gives the lowest latency, directly satisfying 'improved access time'; weighted 50/50 routing (C) does not improve per-user latency. (E) DynamoDB global tables provide managed multi-Region, multi-active replication; you add the second Region to the existing table to create the global table. The current global tables version (2019.11.21) explicitly 'supports you to add and remove replicas to Regions on a table that already contains data' by calling UpdateTable, so there is no need to build a brand-new table and copy data (F) — that is pure extra administrative overhead. E preserves the existing table and data and is the lowest-overhead path, making A, D, E the correct trio.","explanation_zh":"需求為災難復原、未來成長、改善存取時間，並將管理負擔降到最低。(A) 使用參數化的 AWS CloudFormation 範本（將 Region 設為參數），以基礎架構即程式碼方式在第二個 Region 重建整個堆疊，可重複且比用主控台手動記錄/重建 (B) 的負擔更低。(D) Route 53 的 latency-based routing 會將每位使用者導向延遲最低的 Region，直接滿足『改善存取時間』；而加權 50/50 (C) 無法改善個別使用者的延遲。(E) DynamoDB global tables 提供受管的跨 Region、多主動複寫；只需把第二個 Region 加入既有資料表即可建立 global table。目前的 global tables 版本（2019.11.21）明文指出『可在已含有資料的資料表上新增或移除 Region 的副本』（透過 UpdateTable），因此不需要新建一個全新資料表再複製資料 (F)，那只是純粹增加管理負擔。E 保留既有資料表與資料，是負擔最低的做法，故 A、D、E 為正解。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Manually documenting the existing design and rebuilding it in the second Region via the AWS Management Console is error-prone and high administrative overhead, the opposite of the 'minimize administrative overhead' goal. CloudFormation (A) does this reproducibly.","why_zh":"用主控台手動記錄既有設計並在第二個 Region 重建，容易出錯且管理負擔高，與『將管理負擔降到最低』目標相反。CloudFormation (A) 可重複地完成此事。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Weighted routing sending 50% of traffic to each Region distributes load arbitrarily by weight and does NOT route users to their lowest-latency Region, so it fails the 'improved access time to users' requirement. Latency-based routing (D) is the correct mechanism.","why_zh":"加權路由把 50% 流量送到各 Region，只依權重任意分配，並未將使用者導向延遲最低的 Region，無法滿足『改善使用者存取時間』。latency-based routing (D) 才是正確機制。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Creating a brand-new table, enabling Streams, forming the global table, then doing a one-time data copy from the old table is unnecessary work. The current DynamoDB global tables version (2019.11.21) supports adding a replica to a table that already contains data via UpdateTable, so you keep the existing table (E). F adds avoidable administrative overhead and migration risk.","why_zh":"新建一個全新資料表、啟用 Streams、組成 global table，再從舊表做一次性資料複製，是多餘的工作。目前的 DynamoDB global tables 版本（2019.11.21）可透過 UpdateTable 在已含資料的表上新增副本，因此應保留既有資料表 (E)。F 增加了可避免的管理負擔與遷移風險。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/GlobalTables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/V2globaltables_versions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-latency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":510,"question_en":"A company wants to create a single Amazon S3 bucket for its data scientists to store work-related documents. The company uses AWS IAM Identity Center to authenticate all users. A group for the data scientists was created. The company wants to give the data scientists access to only their own work. The company also wants to create monthly reports that show which documents each user accessed. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司希望为其数据科学家创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶，用于存储与工作相关的文档。该公司使用 AWS IAM Identity Center 对所有 用户进行身份验证。已为数据科学家创建了一个组。 该公司希望让数据科学家只能访问他们自己的工作。该公司还希望创建月度报告，显示每个用户访问了哪些文档。 哪种步骤组合可以满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a custom IAM Identity Center permission set to grant the data scientists access to an S3 bucket prefix that matches their username tag. Use a policy to limit access to paths with the ${aws:PrincipalTag/userName}/* condition.","B":"Create an IAM Identity Center role for the data scientists group that has Amazon S3 read access and write access. Add an S3 bucket policy that allows access to the IAM Identity Center role.","C":"Configure AWS CloudTrail to log S3 data events and deliver the logs to an S3 bucket. Use Amazon Athena to run queries on the CloudTrail logs in Amazon S3 and generate reports.","D":"Configure AWS CloudTrail to log S3 management events to CloudWatch. Use Amazon Athena’s CloudWatch connector to query the logs and generate reports.","E":"Enable S3 access logging to EMR File System (EMRFS). Use Amazon S3 Select to query logs and generate reports."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建自定义 IAM Identity Center 权限集，以授予数据科学家访问与其用户名标签匹配的 S3 存储桶前缀的权限。使用策略限制对 具有 ${aws:PrincipalTag/userName}/* 条件的路径的访问。","B":"为具有 Amazon S3 读取和写入权限的数据科学家组创建 IAM Identity Center 角色。添加允许访问 IAM Identity Center 角色的 S3 存储桶策略。","C":"配置 AWS CloudTrail 以记录 S3 数据事件并将日志传送到 S3 存储桶。使用 Amazon Athena 对 Amazon S3 中的 CloudTrail 日志运 行查询并生成报告。","D":"配置 AWS CloudTrail 以将 S3 管理事件记录到 CloudWatch。使用 Amazon Athena 的 CloudWatch 连接器查询日志并生成报告。","E":"启用 S3 访问日志记录到 EMR 文件系统 (EMRFS)。使用 Amazon S3 Select 查询日志并生成报告。"},"answer":["A","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AC":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":511,"question_en":"A company hosts a data-processing application on Amazon EC2 instances. The application polls an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system for newly uploaded files. When a new file is detected, the application extracts data from the file and runs logic to select a Docker container image to process the file. The application starts the appropriate container image and passes the file location as a parameter. The data processing that the container performs can take up to 2 hours. When the processing is complete, the code that runs inside the container writes the file back to Amazon EFS and exits. The company needs to refactor the application to eliminate the EC2 instances that are running the containers. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 Amazon EC2 实例上托管一个数据处理应用程序。该应用程序轮询 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统以查 找新上传的文件。检测到新文件时，应用程序从文件中提取数据并运行逻辑以选择 Docker 容器映像来处理该文件。应用程序启动相 应的容器映像并将文件位置作为参数传递。 容器执行的数据处理最多可能需要 2 小时。处理完成后，容器内运行的代码会将文件写回 Amazon EFS 并退出。 公司需要重构应用程序以消除运行容器的 EC2 实例。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster. Configure the processing to run as AWS Fargate tasks. Extract the container selection logic to run as an Amazon EventBridge rule that starts the appropriate Fargate task. Configure the EventBridge rule to run when files are added to the EFS file system.","B":"Create an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster. Configure the processing to run as AWS Fargate tasks. Update and containerize the container selection logic to run as a Fargate service that starts the appropriate Fargate task. Configure an EFS event notification to invoke the Fargate service when files are added to the EFS file system.","C":"Create an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster. Configure the processing to run as AWS Fargate tasks. Extract the container selection logic to run as an AWS Lambda function that starts the appropriate Fargate task. Migrate the storage of file uploads to an Amazon S3 bucket. Update the processing code to use Amazon S3. Configure an S3 event notification to invoke the Lambda function when objects are created.","D":"Create AWS Lambda container images for the processing. Configure Lambda functions to use the container images. Extract the container selection logic to run as a decision Lambda function that invokes the appropriate Lambda processing function. Migrate the storage of file uploads to an Amazon S3 bucket. Update the processing code to use Amazon S3. Configure an S3 event notification to invoke the decision Lambda function when objects are created."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 集群。配置处理以作为 AWS Fargate 任务运行。提取容器选择逻辑以作为启 动相应 Fargate 任务的 Amazon EventBridge 规则运行。配置 EventBridge 规则以在文件添加到 EFS 文件系统时运行。","B":"创建 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 集群。配置处理以作为 AWS Fargate 任务运行。更新并容器化容器选择逻辑 以作为启动适当 Fargate 任务的 Fargate 服务运行。配置 EFS 事件通知以在将文件添加到 EFS 文件系统时调用 Fargate 服务。","C":"创建 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 集群。配置处理以作为 AWS Fargate 任务运行。提取容器选择逻辑以作为启 动适当 Fargate 任务的 AWS Lambda 函数运行。将文件上传的存储迁移到 Amazon S3 存储桶。更新处理代码以使用 Amazon S3。 配置 S3 事件通知以在创建对象时调用 Lambda 函数。","D":"创建用于处理的 AWS Lambda 容器映像。配置 Lambda 函数以使用容器映像。提取容器选择逻辑以作为决策 Lambda 函数运 行，该函数调用适当的 Lambda 处理函数。将文件上传的存储迁移到 Amazon S3 存储桶。更新处理代码以使用 Amazon S3。配置 S3 事件通知以在创建对象时调用决策 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Two hard technical constraints decide this question. First, processing can take up to 2 hours, but AWS Lambda has a hard maximum timeout of 900 seconds (15 minutes), so Lambda cannot perform the processing itself (eliminates D). Second, Amazon EFS does NOT provide file-level (object-created) event notifications; it only sends service/API-level events to EventBridge via CloudTrail (e.g., CreateFileSystem or mount-target API calls), so there is no native 'new file added to EFS' event to trigger compute. That fabricated trigger eliminates both A ('EventBridge rule to run when files are added to the EFS file system') and B ('EFS event notification to invoke the Fargate service'). Option C is the only design built on real, matching capabilities: migrate uploads to Amazon S3 (which genuinely supports s3:ObjectCreated event notifications), invoke a short-lived decision Lambda that runs the lightweight container-selection logic well within 15 minutes, and have it start the appropriate AWS Fargate task via ECS RunTask. Fargate tasks have no 15-minute limit and easily run the 2-hour processing, while eliminating all EC2 instances. The dump's suggested answer (B) is wrong because it relies on a non-existent EFS event-notification feature.","explanation_zh":"兩個硬性技術限制決定了本題答案。第一,處理時間最長可達 2 小時,但 AWS Lambda 的硬性逾時上限為 900 秒(15 分鐘),因此 Lambda 無法自行執行處理(排除 D)。第二,Amazon EFS 並不提供檔案層級(物件建立)的事件通知;它只透過 CloudTrail 將服務/API 層級事件傳送至 EventBridge(例如 CreateFileSystem 或掛載目標 API 呼叫),因此並不存在原生的「EFS 新增檔案」事件可用來觸發運算。這個虛構的觸發機制同時排除了 A(『EventBridge rule 在檔案加入 EFS 時執行』)與 B(『EFS event notification 觸發 Fargate service』)。選項 C 是唯一建立在真實且相符能力之上的設計:將上傳遷移至 Amazon S3(它確實支援 s3:ObjectCreated 事件通知),由 S3 事件觸發一個短生命週期的決策 Lambda 函式執行輕量的容器選擇邏輯(遠在 15 分鐘以內完成),再透過 ECS RunTask 啟動對應的 AWS Fargate task。Fargate task 沒有 15 分鐘限制,可輕鬆執行 2 小時的處理,同時消除所有 EC2 執行個體。題庫建議答案(B)是錯的,因為它依賴一個不存在的 EFS 事件通知功能。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"EFS does not emit file-level events; you cannot configure an EventBridge rule that fires 'when files are added to the EFS file system.' EFS only sends service/API events via CloudTrail. Also, an EventBridge rule alone cannot host the custom container-selection application logic.","why_zh":"EFS 不會發出檔案層級事件,無法設定『當檔案加入 EFS 時』觸發的 EventBridge rule;EFS 只透過 CloudTrail 傳送服務/API 事件。此外,EventBridge rule 本身也無法承載自訂的容器選擇應用邏輯。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it is technically impossible: there is no such thing as an 'EFS event notification' that fires when files are uploaded. Unlike Amazon S3, EFS has no object-created notification feature, so the trigger cannot be built as described.","why_zh":"這是題庫建議答案,但技術上不可行:並不存在『EFS event notification』在檔案上傳時觸發的功能。與 Amazon S3 不同,EFS 沒有物件建立通知功能,因此無法依描述建立該觸發機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Lambda's maximum execution timeout is 900 seconds (15 minutes). Using Lambda container images for processing that can take up to 2 hours would time out and fail; container packaging does not extend the runtime limit.","why_zh":"AWS Lambda 的最大執行逾時為 900 秒(15 分鐘)。用 Lambda 容器映像執行最長 2 小時的處理會逾時失敗;以容器封裝並不會延長執行時間上限。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-timeout.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-elasticfilesystem.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/EventNotifications.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/task_definitions.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":512,"question_en":"A media company has a 30-T8 repository of digital news videos. These videos are stored on tape in an on-premises tape library and referenced by a Media Asset Management (MAM) system. The company wants to enrich the metadata for these videos in an automated fashion and put them into a searchable catalog by using a MAM feature. The company must be able to search based on information in the video, such as objects, scenery items, or people’s faces. A catalog is available that contains faces of people who have appeared in the videos that include an image of each person. The company would like to migrate these videos to AWS. The company has a high-speed AWS Direct Connect connection with AWS and would like to move the MAM solution video content directly from its current file system. How can these requirements be met by using the LEAST amount of ongoing management overhead and causing MINIMAL disruption to the existing system?","question_zh":"一家媒体公司拥有一个 30-T8 数字新闻视频存储库。这些视频存储在本地磁带库的磁带上，并由媒体资产管理 (MAM) 系统引用。该 公司希望以自动化方式丰富这些视频的元数据，并使用 MAM 功能将它们放入可搜索的目录中。该公司必须能够根据视频中的信息 进行搜索，例如物体、风景项目或人物的脸部。有一个目录可用，其中包含出现在视频中的人物的脸部，其中包括每个人的图像。 该公司希望将这些视频迁移到 AWS。 该公司与 AWS 建立了高速 AWS Direct Connect 连接，并希望将 MAM 解决方案视频内容直接从其当前文件系统移动。 如何以最少的持续管理开销和对现有系统的最小干扰来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up an AWS Storage Gateway, file gateway appliance on-premises. Use the MAM solution to extract the videos from the current archive and push them into the file gateway. Use the catalog of faces to build a collection in Amazon Rekognition. Build an AWS Lambda function that invokes the Rekognition Javascript SDK to have Rekognition pull the video from the Amazon S3 files backing the file gateway, retrieve the required metadata, and push the metadata into the MAM solution.","B":"Set up an AWS Storage Gateway, tape gateway appliance on-premises. Use the MAM solution to extract the videos from the current archive and push them into the tape gateway. Use the catalog of faces to build a collection in Amazon Rekognition. Build an AWS Lambda function that invokes the Rekognition Javascript SDK to have Amazon Rekognition process the video in the tape gateway, retrieve the required metadata, and push the metadata into the MAM solution.","C":"Configure a video ingestion stream by using Amazon Kinesis Video Streams. Use the catalog of faces to build a collection in Amazon Rekognition. Stream the videos from the MAM solution into Kinesis Video Streams. Configure Amazon Rekognition to process the streamed videos. Then, use a stream consumer to retrieve the required metadata, and push the metadata into the MAM solution. Configure the stream to store the videos in Amazon S3.","D":"Set up an Amazon EC2 instance that runs the OpenCV libraries. Copy the videos, images, and face catalog from the on-premises library into an Amazon EBS volume mounted on this EC2 instance. Process the videos to retrieve the required metadata, and push the metadata into the MAM solution, while also copying the video files to an Amazon S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"在本地设置 AWS Storage Gateway、文件网关设备。使用 MAM 解决方案从当前存档中提取视频并将其推送到文件网关。使用人 脸目录在 Amazon Rekognition 中构建集合。构建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数调用 Rekognition Javascript SDK，让 Rekognition 从支持文件网关的 Amazon S3 文件中提取视频，检索所需的元数据，并将元数据推送到 MAM 解决方案。","B":"在本地设置 AWS Storage Gateway、磁带网关设备。使用 MAM 解决方案从当前存档中提取视频并将其推送到磁带网关。使用人 脸目录在 Amazon Rekognition 中构建集合。构建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数调用 Rekognition Javascript SDK，让 Amazon Rekognition 处理磁带网关中的视频，检索所需的元数据，并将元数据推送到 MAM 解决方案中。","C":"使用 Amazon Kinesis Video Streams 配置视频提取流。使用人脸目录在 Amazon Rekognition 中构建集合。将视频从 MAM 解决方 案流式传输到 Kinesis Video Streams。配置 Amazon Rekognition 以处理流式传输的视频。然后，使用流使用者检索所需的元数 据，并将元数据推送到 MAM 解决方案。配置流以将视频存储在 Amazon S3 中。","D":"设置运行 OpenCV 库的 Amazon EC2 实例。将视频、图像和人脸目录从本地库复制到挂载在此 EC2 实例上的 Amazon EBS 卷中。 处理视频以检索所需的元数据，并将元数据推送到 MAM 解决方案，同时将视频文件复制到 Amazon S3 存储桶。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":57,"A":43},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Rekognition Video analyzes stored videos by reading them as objects from an Amazon S3 bucket via asynchronous Start/Get operations (e.g., StartFaceSearch with a face collection built from the catalog of faces). The S3 File Gateway presents an NFS/SMB file interface on-premises but stores every file as a native, durable object directly in Amazon S3, so the MAM solution can push videos through the gateway and Rekognition can then read those same objects from S3. This causes minimal disruption (videos move over Direct Connect via a familiar file interface) and least ongoing overhead (managed gateway + serverless Lambda + managed Rekognition). Option A is therefore correct. Note: Rekognition's StartFaceSearch uses a collection, not the celebrity API, and Lambda would call the standard SDK against the S3 object - but option A is still the only choice whose data path (file gateway -> S3 objects -> Rekognition) actually works.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Rekognition Video 透過非同步 Start/Get 操作（例如以人臉目錄建立的 collection 搭配 StartFaceSearch）來分析存放在 Amazon S3 儲存貯體中的影片物件。S3 File Gateway 在地端提供 NFS/SMB 檔案介面，但會把每個檔案以原生、持久的物件形式直接存放於 Amazon S3，因此 MAM 可透過 file gateway 推送影片，而 Rekognition 隨後可直接從 S3 讀取這些相同的物件。這樣對既有系統干擾最小（影片經由熟悉的檔案介面透過 Direct Connect 上傳），持續維運負擔最低（受管 gateway + 無伺服器 Lambda + 受管 Rekognition）。因此選項 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Tape Gateway stores data as proprietary virtual tapes archived in S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval / Deep Archive, not as browseable S3 objects. Rekognition Video cannot 'process the video in the tape gateway' - it only reads videos as objects from a standard S3 bucket, and Glacier-archived tape contents are not directly accessible. The data path is technically broken.","why_zh":"Tape Gateway 將資料以專屬虛擬磁帶格式封存於 S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval / Deep Archive，而非可直接存取的 S3 物件。Rekognition Video 無法『處理 tape gateway 中的影片』，它只能從標準 S3 儲存貯體讀取影片物件，而 Glacier 封存的磁帶內容無法被直接存取，資料路徑在技術上不成立。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Kinesis Video Streams with Rekognition is for real-time/live streaming face search, not for migrating and cataloging a 30 TB archive of stored files. It does not move content 'directly from its current file system' and adds significant ongoing streaming infrastructure and management overhead.","why_zh":"Kinesis Video Streams 搭配 Rekognition 適用於即時串流的人臉搜尋，而非用來遷移與編目 30 TB 的既有檔案封存。它無法『直接從現有檔案系統』搬移內容，且增加大量持續性的串流基礎設施與維運負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Running OpenCV on a self-managed EC2 instance maximizes operational overhead (build, run, scale, maintain the ML pipeline yourself), does not leverage the managed MAM/Rekognition feature, and copying to EBS first is unnecessary friction. This is the opposite of least ongoing management overhead.","why_zh":"在自管 EC2 上執行 OpenCV 會把維運負擔最大化（需自行建置、執行、擴充與維護整個 ML 流程），未善用受管的 MAM/Rekognition 功能，且先複製到 EBS 也是多餘步驟，這與『最低持續維運負擔』完全相反。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/video.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/faces-sqs-video.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/collections.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/filegateway/latest/files3/what-is-file-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/tgw/WhatIsStorageGateway.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":513,"question_en":"A company needs to optimize the cost of an AWS environment that contains multiple accounts in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company conducted cost optimization activities 3 years ago and purchased Amazon EC2 Standard Reserved Instances that recently expired. The company needs EC2 instances for 3 more years. Additionally, the company has deployed a new serverless workload. Which strategy will provide the company with the MOST cost savings?","question_zh":"一家公司需要优化 AWS Organizations 中组织内包含多个账户的 AWS 环境的成本。该公司 3 年前开展了成本优化活动，并购买了最近 已过期的 Amazon EC2 标准预留实例。 该公司还需要 EC2 实例使用 3 年。此外，该公司还部署了新的无服务器工作负载。 哪种策略可以为公司带来最大的成本节省？","options_en":{"A":"Purchase the same Reserved Instances for an additional 3-year term with All Upfront payment. Purchase a 3-year Compute Savings Plan with All Upfront payment in the management account to cover any additional compute costs","B":"Purchase a 1-year Compute Savings Plan with No Upfront payment in each member account. Use the Savings Plans recommendations in the AWS Cost Management console to choose the Compute Savings Plan.","C":"Purchase a 3-year EC2 Instance Savings Plan with No Upfront payment in the management account to cover EC2 costs in each AWS Region. Purchase a 3-year Compute Savings Plan with No Upfront payment in the management account to cover any additional compute costs.","D":"Purchase a 3-year EC2 Instance Savings Plan with All Upfront payment in each member account. Use the Savings Plans recommendations in the AWS Cost Management console to choose the EC2 Instance Savings Plan."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用全额预付款购买相同的预留实例，额外使用 3 年。在管理账户中购买全额预付款的 3 年计算储蓄计划，以支付任何额外 的计算成本","B":"在每个成员账户中购买 1 年期计算储蓄计划，无需预付款。使用 AWS 成本管理控制台中的储蓄计划建议选择计算储蓄计划。","C":"在管理账户中购买 3 年期 EC2 实例储蓄计划（无需预付款），以支付每个 AWS 区域的 EC2 费用。 在管理账户中购买 3 年期计 算储蓄计划（无需预付款），以支付任何额外的计算费用。","D":"在每个成员账户中购买 3 年期 EC2 实例 Savings Plan，并支付全部预付款。使用 AWS 成本管理控制台中的 Savings Plans 建议选 择 EC2 实例 Savings Plan。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The qualifier is MOST cost savings. Two needs exist: 3 more years of a known, stable EC2 workload (previously covered by EC2 Standard Reserved Instances) and a new serverless workload (Lambda/Fargate). Standard RIs and EC2 Instance Savings Plans both reach up to 72 percent off On-Demand, while Compute Savings Plans cap at ~66 percent but are the only commitment type that covers Lambda and Fargate. For maximum savings, payment-option depth matters: All Upfront yields the deepest discount, then Partial Upfront, then No Upfront. Option A keeps the deepest EC2 discount by renewing the same Standard RIs (72 percent ceiling) with All Upfront for the unchanged, stable workload, and adds a 3-year Compute Savings Plan with All Upfront in the management account to cover the new serverless usage and any additional compute. This combination maximizes discount on both EC2 and serverless. Option C is the same shape but uses No Upfront on both commitments, which gives strictly less savings, so it cannot be the MOST cost-effective choice.","explanation_zh":"題目的限定詞是 MOST cost savings(最大節省)。有兩項需求:再使用 3 年的已知且穩定的 EC2 工作負載(先前由 EC2 Standard Reserved Instances 涵蓋),以及新的 serverless 工作負載(Lambda/Fargate)。Standard RIs 與 EC2 Instance Savings Plans 都可達 On-Demand 的最高 72% 折扣,而 Compute Savings Plans 上限約 66%,但它是唯一能涵蓋 Lambda 與 Fargate 的承諾類型。要追求最大節省,付款方式的折扣深度很關鍵:All Upfront 折扣最深,其次 Partial Upfront,最後是 No Upfront。選項 A 對未變動的穩定工作負載以 All Upfront 續購相同的 Standard RIs(維持 72% 折扣上限),再於 management account 購買 3 年 All Upfront 的 Compute Savings Plan 以涵蓋新的 serverless 用量與其他運算。這個組合在 EC2 與 serverless 上都最大化折扣。選項 C 形態相同,但兩個承諾都用 No Upfront,節省嚴格較少,因此不是最具成本效益的選擇。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Uses a 1-year term (less discount than 3-year), No Upfront (least discount of payment options), and a Compute Savings Plan (~66 percent) for EC2 instead of the 72 percent available via Standard RI/EC2 Instance SP. It also only covers 1 year when 3 years are needed. Lowest savings overall.","why_zh":"採用 1 年期(折扣低於 3 年)、No Upfront(付款方式中折扣最低),且以 Compute Savings Plan(約 66%)涵蓋 EC2,而非 Standard RI/EC2 Instance SP 可得的 72%。又只涵蓋 1 年,但需求是 3 年。整體節省最少。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Correct coverage shape (EC2 Instance SP for EC2 plus Compute SP for serverless), but both are No Upfront, which yields the smallest discount of the payment options. All Upfront (Option A) gives strictly more savings, so C is not the MOST cost-effective.","why_zh":"涵蓋結構正確(EC2 Instance SP 涵蓋 EC2,Compute SP 涵蓋 serverless),但兩者都是 No Upfront,在付款方式中折扣最小。All Upfront(選項 A)節省更多,因此 C 並非最具成本效益。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A 3-year EC2 Instance Savings Plan does not cover Lambda or Fargate, so it fails to address the new serverless workload at all. It only covers EC2, leaving the serverless requirement unmet.","why_zh":"3 年的 EC2 Instance Savings Plan 不涵蓋 Lambda 或 Fargate,完全無法處理新的 serverless 工作負載。它只涵蓋 EC2,使 serverless 需求無法滿足。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/savingsplans/latest/userguide/plan-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/savingsplans/latest/userguide/sp-ris.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/savingsplans/latest/userguide/sp-applying.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/savingsplans/latest/userguide/what-is-savings-plans.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":514,"question_en":"A company operates a static content distribution platform that serves customers globally. The customers consume content from their own AWS accounts. The company serves its content from an Amazon S3 bucket. The company uploads the content from its on-premises environment to the S3 bucket by using an S3 File Gateway. The company wants to improve the platform’s performance and reliability by serving content from the AWS Region that is geographically closest to customers. The company must route the on-premises data to Amazon S3 with minimal latency and without public internet exposure. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司运营一个静态内容分发平台，为全球客户提供服务。客户使用他们自己的 AWS 账户中的内容。 该公司从 Amazon S3 存储桶提供其内容。该公司使用 S3 文件网关将内容从其本地环境上传到 S3 存储桶。 该公司希望通过从地理位置最接近客户的 AWS 区域提供内容来提高平台的性能和可靠性。该公司必须以最小的延迟将本地数据路由 到 Amazon S3，并且不会公开互联网。 哪些步骤组合能够以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Implement S3 Multi-Region Access Points","B":"Use S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) to copy content to different Regions","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function that tracks the routing of clients to Regions","D":"Use an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection to connect to a Multi-Region Access Point.","E":"Use AWS PrivateLink and AWS Direct Connect to connect to a Multi-Region Access Point."},"options_zh":{"A":"实施 S3 多区域接入点","B":"使用 S3 跨区域复制 (CRR) 将内容复制到不同区域","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来跟踪客户端到区域的路由","D":"使用 AWS Site-to-Site VPN 连接来连接到多区域接入点。","E":"使用 AWS PrivateLink 和 AWS Direct Connect 连接到多区域接入点。"},"answer":["C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AE":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The question has two requirements. First, serve content from the AWS Region geographically closest to customers with least operational overhead: S3 Multi-Region Access Points (A) provide a single global endpoint that uses AWS Global Accelerator to automatically route each request over the AWS global network to the closest S3 bucket with an active routing status. This is fully managed, so no custom routing logic is needed. Second, route on-premises data to S3 with minimal latency and no public internet exposure: AWS Direct Connect provides a dedicated, private, low-latency link from the data center to AWS (bypassing the public internet), and AWS PrivateLink (a com.amazonaws.s3-global.accesspoint interface endpoint) lets that traffic reach the Multi-Region Access Point global endpoint over private IPs. AWS docs explicitly list 'Traffic from on-premises data centers traveling over AWS PrivateLink' as a supported MRAP source. Therefore A and E together meet all requirements with the least operational overhead.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個需求。第一,以最少維運負擔從地理位置最接近客戶的 AWS Region 提供內容:S3 Multi-Region Access Points (A) 提供單一全球端點,透過 AWS Global Accelerator 自動將每個請求經由 AWS 全球網路路由到具有 active routing status 且距離最近的 S3 bucket,完全託管,無需自訂路由邏輯。第二,以最低延遲且不暴露於公網的方式將地端資料送往 S3:AWS Direct Connect 提供從資料中心到 AWS 的專用私有低延遲連線(繞過公網),而 AWS PrivateLink(com.amazonaws.s3-global.accesspoint 介面端點)讓該流量以私有 IP 連到 Multi-Region Access Point 全球端點。AWS 文件明確將「來自地端資料中心經由 AWS PrivateLink 的流量」列為 MRAP 支援的來源。因此 A 與 E 合併即以最少維運負擔滿足所有需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"S3 Cross-Region Replication only copies objects to buckets in other Regions; it does not provide any geographic routing of client requests. CRR is a prerequisite that MRAP uses underneath, but by itself it cannot serve customers from the closest Region, so it is not one of the two answers that meet the requirement.","why_zh":"S3 Cross-Region Replication 只是把物件複製到其他 Region 的 bucket,本身不提供任何依地理位置路由客戶請求的能力。CRR 是 MRAP 底層會用到的前提,但單靠它無法從最近的 Region 為客戶提供服務,因此不是滿足需求的兩個答案之一。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Building a Lambda function to track and route clients to Regions is exactly the custom, self-managed routing logic that MRAP eliminates. It maximizes operational overhead rather than minimizing it, directly contradicting the 'LEAST operational overhead' qualifier. This is the dump's wrong pick.","why_zh":"建立 Lambda 函數來追蹤並將客戶路由到各 Region,正是 MRAP 所要消除的自訂、需自行維護的路由邏輯,會大幅增加而非降低維運負擔,直接違反『最少維運負擔』的條件。這是 dump 的錯誤選項。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A Site-to-Site VPN to a Multi-Region Access Point rides over the public internet (encrypted) and offers variable, generally higher latency. The requirement is minimal latency and no public internet exposure, which favors Direct Connect's dedicated private link over a VPN tunnel.","why_zh":"連到 Multi-Region Access Point 的 Site-to-Site VPN 是走公網(加密)且延遲較不穩定且通常較高。需求是最低延遲且不暴露於公網,因此 Direct Connect 的專用私有連線優於 VPN 通道。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/MultiRegionAccessPoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/MultiRegionAccessConfiguration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/MultiRegionAccessPointsPrivateLink.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directconnect/latest/UserGuide/Welcome.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":515,"question_en":"A company is migrating its data center to the AWS Cloud and needs to complete the migration as quickly as possible. The company has many applications that are running on hundreds of VMware VMs in the data center. Each VM is configured with a shared Windows folder that contains common shared files. The file share is larger than 100 GB in size. The company’s compliance team requires a change request to be ­ed and approved for every software installation and modification to each VM. The company has an AWS Direct Connect connection with 10 GB of bandwidth between AWS and the data center. Which set of steps should the company take to complete the migration in the LEAST amount of time?","question_zh":"一家公司正在将其数据中心迁移到 AWS 云，并且需要尽快完成迁移。该公司有许多应用程序在数据中心的数百台 VMware VM 上运 行。每个 VM 都配置了一个共享 Windows 文件夹，其中包含常见的共享文件。文件共享的大小大于 100 GB。 该公司的合规团队要求对每个 VM 的每个软件安装和修改都提交并批准变更请求。该公司在 AWS 和数据中心之间建立了一个 AWS Direct Connect 连接，带宽为 10 GB。 公司应采取哪些步骤才能在最短的时间内完成迁移？","options_en":{"A":"Use VM ImporvExport to create images of each VM. Use AWS Application Migration Service to manage and view the images. Copy the Windows file share data to an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. After migration, remap the file share to the EFS file system.","B":"Deploy the AWS Application Discovery Service agentless appliance to VMware vCenter. Review the portfolio of discovered VMs in AWS Migration Hub.","C":"Create and review a portfolio in AWS Migration Hub. Order an AWS Snowcone device. Deploy AWS Application Migration Service to VMware vCenter and export all the VMs to the Snowcone device. Copy all Windows file share data to the Snowcone device. Ship the Snowcone device to AWS. Use Application Migration Service to deploy all the migrated instances.","D":"Deploy the AWS Application Discovery Service Agent and the AWS Application Migration Service Agent onto each VMware hypervisor directly. Review the portfolio in AWS Migration Hub. Copy each VM’s file share data to a new Amazon FSx for Windows File Server file system. After migration, remap the file share on each VM to the FSx for Windows File Server file system."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 VM ImporvExport 创建每个 VM 的映像。使用 AWS Application Migration Service 管理和查看映像。将 Windows 文件共享数据 复制到 Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) 文件系统。迁移后，将文件共享重新映射到 EFS 文件系统。","B":"将 AWS Application Discovery Service 无代理设备部署到 VMware vCenter。查看 AWS Migration Hub 中发现的虚拟机组合。","C":"在 AWS Migration Hub 中创建并审查产品组合。订购 AWS Snowcone 设备。将 AWS Application Migration Service 部署到 VMware vCenter 并将所有 VM 导出到 Snowcone 设备。将所有 Windows 文件共享数据复制到 Snowcone 设备。将 Snowcone 设备运送到 AWS。使用 Application Migration Service 部署所有迁移的实例。","D":"将 AWS Application Discovery Service Agent 和 AWS Application Migration Service Agent 直接部署到每个 VMware 虚拟机管理程序 上。查看 AWS Migration Hub 中的产品组合。将每个虚拟机的文件共享数据复制到新的 Amazon FSx for Windows File Server 文件系 统。迁移后，将每个虚拟机上的文件共享重新映射到 FSx for Windows File Server 文件系统。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is completing the migration in the LEAST amount of time, and the company has a high-bandwidth 10 Gbps Direct Connect link available. Network-based replication with AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) over that link is the fastest path for hundreds of VMs, and the Windows SMB shared folder must land on Amazon FSx for Windows File Server (a fully managed Windows/SMB file system), not EFS (which is NFS/Linux-oriented). Option D is the only end-to-end, technically valid path: discover with Application Discovery Service, manage in Migration Hub, replicate with MGN over Direct Connect, and migrate the SMB share to FSx for Windows File Server, then remap. The marked answer A is broken because MGN does not 'manage/view images' produced by VM Import/Export (different services) and EFS is the wrong target for a Windows SMB share. The community answer C is also technically impossible: MGN performs continuous block-level replication directly into AWS as EBS snapshots and cannot 'export VMs to a Snowcone device'; furthermore a single Snowcone (~8 TB HDD / ~14 TB SSD) plus physical shipping would be slower and capacity-constrained for hundreds of VMs when a 10 Gbps Direct Connect is already in place.","explanation_zh":"決定性條件是以最短時間完成遷移，且公司已具備 10 Gbps 的高頻寬 Direct Connect 連線。透過該連線使用 AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) 進行網路型複寫，是遷移數百台 VM 的最快路徑；而 Windows SMB 共享資料夾應落在 Amazon FSx for Windows File Server（全受管的 Windows/SMB 檔案系統），而非 EFS（屬 NFS/Linux 導向）。選項 D 是唯一端到端且技術正確的路徑：以 Application Discovery Service 探索、在 Migration Hub 管理、透過 Direct Connect 以 MGN 複寫，並將 SMB 共享遷移至 FSx for Windows File Server 後重新映射。被標記的答案 A 不成立，因為 MGN 不會去『管理/檢視』由 VM Import/Export 產生的映像（屬不同服務），且 EFS 並非 Windows SMB 共享的正確目標。社群答案 C 在技術上也不可行：MGN 會持續以區塊層級直接複寫成 AWS 上的 EBS 快照，無法『將 VM 匯出到 Snowcone 裝置』；況且單一 Snowcone（約 8 TB HDD / 14 TB SSD）加上實體運送，對於數百台 VM 而言容量受限且更慢，尤其在已有 10 Gbps Direct Connect 的情況下。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"MGN does not manage or view images created by VM Import/Export (they are separate, incompatible workflows), and Amazon EFS is an NFS/Linux file system that is the wrong target for a Windows SMB share (FSx for Windows File Server is correct).","why_zh":"MGN 不會管理或檢視由 VM Import/Export 產生的映像（兩者為各自獨立、不相容的流程），且 Amazon EFS 屬 NFS/Linux 檔案系統，並非 Windows SMB 共享的正確目標（正確應為 FSx for Windows File Server）。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"This only performs discovery and assessment (Application Discovery Service appliance + Migration Hub portfolio). It does not actually migrate any VM or file data, so it cannot complete the migration.","why_zh":"此選項僅進行探索與評估（Application Discovery Service 設備 + Migration Hub 投資組合），並未實際遷移任何 VM 或檔案資料，因此無法完成遷移。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Technically impossible: MGN replicates block-level data over the network into AWS as EBS snapshots and cannot 'export VMs to a Snowcone device.' A single Snowcone (~8 TB HDD / ~14 TB SSD) plus physical shipping would be slower and capacity-constrained for hundreds of VMs, especially when a 10 Gbps Direct Connect is already available for fast network replication.","why_zh":"技術上不可行：MGN 透過網路將區塊層級資料以 EBS 快照形式複寫進 AWS，無法『將 VM 匯出到 Snowcone 裝置』。單一 Snowcone（約 8 TB HDD / 14 TB SSD）加實體運送對數百台 VM 而言更慢且容量受限，尤其在已有 10 Gbps Direct Connect 可進行快速網路複寫的情況下。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/mgn/latest/ug/installing-vcenter-overview-mgn.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/mgn/latest/ug/migration_at_scale.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/mgn/latest/ug/replicating-vcenter-aws-mgn.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/WindowsGuide/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/WindowsGuide/using-file-shares.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/snowball/latest/developer-guide/device-differences.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":516,"question_en":"A company has multiple AWS accounts that are in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company needs to store AWS account activity and query the data from a central location by using SQL. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Organizations 中的某个组织内拥有多个 AWS 账户。该公司需要存储 AWS 账户活动并使用 SQL 从中心位置查询数 据。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CloudTraii trail in each account. Specify CloudTrail management events for the trail. Configure CloudTrail to send the events to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Configure CloudWatch cross-account observability. Query the data in CloudWatch Logs Insights.","B":"Use a delegated administrator account to create an AWS CloudTrail Lake data store. Specify CloudTrail management events for the data store. Enable the data store for all accounts in the organization. Query the data in CloudTrail Lake.","C":"Use a delegated administrator account to create an AWS CloudTral trail. Specify CloudTrail management events for the trail. Enable the trail for all accounts in the organization. Keep all other settings as default. Query the CloudTrail data from the CloudTrail event history page.","D":"Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy AWS CloudTrail Lake data stores in each account. Specify CloudTrail management events for the data stores. Keep all other settings as default, Query the data in CloudTrail Lake."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个账户中创建一个 AWS CloudTraii 跟踪。为跟踪指定 CloudTrail 管理事件。配置 CloudTrail 以将事件发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。配置 CloudWatch 跨账户可观察性。查询 CloudWatch Logs Insights 中的数据。","B":"使用委派管理员账户创建 AWS CloudTrail Lake 数据存储。为数据存储指定 CloudTrail 管理事件。为组织中的所有账户启用数据 存储。查询 CloudTrail Lake 中的数据。","C":"使用委派管理员账户创建 AWS CloudTral 跟踪。为跟踪指定 CloudTrail 管理事件。为组织中的所有账户启用跟踪。保留所有其 他设置作为默认设置。从 CloudTrail 事件历史记录页面查询 CloudTrail 数据。","D":"使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 在每个账户中部署 AWS CloudTrail Lake 数据存储。为数据存储指定 CloudTrail 管理事件。保 留所有其他设置作为默认设置，查询 CloudTrail Lake 中的数据。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":517,"question_en":"A company is using AWS to develop and manage its production web application. The application includes an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API that invokes an AWS Lambda function. The Lambda function processes and then stores data in a database. The company wants to implement user authorization for the web application in an integrated way. The company already uses a third-party identity provider that issues OAuth tokens for the company’s other applications. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS 开发和管理其生产 Web 应用程序。该应用程序包括一个 Amazon API Gateway HTTP API，用于调用 AWS Lambda 函数。Lambda 函数处理数据，然后将数据存储在数据库中。 该公司希望以集成方式为 Web 应用程序实施用户授权。该公司已经使用第三方身份提供商为公司的其他应用程序颁发 OAuth 令牌。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Integrate the company’s third-party identity provider with API Gateway. Configure an API Gateway Lambda authorizer to validate tokens from the identity provider. Require the Lambda authorizer on all API routes. Update the web application to get tokens from the identity provider and include the tokens in the Authorization header when calling the API Gateway HTTP API.","B":"Integrate the company's third-party identity provider with AWS Directory Service. Configure Directory Service as an API Gateway authorizer to validate tokens from the identity provider. Require the Directory Service authorizer on all API routes. Configure AWS IAM Identity Center as a SAML 2.0 identity Provider. Configure the web application as a custom SAML 2.0 application.","C":"Integrate the company’s third-party identity provider with AWS IAM Identity Center. Configure API Gateway to use IAM Identity Center for zero-configuration authentication and authorization. Update the web application to retrieve AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) tokens from IAM Identity Center and include the tokens in the Authorization header when calling the API Gateway HTTP API.","D":"Integrate the company’s third-party identity provider with AWS IAM Identity Center. Configure IAM users with permissions to call the API Gateway HTTP API. Update the web application to extract request parameters from the IAM users and include the parameters in the Authorization header when calling the API Gateway HTTP API."},"options_zh":{"A":"将公司的第三方身份提供商与 API Gateway 集成。配置 API Gateway Lambda 授权器以验证来自身份提供商的令牌。要求所有 API 路由都使用 Lambda 授权器。更新 Web 应用程序以从身份提供商获取令牌，并在调用 API Gateway HTTP API 时将令牌包含在 授权标头中。","B":"将公司的第三方身份提供商与 AWS Directory Service 集成。将 Directory Service 配置为 API Gateway 授权者，以验证来自身份提 供商的令牌。要求所有 API 路由都使用 Directory Service 授权者。将 AWS IAM Identity Center 配置为 SAML 2.0 身份提供商。将 Web 应用程序配置为自定义 SAML 2.0 应用程序。","C":"将公司的第三方身份提供商与 AWS IAM Identity Center 集成。配置 API Gateway 以使用 IAM Identity Center 进行零配置身份验证 和授权。更新 Web 应用程序以从 IAM Identity Center 检索 AWS 安全令牌服务 (AWS STS) 令牌，并在调用 API Gateway HTTP API 时 将令牌包含在授权标头中。","D":"将公司的第三方身份提供商与 AWS IAM Identity Center 集成。配置具有调用 API 网关 HTTP API 权限的 IAM 用户。更新 Web 应用 程序以从 IAM 用户提取请求参数，并在调用 API 网关 HTTP API 时将参数包含在授权标头中。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":518,"question_en":"A company has deployed applications to thousands of Amazon EC2 instances in an AWS account. A security audit discovers that several unencrypted Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes are attached to the EC2 instances. The company’s security policy requires the EBS volumes to be encrypted. The company needs to implement an automated solution to encrypt the EBS volumes. The solution also must prevent development teams from creating unencrypted EBS volumes. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司已将应用程序部署到 AWS 账户中的数千个 Amazon EC2 实例。安全审计发现，EC2 实例上附加了多个未加密的 Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) 卷。该公司的安全策略要求对 EBS 卷进行加密。 该公司需要实施自动化解决方案来加密 EBS 卷。该解决方案还必须阻止开发团队创建未加密的 EBS 卷。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the AWS Config managed rule that identifies unencrypted EBS volumes. Configure an automatic remediation action. Associate an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook that includes the steps to create a new encrypted EBS volume. Create an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key. In the key policy, include a statement to deny the creation of unencrypted EBS volumes.","B":"Use AWS Systems Manager Fleet Manager to create a list of unencrypted EBS volumes, Create a Systems Manager Automation runbook that includes the steps to create a new encrypted EBS volume. Create an SCP to deny the creation of unencrypted EBS volumes.","C":"Use AWS Systems Manager Fleet Manager to create a list of unencrypted EBS volumes. Create a Systems Manager Automation runbook that includes the steps to create a new encrypted EBS volume. Modify the AWS account setting for EBS encryption to always encrypt new EBS volumes.","D":"Configure the AWS Config managed rule that identifies unencrypted EBS volumes. Configure an automatic remediation action. Associate an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook that includes the steps to create a new encrypted EBS volume. Modify the AWS account setting for EBS encryption to always encrypt new EBS volumes."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置识别未加密 EBS 卷的 AWS Config 托管规则。配置自动补救措施。关联包含创建新加密 EBS 卷的步骤的 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册。创建 AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) 客户管理密钥。在密钥策略中，包含拒绝创建未加 密 EBS 卷的声明。","B":"使用 AWS Systems Manager Fleet Manager 创建未加密 EBS 卷列表，创建包含创建新加密 EBS 卷的步骤的 Systems Manager Automation 运行手册。创建 SCP 以拒绝创建未加密的 EBS 卷。","C":"使用 AWS Systems Manager Fleet Manager 创建未加密 EBS 卷列表。创建一个 Systems Manager Automation 运行手册，其中包含 创建新加密 EBS 卷的步骤。修改 AWS 账户的 EBS 加密设置，以始终加密新的 EBS 卷。","D":"配置识别未加密 EBS 卷的 AWS Config 托管规则。配置自动补救措施。关联包含创建新加密 EBS 卷的步骤的 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册。修改 EBS 加密的 AWS 账户设置以始终加密新的 EBS 卷。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The solution needs two things: automated remediation of existing unencrypted volumes, and a control that prevents creation of new unencrypted volumes. AWS Config with a managed rule (encrypted-volumes) detects unencrypted EBS volumes and can trigger an SSM Automation runbook for auto-remediation. To enforce encryption going forward, enabling EBS encryption by default at the account/Region level guarantees that every newly created EBS volume is automatically encrypted, which prevents dev teams from creating unencrypted volumes. Option A is wrong because a KMS key policy controls access to a key; it cannot deny the creation of unencrypted EBS volumes (those volumes do not use that key at all). Options B and C misuse Systems Manager Fleet Manager, which manages instances/nodes and does not produce a list of unencrypted EBS volumes.","explanation_zh":"此方案需要兩件事：自動修復現有未加密磁碟區，以及防止建立新的未加密磁碟區。AWS Config 受管規則 (encrypted-volumes) 可偵測未加密 EBS 磁碟區，並觸發 SSM Automation runbook 進行自動修復。要強制未來加密，於帳戶/區域層級啟用 EBS 預設加密 (encryption by default) 可保證每個新建立的 EBS 磁碟區都自動加密，從而防止開發團隊建立未加密磁碟區。選項 A 錯誤，因為 KMS 金鑰政策只控制對金鑰的存取，無法拒絕建立未加密 EBS 磁碟區（這些磁碟區根本不使用該金鑰）。選項 B 和 C 誤用了 Systems Manager Fleet Manager，它管理執行個體/節點，無法產生未加密 EBS 磁碟區的清單。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A KMS key policy governs access to that key; it cannot deny the creation of unencrypted EBS volumes, so it fails the prevention requirement.","why_zh":"KMS 金鑰政策只管控對該金鑰的存取，無法拒絕建立未加密 EBS 磁碟區，因此無法滿足防止建立的需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Fleet Manager manages managed nodes/instances and does not enumerate unencrypted EBS volumes; an SCP can deny CreateVolume without encryption but the detection step is wrong.","why_zh":"Fleet Manager 管理受管節點/執行個體，無法列出未加密 EBS 磁碟區；雖然 SCP 可拒絕未加密的 CreateVolume，但偵測步驟有誤。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Same Fleet Manager misuse for detection as B; the default-encryption part is correct but the listing approach is invalid.","why_zh":"偵測部分與 B 相同地誤用 Fleet Manager；預設加密部分正確，但列出磁碟區的方式無效。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/EBSEncryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/encrypted-volumes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/remediation.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":519,"question_en":"A company is running a large containerized workload in the AWS Cloud. The workload consists of approximately 100 different services. The company uses Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) to orchestrate the workload. Recently the company’s development team started using AWS Fargate instead of Amazon EC2 instances in the ECS cluster. In the past, the workload has come close to running the maximum number of EC2 instances that are available in the account. The company is worried that the workload could reach the maximum number of ECS tasks that are allowed. A solutions architect must implement a solution that will notify the development team when Fargate reaches 80% of the maximum number of tasks. What should the solutions architect do to meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 云中运行大型容器化工作负载。该工作负载由大约 100 种不同的服务组成。该公司使用 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 来编排工作负载。 最近，该公司的开发团队开始在 ECS 集群中使用 AWS Fargate 而不是 Amazon EC2 实例。过去，工作负载已接近运行账户中可用的最 大 EC2 实例数。 公司担心工作负载可能会达到允许的最大 ECS 任务数。解决方案架构师必须实施一个解决方案，当 Fargate 达到最大任务数的 80% 时通知开发团队。 解决方案架构师应该怎么做才能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor the Sample Count statistic for each service in the ECS cluster. Set an alarm for when the math expression sample count/SERVICE_QUOTA(service)*100 is greater than 80. Notify the development team by using Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS).","B":"Use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor service quotas that are published under the AWS/Usage metric namespace. Set an alarm for when the math expression metric/SERVICE_QUOTA(metric)*100 is greater than 80. Notify the development team by using Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS).","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function to poll detailed metrics from the ECS cluster. When the number of running Fargate tasks is greater than 80, invoke Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) to notify the development team.","D":"Create an AWS Config rule to evaluate whether the Fargate SERVICE_QUOTA is greater than 80. Use Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) to notify the development team when the AWS Config rule is not compliant."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 监控 ECS 集群中每项服务的样本计数统计数据。当数学表达式样本计数/SERVICE_QUOTA(service)*100 大于 80 时设置警报。使用 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 通知开发团队。","B":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 监控在 AWS/Usage 指标命名空间下发布的服务配额。当数学表达式 metric/SERVICE_QUOTA(metric)*100 大于 80 时设置警报。使用 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 通知开发团队。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来从 ECS 集群轮询详细指标。当正在运行的 Fargate 任务数量大于 80 时，调用 Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) 来通知开发团队。","D":"创建 AWS Config 规则来评估 Fargate SERVICE_QUOTA 是否大于 80。当 AWS Config 规则不合规时，使用 Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) 通知开发团队。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":520,"question_en":"A company has several AWS Lambda functions written in Python. The functions are deployed with the .zip package deployment type. The functions use a Lambda layer that contains common libraries and packages in a .zip file. The Lambda .zip packages and Lambda layer .zip file are stored in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company must implement automatic scanning of the Lambda functions and the Lambda layer to identify CVEs. A subset of the Lambda functions must receive automated code scans to detect potential data leaks and other vulnerabilities. The code scans must occur only for selected Lambda functions, not all the Lambda functions. Which combination of actions will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司有多个用 Python 编写的 AWS Lambda 函数。这些函数使用 .zip 包部署类型进行部署。这些函数使用包含 .zip 文件中的公共 库和包的 Lambda 层。Lambda .zip 包和 Lambda 层 .zip 文件存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。 该公司必须实施 Lambda 函数和 Lambda 层的自动扫描以识别 CVE。Lambda 函数的子集必须接受自动代码扫描以检测潜在的数据泄 露和其他漏洞。代码扫描必须仅针对选定的 Lambda 函数进行，而不是所有 Lambda 函数。 哪些行动组合可以满足这些要求？（选择三个。）","options_en":{"A":"Activate Amazon Inspector. Start automated CVE scans.","B":"Activate Lambda standard scanning and Lambda code scanning in Amazon Inspector.","C":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty. Enable the Lambda Protection feature in GuardDuty.","D":"Enable scanning in the Monitor settings of the Lambda functions that need code scans.","E":"Tag Lambda functions that do not need code scans. In the tag, include a key of InspectorCodeExclusion and a value of LambdaCodeScanning.","F":"Use Amazon Inspector to scan the 3 bucket that contains the Lambda .zip packages and the Lambda layer .zip file for code scans."},"options_zh":{"A":"激活 Amazon Inspector。开始自动 CVE 扫描。","B":"在 Amazon Inspector 中激活 Lambda 标准扫描和 Lambda 代码扫描。","C":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty。在 GuardDuty 中启用 Lambda Protection 功能。","D":"在需要代码扫描的 Lambda 函数的监控设置中启用扫描。","E":"标记不需要代码扫描的 Lambda 函数。在标记中，包含一个键 InspectorCodeExclusion 和一个值 LambdaCodeScanning。","F":"使用 Amazon Inspector 扫描包含 Lambda .zip 包和 Lambda 层 .zip 文件的 3 个存储桶以进行代码扫描。"},"answer":["A","B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ABE":100},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":521,"question_en":"A company is changing the way that it handles patching of Amazon EC2 instances in its application account. The company currently patches instances over the internet by using a NAT gateway in a VPC in the application account. The company has EC2 instances set up as a patch source repository in a dedicated private VPC in a core account. The company wants to use AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager and the patch source repository in the core account to patch the EC2 instances in the application account. The company must prevent all EC2 instances in the application account from accessing the internet. The EC2 instances in the application account need to access Amazon S3, where the application data is stored. These EC2 instances need connectivity to Systems Manager and to the patch source repository in the private VPC in the core account. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在改变其应用程序账户中处理 Amazon EC2 实例修补的方式。该公司目前使用应用程序账户中 VPC 中的 NAT 网关通过互 联网修补实例。该 公司在核心账户中的专用私有 VPC 中将 EC2 实例设置为补丁源存储库。该公司希望使用 AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager 和核心 账户中的补丁源存储库来修补应用程序账户中的 EC2 实例。该公司必须阻止应用程序账户中的所有 EC2 实例访问互联网。 应用程序账户中的 EC2 实例需要访问存储应用程序数据的 Amazon S3。这些 EC2 实例需要连接到 Systems Manager 以及核心账户中 私有 VPC 中的补丁源存储库。 哪种解决方案可以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a network ACL that blocks outbound tra®c on port 80. Associate the network ACL with all subnets in the application account. In the application account and the core account, deploy one EC2 instance that runs a custom VPN server. Create a VPN tunnel to access the private VPC. Update the route table in the application account.","B":"Create private VIFs for Systems Manager and Amazon S3. Delete the NAT gateway from the VPC in the application account. Create a transit gateway to access the patch source repository EC2 instances in the core account. Update the route table in the core account.","C":"Create VPC endpoints for Systems Manager and Amazon S3. Delete the NAT gateway from the VPC in the application account. Create a VPC peering connection to access the patch source repository EC2 instances in the core account. Update the route tables in both accounts.","D":"Create a network ACL that blocks inbound tra®c on port 80. Associate the network ACL with all subnets in the application account. Create a transit gateway to access the patch source repository EC2 instances in the core account. Update the route tables in both accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个网络 ACL，阻止端口 80 上的出站流量。将网络 ACL 与应用程序账户中的所有子网关联。在应用程序账户和核心账户 中，部署一个运行自定义 VPN 服务器的 EC2 实例。创建 VPN 隧道以访问私有 VPC。更新应用程序账户中的路由表。","B":"为 Systems Manager 和 Amazon S3 创建私有 VIF。从应用程序账户中的 VPC 中删除 NAT 网关。创建一个中转网关以访问核心账 户中的补丁源存储库 EC2 实例。更新核心账户中的路由表。","C":"为 Systems Manager 和 Amazon S3 创建 VPC 终端节点。从应用程序账户中的 VPC 中删除 NAT 网关。创建 VPC 对等连接以访问 核心账户中的补丁源存储库 EC2 实例。更新两个账户中的路由表。","D":"创建一个网络 ACL，阻止端口 80 上的入站流量。将网络 ACL 与应用程序账户中的所有子网关联。创建一个中转网关以访问核 心账户中的补丁源存储库 EC2 实例。更新两个账户中的路由表。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":522,"question_en":"A company in the United States (US) has acquired a company in Europe. Both companies use the AWS Cloud. The US company has built a new application with a microservices architecture. The US company is hosting the application across five VPCs in the us-east-2 Region. The application must be able to access resources in one VPC in the eu-west-1 Region. However, the application must not be able to access any other VPCs. The VPCs in both Regions have no overlapping CIDR ranges. All accounts are already consolidated in one organization in AWS Organizations. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"美国一家公司收购了欧洲一家公司。两家公司都使用 AWS 云。美国公司已构建了一个采用微服务架构的新应用程序。美国公司正在 us-east-2 区域的五个 VPC 中托管该应用程序。该应用程序必须能够访问 eu-west-1 区域中的一个 VPC 中的资源。 但是，该应用程序不得访问任何其他 VPC。 两个区域中的 VPC 没有重叠的 CIDR 范围。所有账户已合并到 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织中。 哪种解决方案能够最经济高效地满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create one transit gateway in eu-west-1. Attach the VPCs in us-east-2 and the VPC in eu-west-1 to the transit gateway. Create the necessary route entries in each VPC so that the tra®c is routed through the transit gateway.","B":"Create one transit gateway in each Region. Attach the involved subnets to the regional transit gateway. Create the necessary route entries in the associated route tables for each subnet so that the tra®c is routed through the regional transit gateway. Peer the two transit gateways.","C":"Create a full mesh VPC peering connection configuration between all the VPCs. Create the necessary route entries in each VPC so that the tra®c is routed through the VPC peering connection.","D":"Create one VPC peering connection for each VPC in us-east-2 to the VPC in eu-west-1. Create the necessary route entries in each VPC so that the tra®c is routed through the VPC peering connection."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 eu-west-1 中创建一个中转网关。将 us-east-2 中的 VPC 和 eu-west-1 中的 VPC 附加到中转网关。在每个 VPC 中创建必要的路 由条目，以便流量通过中转网关路由。","B":"在每个区域创建一个中转网关。将相关子网连接到区域中转网关。在每个子网的关联路由表中创建必要的路由条目，以便流 量通过区域中转网关路由。将两个中转网关对等连接。","C":"在所有 VPC 之间创建全网格 VPC 对等连接配置。在每个 VPC 中创建必要的路由条目，以便流量通过 VPC 对等连接进行路由。","D":"为 us-east-2 中的每个 VPC 创建一个到 eu-west-1 中的 VPC 的 VPC 对等连接。在每个 VPC 中创建必要的路由条目，以便流量通 过 VPC 对等连接进行路由。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":83,"A":17},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":523,"question_en":"A travel company built a web application that uses Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) to send email notifications to users. The company needs to enable logging to help troubleshoot email delivery issues. The company also needs the ability to do searches that are based on recipient, subject, and time sent. Which combination of steps should a solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家旅游公司构建了一个 Web 应用程序，该应用程序使用 Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) 向用户发送电子邮件通知。该 公司需要启用日志记录来帮助解决电子邮件传递问题。该公司还需要能够根据收件人、主题和发送时间进行搜索。 解决方案架构师应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon SES configuration set with Amazon Data Firehose as the destination. Choose to send logs to an Amazon S3 bucket.","B":"Enable AWS CloudTrail logging. Specify an Amazon S3 bucket as the destination for the logs.","C":"Use Amazon Athena to query the logs in the Amazon S3 bucket for recipient, subject, and time sent.","D":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch log group. Configure Amazon SES to send logs to the log group.","E":"Use Amazon Athena to query the logs in Amazon CloudWatch for recipient, subject, and time sent."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon SES 配置集，以 Amazon Data Firehose 作为目标。选择将日志发送到 Amazon S3 存储桶。","B":"启用 AWS CloudTrail 日志记录。指定 Amazon S3 存储桶作为日志的目标。","C":"使用 Amazon Athena 查询 Amazon S3 存储桶中的日志以了解收件人、主题和发送时间。","D":"创建 Amazon CloudWatch 日志组。配置 Amazon SES 以将日志发送到日志组。","E":"使用 Amazon Athena 查询 Amazon CloudWatch 中的日志以了解收件人、主题和发送时间。"},"answer":["A","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AC":40,"DE":40,"CE":20},"tags":["Storage","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識・多選項拉鋸・複選"},{"id":524,"question_en":"A company migrated to AWS and uses AWS Business Support. The company wants to monitor the cost-effectiveness of Amazon EC2 instances across AWS accounts. The EC2 instances have tags for department, business unit, and environment. Development EC2 instances have high cost but low utilization. The company needs to detect and stop any underutilized development EC2 instances. Instances are underutilized if they had 10% or less average daily CPU utilization and 5 MB or less network I/O for at least 4 of the past 14 days. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司迁移到 AWS 并使用 AWS 商业支持。该公司希望监控跨 AWS 账户的 Amazon EC2 实例的成本效益。EC2 实例具有部门、业务 单位和环境的标签。开发 EC2 实例成本高但利用率低。该公司需要检测 并停止任何未充分利用的开发 EC2 实例。如果实例在过去 14 天中至少有 4 天的平均每日 CPU 利用率为 10% 或更低，网络 I/O 为 5 MB 或更低，则为未充分利用。 哪种解决方案可以以最少的运营开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure Amazon CloudWatch dashboards to monitor EC2 instance utilization based on tags for department, business unit, and environment. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes an AWS Lambda function to stop underutilized development EC2 instances.","B":"Configure AWS Systems Manager to track EC2 instance utilization and report underutilized instances to Amazon CloudWatch. Filter the CloudWatch data by tags for department, business unit, and environment. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes an AWS Lambda function to stop underutilized development EC2 instances.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to detect low utilization of EC2 instances reported by AWS Trusted Advisor. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function that filters the data by tags for department, business unit, and environment and stops underutilized development EC2 instances.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function to run daily to retrieve utilization data for all EC2 instances. Save the data to an Amazon DynamoDB table. Create an Amazon QuickSight dashboard that uses the DynamoDB table as a data source to identify and stop underutilized development EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 Amazon CloudWatch 仪表板，根据部门、业务单位和环境的标签监控 EC2 实例利用率。创建一条 Amazon EventBridge 规 则，调用 AWS Lambda 函数来停止未充分利用的开发 EC2 实例。","B":"配置 AWS Systems Manager 以跟踪 EC2 实例利用率并将未充分利用的实例报告给 Amazon CloudWatch。按部门、业务部门和环 境的标签筛选 CloudWatch 数据。创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则，调用 AWS Lambda 函数来停止未充分利用的开发 EC2 实例。","C":"创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则以检测 AWS Trusted Advisor 报告的 EC2 实例利用率低的情况。配置规则以调用 AWS Lambda 函 数，该函数按部门、业务部门和环境的标签筛选数据并停止利用率不足的开发 EC2 实例。","D":"创建一个每天运行的 AWS Lambda 函数，以检索所有 EC2 实例的利用率数据。将数据保存到 Amazon DynamoDB 表。创建一个 Amazon QuickSight 仪表板，使用 DynamoDB 表作为数据源来识别和停止利用率不足的开发 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":60,"A":40},"tags":["Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":525,"question_en":"A company is hosting an application on AWS for a project that will run for the next 3 years. The application consists of 20 Amazon EC2 On- Demand Instances that are registered in a target group for a Network Load Balancer (NLB). The instances are spread across two Availability Zones. The application is stateless and runs 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. The company receives reports from users who are experiencing slow responses from the application. Performance metrics show that the instances are at 10% CPU utilization during normal application use. However, the CPU utilization increases to 100% at busy times, which typically last for a few hours. The company needs a new architecture to resolve the problem of slow responses from the application. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 上托管一个应用程序，用于将在未来 3 年内运行的项目。该应用程序由 20 个 Amazon EC2 按需实例组成，这些实 例在网络负载均衡器 (NLB) 的目标组中注册。这些实例分布在两个可用区中。该应用程序是无状态的，每周 7 天、每天 24 小时运 行。 该公司收到用户报告，称应用程序响应缓慢。性能指标显示，在正常使用应用程序期间，实例的 CPU 利用率为 10%。然而，在繁忙 时段，CPU 利用率会增加到 100%，这种情况通常会持续几个小时。 公司需要一种新的架构来解决应用程序响应缓慢的问题。 哪种解决方案能够以最具成本效益的方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Auto Scaling group. Attach the Auto Scaling group to the target group of the NLB. Set the minimum capacity to 20 and the desired capacity to 28. Purchase Reserved Instances for 20 instances.","B":"Create a Spot Fleet that has a request type of request. Set the TotalTargetCapacity parameter to 20. Set the DefaultTargetCapacityType parameter to On-Demand. Specify the NLB when creating the Spot Fleet.","C":"Create a Spot Fleet that has a request type of maintain. Set the TotalTargetCapacity parameter to 20. Set the DefaultTargetCapacityType parameter to Spot. Replace the NLB with an Application Load Balancer.","D":"Create an Auto Scaling group. Attach the Auto Scaling group to the target group of the NLB. Set the minimum capacity to 4 and the maximum capacity to 28. Purchase Reserved Instances for four instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Auto Scaling 组。将 Auto Scaling 组附加到 NLB 的目标组。将最小容量设置为 20，将所需容量设置为 28。购买 20 个 实例的预留实例。","B":"创建一个请求类型为 request 的 Spot Fleet。将 TotalTargetCapacity 参数设置为 20。将 DefaultTargetCapacityType 参数设置为 On- Demand。创建 Spot Fleet 时指定 NLB。","C":"创建一个请求类型为维护的竞价队列。将 TotalTargetCapacity 参数设置为 20。将 DefaultTargetCapacityType 参数设置为 Spot。 将 NLB 替换为应用程序负载均衡器。","D":"创建一个 Auto Scaling 组。将 Auto Scaling 组附加到 NLB 的目标组。将最小容量设置为 4，将最大容量设置为 28。为四个实例 购买预留实例。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":526,"question_en":"Accompany is building an application to collect and transmit sensor data from a factory. The application will use AWS IoT Core to send data from hundreds of devices to an Amazon S3 data lake. The company must enrich the data before loading the data into Amazon S3. The application will transmit the sensor data every 5 seconds. New sensor data must be available in Amazon S3 less than 30 minutes after the application collects the data. No other applications are processing the sensor data from AWS IoT Core. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"Accompany 正在构建一个应用程序来收集和传输工厂的传感器数据。该应用程序将使用 AWS IoT Core 将来自数百台设备的数据发送 到 Amazon S3 数据湖。公司必须在将数据加载到 Amazon S3 之前丰富数据。 该应用程序将每 5 秒传输一次传感器数据。应用程序收集数据后，新的传感器数据必须在 30 分钟内可在 Amazon S3 中使用。没有其 他应用程序正在处理来自 AWS IoT Core 的传感器数据。 哪种解决方案能够以最具成本效益的方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a topic in AWS IoT Core to ingest the sensor data. Create an AWS Lambda function to enrich the data and to write the data to Amazon S3. Configure an AWS IoT rule action to invoke the Lambda function.","B":"Use AWS IoT Core Basic Ingest to ingest the sensor data. Configure an AWS IoT rule action to write the data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose. Set the Kinesis Data Firehose buffering interval to 900 seconds. Use Kinesis Data Firehose to invoke an AWS Lambda function to enrich the data, Configure Kinesis Data Firehose to deliver the data to Amazon S3.","C":"Create a topic in AWS IoT Core to ingest the sensor data. Configure an AWS IoT rule action to send the data to an Amazon Timestream table. Create an AWS Lambda, function to read the data from Timestream. Configure the Lambda function to enrich the data and to write the data to Amazon S3.","D":"Use AWS loT Core Basic Ingest to ingest the sensor data. Configure an AWS IoT rule action to write the data to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams. Create a consumer AWS Lambda function to process the data from Kinesis Data Streams and to enrich the data. Call the S3 PutObject API operation from the Lambda function to write the data to Amazon S3."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS IoT Core 中创建一个主题来提取传感器数据。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来丰富数据并将数据写入 Amazon S3。配置 AWS IoT 规则操作以调用 Lambda 函数。","B":"使用 AWS IoT Core Basic Ingest 提取传感器数据。配置 AWS IoT 规则操作以将数据写入 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose。将 Kinesis Data Firehose 缓冲间隔设置为 900 秒。使用 Kinesis Data Firehose 调用 AWS Lambda 函数来丰富数据，配置 Kinesis Data Firehose 以将数据传输到 Amazon S3。","C":"在 AWS IoT Core 中创建一个主题来提取传感器数据。配置 AWS IoT 规则操作以将数据发送到 Amazon Timestream 表。创建 AWS Lambda 函数以从 Timestream 读取数据。配置 Lambda 函数以丰富数据并将数据写入 Amazon S3。","D":"使用 AWS loT Core Basic Ingest 提取传感器数据。配置 AWS IoT 规则操作以将数据写入 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams。创建消费 者 AWS Lambda 函数来处理来自 Kinesis Data Streams 的数据并丰富数据。从 Lambda 函数调用 S3 PutObject API 操作以将数据写 入 Amazon S3。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":46,"A":46},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The MOST cost-effective qualifier is decisive. AWS IoT Core Basic Ingest sends device data directly to a rule action while bypassing the publish/subscribe message broker, eliminating per-message messaging charges; this is appropriate because no other application subscribes to the topic. The IoT rule action writes to Amazon Data (Kinesis) Firehose, which natively supports an AWS Lambda transformation to enrich records, then buffers and batches the small 5-second records into fewer, larger S3 objects. A 900-second (15-minute) buffering interval is comfortably under the 30-minute freshness requirement. Batching avoids the per-object S3 PutObject and per-record Lambda invocation cost explosion you would get from invoking Lambda on every individual message, making B the cheapest fully managed pipeline.","explanation_zh":"決定關鍵在於「MOST cost-effective」。AWS IoT Core Basic Ingest 將裝置資料直接送入 rule action，繞過 publish/subscribe message broker，省去每則訊息的 messaging 費用；因為沒有其他應用程式訂閱該 topic，這作法很合適。IoT rule action 寫入 Amazon Data (Kinesis) Firehose，Firehose 原生支援以 AWS Lambda transformation 進行資料 enrich，再緩衝並將每 5 秒的小型記錄批次合併為較少、較大的 S3 物件。900 秒（15 分鐘）的 buffering interval 遠低於 30 分鐘的時效需求。批次化避免了對每則訊息都呼叫 Lambda 與每筆 S3 PutObject 所造成的成本暴增，因此 B 是最便宜的全代管管線。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Invoking Lambda per IoT message and writing one S3 object per record (hundreds of devices every 5 seconds) explodes Lambda invocation and S3 PutObject costs, and uses the broker topic unnecessarily. Not most cost-effective.","why_zh":"對每則 IoT 訊息呼叫 Lambda 並為每筆記錄寫一個 S3 物件（數百裝置每 5 秒），會使 Lambda 呼叫與 S3 PutObject 成本暴增，且不必要地使用 broker topic，並非最具成本效益。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Timestream is a time-series database that adds storage/query cost and complexity purely as an intermediate hop, then still needs Lambda to read, enrich, and write to S3. Unnecessary and more expensive for a plain S3 data lake load.","why_zh":"Amazon Timestream 是時間序列資料庫，僅作為中間環節卻增加儲存/查詢成本與複雜度，之後仍需 Lambda 讀取、enrich 並寫入 S3；對單純載入 S3 data lake 而言多餘且更貴。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Kinesis Data Streams suits multiple/real-time consumers and requires managing shards plus a custom consumer Lambda calling PutObject per batch; with no other consumers and a 30-minute window, fully managed Firehose buffer-and-deliver is simpler and cheaper.","why_zh":"Kinesis Data Streams 適合多個/即時消費者，需管理 shards 並自寫 consumer Lambda 逐批呼叫 PutObject；本案無其他消費者且有 30 分鐘窗口，全代管的 Firehose 緩衝後送 S3 更簡單且更便宜。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/data-transformation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/create-destination.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/iot-rule-actions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot-sitewise/latest/userguide/basic-ingest-rules.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識"},{"id":527,"question_en":"A company is collecting data from a large set of IoT devices. The data is stored in an Amazon S3 data lake. Data scientists perform analytics on Amazon EC2 instances that run in two public subnets in a VPC in a separate AWS account. The data scientists need access to the data lake from the EC2 instances. The EC2 instances already have an assigned role with permissions to access Amazon S3. According to company policies, only authorized networks are allowed to have access to the IoT data. Which combination of steps should a solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在从大量 IoT 设备收集数据。数据存储在 Amazon S3 数据湖中。数据科学家在 Amazon EC2 实例上执行分析，这些实例在 单独的 AWS 账户中的 VPC 中的两个公共子网中运行。 数据科学家需要从 EC2 实例访问数据湖。EC2 实例已分配有访问 Amazon S3 的权限的角色。 根据公司政策，只有授权网络才允许访问 IoT 数据。 解决方案架构师应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a gateway VPC endpoint for Amazon S3 in the data scientists’ VPC.","B":"Create an S3 access point in the data scientists' AWS account for the data lake.","C":"Update the EC2 instance role. Add a policy with a condition that allows the s3:GetObject action when the value for the s3:DataAccessPointArn condition key is a valid access point ARN.","D":"Update the VPC route table to route S3 tra®c to an S3 access point.","E":"Add an S3 bucket policy with a condition that allows the s3:GetObject action when the value for the s3:DataAccessPointArn condition key is a valid access point ARN."},"options_zh":{"A":"在数据科学家的 VPC 中为 Amazon S3 创建网关 VPC 端点。","B":"在数据科学家的 AWS 账户中为数据湖创建一个 S3 访问点。","C":"更新 EC2 实例角色。添加一个策略，其中的条件是当 s3:DataAccessPointArn 条件键的值为有效的接入点 ARN 时，允许执行 s3:GetObject 操作。","D":"更新 VPC 路由表以将 S3 流量路由到 S3 接入点。","E":"添加一个 S3 存储桶策略，其条件是当 s3:DataAccessPointArn 条件键的值为有效的接入点 ARN 时，允许执行 s3:GetObject 操 作。"},"answer":["B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AE":54,"BE":46},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B","E"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The data lake bucket is owned by the IoT account, while the EC2 instances run in the data scientists' separate account, so this is a cross-account S3 Access Point pattern that must also restrict access to authorized networks. Contrary to the first analyst, AWS docs explicitly support cross-account access points: you create one by specifying the bucket name and the bucket-owner account ID, and the access point can live in the data scientists' account (B). Created with a VpcConfiguration, the access point's network origin is VPC, so S3 rejects any request that does not originate from the authorized VPC, satisfying the authorized-networks requirement. Because creating an access point does not by itself grant bucket access, the bucket owner must delegate access with a bucket policy on the data lake that allows s3:GetObject when the s3:DataAccessPointArn (or s3:DataAccessPointAccount) condition matches the access point (E). Together B and E provide both cross-account access and network scoping. A+E is incomplete because a bucket policy conditioning on s3:DataAccessPointArn never matches if no access point exists, and the dump's B+C is incomplete because cross-account delegation via the bucket policy (E) is mandatory while tightening the EC2 role (C) is unnecessary given the role already has S3 permissions.","explanation_zh":"data lake bucket 由 IoT 帳戶擁有，而 EC2 執行個體位於 data scientists 的另一個帳戶，因此這是跨帳戶 S3 Access Point 模式，且須限制只有授權網路可存取。與第一位分析師相反，AWS 文件明確支援跨帳戶 access point：透過指定 bucket 名稱與 bucket-owner 帳戶 ID 即可建立，且該 access point 可位於 data scientists 的帳戶 (B)。以 VpcConfiguration 建立後，其 network origin 為 VPC，S3 會拒絕任何非來自該授權 VPC 的請求，滿足授權網路需求。由於僅建立 access point 並不會授予 bucket 存取權，bucket 擁有者必須在 data lake 上以 bucket policy 委派存取，於 s3:DataAccessPointArn（或 s3:DataAccessPointAccount）condition 符合該 access point 時允許 s3:GetObject (E)。B 與 E 同時提供跨帳戶存取與網路限縮。A+E 不完整，因為若從未建立 access point，以 s3:DataAccessPointArn 為條件的 bucket policy 永遠不會符合；dump 的 B+C 也不完整，因為跨帳戶必須有 bucket policy 委派 (E)，而收緊 EC2 role (C) 並非必要，因該 role 已具備 S3 權限。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A gateway VPC endpoint keeps S3 traffic private and is a practical prerequisite for a VPC-origin access point, but on its own it neither delegates cross-account access to the data lake bucket nor scopes access to the IoT data; without the access point and delegating bucket policy it grants nothing.","why_zh":"gateway VPC endpoint 讓 S3 流量保持私有，且是 VPC-origin access point 的實務前提，但本身無法委派跨帳戶存取 data lake bucket，也無法限縮對 IoT 資料的存取；缺少 access point 與委派的 bucket policy 便無法授予任何權限。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Tightening the EC2 role with an s3:DataAccessPointArn condition is identity-based, does not address the network-restriction requirement, and is unnecessary because the role already has S3 permissions; it also cannot enable access from the bucket-owner side.","why_zh":"以 s3:DataAccessPointArn condition 收緊 EC2 role 屬身分型權限，無法處理網路限制需求，且因 role 已具 S3 權限而非必要；它也無法從 bucket 擁有者端啟用存取。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"VPC route tables route traffic to gateway VPC endpoints via prefix lists, not to S3 access points; you cannot point a route table entry at an access point, so this option is invalid.","why_zh":"VPC route table 透過 prefix list 路由到 gateway VPC endpoint，而非 S3 access point；route table 條目無法指向 access point，故此選項無效。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/access-points-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/access-points-vpc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/access-points.html"]},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識・複選・官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":528,"question_en":"A company wants to migrate its website to AWS. The website uses containers that are deployed in an on-premises, self-managed Kubernetes cluster. All data for the website is stored in an on-premises PostgreSQL database. The company has decided to migrate the on-premises Kubernetes cluster to an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster. The EKS cluster will use EKS managed node groups with a static number of nodes. The company will also migrate the on-premises database to an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database. A solutions architect needs to estimate the total cost of ownership (TCO) for this workload before the migration. Which solution will provide the required TCO information?","question_zh":"一家公司希望将其网站迁移到 AWS。该网站使用部署在本地自管理 Kubernetes 集群中的容器。网站的所有数据都存储在本地 PostgreSQL 数据库中。 该公司已决定将本地 Kubernetes 集群迁移到 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 集群。EKS 集群将使用具有静态节点数 的 EKS 托管节点组。该公司还将本地数据库迁移到 Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL 数据库。 解决方案架构师需要在迁移之前估算此工作负载的总拥有成本 (TCO)。 哪种解决方案将提供所需的 TCO 信息？","options_en":{"A":"Request access to Migration Evaluator. Run the Migration Evaluator Collector and import the data. Configure a scenario. Export a Quick Insights report from Migration Evaluator.","B":"Launch AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) for the on-premises database. Generate an assessment report. Create an estimate in AWS Pricing Calculator for the costs of the EKS migration.","C":"Initialize AWS Application Migration Service. Add the on-premises servers as source servers. Launch a test instance. Output a TCO report from Application Migration Service.","D":"Access the AWS Cloud Economics Center webpage to assess the AWS Cloud Value Framework. Create an AWS Cost and Usage report from the Cloud Value Framework."},"options_zh":{"A":"请求访问迁移评估器。运行迁移评估器收集器并导入数据。配置方案。从迁移评估器导出快速洞察报告。","B":"为本地数据库启动 AWS 数据库迁移服务 (AWS DMS)。生成评估报告。在 AWS 定价计算器中为 EKS 迁移成本创建估算。","C":"初始化 AWS 应用程序迁移服务。将本地服务器添加为源服务器。启动测试实例。从应用程序迁移服务输出 TCO 报告。","D":"访问 AWS 云经济中心网页以评估 AWS 云价值框架。从云价值框架创建 AWS 成本和使用情况报告。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":80,"B":20},"tags":["Migration","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Containers"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":529,"question_en":"An events company runs a ticketing platform on AWS. The company’s customers configure and schedule their events on the platform. The events result in large increases of tra®c to the platform. The company knows the date and time of each customer’s events. The company runs the platform on an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster. The ECS cluster consists of Amazon EC2 On- Demand Instances that are in an Auto Scaling group. The Auto Scaling group uses a predictive scaling policy. The ECS cluster makes frequent requests to an Amazon S3 bucket to download ticket assets. The ECS cluster and the S3 bucket are in the same AWS Region and the same AWS account. Tra®c between the ECS cluster and the S3 bucket ­ows across a NAT gateway. The company needs to optimize the cost of the platform without decreasing the platform's availability. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家活动公司在 AWS 上运行票务平台。该公司的客户在平台上配置和安排他们的活动。这些活动导致平台流量大幅增加。该公司知 道每个客户活动的日期和时间。该 公司在 Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) 集群上运行该平台。ECS 集群由 Auto Scaling 组中的 Amazon EC2 按需实例组 成。Auto Scaling 组使用预测扩展策略。 ECS 集群频繁向 Amazon S3 存储桶发出请求以下载票证资产。ECS 集群和 S3 存储桶位于同一 AWS 区域和同一 AWS 账户中。ECS 集群 和 S3 存储桶之间的流量通过 NAT 网关流动。 公司需要优化平台成本而不降低平台的可用性。 哪种步骤组合可以满足这些要求？（选择两个。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a gateway VPC endpoint for the S3 bucket.","B":"Add another ECS capacity provider that uses an Auto Scaling group of Spot Instances. Configure the new capacity provider strategy to have the same weight as the existing capacity provider strategy.","C":"Create On-Demand Capacity Reservations for the applicable instance type for the time period of the scheduled scaling policies.","D":"Enable S3 Transfer Acceleration on the S3 bucket.","E":"Replace the predictive scaling policy with scheduled scaling policies for the scheduled events."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 S3 存储桶创建网关 VPC 端点。","B":"添加另一个使用 Spot 实例 Auto Scaling 组的 ECS 容量提供商。将新的容量提供商策略配置为与现有容量提供商策略具有相同 的权重。","C":"为计划的扩展策略的时间段内的适用实例类型创建按需容量预留。","D":"在 S3 存储桶上启用 S3 传输加速。","E":"将预测扩展策略替换为针对计划事件的计划扩展策略。"},"answer":["A","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AE":100},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"Two cost optimizations fit the explicit constraint of not decreasing availability. (A) A gateway VPC endpoint for the same-Region S3 bucket routes the frequent ticket-asset downloads directly to S3 instead of across the NAT gateway. Gateway endpoints carry no additional charge, while NAT gateways bill per-GB data processing, so this removes that data-processing cost with no availability impact. (E) The company knows the exact date and time of every event, which is the textbook condition for scheduled scaling. Predictive scaling uses ML over recurring historical patterns and can over-provision (extra cost) or mis-time customer-configured one-off events; replacing it with scheduled scaling lets the Auto Scaling group scale out precisely before each known event and scale back down afterward, cutting idle On-Demand capacity cost while still meeting the surge ahead of time, so availability is preserved. The decisive qualifier is 'without decreasing availability,' which rules out shifting load to Spot.","explanation_zh":"在「不可降低可用性」的明確限制下，有兩個符合的成本優化。(A) 為同一 Region 的 S3 bucket 建立 gateway VPC endpoint，讓頻繁的票券資產下載直接連到 S3，而非經過 NAT gateway。Gateway endpoint 不額外收費，而 NAT gateway 會依每 GB 收取資料處理費，因此可在不影響可用性的情況下消除該資料處理成本。(E) 公司確知每個活動的日期與時間，這正是 scheduled scaling 的典型情境。Predictive scaling 依靠 ML 分析重複的歷史模式，對於客戶自行設定的一次性活動可能過度佈建（增加成本）或時機不準；改用 scheduled scaling 可讓 Auto Scaling group 在每個已知活動前精準擴充、結束後縮減，降低閒置 On-Demand 容量成本，同時提前因應流量高峰而維持可用性。關鍵限制是「不可降低可用性」，這排除了把負載轉到 Spot 的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Adding a Spot capacity provider at equal weight moves roughly half the tasks to Spot, which AWS can reclaim on 2-minute notice. During a scheduled event traffic surge that reclamation directly decreases the ticketing platform's availability, violating the stated constraint.","why_zh":"以同等權重加入 Spot capacity provider 會把約一半工作負載放到 Spot 上，而 AWS 可在 2 分鐘通知後回收 Spot。在排定活動的流量高峰期間，這種回收會直接降低售票平台可用性，違反題目限制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"On-Demand Capacity Reservations are billed at On-Demand rates whether used or not; they guarantee capacity but increase, not reduce, cost.","why_zh":"On-Demand Capacity Reservations 無論是否使用都按 On-Demand 費率計費，保證容量但增加而非降低成本。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 Transfer Acceleration adds a per-GB surcharge and is meant for long-distance internet transfers, not same-Region traffic, so it raises cost.","why_zh":"S3 Transfer Acceleration 額外收費且用於長距離網際網路傳輸，非同區域流量，反而增加成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/vpc-endpoints-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-scheduled-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-auto-scaling-predictive-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/cluster-auto-scaling.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"}];
